window.AKK_MY_BELOVED_CONCUBINE_ONLY_WANTS_TO_EAT_MELONS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MY_BELOVED_CONCUBINE_ONLY_WANTS_TO_EAT_MELONS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["A cold wind whirled through the courtyard, plucking the last withered leaf from the old parasol tree.","Rendong scurried back to Yongning Palace, carrying a food box.","Compared to other palaces in the imperial harem, this place was secluded and remote, with somewhat sparse furnishings.","A single charcoal brazier barely managed to warm the room.","Yanshu was warming herself by the brazier. Seeing Rendong return, she immediately asked, \"What are we eating today?\"","Rendong took out the items from the food box one by one, saying, \"We have stuffed shiitake mushrooms, braised duck with bamboo shoots, stir-fried assorted vegetables, eight-treasure tofu, and since it's the Laba Festival today, we also have Laba porridge!\"","Yanshu came to the table, \"I love stuffed shiitake mushrooms the most, and the palace's Laba porridge is delicious too. Not bad at all!\"","As she spoke, she popped a shiitake mushroom stuffed with three-flavored meat filling into her mouth.","Mmm, the flavor was rich and the juice plentiful. The tender meatiness blended perfectly with the slight chewiness of the mushroom - perfect with rice!","Of course, this was thanks to Rendong's nimble feet. If she had walked slowly and let the dishes cool, the taste would have certainly suffered.","The hierarchy in the imperial harem was strict. Higher-ranking concubines had palace maids from the Imperial Kitchen to serve their meals, but Yanshu was only a beauty, so she could only send her own people to fetch food.","There were only eight eunuchs and maids in total at Yongning Palace, and Rendong, who came from Yanshu's family, knew her tastes best. So Rendong was always the one to fetch meals.","\"By the way, mistress,\" Rendong continued, \"I heard there's a New Year's Eve banquet tonight. Earlier, Dewang from the Office of Imperial Treasures was carrying a package to Concubine Zhang's place. Who knows what he was delivering this time.\"","Mentioning this, Rendong felt indignant on behalf of her mistress—","The clothing and accessories of the concubines were all regulated according to their rank. Yanshu's position was low, so naturally, she couldn't compare her attire with the higher-ranked concubines. However, Concubine Zhang, despite having an even lower rank, managed to bribe the palace eunuchs with her wealthy family background, frequently acquiring fine fabrics, jewelry, rouge, and powder from various sources, always trying to outdo her mistress.","\"I think you're actually prettier than all the other ladies,\" she sighed softly, \"If only we had some spare money to grease a few palms, to get you dressed up even better, you'd surely outshine them all.\"","Yanshu, however, was nonchalant, \"Those things are useless. Even if I dressed up like a celestial maiden, His Majesty wouldn't come tonight anyway.\"","Tsk, this was already her third year in the palace, yet she hadn't even caught a glimpse of the Emperor's robe hem.","Speaking of which, the current Emperor could be considered a legendary figure. When the late Emperor's royal line was weak, and the various princes of the clan were eyeing the throne covetously, he, at a young age, fought his way through, inheriting the throne amidst bloody turmoil. He then used just three years to stabilize the country and put the court affairs in order, showing considerable skill.","Most importantly, rumor had it that he was exceptionally handsome, beyond comparison to ordinary men.","However, during these three years, this monarch had never set foot in the harem, and rarely showed his face even at festival banquets.","Yanshu's rank was too low to qualify for an audience with the Emperor, so she hadn't had the chance to verify whether the rumors of his divine beauty were true.","Nevertheless, despite this, the palace concubines had not given up hope. Some formed cliques, others chose sides, and like Concubine Zhang, they exhausted every means possible in hopes of entering the Emperor's line of sight. Everyone except Yanshu.","Hearing her speak like this now, Rendong hurriedly advised, \"Even if His Majesty doesn't come, you could still make an appearance before the Empress Dowager. What if the Empress Dowager takes a liking to you and often calls you to the Palace of Benevolent Peace for a chat? Wouldn't that increase your chances of seeing His Majesty?\"","Yanshu was just putting a golden-brown piece of eight-treasure tofu into her mouth. She mumbled, \"Forget it. Even Noble Consort Zhou is the Empress Dowager's niece, and she's still in the same boat, isn't she? Mmm, this tofu is crispy on the outside and so flavorful inside!\"","Rendong: \"...\"","Ah, with her mistress's looks, if she had even a bit of ambition, she would have probably already risen above the crowd! But all she cared about every day was what to eat and various gossip she heard from who knows where.","Just then, she heard Yanshu say, \"By the way, Duke Cheng'en and his wife have been having a major fight at home these past couple of days. I wonder if Noble Consort Zhou and the Empress Dowager have heard about it.\"","Rendong's eyes lit up, \"Could it be that the Duchess found the Duke's sixth mistress?\"","\"Correct.\"","Yanshu nodded as she ate, \"This Sixth Concubine is indeed quite scheming. She took advantage of her pregnancy to spread rumors, causing quite a stir with the Duchess. But the Duke will always care for his own flesh and blood. The Duchess can't win against his wishes, so the Sixth Concubine will likely be officially brought into the household.\"","Rendong clicked her tongue, \"If the Fifth Concubine had been this cunning last time, she might not have met such a tragic end. Come to think of it, the Duke is getting on in years. He's still full of such lecherous thoughts, isn't he ashamed?\"","\"Men are mostly like that.\"","Yanshu took a sip of Laba porridge, finding it sweet, smooth, and fragrant all the way down to her stomach.","She tasted a piece of duck meat next. Mmm, the imperial chef had perfect control over the heat. The duck was tender and delicious, with bamboo shoot's fresh aroma permeating its texture. The meat was savory without being greasy, perfectly seasoned.","She had transmigrated from the modern world. In her previous life, her health had been poor, and she had been raised on medicine. There were many things she couldn't eat. She barely made it to her youth before succumbing to the torment of illness.","Although she had transmigrated to ancient times in this life, she was grateful to have a healthy body with no worries about food or drink.","Moreover, after entering the palace, she had obtained a gossip system that occasionally provided her with all kinds of fresh, first-hand gossip. Family secrets, harem stories - every day was filled with excitement. It couldn't be more thrilling.","Just then, the system's voice appeared in her head again, [New gossip: The Linwu Marquis's heir isn't actually his.]","Yanshu almost choked on her Laba porridge. [There's such a thing?]","Everyone in the capital knew that the Linwu Marquis only had one son, whom he cherished like the apple of his eye. How could he not be his?","...","After lunch, the cold wind outside blew even fiercer.","Yanshu was in the middle of consuming the juicy gossip about the Linwu Marquis's household when she heard someone outside the door say, \"Is Li Beauty in?\"","The voice belonged to Concubine Zhang, whom Rendong had mentioned earlier.","Yanshu's rank was low, and other concubines disdained to bother with her. She also didn't seek attention from others. This Concubine Zhang was quite different, though. Despite being the lowest-ranking concubine in the palace, she often came to seek validation from Yanshu, who was second from the bottom.","Since the person was already at the door, it wouldn't be polite to refuse. Yanshu had Rendong open the door.","Sure enough, Concubine Zhang stepped into the room and greeted her, \"Sister Li, have you finished your meal? I came by to chat with you as I had nothing else to do.\"","Yanshu smiled politely, \"Please, have a seat. Isn't it cold outside?\"","\"It's alright, I'm wearing thick clothes, so I didn't feel it much.\"","Concubine Zhang smiled sweetly and slowly removed her brocade cloak with dark patterns, which was clearly expensive at first glance. She deliberately adjusted the snow-white sable fur on the brim of her hat before slowly sitting down in a chair. She said, \"There's a New Year's Eve banquet tonight. I heard His Majesty will also attend. Are you ready, sister?\"","As she spoke, the golden plum blossom hairpin on her temples trembled slightly, catching the afternoon sun that streamed into the room, dazzling to the eye.","Rendong was furious inside. Wasn't this Concubine Zhang deliberately coming to mock her mistress's poverty by wearing a new cloak and new jewelry?","However, she saw Yanshu frown, tiredly rubbing her forehead, and hurriedly covering her mouth to cough twice, putting on a weak appearance as she said, \"Unfortunately, I caught a chill yesterday. I'm feeling a bit unwell today, so I'm afraid I won't be able to go tonight.\"","Rendong: \"???\"","Unwell? Hadn't she just devoured a bowl of rice and two bowls of hot porridge earlier?","Concubine Zhang's eyes lit up, but she quickly tried to hide it, saying, \"That's such a pity, it's a rare chance to see His Majesty. I was thinking if you didn't have any jewelry, I could lend you a couple of pieces!\"","Yanshu covered her mouth and coughed twice more, \"Thank you for your kindness, but I'm afraid I won't be able to use them.\"","Probably fearing catching her illness, Concubine Zhang quickly stood up, \"Then please rest well, sister. I won't disturb you any further.\"","With that, she put on her newly made sable fur cloak again and left with her maid.","The room fell quiet. Rendong looked at Yanshu with a pained expression, \"Didn't you hear that His Majesty will be there tonight? What a great opportunity, why are you pretending to be sick?\"","Yanshu was unconcerned, \"Even if I went, I'd be at the very end of the line. With more than ten people between us, His Majesty wouldn't even have time to look at the others, let alone notice me.\"","Rather than watching those boring concubines vying for favor, she'd rather stay in her room and continue consuming gossip. She had only gotten halfway through the juicy story about the Linwu Marquis's wife earlier, and it was just getting interesting!","But Rendong said, \"You are the hope of all the people in our Ande County! Our county has finally produced a palace lady in history, how can you be so unambitious and self-defeating?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She just wanted to be a happy, carefree fish. She couldn't bear such a heavy moral burden, could she?","However, before she could speak, the little palace maid Lianxin entered the room and said, \"Beauty, just now an edict came from the Empress Dowager's palace. The Emperor will be attending in person tonight, and all the ladies are requested to be present at the New Year's Eve banquet in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, there goes any chance of slacking off.","As dusk fell and the lanterns were lit, the palace grounds became a sea of brilliance.","Living far away, with low status and no palanquin to ride in, Yanshu trudged through the cold wind all the way to the Hall of Gentle Ceremony, her little face flushed red from the chill.","Fortunately, the hall was warm, quickly fading her rosy cheeks, which actually left her complexion looking quite nice.","Due to the news of the Emperor's personal attendance, the concubines arrived especially early tonight, all adorned in gold and silver, with powdered faces and rouged lips, looking extraordinarily splendid.","Even Concubine Zhang was dressed more lavishly than when they had met in the afternoon, wearing a palace gown with golden plum blossom patterns, and a golden hairpin adorned with jeweled flowers and butterflies. Her lips were painted bright red, making her look quite eye-catching.","In comparison, Yanshu wore a light lotus-colored jacket and skirt with subtle patterns, her hair adorned only with a pearl dangling ornament, looking so plain as to seem almost pitiful.","Rendong felt quite helpless. She had wanted to properly dress up her mistress, but Yanshu had insisted on light makeup, to the point of having almost no presence at all, so she had no choice but to comply.","Now, Yanshu sat at almost the very end of the banquet seating, and compared to the heavily made-up consorts at the front, she indeed had very little presence.","In contrast, Concubine Zhang at the same table was quite different. Rendong could clearly sense the daggers being glared at her, intentionally or not, by Noble Consort Zhou, Consort Ning, and others seated higher up.","In an instant, it all became clear, and she finally understood her mistress's intentions - to stand out in such an occasion was simply asking to make powerful enemies!","Concubine Zhang was truly bold.","However, Concubine Zhang herself didn't seem to notice, currently sitting upright with perfect posture, displaying her best manners while waiting for the imperial arrival.","In comparison, Yanshu was just there to make up the numbers, listening to the system's gossip while eyeing the desserts on the table, wondering when they could start eating.","Hmm, the pastries at such a grand banquet were clearly different - those lotus cakes looked especially tempting.","Before long, with a cry of \"The Emperor arrives...\", tonight's main character finally made his entrance.","Everyone saw a figure clad in a black dragon robe stride into the hall, tall and imposing, with a face as if carved from stone beneath the golden crown, each step exuding power.","The concubines in the hall, hearts racing, rose in unison to bow and greet him with tender voices, \"We welcome Your Majesty.\"","Yanshu followed suit perfunctorily, but since it was a rare opportunity, she tried to sneak a peek. Unfortunately, she was too far away and could only vaguely make out his straight nose, thin lips, and chiseled chin. He did indeed seem quite handsome.","Just then, with a 'ding' in her ear, the system's voice sounded, [I've got some big gossip about the Emperor.]"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan strode into the hall, raising his eyes to behold what seemed like an ocean of jewels. The ornaments adorning the women's heads and bodies glittered dazzlingly in the lamplight.","The air was thick with the scent of powder and perfume. He slightly furrowed his brow and said softly, \"You may rise.\"","The women complied, returning to their seats. Though they appeared to sit properly, they all secretly cast glances his way.","\"Your Majesty's arrival seems to have made the hall even brighter,\" remarked Lady Zhou, the Noble Consort seated at the front. Yuwen Lan recognized her as the Empress Dowager's niece and his nominal cousin.","Today she was dressed like a large red lantern at the palace gate. Her smile appeared appropriate, but her inner voice was utterly venomous.","[These cheap women have all dolled themselves up to outshine me. It seems I'll need to teach them a lesson about proper etiquette.]","Having been able to hear others' thoughts for three years now, Yuwen Lan was accustomed to such hypocrisy. He merely said flatly, \"I am no lantern. How could I make the hall brighter?\"","A giggle was heard, and another woman nearby said, \"Your Majesty is so witty. But the Noble Consort has always been so eloquent. How did she stumble today?\"","This was Consort Ning. As the niece of the Princess Royal's husband, she had been forcibly sent into the palace by the Princess Royal. Yuwen Lan had met her a few times before and thus remembered her.","Of course, he could also hear this woman cursing Lady Zhou in her mind. [Hmph, she thinks wearing all red will outshine me. She should look in a mirror to see how ugly she is! My multi-treasure ruyi phoenix hairpin is far superior. It was worth every bit of those two thousand taels of silver. Look, His Majesty is glancing this way.]","This was likely the first time the Emperor had truly looked at her since she entered the palace. Consort Ning hurriedly straightened her back and put on a smile to welcome his gaze.","Unexpectedly, the Emperor merely glanced at the top of her head before lowering his brow and saying, \"The ornament on your head seems quite expensive?\"","Consort Ning froze, but Lady Zhou quickly interjected, \"In my opinion, Consort Ning's hairpin must have cost no less than three thousand taels of silver. But the palace recently tightened its budget to support the snow disaster relief in the capital. I wonder where the Office of Imperial Treasures found the money?\"","Consort Ning hastily explained, \"Your Majesty, this, this was a gift from my aunt, the Princess Royal. It didn't come from the Office of Imperial Treasures.\"","She still felt uneasy, unsure if the Emperor would now investigate the Princess Royal's household.","Fortunately, Yuwen Lan said nothing more.","Because apart from the two women near him trading barbs, his ears were constantly bombarded with various voices—","[Hmph, these two stupid women are usually so arrogant. It's good to see them get a taste of their own medicine today.]","[I haven't eaten for three days just to fit into this corset dress. This Jinling brocade is truly exquisite. How could these coarse and clumsy country bumpkins ever catch His Majesty's dragon eye? Your Majesty, please look this way!]","[What if these two fools anger His Majesty and make him leave? I've been practicing my dance for three months and haven't had a chance to perform for His Majesty yet! Idiots, idiots!]","...","The mind-reading ability had its limits, so Yuwen Lan could only hear those nearby, but even these few were noisy enough.","He sipped his tea boredly, truly feeling that reading some official reports in his palace would be better than watching these women perform their tedious drama. If the Empress Dowager hadn't pressured him so much today, he would never have come.","At this moment, Yanshu, seated at the very back, was discussing the latest gossip with her system.","[There's even gossip about the Emperor? What is it?]","System: [The Emperor is impotent.]","Yanshu: [...What?]","System: [The Emperor is impotent.]","Yanshu: [??? Impotent? You mean he can't... perform?]","System: [Exactly right.]","Yanshu nearly spat out her hot tea. [Is that true? You're not joking, are you?!]","System: [? Are you questioning this system's professional standards? Has this system ever joked?]","Yanshu: [But how can this be? He's the ruler of a nation!!!]","System: [Men, you know, they all have their unspeakable troubles. Isn't an emperor still a man?]","Yanshu: [...]","That was true. In the two years she had been gossiping with the system, she had seen all kinds of peculiar men in the world. Cross-dressers, those preferring men, violent types, drunkards, gamblers, and the like were a dime a dozen among the court officials. In comparison, \"impotence\" didn't seem so bad.","But wait...","This impotent one was the Emperor!!! He was her nominal husband!","She was shocked again. [Why are you only telling me such an important thing now?]","System: [This system only just received the information.]","Yanshu: [Then what am I doing in the palace??? Am I supposed to live as a widow for the rest of my life???]","System: [You didn't have much ambition anyway, so what's wrong with living as a widow? A lifetime passes quickly. You'll blink and it'll be over.]","Yanshu: [...]","Was that even human speech? She had finally obtained a healthy body, and now she was supposed to just blink and let it pass?","System: [Knowing is better than not knowing. What's done is done, take some time to process it.]","Yanshu: [...]","After gossiping for so long, this was the first time she had encountered news that concerned herself, and such major news at that. It was inevitable to feel caught off guard, at a loss, and dazed.","So much so that when she tried to take a sip of tea, she didn't grip the cup properly and it fell to the ground with a clear clinking sound.","At this time, the Empress Dowager had not yet arrived and the banquet had not begun, so the hall was still relatively quiet. This sound inevitably drew the attention of many.","The women at the front all turned to look, but upon seeing her unremarkable attire, which was even less eye-catching than the palace maids of Lady Zhou and Consort Li, they paid her no mind and turned back.","Only Concubine Zhang, who was seated at the same long table, said in a low voice, \"Has Sister Li gotten drunk before the banquet even started? I'm afraid His Majesty won't hear you.\"","Yanshu couldn't be bothered to respond.","Now she finally understood why the Emperor never visited the harem. He couldn't even if he wanted to!","At this moment, she only felt a sense of world-weariness, as if she had seen through everything.","Rather than exerting all her energy to fight a life-or-death battle for an impossible goal, it was indeed more comfortable to give up early.","A palace maid brought a new teacup, and everything returned to normal. From his distant seat, Yuwen Lan also withdrew his gaze.","Compared to the women nearby who were dressed like flowers, birds, lanterns, and even feather dusters, he found that clumsy girl to look more comfortable.","But why did she drop her cup? Was it also to attract his attention?","Unfortunately, she was too far away for him to hear her thoughts.","Soon after, an announcement was heard from outside the hall, \"The Empress Dowager has arrived...\"","Yuwen Lan rose to welcome her, and all the concubines in the hall hurriedly bowed, their voices ringing out in unison, \"We welcome the Empress Dowager.\"","Mother and son met near the center of the great hall. Yuwen Lan stopped and said respectfully, \"I welcome you, Mother.\"","His voice, deep yet clear, was indeed pleasant to the ear. Taking advantage of their close proximity, Yanshu quickly stole a glance, finally getting a clear view of his face.","Hmm...","Words like \"majestic as a dragon\", \"graceful as a phoenix\", \"clear and noble\", \"radiant as a jade tree\", \"dazzlingly brilliant\"...","All the phrases she knew from her two lifetimes suddenly flooded her mind.","The rumors were true, he truly was a beautiful man!","But what a pity!","Yanshu sighed inwardly. Such a handsome face, yet unable to be used. What a waste of heaven's gifts!","Yuwen Lan paused.","\"Handsome yet unable to be used\"?","\"A waste of heaven's gifts\"?","What did that mean?","He tried to use his peripheral vision to find the source of these thoughts, discovering it was that clumsy girl from earlier.","Now that she was closer, he could see that she indeed had delicate features and her face wasn't heavily made up with powder.","\"I've arrived late, have I kept you all waiting?\" The Empress Dowager's laughing voice reached his ears.","Yuwen Lan collected himself and said, \"Mother, you must be tired. Please, take your seat.\"","[Tsk, why on earth would he be impotent? Is it congenital? Or was it caused by some trauma later on?]","Yuwen Lan paused again.","This time he heard very clearly. That girl had used the term \"impotent.\"","Indeed, Yanshu had used exactly that word. Because at this moment, she was calling out to her system.","— It was one thing to gossip about others, but this time the big news had exploded right beside her, even concerning her own fate. Add to that his breathtakingly handsome appearance, how could she remain unmoved?","She felt there might still be hope, so she wanted to clarify the reason first.","System: [The cause is currently unknown, but it's probably not congenital.]","Oh? If it wasn't congenital impotence, then perhaps there was still a chance?","Yanshu's eyes lit up, completely unaware of the murderous intent stirring not far away.","Indeed, the moment those two words were heard, a killing intent had already surged in Yuwen Lan's heart.","Besides himself, no one in the palace had ever known about this matter.","How did this woman know?","But in the next moment, he heard her musing, \"Maybe we could try the 'Plain Girl's Secret Scripture' or the 'Marvelous Book of Bedroom Arts'. If those don't work, we could even try 'The Ode to Great Pleasure of Yin-Yang Intercourse between Heaven and Earth'!\"","Yuwen Lan was utterly bewildered.","What did she mean by that?","As the saying goes, even if you haven't eaten pork, you've seen a pig run. Yanshu had consumed so much juicy gossip that these precious and peculiar books were at her fingertips. She vividly remembered that in the last scandalous tale of \"The Illustrious General and the Young Widow,\" the pure and alluring young widow had used the \"Marvelous Book of Bedroom Arts\" to firmly ensnare the fierce male general within her pomegranate skirt.","Tsk, it was truly a passionate and heart-stirring story that engaged both the heart and the body. Even now, thinking about it still made her pulse race.","\"Everyone may rise. Today is a festival, there's no need for excessive formality,\" the Empress Dowager's voice interrupted the delightful reminiscence. Yanshu quickly composed herself and joined the others in expressing gratitude and standing up.","Yuwen Lan concealed the tumultuous waves in his heart and calmly guided the Empress Dowager to her seat.","The banquet officially began, and the palace servants finally presented the dishes. There was sliced chicken with lotus, braised duck with bird's nest, assorted shark fin soup, fire-roasted lamb's head, golden prawns, stuffed crabs, and more. In an instant, the long tables were covered with a dazzling array of delicacies.","Yanshu's greatest virtue was her ability to let things go. Since the situation was already set, there was no use in dwelling on it. She focused all her attention on the delicious food and began eating in earnest.","Because the Emperor had never attended before, there had never been a New Year's Eve banquet in the palace, and she ordinarily wouldn't have qualified to attend other banquets. So today was truly a feast for her taste buds. The sliced chicken with lotus was smooth and tender, the braised duck with bird's nest was fragrant and delicious, a mouthful of the assorted shark fin soup was better than ambrosia, and the fire-roasted lamb's head was simply divine!","Not to mention the crispiness of the golden prawns and the richness of the stuffed crabs...","Every cold dish and hot entrée was stunning. Today's visit had certainly not been in vain!","She watched as Lady Zhou, Consort Ning, and Consort Duan at the front either vied to flatter the Empress Dowager or toasted the Emperor. Consort Li and Consort Wang even took the initiative to offer music and dance, competing for attention and making the banquet atmosphere very lively.","Only she remained in the corner, eating and drinking without a care in the world.","She completely failed to notice that at this moment, the Emperor, who was the focus of the entire gathering, had his attention entirely on her."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan discovered for the first time that someone knew his secret.","He raised his eyes to look at the seemingly inconspicuous woman in the distant corner.","Who was she?","It didn't take long for the concubines to notice that the emperor's gaze seemed to be constantly directed towards one particular area.","Following his line of sight, they saw a small table near the entrance of the hall, where two women were seated. One was as plain as a palace maid, while the other was dressed to rival Noble Consort Zhou and Consort Ning.","Everyone began to speculate silently.","Rendong whispered to Yanshu, \"My lady, doesn't it seem like His Majesty keeps looking in your direction?\"","Yanshu didn't take it seriously and casually replied, \"I doubt it. He's probably looking at Concubine Zhang. She's quite eye-catching!\"","As she spoke, she tasted the newly served West Lake vinegar fish. Mmm, the fish was tender and sweet-and-sour, with hints of crab flavor. It was truly exceptional.","Their voices carried to the side, further confirming Concubine Zhang's suspicions.","Ever since the Empress Dowager had arrived, the emperor had been intentionally or unintentionally looking in this direction. She felt certain that her attire today had finally caught his attention.","The brocade worth a thousand gold per foot, the jeweled hairpin worth ten thousand gold – they were indeed the finishing touches.","However, the distance was still too great. She needed to find a way to make the emperor remember her, not wanting to miss this golden opportunity.","So she called her personal maid Chun'e to bring her pipa, and walked to the center of the hall, saying, \"On this auspicious occasion, this humble concubine wishes to sing a song for Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager, praying for your good health and fortune.\"","Indeed, the pipa was inlaid with mother-of-pearl and gemstones, perfectly complementing her eye-catching attire.","Noble Consort Zhou, Consort Ning, and Consort Li's eyes flickered with hidden fire, their hearts filled with jealousy and resentment.","Yuwen Lan absent-mindedly said, \"Granted.\"","Palace servants quickly brought a round stool. Concubine Zhang sat down with her instrument, her slender fingers plucking the strings as she began to sing in a delicate voice.","\"A straight stalk of purple bamboo, I'll send it to my love to make a flute...\"","To everyone's surprise, Concubine Zhang was singing a folk song from Jiangnan. The melody was graceful and the lyrics were soft and coquettish, sung in the Su Zhou dialect, truly impressive.","When the song ended, the audience couldn't help but applaud.","The Empress Dowager even asked, \"Are you from Jiangnan?\"","The Chief Eunuch of the Ceremonial Office, Hu An, introduced her, \"Reporting to Your Highness, Concubine Zhang's father is the Imperial Textile Commissioner of the Capital. Their entire family are genuine residents of the capital.\"","Concubine Zhang also smiled and said, \"This humble concubine heard that Your Highness enjoys Su Zhou ballads, so I specially learned one or two. My singing isn't good, please forgive me for the offense.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"That was thoughtful of you.\"","As she spoke, she glanced at the emperor out of the corner of her eye, only to see him lift his teacup for a sip, his expression remaining indifferent, still showing no particular reaction.","Suddenly, Consort Ning was heard saying to Consort Li beside her, \"The tune was indeed pleasant, but I couldn't quite understand the lyrics. Consort Li, your hometown is in Jiangnan, right? Please tell us, what was the meaning of the song just now?\"","Consort Li, however, appeared troubled. She looked around and said, \"Well... I'm afraid it might not be appropriate to discuss in such a formal occasion.\"","This statement immediately piqued everyone's curiosity –","Oh my, not appropriate to discuss? What exactly did Concubine Zhang sing about?","Consort Ning laughed, \"What could be so inappropriate? Surely it wasn't treasonous lyrics?\"","Concubine Zhang's face changed color, and she hastily shook her head, \"How could this concubine dare?\"","Consort Li covered her mouth and smiled, \"Oh, it's nothing like that. Consort Ning is just joking. The song is merely crude talk from the countryside, about love and such. It goes something like 'A straight stalk of purple bamboo, I'll send it to my love to make a flute, the flute to the mouth, the mouth to the flute, a little carp wagging its tail, just like my darling's rosy cheeks. Oh my little sweetie...'\"","\"Oh my!\" Consort Li's words were suddenly interrupted by Consort Ning, who covered her ears in mock reproach, \"Consort Li, how could you! How can such language be spoken in this setting? What if it offends the ears of His Majesty and the Empress Dowager?\"","Hearing this, Consort Li hurriedly stood up, putting on a panicked expression as she bowed to the high seats, \"Please forgive this concubine, Your Majesty and Empress Dowager. I have overstepped...\"","Well, since she was merely repeating someone else's words, the blame naturally couldn't fall on her head. So neither the Empress Dowager nor the emperor said anything, but everyone turned their gaze towards Concubine Zhang.","Only Yanshu, holding a bowl of newly served fish soup, was drinking it while inwardly shaking her head –","As they say, the bird that sticks its head out gets shot. One should only take on what they can handle, not come out to show off unnecessarily. Now look at the mess she's in!","How much better it is to just honestly eat like her!","Mmm, this fish soup is sour and spicy, it's really delicious.","Not far away, Concubine Zhang was sitting on pins and needles, caught in an awkward situation. Her earlier pride had vanished into thin air, and she could only hurriedly kneel and say, \"Please forgive this concubine, Your Majesty and Empress Dowager. I learned this from the people at the Imperial Music Bureau. I'm not from Jiangnan, and I only worked hard to learn the dialect to sing well. I didn't know the meaning of the lyrics...\"","Consort Ning and Consort Li didn't speak further, joining the others in watching coldly from the sidelines.","After a moment, it was the Empress Dowager's lady-in-waiting, Zhushu, who came to smooth things over, \"I suppose folk songs are often like this. Concubine Zhang surely meant no harm.\"","As she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager raised her hand slightly, \"Enough. It's a festive day, everyone return to your seats.\"","Concubine Zhang responded and only then dared to stand up, slinking back to her seat with her pipa, thoroughly embarrassed.","Consort Li also sat back down, and when no one was paying attention, exchanged a glance with Consort Ning, their eyes conveying an unspoken understanding.","The palace servants brought out new dishes, and Consort Ning, Noble Consort Zhou, and others continued to vie for conversation with the Empress Dowager, while Yuwen Lan's face remained impassive throughout.","The Empress Dowager, while responding to everyone, glanced once more towards the distant corner, inwardly pondering, could it be that the emperor has taken a liking to the one who's been quietly eating this whole time?","That's truly... an unique eye.","As cold dishes, hot dishes, desserts, and soups came one after another, just as Yanshu was about to eat herself to bursting, the New Year's Eve banquet finally came to an end.","The Empress Dowager rose to leave, and everyone stood up to bow and respectfully see her off.","Yuwen Lan also rose from his seat, and while watching the Empress Dowager exit the hall and board her palanquin, he tried to listen to that girl's inner thoughts.","He heard her burping silently and smacking her lips, thinking, [Everything was so delicious tonight. If only there were more spicy dishes, it would have been perfect. Let's see, today is the eighth day of the New Year, when's the next feast? The Little New Year? Oh my, that's half a month away...]","Yuwen Lan: ???","Why is it all about food?","Then he heard her sigh inwardly, [Since I'm here, I might as well make the best of it. If I can't have sexual pleasure, at least I can enjoy the pleasure of good food.]","Yuwen Lan: ???","What does she mean by that?","What is this \"sexual pleasure\"?","Why are this woman's inner thoughts so... bizarre?","Yuwen Lan almost stopped in his tracks.","However, if he did so, he might startle her.","He held back with all his might, pretending as if nothing had happened, and stepped out of the hall.","Fu Hai, the head imperial attendant, could sense that His Majesty was a bit different tonight.","After leaving the Hall of Gentle Ceremony, although he went to the study to read memorials as usual, he didn't pick up his brush to make any comments for a long time, seeming lost in thought.","Fu Hai was secretly pondering this when he heard the emperor ask, \"Who was sitting at the end tonight?\"","Having served by the emperor's side for many years, Fu Hai quickly answered, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, the one who came out to perform was Concubine Zhang, the daughter of Zhang Tong, the Imperial Textile Commissioner of the Capital.\"","After he finished speaking, he saw that the emperor had no reaction.","So he hurriedly added, \"The one sitting next to Concubine Zhang was Li Beauty from Yongning Palace.\"","At these words, the emperor finally spoke again, \"Where is she from?\"","Fu Hai knew he had guessed correctly and quickly replied, \"This servant remembers that Li Beauty is from Ande County in Qingzhou Prefecture. She entered the palace three years ago through the imperial selection.\"","Qingzhou...","Yuwen Lan pondered silently. That place is hundreds of miles away from the capital, how could she know about his affairs?","Then he heard Fu Hai thinking to himself, [Well, well, looks like this Li Beauty is about to rise in status. Who would have thought that the first one to catch the emperor's eye in the harem would be a mere Beauty?]","Yuwen Lan was disturbed by these thoughts and raised his hand, saying, \"You may go.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty.\"","Fu Hai bowed and retreated, still contemplating in his mind, [What's going on? If he's taken a liking to her, why not summon her to serve? It's getting late, my emperor, a moment of spring night is worth a thousand gold!]","Just as he thought this, he suddenly felt a cold glare from above. Fu Hai shuddered, unable to pinpoint what had offended the emperor. He could only hasten his steps and retreat out of the hall.","Finally, silence fell around him. Yuwen Lan tiredly rubbed his temples. After a moment's thought, he called out again, \"Someone come.\"","This time, it was a member of the Imperial Guard in a fish-scale armor who entered.","\"Go to Ande County in Qingzhou Prefecture and investigate the matter of the imperial selection from that year.\"","The Imperial Guard acknowledged the order and immediately set out to carry it out.","Yuwen Lan picked up the memorial on his desk again, but his mind still couldn't fully focus.","His thoughts kept returning to the woman at the banquet.","— Three years ago, on his way back to the capital, he had fainted due to a sudden thunderclap. When he awoke, he had gained the ability to read minds, but gradually lost the function a man should have...","For years, he had been secretly sending people to gather information and seek medical help, but to no avail.","This was a grave matter, especially for him as the emperor. He had always kept this secret under tight wraps, not even his confidants or close eunuchs knew about it.","So how did that woman know?","Who exactly was she?","Where had things gone wrong?","As his mind became increasingly tangled, he set aside the memorial and summoned another eunuch wearing a round-collared robe.","\"Keep watch over Yongning Palace. I want to know everything, no matter how trivial.\""]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4","paragraphs":["Regardless of how others felt, Concubine Zhang's mood was absolutely dreadful tonight.","Upon returning to Linhua Hall and sitting before her mirror to remove her makeup, she muttered bitterly, \"Tonight, His Majesty's eyes were not on me.\"","Her maid Chun'e hurried to console her, \"Don't overthink it, my lady. If His Majesty wasn't looking at you, do you think he was looking at Li Beauty? Just look at how shabbily she was dressed.\"","\"It was her,\" Concubine Zhang gritted her teeth. \"She dressed that way on purpose. Tonight, everyone was in their finest attire, yet she came looking plain and simple. Didn't that just make her stand out?\"","Chun'e had a sudden realization, \"In that case, Li Beauty is quite cunning, isn't she?\"","Concubine Zhang scoffed, \"She said she wasn't going this afternoon, then showed up dressed like that. Her scheming nature is obvious!\"","Chun'e quickly added, \"As they say, it's the silent dogs that bite. Those who usually keep quiet are often the most formidable!\"","What a silent dog indeed!","Recalling the scene at the banquet, Concubine Zhang grew increasingly resentful.","Now, not only had she made a complete fool of herself, but she had also nearly been accused of great disrespect. Yet His Majesty hadn't spared her a single glance, his eyes fixed solely on Li Yanshu.","Li Yanshu!","A woman from some remote countryside, yet possessing such great skill!","Chun'e voiced her concern, \"If this continues, won't Li Beauty be the first to gain favor?\"","Concubine Zhang jolted at the thought.","With Li Yanshu's looks, if she were to gain favor, what chance would anyone else have?","This cannot happen!","After some thought, she said, \"Go fetch a bag of silver and make a trip to the laundry.\"","The rest of her instructions were whispered into Chun'e's ear, too quiet for anyone else to hear.","Yanshu had enjoyed a satisfying meal at the Hall of Gentle Ceremony, and her body had warmed up. By the time she returned to Yongning Palace, she didn't feel cold at all. After washing up, she crawled into bed and fell asleep.","In her dreams, she once again saw the New Year's Eve feast – spicy hot pot, crispy roast pork, creamy lobster, flame-grilled fish – all the dishes she had longed for but couldn't eat in her previous life.","After a night of drooling in her sleep, early the next morning, while still groggy and half-asleep, she heard a 'ding' from the system.","[There's new development in yesterday's gossip. The Marquis Xiayi, upon hearing that the Linwu Marquis and his wife have fallen out, plans to rekindle an old flame with the Linwu Marquis's wife.]","Hm?","Yanshu immediately perked up. [Does this mean the young master is the Marquis Xiayi's son?]","System: [No, he's not.]","Yanshu's eyes widened. [And he's still not? The Linwu Marquis's wife is truly something else!]","System: [Never mind others, there's gossip about you today.]","Yanshu: [About me? What gossip could there be about me?]","Before the system could respond, Rendong entered the room carrying clothes, and spoke from outside the bed curtains, \"Are you awake, my lady? I've just ironed your clothes. Put them on while they're still warm.\"","In the cold winter days, getting out of a warm bed in the morning was a great challenge, and putting on ice-cold clothes made it even harder. To make her more comfortable, Rendong would warm up her clothes with an iron every morning.","Yanshu made a sound of acknowledgment and sat up, reaching for the clothes while asking the system, [What gossip about me?]","System: [Someone is trying to harm you.]","What?","Just as these words registered, the clothes reached her hands, and she sneezed. She froze.","Someone was trying to harm her?","The next moment, she sneezed again.","This startled Rendong, \"My lady, have you caught a cold? It must be because you didn't have enough blankets last night. I should have added another one...\"","\"I don't think it's a cold,\" Yanshu rubbed her nose and tossed aside the clothes. \"There must be something on these clothes.\"","Rendong paused, \"Could it be peach blossom pollen?\"","Yanshu was allergic to peach blossoms. Any contact would trigger various reactions, from sneezing and nasal congestion to full-body rashes, even difficulty breathing. It was quite severe.","Judging from her current symptoms, it did seem like her old condition was acting up.","Realizing this, Rendong quickly threw the clothes far away, but then wondered aloud, \"But it's winter now, the peach blossoms haven't bloomed yet.\"","Yanshu thought for a moment, \"What about those in the greenhouse at the Imperial Gardens Bureau? I wonder if they've bloomed?\"","Rendong had a sudden realization, \"That's right, the greenhouse at the Imperial Gardens Bureau has all kinds of flowers!\"","But why would peach blossom pollen appear on freshly washed clothes?","Rendong sighed, \"You hardly ever leave your room, and all you care about is eating. How did you manage to offend someone?\"","Yanshu: \"...The way you put it, it's as if I'm nothing but a glutton.\"","Rendong: \"...Well, more or less... *cough*...\"","Seeing Yanshu glare at her, Rendong quickly changed the subject, \"But who could hate you so much to come up with such a nasty idea!\"","Yanshu pondered, \"In this palace, apart from Concubine Zhang, I don't think anyone else even knows me.\"","Hearing this, Rendong thought carefully, \"Every spring when the peach blossoms bloom, you don't go out. It wouldn't be hard to find out about your allergy. Looking at it this way, could it really be Concubine Zhang's doing? But why would she want to harm you?\"","Yanshu was also puzzled, \"Could it be that I ate too much last night and she didn't get enough?\"","Rendong: \"...\"","What kind of bizarre motive was that? Did she think everyone was like her?","\"Maybe she lost face at the banquet last night and wants to take it out on you!\" Rendong said angrily. \"Whatever the reason, we can't let you suffer for nothing. Let's go complain to the Empress Dowager!\"","But Yanshu suddenly spoke sensibly, \"First of all, it's not certain I can even see the Empress Dowager. Right now, we're just speculating. We have no real evidence that it was her. She could easily deny it, and why would the Empress Dowager believe me over her?\"","Rendong paused, then said reluctantly, \"So we're just going to let you suffer in silence? She's just a concubine, but because her family has money and connections, she can harm others as she pleases! Is there no justice in this palace?\"","Ah, how pitiful her beautiful, good-natured mistress who never fought or competed. Just because her family was far away, her father was an honest official, and her family was poorer, she had to suffer bullying in the palace.","The world was truly unfair!","But to her surprise, her usually non-confrontational mistress suddenly gave a mischievous smile and said, \"Who says we're going to suffer in silence?\"","Rendong was taken aback, \"Then what can we do?\"","\"Come here,\" Yanshu beckoned her to lean in closer, \"This is what you're going to do...\"","...","Around noon, Concubine Zhang was leisurely sipping tea when Chun'e hurried into the hall.","Seeing that no one else was around, Chun'e spoke, \"My lady, a royal physician was just called to Yongning Palace. They're brewing medicine now, and the courtyard reeks of it.\"","\"A royal physician?\" Concubine Zhang raised an eyebrow. \"It must be quite serious. I wonder if she's covered in rashes from head to toe?\"","Let's see how she gains favor now!","Chun'e quickly replied, \"I didn't find out about that. Should I go back and check?\"","Concubine Zhang waved her hand nonchalantly, \"Never mind. In that state, you wouldn't be able to see her anyway. How could she show her face to anyone?\"","Chun'e nodded in agreement, \"I heard Rendong say that this illness won't easily go away for ten days to half a month. She won't be able to scheme for a while!\"","This was exactly what she wanted. Concubine Zhang nodded with satisfaction.","Then Chun'e added, \"Oh, and I just heard some fresh gossip.\"","\"What gossip?\"","\"I heard that something happened at Consort Li's aunt's house!\" Chun'e said.","\"Consort Li's aunt's house?\" Concubine Zhang listened impatiently, \"Why so roundabout? Whose house exactly?\"","\"The Linwu Marquis's mansion!\" Chun'e explained, \"Consort Li's aunt is the Linwu Marquis's wife, so isn't the Linwu Marquis's mansion her aunt's house?\"","Concubine Zhang remembered and asked, \"What happened?\"","Chun'e leaned in closer, \"I heard that the Linwu Marquis recently brought home a concubine, which angered his wife. She caused a big scene, but then the servants provided evidence that the Linwu Marquis's wife had been involved with other men for a long time, and quite a few at that!\"","\"Is that so?\" Concubine Zhang's eyes widened in surprise.","Chun'e nodded vigorously, \"Many people in the palace are talking about it. Think about it, my lady. If such a scandal has made its way into the palace, how could it be false?\"","\"That's true!\" Concubine Zhang sneered, \"Serves her right!\"","If it weren't for Consort Li deliberately stirring up trouble last night, she wouldn't have been so embarrassed.","Hmph, everyone in the capital knew that Consort Li's family, the Earl Yongliang's Mansion, was just an empty title with no real power. The whole family relied on this bit of connection through their aunt's marriage. Now, if this marriage falls apart, Consort Li will be in for it!","Thinking of this, Concubine Zhang instructed, \"Keep gathering information. Let me know immediately if you hear anything new.\"","\"Yes, my lady,\" Chun'e nodded quickly.","At that moment, in Yimei Palace, Consort Li was pacing anxiously.","Seeing the young eunuch Zhang Bao hurrying towards her, she quickly asked, \"Have you found out? Where did this news come from?\"","Zhang Bao said, \"I've found out that this rumor was first spread by a palace maid from Linhua Hall to someone at the Imperial Gardens Bureau.\"","Linhua Hall?","The palace maid Lvxiu said, \"Isn't that where Concubine Zhang lives?\"","\"That's right,\" Zhang Bao nodded, \"I heard that Concubine Zhang's family works at the Imperial Textile Factory of the Capital, and she has connections and many acquaintances throughout the palace.\"","\"That wretched woman!\"","Consort Li gritted her teeth, \"Yesterday I merely spoke the truth, and she dares to retaliate? Hah, fabricating stories about my aunt and tarnishing the reputation of Earl Yongliang's Mansion?\"","Lvxiu and Zhang Bao quickly agreed, \"Your Highness, this is a serious matter. We cannot let her off lightly!\"","For a mere concubine to offend a consort who outranks her by several levels - this was simply outrageous!","Consort Li sneered, \"Very well. She loves to talk and sing, doesn't she? Let her taste my wrath!\"","With allergies, one only needs to remove the allergen to recover quickly. So while Yanshu claimed to be ill, she was actually nestled in her palace, eating heartily.","Concubine Zhang, however, was in a different situation.","First, she suddenly began vomiting and having diarrhea in the middle of the night, accompanied by a high fever. After taking bitter medicine for two days, she finally recovered, but her voice became hoarse and rough. When she spoke, she sounded like a burly man with a full beard, which was quite frightening.","In terms of looks, she wasn't particularly outstanding in the harem. The only thing she could rely on was her voice, and now that was ruined. She was furious.","Gritting her teeth, she spent a large sum of money and finally uncovered some clues. It turned out that someone had drugged her, specifically targeting her voice.","In a fit of anger, she wanted to go complain to the Empress Dowager. However, many people in the palace still resented her for stealing the spotlight at the New Year's banquet, and they certainly wouldn't let her have her way...","When Rendong came to report, Yanshu was curled up on the kang bed, writing.","After Rendong finished speaking, she sighed with a mature air, \"The nail that sticks out gets hammered down. It's better to keep a low profile to stay safe!\"","Rendong nodded vigorously, \"She started it by trying to harm others. She deserves it!\"","Then, curious, she asked, \"What are you writing, my lady?\"","Yanshu replied, \"I'm bored, so I'm trying my hand at writing a story.\"","After all, she had consumed so much gossip, each tale more shocking and intricate than the last. Since she had nowhere to share these stories, she might as well rework them into a novel. Who knows, maybe one day she could publish it and make a fortune.","Just as she was about to pick up her brush again, the young palace maid Lianxin entered and reported, \"My lady, the Empress Dowager has sent an edict summoning you to the Palace of Benevolent Peace for a conversation.\""]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5","paragraphs":["The Empress Dowager wanted to see her?","Yanshu was somewhat surprised.","Rendong, on the other hand, was a bit nervous and whispered, \"It couldn't be about Consort Li and Concubine Zhang...\"","—After all, it was she who had spread the news about Consort Li's Aunt by pretending to be a maid from Linhua Hall.","Yanshu calmly replied, \"It probably isn't.\"","Given her relationship with the system, if there were any bad news, it would have informed her already.","Of course, whether good or bad, since the Empress Dowager had summoned her, she had to go. So she quickly got out of bed, changed her clothes, and left.","At that moment, in the study of Qianming Palace, the Imperial Guard was reporting to the Emperor.","\"Your humble servant went to Ande County in Qingzhou and verified that Li Beauty is indeed from Qingzhou. Her father, Li Huaizhi, is the assistant magistrate of Ande County. Her mother, Ms. Zhu, manages the household and serves her mother-in-law. Li Beauty also has a younger brother, Li Tianrui, who is seventeen and passed the county examination this year.\"","\"Li's father is known for his integrity, and the family lives frugally. They have a good reputation locally. During the selection of palace maids, the Ande County magistrate originally intended to send his own daughter to the palace, but because her appearance and character were barely passable, she didn't make it through. So he recommended Li Beauty, who was then chosen by the court officials.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow upon hearing this. That night, among all the women in the hall, only she had left an impression on him.","Of course, this wasn't the main point. He asked, \"Is the Li family native to Ande?\"","The Imperial Guard replied affirmatively, \"The Li family has lived in Ande for generations. We found no evidence of connections with the court or any other states.\"","In other words, the Li family was simply a small local official family in Ande County, without any backing or influence from other powers.","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"Did anything unusual happen on their journey to the capital?\"","The Imperial Guard answered, \"After investigation, we found no unusual incidents. The only thing worth mentioning is that it rained for a few days during the journey, which delayed them for a bit.\"","Delayed for a few days...","Yuwen Lan pondered silently. Could it be possible that the girl sent into the palace wasn't actually from the Li family? Had she been switched during the journey?","He turned to another small eunuch in the hall, Fu Bao, \"What about you?\"","Fu Bao quickly responded, \"Your Majesty, since entering the palace, Li Beauty has been cautious and low-profile. She rarely leaves her quarters, spending most of her time in Yongning Palace. She doesn't socialize with others; only Concubine Zhang occasionally visits her.\"","He paused briefly, glancing at the Emperor, and seeing no reaction, continued, \"However, a few days ago, Li Beauty fell ill and didn't leave her room. No one went to see her.\"","Yuwen Lan asked, \"What illness?\"","Fu Bao replied, \"An allergic reaction to peach blossoms.\"","Peach blossoms?","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"Where are there peach blossoms at this time of year?\"","Fu Bao explained, \"Your Majesty may have forgotten, but there are peach blossoms in the greenhouse of the Imperial Gardens Bureau. They even sent some to the Empress Dowager a couple of days ago.\"","Yuwen Lan pondered again. If she often stayed in Yongning Palace, how could she have an allergic reaction to peach blossoms from the Imperial Gardens Bureau?","\"However, even when Li Beauty was ill, her appetite remained good. She finished all four dishes and soup at every meal these past few days,\" Fu Bao added.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He couldn't help but recall the inner thoughts he had heard during the New Year's Eve banquet—\"If I can't have happiness in love, at least I can enjoy good food.\"","What kind of woman was she exactly?","What was her true purpose for entering the palace?","Why had their investigation failed to uncover any abnormalities?","As he was deep in thought, Fu Bao suddenly added, \"Oh, Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager just summoned Li Beauty.\"","\"Hmm?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. What did the Empress Dowager want with her?","At that moment, in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu was alone with the Empress Dowager.","After arriving, she had honestly answered the Empress Dowager's questions about her age, her family's hometown, and her parents' occupations.","Just as she was about to speak again, a voice announced from outside, \"His Majesty has arrived...\"","The Emperor was here?","It was worth noting that it was currently early afternoon, a time when the Emperor was usually busy reviewing memorials in his study. Everyone in the hall was somewhat surprised.","In the blink of an eye, he had entered the hall, dressed in a vermilion dragon robe, his hair bound with a golden crown, making his features appear even more handsome and refined.","Everyone hurriedly bowed, \"We welcome Your Majesty.\"","Yanshu felt a bit dazed. What kind of luck had she stumbled upon today? Not only was it her first time in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, but she even encountered the Emperor?","Empress Dowager Zhou glanced discreetly at Yanshu, then asked Yuwen Lan, \"How is it that Your Majesty has found time to visit today?\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"I had just grown weary of reading memorials and realized it had been several days since I last visited Mother Empress, so I came over.\"","As he spoke, he ordered everyone to rise, his gaze sweeping over Yanshu.","She was indeed here.","Empress Dowager Zhou smoothly said, \"A while ago, I received two snuff bottles from Qingzhou. Remembering that Li Beauty's family is from Qingzhou, I called her over to chat.\"","Yanshu thought to herself, the Empress Dowager was certainly quick to apply what she had just learned. She had only just asked about her family's hometown and was already putting that information to use. Truly worthy of the title \"Champion of Palace Intrigue\"!","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What did \"Champion of Palace Intrigue\" mean?","Was it a compliment to the Empress Dowager's capabilities?","Of course, this wasn't the main point.","He looked at her and asked in a calm voice, \"Which part of Qingzhou are you from?\"","Yanshu was startled. Was the Emperor speaking to her?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Emperor?","Well, it was rare to hear a palace consort refer to him like that in their thoughts.","Rendong, who had come with Yanshu, was inwardly rejoicing, [Oh, heavens! His Majesty is finally speaking to my mistress!!! My mistress is about to rise to power and become the most favored in the harem!!! People of Ande County, our mistress has brought glory to us all!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What was all this about?","However, based on this, it seemed her background should be genuine?","Yanshu answered, \"This humble consort is from Ande County in Qingzhou.\"","As she spoke, she secretly glanced at him and couldn't help but exclaim inwardly, [He's even more handsome up close! Isn't this what they call a perfect face? It's flawless from every angle!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","\"Angle\"? \"Perfect face\"?","What did these mean?","Why couldn't he fully understand this woman's inner thoughts?","Then he heard her sigh in her mind, [What a waste! Heavens, how can you create such a handsome man and make him impotent? Don't you have a conscience?!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Alright, feeling stimulated once again, he finally remembered the main issue at hand and asked her, \"What does your family do, and who are the members of your household?\"","Yanshu answered honestly, like an innocent little rabbit, lowering her head, \"My father is the assistant magistrate of Ande County. My family also includes my grandmother, my mother, and a younger brother.\"","In her heart, however, she cursed, [How dare you ask? Why did you have to hold a selection for palace maids? Separating us from our families! How would you feel if you couldn't see your parents for three years?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What did she mean by \"How dare you\"???","This was the most disrespectful thing he had heard so far!","He should have her arrested on the spot!","But if he did so, it would alert others to his suspicions.","And he still hadn't heard the answers he wanted to know.","So he held back, trying hard to maintain a normal expression, and said, \"Ande is quite far from the capital. The journey must have been difficult.\"","As soon as he spoke, the entire hall was shocked.","How long had it been since His Majesty had spoken so much to a consort!!!","He even showed concern about the difficult journey to the capital???","It was well known that in the past, even Consort Zhou could barely get a glance from him!","Everyone couldn't help but look at Yanshu.","They saw her with a demure expression, saying, \"Even if it were a journey of a thousand mountains and rivers, to be by Your Majesty's side is a joy beyond measure.\"","[To hell with that! The journey took a whole month! That stupid county magistrate sacrificed others' happiness for his own glory and wealth, causing me to live as a widow in this prison. If I ever get the chance, I'll make him pay!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, he was hardly surprised anymore. This woman appeared obedient on the surface, but her heart was full of rebellion.","Of course, he couldn't hear the system talking to Yanshu at that moment, [First of all, as a consort, if you want to rise above others, you must gain the Emperor's favor.]","Yanshu: [...]","This task was indeed quite challenging.","Suddenly, an idea struck her. She remembered that besides the \"True Classic of the Plain Girl\" and the \"Extraordinary Book of the Bedchamber,\" there was also a set of rejuvenating acupuncture techniques that were said to be very effective. It was rumored that an emperor from a previous dynasty had used these techniques for health preservation, remaining as strong as a young man even in his fifties and sixties...","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched as he heard this. Re-rejuvenating acupuncture techniques???","How did she even know about such things?","He struggled to keep his handsome eyebrows from jumping up and spoke again, \"How long has your father been in office? Has he always served in Ande?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Your Majesty, as far as I can remember, my father has been the assistant magistrate in Ande County for over a decade without change.\"","Alas, her poor father was upright and honest his whole life, never one for scheming or flattery, which is why he couldn't even become a county magistrate. If it weren't for being bullied by that dog of an official, why would she have entered the palace in the first place?","Oh Emperor, Emperor, don't just look at the capital city. There are plenty of corrupt officials in the small towns too.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How did things suddenly become normal again?","These words did make some sense, though.","Just then, he heard the Empress Dowager ask him, \"By the way, there's been quite a commotion these past two days about the Linwu Marquis's household. I wonder if it's true or false?\"","Yuwen Lan snapped back to attention and said, \"It must be true. Today, the Linwu Marquis came to the palace to accuse the Marquis Xiayi of seducing his wife. He's demanding that his wife be stripped of her noble title and that they be divorced.\"","Thinking about it still gave him a headache. He couldn't help but pinch the bridge of his nose.","But then he heard that girl inwardly clicking her tongue, [The Marquis Xiayi and the Linwu Marquis's wife had a relationship before marriage, not an affair after marriage. The Linwu Marquis has no grounds for accusation!]","\"???\"","What? They had a relationship before marriage?","How did she know about those two?","But before he could process this, he heard her sigh in her heart again, [The Linwu Marquis would be better off putting his energy into trying to have another son. If he ever finds out that even the Heir Apparent isn't his, he'll be devastated!]","Yuwen Lan was severely taken aback.","What? The Linwu Marquis's Heir Apparent isn't his?","And how on earth did she know this???"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6","paragraphs":["How strange!","How could a palace concubine know the secrets of the Linwu Marquis' household?","Yuwen Lan looked at Yanshu in astonishment.","He was so shocked that he forgot to restrain himself, making his gaze too direct and lingering for too long.","It made Yanshu uncomfortable, and she couldn't help but wonder, why is this person staring at her?","Of course, the reason for his staring was known only to Yuwen Lan himself, and no one else.","However, everyone in the hall had noticed.","The Empress Dowager suddenly said to Yanshu, \"You've been out for a while now. Go back and rest early. I have a few words to say to His Majesty.\"","Yanshu felt as if she had been granted amnesty. She hurriedly bowed to the two of them, \"This concubine takes her leave.\"","After speaking, she left the hall with her head bowed, as docile as the small flowers and grass in the courtyard's garden.","But Yuwen Lan knew she was no small flower or blade of grass.","Only after watching her leave the hall and the cotton curtains close again did he barely manage to withdraw his gaze, his mind still in shock.","What was the deal with this woman?","\"As the saying goes, even a wise judge finds it hard to settle family disputes,\" the Empress Dowager began, \"Your Majesty need not worry too much about the affairs of the Linwu Marquis' household. If those two truly cannot get along, let them divorce.\"","Yuwen Lan came back to his senses, \"Mother is right, that was my intention as well.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"It's getting late. Would Your Majesty like to stay for dinner?\"","Yuwen Lan quickly said it wasn't necessary, \"There are still a few memorials in the imperial study. I won't disturb Mother any further.\"","With that, he rose and left the hall.","The hall fell silent. The Empress Dowager moved to the west window, with her lady-in-waiting Zhu Shu following to attend to her. Zhu Shu said, \"His Majesty seems to have a different attitude towards Consort Li...\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"His Majesty is at the right age to have an heir.\"","Zhu Shu agreed and dared not say more.","However, she heard the Empress Dowager add, \"Keep your mouths shut. Don't gossip about the affairs of my palace outside.\"","Everyone in the hall quickly agreed.","Returning from the Palace of Benevolent Peace, it had been just over an hour, and the sky was already pitch black.","After hastily approving a few memorials, Yuwen Lan had no appetite for dinner. As the night deepened, he lay on his large dragon bed without a hint of sleepiness.","He had been thinking for half an afternoon and an entire evening, yet he still couldn't make sense of it.","—Since she was indeed Li Yanshu herself, and there was nothing unusual about the Li family background, how did she know so many things that ordinary people didn't?","It's worth noting that she had been in the palace for three years and had never left. How could she know the secrets of officials' families that even he, the emperor, didn't know?","Could it be... that there was some secret in the Yongning Palace?","From childhood to adulthood, Yuwen Lan had seen all kinds of storms and strange occurrences, but this one thing he just couldn't figure out. It caused him to toss and turn, unable to fall asleep.","As time ticked by, the palace had fallen into complete silence.","He decided to get up, put on his clothes, and leave Qianming Palace.","Before long, Yuwen Lan had arrived at Yongning Palace.","Standing on the roof of the hall, he gently lifted a glazed tile and peeked down, just in time to see that woman sitting in front of a mirror talking to her maid—","Rendong was still excited, \"His Majesty spoke so much with you today, more than with any other mistress in the palace. He must have taken a liking to you!\"","Yuwen Lan had seen plenty of such wishful thinking and remained unmoved.","Yanshu, however, sighed, \"You don't understand. He won't take a liking to me.\"","Rendong thought she was just being modest and smiled, \"You're so beautiful, and His Majesty is in his prime. Why wouldn't he like you? Isn't there a saying, 'A beautiful woman can make a man do anything'?\"","Yanshu didn't say anything, but sighed inwardly.","[...That gentleman in his prime isn't a normal man. No matter how beautiful she is, it won't make a difference!]","The certain someone on the roof twitched his brow, trying hard to calm himself down.","However, if this woman didn't even tell her close maid, did it mean that this secret was known only to her?","In the hall, Yanshu sighed again, \"Not only will His Majesty not like me, it might even bring trouble.\"","Goodness, the harem was full of hungry wolves, each with eyes glowing green with hunger. If they knew the emperor had spoken a few words with her, a mere beauty, wouldn't they rush over to devour her immediately?","They wouldn't even spit out the bones!!!","Rendong disagreed, \"Anyway, it was the Empress Dowager who called you today. It's not like you deliberately sought attention.\"","Yanshu rolled her eyes at her through the mirror, \"Do you think they care whether I sought attention or not?\"","That was true.","Rendong had nothing more to say, so she changed the subject, \"Why did the Empress Dowager suddenly ask you to leave?\"","Yanshu said, \"Perhaps she doesn't want His Majesty talking to any woman other than her niece?\"","Rendong continued, \"Then why did the Empress Dowager call you in the first place? Really...\"","Yanshu also frowned, \"Exactly.\"","First, the Empress Dowager summoned her out of the blue, then the emperor suddenly appeared...","What game were this mother and son playing?","Unable to figure it out, she decided to summon the system first, [System, if anyone is going to harm me again, you must tell me in advance.]","System, [No problem.]","Yanshu pondered in her mind that living in constant fear of retaliation was not a long-term solution. She should start planning early.","Was there still hope of leaving the palace and becoming an ordinary person?","The certain someone on the roof raised an eyebrow. Thinking of running away?","Just then, several palace maids were seen carrying a bathtub into the room, followed by buckets of hot water being poured in. Instantly, hot mist filled the air.","—Yongning Palace was small and unlike larger palaces, it didn't have underfloor heating. Only this main room was somewhat warm, so Yanshu had to bathe like this in winter.","Her hair had already been undone earlier, and taking advantage of the steam, she quickly began to undress.","Yuwen Lan didn't avert his gaze.","Although there was some steam in the room, it didn't obstruct the view.","In his line of sight, the young woman removed her jacket, silk skirt, and undergarments one by one, revealing her exquisite true form.","Soft white snow covered miles of rivers and mountains, with a touch of red plum at the peak of the mountains, a feast for the eyes.","Who would have thought that someone who ate so much every day would have such a slender waist? It seemed as if his hand could encircle it in one grasp.","...","Since losing that ability, he had deliberately avoided women, and this was the first time he had seen such a sight.","He had to admit, it was indeed captivating.","Of course, he didn't get to look for long, as the young woman dove into the water like a fish.","She muttered softly, \"So cold, so cold!\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. He didn't feel cold in the chilly wind, how cold could she be in hot water?","Yanshu was truly a bit cold.","Besides the fact that it was indeed cold today, she also felt a constant chill seeping into the room.","She muttered to herself, \"Why does it feel like there's a draft somewhere?\" As she spoke, she began to look around.","Just as she was about to look up at the ceiling, Yuwen Lan quickly dodged.","It was just a small gap, and she couldn't have discovered anything. But for some reason, he suddenly felt guilty, like a thief.","Not long after, he leapt down and left.","Soon after, Yanshu quickly finished her bath and came out, dried herself off, put on her nightclothes, and swiftly burrowed into her blankets.","Rendong instructed the palace maids to come in and remove the water and bathtub. She heard Yanshu ask from under the covers, \"Why do I feel so chilly? Tomorrow, have someone check if there's a draft somewhere.\"","Rendong agreed, \"I'll have Xiao Dongzi check in the morning. You should sleep now.\"","She tucked two hot water bottles into the blankets and closed the bed curtains.","Fresh from her bath, Yanshu felt most comfortable and fell asleep hugging the warm water bottles.","Yuwen Lan returned to his bedchamber when the night was half over.","He had early court tomorrow; if he didn't sleep now, he might as well not sleep at all.","However, when he closed his eyes, his mind was filled with the scenes he had just witnessed.","It made him toss and turn, even more unable to fall asleep.","Yanshu slept soundly through the night and woke up the next day. Rendong had already called Xiao Dongzi to climb onto the roof to check.","However, after a thorough inspection, they found nothing unusual.","Rendong laughed at her, \"My lady, you're living in the imperial palace, not a thatched cottage. How could there be a draft?\"","Yanshu had nothing to say, but she still felt something was off. Last night while bathing, she definitely felt a cold air circulating in the room.","The system chimed in, [Someone was peeping at you last night.]","Yanshu was stunned, [What? Someone was peeping at me???]","System, [That's absolutely correct.]","Yanshu was full of questions, [Why didn't you tell me earlier?]","System, [You didn't ask me last night.]","Yanshu felt like spitting blood, [You don't speak unless I ask? Didn't we agree that you'd warn me in advance of any danger?!!]","System, [There was no danger, thank you.]","Yanshu, [??? Being peeped at isn't dangerous?]","System: [It's just a peek, no harm done. That's all for now, this system is taking a break today.]","Yanshu: [??? Hey, since when do you get breaks???]","However, no matter how much she raged, the system remained silent.","Yanshu coughed up some blood, and had no choice but to ponder on her own—","The system said there was no danger, could it be that the one peeking at her was a eunuch?","Ugh... that's still disgusting!","But without evidence, everything was just speculation, and it wasn't good to make a fuss.","After much thought, she could only be more vigilant herself.","The busy day passed quickly, and night fell once again.","In the deep of night, Yuwen Lan once more left his sleeping chambers.","With the mystery unsolved, he certainly wouldn't be able to sleep tonight, so he might as well come investigate again.","However, today that girl seemed to have gotten smarter, sending young eunuchs to patrol the courtyard.","He couldn't get on the roof again, so he slipped into the hall when no one was looking.","At this time, Yanshu was lying in wait behind the bed curtains.","She had thought about it all day and decided to catch the thief herself tonight.","So she went to bed early but didn't dare close her eyes, focusing all her energy on listening for any movement.","Just as she was about to doze off, her eyelids fighting to stay open, she suddenly heard faint footsteps outside the curtain.","She jolted awake, immediately grabbing a wooden stick and getting out of bed.","Quietly hiding by the door, she waited for the footsteps to come close, then raised the stick to strike.","But before she could succeed, her arm was swiftly caught.","She was startled and about to scream, but as soon as she opened her mouth, it was covered.","The other person seemed to be tall and strong, one hand gripping her arm, the other covering her mouth, leaving her helpless.","But Yanshu refused to submit. She twisted her body vigorously, trying to break free.","Her soft body, fragrant with a warm scent, fluttered like a fish in his arms. Yuwen Lan instinctively tightened his grip, while his mind inappropriately recalled the scene he had witnessed the night before.","Lost in thought, he suddenly felt a sharp pain in his palm. He quickly snapped back to reality, only to find that the girl was actually biting him."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7","paragraphs":["At that moment, Yanshu had only one thought in her mind: to bite this perverted bastard to death!","How dare he peep on the emperor's concubines, and even enter their chambers directly? Such an audacious lecher must be severely punished!","She used all her strength, biting down with full concentration and without mercy, until the intruder finally couldn't take it anymore and spoke in a low voice, \"It's me, the Emperor.\"","...Huh?","This voice... why did it sound familiar?","It seemed like she had just heard it somewhere.","She froze, looking up to see the intruder's face.","There was no light in the room at this time, but fortunately, the moonlight was decent. As she barely made out the outline of his face, she was completely stunned.","Yuwen Lan was finally freed and quickly pulled his hand out of her mouth.","The next second, Rendong's voice came from outside, \"My lady? Are you alright?\"","Yanshu quickly came to her senses and hurriedly said, \"It's nothing, I just got up to drink some water. You don't need to come in.\"","Rendong made a sound of acknowledgment and went back to sleep.","Yanshu continued to stare in shock at the tall man before her, stuttering, \"Y-Y-Your Majesty, w-why are you here?\"","Yuwen Lan had already prepared an excuse and said with a straight face, \"I came to check on you.\"","Yanshu was full of questions, \"W-w-why would you come to check on this humble servant?\"","Yuwen Lan deliberately probed, \"You don't know why I came?\"","Yanshu shook her head in confusion, \"N-n-no, I don't.\"","[Heavens, what kind of game is this? Sleepwalking?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Unable to detect anything unusual for now, he had no choice but to lie again with a straight face, \"I like you.\"","\"What???\"","Yanshu felt as if she had been struck by lightning, [Even if he's impotent, he can still like women?]","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched, and he was on the verge of anger.","System: [He may be impotent, but he's not gay. Why can't he like women?]","Yanshu: [...Is that so?]","System: [That's right. He already has a defect, you shouldn't discriminate against him.]","Yanshu: [...I'm so sorry, Emperor. You're already so pitiful, I shouldn't discriminate against you. My apologies.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What was this all about now?","Then he heard her muttering in her mind, [But why does he like me? Shouldn't an iron-blooded emperor like those devastatingly beautiful women? Although I consider myself quite good-looking, I don't think I qualify as the type to bring ruin to a nation or cause chaos...]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","At a moment like this, how could she still be pondering such nonsense?","He couldn't help but say, \"What? Are you not happy that I like you?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, that's right, is it a good thing to be liked by you? One wrong move and I'll become the target of the entire harem.","But outwardly, she could only respectfully say, \"This humble servant wouldn't dare. This humble servant is overwhelmed.\"","Yuwen Lan let out a light snort, \"You are audacious.\"","All the women in the harem were dying for him to look at them even once, yet she was the only one who disdained him.","Yanshu shrank back a little, but mustered up the courage to ask, \"This humble servant doesn't understand, why has Your Majesty appeared in such a manner?\"","Yuwen Lan casually lied, \"The gates have already been locked. I didn't want to disturb others.\"","The palace rules were strict. Every night at the hour of Hai, the palace gates were locked on time, and no one was allowed to move about freely. Even if the emperor wanted to come to the harem, he would have to summon the eunuch in charge of the keys to open the doors.","This reason seemed somewhat credible, so Yanshu didn't ask further. However, she suddenly remembered something very important and hurriedly asked, \"This humble servant didn't know it was Your Majesty earlier. Is Your Majesty's hand... alright?\"","Yuwen Lan furrowed his brows and said, \"It hurts.\"","Yanshu was startled and quickly took out the bedside lamp to examine it. She saw that his hand was already swollen, and blood had seeped out.","Tsk, she had indeed bitten down hard earlier.","She was so frightened that she immediately knelt down to beg for forgiveness, \"This humble servant d-d-didn't know it was Your Majesty. Please, please forgive this humble servant. Should I summon the imperial physician for you?\"","Yuwen Lan said with a stern face, \"What crime would you be charged with if the imperial physician came?\"","Yanshu paused.","Indeed, biting the emperor was a capital offense. If the imperial physician came, wouldn't she be walking right into a trap?","Tsk, what rotten luck! Who in their right mind would peep and enter someone's room in the middle of the night? Isn't that what a pervert would do?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Although he didn't know what \"pervert\" meant, he vaguely guessed it wasn't a good word.","Then he heard her say, \"This humble servant didn't mean to bite you. This humble servant thought it was a lecher...\"","\"...\"","This was indeed not a pleasant word to hear. He could only say, \"Forget it, I'll go back and bandage it myself.\"","With that, he turned to leave.","Yanshu hurriedly bowed, \"F-farewell, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan paused and turned back to look at her, \"Don't speak of this to anyone.\"","Yanshu quickly shut her mouth and nodded vigorously.","All the way back to his bedchamber in Qianming Palace, Yuwen Lan lay on the dragon bed and only then realized that the wound on his hand was quite painful.","So he got up and called out, \"Someone come.\"","Fu Hai responded immediately, but before he could speak, he caught sight of the wound on the emperor's hand and his eyes widened, \"Your Majesty...\"","Yuwen Lan raised his hand to stop him and only said, \"Bring the wound medicine.\"","Fu Hai could only comply and hurried to fetch the medicine, not daring to disturb anyone along the way.","As the high-quality wound medicine was applied to the injury, it felt cold with a slight burning sensation. Yuwen Lan furrowed his brows slightly as he endured it, his mind involuntarily recalling what had happened earlier.","The more he thought about it, the more perplexing it seemed—","What exactly had he done when he went there tonight?","He hadn't discovered anything useful, but instead ended up with an injury.","That girl had a soft body, but quite a strong bite.","Was it because of what she ate?","As he was lost in these random thoughts, he suddenly heard Fu Hai, who was bandaging his wound, pondering in his mind, [Oh my, this wound on His Majesty looks like a human bite. Look at these small teeth marks, could it be from a woman??? Good heavens, what was His Majesty up to earlier...]","\"Keep your mouth shut,\" he said sternly.","Fu Hai was startled and quickly complied.","After the bandaging was done, he waved his hand to dismiss everyone.","Lying back on the bed, he still couldn't sleep. He couldn't help but ponder again.","Judging from her reaction tonight, that girl didn't seem to have much courage, so it was unlikely that she was a spy or anything of the sort.","But he still hadn't found the answer he was looking for.","Early the next morning, Noble Consort Zhou had just finished washing up and applying her makeup, not even having had time to eat breakfast, when she saw Consort An leading Consort Wang to pay her a visit.","After hearing what the two reported, Noble Consort Zhou was surprised and suspicious, \"The Empress Dowager summoned Li Beauty the day before yesterday? And His Majesty was there too? How come I haven't heard about this?\"","Consort Wang insisted, \"How dare this humble servant lie to you? The Empress Dowager issued an edict not to spread word of this matter. If it weren't for my palace maid Cuiyan finding out from her fellow townsman in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, even I wouldn't have known.\"","Noble Consort Zhou paused, \"The Empress Dowager even kept it from me?\"","Then she heard Consort An say, \"I heard that His Majesty spoke several sentences to Li Beauty, and even specifically inquired about her father's position. This is probably unprecedented in the harem... The Empress Dowager is likely trying to protect her.\"","Noble Consort Zhou was burning with anger. That was her own aunt, yet she was protecting an outsider no one had even heard of?","Consort Wang added, \"Indeed, this Li Yanshu must have used some trick to calculate so accurately, managing to see His Majesty directly. Her luck seems a bit too good, doesn't it?\"","Hearing this, Noble Consort Zhou's jealousy flared up even more.","Relying on her relationship with the Empress Dowager, she visited the Palace of Benevolent Peace almost daily. Yet in three years, she had barely managed to see the emperor a few times. Even on those rare occasions when they did meet, the emperor said nothing to her beyond \"You may rise.\"","What right did that Li Yanshu have!","She gritted her teeth and said, \"Who is this Li Yanshu? I've never even noticed her before!\"","Consort An said, \"This humble servant hasn't paid attention to her either. Wasn't she the one sitting at the same table as Concubine Zhang during the New Year's Eve banquet the other day?\"","Consort Wang quickly nodded, \"Yes, it's her. That day she deliberately dropped her spoon, causing everyone to look at her.\"","Noble Consort Zhou sneered, \"No wonder, she's quite the schemer!\"","Consort An coughed, \"These people from the backwoods naturally try every means to stand out.\"","She then instructed Consort Wang, \"You're not far from her. Keep a close eye on her these days, and remember to report any movements to the Noble Consort.\"","Consort Wang quickly agreed, \"This humble servant understands.\"","Noble Consort Zhou then looked at Consort An, \"We can't let someone like her have it easy.\"","Consort An also quickly agreed.","Having spent a night worrying and fearing, Yanshu woke up a bit late.","With dark circles under her eyes, her mind was filled with thoughts of biting the emperor last night. She wondered if the emperor's anger had subsided and if anyone had discovered his wound.","Rendong was helping her with her hair when she saw the little palace maid Lianxin running in to report, \"My lady, when this servant went to the Internal Affairs Bureau this morning to collect rouge, powder, and pearl cream, they said they had run out and had no stock left. But later, Consort Wang's people were all able to get some.\"","As the words fell, Rendong paused, wondering if someone had found out about the incident at the Palace of Benevolent Peace the other day and was now seeking revenge.","Yanshu naturally understood as well.","However, at this moment she was facing an even bigger problem—as long as it wasn't the emperor taking revenge on her, it would be fine.","\"It's no matter. If there's no rouge, we'll do without. It's not like I need to go out and see anyone. We can just use the pear blossom fragrant cream we made ourselves.\"","Lianxin complied and obediently went to fetch the pear blossom fragrant cream.","This pear blossom fragrant cream was made by Yanshu and her palace maids using spring pear blossoms, along with various Chinese herbs. It was all-natural and non-toxic, very nourishing for the skin. Besides, her skin was fair, so not wearing powder actually looked more natural.","Rendong, however, felt somewhat indignant. \"How could they do this? His Majesty merely spoke a few words to you, and now they won't even give you rouge and powder! You are His Majesty's consort. What's wrong with His Majesty speaking to you?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, if only it were as simple as \"speaking a few words.\"","Last night, she had even bitten the emperor.","And the emperor had said he liked her.","Tsk, tsk. If those people found out about this, wouldn't they be furious to death?","Just at that moment, they heard an announcement from outside the door, \"Consort Wang has arrived.\"","Simultaneously, the system chimed in with a \"Ding!\" [Bingo! The furious one has arrived. Get ready, old friend.]","Yanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8","paragraphs":["This was truly unprecedented. Apart from the former Talented Lady Zhang, Yongning Palace had never received a new visitor.","Of course, Yanshu understood that the visitor's intentions were not benign. However, as Consort Wang outranked her, she could only rise to greet her.","\"Greetings, Consort Wang.\"","Consort Wang didn't stand on ceremony. Upon entering the room, she sat down on the warm couch and said with an ambiguous tone, \"What's this? I heard someone mentioning me just now?\"","This startled Lianxin, who quickly looked towards Yanshu.","Yanshu's expression remained unchanged as she innocently replied, \"No, we were just discussing what to have for breakfast. We didn't mention you at all, Consort.\"","Consort Wang scrutinized her closely and continued in a sarcastic tone, \"I've long heard that Beauty Li has a sharp tongue. Today, I've truly experienced it firsthand.\"","Yanshu pretended not to understand and laughed carefreely, \"Consort, you're praising me on your first visit. You're making me blush.\"","Seeing that Yanshu wouldn't take the bait, Consort Wang could only snort and say, \"Just now, my maid went to the Internal Affairs Bureau to collect rouge. She happened to run into one of your maids. How is it that I hear your people have been speaking ill of me?\"","She glanced at the maid who had accompanied her and said, \"Cuiyan, take a look. Is that the girl?\"","Upon hearing this, Cuiyan immediately pointed at Lianxin and said, \"It's her. She didn't get what she wanted, and when she saw that I did, she started muttering and speaking ill of Consort Wang.\"","Lianxin, frightened, shook her head vigorously, \"No, no! This servant only asked the people at the Internal Affairs Bureau why Consort Wang got rouge while we didn't...\"","At the same time, the system began to reveal information to Yanshu: [Cuiyan has stolen quite a few pieces of jewelry from Consort Wang over the years. Just two days ago, she stole a red agate pendant and is now falsely accusing others.]","Yanshu understood and pretended to reprimand Lianxin, \"You foolish girl, how can I compare myself to Consort Wang? She outranks me, so of course she should receive the best things first.\"","She then deliberately glanced at Cuiyan and said to Lianxin, \"If only you could be more like Miss Cuiyan, then I'd be at ease.\"","Consort Wang, who had been waiting to find fault with Yanshu, was taken aback by this comment. \"What about Cuiyan?\" she asked.","Yanshu smiled and said, \"Miss Cuiyan is so beautiful and knows how to conduct herself. No wonder she's so well-liked! Just the other day, I heard someone praising her at the Empress Dowager's place!\"","Well, since she was summoned by the Empress Dowager, there was no need to hide it anymore.","As expected, Consort Wang was startled and immediately asked, \"Who praised her?\"","Yanshu, maintaining a calm demeanor, replied, \"Palace Supervisor Chen! Yesterday, when I went to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, I happened to overhear Palace Supervisor Chen talking to the Empress Dowager. She said that Cuiyan was the most intelligent person in the harem and very filial too. I heard that she even personally made a headband for the Empress Dowager recently, with a red agate inlaid in it. The quality was truly exceptional.\"","By the time she finished speaking, even Cuiyan was stunned.","Consort Wang was also taken aback and looked at Cuiyan suspiciously.","Following the system's revelations, Yanshu continued to improvise, \"I heard that during the summer, she also made a set of soft gauze sleepwear for the Empress Dowager. The needlework was so exquisite that even the Empress Dowager praised it.\"","Soft gauze?","Consort Wang paused again.","— Wasn't it during the summer that she had lost a set of soft gauze fabric? She had been so distressed about it...","Yanshu then smiled at Cuiyan and said, \"Oh, and those cloud silk handkerchiefs, you gave those to Palace Supervisor Chen, right? She said the flowers you embroidered on them were particularly beautiful...\"","Before she could finish, Consort Wang turned and slapped Cuiyan, scolding her, \"So that's how it is! Red agate? Soft gauze? And cloud silk handkerchiefs? So all these things I lost were taken by you? And you even gave them to the Empress Dowager? What a girl! I had no idea you had such intentions!\"","Cuiyan was stunned by the slap. When she came to her senses, she quickly covered her face and said, \"My lady, I didn't, I really didn't! She's making it all up!\"","Yanshu covered her mouth in feigned surprise, \"Oh my, Consort Wang didn't know about this? Oh dear, it's my fault for speaking out of turn! I hope this doesn't damage your relationship!\"","Consort Wang slapped Cuiyan twice more, her chest heaving as she took several deep breaths. Finally, she turned to Yanshu with a vicious glare and said, \"Keep your people in check. If they spread rumors again, I'll report to Noble Consort Zhou and have their mouths torn apart!\"","With that, she stormed out, dragging Cuiyan by the ear.","Yanshu watched them leave.","Once the room was quiet again, Rendong and Lianxin looked at Yanshu in surprise, \"Was what you said true? Is Cuiyan really that bold?\"","Yanshu shrugged indifferently, \"Whether it's true or not, she'll find out when she investigates. You two just watch the show.\"","The two nodded eagerly, already rubbing their hands in anticipation.","Who doesn't enjoy a good drama?","Yanshu then turned serious and instructed them, \"Next time something like this happens with the rouge, don't fight, don't argue, don't say a word. Just come back immediately.\"","Her rank was low, and she had no backing. Confrontation would only bring her trouble.","The two quickly nodded, \"Yes, understood.\"","Yanshu then said, \"Now, go and fetch my breakfast. I'm starving.\"","After all the fuss this morning, it was nothing but useless drama. Once she had eaten, she needed to get back to writing her novel. It was best to develop a skill and have an alternative path.","Rendong quickly agreed and hurried to the Imperial Kitchen. Before long, she returned with breakfast: silver thread pancakes, lamb dumplings, pumpkin porridge, and two side dishes.","Hunger is the best sauce, and Yanshu devoured the meal like a whirlwind. Then, she immersed herself in her writing career.","Ahem, after several days of effort, her debut work \"The Dashing Scholar and the Beautiful Lady\" was almost complete.","After a period of intense focus, she was interrupted by Rendong entering the room with a hesitant expression. \"My lady...\"","Yanshu looked up from her papers and asked, \"What's the matter?\"","Rendong said angrily, \"The Internal Affairs Bureau has withheld our fuel and charcoal too. They said they've just run out today and told us to come back the day after tomorrow. Are they trying to freeze us to death these two days?\"","Yanshu understood and thought for a moment before saying, \"We still have some stock left, right? I'll share mine with you. Besides, it's sunny during the day, so we can save some charcoal.\"","Rendong pouted and asked, \"But what about at night?\"","Yanshu's eyes darted around as she replied, \"At night... we'll figure something out.\"","Tsk, that person had already come for two consecutive nights. Would he come again tonight?","As night fell, Qianming Palace was ablaze with lights.","In the imperial study, the emperor was reviewing memorials at his desk, with the Commissioner of State Affairs, the Chief Censor, and several other high officials respectfully waiting nearby.","After browsing through a memorial, Yuwen Lan was about to pick up his brush to write his comments when the bandage on the side of his hand was exposed.","The officials were startled and immediately stepped forward to inquire—","\"What happened to Your Majesty's hand? Have you been injured?\"","\"Has Your Majesty summoned the imperial physician? How serious is the injury?\"","\"How did Your Majesty get injured?\"","Yuwen Lan casually replied, \"I accidentally cut myself while practicing swordsmanship this morning. It's nothing serious.\"","He quickly wrote a few lines, handed the memorial back to the officials, and said, \"You may leave now.\"","The officials complied, each taking their respective memorials and withdrawing. The hall finally fell silent.","Fu Hai, the head eunuch, pondered to himself, [Heh, I wonder which beauty bit him. His Majesty is even covering for her. She must be quite important.]","Yuwen Lan glanced at him and said, \"You may leave too.\"","He then summoned another young eunuch, Fu Bao, and asked, \"How was Yongning Palace today?\"","Fu Bao honestly replied, \"Your Majesty, Beauty Li remained in her palace as usual, not venturing out. However, for some reason, the Internal Affairs Bureau has been withholding her cosmetics and fuel. Oh, and Consort Wang went there with her people today. I'm not sure what she said to Beauty Li, but she left in a fury.\"","Yuwen Lan accurately grasped the key point and frowned, \"Why are they withholding supplies? Who's responsible?\"","Fu Bao said, \"It seems Noble Consort Zhou gave the order to the Internal Affairs Bureau. As for the reason, this servant doesn't know.\"","Noble Consort Zhou, does she think the imperial palace belongs to the Zhou family?","Yuwen Lan then asked, \"How did she handle it?\"","Fu Bao replied, \"Beauty Li only instructed to share her fuel with her maids. She didn't make a fuss about it.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. Why was she being so docile now?","With less fuel, it would indeed be quite cold.","In the dead of night, Yanshu, wearing thick sleepwear, huddled in her blankets and pondered: Would the emperor come tonight?","There had been no movement all day. Surely he wasn't planning to punish her?","Could he be angry about yesterday's events and decide not to come?","What about the fuel situation?","As she was fretting, she heard the door being gently pushed open, followed by the faint sound of footsteps outside the curtain.","Her heart skipped a beat. She quickly lifted the curtain to look, and sure enough, she saw him.","Hurriedly getting out of bed to bow, she said, \"This humble consort respectfully greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan was dressed in a dark brocade robe, his hair uncrowned, giving him a softer appearance.","Glancing down at her, he said without emotion, \"Yesterday you were so bold, yet today you act like this.\"","Yanshu brazenly replied, \"This humble consort has been anxious and uneasy since last night. Um... how is your hand feeling?\"","Yuwen Lan grunted in response, but before he could say more, he sneezed.","Hmm, it did seem rather cold in this room.","However, immediately after, Rendong's voice was heard from outside, \"My lady? What... what was that sound?\"","Yanshu glanced at Yuwen Lan and hastily replied, \"It was me, I sneezed.\"","Rendong quickly responded, \"Let me bring you another blanket, my lady.\"","Before Yanshu could refuse, Rendong had already pushed open the door and entered.","Yanshu was startled, but in that split second, Yuwen Lan swiftly ducked behind the bed curtains.","Outside the door, someone's eyes darted about before quickly going to report the news.","In the room, Rendong efficiently retrieved a blanket from the wardrobe and was about to spread it for Yanshu when she snatched it away, saying, \"I can do it myself. It's the middle of the night, you should go to sleep.\"","Rendong sighed, \"I knew you'd catch a cold. Just because His Majesty spoke to you, these people are worse than wolves! Cutting off your fuel and charcoal in this cold weather, do they want to freeze you to death? I'll bring the brazier from our room right away.\"","Yanshu shook her head vigorously, \"No need. If you all fall ill from the cold, who will attend to me? I'm fine, please go to sleep.\"","Rendong had no choice but to comply, responding with a \"Yes\" before leaving.","As the room fell silent, a certain someone parted the bed curtains and casually sat on the edge of the bed.","Yanshu approached with the blanket, carefully fawning, \"Why don't Your Majesty drape this blanket? My room is cold, I wouldn't want you to catch a chill.\"","Truth be told, the room was indeed quite cold, incomparable to the Qianming Palace with its heated floors.","As for the reason, Yuwen Lan was already well aware.","He took the blanket and said, \"Someone has been withholding your fuel and charcoal. Why didn't you report this to me?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, \"Isn't it because of you that they're withholding my fuel and charcoal? Goodness, how could I possibly confront those people?\"","Moreover, given her position, she'd be devoured before even getting a chance to see him. It was better to let him experience it firsthand now.","Out loud, however, she played dumb, \"The Internal Affairs Bureau just said they were temporarily out of fuel and charcoal, and that it would arrive in a couple of days. This humble consort can wait a few days.\"","Yuwen Lan couldn't be bothered to expose her lie. He was about to speak again when another commotion erupted outside.","It seemed someone was trying to force their way into the hall, and a woman's voice rang out, \"Beauty Li, why are you up so late? Who are you talking to?\""]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Translation of the title \"09\"","paragraphs":["Consort Wang arrived.","Besides herself, she was followed by two palace maids and three eunuchs, quite an impressive entourage.","Rendong led Lianxin and Xiao Dongzi out to investigate, feeling somewhat confused.","But remembering Yanshu's instructions, they tried to speak politely, \"Consort Wang, our mistress has already retired for the night. It's so late, could any matters wait until tomorrow?\"","However, Consort Wang smiled strangely and said, \"Asleep? That can't be right. Someone just heard a man's voice coming from her room.\"","What? A man?","Rendong anxiously said, \"How can you slander our mistress's virtue like this? Where would there be men in the inner palace?\"","Consort Wang laughed again, \"Well said. Where indeed would there be men in the inner palace? So why was there a man's voice in Beauty Li's room?\"","Rendong forgot to be patient in her anger, \"You're just baselessly accusing someone.\"","Consort Wang looked at someone beside her, \"I'm not making this up. Someone from your own Yongning Palace heard it with their own ears.\"","Rendong followed her gaze and saw it was Xiao Chunzi from Yongning Palace, who mumbled with his head down, \"I just heard someone sneeze in the Beauty's room. It was clearly a man's voice.\"","Rendong angrily scolded him, \"Our mistress has always treated you well, yet you betray her and slander her like this!\"","Consort Wang snorted, \"Whether it's slander or not, why doesn't Beauty Li come out and prove it herself? Or we could open the door and go in?\"","She raised her voice again, \"Beauty Li, it's too late to hide now. Come out quickly!\"","Meanwhile, Consort An and Noble Consort Zhou were hurrying towards Yongning Palace.","\"Hurry up!\" Noble Consort Zhou kept urging the palace servants carrying her sedan chair.","If they were late and Consort Wang couldn't control the situation, wouldn't this golden opportunity be wasted? As the saying goes, to catch adulterers red-handed. Tonight she was determined to eliminate that little hussy once and for all.","As soon as they arrived at Yongning Palace, Consort Wang immediately went to greet them, \"Noble Consort, you're here.\" Her voice was exceptionally loud.","Inside the room, Yanshu looked at Yuwen Lan with difficulty, \"Your Majesty, the Noble Consort is here now. Can you still leave?\"","If he left now, leaving her alone to face this, who knows what kind of fuss Noble Consort Zhou would make.","But if he didn't leave, and they really kicked down the door, wouldn't the situation be even worse?","This was truly a case of trouble falling from the sky while sitting at home. How on earth had she offended anyone?","How did this turn into such a dramatic scene without any warning?","Yuwen Lan sensed her strong displeasure and glanced down at her.","Before he could speak, they heard Noble Consort Zhou asking in a pretend manner outside, \"What's going on?\"","Consort Wang raised her voice again, \"Noble Consort, in the middle of the night, a man's voice was heard coming from Beauty Li's room.\"","Noble Consort Zhou feigned surprise, \"Is that so? Where is Beauty Li?\"","Consort Wang gloated, \"Beauty Li is hiding in her room and refuses to come out. I wonder if she has a guilty conscience.\"","Noble Consort Zhou spoke haughtily, \"If she won't come out, then kick the door open.\"","With these words, the two eunuchs who came with Consort Wang immediately stepped forward, pushing aside Rendong, Lianxin, and Xiao Dongzi who were guarding the door, and were about to kick it open.","At this critical moment, the door suddenly opened from the inside.","A tall figure stepped out calmly, looked around at everyone, and said, \"We are here. Is there a problem?\"","The surroundings instantly fell silent.","Everyone stared with wide eyes, all looking as if they had been struck by lightning.","[My goodness, this, this, this is His Majesty???]","[His Majesty, His Majesty, it's actually His Majesty!!!]","[What??? His Majesty is actually, actually in, in our mistress's room???]","Someone took the lead, and everyone quickly knelt down saying, \"Greetings to Your Majesty.\"","Noble Consort Zhou also slowly followed suit, her face full of disbelief as she said, \"Your, Your Majesty, why are you here?\"","Yuwen Lan's expression was cold as he asked in return, \"In Our palace, where can We not be?\"","Noble Consort Zhou choked, then stammered, \"But, but hasn't the palace been locked down for the night?\"","[He's actually spent the night here??? That little hussy Li Yanshu!!! Why didn't anyone tell her!!!]","Yuwen Lan looked around at everyone and said with a cold smile, \"Indeed, the palace has been locked down. So how did you all come here?\"","Noble Consort Zhou was completely at a loss for words.","Consort An was quick-witted and said, \"Your Majesty, Consort Wang came to report to Noble Consort Zhou that there was a man's voice in Beauty Li's room. As it was a serious matter, Noble Consort Zhou came to investigate.\"","Noble Consort Zhou quickly agreed, \"Yes, yes, yes, I only came because I wanted to uphold the rules of the palace.\"","Then she scolded Consort Wang, \"Are you making a fool out of me?\"","Consort Wang, terrified, quickly said, \"Your Majesty, please forgive me. I was only repeating what I heard from others.\"","She then pointed at Xiao Chunzi, \"It was him, he came to tell me that there was a man's voice in Beauty Li's room. I was only concerned for Beauty Li's safety...\"","Yuwen Lan couldn't be bothered to listen to her further and simply said, \"Since you're so fond of not sleeping at night and concerning yourself with others' affairs, We shall grant your wish. From now until the beginning of spring next year, you will be responsible for night patrols and announcing the watches in the inner palace, regardless of wind, frost, rain, or snow. No excuses will be accepted.\"","What?","Consort Wang collapsed to the ground.","Making her patrol on such cold winter nights, did they want to freeze her to death?","Everyone else was also terrified, kowtowing with their faces to the ground, not daring to breathe loudly for fear of attracting the emperor's attention and being punished.","Next, Yuwen Lan looked at Consort An and Noble Consort Zhou, \"If either of you wishes to accompany her, We can grant that wish as well.\"","The two were so frightened that they kept kowtowing, almost crying, \"We wouldn't dare.\"","This late-night commotion had brought everyone who should have come. Even Fu Hai had received the news and hurried over from Qianming Palace. As he waited on the side, he thought to himself, no wonder His Majesty had been going out at night these past few days. So he was coming to Beauty Li's place.","These people, weren't they just asking for trouble!","Just then, the emperor scanned the crowd again and called out a name, \"Pan Luhai.\"","As soon as he spoke, a fat-faced eunuch in a round-collared robe came forward and knelt down, stammering, \"This, this slave is here.\"","Yuwen Lan said coldly, \"Do you still remember who your master is? If you no longer wish to serve, We can replace you.\"","Pan Luhai was already pale as a sheet and could only keep kowtowing, \"This slave knows his crime, this slave knows his crime.\"","Good heavens, how was he to know that Beauty Li had such powerful backing!","Everyone else was also trembling in fear, not daring to make a sound.","They all thought to themselves, Pan Luhai had been the head of the Internal Affairs Bureau for so many years, yet today he had fallen because of this mere beauty.","Mere beauty?","Yuwen Lan's brows furrowed slightly, and he spoke again, \"Fu Hai,\"","Fu Hai quickly came forward, \"This slave is here.\"","\"Proclaim Our decree,\"","Yuwen Lan looked at Yanshu and said each word clearly, \"Beauty Li Yanshu has greatly pleased Us. She is hereby promoted to Noble Lady and granted residence in Ganlu Palace.\"","What?","Everyone was stunned.","Yanshu herself was also dumbfounded.","Pro-promoted to Noble Lady?","And granted residence in Ganlu Palace?","Rendong, Lianxin, and Xiao Dongzi were the first to react, all congratulating her, \"Congratulations, Noble Lady!\"","The others could only follow suit, \"Congratulations, Noble Lady Li.\"","Yuwen Lan looked at Yanshu.","It seemed only she had forgotten to thank him for the honor.","But he heard her inwardly click her tongue, [Oh no, now I've really become the enemy of the entire harem.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","After a heart-stopping and bewildering night, early the next morning, Yanshu moved to Ganlu Palace.","Compared to Yongning Palace, it was like heaven and earth.","Ganlu Palace was the closest palace to Qianming Palace in the inner court. Not only was it spacious and bright, but it also had floor heating, making it as warm as spring.","Rendong and the others were overjoyed, excitedly saying, \"Mistress has finally had her fortunes turn around. Good things really do come to good people. Heaven doesn't disappoint those who persevere!\"","Yanshu sighed inwardly. This wasn't heaven rewarding the persistent, this was heaven deliberately going against her!","Originally, she just wanted to be an unnoticed nobody, but now everyone in the harem would hate her to the bone.","If the emperor were a normal man, it might be a different story. But he wasn't.","She even began to suspect that the emperor might be using her as a cover to hide the fact that he was impotent.","But why did he have to choose her, a poor girl with no background and a distant hometown, when he could have chosen anyone else?","Of course, since things couldn't be reversed, she could only face it head-on.","Actually, thinking about it, her living conditions had greatly improved, her rank had been raised along with her monthly allowance, and her family in Ande County might even benefit from this. Perhaps being a target wasn't entirely in vain.","To her surprise, there was something delightful - after her promotion in rank, the meals became even more satisfying.","Breakfast now consisted of six different pastries paired with soup, porridge, and side dishes that never repeated. Lunch also included several more dishes than before.","The dinner, in particular, was exceptional. The cherry pork was tender and sweet, the roasted chicken was spicy and succulent, the hung roast duck left a lingering fragrance with each bite, and the stuffed dace fish was deliciously fresh.","Yanshu felt like her mouth wasn't enough to savor it all, eating with great gusto.","Well, for the sake of all this delicious food, she grudgingly forgave that dog of an emperor for making her a target practice.","After thoroughly enjoying the sumptuous dinner, night had already fallen. Rendong and the others had prepared hot water, so she moved to the bathroom and indulged in a lovely hot bath.","Mmm, the bathroom was already warm, and Rendong had even placed two braziers beside the bathtub. It couldn't have been more comfortable.","When she finished and came out, Rendong wanted to apply makeup for her.","Yanshu asked curiously, \"Can't I just dive into bed? Why do I need makeup?\"","The large canopy bed was layered with several new quilts, looking soft, warm, and inviting. It would surely be comfortable to sleep in.","But Rendong, blushing, said, \"Just now, someone from Qianming Palace came with a message. His Majesty said he would be coming over tonight. The lighting in this room is good, so if you put on some makeup, His Majesty will find it pleasing to the eye.\"","She then reproached Yanshu, \"My lady, really! You and His Majesty have progressed to that stage, yet you still keep it from us servants.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","What stage had she and the emperor progressed to?","Wasn't it just that the emperor peeped at her, and she bit him in return?","But, he's coming over tonight?","As she was still in shock, she heard an announcement from outside, \"His Majesty has arrived...\""]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10","paragraphs":["Speak of the devil and he shall appear.","Yanshu had just finished bathing and emerged wearing only her nightgown, her hair not yet combed. She hurried to the door to bow, \"Welcome, Your Majesty.\"","Though she had met him a few times before, this was the first time greeting him so openly, and she still felt somewhat awkward.","Yuwen Lan appeared at ease, looking her up and down before saying, \"Just finished bathing?\"","For a moment, the scene he had witnessed on the rooftop flashed through his mind.","Oblivious, Yanshu replied honestly, \"Please forgive my disheveled appearance, Your Majesty.\"","[How do you always pick the perfect timing?]","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"It seems I've arrived at just the right moment.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","What did he mean by \"just the right moment\"?","She watched as he took a few steps into the chamber, glancing at the prepared bed before saying, \"Well then, let's retire for the night.\"","Yanshu: \"...Huh?\"","What did he mean by retire?","While she was still confused, she saw the eunuch Fu Hai respond with a \"Yes, Your Majesty\" before bowing and withdrawing with his feather duster.","Rendong also belatedly followed suit, giving Yanshu a blushing glance before leaving.","In the blink of an eye, only she and the emperor remained in the chamber.","Yanshu looked at him in disbelief, \"Your Majesty intends to rest here tonight?\"","Yuwen Lan cast her a leisurely glance, \"What else did you think I came here for?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Was he being this direct?","Were they really going to sleep together just like that???","While she was still in shock, she saw the man look at her again, raising an eyebrow as he said, \"Aren't you going to help me undress?\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","She had to undress him too?","Of course, as an imperial consort, this was part of her duties.","She could only respond affirmatively and move forward to assist him.","Unexpectedly, this skill she had learned upon first entering the palace was finally being put to use today.","Yuwen Lan wore casual attire tonight, much simpler compared to his formal court robes. Yanshu removed his headdress, untied his belt, and took off his outer robe, leaving him in just his inner garments after a few swift motions.","She could vaguely make out his excellent physique - broad shoulders, narrow waist, long limbs. A faint scent of musk wafted to her nose, which was admittedly quite pleasant.","However, Yanshu still felt awkward and wasn't in the mood to appreciate it.","Next, she watched as he walked naturally towards the bed, turning to say, \"Hurry and get in bed, lest you catch cold.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","On such a night, with a virile emperor and a freshly bathed beauty.","The atmosphere should have been ambiguous, and yet...","Yanshu's face darkened. He wasn't a normal man after all.","Hah, was he just using her as target practice, putting on such an act?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","The emperor's dignity had been repeatedly trampled by this girl lately. It must be said that his temper had improved considerably - hearing her internal criticism of him again, he didn't even feel the urge to kill her anymore.","However, he wasn't using her as target practice at all.","The previous attempts at probing had all failed due to various circumstances, mainly because their clandestine interactions were too brief. So last night, he had seized the opportunity to elevate her rank, allowing him to openly spend time with her and discern her true thoughts.","Of course, they would need to spend as much time together as possible.","Preferably sharing a bed for an entire night.","He couldn't reveal any of this, so he could only force a casual smile and say, \"You are my consort. Isn't it only natural for us to share a bed?\"","With that, he lifted the covers and lay down.","Yanshu looked at him speechlessly.","What nonsense was this? \"Only natural\"?","Where was this attitude for the past three years when you forgot you even had consorts?","Yuwen Lan continued to look at her, \"Why are you still hesitating? Do you want me to carry you to bed?\"","Yanshu could only say, \"I wouldn't dare, Your Majesty.\"","Since there was no way out, she steeled herself. [Fine, target practice it is! I'm not the abnormal one here, let's see what you can do to me!]","With that thought, she climbed into bed.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Hmph, this girl actually dared to disregard him so!","As his temper flared, he heard her say, \"This humble consort has poor sleeping habits. If I disturb Your Majesty in the night, I beg for your forgiveness.\"","With that, she lifted the covers and lay down.","—As the chamber was warm, only one large brocade quilt covered the bed. This meant they would have to share the same blanket tonight.","Yuwen Lan felt a waft of fragrance envelop him, along with the warmth of a young woman. It reminded him of what he had seen on the rooftop that night.","Now those snow-capped mountains and red plum blossoms, that peach grove dusted with spring snow, were separated from him by just a thin layer of fabric...","He recalled her earlier thoughts—","Let's see what he could do to her?","With a hint of complex displeasure, he suddenly reached out and pulled her into his embrace.","Yanshu was startled, letting out a small cry that was cut short as her body pressed against his firm chest.","\"Y-Y-Your Majesty?\"","She stared at him with wide eyes.","What was he doing?","He smiled roguishly, saying in a low voice, \"What's with the formality? Am I not your husband?\"","His deep, magnetic voice so close to her ear made Yanshu go weak. She stammered, \"Th-this consort is not yet accustomed...\"","What was going on here?!","Mmm, his chest muscles were so hard...","As her mind wandered, he pinched her waist, saying, \"You'll get used to it eventually.\"","His warm palm pressed against her skin, making Yanshu dizzy once again.","What was happening?","How was he so smooth?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What did she mean by \"smooth\"?","Still, the feeling beneath his palm was quite nice. He decided to slip his hand under the thin silk, directly caressing her skin.","As his hand roamed aimlessly, he asked in her ear, \"Are you comfortable living here?\"","Yanshu was already in a daze, but couldn't refuse. She struggled to maintain her composure as she answered, \"Yes, thank you for Your Majesty's great kindness.\"","What was going on?!","Why did it feel so good???","Yuwen Lan was secretly pleased and continued questioning, \"What have you been doing since entering the palace?\"","Yanshu bit her lip, \"Just... This consort spends most days reading and writing in the palace, and doing some needlework...\"","Suddenly she shuddered - his hand had reached her... chest!","He seemed quite interested, kneading and squeezing as if playing with a toy.","Yanshu screamed internally, [Stop! If this goes on, I won't be able to control myself!!!]","Yuwen Lan was thoroughly intrigued.","Unable to control herself?","What would that entail?","He heard her thoughts continue, [Should I try stimulating him? If it works, I'll have rendered a great service!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Stimulate... him?","Tsk, thinking about it, he supposed it wouldn't be so bad...","Mmm, regardless, this really did feel quite nice.","As he continued fondling with interest, Yanshu could no longer endure. Throwing caution to the wind, she wrapped her arms around his shoulders and kissed him directly.","Yuwen Lan was stunned.","This was his first time kissing a woman.","Their lips and tongues intertwined, so incredibly close...","Of course, to be precise, he was entirely passive in this.","But he didn't want to stop it, so he simply went along.","He even reciprocated quite enthusiastically.","Yanshu was currently struggling between lucidity and haziness.","Mmm, she had kissed the emperor - surely the first in the harem to do so. If others knew, they would certainly want to tear her to pieces.","But she had to admit, the emperor's lips felt quite nice - soft and springy, tasting like... jelly.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What was this \"jelly\"?","Still... she wasn't bad either, like a freshly ripened peach, impossible to put down.","For some reason, although he hadn't physically reacted, he felt somewhat dazed and intoxicated, momentarily forgetting his original purpose.","The bedside lamp flickered, casting shadows of their entangled figures.","Seeing how responsive he was, Yanshu grew bolder. She flipped their positions, pinning him beneath her as she moved to undo the front of his robes.","However, this was her first attempt, and in her excitement, she accidentally pressed down on his hand.","Immediately after, she heard Yuwen Lan let out a muffled groan.","She froze, hurriedly asking, \"Your Majesty, what's wrong?\"","She saw him furrowing his brow in a pained expression.","This terrified Yanshu. She quickly examined him herself, only then noticing the bandage still wrapped around one of his hands. Carefully unwrapping it, she saw it was where she had bitten him before.","Blood had seeped through.","Yanshu was shocked. Had she pressed on it?","\"This consort didn't mean to, should we summon the imperial physician?\"","Tsk, why hadn't such a small wound healed yet? He looked so strong, surely he couldn't be this fragile?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Now she was blaming him?","Glancing at her, he said, \"Call Fu Hai in.\"","Yanshu responded affirmatively and was about to get out of bed.","But he stopped her again, \"Wait.\"","Yuwen Lan looked at her, seeing her loosened collar, slightly disheveled hair, and rosy cheeks...","How could he let others see her in this state?","\"Stay behind the curtain.\"","After saying this, he got out of bed himself and went to the door to call someone.","At this time, Fu Hai, the head eunuch, was waiting in the antechamber, thinking to himself how difficult it had been, but finally, His Majesty had come to his senses. He imagined the passionate encounter would last at least half the night.","Unexpectedly, he suddenly heard his name being called from inside.","Fu Hai hurriedly responded and entered the hall, wondering to himself, \"Is it over so quickly?\"","As he stepped into the hall, he saw the emperor with his collar slightly open and his black hair somewhat disheveled. The brocade curtains were tightly closed, and the entire hall was filled with an ambiguous atmosphere. He hesitated for a moment and asked, \"Does Your Majesty have any instructions?\"","But he heard the emperor say, \"Bring some wound medicine.\"","Huh?","Fu Hai was stunned, \"Wound medicine?\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"Do I need to repeat myself?\"","\"This servant wouldn't dare.\"","Fu Hai had heard clearly this time and quickly responded, heading towards the door. As he walked, he marveled inwardly, [Such high spirits? Even needing wound medicine? His Majesty is truly formidable!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Was the room not cleaned properly?"]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11","paragraphs":["Soon, the wound medicine was brought. Yuwen Lan didn't call Fu Hai into the hall, but took it to the bedside himself.","Yanshu emerged from behind the curtain, attempting to make amends. \"Your Majesty, may I apply the medicine for you?\"","Yuwen Lan handed her the medicine bottle.","Yanshu began applying it carefully.","Only then did she realize how powerful her teeth were, to have bitten him like this.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Was she proud of this?","He lightly snorted, \"Your bite is indeed quite strong.\"","Yanshu blushed and could only say, \"This concubine is ashamed.\"","In her heart, she couldn't help but retort - how was this her fault? Who wouldn't bite in that situation? It was lucky she didn't take a chunk out of him.","Yuwen Lan hissed.","Yanshu was startled and asked carefully, \"Does it hurt?\"","Yuwen Lan looked at her with a stern face, \"Mm.\"","Not only did it hurt, he was a bit angry too.","But then he saw her pout her small mouth and lean in to blow on the wound.","Her pink lips formed a perfect circle, like a ripe cherry, tempting to taste.","Yuwen Lan's throat bobbed as he couldn't help but recall the earlier sensation.","But he held himself back.","Now that he had calmed down, he found it strange. He had come tonight to investigate, so how had this woman managed to distract him again?","Could she be doing this on purpose?","Just then, voices suddenly came from outside the door.","It seemed Fu Hai was scolding someone, \"Don't you know what time it is? Have you no sense!\"","Another small eunuch mumbled, \"But, but His Majesty said...\"","Oh? Was there some matter?","Yanshu quickly looked at Yuwen Lan.","Yuwen Lan directly called out to inquire, \"What is it?\"","The small eunuch outside hurriedly replied, \"Your Majesty, urgent memorials just arrived from Chuanqian. They report that freezing rain fell suddenly the day before yesterday, affecting over ten thousand civilians.\"","Yuwen Lan immediately stood up, \"Why didn't you say so earlier?\"","Oh, was he leaving?","Yanshu quickly got up to help him dress, carefully asking, \"Will Your Majesty return?\"","Yuwen Lan glanced down at her, \"Do you want me to return?\"","Yanshu blinked her almond eyes and boldly said, \"Yes, this concubine hopes Your Majesty will return soon to rest.\"","In her heart, she kept repeating, [Please don't come back, I want to sleep alone, thank you...]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He knew it.","Although he didn't want to see her so happy, he could only tell the truth, \"I won't be back. Sleep on your own.\"","Chuanqian was an important military region and a crucial granary for Yue Country. A disaster there was no small matter.","He heard her rejoicing in her heart, [Finally I can sleep well!!!]","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"You're very happy?\"","\"No, no,\" Yanshu shook her head like a rattle drum, putting on a gentle and obedient expression, \"This concubine is only concerned for Your Majesty's health. Your Majesty worries for the country and people, but should also rest well.\"","Yuwen Lan snorted, \"As if I'd believe you.\"","What a hypocritical woman.","Mobilizing the national treasury, allocating food and supplies, while also guarding against foreign enemies taking advantage of the situation - Yuwen Lan was busy the entire night.","Yanshu, however, slept comfortably in her new bed all night.","But early the next morning, she dutifully got up, changed her clothes, and went to pay respects to the Empress Dowager.","On the way to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, she saw that Noble Consort Zhou was also there.","The Empress Dowager sat upright on her heated couch, while Noble Consort Zhou stood to the side. Her expression was poor, as if she had just been scolded.","Yanshu pretended not to notice and hurried to bow to both of them. Unexpectedly, Noble Consort Zhou changed her attitude from the previous day and actively apologized to her, \"There was a misunderstanding the other night. I hope Noble Lady Li won't take it to heart.\"","Yanshu could only play along, \"Noble Consort Zhou is too kind.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"As imperial consorts, you should prioritize the emperor in all things.\"","After speaking, she separately awarded Yanshu a bracelet, saying, \"You are the first in the harem to be promoted, showing you meet the emperor's approval. Seize this opportunity well and bear children for His Majesty as soon as possible.\"","Yanshu: \"...Yes.\"","Tsk, this task was truly difficult.","Fortunately, after saying this, the Empress Dowager dismissed them both.","Yanshu felt like she'd been granted amnesty and hurried back to Ganlu Palace to enjoy her breakfast.","However, when Noble Consort Zhou returned to ChongHua Palace, she immediately smashed several teacups.","\"I even apologized to that scheming woman! If this continues, won't she be riding on my head?\"","At the initial conferment of titles, she had been made Noble Consort based on her aunt-niece relationship with the Empress Dowager. She thought she was only one step away from becoming Empress, but who knew that one step would take so many years.","Yet that Li Yanshu, just by dropping a teacup at the palace banquet, gained His Majesty's favor and was the first to be promoted!","Consort An advised from the side, \"My Lady, no matter how angry you are, you must endure it. You've just angered His Majesty, it's not good to act now.\"","Noble Consort Zhou snorted, \"If I endure any longer, she might even give birth to a prince!\"","Consort An said, \"How could that happen? Even if you don't act, there are others in the palace who hate her. Why not reap the benefits without lifting a finger?\"","Noble Consort Zhou paused, then smiled, \"That's true.\"","-- Consort Ning had always prided herself on her beauty and looked down on others. Now that His Majesty had favored Li Yanshu for several days in a row, how could she stand it?","Then she heard Consort An whisper, \"I heard that last night, His Majesty sent Eunuch Fu Hai back to fetch some wound medicine.\"","\"Wound medicine?\" Noble Consort Zhou paused, \"That... requires wound medicine?\"","Consort An leaned close to her ear and said softly, \"My Lady may not know, but a few days ago some ministers saw wounds on His Majesty's hands in the study. His Majesty said he was injured while practicing swordsmanship early in the morning, but I've inquired and His Majesty didn't go to the training grounds that day at all.\"","Noble Consort Zhou was surprised again, \"Could someone have injured His Majesty, and His Majesty is covering for them?\"","Consort An nodded, \"The one who injured His Majesty must be someone he cares for deeply.\"","Noble Consort Zhou pondered, then suddenly realized, \"Could it be Li Yanshu? She's so bold, daring to harm His Majesty! This won't do, I must report to the Empress Dowager!\"","Consort An quickly stopped her, smiling, \"My Lady is being hasty again. We're only guessing, without real evidence. How can we report to the Empress Dowager? Why not let someone else handle it? This is a serious crime, she certainly won't escape punishment.\"","In the afternoon, it began to snow. The flakes drifted down for half the day, and by late afternoon, a thick layer had accumulated on the ground.","Yuwen Lan was busy at his desk. As the time approached for lamps to be lit, he showed no signs of stopping.","Fu Hai couldn't bear it any longer and reminded him, \"Your Majesty, it's time for dinner.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't even look up, \"Wait a bit longer.\"","Fu Hai couldn't help but worry. His Majesty had been busy for a night and a day, hadn't slept well, and wasn't eating properly. How could this go on?","After some thought, he suddenly had an idea and said, \"I just saw Noble Lady Li send someone to the kitchens. She said she wanted hot pot tonight.\"","Sure enough, as soon as he finished speaking, the emperor looked up and said, \"Hot pot?\"","Fu Hai quickly nodded, \"Indeed. Noble Lady Li is quite particular. Hot pot on a snowy day is most fitting.\"","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment, put down his brush and walked towards the door, \"Let's go take a look.\"","It was still early today. He definitely couldn't let her distract him again.","When Yuwen Lan arrived, the hot pot was already set up on the table.","Charcoal burned slowly under the copper pot, the bone broth inside bubbling away. The entire hall was filled with a warm, fragrant aroma.","Yanshu was smiling happily as she looked at the pot.","Tsk tsk, meatballs and crispy pork, cabbage, vermicelli, and tofu, along with freshly sliced lamb - each a perfect hot pot ingredient. This upgrade really made a difference; she'd never been able to eat so well before.","As she was secretly salivating, she saw Yuwen Lan enter the hall. Startled, she quickly led the others in bowing, \"Greetings to Your Majesty.\"","Why did he come at this time? Don't interfere with my meal!","Yuwen Lan pretended not to hear and glanced at the table, saying, \"What made you think of having hot pot?\"","Yanshu tried hard to smile, \"It's snowing today and cold. This concubine thought hot pot would be warming.\"","[You're the emperor, of course you don't understand the troubles of us lowly concubines. I've been in the palace for three years and finally get to eat hot pot today. Do you know how rare this is for me!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How did this become his fault?","So eating hot pot was actually a rare treat?","\"It seems I've come at just the right time,\" he walked over to the table and sat down, beckoning to her, \"Let's eat together.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","So he came to mooch a meal?","She could only agree and walk over.","Rendong quickly brought new bowls and chopsticks. Just as she was about to withdraw, she saw Fu Hai winking at her repeatedly, looking at her and then at the silver chopsticks on the table.","Rendong slowly understood - he wanted her to serve food for the masters.","Good heavens!","In the past, the master never needed her help with meals, but today she was to serve dishes to the Emperor? If she accidentally displeased His Majesty, would she be beheaded? Oh no...","Yuwen Lan found it annoying and raised his hand, saying, \"I'll do it myself.\"","Rendong was overjoyed and retreated to the side, feeling greatly relieved.","The aroma at the tip of her nose grew stronger, and Yanshu couldn't count how many times she had swallowed. If the Emperor wasn't beside her, she would have started eating already!","The Emperor seemed oblivious to the fragrance. Instead of reaching into the pot with his chopsticks, he leisurely asked her, \"What did you usually eat in your hometown?\"","She had to reply, \"Your subject's hometown of Ande is not as prosperous as the capital. The common people mainly eat flour-based foods, such as noodles, dumplings, steamed buns, and bao. There are also a few famous snacks like pan-fried buns, noodles with gravy, donkey meat, and braised chicken.\"","Fu Hai interjected from the side, \"Your Highness is indeed fortunate. The braised chicken from Ande is famous far and wide!\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, \"Master Fu truly knows his stuff! Our Ande braised chicken uses a centuries-old recipe. The fresh chicken is stewed over high heat and then simmered over low heat. When it's done, the meat is tender and flavorful. With a gentle pull, the meat separates from the bone. Not only is the meat infused with flavor, but even the bones are soft and crumbly. It's absolutely delicious!\"","Just talking about it made her even hungrier.","Leaving home young and returning old, one's accent remains unchanged while the temples turn gray. No matter how many delicacies she had eaten in the palace, she still missed the food from her hometown the most.","Alas, the palace gates were as deep as the sea. She wondered if she would ever be able to taste the authentic braised chicken from her hometown again in this lifetime.","She cast a wistful glance at the person beside her, thinking to herself that the Emperor should do her a favor and send her back home one day!","Yuwen Lan heard every word, and inwardly raised an eyebrow —","Let her go back? That was impossible.","\"Eat,\" he finally extended his chopsticks into the pot.","Yanshu was overjoyed and quickly followed suit, picking up a beef meatball with her first attempt.","After cooling it slightly, she put it in her mouth and felt instantly satisfied. The meatball had a smooth exterior and a salty, juicy interior. It was delicious even without dipping sauce!","Next came the crispy meat. The originally crisp outer layer had now absorbed the broth, offering a different flavor compared to eating it dry.","After the crispy meat, she picked up a piece of tofu. Wow, the fried tofu absorbed even more broth. Besides its inherent bean flavor, it was infused with the savory taste of the scalding bone broth, not at all inferior to the meat.","Then she tried a piece of blood tofu. It had a unique elasticity amidst its tenderness, with an extremely delicate texture and rich flavor.","The most impressive was the lamb. Thinly sliced tender leg of lamb, cooked with just a few swishes in the hot soup, then dipped in a bowl of sesame paste mixed with chive flower and fermented bean curd sauce. The taste was simply irresistible.","Yuwen Lan had been listening attentively, but he didn't expect to hear so much about delicious food.","— Meatballs, tofu, crispy meat, lamb, there seemed to be nothing she didn't like.","Come to think of it, he rarely paid attention to such culinary pleasures in his daily life. Only after listening to her today did he realize how delicious these things really were.","Moreover, smooth, tender, savory, rich — there were so many words to describe them.","Especially the lamb. When dipped in the sauce and put in the mouth, layers of fresh, salty, fragrant, and rich flavors burst forth. It was truly excellent.","Yuwen Lan ate several bites in succession, feeling quite pleased. But then he heard her thinking anxiously, [Oh no, just one plate of lamb is not nearly enough!]","[Doesn't he eat well enough in his own palace? Why does he have to come and compete for food with others?]","[If he had given some advance notice, I could have asked the kitchen to send more dishes!]","[How annoying!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","This was truly audacious."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12","paragraphs":["The dignified emperor could not bear such complaints. Yuwen Lan immediately said to Fu Hai, \"Tell someone to bring a few more plates of lamb.\"","After speaking, he looked at the girl who was grumbling about him and asked, \"What else would you like to eat?\"","Yanshu was taken aback. She had originally wanted to be reserved, but smiled and said, \"This humble consort doesn't have anything particular in mind. Whatever pleases Your Majesty is fine.\"","In her heart, however, she was shouting, [Meatballs! I want meatballs!]","Yuwen Lan looked at Fu Hai and said, \"Bring another plate of meatballs.\"","Yanshu: \"??\"","What's going on? Does he also want to eat meatballs?","What a coincidence!","But she also wanted to eat crispy meat, freshly fried - that crispy, crunchy texture was simply divine!","Yuwen Lan then said, \"Bring another plate of crispy meat, freshly fried.\"","Yanshu: \"??\"","Could this be... a meeting of minds?","While she was still in a daze, she saw him looking at her calmly, asking again, \"Why that expression? Don't you want to eat?\"","\"No, no, it's not that,\" Yanshu hurriedly shook her head. \"This humble consort just thinks Your Majesty is really good at ordering dishes. These two are indeed delicious.\"","[If only there was a serving of hand-pulled noodles, it would be perfect! Lamb soup with hand-pulled noodles, what an amazing combination!]","\"Bring a serving of hand-pulled noodles,\" he said.","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","What on earth is going on??","Why did he order everything she was thinking of???","Could it be that he has mind-reading abilities??","Yuwen Lan stopped talking and simply picked up some cabbage from the pot with his chopsticks and started eating quietly, as if concealing his talents.","Hmm, come to think of it, even this most ordinary cabbage is quite flavorful.","Meanwhile, Fu Hai hurriedly sent someone to relay the message to the kitchen, inwardly delighted - indeed, they had found the right person. When had the Emperor ever been so good at eating before?","Before long, all the additional dishes were served.","The freshly fried crispy meat was fragrant and crunchy, the tender lamb slices paired perfectly with the chewy hand-pulled noodles in a full bowl, topped with a few round beef meatballs - Yanshu ate to her heart's content.","Being an emperor is indeed good! She thought, rubbing her belly with immense satisfaction. Having power and influence is wonderful, you can eat whatever you want.","The system suddenly spoke up, [Cling to his leg, be a favored consort, and you can have this too.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","This was indeed the hard truth. Since she had already been assigned the fate of a target, there was no turning back. She might as well go all in and cling tightly to the Emperor's golden thigh.","Although the Emperor was lacking in that particular area, she figured she could still please him in other ways by catering to his interests.","So she quietly asked the system, [What does the Emperor like?]","System: [He's a workaholic, a machine for reviewing memorials. He likes governing the country.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","[Doesn't he have any other small hobbies?]","System: [Yes, he likes reading, practicing swordsmanship, playing cuju, polo, touhu, and so on.]","Touhu?","Yanshu's eyes lit up. She might not be good at the others, but this one she could do!","So she smiled at Yuwen Lan and said, \"It's still early. I wonder if Your Majesty would be interested in playing a game of touhu with this humble consort? It would help with digestion as well.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. \"You want to play touhu with me?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"May this humble consort have such an honor?\"","How about that, surprised? Isn't this suggestion right up your alley?","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but smile and said, \"Very well.\"","Yanshu quickly ordered for the equipment to be set up.","Soon, the bronze pot and feathered arrows were in place.","Yuwen Lan picked up an arrow, weighing it in his hand, about to throw it into the pot when Yanshu suddenly stopped him, saying, \"Your Majesty, please wait. Shouldn't we set the rules first?\"","Yuwen Lan looked at her. \"How do you want to play?\"","Usually, touhu was a banquet game, meant to liven up drinking. They certainly couldn't drink any more tonight. Yanshu's eyes darted as she thought, then said, \"How about this: the winner can make a request, and the loser must agree to the other's request.\"","Hehe, she used to play bird-shooting with her brother when she was young, so her aim was quite good. Besides, with one mouth and two ears on the pot, she should be able to hit something, right?","Yuwen Lan listened silently, then nodded, \"Agreed.\"","He then handed her the arrow in his hand. \"You go first.\"","Yanshu took it, carefully aimed at the mouth of the pot, and threw.","To her surprise, she missed.","As she stood there dumbfounded, Yuwen Lan picked up another arrow, tossed it lightly, and it went straight into the pot's mouth.","Fu Hai immediately announced, \"The Emperor wins.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, perhaps she had eaten too much, affecting her performance.","She looked at Yuwen Lan and said, \"What would Your Majesty like this humble consort to do?\"","He looked her up and down and said, \"How about this: I'll ask you a question, and you must answer truthfully.\"","Yanshu thought for a moment, then nodded, \"Please, Your Majesty, ask away.\"","Ever since confirming that her background was not an issue, Yuwen Lan had begun to suspect that perhaps someone else in the palace who knew his secret had told her.","So he asked, \"Since entering the palace, have you had contact with any unusual people?\"","This question... was rather strange.","Yanshu said, \"The most unusual person this humble consort has met is Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan paused, then asked warily, \"How am I unusual?\"","Yanshu tried her best to flatter him, \"Your Majesty is the Son of Heaven, naturally different from others, of course you're unusual.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Fu Hai chimed in from the side, \"Well said, Noble Consort.\"","Unexpectedly, a cold gaze shot down from above.","Fu Hai shuddered, quickly lowering his head, wishing he could slap himself twice.","- Why are you butting in on the couple's sweet talk?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What sweet talk? Yanshu's answer was clearly not what he wanted.","But strangely, there was nothing unusual in her heart either, she was just proud of her ability to speak well.","He had no choice but to continue the game of touhu.","This time, Yanshu went first again.","Learning from her previous failure, Yanshu had been quietly aiming for a long time. This time she carefully lined up her shot again and again, and finally managed to hit one of the pot's ears.","Just as she was about to rejoice, Yuwen Lan had already picked up an arrow.","Yanshu chanted in her heart, [Miss, miss, miss...]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He decided to cut to the chase, lightly tossing the arrow, and once again it went straight into the pot's mouth.","Then he looked at her smugly.","He saw the light in Yanshu's eyes instantly dim, but she still insincerely praised him, \"Your Majesty is amazing, this humble consort can't even compare. What would you like this humble consort to do this time?\"","\"Again, answer my question.\"","Yuwen Lan paused, then said word by word, \"Do you have any secrets that others don't know?\"","Secrets?","Yanshu hesitated.","This... she had plenty!","The Linwu Marquis's son wasn't his; the Chancellor of the Wenhua Court had been a kept man for a famous courtesan in his youth; the Minister of War was actually homosexual...","My goodness, she had been keeping these secrets for so long, how could she dare to speak them?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What?","He already knew about the Linwu Marquis's affair, but Wei Ruzhang, the Chancellor of the Wenhua Court, had been a kept man? And for a courtesan???","That old man had been a top scholar in his youth, always eloquent, and now in his seventies, he constantly preached about Confucian doctrines!","And Chai Weizhong, the Minister of War, was actually homosexual???","Didn't he have several concubines at home???","Was all this... true or false?","And how did she know about it???","He could barely suppress the surprise in his eyes.","But he saw Yanshu cautiously say, \"If this humble consort speaks, Your Majesty must not punish me for it.\"","Yuwen Lan composed himself and said, \"If you tell the truth without hiding anything, I will deal with it at my discretion.\"","He saw her clear her throat, \"Actually... at last year's Mid-Autumn Palace Banquet, when this humble consort claimed illness and asked for leave, it was... it was fake.\"","\"What?\" Yuwen Lan frowned.","Last year's Mid-Autumn Palace Banquet?","He tried to recall, but couldn't remember the scene at all.","Who asked her about this?","He spoke again, \"I want to know...\"","But she interrupted him, \"No, you can only ask one question at a time, that's the rule.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What? There's actually someone in this world who dares to interrupt him?","Fu Hai had also noticed the impropriety and was pondering how to remind her, when he saw Yanshu had already picked up an arrow on her own, aiming at the bronze pot again and again, then threw it with all her might. Surprisingly, it went straight into the pot's mouth.","As they say, a late victory is all the more joyful. She couldn't help but cheer, \"I did it!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He also picked up an arrow and casually tossed it forward. Needless to say, it went straight into the pot's mouth again.","He raised an eyebrow at her and said, \"It's a tie.\"","Is it that difficult?","But to his surprise, she said, \"The first to throw wins.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"Since when is that a rule?\"","Yanshu argued righteously, \"Of course it is, otherwise how do we determine the winner and loser?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Let's continue the competition. Each person gets ten feathered arrows, and whoever hits the target more times is the winner.\"","Yanshu's eyes glinted mischievously. \"But you said earlier that I could set the rules. An emperor's word is his bond, you know.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Had he unwittingly fallen into her trap?","Fearing that further argument might compromise his imperial image, he asked, \"Well then, what do you want?\"","Yanshu thought for a moment, then said with a giggle, \"Why don't Your Majesty reward this humble servant with some gold, silver, and jewels?\"","[I want money!!! Money, money, money!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"??? Are you short on funds?\"","Indeed she was!","Yanshu thought to herself, she never had much money to begin with. The monthly allowance for a palace beauty was meager, and sometimes when she saw a palace maid from Yongning Palace in need, she would generously help out. For instance, just yesterday, when someone was promoted and moved, she had rewarded the palace servants with money.","That handful of silver pieces had taken her nearly half a year to save up, tsk tsk.","With her heart bleeding, she could only force a smile and make excuses, \"Isn't it said that wealth is but a worldly possession? This humble servant wouldn't dare to ask for anything else.\"","Hearing this tearful plea of poverty, Yuwen Lan felt somewhat sympathetic. He thought to himself, why not grant her wish? Otherwise, he might appear stingy.","But before he could speak, a voice suddenly reported from outside, \"Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager has suddenly taken ill and has urgently summoned the Imperial Physician.\"","Yuwen Lan paused, then said, \"I'll go and check on her.\"","He was about to leave when Yanshu hesitated, wondering if she should go too.","At that moment, Yuwen Lan turned back to look at her and said, \"You'd better come along as well.\"","Yanshu could only comply, following in his footsteps while inwardly lamenting the loss of her gold, silver, and jewels.","She had finally won against the emperor for once! Who knew when the next opportunity would come?","Yuwen Lan inwardly chuckled, thinking he wouldn't fall for such tricks again next time."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: 《013》","paragraphs":["Thanks to the Emperor's favor, Yanshu unexpectedly had the privilege of riding in the imperial carriage.","The imperial carriage was spacious and stable, not to mention fast. In less than half a cup of tea's time, the two of them arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Upon entering the hall, they discovered that Noble Consort Zhou, Consort Ning, Consort An, Consort Li, and others had already arrived.","Seeing her arrive with the Emperor, fire almost shot from their eyes, but they still had to bow respectfully to Yuwen Lan, saying, \"We pay our respects to Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan said \"Rise\" and took a few steps to the Empress Dowager's bedside.","The Empress Dowager had let down her hair, wore a headband, and looked pale. Several palace maids were kneeling by her bed, massaging her forehead and chest.","Yuwen Lan said, \"Your son has come late. How is Mother feeling now?\"","Zhang Shengkang, the Chief of the Imperial Medical Academy who was waiting in the hall, hurriedly said, \"Your Majesty, the recent cold weather has triggered the Empress Dowager's old illness. The Empress Dowager needs to rest quietly for the next few days, take medicine regularly, and recover slowly.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly and said to the Empress Dowager, \"I have neglected to inquire after Mother's health these past few days. You have suffered.\"","The Empress Dowager slowly opened her eyes and said weakly, \"How can I blame Your Majesty? When I developed this condition, Your Majesty wasn't even born yet.\"","Most people in the palace knew something about the Empress Dowager's past -","It was said that the Empress Dowager came from a noble family and was the first wife of the late Emperor. She was also the first to give birth to the eldest prince, seemingly blessed with good fortune. However, heaven was unkind, and the eldest prince passed away before reaching his first birthday.","The Empress Dowager, a first-time mother, couldn't accept this blow. For half a year, she cried constantly, which led to her chronic headaches and heart palpitations.","She was never able to conceive again. Coincidentally, Consort Hui, the current Emperor's birth mother, passed away early, so she took the Emperor under her care.","The outside world knew of their deep mother-son bond, forged through years of nurturing that surpassed blood ties.","Thus, Yuwen Lan reproached himself again, \"If I had paid more attention to Mother, you wouldn't have triggered your old illness.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"Your Majesty governs the country and is loved by all people. I am proud of Your Majesty. There's no need to waste time on me.\"","But then she suddenly asked, \"I heard Your Majesty was injured a few days ago? Is it serious?\"","Yuwen Lan paused slightly, but revealed no emotion as he said, \"It was just a small cut while practicing swordsmanship, nothing to worry about.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he heard the thoughts of the women beside him -","Noble Consort Zhou thought, [It's true after all.]","Consort An was somewhat smug, [How could my information be false?]","Consort Ning and Consort Li were surprised, [So it's actually true?]","Yanshu, however, sensed something amiss. How did even the Empress Dowager know about the Emperor's injury?","Yuwen Lan, maintaining his composure, said to the Empress Dowager, \"Such a small matter has reached your ears? I wonder who was so loose-tongued as to make you worry.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"I just happened to overhear it. I'm glad Your Majesty is alright, but please be more careful in the future.\"","Yuwen Lan agreed, and then heard the Empress Dowager sigh in her mind, [They've all gathered here, aren't they just here to pry for information?]","Just then, a palace maid brought in a freshly prepared medicinal soup. Zhu Shu, the Empress Dowager's lady-in-waiting, was about to take it, but Noble Consort Zhou beat her to it, coming forward with the bowl and saying, \"Let me serve the medicine to the Empress Dowager.\"","The Empress Dowager couldn't refuse and allowed her to feed her the medicine.","On the side, Consort Ning snorted in her mind, [Does she think others don't know they're aunt and niece? She's just showing off!]","Consort Li mocked, [Does Noble Consort Zhou even know how to feed medicine? Don't scald the Empress Dowager!]","Consort An was envious, [When will it be my turn?]","Yuwen Lan was used to these women's behavior, but he curiously glanced at Yanshu.","Her rank was low, so she stood a bit far away, and he couldn't hear her thoughts clearly at first.","He quietly shuffled a bit outward and finally heard clearly, [Now that the Empress Dowager has taken her medicine, can we leave? Will the Emperor come back with me? Will I have another chance to ask for money tonight?]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","After about a cup of tea's time, the Empress Dowager finally finished her medicine, but she still frowned, looking pained. She weakly waved her hand and said, \"You may all withdraw. Your Majesty should also retire early.\"","Noble Consort Zhou offered her services again, \"Let me stay and watch over you tonight, Empress Dowager.\"","Consort Ning followed, \"Noble Consort Zhou must be tired from feeding the medicine. Let me do it instead.\"","Yuwen Lan found them all annoying and simply said, \"Everyone withdraw. I will stay here tonight to watch over Mother.\"","Everyone had to comply. They bowed to the mother and son, and withdrew from the hall.","Noble Consort Zhou cursed in her mind, [You bitch, what right do you have to compete with me!]","Consort Ning sneered, [Serves you right for trying to show off!]","Yuwen Lan looked at Yanshu again.","She appeared like an obedient little rabbit, but in her mind she thought, [Oh no, he's not coming back with me. That money is probably gone for good! I finally won for once!]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Was she really so persistent?","Maybe he should have someone send it to her tomorrow?","The night passed.","The next day, there was a small court session. With important ministers in attendance, Yuwen Lan wore his nine-dragon robe and a serious expression. He began by inquiring about the progress of the freeze disaster relief in Chuanqian.","The Chuanqian Commissioner reported, \"Your Majesty, this morning the funds and grain from the national treasury have arrived in the southwest. Each prefecture is sending people to collect them. Currently, the freezing rain has stopped, and the situation is improving.\"","This was good news. Yuwen Lan then asked the Ministry of War, \"How is the southwestern garrison?\"","The Minister of War answered, \"The soldiers in the camp are on high alert. It's reported that due to several days of heavy snow in the snow mountains, many areas in Tibet have also been affected by disasters. There have been no unusual movements so far. Please rest assured, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded.","Then he saw Chai Weizhong, the Vice Minister of War, step forward and say, \"Your Majesty, the vanguard camp and guard camp in the outskirts of the capital have been training for over a month. May I ask if the ice games will proceed as scheduled tomorrow?\"","The so-called ice games were an important winter activity in the palace.","Though called \"games,\" they were actually drills, a way for the royal family to review the army's various skills and tactics for winter warfare. In previous years, they were held on the fifteenth day of the last lunar month.","But this year, with the freeze disaster in the southwest and the Empress Dowager's illness last night, people were a bit uncertain.","Yuwen Lan said, \"I have already discussed it with the Empress Dowager last night. The ice games will be held as scheduled tomorrow, not in the Western Garden, but in Jinbo Garden.\"","After he finished speaking, Chai Weizhong acknowledged and stepped back. Suddenly, Yuwen Lan remembered Yanshu's \"secret\" from last night...","Was Chai Weizhong... homosexual?","Of course, besides Chai Weizhong, there was another person near him, Wei Ruzhang, the Grand Scholar of Wenhua Court.","He was the one Yanshu had said \"was a gigolo for courtesans in his youth\"...","Yuwen Lan's mouth twitched slightly.","People he had been very familiar with now seemed increasingly awkward to look at.","—— Last night he had stayed in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, only taking a short nap after the Empress Dowager retired, and rushed to the morning court early. Only now did he remember this matter.","Along with the awkwardness, his doubts about Yanshu grew.","How did a lowly concubine know so much?","Or...","Were these things she made up?","Was she so bored in the palace that she spent all day fantasizing?","\"Your Majesty,\"","Perhaps because he had glanced at him several times, Wei Ruzhang, the Grand Scholar of Wenhua Court, took the initiative to stand up and say, \"Your Majesty, we're already halfway through the last lunar month, with spring approaching. We should put the matters of next year's spring imperial examination and the Imperial Academy's recruitment on the agenda.\"","Yuwen Lan came back to his senses and nodded, \"Indeed. Discuss it with the Ministry of Rites and the Ministry of Personnel, and report to me in the imperial study the day after tomorrow.\"","Wei Ruzhang and the officials from the two mentioned ministries acknowledged.","Shortly after, the court session ended, and Yuwen Lan returned to his chambers to change.","His mind was still on that matter.","After much thought, he made two decisions -","First, send people to investigate Wei Ruzhang's hometown and Chai Weizhong's private residence;","Second, have Fu Hai send a box of jewels to Ganlu Palace.","He didn't want to hear that girl constantly thinking about money anymore.","It was as if he owed her a debt.","Yanshu woke up and immediately heard the news about tomorrow's ice games.","In the long, dull days of the inner palace, the ice games in winter and the water games in summer were the most anticipated events. Not only could they see soldiers showcasing their skills on water or ice, but they could also leave the palace to breathe some fresh air. The imperial consorts naturally looked forward to it.","In previous years, her rank wasn't high enough, so she could only stay in her own palace. But this time, having been promoted to Noble Lady, she finally had the chance to see it.","This was truly exciting. She happily got out of bed and was about to wash up. Her hand hadn't even touched the water in the basin when she heard the system's alarm, [The water is poisoned.]","Poisoned?","She retreated in shock, [What's going on?]","The system said, [Someone wants to harm you.]","Rendong was startled by her reaction and hurriedly asked, \"What's wrong, my lady?\"","Yanshu thought for a moment and asked, \"Where did this water come from?\"","Rendong said, \"Is the water prepared by Lv Yan too hot? Let me add some cold water for you...\"","\"No need,\" Yanshu replied, \"Call her in.\"","Rendong complied, though somewhat puzzled, and did as instructed.","Soon after, the palace maid called Lv Yan entered the hall.","— Earlier in Yongning Palace, Yanshu only had Rendong and Lianxin as her close attendants. After being promoted to Noble Lady, the Internal Affairs Bureau assigned four more palace maids and two eunuchs to her, and this girl was one of them.","At this moment, Lv Yan kept her eyes lowered, appearing obedient, and said with her head bowed, \"May I ask if the mistress has any instructions?\"","Yanshu didn't waste words with her and said directly, \"Come and wash your face with this water.\"","Immediately, Lv Yan's expression changed, and she stammered, \"This... This servant has already washed her face.\"","Yanshu then understood seven or eight tenths of the situation and sighed, \"I have no grudge against you, so why do you want to harm me?\"","The girl fell to her knees but still tried to defend herself, \"This servant doesn't know where she has erred to anger the mistress...\"","Yanshu gave up and said to Rendong, \"Go help her wash her face, and remember, don't let your hands touch the water.\"","Seeing the situation unfold, Rendong had mostly figured it out. She went directly to Lv Yan and pushed her face into the water.","In an instant, Lv Yan began to wail as if being stabbed with needles. Soon after, red rashes appeared on her face, some even oozing yellow fluid, making it unbearable to look at."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14","paragraphs":["It's worth noting that this scene was originally meant to happen to Yanshu.","Rendong angrily scolded on the spot, \"Who told you to harm your mistress like this? Speak up quickly!\"","However, Lv Yan only cried and kowtowed to Yanshu, \"Please spare my life, Noble Lady. I accidentally put lye in the water earlier...\"","Rendong couldn't resist kicking her, \"Still lying even when facing death!\"","Yanshu, however, began to ponder.","She had long understood that she was hated bitterly, but the palace was divided into two factions: Noble Consort Zhou's and Consort Ning's. So who was behind this attempt?","As she was thinking, she saw Fu Hai enter carrying a box.","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she immediately said, \"Fu Hai, you've come at the right time.\"","Fu Hai had already noticed the situation in the hall and quickly asked, \"Has something happened here, Noble Lady?\"","Yanshu asked Rendong to explain the situation to him.","After listening, Fu Hai secretly pondered in his heart.","This matter would not be easy to handle—","Even if they found out who was behind it, Li Beauty might not be able to withstand the consequences.","After all, Noble Consort Zhou had the Empress Dowager's support, while Consort Ning had the Princess's backing. Neither was easy to deal with...","Just then, he heard Yanshu say, \"This maid was only assigned from the Internal Affairs Bureau the day before yesterday. It's my fault for trusting such a person to serve me. What if His Majesty came by one day and accidentally fell victim to her schemes? I hear the new head of the Internal Affairs Bureau hasn't taken office yet, so I don't know who to turn to.\"","These words startled Fu Hai.","Indeed, although Li Beauty couldn't stand against those two, she had the Emperor on her side! Look how happy she had made the Emperor these past few days!","The night Pan Luhai was dismissed, the Internal Affairs Bureau hadn't found a new head yet, so he had been temporarily in charge these days. This way, wouldn't it become his responsibility?","He hurriedly said, \"If Noble Lady trusts me, I can handle this matter.\"","Yanshu nodded with satisfaction, \"Thank you for your trouble.\"","Then she asked, \"What brought Fu Hai here?\"","Fu Hai suddenly remembered his original purpose and quickly presented the box in his hands, saying, \"His Majesty instructed me to bring jewels to Noble Lady.\"","Yanshu was surprised, \"Jewels?\"","Fu Hai nodded vigorously, \"Didn't His Majesty play pitch-pot with Noble Lady last night? Afterwards, His Majesty stayed with the Empress Dowager until this morning. He had just finished the morning court session when he instructed me to bring these to you.\"","The disappointment from last night and the unpleasantness from earlier instantly vanished. Yanshu quickly said, \"Thank His Majesty for the reward.\"","Hey, who would have thought the flying treasures could fly back? It seems the Emperor has a good memory!","She hurriedly asked Rendong to accept the box and gave Fu Hai a reward. With a box full of heavy treasures, a little silver didn't seem like much anymore.","\"Thank you for the reward, Noble Lady.\"","Fu Hai accepted the reward, still pondering about Lv Yan's matter.","However, Yanshu spoke again, \"There's another matter, I'm not sure if I should mention it?\"","Fu Hai quickly said, \"Please, Noble Lady, do tell.\"","Yanshu acted mysteriously, purposely sending away the people around her before saying, \"Last night in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, the Empress Dowager asked about His Majesty's injury... I'm not sure who spread this information, as I remember His Majesty didn't want people to know about it? You manage the Qianming Palace, do you have any idea?\"","Fu Hai was stunned.","He hadn't been able to enter the inner chambers of the Palace of Benevolent Peace last night and didn't know what had happened inside. Now he learned that even the Empress Dowager knew about His Majesty's injury?","Tsk, His Majesty had only asked him to fetch some wound medicine and specifically ordered not to spread the word...","This matter was even more serious!","Fu Hai shuddered and quickly said, \"Noble Lady, please understand, how could I dare to speak carelessly about such an important matter?\"","Yanshu smiled, \"Chief Steward, you're taking this too seriously. You are His Majesty's most trusted person, so it certainly wasn't you. I was just wondering, since there are so many people in Qianming Palace, could there be one or two who like to gossip?\"","Fu Hai immediately understood and said, \"Thank you for the hint, Noble Lady. I'll investigate right away.\"","Yanshu nodded, smiling warmly, \"Please go ahead then.\"","Fu Hai agreed, wiping the cold sweat from his forehead, and hurried back to Qianming Palace.","After sending Fu Hai away, Yanshu didn't dare use the newly arrived maids anymore, only letting Rendong and Lianxin handle her personal matters.","Fortunately, Fu Hai was thoughtful and quickly assigned a few trustworthy palace maids for her to command.","The system didn't issue any more warnings, so Yanshu felt temporarily relieved. After finishing her morning toilette and breakfast, she happily opened the treasure box and counted her new wealth.","Hey, although the box wasn't large, it could hold quite a lot. Pearls of various sizes, colorful gemstones, and exquisite white jade, emerald, and agate dazzled the eyes.","Now that her heart was satisfied, she happily put away the treasures and took out paper and brush to continue writing her novel.","With food, drink, and money taken care of, all she needed to do now was stay alive and pursue her ideals. Who knows, maybe one day her work would indeed be passed down through generations.","In contrast, Yuwen Lan was much busier.","As the year-end approached, with natural disasters to deal with, he received local officials coming to the capital to report in the morning, continued to arrange disaster relief for Sichuan and Guizhou and deploy troops in the afternoon, and barely had time for his three meals a day.","It wasn't until nightfall that he finally had some free time.","He first asked about the situation in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, and Fu Hai reported, \"Judge Zhang from the Imperial Hospital has been personally attending to the Palace of Benevolent Peace today. It's said that the Empress Dowager has shown some improvement, but she's still bedridden.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"I'll go to watch over the Empress Dowager again tonight.\"","After saying this, he casually asked another young eunuch, Fu Bao, \"What did Li Beauty do today?\"","Fu Bao replied, \"Your Majesty, Li Beauty visited the Empress Dowager early in the morning, then stayed in Ganlu Palace without going out. No other consorts visited her during this time.\"","Yuwen Lan furrowed his brow again.","He really couldn't understand how she knew so much random information when she stayed in her palace all day and barely interacted with anyone.","During the day, his mind was occupied with matters of state, but now that he had some leisure time, the doubts in his heart grew stronger, like a hundred claws scratching at his heart, making him restless.","He thought for a moment and decided to go out.","Fu Hai hurriedly followed, initially thinking the Emperor was heading to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, but after a few steps, he realized they were going to Ganlu Palace.","Indeed, Yuwen Lan just wanted to investigate further, to find out what secrets that girl held.","Ganlu Palace wasn't far from Qianming Palace, so there was no need for a palanquin. They arrived after just a few steps.","He specifically ordered the palace guards not to announce his arrival and entered the hall himself, only to find that Yanshu was bathing in the washroom.","This was fine with him. He dismissed the maids and looked around the hall on his own. Suddenly, he noticed a stack of papers on a small kang table by the west window, with brush and ink beside it.","Hmm, what's this?","He picked up the papers and found that they contained coherent sentences.","However... the handwriting wasn't very good, making it a bit difficult to read.","Trying to read it, Yuwen Lan discovered that these weren't just ordinary sentences, but seemed to be a story, with characters, dialogues, and scenes.","He flipped through the papers, finally finding the first page of the story, which bore the title — \"The Romantic Scholar and the Beautiful Lady\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Looking aside, there was another stack of completed writings, titled \"The Heroic General and the Young Widow.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Why were they all in this style?","He tried to skim through \"The Romantic Scholar and the Beautiful Lady\" and saw that it was about a poor scholar who, by coincidence, caught the eye of a courtesan. The courtesan appreciated his talent and gave him gold and silver to help him take the imperial examination. Later, the scholar ranked second in the exam but married the daughter of a high-ranking official in the capital for the sake of his career, abandoning his former lover...","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","A scholar and a courtesan?","Thinking about last night, he vaguely felt that this scholar character might be based on Wei Ruzhang, the Grand Secretary of Wenhua Court.","Just then, the sound of water stopped in the washroom, and a freshly bathed beauty entered the bedchamber wearing a night robe.","Their eyes met, and Yanshu was startled, instinctively clutching her chest as she asked, \"When did Your Majesty arrive?\"","Yuwen Lan looked her over and said, \"Just now.\"","Hmm, her hair was slightly damp, her cheeks rosy, her skin like congealed cream — quite a pleasing sight.","But why was she covering her chest?","He had already kissed her last night.","He felt a bit displeased and asked, \"Why are you bathing so early?\"","Yanshu replied, \"I accidentally stained my clothes while writing earlier, so I decided to take a bath and change.\"","Yuwen Lan took the opportunity to ask, \"Did you write the papers on the table?\"","Yanshu nodded frankly, \"Yes, I was bored and wrote some stories to pass the time.\"","Then she asked him, \"Has Your Majesty read them? How is my writing?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"A bit vulgar.\"","Vulgar?","Yanshu immediately protested, \"Your subject boldly requests Your Majesty to enlighten me, where is it vulgar?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Isn't this kind of story about betrayal and disloyalty very common?\"","Yanshu pouted, \"That's because I haven't finished writing it yet. Your Majesty has only read the first half.\"","\"Oh?\"","Yuwen Lan became curious, \"Then what happens next?\"","Yanshu cleared her throat, \"Later, the courtesan discovers she's been betrayed, so she buys her freedom and ventures into the business world. She builds her enterprise bigger and bigger, and along the way finds a good man. After they marry, they live in harmony and have a son. The son is intelligent and studious from a young age. When he grows up, he takes the imperial examinations, progresses smoothly, and becomes a pillar of the court.\"","\"As for that scholar, blinded by greed and opportunism, he commits many evil deeds. Eventually, his misdeeds are exposed, and it happens to fall into the hands of the courtesan's son. With a wise emperor presiding over justice, the scholar finally gets his comeuppance and is demoted to a commoner. The courtesan, meanwhile, travels the world with her husband, living a life of leisure.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, it did sound somewhat different.","But after thinking for a moment, he said, \"According to our dynasty's laws, the children of merchants cannot take the imperial examinations.\"","Yanshu almost rolled her eyes at him, \"This is an alternate reality.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't understand, \"What do you mean by 'alternate reality'?\"","Yanshu explained, \"An alternate reality is a made-up world, not the actual present. Just like the characters in the story are all fictional.\"","Fictional?","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"What made you think of writing these things?\"","Yanshu casually replied, \"Your subject has read story books before. When I'm bored and want to pass the time, I just write.\"","Yuwen Lan probed further, \"Is there a real-life model for this scholar in the story?\"","A real-life model?","Yanshu thought to herself, there is one, but I certainly can't let you figure it out. How could I let you know it's Wei Ruzhang, the Grand Secretary of Wenhua Court?","But outwardly, she smiled and said, \"Didn't Your Majesty say that these kinds of stories are common? Your subject heard such a story in my hometown before and just adapted it a bit.\"","So it is Wei Ruzhang.","Yuwen Lan had figured it out in his heart. He then turned his gaze to the book titled \"The Passionate General and the Charming Widow,\" and said, \"Let me take a look at that one.\"","But as soon as he finished speaking, she swiftly snatched the manuscript into her hands and nervously said, \"Your Majesty shouldn't read this one yet.\"","Yuwen Lan was taken aback, \"Why not?\"","Yanshu stammered, \"It's just... it's just that I haven't finished writing this one yet.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Wasn't the previous story unfinished as well?\"","As he spoke, he still reached out to take it.","But Yanshu quickly dodged and said, \"No, this story isn't suitable for Your Majesty. It's meant for women to read.\"","Good heavens! This book is quite racy. What if he gets shocked after reading it?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan did not know what \"walking kidney\" meant.","But regardless, her unusual behavior must be suspicious.","He became even more determined to see it, so he reached out to take it again.","Unexpectedly, she panicked and hastily stuffed the manuscript into her nightgown.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Was she really so resistant to him?","He thought for a moment, then asked, \"You truly won't let me see it?\"","Yanshu nodded vigorously, \"Yes, I beg Your Majesty to spare me...\"","Before she could finish speaking, he suddenly pulled her into his arms.","Taking advantage of her being caught off guard, Yuwen Lan reached into her bosom with one hand and successfully retrieved the manuscript.","Hmm, his fingers brushed against softness like clouds, causing his heart to flutter.","Yanshu, slow to react, exclaimed \"Your Majesty!\"","But he whispered in her ear, \"Why are you acting like this? Are you deliberately trying to seduce me?\"","Yanshu's face turned red, \"I wouldn't dare!\"","He reached into her chest again, chuckling softly, \"Too bad, I have to go to the Palace of Benevolent Peace tonight to look after the Empress Dowager.\"","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","What a scoundrel!","However, he began reading the manuscript with great interest.","Yanshu couldn't snatch it back, feeling both embarrassed and annoyed. She wanted nothing more than to run to the bed and wrap herself up in the quilt.","But as he read, he started reciting aloud:","\"The moonlight was beautiful. Her smooth shoulders were half-exposed, and she cast a coquettish glance at the man before her. 'General, don't bother with me. Just let those people capture me and abandon me in the wilderness to feed the dogs...'\"","\"The general could no longer restrain himself. He embraced her, feeling her soft, warm body like jade in his arms, unable to let go...\"","...","Yuwen Lan couldn't bring himself to read the next lines out loud.","Yanshu snatched the manuscript back, her face as red as blood. \"I told Your Majesty it wasn't for you to read.\"","Yuwen Lan looked at her with an unreadable expression.","Yanshu suddenly felt guilty and hurriedly said, \"I was just writing for fun...\"","Damn, had she actually aroused him?","Was he going to kill her now?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","After staring at her for a while, he finally frowned and said, \"How could a girl from a scholarly family write such...\"","Lewd and obscene words.","Tsk, even he couldn't bring himself to say it.","Yanshu stubbornly defended herself, \"...As they say, food and sex are human nature. Besides, if I didn't write it this way, people wouldn't want to read it.\"","What?","People wouldn't like it if it wasn't written this way?","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"How do you know that?\"","Yanshu sighed inwardly, [I like reading this kind of thing, how could I not know?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What was wrong with this girl?","He heard her stammer out a lie, \"I'm just guessing. After all, when emotions are heightened, isn't it unsatisfying if nothing happens...\"","What nonsense!","Yuwen Lan was so angry he didn't know what to do. He reached out again and pulled her close, staring into her eyes. \"What kind of woman are you really?\"","His expression was unreadable, and his tone was a bit fierce. Yanshu felt scared and said, \"Your Majesty...\"","Her damp hair still clung to her cheeks, and her almond eyes looked frightened and innocent. Even her voice had suddenly softened to the core.","Yuwen Lan still showed no emotion, his dark eyes reflecting her fear.","Time seemed to stand still.","But in an instant, he suddenly lowered his head and captured her lips.","Entangling, intertwining, savoring at will.","He left Yanshu dizzy and weak, her body tingling as if she had lost her soul.","After who knows how long, a woman's voice suddenly came from far outside the hall, \"The air is dry, be careful with fire...\"","Yanshu came back to her senses from her daze, suddenly remembering... Wasn't that Consort Wang who had been punished?","Tsk, she was still making her rounds outside.","Yuwen Lan also regained his composure, finally releasing her and resting his forehead against hers to catch his breath.","After a moment, he said, \"I must go to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.\"","His voice had softened considerably compared to before.","Yanshu carefully acknowledged.","Then, she saw him abruptly let go of her and stride out of the hall.","Yanshu frowned as she watched his retreating figure, unsure of what had come over him.","Was he pleased or angry?","It was like a fog, impossible to see through.","Yuwen Lan didn't take his palanquin, walking alone in the night.","His steps were so quick that Fu Hai could barely keep up.","Fu Hai chased after him while pondering to himself - why did the emperor seem angry?","Had he quarreled with Consort Li?","In fact, even Yuwen Lan didn't know what had come over him.","In that moment earlier, his mind had lost control, yet his body still didn't fully cooperate.","An inexplicable irritation built up in his heart. He just wanted to walk quickly, hoping the cold wind would help clear his head.","That night, Yanshu slept uneasily.","In her dreams, there was a big tiger that alternated between acting cute and trying to bite her, truly terrifying.","Early the next morning, she emerged from behind the curtains with dark circles under her eyes, startling Rendong. \"What happened to you, my lady? Did you not sleep well last night?\"","Yanshu sighed, \"I spent the whole night running for my life in my dreams. It was exhausting.\"","After washing her face, she felt a bit more awake. Rendong brought over the makeup box and started applying powder to her face while nagging, \"You're going with His Majesty to watch the ice show at Jinbo Garden today. You must dress up nicely.\"","Ah yes, the ice show at Jinbo Garden. Yanshu finally remembered.","Oh, she could leave the palace!","She suddenly felt happy. Even though she would have to return, it was nice to get some fresh air!","Since staying low-key was useless now anyway, she let Rendong and Lianxin work their magic. When her makeup was done, she looked in the mirror to see bright eyes, white teeth, and an ethereal beauty.","The palace maids all praised her, \"My lady has such a good foundation, you should dress up like this every day!\"","Yanshu didn't think much of it, only instructing, \"Bring me a thick cloak.\"","She estimated it would be cold there and didn't want to freeze.","\"Oh, and,\" she added, \"I need to eat more at breakfast later. It's easy to get hungry in cold weather.\"","Rendong: \"...\"","Other ladies would be too focused on dressing up to eat, but her mistress never forgot about food.","After finishing a basket of crab roe soup dumplings, a bowl of shrimp noodle soup, a beef pastry, and two small side dishes, Yanshu was finally satisfied and boarded the carriage to leave the palace.","Jinbo Garden was located within the capital city, only about half an hour's journey by carriage.","Due to the emperor and consorts' outing, the roads were heavily guarded. Yanshu was disappointed she couldn't see the bustling streets.","However, when they arrived and she got out of the carriage, she saw the beautiful scenery of Jinbo Garden.","It had snowed just days ago, and white snow still clung to the golden roof tiles and flower bushes, creating a striking contrast with the vermilion walls.","Of course, the most attractive feature of the garden was Jinbo Lake.","Legend had it that in summer, when gentle breezes rippled across the lake's surface, the sparkling waves under the setting sun resembled thousands of golden ripples, hence the name.","Of course, now in the depths of winter, the lake surface had long since frozen into thick ice. Though there were no golden waves, it was as smooth as a mirror, perfect for ice performances.","However, the weather was extremely cold, with the wind feeling like knife cuts on one's face, making it impossible to enjoy the scenery. So after getting out of the carriages, everyone went directly to the lakeside viewing pavilion.","The viewing pavilion had three floors, with the highest offering the best view. To show his approachability, the emperor specially allowed several important court officials and royal clan members to watch together.","Yanshu followed the other consorts into the hall and took her seat.","Consort Ning and Consort Li exchanged a complicated look.","-- This bitch actually hadn't fallen for their trap. Her face was still smooth.","But it didn't matter. There was still a big scene waiting for her later. This time they would surely finish her off completely!","At the same time, the system chimed in Yanshu's mind, [There will be a big scene today.]","Yanshu: [I'll just wait and see how it unfolds.]","Not long after, Yuwen Lan arrived as well.","Everyone hurriedly stood up and bowed, calling out in unison, \"We welcome Your Majesty.\"","Yanshu followed along perfunctorily, sneaking a glance at him. She saw that he was wearing an ink-blue dragon robe with a black crane-patterned cloak over it. His dark hair was tied up high with a purple-gold crown, making him look even more handsome and dignified.","It was supposed to be a solemn occasion, but for some reason, Yanshu suddenly recalled the scene of him kissing her last night, and her face grew hot.","She had to admit, his kissing skills were... quite impressive, ahem.","Today, only the higher-ranking consorts above Talented Lady had come from the harem. There weren't many to begin with, and Yuwen Lan easily distinguished her thoughts among the fangirling inner voices of the others.","He almost lost control of his expression for a moment.","What?","His kissing skills were quite good?","This woman!","However, at the same time, he couldn't help but recall last night's events, as well as that book \"The Hot-Blooded General and the Flirtatious Widow\"...","Fu Hai suddenly noticed that the tips of the emperor's ears had quietly turned red.","What's going on? Could it be that the hall is too cold, and His Majesty has frozen up?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had no choice but to endure, barely maintaining his dignified expression as he took his seat.","Next, the imperial clan, royal relatives, and court nobles filed into the hall to pay their respects.","According to rank and closeness, the first to appear were Princess Yuwen Yan and her consort Zhao Chengwen.","Everyone knew that the late emperor had few descendants, with only the current emperor and the princess as his children. Thus, the princess's status was evident.","Yanshu rarely attended such grand occasions. She observed that the princess appeared to be three or four years older than the emperor, dressed in extremely rich and elegant attire.","She recalled how Consort Ning's jeweled hairpin had dazzled everyone at the New Year's Eve banquet, but the princess's outfit today was even more extravagant - a gold and jade step-shake ornament, an eight-treasure pearl-wrapped gold hairpin, a gold-embroidered long jacket, and a bright red fox fur cape with gold plum blossom patterns.","Her aura was even more powerful than Noble Consort Zhou's.","However, her consort Zhao Chengwen maintained a meek and submissive demeanor.","Tsk, it seems that being the consort of a princess isn't an easy job either.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What kind of talk is this? What does she mean by \"easy job\"?","Unable to be distracted at this moment, he first addressed the princess, \"Royal Sister, please don't stand on ceremony. Have a seat.\"","Yuwen Yan complied and sat down with her consort in a nearby position.","Not far away, Consort Ning's back straightened a bit.","After all, these were her paternal uncle and aunt. Among all the people present today, who could outrank this couple?","Noble Consort Zhou was naturally displeased, especially since the Empress Dowager was resting in the palace today and hadn't attended.","However, her parents were about to make their entrance as well.","Duke Cheng'en and his Madame came forward to pay their respects, \"We pay our respects to Your Majesty.\"","Yanshu and Rendong exchanged glances, thinking to themselves, [This is that old lecher. Look at those dark circles under his eyes, it's obvious he's suffering from kidney deficiency!]","[And yet he still keeps concubines numbered five, six, seven, eight... He's not afraid of dying from overexertion one day, expiring in some concubine's bed...]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Dying from overexertion???","This girl is really...!","However, he had to admit that Duke Cheng'en did indeed have some dark circles under his eyes. He thought for a moment and asked, \"Uncle, how has your health been lately?\"","Duke Cheng'en paused, then quickly smiled and said, \"Thank you for Your Majesty's concern. I am quite well.\"","His Madame, however, gave him a side glance and inwardly spat, [Bah! Shameless scoundrel! Even His Majesty can see it. You deserve to be embarrassed! You've disgraced all the ancestors of your Zhou family!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","It seems it's actually true."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan was struck with astonishment.","He couldn't help but glance at Yanshu, feeling extremely puzzled in his heart - how did she even know about the affairs of the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion?","He himself wasn't even that clear about it...","Just then, he heard the Duke of Cheng'en ask, \"I've heard that the Empress Dowager's health is poor. How is she now?\"","Yuwen Lan snapped back to attention and replied, \"Mother is resting in the palace. She's better than she was a couple days ago. Uncle, there's no need to worry too much.\"","With that, he invited the two to be seated.","Noble Consort Zhou straightened her back a little.","Next, other people entered the scene, such as the Three Excellencies and Six Ministries, all of whom were important court officials.","Seeing these protagonists of the drama appear in the flesh, Yanshu's eyes could hardly keep up -","[So the supposedly gay Assistant Minister of War is actually a rugged man with a full beard? And he's the bottom?]","Yuwen Lan, who was silently listening, went \"???\"","What did \"bottom\" mean?","He couldn't quite understand.","Before he could recover, he heard her exclaim internally again, [That white-haired old man who looks so upright is actually Wei Ruzhang, the Grand Secretary of Wenhua Court? Tsk tsk, you really can't judge a book by its cover! Isn't this what they call a wolf in sheep's clothing?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","To be honest, ever since he read that book \"The Charming Scholar and the Beautiful Lady\" last night, he increasingly felt that Wei Ruzhang had a treacherous look.","However, the people he sent to investigate hadn't returned yet, so he couldn't do anything to him for now.","Next to enter was Linwu Marquis Sun Xiaoguang, followed by his heir Sun Zhanpeng.","— After quite a commotion in recent days, the Linwu Marquis had finally divorced his wife, but his heir remained in the household as his flesh and blood.","Yanshu, hiding to the side, tsked, [Poor man, haven't you noticed that your son doesn't look like you? You have a square face, he has a round face, you have a high nose bridge, he has a flat nose!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He couldn't help but silently compare the father and son, and suddenly felt that this son indeed didn't look much like the Linwu Marquis...","Could it be that he really wasn't his?","What should be done about this? Should he warn him?","But he had no evidence...","...","After that, he learned many small secrets about various people such as the Minister of Works, the Southwest Communications Commissioner, the Marquis of Guangyang, and many others.","For instance, the Minister of Works had a strange eating habit - he liked to eat writing paper while writing. Once he claimed to be sick and didn't come to court, but in fact, he had a stomach ache from eating too much paper.","The Southwest Communications Commissioner actually loved visiting brothels. Whenever he left the capital, he would seek out courtesans every night...","As for the Marquis of Guangyang, despite his outwardly rough appearance, he was actually very prone to crying and often secretly wept in his study...","After a round of greetings, the emperor's worldview was severely shaken - what kind of people did he have around him?","Were there any normal ones at all???","As the formalities were completed and everyone took their seats, the ice games were about to begin.","The first event was the ice dash.","At one end of the vast ice surface stood a banner. With the sound of a gong, more than twenty soldiers wearing specially made iron-toothed ice skates began to skate forward on the ice with all their might. They moved like shooting stars and flashing lightning, racing towards the banner, with the first to arrive being the winner.","There was also a tight drumbeat accompanying the race, making people's heartstrings tense with excitement.","Everyone watched with rapt attention, and Yanshu didn't dare to blink.","She realized that this ice dash was actually like speed skating in modern times, and just as thrilling!","There were five preliminary rounds for the ice dash. After all rounds were completed, the top three from each round were selected for the finals. This way, only the best of the best participated in the finals, naturally making it even more exciting.","It got everyone's blood pumping.","Next was the dragon turn and ball shooting.","In the center of the ice, a banner gate was suspended high, with a ball placed above and below it. Six groups of soldiers wore different colored clothes, with one person at the front of each team holding a flag of the same color as their clothes, while those behind carried bows and arrows.","At the sound of a command, the six teams began to skate in a serpentine pattern on the ice, starting from the lake shore and heading towards the banner gate.","Viewed from the viewing platform, it looked like six colorful dragons winding their way, which was quite a sight.","As they approached the banner gate, the archers began to draw their bows towards the balls on the gate, and then returned by the same route, not only demonstrating accurate archery but also maintaining their formation throughout, creating a very pleasing visual effect.","After this, there were other events such as handstands on ice, pole climbing, and ice combat, all of which were spectacular and dazzling to watch.","Of course, for Yanshu, the most wonderful part was the food on the table.","Besides various pastries and fried sweets, there was even freshly roasted pork and mutton.","It's worth noting that such hearty fare was rarely seen in the palace!","Tsk, the crispy skin of the roast pork was extremely crunchy, while the meat inside was perfectly marbled and well-seasoned. The combination of textures was truly satisfying!","The roast mutton was even better! The juicy lamb meat was still bubbling with oil, permeated with the aroma of charcoal fire down to the last fiber. It was so delicious it made one want to dance!","Savoring these rare delicacies while watching the exciting competitions outside - it was worth braving the cold!","Yuwen Lan, who had been quietly observing her, \"...\"","While everyone in the viewing pavilion had their own thoughts, her mind was full of gossip and food.","Ever since the dishes were served, her mouth hadn't stopped moving.","How could she eat so much without getting fat?","Though... a little plumpness might not be bad, ahem.","Seeing her eat with such relish, he couldn't help but take a few bites himself.","After the ice combat ended, it was time for today's main event - ice ball snatching.","This was the largest and most intense event of the day.","With a drumroll, two teams of soldiers entered the field, wearing red and yellow clothes respectively.","The Imperial Guard Commander, holding a leather ball, came to the viewing pavilion and bowed to the emperor, saying, \"Your Majesty, please start the game.\"","This was the ball that the two teams would be fighting for.","A dragon was painted in vermilion on the golden leather ball, requiring the emperor to personally dot its eyes to show its importance.","This had been the custom of the dynasty for generations. Yuwen Lan had already done this twice before. He once again picked up the brush to dot the eyes and handed it to the Imperial Guard Commander.","The Commander took the ball and went down, and the ball-snatching battle began.","The red and yellow teams fought fiercely for the ball, creating a spectacular scene. The audience in the pavilion watched the match intently.","Influenced by Yanshu, Yuwen Lan idly started eating roast meat again during his free time.","The rich flavor of the roast meat made him unable to resist having a few more sips of wine.","As he reached out to pick up his cup, he exposed his left hand, revealing faint dark red marks on the side, seemingly traces of an injury.","Beside him, Consort Ning immediately glanced at the Princess.","Princess Yuwen Yan spoke up, \"Has Your Majesty injured your hand?\"","Yuwen Lan showed no unusual expression and simply said, \"It's nothing.\"","However, the Princess continued, \"Your Majesty must not conceal anything from us. Your body is worth ten thousand in gold, any injury is no small matter.\"","She then turned to Fu Hai and scolded, \"How are you doing your job? Quickly tell us, who exactly harmed His Majesty?\"","This startled Fu Hai, who hastily said, \"Your Highness, please calm down. His Majesty accidentally injured himself while practicing swordsmanship a couple of days ago.\"","Yuwen Yan snorted again, \"Don't try to fool me! His Majesty has practiced martial arts since childhood, when has he ever injured himself? Moreover, His Majesty clearly got injured in the middle of the night, how could it be from sword practice? Who exactly was it, you slave, why are you covering for someone?\"","Fu Hai dared not speak anymore.","Yuwen Lan's brows furrowed.","Very well, even the fact that he was injured in the middle of the night was known?","Just then, another official spoke up, \"His Majesty's body is of utmost importance. If he was indeed harmed by someone, that person must be severely punished!\"","As soon as these words were spoken, several others chimed in, \"Someone actually dared to harm His Majesty? Who was it? We implore Your Majesty to bring them to justice!\"","...","To the side, Yanshu inwardly exclaimed, \"Oh my, I guessed right.\"","These people were trying to make a big deal out of the emperor's injury, probably thinking he got hurt while favoring her, so they wanted to force him to punish her?","Unfortunately, that wasn't the case at all.","Yuwen Lan's ears suddenly became filled with noise.","He could hear Consort Ning thinking nearby, [With so many people speaking up, surely His Majesty won't protect that harlot anymore! Hmph, we must get rid of her this time.]","Noble Consort Zhou was thinking smugly, [Consort Ning is quite clever, knowing to have the Princess speak up. Only that foolish woman would do such a thing. It's a good thing I listened to Consort An's advice, I'll just watch the show today.]","Consort An was thinking, [With so many people speaking up together today, His Majesty will surely have to give an explanation.]","...","He had known that some people were restless and wanted to use his injury to cause trouble. Sure enough, they all came out today.","He said, \"I should thank my elder sister for her concern, but my injury has nothing to do with anyone else. It really was self-inflicted.\"","Then, he turned to look at the Minister of Communication and Chief Censor who were kneeling on the ground, saying, \"I have already spoken to you about this matter. Are you joining in the commotion today because you're deaf or because your memory is poor?\"","The officials quickly replied, \"We wouldn't dare, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Yan hurriedly chimed in, \"Your Majesty, they are all senior officials who only want the best for you. Please don't shield the main culprit!\"","As she spoke, she glanced at Yanshu from the corner of her eye, thinking to herself, [Li Yanshu? Isn't she the one who's always eating? What's so great about a country bumpkin that you'd reject Consort Ning whom I chose for you? How shortsighted! The power in the harem must not fall into others' hands!]","Yuwen Lan sneered, \"Is my elder sister trying to force me to admit to something that didn't happen?\"","Yuwen Yan said, \"I wouldn't dare, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan scoffed, \"You wouldn't dare? Then how did you know about my injury? Who told you?\"","Yuwen Yan replied, \"I saw it with my own eyes. Didn't Your Majesty just show your hand?\"","Yuwen Lan gave a cold laugh, \"The hand I showed just now was my left hand, but my injury is on my right hand.\"","Princess Yuwen Yan was stunned and glanced at Consort Ning.","Damn it, this girl hadn't told her which hand the Emperor had injured!","Consort Ning was also taken aback, wondering how she could have gotten it wrong. Wasn't the color on the side of his hand from a scar?","Yuwen Lan spoke coldly, \"The color on my left hand is paint from the leather ball earlier.\"","What? It was just discoloration from the ball!","Princess Yuwen Yan and Consort Ning exchanged glances, both feeling somewhat flustered.","Yuwen Lan asked Princess Yuwen Yan in a stern voice, \"I want to know who planned this farce today and even invited my royal sister to participate?\"","The Princess hesitated, then quickly said, \"I wouldn't dare, Your Majesty. No one planned anything. I was simply too worried when I heard Your Majesty was injured.\"","Yuwen Lan said \"Oh,\" then asked, \"Then who told you I was injured in the middle of the night? Why is it that even the slightest movement in the palace is known so clearly outside?\"","These words carried significant weight, and Yuwen Yan's face changed. She hurriedly said again, \"Your Majesty's words are too severe. I truly wouldn't dare.\"","As she finished speaking, Fu Hai suddenly addressed Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, this foolish servant only discovered yesterday that there was a sneaky little thief in Qianming Palace, secretly reporting Your Majesty's movements to others.\""]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17","paragraphs":["As soon as these words were spoken, everyone looked surprised.","Who would dare to be so bold?","Yuwen Lan said, \"Bring him up.\"","Fu Hai complied, quickly directing people to bring a tightly bound young eunuch before the emperor.","The young eunuch, with a bruised and swollen face, was already terrified out of his wits. He kowtowed desperately, pleading, \"Your Majesty, spare my life, please spare my life...\"","Meanwhile, Consort Ning, Consort Li, and the others instantly changed their expressions.","This was bad - how did they even find out about the little eunuch?","Yuwen Lan only asked the young eunuch, \"Who instructed you to spy on me?\"","The young eunuch trembled and stuttered, \"It was... it was...\"","At this critical moment, Consort Ning suddenly knelt down and said, \"I beg Your Majesty to calm your anger. It was Consort Li who told me a few days ago about Your injury. I was only concerned about Your health, so I...\"","What?","Consort Li's face turned pale, and she exclaimed in surprise, \"Consort Ning, you...\"","\"Silence!\"","Consort Ning scolded harshly, \"You are truly reckless and have lost all sense of propriety. How dare you spy on His Majesty? Don't you know the consequences?\"","As she spoke, she cast a warning glance at Consort Li.","Princess Yuwen Yan also gave her a cold look.","Consort Li was stunned and hesitated.","—Her aunt had just divorced the Marquis of Linwu, and how could her own declining family contend with the Princess?","But if she admitted to it, it would be a serious crime!","She was unwilling to accept this fate and secretly searched the hall, her gaze falling on the Marquis of Linwu and his son Sun Zhanpeng.","That was her former uncle, and Sun Zhanpeng was her aunt's son. Surely they would speak up for her, given their relationship?","However, the Marquis of Linwu didn't even look at her, his expression cold and indifferent.","She then looked to her cousin Sun Zhanpeng, but saw the young man hesitate for a moment before averting his gaze as well.","Consort Li was in despair.","All these years she had relied on Consort Ning, and everything she had was due to her relationship with Consort Ning. Now that Consort Ning wanted her to take the blame, no one would help her.","So she could only kneel and cry, \"This concubine was only concerned about Your Majesty's health. Please have mercy and forgive me this once...\"","Then Fu Hai spoke again, \"Your Majesty, there's another matter. Yesterday, a palace maid in Ganlu Palace attempted to poison Li Beauty's face-washing water, intending to damage her appearance. Fortunately, Li Beauty discovered it in time and avoided harm. Upon questioning, the palace maid claimed she was acting on Consort Li's orders.\"","As these words fell, Yanshu finally knew who was behind this attempt to harm her.","Of course, Fu Hai was indeed a cunning old fox. Seeing that Consort Li was now powerless, he chose this moment to reveal this information, leaving her unable to defend herself.","Looking at Consort Li again, she indeed wanted to say something, but ultimately remained silent.","After a moment, the emperor spoke coldly, \"Send her to the Cold Palace as a warning to others.\"","Consort Li collapsed to the ground.","It was over, completely over...","Not far away, Consort Ning felt a chill run through her body, her heart pounding. She didn't even dare to glance at Consort Li.","However, Yuwen Lan didn't let her off. He turned his cold gaze to her and said, \"You hold the position of consort, yet you cannot distinguish right from wrong, causing today's uproar. You've made us a laughingstock. From this day forward, you are confined to your palace for thirty days. Reflect on your actions in seclusion, and you are not allowed to leave.\"","\"Your Majesty...\"","Consort Ning wanted to argue, but caught sight of the Princess shaking her head at her from the corner of her eye.","She dared not say more and could only kneel and cry, \"This concubine obeys.\"","Yuwen Lan instructed Fu Hai, \"Send people to escort them back.\"","Fu Hai quickly complied, calling several palace maids and eunuchs to \"invite\" the two back to their quarters.","Yuwen Lan glanced at the young eunuch again and said, \"Deal with him according to palace rules.\"","—According to palace rules, this meant being beaten to death.","Everyone else in the hall trembled in fear, not daring to make a sound.","Then the emperor looked at the Princess and said, \"Elder sister, you are at this age, yet still so rash. It truly goes against your status. Go back and also confine yourself for a month. Think carefully about how to conduct yourself properly. I hope you will show some improvement.\"","This was the first time in her life that she had been punished by her younger brother. Yuwen Yan's face flushed red and white. However, her consort beside her didn't dare to utter a word, his head almost buried in the ground.","Yuwen Yan was filled with resentment and anger, but could only respond with a \"Yes\" and left with her silent consort.","Noble Consort Zhou felt somewhat smug inside, but didn't dare to show it. She only thought to herself that since Fu Hai had managed to root out even Consort Ning's spies, she would need to be even more careful in the future.","However, those few ministers were trembling like ants on a hot pan. Before Yuwen Lan could speak, they all knelt and kowtowed, saying, \"We know our crimes...\"","Yuwen Lan said coldly, \"Those who caused a commotion earlier will each be fined half a year's salary and demoted three ranks. If anyone dares to offend again, they will be demoted to commoners.\"","The men obediently agreed and retreated, trembling.","After all this commotion, the ice ball game on the frozen lake had also ended.","Originally, there were supposed to be ice dances and a banquet afterwards, but the emperor was no longer in the mood and directly announced their return to the palace.","Everyone could only comply. Seeing him stand up and walk out, Noble Consort Zhou, Consort An, Consort Xu, Yanshu, and others hurriedly followed.","The emperor walked with purposeful strides. Behind him, Noble Consort Zhou and Consort An exchanged glances, both silently lamenting that they hadn't been able to touch Yanshu this time!","However, it was good that one of Consort Ning's arms had been cut off. They would have to find another opportunity to deal with Yanshu next time.","Yuwen Lan silently listened to this, and couldn't help but try to eavesdrop on the thoughts of the protagonist of their conversation.","She was thinking, [There's still half a roast pig left uneaten, what a waste.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","At a time like this, she was still thinking about food?","He couldn't help but turn back to look at her, his gaze appearing somewhat cold.","At that moment, Yanshu was also looking up at him, and their eyes unexpectedly met.","She looked panicked and quickly lowered her head, seemingly finally afraid.","But Yuwen Lan heard her grumbling in her mind, [What are you looking at? If you hadn't been a pervert and peeped at me back then, we wouldn't have all this trouble!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Huh, so now it was his fault?","By the time they returned to the bedchamber, it was pitch dark outside.","Yanshu had eaten her fill of roast pig and lamb, so she wasn't hungry anymore. She only drank a bowl of hot jujube tea.","However, having worn heavy makeup all day and with a lot of osmanthus oil in her hair, she felt quite uncomfortable. So she went to take a hot bath.","After all, the emperor was in a bad mood today, so he probably wouldn't come over.","Indeed, when she came out after her bath, there was no sign of the emperor.","Seeing that it was already quite late, she climbed into bed and snuggled under the covers, falling into a sweet sleep.","As the lights in Ganlu Palace were being extinguished, Qianming Palace was still brightly lit.","The people sent out to investigate a few days ago had all returned and were reporting to Yuwen Lan.","\"Your Majesty, after our investigation, we found that Lord Chai's original wife is still in their hometown serving his parents and raising their two children. In the capital, Lord Chai has three concubines in his mansion, but they are actually men disguised as women.\"","\"Men?\"","Yuwen Lan frowned.","The imperial guard confirmed, \"Yes, they are indeed men. In addition, he has a separate courtyard in Huanhua Lane in the capital, where he keeps about five or six catamites.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So it was true.","That Chai Weizhong... was indeed homosexual!","Moreover, he actually left his first wife in their hometown to serve his parents and raise their children, while he himself was being so... outrageous in the capital?","He said, \"Continue to keep an eye on him. If there's any illegal activity, report to me immediately.\"","The imperial guard complied.","He then looked at another person, \"How about the other matter?\"","\"Your Majesty, during our investigation in Jinling City, we discovered that Chancellor Wei came from a poor family background. He once made a living by writing letters and painting for others in the brothels, and he became involved with a courtesan. Later, with financial support from that woman, he was able to go to the capital to take the imperial examination.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This plot was indeed very similar to the first half of that \"The Romantic Scholar and the Beautiful Courtesan\" story?","He asked, \"What about that woman?\"","\"We heard that the woman waited for Chancellor Wei in vain. Later, when she heard that he had passed the examination, become an official in the capital, and married and had children, she became disillusioned. She ended up becoming a concubine to a merchant and disappeared after that.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded.","The second half of that story was certainly unrealistic; it was indeed something she had made up herself.","At this point, he had a clear understanding in his heart.","At the same time, he was even more puzzled.","Everything she had said turned out to be true. Where did she get such supernatural abilities?","This question remained unclear, and in fact, it confused him more and more. As the night deepened, Yuwen Lan couldn't sleep at all.","He had considered many possibilities—","First, did that girl have mind-reading abilities like him? Obviously not. If she did, how could she not guess what he was thinking, always managing to anger him to the point of speechlessness?","Moreover, she had never even met these people, so there was no opportunity for her to use mind-reading abilities.","Second, was there another powerful figure in the palace who had told her these things?","But he had already ordered a search of every corner and had personally visited Ganlu Palace multiple times, without finding any trace or clue.","This girl, what secret was she really hiding?","Watching the emperor pacing silently in the hall with furrowed brows, Fu Hai, who was serving nearby, sighed inwardly, [His Majesty is furious! Those wretches deserve to be punished! Fortunately, Li Beauty gave him a heads up in advance, otherwise it would have been my own head on the chopping block today, tsk.]","As Fu Hai finished his silent reflection and looked up, he saw the emperor staring at him with a shocked expression.","\"I forgot to ask you,\" Yuwen Lan said in a deep voice, \"How did you discover that little eunuch's misconduct? You must tell me the whole truth!\"","Fu Hai trembled and had no choice but to honestly reply, \"Your Majesty, please forgive me. This matter... it was Li Beauty who alerted your servant...\"","...","Deep in the night, the cold was biting.","Yuwen Lan forgot even to put on his fox fur coat as he strode quickly through the night wind.","By the time he realized it, he had already arrived at Ganlu Palace.","The lights in the palace had been extinguished. He didn't call for anyone to announce him, but pushed the door open and went straight in.","The person he was looking for was sound asleep behind the curtains.","Having just learned with surprise that it was she who had tipped off Fu Hai to catch the culprit, his mind was bursting with questions!","Could she really have the power of foresight?","However, when he abruptly pulled back the curtain, he was stunned by the scene before him.","The girl was sprawled out in her sleep, not even covered by the blanket. Her thin nightgown was in disarray, and even... exposed her chest and belly."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18","paragraphs":["Perhaps due to eating too much lamb during the day, Yanshu felt somewhat feverish tonight.","Combined with the warmth from the floor heating in the palace, she felt unbearably hot, so she kicked off her blanket and loosened her collar.","But how could she have known that someone would come at this time?","And without any announcement, he entered the hall and lifted the curtain directly.","However, at this moment, she was in a deep sleep, completely unaware that someone was staring at her.","Yuwen Lan stood there looking at her for a while, silently taking in the beautiful sight, but he didn't easily show his emotions.","After all, he still had a belly full of doubts.","At first, he couldn't tell if she was really asleep or pretending, so he spoke, \"Asleep so early?\"","But there was no response.","The girl still had her eyes closed, her long eyelashes resting on her jade-like face, her cherry lips slightly pouted, her chest rising and falling with her breath. She seemed to be sleeping soundly.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This wasn't getting anywhere. He decided to wake her up, so he called out again, \"Li Beauty.\"","His voice unconsciously deepened, sounding quite authoritative.","But still, there was no response.","The girl was sleeping like a dead pig, not even lifting an eyelid.","Yuwen Lan's face darkened, and he simply said, \"Li Yanshu!\"","This time there was finally a reaction. Yanshu mumbled, \"So tired, don't bother me...\" and then she actually turned her back to him and continued to sleep soundly.","Throughout all of this, she never opened her eyes.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Even thunder couldn't wake her up?","After some thought, he simply lay down beside her.","The curtained bed was dim, with only the light from a small bedside lamp outside.","Yuwen Lan sighed and said, as if talking to himself, \"How did you know about those things?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the sleeping person actually giggled, \"Gossip, of course.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What? Gossip?","He tried asking again, \"What kind of gossip?\"","But she didn't speak anymore.","Yuwen Lan: \"...Hey!\"","She continued to sleep soundly, her breathing deep and long.","Yuwen Lan watched her, suddenly pulling her into his arms.","She was still sound asleep.","He sought out her cherry lips and kissed her.","And just like before, an indescribable feeling rose in his heart.","However, that numb place.","Still disappointed him.","But at this moment, the person in his arms suddenly opened her eyes.","\"Your Majesty...\"","She seemed a bit surprised, yet still in a daze. Yuwen Lan paused, and as if possessed, suddenly tucked her head against his chest, saying softly, \"Sleep.\"","After a moment, she indeed fell back into a deep sleep.","Yuwen Lan put aside that hint of vexation and disappointment, and simply closed his eyes as well.","He still believed that it wouldn't always be like this, that heaven couldn't be so cruel to him.","The fragrant softness in his arms, the long breaths by his ear, were like gentle waves, engulfing him sound by sound.","Finally, he too gradually fell asleep.","That night, Yuwen Lan actually had a dream.","It's worth noting that since ascending to the throne, he hadn't dreamed at all.","He dreamed that he was lying in a soft cloud, surrounded by spring sunshine, warming him comfortably.","His body floated along with the cloud, just like swinging on a swing as a child.","Such was the night, and when he woke up, it was already dawn.","Come to think of it, this was the first time he had slept with a woman for an entire night, and he had slept quite well.","However, he still remembered the purpose of his visit last night.","Seeing that she had delayed him for another night, it was time to stop procrastinating.","He lowered his eyes to look at the girl beside him.","But he saw that at some point, she had messed up her nightgown again, revealing a patch of snow-white skin.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He silently pulled her collar closed, and then spoke, \"Li Beauty.\"","Yanshu, having slept enough, gradually opened her eyes.","At first, she was a bit dazed, but when she saw him clearly, her eyes suddenly widened in surprise, \"Your Majesty? When did you arrive?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"I've shared a bed with you all night, and you didn't notice?\"","What? This man had slept beside her all night?","Yanshu shook her head in bewilderment.","—To be honest, she had a habit that could hardly be called a flaw: she slept very deeply, and once asleep, even thunder wouldn't wake her.","She tried to recall, vaguely remembering someone talking to her in her dream last night. Could it have been the emperor?","Her heart skipped a beat, and she looked at him uncertainly—she hadn't said anything strange in her sleep, had she?","Yuwen Lan was about to question her, so he took the opportunity to speak, \"I have questions for you.\"","Yanshu felt a bit guilty, \"...Yes.\"","But she heard him say, \"Was it you who told Fu Hai to investigate that young eunuch in Qianming Palace?\"","So that's what he wanted to ask about.","Yanshu felt relieved and said, \"I merely mentioned it in passing to Lord Fu, he found the person himself.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Then why did you remind him to investigate?\"","Yanshu said, \"Your Majesty didn't want others to know about your injury, but even the Empress Dowager knew about it. There must have been someone who gossiped. Anyway, there's no harm in investigating.\"","[This is what they call a blind spot. No matter how brilliant and powerful you are, there are always things you can't cover.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had to admit, that was indeed the case.","Although he had the ability to read minds, he could only hear the thoughts of those close to him. There were so many people in Qianming Palace, he couldn't possibly see everyone.","Moreover, various forces from the court were entrenched, and the Princess and the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion had infiltrated the harem even when the late emperor was still alive. He hadn't completely cleaned them out yet, and that was a fact.","He asked again, \"Then how did you detect the poison in the face-washing water?\"","Yanshu said, \"I have a keen sense of smell. That day, I knew something was wrong with the water as soon as I smelled it.\"","In her heart, she thought, [That sounds really uncomfortable. Did I have to be poisoned and disfigured for it to count? When all is said and done, isn't it because of you? Isn't this the fate of a target?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Now she was blaming him?","But to be honest... it did seem to be the case.","Because of his approach, other women in the palace had murderous intentions towards her.","Well, she did face danger this time, so he had to say, \"I will have Fu Hai assign a few more reliable palace maids to you. Such incidents should not happen again.\"","Yanshu said, \"Thank you, Your Majesty.\"","But in her heart, she pouted, [Is that all? No emotional compensation? I was scared out of my wits, after all.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Emotional compensation?","Huh, he knew she was always pushing her luck.","At this moment, he saw her pulling her collar closed again, seeming to look at him with a guarded expression.","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but feel mischievous and said, \"Why are you covering up? When I came last night, you were almost naked.\"","What?","Yanshu's eyes widened. No, naked???","Then, then, then what did he do to her?","But she saw Yuwen Lan lean close to her ear and say, \"What do you think I would do?\"","Yanshu: \"...Your Majesty!\"","Scoundrel!!!","But she saw him raise an eyebrow with a nonchalant face, \"Why so reserved? Aren't you my consort?\"","With that, he lifted the bed curtain and said, \"I have important matters to attend to later.\" Then he got out of bed.","This meant she was to help him dress. Yanshu was angry for a while, but there was nothing she could do. She could only comply and get out of bed as well.","As she was helping him dress, she heard him say to the door, \"Fu Hai, inform the imperial kitchen that I will have breakfast here.\"","Huh?","Before Fu Hai could respond, Yanshu's eyes lit up.","Did this mean she could have the imperial meal too?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She was just complaining about him, and now she's happy over a meal?","Of course.","By the time the imperial kitchen had delivered and set up the meal, and the two had finished washing up and sat down at the table, Yanshu was beaming with joy, her eyes sparkling.","She looked around the table, almost wanting to exclaim out loud.","—This was quite different from the hot pot they had on that snowy day.","That time, she had ordered the hot pot herself, and the kitchen had sent dishes according to her rank. This time, however, it was a meal for the emperor.","The original round table wasn't enough, so the palace servants brought another one, barely managing to fit all the dishes.","In the middle of the table were two hot pots, one bubbling with bird's nest duck soup and the other with deer tendon and winter bamboo shoot chicken soup. Around them were three flat plates, containing five-spice roast goose, grilled lamb leg, and wine-marinated fish. There were also two desserts: osmanthus milk pudding and white jade paste. The main course was a plate of plump venison buns, and a white porcelain pot contained steaming hot bone marrow soup.","Yanshu was so shocked she didn't know what to say.","What was all this?","Was this really just breakfast???","Did people really eat hot pot in the morning?","And two at once!!!","However, the man in the dragon robe glanced at her calmly and said lightly, \"Eat up.\"","Yanshu nodded, but as she picked up her chopsticks, she didn't know where to start. Fortunately, Fu Hai called over a young eunuch to serve the dishes, allowing the inexperienced Yanshu to learn how to begin.","She first tasted the warm pot. As the flavors touched her tongue, her eyes immediately lit up.","The bird's nest complemented the duck meat perfectly, and the deer tendon melted in her mouth, making the chicken soup even more delicious. Indeed, everything was of the highest quality.","Next, she tried the marinated goose, finding it extraordinarily fragrant and delicious.","The fish in wine lees was also outstanding; the meat was well-seasoned and tender, and even the bones had softened.","The thinly sliced leg of lamb, grilled on an iron plate, retained its juiciness while being tender – simply marvelous!","After the dishes, she tried a venison bun. To her surprise, the venison filling burst with juice in one bite, its flavor rich and mellow!","The desserts were even more impressive. The osmanthus milk pudding was fragrant, soft, and melted in the mouth, with the sweet scent of osmanthus flowers making one want to dance. The white jade cake made of steamed lotus seeds and glutinous rice was sweet and soft; Yanshu devoured three in one go.","Finally, she drank a bowl of incredibly rich bone marrow soup, feeling as if she could live for three hundred years.","...","This was the noisiest breakfast Yuwen Lan had ever eaten.","He had to listen to her various exclamations and mental screams while eating.","He even began to doubt himself: had something happened to his taste buds? Why hadn't he noticed all these flavors she described before?","Just as Yanshu was about to eat another bun, she saw Yuwen Lan suddenly put down his chopsticks.","This signaled the end of the meal, so she had to follow suit.","However, she felt a bit regretful, thinking, \"Are we not eating anymore? I'm not full yet...\"","\"...\"","Yuwen Lan looked at her and said, \"We're leaving. Take your time to finish.\"","With that, he stood up.","Yanshu was delighted and hurriedly rose to see him off.","Just as they were about to exit the hall, Yuwen Lan suddenly turned back to glance at her, saying meaningfully, \"If there's nothing else, We shall come again tonight.\"","Yanshu's eyes brightened. \"Yes, Your Majesty.\"","In her mind, she thought excitedly, \"Great! This means I can have another imperial meal tomorrow!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\""]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19","paragraphs":["After Yuwen Lan left, Yanshu ate another bowl of osmanthus yogurt, two white jade cakes, and a bowl of bone marrow soup.","This breakfast was truly nourishing, leaving her feeling warm from the inside out.","Unexpectedly, she felt especially energized to write her novel, and wrote steadily until noon without feeling hungry.","After a short nap in the afternoon, she continued writing. Recently, the words had been flowing smoothly, and she found herself writing until dusk.","As the sky gradually darkened, Rendong came to the desk to light the lamps. Seeing Yanshu rubbing her eyes, she quickly advised, \"You've been writing all day, you should rest your eyes now.\"","Yanshu made a sound of agreement and blinked, saying, \"I am feeling a bit tired.\"","Rendong said, \"Then continue writing tomorrow. What would you like for dinner?\"","Yanshu rubbed her stomach, feeling as if the morning meal hadn't fully digested yet, and replied, \"I'm not very hungry. Just a bowl of soup will do.\"","Rendong agreed and sent someone to the kitchen with the request. Soon after, a hot chicken soup was brought.","The soup was made with black-bone chicken, with added longan, red dates, and goji berries. It was delicious with a hint of sweetness, and Yanshu felt comforted after drinking a bowl.","However, her eyes were still uncomfortable, so she rubbed them again, feeling they might be a bit swollen.","Tsk, it seems she really had overused her eyes today.","She thought for a moment, then decided to take a bath to relax.","But after bathing, her eyes still felt uncomfortable, so she rubbed them again.","Then, she saw Rendong looking at her with a shocked expression, \"My lady, your eyes!\"","Startled, she hurried to look in the mirror, only to discover a small, red, swollen bump on her right eyelid.","Rendong was even more anxious than her, \"How did this happen so suddenly? Could it be someone's evil doing?\"","Evil doing?","Yanshu thought, \"...Surely not.\"","If anything were wrong, the system would have alerted her.","So she called out to the system, [System, why is there a bump on my eyelid?]","The system replied, [Not within this system's scope of service. It is recommended you see a doctor yourself.]","Yanshu, \"...\"","It seemed no one was trying to harm her after all.","She had no choice but to instruct, \"Go find a doctor to take a look.\"","Rendong agreed and hurried to the Imperial Pharmacy to find someone.","At this hour, the Imperial Medical Academy had already closed, so only that place would have doctors available.","Not long after, she returned with someone, but looked a bit uncomfortable.","Yanshu glanced at her and asked, \"What's the matter?\"","Rendong leaned close to her ear and whispered, \"There's only one imperial physician on duty tonight, and he happens to be at the Empress Dowager's palace taking her pulse. We only have this medical apprentice.\"","— It should be noted that imperial physicians are ranked, such as Chief Physician, Academy Director, Imperial Physician, Registrar, and so on. This medical apprentice was of the lowest rank, usually only treating palace servants.","However, Yanshu didn't care about this. True skill was never about rank; even in the jianghu there were plenty of miracle doctors!","She looked over the newcomer again, seeing he was about thirty years old, thin, and though his eyes were downcast, there seemed to be a hint of pride in his demeanor.","Someone like this shouldn't make mistakes, right?","So she said, \"Thank you for your trouble, doctor. This thing suddenly appeared on my eyelid, and it's a bit painful. Do you know what it could be?\"","He agreed and came closer, first examining her eyelid, then taking her pulse. He asked, \"What has the Noble Consort eaten recently?\"","Rendong quickly replied, \"Yesterday during the day, the Noble Consort ate some roast pork and lamb. In the evening, she had a bowl of sweet porridge. This morning, she dined with His Majesty and had deer tendon and bamboo shoot stewed chicken, bird's nest stewed duck, venison buns, smoked goose, fish in wine lees, and crispy white jade cakes with bone marrow soup. She didn't eat much at noon, and in the evening only had a bowl of black chicken soup with goji berries and longan.\"","As she finished speaking, they saw the doctor frown.","Rendong immediately became nervous and asked, \"What's wrong? Has the Noble Consort been poisoned?\"","The doctor, \"...The Noble Consort has internal heat.\"","\"Ah?\"","Rendong was stunned.","They heard the doctor explain, \"Bird's nest, venison, bone marrow, and black chicken are all very nourishing foods. The Noble Consort ate so much in one meal, and yesterday she also had roast pork and lamb, which are hot and dry foods. Her body couldn't handle it, so naturally, she developed internal heat. The bump on your eyelid is commonly called a stye.\"","Yanshu, \"...\"","Well, no wonder the system told her to see a doctor. It turned out she had eaten too many heaty foods.","She felt a bit embarrassed and asked, \"So what should I do?\"","The doctor said matter-of-factly, \"You just need to drink two doses of heat-clearing medicine and apply some ointment. There's no need for the Noble Consort to worry.\"","With that, he quickly wrote out a prescription and advised, \"The Noble Consort should remember not to eat any more heaty foods for the next few days. Keep your diet as bland as possible.\"","Yanshu could only agree and instructed Rendong, \"Give the doctor a reward.\"","Rendong agreed and was about to fetch some silver.","However, the doctor didn't accept it, saying, \"The Noble Consort's illness is not yet cured. I dare not accept this. Please take it back.\"","Rendong glanced at Yanshu, greatly surprised. Was there really someone in this world who didn't like money?","Yanshu was also surprised, but since he wouldn't accept it, she couldn't force him. So she said, \"If that's the case, I'll reward you after I've recovered.\"","The man replied neither humbly nor proudly, \"Thank you, Noble Consort.\"","And so, the consultation was over. Rendong went with the doctor to get the medicine and personally brewed it. Yanshu endured the bitter taste and drank a large bowl, then carefully applied the ointment to her eyelid.","After doing all this, she suddenly remembered an important matter and quickly said to Rendong, \"Send someone to Qianming Palace to inform His Majesty that I'm unwell, and ask him not to come over.\"","Tsk, this stye was affecting her appearance a bit, and she didn't want to frighten the emperor.","Rendong agreed and sent Little Dong to Qianming Palace with the message.","Soon after, the emperor in his study received the news.","Yuwen Lan found it strange. This morning she had eaten more than him, how had she suddenly fallen ill?","Could it be... someone had harmed her again?","After sending the message, Yanshu lay down on her bed.","She was tired from writing all day, and sleepiness quickly overcame her.","However, just as she was about to fall asleep, a voice suddenly announced from outside, \"His Majesty has arrived...\"","Yanshu, \"???\"","The emperor had come?","Indeed, the emperor had arrived. Before she could get out of bed, he was already by her side.","She was startled and quickly covered the stye on her eye with one hand, hurriedly getting up from under the covers, somewhat flustered as she said, \"This concubine greets Your Maj-\"","Before she could finish, she accidentally stepped on the hem of her skirt and stumbled forward.","Quick as lightning, Yuwen Lan reached out to steady her, frowning as he asked, \"What's wrong with you?\"","Was she so ill she couldn't even stand up?","Yanshu, still covering her eye, stammered, \"This concubine is fine, just... my eye is a little uncomfortable...\"","Yuwen Lan became even more convinced that she was seriously ill and urgently said, \"Let me see.\"","Yanshu could only try to deflect, \"Your Majesty, it's better not to look, lest you catch my illness... This concubine has already taken medicine, I'll be fine soon...\"","Yuwen Lan simply took hold of the hand covering her face.","He saw that her right eyelid was red and swollen like a bell.","He was taken aback again, \"What happened?\"","Yanshu was a bit annoyed and quickly covered her eye again, saying, \"This concubine is fine, it's just a stye.\"","\"A stye?\"","Yuwen Lan was still confused, \"Why did you get this?\"","Yanshu's face darkened, \"This concubine has eaten too many nourishing foods recently and developed internal heat.\"","How annoying, didn't she have any face left? Did she have to say it out loud in front of so many people?","Yuwen Lan, \"...From eating?\"","Yanshu felt like killing someone, \"...Yes.\"","It was just from being greedy and eating too much, what could he do about it!","Tsk, but come to think of it, this was from eating meals with him, shouldn't it count as a work injury?","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","Work injury?","He couldn't help but laugh a little.","Seeing her dissatisfied glance, [Still laughing!]","He had to compose himself and said, \"Even the most delicious food should be eaten in moderation. There's no good in indulging in momentary pleasures.\"","Yanshu replied woodenly, \"...This concubine obeys.\"","But in her heart, she felt a bit unbalanced and couldn't help saying, \"This concubine only ate like this once and got internal heat. Your Majesty eats like this every day, how come you don't get internal heat?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"I have a good constitution, and besides, I'm not greedy.\"","Yanshu \"...\"","She couldn't help but pout and mutter softly, \"Then isn't it a bit wasteful for Your Majesty to have so much prepared for just one person every day?\"","Logically, these words were a bit presumptuous, but Yuwen Lan wasn't angered. After thinking for a moment, he actually nodded and said, \"Indeed, it is.\"","He then instructed Fu Hai, \"Starting tomorrow, reduce my meals by half.\"","Fu Hai agreed, and he asked Yanshu, \"What did the imperial physician say?\"","Yanshu said, \"The doctor said I'll be fine after taking the medicine and resting a bit. It's nothing serious.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Then you should rest.\"","After speaking, he instructed Fu Hai, \"Go prepare some water.\"","Prepare water?","Yanshu was startled and quickly asked, \"Is Your Majesty planning to stay here tonight?\"","Yuwen Lan, who had already removed his outer robe, nodded and said, \"Of course.\"","Yanshu was shocked, \"But this subject is ill.\"","He glanced at her and said, \"I don't mind.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","Is this really about minding or not minding? Couldn't he just let her sleep properly on her own?","She hastily added, \"This subject fears passing the illness to Your Majesty...\"","Yuwen Lan, now dressed only in his nightclothes, replied with a puzzled expression, \"I've never heard that one could pass on a fever.\"","With that, he went straight into the bathroom.","Yanshu: \"???\"","Was he expecting her to perform her duties even when she was ill?","Where was the justice in this?","In truth, Yuwen Lan simply found it comfortable to sleep there. For instance, last night he had such a pleasant dream, and he merely wanted to relax again tonight.","He wasn't unreasonable. Mindful of her discomfort, after bathing he lay quietly beside her, not even reaching out to touch her.","Perhaps because she had let her guard down, before long, the young woman drifted off to sleep.","Lulled by the sound of her quiet, steady breathing, he too gradually fell asleep.","In the middle of the night, something suddenly burrowed into his embrace, startling him awake.","Upon waking, he realized it was her. Like a fish, she was pressed tightly against him, even hugging his neck.","He wanted to ask her about it, but noticed her eyes were closed and her breathing was rapid and shallow, as if she were having a nightmare.","So he reached out and gently stroked her back, then drifted back to sleep.","That night, while the cold wind howled outside the palace, inside the chamber it was as warm as spring.","The next day, Yuwen Lan awoke in the hazy morning light.","There was another court session today, and he was about to get up when he suddenly noticed something unusual about his body.","A certain part of him, long numb, seemed different from before."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20","paragraphs":["In truth, it wasn't a drastic change from before, but rather like a ripple on still water - enough to surprise him.","Yuwen Lan was stunned.","This kind of scene had been absent from his life for nearly three years, and now it had suddenly reappeared?","Of course, this was a normal state for a man, and it quickly subsided after he woke up.","But he remained lost in thought for a long while.","Suddenly, Fu Hai's voice came from outside the curtain, \"Your Majesty, it's time to rise.\"","There was a court session today, and if he didn't get up soon, he'd keep the ministers waiting.","Yuwen Lan responded and got out of bed. He instinctively looked back and saw the girl still sleeping, her long hair slightly disheveled, her cheeks rosy, and the covers kicked off, her neckline in disarray.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What kind of sleeping habit was this?","He quietly pulled the covers over her and closed the bed curtains without waking her.","Yuwen Lan, showing no signs of disturbance, returned to Qianming Palace to wash up and change clothes. He then went to the Hall of Diligent Government for the court session. While he listened to the officials' reports on state affairs, his mind kept wandering back to that incident.","He was certainly pleased, but he was even more curious about what had caused this morning's change.","Thinking back, yesterday had been just like any other day - he had read memorials and handled important matters, met with a few ministers and royal family members who had returned to the capital. His schedule hadn't differed from the usual, his diet was the same as always, except that he had gone to sleep in Ganlu Palace.","That's right, Ganlu Palace.","His heart skipped a beat. In fact, ever since he had discovered Li Yanshu, his days had gradually begun to change.","He had always been calm before, like a deep pool that couldn't be stirred. But every time he faced her, he found himself losing control.","She made him wary, angry, helpless, amused, and even... passionate.","Yes, every time he was close to her, he always found himself uncontrollably aroused.","So, could it be because of her?","He still remembered that first night in Ganlu Palace when she had intended to treat him... From the first time she actively kissed him, to last night when she inexplicably snuggled into his arms...","Could it be?","Was this her method?","...","On this day in court, the ministers were surprised to find that the emperor seemed distracted for the first time.","Early in the morning, Noble Consort Zhou arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Seeing a palace maid bringing in freshly prepared medicine, she volunteered, \"Let me serve the Empress Dowager her medicine.\"","However, the Empress Dowager said, \"Let them do it. You don't need to come every day, go and attend to your own affairs.\"","This girl had been pampered since childhood, how could she know how to serve others? Every time she fed medicine, she either burned or choked someone. Even the Empress Dowager, her aunt, was wary.","Hearing this, Noble Consort Zhou said dejectedly, \"I don't have much to do, I might as well keep you company and chat.\"","She continued, \"His Majesty still goes to Ganlu Palace every day, it's hard for me to even see him... I heard that Noble Lady Li was ill yesterday, yet His Majesty still spent the night there...\"","The Empress Dowager impatiently said, \"In all matters, one should reflect on oneself, think about whether there's something you're lacking in.\"","Noble Consort Zhou felt wronged, \"I heard that His Majesty was even distracted during the morning court session, could it be that Noble Lady Li has bewitched...\"","\"Silence!\"","Before she could finish, she was interrupted by a stern voice. Noble Consort Zhou trembled, seeing the Empress Dowager's face turn livid as she said, \"Haven't you learned your lesson from the ice performance incident a few days ago? As a consort, what are you trying to achieve by prying into matters of the court?\"","Frightened, Noble Consort Zhou quickly knelt down and said, \"Please calm your anger, Empress Dowager. I didn't intentionally pry, it's just that everyone at court noticed it this morning, and the gossip spread to the palace, that's how I knew...\"","The Empress Dowager scolded her again, \"The examples of Consort Ning and the Eldest Princess are right before your eyes, and you still haven't learned your lesson! Do you need to taste the consequences yourself to understand the severity?\"","Noble Consort Zhou cried, \"It's all my fault, please calm down, Empress Dowager. I was just worried that His Majesty might be bewitched...\"","\"Shut your mouth at once!\"","The Empress Dowager was so angry she almost wanted to kick her, \"There's no need for you to come before me these next few days. Go back and think carefully. If you had half the brain of Consort An, you wouldn't be in this state!\"","\"Yes.\"","Noble Consort Zhou left, covering her face.","While Noble Consort Zhou was throwing a tantrum in her own palace, Li Yanshu was having breakfast.","When she looked in the mirror this morning, she found that the boil had indeed subsided. Her almond-shaped eyes were bright, and her beauty remained undiminished.","Finally feeling relieved, she quickly asked Rendong to take some silver pieces to the physician from last night.","She had promised to reward him after she recovered, and she couldn't go back on her word.","After taking care of these matters, it was time for breakfast.","However... today's breakfast was indeed quite light.","Millet and pumpkin porridge, two plates of vegetable dishes, a dish of salted tofu, and the main course was vegetable dumplings. Tsk, not even a bit of meat to be seen.","Seeing her sour expression, Rendong advised patiently from the side, \"The physician said yesterday that fish causes inflammation and meat produces phlegm. You must eat lightly these days. Please bear with it, Master. The imperial chef's skills are superb, even vegetarian dishes must be delicious.\"","Li Yanshu sighed. Although unwilling, she was truly afraid of growing that unsightly thing again, so she reluctantly picked up her chopsticks.","To be honest, the imperial chef's skills were indeed impressive. The millet and pumpkin porridge was subtly sweet, the salted tofu was full of bean flavor, the vegetable dumplings were very tasty, and even the two small vegetable dishes were flavorful.","Although this meal had no meat, it was a return to simplicity, allowing one to taste the true flavor of the food.","Just as she finished breakfast, Xiao Dongzi came to report, \"Master, the Empress Dowager has summoned you.\"","Li Yanshu was startled.","The Empress Dowager had been ill for the past few days and hadn't allowed anyone to visit. Why was she suddenly calling for her?","However, the system didn't give any warning, so it probably wasn't anything bad. She responded with a \"Very well\" and hurried to change her clothes before going to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Upon arriving, she obediently paid her respects, still looking like a harmless little rabbit.","The Empress Dowager told her to rise but didn't offer her a seat. She simply said, \"Since your rank was promoted, I've heard that His Majesty's mood has improved greatly. This is your achievement.\"","Li Yanshu detected a note of warning in her tone.","It seemed that the Emperor's frequent overnight stays at Ganlu Palace had caught someone's attention.","But this was within expectations. After all, she was the Emperor's target.","She could only pretend to be alarmed and say, \"The Empress Dowager's words are too kind. It's my honor to serve His Majesty.\"","The Empress Dowager then asked, \"I heard you were ill yesterday. Are you better now?\"","Li Yanshu replied, \"Thank you for your concern, Empress Dowager. It was just a minor ailment, I'm better now.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"Ah, youth is good. Illnesses heal quickly too, unlike me.\"","Just as she finished speaking, a palace maid came forward to report, \"Empress Dowager, Judge Zhang has come to check your pulse.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Let him in.\"","The palace maid complied and lifted the curtain. Soon after, an old man about fifty or sixty years old entered the room. It was Zhang Shengkang, the head of the Imperial Medical Academy.","Li Yanshu stood to the side, quietly observing him. She thought to herself that this old man, with his ruddy complexion and official bearing, truly looked the part of the head of the Imperial Medical Academy.","However, now that the imperial physician had come to check the pulse, why didn't the Empress Dowager dismiss her?","Was she going to be admonished again later?","She saw Judge Zhang pay his respects and then kneel down to take the Empress Dowager's pulse. After a moment, he said, \"The Empress Dowager's health has almost fully recovered, but as the weather is cold and windy lately, you should still avoid going outdoors for a while.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded.","Suddenly, she turned her gaze to Li Yanshu and said, \"Why don't you let the imperial physician examine you as well, to see if you've fully recovered?\"","Li Yanshu: \"...\"","How did this turn into a check-up session?","Getting examined wasn't a problem, but if she did, wouldn't her embarrassing situation of overindulgence and inflammation be exposed...","However, this was the Empress Dowager's grace, and there was no way to refuse.","After all, besides the Empress Dowager and the Emperor, who else in the palace had the privilege to be examined by the head of the Imperial Medical Academy?","She could only respond, \"Then I'll trouble Judge Zhang,\" and sat down nearby.","Rendong quickly brought a silk handkerchief to cover her wrist, and Judge Zhang placed his fingers on it. He furrowed his brows in deep thought, seeming even more meticulous than when he had examined the Empress Dowager.","During this pause, the system chimed in, [There's some gossip about Judge Zhang.]","Li Yanshu, who was feeling a bit bored, immediately asked, [What gossip?]","The system replied, [In his youth, this man apprenticed under a legendary doctor. He studied medicine for twenty years, but after becoming an official, he betrayed his master's kindness. Not only did he steal his master's ancestral secret formulas, but he also drove his master out of the capital, ultimately causing him to die of depression.]","Li Yanshu: [...]","In an instant, all her goodwill towards the old man before her vanished.","Fortunately, at this moment, he finally removed his hand and said, \"Noble Lady Li is in good health, just slightly inflamed. Your diet should focus on nourishing and moistening foods, and be careful not to consume too many warming and tonic foods.\"","The diagnosis seemed quite accurate. This doctor must have some real skill, Yanshu thought. She politely said, \"Thank you for your advice, Judge Zhang.\"","The Empress Dowager waved her hand and said to her, \"You may go now.\"","Yanshu complied, obediently withdrawing from the hall.","After she had gone, the Empress Dowager dismissed her attendants and asked Zhang Shengkang, \"Well?\"","Zhang Shengkang said in a low voice, \"If Your Majesty wishes for a royal grandson, you'll have to wait longer. I'm afraid Noble Lady Li is still a virgin.\"","Leaving the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu snacked on the melon Zhang Shengkang had given her as she returned to Ganlu Palace. But the more she thought about it, the more uneasy she felt.","Why did the Empress Dowager have the imperial physician check her pulse?","At first, she thought the Empress Dowager was eager for a royal grandson and wanted to see if she was pregnant.","But thinking carefully, it had only been half a month since the Emperor first visited Ganlu Palace. Even if she were pregnant, it wouldn't be detectable yet, would it?","The Empress Dowager had given birth before - surely she knew this basic fact.","Moreover, Judge Zhang was a direct disciple of the miraculous doctor. His medical skills must be exceptional, or the Empress Dowager wouldn't trust him so...","Suddenly, she was startled by a thought—","Could this man have detected that she had never actually slept with the Emperor?","And thus know that the Emperor was impotent!","As dusk fell, Yuwen Lan once again entered Ganlu Palace.","He had been rather impatient all day, eager to verify if this morning's changes were related to her.","So he hurried all the way, not even waiting for the palace servants to announce him before entering the hall.","Looking up, he saw the young woman sitting on the warm couch, chin in hand, brows furrowed as if pondering some difficult problem.","It wasn't until she caught sight of him in her peripheral vision that she belatedly stood to bow, \"Greetings, Your Majesty.\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan looked her over curiously and asked, \"What are you thinking about?\"","Yanshu made a noncommittal sound and casually replied, \"This subject was just thinking about how to write a story...\"","She glanced at him out of the corner of her eye and suddenly sighed inwardly, \"Oh Emperor, do you know your secret is about to be exposed?\"","What?","Yuwen Lan froze. His secret was about to be exposed?","What did she mean?","He thought warily, had she told someone?","But then she volunteered, \"The Empress Dowager summoned this subject to speak with her this morning. We happened to encounter Judge Zhang checking her pulse. The Empress Dowager graciously had Judge Zhang examine this subject's health as well.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't immediately grasp her intent and remained cautious, asking, \"How was the examination?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Nothing major. Judge Zhang said this subject is just a bit feverish.\"","But inwardly she thought urgently, \"Don't you understand? They say Judge Zhang's medical skills are superb. He may have detected that I haven't slept with you!\"","\"Leaving such a beautiful woman untouched - don't you know they'll suspect you?\"","\"Quick, think of a way to deal with this! Otherwise, they'll all know you can't perform in bed!!!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Alright, he finally understood.","Given what he knew of the Empress Dowager, she would never have Zhang Shengkang check Yanshu's pulse without reason. So the Empress Dowager was indeed trying to find out something.","Of course, compared to Yanshu, the Empress Dowager would certainly prefer Noble Consort Zhou to receive his favor.","But that woman was selfish, foolish, and vicious. Moreover, she was from the Zhou family. He couldn't even put on a show of affection for her.","The empire belonged to the Yuwen clan, not the Zhou clan. Giving her the position of Noble Consort and maintaining the Zhou family's wealth and status was already the limit of his gratitude for the Empress Dowager's care in raising him.","He could be filial to the Empress Dowager, but he couldn't completely trust her. So even though he knew Zhang Shengkang's medical skills were excellent, he had never had him check his pulse since his body started showing abnormalities.","Of course, he hadn't entered the harem for three years, so the Empress Dowager probably had some suspicions about him. That's why she had Zhang Shengkang examine Yanshu's pulse this time.","But he had long been prepared, and now there were signs of improvement.","He turned his gaze to the young woman before him, feeling something indescribable in his heart — so all her deep thinking was out of concern for him?","However, under his gentle gaze, the young woman suddenly yawned, her eyes brimming with tears.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Seeing how she had spent the whole day worrying for him, he said, \"If you really can't think of anything, continue tomorrow. You've just recovered from illness, don't overtax yourself.\"","Yanshu thought to herself that she had said so much, surely the Emperor should understand by now. If he still didn't get it, there was nothing more she could do. So she simply replied \"Yes\" and went to the washroom to clean up.","When she came out after washing, she saw the Emperor had already loosened his clothes and was waiting on the bed.","Yanshu: \"...\"","She had to admire his dedication to keeping up appearances. He even insisted on squeezing onto the bed with her every night.","Yuwen Lan, who was patiently awaiting his beauty: \"???\"","What kind of thought was that?","Shouldn't she feel touched?","He patted the space beside him on the bed, \"Come up quickly, don't catch cold.\"","Yanshu complied and climbed onto the bed.","As soon as she lay down, he pulled her into his embrace.","Then she heard him say softly in her ear, \"Why did you burrow into my arms last night?\"","His tone was unprecedentedly gentle.","What?","Yanshu looked utterly confused.","She had burrowed into his arms last night? She didn't remember that at all.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","She didn't remember?","So she hadn't intentionally been trying to help him recover?","He saw her put on a fake smile and laugh it off, \"This subject must have been dreaming last night and accidentally disturbed Your Majesty...\"","Yuwen Lan made a noncommittal sound, \"So what did you dream about last night?\"","Yanshu tried to recall, \"This subject dreamed of being chased and hunted. At first, I was fleeing across hills and plains, then I finally found a tree hollow big enough for a person and hid inside...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well then, it turns out he had been treated as a tree hollow.","He had overthought things.","Suddenly feeling inexplicably dejected, he reconsidered — besides her, he couldn't think of any other reason for this morning's changes...","Never mind. Even if it wasn't her doing, it must be related to her somehow.","So tonight he was determined to try again, to see if there would be another pleasant surprise in the morning.","Thinking this, he said, \"Let's sleep then.\" And closed his eyes.","However, not long after, he heard her voice in his mind—","\"Ah, freshly pan-fried buns! Crispy on the bottom, soft on top, and the best part is the filling inside. One bite of the fennel pork, and juices burst in your mouth. The chive and shrimp filling is bursting with flavor, mmm!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Before he could ask, he heard her continue, \"No, eating just buns is too dry. Need some millet porridge to wash it down. Mmm, newly ground millet cooked until thick and sticky, the whole mouth full of that grainy aroma...\"","\"No, no, no, millet porridge is a bit bland. It must be paired with five-spice lamb to have enough flavor. And the buns need to go with hot, freshly made tofu pudding. That silky smooth tofu pudding topped with piping hot gravy, add a bit of chili oil and chive flowers, and don't forget the cilantro!\"","\"Oh, but the spicy tofu pudding might be too salty with the pan-fried buns. It should be paired with freshly fried crullers instead! That crunch when you bite into it!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What was going on?"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan was puzzled when he heard her sobbing in her heart again, [I want to eat shredded chicken noodles, donkey meat sandwiches, and big pancakes...]","\"What's wrong with you?\" He finally couldn't help but ask.","Why was her mind full of food???","Yanshu was startled and stammered, \"This humble consort is... is fine...\"","Before she could finish, her stomach made a timely \"gurgle\" sound.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","He looked her up and down and suddenly said with amusement, \"Didn't eat dinner?\"","Yanshu felt a bit embarrassed, but even more aggrieved, \"I did eat...\"","It was just too plain!","Today from morning to night, she had only eaten vegetarian food. For dinner, she only had two bowls of plain porridge. Although there were four dishes on the table, they were bitter gourd soup, crispy fried lotus root, vinegar cabbage, and golden tofu.","Damn it, once on duty she had to become a monk. Not even a bit of meat in sight. How was a carnivore like her supposed to survive?","Yuwen Lan understood and could only try to persuade her while holding back his laughter, \"The kitchen is also following the doctor's orders to prepare for you. For the sake of your health, just bear with it for now. You can eat what you want after you're better.\"","Yanshu deflated and responded with a weak \"...Yes.\"","The two closed their eyes again.","Yuwen Lan's breathing gradually became long and even, but Yanshu still couldn't fall asleep.","After thinking for a while, she tried to call the system, [System, do you have any mukbangs?]","System: [??? What nonsense? That's beyond my scope of service.]","Yanshu: [I'm starving to death. Why don't you tell me what delicious food someone's family ate, just to comfort me a little.]","System: [...First time I've heard of using this to satisfy cravings. But as it happens, let me tell you about the family banquet at the Minister of Revenue's house tonight, fresh off the press.]","Yanshu: [? Is there anything special about their family?]","System: [Ever heard of fish brain tofu? It takes the brains of five hundred carp to make one plate.]","Yanshu: [What? Tofu made from five hundred carp brains? Doesn't that old man worry about burning through money!]","The emperor, who was in the middle of a dream, was awakened by this exclamation.","— That old man? Which old man?","As he was puzzled, he heard her say, [Braised bear paw in peony sauce? That's too cruel! How much pain must the bear have suffered!]","[What? A thousand yellow croakers from the East Sea, but only taking the meat from the gills to steam into fish cakes? Tsk, this Minister of Revenue is more extravagant than the emperor. How many lives must be sacrificed just for a birthday celebration!]","Yuwen Lan then realized she was talking about Qi Weizhai, the Minister of Revenue.","Indeed, today was Qi Weizhai's birthday.","But what was this about fish brain tofu, peony bear paw, and yellow croaker cakes?","If what she said was true, wouldn't this meal cost tens of thousands of taels of silver?","Yet this old man had been crying poverty to him just days ago during disaster relief efforts.","This won't do. It seems he needs to send someone to check on the Qi household.","Thinking this, he suddenly realized - how did she know about all this?","Of course, there were already so many mysteries about her that he couldn't solve, and he had even... gotten used to it to some extent.","With mixed feelings, Yuwen Lan spoke, \"Are you still hungry? Should I have the kitchen prepare some midnight snacks to be sent over?\"","But he heard her smile and say, \"Thank you, Your Majesty, but this humble consort is no longer hungry. Let's just sleep.\"","You see, the effect of watching mukbangs is that seeing others eat feels like it's going into your own stomach, thus gaining a sense of satisfaction. In her previous life, when she was seriously ill and couldn't eat, she greatly enjoyed watching mukbangs.","Of course, things like fish brain tofu and bear paws, although precious, she didn't want to eat at all. It was too sinful!","So it's better to go to sleep quickly, and when she opens her eyes in the morning, she can eat breakfast.","After saying this, she closed her eyes and fell asleep.","Yuwen Lan was left behind, \"???\"","What was all this?","Also, what did he come here for tonight?","Seeing that she had fallen asleep on her own, he lost his sleepiness, his mind full of thoughts about investigating corrupt officials...","Meanwhile, in Zhongcui Palace, Nanny Zhuang, who was by the Empress Dowager's side, was talking to Noble Consort Zhou.","\"Noble Consort, you must not be anxious. There are so many women in the palace, even if it's not Noble Lady Li, it would be someone else. So you must not focus on what's right in front of you, but grasp what's most important.\"","Noble Consort Zhou pouted and said, \"But how can I grasp it? His Majesty doesn't give me a chance, and he never mentions the matter of establishing an empress. Am I supposed to just wait for death?\"","Anyway, Nanny Zhuang was the Empress Dowager's confidant, so these words were meant for the Empress Dowager to hear.","But Nanny Zhuang smiled and said, \"You come from a noble background, and moreover, you have the Empress Dowager in the palace to support you. How could you lack opportunities? As long as you don't touch His Majesty's sore spots, everything else will naturally fall into place.\"","These words... could it be that there was hope for what she had been waiting for?","Noble Consort Zhou's eyes darted around, and she quickly responded with a \"Good.\"","In Ganlu Palace.","After tossing and turning for who knows how long, the emperor finally fell into a dream.","Gradually, he had another dream.","In the dream, there was a vast prairie, with blue sky and white clouds overhead. He lay on the soft grass, with the fragrance of wildflowers at the tip of his nose. The gentle breeze caressed his ears, making one inexplicably relaxed.","Thus, a night passed. The next day, when the sky was just beginning to lighten, Yuwen Lan woke up as usual.","He was anxious about important matters and hurried to check, only to find that yesterday's scene had indeed appeared again.","And it seemed to have made some progress compared to yesterday.","His heart settled, there was hope.","If once was a coincidence, then consecutive breakthroughs were certainly not by chance. He had hope.","Turning his head to look, the girl was still sleeping, her cheeks rosy, her face lazy, like a begonia woven on the bed curtains.","Especially those slightly pouted lips, pink and moist, as tempting as cherries.","There was no morning court today, so he was in no hurry to leave. At this moment, his heart moved, and he lowered his head.","However, before he could touch her, a foot suddenly kicked out unexpectedly.","Quick as a flash, he reached out and grabbed that foot, and the girl gradually opened her eyes.","Yuwen Lan frowned and asked, \"Why did you kick the emperor?\"","Yanshu, who had just woken up and was still a bit dazed, said hazily, \"This humble consort didn't kick Your Majesty, I was kicking a lecher...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"A lecher?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"This humble consort dreamed that I was walking along the road when suddenly someone pulled me into the bushes. That person wanted to take liberties with me, so I kicked him...\"","Damn, this time was light. Next time I have such a dream, I must beat him to death.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He tried to ask, \"What did that lecher look like?\"","But he heard her say, \"This humble consort didn't see clearly, but vaguely remember he had a face full of stubble, looking quite sleazy.\"","Yuwen Lan silently touched his chin. Fortunately, he didn't have a face full of stubble, so it definitely wasn't him.","After saying this, Yanshu also woke up completely.","Having finally endured through the night, today's breakfast was beckoning. She hurriedly got up and said, \"This humble consort will assist Your Majesty in getting up.\"","[Quick, get up and eat!]","Yuwen Lan's mood from earlier had completely disappeared, so he also made a sound of acknowledgment and got out of bed.","After the two finished washing up, breakfast had already been set on the table.","Hey, since he was here this morning, she could freeload another imperial meal. Yanshu excitedly came to the table, but was dumbfounded.","She saw that there were more than a dozen bowls and plates on the table, with side dishes, soup, porridge, and main dishes, but they were all vegetarian.","\"Why is Your Majesty also eating vegetarian?\"","She asked with a puzzled face.","Fu Hai bowed beside them and explained, \"Has the Noble Lady forgotten? The day after tomorrow is the Fengxian Hall ceremony, so starting from today, the palace will observe a three-day fast.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Heavens, she had completely forgotten about this.","The most terrifying three days of the year had finally come.","You should know, these three days weren't just about not eating meat. Fried foods with lots of oil also couldn't appear. Only steamed and boiled foods could be on the dining table.","It could be said that after three days, even those who didn't want to lose weight would lose a couple of pounds.","As she was deflating, Yuwen Lan had already picked up his chopsticks and deliberately said, \"Today's meal is light and refreshing, just suitable for you to eat.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","There was no choice. If she didn't eat now, even this little bit would be gone.","She had to pick up her chopsticks as well.","Soon, as breakfast was finished, it was time for Yuwen Lan to return to Qianming Palace.","Yanshu escorted him to the door, but saw him suddenly turn back and say to her, \"For these three days, the emperor also cannot come over.\"","The so-called fasting meant not only eating vegetarian food, but also that the emperor could not visit his consorts, and all banquets and entertainment activities were suspended.","He wanted to see how she would react.","But he heard her cheer in her heart, [Great! I can finally sleep in the big bed by myself!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He knew it, huh.","Returning to Qianming Palace, Yuwen Lan immediately dispatched the Imperial Guard to investigate the matter of Minister of Revenue Qi Weizhai's birthday celebration.","Meanwhile, in Zhongcui Palace, Noble Consort Zhou was about to leave with a food box in hand.","Xiu Yun, the close-attending palace maid, hesitated and couldn't help but call out, \"Your Highness, is this really appropriate?\"","Xiu Yun knew that her mistress had put something improper in the pastries. She worried about what would happen if His Majesty discovered it...","Noble Consort Zhou glanced at her and said, \"What's inappropriate about it? This is a rare opportunity for me.\"","After three days of fasting, most people couldn't endure a vegetarian diet and usually needed some snacks in the morning and afternoon. That's why the Empress Dowager had specially arranged this opportunity for her.","His Majesty surely wouldn't refuse.","This medicine was something she had obtained with great difficulty. It was said to be infallible. If she didn't seize this chance to succeed, who knew when the next opportunity would come?","Meanwhile, in Ganlu Palace, Yanshu, who was writing a story, received a message from the system: [Big news! Noble Consort Zhou plans to give the Emperor an aphrodisiac.]","What the heck???","Yanshu nearly made a mistake in her writing. [An aphrodisiac???]","The system replied, [That's right. She's already left with chestnut pastries. Tsk, she's almost at Qianming Palace.]","Yanshu: [...Wait a minute, if she suddenly goes to deliver snacks, would the Emperor let her in?]","System: [Using the Empress Dowager's name, she'll definitely get in. Otherwise, wouldn't the Emperor appear unfilial to the Empress Dowager?]","Yanshu: [...That's true, but the Emperor is impotent. Even if he takes an aphrodisiac, it probably won't have much effect. It's fine.]","System: [That's not necessarily true. Noble Consort Zhou is using the Love-Locking Powder this time, one of the top three aphrodisiacs in the jianghu. For a normal man, it would work for that purpose, but for someone with the Emperor's condition who can't release, it could very likely cause his meridians to become chaotic and lead to qi deviation.]","Yanshu: [!!! Damn, it's that potent?]","She imagined what might happen to her meal ticket if he experienced qi deviation...","Just then, the system said, [Noble Consort Zhou has already entered the Imperial Study.]","Yanshu could no longer sit still. After a moment's thought, she grabbed something random from the palace and hurriedly left."]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22","paragraphs":["When Yanshu arrived, Noble Consort Zhou's chestnut cakes had already been placed on the kang table in the imperial study.","She quickly glanced over, seeing that the food box lid had not yet been opened and there were no dishes in front of the emperor. It seemed he had not yet had a chance to eat, so she quietly felt relieved.","However, Noble Consort Zhou asked her with a look of disdain, \"Why has Li Beauty come over as well?\"","She had just spent a great deal of effort, using the Empress Dowager's name to gain entry to this imperial study. How was it that this cheap woman was called in by His Majesty with just one announcement?","Yanshu hurriedly bowed to the emperor and her, saying, \"This concubine just found a tassel in the hall that seems to be Your Majesty's, so I rushed to bring it to you.\"","As she spoke, she presented a purple tassel she had hastily grabbed from the hall earlier.","Tsk, this color - one glance and you could tell it wasn't for a man's use.","But Yanshu had no choice. She was in a hurry to save the emperor; how could she have time to choose colors?","Noble Consort Zhou, however, thought she had come to brag about the emperor staying in her chambers again last night. Her eyes were practically shooting sparks.","However, the emperor did not expose her lie. He made a sound of acknowledgment and put the tassel away.","Yanshu's heart steadied, and she casually said, \"By the way, Your Majesty, you had persimmon cakes for breakfast today. The imperial physician has advised against eating chestnuts, as the two foods don't mix well and may cause stomach pain.\"","[Oh Emperor, this is all I can do to help you. Those chestnut cakes contain a love potion. Other men who eat it will become lustful, but if you eat it, your meridians will become chaotic and you'll suffer internal injuries!]","Yuwen Lan inwardly paused.","He had already learned from Noble Consort Zhou's thoughts that there was something wrong with the pastries.","But he didn't know it would be such a vicious substance. Was it true or false?","And how did she know such details? She even knew what would happen if he ate it?","Meanwhile, Noble Consort Zhou's face was turning green. What she had brought today were precisely chestnut cakes. What was this cheap woman implying?","She said, \"Starting today, I'm fasting for three days. These chestnut cakes were sent by me on the Empress Dowager's behalf, worried that Your Majesty might be hungry. I've never heard that chestnut cakes and persimmon cakes don't mix well.\"","As she spoke, she shot a threatening glare at Yanshu.","You cheap woman, if you dare ruin my plans again, I'll have you torn to pieces!","However, it was too late. The emperor was already addressing Yanshu, \"I nearly forgot. Fortunately, you reminded me.\"","He then turned to Noble Consort Zhou, \"The Empress Dowager is thoughtful, but unfortunately, I cannot eat these chestnut cakes today.\"","Noble Consort Zhou secretly clenched her fists, but could only smile and say, \"As long as Your Majesty is well.\"","Yet in her heart, she was gnashing her teeth and cursing, [Yanshu, you cheap woman, I will definitely turn you into human swine!!!]","Human swine?","Yuwen Lan temporarily set aside his doubts about Yanshu and said to Noble Consort Zhou, \"I recall that Duke Cheng'en looked unwell a few days ago. It seems his qi and blood might be deficient. These chestnut cakes are good for that. Let's bestow them on Duke Cheng'en.\"","At these words, even Yanshu was stunned.","Give them to Duke Cheng'en?","This... this is a great idea!!!","Just not sure if that old man can handle it?","Noble Consort Zhou hurriedly said, \"But Your Majesty, these were sent by the Empress Dowager for you.\"","Yuwen Lan smiled, \"Is Duke Cheng'en an outsider?\"","Noble Consort Zhou choked, then said, \"But in this weather, they might be cold by the time they're delivered.\"","Yuwen Lan looked at her and said, \"I'll have the guards deliver them at full speed. The Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion isn't far; they won't get cold.\"","Noble Consort Zhou finally panicked and repeatedly said, \"Perhaps we shouldn't, it's too much trouble...\"","Yanshu quickly added fuel to the fire, \"Noble Consort is too modest. Pastries bestowed by Your Majesty are a great honor. Duke Cheng'en will surely be grateful and feel extremely honored.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan nodded and directly ordered Fu Hai, \"Have someone deliver these chestnut cakes from Noble Consort to Duke Cheng'en. Remember to go at full speed so the pastries don't get cold.\"","Fu Hai quickly agreed, took the food box, and went out to find someone.","Noble Consort Zhou could only suppress her urgent anger and say, \"This concubine thanks Your Majesty for the honor on behalf of my father. This concubine won't disturb Your Majesty further and will take her leave.\"","With that, she hurriedly left.","Yuwen Lan looked at Yanshu, pondering how to ask her questions, but saw that she too was in a hurry, saying, \"This concubine won't disturb Your Majesty either and will take her leave.\"","Damn, I need to hurry back and watch the drama unfold, see what happens to that old Duke Cheng'en after eating those chestnut cakes!","And with that, she also left the hall.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She said... watch the drama unfold?","He remembered she had said something similar the night before last.","What exactly was this... drama?","Meanwhile, Noble Consort Zhou rushed back to Zhongcui Palace in a panic. She immediately ordered her eunuch Zhou Laishun, \"Quickly send someone to the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion and tell my father not to eat those chestnut cakes!\"","Zhou Laishun agreed and hurried out to find someone.","However, they were ultimately a step too slow. By the time the message was delivered, Duke Cheng'en had already eaten two cakes, overjoyed at receiving such an honor from the emperor.","Tsk, this was a gift bestowed by the emperor, an immense favor from heaven!!!","Noble Consort Zhou fretted for an hour until noon when Zhou Laishun finally returned with news.","\"Your Grace, by the time our people arrived, the Duke had already eaten half of the chestnut cakes...\"","What!","Noble Consort Zhou immediately asked, \"How is my father?\"","\"Well...\"","Zhou Laishun was terribly embarrassed and had to lean in close to whisper his report.","Noble Consort Zhou was about to die of anger. She immediately smashed a nearby blue and white porcelain vase.","Zhou Laishun hurried to comfort her, \"Please don't worry, Your Grace. Fortunately, the doctor arrived in time and has already given the Duke some medicine. With a few days of rest, he should be fine.\"","Noble Consort Zhou gritted her teeth and said, \"Yanshu!\"","If it weren't for her interference today, how could this situation have occurred?","Her father was suffering outside the palace, and she herself couldn't even speak of her grievances!","Just as she finished speaking, a palace maid announced from outside, \"Your Grace, Fu Hai from Qianming Palace has arrived.\"","Fu Hai is here?","Noble Consort Zhou's heart tightened.","Fu Hai had never come to Zhongcui Palace before. Could it be... that the emperor had noticed something and was coming to question her?","Although she felt extremely guilty, she couldn't refuse to see him. She hurriedly composed herself, tidied her clothes and makeup, and said, \"Quickly invite him in.\"","The palace maid outside quickly agreed, lifted the cotton curtain, and Fu Hai entered carrying a scroll.","The moment he stepped into the hall, Fu Hai immediately noticed the shattered vase on the floor. He quickly played dumb and exclaimed, \"Which clumsy servant dropped this, breaking such a fine vase and upsetting Noble Consort?\"","Noble Consort Zhou felt a bit better and forced a smile, saying, \"It was just that clumsy Xiuyun. I'll punish her to sweep the courtyard later. What brings Fu Hai here?\"","Fu Hai hurriedly presented the scroll in his hands, saying, \"This servant comes on His Majesty's orders to deliver this to Noble Consort. His Majesty said it must be hung in the hall for Noble Consort to study carefully.\"","A scroll?","Noble Consort Zhou was stunned.","This was the first time His Majesty had bestowed a gift on her.","She had heard that the previous emperor would bestow palace instruction paintings on consorts at the end of each year as a sign of favor. Could this be one?","Her heart leaped with joy, and her previous anger instantly dissipated. She smiled and said, \"Thank His Majesty for this gift. This concubine will certainly study it carefully.\"","She then ordered someone to reward Fu Hai.","Fu Hai thanked her and took his leave, thinking he'd better leave quickly to avoid getting caught in the crossfire.","No sooner had Fu Hai left than Consort An, who had received the news, rushed over.","Looking at the scroll displayed on the table, she said enviously, \"Is this the palace instruction painting? You're the first to receive one since the new emperor ascended the throne. It shows your position in His Majesty's heart.\"","Noble Consort Zhou's head was already in the clouds. She said proudly, \"As the head of the inner palace, of course His Majesty would bestow it on me first.\"","\"Naturally,\" Consort An nodded in agreement. Then, curious, she asked, \"I wonder which story His Majesty has bestowed? Please let this concubine have a look too.\"","Noble Consort Zhou was eager to know herself, so she ordered a palace maid, \"Open the scroll.\"","The maid complied, carefully doing as instructed.","Consort An hurried forward to look, but was stunned.","It wasn't a painting at all, but two lines of poetry:","\"Those who commit ten evils will receive evil retribution; those who perform ten good deeds will receive good rewards.\"","Everyone was dumbfounded.","Noble Consort Zhou was also stunned. \"What... what does this mean? Is it saying that I have evil thoughts and am unforgivably wicked?\"","The hall fell silent for a moment. Consort An forced herself to comfort her, \"Noble Consort is overthinking. This is just an old poem...\"","\"You think I don't know that!\" Noble Consort Zhou gritted her teeth. But isn't this exactly what the poem means!","\"That Yanshu, to actually make His Majesty humiliate me like this. I definitely won't let her get away with it!\"","Noble Consort Zhou hurriedly advised, \"Your Highness, while this matter is indeed excessive, she is currently in favor. It would be unwise to anger His Majesty.\"","Noble Consort Zhou angrily retorted, \"So I'm just supposed to be infuriated to death?!\" And there was still the matter of the chestnut cakes!","After fuming for a while, she suddenly turned to Consort An with a cold smile and said, \"The other day, the Empress Dowager praised your intelligence in front of me. I've treated you well, so now it's time for you to think of a way for me to get rid of that tramp Li Yanshu.\"","Consort An hesitated, not daring to refuse, and could only respond, \"To share Your Highness's worries is my duty.\"","...","After leaving Zhongcui Palace, Consort An returned to her own chambers, lost in thought the whole way.","Her maid Liu Di worriedly said, \"With Noble Consort Zhou pressuring you like this, what will you do...\"","Everyone in the palace knew that Li Beauty was currently in favor. Harming her would be like opposing His Majesty! And last time, Consort Li was even banished to the Cold Palace!","But Consort An didn't let her continue, only saying, \"I know what I'm doing.\"","Her grandfather, the Minister of Rites, was an old official of the Empress Dowager, so she naturally relied on the Empress Dowager's support in the palace. If she didn't listen to Noble Consort Zhou, wouldn't that be like asking for trouble?","Liu Di was still concerned, \"But if it's exposed, won't you end up like Consort Li?\"","At that time, Consort Li was loyal to Consort Ning, but when things went wrong, Consort Ning pushed all the blame onto Consort Li.","Consort An sighed, \"At critical moments, everyone will abandon the cart to save the horse. But Consort Li was foolish; I won't be like her.\"","Suddenly remembering something, she asked, \"By the way, who was sitting at the same table as Li Beauty on the night of the New Year's Eve banquet?\"","...","That night, the Imperial Guard came to report to the Emperor about the situation at the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion.","\"Your Majesty, after eating two chestnut cakes today, the Duke of Cheng'en began showing symptoms within 15 minutes. He spent two hours in his concubine's chambers, and when he emerged, he was completely exhausted. It's unclear if he'll be able to attend the ceremony at Fengxian Hall the day after tomorrow.\"","Yuwen Lan understood.","That foolish woman Zhou's actions today were enough to warrant confiscation of property and stripping of titles.","But today she was acting under the Empress Dowager's banner. If he were to pursue the matter, the Empress Dowager would surely come to her defense.","So, he might as well let it ferment for a while longer. It wouldn't be too late to settle accounts in a couple of days.","However, at the same time, he found himself puzzled once again.","Yanshu had verified this matter as well.","What kind of powers did she possess?","Surely she couldn't have planted spies in Zhongcui Palace?","And what exactly was this \"melon\" she spoke of?","After pondering for a while, he couldn't help but summon the young eunuch Fu Bao and asked, \"What has Li Beauty been doing today?\"","Fu Bao honestly replied, \"Apart from coming to Qianming Palace, Li Beauty didn't leave her chambers after returning.\"","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"Then... how was her appetite?\"","He had been eating vegetarian food all day and wondered if she had been craving any delicacies.","Fu Bao said, \"Li Beauty's three meals were as usual, but just now she ordered some supper from the imperial kitchen.\"","Supper?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. So when he wasn't around, she felt free to eat supper?","Curiously, he asked, \"What kind of supper?\"","Fu Bao was also puzzled and said, \"Li Beauty asked for some tofu, eggplant, potatoes, sweet potatoes, and so on, but they were all raw.\"","\"Raw?\"","Fu Bao nodded and added, \"Oh, and Li Beauty also asked for two steamed buns.\"","Steamed buns?","Yuwen Lan frowned. What did she want these for?","Had she gone mad with hunger?","After thinking for a moment, he suddenly said, \"I'm going out for a while.\"","Fu Bao was startled and was about to remind the Emperor that it was currently the fasting period and he shouldn't go to the harem...","But before he could speak, his master Fu Hai stopped him with a glance.","— This was the Emperor. The whole world belonged to him, couldn't he do whatever he wanted?","Fu Bao immediately understood and quickly lowered his head, not daring to say more.","Fu Hai hurriedly brought an outer robe for the Emperor to put on and personally escorted him to the hall entrance.","At this moment, they heard the Emperor say in a deep voice, \"Keep your mouths shut.\"","The two hurriedly agreed.","In the quiet of the night, Yuwen Lan made his way to Ganlu Palace. He didn't see any palace servants guarding the entrance.","The lights inside were still on.","As he walked a few steps further, he faintly smelled a fragrant aroma. Looking carefully, he saw that a window in the hall was open, and he could vaguely hear voices.","The closer he got, the more distinct the aroma became.","He simply walked up the steps and pushed open the door.","Inside the hall, there was a haze of smoke.","\"These potato slices are ready, eat them quickly. Mmm, the tofu is so tender, it would be even better with some spice. Oh, and add some steamed bun slices, crispy from grilling...\"","It was clearly her voice.","Yuwen Lan followed the sound and discovered that below the window, several people were gathered around a charcoal brazier with an iron plate on top, sizzling with something cooking.","The fragrant aroma was coming from there.","\"Your Majesty!\"","Rendong, Lianxin, and the others were the first to see him. They stood up in fright, their faces turning pale.","And the person who was still frying tofu finally raised her head and noticed him.","Yanshu looked surprised and said, \"Your Majesty? Why have you come?\"","Why had he come?","Yuwen Lan glanced at the delicious food on the iron plate. The tofu was golden, sprinkled with some red chili powder and yellow Sichuan pepper powder, which looked quite appealing when mixed together.","There were also some potato slices, golden and glistening with oil.","Next to the charcoal brazier were a few roasted sweet potatoes, emitting a sweet aroma...","Yuwen Lan turned his gaze to her, clearly seeing the remnants of seasoning on her lips.","Hmph, she seemed to be enjoying herself quite well in his absence.","However, after looking around, he didn't find any... melons.","Winter melon, pumpkin, watermelon, gourd - none of these were in the hall.","As he was puzzled, he heard her muttering in her mind, [Why is he looking at me like that? It's just some teppanyaki, is that against the law?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","True, there was no palace rule forbidding midnight snacks.","And because of the three days of vegetarian diet, many people in the palace would have extra meals at night.","But doing it like this... Yuwen Lan had never seen before.","He said, \"What are you doing?\"","Yanshu smiled gently and said, \"This concubine is eating teppanyaki. Would Your Majesty like to try some?\"","Teppanyaki?","Yuwen Lan frowned slightly. So this was it, sitting by the charcoal brazier, grilling and eating on the spot?","He tried asking, \"Is it just these dishes? Nothing else?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, why is he asking like this? Is he trying to catch her out? To see if she had broken the fast and eaten meat?","She said, \"Currently the palace is observing a fast, even the imperial kitchen has no meat dishes. This concubine truly only has vegetables here.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't understand what she meant by \"catching her out.\"","But clearly this wasn't what he wanted to know.","So he asked again, \"You haven't eaten any melons or fruits?\"","Melons and fruits?","Yanshu was increasingly confused.","At this time of year, apart from tangerines and apples, there weren't many other fruits in the palace. The few honeydew melons available were reserved for the Empress Dowager and him. Even if she wanted to eat some, she couldn't get her hands on any!","However, she had certainly enjoyed her fill of the juicy \"melon\" today.","Tsk tsk, that old lecher Duke Cheng'en had been set up by his own unfortunate daughter. Today he had truly almost died in his concubine's bed.","The way that old pervert had fallen from grace - just thinking about how he was carried out of bed with his face twisted and eyes unfocused made her want to laugh herself to death, hahahahaha.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23","paragraphs":["What? His mouth is crooked and eyes are askew???","Yuwen Lan's eyebrow twitched. Had she seen it???","He tried to imagine Duke Cheng'en's appearance...","Yuwen Lan shuddered and said to Rendong and the others, \"You may leave first.\"","Rendong, Lianxin and the rest had been on tenterhooks. Hearing this, they felt greatly relieved and immediately complied, exiting the hall.","The hall was finally quiet. Just as Yuwen Lan was about to speak, he heard Yanshu exclaim, \"It's about to burn!\"","She quickly took three steps in two towards the charcoal brazier.","The fire in the brazier was blazing. Yanshu quickly flipped the food items over and took the opportunity to pop some of the cooked ones into her mouth. As she ate, she remarked, \"Tofu must be eaten while it's hot! Whew!\"","The potato slices had also been grilled to a crisp. She tried a piece and found it had the texture of potato chips.","The most amazing were the steamed bun slices - fragrant and crispy, absolutely delicious.","After eating for a while, she suddenly remembered a certain someone. She looked up and saw the emperor gazing at her intently.","Yanshu: \"...\"","What did that look mean?","Was he craving some?","She coughed and said, \"Your Majesty, won't you try some? It's very tasty.\"","Tsk, just say something if you want to eat or not! If you don't eat soon, I'll finish it all.","Just as she finished that thought, she heard him suddenly say, \"Alright then.\"","With that, he picked up the chopsticks and started eating the tofu directly.","Mmm, hot!","That was Yuwen Lan's first impression.","However, it was crispy on the outside and tender inside. The salty and spicy seasoning blended with the tofu's natural bean flavor - it was indeed quite good.","After finishing the tofu, he saw Yanshu munching on potato slices, making crisp sounds between her lips and teeth.","He followed suit and tried some. Hmm, it was unexpectedly good. Prepared this way, the potato had a strong roasted aroma and was quite interesting to eat.","After finishing the potatoes, he asked, \"What else is there?\" His tone had already become expectant.","Yanshu handed him a piece of steamed bun, saying, \"Your Majesty, try this.\"","Yuwen Lan took it, still somewhat doubtful. Could this be tasty?","But seeing how she enjoyed eating it, he reluctantly gave it a try. His eyes lit up.","The pan-fried steamed bun had formed a crispy shell on the outside from the seasoning and oil, while the inside remained soft. Taking a bite, it was crispy outside and soft inside, full of wheat fragrance and rich in flavor.","After finishing the steamed bun, Yanshu broke off a piece of sweet potato for him. It was sweet and soft, with one bite feeling as sweet as honey in his heart.","The two ate like this together, and in less than half an hour, they had successfully demolished all the food items.","Yuwen Lan still felt somewhat unsatisfied and asked, \"Is there no more?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"We've eaten it all.\"","For a late-night snack, there's no need to be too full - just satisfying a craving is enough.","Speaking of which, she suddenly remembered the main issue and asked him, \"Wasn't Your Majesty not supposed to come to the harem for these three days? Why did you come tonight?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Distracted by all that food, he had also just remembered the main issue. So he smoothly said, \"I remembered that this cord is not mine.\"","As he spoke, he took out the purple cord she had given him earlier that day.","Yanshu could only laugh it off, \"Is that so? Then perhaps I remembered incorrectly...\"","As she spoke, she took back the purple cord.","In her heart, she thought, [You only realized it wasn't yours now? Could it be you deliberately came to sneak a late-night snack?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Did she think he was like her, only knowing how to eat?","He said meaningfully, \"Did you really remember incorrectly? Or did you have something you wanted to see me about?\"","Yanshu blinked her big eyes innocently and said, \"How dare I deceive you? Of course I remembered incorrectly. Besides, I don't have anything I need to see you about.\"","In her heart, she thought, [What a thing to say. If I hadn't informed you, who knows what state you'd be in now. Not only are you ungrateful, you even suspect me. Hmph, heartless!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","She dared to say he was heartless?","But thinking carefully, regardless of how she knew about this matter, her rushing to the imperial study today was out of concern for him.","Moreover, from what he could see so far, although she knew about his hidden ailment, she had never told anyone else about it, nor had she ever used this information to do anything. On the contrary, she had twice reminded him to be careful of others.","So, at the very least, she wasn't dangerous.","Thinking of this, Yuwen Lan softened his tone and said, \"I was just a bit curious, since you've never come to see me before.\"","He then casually asked her, \"What did you do after you returned today?\"","Yanshu replied, \"I was just doing the same as always, writing novels in my palace.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Any new works?\"","Yanshu proudly said, \"Of course, I've written five or six more these past few days.\"","Seeing his very interested expression, she asked, \"Would you like to take a look?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She wanted to say no.","Not only did he like to nitpick, but reading the steamy parts would also stimulate him.","The silently listening person coughed and said, \"I can now accept things like 'The Passionate General and the Young Widow'...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She still didn't really want to show him, but considering his status as emperor, she reluctantly said, \"Alright then, but please keep your word. If you read something you don't like, you mustn't blame me.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded in agreement.","She then brought out several stacks of manuscript papers.","Yuwen Lan picked up the thickest stack and tried reading it. He saw the title was \"The Amorous Beautiful Wife\".","\"...\"","Indeed, it was still this style.","Since he had nothing better to do, he might as well have a look. He started reading from the beginning.","However, before long, he discovered that this seemed to be a story about the Linwu Marquis's household.","That was good, as he wanted to know whose child the Linwu Marquis's heir really was. So he continued reading with interest.","-- Xia Chunlan, a beauty from Jiangnan, came from an already declined noble family. Young and beautiful, she was as lovely as the moon and as delicate as a flower. By chance, she met a young nobleman.","-- Yuwen Lan guessed this referred to the Marquis Xiayi.","The young nobleman fell in love with Xia at first sight, and Xia also experienced the first stirrings of young love. However, the young nobleman's parents strongly disapproved of the girl's background and firmly opposed the match.","The young nobleman had no choice but to marry someone else. In a fit of anger, Xia turned to the arms of another young nobleman and successfully became his official wife. She even received a title thanks to her husband's military accomplishments.","-- Needless to say, this young nobleman was naturally the Linwu Marquis.","This marriage allowed Xia to vent her anger and also helped her declining family regain some status. However, her husband was cold by nature and often away on duty. Xia, being in her passionate years, by chance met an actor and fell in love again.","Reading to this point, Yuwen Lan couldn't help but guess - could the heir be this actor's child?","However, as he continued reading, he saw her write -- The actor was at the height of his popularity and had many other admirers. Soon, Xia discovered that while he was meeting her in secret, he was also involved with a princess and a noblewoman. She immediately cut off all ties and kicked the actor out of her bed.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","So it wasn't the actor's child?","He hurriedly read on and saw that not long after, Xia met a wealthy merchant. The merchant was captivated by her beauty and gifted her many treasures. Xia, in turn, admired his handsome looks, wealth, and worldly knowledge, so they had an affair for a while.","But later, when her husband returned to the capital, they had to end it.","Yuwen Lan pondered silently, could this be the real father of that heir?","Calculating the age, the Linwu Marquis's heir Sun Zhanpeng was about the same age as himself. The Linwu Marquis had also returned to the capital from his border posting in the southeast about twenty years ago, after which his son was born.","If so, it was very possible!","However, before he could read further, he saw Yanshu yawn beside him. With tears in her eyes, she said, \"Your Majesty, I'm tired. Why don't you continue reading tomorrow?\"","Then suddenly remembering that tomorrow was still a fasting day, she added, \"Or the day after tomorrow is fine too. I've finished writing it anyway.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and looked at her, \"Eat and sleep, are you a pig?\"","Yanshu grumbled discontent, \"You ate earlier too.\"","If you're so capable, go back and don't sleep!","Her cherry-like small mouth pouted high.","Yuwen Lan laughed and reached out to poke her cheek, saying, \"Then you sleep. I'll take it back to read.\"","\"Huh?\" Yanshu was stunned, \"Take it back to read?\"","Yuwen Lan made an affirmative sound and tucked the manuscript into his sleeve.","-- He had read to a crucial point. If he didn't figure out whose child that heir was, he probably wouldn't be able to sleep tonight.","But he heard her exclaim in her heart, [So my writing is this engaging? He even wants to take it back to read! There's hope! It looks like it's going to be a hit in the future!!! Tsk, maybe I can add a selling point later, something like \"The novel that the Emperor couldn't put down!\" It will definitely be a bestseller!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What nonsense is this?","Late at night, when all was quiet, Yuwen Lan returned to his bedchamber and continued reading the storybook.","As he had expected, since Madam Xia's husband returned to the capital, she had no more dealings with other men. However, her son was born soon after, confirming that the child was indeed the merchant's.","Putting down the story, Yuwen Lan felt rather conflicted. Fortunately, the Linwu Marquis had divorced her - how many times had he been cuckolded over the years!","With his doubts resolved, he finally closed his eyes and drifted off to sleep.","Little did he know that on this night, he would once again lose his dreams.","He slept fitfully until dawn. Upon waking, he discovered something else—the changes that had been occurring in his body for two consecutive days had abruptly ceased.","Yuwen Lan's heart sank, but he became even more convinced that the changes were related to Yanshu.","Only when he was near her, by her side, would he have dreams and experience changes. Without her presence, he would become numb again, just as before.","Suddenly feeling restless, he realized for the first time how excruciatingly long these three days of abstinence felt.","However, no matter what, he couldn't rush things. He forced himself to eat breakfast, then saw that the Imperial Guards he had sent to investigate the Minister of Revenue's household had returned to report.","Yuwen Lan composed himself and asked, \"What did you find?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"Your Majesty, we have confirmed that the Minister of Revenue's household spent 8,000 taels of silver on food and wine for the birthday celebration alone. In addition to that, there were expenses for decorating the mansion, purchasing flowers, gifts, and so on, totaling 13,000 taels of silver.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned.","Very well, spending 13,000 taels of silver just for a birthday celebration - truly more extravagant than the imperial palace.","\"Where did he get the money from?\"","The Imperial Guard said, \"We found several account books in his home, Your Majesty. Please take a look.\"","Yuwen Lan took them and opened them. As he looked, the Imperial Guard continued, \"Apart from the accumulated embezzlement since he took office, and tributes from his subordinates over the years, the bulk of the funds for this birthday celebration came from Duke Cheng'en, who gifted him 10,000 taels of silver.\"","\"Duke Cheng'en?\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","Due to his connection with the Empress Dowager, Duke Cheng'en's family was currently the most powerful clan in the capital. As a result, for many years, although Duke Cheng'en was unlearned and incompetent, countless people had curried favor with him.","Under normal circumstances, others would be bribing him. Why was he now sending money to the Minister of Revenue?","He asked further, \"Besides Qi Weizhai, has Duke Cheng'en sent anything to anyone else?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"In addition to gifting silver to the Minister of Revenue, Duke Cheng'en also presented four concubines to the Minister of Rites, and precious treasures to the Chancellor of the Wenhua Court and Tutor Sun of Crown Prince, among others.\"","Yuwen Lan understood.","These were all high-ranking officials. It seemed that his uncle was planning something big.","Very well, he would settle the account for those chestnut cakes along with this.","In Ganlu Palace.","Early in the morning, Yanshu washed up, changed her clothes, and came to the dining table to find breakfast already laid out.","Of course, it was still all vegetarian fare, without even a single egg.","She felt as if she had turned into a rabbit or a sheep, having completely forgotten what meat tasted like.","Seeing her dejected expression, Rendong quickly consoled her, \"My lady, just bear with it a little longer. You'll be able to eat meat tomorrow.\"","Yanshu replied, \"...Forget it. The ancestral worship is only tomorrow morning. We still have to eat vegetarian for breakfast and lunch. We won't see meat until dinner.\"","Unexpectedly, as soon as she finished speaking, she heard the system alert, [Warning: There's a situation. Someone plans to harm you during tomorrow's ancestral ceremony at Fengxian Hall.]","Yanshu was startled. [What? Who's causing trouble now?]","System: [Guess?]","Yanshu: [...Do I have to guess?]","System: [Use your little brain. Who hates you the most right now?]","Yanshu: \"...\"","What a question to ask. As the target of everyone's enmity, who in the harem didn't hate her?","But thinking about it, Consort Ning was under house arrest, Consort Li was in the Cold Palace, and that Consort Wang was still busy striking the night watch every day.","These three were unlikely candidates.","Moreover, tomorrow's ceremony was a grand occasion. The Emperor, consorts, royal relatives, civil and military officials would all attend. Who would dare to cause trouble at such a time?","It seemed that only... Noble Consort Zhou could pull it off.","System: [Bingo! Correct answer. Noble Consort Zhou has instructed Consort An to get rid of you tomorrow.]","Yanshu: [Consort An? As far as I know, she's quite cunning. Isn't she afraid of ending up like Consort Li?]","System: [Indeed, that's why she's not acting personally. She's found an old acquaintance of yours. Get ready.]","Yanshu: [An old acquaintance?]","She thought for a moment about her old acquaintances in the palace...","Tch, there was only one, wasn't there?","Well then, she hadn't settled the score for the humiliation she suffered last time. This was a perfect opportunity to sort things out.","The twenty-fifth day of the twelfth lunar month was the day for ancestral worship in the palace.","At the hour of Mao, before dawn, everyone had already risen, washed up, and eaten a simple breakfast. They then dressed in their ceremonial robes and headed to Fengxian Hall.","This was Yanshu's first time participating in such a grand ceremony, and even Rendong felt a bit nervous.","After all, all the civil and military officials and royal relatives would be present today. If they made the slightest mistake and embarrassed His Majesty, who knew what punishment they might face.","The mistress and maid arrived at Fengxian Hall to find many ancestral tablets arranged inside, representing the imperial ancestors of past dynasties. Giant candles burned brightly in the hall, and various pastries and dishes were laid out on the offering table.","The royal clan members and civil and military officials of the court stood quietly in their places, some even standing outside the hall.","Yanshu discreetly surveyed the scene and raised an eyebrow—wasn't that Duke Cheng'en standing near the front?","Tch, the man who couldn't even get out of bed three days ago had actually shown up today?","This was truly... impressive!","However, looking at his pale face and dark circles under his eyes, it was clear he was forcing himself to attend.","Then again, this was one of the most important days of the year, and important court officials couldn't be absent without good reason.","If he didn't come, he'd have to provide an explanation, but if he said he was unwell, wouldn't that risk exposing the chestnut cake incident?","Thinking about this, Yanshu couldn't help but want to laugh.","However, today was an extremely solemn occasion, and she absolutely couldn't laugh.","As she struggled to hold it in, she felt Rendong gently tug at her sleeve.","Yanshu followed Rendong's gaze and saw that Concubine Zhang had also come today.","Since damaging her voice, this woman hadn't appeared in public, and given her rank, she shouldn't have been allowed into Fengxian Hall.","Yanshu closed her eyes briefly to maintain her composure.","Ever since Consort Ning had been confined, Noble Consort Zhou had complete control over the harem. With so many people here today, she could summon whoever she wanted.","Besides, the system had already warned her, so she just needed to be ready to adapt to the situation.","Everyone had arrived, and after a short while, the Emperor finally made his appearance.","Yuwen Lan wore the twelve-dragon robe, looking majestic and solemn. Yanshu sneaked a glance and couldn't help but think, \"Damn, he's so handsome!\"","This jade-like face, this powerful aura, who could compare?","Yuwen Lan silently twitched the corner of his mouth. Calling him handsome was fine, but the first two words were unnecessary.","\"Greetings to Your Majesty.\"","A thunderous voice resounded through the hall as everyone knelt down in salutation. He calmly ordered everyone to rise, then signaled the ceremonial official to begin the ritual.","Musicians struck the bells and chimes, and ceremonial music filled the hall as the official began to recite the sacrificial text.","After the text was read, Yuwen Lan stepped forward to offer incense. Everyone in the hall knelt with him, performing the grand ceremony of three kneelings and nine kowtows to the ancestors of the Yuwen family.","Once the ceremony was complete, the ancestral worship was considered finished, and a sacrificial banquet awaited everyone at noon.","Just as people were about to leave the hall, a voice suddenly called out, \"This concubine has been wronged and begs Your Majesty to uphold justice.\"","The voice was coarse and hoarse, almost like a man's.","But everyone saw a woman dressed as a palace concubine suddenly kneeling on the ground.","It was none other than Concubine Zhang.","Yanshu's heart steadied. Well, she had been waiting for two days and nights, and it had finally come.","To cry injustice at such an occasion, and from a consort no less—while surprised, people began to speculate internally.","The Emperor naturally couldn't ignore this and stopped to ask, \"What injustice have you suffered?\"","Concubine Zhang said, \"This concubine's voice was originally fine. On the night of the eighth, I even sang for Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager. But after that night, I fell victim to someone's malicious act, and my voice became like this. I beg Your Majesty to severely punish the culprit...\"","As she spoke, she began to cry.","Indeed, with her harsh voice and such a narrative, it was easy to move people's hearts at first hearing.","A court official was heard saying, \"How could such a thing happen in the palace?\"","Yuwen Lan's expression remained unchanged as he asked, \"Then who did this to you? Do you have any evidence?\"","\"I do!\"","Concubine Zhang immediately said, \"At first, I didn't know I had been poisoned. It wasn't until a few days ago that I learned from my father's acquaintance in the Imperial Medical Institute that I had caught a cold, and someone had bribed a palace doctor to add poison to my medicine, causing my voice to become like this. That person was Li Guiyi.\"","As she spoke, she pointed directly at Yanshu.","Everyone turned to look at Yanshu.","Ah, finally it was her turn to enter the scene.","Yanshu immediately put on a surprised expression and said, \"Could Concubine Zhang be mistaking me for someone else? I have no grudge against you, why would I poison you?\"","Concubine Zhang spoke with conviction, \"Because you were jealous that my clothes and accessories were better than yours, and you were also jealous that I sang for His Majesty and the Empress Dowager that night, so you deliberately ruined my voice!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, before Yanshu could say anything, Yuwen Lan asked, \"Do you have any evidence?\"","Concubine Zhang immediately replied, \"I have a female doctor from the Imperial Medical Institute as a witness.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Bring her in.\"","Concubine Zhang complied and immediately instructed her maid Chun'e. Soon, a female doctor was brought in from outside the hall. She knelt down and said, \"Your Majesty, on the tenth day of the twelfth lunar month, Li Guiyi sent someone to find me and gave me fifty taels of silver, asking me to add some powder to Concubine Zhang's medicine. I was tempted by greed and couldn't resist the temptation, so I...\"","She then took out a package from her bosom and said, \"These are the fifty taels of silver. I've been regretting it ever since and didn't dare to spend it. Please forgive me, Your Majesty.\"","Fu Hai stepped forward to take the package. When he opened it, he saw that it indeed contained shiny silver ingots.","With this, everyone once again turned their gaze towards Yanshu.","However, she remained calm and even smiled, saying to the female doctor, \"You really think too highly of me. To be honest, on the tenth day of the twelfth lunar month, I didn't even have fifty taels of silver myself.\"","What?","Everyone looked doubtful upon hearing this.","Yanshu sighed, \"Since I entered the palace until recently, I was only a Beauty, with an annual salary of just fifty taels. After sending some to my family in Ande County every year, and often helping people in my palace, I didn't have much left. Last month, Xiao Dongzi's mother fell ill, and I gave him twenty taels. In summer, Lianxin's brother got married, and I gave her ten taels. Last year, when Xianghe's father who boiled water passed away, his family couldn't even afford a coffin, so I gave them money too. Let alone fifty taels, I only had small silver pieces, not such large ingots.\"","She then looked at Concubine Zhang and continued, \"My family is not as prominent as the other ladies here. I have neither power nor money in the palace. Even Xiao Chunzi was once bribed to frame me. How could I possibly command others to harm you?\"","As she finished speaking, Rendong also quickly knelt down and said to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, please see the truth. I can swear to heaven that everything my mistress said is true. Whenever anyone in the palace had difficulties and sought help from my mistress, she always generously gave what she could. She never turned anyone away.\"","Of course, the salaries of concubines were all clearly stipulated by court etiquette. Those of higher rank naturally received more, but those of lower rank like Beauties indeed only received this much.","Everyone also knew that her family held a low official position in the poor and remote Ande County. According to her words, she indeed wouldn't have much left.","Yuwen Lan instructed Fu Hai, \"Have someone investigate these silver ingots and see where they came from.\"","— The silver used in the palace was different from that used by commoners, with official serial numbers on them, so this wouldn't be difficult to investigate.","Fu Hai quickly complied and had someone take away the bag of silver ingots.","Seeing this, Concubine Zhang paused for a moment, then said to Yanshu, \"But the witness is right here. That day, someone also saw you sending Rendong to find her at the Imperial Pharmacy!\"","Rendong quickly said, \"Doesn't the Concubine know? Our mistress was also unwell those two days. I went to the Imperial Pharmacy to get medicine for my mistress, but I never saw this female doctor. If you don't believe me, you can ask the doctors at the Imperial Medical Institute to check.\"","Yuwen Lan then instructed Hu An, the Chief Eunuch of the Ceremonial Office, \"Go to the Imperial Pharmacy and see who was on duty that day.\"","Hu An complied and hurried to the Imperial Pharmacy.","Not long after, two imperial doctors arrived at the hall.","One of them was familiar to Yanshu, the doctor who had treated her carbuncle that day.","Fu Hai pointed at Rendong and asked the two, \"Did either of you see this young lady from Ganlu Palace, oh no, it was Yongning Palace at that time, on the tenth?\"","One of them lowered his head and said, \"This official did see this young lady on the tenth. She first came to get medicine for Li Guiyi, and then she went to talk with the female doctor Chunjin.\"","Upon hearing this, Rendong was about to argue anxiously, but Yanshu stopped her with a look.","Then Fu Hai looked at the doctor who had cured her carbuncle and asked, \"What about you?\"","The doctor said, \"This humble servant was consulting with patients and didn't pay attention to whether this young lady came or not. However, the female doctor Chunjin was not on duty at the Imperial Pharmacy on the tenth.\"","Fu Hai quickly asked, \"Is that true?\"","The doctor affirmed confidently, \"I stake my life on it. Chunjin is on duty on the 2nd, 4th, and 7th of each month. She wasn't even in the palace on the 10th.\"","As he finished speaking, everyone looked at the Emperor.","These two had completely contradictory statements. How would the Emperor decide?","Then Yuwen Lan said, \"Go check the duty roster at the Imperial Pharmacy.\"","He had already discerned the truth from everyone's inner voices, but what was needed now was for the people present to know the truth and falsehood.","In a moment, a guard brought over the duty roster from the Imperial Pharmacy.","At first glance, there was indeed a record of Chunjin being on duty on the 10th.","But Fu Hai leaned in to smell it and immediately said, \"Your Majesty, the ink here seems to have been newly applied.\"","The smell hadn't even dissipated yet.","The Minister of Justice was present, and Yuwen Lan said, \"Take a look.\"","The Minister of Justice complied, immediately stepping forward to smell and wipe with water. After a series of examinations, he reported to the Emperor, \"Your Majesty, this ink was newly applied in the past few days.\"","With these words, everyone had already made their judgment.","Yuwen Lan looked at the first imperial doctor who had spoken and said, \"As a doctor, one should heal the sick and save lives. If you harm an innocent person for a little personal gain, where is your conscience?\"","The man's face turned pale. After hesitating for a moment, he suddenly fell to his knees and started kowtowing desperately, \"Please forgive me, Your Majesty. Someone threatened the lives of my entire family, which is why I told a lie...\"","Yuwen Lan said sternly, \"What's the truth? I may spare your life.\"","The imperial doctor wept bitterly, \"On the 10th, this humble servant only prescribed medicine for peach blossom allergy to Miss Rendong. Chunjin was indeed not on duty.\"","Everyone turned to look at the female doctor Chunjin, who had already turned pale and was trembling uncontrollably.","Yuwen Lan said coldly, \"Take her away for severe interrogation. Find out who instructed her to falsely accuse Li Guiyi.\"","Everyone complied, and someone immediately dragged her out.","The remaining Concubine Zhang was extremely nervous and could only say, \"I don't know who instructed Chunjin, but my voice has indeed been ruined. I have truly been harmed by someone. Since I entered the palace, I've only been close to Li Guiyi. Apart from her, no one would harm me.\"","This reason was too far-fetched, and everyone clearly didn't believe it anymore.","But Yanshu spoke up, \"It's strange, actually. Around that time, I also had a peach blossom allergy, with rashes all over my body and even some difficulty breathing. It's odd to have a peach blossom allergy in the depths of winter, isn't it? I found it peculiar when I thought about it a few days ago, so I mentioned it to Chief Eunuch Fu. I wonder how your investigation is going?\"","Hearing this, Fu Hai quickly said, \"Indeed, this matter is strange. In the depths of winter, where would peach blossoms be blooming except in the greenhouse of the Imperial Gardens Bureau? I sent someone to inquire at the Imperial Gardens Bureau and found out something interesting. It turns out that on the night of the 8th, someone went there to get some peach blossom pollen.\"","Peach blossom pollen?","Everyone became interested. Could this be the source of Li Guiyi's peach blossom allergy? So she was actually the one who had been poisoned!","Yuwen Lan had just learned about this matter as well and asked, \"Who requested the peach blossom pollen?\"","Fu Hai quickly answered, \"This servant was planning to report to Your Majesty after the ceremony. It was Chun'e, the maid from Linhua Hall, who requested the peach blossom pollen.\"","Upon hearing this, Chun'e, who was standing beside Concubine Zhang, immediately fell to her knees and said, \"Your Majesty, please see the truth. This servant only requested some peach blossom pollen to make perfume for the Concubine. I never went to Yongning Palace.\"","Fu Hai smiled coldly, \"Indeed, you didn't go to Yongning Palace. You went to the Laundry Bureau.\"","Chun'e shuddered visibly.","Fu Hai continued to report to Yuwen Lan, \"This slave thought about how the peach blossom powder could have gotten on Li Guiyi's body to cause her displeasure. It seemed sprinkling it on clothing would be the best method, so this slave sent someone to the Laundry Bureau to investigate. We discovered that on the evening of the 8th, after Chun'e obtained the peach blossom powder from the Imperial Gardens Bureau, she went directly to the Laundry Bureau and bribed a washerwoman to sprinkle it on Li Guiyi's clothes.\"","Upon hearing this, Concubine Zhang turned deathly pale.","The Emperor coldly ordered, \"Bring her in.\"","Fu Hai complied and sent people to fetch her. Soon after, a bloodied and barely conscious palace maid was dragged into the hall. She weakly pleaded, \"Your Majesty, spare me... Concubine Zhang told Chun'e to come... She gave this slave fifty taels of silver...\"","Everyone realized that this was where the fifty taels of silver had been used.","Suddenly, sobbing could be heard in the hall. Yanshu looked at Concubine Zhang with tears in her eyes and said, \"You just said that since entering the palace, we've been good friends. At that time, besides you, no one else knew me. I considered you my closest sister, yet you would harm me like this... *sob*...\"","Come on! Let's cry together! See who can shed the most tears!","As if others wouldn't know how to do it. The one who harmed others first still thinks she's in the right!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He knew it.","Beside him, Concubine Zhang still shook her head in denial, \"No, it wasn't me, it wasn't me...\"","Yuwen Lan had already lost patience. He glanced at Chun'e and directly ordered, \"Take this woman away and torture her severely.\"","Severe torture?","Chun'e looked at the washerwoman lying on the ground, now barely recognizable as human. Her soul had already fled. Trembling, Chun'e could only say, \"Your Majesty, please spare me. It was the Concubine who ordered this slave to do it. This slave was forced...\"","Yuwen Lan disdained to speak to her. Fu Hai quickly asked, \"Then why did Concubine Zhang want to harm Li Guiyi?\"","Chun'e cried, \"Because on the night of the New Year's Eve banquet, Li Guiyi deliberately dressed simply to attract His Majesty's attention. The Concubine misunderstood that His Majesty was looking at her, so she took the initiative to perform. Unexpectedly, she was ridiculed by Consort Li and lost face. My mistress couldn't bear it, so she ordered this slave to disfigure Li Guiyi...\"","It's over. Everything is over.","Concubine Zhang completely collapsed on the ground.","The Emperor's cold voice was heard, \"You committed evil first, showed no remorse, and then did it again. Who gave you such audacity?\"","Concubine Zhang could only glance secretly at Consort An, thinking, \"Save me! Wasn't it agreed that Noble Consort Zhou would ensure nothing would happen to me?\"","However, Consort An only looked at her coldly, her eyes conveying an unspoken warning.","If she dared to say a word, the entire Zhang family would be finished.","Concubine Zhang hesitated, and finally could only say with difficulty, \"It was this concubine's own idea.\"","-- That day Consort An had found her and asked if she could remain calm seeing Yanshu so favored.","Indeed, for the past half month, she had spent every day in jealousy.","Why was she unable to speak again, while Yanshu could accompany the Emperor in bed every day?","So she decided to take a gamble.","She thought that with Noble Consort Zhou's support, she could bring down Yanshu no matter what.","But how could it turn out like this?","His Majesty actually trusted her so much! In front of so many people, he was actually so biased towards her!","Concubine Zhang gritted her teeth and said, \"This concubine couldn't accept it! Why is she the only one among all the palace concubines to receive Your Majesty's favor?\"","The hall fell silent, with everyone coldly observing.","Only Yuwen Lan answered her coldly, \"Because her heart is pure and she has never thought of harming others.\"","As his words fell, many in the hall felt uneasy.","The Emperor continued, \"Your character is vicious, and you deliberately disrupted the sacrificial ceremony. Your crime is unforgivable. You are sentenced to death by white silk. Your mother's clan members will all be exiled and can never enter official positions again.\"","With these words, Concubine Zhang was dragged away, leaving everyone terrified.","Only Noble Consort Zhou spoke up, \"The evil person has received her just deserts. I hope Your Majesty will calm your anger and not harm your health.\"","As she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan suddenly looked at her and said meaningfully, \"Why are there repeatedly such evil people in the palace?\"","Noble Consort Zhou's heart skipped a beat, but she forced herself to say, \"This concubine does not know.\"","What does he mean? Does he suspect her?","Yuwen Lan gave a cold laugh, \"Previously, the Empress Dowager entrusted you with the authority to manage the six palaces, yet the palace is in such chaos. Even a washerwoman from the Laundry Bureau can be bribed to harm her masters.\"","Noble Consort Zhou bit her lip and could only say, \"This concubine is incompetent and has disappointed Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Since you know you're incompetent, then step down.\"","Noble Consort Zhou paused. What did he mean? Was he going to strip her of her powers?","She hurriedly looked towards the group of ministers.","\"Your Majesty, please allow this old minister to say a word.\"","Everyone looked over to see that the speaker was Qi Weizhai, the Minister of Revenue who had just celebrated his birthday a few days ago.","Yuwen Lan stopped and said, \"Oh? What does Minister Qi want to say?\"","The minister replied, \"In this old minister's opinion, we cannot entirely blame Noble Consort Zhou for evil people giving in to greed and committing wrongdoings. Since Your Majesty ascended the throne, there has been no Empress, which has led to disorder in the rear palace. Perhaps Your Majesty should establish an Empress soon to pacify the people's hearts.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, another white-haired old man chimed in, \"Minister Qi speaks wisely. We implore Your Majesty to establish an Empress soon, to act as mother of the nation and bring stability to the rear palace.\"","It was the Minister of Rites.","After he finished, three or four others followed suit, \"We beseech Your Majesty to establish an Empress soon, to pacify the people's hearts.\"","Yuwen Lan's face showed no emotion as his gaze swept over each person. He said, \"Who do you think I should make Empress?\"","At these words, Noble Consort Zhou suddenly became excited. She had waited for countless days and nights, and finally, the moment had come!","With so many important ministers recommending her today, and in front of the ancestral temple no less, surely he couldn't refuse this time?","The Minister of Revenue, Qi Weizhai, said, \"In this old minister's opinion, Noble Consort Zhou comes from a noble family and has received the Empress Dowager's teachings for three years. She is worthy of the position of Empress.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Oh? Is this truly what you think, or is it because Duke Cheng'en sent you ten thousand taels of silver a few days ago that you say this?\"","Hearing this, everyone was stunned. Duke Cheng'en had sent the Minister of Revenue ten thousand taels?","Qi Weizhai was startled and hurriedly said, \"Your Majesty, it's not like that. Duke Cheng'en has never given this old minister any silver. These are truly my heartfelt words, unrelated to anything else.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Yuwen Lan threw an account book in front of him and said, \"This book records every single transaction you've made over the years. The largest recent entry is ten thousand taels of silver from Duke Cheng'en.\"","Saying this, he suddenly turned to Duke Cheng'en, \"Why did Duke Cheng'en give the Minister of Revenue so much money? Did you have some favor to ask of him?\"","His gaze was sharp, and Duke Cheng'en was startled. He hurried to step forward and kneel, but his body was already weak, and he lost control, falling flat on the ground.","Everyone: \"???\"","How guilty must one be to perform such a grand gesture?","Yanshu, who was watching the drama unfold, tried hard to suppress her laughter.","Duke Cheng'en, with the help of those around him, finally managed to kneel properly and hurriedly said, \"Your Majesty, this old minister and the Minister of Revenue were classmates many years ago. Our friendship is deep. The gift of silver was merely to congratulate him on his birthday, with no other intention.\"","However, the Emperor asked again, \"Then why did uncle also send several concubines to the Minister of Rites? Are you also old classmates with deep friendship?\"","What? Concubines?","Everyone widened their eyes and looked at the white-haired Minister of Rites.","Isn't he over seventy years old?","At such an age... can he still... manage?","The Minister of Rites hesitated, then quickly said, \"Your Majesty, please understand. Duke Cheng'en did indeed send several maids to this old minister's household recently, but I have already distributed them to my sons' and grandsons' quarters. At my age, how could I do such an outrageous thing?\"","-- He knew that since the Emperor asked in this way, he must have already investigated. In such a situation, denial would not be wise, so it was better to find an excuse to cover it up.","Although he said this, everyone began to speculate in their hearts --","So the Minister of Rites is like this... Still vigorous in his old age!","Yanshu also internally exclaimed, she had just learned about this, which was unusual!","She hurriedly called out to the system, \"How come you didn't tell me about such an interesting piece of gossip? This old man, at his age, can still handle concubines? Could it be that Duke Cheng'en sent over his own mistresses?\"","The system replied, \"More or less. But this is just an appetizer. Do you want to know an even bigger piece of gossip?\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, \"What gossip?\"","The system said, \"This old man is having an affair with his daughter-in-law.\"","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","Scandalous!"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24","paragraphs":["This was truly exhilarating.","You must understand, this was the Minister of Rites! The highest official in charge of the five rites and ceremonies at court!","Who could have imagined that this old man, who constantly preached about propriety and morality, could do something so morally bankrupt!!!","At this moment, everything else happening around became secondary, as Yanshu eagerly began to indulge in this juicy gossip.","[What's the situation? Tell me quickly.]","System: [You know the Minister of Rites has two sons, right?]","Yanshu: [I know, isn't his eldest son Consort An's father? The one who's currently the Assistant Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial?]","Suddenly her eyes widened, [Don't tell me the one he's having an affair with is Consort An's mother?]","Not far away, the emperor accurately picked up on this sentence amidst the surprised inner voices, and couldn't help but pause quietly.","An affair?","Consort An's mother?","Could it be... she's talking about the Minister of Rites?","System: [You're overthinking it. Even if that lady wanted to, this old man probably wouldn't be interested. His younger son has been sickly since childhood and doesn't have much ability. But his wife, Lady Zhao, is quite shrewd. After marriage, seeing that she couldn't rely on her husband, she started an affair with the old man to secure benefits for herself. Because of this, the old man often favors the second household, causing much dissatisfaction in the first household.]","Yanshu clicked her tongue, [So it seems this father-in-law and daughter-in-law have been having an affair for many years? Hasn't anyone in the Minister of Rites' household discovered it? Is his younger son content with wearing a green hat for so many years?]","Yuwen Lan, who had been quietly listening, paused. It really was about the Minister of Rites?","System: [The old man's wife died many years ago, so there's no one to keep an eye on things. That younger son gets out of breath just walking a few steps, and usually sleeps separately from his wife, so of course he hasn't discovered anything.]","Yanshu clicked her tongue again, [With his younger son in such poor health, how could this father be so heartless as to steal his son's wife? Doesn't he fear that one day his younger son might die and come back as a ghost to seek revenge?]","As she spoke, she secretly glanced at the Minister of Rites who was talking to the emperor, and inwardly spat, [What a scoundrel!]","Nearby, Yuwen Lan, who had silently listened to everything, \"...\"","Well, he could probably guess what this was all about now.","Glancing at the Minister of Rites in front of him, who was vehemently denying the matter of a concubine, he said, \"Given to your son? Your eldest son is also not young, and your younger son is congenitally weak, right? Tell me, which son did you give her to? Is your daughter-in-law... willing?\"","He deliberately emphasized the words \"daughter-in-law\", and sure enough, he saw the Minister of Rites pause, panic rising in his heart.","[What, what does this mean? Could it be... could it be that His Majesty knows???]","Yuwen Lan was inwardly certain now, so it really was true!!!","He temporarily concealed his shock and spoke again meaningfully, \"If you don't want others to know, then don't do it yourself.\"","The Minister of Rites stood dazed for a few seconds.","But then he suddenly knelt down and wept bitterly, \"This old minister knows his crime, please forgive me, Your Majesty. This matter was originally because Duke Cheng'en was concerned about Noble Consort Zhou and wanted this old minister to find an opportunity to put in a good word. But Noble Consort Zhou is virtuous and gentle, there was no need for this minister to say anything... I will return them immediately.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, before Yuwen Lan could say anything, Duke Cheng'en, who was kneeling nearby, suddenly went limp and fell to the side.","The hall immediately erupted in shocked cries.","Noble Consort Zhou couldn't help but rush forward, crying out, \"Father!\"","However, after calling several times, Duke Cheng'en showed no response.","Noble Consort Zhou hurriedly turned back to plead with Yuwen Lan, \"I beg Your Majesty to quickly summon the imperial physician to save my father.\"","Yuwen Lan coldly said, \"Isn't there already one in the hall?\"","Saying this, he looked at the physician who had just spoken truthfully for Yanshu, and said, \"You come and take a look at Duke Cheng'en.\"","The physician complied and went to Duke Cheng'en's side to examine him.","Everyone watched intently, not understanding what was happening.","Only Yanshu continued to enjoy the drama while clicking her tongue, [This physician has a straightforward personality and high medical skills. If he diagnoses that Duke Cheng'en has overdosed on pure aphrodisiacs and says it out loud... Hahaha, that would be so exciting, hahaha!!!]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","She really does love to watch the drama unfold!","However, things turned out exactly as she predicted.","After a short while, the physician said to the emperor, \"Your Majesty, Duke Cheng'en has fainted due to kidney yang deficiency. It seems he has recently indulged in excessive sexual activity, severely depleting his body.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, everyone's eyes widened—","Excessive sexual indulgence?","Tsk tsk, it's worth noting that not only the people in the palace, but all those participating in the ceremony today were supposed to observe abstinence for three days.","Duke Cheng'en actually managed to... indulge in sexual activity during this period???","And to excess???","Noble Consort Zhou panicked and immediately rebuked, \"Don't talk nonsense! It's currently the fasting period, how could Duke Cheng'en do such a preposterous thing?\"","But the physician replied, \"As a medical practitioner, I would never falsely state a patient's condition. If I were to delay treatment due to false diagnosis, I would fear divine punishment. Duke Cheng'en's condition is critical now. If we don't treat him quickly according to his symptoms, I'm afraid he might not wake up.\"","\"This...\"","Noble Consort Zhou was frightened by his words.","It was Yuwen Lan who spoke, \"Then quickly treat him.\"","The physician complied and immediately took out a set of silver needles from his sleeve, beginning to insert them into several acupoints on Duke Cheng'en's body.","Everyone craned their necks, watching intently.","After a short while, Duke Cheng'en indeed slowly regained consciousness.","However, his face was now distorted, his body extremely weak. He wanted to call out \"Your Majesty\", but couldn't make a sound for a long time.","Let alone stand up.","Seeing this, everyone inwardly clicked their tongues—at such an age, still indulging in excessive sexual activity, how embarrassing to lose face in front of the ancestors.","But how should they address this breach of abstinence? Surely His Majesty couldn't cover it up?","Just then, they heard the emperor say sternly, \"Duke Cheng'en, as a royal relative, you indulged in sexual activity during the fasting period, which is truly outrageous! Even if I could tolerate it, the ancestral laws and the common people cannot. Moreover, you bribed officials, attempting to disrupt the court! Effective immediately, you are stripped of your official position, fined three years' salary, and Noble Consort Zhou is demoted to the rank of consort.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the hall was stunned into silence.","Noble Consort Zhou nearly fainted, hurriedly kneeling down and pleading, \"Your Majesty, please show mercy. Duke Cheng'en just accidentally...\"","But Yuwen Lan cut her off, saying, \"Was it really an accident? Then who caused this accident?\"","Noble Consort Zhou was stunned, suddenly feeling extremely panicked.","Could it be... he knows?","If he investigates the matter of drugging...","Wouldn't the consequences be even more severe?","She dared not say anything more, and then heard Yuwen Lan continue, \"This is already a lenient punishment, considering the Empress Dowager's feelings. If you dare to commit any other offenses, there will be no leniency!\"","After speaking, he looked at the crowd in the hall and said sternly, \"Let this be a warning to all present today!\"","Everyone responded in unison, while inwardly they were extremely shocked—","The Empress Dowager's own niece, just like that, lost her position as Noble Consort!!!","Of course, given the offense Duke Cheng'en committed, it wouldn't have been excessive even to strip the Zhou family of their ducal title. But clearly, the emperor had considered the Empress Dowager's face and didn't push things to the extreme.","However, for others... that might not be the case.","At this moment, the Minister of Revenue, Chai Weizhong, was already drenched in sweat, his legs trembling.","The white-haired Minister of Rites was shaking like a sieve.","Then, they saw the emperor address the two Chief Censors, saying, \"Fish brains from a thousand fish made into tofu, crab meat from ten thousand crabs made into crab paste, the Minister of Revenue's household spending over ten thousand taels of silver on a single meal – do I need to tell you about this?\"","The two men fell to their knees in fear, saying in unison, \"It was our negligence.\"","Yuwen Lan said coldly, \"Was it really negligence, or were you also involved?\"","The two kept kowtowing, saying, \"We wouldn't dare.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"If you don't investigate this matter thoroughly, you two can also step down.\"","The two hurriedly agreed.","Yuwen Lan then walked towards the hall entrance.","He could still hear various people's inner thoughts—","[Indeed, nothing escapes His Majesty's eyes!]","[It seems the Zhou family's glory and favor ends here today.]","[Moving against the Zhou family like this, I wonder if it will cause a rift between His Majesty and the Empress Dowager? I hope nothing major happens!]","Among them, only one person caught his particular attention—","[Damn, was he just bluffing the Minister of Rites earlier, or does he really know about that old man's affair with his daughter-in-law?]","Yanshu looked bewildered, [Damn, was I not the first to know about this juicy gossip??? Help!!!]","Yuwen Lan inwardly smiled faintly, leaving with an inscrutable expression.","In the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Having lost her position as Noble Consort and watching her father being carried away with a distorted face, Consort Zhou could only come here to appeal to the Empress Dowager.","It was only now that the Empress Dowager learned what a monumentally stupid thing her niece had done.","After hearing her out, the Empress Dowager nearly fainted. Several palace maids, including Zhushu Matron, hurriedly came forward, patting her back and helping her breathe, preventing her from passing out.","When she had somewhat recovered, the Empress Dowager pointed angrily at her niece's nose and said, \"You truly are a hopeless case! I only told you to deliver some snacks, who told you to go beyond that? Do you know what a grave offense it is to drug the emperor? Not to mention you, even I might not be able to protect myself!\"","Even if she didn't know before, Noble Consort Zhou now understood. She could only cover her face and cry bitterly, \"Niece knows her crime, please save niece, aunt...\"","Without her position as Noble Consort, what did she have left to live for?","So she deliberately addressed the Empress Dowager as aunt, vainly hoping that the Empress Dowager would help her for the sake of family ties.","However, the Empress Dowager merely slapped her face and told her to get out.","\"From now on, you are forbidden to come to the Palace of Benevolent Peace. Don't let me see you again!\"","After speaking, she ordered her servants to drive her out.","Noble Consort Zhou, oh no, now she should be called Consort Zhou — the emperor had just lowered her rank, not even giving her an honorary title.","Consort Zhou could only cry all the way back to her own Zhongcui Palace.","When Yuwen Lan arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace, the Empress Dowager was reclining on her couch, looking unwell.","He immediately went to the couch and bowed his head, saying, \"I've come to ask for Mother's forgiveness. A most absurd incident occurred during today's ceremony, and I had no choice but to punish Uncle and demote the Noble Consort.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed and said, \"It's my fault for not managing the Zhou family properly, causing trouble for Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"I believe Uncle was just momentarily confused, but it happened during the ceremony in front of everyone. If we don't punish him, I'm afraid others might follow suit, and our rituals will become a laughingstock.\"","\"Your Majesty prioritizes the bigger picture, which is a blessing for the empire.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed again softly, but then suddenly changed the subject, saying, \"However, it's not right for the six palaces to be without a mistress. I still hope Your Majesty can quickly determine the position of Empress to put everyone's mind at ease.\"","\"Although Li Beauty suits Your Majesty's taste, her family's official rank is too low to truly command respect. Why not have the Ministry of Rites recommend noble ladies from prestigious families after spring, so that the selection of an Empress can be settled soon?\"","Yuwen Lan knew that the Empress Dowager had given up on the Zhou family women and was planning to cultivate new talent.","But he didn't want to give in, so he said, \"It's my fault for making Mother worry about this. I will keep it in mind, but after spring, the Ministry of Rites needs to prepare for the spring imperial examinations. The matter of recommendations will have to wait for now.\"","The Empress Dowager closed her eyes and said, \"Let it be as Your Majesty wishes. I'm tired, Your Majesty should go rest as well.\"","Yuwen Lan agreed and took his leave.","As he reached the door, he heard the Empress Dowager sigh in her heart, [After all, he's not my own flesh and blood. Never mind.]","His heart sank, but he didn't stop walking and left the Palace of Benevolent Peace directly.","Yuwen Lan didn't take the imperial carriage, instead walking aimlessly in the cold wind. When he came to his senses, he was already outside the Ganlu Palace.","He heard Fu Hai clicking his tongue in his mind, [Your Majesty really misses Li Beauty, rushing here as soon as the ceremony ended.]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Actually, he hadn't rushed over, he just somehow ended up here.","However, since he had something to ask her anyway, he stepped into the hall.","Upon entering, he saw Yanshu writing at a table. She only put down her brush and hurriedly rose to greet him when she heard the announcement, \"This humble consort greets Your Majesty.\"","As she spoke, she secretly glanced at his expression, pondering in her heart, [He seems a bit unhappy? Could it be that the Empress Dowager scolded him?]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Had his emotions become so apparent on his face?","So he quickly composed himself and said, \"Rise,\" then asked her, \"Writing another novel?\"","Yanshu said yes.","Yuwen Lan became a bit interested and asked her, \"What new story have you written this time?\"","Yanshu coughed and said, \"This humble consort is writing about a woman who was deceived by a scumbag, but after discovering the truth, she bravely fought back and became self-reliant.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't quite understand and asked, \"What does 'scumbag' mean?\"","Yanshu explained, \"It means a bad man. They deceive women's feelings at will, without any sense of propriety or shame, just like the useless pulp left after we finish eating sugarcane.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"This term is quite unique.\"","He then asked, \"So, how did this scumbag deceive the woman?\"","Yanshu coughed and said, \"This man actually had a preference for men, and he didn't like women at all. But to keep up appearances, he still married and had children. However, after that, he left his wife in their hometown to take care of his parents, while he kept male lovers elsewhere, which was very outrageous.\"","Yuwen Lan listened and secretly raised an eyebrow. Wasn't this talking about Chai Weizhong, the Vice Minister of War?","It seemed that each of her stories corresponded to a real person.","He lightly coughed and said, \"Indeed outrageous. However, it's not uncommon for men to work outside while women stay at home to serve their in-laws. How did his wife discover that she had been deceived?\"","Yanshu thought as she spoke, \"One winter, the man's elderly mother suddenly fell ill. After receiving treatment in their hometown for a long time without improvement, she wanted to seek her son's help to invite a famous doctor in the city to examine her.\"","\"Originally, they should have sent a letter, but it happened that it had been snowing for days, delaying the mail. The wife was also worried about her mother-in-law's condition, so she simply took the whole family on the journey.\"","\"However, after a long and tiring journey, when they arrived at the mansion in the city, she discovered that her husband was actually involved with men, and all the women in the mansion were actually men in disguise.\"","Yuwen Lan played along, feigning surprise, \"How could such a thing happen?\"","Yanshu nodded and continued, \"After all, this lady had been managing the household for so many years. She wasn't a fool. After a bit of thought, she understood her husband's secret.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"That's one way to do it.\"","Yanshu found this remark strange, \"Why does Your Majesty say it like that?\"","Yuwen Lan coughed and said, \"I mean, your way of writing is very good.\"","He quickly changed the subject and asked, \"So how did this lady become self-reliant?\"","Yanshu began to imagine, \"After discovering the truth, she cried her heart out. After that, she insisted on divorcing the scumbag and used her excellent embroidery skills to open an embroidery shop. Through hard work and management, she finally lived a life of her own making. As for the scumbag, his ugly deeds were exposed, bringing him great shame. Not only did he lose his job, but he also angered his parents half to death. From then on, he was ruined and left with nothing!\"","Then she asked him, \"What does Your Majesty think of this ending?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"A weak woman who has long been managing household affairs might be too simple-minded to open an embroidery shop.\"","Yanshu pouted and said, \"This is just a novel. It's meant to make people feel good when they read it. If we have to write it exactly like reality, people might feel depressed after reading it.\"","Ah, it was just her beautiful imagination. She had heard that the poor Mrs. Chai was just a simple housewife, and it was uncertain whether she could escape her misery in this lifetime.","But Yuwen Lan nodded, \"That makes sense. Where there's a will, there's a way. Anything is possible.\"","Yanshu nodded, suddenly remembering something important, and hurriedly asked him, \"By the way, did Your Majesty bring back the manuscript you took away a few days ago?\"","Yuwen Lan was stunned, \"...Not yet.\"","Yanshu became a bit anxious, \"That's a very important thing for me. You didn't lose it, did you?\"","Damn, that piece took her three whole days to write! If it was lost, she might just want to kill someone!","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","So scary.","He quickly explained, \"Of course I didn't lose it. I came from the Palace of Benevolent Peace and didn't bring it with me. I'll have someone send it to you later.\"","Yanshu could only agree.","Yuwen Lan paused and then asked, \"Why didn't you tell me about Taohua's insubordination before?\"","Yanshu thought to herself that at that time, she was just a nameless beauty. Even if she wanted to tell him, he wouldn't have heard.","Out loud, she said, \"This humble consort had no concrete evidence at the time, so it wasn't appropriate to say anything even if I wanted to.\"","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"Then why did you ask Fu Hai to investigate?\"","Could it be that she could foresee that Zhang Cairen would make false accusations today?","But he heard her think, [Times have changed. Now I have you as a powerful backer to rely on, so of course I should seek revenge when I can. They've bullied me to this extent, if I don't fight back, wouldn't I be a pushover?]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","But he heard her say out loud, \"This humble consort just suddenly remembered it a few days ago, so I mentioned it to Chief Eunuch Fu.\"","Yuwen Lan glanced at Fu Hai and said, \"It seems Fu Hai is more useful than me.\"","Upon hearing this, Fu Hai was so frightened that he immediately knelt down, \"This slave wouldn't dare. Actually, Li Beauty knew that Your Majesty was busy with state affairs and didn't want to trouble you with this, so she just mentioned it to this slave. This slave also felt that this matter was indeed suspicious, so I had someone ask around.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Considering that you caught the culprit this time, you may rise.\"","Fu Hai dared to stand up again only after hearing this.","Yanshu watched from the side, her heart pounding.","She thought to herself, \"Indeed, serving the emperor is like serving a tiger. This Grand Steward Fu doesn't have it easy.\"","At that moment, she suddenly remembered something important and hurriedly said, \"Your Majesty, I think the physician at today's ceremony was quite remarkable. I hope he won't face retaliation for speaking the truth.\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"I have my own arrangements. Don't worry.\"","These days, it was rare to find someone who dared to speak the truth without fear of power. He would naturally take this opportunity to reward him, to show his determination to punish evil and promote good.","Yanshu felt somewhat relieved, but then heard the emperor ask her, \"Is the matter about the salary true?\"","Yanshu looked puzzled and said, \"How dare I deceive you, Your Majesty? If you don't believe me, you can call in Xiao Dongzi and the others to verify.\"","Hearing this, Lianxin immediately knelt on the ground, her eyes filled with tears, and said, \"This servant swears to heaven that my mistress has never spoken falsely to Your Majesty. A few years ago, when my father fell ill and our family's savings were exhausted, it was thanks to the silver my mistress gave me that my brother was able to start a family.\"","Yanshu inwardly scoffed, [Do they think everyone's life is so easy? Behind the gates of the rich, meat and wine go to waste, while the poor freeze to death on the streets!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So now he was in the wrong?","He glanced at her and said, \"You're tight on money yourself, yet you help others?\"","Yanshu pouted, \"No matter how tight I am, I still have food and shelter in the palace. If I don't help them, their families won't be able to get by. Besides, keeping them content helps them stay in the palace, doesn't it?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"You do have a point.\"","But then he heard her mutter in her mind, [After saying all this, shouldn't he reward me with some silver?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Why was this girl's mind always on money?","He felt playful and decided to test her, asking, \"You've been wronged this time. Should I compensate you somehow?\"","Really?","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she quickly said, \"Thank you for your consideration, Your Majesty. Actually, I don't need any compensation. As long as Your Majesty believes me, I'm content.\"","[Actually, it doesn't need to be much, just a casual reward of eight hundred or a thousand taels would be enough, hehe. If not, even three to five hundred taels would do. I'm not picky.]","She was rubbing her hands together in her mind, but then heard him say, \"Very well, it's rare to see you so magnanimous and sensible.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","What?","What did that mean???","She was just being polite, couldn't he tell???","Yuwen Lan hid his smile and said with a serious face, \"It's getting late. I need to go back and read some memorials. You can continue writing.\"","With that, he stood up and walked out.","Yanshu: \"???\"","Hey, hey, is that it? What about my compensation?!","That's so unfair!","Yuwen Lan silently listened, and as he stepped out of the hall, he finally couldn't help but curl his lips into a smile.","He had to admit, spending a little time with her had greatly improved his mood.","Returning to Qianming Palace, Yuwen Lan changed his clothes in the bedchamber before heading to the study.","Before leaving, he casually instructed Fu Hai, \"Remember to have someone send the manuscript I read the other night to Ganlu Palace.\"","If he forgot again, who knows how she would grumble about him.","Fu Hai complied and quickly pointed to Xiao Shunzi at the door, \"You're quick on your feet, go deliver this to Li Beauty.\"","Xiao Shunzi agreed, took the manuscript, and headed out.","When he reached the gate of Qianming Palace, he ran into Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong.","Scholar Zou, in his forties and quite erudite, immediately became curious upon seeing the stack of papers in Xiao Shunzi's hands. \"Is this an imperial edict?\" he asked.","Xiao Shunzi scratched his head and replied, \"I don't think so. It's from His Majesty's bedchamber, and I was told to deliver it to Li Beauty.\"","Oh, so it was for a consort.","Zou Mozhong knew he shouldn't pry, but seeing the papers densely covered in writing, seemingly like an article, he couldn't help but grow more curious. He asked, \"Could this be an article personally written by His Majesty?\"","Xiao Shunzi shook his head again, \"I don't know.\"","Scholar Zou boldly took a closer look and saw that the handwriting was messy and clearly not His Majesty's.","However, the sentences were quite interesting, like some kind of story.","He wanted to ask more, but Xiao Shunzi, worried about delays, hurried off.","Scholar Zou had no choice but to head to the imperial study first.","-- As a Hanlin Academy Scholar responsible for drafting imperial edicts, and due to the day's events at the Hall of Supreme Harmony, the emperor had issued three edicts to investigate officials for corruption, bribery, and accepting bribes. Zou Mozhong had come to draft these edicts for the emperor.","Soon, all three imperial edicts were drafted and presented to the emperor for review. Yuwen Lan looked them over and then ordered the Department of Imperial Ceremonies to go out and proclaim the edicts.","Zou Mozhong, however, did not take his leave. He hesitated, seeming to have something to say.","Yuwen Lan asked, \"Is there something else?\"","Zou Mozhong smiled and said, \"Just now, at the palace gate, I happened to see the manuscript Your Majesty bestowed upon Li Beauty. I wonder whose masterpiece it is?\"","Masterpiece?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"You saw it?\"","Zou Mozhong smiled, \"I only caught a glimpse, but I could see that the words and phrases were brilliant, certainly not an ordinary work.\"","Brilliant?","Yuwen Lan continued to raise his eyebrow, \"Does Scholar Zou truly think so?\"","Scholar Zou nodded firmly, \"I wouldn't dare speak falsely.\"","Ahem, the literary merit was secondary. He mainly felt that the story was quite different from the current popular novels, with a very unique style.","Moreover, this was personally bestowed by the emperor to his beloved consort. It must be a masterpiece to have caught the emperor's eye!","As a close minister to the emperor, he must closely follow His Majesty's tastes and not fall behind.","Yuwen Lan silently listened and then nodded, \"Scholar Zou indeed has good taste.\"","But then he heard the other say, \"So I dare to ask, might I have the honor of admiring this masterpiece?\"","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment, \"I need to get the author's consent first. Wait for news.\""]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25","paragraphs":["As night fell, Yanshu was still feeling heartbroken over the silver coins that had flown away during the day.","Fortunately, there was finally some meat for dinner. She ate half a chicken, a whole fish, and a pot of braised beef brisket in one go, which brought her some comfort.","After dinner, she went to bathe. When she returned to her room, she saw that the emperor had arrived at some point and was engrossed in reading her newly written novel at the desk.","She could only bow in her nightgown, \"This humble concubine greets Your Majesty.\"","In her heart, however, she scoffed. This man who had played deaf and dumb actually had the nerve to come here.","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched.","What did she mean by \"had the nerve to come here\"?","He had just been teasing her a little. Was her temper really so bad?","However, looking at her lowered eyes and pouting lips, he inexplicably felt a bit guilty. So he coughed and said, \"I have something I want to hear your opinion on.\"","Yanshu was a bit curious. She couldn't help but raise her eyelids to look at him and said, \"Please instruct me, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Someone has taken an interest in your novel and wants to publish it on the market. What do you think about that?\"","Yanshu was stunned for a moment. Publish? Did this mean someone wanted to help her publish her novel?","She immediately perked up, her almond eyes wide open. \"Really?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Would I lie to you about this?\"","Yanshu said, \"This concubine wouldn't dare to think so. But, but how could someone take an interest in this concubine's novel? Besides you, no one else has seen what I've written.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Today when I had someone deliver the manuscript to you, Zou Mozhong of the Hanlin Academy took a look. He thought it was quite good.\"","A scholar from the Hanlin Academy? Yanshu's eyes lit up. That was a person of great learning! For him to take an interest in her novel meant her skills must be quite high!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She certainly had an active imagination.","He continued, \"If you're willing, you can let him take a look first. He knows many book merchants, so publishing would be easy.\"","Yanshu nodded eagerly, \"I'm willing, I'm willing! This concubine wrote it hoping people would read it, of course I'm willing.\"","Ah, her sleepless nights and forgotten meals hadn't been in vain. Finally, someone would see her work!","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"That's good then. I'll take the manuscript to Zou Mozhong tomorrow.\"","\"Thank you for Your Majesty's great kindness!\"","Yanshu asked again, \"Should this concubine choose a pen name? I can't use my real name, right?\"","Tch, she had written mostly about the gossip of court officials. It wouldn't be good if the people involved saw it and came to settle accounts with her.","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"That's fine. What pen name do you want to use?\"","Yanshu pondered deeply for a while, then said, \"How about 'Carefree Gentleman'?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...That name sounds like a man's.\"","Yanshu said wisely, \"That's the point. Nowadays, people generally believe that 'a woman with no talent is virtuous'. If they knew this novel was written by a woman, they would be prejudiced and think it wasn't well-written.\"","It seemed to make sense, so Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"Then we'll go with that.\"","He looked her over again and said, \"Get into bed quickly, or you'll catch a cold.\"","\"Yes.\"","Contrary to her previous listlessness, Yanshu now actively came forward to help him undress, and even crawled to the inside of the bed to pull up the covers for him, being the epitome of gentle and attentive.","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. Publishing a novel had made the sun rise from the west?","Of course, seeing her like this also made him happy. So he pulled her into his arms, feeling the smoothness of her nightgown with his palm, and asked, \"Are you this happy?\"","Yanshu tried hard to suppress a wave of goosebumps and smiled, \"This concubine is indeed very happy. By the way, Your Majesty, which stories will be published first?\"","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment and said, \"That story about the scholar and the courtesan is good, it warns people to keep their promises. The beautiful young wife... is also decent. Let's start with these two.\"","Yanshu quickly agreed, then tried to promote another, \"The 'Hot-Blooded General and the Charming Widow' is also quite good. Why don't we publish that one too?\"","Hot-Blooded General and the Charming Widow...","Wasn't that the sensual one?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow at her, \"What's the significance of that story?\"","Yanshu said righteously, \"That story encourages people not to give up because of temporary circumstances, but to bravely pursue true love!\"","Yuwen Lan was amused and raised an eyebrow to ask, \"How can you see all that in it?\"","She tried hard to make it sound better, \"The young widow didn't feel inferior because she had been married before. When she met the general, she bravely se... I mean, bravely pursued him. In the end, she married the general, had three children, and finally had a perfect life with a loving husband. Isn't that very meaningful?\"","Yuwen Lan chuckled again, \"You certainly make it sound that way.\"","Yanshu looked at him expectantly, \"So, does Your Majesty think it's acceptable?\"","\"No,\" he flatly refused.","Yanshu was stunned, \"Why not?\"","Yuwen Lan coughed, \"It's written too explicitly. I'm afraid it might have a bad influence on people.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","How could this have a bad influence? The readers of novels are all adults! And she didn't write it explicitly at all. Compared to \"The Plum in the Golden Vase\", hers was much more innocent!","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","She even knew about \"The Plum in the Golden Vase\"?","But thinking about it, of course she would. How else could she have written the \"Charming Widow\"?","Recalling the sentences he had read that night, he couldn't help but want to squeeze and pinch her...","But just at this moment, he heard her muttering in her heart, [Tch, such an amateur! This is what makes money! Missing out on a chance to get rich, could he be stupid?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Before he could say anything, he heard her think again, [But let's focus on the present and get these two books out first. Tch, finally someone will read what I've written, hahaha!!!]","[And the best part is that the emperor made the connection. So if anyone causes trouble in the future, I can just push it onto the emperor!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","So he had become her scapegoat?","He finally couldn't help but pinch her waist and said, \"Don't you think you should thank me?\"","Thank him?","Yanshu was stunned, thinking how she should thank him. Should she give him a share of the manuscript fee?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","[That's impossible, he doesn't lack money! Or does he want me to offer myself to him? Tch, that wouldn't be of any use anyway...]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","The dignity of the monarch was trampled once again. He frowned and pulled her tightly into his arms.","Yanshu was startled, but seeing his displeased expression, she hurriedly said, \"Your Majesty's kindness is vast, this concubine is indeed extremely grateful. But Your Majesty owns the wealth of the entire country, this concubine doesn't know how to repay you.\"","Yuwen Lan snorted and looked down at her, \"I want you to be sincere to me.\"","Sincere...","Yanshu became wary. What did he mean?","Had he noticed that she had been too careless recently?","Tch, this wasn't good!","She knew that once she became his target, there was no possibility of escaping that role.","If her golden thigh became dissatisfied and kicked her away, her fate would certainly be miserable.","So, she had to firmly hold onto the emperor, her golden thigh!","Yes, be more sincere!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Then, he saw her try hard to smile and say, \"This concubine wouldn't dare to have any other thoughts about Your Majesty. I will certainly serve you faithfully before and behind... no, I mean, I will be loyal and devoted, sincere and unwavering. This concubine's heart only has Your Majesty in it!\"","As she spoke, her almond eyes sparkled, trying to move him.","Yuwen Lan didn't believe her at all.","In her heart, there was money and food, but not him. Huh.","But for now, he indeed couldn't do anything to her.","Tch, sometimes being able to read minds wasn't necessarily a good thing.","He looked at her coldly and pulled her closer into his arms, saying, \"Go to sleep.\"","Then he closed his eyes.","Yanshu responded with a \"yes\" and felt slightly relieved.","But...","Why was his hand on her chest?","And he wasn't moving it away.","Was he planning to leave it there all night?","How did he develop this habit after not sleeping together for a few days?","She really wanted to move his hand away, but she still needed to hold onto her golden thigh, so she had to endure it and closed her eyes as well.","Ah, making a living wasn't easy!","The person who had been silently listening: \"???\"","The night passed, and as dawn broke, Yuwen Lan naturally woke up.","He hurriedly checked and indeed saw the change in that place again.","His heart settled. It seemed this matter could only be resolved with her.","Just as he was thinking this, he saw Yanshu open her eyes as well.","She asked him, \"Oh, is Your Majesty getting up?\"","Her voice still had a thick nasal tone.","Yuwen Lan made an \"mm\" sound, \"There's a morning court session today.\"","He was about to get out of bed.","Little did he know that the young lady's movements were even faster than his. In a flash, she leapt out of bed and ran to the clothes rack to fetch his court robes, saying, \"Let this humble servant help Your Majesty dress.\"","Yuwen Lan was somewhat surprised and looked her over, asking, \"You're not going back to sleep?\"","He saw her straining to smile as she replied, \"This servant used to wake up too late. From now on, I will certainly rise early with Your Majesty.\"","She then called out towards the door, \"Rendong, Lianxin, quickly bring in water!\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, thinking to himself that she had indeed developed a sense of crisis and was being so attentive.","He didn't say anything and allowed her to help him dress and wash up, feeling somewhat amused.","After finishing these tasks, he saw her smiling and asking, \"Would Your Majesty like to have breakfast here?\"","He replied, \"No need. There's a court session this morning. I'll eat at Qianming Palace later.\"","Yanshu acknowledged this and escorted him to the door. She then took out the two manuscripts they had finalized yesterday and respectfully said, \"Please trouble Your Majesty to give these to Lord Zou.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and reached out to take them. Suddenly he said, \"You...\"","Yanshu immediately lowered her head obediently, in a posture of attentive listening.","However, Yuwen Lan didn't continue speaking. He only said, \"Go back inside. It's cold out here.\" Then he boarded the imperial palanquin.","After the morning court session, the emperor handed the manuscripts to Zou Mozhong.","The scholar excitedly accepted them and immediately began reading them in the imperial study.","As he read with great interest, he couldn't help but exclaim, \"This story of 'The Dashing Scholar and the Beautiful Lady' is truly intricate and surprising. I never expected this courtesan to be so loyal and righteous. Although she misjudged people at first, she was able to make a comeback later on. Her resilience and self-improvement are truly admirable!\"","When he got to \"The Charming Wife,\" he shook his head repeatedly, \"This Xia Shi is simply morally corrupt! Once married, one should be devoted. How could she be so fickle? Her husband is truly pitiful. I fear even the child might not be his own!\"","Yuwen Lan asked, \"What does Lord Zou think of the writing?\"","Zou Mozhong quickly nodded, \"It's written very well. Ordinary novels rarely focus so much on female characters. This writing is truly a breath of fresh air. I imagine this 'Carefree Gentleman' must be a person of great talent.\"","[Ahem, it's just that the handwriting is really not that good... Perhaps this is the unique charm that attracts His Majesty?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","But this was also true. Yanshu's handwriting was indeed not very good, barely legible. She probably hadn't practiced calligraphy properly before.","He asked again, \"So do you think people would like to read these if they were published?\"","Zou Mozhong was stunned for a moment, \"Your Majesty means to say these two stories haven't been published yet? I thought they were already well-known works. No wonder they're so novel!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He said, \"Indeed, they haven't been published yet. How about this - you take them to find a publisher to print them.\"","Zou Mozhong's eyes lit up, and he immediately replied, \"I obey Your Majesty's command. It is my honor to be able to recommend such an excellent work to the public in my lifetime.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...Then you may go.\"","Ahem, if he let him stay any longer, who knows what other praises he might come up with.","He was already feeling embarrassed listening to it.","Zou Mozhong thus took his leave, but before he could step out the door, he heard the emperor add, \"By the way, this 'Carefree Gentleman' is very concerned about income. If there are any profits, remember to bring them back promptly. I will pass them on to her.\"","Zou Mozhong paused, then quickly acknowledged.","In his heart, he marveled, [So it turns out to be a talented scholar from a poor family. How admirable!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Where is she poor?","As evening approached, officials were still coming and going in the imperial study where lamps had been lit.","Xiao Shunzi also quietly entered the hall and whispered something in Fu Hai's ear.","Yuwen Lan caught a glimpse of this and asked, \"What's the matter?\"","Fu Hai immediately reported, \"Your Majesty, Li Beauty has sent someone to ask if you will be going over for dinner tonight?\"","Hmm?","At these words, all the officials in the hall paused and began exchanging glances—","This was unprecedented! A consort actually inquiring if His Majesty wanted to have dinner?","It seems Li Beauty is indeed favored!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He just thought that the girl probably wanted to taste the imperial cuisine again.","If he refused, she would be very disappointed, wouldn't she?","Feeling somewhat reluctant, he thus said, \"I'll go over in a while. Tell the Imperial Kitchen to prepare.\"","Xiao Shunzi acknowledged and hurried out to relay the message.","Next, Yuwen Lan quickly dealt with the matters at hand and instructed several officials, \"It's getting late. You should all go home for dinner.\"","Everyone acknowledged this, and as they took their leave, they all marveled inwardly, [After all, someone is waiting for dinner. His Majesty can't even sit still.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","When did he become unable to sit still?","Thus, by the time he arrived at Ganlu Palace, dinner was already laid out on the table.","Yanshu led a group of palace maids in greeting, \"This humble servant welcomes Your Majesty.\"","Her posture was perfectly correct, her face beaming like a flower, and her voice as sweet as honey.","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. Such enthusiasm - it seems today's dishes must be very much to her liking?","He said \"Rise\" and came to the table, only to see common dishes like crispy fish fillets, braised ox tendon, scallion-braised sea cucumber, and cherry pork.","—A few days ago, he had issued an edict to strictly investigate corruption in the court and to clean up the palace customs as well. As a result, the imperial meals had become much simpler compared to before.","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but wonder, do these dishes make her so happy?","But he saw Yanshu following him, smiling as she said, \"This servant inquired with Lord Fu earlier. These are all dishes Your Majesty enjoys, aren't they?\"","Yuwen Lan was somewhat surprised. Were these really his favorites?","But he heard her thinking proudly, [How about that? Aren't I virtuous? Now I can prove that I care about you, right?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He finally understood. It was still because of what he said last night. She was trying hard to \"please him.\"","He made a sound of acknowledgment, both helpless and amused, and said, \"Let's eat.\"","Then he picked up his chopsticks.","But he saw that she hadn't sat down. Instead, she stood beside him with chopsticks in hand and said, \"This servant will serve the dishes for Your Majesty.\"","\"What would Your Majesty like to eat... Let's try these fish fillets first. The color is so golden, you can tell at a glance that they're cooked just right. They must be very crispy.\"","Saying this, she picked up a piece of crispy fish fillet with her chopsticks and placed it in his bowl.","Yuwen Lan obligingly picked it up and put it in his mouth. As soon as he bit down, a crisp sound burst between his lips and teeth.","Right after, he heard her thinking, [It must be very delicious, right? I wonder if it will still be crispy when it's my turn to eat QAQ.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","After he finished the fish fillet, Yanshu extended her chopsticks towards the scallion-braised sea cucumber, \"Your Majesty, please try this sea cucumber. The scallion fragrance smells rich. It should be quite good.\"","Yuwen Lan took a bite of the sea cucumber, and before he could swallow, he heard her thinking, [How is it? It must be tender and chewy, right? Don't eat it all, leave some for me.]","She sounded like she was already salivating.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He nodded slightly, \"Not bad.\"","Then he saw her place a piece of ox tendon in his dish, smiling gently as she said, \"This ox tendon is cooked to perfection. It must melt in your mouth. Your Majesty, please try it.\"","Yuwen Lan said alright and tasted the ox tendon while listening to her inner exclamation, \"Look at all that collagen in one bite, it must be especially delicious! Waa waa remember to mix the sauce with rice, that's the essence!\"","She seemed to be on the verge of tears.","[And this beef soup, look how well it's been simmered, you must drink it while it's hot...]","Before he could pick up the soup spoon, he heard her think, [I haven't even had a chance to eat myself, serving you dishes first. You're the first to enjoy this treatment! I'm being so good to you! Wuwu leave some for me, don't eat it all!!!]","\"...\"","How could he continue eating like this?","So he simply said, \"You sit down and eat too. No need to serve the dishes anymore.\"","But he saw her still feigning modesty, \"No need, this servant will attend to Your Majesty's meal.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"If you wait any longer, I'm afraid these fish fillets won't be crispy anymore.\"","She hurriedly curtsied and said, \"This servant thanks Your Majesty.\"","Then she immediately sat down beside him and picked up her chopsticks to start eating.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Yanshu hurriedly tasted a piece of crispy fish fillet first. Fortunately, the outer layer was still crispy, while the inside was soft and tender, wrapped in the savory sauce from the outside. It was truly delicious.","The scallion-braised sea cucumber was also excellent, soft and smooth with a rich scallion flavor that was exquisite.","She finally got to eat the ox tendon! It really did melt in her mouth, with a sticky collagen texture between her lips and teeth, and it was very flavorful - truly a perfect dish to eat with rice.","Then a bowl of hot beef soup, salty, savory, and rich, made all her internal organs feel comfortable.","As she ate, she mused to herself that it was indeed more comfortable to sit and eat, and that serving others was no easy task.","Yuwen Lan listened silently, thinking to himself that he also found it more comfortable to eat this way.","Finally, when the meal was finished, Yanshu remembered an urgent matter and hurriedly asked, \"Your Majesty, what about the story book? When will people be able to see it?\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"As early as tomorrow.\"","In fact, from what he knew, it had already been circulating among the ministers today.","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she immediately became excited, \"As expected, Your Majesty is indeed capable! I've heard before that it's not easy to publish story books, and those book merchants all look at the author's reputation. If you don't have a reputation, no one will pay attention to you.\"","Yuwen Lan gave a sound of acknowledgment, accepting her compliment.","He then heard her thinking to herself, [Clinging to a powerful patron really works, I must continue.]","He couldn't help but be curious about how she planned to continue her efforts.","Soon after, dinner was finally over, and the palace servants cleared away the dishes. Yanshu coughed and said to Yuwen Lan, \"It's still early, why don't I accompany Your Majesty in playing a game to aid digestion? How about arrow throwing?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow at her, \"Want to win money again? This time I won't lose so easily.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Indeed, he was too skilled at arrow throwing.","Last time she had won by luck, but this time it would be much more difficult to win again.","Tsk, it's no fun to keep losing. So she rolled her eyes and said, \"Oh right, today is the palace lantern lighting ceremony. Why don't I accompany Your Majesty to see the lanterns?\"","See the lanterns?","Yuwen Lan was actually not very interested.","He had grown up in the palace and had seen those palace lanterns for many years.","But he heard her pleading in her mind, [Please go! In the past, I didn't dare to go out easily even when I wanted to see them. This time, with you leading the way, we can go!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Why did she make it sound so pitiful, not daring to even see the lanterns?","His heart softened, and he nodded, \"Alright, let's see if there are any new designs this year.\"","He then stood up.","Yanshu was overjoyed and quickly helped him put on his brocade robe. She also put on her cloak, and they went out together.","It was warm in the palace hall, and since they hadn't gone out much today, Yanshu only realized how cold it actually was when they stepped outside. The wind was strong too!","The cold wind felt like knives cutting the face, and even taking a deep breath hurt the lungs.","Seeing Yanshu shrink entirely into her cloak, her little face immediately turning red from the cold, Yuwen Lan was about to ask if she wanted to go back.","But he heard her thinking, [Tsk tsk, this wind is so cold, it's just like the day Zhang Shengkang's master died of anger!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Zhang Shengkang?","Isn't that the Head of the Imperial Medical Academy?","Why did she say his master died of anger?","What was this situation?","He heard her sigh again, [Poor divine doctor, saved countless lives but couldn't see through human nature, took in such an ungrateful disciple, passed on his lifelong skills to him, and in the end was driven out of the capital!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Could there really be such a thing? This was the first time he had heard of it.","Before he could come to his senses, he heard her mumble again, [Tsk tsk, if that old man was still around, he might be able to cure the emperor's illness! I heard he had a set of acupuncture techniques that were very powerful, specifically for treating infertility.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Is, is that true?","He carefully recalled that he seemed to have indeed heard of a divine doctor in the capital before, but later his whereabouts became unknown.","He had sent people to search for him earlier, but to no avail.","Could it be Zhang Shengkang's master?","\"Oh, Your Majesty, look, isn't that the Eight Immortals Crossing the Sea lantern?\" Yanshu suddenly pointed to a lantern under the eaves.","Yuwen Lan composed himself inconspicuously, glanced at the lantern, and said, \"It's all old designs, we've had them before.\"","Yanshu, however, said, \"This is the first time I've seen it!\"","She ran to the lantern and examined it carefully for a while.","After she had looked enough, they moved on. Not long after, she exclaimed again, \"This flower basket lantern is so well made, the peonies inside look real!\"","Yuwen Lan looked at it and casually said, \"Indeed.\"","But it was also an old design, and especially now that he had something on his mind, he had no interest in appreciating them.","After a few steps, he saw her excitedly go under another lantern, \"Your Majesty, look quick, isn't this a revolving lantern? It's really turning, how amazing!\"","Yuwen Lan found it amusing, \"You've never seen a revolving lantern?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"In a small place like Ande, no one could make such lanterns. I remember when I was little, once the county magistrate's daughter got one from somewhere else, I wanted to get a closer look but she wouldn't let me.\"","These words sounded truly pitiful. Yuwen Lan instructed Fu Hai, \"Take down this lantern and give it to Li Beauty.\"","Fu Hai quickly agreed and immediately called for people to bring a ladder to take down the lantern.","Yanshu was stunned.","Holding the revolving lantern that had just been taken down from the eaves, she asked in disbelief, \"This lantern is for me?\"","Wasn't it said that once these lanterns were hung up today, they couldn't be taken down at will until after the Lantern Festival?","But Yuwen Lan smiled and said, \"Consider it a reward for your attentive service to me today.\"","Oh, is that so?","Yanshu slowly thanked the Emperor, a complex feeling welling up in her heart.","It was as if...","She was being doted on.","She could have whatever she wanted.","Yuwen Lan coughed quietly to himself. If all her wishes were as simple as this lantern, there was no harm in giving them to her.","But then he heard her muse in her mind, [So efforts really do pay off. It wasn't in vain that I got up early to help him dress, endured hunger to serve dishes. It really had a good effect!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She seemed to have misunderstood.","Early the next morning, Yuwen Lan returned to Qianming Palace and immediately sent someone to investigate Zhang Shengkang, the Head of the Imperial Medical Academy.","—If what Yanshu said was true, and Zhang Shengkang was indeed the divine doctor's disciple, then perhaps by starting with Zhang Shengkang, they could find traces of the divine doctor from back then.","He couldn't let Zhang Shengkang treat him, but perhaps the divine doctor had other disciples.","After a busy day, by evening, he heard a report from the Imperial Guard that Yanshu's story book had started being hand-copied and printed since yesterday. Many court officials had already read it, and everyone was praising the intricate and surprising plot. The response was intense.","Yuwen Lan asked, \"Has there been anything unusual at the Linwu Marquis's mansion recently?\"","The Imperial Guard reported, \"The Linwu Marquis has suddenly started investigating the servants in his household, especially the maids who used to serve the former lady. Besides this, he has also sent people out of the mansion to Jiangnan, for unknown reasons.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded.","It seemed that in a few days, this pitiful man would know that the heir was not his own.","Tsk, as the emperor, he couldn't interfere too much. He could only help to this extent.","He asked the Imperial Guard again, \"What about Wei Ruzhang? Any unusual movements?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"It's strange to say, but Wei Daren has suddenly started investigating the source of the story book. He seems quite nervous.\"","He should be nervous.","Yuwen Lan gave a cold smile and said, \"Continue to keep an eye on them.\"","The Imperial Guard agreed.","Meanwhile, Yanshu, who was eating snacks in Ganlu Palace, suddenly received new gossip, [The Linwu Marquis has already realized that his son is not his own, and has started investigating the whereabouts of that rich merchant from back then.]","Yanshu: [!!! How did he find out?]","System: [He read your story book.]","Yanshu: [???]","To be honest, she had indeed considered this consequence, but she didn't expect it to be so immediate.","But anyway, helping one person is better than none. It's better to know now than to be deceived into raising someone else's son for a lifetime.","So next, she was waiting for her author's fees. Hehe, this was her first income in life, just thinking about it made her excited.","Two days later, the author's fees indeed arrived.","Twenty taels of silver for two stories, and this was just the initial payment. It was said that if the story book sold well in the future, she would continue to receive royalties.","Of course, for people like Empress Zhou and Consort Ning, these twenty taels were not even enough to fill a tooth gap, but Yanshu was very satisfied.","—This was the first sum of money she had earned with her own hands. If two stories were worth twenty taels, wouldn't ten stories be a hundred taels?","Hehe, with all the gossip in her head, writing a thousand or two thousand stories wouldn't be a problem. Even if one day she was no longer a consort, she could still make a living by just moving her pen a bit. How reassuring.","And most importantly, she had readers now!","Finally, there were people to share her gossip with!","Heaven knows how hard it was for her to keep it all to herself before. Now that she had readers to share the gossip with, even if they couldn't communicate face to face, it was still exciting!","Yanshu happily counted her money while brewing ideas for five or six more books.","But before she finished counting, she heard the system say, \"New gossip, the book merchant who published your story book has disappeared.\"","Yanshu: [??? The book merchant disappeared? What's going on?]","System: [His wife reported to the Capital Official this morning that her husband was abducted on his way home last night, and his whereabouts are unknown.]","Yanshu: [What? Abducted on his way home? Is the security in the capital so poor? Is that bookseller very rich? Does wealth attract trouble?]","System: [It's not about money, it's somewhat related to you.]","Yanshu: [Related to me?]","She thought for a moment, [Could it be that other booksellers saw my novels selling too well and deliberately retaliated against him?]","System: [...You're overthinking it. This bookseller has some background among the booksellers in the capital, ordinary people wouldn't dare to touch him.]","Yanshu was full of questions, [Then what's going on, why is it related to me?]","As she was thinking this, she suddenly paused, [Could it be the Linwu Marquis or Wei Ruzhang?]","Hmm, but thinking about it further, the Linwu Marquis wouldn't stoop so low.","But that old man Wei...","System: [Correct, old man Wei saw his story spreading all over the streets in novels, became furious, wanted to find out who wrote the novels, but couldn't find out immediately, so he kidnapped that bookseller and is planning to torture him severely these days.]","Yanshu immediately became angry, [This old man is lawless now? Has the Capital Official found him yet?]","System: [You think the Capital Official has a system like me? They just received the case this morning and are planning to send people to search now. It's not certain if they can find him.]","This won't do!","Yanshu became anxious.","How could an ordinary person withstand severe torture for days?","Moreover, this bookseller was her business partner, and she still had other novels to publish in the future!","What if Wei killed him?","So she thought for a moment and quickly asked Rendong, \"Are there any nourishing herbs or the like in the palace?\"","Rendong said, \"Yes, Eunuch Fu sent some when you had a fever last time, they're still here.\"","\"Then bring them out,\" Yanshu said, \"And go to the Imperial Kitchen to get a chicken or some bones, I'll make a pot of soup.\"","\"Huh?\" Rendong was stunned. The mistress who had never cooked before wanted to make soup?","But seeing Yanshu urge her, \"Hurry up! I need it urgently.\"","So Rendong didn't dare to ask more and hurried to the Imperial Kitchen to get the ingredients.","Half an hour later, Yuwen Lan, who was reading memorials in the Imperial Study, heard Fu Hai report, \"Your Majesty, Li Beauty has brought you some soup.\"","Soup?","Yuwen Lan was indeed surprised.","It was still morning, why was she bringing soup out of the blue?","Since there was nothing urgent at the moment, he said, \"Let her in.\"","Fu Hai complied and went to invite her in from outside.","Sure enough, Yanshu came in carrying a soup pot.","\"Greetings to Your Majesty,\" she said with a forced smile on her small face, \"I was afraid you might be tired from reading memorials, so I specially made an invigorating soup for you to drink.\"","Yuwen Lan hadn't yet figured out what she was up to, but he nodded and said, \"Thank you for your trouble.\"","Yanshu quickly demurred, \"It's no trouble at all for me.\" She then placed the soup pot in front of him.","However, when the lid was lifted, both of them were stunned.","The soup inside was black and oily, and the meat was barely visible.","Yanshu: [...]","Oh no, she was in such a hurry when she left that she didn't look closely, how did it turn out this color?","Yuwen Lan frowned and asked, \"What is this?\"","Although he didn't care much about food, this was too strange.","It was hard not to suspect if it was poisoned.","Yanshu forced herself to say, \"It's rehmannia and angelica root stewed with pork ribs. I heard it's good for nourishing the kidneys and invigorating energy, best to drink in winter.\"","Yuwen Lan: [...]","Alright, he of course knew she had come to ask him for something, so he pushed the soup pot aside and asked directly, \"Do you have something to ask of me?\"","\"No, no,\" she said with a smile, \"Actually, I received the payment for my novel this morning, so I wanted to come and thank Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan thought, coming to say thanks for twenty taels of silver?","This doesn't seem like her style.","Then he heard her thinking to herself, [Think, how should I bring up that the bookseller has been kidnapped?]","Yuwen Lan then understood that it was about the bookseller's matter.","However... he had only just received the news, how did she know so quickly?","Just then, Yanshu coughed and said, \"It's just... I wrote a new story yesterday, and I was wondering if Your Majesty could help ask that bookseller if he's still willing to publish it?\"","Yuwen Lan said calmly, \"As it happens, I just received news that the person has gone missing.\"","-- Let's see what else she knows.","But he saw her look surprised and say, \"Missing? How could he just go missing? Did something happen to him?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of assent and said, \"His family has already reported to the Capital Official, and I hear the Capital Official has sent people to search for him.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he heard her cry out in her mind, [What use is that? The Capital Official doesn't know anything! Just searching isn't enough, the person was captured by that damned Grand Scholar!]","Yuwen Lan: ???","She even knows the culprit is Wei Ruzhang?","Then he saw her nod and say, \"That's good then, I hope the Capital Official finds him quickly, and nothing bad happens to him.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't show any sign of suspicion, only asked her, \"You're so concerned about someone you've never met?\"","Yanshu said, \"After all, he's my bookseller. The fact that he can publish my novels shows he has good judgment and must be a talented person.\"","[Of course I'm anxious! I'm still waiting to continue publishing picture books to make money!!!]","She continued, \"By the way, Your Majesty, don't you think it's strange that this person suddenly disappeared right after publishing my novel? Could it be related to me?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and said, \"How so?\"","As he spoke, he stared at her intently, waiting for both her words and her thoughts.","Perhaps now he could finally find out how she knew all these things.","Yanshu pretended to ponder and said, \"Perhaps my novel was too well-received, and someone who read the story saw themselves in it and actually wants to take revenge on me, the author, so they captured the bookseller to find out my identity.\"","Yuwen Lan probed further, \"Then who do you think it might be?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, who else could it be but your Grand Scholar Wei Ruzhang?","But outwardly she respectfully said, \"I dare not speculate rashly, otherwise if I wrongly accuse someone that would be terrible. I believe the court is full of talented people who will surely solve the case.\"","[Damn it, I've tried my best, I can't just directly tell you the person was captured by Wei Ruzhang's men and taken to the retired farmstead at the foot of Great Green Mountain in the suburbs.]","Yuwen Lan: ???"]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan was truly surprised that Yanshu even knew where Wei Ruzhang was hiding someone. After all, the Imperial Guard hadn't even reported to him yet...","Just as he was shocked, he heard Fu Hai at the door say, \"Your Majesty, the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial requests an audience.\"","Immediately after, Yanshu said, \"Then I won't disturb Your Majesty any longer. I'll take my leave.\"","As she spoke, she glanced at the stewing pot on the table and smiled awkwardly, saying, \"I'll make another pot for you to drink in the evening.\"","Tsk, looking at the blackish color, it's better not to poison the emperor.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Although he was still puzzled, he couldn't think of how to ask her at the moment.","He could only nod slightly, watching her leave with the pot of soup.","Shortly after, the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial came in to report, \"Your Majesty, the King of Liaodong has arrived in the capital and is expected to enter the city tomorrow. The welcoming banquet is set for tomorrow evening. What does Your Majesty think?\"","Yuwen Lan had other things on his mind at the moment and only casually replied, \"Very well.\"","The Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial then took his leave.","The room fell quiet. Yuwen Lan thought for a moment, then summoned the Imperial Guard and asked, \"Have you found out where Wei Ruzhang is holding the person?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"We just received news that it should be at the retired farmstead of Wei Manor at the foot of Great Green Mountain in the outskirts of the capital.\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","She had guessed correctly again.","If the previous incidents were old stories from years ago, there was a possibility she had heard them from somewhere else. But this one had just happened.","Could it be... that she had some extraordinary ability?","As he was pondering, he heard the Imperial Guard ask beside him, \"Your Majesty, should we go rescue the person now?\"","Yuwen Lan snapped back to reality and said, \"Make preparations first. We'll act when Wei Ruzhang appears.\"","After all, to catch a thief, you must catch them red-handed. There must be solid evidence to convince everyone.","The Imperial Guard acknowledged the order.","In the afternoon, a carriage drove into the retired farmstead at the foot of Great Green Mountain on the outskirts of the capital.","Wei Ruzhang, Grand Secretary of the Wenhua Court, wore a cloak covering half his face. Led by a servant, he entered a dark shed inside the estate.","At this time, a person was kneeling on the ground in the room with his hands tied behind his back and eyes covered with a black cloth. It was none other than the missing bookseller.","Hearing movement, he immediately said in panic, \"I have no grudge against you, sir. Why have you captured me? If you want money, I can have my family send it. Or if you want the bookstore, I can offer it to you. I only beg you not to harm my life. I have elderly parents and young children at home. Please have mercy!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he heard someone say fiercely, \"So much nonsense! Do you think our master lacks your little bit of money?\"","The bookseller was startled and said with a sob, \"Then what do you want?\"","He heard a voice say, \"This old man only wants to know who that 'Carefree Gentleman' who writes novels really is.\"","The bookseller cried, \"I don't know either!\"","\"You don't know?\" The other person sneered, \"Wasn't that novel published by your bookstore?\"","The bookseller said helplessly, \"It was indeed published by my bookstore, but I've never met that 'Carefree Gentleman.' Both novels were brought by an official from the Hanlin Academy. He said he was publishing them for someone else. As for that 'Carefree Gentleman,' none of us have ever seen him...\"","Hanlin Academy?","Wei Ruzhang narrowed his eyes.","Although he had also come from the Hanlin Academy years ago, not only did no one know about his past affairs back then, but now the Hanlin Academy was full of young people who couldn't possibly know about things from fifty or sixty years ago.","He lowered his voice and said, \"It seems you're still not telling the truth. Then let's start the torture.\"","The servant acknowledged and immediately brought a set of torture instruments to put on the bookseller's hands.","In an instant, screams echoed through the shed.","A cold smile appeared on Wei Ruzhang's deeply wrinkled face.","— First there were novels, who knows if someone would come out next to testify about his past frequenting brothels?","He had been a Grand Secretary for so many years; he absolutely couldn't let a novel writer ruin his reputation!","No matter who it was, he definitely wouldn't let them off.","But just then, the door was suddenly kicked open.","Someone said coldly, \"What is Grand Secretary Wei doing? Kidnapping a civilian and using torture to extract a confession?\"","Wei Ruzhang was stunned. He saw that more than ten burly men had suddenly appeared at the door, all wearing uniforms with fish embroidery and carrying swords at their waists.","This... this is the Imperial Guard?","He suddenly panicked — they were the emperor's men!","Early the next morning, news spread throughout the court that Wei Ruzhang, Grand Secretary of the Wenhua Court, had kidnapped a civilian and used torture to extract a confession.","The entire court was shocked.","Who could have imagined that the usually gentle and elegant Grand Secretary would do such a thing?","Only Yanshu calmly continued writing her novel.","— Good, that bookseller had safely returned home, and she could continue selling her novels.","But before she could write more than a few words, she saw Yuwen Lan arrive.","Yanshu hurriedly paid her respects, but found it strange in her heart — at this hour, this workaholic should be in the study managing state affairs, how did he have time to come see her?","Yuwen Lan heard her thoughts and took the initiative to answer her doubts, \"I came to tell you that the bookseller has been found and has safely returned home.\"","Yanshu hurriedly put on a delighted expression, \"Really? That's wonderful! Your Majesty is indeed wise and mighty, finding the person in just one day.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Very well acted.","He looked at her and deliberately said, \"He was captured by the Grand Secretary of the Wenhua Court.\"","Yanshu also pretended to be surprised, \"Heavens! Why would the Grand Secretary do such a thing?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Her heart didn't even skip a beat and her face didn't change color?","He continued looking at her and said, \"Didn't you say yesterday that someone took it personally?\"","Seeing her ponder for a moment, she suddenly opened her mouth wide and said, \"Could it be that the Grand Secretary did those despicable things I wrote about in my novel when he was young?\"","\"People really can't be judged by appearances! What a coincidence!\"","In her heart, she thought, [Tsk tsk, now you know what kind of person your Grand Secretary is! This old bastard is full of evil schemes. He deserves to lose face in his old age and be despised by everyone!]","Yuwen Lan silently listened, then nodded and said, \"It is indeed quite a coincidence. I almost thought you knew about his affairs.\"","Yanshu was stunned for a moment, then quickly smiled and said, \"Your Majesty is joking. I grew up in Ande and then entered the palace. I've never met this Grand Secretary, how could I know about his affairs? But it is indeed a great coincidence.\"","In her heart, she thought, [It seems I'll have to be more careful in the future, or I might scare the emperor!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He couldn't get anything out of her at all?","He sighed, half-truthfully and half-falsely, \"I also found it strange. I thought you had some magical ability.\"","Yanshu quickly laughed and said, \"Your Majesty overestimates me.\"","Ahem, she didn't have any special abilities, she just had a belly full of gossip.","But the gossip wasn't wasted. It accidentally caused the bad guy to finally face retribution.","It seems these novels have quite a social function.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What's with \"eating melons\" again?","What exactly is this \"melon\"?","Could it be... that she knows magic? Is this \"melon\" some kind of magical treasure?","But he had come here so many times and never discovered anything special in this palace.","At this moment, Yanshu, completely unaware of his thoughts, was pondering in her mind —","[What should I write about in the next novel? How about writing about Duke Cheng'en's womanizing ways, finding his fifth, sixth, seventh, and eighth mistresses?]","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched.","No matter what, that was the Empress Dowager's brother. If anything happened, it would definitely affect the Empress Dowager's face.","Then he heard her think, [No, no, Duke Cheng'en is the emperor's uncle in name. Besides, there's still the Empress Dowager in the palace. If the Empress Dowager found out I exposed her brother's scandals, wouldn't she have me killed? Forget it, forget it.]","Yuwen Lan secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","Fortunately, she still knew the gravity of the situation.","Then he heard her think, [How about writing about the Minister of Rites' incest scandal?]","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly to himself. This could work.","After all, he also wanted to know what exactly this was about, ahem.","However, at this moment, Fu Hai came to report from outside the hall, \"Your Majesty, the King of Liaodong has entered the palace.\"","He paused for a moment, then had to say to Yanshu, \"I'll return to Qianming Palace first. You can continue writing.\"","With that, he stood up.","Yanshu acknowledged and hurriedly stood up to see him off.","Watching his figure disappear into the distance, she couldn't help but wonder, who is this King of Liaodong?","He sounds quite important, the emperor left as soon as he arrived.","The system immediately provided her with answers to her questions: [Yuwen Hao, the King of Liaodong, is the emperor's cousin. Years ago, the emperor's grandfather, Emperor Zhenglong, had five sons. He later passed the throne to the emperor's father, Emperor Qinglong, while the other four princes were enfeoffed as vassal kings.]","[Later, when these vassal kings died and their sons inherited their titles, Emperor Qinglong took the opportunity to demote them to commandery princes. Although they were greatly dissatisfied, they could only endure it silently.]","[After Emperor Qinglong passed away, several of them seized the opportunity to cause trouble, all hoping to compete for the throne. Of course, they were all eventually defeated by the emperor, who then either confined them or ordered their deaths.]","[Yuwen Hao, the King of Liaodong, was the only one who didn't rebel at the time, so the emperor holds him in high regard.]","Yanshu understood and nodded, [I see.]","The system said, [Hey, there's some juicy gossip about the King of Liaodong.]","Yanshu eagerly replied, [Tell me, tell me quickly.]","...","On the day the King of Liaodong arrived in the capital, he first paid his respects to the emperor. The next morning, his wife, the Princess of Liaodong, brought their children to the palace to pay respects to the Empress Dowager.","As a matter of etiquette, Yanshu and the other consorts were all present at the Palace of Benevolent Peace to accompany them.","The Princess of Liaodong, Madam Xiao, appeared to be about twenty-five or twenty-six years old, with a plump face. Her three sons, the eldest about eight or nine, the second about six or seven, looked sturdy and were well-mannered.","Only the four-year-old youngest son seemed small and thin, and very shy. When paying respects to the Empress Dowager, he was timid, and after staying in the hall for just a short while, he began to cry, making a fuss about wanting to go home.","The Princess of Liaodong, looking embarrassed, apologized to the Empress Dowager, \"This child is probably unfamiliar with the capital. Please forgive him, Your Highness.\"","She then sternly reprimanded the boy, \"Jing, have you forgotten what your mother told you?\"","— In fact, everyone in the palace had heard that this third son was not born to the Princess of Liaodong, but to one of the King of Liaodong's concubines.","So it was not surprising that this child was different from his older brothers.","It was also understandable that the Princess of Liaodong didn't like him.","However, this tactic was indeed effective. Seeing her reaction, the little one immediately held back his tears and dared not make a sound.","But his eyes were still brimming with tears, looking pitiful.","None of the consorts had experience with children and didn't know what to do. The Empress Dowager, however, smiled and beckoned to the little one, her voice very gentle, \"Come to your royal grandmother.\"","Royal grandmother?","The crowd secretly exchanged glances, each wondering to themselves — Has the Empress Dowager gone mad with longing for grandchildren? This isn't the emperor's child, how can he call her royal grandmother?","The Princess of Liaodong, also looking anxious, quickly said, \"Jing doesn't dare.\"","But the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"His grandfather and the late emperor were brothers. If the late emperor were here, wouldn't he call him royal grandfather? So what's wrong with calling me royal grandmother?\"","The Princess of Liaodong breathed a sigh of relief and finally dared to smile, \"The Empress Dowager makes a good point.\"","She then pushed Jing towards the Empress Dowager, \"Royal grandmother is calling you, hurry up and go.\"","The little one timidly came before the Empress Dowager, who took his small hand and looked at it, then used her handkerchief to wipe the tear stains from his face. She called for Zhu Shu to bring out some winter melon candy and honey dates, saying, \"Are you hungry? Grandmother has some snacks here, have a little something to eat first.\"","Seeing the treats, the little one finally broke into a smile through his tears.","The Empress Dowager then said to the Princess of Liaodong, \"The weather is cold, and you've come such a long way. It's normal for the little one to feel uncomfortable. Stay for a while longer this time, and return when he's more accustomed to the warmth here.\"","The Princess of Liaodong quickly agreed.","The Empress Dowager then asked Zhu Shu to bring out a cloth tiger and a small leather ball for the little one to play with.","The child finally settled down.","The others watched all this, feeling somewhat stunned.","The Empress Dowager even had toys for small children?","It seems she truly does love little ones.","If they could bear an heir, not only would they win the Empress Dowager's favor, but the child would surely have a bright future.","But...","Several of them, led by Consort Zhou, glared at Yanshu.","With this woman currently holding the emperor's exclusive favor, how could they have a chance?","At this moment, Yanshu was leisurely drinking tea and eating snacks.","Sensing everyone's gaze, she inwardly clicked her tongue.","What are you all looking at?","Even without me, you still couldn't bear children."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27","paragraphs":["After the Liaodong King's Wife paid respects to the Empress Dowager, that evening the palace held a welcoming banquet for the Liaodong King's family.","The Liaodong King was a member of the imperial clan and a descendant of the Founder Emperor. To show their importance, not only did Yuwen Lan lead a group of concubines to attend, but even the Empress Dowager made a rare appearance.","It could be said this was a family gathering for the Yuwen Clan.","In fact, ever since the new emperor ascended the throne, the Liaodong King's family would come to the capital at the end of each year to pay their respects.","Therefore, there would be a welcoming banquet at the end of every year.","But Yanshu had only recently been promoted in rank, so this was her first time attending.","To be honest, she didn't really want to come.","— After all, not only were there guests at today's banquet, but she now also bore the responsibility of being a target, with who knows how many eyes watching her.","Even if she wanted to focus solely on eating, she wouldn't be able to enjoy it!","If one couldn't fully enjoy the food, what was the point of this banquet?","However, times had changed, and even if she wanted to make up an excuse to be absent, she couldn't.","So despite her reluctance, she obediently came.","But come to think of it, having just heard gossip about the Liaodong King yesterday, it would be good to see the main characters today.","At this moment, the hall was brilliantly lit, and both hosts and guests had taken their seats.","Yanshu quietly looked around and saw that today, aside from Consort Ning who was still confined and Consort Li in the Cold Palace, everyone from the harem had come.","This included Consort Zhou, who had recently been demoted, and Consort Wang, who was responsible for announcing the time.","Of course, Consort Zhou's demeanor was already different from before, and Consort Wang was huddled in a corner, seemingly not wanting the emperor to notice her.","Today, Yanshu was seated at the same table as Consort Xu.","She was also someone who didn't like to talk much and hadn't participated in any of the harem factions, so her presence was somewhat low-key.","The emperor and Empress Dowager sat at the head, followed by the various consorts, and below the consorts were the Liaodong King's family.","Yanshu secretly observed the Liaodong King, Yuwen Hao. She saw that he looked a few years older than the emperor. As cousins, the two had somewhat similar facial features.","However, the Liaodong King was more robust in build, perhaps due to the nourishing environment of Liaodong. His face also looked more good-natured, bearing some resemblance to his wife.","As soon as the banquet began, Yuwen Lan raised his cup and said, \"Cousin, you must be tired from your long journey.\"","Yuwen Hao hurriedly stood up with his wife and children and replied, \"Your Majesty is too kind. It is an honor for my family to return to the capital each year to pay respects to Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager.\"","He then instructed his three sons, \"No matter when, even if I'm not around anymore, you must always remember that you are of the Yuwen bloodline. During festivals and New Year, you must pay respects and offer greetings to His Majesty and the Empress Dowager without fail.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, his eldest and second sons immediately responded in unison.","Only the youngest son, Jing, was a bit slow, responding with a \"Yes\" after his two brothers had finished.","For a moment, his little voice echoed in the hall, sounding very adorable.","The Empress Dowager smiled and said to Yuwen Lan, \"When Your Majesty first came to me, you weren't even as big as Jing.\"","The Liaodong King said, \"This child is young and doesn't know better. We've embarrassed ourselves in front of the Empress Dowager and Your Majesty.\"","But the Empress Dowager said, \"Children are naturally like this. Your Majesty used to cry often when you were young. Now you can't tell at all what you were like back then.\"","At these words, everyone in the hall laughed.","Yuwen Lan also smiled and said, \"Thanks to Mother's careful nurturing, I was able to grow up safely. Mother, you've worked hard.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"Being able to be mother and son with Your Majesty is also my good fortune.\"","But then she sighed and said, \"Having children brings life. Your Majesty, look at how good their family is? If there were a few children in the palace, the atmosphere would surely be even better.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, all the consorts quietly paused.","The Liaodong King, however, laughed heartily and said, \"If the Empress Dowager doesn't mind, we could have these three come to the palace often to pay their respects to you in the coming days.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and smiled, \"That would be wonderful.\"","Yuwen Lan finally spoke up, \"It's my fault for making Mother worry. I will try harder in the future.\"","As he said this, he actually glanced at Yanshu.","Yanshu thought, \"???\"","Why was he looking at her?","This wasn't her problem either!","Oh...","She suddenly understood a little. Was the emperor trying to shift blame?","— Later, when no children were born for a long time, he would blame it on her, saying she couldn't bear children?","Tsk, truly sinister!","Yuwen Lan thought, \"???\"","This girl!","That wasn't what he meant at all!","He really wanted to teach her a lesson right then and there!","However, they were in the great hall at the moment, with so many eyes watching, so he could only endure again and again, not letting his expression show any abnormality.","But the Liaodong King and his wife caught this moment.","The couple exchanged a glance, both pondering in their hearts —","The rumors that only Yanshu was favored in the palace seemed indeed to be true.","After drinking the opening toast, palace servants began to bring out the dishes.","Yanshu had originally planned to just go through the motions like everyone else, not eating much.","However, with those delicious dishes right in front of her eyes, various sweet, fragrant, sour, and spicy aromas tempting her, she struggled briefly before finally giving up and starting to eat in earnest.","Mmm, the crispy pork tenderloin was crispy on the outside and tender on the inside;","The yellow croaker with tofu was soft and fragrant; the sweet and sour pork was tangy and delicious.","The most wonderful was the snow chicken dish. When first served, it looked like white clouds, and you could hardly tell what ingredients it was made from. Upon tasting it, it felt soft and smooth. After savoring it a bit more, she could taste the unique flavor of chicken, only then realizing it was actually made from chicken.","Indeed, eating chicken without seeing chicken – how marvelous!","And just as the snow chicken dish was finished, the Peking duck came out.","Those thin slices of duck with skin, permeated with the aroma of fruit wood, were wrapped in paper-thin pancakes. One must not forget to add scallions, sweet bean sauce, and cucumber strips. After carefully wrapping it up and putting it in your mouth, chewing slowly, the unique richness of duck meat spread layer by layer between your lips and teeth, making one utterly satisfied.","She declared that Peking duck was the best way to eat duck!!!","Yanshu was immersed in the deliciousness of the Peking duck, and it wasn't until she had eaten three duck wraps in a row that she belatedly noticed a little fellow curiously watching her from not far away.","It was none other than the Liaodong King's youngest son, Jing.","Tsk, look at this little one, staring at her mouth moving without even blinking.","Yanshu thought, \"...\"","Why was he looking at her? The Peking duck on the table smells so good, little baby!","She suddenly felt sympathetic, so she asked, \"Does Jing want to eat too?\"","The little one shyly nodded.","His little face was quite adorable, and Yanshu's heart suddenly overflowed with love. She wrapped a duck pancake and reached out to hand it to him.","The little one also reached out to take it and put it in his mouth to eat.","Seeing this, the Liaodong King's Wife quickly scolded, \"This child, don't you have some in front of you? Why are you asking Yanshu for food?\"","Yanshu hurriedly said, \"It's no trouble, I just did it without thinking. Please don't blame him, Your Highness.\"","Hey, they say kind people attract children's favor. This proves she's very kind, surely just like an angel.","Yuwen Lan, who had been quietly observing her from the head table, thought, \"...\"","— You're overthinking it. That child just saw you eating so deliciously and got hungry.","Just then, someone said, \"Does Yanshu perhaps have some special secret? How is it that even such a young boy likes you?\"","The speaker was none other than Consort Zhou, who had recently been demoted.","Tsk, it's impressive that even though she's no longer a Noble Consort, her tone is still so sarcastic.","Yanshu pretended not to understand and said, \"Noble Consort is joking. I'm just closer to Jing, so he wanted to play with me.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Consort Xu at the same table suddenly also wrapped a duck pancake and handed it to Jing, saying, \"Little prince, try mine too and see if it's good?\"","Jing immediately took it.","Everyone was somewhat surprised —","What was Consort Xu's intention? Was she actively helping Yanshu out of the situation?","Consort Zhou laughed again and said, \"Is Consort Xu learning from Yanshu? Forgive me for saying, but you're different from Yanshu. I'm afraid you can't learn it.\"","Consort Xu said, \"I just think Jing is cute, that's all.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, they heard the emperor address Consort Zhou, \"Has your alcohol tolerance become so much worse than before? You're drunk after just one cup?\"","Yuwen Lan's eyes held no trace of a smile, looking rather frightening.","Consort Zhou then paused and lowered her head, saying, \"Yes, I spoke out of turn.\"","The atmosphere became somewhat awkward, until the Empress Dowager spoke up to ease the tension, \"Such an adorable child, who wouldn't like him?\"","As she spoke, she also personally wrapped a duck pancake and called the little one over, \"Come to Great-grandmother.\"","The little one obediently ran over, his little face stuffed like a bun, causing everyone to laugh.","The atmosphere finally eased a bit, and the banquet continued.","While savoring the delicacies, Yanshu inwardly clicked her tongue. Despite such a big setback, Consort Zhou still hadn't grown any wiser.","What was the point of making sour remarks to hurt others in such an occasion?","Moreover, how was Consort Xu trying to imitate her?","She was clearly just greeting Yuwen Hao.","Indeed, according to the gossip she had heard yesterday, this seemingly good-natured King of Liaodong, Yuwen Hao, had actually planted spies in the palace as early as when the emperor ascended the throne.","And this spy was none other than Consort Xu.","Not far away, the emperor, who was chatting and laughing with Yuwen Hao, felt a subtle pause in his heart.","That Consort Xu is Yuwen Hao's spy?","He had long known that Yuwen Hao was not as obedient as he appeared on the surface.","He had also anticipated that spies had been planted in the palace.","He just hadn't figured out who it was yet.","Until now, when he heard Yanshu's inner thoughts.","Just then, he heard Yanshu think, [Hmm? Wasn't she trained in martial arts? How are her hands still so delicate? What kind of hand care does she use?]","This, Yuwen Lan wasn't surprised about.","Any spy would necessarily have superior martial arts skills.","However, the fact that the other party had arranged for her to enter the harem suggested that she might be more than just a simple spy.","He calmly took a sip of wine.","Suddenly, Yuwen Hao said, \"Your subject has brought some gifts for Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and all the consorts on this visit to the capital. It's a small token of my respect.\"","With that, he ordered his personal servants to bring the gifts into the hall.","The gift for Yuwen Lan was a large sable fur cloak, made entirely of dark gray sable fur, looking extremely valuable.","For the Empress Dowager, it was a ginseng from Changbai Mountain, which probably cost tens of thousands of taels of silver.","Yanshu and the other consorts also received sable fur scarves.","Of course, Consort Zhou's was of better quality to demonstrate her noble status.","Everyone expressed their gratitude to the King of Liaodong.","Yuwen Lan also nonchalantly invited Yuwen Hao to raise a glass again, \"I must thank my cousin for his thoughtfulness.\"","Yuwen Hao smiled good-naturedly, \"Your Majesty is too kind. These are just specialties from Liaodong. I'm glad if you don't mind them.\"","As he spoke, his eyes glanced over to Consort Xu's position, and he inwardly sneered, [Useless thing.]","Before they knew it, the banquet was coming to an end.","The Empress Dowager left first, and the King of Liaodong's family also bid farewell and left the palace.","Yuwen Lan returned to Qianming Palace and immediately dispatched his men.","From Yuwen Hao's inner thoughts earlier, he had already deduced that Yuwen Hao must have made more preparations for this visit to the capital.","Just as this group of men left, the Imperial Guard came to report.","\"Your Majesty, we have confirmed that Zhang Shengkang, the Chief of the Imperial Hospital, indeed once studied medicine under a physician named Xun Ji, who used to run a clinic in the northern alley of the capital. It's said his medical skills were quite exceptional, and those seeking treatment were endless.\"","Yuwen Lan's heart steadied.","Yes, Xun Ji.","That was the name.","\"Where is he now?\" he asked.","The Imperial Guard lowered his head, \"He passed away many years ago.\"","Having already known this from Yanshu, Yuwen Lan wasn't too disappointed. He simply asked, \"Did Xun Ji have any other disciples besides Zhang Shengkang?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"No, but it's said he had a son who disappeared after his death. We haven't been able to find any information about him yet.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Keep searching, increase the manpower, and find him as soon as possible.\"","The Imperial Guard complied.","—Usually, medical skills are passed down within the family, so Xun Ji's son should have learned his medical skills.","After tonight's events, he felt an even more urgent need to cure himself.","The Empress Dowager's reaction to that child tonight was far from normal.","Although there was nothing unusual in the Empress Dowager's thoughts, having been mother and son for so many years, he knew that the Empress Dowager wasn't particularly fond of children.","Even when Duke Cheng'en had brought his grandson to pay respects to the Empress Dowager in the past, she had never been so enthusiastic.","Let alone Yuwen Hao's children, who had no blood relation to her at all.","After bathing and changing clothes in Qianming Palace, Yuwen Lan still came to Ganlu Palace.","It was late, and Yanshu had also just finished washing up, so the two went to bed.","Yuwen Lan wasn't sleepy for a moment, and unconsciously placed his hand on Yanshu's lower abdomen, asking, \"If we have our own children in the future, would you want a son or a daughter?\"","—Although she often angered him to the point of losing his reason, judging from her reaction to that child tonight, he felt she would be a good mother in the future.","Yanshu was taken aback and said, \"...Forgive this concubine, Your Majesty, but I haven't thought about this question yet. However, a son or daughter would be fine. Whatever heaven gives us would be the best.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of agreement, \"That makes sense.\"","But he still looked deep in thought.","Yanshu observed his expression and silently pondered, [Why would he suddenly ask about this?]","[Could it be... he was affected by seeing the King of Liaodong's three sons?]","[Tsk, poor emperor, especially with what the Empress Dowager said tonight, he must be feeling a lot of pressure.]","[Imagine if his condition never improves, wouldn't that mean he'll never have children?]","[Tsk tsk, this is a big deal!]","[It would be just like when the late emperor passed away, with the imperial clan restless. There might be another bloodbath!]","[Oh no, the late emperor at least had two children, but the emperor doesn't have any. It would probably be even more brutal then.]","Yuwen Lan silently nodded.","This girl finally seemed to understand a bit.","—If Yuwen Hao was already impatient now, what more if he continued to have no children?","So, this matter was extremely important to him, and he was indeed facing great pressure.","Just then, he heard her think, [But come to think of it, is this condition hereditary? The late emperor also had weak offspring, tsk.]","Yuwen Lan immediately dismissed this possibility in his mind—","In fact, the late emperor just had few children who survived.","Before he was born, the late emperor already had two sons and two daughters, but unfortunately, three of them died young, with only Princess Yuwen Yan living to adulthood.","However, after he was born, indeed no more siblings were born in the palace.","He recalled that the late emperor later became obsessed with elixirs, which might have affected his fertility.","But in any case, he had never taken any elixirs, and had always been normal before. It was only after ascending the throne that he mysteriously began to gradually lose that function.","At first, he thought it was due to the stress and fatigue of state affairs.","But later, when he suddenly gained the ability to read minds, he couldn't help but wonder if this was a joke played on him by heaven?","Or was it some kind of test?","To make him exchange this price for the ability to read minds, to be a good ruler.","However, this seemed impossible too, because he was now showing signs of improvement.","Every night he slept here, he would experience changes the next day.","These changes must be related to her.","Thinking of this, he unconsciously stroked her hair, his movements very gentle.","But then he heard her think, [It's not like there's no solution.]","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan paused. What solution?","[I could pull a switch!]","Yuwen Lan was confused. What did she mean by pulling a switch?","Then he heard her continue, [First pretend to be pregnant, then when it's time to give birth, adopt a child from outside the palace, and then say it's the emperor's flesh and blood!]","After all, that's how it always happened in those melodramatic TV dramas.","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","How could she have such an idea???","[No, no, first of all, this would require the emperor's cooperation, but he definitely couldn't cooperate with me. Because once he knows that I know his secret, he would definitely chop me up first!]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Tsk, he had known for a long time, and still hadn't done anything to her.","She continued to ponder, [Besides, his child is supposed to inherit the throne, how could an outside child do? It's also not good to separate a child from their birth parents, that's too cruel!]","Yuwen Lan listened silently, almost unable to hold back his laughter—","Was she writing a novel?","How could her mind be filled with so much nonsense?","Just then, he heard her say, \"By the way, Your Majesty, this concubine plans to write a novel and would like to ask for your opinion.\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan found it intriguing. She actually wanted his opinion?","Although unexpected, he decided to see what she was up to for now.","So he said, \"Let's hear it.\"","He saw her clear her throat and say, \"Once upon a time, there was a wealthy family. The head of the family was extremely rich and had five sons. Before the first family head died, he passed the position to one of his sons. Later, when this son grew old, he passed it on to his own son.\"","At first, Yuwen Lan listened with some confusion.","Was this story of hers different from her previous ones in style?","She continued, \"Unfortunately, the rest of the old patriarch's descendants met with accidents and passed away one after another. After a few years, only this young master and his cousin remained in the family.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan finally understood—","Ah, she was talking about him.","The old patriarch was the Founder Emperor, his grandfather, and the second master was the late emperor.","This young master was naturally himself.","And Yuwen Hao was that cousin.","Sure enough, he heard her think, \"【I'm talking about you, did you get it?】\"","Yuwen Lan nodded with a suppressed smile, \"Indeed very unfortunate. What happened next?\"","She continued, \"It was only natural for the current master to inherit the family business, and he always took good care of his only remaining cousin. However, greed got the better of the cousin, who harbored ill intentions and sent a spy to the master's side to gather important information.\"","At this point, she looked up at Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, do you think the cousin should choose a beautiful woman or a man to approach the master?\"","Yuwen Lan pretended to ponder for a moment, then said, \"I think it should be a beautiful woman. A man would certainly not be able to get close to the master easily.\"","Yanshu nodded eagerly, \"I think so too, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan deliberately asked, \"Then, did this master fall for his cousin's trap?\"","Yanshu hurriedly replied, \"The master is no ordinary person and has always been very vigilant. To successfully send the beauty to the master's side, the cousin went to great lengths to change her identity, making it impossible to tell she was his person.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded seriously, \"This person is indeed full of schemes. What happened next?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, \"What do you mean 'what happened next'?","Haven't you realized this is about you?","You're that fooled master, and Yuwen Hao is that relentless scheming cousin!","Although we don't know what Consort Xu is up to yet, Yuwen Hao is up to no good, you need to be on guard!\"","Yuwen Lan listened silently, feeling both amused and touched.","So, she had gone to such lengths tonight to warn him.","So, she did care about him after all.","He looked at her with a smile, as she said, \"I wanted to ask Your Majesty, do you think this master will discover the beauty's plot, or will he fail to? After all, a man's thoughts are hard to guess.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"A man's thoughts are hard to guess? I think you've got it wrong. It's a woman's thoughts that are hard to guess.\"","Just like her, who appeared greedy, gluttonous, and timid on the surface, but in fact cared about him the most, didn't she?","Yanshu didn't want to waste words on this issue, so she hastily said, \"Your Majesty has a point, but please answer my question first.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"I think he should be able to discover it. After all, this master is wise and powerful, how could he be easily fooled by such a small trick?\"","Yanshu nodded meaningfully, \"I think so too.\"","In her heart, she was shouting, \"【I've said this much, have you understood yet???】\"","Touched by her efforts in crafting such a story, Yuwen Lan's heart warmed even more. After some thought, he added, \"But for such a wise and powerful master to remain alone is not ideal. He should be paired with a beautiful and intelligent woman who can share his burdens, bear his children, and spend the rest of their lives together...\"","Before he could finish, he heard her exclaim in her thoughts, \"【What? Another beauty?】\"","\"【I went through all this trouble to make up this story to warn you, and now you want a bicycle?】\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What did she mean by \"bicycle\"?","He couldn't understand again.","Then he heard her think indignantly, \"【Indeed, all men are the same. Whether capable or not, they only know how to like beauties. Scumbag!!!】\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What did she mean by \"whether capable or not\"???","And how did he suddenly become a... \"scumbag\"?","He remembered that \"scumbag\" referred to people like Chai Weizhong who deceived women.","But why was she calling him that?","Was it wrong to like beautiful women?","Wasn't she a beautiful woman herself?"]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28","paragraphs":["After the welcoming banquet that day, the Liaodong King's Wife indeed brought her three sons to the palace every day to pay respects to the Empress Dowager.","The Empress Dowager visibly cheered up quite a bit, and even issued an order for their family to attend the New Year's Eve feast on the 30th.","The Emperor had always been a filial son and had no objections to this.","Thus, on New Year's Eve, the banquet hall was graced with the presence of the King of Liaodong's family.","The New Year's Eve feast was the most important meal of the year.","The palace ladies had been preparing since the afternoon.","Yanshu was no exception.","However, while others started dressing up in the afternoon, she had stopped eating snacks since then.","Tsk, she didn't know how many delicacies there would be tonight, so she had to save room to properly taste them all.","As the lanterns were lit and night fell, everyone gathered for the grand New Year's Eve feast in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony.","Similar to the recent welcoming banquet, everyone who should be there was present, except for Consort Ning who was still confined and Consort Li who was in the Cold Palace.","With the addition of King of Liaodong Yuwen Hao's family, the scene was very lively.","Yuwen Lan presided over the head of the banquet hall, secretly glancing to his right.","He saw Yanshu wearing a peach-pink jacket and skirt, her hair in a neat peach-shaped bun, with two small agate earrings. Her cheeks were peach-pink, her lips cherry-red, looking quite vivacious and adorable.","However, listening carefully, he heard her thinking, [Wow, hot pot duck, stir-fried lamb, sour and spicy tripe, jade-green shrimp! And there's soft-shelled turtle with long fish, crab roe lion's head meatballs, bird's nest with duck slices, and three-strand shark fin soup! What's that? Twelve-flavor hot pot! How extravagant!!!]","[I hope the Emperor's opening speech is quick, so I can start eating soon.]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He knew it.","Well, to fulfill her wish, he simply said, \"Everyone has worked hard this past year. For this last meal of the year, there's no need to be too formal.\"","Then he turned to the Empress Dowager and said, \"I wish Mother Empress good health and everything goes smoothly in the coming year.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and nodded, \"Your Majesty has worked the hardest for the country. I also wish Your Majesty good health and everything goes smoothly.\"","Yuwen Lan bowed his head and said, \"Thank you, Mother Empress.\"","Everyone then chimed in unison, \"We wish Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager good health and everything goes smoothly in the coming year.\"","With that said, they could finally start eating.","Yanshu smiled brightly and immediately started with a bowl of hot duck soup to whet her appetite.","Mmm, the duck soup was sour and spicy, making her whole body feel comfortable.","The jade-green shrimp was fresh and crisp, the smoked cabbage was very flavorful, and the mushroom braised chicken was rich in taste.","The soft-shelled turtle with long fish was tender and delicious, the crab roe lion's head meatballs were rich but not greasy, and the three-strand shark fin soup was full of umami.","Not to mention dishes like the assorted hot pot, fat chicken with tofu, spicy stir-fried liver, bird's nest with duck slices, and so on, each with its own unique deliciousness.","Especially that twelve-flavor hot pot which encompassed a wide variety of ingredients: venison, chicken breast, deer back, wild boar leg, as well as sea cucumber, scallops, squid, and lobster balls. Various delicacies from mountains and seas gathered in one pot, with a taste beyond compare.","The New Year's Eve dinner was indeed extraordinary!","This meal was extremely satisfying!","As she was happily eating, she heard the Empress Dowager speak again, \"The dishes today are quite good, especially this sour and spicy tripe. It's tender and flavorful, very suitable for my taste.\"","Yuwen Lan also nodded and said, \"Indeed, it's very good. The kitchen should be rewarded.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the Chief Eunuch of the Ceremonial Office, Hu An, who was serving nearby, quickly announced, \"His Majesty rewards the Imperial Kitchen...\"","Zhu Shu, the lady-in-waiting from the Palace of Benevolent Peace, served more dishes to the Empress Dowager and smiled, \"Empress Dowager, please try this white jade cake.\"","The Empress Dowager tasted it.","After a moment, she nodded again and said, \"Smooth and delicate, sweet but not cloying, indeed very good.\"","As she spoke, she didn't forget to invite the King of Liaodong's family, \"You should try it too. This white jade cake, Jing should like it.\"","Yuwen Hao and his wife quickly agreed and led their three children to taste the white jade cake.","After a while, the Liaodong King's Wife smiled and said, \"The food in the palace is indeed different, much better than in Liaodong.\"","She then asked Jing, \"Quick, tell your great-grandmother, is the cake delicious?\"","The little one, with his cheeks puffed out full of food, nodded and said, \"It's good.\"","This caused everyone to smile fondly.","After eating the white jade cake, the Empress Dowager had a bowl of three-strand shark fin soup and smiled, \"I'm afraid I've eaten too much today.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Tonight is special, and we still need to stay up to see the New Year in. It's fine for Mother Empress to eat more if you have a good appetite.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded.","Then Zhu Shu said, \"Ever since the three young masters came to the capital, the Empress Dowager has been happy and her appetite has improved.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't show any unusual expression, just said \"Oh\" and then, \"It seems I should reward the three of them as well.\"","Upon hearing this, Yuwen Hao quickly said, \"Your Majesty's words are too kind. As juniors, it's only right for them to come to the palace often to pay respects to the Empress Dowager. There's no need for rewards.\"","He then instructed his three children, \"It's New Year's Eve today. Shouldn't you go and kowtow to the Empress Dowager and His Majesty to wish them well?\"","The eldest and second immediately agreed and stood up. The Liaodong King's Wife also pushed little Jing, so the little one also stood up bewilderedly and followed his two brothers to the center of the hall. They kowtowed to the Empress Dowager and Yuwen Lan, saying, \"We wish the Empress Dowager and Your Majesty longevity and good health.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled from ear to ear, repeatedly nodding and saying, \"Good, good, they're all good children. Get up and eat now.\"","Yuwen Lan also smiled and said, \"They know etiquette and are obedient. They should be rewarded.\"","Hearing this, the Chief Eunuch of the Ceremonial Office announced, \"Rewards are bestowed upon the three young masters of the King of Liaodong's household.\"","The three children knelt down again to express their gratitude before returning to their meal.","With this, the hall became even more lively.","At this moment, Nanny Zhuang, who was by the Empress Dowager's side, was heard saying, \"It would be wonderful if the young masters could come to the palace often in the future. It's just a pity... Liaodong is so far away.\"","Hearing these words, everyone paused—","Nanny Zhuang's words seemed to have hidden meanings.","Sure enough, the Empress Dowager sighed next, \"Isn't it? The weather is cold in Liaodong, and it would be worrying if the children caught colds from traveling back and forth. The eldest and second are older so it's fine, but little Jing is only four years old. Wouldn't he suffer if he fell ill?\"","Nanny Zhuang then said, \"Why not have the little young master stay for a few more days, to keep you company? When the weather gets warmer, we can send the little young master back to Liaodong.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, everyone started to speculate in their hearts.","—What is the Empress Dowager's intention?","Does she want to keep the King of Liaodong's youngest son by her side to raise?","Yanshu finally snapped out of her food-induced trance.","—What? The Empress Dowager wants to raise the King of Liaodong's son?","Is she really that kind-hearted?","Could it be that she wants to keep Jing as a hostage?","Tsk, that's not right either. Jing isn't the King of Liaodong's legitimate son. If she really wanted a hostage, why wouldn't the Empress Dowager choose their eldest or second son?","Yanshu suddenly paused. Could it be that the Empress Dowager has discovered that the Emperor can't... you know... and wants to adopt a son for the Emperor?","At the same time, Yuwen Lan also heard the Empress Dowager's thoughts—","[Jing is not of legitimate birth, and his age is suitable. It can only be him.]","He remained impassive, but his heart was already clear.","The Empress Dowager deliberately chose Jing, who was born out of wedlock, fearing that Yuwen Hao and his wife wouldn't be willing to part with a legitimate son.","The Empress Dowager had indeed discovered his secret and was making other plans.","He concealed the complexity in his heart and even smiled at Yuwen Hao and his wife, saying, \"Mother Empress's idea is excellent, but I wonder if my elder cousin and his wife are willing to part with him?\"","Yuwen Hao hesitated for a moment, but then smiled and said, \"To be able to accompany the Empress Dowager is Jing's good fortune. I'm happy for him, how could I be unwilling?\"","Seeing her husband's response, his wife, the Liaodong King's Wife, also quickly smiled and said, \"What kind of blessing has this child cultivated in his previous life to be able to accompany the Empress Dowager? Jing, quickly thank your great-grandmother for her grace.\"","Then, the little one who was eating dessert was pushed forward with a confused look. Under the guidance of the Liaodong King's Wife, he kowtowed to the Empress Dowager and said, \"Jing thanks great-grandmother...\"","The little voice once again made everyone smile.","However, Yanshu keenly noticed that at this moment, Consort Xu beside her seemed to pause for a moment.","Hiss...","For a spy with such high psychological quality, this kind of reaction seemed a bit off.","She immediately called out to the system, [Judging from Consort Xu's reaction, could this Jing be the child she bore for Yuwen Hao?]","System, [It should be, but it's not.]","Yanshu, [??? What does that mean? What do you mean by 'should be but is not'?]","System, [It means that Consort Xu herself thinks this child is hers, but in fact, her child died young due to congenital weakness. But Yuwen Hao wanted to keep her in check, so he found another child as a substitute, making her believe it was her child.]","Yanshu, [...]","That's complicated.","However, she managed to understand.","In other words, Consort Xu's child was actually long gone, but Yuwen Hao found a fake child to deceive her in order to make her obey him.","Yanshu couldn't help but click her tongue. This King of Liaodong was truly full of schemes.","But as a man, to use women in such a way was truly disgusting!","Not far away, Yuwen Lan heard her inner thoughts word for word.","Very well, the Empress Dowager was eager to adopt another pawn, but this little child wasn't of the Yuwen family bloodline.","Without showing any sign of surprise, he said to the Empress Dowager and the Yuwen Hao couple, \"If that's the case, let the child stay here for a while. Being able to bring joy to the Empress Dowager is a great merit for him.\"","Yuwen Hao immediately laughed, \"Your Majesty is too kind. This is indeed a great fortune for him, haha!\"","Yanshu found this fat man's laughter truly revolting.","For the sake of ambition, he separated an innocent child from his family, and so brazenly used him as a tool.","If this child were truly his own flesh and blood, would he be able to part with him so easily?","However, in this case, wasn't the Empress Dowager raising a child with no relation to the royal family?","If it were the eldest or second child, it would be more understandable, as they at least had the blood of the great ancestor!","Just then, the system suddenly popped up again, [You're overthinking. Those two aren't from the Yuwen family either.]","Yanshu, [???]","[What does this mean? Those two children aren't Yuwen Hao's either?]","System, [That's right.]","Yanshu's eyes lit up, [Could it be that the Liaodong King's Wife also cuckolded the King of Liaodong?]","Yuwen Lan, who overheard this nearby, \"???\"","The Liaodong King's Wife cuckolded Yuwen Hao???","What was this situation?","System, [You think everyone is as unlucky as the Marquis of Linwu? These two children were actually also found elsewhere by the Liaodong King couple, to replace their own flesh and blood in coming to the capital.]","What???","Yanshu felt that her brain might not be sufficient for tonight, [Using fake children to bring to the capital? What are these two up to?]","System, [You think it's a good thing for a feudal king to come to the capital? If the Emperor is displeased, he might detain them, at best punish them, at worst execute them. The King of Liaodong certainly doesn't want to take that risk!]","Yanshu, [....]","Alright, she finally understood.","This was truly a case of one mountain being higher than another between the Empress Dowager and the King of Liaodong!","How could people be so cunning?","But this was a serious crime, once discovered, it would lead to execution.","Wasn't this fat man afraid?","The system said very maturely, [It's very difficult to discover. They come to the capital at most once a year, and they always find children who look similar to their own. Who could recognize them except their own people?]","Yanshu, [....]","That was true.","In this era without photographs, even the best portrait would have some discrepancies, not to mention children grow every year. When children who haven't been seen for a long time suddenly appear, as long as there aren't significant differences in their features, it's really hard to notice.","Tsk tsk tsk, this fat Yuwen Hao was truly sly!","What did he eat to grow so many schemes in his mind!","As she was sighing inwardly, Yuwen Lan, who had heard everything, also understood.","Huh, so that's how it was.","It turned out that none of the children Yuwen Hao and his wife brought to the capital this time were their own flesh and blood?","This sounded absurd at first, but for Yuwen Hao, it was entirely possible.","Moreover, after experiencing so many shocks before, he no longer doubted Yanshu at all.","Good, very good.","It seemed that this cousin had made up his mind to do something big this time.","Outside the hall, the sound of firecrackers continued, while inside, people were still eating, drinking, and exchanging New Year's greetings happily.","Yuwen Lan drank a cup of wine without showing any change in expression.","Huh, did they think this throne was something one could sit on just because they wanted to?","Before they knew it, night had fallen deep, and the New Year's Eve banquet had finally come to an end.","After respectfully sending off the Empress Dowager and the Emperor, everyone dispersed.","Yanshu returned to her palace to change clothes and wash up, while Rendong and others prepared some melon seeds, snacks, and fruits, ready for tonight's vigil to welcome the New Year.","However, when Yanshu finished washing up and came out, she had no mood for the vigil.","She thought back and forth, feeling that the gossip she had heard tonight was indeed significant, and closely related to the Emperor. As the Emperor's leg accessory, she couldn't stand idly by, she had to find a way to let the Emperor know.","If it were usual, she could remind him through hints in conversation as she had done before, but tonight was New Year's Eve, and according to custom, the Emperor had to spend the night in the central palace. Since there was no Empress now, he could only sleep in Qianming Palace and couldn't come to the consorts' quarters.","So she couldn't see him.","After much thought, she could only go to the writing desk and start writing.","Seeing this, Rendong asked curiously, \"Aren't you going to rest a bit for tonight's vigil, mistress?\"","Yanshu sighed silently, and could only make an excuse, \"I suddenly thought of a very good story, I have to write it down quickly, otherwise I'll forget it tomorrow. You all go ahead with the vigil, don't mind me.\"","With that, she started writing.","Rendong didn't understand but could only comply and retreated to the side without disturbing her further.","Yanshu wrote while thinking, and soon became fully absorbed in her task.","Damn, this story was really brain-taxing.","With the adoptive mother having ulterior motives, and the cousin constantly causing trouble, Emperor, oh Emperor, you must thank me for this!","That night, while firecrackers continued to sound outside the window, Yanshu almost forgot it was New Year's Eve.","It wasn't until the sky began to lighten that she finally finished writing.","Putting down her brush and yawning, she called out to the people outside.","Rendong entered the room and was shocked to see her still sitting at the table. She hurriedly asked, \"Has the mistress been writing until now?\"","Yanshu nodded and said, \"When it's daylight, find an opportunity to send this stack of papers to Qianming Palace. Say it's a new story I've written and ask His Majesty to take a look.\"","Rendong complied and tidied up the papers.","Turning around, she saw Yanshu collapse onto the bed and fall into a deep sleep.","Rendong shook her head, thinking to herself that the mistress was going through unnecessary trouble. She was already a favored consort, yet she still thought about writing stories to earn money every day.","Tsk, she was truly a hardworking person.","On New Year's Day, the Emperor was very busy.","At the fifth watch, Yuwen Lan had already washed up and changed clothes, coming to Fengxian Hall to worship the ancestors and deities.","After daybreak, he led the consorts to pay New Year's greetings to the Empress Dowager.","After paying respects to the Empress Dowager, he returned to the palace to change clothes again and attended the New Year's court ceremony.","After the court ceremony, there was the New Year's grand banquet, where the emperor, officials, and royal relatives shared the first feast of the new year.","By the time the grand banquet ended and he returned to Qianming Palace, it was already afternoon.","While changing clothes, he heard Fu Hai report, \"By the way, Your Majesty, earlier Consort Li sent over a stack of papers. She said it was a new story she had written and asked for your perusal.\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan was a bit surprised. She had time to write a new story during the New Year?","So he said, \"Bring it here.\"","Fu Hai complied and presented the papers.","Yuwen Lan took them and started reading.","After a while, he realized that this was still the story about the young family master and his cousin that she had told that night.","However, this time she had added some new plot elements, such as the cousin and the beautiful spy having once been lovers and having a child together, and this person using the child to control the beauty;","The family master's adoptive mother had ulterior motives and planned to support someone else...","The scheming cousin had also arranged a stand-in for his own child, attempting to deceive the family master...","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Alright, he understood now. She was trying to remind him of what happened at the New Year's Eve banquet.","And the fresh ink smell on the paper told him that she must have just written this story not long ago.","Actually, after returning to Qianming Palace last night, he had already sent people to Liaodong.","He didn't expect her to worry about him and specially write such a story to remind him.","To think that such a person who loved eating and sleeping would stay up late to write a story, it was truly not easy.","Being an emperor might not be easy, but in that harem, there was a little girl who cared for him.","Yuwen Lan suddenly wanted to go to Ganlu Palace.","But he couldn't.","Because today was New Year's Day, according to custom, he was not allowed to visit the consorts' quarters for three consecutive days.","After pondering for a while, he suddenly called out, \"Come here.\"","Fu Hai hurriedly came before him and said, \"This servant is here.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Go to Ganlu Palace and send something to Consort Li.\"","...","Yanshu was also very busy today.","She couldn't sleep in on New Year's Day. As soon as it was dawn, she went with the other consorts to pay New Year's greetings to the Empress Dowager along with the Emperor.","Afterward, there were noble ladies and royal relatives entering the palace to pay New Year's calls, and at noon she attended another New Year's lunch banquet. She had only just returned not long ago.","Having stayed up late the previous night writing her story, she was feeling waves of drowsiness and was about to take a nap when Fu Hai arrived carrying a box.","\"This servant wishes Consort Yanshu a happy New Year,\" Fu Hai said with a smile. \"His Majesty has sent me to deliver a treasure to you.\"","Oh? A treasure?","Yanshu immediately asked curiously, \"What kind of treasure?\"","Fu Hai carefully opened the box. \"Please have a look, Consort.\"","In an instant, a dazzling light filled the hall.","Yanshu was shocked.","It turned out the box contained a golden bowl.","The bowl was about the size of a palm, exquisitely crafted, and inlaid with red and blue gemstones. It was so bright it could nearly blind someone.","She was stunned for two seconds before remembering to ask, \"Why has His Majesty given me this?\"","Fu Hai replied, \"His Majesty said it's because you wrote your story so well. This is your reward.\"","A reward?","Yanshu thought for a moment. He must have understood, right? That's why he gave her this, to reward her loyalty?","Haha, excellent! Very good!!!","She quickly called Rendong to receive it, saying delightedly, \"Thank His Majesty for his great kindness.\"","Well, well, that late night certainly wasn't wasted.","Her choice had indeed been correct - writing stories was truly the path to wealth and riches!","...","Not long after, the Emperor saw his head eunuch return to report.","\"Your Majesty, the golden bowl has been delivered to Consort Yanshu. She was very pleased,\" Fu Hai said with a smile.","Yuwen Lan nodded, seeming to envision her beaming face.","For such a money-loving little girl, the way to make her happy was certainly to give her gold, silver, and jewels.","He couldn't help but smile as well, then asked, \"Did she say anything else?\"","Fu Hai quickly replied, \"Consort Yanshu said she thanks Your Majesty for his great kindness, and that this was the most expensive payment she's ever received for her writing.\"","Payment for her writing?","Yuwen Lan paused.","Had she misunderstood?","For three consecutive days, there were various New Year's banquets and feasts in the palace.","On the third day, the palace held a family reunion banquet for the imperial clan.","As night fell and the lanterns were lit, the palace grounds glowed with brilliant lights.","Tonight's banquet was held to entertain the imperial relatives. In addition to the Emperor and his consorts, there was also the King of Liaodong and his family, the Prince of Pingyi County and his family, the Grand Princess Leping and her husband, and Princess Yuwen Yan and her husband.","To save face for the royal family, the Emperor had given his sister some face, allowing Princess Yuwen Yan to reappear before everyone.","However, Consort Ning was still under confinement, so she was not present at the banquet.","Everyone had thought that after being sent away last time, the Princess would be more low-key today. Unexpectedly, she wore a fiery red fox fur cape over an embroidered satin robe, her hair in a high bun adorned with gold hairpins, pearl combs, and various jeweled accessories - it was almost blinding.","Once everyone had arrived, the banquet began.","As in previous occasions, Yanshu was seated at the same table as Consort Xu today.","She saw that Consort Xu was wearing a crimson brocade jacket today, with her hair also in a high bun, adorned with two multi-jeweled gold hairpins, looking particularly glamorous.","Because of this, Consort Zhou had already thrown several sharp glances her way.","Yanshu, however, felt something wasn't quite right.","Consort Xu had never been so high-profile before.","Could it be that she had been pushed to desperation by Yuwen Hao and was now trying to attract the Emperor's attention?","However, even stranger things were yet to come.","As the second round of drinks was being served and the atmosphere in the hall was at its liveliest with everyone offering toasts, Consort Xu suddenly stood up and came to the center of the hall. She addressed the Emperor, \"Your servant has prepared a dance and music performance to respectfully offer to Your Majesty.\"","As her words fell, everyone paused.","Although it wasn't unusual for consorts to dance for the Emperor, it was always done when there were no outsiders present.","Tonight, there were quite a few outsiders.","However, the Emperor on his throne did not refuse, and actually nodded, saying, \"Granted.\"","Consort Xu acknowledged and summoned musicians to accompany her as she began to dance in the hall.","Seeing this, the eyes of Consort Zhou, Consort An, and others were almost murderous.","The Princess also cast a look of contemptuous mockery.","Was this woman willing to discard even her dignity in order to compete for favor?","In the entire hall, only Yanshu felt something was amiss.","Consort Xu was no brainless cannon fodder.","She was a spy with a very strong psyche!","Was she planning to do something with this move?","Yanshu quietly called out to her system, [Why is Consort Xu coming out to show off at this kind of banquet with outsiders present? Is she dancing for Yuwen Hao to see?]","The system replied, [Because she plans to assassinate the Emperor.]"]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29","paragraphs":["Yanshu almost thought her ears were playing tricks on her.","[What did you say? Assassinate the Emperor???]","The System calmly told her, [That's right.]","Yanshu's eyes widened in disbelief. [Has she gone mad? Why suddenly assassinate the Emperor???]","System: [Because the King of Liaodong can't wait any longer. Think about it - last night the Empress Dowager said she wanted to adopt Jing. This will inevitably affect Consort Xu as the boy's mother. If the mother and son can see each other every day right before their eyes, it's hard to guarantee Consort Xu will still listen to him!]","Hmm, that made sense. If she were Consort Xu, with her child right in front of her, as long as his safety could be ensured, why would she still listen to that man?","However, this meant the King of Liaodong had to force her to act now, while this \"fake Jing\" was still in his hands.","But with so many people present today, whether she succeeded or not, there would surely be no way out alive!!!","The System reminded her again very calmly, [Isn't that the fate of spies, always at risk of being discovered and killed? Besides, Yuwen Hao made her a grand promise.]","Yanshu hurriedly asked, [What promise?]","System: [Yuwen Hao said that if she succeeded, he would guarantee Jing the position of Crown Prince.]","Yanshu: [...]","How the hell was that possible?","That child wasn't even Yuwen Hao's.","Moreover, even if it really was her child, even if she really succeeded, would the Liaodong King's Wife agree to make her child the Crown Prince?","Tsk, how could even a spy be so lovesick and muddle-headed!!!","System: [Love makes people stupid, evidently.]","Yanshu felt exactly the same way, but before she could nod in agreement, she suddenly realized a critically important issue—","[Why didn't you tell me earlier that she was going to assassinate the Emperor!!!]","System: [??? It's not like she's going to assassinate you, and the Emperor isn't this system's host, so why should this system mention it early?]","But Yanshu was anxious, [What if she really kills the Emperor?!!!]","System: [Just wait and see. The Emperor isn't stupid.]","The Emperor wasn't stupid most of the time, but Yanshu simply couldn't stay calm now!","[What do you mean stupid or not? This is a matter of life and death!!!]","[What if something really happens? Consort Xu must be highly skilled to have hidden in the palace for so long, not to mention Yuwen Hao is here today!!!]","She could already imagine that if the Emperor were assassinated, Yuwen Hao would usurp the throne claiming his bloodline from the founding emperor, since the Emperor had no children, and there were no other grandsons of the founding emperor left!!!","Even if the ministers wanted to oppose, they wouldn't be able to!!!","Look around - these people still knew nothing. Consort Zhou, Consort An, and the others were just glaring daggers at Consort Xu who was dancing. That feather duster of an Eldest Princess only knew how to give others the side-eye.","And her honest and simple Imperial Son-in-law, occasionally glancing at the dancing Consort Xu, would be intimidated by her glare and could only lower his head to eat his food obediently...","The others were all toasting the Emperor, while the Emperor also had a look of complete ignorance on his face.","Did he really not know someone was trying to kill him and was still drinking?!!!","If she had known earlier, she could have thought of a way to warn him, but what could she do now?","Should she stand up now and tell him Consort Xu was an assassin?","Then Consort Xu would definitely not make her move, and she would be thrown out as a lunatic...","She was anxious like an ant on a hot pan, but the System remained calm.","[Why so nervous?]","Yanshu felt like she was about to cough up blood, [The Emperor is my meal ticket! If anything happens to him, forget everything else, Consort Zhou and the Empress Dowager would kill me first!]","So, the Emperor absolutely could not come to harm!!!","However, at that moment, Consort Xu, who had been dancing gracefully in the hall, suddenly pulled out a golden hairpin and rushed towards the Emperor.","Yanshu was startled and, without thinking, rushed out instinctively, shouting, \"Your Majesty, be careful!\"","Damn it, she'd take a gamble today. The Emperor's martial arts were so good that he could easily avoid others and sneak onto rooftops to peep at her, so with her warning, he should be able to escape this calamity.","Unfortunately, she was a bit too slow and couldn't even grab the hem of Consort Xu's skirt.","Luckily, the Emperor seemed to have been prepared.","Just as Consort Xu's golden hairpin was about to strike, he swiftly moved away from his seat. At the same time, more than ten people jumped down from the ceiling of the hall and stood in front of him, forming a solid wall that immediately isolated Consort Xu.","Yanshu was about to breathe a sigh of relief when Consort Xu unexpectedly turned back and stabbed towards her.","In that instant, she only saw a flash of gold and ducked in fear, covering her head.","At the same time, she heard Yuwen Lan's voice, \"Be careful!\"","But it was too late, Consort Xu's golden hairpin had already fallen.","Meanwhile, the hall had descended into chaos.","Consort Zhou, Consort An, Consort Wang, and others screamed in terror;","The Eldest Princess, who had been looking at everyone with disdain just moments ago, also turned pale with fright.","However, her Imperial Son-in-law had hidden even further away than her.","The seemingly plump Grand Princess and her husband had already hidden under their seats...","But Yanshu didn't see any of this. She only felt that she was probably done for.","Consort Xu's golden hairpin would surely pierce her heart, neck, or head, and her second life was about to end here.","Tsk, if she had known the Emperor was prepared, she wouldn't have jumped out. What the hell was this?","Indeed, not heeding the System's words leads to immediate regret, wuwuwu...","Yanshu thought a lot, but the anticipated pain never came.","She hesitantly looked up and found that Yuwen Lan had somehow jumped in front of her, grabbing Consort Xu's arm just before she could stab her.","Yanshu's eyes lit up - she was saved!","However, in the next moment, she felt a sudden pain in her arm.","It turned out that when Yuwen Lan gripped Consort Xu's arm, it instantly broke, causing the golden hairpin in her hand to fall, barely grazing Yanshu's right forearm.","Tsk, that was no hairpin, it was a knife, and an extremely sharp one at that!","With just that slight touch, it had cut through several layers of clothing and sliced her skin.","Yanshu watched as her sleeve slowly turned red.","Blood?","She suddenly felt weak all over and collapsed to the ground.","Damn, she was hemophobic.","As she fell, Yanshu could still hear a chorus of screams in the hall.","The closest to her ear was the Emperor's voice.","\"Yanshu...\"","Huh? He actually called her like that?","Yanshu thought it sounded quite nice, apart from sounding a bit anxious.","However, before she could think any further, she lost consciousness.","When she woke up again, she was lying on the bed in Ganlu Palace.","The imperial physician was checking her pulse, Rendong was calling her anxiously, the Emperor was standing by with a deeply furrowed brow, and Lianxin's eyes were already brimming with tears.","Seeing her open her eyes, everyone's eyes lit up, but no one was faster than the Emperor. He immediately leaned in close and asked urgently, \"How are you feeling?\"","Yanshu called out \"Your Majesty\" and said, \"This concubine is fine...\"","But Yuwen Lan still frowned, \"How can you be fine? You fainted just now.\"","He then asked the imperial physician, \"Was there poison on that weapon? Has Noble Consort been poisoned?\"","The physician hurriedly replied, \"Your Majesty need not worry, we have thoroughly examined it, and that weapon should not have been poisoned.\"","Yuwen Lan was still not at ease and said, \"Then check Noble Consort's pulse again.\"","The physician could only comply and checked Yanshu's pulse again. After quite a while, he dared to report to the Emperor, \"Your Majesty, Noble Consort's pulse has returned to normal.\"","Only then did Yanshu finally manage to interject, saying, \"Your Majesty, this concubine is fine, it's just that I'm a bit hemophobic. I fainted earlier because I saw blood.\"","Tsk, this had been her problem since childhood.","— Once when she was young, she watched a servant killing a chicken at home. The chicken struggled fiercely, and the servant didn't hold it properly, causing the chicken to suddenly jump near her, splattering chicken blood all over her. She fainted on the spot and had this problem ever since.","Seeing that Yuwen Lan was still frowning, she intended to get out of bed to prove it to him.","However, as soon as she tried to use force with her arm, a sharp pain shot through it, as if being pricked by needles. She couldn't help but hiss in pain.","Yuwen Lan hurriedly asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Yanshu: \"...My arm hurts a bit.\"","The imperial physician quickly said, \"Noble Consort's right arm was injured by the weapon. It's best not to move too much. Rest for a few days, and it will be fine once the wound heals.\"","Yuwen Lan then hurriedly said to her, \"Don't move. Just rest well in bed.\"","Rendong also nodded quickly, \"If the Mistress needs anything, just order us servants.\"","Yanshu, \"...\"","Tsk, hearing this, she also feared the wound might start bleeding again, so she could only respond with a \"yes\" and temporarily leaned on the bed without moving.","Immediately after, she saw the emperor address her with a complex expression, \"I didn't expect you to come out. Weren't you afraid of danger?\"","Yanshu, \"...This concubine acted on impulse and didn't think that far.\"","[Damn it, I was just worried that Consort Xu might hurt you, okay? Who knew you were already prepared!]","Yuwen Lan silently listened.","Although these words were still complaining about him internally, he wasn't angry at all.","In fact, he was filled with emotion—","He had actually anticipated that earlier scene, so he had arranged manpower in advance.","The assassin was targeting him, so others wouldn't be in danger.","But he never expected that she would jump out.","Just now, when the entire hall was in panic, apart from the guards, everyone else was fleeing for their lives. Only she still remembered his safety and came out to warn him.","With her small, delicate frame, she actually intended to stop the assassin?","It turns out that she was already willing to risk her life for him.","It seems he had misunderstood her before; she actually cared about him so much.","For the first time in his life, Yuwen Lan felt such emotion. But then he saw her suddenly remember something and hurriedly ask him, \"Your Majesty, how is Consort Xu?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"She's been restrained, don't worry.\"","Yanshu nodded, finally feeling relieved.","However, in his haste to carry her back earlier, Yuwen Lan hadn't had time to deal with this matter.","So he turned and instructed Fu Hai, \"Issue an imperial edict, order the Ministry of Justice and the Inner Court to thoroughly investigate this matter. I want to know who instigated this woman and how she infiltrated the palace to attempt assassination.\"","Fu Hai quickly responded and went out to announce the edict.","But he heard Yanshu anxiously say in her heart, [It was that bastard Yuwen Hao who did it, we can't let that son of a bitch escape!]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Tsk, how does she have such a repertoire of vulgar language.","But it doesn't matter. This side of her is also irreplaceable, unique in the world.","Of course, Yuwen Lan was also very clear that the culprit was Yuwen Hao, but he needed evidence to convince others.","He gently comforted her, \"Don't worry, I won't let any evil-doer go unpunished.\"","Yanshu nodded and hurriedly flattered him, \"Your Majesty is wise.\"","But as soon as she finished speaking, a palace maid from the Palace of Benevolent Peace came to Yuwen Lan and said, \"The Empress Dowager just learned about the assassin in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony and is very worried. She sent this servant to ask if Your Majesty is safe and well.\"","Yuwen Lan paused, then said to Yanshu, \"You rest well first, I'm going to visit the Empress Dowager.\"","Yanshu said okay and watched him leave.","All the way to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yuwen Lan stepped into the hall and saw the anxious expression on the Empress Dowager's face at a glance.","Seeing him arrive, before he could speak, the Empress Dowager asked first, \"How is Your Majesty? Were you injured?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"I was not injured, please don't worry, Mother.\"","The Empress Dowager looked him up and down, and seeing that he indeed didn't appear to be injured, she nodded, clasped her hands together and chanted \"Amitabha Buddha, thank the ancestors and gods for protecting Your Majesty's great fortune.\"","She looked truly like a mother concerned for her son.","However, Yuwen Lan heard the Empress Dowager sigh in her heart, [Fortunately, it was just a scare. The time is not right yet, how could anything happen now?]","He secretly frowned.","What did she mean by \"the time\"?","Then he heard the Empress Dowager ask him, \"I heard Lady Li was injured?\"","Yuwen Lan composed himself and replied, \"Yes, she was stabbed by Consort Xu's weapon while trying to protect me.\"","The Empress Dowager clicked her tongue in sympathy, \"Poor child, how severe is her injury? Should we send Judge Zhang to take a look?\"","[Last time Zhang Shengkang was only 70% certain, I wonder if he can be sure this time?]","Yuwen Lan's heart sank, but he maintained a neutral expression and said, \"There's no need to trouble Judge Zhang. The imperial physician has already seen her and said it's just a flesh wound, nothing serious.\"","The Empress Dowager could only nod and say, \"That's good. I didn't expect Lady Li, at such a young age, to have such courage and loyalty. Your Majesty should reward her well.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"I was thinking the same. Once her wound is better, I will reward her.\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound of agreement, then said, \"Don't forget to thoroughly investigate that assassin. To have hidden in the palace for three years, it's truly frightening.\"","\"I have already detained her and brought people from her mother's family to the capital. We will certainly deal with this severely.\"","Yuwen Lan looked at the Empress Dowager and said, \"It's my fault for being negligent in security that Mother was frightened this time.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"There are always gaps even in the tightest security. Your Majesty is busy with affairs of state every day, how could you pay attention to such things? Don't blame yourself too much, but if anyone was derelict in their duties in this matter, they certainly can't be let off.\"","Yuwen Lan agreed, \"Mother, please rest now. I'll go take care of this matter.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, and Yuwen Lan left the hall.","On his way back to Qianming Palace, he pondered in his heart. When the Empress Dowager saw him earlier, she thought to herself how fortunate it was that nothing had happened.","It seems she didn't know about this assassination attempt beforehand.","So her plan to adopt Jing probably has nothing to do with Yuwen Hao.","But she still wanted to send Judge Zhang to examine Yanshu's body just now.","This confirms that the Empress Dowager has indeed guessed his problem, so she plans to adopt Jing as a way of choosing the next heir.","Having figured this out, his heart sank even further.","It turns out that after so many years of nurturing, there was still not a shred of true affection.","The night was deep, and because Yanshu was injured, Yuwen Lan didn't want to disturb her rest, so he returned to Qianming Palace.","After washing up and changing clothes, he heard that the Minister of Justice, Vice Minister of Rites, and Chief Eunuch of the Inner Court were already waiting outside the hall.","He summoned them before him and asked, \"What have you found?\"","The Minister of Justice bowed his head and said, \"Your Majesty, the Xu family members were just brought to the imperial prison for identification. They said the current Consort Xu is not the original Xu family daughter.\"","This result was within expectations.","Originally, Consort Xu's family was the prefect of Suizhou, but Suizhou was close to the capital and had no connection with Yuwen Hao. For Yuwen Hao to use their identity to plant an agent, he must have switched the original Consort Xu.","Fortunately, he had noticed in advance and sent the Imperial Guard to verify in Suizhou, otherwise the Xu family wouldn't have been able to rush to the capital so quickly.","At this moment, he gave a cold laugh, \"Very well, a palace consort was replaced with an assassin, and no one noticed.\"","The selection of palace ladies was the responsibility of the Ministry of Rites. Hearing this, the Vice Minister of Rites immediately broke out in a cold sweat, falling to his knees and kowtowing, \"We know our crime.\"","Yuwen Lan said coldly, \"Investigate further. I want to know who this woman really is.\"","Everyone responded affirmatively.","The Minister of Justice then reported, \"We have just searched the Lingbo Palace and haven't found any secret correspondence with the outside world for now.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"If there were secret letters, would she keep them by her side for you to find?\"","The Minister of Justice flushed with shame and quickly bowed his head, saying, \"We are incompetent.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Check the scarf that the King of Liaodong gave her that day.\"","Scarf?","The Minister of Justice was stunned for a moment, then realized. Indeed, among recent items from outside, there was only that scarf.","He hurriedly agreed and withdrew to investigate again.","The Chief Eunuch of the Inner Court, Yao Shun, then came forward and said, \"Your Majesty, we have already tortured her, but that assassin is very tight-lipped and refuses to confess.\"","Refuses to confess?","The emperor gave a cold smile and said, \"Just tell her one thing: her child died long ago, and the one she has now is a substitute found by that man.\"","The Chief Eunuch of the Inner Court paused, and although he couldn't quite make sense of it, he quickly agreed and returned to the imperial prison.","About an hour later, the Minister of Justice and the Chief Eunuch of the Inner Court, Yao Shun, returned together to report.","Yao Shun spoke first, \"Your Majesty, she confessed. She said it was the King of Liaodong who instructed her!\"","The Minister of Justice also hurriedly said, \"We took apart that sable scarf, and after wetting and heating it, we discovered a line of secret writing inside. It indeed was the King of Liaodong ordering her to act during this visit to the capital.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Arrest the King of Liaodong immediately.\"","Just as Yanshu had predicted, by the time the fake Consort Xu's assassination attempt failed, the King of Liaodong and his wife had already fled.","However, the emperor was prepared and had them captured just as they reached the outskirts of the capital.","That night in the Hall of Diligent Government, all the important court officials gathered.","From his throne, Yuwen Lan coldly looked down at the kneeling King of Liaodong and his wife.","\"I believe I have treated you well. Why did you send someone to assassinate me?\"","But Yuwen Hao said, \"I have been wronged, Your Majesty. That assassin was not sent by me.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment, \"If it wasn't you who sent her, why were you two in such a hurry to escape back to Liaodong?\"","Yuwen Hao said, \"Because I heard rumors that the assassin had implicated me, and I was afraid of misunderstandings.\"","Upon hearing this, the entire court of civil and military officials laughed. What kind of nonsensical logic was this?","At that moment, an official from the Ministry of Justice presented the fur scarf found in the Lingbo Palace. After washing and heating it, a line of text appeared inside: \"This is the best opportunity.\"","Yuwen Hao continued to quibble, \"I don't know why this is so. This seems like a false accusation.\"","\"Is that so?\" Yuwen Lan continued, \"You claim the evidence is fabricated, but why did you two leave the capital without imperial permission? If you were afraid of misunderstanding, why did you leave your own child in Liaodong and bring someone else's child to the capital, falsely claiming it as your own? This alone is a capital offense of deceiving the emperor!\"","As he finished speaking, the two were indeed stunned.","However, Yuwen Hao still insisted, \"Your Majesty, I truly don't understand what you're saying. The child I brought to the capital is indeed my own flesh and blood.\"","Yuwen Lan coldly smiled, \"You'll understand soon enough. They're already on their way to the capital.\"","At these words, the Liaodong King's Wife visibly panicked and quickly looked at Yuwen Hao, \"My lord...\"","Yuwen Hao, however, maintained, \"I have a clear conscience.\"","The Liaodong King's Wife, now like an ant on a hot pan, thought for a moment and couldn't help but address the emperor, \"Your Majesty, please don't punish the innocent children, especially since we are innocent.\"","Yuwen Lan said coldly, \"If you confess truthfully, I can spare them from being implicated by their father's crimes.\"","Yuwen Hao shouted harshly, \"Don't believe him! We're in his hands now, he can kill us with just a word.\"","Yuwen Lan, however, smiled, \"I never lie. Moreover, with all the court officials here as witnesses, if I were to go back on my word later, I would be the laughingstock of the empire.\"","Seeing the situation, the Liaodong King's Wife thought for a moment and suddenly said, \"I beg Your Majesty for mercy. This was all the King of Liaodong's idea alone. I tried hard to dissuade him, but he wouldn't listen...\"","...","Early the next morning, Yuwen Lan came to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","\"The King of Liaodong attempted assassination and rebellion, deceiving the emperor. I have stripped him of his title and confined him to the outskirts of the capital. Considering his wife's voluntary confession, she will be sent to the Yuzhen Palace to practice cultivation.\"","After he finished speaking, the Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Your Majesty is merciful. The spirit of our ancestor in heaven will be comforted.\"","Yuwen Lan continued, \"Although Mother likes those three children, they are not actually Yuwen Hao's flesh and blood, but replacements he found. I have already sent them back to their birth parents.\"","He paused, then deliberately added, \"However, if Mother likes Yuwen Hao's real children, I can bring them into the palace to keep you company. They are still young, and with proper nurturing, they should grow up well.\"","The Empress Dowager, however, said, \"They are still the offspring of a traitor. I fear they might be used to cause trouble in the future. Let's not.\"","Yuwen Lan then said, \"If that's the case, I'll have them sent to Yongfu Temple. Considering they are of our ancestral bloodline, I will assign people to educate them, to prevent them from following their father's path.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Your Majesty is merciful.\"","In her heart, however, she laughed coldly, [Well, isn't this perfect? The Yuwen clan might just die out.]","Yuwen Lan said, \"I know Mother is lonely in the palace. In the future, I will strive to produce heirs, so you can enjoy family life to the fullest.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"That's what I want to see the most.\"","In her heart, she thought, [I hope you can.]","Yuwen Lan, not wanting to say more, took his leave from the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Yanshu, in her nearly twenty years of life, had never been \"injured\" so severely.","Well, actually, the hairpin hadn't cut very deep. Apart from some skin pain, she was fine.","But Rendong had followed the emperor's orders and wouldn't let her get out of bed.","She endured for three days, but by the fourth day, she couldn't take it anymore.","Damn, if she had known being injured would be so uncomfortable, she would have definitely jumped in front that day.","This was like being in prison - she couldn't get out of bed, couldn't write her novels, and had to eat bland, low-fat, low-salt meals for the sick.","Who could stand this?!!","The System spoke up to comfort her, [Misfortune might be a blessing in disguise. A small wound might bring good fortune.]","Yanshu was skeptical, [What good fortune? Being forced to lie in bed and gain weight?]","Just then, an announcement came from outside the hall, \"His Majesty has arrived...\"","The System chimed, [Here comes the good fortune.]","Yanshu, [???]","Before the System could answer her, Yuwen Lan had already entered the hall.","Yanshu thought it was too late to get out of bed anyway, so she just leaned back and said, \"This concubine greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan walked to the bedside in a few steps, his eyes full of concern, \"How are you? Have you gotten better these past few days?\"","Yanshu was about to say she was fine, but remembering what the System had just said, she suddenly changed her mind and said with a pained expression, \"It still hurts a bit.\"","Hehe, maybe he'd feel touched and guilty and reward her with some silver!","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Still so fond of money?","But what use was money in the palace?","So he smiled and said, \"You've done a great service in saving me. I must reward you properly.\"","Reward?","Yanshu pondered, could this be the good fortune the System mentioned?","Great, great, come on, give her lots of money!!!","But then she heard him say, \"I will order the Ministry of Rites to issue a decree promoting you to the rank of Consort.\"","Yanshu was stunned, \"Consort?\"","At the same time, the System spoke again, [As they say, fortune favors the bold. Congratulations, my friend!]","Yanshu, \"...\"","Some fortune favoring the bold indeed."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30","paragraphs":["Yanshu hadn't expected to be promoted to the rank of Consort.","After all, she knew that a consort's rank in the harem was closely tied to her family's status - the higher the rank, the higher her family's position.","For example, the former Consort Li came from Earl Yongliang's Mansion, while the current Consort An's grandfather was the Minister of Rites.","But her father was just an Assistant Magistrate in a small county...","Yuwen Lan heard her doubts and smiled, saying, \"I will also transfer your father to work in the capital and move your whole family to the imperial city.\"","Yanshu was shocked: \"!!!\"","Even her father was getting promoted?","And her family would all move to the capital?","Didn't this mean she might have a chance to see her grandmother, parents and brother in the future?!","Just then, she heard Yuwen Lan say, \"If there's an opportunity, I can arrange for you to meet them.\"","Yanshu couldn't help exclaiming in delight, \"Is Your Majesty telling the truth?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and smiled, \"Why would I need to deceive you?\"","Yanshu was so happy she couldn't stop grinning. She quickly said, \"This humble consort thanks Your Majesty for your great kindness!\"","Although it wasn't a lot of money, she preferred this even more!","She could finally see her family again!","Yuwen Lan's lips curled into a smile as he asked, \"Are you happy now?\"","\"Yes,\" Yanshu said, trying hard to keep her smile from being too exaggerated.","Hehe, it seems this injury wasn't suffered in vain. The saying \"fortune favors the bold\" really is true.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Fortune favors the bold???","Then he heard her think: [So no matter what situation I'm in from now on, even if it means risking my life, I've got to hold tight to this golden thigh! Go for it!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Is it really necessary to go that far?","True to the emperor's word, by afternoon, the imperial edict promoting her to consort had been issued.","Hu An, the head eunuch of the Department of Imperial Ceremonies, came in his official robes holding the edict, smiling at Yanshu and saying, \"Please receive the imperial edict, my lady.\"","Yanshu complied. Since she was still \"injured,\" she knelt on the ground supported on either side by Rendong and Lianxin, and respectfully said, \"This humble consort receives the edict.\"","Hu An then read aloud above her head: \"By the grace of Heaven, the Emperor decrees: Lady Li of Noble Deportment is virtuous and talented, outstanding in beauty and character, noble in personality, quick-witted in nature. She is hereby granted the title of Consort Yi. May she be diligent and respectful in the palace, further displaying the glory of the imperial harem. By imperial order!\"","Yanshu kowtowed and said, \"This humble consort thanks His Majesty for his great kindness.\"","Tsk, the officials who draft these edicts really are talented!","Look at all these fancy words - so unique. Especially that last line - she probably couldn't even write some of those characters.","After musing on this, Rendong and Lianxin carefully helped her up, and the palace maids around her began to offer congratulations: \"Congratulations to Consort Yi.\"","Yanshu was also delighted and quickly told Rendong to reward everyone.","Ahem, now that she'd been promoted, her monthly allowance had tripled. She wasn't short on money anymore!","Everyone was happy, and Hu An also left cheerfully with his reward to report back, thinking to himself as he walked:","She was only promoted to Noble Lady on the 12th of the last lunar month, and now she's been made a consort on the 6th of the first month - this is rare even in the history of the palace!","Her future prospects are limitless!","On the 6th day of the first lunar month, the New Year's holiday for the imperial court was over. All government offices resumed operations, and the emperor became busy again.","At the start of the new year, Yuwen Lan issued five decrees in succession, covering taxes, imperial examinations, water conservancy, official transfers, and more.","As a result, Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong had been busy drafting edicts and imperial orders in the imperial study.","Seeing that it was almost noon and official business was finally winding down, Scholar Zou seized the opportunity to ask, \"Your Majesty, have you had any news lately of that Carefree Young Master?\"","Carefree Young Master?","Yuwen Lan was a bit surprised and asked, \"Do you need something from her?\"","Scholar Zou hurriedly said, \"Your subject does indeed have a matter... Now that the New Year has passed, I wonder if this young master has any new works coming out? Many booksellers have been hounding me for information, wanting to print and sell new stories. People both in and outside the city are eagerly anticipating them.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","There are actually booksellers chasing after Yanshu's stories?","He said, \"Is that really true?\"","Zou Mozhong said with a serious face, \"How could your subject dare to speak falsely before Your Majesty? Some booksellers have already doubled their prices, and some have even come to my home with gifts, all hoping to get their hands on the Carefree Young Master's manuscripts.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This was truly beyond his expectations.","He coughed and said, \"...She's been feeling unwell recently and isn't able to write.\"","Scholar Zou immediately looked worried and said, \"She's ill? What kind of illness? Is it serious? Has she seen a doctor? Should I send someone to check on her?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He could only say, \"That's not necessary. She's already seen a doctor and just needs to rest for a few days to recover.\"","Scholar Zou finally relaxed a little.","Then he asked again, \"Well... does this young master need any money? If there's a need, please tell Your Majesty to let her know she can ask me...\"","Before he could finish, he saw the emperor's brow furrow. \"Why do you ask such a thing?\"","Scholar Zou hurriedly explained, \"Your subject just noticed that this young master always seems in a rush for book fees, so I thought perhaps her family circumstances might not be very good. And now that she's fallen ill... In any case, we can't let such a talented person go hungry.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What? Poor family circumstances???","He felt quite speechless, but couldn't explain the real situation to Zou Mozhong. After holding back for a while, he could only say, \"She's not short of money. There's no need to worry.\"","\"That's good, that's good.\"","Scholar Zou finally set his mind at ease. After thinking for a moment, he asked again, \"Well, doesn't this young master have any manuscripts already written? The booksellers are really quite anxious. If there are any, we could print those first.\"","This...","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment and said, \"I'll have to ask her.\"","Yanshu was also very busy today.","After receiving the promotion edict in the morning, palace maids from the Imperial Wardrobe Bureau came to take her measurements, preparing to make various everyday and formal outfits for her new rank.","As soon as the Wardrobe Bureau people left, the Office of Imperial Treasures sent her several sets of jewelry, all exquisitely crafted and extraordinary.","She had just put away the jewelry and hadn't even eaten lunch when she saw Fu Hai arrive, followed by two young eunuchs, each carrying a box.","Yanshu asked curiously, \"What brings Eunuch Fu here?\"","Fu Hai smiled like a flower and said, \"This servant comes on His Majesty's orders to bring treasures for Consort Yi.\"","Treasures?","Yanshu was a bit confused, but could only say, \"This humble consort thanks His Majesty for his kindness.\"","Then she asked curiously, \"What exactly is it?\"","Fu Hai smiled and said, \"My lady will know when you open the boxes.\"","Tsk, still being mysterious?","Yanshu thought to herself, fine, she'd open them. The emperor wouldn't possibly give her two boxes of silver.","So she told Rendong to open the boxes.","But the moment the lids were lifted, her eyes were nearly blinded by the glare.","It wasn't silver indeed, it was gold!!!","That's right!","Two boxes of genuine gold ingots! Glittering and shining, almost blinding her eyes!!!","Yanshu was stunned.","After a long while, she finally remembered to ask Fu Hai, \"This... this... why has His Majesty given me these?\"","Was this some kind of hidden benefit of being a consort?","Fu Hai was actually a bit confused himself, only knowing that as soon as Scholar Zou had left, His Majesty had ordered him to bring these over.","He could only tell her, \"Naturally, it's because His Majesty is considerate of my lady and has specially bestowed these upon you.\"","He's being considerate of her?","Yanshu thought to herself, could this be compensation for her injury?","Well, that's fine too!!!","In any case, this was given to her by him! It's not like she stole it!","Today was truly an auspicious day. First a promotion and now money, the good news just kept coming one after another, almost too much to handle!","Yanshu was beaming with joy and quickly told Rendong to reward Fu Hai.","Ha, she wasn't just not short of money now! She was suddenly rich!","Just these two boxes of gold ingots were enough for her to live comfortably for two lifetimes!","She had to say, this injury was really worth it!","She'd be happy even if it left a scar!","Fu Hai also smiled as he accepted the reward and thanked her, thinking to himself as he walked out:","In the past, when emperors bestowed gifts on favored consorts, it was usually jewelry, silk, or various rare treasures.","This emperor is something else - the other day he gave a golden bowl, and today he directly gave two boxes of gold ingots!","The key is, this consort is also happy with it. Look how delighted she was just now, her eyes almost disappeared from smiling so much.","Tsk tsk, you couldn't find a more perfectly matched pair even if heaven made them.","They're so compatible!","With two boxes of gold ingots falling from the sky, Yanshu was overjoyed.","Even her bland recuperation meal at noon tasted delicious.","Ha, what did it matter if there was less oil and salt now?","In the future, she'd be able to eat and drink to her heart's content!!!","After being promoted to a consort, the food would definitely be better!","Feeling delighted after lunch, she woke up from her nap with a smile.","Haha, now it seemed that as long as she clung tightly to the emperor's thigh, she would have money, power, and status. Happiness could be completely ignored.","Yanshu remained cheerful for most of the day. Even when Yuwen Lan came in the evening, she still had a bright smile on her face.","\"This concubine greets Your Majesty,\" she said, bowing sideways with one hand, her voice much sweeter than before.","Tsk tsk, this was her golden meal ticket!","Look at him, so sturdy, so tall, so handsome and dashing!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How did this turn into a rhyme?","And was \"golden meal ticket\" referring to him?","Ahem, hearing that made him blush a little...","However, seeing her like this put him in a good mood as well. He asked gently, \"How is your wound? Have you been changing the dressing regularly?\"","Yanshu nodded quickly, \"Thank you for Your Majesty's concern. This concubine's wound is much better now. The imperial physician has been coming to change the dressing on time. He says it should heal in two or three days.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly and continued, \"Recover quickly so you can do what you want. Today I heard that many booksellers outside want to publish your stories. But since you're still unwell, I had to tell them to wait a while longer.\"","Upon hearing this, Yanshu was surprised. \"Is what Your Majesty said true? Many booksellers want to publish this concubine's stories?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded leisurely, \"Of course it's true. Why would I lie to you?\"","But she suddenly became anxious, \"Then how could Your Majesty refuse such a good opportunity? This concubine only injured her right hand. If necessary, I could write with my left hand!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"??? You can write with your left hand?\"","\"Yes!\" Yanshu nodded eagerly, \"It would just be slower. If worst comes to worst, this concubine could even write by holding the brush in her mouth.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Write by holding the brush in her mouth?","Come to think of it, her right-handed writing was barely legible as it was.","If she wrote with her mouth, would it even be readable?","Tsk, feeling a bit afraid she might actually try writing with her mouth, he decided to stop teasing her and told her the truth, \"They asked if you have any manuscripts already written. If so, they could take those first.\"","\"I do, I do!\" Yanshu immediately nodded and ran to her desk to fetch a large stack of papers to show him.","\"These are all stories I've already written. Any of them would be fine to publish.\"","Yuwen Lan took them and looked through them, seeing there were four or five stories.","The title of the one on top was \"The Shrew's Clever Handling of the Philanderer.\"","He raised an eyebrow, \"This title seems quite different from your previous ones. What is it about?\"","Yanshu cleared her throat and explained, \"This story is about a merchant who appears proper on the surface but actually loves visiting brothels. Every time he leaves home on business, he stays in the red-light district, having such a good time that he forgets to return home. He even lavishly tips the prostitutes, but when it comes to household expenses, he's extremely stingy.\"","\"...\"","Yuwen Lan secretly wondered if this was talking about Xie Pei, the Southwestern Communications Commissioner.","He remembered hearing her say during the ice festival banquet that this man loved visiting brothels.","Moreover, that Xie Pei did indeed maintain a frugal appearance.","Sometimes he even wore old clothes to court, creating an image of being poor and honest.","So it turned out this man was actually two-faced?","He grew curious and asked, \"Then why is his wife called a 'shrew'?\"","Yanshu gave a knowing smile and said, \"That's just a reverse psychology technique to attract readers. Actually, his wife is quite virtuous. She's frugal in managing the household and works hard to raise the children. Because her husband doesn't give her enough money for household expenses, she even weaves and embroiders to earn extra money to supplement the family income.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Indeed virtuous. It's a pity to work so hard for such a man. It's really not worth it.\"","Yanshu said, \"Exactly! The most infuriating part is that this man doesn't show any gratitude. Every time he comes back from the brothels, he nitpicks at his wife, complaining about this and that!\"","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"Could it be that his wife doesn't know he frequents such places?\"","Yanshu replied, \"At first she didn't know, but eventually she found out. After the initial shock and heartbreak, this lady finally came to her senses.\"","Came to her senses?","Yuwen Lan thought to himself, according to her usual pattern, wouldn't this lady first divorce her husband and then work hard to establish her own business?","However, he saw her give a dark smile and say, \"This lady felt that all her past suffering had been in vain. In a fit of anger, she hired someone to pretend to be a robber and beat up her husband just as he was about to go out philandering. They beat him until his arms and legs were broken, leaving him unable to take care of himself.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"??? Then what happened?\"","Yanshu continued, \"After being beaten, of course he couldn't go philandering anymore. When he was carried back home, his wife took care of him, feeding him, giving him water, even helping him use the toilet, attending to his every need.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What kind of development was this?","He listened as she went on, \"It was only then that this man realized how good his wife was. Moved by her actions, he vowed to mend his ways and live a good life with his wife from then on.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"Is it just a story of a prodigal son returning home?\"","\"Of course not,\" Yanshu gave another knowing smile and continued, \"Just as he was finally recovering after three months, he forgot the vow he had made and started flirting with those prostitutes again. When his wife discovered this, she was finally furious beyond measure. So she had someone tamper with her husband's carriage. The next time her husband went out, the carriage had an accident and fell down a hillside.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","\"Did he die?\" he asked.","But he saw her smile contemptuously, \"Wouldn't that be too easy for him?\"","\"This lady had already prepared people to wait in the surrounding area. As soon as the accident happened, they went forward to rescue him, so this man had a narrow escape from death.\"","\"However, his injuries were even more severe than last time. He lost one eye, one arm was broken, one ear became deaf, and one leg was crippled.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Brutal.","But the story wasn't over yet.","He heard her continue, \"This time his wife refused to take care of him. She left him in a corner of the house, like a cat or dog, left to fend for himself. When she remembered, she would throw him a steamed bun. After enduring this for half a year, the man was finally able to get out of bed, but with a lame leg, blind eye, and deaf ear, he couldn't even go out if he wanted to. He could only stay at home obediently, like an invalid.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","It seemed this was finally the ending.","He was silent for a moment, then said, \"This story is quite different from your previous ones.\"","Yanshu asked, \"Does Your Majesty find it a bit dark?\"","\"Indeed,\" Yuwen Lan nodded, then asked her, \"Why did you choose this direction?\"","Yanshu gave a wicked smile and said, \"Because fighting violence with violence is also a kind of catharsis, so occasionally changing the style might be good. Who knows, maybe readers will like it!\"","She then added, \"Why don't Your Majesty take this story to the booksellers and see how readers respond?\"","\"Alright,\" Yuwen Lan nodded, then said, \"It's getting late, you should rest.\"","As he spoke, he seemed to be preparing to wash up.","Yanshu: \"???\"","Did this mean he was planning to sleep here?","She quickly said, \"But this concubine's injury hasn't healed yet.\"","Hey, her hand was still bandaged! Wouldn't it be too inhumane to squeeze in with her like this?","Yuwen Lan pretended not to hear and only said, \"Don't worry, I won't touch you.\"","Saying this, he entered the bathroom.","— Because of her injury, he hadn't come for several days, so that place had become uncomfortable again.","Heaven knows how anxious he was?","Now seeing that she was a bit better, of course he had to hurry over.","Yanshu, however, didn't understand and stood there in a daze for a while. Seeing there was really no way out, she had no choice but to call Rendong and the others in to make the bed and spread the bedding. She also sent someone to Qianming Palace to fetch his morning court robes for tomorrow.","Well, where in the world do free lunches fall from the sky?","Since she had been promoted, she had to work, right? In the adult world, there's no such thing as \"easy,\" alas.","Yuwen Lan, who was bathing in the bathroom: \"???\"","Work? Work?","Did it have to be like this???","When everything was ready and Yuwen Lan came out after washing, the two of them got into bed.","True to his word, Yuwen Lan didn't touch her even with a finger. He only said, \"Sleep,\" and closed his eyes.","— Whether it was psychological or not, he felt that this bed was more comfortable than the imperial bed in Qianming Palace.","As for Yanshu, she was even more carefree. Although she had been complaining about him earlier, it didn't take long before she was sound asleep.","Lulled by her long and peaceful breathing, Yuwen Lan also gradually drifted off to sleep.","Unlike his previous dreams, this time he dreamed of entering a peach orchard.","The warm sunlight shone overhead, and a gentle breeze caressed his body. Yuwen Lan strolled leisurely through the peach orchard, seeing clusters of peach blossoms adorning the branches. Some even had peaches growing among them, creating a fantastical scene like a fairyland.","Suddenly, two peaches fell from a branch. His heart tightened, and he quickly reached out to catch them, successfully cradling them in his arms.","To his surprise, the peaches were soft and fluffy, just like clouds...","Yuwen Lan woke from his dream to find that Yanshu had somehow snuggled into his arms.","They were face to face, and looking down, he saw that indeed, two \"peaches\" were in his embrace.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He wondered how he could have such a strange dream out of nowhere.","Wasn't someone complaining about being crowded earlier before sleep?","Looking again, he saw her injured arm draped over his shoulder, as if embracing a large tree.","Yuwen Lan thought to himself, could she be treating him like a tree hollow again?","It was still early, and the night remained deep.","He wanted to move her arm back but feared touching her wound.","After some thought, he decided to let it be, closed his eyes, and went back to sleep.","Unexpectedly, she pressed even closer.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He tried calling out softly, \"Yanshu...\"","But there was no response.","Right, this girl wouldn't wake up until she'd had enough sleep.","He had no choice but to give up.","However, the peach orchard from his dream seemed to press tightly against his chest...","Yuwen Lan reached out and embraced her.","Mmm, it felt quite nice.","He curled his lips into a smile and finally fell asleep again.","The next morning when Yuwen Lan woke up, he found that... he had indeed recovered even more.","And, unprecedentedly so.","Yes, better than any time before.","Could it be thanks to the peach orchard?","But before he could ponder further, Fu Hai was already reminding him from outside the hall, \"Your Majesty, there's a court session today.\"","He responded with a sound of acknowledgment and got out of bed first.","Yuwen Lan was in a very good mood today, walking briskly back to Qianming Palace to hold court. After the court session ended, he didn't forget to give Yanshu's manuscript to Zou Mozhong.","Zou Mozhong quickly read through it once, praising it effusively again, and hurriedly took the manuscript to the book merchant.","However, just two days later, as Yanshu was eating breakfast, she heard the system say, [Someone is reporting you to the emperor.]","Yanshu was startled, [What? Reporting me? For what?]","The system said, [Your new story is once again extraordinary, so someone has taken it personally, saying your story is too dark and might corrupt the common people. They're currently memorializing against you in court.]","Yanshu immediately became interested—","Previously, Wei Ruzhang had only secretly arrested people, but now someone was actually openly memorializing against her because of a story?","Meanwhile, in the court—","Xie Pei, the Southwestern Communications Commissioner, said, \"Your Majesty, recently there's a person called 'Carefree Young Master' who has written several unorthodox stories, attempting to sensationalize. According to what I know, the stories from this person's pen are all shocking, and even seem to encourage women to harm their husbands. Their intentions are malicious, and I humbly request Your Majesty to arrest this person.\"","Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow, but before he could speak, Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong immediately refuted, \"Lord Xie must have misunderstood. As far as I know, the story you mentioned about a woman harming her husband is called 'The Clever Evil Wife's Treatment of a Philanderer'. It's actually a story about evil being repaid with evil.\"","\"In the story, a merchant has a virtuous wife, but he still goes out seeking pleasure. He pretends to be an upright person on the surface while secretly despising his lawfully wedded wife. Since the law can't do anything about such a hypocritical person, his wife had no choice but to resort to this strategy. Not everyone is as unscrupulous as this merchant, so how could it be accused of 'encouraging wives to harm their husbands'?\"","Wang Huaijin, the Vice Minister of Rites, also smiled and said, \"Indeed, these stories are all fictional. Moreover, most of the people reading these stories are men. Few women are literate, let alone reading stories. Lord Xie is overthinking it.\"","Unexpectedly, Xie Pei immediately jumped up and said, \"Lord Wang speaks too lightly of it. Women may not be very literate, but what if storytellers take these stories to recite? Then not only women, but children and the elderly will all know about these unorthodox and shocking stories!\"","Zou Mozhong shook his head again and said, \"Haven't storytellers been telling tales since ancient times? Isn't King Zhou killing his wife and son in 'Investiture of the Gods' shocking enough? How many people have imitated him in later generations?\"","Wang Huaijin also looked puzzled and said, \"Exactly, it's just a story, something for entertainment. Why is Lord Xie making such a big fuss about it?\"","As these words fell, everyone secretly muttered in their hearts—","[There are so many stories in the world, why is Xie Pei so worked up about this one? Could the story be about him?]","Yuwen Lan, sitting on the dragon throne, heard everyone's thoughts and spoke before Xie Pei could open his mouth again, \"Lord Xie's opinion alone is not enough to explain the issue. I have also read these stories and didn't find anything wrong with them.\"","Hearing this, Xie Pei was stunned.","What? The emperor had read them?","Then, then, then, would he suspect...","But before he could say anything else, he heard the emperor say, \"Court is dismissed.\"","And then he left the throne.","Meanwhile, in Ganlu Palace, Yanshu, who had learned about the whole process through the system, slapped the table and picked up her pen again.","How dare they say she's corrupting social morals?","Hmph, she had originally planned to leave this person some dignity, but now they can't blame her for not being polite!"]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31","paragraphs":["As night fell, Yuwen Lan entered Ganlu Palace to find Yanshu furiously writing at her desk.","She was so focused that she didn't even notice him enter.","It was Rendong who finally spoke up, \"My lady, His Majesty is here.\"","Only then did Yanshu look up and see him. She hurriedly stood up from her desk and bowed, \"This humble consort greets Your Majesty.\"","She then glanced out the window with a surprised look, \"What time is it?\"","\"It's 9 PM,\" Yuwen Lan answered, somewhat amazed. \"Have you lost track of time writing your novel?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"This consort wanted to finish quickly, so I didn't pay attention to the time.\"","\"Oh?\" Yuwen Lan grew curious, \"What kind of story is it this time?\"","Since she was nearly finished anyway, Yanshu cleared her throat and said, \"Today this consort wrote about an ungrateful person who ultimately gets their just deserts.\"","Yuwen Lan had already sat down nearby, looking ready to listen attentively. \"Let's hear it then.\"","Yanshu continued, \"Many years ago, there was a poor scholar who lived a very frugal life from childhood due to his family's poverty. So he resolved to study hard and make something of himself in the future.\"","\"This scholar did indeed have some talent. He passed the county and provincial exams, and was about to go to the capital for the Spring Imperial Examination. On his way to the capital, he met another candidate. This candidate came from a wealthy family, was generous, and liked to make friends. Hearing that the poor scholar was quite talented, he invited him to travel together. Along the way, he not only treated him to meals, but also shared boats and carriages with him, helping to pay his travel expenses. He took very good care of him.\"","\"But this scholar was narrow-minded and envious. He actually took advantage when the other wasn't paying attention, stole his travel money and ran off on his own.\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Then what happened?\"","To be honest, he still couldn't determine this person's identity from what he'd heard so far. He couldn't help but wonder if this was just a fictional story.","But logically, someone who repays kindness with evil shouldn't have a good ending, right?","Yet he heard her say, \"Later, unexpectedly, this scholar actually placed highly in the exam, while the one whose money he stole unfortunately failed.\"","Yuwen Lan hissed, \"His companion didn't report the theft?\"","Yanshu looked at him as if he were naive, \"This scholar had actually planned to steal the other's money from the beginning, so he gave a fake name at first. Even if the other wanted to report him, he couldn't find the person, let alone know about his success in the exam.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"This person was so calculating? Then what happened next?\"","Yanshu continued, \"Afterwards, this person smoothly entered officialdom, while his companion returned home in disappointment. When he tried to take the exam again, the scholar secretly used his position to sabotage him, causing him to fail repeatedly. Meanwhile, the scholar himself climbed higher and higher, eventually becoming an important court official.\"","An important court official?","Yuwen Lan was stunned. So it wasn't fictional?","The person was actually a court official?","Who could be so ungrateful that he didn't know about?","Not wanting to ask directly, he said, \"Then what happened after that?\"","He heard her say, \"Later, because he failed the exam repeatedly, that companion finally became discouraged and decided to go into business instead. However, because of his open and friendly nature, his business actually did quite well.\"","\"As for the scholar, because he was skilled at scheming and currying favor, his official career was very smooth at first. But later, he began to frequent brothels, and in the end died of venereal disease.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, this ending...","He knew who it was now.","However, he still didn't quite understand why she had written such a story about Xie Pei again?","Could it be that this was also Xie Pei's past experience?","He tentatively said, \"To me, this person seems somewhat similar to that merchant who visited brothels from the other day.\"","Yanshu nodded, \"Indeed they are quite similar. Your Majesty can think of it as an alternate life for that merchant. In any case, they both loved visiting brothels.\"","[Don't doubt it, it's him, your Southwestern Communications Commissioner Xie Pei! The most ungrateful bastard in history!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So it really was Xie Pei.","To think this person had done such an evil deed in his youth?","He thought for a moment, then said, \"It seems this person truly has poor character. This ending is even harsher than the last one.\"","Yanshu snorted, \"Bad people must face retribution, otherwise wouldn't everyone go do bad things? Regardless of reality, in this consort's stories, villains must always face their deserved fate.\"","[Hmph, if I wanted to wrong him I'd just stop writing! He even dared to file an imperial complaint? I'll let him know the consequences of messing with me!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, he was wondering why she had suddenly killed off Xie Pei again.","So it was because she learned about what happened in court this morning.","He nodded and said, \"This story is excellent. I think it should be spread far and wide, to let people understand the principle that evil deeds will be punished.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she quickly nodded, \"This consort thinks the same. Why not have Your Majesty take it to Scholar Zou tomorrow morning, and have the book merchants publish it quickly?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Why wait until tomorrow morning? We can send it over now.\"","Saying this, he instructed Fu Hai, \"Find someone to deliver Consort Yi's manuscript to the Hanlin Academy scholar's residence.\"","Fu Hai acknowledged and went to find a guard.","Yanshu: \"???\"","Why was he even more eager than her?","She saw him turn to look at her again and ask, \"By the way, have you finished writing?\"","Yanshu came back to her senses and hurriedly said, \"Just two more sentences.\"","Saying this, she quickly went back to her desk and finished the ending with a few brushstrokes.","That's right, revenge should be carried out as quickly as possible.","Not worrying about anything else for now, once Fu Hai found a guard, she handed over the newly dried manuscript.","Tsk, now to wait for that ungrateful Southwestern Communications Commissioner's reaction.","She was quite looking forward to it.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Was this... addicted to arguing?","A night passed.","Early the next morning, as Yanshu was leisurely enjoying her breakfast, she heard a message from the system.","[Your new novel has been printed overnight by book merchants. This morning as soon as the bookshops opened, over a hundred copies were sold.]","Over a hundred copies?","Yanshu's eyes lit up. [So my novels are already bestsellers?]","Selling over a hundred copies first thing in the morning, let's calculate how much silver this wave will bring in.","System: [Hey, is silver the focus right now?]","Yanshu: [...You're right. Has that damn Southwestern Communications Commissioner seen it yet?]","System: [This guy just bought a copy on his way home from court. Now he's hiding at home reading it.]","Tsk tsk, Yanshu really wanted to know what expression this person had.","Especially when he got to the part about himself dying of venereal disease.","She took a bite of her beef pastry, not forgetting to tell the system, [Remember to show me what he looks like after he finishes reading.]","System: [Gotcha.]","Yanshu then contentedly enjoyed her delicious meal.","Mmm, this beef filling burst with juice with each bite, the pastry crispy on the outside and soft on the inside. It was truly delicious!","Just as she was about to finish her beef pastry, the system finally sent another message: [There, that guy has finished reading. He angrily threw the book into the coal stove to burn it, and raged about finding a way to catch you.]","Yanshu raised an eyebrow. [He actually plans to catch me? Looks like he won't learn his lesson until it's too late.]","Alright, after she finished a bowl of pumpkin porridge, she would write in detail about how this person \"battled\" with various courtesans.","Oh right, she couldn't use the word \"battle\".","Given his abilities, she should use \"skirmish\" to describe it.","So, once she had filled her stomach, she prepared to get started.","But just as she picked up her brush, she heard the system ding again. [The emperor just issued two edicts.]","Yanshu: [Edicts? Doesn't the emperor issue decrees every day? What's special about these?]","System: [First, officials are strictly prohibited from visiting brothels. Second, there will be a strict investigation into the lifestyles of court officials. Anyone who has ever been involved in theft, robbery, illegal detention or other crimes, regardless of when they occurred, will be dismissed from office and held strictly accountable.]","[Think about it. Think carefully.]","\"...\"","Yanshu: [Ummm could it be that these edicts were inspired by my novel?]","Otherwise, how could they come so perfectly timed and so targeted?","However, she was also a bit worried for the emperor. After all, based on the gossip she had heard, most of the current court officials, especially the older ones, were basically not clean.","Once this edict came down, he might lose quite a few people.","System: [You think the emperor is stupid? Those old guys are either the previous emperor's people or the empress dowager's people. Isn't it better for the emperor to take this opportunity to remove them one by one and replace them with his own people?]","I see.","Yanshu suddenly understood.","Tsk, the Emperor is intelligent and capable, and even good-looking. If only he didn't have that one flaw.","Anyway, she no longer needed to write any \"instant battles\" now. She could just sit back and enjoy the show.","Tsk tsk, these two imperial edicts were so targeted. One wonders if that Southwestern Communications Commissioner was scared out of his wits?","In Qianming Palace.","Besides those two edicts, Yuwen Lan also ordered an increase in personnel for the Censorate and commanded the Ministry of Personnel to reform the official evaluation system, in order to strengthen supervision of the court and thoroughly rectify conduct.","So he spent the entire day busy with work.","As dusk fell, lamps were lit in the hall.","Fu Hai stepped forward and said to the monarch who was still reading memorials, \"Your Majesty, it's time for the meal to be served.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment, but then asked, \"What has Consort Yi been doing today?\"","Fu Bao hurriedly came forward to answer, \"Your Majesty, Consort Yi has been in Ganlu Palace all day. She had the kitchen send over many snacks like melon seeds and preserved fruits. She seems to be in a good mood.\"","In a good mood?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow.","Could it be because Xie Pei was frightened after reading her newly published story?","He decided, \"Have the imperial meal set up in Ganlu Palace. I'll dine there.\"","Fu Hai quickly acknowledged the order.","Meanwhile in Ganlu Palace, Yanshu had been eating melon seeds for most of the day and was just about to have dinner when she saw Fu Hai arrive.","Behind him followed a long line of palace servants, carrying various bowls, plates and food boxes.","Fu Hai said with a smile, \"His Majesty will dine here tonight. Please wait a moment, Consort.\"","Oh?","Yanshu's eyes immediately lit up - another chance to share the imperial meal?","She quickly agreed and went to one side to wait as the servants set the table.","Before long, an array of dishes blossomed on the table like flowers.","Yanshu scanned them: there was braised pork with melon, spicy tripe strips, fish fillets in milk sauce, duck feet with mushrooms, as well as eight-treasure chicken, salt and pepper chicken wings, mandarin fish slices, peppery fish soup, and three desserts - bird's nest pastries, two-colored bean cakes, and ruyi rolls.","This was actually a simplified menu compared to before, with ingredients like sea cucumber, abalone, deer tendon and quail tongues replaced by more down-to-earth options. But the imperial chefs' skills were superb, and the dishes were exquisite in appearance, aroma and flavor.","At this moment, the various fragrances assaulted Yanshu's nose all at once, making her stomach growl.","For the first time, she eagerly anticipated seeing the Emperor appear.","Fortunately, it wasn't long before Yuwen Lan showed up amid her eager expectations.","Yanshu's eyes brightened and she hurriedly led the others in a bow, saying, \"This consort greets Your Majesty.\"","[Finally he's here!!! Do you know how long I've been waiting for you???]","This made Yuwen Lan secretly raise an eyebrow -","Was she... finally missing him?","How rare.","However, her next thought was: [Hurry up and sit down at the table, don't waste time talking!!! Otherwise the salt and pepper wings and bird's nest pastries won't be crispy anymore!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Alright, so it was still about the food.","He could only say \"Rise\" and went to the table.","He wanted to say something more, but fearing her nagging, he simply started eating.","Seeing him pick up his chopsticks, Yanshu hurriedly followed suit.","Mmm, thankfully the salt and pepper wings were still crispy on the outside, while the chicken inside remained juicy. Not bad, not bad.","The braised pork with melon and fish fillets in milk sauce were both light and delicious. The duck feet with mushrooms were tender and flavorful. The eight-treasure chicken had hidden delights inside. The fish soup was fresh and spicy.","Especially the spicy tripe strips went very well with rice. Before she knew it, Yanshu had finished a whole bowl of rice.","Seeing her leisurely eating dessert and sipping fish soup, while inwardly marveling at how refreshingly sweet the bean cakes were, Yuwen Lan couldn't help asking, \"How come you have such a good appetite today?\"","Yanshu said with a grin, \"Because this consort is in a good mood today.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Why are you in a good mood? Did something good happen?\"","Yanshu casually replied, \"It's nothing much, just that my story writing is going smoothly, so I feel happy. Oh, Your Majesty should try these bird's nest pastries, they're so crispy they crumble!\"","But inwardly she thought, [Do you even need to ask? Of course it's because I'm delighted to see my opponent in trouble!]","[Ever since those two edicts were issued today, that damn Southwestern Communications Commissioner immediately panicked, fidgeting like an ant on a hot pan. He even slipped while going to the toilet and nearly fell into the latrine, hahahahaha]","Just thinking about it made Yanshu want to die laughing.","Yuwen Lan, however, twitched his lips imperceptibly.","What? Xie Pei nearly fell into the latrine?","He hadn't even received news of this yet, how did she already know in such detail?","Still, imagining that scene... it was indeed quite amusing.","Yuwen Lan picked up a bird's nest pastry to try.","Mmm, crispy on the outside with sweet and sour hawthorn filling inside. It really was delicious.","Perhaps infected by her mood, he was unable to suppress his expression and also curled up the corners of his mouth.","After dinner, it was still early, so the two decided to play chess to aid digestion.","However, Yanshu's skills were inferior and she was utterly defeated in three consecutive games.","Just as she was losing interest, Fu Hai entered the hall and said to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, the Imperial Guard has something to report.\"","The Imperial Guard were the Emperor's confidants, and usually reported matters that outsiders shouldn't know about.","Yanshu's eyes rolled and she hurriedly said, \"This consort will go take a bath first and not disturb Your Majesty.\"","Damn, clinging to the big boss was really not easy. It was too difficult to endure with her meager chess skills just to please the Emperor.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had already gone easy on her to save face.","Oh well, it seemed this activity could be eliminated from their interactions in the future.","So he nodded, \"Very well.\"","He rose and went to the outer hall.","Upon seeing him, the Imperial Guard immediately reported, \"Your Majesty, since receiving the edict today, the Southwestern Communications Commissioner Xie Pei has been in a panic. In the evening he fell at home and injured his tailbone. He's currently bedridden and likely won't be able to attend court tomorrow.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. Injured his tailbone?","It seems he really might have fallen while using the toilet?","Then he heard the Imperial Guard continue, \"We have gone through the examination records from twenty years ago one by one, and found a candidate from Jingyang who is likely the person Your Majesty mentioned. His name is Hu Zi'ang, and he's from a neighboring hometown to Xie Pei, so it's very possible they traveled together. Moreover, the year Xie Pei passed the exam with high honors, this man failed. Afterwards, he came to the capital six times in a row, all ending in failure. Later he started doing business, and now owns several silk shops and tea houses in Chang'an, doing quite well.\"","So there really was such a person...","Yuwen Lan said, \"Summon him to the capital to identify Xie Pei. If the incident from back then is true, submit it to the Ministry of Personnel and the Court of Judicial Review for investigation.\"","- Since the edict had already been issued, there had to be results. If they didn't make an example of someone, the officials wouldn't take it seriously.","The Imperial Guard acknowledged the order and withdrew.","In Zhongcui Palace.","After Consort Zhou was demoted, the Emperor had her continue living here out of consideration for the Empress Dowager's face, and the interior decorations had not been removed.","However, the palace that still looked lavish and grand was no longer as lively as before.","Tonight, Consort Zhou also waited for a long time before finally seeing Consort An enter with her maid Liu Di.","\"This consort greets Your Highness.\"","Consort An unhurriedly performed a curtsy.","Consort Zhou coldly looked her up and down, then said with a sneer, \"In the past you used to come to me all the time for no reason. Now it's hard for me to even see you once. I waited half an hour for you tonight!\"","Consort An said, \"Please calm your anger, Your Highness. I was ill the past two days and didn't dare come for fear of passing on the illness to you. Just now the imperial physician was checking my pulse, so I was delayed a bit.\"","Consort Zhou knew the other party already looked down on her, so she snorted rudely, \"Don't think that just because Consort Li is in the Cold Palace and Consort Ning hasn't finished her confinement, you're now the top-ranked in the harem. That Li Yanshu has been promoted to Consort and is now of the same rank as you.\"","How could Consort An not hear the provocation in those words?","So she simply continued with her head bowed, \"Your Highness speaks truly. At this rate, it may not be long before she's of the same rank as Your Highness.\"","\"You...\"","Consort Zhou choked with anger.","After a moment, she deliberately laughed and said, \"So you're just going to watch that country bumpkin become your equal? Aren't you upset?\"","Consort An only said, \"There's nothing to be done about it. Haven't you seen it yet, Your Highness? His Majesty's heart is with Consort Yi. No matter what happens, he will always protect her. Ordinary tricks won't work on her at all.\"","It was meant as honest advice, but who knew Consort Zhou would deliberately provoke her again, \"Weren't you always so clever and resourceful? Even the Empress Dowager thought highly of you. What, have you run out of tricks now too?\"","Consort An gave up.","An smiled and said, \"Your Highness flatters me. I'm but an ordinary person. Besides, since that day after the ceremony, my grandfather has been staying at home and hasn't attended court. I have no way to help right now.\"","Hah, only someone as foolish as her would still try to use others as pawns in such a situation.","Consort Zhou became angry and snorted, \"If the Minister of Rites hadn't been so quick to admit guilt that day, would we be in this situation now? If there's anyone to blame, it's him for losing his nerve!\"","But Consort An replied, \"Even if my grandfather hadn't admitted guilt, the Duke of Cheng'en would still have fainted during the ceremony. Surely Your Highness can't blame my grandfather for your current predicament.\"","\"You...\"","Consort Zhou's eyes widened, looking as if she was about to raise her hand to strike.","What an insolent wretch, daring to talk back to her now!","Just then, the sound of the night watchman came from outside.","\"The air is dry... mind your fires...\"","Unmistakably, it was Consort Wang's voice again.","Consort An lowered her head and said, \"It seems they're about to lock up for the night. I won't disturb Your Highness any longer. I must pay respects to the Empress Dowager in the morning.\"","With that, she turned and left the hall.","The Lantern Festival was approaching, but the night wind still held a biting chill.","Liu Di followed behind her mistress and, recalling the earlier scene, asked with concern, \"My lady, Consort Zhou is known for her cruelty. After how you spoke to her today, do you think she might retaliate against you?\"","Consort An gave a contemptuous smile. \"Retaliate against me? Who in the palace still listens to her now? Can she order anyone around? Even the Empress Dowager won't see her anymore.\"","That was true.","The Empress Dowager used to favor Consort Zhou the most, but ever since her father had disgraced himself at the ceremony and she was demoted, the Empress Dowager no longer received her.","Even on the rare occasions they met at palace banquets, the Empress Dowager wouldn't spare her a glance, her disdain quite evident.","On the contrary, the Empress Dowager had been summoning her mistress frequently for conversations lately, showing clear signs of favor.","Liu Di felt somewhat reassured at this.","As the two walked on, they saw two guards in fish-scale armor striding quickly from not far away.","Liu Di was startled and said, \"Why are there Imperial Guards in the rear palace?\"","Consort An looked in the direction they had come from and said, \"Isn't that the direction of Ganlu Palace? They must be going to see His Majesty.\"","Liu Di sighed softly and said in a low voice, \"Even though Consort Zhou has lost favor, His Majesty still only visits Ganlu Palace. When will he come to see you?\"","Consort An smiled and said, \"The opportunity will come eventually.\"","Though as she had said earlier, ordinary tricks wouldn't work on Li Yanshu, no one was perfect.","She didn't believe Li Yanshu would never make a mistake.","The road ahead was long; she would wait and see.","After the Imperial Guards had passed, Yuwen Lan paced back to the inner chamber alone, his mind still pondering.","Xie Pei's fall, as well as the events of his imperial examination years ago... she had predicted it all accurately again.","Since all other possibilities had been ruled out, there seemed to be only one explanation left.","— She likely possessed an extraordinary ability like himself, just different from mind-reading.","But it seemed even more powerful than mind-reading.","No wonder she wanted to write novels. With so many secrets bottled up inside, she must have felt the need to write them out.","He was shocked, of course, but also somewhat moved.","It was fortunate that she had a pure heart. If such an ability fell into the hands of an evil person, what then?","But was it not a waste of talent to let her just write novels?","Imagine if a man had this ability, he could use it in many positions to benefit the country and accomplish great things...","Suddenly, the sound of footsteps reached his ears. Yuwen Lan looked up to see Yanshu emerging from her bath.","Her eyes were bright, her cheeks rosy, her thin lips red as cherries in May.","Yuwen Lan suddenly felt thirsty.","His earlier thoughts were temporarily set aside.","— With such a beauty by his side, he'd better focus on getting well soon.","Thinking thus, Yanshu had already climbed onto the bed.","Yuwen Lan pulled her into his arms and asked softly, \"What did you do today?\"","Yanshu, completely unaware of what had transpired, replied truthfully, \"This consort didn't do much today, just had some snacks and played cards with Rendong and the others.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. \"Didn't write your novel?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"This consort felt a bit tired these past couple of days and wanted to rest, so I didn't write today.\"","[Hehe, mainly I was too busy enjoying the drama! Just watching old man Xie panic like an ant on a hot pan today was enough to kill me with laughter!]","[Imagine if one day this man sees the intimate details of his encounters with courtesans in a novel, wouldn't he just faint on the spot? Hahaha, I can hardly wait!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What?","Bed... intimate details?","How could she even know about this?!!","This ability didn't seem so good after all.","So he said, \"Don't stay cooped up in the palace all day. The weather is getting warmer, you should go out for walks more often.\"","Yanshu thought to herself, [Easy for you to say. If I, the target of everyone's hatred, go out for a walk, how much more resentment would I invite! Who knows if someone might push me into a lake again. Or oil the ground to make me slip? Frightening!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What nonsense was all this?","But he heard her say aloud, \"This consort is still somewhat afraid of the cold. Moreover, the weather hasn't fully warmed up yet. It wouldn't be good if I carelessly caught a chill.\"","Unexpectedly, as soon as she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan suddenly took her hand and said, \"Don't be afraid. You are mine, and I will protect you well.\"","As he spoke, he gently kneaded her hand in his palm, feeling her long, delicate fingers, soft as tender spring onions.","Just as he was enjoying the moment, he heard her think to herself, [Those words sound nice, but if one day you no longer need me as your shield, wouldn't you just kick me aside?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Is this really what she thinks?","He looked at her seriously and said, \"I never speak empty words. Whatever I say, I will certainly do.\"","At these words, she finally paused and looked at him intently.","After meeting his gaze for a moment, she suddenly thought, [Oh my god, he looks so attractive when he's serious!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Why did she always add those two words before complimenting him?","But still...","She was finally captivated by him.","Yuwen Lan felt pleased and wanted to kiss her.","But just as he was about to lean in, he heard her think, [Tsk, if I were to write a novel about an emperor one day, would it be a hit?]","[A man perfect in every way but with a fatal flaw! Just thinking about this premise is exciting!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Quick, stop right there!"]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32","paragraphs":["Of course, Yanshu was just imagining.","This was an enormously serious matter. Even if the subject matter was explosive, it wouldn't matter - how could she actually write about it?","Yuwen Lan breathed a sigh of relief.","Then he heard her pondering, [Perhaps I should write about those ministers and help the emperor clean up the court politics. At least that would benefit the country and people. What should I write about tomorrow? Maybe the incident from last year when the nephew of the Vice Minister of Personnel bullied his classmates at the Imperial Academy?]","Yuwen Lan frowned to himself. Was there really such an incident?","Well, it seemed he wouldn't be getting much sleep tonight either.","The next day at court, everyone was surprised to discover that Xie Pei, the Southwestern Communications Commissioner, had suddenly fallen ill.","Tsk, the timing of this illness was certainly suspicious. After all, just two days ago he had been bouncing around insisting on impeaching a writer of story books. How could he suddenly be sick?","Two days later, the Imperial Censorate formally impeached him in court. It turned out to be related to a theft case from many years ago.","Apparently, over twenty years ago, while on his way to take the imperial examinations, he had stolen money from a fellow traveler. After luckily passing the exam, he had repeatedly abused his power to persecute the victim, causing him to fail the exams time and again.","\"...\"","Everyone suddenly realized that the popular story book from a few days ago, \"The Greedy Man Dies Under the Flowers,\" had actually been about him.","Tsk tsk tsk, not only had he stolen from his companion back then, but he was also apparently fond of visiting brothels?","Who knows if he had contracted any venereal diseases...","While everyone was speculating, more news came - upon investigation by the Imperial Censorate, his subordinates and personal servants all testified that he indeed loved to visit prostitutes. He had even gotten into a brawl with a merchant over a famous courtesan by the Qinhuai River, hiring people to beat and cripple his rival...","Everyone: \"...\"","It matched up with that previous story \"The Wicked Wife Cleverly Cures Her Philandering Husband\"...","Tsk tsk tsk, who knew his character was so despicable! He deserved to be the first sacrifice to the new edict!","Half a month later, Xie Pei was dismissed from his post as Southwestern Communications Commissioner. The crime of stealing money from others years ago was added to his offenses, and he received twenty lashes.","However, considering his family was unaware of his misdeeds, the punishment did not extend to them.","As for Xie Pei himself, he had already taken a fall, and now with twenty lashes on top of that, one can imagine his miserable state. It was said he had to be carried home in the end.","After all his scandals were exposed, even his wife became angry. Her previously virtuous attitude vanished, and she left him to fend for himself.","It truly matched the ending in the story book.","But this turn of events made people even more curious - who exactly was this \"Carefree Scholar\" who wrote the story books?","How could he know the details of events from so many years ago so clearly?","As the first major \"case\" of the new year, by the time it was all over, the Lantern Festival was approaching.","One morning, while the emperor was reading memorials in his study, Fu Hai came to report, \"Your Majesty, the lanterns offered as tribute from Quanzhou have arrived.\"","This was one of the palace rituals for the Lantern Festival.","Every year, lanterns would be offered as tribute from the common people to the palace, symbolizing peace and prosperity for the nation. The emperor would then present some of these lanterns to the Empress Dowager in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, and award the rest to the various consorts, symbolizing the royal family celebrating together with the people.","As soon as Fu Hai finished speaking, Yuwen Lan suddenly remembered something.","There seemed to be a young lady who loved lanterns very much.","Even an ordinary revolving lantern could make her happy for days.","So he said, \"First send them to Ganlu Palace, and let Consort Yi choose a few.\"","Fu Hai acknowledged the order, thinking to himself that Consort Yi was indeed favored by His Majesty, and was about to leave.","But before he had taken more than a few steps, he heard the emperor say, \"Wait.\"","Fu Hai quickly halted his steps, \"This servant is here.\"","Was there something else to be bestowed?","Yuwen Lan had simply changed his mind at the last moment, and said, \"Have Consort Yi come here to choose instead.\"","Fu Hai was stunned - have Consort Yi come to Qianming Palace to choose lanterns?","Indeed, that was what Yuwen Lan had said.","-- He felt that although Yanshu's special ability was useful, she seemed to lack discretion, even knowing about others' bedroom affairs...","It really wasn't good.","So when there was an opportunity, it was better to have her come out more, to divert her attention.","Others didn't understand his good intentions.","Fu Hai was stunned for a moment, then realized - could it be that His Majesty was missing his beauty, and thus found an excuse to summon her?","Heh, they had only parted this morning, yet their affection was truly as close as glue.","So he quickly acknowledged the order and happily ran off to Ganlu Palace.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Although... but...","Ahem, did he really seem so obvious now?","At that time, Yanshu was bored in her palace.","After taking down Xie Pei, she had been happy and relaxed for a few days, and had become somewhat lazy.","Just as she was idly holding her brush, she saw Fu Hai arrive.","\"This servant pays respects to Consort Yi. The Lantern Festival lanterns offered as tribute from Quanzhou Prefecture have just arrived. His Majesty requests that you go to Qianming Palace to make your selection.\"","Yanshu was surprised, \"He wants me to go to Qianming Palace to choose?\"","Fu Hai nodded quickly, \"Yes, before they are distributed to the various places, His Majesty wants you to choose the ones you like first.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up. Well, that was wonderful! She loved lanterns the most!","She was bored anyway, so she quickly agreed, changed her clothes, and went to Qianming Palace.","When she entered the gates of Qianming Palace, she saw Yuwen Lan standing in the corridor.","His tall and straight figure, in indigo wide-sleeved robes, with his black hair tied up in a purple-gold crown, made him look even more handsome.","The sight of the beautiful man put her in a good mood. Yanshu came forward and curtsied, \"Your humble consort pays respects to Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and looked her over as well.","He saw that she was wearing a double-sided brocade jacket with a horse-face skirt, looking as pretty as the welcoming spring on early branches.","He was also in a good mood, so he said gently, \"These are the lanterns offered as tribute from Quanzhou, which have always been famous. I had them placed here, go choose two that you like.\"","In fact, as soon as Yanshu had entered the palace gates, she had seen them - dozens of lanterns hanging under the eaves, colorful and beautiful beyond words.","She happily agreed and began to choose.","Hmm, she hadn't realized until she looked closely, but these lanterns were even better!","Especially since they came from another region, the style was different from those made in the palace.","Besides revolving lanterns and lotus lanterns, there were even boneless lanterns made directly from hard paper, painted with various landscape patterns, which were very beautiful.","There were also eight-sided transparent gauze lanterns. Seeing Yanshu's curious expression, a young eunuch quickly lit the candle inside to show her. It turned out the entire lantern was transparent, like a small moon.","She couldn't help but clap her hands, \"Wow, this is great!\"","Yuwen Lan asked, \"So you want this one?\"","Yanshu nodded with a smile, \"Thank you, Your Majesty! But one is enough for your humble consort.\"","There weren't many of these gauze lanterns, and one could tell at a glance that they were precious. Several still needed to be presented to the Empress Dowager, so she didn't dare compete with the Empress Dowager.","\"Please give your humble consort that lotus lantern as well.\"","She had wanted one last time, but hadn't had the chance to ask.","Yuwen Lan nodded and told a young eunuch to take it down for her.","Just then, Fu Hai reported, \"Your Majesty, Lord Zou requests an audience.\"","Lord Zou?","Yanshu's eyes lit up. Could it be that Hanlin Academy scholar with excellent taste who helped publish her story books?","Then she heard Yuwen Lan say, \"Let him in.\"","Fu Hai acknowledged and went to relay the message.","Not long after, Zou Mozhong entered. Seeing Yanshu was also present, he quickly bowed and said, \"This minister pays respects to Your Majesty and Consort Yi.\"","Yanshu nodded, then heard Yuwen Lan ask, \"Have the Imperial Academy matters been settled?\"","-- The Imperial Academy admitted new students every spring. In the past, it had always been led by Wei Ruzhang, the Grand Secretary of Wenhua Court. Since Wei Ruzhang had been dismissed from office at the end of last year for kidnapping commoners, this task had fallen to the Hanlin Academy this year.","Zou Mozhong quickly replied, \"After discussions with the Imperial Academy, we plan to first select forty people from among the children of court officials and noble families; then select sixty people from outstanding students recommended by various regions; finally, select about fifty people from among those who failed the imperial examinations. May I ask Your Majesty's opinion on this?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Reduce the first batch by ten people and add them to the second batch.\"","Most of these children from noble families were uneducated and only hoped to use such opportunities to enter the Imperial Academy and idle away their time. Some, like the nephew of Kang Guangliang, the Vice Minister of Personnel, even bullied commoner students in the Imperial Academy, corrupting the atmosphere.","If so, what was the point of having them?","Zou Mozhong quickly agreed.","Then he heard the emperor add, \"Even for the remaining thirty people, they must be strictly selected. Under no circumstances should anyone be admitted based on personal connections or power. If any favoritism is discovered, it will be treated as dereliction of duty.\"","Zou Mozhong quickly replied with a serious expression, \"Your Majesty's words are absolutely correct. This will make the selection process more intense and encourage everyone to study diligently to become talented individuals.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"I'm glad you understand, Minister Zou. The Imperial Academy represents the face of the court and cultivates pillars for the state. It must not become a laughingstock.\"","Zou Mozhong nodded repeatedly.","With that, the important matters were concluded.","Zou Mozhong paused for a moment, then suddenly asked, \"By the way, Your Majesty, we haven't seen any new manuscripts from the Carefree Scholar in the past few days. Has his illness worsened?\"","Hmm? The Carefree Scholar?","Yanshu accurately caught her pen name and immediately pricked up her ears.","Yuwen Lan glanced at her and said, \"No, she has basically recovered.\"","The Scholar Zou asked again, \"If that's the case, why haven't we seen any new works from her in the past few days?\"","Well, about that...","Yanshu felt a bit guilty.","Yuwen Lan glanced at her again from the corner of his eye and smiled, \"She's probably been busy with other things.\"","Yanshu's face reddened slightly.","Tsk, she had been too indulgent these past couple of days, basking in the joy of defeating her opponents, and hadn't managed to write any new stories for several days in a row.","Then she heard Scholar Zou exclaim, \"Oh my! I wonder what's keeping him so busy? Your Majesty doesn't know, but people outside are all waiting to read his new stories!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Yanshu couldn't help but ask, \"Minister Zou, are you saying that readers outside are waiting for the Carefree Scholar's stories?\"","Zou Mozhong quickly replied, \"I wouldn't dare to speak falsely. Your Highness doesn't know, but in recent days, many readers have been waiting at the bookshop doors early every morning, not for anything else, but just to see this Carefree Scholar's new stories. Some who can't get them become so anxious they can't eat or sleep, scratching their heads in frustration.\"","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","She had no idea she was so needed!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Before he could say anything, she excitedly told Zou Mozhong, \"Tell everyone not to worry, new stories will be coming out soon.\"","Zou Mozhong was somewhat surprised and quickly asked, \"Could it be that Your Highness also knows this Carefree Scholar?\"","\"I know him, quite well actually,\" Yanshu smiled, \"Don't worry, I'll help you urge her on.\"","The Scholar Zou was delighted and repeatedly expressed his thanks, \"Then this official thanks Your Highness on behalf of the readers.\"","\"No need for such formalities.\"","Yanshu waved her hand, smiling generously.","Yuwen Lan spoke up, \"If Minister Zou has no other matters, you may take your leave.\"","Zou Mozhong quickly agreed and left the Qianming Palace.","Finally without outsiders present, Yuwen Lan looked at Yanshu and was about to speak, but saw her hurriedly bow to him, \"This consort will take her leave first.\"","She was about to walk out.","Yuwen Lan grabbed her arm with a frown, \"Where are you going?\"","It was almost noon, and he had planned to have lunch with her.","However, Yanshu urgently said, \"Didn't Your Majesty hear? So many readers are waiting for me, I must hurry back to write stories!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...What's wrong with waiting a little longer? There's no need to be so rushed.\"","What's wrong with waiting a little longer?","Yanshu immediately raised an eyebrow and said, \"It's just like when ministers urgently need to report important matters to you. How could you bear to wait?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Indeed, he couldn't wait.","Then he heard her clicking her tongue, [As a storyteller, aren't the readers her meal ticket? How could she keep the sugar daddies waiting for so long!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Sugar... daddies?","What did that mean?","However, before he could say anything else, he saw her pick up the lantern she had chosen, bow to him, and hurry out.","Upon returning to the Ganlu Palace, Yanshu immediately began writing furiously, even eating lunch casually.","Tsk, upon hearing how much she was needed by her readers, her inspiration suddenly exploded and she wrote tirelessly until the afternoon.","It wasn't until Rendong came to remind her, \"My Lady, there's the Lantern Festival banquet tonight. You need to get dressed and made up, or you'll be late.\"","Lantern Festival banquet?","Yanshu only then remembered this and had to stop writing, replying, \"Alright.\"","— This was her first banquet since her promotion, and on such an important day as the Lantern Festival. She indeed needed to dress up properly, otherwise wouldn't it lose face for the Emperor?","So after the efforts of Rendong, Lianxin, and the others, she wore a cherry-colored off-shoulder crossed-collar long robe sent by the Imperial Wardrobe a few days ago, embroidered with exquisite chrysanthemum patterns. Her black hair was styled in a slanted bun with a jeweled plum blossom hairpin, making her look gorgeous and noble.","Twilight had already fallen outside, and Rendong brought her a sable cloak. After putting it on, Yanshu set out.","Unfortunately, when she arrived at the Hall of Gentle Ceremony, she happened to meet Consort Zhou getting down from her sedan chair.","Yanshu quickly stopped to bow, \"Greetings to Consort Zhou.\"","A consort without a title still felt a bit awkward to address.","Moreover, in the past, Consort An would always have followed behind her, but today she was alone, looking much less imposing.","Consort Zhou merely gave her a sidelong glance and said with a strange smile, \"Isn't this Noble Lady Li, oh no, it should be Consort Yi now. You're dressed quite eye-catchingly today. I remember you used to prefer plain styles, didn't you?\"","Yanshu pretended not to hear the sarcasm in her words and just smiled foolishly, \"This consort wouldn't dare. This consort doesn't come close to even a fraction of Your Highness's beauty. Your Highness is truly the most eye-catching.\"","Eye-catching?","Consort Zhou felt something was off about this remark and was about to lash out when another sedan chair stopped nearby.","The palace maid by the sedan quickly lifted the curtain, and someone stepped down.","It was none other than Consort Ning, who had been confined to her quarters a month ago at the ice skating banquet.","Oh right, that was on the fifteenth day of the twelfth lunar month, and today was the fifteenth of the first month. It had been exactly a month, so her confinement was over.","Yanshu had no choice but to bow again, \"Greetings to Consort Ning.\"","There was no way around it, as this consort also outranked her. If she didn't bow, people would only seize on her mistake.","However, Consort Ning didn't bother to acknowledge her, instead looking first at Consort Zhou.","After being confined for a whole month, she had finally figured it out. Back then, it was this woman who had someone leak information to her, using her as a pawn.","Afterward, she had been locked in her palace for an entire month, lost Consort Li, and implicated her aunt, the Eldest Princess!","In her heart, she had stabbed the other party with a knife countless times. Now, Consort Ning raised an eyebrow and smiled, \"Well, if it isn't Noble Consort, oh no, it's Consort Zhou now. Long time no see.\"","At present, what Consort Zhou hated most was people mentioning her demotion. Hearing this, her face immediately turned cold, and she said, \"Weren't you confined to your quarters? So you've been released today?\"","Consort Ning struggled to suppress her anger and continued to smile, \"Yes, I've been away for a while, and so many things have happened? We're actually of the same rank now? In that case, I don't need to bow to you anymore. I remember you're half a year younger than me, so I'll call you Sister Zhou.\"","Consort Zhou gave her a cold look and said, \"I have no need to discuss sisterhood with you. Listen to my advice, be careful since you've just been released. Don't anger the Empress Dowager again and get locked up once more.\"","With that, she took a step onto the stairs and entered the hall.","\"You...\"","Consort Ning was a step too late and had to swallow her words. Only then did she remember Yanshu, looking her up and down before saying, \"Noble Lady Li, oh no, it's Consort Yi now. I heard you bravely protected the Emperor and were injured. How are you doing now?\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"This consort has recovered much. Thank you for your concern, Your Highness.\"","But then she heard the other say, \"Although you were injured, getting promoted to consort makes it worth it for you, I suppose.\"","At these words, Rendong beside Yanshu immediately stiffened. Was Consort Ning implying that her mistress had exchanged her injury for a higher rank?","This was really too much. Who would risk their life just for a promotion?","However, Yanshu smiled and said, \"Actually, this consort just acted on instinct. Fortunately, it was only a minor injury. The promotion was purely due to His Majesty's great benevolence. However, this consort believes that if Your Highness had been present at the time, you would have done the same.\"","Consort Ning paused. Was this a jab at her recent confinement?","Just as she was about to lash out, the imperial carriage suddenly arrived and stopped. To everyone's surprise, the Emperor himself alighted from it.","Yuwen Lan wore a black dragon robe, his face cold and his gaze sharp as a knife. Consort Ning hurriedly bowed her head and greeted, \"Greetings to Your Majesty.\"","Yanshu also followed suit with her greeting.","Yuwen Lan only said, \"It's cold outside. Why aren't you entering the hall?\"","Consort Ning dared not say anything more and could only respond with a \"Yes,\" following the imperial procession inside.","After entering the hall, everyone took their seats.","Not long after, the Empress Dowager also arrived, surprisingly accompanied by Consort An.","Consort Zhou was stunned and immediately shot a piercing glare their way.","Well well, she had been wondering why this wretched woman suddenly dared to defy her.","So she had cozied up to the Empress Dowager!","Consort Ning, however, smiled sarcastically.","This stupid woman, now abandoned by all, even the Empress Dowager, her own aunt, had given up on her. What right did she have to be so arrogant?","After everyone had paid their respects to the Empress Dowager, the Eldest Princess and her husband Zhao Chengwen entered the hall.","Due to the assassination attempt at the beginning of the year, the palace had become extremely cautious lately. The usual Lantern Festival banquet for officials had been canceled, and tonight's feast only included the Empress Dowager, Emperor, Empresses, and the Eldest Princess and her husband.","The Eldest Princess still exuded a powerful aura. Looking around, no woman in the room could compare to her. As she approached, she bowed to the Emperor and Empress Dowager, saying, \"Your subject pays respects to Mother Empress and Your Majesty. On this auspicious Lantern Festival, I wish you both good health and prosperity.\"","My goodness, she completely ignored all the other consorts in the hall.","In contrast, her husband beside her was as quiet and reserved as ever, simply bowing along with her, like a shy wife next to her husband.","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly. \"No need for such formalities. We're all family here. Please, take your seats.\"","The Eldest Princess complied and led her husband to their seats.","She glanced at Consort Ning and gave a slight nod.","At that moment, Consort Ning felt much more confident.","That fool Consort Zhou had lost the Empress Dowager's favor, but she still had the Eldest Princess as her aunt. So in the end, she had won.","With everyone present, the banquet began.","Everyone took turns toasting the Empress Dowager and Emperor. The Empress Dowager sighed, \"The New Year celebrations have passed in the blink of an eye. The events of the past fortnight have been truly frightening. I hope you all cherish the present and mind your duties.\"","Everyone agreed in unison. As the court musicians began to play and dancers performed, the guests started eating and drinking.","After a while, the Empress Dowager said to Yuwen Lan, \"With spring's arrival, tributes are coming in from various regions, and both masters and servants are changing into spring attire. Palace affairs are complex. I was thinking of finding someone to help oversee the Internal Affairs Bureau, lest they make any mistakes.\"","At these words, everyone's hearts skipped a beat. Who was the Empress Dowager planning to promote?","Consort Zhou had clearly been abandoned, and Consort Ning was the Eldest Princess's person, so the Empress Dowager would certainly not use her. Did that mean only Consort An was left?","Unexpectedly, the Eldest Princess immediately said, \"If Mother Empress doesn't mind, I can recommend someone. Consort Ning is meticulous and handles matters carefully. She could take on this important task.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu, who was eating, inwardly clicked her tongue. The Eldest Princess was too forceful. The Empress Dowager was clearly intending to promote Consort An, yet she recommended Consort Ning. Was she trying to force the Empress Dowager to agree?","But the Empress Dowager wasn't a pushover either. She certainly wouldn't agree.","Sure enough, the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"You've been away from the palace for too long. I see things more clearly from inside. When it comes to meticulousness, Consort An is superior. I think it's better to let her handle it.\"","The meaning was clear - the Eldest Princess was like water spilled from a bucket, having no right to interfere in palace affairs now that she was married off.","Yanshu, who had been secretly watching the drama unfold, thought to herself, \"Well played!\" As expected, the older ginger is spicier. With the Empress Dowager's words, the Eldest Princess and Consort Ning were left in an awkward position.","However, the Eldest Princess persisted, \"Consort An is good, but her rank...\"","Before she could finish, the Empress Dowager interjected with a smile, \"Rank is temporary. Besides, it's just helping to manage the Internal Affairs Bureau. They're all mistresses of the palace. Surely the Internal Affairs Bureau doesn't discriminate based on rank?\"","At these words, Zhang Laishun, the head of the Internal Affairs Bureau who had been waiting nearby, immediately knelt and said, \"This servant would not dare.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and smiled, \"That's right. Let's have Consort An do it. If she doesn't perform well, we can always replace her.\"","Though her tone was gentle, her meaning was quite firm.","As soon as she finished speaking, Consort An hurriedly stood up and said, \"This consort is unworthy. I fear my clumsiness will not live up to the responsibility.\"","The Empress Dowager replied, \"Don't disappoint my trust in you. Just do your best.\"","Only then did Consort An agree, sitting back down with a pleased expression.","Consort Ning was naturally displeased.","However, she didn't miss this opportunity to stab at her old rival.","So she smiled at Consort An and said, \"Consort An often used to follow Consort Zhou. She must have learned many good methods and will certainly be able to handle this task.\"","Hearing this, Consort An froze, while Consort Zhou was about to explode.","This bitch! How dare she mock her like this!","So she smiled back and said, \"Consort Ning is not bad either. By the way, who was it that you used to follow around? It's been so long, I can't quite remember.\"","...","Yanshu secretly hid to the side, eating while observing the battle.","\"Fight, fight!\" she thought to herself.","She had been feeling bored, so why not observe this multi-sided conflict closely, to see who would come out on top? Perhaps she could gain some experience for writing a novel in the future.","Yuwen Lan, who had been discreetly watching her with nothing better to do, thought, \"???\"","How could she think about writing a novel at a time like this?","Was she going mad?","But she hadn't forgotten to eat. While secretly watching the drama unfold, she helped herself to the freshly served fire-roasted lamb chops.","\"Mmm, these lamb chops are very flavorful. One bite and the rich fat melts in your mouth, leaving a lingering aroma.\"","\"This evening jasper soup is also delicious and fragrant, perfect for cleansing the palate. Especially the evening jasper, which is quite rare. We might not get to eat it more than a few times a year. Miss this chance and you might not get another.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Truly nothing could affect her appetite.","Of course not.","For Yanshu, eating delicious food while watching drama unfold was one of life's greatest pleasures!","As she watched, she couldn't help but comment to herself:","In a clash between the Empress Dowager and the Eldest Princess, the Empress Dowager would certainly be more formidable. The Empress Dowager was cunning and experienced, while the Eldest Princess was bold but unwise.","Consort Zhou and Consort Ning were evenly matched. One had just been released from punishment, the other had just been demoted, yet neither showed any signs of restraint, openly quarreling in front of the Emperor.","However, while the Empress Dowager had abandoned Consort Zhou, the Eldest Princess was still supporting Consort Ning. In this aspect, Consort Ning was luckier.","Just as she was thinking this, she heard the system sigh, \"Consort Ning's position isn't secure either. Her uncle, the Imperial Son-in-law, has several mistresses outside the palace. If the Eldest Princess finds out, it's basically over for her.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","What an interesting piece of gossip!"]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33","paragraphs":["Having started to enjoy such an interesting bit of gossip, one must naturally continue to savor it in detail.","Yanshu immediately turned her attention away from the scheming at the banquet and said to the system, [The Eldest Princess is so formidable, yet her consort dares to keep mistresses? Has he eaten a bear's heart and a leopard's gall?]","At this moment, Yuwen Lan, who was feeling deeply bored with Consort Zhou, Consort Ning, the Empress Dowager, and the Eldest Princess, thought, \"???\"","What?","Zhao Chengwen is keeping mistresses?","The system calmly explained, [It all started with the consort Zhao Chengwen. He was originally the third-place winner in the imperial examinations. He's quite talented, good-looking, and comes from a noble family. After he passed the exams with flying colors, the Eldest Princess set her sights on him at first glance and immediately went to ask her imperial father to issue a marriage decree.]","Yanshu clicked her tongue, [Indeed, who could compete with the Emperor's daughter?]","But what did this have to do with him keeping mistresses?","The system continued, [Actually, this consort originally had a favored concubine in his household, but the Eldest Princess certainly wouldn't tolerate any rivals. So before their marriage, his family sent the concubine away. Zhao Chengwen was heartbroken, but he couldn't disobey the imperial decree, so he had no choice but to accept it.]","[At first, he thought the Eldest Princess was noble and beautiful, but once they started living together, he discovered that her personality was too strong. The household was essentially a matriarchy, and how could he, a noble scholar and top exam candidate, willingly submit to such treatment?]","[That's when he started thinking about his former concubine again. He secretly sent people to find her, and once they did, the consort bought a residence to house her.]","Yanshu asked, [So it seems the first mistress was an old flame he couldn't forget. What about the others?]","Yuwen Lan, who was eavesdropping, thought, [??? Old flame? There are others???]","The system continued, [Once this consort got a taste for keeping mistresses, he found it sweet. He felt so stifled in front of the Eldest Princess that just one mistress wasn't enough to restore his confidence! So he quickly sought out a young and beautiful courtesan from Yangzhou and set her up in another residence.]","Yanshu said, [Oh, so the second one was from Yangzhou. Are there more?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","There's more?","The system replied, [Not half a year after the second one, he bought a singing girl from Nanjing; later, he bought a girl who had just come of age from a matchmaker, intending to groom her... As time went on, he became addicted.]","Yanshu: [...You can get addicted to this? Let's count: the concubine, the Yangzhou courtesan, the singing girl, and the young one he's grooming... that's four mistresses already, plus the Eldest Princess at home... This is even more extravagant than the Emperor! How does he manage his time with so many? Hasn't the Eldest Princess noticed?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What does she mean, more extravagant than him???","He discreetly glanced to the side and saw Zhao Chengwen attentively serving dishes to the Eldest Princess, showing no signs of being such a daring character.","The system explained, [The Eldest Princess never imagined he would be so bold. Besides, he is a talented scholar after all. The Eldest Princess is often out socializing and rarely at home. He's served her for so many years, so he can find opportunities.]","However, just as the system finished speaking, the Empress Dowager suddenly asked Yanshu, \"When will Consort Yi's family arrive in the capital?\"","Yanshu paused, then quickly responded, \"Your Majesty, I received a letter recently. My parents left our hometown on the tenth and should arrive in the capital in four or five days.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, smiling warmly, \"Soon, then.\"","Yanshu smiled and agreed, but inwardly she thought, the Empress Dowager's tactic of changing the subject was truly masterful.","Sure enough, as soon as she finished speaking, she noticed Consort Ning and Consort Zhou, who had been glaring at each other, turn to look at her. The Eldest Princess also cast her a contemptuous glance.","\"Well, congratulations to Consort Yi,\" Consort Ning said with an odd smile. \"Your family can finally come to the capital. These past few years must have been difficult for you.\"","Yanshu hurriedly replied, \"I thank Your Highness. His Majesty's kindness is boundless, and I am filled with gratitude.\"","Consort Zhou chimed in with a smile, \"His Majesty's kindness is indeed boundless. Your family must be overjoyed, right? To have raised a daughter like you, your Li family's ancestral graves must be glowing with pride.\"","Yanshu responded with another smile, \"I am unworthy. I cannot compare to even a fraction of Your Highness's virtues.\"","Hmph, these two are just trying to mock her family's low status and lack of experience in the capital. How unoriginal.","At that moment, the Eldest Princess lazily fanned herself with a feather fan and asked, \"So where will they stay when they arrive? Have you found a residence for them? Does your family have a mansion in the capital?\"","Yanshu inwardly scoffed. Was she worried that her family couldn't afford a house?","Hmph, with her current wealth, she could buy a mansion just by writing a couple of novels!","But before she could answer, the Emperor suddenly spoke up, \"Speaking of which, Consort Yi's bravery in protecting me last time shows that her parents have raised her well, teaching her to be loyal to me. I must reward them appropriately.\"","Reward?","Everyone was stunned and turned to look at him, wondering what else he could reward her with.","Hadn't he already promoted her rank?","Yanshu was also surprised. Could it be that the Emperor wanted to reward her parents with a lot of money?","That would be great! Hehe.","One can never have too much money, after all.","However, they saw Yuwen Lan turn to the Empress Dowager and say, \"I intend to bestow the title of Marquis of Loyal Righteousness on Consort Yi's father, grant him a mansion in the capital, an annual salary of a thousand dan of grain, and a hundred mu of farmland.\"","What? Marquis of Loyal Righteousness?","Everyone was stunned once again.","Yanshu herself was shocked.","Marquis of Loyal Righteousness?","Is... is the Emperor planning to grant her father a noble title?","Yes, that's exactly what Yuwen Lan had said.","And his tone made it clear that he wasn't consulting with the Empress Dowager about this decision.","Especially since the Empress Dowager had just given Consort An authority over internal affairs without consulting him.","He hadn't opposed the Empress Dowager, so she had no reason to oppose him.","Sure enough, the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"It is indeed appropriate. Consort Yi's bravery in protecting Your Majesty that day is worthy of emulation throughout the empire. Your Majesty may proceed as you see fit.\"","Everyone turned to look at Yanshu again, their hearts filled with envy and resentment—","How could such an enormous stroke of luck fall on her head???","Yanshu could only hurriedly stand up, bow her head to Yuwen Lan, and say, \"This consort thanks Your Majesty for your great kindness.\"","Yuwen Lan smiled magnanimously, \"No need for formalities. This is what your father deserves.\"","Yanshu thanked him again and sat down.","However, the others felt quite uneasy.","Especially Consort Ning and Consort Zhou.","—What kind of situation was this?","They had barely finished mocking Consort Yi, and now her family was being granted a noble title???","The Eldest Princess also secretly rolled her eyes—","Hmph, it's just a marquis title, and she's so excited about it.","How unsophisticated!","At that moment, someone in the hall was the first to congratulate Yanshu, \"Congratulations, Consort Yi.\"","It was Consort An.","Following her lead, everyone had no choice but to say, \"Congratulations, Consort Yi.\"","In truth, if anyone was the most displeased, it was probably Consort An.","In just over a month, Li Yanshu had leaped from a lowly Beauty to nearly her equal.","And now she had unexpectedly gained a noble title!","Yet her own grandfather, implicated in the Cheng'en Duke's case, still hadn't been allowed to return to court.","Wouldn't this mean that she would be overshadowed by Yanshu?","How is this fair!","At the hour of Xu, the banquet ended, and everyone dispersed.","Yanshu also returned to her chambers, carrying the unexpected joy of the day with her.","Hehe, now that her family had a noble title, her parents, grandmother, and younger brother wouldn't lack for money. They would have more food than they could eat and collect a substantial amount of land rent each year!!!","She was so happy that she even hummed a tune while bathing.","Rendong was also delighted, scrubbing her back while saying with a smile, \"With this, the master won't have to secretly use his own salary to help others anymore, and the mistress won't have to be angry about it.\"","\"That's right!\"","Yanshu closed her eyes contentedly in the bathtub.","Now that her loved ones' lives had improved, she could focus on writing novels to give back to her readers!","Thinking this, after she got out of the bathtub and dressed, she went to her desk.","—Tonight was the fifteenth, and the Emperor wouldn't be visiting any consorts, so she planned to have a productive writing session!","However, before she could put pen to paper, Fu Hai arrived, urgently saying to her, \"Please change your clothes quickly, Your Highness. His Majesty is waiting for you outside!\"","Yanshu was stunned, \"His Majesty is waiting for me? But he's not supposed to come to the harem tonight...\"","Fu Hai smiled and said, \"His Majesty wants to take you out. Every year on the Lantern Festival, His Majesty goes out to observe the people's conditions, and today is no exception. He specifically sent me to ask if you would like to accompany him. The carriage is waiting outside right now.\"","Go out?","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she immediately put down her pen and stood up. \"Alright, just wait a moment, I'll be quick!\"","She hurriedly called for Rendong to help her change her clothes.","It had been three years since she'd left the palace, so of course she wanted to go out and get some fresh air!","Naturally, since they were going out, she couldn't wear her palace attire. Fortunately, she still had her old clothes from before. It didn't take long for her to change and head out, following Fu Hai onto the carriage that had already been prepared.","Tsk, this carriage looked ordinary on the outside, clearly not from the palace. It seemed the emperor indeed went out frequently.","When she got into the carriage, she saw that Yuwen Lan was already sitting inside.","He was wearing a dark cyan brocade robe, with no crown on his head, looking like some wealthy young master.","Of course, his looks and aura were incomparable to any ordinary rich young man.","She hurriedly bowed, \"This humble consort greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan reached out and pulled her to the seat, raising an eyebrow, \"We need to change how we address each other now.\"","Oh, that's right. Yanshu then called him, \"Young Master.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Shouldn't it be husband?\"","If he was a young master, wouldn't that make her a maid?","But Yanshu thought to herself, [So his alias is a married man, I thought he was planning to go out to see beautiful women.]","Yuwen Lan: ???","What did she mean by \"alias\"?","Just as he was curious, he heard her softly call out, \"Husband.\"","Ahem, this was the first time she had addressed someone like this, and her face couldn't help but redden.","Yuwen Lan, however, found her voice pleasing to the ear.","Looking at her appearance again, his heart grew increasingly joyful. He let out an \"Mm\" and held her hand in his palm, then ordered towards the window, \"Let's go.\"","The carriage began to move.","After leaving the palace gates, the bustling streets gradually appeared before their eyes.","The capital had always been prosperous, and today being the Lantern Festival, the streets were even more crowded with people.","Yanshu peeked out curiously while asking, \"Your Maj-, husband, where are we going?\"","Yuwen Lan instead asked her, \"Where do you want to go?\"","Oh, so she could choose?","Yanshu quickly said, \"This humble wife is not familiar with the capital, but I've heard that Tianjing Lane has many delicious foods. Why don't we go there and take a look?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Why was it still about food?","\"Didn't you eat enough earlier?\" he looked at her amusedly.","Yanshu pouted, \"Tianjing Lane is all about street food, naturally different from the palace cuisine.\"","It was normal to want a change of taste after eating grand meals every day.","But Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow again, \"Oh? If you're not familiar with the capital, how do you know Tianjing Lane is all about street food?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She had accidentally let something slip?","She hurriedly covered up, \"This wife just heard it from the palace servants. Many of their families are in the capital, so they naturally know more.\"","-- In fact, she had learned all this while \"eating melons\" (listening to gossip).","Besides Tianjing Lane, she also knew that Embroidery Lane sold cosmetics and silk threads; near Junyi Bridge, because it was close to the imperial examination hall, they mostly sold writing brushes, ink, paper, and inkstones; Silver Street sold tea leaves and cloth, while the area around Hundred Flowers Lane was the capital's famous red-light district.","Speaking of which, there was reportedly a restaurant on Yang Lou Street that catered to wealthy women. The men inside were all as handsome as Pan An, and had many special skills – playing the zither and flute, composing poetry and painting. Each had eyes like autumn waters, broad shoulders and slim waists, suave and elegant...","Hehe, in short, completely different from those greasy bearded men.","Yuwen Lan: ???","What? There was such a place in the capital???","And what did she mean by that \"hehe\" just now???","He shuddered and immediately ordered the carriage, \"Go to Tianjing Lane.\"","And unconsciously tightened his grip on her hand.","Before long, they arrived at Tianjing Lane.","The two got off the carriage and saw that the surroundings were as bright as day with lanterns, bustling with crowds.","It turned out that Tianjing Lane not only sold food, but tonight there was also a lantern market, attracting half the city's population to come and admire the lanterns.","Yanshu hadn't seen such a lively scene for a long time. She felt as if she was in another world, her eyes darting here and there, almost not enough to take it all in.","Yuwen Lan, still feeling uneasy, held her hand tightly the whole way.","After walking through the crowd for a while, suddenly Yanshu said, \"Look, there are so many people at this wonton stall, it must be delicious.\"","Yuwen Lan looked in the direction she pointed and indeed saw a wonton stall in front of a shop, with five or six small tables beside it, all full of people.","He frowned, \"You want to eat this?\"","Yanshu nodded with a smile, \"Since we're here, why not give it a try?\"","Yuwen Lan still frowned, \"But there's nowhere to sit.\"","Yanshu said expertly, \"Let's order first, by the time the wontons are ready, there will be seats available.\"","She then called out to the wonton vendor, \"Two bowls of wontons, please.\"","Yuwen Lan quickly corrected, \"One bowl is enough, I'm not hungry.\"","But Yanshu said, \"We've already ordered, if you don't eat, Your Maj-, husband, I'll eat it.\"","Then her eyes lit up again, \"Look, there are seats over there.\"","She quickly pulled him over.","Just as they sat down, the stall owner brought over the freshly cooked wontons.","Yuwen Lan looked down and saw that they were just two ordinary ceramic bowls, each containing about twenty wontons, with steaming clear soup poured over them, and a few bits of green onion floating on top.","He raised an eyebrow, wondering if this could really taste good?","But when he looked up, he saw that the girl had already started eating.","\"Mmm, this soup must be made from chicken bones, with some lard added. The wontons are delicious too, not bad at all.\"","Yanshu had eaten three wontons in a row before she noticed that someone was sitting still, watching her eat.","\"...\"","She tried to persuade him, \"It's a rare opportunity, husband, don't you really want to try? After drinking earlier, a bowl of this would be very comforting.\"","This \"husband\" made Yuwen Lan feel pleased. He paused for a moment, and finally picked up the spoon to taste it.","Hmm, he could tell the seasoning was simple, but there was a unique fragrance.","The hot soup with the smooth wontons entering his stomach, in this chilly weather, indeed made one feel warm and comfortable.","Then he saw Yanshu ask him, \"Isn't it delicious? This kind of street flavor can't be made at home.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly. He was about to eat more when he saw her extend her spoon into his bowl to scoop up some wontons. \"Don't waste it. If husband isn't hungry, I'll eat it for you.\"","She then proceeded to scoop five or six wontons from his bowl.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He wasn't hungry, but could her small body really eat so much?","It would be better not to let her eat too much and get bloated, so he quickly started eating as well.","Before long, they finished the wontons, paid, and continued walking.","Yanshu hadn't expected that there would be even more street food ahead.","After walking a few steps, they saw a restaurant grilling lamb skewers at its entrance. The fat from the lamb was dripping onto the charcoal fire, releasing an intense aroma.","Not far away, there was a vendor selling baked flatbread from a hanging oven. The freshly baked flatbreads were golden yellow, covered in sesame seeds, looking crispy at first glance.","Walking a few more steps, they came across a stall selling freshly cooked tangyuan (sweet rice balls). The plump white tangyuan actually came in five flavors, including black sesame, red bean paste, jujube paste, winter melon sugar, and so on, dazzling Yanshu's eyes.","Tsk tsk tsk, each dish looked so tempting, but her stomach was too full, she really couldn't fit anymore.","[Wuwuwu, if I had known we were coming out, I should have eaten less earlier. Look at how that lamb is grilled, crispy on the outside and tender inside, and it's even dripping oil! And that big flatbread, if it were cut open and stuffed with some roasted lamb, it would be perfect...]","[Should I try to press down a bit and eat a flatbread?]","Yuwen Lan, who had been silently listening, thought: \"...\"","Could one really press down food like that?","Truly afraid she might get bloated, he had to speak up, \"If there's a chance, we can come out again.\"","Yanshu quickly looked at him, \"Do you really mean it, husband?\"","Yuwen Lan smiled, \"Next time we come out, I'll definitely bring you along.\"","Only then did she finally feel at ease, quickly agreeing and abandoning her previous thoughts.","However, the small items sold along the way were also quite nice. Since it was a rare outing, she bought two skeins of silk thread for making tassels and a peach wood comb.","Seeing that they had been out for nearly half an hour and the crowd on the street was thinning, the two decided to head back.","On the way to the carriage, just as Yuwen Lan was about to get in, Yanshu suddenly pulled him back.","Yuwen Lan was puzzled, \"What's wrong?\"","She pointed across the street and said in a low voice, \"Husband, look, that person... looks like the Prince Consort.\"","Prince Consort?","Yuwen Lan looked in the direction she pointed. At the entrance of a pastry shop diagonally across from them, a man had just come out carrying some pastries. His figure and appearance did indeed resemble Zhao Chengwen, the Eldest Princess's consort.","Then he heard Yanshu think to herself, [Tsk tsk, it really is Zhao Chengwen! The banquet just ended, and he's out on the streets? Surely he's not going to visit a mistress?]","Yuwen Lan was thinking the same thing.","The Eldest Princess's household had thousands of servants, why would he need to come out to buy pastries himself?","While pondering, she saw the other person carrying some snacks and getting onto a nearby carriage.","Yanshu's heart tightened, and she hurriedly said to him, \"Isn't it a bit strange for the princess consort to be out buying snacks so late?\"","[This fresh gossip is the most delicious! Judging by the direction, could he be going to see Little Six? I must hurry and follow, I can't let him get away!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","But it's just as well.","He immediately pulled her into the carriage and instructed outside, \"Follow that carriage.\"","The coachman complied, and as soon as Zhao Chengwen's carriage started moving, he quietly followed.","The Tianjing Lane area was densely populated with residences, and after numerous twists and turns, the wheels gradually came to a stop.","The coachman reported from outside, \"Master, the alley ahead is too narrow to enter.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu glanced at Yuwen Lan and said, \"Husband, shall we get off the carriage?\"","[Tsk tsk, the exciting scene is about to unfold, we can't miss it just because we can't go in!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","To have him get off and follow, how big of a face would that give Zhao Chengwen?","He instructed out the window, \"Chang Feng, go take a look.\"","Someone immediately complied and went in the direction Zhao Chengwen had gone.","After waiting for a while, someone reported from outside the window, \"Master, the son-in-law went into a courtyard inside. A young woman came out to greet him, and as soon as they met, he embraced her and went into the room. Besides them, there were two maids and an old woman.\"","Yanshu thought to herself, [A young woman? Can't tell if this is number two or three or four. It's a pity I can't see it with my own eyes.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Glancing at her, he said, \"Remember this place, keep someone watching, and see how often he comes.\"","A voice outside acknowledged the order.","With that, he was about to leave.","However, at that moment, they saw Zhao Chengwen come out again.","Yanshu: [??? So quick? Is this prince consort so... lacking in stamina?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What stamina?","This girl!","Before he could speak, they saw Zhao Chengwen get back into his carriage and continue forward.","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she quickly said to Yuwen Lan, \"Oh, it seems the prince consort doesn't intend to go back yet.\"","How could Yuwen Lan not know what she was thinking? He instructed the coachman again, \"Continue following.\"","The coachman complied and continued driving.","After another series of twists and turns, the carriage stopped again. This time, Zhao Chengwen got off and went into another courtyard.","Yuwen Lan again sent a secret guard to investigate.","Before long, the secret guard came back to report, \"The son-in-law went to a place with a young woman and two young children this time. The older one is four or five, the younger one is two or three. There are about six servants.\"","Yanshu feigned surprise and said, \"There are even two children? What's going on here?\"","[This must be the concubine, otherwise the others couldn't have children this old.]","Yuwen Lan glanced at her, almost wanting to tell her that he already knew what was going on with Zhao Chengwen, and she didn't need to pretend anymore.","But he held back and only instructed the secret guard outside the window, \"Keep someone watching this place too.\"","The secret guard acknowledged.","After a while, they saw Zhao Chengwen come out again, get into his carriage, and continue forward without turning back.","Yanshu rubbed her hands together, ready to continue following and enjoying the drama.","Hehe, let's see how many places this man can go in one night.","However, Yuwen Lan only told the secret guard to follow him, while instructing the coachman to return to the palace.","Yanshu, still unsatisfied, immediately asked, \"Your Majesty doesn't want to keep following and watching? He might go to many more places tonight!\"","[This is her first time witnessing gossip in person!!! It's so frustrating not to see it through to the end!!!]","However, Yuwen Lan asked her with a half-smile, \"Could it be that you knew about this beforehand?\"","Yanshu choked, hurriedly saying, \"Your Majesty jest. I spend all my days in the palace, and today is the first time I've toured the capital. How could I know about the prince consort's affairs?\"","But Yuwen Lan asked her again, \"If that's the case, how do you know he will go to many more places?\"","Yanshu stubbornly said, \"Because... because I see that the prince consort seems full of energy. After all, it's rare for him to come out, so I thought he wouldn't go back until he's had his fill of fun, right?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Had his fill of fun?","This girl is simply!","Before he could say anything, he heard her think to herself, [And here I thought this man was something special! Judging by what just happened, he was in and out of that courtyard in less than the time it takes to drink two cups of tea. Looks like he's just a novice, no wonder the Eldest Princess is always out having fun.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What?","Novice???","But she wasn't finished.","[And he's keeping so many mistresses with skills like that? Tsk, it's truly a case of having more ambition than ability!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","More ambition than ability???","Where did she learn all these phrases!!!"]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34","paragraphs":["After this, it was already getting late.","The crowd watching the lanterns gradually dispersed, and the roads became clearer. Before long, the carriage passed through the palace gates.","Yanshu had thoroughly enjoyed eating melons tonight. Just as they were about to disembark, she tentatively asked Yuwen Lan, \"Does Your Majesty intend to inform the Eldest Princess about this matter?\"","Tsk tsk, if he told her, there would surely be a great battle! She'd better prepare in advance to eat melons, hehe.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Always looking for drama.","But he had much more to consider.","So he simply said, \"Let them investigate thoroughly first. The Eldest Princess is impulsive. If we rashly let her know, I'm afraid there will be bloodshed.\"","Yanshu nodded, \"That's for the best.\"","— She actually knew that although the Eldest Princess and the Emperor were siblings, their relationship was ordinary. The Eldest Princess only viewed her brother as a tool to maintain her wealth and status.","Otherwise, how could she have joined with a group of officials to force the Emperor to punish her before the ice games banquet?","So this was for the best. After all, they were the first to know about this matter, and they held the initiative.","Yuwen Lan, who had been quietly listening, felt his heart stir.","— She used \"they\"?","This was the first time in his life someone had referred to them in this way. It gave him a special feeling.","Just then, they arrived at Ganlu Palace, and the carriage came to a stop.","Yanshu said to him, \"Your humble consort will retire first.\"","She was about to get off the carriage.","Yuwen Lan instinctively held her back.","Yanshu asked curiously, \"Does Your Majesty have any further instructions?\"","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment. He felt like he had something else to say, but couldn't remember what it was.","After a moment, he could only say, \"It's getting late. Go back and rest early.\"","Ahem, in any case, don't think about those messy things anymore.","Like novices and such...","Yanshu didn't understand, but simply replied, \"Yes.\"","In her heart, however, she giggled, [Tonight was so exciting, I must hurry and ponder writing a story about it. I've even thought of a title: \"The Two-Faced Scholar Dies Under the Flowers\".]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","But before he could say anything, she had already gotten off the carriage and entered Ganlu Palace.","With the Lantern Festival over, the New Year celebrations were considered complete.","Early the next morning, Consort An took up her new post, assisting with the affairs of the Internal Affairs Bureau.","Having finally gained the favor of the Empress Dowager, Consort An naturally didn't dare to slack off. She spent the entire morning reviewing warehouse records and ledgers.","As noon approached, Zhang Laifu, the head of the Internal Affairs Bureau, came to Lanlin Hall to report to her, \"Reporting to Your Highness, as the weather is turning warmer, the silk and fabrics ordered by the Weaving Bureau from Jinling City should arrive in about half a month. We've tentatively set the third day of the second month for taking measurements for new clothes for all the masters. I wonder if this meets with Your Highness's approval?\"","Consort An nodded and said, \"This is similar to previous years, it's suitable. Remember to measure the Empress Dowager first, and also send the fabric samples to the Palace of Benevolent Peace for the Empress Dowager's approval.\"","Zhang Laifu quickly agreed, \"Your Highness is so thoughtful. This servant will certainly remember.\"","Consort An handed over the few ledgers she had just finished reviewing and smiled, \"Since Manager Zhang took charge of the Internal Affairs Bureau, everything has been running smoothly. His Majesty and the Empress Dowager have had much less to worry about.\"","Everyone likes a kind master. Zhang Laifu quickly smiled and said, \"Your Highness is too kind. It's just what we should do.\"","Consort An smiled and nodded, but suddenly asked, \"By the way, I noticed that recently, the palace has been ordering more letter paper, ink, and brushes than usual?\"","\"That's correct.\"","Zhang Laifu hurriedly explained, \"Actually, the other masters' orders are the same as before. Recently, it's mainly Ganlu Palace's Consort Yi who has been requesting more letter paper. I heard that Consort Yi has taken up calligraphy practice lately. However, this was all approved by His Majesty, and the funds were specially allocated by him.\"","\"I see.\"","Consort An nodded and didn't ask anything further. She simply smiled and said, \"I have nothing else here. Manager Zhang should go rest as well.\"","Zhang Laifu quickly agreed and took his leave.","With no outsiders in the room, there was no need to be so cautious. Liu Di, her personal maid, said, \"His Majesty goes to Ganlu Palace every day, how does Consort Yi have time to practice calligraphy?\"","Consort An, however, said, \"She's requesting letter paper, which doesn't seem like it's for calligraphy practice.\"","— People who have studied know that letter paper is suitable for writing small regular script, usually used for writing letters or documents. Calligraphy practice mostly uses xuan paper.","Consort An pondered carefully. Consort Yi using letter paper, could she be corresponding with someone?","But that didn't seem likely either.","With her background, who would she correspond with besides her poor rural family?","Moreover, her family members were already on their way and about to arrive in the capital soon. She wouldn't need to write so many letters, would she?","Could it be... that she was writing some kind of manuscript?","Consort An thought this was unlikely too — given Li Yanshu's humble background, it was already impressive that she could read and write. How could she possibly be writing a manuscript?","Unable to figure it out, Consort An thought for a moment and simply summoned the young eunuch Shuang Xi from her palace.","...","Meanwhile, Yanshu, who was enthusiastically writing her new story, suddenly received a message from the system, [Heads up, someone is preparing to go through your trash.]","Yanshu was full of question marks, [What does that mean? What do you mean by going through my trash?]","The system replied, [Because someone has noticed that you've been using a lot of letter paper recently, so they're trying to find out what you're using it for.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Although this was a roundabout way of saying it, after thinking for a moment, she understood.","Who would be constantly pondering her activities?","It must be someone from the harem.","Who would notice that she's been using a lot of letter paper?","That would most likely be the newly appointed assistant of the Internal Affairs Bureau, Consort An.","Moreover, with Consort Zhou and Consort Ning's level of intelligence, even if they noticed she was using a lot of letter paper, they probably wouldn't think of going through her trash to spy on her.","So it could only be Consort An.","Tsk, Yanshu sighed. This one was indeed quite clever, but why did she have to be at odds with her?","Of course, no matter how clever she was, this tactic wouldn't work.","— To avoid others discovering that she was writing stories, Yanshu always threw her drafts and waste paper directly into the brazier to burn, never throwing them out.","However...","Considering how much effort the other party was putting in, she could leave some bait.","Yanshu raised an eyebrow and smirked to herself. First, she set aside the \"The Two-Faced Scholar Dies Under the Flowers\" that she was currently writing, and began writing on a new sheet of letter paper...","Shuang Xi waited for three full days before finally getting hold of the discarded letter paper from Ganlu Palace.","After the people from Ganlu Palace left, he immediately ran back to Lanlin Hall with the discarded items.","\"Your Highness, these are all thrown out from Ganlu Palace. Please take a look.\"","Consort An immediately looked. She saw that the bag was full of waste paper, some crumpled into balls, some torn into pieces.","She immediately called her personal maids to help.","Some unfolded the papers, some pieced them together. It took nearly half a day's effort.","Consort An then discovered that most of the waste paper was just random scribbles, unrecognizable.","However, fortunately, there was one sheet with some text on it. Although messy, it was barely legible.","Consort An hurriedly read it herself and saw that it seemed to be a story.","It was roughly about a high-ranking court official who appeared proper on the surface, full of talk about propriety and integrity, but was actually lecherous and vulgar. Despite his advanced age, he still took advantage of the maids in his household. Later, someone learned of his predilection and sent him many young and beautiful women to curry favor...","Reading to this point, Consort An suddenly froze.","Advanced age, sending concubines...","Could this, could this be talking about her grandfather?","That Li Yanshu! How dare she fabricate such stories about her family!","Consort An angrily read on, only to see that she had written that the old man actually had an even bigger secret. Taking advantage of his son's poor health, he had been carrying on with his daughter-in-law for many years...","Consort An paused.","What, what is this???","Her second uncle indeed had poor health. Was Li Yanshu implying that her grandfather and her second aunt...","That vile woman Li Yanshu!!!","How dare she slander her family like this!","However, the story wasn't over yet. She tried to read on and saw that it was written — The old man originally had two sons. Although the elder son's family was more accomplished, because of his improper relationship with the second daughter-in-law, he always favored the second branch of the family, causing great dissatisfaction in the first branch.","Consort An was stunned again.","Although angry, she had to admit that there was some truth in this.","Since she was young, she had noticed that her grandfather always showed particular favor to the second branch of the family. For example, whenever he got some rare items, he would always secretly give them to her cousin from the second branch first, while she and her brother never received anything...","If there was any unpleasantness between her mother and her second aunt, her grandfather would always tell her mother to be forbearing, saying that as the elder sister-in-law, she should be more broad-minded...","Reflecting on this, Consort An still felt resentful.","But how did this Yanshu know about her family situation?","She was just a country girl, how could she possibly know any important officials in the capital to find out about affairs in the Minister of Rites' residence?","Consort An thought for a moment, then suddenly turned to Liu Di and asked, \"Have you been gossiping about me to outsiders?\"","Liu Di was startled and quickly shook her head, \"My lady, how could that be possible? I'm with you all day, how could I go out and gossip about you, and to whom?\"","Of course, Consort An knew this was true.","Liu Di had grown up with her since childhood and was the most honest person she knew. Otherwise, she wouldn't have brought her into the palace.","But if it wasn't Liu Di, how did Yanshu know about her family matters?","Could it just be a coincidence that she made it up?","Liu Di didn't know what had happened, but seeing her mistress frowning deeply in thought, she became very nervous and had to ask, \"My lady, has something happened?\"","Consort An suddenly instructed her, \"Tell Shuang Xi to keep watching, and if there's any more waste paper, bring it back.\"","Liu Di had to quickly agree and went out to find someone.","But Consort An still felt something was off.","What was going on with this Yanshu?","Why was she fabricating stories about her family at the Minister of Rites' residence? What was she trying to do?","Meanwhile, in Ganlu Palace, Yanshu, who had just learned the whole story, shrugged her shoulders—","Sorry, but she'd only drop this little bit of gossip once. Next time it might be a bombshell.","But it was still too early for that. For now, let Consort An squirm like an ant on a hot pan.","Yanshu unconsciously started humming a tune, planning to continue writing her novel.","However, at that moment, Fu Hai entered the hall and reported to her, \"This servant has come to inform the Imperial Consort that the Marquis of Loyal Righteousness, along with the Madam, Old Madam, and young master have just arrived in the capital.\"","Yanshu was stunned for a moment before realizing he was talking about her father, mother, grandmother, and brother.","Right! On the night of the Lantern Festival, the Emperor had bestowed the title of Marquis of Loyal Righteousness on her father in front of everyone. It must be them!","So that meant her parents had arrived in the capital?!","Yanshu suddenly became excited, \"Really? When did they arrive?\"","Fu Hai quickly answered, \"They arrived this morning. His Majesty arranged for people to receive them. Right now, the Marquis and his family are settling into their residence. His Majesty's intention is to let them rest for a while, and then arrange for you to meet with the Old Madam and Madam tomorrow.\"","\"Good, good, good.\"","Yanshu happily agreed, then said, \"I'll prepare some silver later. Chief Steward Fu, could you find someone to help me send it to my parents?\"","— Although they now had a house and land, the whole family had just arrived and would inevitably need to take care of various matters and add some things.","She knew her family's situation best. Whenever there was extra money, her father liked to help others, so she guessed they probably didn't have much money on hand.","But Fu Hai smiled and said, \"Don't worry, Imperial Consort. His Majesty has already sent someone to deliver money.\"","What?","Yanshu was stunned. The Emperor had sent money to her parents?","Was he really so considerate?","So she hurriedly said, \"Then please convey my thanks to His Majesty on my behalf.\"","She then called Rendong to bring some silver pieces and handed them to Fu Hai, saying, \"Thank you for coming to deliver the message, Chief Steward. Please take this for some tea.\"","Fu Hai happily accepted, \"Thank you for your kindness, Imperial Consort.\"","Then he took his leave.","Thus, Yanshu waited contentedly to meet her family.","The next morning, as promised, the Emperor sent people to bring Yanshu's grandmother, Old Lady Li, and her mother, Ms. Zhu, into the palace.","Having not seen her family for three years, heaven knows how excited Yanshu was. She got up early and asked Rendong and the others to clean the courtyard and tidy up the palace hall, and also prepared some snacks and fruits.","Finally, when Xiao Dongzi led them into the hall, as soon as she saw her mother and grandmother, Yanshu immediately rushed over to them.","\"Grandmother, Mother!\"","Separated for three years, the grandmother, mother, and daughter couldn't help but burst into tears.","Rendong, watching from the side, also started tearing up.","However, as they were still in the palace, after a brief cry, Old Lady Li said, \"This is a joyous occasion, let's stop crying, lest others see and say something.\"","Yanshu quickly wiped her tears and asked, \"Was your journey smooth? Was it tiring?\"","Her mother, Ms. Zhu, also wiped her tears and said, \"It wasn't too tiring. We had plenty to eat and drink along the way, and the weather was good. Everything went quite smoothly.\"","As she spoke, she carefully examined her daughter, checking to see if her precious child had suffered or grown thin from hunger.","However, after looking for a while, Ms. Zhu discovered that her daughter hadn't lost weight at all. In fact, she seemed to have become a bit rounder, her skin was fair and glowing, and she looked even more beautiful than when she was at home.","Ms. Zhu nodded and sighed, \"It seems the palace really does nurture people!\"","It was good. Her daughter hadn't suffered, which put her mother's heart at ease.","As soon as she finished speaking, Old Lady Li quickly urged her daughter-in-law, \"Hurry and take out the things, before we forget.\"","Ms. Zhu quickly complied, taking out several cloth bags from the bundle she had brought with her. Peeling back layer after layer, she finally revealed the treasures inside.","They turned out to be plump, white steamed buns and golden pan-fried flatbreads.","Yanshu's eyes lit up as she saw her mother smile and say, \"These were all made just this morning. They're still warm. Quick, try them.\"","Before she finished speaking, Yanshu had already stuffed a bun into her mouth.","Mmm, a large steamed bun filled with chives, vermicelli noodles, and the perfect touch of pork crackling in the center. The bun skin was soft yet chewy – it was indeed her mother's flavor.","After finishing the fist-sized bun in a few bites, she picked up a flatbread. One bite filled her mouth with the fragrance of scallions and wheat, along with the unique rich aroma of peanut oil. It was truly satisfying!","Her mother smiled beside her, \"You've become an Imperial Consort now, but you're still the same as before.\"","Yanshu also smiled and said, \"No matter what I've become, I'm still your daughter.\"","She then asked, \"How's the new residence? How are you all settling in?\"","\"It's wonderful,\" Old Lady Li immediately nodded. \"It's a large compound with five courtyards, and even includes a garden. It's spacious and beautiful, absolutely stunning! We each have our own courtyard and there's still room to spare. His Majesty's grace is truly boundless!\"","Yanshu also smiled and said, \"Then keep one courtyard vacant for when Tian Rui takes a wife in the future.\"","She then asked, \"How is Father's new position? How is Tian Rui?\"","Ms. Zhu quickly replied, \"This morning we came to the palace together. Your father took Tian Rui to pay respects to His Majesty, so we don't know about the position yet. Qingzhou Academy has written a letter of recommendation for Tian Rui, and he's planning to report to Songhe Academy in the capital tomorrow.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she said, \"That's great, he needs to hurry. If there's enough time, he might even be able to take this year's annual examination. If he does well in the annual exam, he might be able to enter the Imperial Academy.\"","She still remembered that the Emperor had mentioned reducing the number of first-round admissions to the Imperial Academy this year, shifting them to the second and third rounds.","Her family wasn't considered nobility, but her brother was a good student and could potentially enter the Imperial Academy through examinations.","However, Ms. Zhu said, \"We don't dare to think that far. It's good enough if he can study well.\"","\"That's true,\" Yanshu smiled. \"Even if he can't enter the Imperial Academy, brother is intelligent and talented. He'll surely be able to pass the imperial examinations in the future.\"","Ms. Zhu and Old Lady Li both smiled and agreed.","The palace rules were strict, and although they were allowed to meet today, Ms. Zhu and Old Lady Li couldn't stay for too long. After chatting with Yanshu for a while, they bid farewell and left the palace.","As they were leaving the palace and getting into their carriage, another carriage had just arrived at the palace gates.","When the carriage stopped, a person alighted – it was Lady Tian, Consort An's mother.","Ever since seeing that piece of \"waste paper\" thrown out from Ganlu Palace, Consort An had been anxious. She had endured for several days, and finally, taking advantage of the opportunity when Yanshu's family entered the palace, she had made great efforts in front of the Empress Dowager to obtain permission for her mother to enter the palace for a visit.","Time was limited. As soon as Lady Tian entered the palace gates, she headed straight for her daughter's Lanlin Hall.","When the two met, Consort An immediately dismissed all unnecessary personnel and asked Lady Tian, \"Mother, how have things been at home lately?\"","— She actually wanted to probe her mother to see if the matters mentioned on the waste paper were true.","However, after pondering for a long time, she still couldn't bring herself to ask directly, so she could only ask in this roundabout way.","Lady Tian replied, \"Don't even mention it. The second branch of the family has been causing trouble again these past couple of days.\"","Consort An's heart skipped a beat, and she quickly asked, \"What happened?\"","Lady Tian sighed, \"The Imperial Academy is recruiting new students, and your second aunt planned to send her son Chang there. Who knew that this year the number of spots would be reduced and the exam would be stricter? Chang has been spoiled by her, how could he be up to the task? So he was eliminated in the first round. Your second aunt wanted your grandfather to pull some strings to get Chang into the Imperial Academy.\"","Upon hearing about her grandfather and second aunt, Consort An felt a pang in her heart and quickly asked, \"Did grandfather agree?\"","Lady Tian gave a mocking smile, \"Your grandfather can't even attend court these days, how could he refuse her? Unexpectedly, she then went to your father, wanting him to help.\"","Consort An immediately frowned, \"With the recent imperial edict, the court is extremely strict now. If father really helped her do such a thing, it would be disastrous if discovered later!\"","Lady Tian nodded hurriedly, \"Exactly. Your father naturally didn't dare agree, but who would have thought she even wanted to come find you. When she learned I was entering the palace, she insisted on coming along.\"","Consort An angrily said, \"Don't let her come under any circumstances! I've finally gained the Empress Dowager's trust, how could I let her come and cause trouble?\"","Lady Tian quickly said, \"I understand, don't worry. That Chang of hers is ignorant and unlearned all day long. It would be a miracle if he could enter the Imperial Academy. Let's look to our Qi next year instead. If your grandfather helps her this time but doesn't help our Qi next year, I'll go make a fuss too!\"","Qi was Consort An's younger brother, a year younger than her second aunt's son Chang, and would be ready to enter the Imperial Academy next year as well.","Consort An made a noncommittal sound, her thoughts still on that matter—","Given grandfather's current situation, would he really help Chang?","If he did help, wouldn't that mean he and second aunt...","Just then, she heard Lady Tian suddenly lower her voice and say, \"By the way, I heard a few days ago that His Majesty bestowed that golden bowl from Tibet's tribute to Consort Yi. Do you know about this?\"","\"Golden bowl?\" Consort An paused.","That golden bowl was part of Tibet's tribute to the emperor when seeking peace. It was made of pure gold with red and blue gemstones, extraordinarily beautiful.","At the time it was first revealed, it had attracted everyone's gaze, even Consort Zhou stared at it.","Now it had actually been given to Consort Yi?","She immediately asked, \"Why did His Majesty give it to her?\"","But Lady Tian shook her head and said, \"I only heard about it, I don't know the specific reason.\"","She raised an eyebrow and asked in a low voice, \"Such a precious thing, I wonder if the Empress Dowager knows about it?\"","After seeing Lady Tian off, Consort An went to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Using the opportunity to thank the Empress Dowager, she planned to mention the golden bowl matter.","Mother was right, such a precious thing, His Majesty didn't even present it to the Empress Dowager as a filial gift, but gave it to Consort Yi...","The Empress Dowager would surely be displeased if she knew about this.","...","Meanwhile, Yanshu was still leisurely eating the buns and pancakes her mother had made in Ganlu Palace.","Mother's cooking was truly delicious!","In comparison, even the imperial kitchen's dishes had to take a step back.","She wanted to save a few for the emperor, but wasn't sure if he would care for them.","While she was hesitating, she saw Yuwen Lan enter the hall.","She was startled and quickly put down the bun to rise and curtsy, \"This consort greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and sat down at the table. Glancing at the large buns on the table, he asked curiously, \"What are these?\"","Yanshu could only introduce them, \"These are buns that this consort's mother made herself and brought this morning. Would Your Majesty like to try some?\"","Tsk, she had just been thinking of not giving him any, after all he was used to fine cuisine and probably wouldn't appreciate such hearty fare.","Who knew that as soon as she finished speaking, he said, \"Alright,\" and picked one up to eat.","As he ate, he even commented, \"Fresh and flavorful, with a nice chew to the wrapper.\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"Since Your Majesty enjoys them, please have some more.\"","She even proactively poured him a cup of tea, \"Your Majesty, drink some tea, be careful not to choke.\"","In her heart though, she thought, [Eat a couple less, leave some for me!!! These were made by my mother, it's been three years since I've gotten to eat them!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","However, these buns really were quite good. He pretended not to hear her mental cries and ate four in a row.","This left Yanshu's heart dripping blood.","But before she could say anything, she heard the system say, [Don't worry about the buns now, Consort An has been gossiping to the Empress Dowager lately about the emperor giving you the golden bowl!]","Golden bowl?","Yanshu raised an eyebrow. She even knew about that?","Quite capable, isn't she!","Well, in that case, she could feel free to use her trump card.","So she said to the person contentedly eating her buns in front of her, \"Your Majesty, this consort has written a new story. Would you like to take a look after you finish eating?\"","Yuwen Lan had just finished the fourth bun and was feeling a bit full, so he wiped his hands and said, \"Alright, let me see it.\"","Yanshu then took a stack of manuscript papers from the table and handed them to him.","Yuwen Lan picked them up and saw the title was \"A Real Man Stands Up\".","Hmm?","He raised an eyebrow. \"...This name is quite special. What's it about?\"","But he heard her say, \"The protagonist of this story is a young master. This young master was weak from birth due to issues in the womb, so he was sickly as a child. But he persevered and studied hard, learning many skills. Unfortunately, he married a rather scheming wife who, thinking her husband was in poor health with no future, actually became involved with her father-in-law.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Wasn't this about the Minister of Rites and his daughter-in-law's affair?","But... he had been wanting to know more about it too.","So he hurriedly read on.","However, after a while he was surprised to discover that this matter was not as simple as just an affair.","In her story, she wrote that the father-in-law and daughter-in-law had even had a child together.","\"???\""]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35","paragraphs":["Could such a thing really happen?","The emperor was once again shocked...","Could it be that the grandson of the second branch of the Minister of Rites... was actually his son???","Yuwen Lan tried asking, \"Is that really true? That child is actually that old man's?\"","Yanshu nodded and said, \"Of course it's true. Because that young master is weak and actually unable to have children, so the child must be his father's!\"","[Look at you, so shocked just from a story. If you knew this actually happened in real life at the Minister of Rites' household, wouldn't you be scared to death?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So it was actually true!","How could the Minister of Rites be so outrageous!!!","He tried hard to suppress his shock and anger, and asked again, \"Then, did no one in the family discover this?\"","Yanshu said, \"This old man is the head of the family, his wife passed away many years ago, so no one manages him. Even if a few servants in the house know about it, they wouldn't dare say anything. Moreover, this old man appears very righteous on the outside, people never imagined he could be so morally bankrupt and shameless! He usually favors this grandson, and outsiders just thought he was considerate of his son's weak health, so he especially valued his grandson.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan thought to himself that he seemed to have heard that the Minister of Rites was particularly fond of his young grandson.","So this was the reason???","Tsk, it's really too outrageous, too outrageous, too outrageous!","He tried to calm himself down, and then heard Yanshu continue, \"Of course, later the son himself discovered this matter. Angry, he simply left home to struggle on his own. Later he was fortunate enough to meet a miraculous doctor from the jianghu, who gradually nursed his body back to health, and he even expanded his business more and more.\"","This was clearly another plot she had added. Yuwen Lan nodded slightly and asked, \"Then what about his father?\"","Yanshu said, \"As they say, if you don't want others to know, unless you don't do it yourself. That father and daughter-in-law were too outrageous, and one day the truth was revealed and they were despised by everyone. Other family members also angrily cut ties with them, and the large mansion gradually fell into decline. When the old man saw he was about to die, he finally thought of repenting to his son and went to beg him several times.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Did his son forgive him?\"","\"Of course not!\"","Yanshu said, \"How could such a thing be forgiven? The son was certainly unmoved. Later, that daughter-in-law also went to beg him shamelessly, and he directly had people chase her out to fend for herself.\"","Yuwen Lan sighed, \"If only it were really like that. People often can't distinguish right from wrong, especially when entangled with family ties.\"","\"Exactly!\"","Yanshu also said, \"That's why stories should break free from the constraints of reality. What's difficult to achieve in reality can be realized in stories, making readers feel more satisfied.\"","Then she asked him, \"What does Your Majesty think of this story?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of agreement, \"Not bad.\"","Then he saw her hurriedly say, \"Then please help your subject pass it to Chancellor Zou and have the booksellers publish it.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"In such a hurry? Didn't you just publish two yesterday?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"The more the better, after all, readers like it.\"","But in her heart, she thought, [Consort An has already gone to complain to the Empress Dowager about the golden bowl, I must also have some response! There must be give and take for this fight to be interesting!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Fine, it turns out she not only likes to watch the excitement, but also likes to fight.","But what's the matter with Consort An?","Did she go to the Empress Dowager to talk about him giving Yanshu the golden bowl?","Hmph, that's fine too.","He nodded and said, \"Zou Mozhong will enter the palace later, I'll help you pass it to him.\"","Then he picked up the manuscript and was about to walk out.","Yanshu said, \"This subject thanks Your Majesty.\" But she was also a bit puzzled, \"Why did Your Majesty come just now?\"","It wasn't even noon yet, still far from nighttime for sleeping, yet he suddenly came, and as soon as he arrived he ate four of her large buns.","Yuwen Lan made a sound and said, \"I got tired of reading memorials, so I came out for a walk.\"","Ahem, actually it was because he knew she had just met with her family members and wanted to come see if she was happy.","But... judging by how enthusiastically she was eating buns earlier, she should be very happy.","Speaking of which, these buns were really quite delicious.","So he picked up another one and said, \"I'll go back first, and come again in the evening.\"","Then he walked out.","Hmm, walking while eating, he couldn't stop for a moment.","Behind him, Yanshu, who had just finished respectfully seeing him off, returned to the table and looked at the few buns left, twitching the corner of her mouth.","If she had known this would happen, she wouldn't have asked him earlier.","Eating five of hers in one go, this person really wasn't polite.","Meanwhile, in the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","After Consort An thanked the Empress Dowager for her grace, she accompanied her in conversation for a while before finally turning to the main topic.","\"Yesterday, the Ankang county lord came to find this subject, saying she wanted to take a look at that golden bowl that Tubo offered as tribute last time. She wanted to have craftsmen make a small copy as a birthday gift for the Grand Princess next month.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"Ankang has always been filial, but I wonder about the skills of the outside craftsmen? Can they make something that looks proper?\"","Consort An smiled and said, \"This subject is also curious, but unfortunately there's no way for the Ankang county lord to see it.\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound and looked at her, \"Why is that?\"","Consort An lowered her eyes and said, \"This subject asked Zhao Shun, the manager of the Qianming Palace storehouse yesterday, and found out that His Majesty had bestowed that golden bowl to Consort Yi some days ago.\"","After finishing, she carefully waited for the Empress Dowager's reaction.","The Empress Dowager was indeed surprised for a moment and asked, \"Bestowed to Consort Yi?\"","Consort An nodded and said, \"Indeed so, and it seems to have been before Consort Yi was injured.\"","— She couldn't say too much, just enough to let the Empress Dowager know that the golden bowl was not bestowed because of Consort Yi's injury while protecting the emperor, but was given without any reason.","However, after a moment, the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"His Majesty indeed values Consort Yi, but after all, this is His Majesty's own possession. Whoever His Majesty wishes to reward is his own decision.\"","Consort An paused. The Empress Dowager wasn't angry?","Or perhaps she was actually displeased but didn't want to let her see it?","But in any case, she could only nod and say at this point, \"The Empress Dowager's words are absolutely correct. So this time we can only let the county lord return disappointed.\"","But the Empress Dowager's smile faded, and she said, \"Those words are inappropriate. It wasn't something she should have seen in the first place, so how can you speak of disappointment? Are His Majesty's possessions something anyone can see?\"","Consort An paused, hurriedly kneeling to pay respects, \"This subject spoke wrongly, please forgive me, Empress Dowager.\"","She knew that while the Empress Dowager seemed to be talking about the Ankang county lord, she was actually speaking for her to hear.","The Empress Dowager closed her eyes and said, \"I'm tired, you may leave.\"","Consort An didn't dare say anything more, could only respond and retreat out of the hall.","As the hall quieted, Zhushu came forward to massage the Empress Dowager's shoulders, saying, \"This is the first time the Empress Dowager has spoken such harsh words to Consort An.\"","The Empress Dowager closed her eyes and said, \"No matter who it is, thoughts that shouldn't exist must not exist.\"","She had just promoted this girl a few days ago, and she already wanted to use her as a pawn?","People shouldn't be too stupid, but being too clever is also not good.","When Consort An returned to Lanlin Hall, her mother Lady Tian had just arrived back at the Minister's mansion.","As soon as Lady Tian alighted from the carriage, she saw her sister-in-law Lady Yang rush up to her, urgently asking, \"Did elder sister-in-law mention Chang's matter to the Consort?\"","Lady Tian said coldly, \"The Empress Dowager just gave the Consort authority to manage internal affairs a few days ago. The Consort has been extremely busy lately. I only saw her briefly and exchanged a few hurried words. How could there be time to mention such things?\"","She walked on by herself.","Probably afraid the other would keep pestering her, after a few steps, she added, \"Even if I had mentioned it, the Consort wouldn't be able to help.\"","Of course, Lady Yang was disappointed with such a result.","Plus her disdainful expression, Lady Yang immediately became angry too, snorting, \"No matter how busy the Consort is, shouldn't she still care about the life and death of her own family? She can't have forgotten her surname and where she came from, right?\"","As soon as these words came out, Lady Tian immediately stopped walking again and angrily said, \"Sister-in-law, how dare you be so disrespectful to the Consort? Be careful not to let others hear, or the nobles in the palace will punish you!\"","Hmph, using the palace to pressure her again?","But Lady Yang simply put her hands on her hips and started making a scene, \"Punish me? Fine, I'll wait right here! Let's see if the Consort really punishes me someday, to gain a good reputation for putting righteousness before family!\"","Before Lady Tian could say anything else, she actually covered her face and started crying, \"Everyone bullies us mother and son! Outsiders bully us, even our own family bullies us! Do we have any way to live anymore!\"","Here we go again!","Seeing that all the servants in the courtyard were laughing at her, Lady Tian no longer wished to argue. She muttered \"shameless woman\" under her breath and quickly walked away.","Lady Yang cried for a while, but seeing it had no effect, she wiped her tears and stormed off to the front courtyard of her father-in-law, the Minister of Rites.","However, no matter how much she pleaded, the old man refused to see her.","He only sent a page boy to tell her, \"Second Madam, the Master truly has no way to help. Currently, His Majesty is strictly governing officials and has issued an order to the Imperial Academy. This time, no matter who it is, if anyone dares to use backdoor connections to admit people arbitrarily, it will be a serious crime if discovered. Moreover, many government offices have recently changed personnel, and the Master is not familiar with those now in charge of this matter. Even if he wanted to help, there's really no way.\"","\"No way?\" Lady Yang laughed coldly, raising her voice, \"So now the Master doesn't even care about Chang? Fine then, a father who doesn't care if his child lives or dies, no one in this household cares, we might as well all tear off our masks one day and stop living!\"","In Qianming Palace.","Recently, with the Imperial Academy opening admissions for new students, Zou Mozhong needed to frequently enter the palace to report various matters to the emperor.","This time, he presented the list of proposed admissions for the first batch to the emperor.","After Yuwen Lan looked it over, he returned the list to him and also gave him a stack of manuscripts.","Zou Mozhong was startled for a moment, then immediately asked, \"Is this a new work by the Carefree Young Master?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Indeed. Chancellor Zou, please take a look first.\"","Zou Mozhong was eager to do so and began reading it on the spot.","After reading, he repeatedly exclaimed, \"The Carefree Young Master's stories always have unexpected beginnings, but the protagonists always have satisfying endings. Take this story for example - the immoral ones receive karmic retribution and are ultimately punished by heaven, while those who refuse to give up are able to break free from the mire in time, experiencing rebirth. It's thought-provoking and a good story.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"If that's the case, then have the booksellers publish it quickly. Let the people read this good story; perhaps they can gain something from it.\"","Zou Mozhong quickly agreed and left the palace with the manuscript. On his way back to his residence, he delivered it to a bookseller.","Seeing that it was a new work by the Carefree Young Master, the bookseller immediately arranged for people to print or copy it. Before sunset, the first batch of story books was ready.","Needless to say, as soon as this new story book went on sale, it sparked another buying frenzy.","After reading the story, everyone unanimously condemned the father-in-law and daughter-in-law who had an incestuous relationship, and deeply sympathized with and admired the young man who persevered through hardship.","Of course, many people also remembered the Carefree Young Master's prophetic revelation about Xie Pei, the Communications Commissioner of the Southwest, some time ago. So they began speculating again -","Who exactly was this old man who had an affair with his daughter-in-law?","... Could it be some high-ranking official in the court?","But judging by the age, if so, they would have to consider those among the older generation...","Early the next morning, as Yanshu was leisurely enjoying her breakfast, she heard the system say, [The readers have already narrowed it down to about a dozen people. It's estimated that by tonight, they'll be close to guessing who it is.]","While sucking the soup from a xiaolongbao, Yanshu thought to herself that she had already shown restraint. Otherwise, if she had directly written that the old man had two sons, and the eldest son had a son and a daughter, the outside world would have immediately guessed it was Song Zhiyun, the Minister of Rites.","[By the way, has that old man read it?] she asked.","The system replied, [He sent someone to buy the story book this morning and is reading it now.]","A moment later, [He's finished reading.]","Yanshu quickly asked, [What was his reaction?]","The system answered, [He was so angry he smashed his teacup, vase, inkstone... tsk, now he's fainted.]","Yanshu, [??? He fainted?]","The system, [That's right. The servants heard the commotion and discovered him. They're now carrying him to bed and hurriedly looking for a doctor.]","Yanshu, [Tsk tsk, I thought he would be like Xie Pei and fall down in fright first, but he directly fainted? With such weak mental fortitude, how did he manage to carry on his misdeeds for so many years?]","The system sighed, [Mainly because this old man has been living in constant fear ever since the sacrificial ceremony. After hearing about the incident with the Southwest Communications Commissioner, he's been worried that your story would expose his secrets. Today, when he saw that not only was he exposed, but it was written even more harshly than Xie Pei's case, of course he couldn't handle it.]","Yanshu curled her lip. Serves him right!","Now it's up to Consort An. That day she only revealed a small tidbit about her, but now that the big news is out, wonder when she'll see it?","The system, [Don't worry, the Song family is about to send a message to the palace. She'll know soon.]","Yanshu's eyes lit up, [That's great then.]","So, she'll just wait to continue enjoying the drama.","Hmm, come to think of it, eating xiaolongbao while following the drama makes them taste even more delicious!","Soon after, news from the Minister of Rites' mansion was indeed delivered to the palace.","Upon hearing that her grandfather had fainted, Consort An was startled and hurriedly asked, \"How could this happen? Hasn't grandfather always been in good health?\"","The housekeeper who came to report the news cried, \"Yesterday, the Second Madam caused another big scene in the mansion over the matter of the Second Young Master entering the Imperial Academy. Not only did she argue with the Madam, but she also went to find the Master. When the Master refused to see her, she made a fuss outside the door, saying things like 'the whole family doesn't care if she and her son live or die,' 'can't even rely on one's own father,' and even 'one day we'll all tear off our masks and stop living.' I think these words must have greatly angered the Master.\"","Consort An immediately said angrily, \"Second Uncle's health has always been poor, it's already good enough if he can take care of himself, how can he be expected to look after Chang? How could she say such things!\"","The housekeeper said, \"Exactly! No matter how good the Master's health is, he can't withstand such a disturbance! This morning, while the Master was reading a book, he suddenly fainted. Before fainting, he smashed quite a few things. He must have been extremely angry.\"","Hearing this, Consort An was also angry.","But after thinking about what the housekeeper said, she suddenly paused.","-- Grandfather fainted while reading a book?","She hesitated for a moment, then tried asking, \"What book was Grandfather reading before he fainted?\"","The housekeeper had no idea and simply said, \"This servant doesn't know, only heard that it was a book the Master had someone buy from the street this morning... Now the Young Master and Madam have already called for a doctor, but to be safe, they hope that the Consort can find an imperial physician to examine the Master, just to be more thorough...\"","Consort An understood her parents' intentions.","-- Grandfather was the pillar of the family. Her father was currently only an Assistant Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial, a sixth-rank official. How could he compare to her grandfather's second-rank official position?","So if anything were to happen to Grandfather, the family's loss would be significant.","Naturally, the imperial physicians in the palace would be better than doctors outside, so her parents could only do their utmost to save Grandfather, the head of the family.","At this point, the housekeeper had finished speaking, and Consort An immediately nodded, \"I'll go ask for the Empress Dowager's permission right away.\"","Grandfather was an old minister of the Empress Dowager, so she thought the Empress Dowager would likely grant this request.","The housekeeper also agreed and was about to take her leave when she heard Consort An say, \"Wait, when you go back, have someone send me the book Grandfather was reading before he fainted.\"","The housekeeper didn't understand why, but quickly agreed and hurried out of the palace.","Half an hour later, an imperial physician arrived at the Minister's mansion.","And the item Consort An had requested was also delivered to Lanlin Hall.","Consort An saw that it was actually a story book, and the author was none other than the recently famous Carefree Young Master.","Her heart jolted, and she quickly opened it to read. Soon, her mouth fell open in shock.","-- How was this story somewhat similar to what was written on that discarded paper in Ganlu Palace the other day? It also described a father-in-law and daughter-in-law violating human ethics...","But, but, but, how did Li Yanshu know what the Carefree Young Master was going to write?","However, as she continued reading, she became even more shocked.","-- The father-in-law and daughter-in-law in the story even had a child together?","Because she already harbored doubts, at this moment, she inevitably associated it with her own family.","Could it be...","Chang was actually...","This was too terrifying!","Consort An threw the book to the ground, her heart pounding.","She shook her head vigorously, trying not to think about it anymore.","However, that thought had already taken root in her mind like a seed, sprouting and growing.","She tried to calm herself down and think through this matter carefully.","-- At Grandfather's age, he normally wouldn't enjoy reading these kinds of popular story books.","But this morning, Grandfather had someone buy it and bring it back.","And he fainted right after finishing this book...","Could it be... really related to this book?","If that's true, thinking back to what Second Aunt Yang said yesterday...","She said Chang's real father couldn't be relied upon...","And that they might as well tear off their masks and stop living...","Consort An jolted awake and immediately called a young eunuch in the hall, \"Quickly go to the Minister of Rites' residence and tell my father two things...\"","Yanshu, following the system, had spent almost the entire day observing the drama at the Minister of Rites' residence, which proved to be both exciting and fulfilling.","In the morning, the household members were in a flurry trying to treat the old man's illness. However, due to his advanced age, even after the imperial physician arrived, they could only barely rouse him, and he still couldn't get out of bed.","The imperial physician diagnosed that the old man was likely to have a stroke, which greatly alarmed the Song family.","Meanwhile, Consort An sent two messages from the palace:","First, she instructed her parents to quickly confine her second aunt, Lady Yang, to prevent her from speaking nonsense that outsiders might hear.","Second, she told the family to find a way to stop the circulation of her new novel, ensuring that no more people could read it.","So, in addition to frantically searching for doctors to treat the old man, Consort An's parents also had to handle these two tasks.","The couple was in complete disarray, overwhelmed with tasks. As a result, Consort An's father accidentally fell down the stairs, while her mother scalded herself with hot tea...","In contrast, Yanshu was thoroughly enjoying the spectacle, munching on melon seeds while watching the chaos unfold.","Just then, she heard the system say, [Latest news! The people sent by the Minister of Rites' residence tried to buy up all the copies of the novel, offering to pay to stop its printing. But the booksellers refused, saying the price was too low. So they started vandalizing the bookshops and were caught red-handed by passing government officials.]","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, [Tsk, why did the officials show up so promptly this time?]","The system replied, [That's because of the Emperor's recent decree. The entire court, from top to bottom, is enforcing stricter regulations, making them much more efficient.]","Yanshu nodded, [My golden thigh has indeed done quite a few good deeds.]","Well, this worked out perfectly.","— The Capital Official was still under the Emperor's direct control, and the Minister of Rites was currently out of favor with the Emperor due to the ceremonial issues. It was likely that the Capital Official wouldn't side with the Minister's residence and would investigate the case thoroughly.","Tsk tsk, it would be even better if they could uncover the reason why the Song family didn't want the novel to be printed.","She took a leisurely sip of tea.","After all, there was no fear of things getting out of hand now – the bigger, the better!","Meanwhile, in Qianming Palace, the Imperial Guard was also reporting the situation to Yuwen Lan.","\"Your Majesty, the people from the Minister of Rites' residence who vandalized the bookshops have been apprehended by the Capital Official.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Tell the Capital Official to investigate the cause thoroughly. Punish those who deserve punishment, judge those who need judgment. If any officials are found to have violated the law, report it to the Imperial Censorate immediately. There must be no favoritism.\"","The Imperial Guard immediately complied and then reported, \"In addition, the Song family has confined Lady Yang of the second branch. We're not sure if they will take any further actions.\"","Hm, they've confined Lady Yang?","They truly are a nest of vipers.","Yuwen Lan only said, \"This woman may be useful later. She must not die.\"","The Imperial Guard acknowledged the order and withdrew to carry it out.","Yuwen Lan glanced out the window, noticing that dusk had fallen, and instructed Fu Hai, \"Set up dinner in Ganlu Palace. I'll dine there.\"","Soon after, Yanshu welcomed the Emperor, along with a table full of delicious dishes.","As she bowed to Yuwen Lan, she watched the palace servants set the table. When they finished arranging the bowls and plates, she glanced over and her eyes lit up.","Tonight's dinner included mountain delicacies like dragon shoots and fiddlehead ferns, chicken with white fungus, osmanthus fish strips, eight-treasure diced rabbit, and the main courses were roast pheasant and roast lamb. There were also her favorites: two-colored bean cakes and lotus seed tofu.","She asked excitedly, \"Why is the meal so lavish today?\"","And it was all her favorites too!","Yuwen Lan glanced at her, sat down at the table, and said casually, \"I ate your steamed buns today. Fearing you might complain, I consider this compensation.\"","Complain to him...","Yanshu paused briefly, then smiled shamelessly, \"How could I be so petty, Your Majesty? Besides, isn't everything that belongs to me also yours? I wouldn't complain no matter how much you ate.\"","As she finished speaking, she saw him look her up and down with deep, dark eyes. He nodded, \"Indeed, what's yours is mine.\"","Then, with a hint of a smile, he picked up his chopsticks and said, \"Eat.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, what was that look about?","Why did it make her feel a bit uneasy?","But...","With so many delicious dishes before her, eating was the priority.","So she picked up her chopsticks and started eating too.","Mmm, everything was indeed delicious tonight—","The dragon shoots, fiddlehead ferns, and bamboo shoots were all mountain delicacies, prepared to perfection by the imperial chefs;","The chicken with white fungus and eight-treasure diced rabbit each had their own unique charm, with the ingredients complementing each other beautifully;","The osmanthus fish strips were crispy on the outside and tender inside, and the roast pheasant and lamb were even more impressive, their savory flavors infused with the aroma of charcoal, leaving a lingering taste.","Her favorite two-colored bean cakes were fragrant and smooth, while the lotus seed tofu melted in her mouth, perfectly satisfying her tastes.","Yanshu thoroughly enjoyed this meal.","After dinner, they played a game of pitch-pot to aid digestion.","— Ever since she had \"struggled\" to win against the Emperor last time, Yanshu had been practicing in secret.","This time, her improvement was evident, as she managed to land the arrow in the pot's mouth several times, impressing Yuwen Lan.","As the night deepened and they both worked up a sweat from playing, having digested their meal, they each went to bathe and prepare for bed.","Perhaps due to the excitement of the game earlier, Yanshu's face was flushed when she emerged from her bath.","Yuwen Lan felt a twinge in his heart at the sight. As soon as she climbed onto the bed, he pulled her into his embrace.","\"The novel is written for others to read, but remember, what's between us is far more important,\" he said softly.","Yanshu, nestled in his arms, obediently responded, \"I understand, Your Majesty.\"","As she spoke, she nuzzled against his chest.","— Yes, she had to constantly remember that the Emperor was her golden thigh, and she must cling to him tightly no matter what.","With a golden thigh, she could have everything!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This girl, clearly in love with him, why did she always call him her golden thigh?","Was she still worried that he might abandon her one day?","Did she doubt the sincerity of his feelings?","He reached out and gently lifted her chin, saying earnestly once more, \"I will protect you. There's no need to worry about things that won't happen.\"","Yanshu was taken aback.","For a moment, she saw her own reflection in his eyes.","Hmm, was he being so gentle to say words of love?","So the Emperor knew how to speak romantically after all...","Yuwen Lan chuckled inwardly.","He wasn't made of stone, how could he not know how to speak words of love?","Silly girl.","Thinking this, he leaned down.","However, before he could touch her, she suddenly said, \"There's something I want to report to Your Majesty.\"","Hm?","Yuwen Lan asked in a husky voice, \"What is it?\"","She replied, \"If anyone tries to cause trouble for me because of the novel in the near future, please tell them you wrote it.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36","paragraphs":["Those cherry-like lips were right before his eyes. Just a slight dip of his head and he could touch them.","But he never expected to hear her say such a thing at this moment.","Yuwen Lan was stunned. \"What?\" he asked.","Yanshu repeated herself, \"If in the coming days anyone tries to link me with the Carefree Young Master, I request Your Majesty to help deflect such rumors on my behalf.\"","YuwenLan frowned and asked, \"Why would anyone link you with the Carefree Young Master?\"","Had something happened that he wasn't aware of?","Sure enough, she coughed lightly and said, \"Well... recently I discovered someone was secretly stealing the discarded papers from my palace, probably trying to find out what I've been writing.\"","Yuwen Lan's brow furrowed deeper. \"Someone's been stealing your waste paper? Why didn't you tell me earlier?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, where's the fun in telling you early?","If she had told him earlier, he would have at most sent people to catch the servant stealing the papers.","Even if they found out the culprit was from Consort An's palace, Consort An could easily deny any knowledge and absolve herself of suspicion. After all, stealing a bit of trash in the palace wasn't a serious crime.","How could that compare to the thrill of first throwing the opponent's camp into disarray, then watching them panic, question everything, and have their beliefs crumble?","Of course, given Consort An's intellect, after seeing the small tidbits she had deliberately leaked earlier and then reading the official work today, she was quite likely to make a connection between her and the Carefree Young Master.","She wasn't afraid of what Consort An might do; she just wanted to lay the groundwork with the Emperor first.","After all, as she wrote more and more novels in the future, it was bound to invite more speculation. Only the Emperor's identity could perfectly quell all doubts and make people accept it without complaint.","Hehe, it was fortunate that she had thought ahead to use a male pen name. It would be even more suitable for the Emperor to use.","Yuwen Lan, who had been listening silently, was bewildered.","So she had dug this pit long ago, waiting for him to fall in?","And now, she was making excuses with an innocent face, \"Because I didn't know who was stealing the trash, I had no way to report it to Your Majesty even if I wanted to.\"","Yuwen Lan let out a mocking laugh. \"Then why have you decided to tell me now?\"","Yanshu replied with a clear conscience, \"Because Your Majesty just said you would protect me. So I'm telling you now.\"","[Cut the nonsense, it's time to use you now. After all, you were half responsible for the idea of publishing novels, so you have to take care of it whether you want to or not!]","Yuwen Lan was speechless.","She was so brazen in shirking responsibility?","However, it was rare for her to come asking for his help. Besides, if he didn't help his own woman, who else would?","So he said, \"Of course I keep my word, and you should have come to me earlier about this matter. But it's late now, I'll make arrangements in the morning.\"","Yanshu quickly agreed, \"Thank you for Your Majesty's grace.\"","[Tomorrow morning isn't too late. I bet Consort An and her family won't be able to sleep a wink tonight, hehe...]","As she was secretly rejoicing, she saw Yuwen Lan pull her into his embrace. \"I'm right here in front of you, don't think about other things.\"","Yanshu was taken aback, and stubbornly said, \"I wasn't...\"","Before she could finish, her waist was gently pinched.","Yanshu jolted, and saw him raise an eyebrow, saying, \"That's the price for lying.\"","Yanshu was startled and quickly said, \"I wouldn't dare...\"","Tsk, how did this man seem to have the ability to read minds...","But before she could finish that thought, she was silenced by a kiss.","Just as Yanshu had predicted, the residence of the Minister of Rites was brightly lit all night.","In Lanlin Hall, Consort An also barely closed her eyes the entire night.","Consort An had many thoughts—","The affair between her grandfather and her second aunt was most likely true. Ah Chang might really be their child...","Although she desperately didn't want to face it, it was already a fact.","But now the most crucial thing was—what was the deal with Yanshu's discarded papers?","And what was her relationship with the Carefree Young Master?","Why did her waste paper and the Carefree Young Master's novel talk about the same thing?","Why did both of them know her grandfather's secret?!","The more she thought about these things, the more chilled to the bone she felt.","Could it be... that Yanshu was actually the Carefree Young Master?","But how could she have such ability to know so many secrets of the officials?","After tossing and turning for a long while, she finally crawled out of bed and called for Liu Di, saying, \"Go tell Shuang Xi to wait outside Ganlu Palace now. Don't miss anything thrown out from inside, bring everything to me.\"","Liu Di quickly agreed and hurried out to relay the message.","Shuang Xi had no choice but to go to Ganlu Palace.","He waited from the early hours until dawn, and from dawn until the sun was high in the sky, before finally seeing someone come out of Ganlu Palace with a paper basket.","He immediately followed quietly, and when the person had finished emptying the trash from the basket, he quickly picked it up and ran towards Lanlin Hall.","However, before he had gone far, several people suddenly rushed out from the roadside and shouted at him, \"Stop! What are you up to, sneaking around like this?\"","Shuang Xi was startled and quickly looked up, only to see that it was Yao Shun, the head of the Inner Court Supervisory Office.","The Inner Court Supervisory Office was known for its ruthlessness. Shuang Xi immediately panicked and said, \"Nothing, I wasn't doing anything...\"","Before he could finish speaking, the other party had already grabbed him and began searching him without a word.","The waste paper he had hidden immediately spilled out.","Yao Shun picked up a piece of paper, looked at it, and suddenly frowned, saying, \"You dare to steal His Majesty's handwriting? Arrest him and interrogate him under torture!\"","...","Consort An hadn't slept all night. At dawn, she finally received news from her family, saying that her grandfather still couldn't get out of bed, and several doctors who had been called all said he had suffered a stroke.","This news was undoubtedly a bolt from the blue. Once her grandfather had a stroke, it was tantamount to directly bidding farewell to officialdom. The Song family's path forward would be difficult.","However, before she could think of a good solution, she saw her maid Mei Xue hurrying in to report, \"It's terrible, my lady, Shuang Xi has been arrested by the Inner Court Supervisory Office!\"","\"What?\"","Consort An was shocked.","—Even if Shuang Xi was seen picking up trash from Ganlu Palace, it wasn't a major offense. People in the palace often picked up leftover food and tattered clothes.","How did the Inner Court Supervisory Office get involved?","Then she heard Mei Xue say, \"It turns out that among the trash he picked up from Ganlu Palace, there was His Majesty's handwriting.\"","His Majesty's handwriting?","Consort An was stunned, suddenly struck by a bad premonition.","However, at this moment, she saw Fu Hai enter the hall with a serious face, saying, \"His Majesty is in the Palace of Benevolent Peace and requests your presence for questioning.\"","...","As Consort An walked, she kept wondering why His Majesty's handwriting would appear in the waste paper basket.","She suddenly had a vague feeling that this matter had been Yanshu's scheme to lure her from the very beginning.","When she arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace, she saw not only the Empress Dowager and the Emperor, but Yanshu was also standing to one side. Besides them, there was also Yao Shun, the head of the Inner Court Supervisory Office.","After she had paid her respects to the Empress Dowager and the Emperor, she heard Yao Shun say, \"Just now, this servant caught a young eunuch outside Ganlu Palace, sneakily attempting to steal His Majesty's handwriting. Upon investigation, he turned out to be from Lanlin Hall. May I ask Consort An, did you send him?\"","Consort An quickly said, \"I only just learned of this matter. I beg Your Majesty to understand, I knew nothing about this.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Yao Shun beckoned to one side, and someone dragged in a person with a bruised and bloodied face. It was none other than Shuang Xi.","Consort An was shocked by the sight, but she still said firmly, \"This is indeed a servant from my palace, but I don't know why he did this. I absolutely did not instruct him to do so.\"","Having been in the palace for so long, she knew that as long as she didn't admit guilt and Shuang Xi didn't confess, no one could forcibly pin the crime on her.","As soon as she finished speaking, she heard the Emperor say, \"Take him away and continue the interrogation.\"","Yao Shun complied and had people drag Shuang Xi away again.","Consort An maintained a calm exterior, but she was very nervous inside.","Stealing trash was a minor offense, but stealing His Majesty's handwriting was a serious crime.","Once implicated, it could even be punishable by death.","At this moment, she heard the Emperor speak again, \"Even if you didn't instruct him, he is still from your palace.\"","Consort An immediately knelt down and bowed her head, saying, \"It is my fault for not managing my palace people well. I have indeed failed in my duty. Please, Your Majesty, punish me.\"","Yuwen Lan then looked at the Empress Dowager and said, \"This is not a small matter. If we let it go, who knows how many people in the back palace will follow suit. It would be a joke if word got out.\"","The Empress Dowager could only nod slightly and say, \"Indeed so.\"","Yuwen Lan then turned back to Consort An, \"You no longer need to manage the Internal Affairs Bureau. Until this matter is cleared up, you are confined to your palace and may not come out.\"","Consort An's heart tightened.","Once confined, she would no longer be able to help her grandfather in any way!","However, at this moment, she herself was also in imminent danger.","She could only kneel and respond, \"This concubine obeys the command.\"","Then she rose and left the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","— The only plan now was to wait for Shuang Xi to take the blame himself. Once he died, she would be able to clear her name.","But how could she continue investigating Li Yanshu's matter?","Behind her, the Empress Dowager suddenly spoke, \"How could this little eunuch who was picked up as trash in the harem steal His Majesty's handwriting?\"","Yuwen Lan replied without changing his expression, \"I saw that Consort Yi's handwriting was not good, so I've been having her practice writing lately. Sometimes when there are no copybooks, I would write something myself for her to imitate. Perhaps recently, Ganlu Palace has been using more paper, which aroused the suspicions of those with ulterior motives.\"","The Empress Dowager already understood and didn't say anything more.","After all, she was the one who gave Consort An the job of assisting with the Internal Affairs Bureau. She didn't expect something to go wrong so quickly.","The Emperor making a scene in her palace today was just to leave her speechless, wasn't it?","What a fool. Never mind.","On the surface, she nodded and said, \"That's indeed a good habit.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of agreement, then suddenly said, \"I heard the Minister of Rites is ill.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"Yes, yesterday Consort An came to ask for my permission to send an imperial physician to examine him. Later, the physician came to report to me that the Minister of Rites had suffered a stroke. Poor man, this illness is troublesome. He will suffer greatly.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly and casually said, \"He is after all an old minister. I should send someone to check on him.\"","The people in the Palace of Benevolent Peace who heard this all thought he was taking the initiative to repair his relationship with the Empress Dowager.","After all, that Minister of Rites was the Empress Dowager's man. The Emperor sending someone to express sympathy, wasn't that equivalent to giving face to the Empress Dowager?","The Empress Dowager didn't think much of it either, just nodding and saying, \"It's his fortune that Your Majesty can have such a considerate heart.\"","Not long after, Yanshu followed Yuwen Lan out of the Palace of Benevolent Peace to bid farewell.","Fortunately able to hitch a ride on the imperial carriage again, she hurriedly asked Yuwen Lan when no one else was around, \"When does Your Majesty plan to send people to the Song family?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Wait until I've decided on the right personnel. Why do you ask?\"","Yanshu said, \"It's nothing. This concubine was just thinking that the Song family is probably quite busy recently, so Your Majesty's people should go at the right time.\"","[Tsk, the timing must be just right. It would be best to catch them when their household is in chaos, to see all the excitement at once!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She spoke as if she could go herself.","But then he heard her sigh regretfully in her heart, [If only I could go too.]","— After catching cheaters in the act on the main street last time, she discovered that watching drama unfold in person was truly different.","For example, if she hadn't followed that Zhao Chengwen, how would she have known that even the Eldest Princess's Imperial Son-in-law could be so lacking in stamina?","So if you can watch in person, you should go in person. The details are also very important!","Little did she know that the man beside her was struggling to control his twitching brow. He hurriedly said, \"I will find a time to send a trustworthy minister. Don't worry. You should go back and think about your story instead.\"","Tsk, this girl, bringing up stamina again!","At the Ministry of Rites Minister's Residence.","Seeing that Lady Yang had been confined for a day, her anger still hadn't dissipated. She was still smashing bowls and kicking furniture, still making a fuss about wanting to go out.","After quite a commotion, finally a housekeeper came to the door and said to her, \"Second Madam, the Master has already spoken. It was you who upset the Old Master to this state. Until the Old Master recovers, you should stay obediently in your room and not think about coming out.\"","Lady Yang immediately cursed, \"You're really good at pinning the blame on others! You're bullying me for being honest, bullying me because no one will stand up for me, right? Be careful, if you push me too far, we'll all go down together!!!\"","At this time in the front courtyard, the couple of the Song family's eldest branch had just received a letter from the palace, saying that their only hope, their daughter Consort An, had also been confined.","The couple was naturally shocked. They wanted to ask for the reason, but the person who delivered the message just coldly threw down a sentence and left.","Just as the couple was anxious like ants on a hot pan, they heard the cursing of Lady Yang from the second branch again.","Lady Tian cursed, \"This ignorant thing, isn't the family chaotic enough? I really want to sew her mouth shut!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, she saw her husband Song Yuankui pause, then suddenly lower his voice and say, \"Then don't let her shout anymore.\"","Lady Yang made a fuss until evening, and finally tired out.","Just as dinner was being sent in, a servant boy suddenly entered the room and said, \"Second Madam, please wait. Be careful, there might be poison in the food.\"","She was startled and immediately put down her chopsticks, but then looked at him suspiciously and asked, \"How do you know?\"","The servant boy didn't answer her, but just took a bit of rice and vegetables and threw them into the fish tank in the room. In an instant, all the fish in the tank turned belly up.","Lady Yang was shocked and immediately raged, \"How dare they! They actually dare to kill people! I'm going out right now to reason with them!\"","But that servant boy stopped her, \"Second Madam, please calm down. They are determined to kill you anyway. If you go out now, you'll only alert them. When they resort to force, how can you escape?\"","Lady Yang then came to her senses, her face full of fear as she asked, \"Then what should I do? Wait here to die?\"","The boy then asked her, \"Second Madam, do you know why they want to harm you?\"","Lady Yang felt guilty inside, and stammered, \"They probably fear that if something happens to the Old Master, the second branch will fight with them for the family property...\"","The servant boy just smiled and said, \"You should know clearly in your heart. There's no need to tell me. However, now there is only one chance to save you.\"","Lady Yang hurriedly asked, \"What chance?\"","He replied, \"His Majesty has sent several officials to visit the Old Master. They are about to arrive at the residence. This is your only opportunity to call for help from outside. If you miss it, even the gods won't be able to save you.\"","Lady Yang was stunned, furrowed her brow in thought for a moment, and finally nodded.","Soon after, the special envoys sent by the Emperor indeed arrived at the Song residence.","The visitors didn't give notice, so Song Yuankui, the eldest son of the Song family, could only hurriedly go out to welcome them.","When he saw them, he was surprised to find that there were actually three special envoys —","They were Li Hongsheng, the Minister of Personnel; Ji Wenchi, the newly appointed Minister of Revenue; and Xun Fei, the Commander of the Imperial Guard.","Song Yuankui's heart skipped a beat.","This lineup was truly unexpected.","The other two could be considered officials of the same rank as his father, but the Commander of the Imperial Guard... what was this about?","Although puzzled, he still first welcomed the three into the residence.","The three naturally went to see the Minister of Rites first.","Seeing that he was already unable to speak or move, only able to lie in bed, they could only express the Emperor's sympathy before coming out.","Song Yuankui accompanied them all the way, but heard the Minister of Personnel say, \"Minister Song has always been quite healthy. We hadn't heard of any discomfort in the past few days. How did he suddenly end up like this?\"","Song Yuankui could only say, \"Perhaps there have been too many family matters recently, and we younger generations have also been negligent in caring for father... After all, it's our fault.\"","The three didn't say anything more, just comforted him with a few words before preparing to take their leave.","Song Yuankui was about to see them out.","However, just as they left the room, they heard a burst of violent wailing. A woman with disheveled hair rushed up to them, crying and shouting, \"Please save me, my lords! The Song family wants to kill me to silence me!\"","...","The next day, news shocked the court and the public, leaving the citizens of the entire city dumbfounded.","— Song Zhiyun, the Minister of Rites, was morally corrupt and disregarded human ethics, actually forcibly occupying and abusing his daughter-in-law for nearly twenty years.","After the initial shock, officials and commoners from top to bottom all despised this man.","However, immediately afterwards, another piece of news that left people wide-eyed was spread —","It turned out that even the son born to his second daughter-in-law, Lady Yang, was actually this old man's own flesh and blood.","Song Yunchang, the young master of the Song family's second branch, who was nominally his grandson, was actually his son.","People didn't know what to say anymore, they could only shake their heads in disgust, all cursing this old man for being outrageous.","— Actually, Lady Yang hadn't originally mentioned her son's matter.","But unexpectedly, at the crucial moment, her weak husband Song Yuanwei, who couldn't even walk without panting, stood up himself and declared that the son wasn't his.","It turned out that Song Yuanwei had known everything all along.","After getting married back then, he had only shared a bed with Lady Yang twice, and each time didn't match up with the dates of when that child was later born.","Because of this, he had been depressed for years, making his condition even worse, but he didn't have the courage to break free from the shackles of family ties. He could only numb himself and let those two do as they pleased.","It wasn't until he saw the Carefree Young Master's new work recently that he realized his life might have another possibility.","Once this matter came to light, the emperor immediately stripped that old man Song Zhiyun of all his official positions and titles, demoting him to a commoner.","Shortly after, his eldest son Song Yuankui, Consort An's father, was also dismissed and held accountable for attempted murder and openly oppressing civilians, among other crimes. In the end, he was punished for multiple offenses and exiled to the border.","Consort An was also stripped of her rank for instructing palace maids to steal the emperor's handwriting, and was sent to Jade Truth Palace, which specifically detained royal female offenders, never to see the light of day again.","Fortunately, the emperor was fair in rewards and punishments. Considering that the Song family's second son, Song Yuanwei, was a victim and bravely exposed his father's evil deeds, he was exempted from being implicated in his family's crimes.","After expressing his gratitude, Song Yuanwei packed his belongings and left the capital, disappearing from everyone's sight.","It's uncertain whether he could truly achieve the ending depicted in the novel.","Although the curtain had fallen on this affair, it continued to be a topic of discussion both inside and outside the palace, in streets and alleys, for a long time during people's leisure time.","While making macramé in her free time, Rendong also sighed to Yanshu, \"I never imagined that the bigger the household, the more filth it could hide. Look at what kind of people this family turned out to be! It's good that the Song family's second young master left the capital. If he had stayed, how could he have lived?\"","\"But come to think of it, where did that Lady Yang and her son go?\" she added.","Yanshu, cracking melon seeds, replied, \"Didn't they go to serve that old man? After all, they've already done the deed as husband and wife, and there's no one left in the Song family. If she doesn't take care of him, who will? Her son is still the old man's, so I guess they'll be there to see him off in his final days.\"","Thinking about this, Rendong couldn't help but spit in disgust, \"It's so revolting. They deserve to disgust themselves in the end.\"","She then curiously asked, \"Why hasn't the mistress written any novels these past few days?\"","Yanshu sighed, \"She's tired and wants to rest for a while.\"","-- Ahem, actually, she was laying low.","This time, her novel \"A Real Man Stands Up\" once again accurately portrayed the events at the Minister of Rites' residence, shocking the outside world and sparking renewed speculation about her identity.","Some even said she was a deity who had descended to the mortal world specifically to punish evil people.","Of course, some clever individuals guessed that her identity was extraordinary --","To be so fearless in exposing officials' scandals and to do so with such accuracy, she was likely to be a close confidant of the emperor or a high-ranking official.","In any case... she needed to cool down the hype.","It was better for the common people to focus their enthusiasm on production and daily life rather than spending all day reading novels.","Calm down, calm down.","Of course, the most important thing was that the novels she had written recently were not suitable for publication.","For example, the one about the imperial son-in-law Zhao Chengwen - if the emperor hadn't told the Eldest Princess yet, he must have his reasons. If she rashly published a novel letting the Eldest Princess know about being cheated on, it could lead to a bloody incident, which wouldn't be good.","She did have a few novels in stock, but they all had some risqué content, which the emperor wouldn't allow.","It was truly frustrating.","As she was cracking melon seeds and pondering what to write next, Lianxin came in to report, \"Mistress, the Empress Dowager has sent a message saying that some pastries have been made in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, and she invites you to come and taste them.\"","Yanshu was startled. The Empress Dowager inviting her to eat pastries?","Tsk, what was she up to this time?","Of course, she couldn't refuse, so she quickly changed her clothes and went to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","When she arrived, she found that the emperor was also there, wearing an ink-blue dragon robe, listening to the Empress Dowager speak.","\"I truly misjudged her. I thought she was a well-bred young lady from a noble family, cultured and sensible. I never imagined that not only was her family not noble, but she herself was also malicious. They were truly in cahoots, utterly corrupt.\"","Yanshu understood that the Empress Dowager was talking about Consort An.","Tsk, come to think of it, the Empress Dowager must be quite exhausted.","-- Seeing that her own niece couldn't be relied upon, she had finally found someone with a bit of intelligence, only to discover that her family was so disgraceful.","Then she heard Yuwen Lan say, \"This matter is their fault, and has nothing to do with you, Mother.\"","The Empress Dowager murmured in agreement, then turned her gaze to Yanshu and said, \"Come, sit down. Today I had them make some taro pastries and double bean cakes. I heard you like them, so I called you to come and taste them.\"","Yanshu curtsied and replied, \"This concubine thanks the Empress Dowager for her kindness.\"","She then sat down nearby.","Palace maids brought in the tea and pastries, which looked quite appealing.","Although Yanshu was a bit of a glutton, she still knew right from wrong and realized that the Empress Dowager hadn't simply invited her for pastries.","However, she still had to go through the motions.","So she picked up a double bean cake.","Before she could put it in her mouth, the Empress Dowager spoke, \"By the way, I've heard that there's a very talented novelist in the market recently, someone called... Young Master? It's said that what he writes is exactly like real events. Even the matters of Xie Pei and the Song family were accurately portrayed by him. I wonder who has such great ability. Could they really predict the future?\"","Yanshu was taken aback, thinking to herself that the moment had finally come.","But it didn't matter, since the emperor was here today.","It was his time to take the stage.","Sure enough, Yuwen Lan said to the Empress Dowager, \"I had someone write it.\"","The Empress Dowager looked surprised, \"What? Your Majesty had someone write it? Why did Your Majesty do such a thing?\"","Yuwen Lan replied calmly, \"I had actually heard about their affairs earlier, so I had someone investigate. Having it written as a novel serves two purposes: first, to warn the world and prevent others from following in their footsteps; second, to save face for them. If they were to voluntarily confess, I could have been lenient in their punishment.\"","\"However, not only did they not repent, but they became even more brazen. It's truly disappointing.\"","After he finished speaking, the Empress Dowager paused for a moment before nodding, \"This method is indeed good. It's a pity they didn't take the hint. Hopefully, after these incidents, others will take warning.\"","Inwardly, she thought, [So it wasn't Li Yanshu, but the emperor. I knew that girl couldn't have such great abilities. But... has the emperor become so capable already?]","Yuwen Lan silently took note of this but said nothing.","Meanwhile, Yanshu was quietly marveling to herself --","As far as she knew, although Consort An had her suspicions, she was confined to Lanlin Hall before confirming the truth, with no way to communicate with the outside world.","So the Empress Dowager's question today was entirely based on her own judgment.","Inviting both her and the emperor here today, and suddenly asking this question - the Empress Dowager probably wanted to see if she would reveal any flaws.","Damn, the Empress Dowager was indeed formidable. Fortunately, she wasn't born in this era, otherwise, who knows how many times she would have died at the Empress Dowager's hands!","Just then, she heard the system chime in, [Hey, the Empress Dowager used to be a pure and innocent little sweetie too.]"]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37","paragraphs":["\"What, a pure and innocent little darling?\"","Yanshu immediately became interested and quickly asked, \"So how did the Empress Dowager grow from a pure, innocent, and adorable young girl into a top-level palace intrigue expert?\"","The system replied, \"Well, that's a long story. The Empress Dowager came from a noble family. She was graceful and beautiful from a young age. After she came of age, countless princes and young noblemen in the capital wanted to marry her. Once, when she accompanied her parents to a palace banquet, Emperor Gaozu took a liking to her at first sight and immediately bestowed her in marriage to the Late Emperor.\"","\"At sixteen or seventeen, she was just like a blank sheet of paper. When the imperial decree of marriage came down, her heart was filled with thoughts of the Late Emperor. After marriage, she devoted herself wholeheartedly to her husband. She sewed clothes and shoes for him by hand, stayed up late reading with him, and made soup and snacks for him. In the beginning, the two were affectionate and supportive of each other, truly in love. The Late Emperor even said he only wanted her as his woman.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but twitch the corner of her mouth. Sure enough, all scumbags have said such things.","It would be a miracle to believe him. If he really only had the Empress Dowager as his woman, how did the Emperor come to be?","Sure enough, the system continued, \"After waiting for her husband to ascend the throne and becoming the Empress herself, the good days were gone forever. The Late Emperor began to take many concubines into the palace. The huge difference from before, coupled with all the scheming in the harem, made the Empress Dowager very unhappy. She also had to manage the harem affairs. Despite the difficulties, she became pregnant, but the child was not healthy and was born weak and sickly.\"","\"Later, other consorts successively gave birth to two daughters and a son. Among them, Concubine Shu was greedy and actually plotted to harm her legitimate son, attempting to replace him with her own son. However, by the time she discovered this, it was already too late. The already weak child contracted tuberculosis and died not long after. From then on, in addition to her heartbreak, the Empress Dowager finally woke up. She quickly eliminated her enemies and began to develop connections in the court. She also adopted the Emperor. Later, when the Late Emperor died, she supported the Emperor's ascension to the throne and finally became the Empress Dowager herself.\"","Yanshu couldn't help but marvel inwardly, \"Growing into a boss through blood and tears, the Empress Dowager is truly a great female protagonist! Especially being able to raise the Emperor to be so excellent in such an environment is truly remarkable.\"","Yuwen Lan, who was quietly listening nearby, raised an eyebrow. He was indeed very excellent.","But then he heard her sigh, \"However, this bloody turmoil is really terrible. I'd rather be a salted fish, eating and drinking well with money every day.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So that's what \"salted fish\" means?","In that case, she is indeed very salty.","Then he heard her ponder in her heart, \"Counting like this, the Late Emperor had four children before the Emperor, but now only he and the Princess Royal are left. Apart from the Crown Prince who died young, the other two... couldn't have been done by the Empress Dowager, could they?\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","To be honest, he had thought about this question before.","But having been mother and son with the Empress Dowager for many years, he knew that although she was deep in thought, she didn't seem like someone who could harm children.","The system said, \"You're overthinking. The Empress Dowager only took revenge on adults and never harmed children. Those two children were implicated by the evil Concubine Shu and also died of tuberculosis.\"","Yanshu understood, \"So it wasn't the Empress Dowager. Tsk, Concubine Shu poisoned the Crown Prince and ended up killing her own children too. She really deserved it.\"","\"But come to think of it, the Emperor being alive today is also partly thanks to the Empress Dowager. Otherwise, if the Empress Dowager hadn't adopted him, he probably would have ended up like his older brothers and sisters.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan felt conflicted.","Indeed, the Late Emperor's harem at that time was even larger than now, and the bloody turmoil was indeed more intense than today.","If it weren't for the early death of the Crown Prince and the Empress Dowager adopting him, he might have long since perished along with his birth mother.","Therefore, he always remembered the Empress Dowager's kindness in raising him and didn't want to be too ruthless in many matters.","Just then, he heard Yanshu sigh in her heart again, \"It's just a pity that someone as clever and talented as the Empress Dowager encountered a scumbag like the Late Emperor. If she had met a steadfast and devoted man, she probably would have lived quite happily.\"","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched.","This girl actually called the Late Emperor a scumbag?","But...","For the Empress Dowager, and even his own birth mother, the Late Emperor was indeed not a good husband.","Especially later, when the Late Emperor became obsessed with Taoist cultivation and alchemy, neglecting even him, his only surviving son, he could hardly be considered a good father either.","He silently sighed.","The system, however, was still gossiping with Yanshu, \"Actually, the Empress Dowager did encounter someone who moved her heart later. There was a time when the Late Emperor was obsessed with Taoist cultivation and almost ignored state affairs. All major court matters were handled by a group of ministers helping the Empress Dowager. Among them was a Chancellor of the Zhongji Court who was uniquely insightful and wise, greatly admired by the Empress Dowager.\"","Oh, there's a situation here!","Yanshu's eyes immediately lit up, \"Did the Empress Dowager and this Chancellor of the Zhongji Court spark a romance?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Chancellor of the Zhongji Court?","Empress Dowager?","Sparks of love???","What does this mean?","The system: \"It's a bit regrettable, but before any sparks could fly, the Late Emperor had already become suspicious. To protect the Empress Dowager, the Chancellor voluntarily resigned and went home.\"","Yanshu: \"??? Ah?\"","This is too regrettable!","Imagine if the Empress Dowager could have sparked a romance with this Chancellor, and then something uncontrollable happened...","Tsk tsk tsk, what a shocking and earth-shattering love story that would have been!!!","Hmph, since the scumbag was unfaithful first, wearing a green hat wouldn't be a big deal.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What, wearing a green hat is not a big deal???","And an earth-shattering love story???","This girl...","But who exactly is this Chancellor she's talking about?","Just then, he heard her ponder in her heart again, \"But thinking about it, this Chancellor had already reached the position of Chancellor of the Zhongji Court, that's the Prime Minister!!! The fact that he was willing to resign and go home for the Empress Dowager shows that his love for her was true!\"","Chancellor of the Zhongji Court?","Resigned?","Alright, Yuwen Lan probably knew who it was now.","That person was called Qi Shuguang. He was indeed a very talented man who had even taught him before. He became Prime Minister at a young age but suddenly resigned and went home later...","Could it be...","Did that man really have something with the Empress Dowager...","He secretly glanced at the Empress Dowager, but saw no unusual expression on her usually dignified face.","In her heart, apart from surprise at him having someone write novels, there were no other thoughts.","Looking at Yanshu again, he saw her lowering her eyes with an obedient expression, but in her heart, she was still thinking, \"I've got inspiration! When I go back, I'll write an earth-shattering love story and fulfill the Empress Dowager's wishes in the novel.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","This novel can't be published either!","He had just told the Empress Dowager that this was a novel he had someone write!!!","Yuwen Lan's heart was truly in turmoil as he ate this snack.","Fortunately, not long after, the head eunuch of the Imperial Household Department suddenly came to report that officials were seeking an audience at Qianming Palace.","He felt as if he had been granted amnesty and hurriedly bid farewell to the Empress Dowager, taking Yanshu with him.","The imperial carriage was already waiting outside. Yuwen Lan said to Yanshu, \"Get in the carriage, I'll send you part of the way.\"","But Yanshu said, \"This concubine is not in a hurry, please go ahead, Your Majesty.\"","Now that the first month of the year had passed, the weather was mild and the imperial garden was in full spring bloom. She wanted to appreciate the beautiful scenery.","Not wanting to keep the ministers waiting, Yuwen Lan could only say, \"You don't need to rush to write the novel when you get back. If you're tired, just rest for a while.\"","In any case...","Don't write the Late Emperor as a scumbag despised by everyone...","At least leave him some face, ahem.","But he couldn't say these words out loud.","Yanshu, oblivious, responded with a yes. After he boarded the imperial carriage and left, she leisurely began to stroll around the palace.","After wandering outside for about half an hour, Yanshu returned to Ganlu Palace.","She changed her clothes and was just about to start writing the novel when she suddenly began to feel unwell.","At first, her neck itched. She scratched it a few times, but then her eyes started to itch as well.","Before she could rub her eyes again, she suddenly began to sneeze, and sneezed five or six times in a row.","Rendong was startled and hurriedly came to feel her forehead, anxiously saying, \"Did the mistress catch a cold outside just now?\"","But Yanshu shook her head in confusion, \"No, it was quite warm earlier...\"","Before she could finish speaking, she sneezed twice more.","After sneezing, her eyes had also swollen up.","She finally felt something was wrong and quickly said, \"Go and call for the imperial physician.\"","...","Yuwen Lan was in the study, busy until it was time to light the lamps.","Seeing that the ministers had finally dispersed, Fu Hai dared to come forward and said, \"Your Majesty, it's time to set the evening meal.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound and casually asked, \"Has Concubine Yi eaten yet?\"","If not, perhaps they could dine together in Ganlu Palace.","However, Fu Hai frowned and said, \"I heard Concubine Yi was feeling unwell this afternoon, so she probably hasn't eaten yet...\"","What?","Before he could finish, Yuwen Lan immediately asked, \"What's wrong with Concubine Yi?\"","Fu Hai hurriedly replied, frightened, \"Your servant doesn't know the details, but this afternoon I saw a royal physician going to Ganlu Palace, so I asked casually. The physician said Concubine Yi had summoned him.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"This happened in the afternoon. Why wasn't I informed earlier?\"","Fu Hai looked aggrieved and said, \"Your servant wanted to report it, but you were busy and had no time...\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","Indeed, earlier the ministers from the Ministry of Revenue and the Ministry of Works had come to report on spring planting and water conservancy projects. He had been so busy he barely had time to drink water.","So he didn't pursue the matter further and simply said, \"Prepare the carriage. I'll go see her.\"","He then got up and left.","As the imperial carriage rolled along, Yuwen Lan wondered: if Yanshu had fallen ill right after returning from the Palace of Benevolent Peace, could there have been poison in the Empress Dowager's refreshments?","— That seemed unlikely.","Not to mention that Yanshu had special abilities, he himself had been with the Empress Dowager and hadn't noticed any ill intentions towards her.","So what could it be?","As they arrived, he immediately alighted and rushed into the palace. He saw Yanshu with a red nose, teary eyes that were a bit swollen.","Seeing him arrive, she hurriedly tried to bow, \"This concubine greets Your Majesty...\"","Before she could finish, she sneezed three times in a row.","He quickly said, \"No need for formalities, sit down quickly.\"","Noticing a royal physician in the hall, he asked, \"What's wrong with Concubine Yi?\"","The physician frowned and replied, \"Your Majesty, Concubine Yi's symptoms resemble a cold, but her pulse doesn't indicate a cold.\"","Yanshu, with a stuffy nose, said from the side, \"This concubine hasn't caught a chill. I suddenly started sneezing... It's a bit like an allergic reaction to peach blossoms.\"","The physician responded, \"But peach blossoms haven't bloomed yet.\"","True, although spring had begun, it was still some time before peach blossoms would bloom.","Moreover, Yanshu had just asked her system and confirmed that no one was harming her, so she was also puzzled.","She had hoped the royal physician could figure it out, but after taking her pulse for a long time, he still couldn't determine the cause.","Just then, Fu Hai spoke up, \"I heard two peach trees by Taiye Pool bloomed today. Could the wind have blown pollen over?\"","Yanshu was stunned, \"Peach blossoms have bloomed by Taiye Pool?\"","Fu Hai nodded quickly, \"Yes, your servant heard about it this morning.\"","Yanshu paused, suddenly realizing.","Of course, the weather had been warm these past few days with an east wind blowing. Taiye Pool was just east of the imperial garden. She must have come into contact with peach pollen blown by the wind while strolling in the garden that afternoon.","Hearing this, the physician said, \"This humble one will prescribe a remedy for the Concubine.\"","But inwardly he mused that while he had seen many cases of willow pollen allergies, this was the first time he'd encountered a peach blossom allergy.","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched upon hearing this.","First time seeing this?","How could he prescribe medicine with such limited experience?","He thought for a moment, then asked Fu Hai, \"That doctor who treated the Duke of Cheng'en at the sacrifice ceremony last time... What was his name?\"","Fu Hai pondered, then quickly replied, \"His name is Jiang Nianqi.\"","\"That's right.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Summon him to examine Concubine Yi.\"","Fu Hai promptly agreed and immediately sent a swift eunuch to the Imperial Pharmacy to find him.","Fortunately, the Imperial Pharmacy had not yet closed for the day, and before long, Physician Jiang hurried over.","Oh, by the way, after his forthright speech at the sacrifice ceremony last time, the emperor had promoted him two ranks, and now he was already a medical official.","\"This humble one greets Your Majesty,\" Physician Jiang bowed. Before he could stand up straight, he heard the emperor instruct, \"Go examine Concubine Yi and see what's wrong with her.\"","Physician Jiang complied and immediately went to Yanshu's side.","He first inquired about her symptoms, then examined her eyes and nose, and finally took her pulse. He quickly made a diagnosis, saying, \"The Concubine is suffering from an allergic reaction. Do you usually have allergies to anything? Peach blossoms? Willow catkins? Or perhaps apricot blossoms?\"","He had figured it out at once.","Yuwen Lan, now reassured, answered for Yanshu, \"Concubine Yi is allergic to peach blossoms. Do you have a way to alleviate her symptoms?\"","Jiang Nianqi immediately replied, \"Yes, this humble one will write a prescription for the Concubine right away.\"","He then picked up a brush and began writing swiftly on paper.","Once the prescription was ready, Rendong immediately sent Little Dong to fetch and brew the medicine.","Physician Jiang also gave Rendong a separate package of herbs, saying, \"Use these to prepare bath water for the Concubine. It will help alleviate her symptoms.\"","Rendong accepted it and followed the instructions.","When the bath water was ready, Yanshu went to take a soak.","Remarkably, when she emerged a quarter of an hour later, her eyes were no longer swollen or itchy, and her nose was clear.","After drinking the prepared decoction and waiting another half hour, all her previous symptoms had indeed subsided.","Everyone was convinced, and Yuwen Lan nodded, saying to Jiang Nianqi, \"Your medical skills are indeed exceptional. It's a waste for you to be just a medical official. From today on, I promote you to Imperial Physician, specifically assigned to Ganlu Palace.\"","Jiang Nianqi immediately knelt and said, \"This humble one obeys and thanks Your Majesty for the grace.\"","Having been promoted four ranks in such a short time, everyone cast envious glances at him.","However, he maintained a calm demeanor, seemingly unmoved by favor or disgrace.","Yanshu thought to herself that he was truly talented.","Then she saw Fu Hai asking Yuwen Lan, \"It's getting late, and now that Concubine Yi is feeling better, would Your Majesty like to eat something? You haven't had dinner yet.\"","Yanshu looked at him in surprise and said, \"Your Majesty hasn't had dinner yet? This concubine is fine now, please go back and eat.\"","But Yuwen Lan remained seated and only asked her, \"Have you eaten?\"","Yanshu shook her head, \"No, I was feeling unwell this afternoon and didn't have a chance to eat.\"","He then said, \"In that case, have the imperial kitchen prepare something simple. I'll eat with you.\"","Well, that sounded good.","Yanshu was feeling better now and realized she was quite hungry, so she quickly nodded in agreement.","Before long, the imperial kitchen sent over a late supper.","There were four dishes: vinegar-dressed cabbage, eight-treasure lotus root dice, pan-fried tofu, and pork tenderloin in egg pouches, along with two bowls of porridge.","— It was already late, so it wasn't appropriate to have heavy meat dishes. Moreover, Yanshu had just taken medicine, so she couldn't eat too much rich food. Therefore, the meal consisted mainly of vegetarian dishes.","However, the imperial chef's skills were superb, and even the vegetarian dishes were prepared with great flavor.","After they finished eating, Yuwen Lan ordered, \"Prepare water, I want to bathe.\"","Yanshu looked at him in surprise, \"Your Majesty plans to rest here tonight?\"","He nodded, \"That's right.\"","Yanshu was stunned, \"But this concubine is ill.\"","Yuwen Lan smiled, \"Don't worry, I won't disturb you.\"","He paused, then raised an eyebrow at her and said, \"Unless you decide to snuggle into my arms yourself.\"","What? Her snuggling into his arms?","Yanshu was speechless, \"Isn't Your Majesty afraid of catching my illness?\"","He didn't seem concerned at all, \"Your illness isn't contagious.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She was at a loss. Why did this man enjoy sleeping so close to others?","Yuwen Lan's heart said yes.","Indeed, he was now very reluctant to return to Qianming Palace to sleep alone.","Because once he went back to sleep alone, things wouldn't be right.","The bedchamber in Qianming Palace seemed like a curse, eerily strange. He had become a bit afraid of it.","So no matter how much she grumbled inwardly, he didn't care.","After all, he just liked squeezing into this bed with her.","The night passed uneventfully.","When Yanshu woke up, Yuwen Lan had already gone to attend court.","The medicine from last night had been effective; she had slept soundly and no longer felt unwell.","However, she still didn't dare to be careless and decided not to go out for a while.","— She knew that the east wind was still blowing outside. If she went out, she would surely come into contact with peach pollen again and fall ill.","Ah, the difficult days were starting again.","Fortunately, the imperial kitchen sent a sumptuous breakfast, giving her some consolation.","Mmm, the juicy xiaolongbao and sweet pumpkin porridge were a perfect combination, and the pearl glutinous rice meatballs were her favorite.","As she was eating with relish, Lianxin came running to tell her, \"Mistress, His Majesty just ordered the two peach trees by Taiye Pool to be uprooted.\"","\"Uprooted?\" Yanshu was surprised, \"Why did His Majesty want those two trees uprooted?\"","Lianxin smiled and said, \"It's because he's worried about you feeling unwell again. His Majesty ordered them to be moved away. I heard those two trees were decades-old peach trees.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu was momentarily speechless.","Tsk, the last man who had been this good to her was her father.","When she was young and first had an allergic reaction to peach blossoms, her father cut down the old peach tree in their courtyard. He even persuaded the neighbors to replace their peach trees with apricot and pear trees.","Her father rarely troubled others, but that was the first time.","And now, the man who uprooted peach trees for her had become the emperor.","A warm feeling spread through her heart.","She took a bite of the lotus seed cake.","Mmm, the sweetness spread from her mouth to her heart.","Rendong smiled beside her, \"His Majesty truly cares for you, my lady. But now only two peach trees are blooming. What will happen in a few days when peach trees elsewhere start to bloom?\"","Yanshu was taken aback.","Indeed, were they going to cut down all the peach trees in the palace?","Besides, there were peach trees outside the palace too. When the wind blew, wouldn't the pollen still come into the palace?","They couldn't possibly ask all the citizens in the city to cut down their peach trees and never eat peaches again, could they?","The poor innocent peach trees!!!","No, although she was touched, this wasn't the solution...","As she was pondering this, she saw the court physician Jiang from last night arrive at the door, saying, \"This humble official is here to check Your Highness's pulse.\"","Her eyes lit up and she quickly said, \"Please come in. I have a question I'd like to ask you.\"","Physician Jiang complied and entered the hall with his medical kit.","Yanshu tentatively asked him, \"Doctor, is there any way to prevent me from having allergic reactions to peach blossoms in the future?\"","She had only meant to try asking, but to her surprise, he nodded directly and said, \"There is a way, but it depends on whether Your Highness can endure the hardship.\"","Yanshu was startled and quickly asked, \"What kind of hardship?\"","Physician Jiang explained, \"To treat this condition, we essentially need Your Highness's body to accept peach pollen without an extreme reaction. I will have Your Highness exposed to small amounts of peach pollen daily, while also taking medication. If we persist with this for a while, until Your Highness's body adapts, you won't have allergic reactions to peach blossoms in the future.\"","Yanshu thought for a moment, then decisively gritted her teeth and said, \"Alright.\"","It was better to try than not to try at all. If it really worked, she wouldn't have to fear peach blossoms anymore, would she?","It was a good solution that would solve the problem once and for all.","Having agreed to this, she began her treatment journey.","Every day, Physician Jiang would prepare a tiny amount of peach pollen for her to hold in her mouth for a while, followed by drinking a medicinal decoction.","As time went on, they gradually decreased the amount of medicine while increasing the amount of peach pollen.","Sure enough, after seven or eight days, when the peach blossoms outside began to bloom, her reaction was much milder than in previous years.","However, her family outside the palace didn't know about this. As the time for peach blossoms to bloom in full arrived, her parents and grandmother were all very worried about her.","On this day, with the emperor's permission, Ms. Zhu finally had the opportunity to enter the palace and visit her daughter.","As soon as they met, Ms. Zhu took out a package of pills and said to Yanshu, \"This is something I bought from a doctor in our hometown earlier. It's said to specifically treat your peach blossom allergy. Why don't you give it a try?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"There's no need. There's an exceptionally skilled imperial physician in the palace. I've been using his method for treatment, and I'm almost cured now.\"","She then cautioned her mother, \"That doctor must have been trying to deceive you. Medicine only works when it's properly prescribed, and everyone's constitution is different. How could he prescribe medicine without even examining my pulse? Please don't be deceived like this in the future.\"","Ms. Zhu nodded and agreed, \"I won't fall for such tricks again in the future. It's just a waste of money.\"","However, Yanshu noticed that her mother's smile seemed a bit tired.","So she quickly asked, \"Is everything alright at home? Has something happened?\"","But Ms. Zhu said, \"Nothing, everything's fine.\"","Yanshu didn't believe her, so she secretly asked the system, [Has something happened to my family?]","The system replied, [Yes, your brother Li Tianrui was bullied at Songhe Academy a couple of days ago. He fought back and punched the other person twice, but unexpectedly, the headmaster there was biased and told your brother to apologize to the other party.]","Yanshu was shocked, [What? Isn't Songhe Academy supposed to be the top academy in the capital, known for its excellent academic atmosphere? How could such a dark incident occur?]","The system sighed, [That was many years ago. Songhe Academy was originally founded by two great scholars and produced many outstanding talents. It was indeed the best back then. But after it became famous, nobles and aristocrats started sending their children there. Those unruly children of officials gradually corrupted the atmosphere. Now it has become a playground for the powerful.]","Yanshu was speechless.","If she had known this, she wouldn't have let her brother go there. And she had thought it was such a good academy!","But still...","She was puzzled.","— She was now a royal consort. How could her brother, as a member of her family, still be bullied?","Then she heard the system continue, [You don't know your father's personality yet? He didn't want to cause trouble for you, so when he sent your brother to the academy, he didn't reveal his identity. As a result, everyone thought your brother was just a commoner's son.]","Yanshu understood now, but she was still angry, [Even so, they shouldn't bully people without reason! Are commoners' children destined to be bullied by them without being able to fight back? And that headmaster even told Tianrui to apologize? What nonsense!]","The system replied, [Indeed, he's not a decent person. That headmaster appears to be very learned, but in reality, he only cares about profit. He has done many despicable things for fame in his life. Back then, to climb to the position of headmaster, he even sent his own wife to the bed of a government official.]","Yanshu was shocked, [What???]","Tsk, how interesting, offering himself up on a platter!"]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38","paragraphs":["After briefly understanding the situation from the system, Yanshu said to her mother, \"I can see you have something on your mind. Have you and father stopped treating me as family after I've been away for three years? How could you not tell me when something happened at home?\"","Ms. Zhu was taken aback. Seeing her daughter's angry expression, she sighed and said, \"It's not that we don't treat you as family. Your father forbade me from telling you. He was afraid you'd get angry if you knew, and if you accidentally let the Emperor know, it might incur his wrath and implicate you.\"","Yanshu deliberately asked, \"Incur his wrath? Have you committed some wrong?\"","Ms. Zhu looked aggrieved, \"How would we dare? It's probably because we're too honest that we're being bullied.\"","Yanshu then said, \"If that's the case, what's there to fear about the Emperor's anger? Do you think he's an incompetent ruler...\"","\"My dear child, how can you say such things?\" Ms. Zhu hurriedly covered her mouth in fright. She continued, \"Alright, alright, I won't listen to your father anymore. Actually, Tianrui got into trouble at Songhe Academy - some people were bullying him for being from out of town, deliberately mocking his way of speaking to tease him. Tianrui ignored them, but who knew they would actually tear up his books. You know how much Tianrui values his books, so he couldn't hold back and got into a fight with them. Tianrui is taller, so the other party, being shorter, probably didn't gain any advantage. They actually went to complain to the headmaster, demanding Tianrui apologize to them, otherwise they'd expel him from the academy.\"","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, \"Did Tianrui apologize?\"","Ms. Zhu sighed, \"You know that stubborn boy's temper. He got angry and came straight home. He hasn't been to the academy for three days now.\"","Yanshu said, \"Good for Tianrui, he's got backbone! This wasn't his fault to begin with. If he had apologized, he'd only be bullied more.\"","Ms. Zhu sighed, \"That's easy to say, but what do we do now? Is he never going to the academy again? That's the best academy in the capital, there are hardly any people from Qingzhou who can get in.\"","Yanshu quickly comforted her mother, \"The capital is big. Besides this academy, there are others. I recently heard that this academy is actually overrated and not that good. You and father don't need to worry yet, I'll find another one for Tianrui.\"","Hearing her daughter say this, Ms. Zhu was still a bit worried and said, \"Your father was afraid of causing trouble for you, that's why he didn't want me to tell you.\"","Yanshu laughed, \"Father is too honest, that's why he's been bullied so much. You can go back and tell him, I'm at least a concubine now. How can I save face if word gets out that my own brother is being bullied like this?\"","Ms. Zhu nodded, her worried expression finally easing a bit. She sighed, \"Talking to you about this has made me feel much better. Otherwise, I was about to suffocate from keeping it in.\"","Suddenly remembering something, she quickly took out the bundle she had brought with her and said, \"Look at my memory! I made some vegetable dumplings for you at home earlier, I almost forgot to take them out.\"","With that, just like last time, she took out a bag of hot, delicious food.","Vegetable dumplings?","Yanshu's eyes lit up, \"That's great! I've been craving vegetable dumplings these past few days. Mother, we truly are connected.\"","She quickly accepted them and started eating right away.","Mmm, chive and egg filling in the vegetable dumplings, with bits of vermicelli inside, and some dried shrimp added for extra flavor. It was most delicious. In the blink of an eye, she had already eaten one.","Ms. Zhu laughed, \"Look at you eat! Anyone who didn't know better would think I cook better than the imperial chefs!\"","\"It really is delicious,\" Yanshu nodded with a smile. \"The big buns you made last time, even the Emperor praised them.\"","\"What?\" Ms. Zhu looked surprised, \"The Emperor ate the buns I made?\"","Yanshu nodded, holding up her palm for her mother to see, \"He even ate five in one go.\"","Ms. Zhu's mouth fell open.","So the Emperor could eat that much too!","Well, it seems that next time she comes to the palace, if she makes any food, she'll have to make more.","Yanshu ate three vegetable dumplings in front of her mother. Seeing that it was getting late, Ms. Zhu left the palace.","Yanshu thought for a moment, then asked Renchun to bring a food box. She put three dumplings in it, then left as well, carrying it to Qianming Palace.","Not long after, the Emperor in the study smelled the aroma of vegetable dumplings.","\"These are vegetable dumplings made by my mother. She just brought them when she came to the palace. If Your Majesty doesn't mind, please try them.\"","Yuwen Lan looked at the dumplings, then at Yanshu's smiling face, and raised an eyebrow, \"Why are you so generous this time, bringing them to me on your own initiative?\"","Yanshu tried hard to smile sincerely, \"When I have something good to eat, I always think of Your Majesty first.\"","In her heart, she thought, [It's better to bring them to you proactively than have you come over to eat them yourself. Now there are four left in my chambers. If you went there to eat, I'd be lucky if you left me two.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He knew it.","However, the dumplings looked golden in color and emitted a simple, fresh aroma that was indeed tempting.","He was feeling a bit hungry anyway, so he picked one up and started eating, casually asking, \"Did you have a good chat with your mother earlier?\"","Yanshu said, \"It was good, thank you for Your Majesty's concern.\"","But in her heart, she thought, [Good my foot! If I hadn't seen my mother, I wouldn't have known that my own little brother was being bullied like this!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Before he could ask further, he heard her angrily think, [This capital simply can't tolerate honest people. What damned Songhe Academy, what damned headmaster, I'll make sure to destroy you!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Songhe Academy?","He vaguely remembered that when her father brought her brother to pay respects to him last time, he seemed to have mentioned that her brother was going to enter Songhe Academy.","Hearing this... could it be that the young man was being bullied at the academy?","So he tried saying, \"If there's anything wrong, you can tell me.\"","However, she shook her head as if nothing was wrong and said, \"This concubine has nothing wrong. Your Majesty, please continue eating. This concubine will go back to write her novel now, and will present it for Your Majesty's review when it's finished.\"","But in her heart, she thought, [Wait until I write out that scoundrel's crimes one by one for you to see, you'll definitely be angry too!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","It was the first time he had seen her so angry.","So he didn't dare to ask further for the moment, only nodding slightly as he watched her leave.","However, his curiosity was piqued. After thinking for a moment, he summoned the Imperial Guard.","About half an hour later, the Imperial Guard who had gone out to investigate returned to report to the Emperor.","\"Your Majesty, it turns out that Young Master Li was bullied at the academy because of his outsider status. The other party, seeing his erudition and quick wit, became jealous and deliberately teased him and tore up his books. Young Master Li, unable to bear it, retaliated with two punches, and is now ordered by the academy headmaster to go home and reflect.\"","What?","Yuwen Lan almost thought he had misheard, \"He was bullied? And he's the one ordered to go home?\"","The Imperial Guard confirmed, \"Yes. The bullies are led by Jiang Mingzhi, the grandson of the Marquis of Wuyang. When Young Master Li enrolled, he didn't reveal his identity, so the academy thought he was a commoner and handled it this way.\"","Yuwen Lan almost laughed in anger, \"So commoners deserve to be bullied? A place for studying and understanding principles has become such a place where status is everything.\"","No wonder Yanshu was so angry earlier.","He thought for a moment and said, \"Tell the Imperial Censorate to send someone to see what's going on at that academy.\"","The Imperial Guard acknowledged the order.","Meanwhile, after Ms. Zhu returned home, she quickly told her husband and son what her daughter had said.","\"Shu'er said this isn't Tianrui's fault, and told us not to be afraid. She said she would find another academy for Tianrui.\"","However, Li Huaizhi, the Duke of Loyalty and Righteousness, said, \"How can she find an academy for Tianrui while she's in the palace? Besides, the teacher in Qingzhou went to great lengths to use his connections to get us this opportunity. If we leave so easily, wouldn't it be a waste of his efforts?\"","Ms. Zhu said, \"Then what should we do? Surely you don't want Tianrui to go apologize and be humiliated?\"","Li Huaizhi thought for a moment, then said to his son, \"Come on, I'll accompany you there again today, and see if we can reason with them.\"","Li Tianrui agreed, and left with his father.","Li Huaizhi was a man of strict principles. Even when he arrived at the academy in person, he still didn't reveal his status as a duke.","As a result, they waited outside for a full hour before finally meeting the headmaster, Bi Jinghuai, who had been unwilling to see them.","Li Huaizhi, intending to use kind words, first bowed to the other party and said, \"My son is straightforward by nature. Although he can be mischievous, he wouldn't do anything excessive. There must be some misunderstanding in this matter. I request the headmaster to investigate the rights and wrongs clearly, and allow my son to return to his studies.\"","Unexpectedly, the seemingly scholarly headmaster smiled and said, \"You've just arrived in the capital. Given your son's talent, let me offer some advice - go apologize to those classmates. If they forgive you, you can naturally return to study. Otherwise, I'm afraid you won't be able to stay at this academy.\"","Li Tianrui was so angry he couldn't help but say, \"Father, let's not study here anymore. Let's go home.\"","See? Even with his father here, the headmaster was still so biased, not being reasonable at all!","\"Young Master Li, please wait.\"","Just as those words were spoken, a man around 40 years old came in from outside.","Seeing the surprise on the faces of the Li father and son, the man proactively explained, \"Mr. Li, don't worry. I was sent by your daughter to look into your son's matter.\"","Li Huaizhi, being new to the capital, didn't really know the officials yet. He could only nod slightly and say, \"Thank you for your trouble, sir.\"","The other man nodded and then said to Headmaster Bi Jinghuai, \"I've already spoken with several students at the academy. The other side disrespected Young Master Li first, tearing books and physically grabbing him. Young Master Li fighting back was understandable. As the head of the academy, you should distinguish right from wrong, comfort those who have been wronged, and punish those who are violent. Otherwise, how can you educate and nurture people?\"","Upon hearing this, Headmaster Bi Jinghuai quietly sized him up.","Though the man had an extraordinary demeanor, he seemed unfamiliar, apparently not someone from official circles.","So Bi Jinghuai smiled and said, \"You must also be new to the capital, sir. The capital is full of powerful and noble families, unlike other places. Any random student in my academy could be the son of a prince or duke.\"","The other man looked puzzled and said, \"Even so, what does that have to do with this matter? The law applies equally to princes and commoners. Just because the violent ones have different status, can right and wrong be reversed?\"","Bi Jinghuai smiled again and said, \"I'm not reversing right and wrong. There's a saying that it takes two hands to clap. If Li Tianrui hadn't made a mistake first, the others wouldn't have bullied him. Otherwise, with so many people in the academy, why don't they bully others?\"","These words angered all three of them.","The 15-year-old Li Tianrui snorted again and said, \"My mistake was thinking this Songhe Academy was a good place! I shouldn't have come here in the first place.\"","Then he looked at Li Huaizhi and said, \"Father, let's go.\"","At this point, Li Huaizhi had lost hope as well.","He sighed heavily and said to the man who had come, \"Thank you for taking the trouble to come here, sir. Since this is the case, I'll find another place for my son to study. It seems this academy is too high for us to reach.\"","He was about to turn and leave.","But then he heard the man say, \"Lord, please wait.\"","Lord?","Bi Jinghuai paused upon hearing this.","Was he calling that country bumpkin \"Lord\"?","Then he heard the man shake his head and sigh, \"If I hadn't witnessed this myself, I would hardly believe that such a reversal of right and wrong could happen at the prestigious Songhe Academy right under the Emperor's feet. I will report this to the court immediately. It seems this academy needs to be thoroughly investigated.\"","Li Huaizhi nodded and left the academy gates together with the man.","Bi Jinghuai was stunned.","Report to the court?","Who were they exactly?","Had he misjudged the situation?","As the Li father and son returned home after leaving Songhe Academy, the Emperor in the palace had also just finished listening to the report from Zuo Junliang, the Right Vice Censor-in-Chief.","He frowned and said, \"How did this Bi Jinghuai become the headmaster of Songhe Academy?\"","Zuo Junliang said, \"This man entered Songhe Academy twenty years ago, working his way up from clerk to senior student. When the previous headmaster was getting old, the position was supposed to be passed to the then hall master Xu Daoguang. But the Department of Ceremonies in the Ministry of Rites suddenly intervened, helping this man become the headmaster.\"","The Ministry of Rites intervened?","Hmph, it seems the remnants of the former Minister of Rites haven't been completely cleared out.","Yuwen Lan said, \"Investigate the Department of Ceremonies from that year. If there are any who abused their power or neglected their duties, don't let a single one go.\"","Zuo Junliang quickly agreed.","Perhaps because she was so angry, Yanshu's writing speed today was almost divinely inspired.","She had only started writing in the morning, but by dinnertime, she had finished the story.","Just as she put down her pen, she heard the system say, [There's been a new development. That Headmaster Bi Jinghuai of Songhe Academy found out your father is the Earl of Loyalty and Righteousness. He was so shocked that he ran to your home to apologize.]","Apologize?","Yanshu raised an eyebrow and said, [Did my father and Tianrui forgive him?]","The system replied, [Your father was polite in his words, but he's determined not to go back. He's already inquired at three other academies for your brother. When they learned your brother had once been the top scorer in the county examination, they all eagerly wanted him.]","Yanshu said proudly, [Of course! If one place doesn't appreciate you, there are always others that will! If apologies were enough, what would we need laws for? This scum has already angered me, he must be destroyed!]","But she had another question, [Why would he rather go apologize himself, but insist on shielding those three punks who bullied Tianrui?]","The system explained, [Because the leader of those who bullied your brother is called Jiang Mingzhi, and he's the grandson of the Marquis of Wuyang. You know the Marquis of Wuyang, right? He's the Eldest Princess's father-in-law.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","So that's how it is.","Tsk tsk, no wonder this scum was so protective of the bullies. It turns out he's the nephew of the Eldest Princess's in-laws. He simply can't afford to offend them.","Birds of a feather really do flock together. What a bunch of lowlifes.","Just then, she heard the system say, [Bi Jinghuai saw that your father wouldn't forgive him and realized this matter couldn't be easily resolved. Now he's gone to the house of a Director in the Ministry of Rites to discuss countermeasures.]","Yanshu narrowed her eyes, [The Director in the Ministry of Rites? The one whose wife he slept with? He dares to protect this scum and go against me?]","The system replied, [He doesn't dare. Wei Guangze, the Director in the Ministry of Rites, told him to figure it out himself and kicked him out.]","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, [Good! I love seeing these scumbags panic and scramble around!]","But then she heard the system say, [Don't celebrate too early. Bi Jinghuai has now gritted his teeth and gone directly to the Jiang family, saying he can use the condition of recommending Jiang Mingzhi to the Imperial Academy to ask for the Jiang family's protection.]","Yanshu scoffed, [Listen to him boast! Recommending someone to the Imperial Academy? The Imperial Academy is so strict now that not even a fly can get in. It would be a miracle if that little punk from the Jiang family could get in!]","Just then, she saw the Emperor stroll in from outside.","So she first said goodbye to the system, then went forward to bow and greet him, \"Your humble consort welcomes Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan said \"No need for formalities\" and asked, \"Have you eaten yet?\"","Yanshu said she hadn't, \"I just finished writing a story and was about to call the kitchen to send food.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"That's perfect, I'll eat with you.\"","Ahem, when he was with her, even food seemed to taste especially delicious.","Yanshu happily agreed and called for the palace servants to bring the meal.","While waiting, Yuwen Lan asked again, \"What kind of story did you write today?\"","Yanshu was just wanting to tell him and quickly said, \"Your humble consort wrote a story about an extremely scummy person getting his just deserts.\"","Scummy person?","Yuwen Lan pondered silently. This term sounded a bit like that \"scumbag\" he'd heard before.","But judging from the literal meaning, a \"scummy person\" seemed to be even worse.","Well, her stories were always faster than the Imperial Censorate anyway, so he nodded and said, \"Interesting, tell me about it.\"","Yanshu cleared her throat and began, \"There was a scholar who grew up in poverty and had no status, so he suffered a lot. He was determined to make a name for himself and was extremely pragmatic. As he approached marriageable age, he still couldn't find a wife because his family was too poor.\"","\"But this scholar discovered that there was a rich family in the village with a pretty daughter who was very naive. So he schemed and, taking advantage of a rainy day, he sabotaged the ox cart the girl was riding in, then pretended to pass by and offer an umbrella, causing the girl to secretly fall for him. The rich man loved his daughter, and finally married her to him. With his father-in-law's financial support, this man was able to focus on preparing for the imperial examinations, while his wife took care of all household matters.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"This man seems to have married a good wife. What happened next?\"","Yanshu continued, \"Later, this man was fortunate enough to pass the provincial examination, but unfortunately, he had no connections or power, and not much ability, so he remained a minor official, far from his goal. Later, by chance, this man started teaching at a prestigious academy. He discovered that many students from this academy became officials, which could help him expand his network and gain powerful connections. So he began to take advantage of this opportunity to actively network.\"","\"His wife had been raising their child in their hometown, but when the child reached school age, the mother and son came to the capital to join him. However, just at this time, his wife's misfortune arrived.\"","\"An official took a liking to the scholar's wife and secretly lusted after her. Though the scholar was clearly aware of the official's intentions, he surprisingly did not protect his wife. In fact, to obtain the position of headmaster, he even forced his wife to serve that official. Later, he also bribed heavily with money, and finally became the headmaster.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan was shocked, \"This man forced his wife to serve others just for fame and fortune?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"That's right.\"","Indeed, he was scum.","Yuwen Lan asked, \"What about his wife?\"","Yanshu regretfully said, \"His wife was naturally overwhelmed with shame. She later fell ill from depression and died early.\"","Yuwen Lan sighed, \"What happened after that?\"","Then he heard her continue, \"With his control, the once academically excellent school began to gradually lean towards the wealthy and powerful, accepting many rich kids and continuously raising tuition fees, allowing him to profit from it. Meanwhile, those children from common families could only look on helplessly.\"","\"Later, this person even established connections with court officials and secretly became a broker for buying and selling official positions, gaining enormous profits from it.\"","What?","Yuwen Lan couldn't hold back and directly scolded, \"This is absolutely outrageous!\"","A scholar driven solely by profit and full of scheming had ruined the most important academy in the capital to such an extent.","No wonder, no wonder!","Calculating the time, this person became the headmaster of Songhe Academy about fifteen years ago. How many parasites had been bred in these fifteen years!","Father Emperor, oh Father Emperor, how badly you've neglected the court while being obsessed with cultivating the Dao!","Yanshu leaned close to him and said, \"Your Majesty also finds it outrageous, right? If such a thing happened today, this scholar would definitely be severely punished by the law.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded in agreement, \"Indeed. To prevent future occurrences, I will immediately order an investigation.\"","Yanshu nodded vigorously, \"Your Majesty is wise.\"","Yuwen Lan asked, \"You haven't told me the scholar's ending yet.\"","He wanted to know what kind of death she would give to such a scumbag.","Then he heard her say, \"Because this person had made the academy so corrupt, his successors all followed in his footsteps. To quickly take the position of headmaster, they poisoned his food, and he died from it. After his death, his soul arrived in the underworld, where ghost officials listed his crimes. King Yama, in a fit of rage, sentenced him to endure all the punishments of the underworld. First, he was sliced by knives and chopped by axes, then fried in oil and cooked in fire. Finally, he was turned into a stone in a latrine, where people would excrete their filth on him every day.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","\"Why did the underworld suddenly appear?\"","This was too unexpected, suddenly turning into a supernatural novel?","Yanshu gave an evil smile, \"Because his crimes were truly too numerous to list, dying once in the mortal world clearly wasn't enough. Of course, he had to go to the underworld to suffer all punishments.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, it was indeed evident that she was very angry.","Of course, just hearing about it made him want to tear this person to pieces too.","At this moment, the evening meal had been prepared. Fu Hai bowed beside them and said, \"Your Majesty and Her Highness, dinner is served.\"","Yuwen Lan put aside his thoughts and went to the table with her.","Then he heard Yanshu exclaim, \"Oh, there's marinated crab!\"","Yuwen Lan glanced at the table.","However, his mind suddenly flashed back to the story she just told—","Turning that person into a stone in a latrine...","\"...\"","Tsk, he felt a bit unable to eat now.","That night, the new story was delivered to the bookseller.","Since it had been a while since Carefree Master had published a book, people's appetites had been thoroughly whetted. Seeing that this story was so explosive, the bookseller immediately had people print copies overnight. By early the next morning, over a hundred copies had been sold.","After reading it, everyone was shocked.","It could be said that this person's level of shamelessness was beyond compare to previous ones.","Of course, his final fate was truly satisfying.","While feeling satisfied, people also began to speculate about this person's identity.","Because Yanshu hadn't changed his identity, directly writing that he was an academy headmaster, and of a long-renowned academy in the capital...","Tsk, even a toe could figure out who it was.","Just at this time, news spread that after an investigation by the Imperial Censorate, the headmaster of Songhe Academy, Bi Jinghuai, was involved in buying and selling official positions, bribery, and corruption. He was directly thrown into the imperial prison.","Within a month, he was sentenced to beheading. Over ten other involved officials were all dismissed and held accountable, without exception.","Songhe Academy was also taken over by the court for reform, to be reopened to the public after the reforms were completed.","As for the cause of the incident, that Young Master Jiang Mingzhi who bullied out-of-town classmates in the academy didn't escape punishment either.","In the end, he was punished by the emperor with sixty strokes of the cane, after which his legs were almost crippled.","As this matter concluded, people couldn't help but marvel at Carefree Master's prowess, and speculations about their identity surged like a tidal wave.","This was a story that took down an entire academy, truly the work of a divine being!","Of course, Yanshu was very calm about this. After all, with the emperor covering for her, many people outside already believed she was part of a new organization under the emperor's command, similar to the Imperial Guard or Imperial Censorate, specializing in collecting secret information to create public opinion for investigating corruption and darkness.","Just as she was quietly enjoying her achievements in the back palace, eating melon seeds and knitting, the system brought her new information.","[Pay attention now, the Jiang family has been harboring resentment since their little rascal was caned. Lately, they've been reaching out to Imperial Consort Ning in the palace and to the imperial son-in-law Zhao Chengwen, planning to cause trouble for your Li family.]","Yanshu's eyes lit up.","Great, it seems that the book \"The Two-Faced Scholar Dies Under the Flowers\" can finally be published.","This is truly a windfall of good fortune, unstoppable!"]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39","paragraphs":["After the incident at Songhe Academy, Consort Ning's mother Lady Cui and her aunt Lady Zhao found an opportunity to visit her in the palace together.","In this incident, besides the already beheaded headmaster of the academy Bi Jinghuai and a group of corrupt officials, Lady Zhao's family was affected the most.","Consort Ning was also worried about her cousin Jiang Mingzhi who had been given sixty lashes. As soon as she saw her aunt, she immediately asked, \"How is Mingzhi doing now?\"","As soon as the words left her mouth, she saw her aunt Lady Zhao burst into tears, saying, \"Mingzhi still can't get out of bed. Your uncle and I asked the Princess to send an imperial doctor to examine him. The doctor said he might be crippled for life... My poor Mingzhi hasn't even taken a wife yet!\"","Lady Zhao became more and more aggrieved as she spoke. However, since the lashes were ordered by the Emperor and they were in the palace, she could only sob quietly, afraid others might hear and cause trouble.","Consort Ning said angrily, \"Mingzhi at most tore up that Li boy's book, and he was also beaten by that boy. Yet His Majesty dealt with him so harshly. It's really too much.\"","Hearing this, her mother Lady Cui also nodded, \"Isn't that so? Mingzhi was wrong first, but it wasn't a big mistake. Besides, boys of this age are all a bit mischievous. Wouldn't it have been enough to make them apologize properly? Now he's been beaten like this, what are we to do!\"","As she finished speaking, her aunt Lady Zhao cried even louder.","Consort Ning became even more angry and snorted, \"If it wasn't for the fact that he's Li Yanshu's family, how could this have happened? She must have been whispering in His Majesty's ear, causing Mingzhi to end up like this! Huh, her brother is worth ten thousand gold and can't be touched, while other people's children deserve to become cripples?\"","Hearing this, Lady Cui sighed deeply, while Lady Zhao could only keep wiping her tears.","At this moment, a palace servant announced from outside the door, \"Your Highness, there's an edict from the Empress Dowager.\"","Lady Cui and Lady Zhao immediately closed their mouths, not daring to make a sound.","Consort Ning also composed herself and asked, \"What is it?\"","The palace servant outside the door said, \"The day after tomorrow is the Shangsi Festival. The Empress Dowager requests that the masters prepare well, and on that day accompany the imperial procession to Diehui Mountain Hot Spring Palace for bathing and spring outing.\"","Diehui Mountain was a royal forest located in the outskirts of the capital. Because there was a hot spring flowing from the mountain, the founding emperor had built a hot spring palace there.","Every Shangsi Festival, common people would go to the waterside to bathe and enjoy the spring, while the royal family would go to this hot spring palace to bathe and pray for blessings.","Consort Ning heard this and said, \"I understand.\"","Just as she was about to continue talking to her mother and aunt, she suddenly paused.","Bathing?","She raised an eyebrow, suddenly getting an idea.","Meanwhile, Li Yanshu also received the news about going to the Hot Spring Palace.","Tsk, hot springs weren't available everywhere, and since she had a low status before, she never had the chance to go out of the palace. So this would be her first time bathing in a hot spring in this life.","Especially after hearing that the hot spring in the palace had beauty-enhancing properties, she became even more excited and immediately ordered people to prepare things.","However, at this moment, she heard the system say, [Don't be so happy, someone is planning to take revenge on you while bathing in the hot spring.]","Li Yanshu: \"???\"","Take revenge on her?","Thinking of the Jiang family matter that the system had mentioned to her a few days ago, she immediately guessed who it was.","Huh, fine, she had been waiting for this. The sooner the better.","In the blink of an eye, it was the day of the Shangsi Festival.","On this day, commoners poured out of the city to enjoy the spring outing, while the Empress Dowager and the imperial consorts boarded carriages and left the palace early.","However, Diehui Mountain was really far away. It took a whole morning before everyone arrived at the Hot Spring Palace.","After sitting in carriages for half a day, it was now noon, so naturally they had to fill their stomachs first.","The lunch consisted of specialties from the mountain, including freshly stewed pheasant, tender but not tough; whole roasted lamb, sizzling with oil, fragrant but not gamey.","There were also fat fish grown in the mountain spring water, with tender meat and few bones, whether sweet and sour or braised, all delightful to the eye.","Various wild vegetables and delicacies were also fresh and delicious. Li Yanshu ate with great pleasure.","She felt that the things from the mountain were more natural and tasted even better than those in the palace.","Mmm, it was indeed worth coming.","— There weren't many people in the harem now, and those who came out this time, besides the Emperor and the Empress Dowager, were only her, Consort Zhou, and Consort Ning.","For this noon meal, they all sat at the same table.","At this time, seeing her eating with relish, Consort Ning inwardly sneered —","[Li Yanshu, ah Li Yanshu, today I'll let you eat your fill first. You'll have plenty to cry about later!]","Hearing this voice in his ear, Yuwen Lan paused quietly.","After finishing lunch, while everyone was going to rest, he summoned a secret guard and said, \"Keep a close eye on Noble Consort Yi. If anyone tries to harm her, report to me immediately.\"","The secret guard complied and went to carry out his orders.","About an hour later, he returned to report, \"Your Majesty, someone has put drug powder in the water inlet of Qinglin Garden where Noble Consort Yi is staying.\"","— This Hot Spring Palace was built around the hot spring, with each garden having a water inlet that converged into a bathing pool for the residents to use.","Putting drugs in the water inlet, one could guess the intention.","Yuwen Lan immediately ordered Fu Hai, \"Tell Noble Consort Yi not to bathe yet.\"","However, before Fu Hai could leave, Xiao Shunzi reported, \"Your Majesty, Noble Consort Yi requests an audience.\"","Hmm?","She came herself?","Yuwen Lan's heart tightened, thinking she might have already fallen victim to the plot. He immediately said, \"Enter.\"","Then, he saw Li Yanshu come before him unharmed. After paying her respects, she said to him, \"Your Majesty, I have an unreasonable request. The water in my bathing pool is a bit cold. Could I change to another one?\"","Change to another one?","Yuwen Lan understood that she had already discovered something was wrong.","That's good.","But without worry, he suddenly felt a bit playful and said, \"The temperature in my bathing pool is just right. You can come bathe here.\"","What?","Li Yanshu was stunned. She just wanted to quietly enjoy a hot spring bath, not to seek favor.","There were many vacant places in the palace, why should she come to his?","So she politely declined, \"I wouldn't dare. I just need to change to another place. I think that Yulan Hall looks nice...\"","Before she could finish, she saw him smile and say, \"I grant you permission to come here. What's there to be afraid of? This is the first pool the hot spring flows into, it's hotter than the others.\"","\"...\"","Somehow, looking at his smile, Li Yanshu suddenly had a not-so-good premonition.","So she said again, \"Thank you for Your Majesty's kindness, but I'm afraid of scalding water. I'd better go back...\"","Damn, at worst she wouldn't bathe. Staying here suddenly gave her a feeling of a sheep entering a tiger's den.","However, before she could take a step, he grabbed her arm and smiled again, \"Just now you were afraid of cold, now you're afraid of heat. What's really going on with you?\"","After speaking, without allowing any objection, he directly pulled her to the edge of the bathing pool.","At this moment, Fu Hai, who had accidentally observed the entire interaction between the Emperor and his consort, had a smile bloom on his face —","Tsk, even their flirting was so interesting. It truly was a case of envying the mandarin ducks, not the immortals.","But just as he finished this thought, he saw the Emperor return by himself and order the secret guards in the hall, \"Whoever tampered with Qinglin Garden, let her taste her own medicine.\"","The secret guard complied.","Although Li Yanshu was a bit confused, she finally couldn't resist the temptation of the hot spring and got into the Emperor's bathing pool.","Ahem, anyway, that man couldn't do anything.","Besides, after bringing her over, he had left. It would be a waste not to bathe!","The hot spring was clear and warm. As she tried getting in the water, her whole body immediately felt comfortable. She lay in the pool for a while, not forgetting to use the spring water to moisturize her face.","Just as she was enjoying herself, she saw that man return and stand by the pool, looking down at her.","\"Your Majesty...\"","She was startled and instinctively covered her chest with both hands —","Tsk, although she was wearing special clothes for hot spring bathing, the material was thin and transparent, and now soaked with water, it was even more revealing.","However, that person raised an eyebrow and smiled, saying, \"What are you covering? It's not like I haven't seen it before.\"","Li Yanshu: \"...\"","She couldn't help but blush a little, muttering in her heart, [Rascal...]","But then, she saw him take off his clothes and also get into the pool.","Li Yanshu was momentarily stunned —","Those pecs...","Those arms...","Those muscle lines...","Tsk tsk.","Although they had shared a bed many times, he always wore nightclothes. Now he was only wearing a pair of shorts...","As she was secretly admiring, she saw him suddenly come close. Before she could react, he cupped her face and kissed her on the lips.","He could tell that this \"rascal\" was pretty much the same as calling him a \"lecher\".","Since they had been told as much, it would be remiss not to do something about it.","Li Yanshu: \"...\"","Alright, considering he had shown her as well, she wouldn't hold it against him.","So the two of them began to soak together.","Yuwen Lan rarely gave himself time off, so this was a rare chance to relax. He lay on the steps in the pool with his eyes closed, resting.","Li Yanshu also lay there for a while, but feeling the buoyancy of the water, she tried swimming a bit.","This pool was far too large to just be for bathing - it was clearly a swimming pool!","Hearing movement, Yuwen Lan opened his eyes to look at her and asked, \"Do you know how to swim?\"","Li Yanshu replied with a grin, \"Nope.\"","She then asked him, \"Does Your Majesty know how to swim?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. \"Of course.\"","With that, he began swimming in the pool.","His movements were graceful and effortless, his strong arms exposed above the water, quite pleasing to the eye.","After swimming for a while, he returned to her side and began to teach her how to swim.","\"First, take a deep breath, relax your body, and try to float on the surface of the water...\"","Li Yanshu followed his instructions, but was still a bit nervous, one hand tightly gripping his arm and afraid to let go.","Yuwen Lan smiled and said, \"I will support you, don't worry.\"","As he said this, he grasped her waist.","But he accidentally touched her ticklish spot.","Li Yanshu couldn't help but burst into giggles...","The two of them were half playing, half learning, and it was quite fun.","After some time had passed, they suddenly heard Fu Hai reporting from outside, \"Your Majesty, something has happened to Consort Ning...\"","Li Yanshu paused. \"Something happened to Consort Ning?\"","Yuwen Lan's smile faded as he said, \"We've soaked long enough anyway. Let's go see.\"","They exited the hot spring pool.","When the two arrived at Consort Ning's Xiangyu Garden, they found her lying in bed wailing.","Yuwen Lan didn't approach, but Li Yanshu gathered her courage to take a peek by the bedside.","She saw that Consort Ning's exposed hands, feet and face were bright red, her eyes tightly shut as if unable to open.","Yuwen Lan asked the imperial physician who had accompanied them, \"What has happened to Consort Ning?\"","The physician replied, \"Your Majesty, it appears Consort Ning's body has been burned by some sort of poison.\"","\"Poison?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and looked around the room, noticing that Consort Ning's personal maids looked rather panicked.","He said meaningfully, \"How could there be poison in the hot spring water?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, someone chimed in from the side, \"That's right, everyone else bathed without issue, so how did Consort Ning end up poisoned?\"","It was Consort Zhou, who had come to see what the commotion was about.","At this moment, she was thinking to herself, [Could it be that Li Yanshu poisoned that bitch? Perfect! I hope His Majesty finds out it was her, so she and that bitch Consort Ning can both go down together, while I reap the benefits.]","Yuwen Lan ignored her and just looked at Li Yanshu.","He heard her thinking, [This is rather strange. Who poisoned Consort Ning?]","-- Li Yanshu had known Consort Ning was planning to tamper with the hot spring water, which is why she had gone to find Yuwen Lan earlier to change pools.","As for the pool water issue, she had planned to deal with it after finishing their soak.","Who would have thought that before she even finished bathing, Consort Ning would end up poisoned first?","What on earth was going on?","Yuwen Lan kept his composure and simply ordered the guards, \"Investigate and find out where this poison came from.\"","The guards all responded affirmatively and sprang into action.","However, Consort Ning continued to wail on the bed, her cries becoming more and more agonized.","Li Yanshu heard her personal maid trying to comfort her, \"Please don't move, Your Highness. Your skin is starting to split open. I'm afraid the more you move, the more it will split...\"","Li Yanshu thought to herself, damn, this poison is brutal. To think this was almost inflicted on her instead.","Serves her right!","About half an hour later, a guard entered the hall to report, \"Your Majesty, we found some unburned paper scraps in the tea room of Xiangyu Garden with traces of white powder on them.\"","He then presented the evidence they had found.","Yuwen Lan said, \"Have the imperial physician take a look.\"","The physician came forward in response.","After examining it, he reported, \"Your Majesty, this appears to be bone-melting powder. When dissolved in water, it can melt bone and flesh, enough to burn a person's skin. This matches Consort Ning's current symptoms.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and said, \"Since this was found in Xiangyu Garden, arrest everyone here and interrogate them harshly to find out who used such a vicious method to harm Consort Ning.\"","The guards responded affirmatively.","Immediately, the hall was thrown into chaos...","The next day, as the imperial procession returned to the palace, they brought back shocking news --","Yesterday at the hot spring palace, the maids in Consort Ning's palace had poisoned their mistress, not only blinding and disfiguring Consort Ning, but also severely burning her skin all over her body.","While everyone was shocked, they all speculated internally: tsk tsk, to think such a thing would happen in the palace.","Just how cruelly must Consort Ning have treated her servants, to make them poison her like this?","Meanwhile, Li Yanshu, who had returned to Ganlu Palace, was also puzzled.","-- How did that poison end up on Consort Ning's body?","She went to ask the system, which said, [The Emperor did it.]","The Emperor?","Li Yanshu was surprised. [Why did he do that?]","The system replied, [Because the Emperor discovered Consort Ning was trying to harm you, so he had someone switch her water with the water from your garden.]","Li Yanshu: [...]","It was actually the Emperor?","But why didn't he say anything?","Tsk, what impressive acting skills. His performance yesterday fooled even her!","However, before the system could say anything else, she saw Rendong run over with an excited expression and tell her, \"My lady, good news! Our young master has been accepted into the Imperial Academy!\"","-- After leaving Songhe Academy, Li Yuanrui had gone to another academy to study for a while. When the Imperial Academy announced its second round of admissions, he decided to try taking the exam.","Who would have thought he'd actually pass?","Hearing Rendong say this now, Li Yanshu immediately stood up from her seat and asked, \"Really?\"","Rendong nodded vigorously. \"Of course it's true. They just posted the results. The master specifically sent someone to deliver the news to you.\"","\"This is wonderful news!\"","Li Yanshu couldn't stop smiling.","She knew her brother had talent. Sure enough, he had passed the exam.","But before she could celebrate for long, she heard the system chime in, [Hey, just so you know, Princess Changping's husband Zhao Chengwen is currently sending people to cause a commotion in front of the Imperial Academy's announcement board, saying your brother cheated.]","What?","Li Yanshu was stunned. [Causing a commotion saying Tianrui cheated? Why is that bastard doing this?]","The system replied, [Do you even need to ask? His nephew was crippled because of your brother, and his niece was ruined because of you. How could he not hate you? He's been preparing for this ever since your brother applied to the Imperial Academy, planning to use this opportunity to slander you.]","Li Yanshu: [Well well, it seems the previous stories didn't do him justice.]","Damn, one can't go easy on this kind of scum!","Time to add a few more strokes to his portrait!","Not long after, news of the situation at the Imperial Academy's announcement board reached the Emperor's ears.","After listening to the report from Yan Zhengping, the Director of the Imperial Academy, Yuwen Lan frowned and asked, \"Who is causing this commotion?\"","Yan Zhengping replied, \"At first it was four or five people, then it grew to over ten. Now many of the failed candidates have joined in as well, so there are several dozen people. They are all demanding that the court hold a re-examination.\"","\"A re-examination?\"","Yuwen Lan sneered, \"On what grounds are they demanding the court hold a re-examination?\"","Yan Zhengping frowned and said, \"Someone claimed that the third-ranked candidate on the list, a certain Li Tianrui, is the younger brother of Noble Consort Li. They're saying the examiners leaked the exam questions to this Li Tianrui in advance to curry favor with Noble Consort Li.\"","\"Preposterous!\"","Yuwen Lan shouted angrily.","The officials present were startled and immediately bowed their heads, saying, \"Your Majesty, please calm your anger.\"","From the side, Hanlin Academy scholar Zou Mozhong said, \"Your Majesty, this matter seems to be the deliberate work of someone with ulterior motives. There were over a thousand candidates in this exam, and it's not uncommon for some to share the same name. From what I know, young Master Li has only recently arrived in the capital, so he likely doesn't know many of the other candidates. How could someone immediately recognize him as Noble Consort Li's younger brother and make such a big fuss over it?\"","\"A re-examination would waste manpower and resources, and make the court's authority a laughingstock! Therefore, I believe we absolutely cannot allow a hasty re-examination. In my opinion, the person behind this has malicious intentions, perhaps even hints of trying to subvert the state. They must not be dealt with lightly.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"Scholar Zou makes a good point. The people causing this commotion indeed have sinister motives. Issue an order to arrest everyone who participated in the commotion today and thoroughly investigate their backgrounds.\"","After the officials acknowledged the order, he added one more command: \"Summon Li Tianrui for an audience.\"","Before long, Li Tianrui appeared before the Emperor.","The young man first bowed to the emperor and said, \"This humble subject Li Tianrui greets Your Majesty.\"","Unlike the last time when he followed his father to have an audience with the emperor, this time he came alone.","However, at just fifteen years old, his composure was remarkable, causing others to take notice.","Yuwen Lan got straight to the point and asked him, \"Today the Imperial Academy posted its results. Some say you cheated. What do you think about that?\"","The youth's voice was very clear as he immediately replied, \"This humble subject has a clear conscience and would not fear even if tested again.\"","The emperor on the throne nodded, \"Good. I will test you again now in front of the court officials. If you can answer, I will personally clear your name of these slanders.\"","Li Yuanrui kowtowed deeply, \"This subject obeys the imperial command.\"","Thus, in front of the Qianming Palace's Hall of Diligent Government, under the watchful eyes of several important court ministers, Li Yuanrui took the exam once again.","The Imperial Academy entrance exam was not as difficult as the imperial examinations. It mainly focused on the Four Books and Five Classics, along with principles of human nature and law. Several court officials asked questions on the spot, and the young man answered them all fluently, showing a very solid foundation.","Moreover, his demeanor was poised and graceful, not at all like someone who had just arrived in the capital from a small place like Ande.","After about two hours, the exam ended, and all the ministers nodded to him, expressing their approval.","Yan Zhengping, the director of the Imperial Academy, also breathed a sigh of relief and hurriedly said, \"Today, Your Majesty and several officials have witnessed firsthand that this young Master Li is intelligent and truly learned. It is impossible that he could have gained admission through leaked exam questions. Clearly, those earlier accusations were pure slander.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Indeed. Announce today's results to the world to quell any doubts. As for those who maliciously caused trouble, deal with them strictly and show no leniency.\"","Everyone responded in agreement.","As the young man Li Tianrui was returning home from the palace, his sister Li Yanshu had just finished revising her story \"The Two-Faced Scholar Dies Under the Flowers.\"","Tsk, last time she had held back a lot to save face for the imperial family, but this time she decided to let it all out about that dog.","She blew on the ink on the paper and looked out the window, seeing that it was still early.","Figuring the emperor wouldn't come for a while, she couldn't wait and decided to take her manuscript to the Qianming Palace.","At this time, the ministers had just left, and Yuwen Lan had a moment of free time. He was about to take a sip of tea when he saw Li Yanshu arrive.","At first, he thought she had come because of her brother's matter.","But after she paid her respects, she placed the manuscript directly in front of him and said, \"This humble consort has just finished writing a story and finds it quite interesting. I wanted to share it with Your Majesty.\"","A story?","Yuwen Lan was somewhat surprised. He made a sound of acknowledgment, took it in his hand, and asked, \"What kind of story is it this time?\"","She replied, \"This story is called 'The Two-Faced Scholar Dies Under the Flowers.' It's about a man who appears honest on the surface but is actually extremely licentious. He does many outrageous things and eventually dies from his romantic entanglements.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Appears honest but is extremely licentious?","Is she talking about... Zhao Chengwen?","Well, let's see how she wrote it.","So he said, \"Tell me about it.\"","Li Yanshu cleared her throat and began to tell the story, \"There was a young man who was intelligent and studious from childhood, and quite talented. At nineteen, he showed promise in his first imperial examination and thus caught the eye of a wealthy family, who took him as a son-in-law. From then on, his future seemed bright.\"","\"However, his wife came from a wealthy background and was not like ordinary virtuous wives. His father-in-law had a vast family business, so he didn't need to work hard to build a career. With his talents unused, he could only live in luxury at home. As time passed, he began to feel bored. To seek excitement, this man began to keep mistresses behind his wife's back.\"","\"One wasn't enough, so he kept two. Two weren't enough, so he kept three. Later, this man ended up keeping five or six, but still wasn't satisfied. He even bought a mansion in Jiangnan, specifically for raising young and beautiful women. Once these women were trained to his liking, he would keep them for himself. Those who didn't meet his standards were sold to brothels for profit...\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan was taken aback.","He had no idea Zhao Chengwen had done such things!","This was outrageous!","He frowned and asked, \"If this man did such things, didn't his wife notice? Buying a mansion must cost quite a bit of money, right?\"","Li Yanshu sighed and said, \"His family was as wealthy as a small country, and his wife had her own social engagements. She didn't pay much attention to his finances. Besides, this man had long been saving his own private funds. How else could he keep so many mistresses?\"","That made sense.","Yuwen Lan then asked, \"So what happened next?\"","Li Yanshu continued, \"This man had a favorite mistress who was actually a maid he had before marriage. Over the years, she bore him several children. As the children grew older, the mistress wanted them to be officially recognized as part of the family. She begged him. The man couldn't resist her pleas, but his wife would never agree to him having another woman. Caught in this dilemma, the man began to plot to get rid of his wife.\"","This was going too far.","Yuwen Lan frowned again, \"There were even such matters?\"","She nodded firmly, \"Of course. Your Majesty, think about it. This man had seen so many young and beautiful women over the years, his heart was no longer at home. Moreover, his wife had only given him one daughter, while his mistress had two sons. Weighing the pros and cons, he decided he wanted the mistress and the sons.\"","\"But before he could finish his plan, his other mistresses found out about this and all started demanding to be officially recognized. He could only try his best to appease them, but his energy was limited after all.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Limited energy???","For the first time, he realized how fitting this phrase was...","After all, with so many women, it truly would be limited. Ahem.","He tried to maintain a serious expression and asked, \"Then what?\"","Li Yanshu said, \"Then, those young women were certainly not satisfied. Some began to give him drugs. This man found that after taking the drugs, his abilities were greatly enhanced, so he became addicted. But over time, his body couldn't handle it. One day, he didn't control the dosage well and collapsed directly on the bed.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Drugs???","Enhanced abilities???","Yuwen Lan thought to himself, this girl knows far too much!","But before he could speak, she continued, \"The mistress was terrified and quickly went to find a doctor. However, the doctor she found happened to know this man's wife and secretly informed her. When his wife found out, she rushed over immediately. Seeing that it was indeed him, she flew into a rage and directly cut off his precious thing with a sword.\"","\"This man was already weak, and after suffering such a severe injury, he died directly from excessive blood loss.\"","With that, the story was finished.","Yuwen Lan let out a breath and said, \"He deserved to die. Otherwise, it would have been too unfair to his father-in-law.\"","Li Yanshu quickly leaned in and asked, \"Does Your Majesty think this story can be published?\"","Unexpectedly, he replied directly, \"It can, and it should be done quickly.\"","Otherwise, if it was any slower, the Princess might be harmed by him."]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40","paragraphs":["At the emperor's command, Yanshu's new novel manuscript reached the booksellers that very afternoon.","After a hurried printing process by the publishing house staff, \"The Two-Faced Scholar Dies Under the Flowers,\" the latest work by the Carefree Genius, went on sale early the next morning.","Needless to say, it sold out immediately.","The booksellers rushed to print two or three more batches, yet still couldn't meet the demand.","In the morning, after drafting an imperial edict for the emperor, Hanlin Academy scholar Zou Mozhong saw the emperor had a free moment. He quickly took out a bank note from his pocket and presented it, saying, \"Your Majesty, this is the Carefree Genius's manuscript fee for this month. Please pass it on to her.\"","As her novels continued to be bestsellers, Yanshu's value had also risen sharply. Now she could earn fifty or sixty taels of silver for a single novel.","In a month, she could easily make two or three hundred taels.","For such a large sum, it wasn't convenient to handle actual silver, so the booksellers had started paying royalties with bank notes.","Yuwen Lan accepted it and casually asked, \"How are sales for the new book?\"","Zou Mozhong replied, \"You mean 'The Two-Faced Scholar,' Your Majesty? Naturally, it's selling extremely well! The bookseller who brought me the bank note earlier said they've already sold over a thousand copies.\"","Over a thousand copies? And it was only morning.","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and asked, \"So, what's the reaction from those who've read it?\"","Scholar Zou immediately replied, \"It's excellent, of course. The Carefree Genius's books always spark widespread discussion among the people, but this time even more so. Readers are exclaiming in wonder - who could have imagined there were such two-faced people in the world, if it hadn't been written in the book?\"","Ahem, this was of course just polite official speak. What Scholar Zou was really thinking was:","[They're all trying to guess who it's about, my dear emperor! Some even suspect it's about the Eldest Princess and her consort! After all, he's both a scholar and from a wealthy family - can someone tell me if it's true?! Is the princess's consort really so daring???]","[Tsk, of course, the most important thing now is, I wonder how the Eldest Princess will react when she reads it.]","[But I've heard that princess doesn't like reading books, she only enjoys socializing and entertaining. I guess it'll be a while before she sees it!]","Yuwen Lan, who was listening silently, thought the same, so he said, \"Bring me two copies of the printed novel.\"","Zou Mozhong was startled, somewhat puzzled. Didn't His Majesty already read the original manuscript? Why did he want the printed version?","Nevertheless, he quickly agreed. Upon leaving the imperial study, he immediately went to the street to buy two newly printed copies and delivered them to the emperor in the palace.","Yuwen Lan received the new novels and flipped through them, feeling that the printed text was indeed clearer and easier to read.","Ahem, it was much more comfortable to look at compared to Yanshu's crooked handwriting in the original manuscript.","It seemed he should make her practice her calligraphy.","Just as he was thinking this, he was informed that officials from the Ministry of Justice and the Court of Judicial Review were seeking an audience.","He set aside the novels and had them brought in.","After the two men paid their respects, they reported, \"Your Majesty, after interrogation and investigation, we have confirmed that those who caused a disturbance at the Imperial Academy's notice board yesterday were all candidates from this examination. Most of them were resentful about failing and joined in when they saw others causing trouble. However, about five or six individuals started spreading rumors as soon as the results were posted. Upon careful investigation, we found that these few were extremely poor students, and some didn't even qualify to take the Imperial Academy exam.\"","It should be noted that not just anyone could take the Imperial Academy exam. For instance, this second batch of candidates all needed recommendations from local education officials or famous academies to be eligible.","Yuwen Lan asked, \"Then how did they participate in the exam?\"","The Vice Minister of Justice hurriedly answered, \"These individuals confessed after some interrogation that someone had helped them secretly manipulate their way into the exam. They were instructed that if they saw Li Tianrui's name on the results list, they should immediately spread rumors and cause a disturbance to create trouble.\"","Just as suspected.","Yuwen Lan asked, \"Have you found out who's behind this?\"","At this, the Vice Minister of Justice and the Junior Chief Justice exchanged a glance before replying, \"It was a senior servant named Feng Dejin, who works for Consort Zhao in the Eldest Princess's mansion.\"","Hmph, Zhao Chengwen's subordinate?","Yuwen Lan had already guessed what was going on.","The one who had been caned was his nephew, and Consort Ning was his niece. It seemed this was deliberate retaliation against Yanshu.","He said sternly, \"Go to the Eldest Princess's mansion and arrest this person. Continue the interrogation to see if someone was directing this servant's actions.\"","The Vice Minister of Justice and the Junior Chief Justice immediately agreed.","Since it involved the Eldest Princess's mansion, they initially didn't dare to make arrests rashly.","Now with the emperor's direct order, they had nothing to fear.","After the two officials took their leave, it was already noon.","Yuwen Lan had lunch in Qianming Palace. Not feeling sleepy, he decided to take advantage of the momentary lull in urgent matters to bring the bank note to Ganlu Palace.","Ahem, today was the day the booksellers paid royalties, and that money-loving girl must be eagerly waiting.","However, when he arrived, he found her casually eating melon seeds on the warm couch, seemingly not in a hurry at all.","Seeing him arrive, she quickly put down the melon seeds, stood up, cleared her throat, and said, \"This concubine greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and sat down at the table, asking, \"Not writing a novel?\"","Yanshu replied, \"This concubine was tired from writing yesterday and wanted to rest today.\"","Ahem, mainly she was focused on waiting for drama to unfold today, how could she have the mood to write?","Come to think of it, it was strange. It had been most of the day, and many people in the city had already guessed that the new novel was about that consort Zhao Chengwen, so why hadn't the Eldest Princess shown any reaction yet?","It left her with no desire to do anything else, truly making her anxious.","Yuwen Lan, listening silently, \"...\"","Glancing at the melon seed shells on the table, he was convinced that she was indeed wholeheartedly waiting to watch the drama unfold.","To help her shift her attention, he took out the bank note and said, \"This is your manuscript fee. It was just delivered today.\"","Sure enough, her eyes lit up, and she happily accepted it with a smile, saying, \"Thank you, Your Majesty.\"","Hehe, another three hundred taels in the account, money truly brings comfort!","Yuwen Lan found her reaction amusing and asked, \"You don't need to spend money in the palace, and your monthly allowance is enough now. Why are you still so fond of money?\"","Yanshu pouted and said, \"This concubine didn't live very comfortably before, so I think money is a good thing. Your Majesty wouldn't understand.\"","Hmph, anyway, this is all money she earned herself, so what's wrong with liking it?","Especially since there seemed to be fewer and fewer people in the palace, who knows when the emperor might not need her as a scapegoat anymore and kick her out.","Of course, she had to ensure her own security!","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","How could she still think he would abandon her after everything that had happened?","He wanted to have a good talk with her about this issue, but before he could speak, someone announced from outside, \"My lord, Aunt Zhu Shu from the Palace of Benevolent Peace has arrived.\"","The Palace of Benevolent Peace?","Yanshu was startled, looked at Yuwen Lan, and quickly said, \"Please show her in.\"","Soon enough, the Empress Dowager's lady-in-waiting, Zhu Shu, entered the hall.","Seeing Yuwen Lan was also present, Zhu Shu hurriedly bowed, \"This servant greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and asked, \"Does the Empress Dowager have some matter?\"","Zhu Shu said, \"The Palace of Benevolent Peace has just made some water chestnut cakes, which are very refreshing. The Empress Dowager said to invite Consort Yi to come and taste them.\"","Water chestnut cakes?","Yanshu wondered to herself if the Empress Dowager wanted to probe for information again, so she called her over?","Just then, she heard Yuwen Lan ask, \"I'm also in the mood for water chestnut cakes. May I come along?\"","Zhu Shu smiled and said, \"Your Majesty is joking. If you were to visit, the Empress Dowager would be delighted.\"","Ahem, actually, the Empress Dowager knew His Majesty was here, which is why she sent for Consort Yi.","Yuwen Lan understood. It seemed the Empress Dowager's real target was him.","He made a sound of acknowledgment and said to Yanshu, \"Then let's go together.\"","Although Yanshu didn't quite understand, she thought it would be much better to have the emperor accompany her, so she agreed and left with him.","When they arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu paid her respects to the Empress Dowager. Yuwen Lan took the initiative to say, \"I heard there were water chestnut cakes to eat, so I shamelessly came to partake. I hope Mother Empress doesn't mind.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"How could you say that? I'm more than happy that Your Majesty has come.\"","She then instructed the palace servants to serve tea and snacks.","In her heart, however, she snorted with amusement, [I knew you wouldn't be at ease letting Consort Yi come alone, so you came along. What, did you think I would eat her alive?]","Soon, the water chestnut cakes and hot tea were served.","Yanshu observed that the pastry was semi-transparent and tea-colored, resembling jelly from modern times.","She tried a bite and found it soft, smooth, and chewy, with the sweet fragrance of water chestnuts.","She had heard that the best pastry chefs in the palace were in the Empress Dowager's quarters, and it seemed this was indeed true.","However, she wondered why the Empress Dowager had summoned her.","Feeling cautious, she didn't dare to eat too much for the moment.","Looking to the side, she saw that Yuwen Lan had also eaten a piece of water chestnut cake. He nodded and said, \"It's been a while since I've had water chestnut cake. It's indeed excellent.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"If you like it, eat more. It's moisturizing and noise-reducing, perfect for spring consumption.\"","Then, changing the subject, she said, \"Speaking of which, I just read the Carefree Gentleman's novel this morning, and somehow the characters seemed a bit familiar...\"","Before she could finish, a coughing sound interrupted her.","It turned out Yuwen Lan was drinking tea and had choked on it.","The Empress Dowager hurriedly asked, \"Is Your Majesty alright?\"","Yuwen Lan composed himself and said, \"I'm fine.\"","He glanced at Yanshu, only to see her carelessly picking up another piece of water chestnut cake and putting it in her mouth.","[Oh, so the Empress Dowager wants to inquire about the novel. Since the Emperor had it written, it's got nothing to do with me. I'll just keep eating.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She really knew how to dodge responsibility cleanly.","But before he could respond, Xiao Shunzi came to report from outside the door, \"Your Majesty, the Eldest Princess and her consort are seeking an audience at Qianming Palace.\"","Suddenly, two voices echoed in his ears.","Yanshu: [Huh? The Eldest Princess and Zhao Chengwen came together? Could it be that I'll get to witness some drama in person today?! Quick, tell them to come here, Emperor!!!]","Empress Dowager: [Why are they coming at this time? Could it be that they've read the novel and are here to confront the Emperor? I thought that rascal resembled Zhao Chengwen!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Before he could speak, the Empress Dowager said, \"Your Majesty hasn't finished the pastries yet. Why don't we have them come directly to the Palace of Benevolent Peace?\"","Yanshu: [!!! The scene will be even grander then? Wonderful, I'll get to witness some drama in person today!!! The Empress Dowager gets me!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So there's another person eager to watch the show?","However, the Empress Dowager was after all an elder, and it might be good to discuss some matters in her presence.","So he ordered, \"The Empress Dowager is right. Have them come here, it's a good opportunity for them to pay their respects to the Empress Dowager as well.\"","Xiao Shunzi acknowledged and hurried off to relay the message.","Yuwen Lan then instructed Fu Hai, \"Go to the imperial study and bring those two novels.\"","Fu Hai also acknowledged and quickly went to fetch them.","Soon after, Eldest Princess Yuwen Yan and her consort Zhao Chengwen arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Upon entering the hall, they first paid their respects to everyone present.","Zhao Chengwen, as always, hid behind his wife, looking very simple and honest.","Moreover, he seemed to carry a hint of grievance.","Yuwen Lan observed this and asked, \"What brings Elder Sister here so suddenly?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Eldest Princess Yuwen Yan said angrily, \"Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager may not know, but just now, people from the Ministry of Justice and the Court of Judicial Review came to the Princess's mansion to arrest someone. They claimed that someone from our household had instigated trouble at the Imperial Academy and wanted to take them back for interrogation.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"I ordered them to do so. Yesterday, someone caused trouble in front of the Imperial Academy's notice board, attempting to disrupt the court's prestige. The Ministry of Justice and the Court of Judicial Review discovered that it was the consort's personal attendant who was behind it, so they went to your mansion to make the arrest.\"","He then asked, \"It's just the arrest of a servant. Why has Elder Sister come to me for this?\"","Yuwen Yan faltered, but still said, \"I'm just worried they might wrongly accuse an innocent person. They're investigating Feng Dejin now, but who knows if they'll implicate the consort next?\"","Yuwen Lan smiled and gave Zhao Chengwen a meaningful look, \"The court would never wrongly accuse an innocent person. If the consort hasn't done anything, naturally, he won't be implicated.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Zhao Chengwen hurriedly said, \"I beg Your Majesty to be clear-sighted. I have never been involved in court affairs, how could I possibly commit such a heinous act?\"","These words sounded as if he was complaining that the emperor hadn't given him any official duties.","Sure enough, the Eldest Princess immediately said, \"Exactly, how come we never get any good opportunities, but bad things are arbitrarily pinned on us?\"","As she said this, Zhao Chengwen tugged at her sleeve, appearing very timid and afraid of trouble.","Yanshu couldn't help but marvel inwardly, [Damn, he's quite the actor! He's fooled the Eldest Princess so thoroughly, she'd probably still count money for him even if he sold her out.]","However, upon hearing these words, the Emperor's face showed a hint of anger as he said, \"What do you mean by 'good opportunities'? Many people exhaust themselves working for a year just to barely feed themselves, while you receive an annual salary of thousands of taels of silver and spend your days in leisure and pleasure. Is this not considered good enough?\"","His voice had become sharp, and everyone in the hall was startled, lowering their heads.","Yuwen Yan also paused, then said, \"I misspoke. Please calm your anger, Your Majesty. I'm just worried about the consort. You know he's not good with words, and I fear he might not be able to defend himself if wrongly accused.\"","Wrongly accused?","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but laugh bitterly.","He gestured for Fu Hai to bring the recently fetched novels forward and said to Yuwen Yan, \"There's a story here that Elder Sister might want to read.\"","But Yuwen Yan said, \"I don't like reading such idle gossip written by commoners.\"","Before Yuwen Lan could say anything more, the Empress Dowager spoke up, \"You should take a look. These novels are quite interesting, and the events described in them are quite accurate.\"","Yuwen Yan laughed and said, \"Mother Empress has been confined in the palace for too long and must be quite bored. Such vulgar tales are nothing but sensationalism, how could they be accurate?\"","Yuwen Lan didn't argue further and simply instructed Fu Hai, \"Tell the Eldest Princess about this story.\"","Yanshu: \"?!!!\"","Having Fu Hai tell the story to the Eldest Princess in front of so many people?","As expected, the Emperor knows how to handle things! This method is excellent, having the entire hall of palace servants listen to the story of the consort keeping a mistress! Hahaha! Brilliant, brilliant!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She really didn't mind stirring up trouble.","Fu Hai acknowledged the order and began to tell the story from the novel.","\"There was a talented young man in the capital, born into a wealthy family. He was intelligent, studious, and naturally gifted. At the age of nineteen, he took the imperial examinations for the first time and immediately stood out...\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Yan said proudly, \"This person seems quite similar to the consort.\"","The Emperor, Empress Dowager, and Yanshu all remained silent, but they couldn't help looking at Zhao Chengwen.","He was looking down, lost in thought.","Fu Hai continued, \"A wealthy merchant family noticed his talent and took him in as a son-in-law. From then on, he lived a life of luxury and success... However, his in-laws' business was so vast that they didn't need him to work hard. The talented young man found his abilities wasted and gradually became frustrated. He could only secretly keep young and beautiful women as mistresses behind his wife's back, indulging in carnal pleasures to vent his frustrations...\"","Hearing this, the Eldest Princess finally began to sense something was amiss. She thought for a moment and glanced at Zhao Chengwen.","She saw that Zhao Chengwen's eyes had become panicked...","\"Having tasted the sweetness of beautiful women, the talented young man's appetite grew insatiable. Not satisfied with six mistresses in the capital, he also lavishly purchased mansions in Jiangnan, keeping countless beauties for his own use. The grand scale of his harem rivaled that of the imperial palace...\"","Yuwen Yan paused again—","Zhao Chengwen traveled to Jiangnan several times a year under the pretext of business...","While she was in shock, Fu Hai had already reached the crucial part, \"His mistresses were deeply in love with him, and most importantly, they had borne him two sons. How could he bear to let his sons live in obscurity? After much difficult deliberation, he finally made up his mind to get rid of his wife...\"","Yuwen Yan's heart skipped a beat. She could no longer care about anything else and snatched the book from Fu Hai's hands to read it herself.","The more she read, the more her face turned ashen.","Zhao Chengwen's face had already turned pale. He hurriedly said, \"Your Highness, this is all fabricated by the novel writer... You mustn't take it seriously!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the Emperor suddenly asked him, \"If that's the case, why are you so nervous?\"","Zhao Chengwen quickly replied, \"I, I'm not nervous...\"","But before he could finish, the Eldest Princess suddenly threw the book to the ground and said, \"Zhao Chengwen, could this book be writing about you?\"","Zhao Chengwen hurriedly said, \"Of course not! This is clearly malicious slander. The person who wrote this novel has evil intentions!\"","Evil intentions?","Yanshu, uninvolved, ate another piece of water chestnut cake.","The Empress Dowager glanced at Yuwen Lan.","Suddenly, Zhao Chengwen threw himself before her and the emperor, saying, \"I beg Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager to see clearly. This storyteller's baseless slander is truly despicable. He should be arrested immediately and not allowed to spread more lies!\"","Yuwen Lan smiled and said, \"It's just a story, naturally it's fiction. Why are you so agitated?\"","Zhao Chengwen hesitated, wanting to say he wasn't agitated.","But the emperor continued, \"Speaking of which, when I went out to observe the people's conditions on the fifteenth day of the first month, I happened to run into you.\"","At these words, Yuwen Yan looked at Zhao Chengwen with suspicion.","Zhao Chengwen hurriedly said, \"This subject didn't know Your Majesty was there. I was disrespectful.\"","Yuwen Lan went on, \"You bought some snacks from Tianjing Lane, then visited five or six homes. What was that about? Were you visiting friends?\"","Before Zhao Chengwen could answer, Yuwen Yan frowned and said, \"I didn't know you had friends living near Tianjing Lane. Tell me, what were you really doing that night?\"","Zhao Chengwen struggled to lie, \"There's a famous snack shop there. I thought the princess might be hungry after drinking, so I wanted to buy some snacks for her.\"","Yanshu, sitting nearby and eating water chestnut cake, thought to herself —","[He's still lying even when he's about to die. Those snacks were clearly for his two mistresses.]","Then Yuwen Lan said, \"Didn't you deliver the snacks to the second house? I heard a young woman lives there with two boys.\"","At these words, before Zhao Chengwen could say anything, Yuwen Yan's eyes widened in shock.","\"Two boys? So the story was true! Were you planning to get rid of me so you could bring that whore and her three children into the family?\"","Zhao Chengwen hurriedly shook his head, \"No, no, no, how could I dare do such a thing to Your Highness...\"","Before he could finish, Yanshu quickly interjected, \"So the mistresses are real, you just weren't planning to harm the Eldest Princess?\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Yan's face turned ashen and her eyebrows furrowed in anger.","Her gaze swept around the hall, suddenly spotting the exorcism sword hanging on a pillar. She strode over, pulled out the sword, and swung it at Zhao Chengwen.","\"You dog! I'll kill you today!!!\"","Zhao Chengwen was so frightened he turned and ran.","But Yuwen Yan pursued him relentlessly, shouting in rage, \"Mistresses? Courtesans? Even buying a house in Jiangnan to keep beauties!!! If I don't cut you down today, I'll have failed my Yuwen ancestors!!!\"","Everyone in the hall was shocked and terrified, except for Yanshu who watched intently, thinking excitedly —","[Now we'll see if the Eldest Princess's swordsmanship is accurate enough to hit him! Tsk, she won't really cut off his thing right there, will she? So exciting!!!]","Just as she was thinking this, the Eldest Princess's blade swept across Zhao Chengwen's arm. The man let out a howl as blood immediately began to flow from his arm.","Yanshu froze, then suddenly felt weak all over, nearly falling off her chair.","She was fainting at the sight of blood again.","But how could she faint at a time like this?","She mentally screamed at herself, [No! I absolutely can't faint now!!! Pull yourself together, you can't miss this exciting scene!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Her face had gone pale, yet she still wanted to watch the commotion?","He immediately stood up from his seat, walked over in a few steps and pulled her into his arms, saying to the two, \"Stop.\"","The Empress Dowager also hurriedly said, \"His Majesty is present, how can you behave like this? Stop immediately!\"","However, Yuwen Yan's eyes were red with fury, as if possessed, and she showed no signs of stopping.","In the blink of an eye, she swung her sword at Zhao Chengwen's face again, instantly causing blood to gush from his face.","Seeing this, Yanshu felt even weaker, and nearly rolled her eyes back.","Yet her mind was still clinging to the last shreds of consciousness —","[Don't faint!!! Stay awake!!! He might really lose his precious part!!! This is a once-in-a-lifetime scene!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","He could feel her fainting more severely and didn't dare delay any longer. He quickly said, \"Guards, stop her immediately!\"","The guards rushed into the hall and finally restrained Yuwen Yan.","Meanwhile, Zhao Chengwen knelt on the ground, howling and covering his face.","Yuwen Lan said, \"Elder sister, don't be hasty. I've already ordered an investigation. If he has truly wronged you, he will be dealt with according to the law and family rules.\"","Yuwen Yan's hair was disheveled, her jewelry scattered on the ground. She pointed at Zhao Chengwen, panting with rage, \"You dog! I've spoiled you all these years! Your father's marquis title, your niece's consort position - I should have fed them to the dogs instead!\"","As she finished speaking, Yanshu, still in Yuwen Lan's arms, mustered her fading consciousness to yell internally, [That's right! So two cuts aren't enough!!! One more strike, aim for his vital spot!!!]","Yuwen Lan: [...]","This girl was beyond saving.","He ordered, \"Escort the princess to rest, find an imperial physician to bandage the consort's wounds, but don't let him leave the palace.\"","Everyone acknowledged the order and escorted the couple out of the hall.","The hall finally quieted down. Yuwen Lan asked the Empress Dowager, \"Did this frighten Mother?\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"I'm fine. This girl's temper hasn't changed one bit!\"","Yuwen Lan was about to nod when he heard the Empress Dowager think, [That Zhao boy got off easy today!]","\"???\"","Then he heard the Empress Dowager sigh again, [Ah, the princess has it good, being able to cut men as she pleases.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","The Empress Dowager then asked him, \"What's wrong with Consort Yi?\"","Yuwen Lan snapped back to attention and said, \"She faints at the sight of blood. I'll take her back first.\"","The Empress Dowager quickly nodded, \"Poor dear, go quickly then.\"","Yuwen Lan acknowledged and carried Yanshu away."]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41","paragraphs":["Upon leaving the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu's limbs were still weak, and her body felt devoid of strength.","Yuwen Lan hadn't had time to summon the imperial carriage, so he simply carried her all the way back to Ganlu Palace.","When the people in the palace saw this, they were all startled and hurried forward to ask, \"What happened to the mistress? Mistress...\"","Yuwen Lan placed her on the bed, and seeing that her eyes were still open, he asked, \"How are you feeling? Any better? Should I call for the imperial physician?\"","Yanshu's voice was as faint as a mosquito's buzz, \"No, no need...\"","It was as if even speaking had become difficult, and her face was deathly pale, with sweat beading on her nose, looking extremely weak.","Yuwen Lan, both worried and puzzled, said, \"Last time, didn't you feel better after resting for a while? Why is it so severe this time?\"","But he heard her thinking to herself — How could it be the same as last time? Last time she only had one wound, but just now Zhao Chengwen's blood was all over her body!","It was too intense!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, perhaps she had used all her willpower to watch the commotion earlier, and now that the excitement was over, her willpower had relaxed, causing her to feel so weak.","The fact that she could still think of so many random things meant she was probably fine.","He then instructed Rendong to give Yanshu some water.","Sure enough, about a quarter of an hour later, Yanshu's complexion had become rosy again, and she had the strength to thank him, \"Thank you, Your Majesty, for carrying this humble concubine back.\"","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but smile, raising an eyebrow as he asked her, \"You clearly faint at the sight of blood, yet you insist on watching?\"","Yanshu stubbornly replied, \"It's not that this humble concubine insisted on watching. The Eldest Princess suddenly became so agitated, who could have imagined she would actually slash the Prince Consort?\"","Yuwen Lan continued to raise his eyebrow, \"You really didn't expect it? The stories in your novels are far more violent than what just happened.\"","Yanshu choked a bit, \"...Well, novels are fiction after all. They need to be more exaggerated for people to enjoy reading them. How can they be compared to reality?\"","In her heart, however, she was quite disappointed, thinking, [It's a shame, I overestimated the Eldest Princess. She chased him for so many circles only to land two cuts, and didn't even hit any vital spots. What a waste of a great opportunity.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Who's disappointed?","The Eldest Princess?","Or is she disappointed she didn't see enough excitement???","Then immediately after, he heard her sigh in her heart, [The ceiling for women is indeed still being a princess. When the man misbehaves, just slash him! Who else would dare to do such a thing?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","...How come one after another, they all think like this?","Are all women so ferocious???","Then he saw her secretly glance at him, thinking to herself, [Of course, this kind of problem would never happen with him.]","Yuwen Lan breathed a sigh of relief.","That's more like it.","But then, he heard her continue, [Because he has no way to misbehave anyway!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","His feelings were quite complex, and he very much wanted to say something.","However, at that moment, Fu Hai came running to the door in a panic, reporting, \"Your Majesty, the Eldest Princess has gone to slash the Prince Consort again.\"","Huh?","Yanshu was startled and immediately asked, \"Where did she slash him?\"","Fu Hai, however, was stammering and looked very troubled, \"She slashed... uh, she slashed...\"","After a long while, he still couldn't say it.","Seeing this situation, Yanshu secretly guessed in her heart, [Could it be that the Eldest Princess really went and cut off Zhao Chengwen's precious thing???]","[It must be! Otherwise, if it were somewhere else, why would Fu Hai take so long to say it? No, I must go and see!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Who was it that was so weak from seeing blood earlier?","He glanced at her and said, \"I'll go take a look. You stay here and rest well.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the girl had a reluctant look on her face, \"But, but this humble concubine...\"","[Leaving me behind to go watch the excitement alone seems a bit too unkind!!!]","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow at her, \"You want to faint again? And have me carry you back?\"","Yanshu could only say, \"I don't want to.\"","Then she heard him say, \"Then stay here obediently.\"","With that, he stood up and walked straight out of the palace doors.","Yanshu could only watch him leave with longing eyes, feeling extremely resentful in her heart.","Why did she have to faint at the sight of blood!!!","What an incredibly exciting scene she was missing!!!","It was truly a lifelong regret!!!","Yuwen Lan boarded the imperial carriage and made his way to Spring Scenery Garden, where the Eldest Princess and her husband were located.","As soon as he got off the carriage, he heard a commotion.","He went to Hunchun Hall where the noise was coming from, and saw Zhao Chengwen lying on the ground, with two new wounds on his left shoulder and face. Most importantly, his lower body was covered in blood.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Did she really cut it off?","Looking at the Eldest Princess again, he saw that she was being held back by palace servants, but her sword was still flailing wildly in her hand, and she was still cursing angrily, \"I'll hack you to death, you dog...\"","He simply stepped forward, snatched the sword away, and said, \"If you keep slashing like this, he's going to die.\"","The Eldest Princess snorted, \"He deserves to die! Even death can't quell the hatred in my heart!!! I want to chop him into pieces and mince him into meat paste to feed the dogs!!!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He first ordered the imperial physician to stop Zhao Chengwen's bleeding, then said to the Eldest Princess, \"Even if he deserves to die, we need to give an explanation to the world. Otherwise, people will think you killed him for no reason.\"","The Eldest Princess was still angry, and suddenly remembering something, she immediately asked him furiously, \"Your Majesty, since you knew about his treachery early on, why didn't you tell me sooner?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"At that time, you had complete faith in him. If I had told you, would you have believed me? Naturally, I had to wait until the evidence was irrefutable and he couldn't defend himself before telling you.\"","Yuwen Yan cursed again, \"Letting him live these extra days was a waste of my food!\"","Especially when she thought about how this dog actually kept so many women behind her back, she wanted to go and slash him a few more times.","So she pointed at him and cursed, \"Zhao Chengwen, I struggled and escaped death to give birth to a daughter for you, and you dare to plot against me for those two illegitimate sons? Just you wait, I'm going to throw those two bastards into the mountains to feed the dogs!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Zhao Chengwen, who was on the brink of unconsciousness, hurriedly said, \"No! I beg the Princess not to harm them! The wrongdoing was mine, I'll accept any punishment, but they are young and innocent. I beg the Princess to show mercy.\"","After he finished speaking, Yuwen Lan also said, \"Elder sister, calm down first. He should pay for his own mistakes, there's no need to involve innocent children.\"","Then he rebuked Zhao Chengwen, \"You only remember that those two boys are your flesh and blood, but have you thought about Lan Jun? For the sake of having your illegitimate sons recognized by the ancestors, you were willing to let Lan Jun lose her mother?\"","Lan Jun was the only daughter of this couple, only five years old this year. She had been doted on by the late emperor and was granted the title of Yi'an County Princess at birth.","Upon hearing this, the Eldest Princess was about to step forward to kick Zhao Chengwen again.","But then she heard the emperor rebuke her, \"Elder sister, you also need to reflect on this matter. You are usually harsh and contemptuous towards others, so why did you have such blind faith in this man? Moreover, even though he was already suspected of violating the law, you still tried to obstruct my investigation?\"","Yuwen Yan choked, and finally said, \"I acknowledge my guilt.\"","Yuwen Lan straightened his expression and said, \"In this matter, I will handle it according to the law. Before that, you are not allowed to interfere anymore.\"","Yuwen Yan had no choice but to agree.","The next day, news of the Eldest Princess angrily slashing her husband spread throughout the court and commoners.","People only heard that Prince Consort Zhao Chengwen had kept many young women outside the palace, and even built a mansion in Jiangnan to select concubines, attempting to rival the emperor. This enraged the Eldest Princess so much that she directly drew her sword and cut off his manhood...","For a time, the whole world was in an uproar.","However, at the same time, it also confirmed the previous speculation of many —","It turned out that the \"Two-faced Scholar\" written in the Carefree Young Master's new novel was indeed Prince Consort Zhao Chengwen.","Tsk tsk tsk tsk, thinking of the once glorious Top Scholar, the Prince Consort appointed by the late emperor, who turned out to be such a lecherous scoundrel!","It was truly eye-opening, leaving people at a loss for words.","One had to say, the Carefree Young Master's title was truly fitting, \"Two-faced Scholar Dies Under Flowers\". Indeed, one face in public, another in private!","Of course, now he was just short of dying...","And then, the Ministry of Justice and the Court of Judicial Review announced more news: it turned out that the person who had instigated the students to cause trouble in front of the Imperial Academy's notice board was also Zhao Chengwen.","His family had committed evil first and then suffered the consequences, yet he harbored resentment towards the Household of the Earl of Loyalty and Righteousness. That's why he spread rumors and caused trouble, attempting to make Li Tianrui lose his qualification to study at the Imperial Academy.","When the news came out, everyone spat on him in disgust.","To commit evil first and then attempt to harm others is truly wicked behavior that must be severely punished by the law.","On this day in court, faced with the passionate outrage of his ministers, the emperor issued an edict on the spot: Zhao Chengwen, for trafficking humans in Jiangnan and disrupting the Imperial Academy examinations, was to be stripped of his position as imperial son-in-law, thrown into the imperial prison, and executed after autumn. His father, the Marquis of Wuyang, for failing to properly raise his son, was stripped of his title, and the entire family was to be exiled to the border regions.","Perhaps due to this shock, Consort Ning, who had been injured at the hot springs imperial palace previously, suddenly took a turn for the worse and passed away within a few days.","In the blink of an eye, an entire noble household vanished from public view.","Everyone couldn't help but sigh—","\"Those who enjoy good fortune must pay a price accordingly.\"","\"Marrying a princess and still wanting to open a harem? Isn't that like pulling whiskers from a tiger's mouth?\"","\"They got what they deserved!\"","With Consort Ning's death, there were even fewer people left in the imperial harem.","However, the Empress Dowager still did not favor her niece Consort Zhou, and refused to summon her again no matter what.","Instead, her attitude towards Yanshu seemed somewhat different than before.","The day Yanshu fainted at the sight of blood, the Empress Dowager even sent some precious medicinal ingredients to Ganlu Palace.","This made Yanshu feel both flattered and frightened. Bound by etiquette and rules, she had no choice but to go to the Palace of Benevolent Peace again to express her gratitude.","It was morning, and Zhang Shengkang, the head of the Imperial Hospital, had just finished checking the Empress Dowager's pulse for her well-being.","So when Yanshu entered the hall, she immediately spotted him.","She remained composed and first bowed to the Empress Dowager, saying, \"Thank you for your kindness, Your Majesty. I have recovered now, please do not worry.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"This is the first time I've heard of someone fainting at the sight of blood. It must not be easy for you.\"","She then asked Zhang Shengkang, \"Is there any way to cure this condition?\"","Zhang Shengkang bowed and replied, \"Your Majesty, fainting at the sight of blood is actually a psychological issue. Medication cannot completely cure it.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and sighed to Yanshu, \"You poor thing. From now on, you should avoid bloody scenes as much as possible.\"","Yanshu agreed.","Then she heard the Empress Dowager say, \"By the way, I heard you also have an allergy to peach blossoms? This year, before the peach blossoms bloomed, His Majesty had all the peach trees in the palace replaced with other trees.\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"His Majesty's love is truly overwhelming, making me feel ashamed. I have indeed been allergic to peach blossoms since childhood.\"","The Empress Dowager continued, \"Why don't you let Doctor Zhang examine you and see if there's any solution?\"","Yanshu paused.","Let Zhang Shengkang check her pulse again?","Goodness, was this some kind of impromptu medical examination?","She became wary and hurriedly said, \"Thank you, Your Majesty, but my peach blossom allergy has already improved significantly. There's no need to trouble Doctor Zhang.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhang Shengkang immediately said with surprise, \"To my knowledge, peach blossom allergy is a stubborn condition that doesn't easily improve. May I ask how Consort Yi managed to recover?\"","Yanshu secretly rolled her eyes.","—Zhang Shengkang was not a good person, she knew that.","So, if she told him that another imperial doctor had cured her illness, would he become jealous and harm that doctor?","She therefore lied, \"Actually, it was a prescription my parents brought from our hometown. They said they got it from a traveling doctor. After taking it, I indeed felt much better.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager looked surprised, \"There are such skilled traveling doctors?\"","Zhang Shengkang smiled and said, \"There are indeed hidden talents among the common people, truly not to be underestimated.\"","He appeared so humble, completely unlike someone who had once ungratefully caused his master's death.","However, at that moment, Yanshu heard the system say, [Well done! That Doctor Jiang owes you a favor now.]","Huh?","Yanshu didn't quite understand, [What do you mean? Would Zhang Shengkang really harm someone out of jealousy?]","The system replied, [It's not exactly jealousy, but Jiang Nianqi and Zhang Shengkang were actually enemies to begin with.]","Enemies?","Yanshu was even more confused, [What do you mean by that?]","The system explained, [The master that Zhang Shengkang angered to death years ago was none other than Jiang Nianqi's father. This is a blood feud!]","What?","Yanshu was stunned, [Jiang Nianqi's father was Zhang Shengkang's master? You mean the legendary doctor Xun Ji?]","The system confirmed, [That's absolutely correct. Xun Ji had only this one son, no doubt about it. His real name is Xun Lan, Jiang is his mother's surname.]","Yanshu suddenly realized—","If you remove the \"water\" radical from the character \"Ji\", doesn't it become \"Qi\"?","So he was called \"Nianqi\" to commemorate his father!","[But he's been in the Imperial Hospital for some time now, hasn't he? How has Zhang Shengkang not discovered this?]","The system explained, [Well, Zhang Shengkang is the head of the hospital, he's usually busy with many affairs. Xun Lan has always been just a regular doctor, so the two hardly ever cross paths. Moreover, after his father's death, Xun Lan began planning his revenge. He's undergone bone reshaping and facial reconstruction over the years, so he no longer looks like his former self.]","Bone reshaping and facial reconstruction?","Yanshu was shocked, [There's such advanced medical skill?]","The system said, [Well, he is the son of a legendary doctor after all, of course he's quite capable.]","Yanshu exclaimed inwardly, if she could learn this skill, it would be incredibly profitable!","The market prospects were quite broad indeed!!!","As she was marveling at this, she heard the Empress Dowager say, \"I have no more business here, you may all return now.\"","Yanshu agreed and took her leave from the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","However, upon returning to Ganlu Palace, her mind was still on the matter from earlier—","Since Jiang Nianqi was the son of a legendary doctor, and his medical skills were so advanced...","She quickly called out to the system, [Can Jiang Nianqi treat impotence? Can he cure the emperor?]","The system replied, [That's hard to say. This system is only responsible for providing information about events that have already occurred. I can't predict things that haven't happened yet.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Although the system couldn't guarantee anything, she still felt there might be a possibility, after all, the legendary doctor Xun Ji had been a specialist in treating infertility.","So perhaps Jiang Nianqi could do it too.","However, the system interjected, [The problem now is—how can he treat the emperor?]","Yanshu: \"...\"","That's true, tsk.","The emperor had always strictly guarded his secret, never allowing the palace doctors to examine him. How would he easily allow Jiang Nianqi, a mere imperial doctor, to examine him?","Most importantly, how could she let the emperor know that Doctor Jiang was the disciple of a legendary doctor and might be able to cure his condition?","Write a story?","This seemed to be the only feasible option, but there was still one problem—","What if Doctor Jiang couldn't cure the emperor?","Would the emperor kill him to silence him?","If that happened, wouldn't she indirectly cause the death of a skilled doctor?","...","While Yanshu was lost in deep thought and difficult decisions in Ganlu Palace, Yuwen Lan was completely unaware, listening to his ministers' reports in the imperial study.","With the second batch of new students already enrolled in the Imperial Academy, it was time to prepare for the third round of examinations.","Today, Yan Zhengping, the Chancellor of the Imperial Academy, and Zou Mozhong, the Hanlin Academy scholar, among others, were here to report the plan for the third round of examinations to him.","After hearing the report, he nodded and said, \"This time, we must strictly examine the qualifications of the candidates. What happened last time must not occur again.\"","Everyone quickly agreed in unison.","Seeing that the important matters had been reported, the others took their leave from the imperial study, but Zou Mozhong lingered for a moment.","When there was no one else in the room, he asked, \"Your Majesty, has the Carefree Young Master produced any new works recently? It's been several days since the last book 'The Two-Faced Scholar', and the booksellers have been urging for more.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"Don't they have any other books to publish?\"","Why are they rushing so urgently, not even allowing people to rest for a few days?","However, he heard Zou Mozhong say, \"There are indeed other books, and recently some people have been deliberately imitating the Carefree Young Master's style in their writing. However, they have the form but not the essence, falling far short. Readers aren't buying it.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow.","That's true, after all, Yanshu's stories all had real-life prototypes, and each one was shocking and tongue-wagging.","He said, \"I'll ask her about it later.\"","Zou Mozhong agreed and also took his leave.","Yuwen Lan busied himself in the imperial study for a while longer, then after a simple dinner, he got up and left.","Dusk was falling, and the palace lanterns were just being lit.","When the emperor arrived at Ganlu Palace, the palace servants were just clearing away the bowls and dishes.","Yuwen Lan glanced at them and noticed that a lot of food was left over, which he found strange.","So he asked Yanshu, \"Did you not have much appetite today?\"","She smiled and said, \"I ate too much at lunch, so I didn't feel like eating much for dinner.\"","However, in her heart, she sighed, [Oh emperor, emperor, you are a wise ruler, please don't kill innocent people!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Kill innocent people?","What did she mean by that?","Had something happened today that he didn't know about?","He sat down calmly on the warm couch and asked, \"What have you been doing today?\"","She replied, \"This humble consort hasn't done much, just eating, sleeping, and planning to write a new story.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and then asked, \"What kind of story is it this time?\"","As his words fell, he heard her pondering in her mind, [Should I show it to him? What if it gets someone killed?]","[But what if it could cure him? Wouldn't that be a waste?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Get someone killed? Waste for him?","What could this mean?","Just then, he heard her steeling herself, thinking, [Damn it, I'll take a gamble! If it works out, everyone will be happy. If it fails and he really wants to kill someone, I'll find a way to stop him. After all, he seems to be quite a reliable emperor so far, so he should be worth saving.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Reliable?","Was that meant as a compliment?","Just as he was thinking this, Yanshu spoke up, \"Actually, this story is something I've just started to conceptualize. Would Your Majesty like to hear it?\"","Yuwen Lan, whose curiosity was already piqued, naturally nodded and said, \"Yes, tell me.\"","Yanshu began, \"There was a young man from a family of physicians. His father was a renowned divine doctor, known far and wide for saving lives. The young man was naturally gifted but was somewhat playful in his youth. In contrast, his father's apprentice, who was also his senior, was steady and diligent. Because of this, the divine doctor often praised his apprentice but scolded his son.\"","\"The divine doctor was broad-minded and never treated his apprentice differently from his son. In fact, he taught his eager apprentice everything he knew, without any reservations, hoping that once the apprentice mastered the skills, he would follow in his footsteps to heal the world. However, he misjudged the person. This apprentice was actually someone who coveted power and status. Moreover, because the young son's talent surpassed his own, he had always been jealous, even suspecting that the master was withholding knowledge from him.\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","Divine doctor...","He thought of someone.","He heard her continue, \"After completing his apprenticeship, this person became a physician for a prominent family and quickly gained the favor of the family head with the medical skills taught by his master. However, as his master's skills were still superior to his own, he feared that his master might threaten his position. He devised a vicious plan, having people place a dead body outside his master's clinic and causing a commotion, falsely accusing his master of killing a patient. This forced the master to leave the capital, eliminating any future threats to his position.\"","By this point, Yuwen Lan was growing eager.","Indeed, he had already realized she was talking about Zhang Shengkang, the Chief Medical Officer.","After all, he had previously overheard from her thoughts about how Zhang Shengkang had ungratefully forced his master to his death.","For the first time, he was so anticipating her storyline that he hurriedly asked, \"What happened next?\"","He heard her say, \"The divine doctor had saved lives his entire life, yet he never imagined he would be ruined by the betrayal of his ungrateful apprentice. Filled with anger and indignation, he couldn't come to terms with it. The resentment festered in his heart, and not long after leaving the capital, he died coughing up blood.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan asked, \"What about the divine doctor's son? Did he remain unmoved seeing his father die in such anger?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Of course not. This story's protagonist is that young man. How could he remain unmoved?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and asked, \"Then where did this young man go? What did he do?\"","No one knew how eagerly he awaited her answer at that moment.","Ever since he had heard the news from her that day, he had sent people to search. Yet from winter to spring, and now almost summer, they had still found nothing.","Unexpectedly, she seemed to know.","At this moment, he stared intently at her cherry lips, almost holding his breath.","However, to his surprise, she said, \"Before I continue, Your Majesty must agree to one... no, two conditions for me.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","\"What conditions?\"","He frowned and said, \"You never did this before when showing me your stories.\"","This girl, was she deliberately teasing him?","But he saw her looking quite righteous as she said, \"That's because I'm different from before. The royalties from publishers have doubled. As the first person to hear the story, and from my own lips no less, naturally, there should be some... special conditions. In any case, Your Majesty can consider it as paying in advance. After all, it's not like you can't afford it.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What, pay?","He was her husband..."]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42","paragraphs":["What?","To continue listening, she had two conditions to be met?","And she even had such twisted reasoning?","Yuwen Lan found it inconceivable and was full of questions.","But there was no choice, as she was the only one who knew about this matter, and he was so anxious he could barely sit still.","Yuwen Lan had to say, \"What do you want Us to agree to?\"","This little money-grubber, could it be that she still wants money?","Unexpectedly, Yanshu smiled and said, \"Actually, it's very simple. First, I request that Your Majesty, regardless of the situation or circumstances in the future, never behead this humble servant, and spare this servant's life.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","With this, he became even more confused and couldn't help but hiss, saying, \"Why would you have such a condition? Do you think We would kill you?\"","Yanshu pouted and said, \"This servant is just taking precautions. This servant doesn't know if there will be a day when something angers Your Majesty, so it's better to ask for a golden token of immunity first.\"","In her heart, she thought, [Tsk, if you knew that I know your secret, wouldn't you want to kill me?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He finally understood.","...And felt a bit guilty.","Ahem, to be honest, when he first realized she had discovered his secret, he did have thoughts of killing her.","But, after knowing she wasn't a spy or an informant, and had no malicious intentions, he had cast that thought aside.","How could he bear to kill someone as adorable as her?","Seeing that he didn't immediately respond, Yanshu felt anxious and urgently asked, \"What's wrong? Does Your Majesty refuse to agree?\"","Damn it, after accompanying him for so long, does he still want to kill her?","Fortunately, at this moment, he finally spoke, \"Of course We can agree to this, and from now on, you need not worry about such things.\"","After a pause, he looked at her seriously and said, \"You are different from others. Never doubt Us again.\"","Hearing these words, Yanshu was stunned for a moment.","He said \"she was different from others\"... what did that mean?","Was he referring to her ability to write stories?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How could she still not understand?","But before he could say anything more, he heard her think, [Whatever, at least my life is safe!]","So she continued, \"This servant thanks Your Majesty for your great kindness. However, this servant has a second condition.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment, \"Let's hear it.\"","He probably thought she wanted money again.","But unexpectedly, he heard her say, \"This servant requests that Your Majesty be a wise ruler and never kill innocent people indiscriminately. Some people are truly useful to the common people and the state. Please, Your Majesty, do not kill them because of momentary anger or pleasure.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","After a moment, he began to understand that she was probably speaking on behalf of Xun Ji's son.","She was afraid he would kill to silence people.","Silly girl, if he found this person, he could completely disguise himself as a commoner to seek treatment, just as he had done in the past when seeking medical help.","With a bit of disguise, no one would know he was the emperor, so even if he went and gained nothing, he had never killed anyone because of it.","He smiled and said, \"Of course We are a wise ruler. You need not worry about this. We promise you. Now, can you continue with your story?\"","Only then did Yanshu feel relieved and continued, \"After his father passed away, the young man matured overnight, restrained his temperament, and began to plan revenge for his father. But that ungrateful enemy had already been favored by the master and gained some power, so if the young man wanted revenge, he had to plan meticulously.\"","\"First, he diligently studied medicine, carefully exploring and learning all the medical books and case files left by his father. Given his innate intelligence and his father's subtle influence, this wasn't a problem.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan thought that this meant Xun Ji's son now had medical skills comparable to his father's?","This was good news.","He then heard her say, \"At the same time, the young man began to use bone-setting techniques to change his appearance.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly again.","—So he had already changed his appearance, no wonder the people he sent out couldn't find any clues.","\"Then what?\" he asked.","The most important thing was where this person was now.","But he heard her say, \"Then, the young man also entered the mansion where his enemy was and became a house physician.\"","What?","Yuwen Lan was stunned.","Did this mean... the person he was looking for was in the palace?","He tried asking, \"This person also entered the enemy's mansion?\"","She nodded and said, \"That's right, it was the only way.\"","It seemed he hadn't misheard.","But who exactly was it?","Yuwen Lan then asked, \"So after he entered the mansion, did he meet his enemy? With his medical skills, wasn't he quickly recognized by the master?\"","Yanshu said, \"...Not really. This person was too straightforward, and the relationships in that large mansion were complex. There were many house physicians, and he didn't quite understand social niceties, so even after entering the mansion for several years, the master still didn't know of his existence.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan began to ponder—","Entered the mansion for several years?","...There were dozens of people in the Imperial Medical Academy, and he indeed didn't know many of them.","So he couldn't judge who it might be.","\"But,\" she suddenly said, \"as luck would have it, the master had a beautiful woman who was intelligent as ice and snow, with a heart as pure as orchids, well-versed in etiquette, and exceptionally talented.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","At a time like this, she still didn't forget to praise herself...","He suppressed his smile and nodded, saying, \"To have such a beauty is truly the master's fortune.\"","Yanshu nodded seriously, \"Indeed, the master must have saved the world in his previous life for heaven to send such a beauty to his side.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He continued to suppress his laughter and asked, \"What does this beauty have to do with the matter?\"","He heard her say, \"As it happens, heaven was unkind, and this flawless beauty was born with a stubborn ailment that couldn't be improved despite years of seeking medical treatment. By chance, this person went to treat the beauty and miraculously cured her.\"","\"The beauty, with her discerning eye, recommended him to the master, and from then on, the young man finally gained the master's recognition.\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","Beauty, stubborn ailment?","Could it be...","Just then, he heard her mind shout, [Do you understand? This person is Jiang Nianqi! Jiang Nianqi is Xun Ji's son, Xun Lan!!! He might be able to cure your illness!!!]","Yuwen Lan's heart skipped a beat.","It was indeed that Jiang Nianqi, the one who had cured her peach blossom incompatibility.","He never expected it would be him!","At this moment, Yuwen Lan finally realized why she had insisted on asking for this person's immunity earlier...","Indeed, if this person were outside the palace, he could easily visit in disguise.","However, this person happened to be a palace physician, and one he knew.","If he were to seek treatment, wouldn't his identity be exposed?","Of course, there were still ways around it.","...","At this time, seeing his contemplative expression, Yanshu was also pondering in her heart, wondering if he had understood.","It would be good if he did. After all, Jiang Nianqi's father, Xun Ji, was once a miracle doctor for infertility, so there was great hope for Jiang Nianqi too!","The most important thing now was to ensure that Jiang Nianqi wouldn't be silenced if he couldn't cure the illness.","Of course, Yanshu thought she was quite clever. Throughout the story, she hadn't revealed that the beauty knew the master's secret, so she should be safe, hehe.","Yuwen Lan was brought back to reality by this \"hehe.\"","He glanced at her and deliberately said, \"In that case, it seems the master should thank the beauty for discovering this miracle doctor. In the future, if there are any tricky illnesses, they can be treated.\"","Tricky illnesses?","Yanshu raised an eyebrow secretly. Could he be referring to himself?","It seemed he had truly understood!","She quickly nodded and said, \"Yes, having such a miracle doctor is like having a treasure. The master is a wise person and will surely treat him well.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of agreement.","Finally, she had praised him too, which was more like it.","He then asked, \"So what happened next? What kind of ending do you plan to give him?\"","But he heard her say, \"Later, under the master's justice, the young man avenged his family, cleared his father's name, and even opened a medical clinic in the capital. He took on many apprentices and, like his father, devoted himself to healing and benefiting the people. As for that ungrateful villain, he got his just deserts, became infamous, and lost everything.\"","\"That's the end of this servant's story.\"","Yanshu coughed and said, \"It's getting late. This servant will go take a bath now. Please wait a moment, Your Majesty.\"","[Tsk tsk, now the time is yours to decide. Whether to treat it or not, think it over yourself. But no matter what, you can't kill anyone!]","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Go ahead.\"","He watched as she entered the washroom.","Of course he had to treat it.","He was the emperor, and needed heirs.","Moreover, he wanted to experience the pleasures of the world with this \"clever as ice and snow\" beauty that he had not yet tasted.","— Ahem, although his body had improved somewhat since sharing a bed with her, it was always before dawn, when he was unconscious.","Once he was awake, whenever he wanted to be intimate with her, he still couldn't.","Fortunately, there was finally hope again now.","Taking advantage of this moment, Yuwen Lan immediately got up and went outside the hall to summon an Imperial Guard, saying, \"Investigate that royal physician named Jiang Nianqi from the Imperial Hospital - when he is on duty each month, when he is on leave, and his address outside the palace.\"","The Imperial Guard acknowledged and went to carry out the order immediately.","The next day, it happened to be his day off, and the royal physician Jiang Nianqi, also known as Xun Lan, was rarely at home outside the palace.","— In recent years, he had changed his name and left his hometown to study medicine in various places. As a result, he married late, only settling down after coming to the capital and passing the exam to enter the Imperial Hospital. His youngest son was only five years old now.","Fortunately, his wife was virtuous and his young son was obedient. At this moment, he was teaching the little one to write when he heard someone calling from outside, \"Is Dr. Jiang at home?\"","Knowing his medical skills were good, usually neighbors would come to see him if they had any aches or pains, and he never refused. So when he heard the inquiry, he put down his pen and came out.","However, he saw that the visitors were not neighbors, but two men.","One of them was wearing a blue brocade robe, tall in stature, with a dark veil on his head, looking like a master.","Before he could inquire, the attendant spoke, \"We've heard that the doctor's medical skills are excellent. My master would like to ask the doctor to examine an illness. If you can cure my master, the consultation fee can be doubled.\"","Jiang Nianqi looked them over and said, \"If I can treat it, I will naturally cure it. There's no need to mention doubling the fee. Some illnesses can't be cured even if you double the fee.\"","Hearing this, the attendant paused.","The veiled man raised his hand and said, \"Thank you for your trouble, doctor. I have sought treatment in several places without success. Hearing that your medical skills are excellent, I came specially to seek a consultation.\"","At this time, Yuwen Lan had deliberately changed his voice, so the other party did not notice anything unusual, and only said, \"Follow me.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and followed him into the courtyard.","The Jiang residence had a study where Jiang Nianqi usually examined patients.","Yuwen Lan followed him into the room and sat down, then extended his hand for the other to take his pulse.","After a moment, before he could speak, he heard the other ask, \"Sir, do you have difficulties in the bedroom?\"","Yuwen Lan's heart steadied, and he said, \"Yes.\"","It seemed Yanshu was not wrong; this man indeed had some skill.","He heard the other ask again, \"How long has this problem been occurring?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Three years.\"","The other nodded and asked, \"To what degree of difficulty?\"","Yuwen Lan was a bit uncomfortable, coughed and then said, \"There's morning arousal when I wake up... but whenever I want to be intimate with a woman... it doesn't work.\"","The other remained calm, nodded, and asked, \"Have you ever suffered any external injuries, sir?\"","Yuwen Lan said no.","He was very certain that it had suddenly stopped working without any warning signs.","The other asked again, \"Then, is everything else normal with your body?\"","Yuwen Lan made an affirmative sound, \"I am in good health, with only this one symptom.\"","The royal physician then asked him, \"Do you usually take any medications, sir?\"","Yuwen Lan again said with certainty, \"No, I rarely get sick and have hardly ever taken any medicine.\"","After saying this, he really couldn't wait any longer and actively asked, \"Does the doctor think it can be treated?\"","But he saw the other withdraw his hand from taking the pulse and say, \"The problem is a bit complex. It can be treated, but it's rather troublesome.\"","Troublesome?","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"How troublesome?\"","But he heard the other say, \"From your pulse, there's something in your body suppressing your yang energy, which is affecting that area. If you haven't taken any medication, then you've probably been poisoned.\"","Poisoned?","Yuwen Lan's brow furrowed.","He had been poisoned?","But why had he never noticed?","He thought for a moment and asked, \"Can the doctor cure this poison?\"","But he saw Jiang Nianqi nod, \"It's possible, but first you need to stay away from the poison's influence, expel the accumulated toxins from your body, then take medicine to recover, and only then can you return to normal.\"","\"But do you know how this poison entered your body, sir?\"","Yuwen Lan was momentarily speechless.","He had been carefully thinking back, but the Imperial Kitchen was his people, and those close to him in Qianming Palace were all his people. There shouldn't have been any opportunity for someone to poison his food and drink.","Perhaps seeing his confusion, Jiang Nianqi voluntarily explained, \"Poison doesn't necessarily enter through the mouth. You can be poisoned through bathing or incense, or even by smelling the scent of certain medicines for a long time.\"","Yuwen Lan's brow furrowed.","...","After seeing the doctor outside the palace, Yuwen Lan returned to the palace and went directly to Ganlu Palace.","Jiang Nianqi had just prescribed medicine for him, which he needed to drink daily for five days.","However, he couldn't drink the medicine in Qianming Palace.","Once the smell of medicinal soup wafted out from Qianming Palace, it would be discovered by the ministers, causing speculation and panic, and even alerting the culprit.","So, he could only come here.","Yanshu was actually waiting for him too.","Today she had already learned from the system that he had gone to see Jiang Nianqi for treatment, but she didn't know how it went or if there was any hope.","So she had done nothing for most of the day, just waiting for him.","Now, hearing the announcement of his arrival, she immediately went to the door to welcome him, \"This concubine respectfully welcomes Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan made an affirmative sound, told her to dispense with formalities, and walked a few steps to sit on the warm couch, looking as if he had something to say.","Yanshu, very perceptively, sent all the unnecessary people away.","Yuwen Lan then spoke, \"I'm feeling a bit unwell. I went out of the palace to see a doctor today and brought back some medicine, but I'm afraid others might overthink things, so I can only come to your place to brew it.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu's eyes lit up —","He got medicine? That means it can be treated!","Great, no need to worry about him killing anyone now!","So she quickly nodded, \"This concubine understands. This concubine will tell others that it's this concubine who is unwell and needs to drink medicine. Your Majesty can feel at ease to come and drink it.\"","Yuwen Lan said \"Good,\" feeling warmth in his heart.","But then he heard her think, [Alright, Emperor, considering you've been decent to me, I won't charge you for brewing the medicine this time.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","The way she put it, was she originally planning to charge him?","After a pause, he said again, \"There's one more thing. From now on, I'll be staying here with you.\"","At these words, Yanshu was stunned, \"What does Your Majesty mean by this?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"From now on, except for going to the study and attending court, I will spend all other time here.\"","— He had been thinking all the way back about who had poisoned him and how he had been poisoned.","Since the time he ascended the throne, all those who coveted the throne had been dealt with by him, and all those close to him had been replaced with his own people.","Those women in the harem couldn't have done such a thing, especially since he had the ability to read minds.","He had also thought about the Empress Dowager, but... for so long, he had never detected anything unusual in her thoughts.","Because of her private feelings for the Zhou family, the Empress Dowager even very much hoped that he would favor Consort Zhou, allowing her to give birth to an heir to secure her position.","Therefore, he really couldn't think of who the culprit might be.","But regarding how the poison entered his body, he did have some guesses —","Previously, when sleeping in Qianming Palace, he had no dreams and his body was lethargic; but since coming to Ganlu Palace, not only did he have dreams, but morning arousal had also appeared.","At first, he thought it was because Yanshu had some special ability.","But now it seemed that there might be a problem with the bedchamber in Qianming Palace.","So he planned to have people thoroughly investigate the bedchamber.","And before discovering the problem, he would stay in Ganlu Palace.","However, this would also provide an opportunity to spend more time with her.","He thought she would be very happy.","But unexpectedly, he heard her think, [Oh no, doesn't this mean I'll have no privacy anymore? Suffocating!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Suffocating?","Before he could frown, he heard her suddenly have another thought, [But this way, won't the chances of getting imperial meals increase? Okay, I guess it's barely acceptable then.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","If he had no money, no imperial meals, would she still love him?","Thus, from this day on, Ganlu Palace began brewing medicine.","Yanshu only told others that she had caught a cold and was taking medicine, so no one suspected anything about the Emperor.","Since the Emperor often stayed overnight here, outsiders simply assumed that Yanshu was increasingly favored.","Five days passed like this, and Yuwen Lan was due for another check-up.","On this evening, seeing him change into clothes he wore when leaving the palace, Yanshu immediately asked, \"Is Your Majesty going to see the doctor?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of agreement.","But then he heard her say, \"I have something to say, but I'm not sure if I should.\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"What is it?\"","Yanshu smiled sincerely and said, \"Although Your Majesty is well-prepared, there are so many people in the palace. We can't guarantee that someone sharp-eyed won't notice you leaving and cause some trouble. If the outside world learns that Your Majesty is leaving the palace to see a doctor, wouldn't that be problematic?\"","Yuwen Lan sensed she had more to say, so he asked, \"Then what do you suggest?\"","She immediately replied, \"Why don't I accompany Your Majesty out of the palace? This way, if anyone discovers us, Your Majesty can put the blame on me, saying that I wasn't feeling well and needed to see a doctor outside the palace. After all, Ganlu Palace has been brewing medicine these days.\"","At first glance, this seemed quite reasonable.","However, immediately after, Yuwen Lan heard her think, [I still haven't eaten the roast lamb and baked flatbread from Tianjing Lane last time! And just thinking about the wonton from that shop makes my mouth water!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He thought, why is she suddenly so considerate?","It turns out it's still about food.","So he said, \"I'm only going to see the doctor, not anywhere else.\"","But she replied, \"I understand. I'll just wait in the carriage for you. We'll return as soon as you finish seeing the doctor.\"","In her heart, she grumbled, [Sure enough, he's forgotten what he said last time! Hmph, if I had known this, I should have insisted on eating at least two flatbreads that night! Does he think I don't know that the Jiang family is near Tianjing Lane? Let's go there first and then decide!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She's actually this angry?","If he doesn't let her go, wouldn't he become a scumbag?","Well, he did make a promise before, so he had to say, \"Alright, since there's nothing important tonight, let's go together.\"","Yanshu was overjoyed, immediately smiling from ear to ear as she agreed and hurried to change her clothes. They then boarded the carriage together.","Soon, they arrived at their destination.","Yuwen Lan still wore a veil as he got off the carriage, while Yanshu waited in the carriage.","She kept wondering in her heart whether the medicine was effective.","After a while, she saw him return to the carriage, seemingly in a good mood.","Yanshu thought, it seems the condition has improved!","Yuwen Lan heard this in his mind and thought indeed it was not bad—","Just now, after Doctor Jiang's diagnosis, more than half of the poison in his body had been eliminated.","This meant that his previous judgment was correct; the poison was in the bedchamber.","During these five days, he had already ordered people to investigate the bedchamber, but perhaps due to limited abilities, neither the Imperial Guard nor the Inner Court Supervisory Office had found anything.","Regarding this, he could only wait until he recovered and find a way to have this Doctor Jiang personally inspect it.","However, at the current rate, he would likely return to normal in about ten more days.","Because he was in such a good mood, he generously said, \"This place is not far from Tianjing Lane. I'll take you to eat the roast lamb and baked flatbread from last time.\"","Oh, isn't this exactly what she was thinking?","Yanshu's eyes lit up, \"Thank you, husband!\"","Yuwen Lan smiled and pinched her cheek, then instructed the coachman, \"Go to Tianjing Lane.\"","The coachman acknowledged and was about to turn the horse around to set off.","However, at this moment, they heard a shrill cry, \"A-Bao! Give me back my A-Bao!\"","The two inside the carriage were startled.","Yanshu carefully lifted the carriage curtain and saw a woman running and shouting, her face covered in tears.","Yuwen Lan asked those outside, \"What's happening?\"","Immediately, a secret guard replied, \"Someone has snatched that woman's child.\"","Snatching a child in broad daylight?","Yanshu immediately widened her eyes, \"How could this happen?\"","Yuwen Lan also ordered the secret guard, \"Go after them.\"","The secret guard acknowledged and immediately headed in the direction the woman was running.","About the time it takes to drink a cup of tea later, the secret guard returned carrying a four or five-year-old boy and handed him back to the woman.","The woman, hugging her child, cried loudly, thanked the secret guard, and quickly returned home.","When the surroundings quieted down, Yuwen Lan asked the secret guard again, \"What happened?\"","The secret guard reported quietly, \"There were about three of them. One person blocked the woman, while two took the child. They got onto a pre-prepared carriage and sped towards the south of the city. But these three people had good martial skills, unlike ordinary people or traffickers.\"","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment and ordered, \"Go to the Capital Official to see if there have been similar cases recently.\"","The secret guard acknowledged and went to the Capital Official.","After this incident, Yanshu no longer had the appetite to eat and returned to the palace with lingering fear.","After returning to Ganlu Palace, not long after, the person who went to the Capital Official came back to report to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, according to the Capital Official's records, there have been nearly six or seven cases of missing children recently. There are also four or five cases in various parts of the capital region, all involving missing boys.\"","This wasn't surprising. In the current society where male children are favored over female ones, many child traffickers target boys because they can fetch a good price.","However, the secret guard had just said that these people's martial skills didn't seem like those of traffickers.","As Yanshu was pondering this, she heard the system ding and say, [There's some gossip. Remember Chai Weizhong, the Vice Minister of the Ministry of War?]","Yanshu quickly replied, [Yes, isn't he that bearded scumbag who deceived women into marriage?]","The system said, [That's right. Tonight's child abduction case is related to him.]"]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43: 《043》","paragraphs":["In a short period of time, over ten cases of missing children occurred near the capital, and surprisingly, they were all boys.","If Yuwen Lan hadn't witnessed it himself today, he would have been completely unaware of the situation.","Upon hearing the guard's report, he immediately summoned officials from the Capital Office, the Ministry of Punishment, and the Ministry of Justice to the palace. He also went to Qianming Palace himself.","Meanwhile, Yanshu quickly consulted her system—","[You say that Chai Weizhong, the Vice Minister of War, is involved in this? Are you telling me he kidnapped all these children? What is that scoundrel up to?]","System: [Actually, he's not the one who kidnapped them. It's one of his recent lovers, called Hu Yichun.]","Hu Yichun?","Yanshu frowned. [Who is this person? Is he also an official?]","System: [This person has quite a story. Hu Yichun was originally an actor who became the male favorite of Prince Yuwen Hu of Shu.]","Hearing this, Yanshu's eyes widened. [Isn't Prince Yuwen Hu of Shu the emperor's third uncle's cousin? He's also into men?]","System: [To be precise, he swings both ways.]","Yanshu: [...]","Indeed, the royal family has always been full of eccentrics...","What the hell, are they so bored they need to swing both ways?","But then she wondered, [But didn't Yuwen Hu die three years ago for treason?]","System: [That's right. When Yuwen Hu died, all the people in his household were buried with him, but this Hu Yichun managed to escape. He knew that many officials and nobles had this preference, so to make a living, he returned to his old profession, mingling in gay circles in various places and attaching himself to the powerful. After accumulating some wealth, he made his way to the capital. Then he set his sights on Chai Weizhong.]","Yanshu clicked her tongue. [He certainly aimed high. Chai Weizhong is probably the highest-ranking official in the capital who's into men.]","System: [Exactly. If he was going to target someone, of course he'd go for someone with real power and a certain position in officialdom.]","But Yanshu remembered something else. [Wait a minute, isn't Chai Weizhong a bottom? This Hu Yichun served the Prince of Shu, so he must be a bottom too. How could they get together?]","System: [You think Hu Yichun mingles in these circles for true love? He's after power and money. Changing his persona is nothing to him. Chai Weizhong is getting on in years, and only this man has him wrapped around his finger.]","Yanshu: [...That's actually quite inspiring in a way. But if Chai Weizhong has money and power, why is he kidnapping children?]","System: [Sister, you're still too naive. Hu Yichun was once the Prince of Shu's favorite. How could he be satisfied with just a Vice Minister of War? He's only using Chai Weizhong's power to do bigger business in the capital.]","Business?","Yanshu thought for a moment, then suddenly froze. [...Don't tell me he plans to turn the kidnapped children into catamites to sell to perverts?]","System: [Correct. That's exactly what he intends to do. He first scouts for good-looking boys in and around the capital, then kidnaps or abducts them to train as catamites. Then he sells them to rich perverts all over the country for their pleasure, to make a profit.]","Hearing this, Yanshu almost cursed out loud. [That despicable, perverted scum!!! He deserves to rot in the deepest pits of hell!!!]","After cursing, she still had questions.","[But why is he kidnapping children from the capital? The capital is right under the emperor's nose, with much better security than other places. He could easily get caught, couldn't he?]","System: [Because this person has set up a special training facility in the capital. It's more secure to bring the kidnapped children directly there for training than to transport them from elsewhere. Moreover, in their perverted circles, catamites sold from the capital fetch a higher price than those from other places.]","Yanshu still didn't understand. [Why are they more expensive?]","System: [Because many people like the capital accent. This guy has mingled in various places and knows too much.]","...They even care about the capital accent???","Yanshu cursed again at the perverted scum.","Every single pervert in that circle deserves to be cut into a thousand pieces!","After cursing, she asked again, [But Chai Weizhong has kept catamites before, and they were all purchased. Why can't this guy just buy them instead of stealing and kidnapping? Isn't he afraid of getting caught?]","System: [He's running a business and needs to consider costs. How could buying be as profitable as kidnapping? Besides, with Chai Weizhong covering for him, he's feeling quite bold.]","Yanshu gritted her teeth and said, [Chai Weizhong, that marriage-fraud scumbag!]","—When she wrote that novel back then, she originally wanted to expose this man. However, in the current society, homosexuality wasn't illegal, and even keeping catamites was tacitly allowed. She couldn't really touch him with just a novel, so she had put it aside.","She never expected this scumbag would help his perverted lover do such disgusting things!","Damn, it's so infuriating!!!","But after her anger subsided, she tensed up again and asked, [So all those children who went missing before were stolen by this Hu Yichun?]","System: [That's right. Since the emperor ascended the throne, the capital's security has improved a lot, and you rarely see child traffickers. Of course it's this guy's doing.]","Yanshu's heart tightened. Doesn't this mean that those children are about to face a tragic fate?!","No, she had to tell the emperor quickly so he could arrest them!","Thinking this, she immediately left Ganlu Palace and headed straight for Qianming Palace.","Yanshu ran so fast that even Renwinter couldn't keep up with her. When she arrived at Qianming Palace, she ran into Yuwen Lan coming out, followed by several officials from the Ministry of Punishment, the Ministry of Justice, and the Capital Office.","\"Your Majesty...\"","She was too rushed to care about anything else and called out breathlessly.","Seeing her like this, Yuwen Lan thought something had happened to her and stepped forward to ask, \"What's wrong? Why are you in such a hurry?\"","The officials behind him also looked on curiously.","Yanshu caught her breath and thought about how to phrase it, then said, \"This concubine is just concerned about those missing children. How are they? Do the gentlemen have any strategies?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"We have ordered the three departments to investigate together. Based on the reports to the Capital Office so far, it seems to be the work of the same group of people.\"","Hearing this, the Prefect of the Capital Office quickly volunteered, \"Since that group headed south of the city tonight, we believe their lair should be in the southern part of the city. I will dispatch officers to search there immediately.\"","Yanshu nodded and said, \"The gentleman's words make sense, but I think, since this group has already committed over a dozen cases, they must be very cunning. After their failure today, they might become alert and move to a different location.\"","In her heart, she urgently thought, [That Hu Yichun has Chai Weizhong as his informant. Seeing the emperor urgently summon these officials, he would have sensed something was wrong and already moved to Lihua Lane in the east!]","Yuwen Lan took this to heart and paused.","Chai Weizhong is the informant?","This matter is related to Chai Weizhong?","It seems she knows about this and rushed here to warn him.","So he said, \"Yipin's words are reasonable. Let's expand the search area and investigate the residences in the eastern part of the city as well. Remember, we can't alert them, and not a word of this should leak out. Anyone who violates this order will be executed.\"","Hearing this, the group immediately bowed their heads in agreement, all looking very solemn.","They then heard the emperor add, \"The key now is to find the missing children, and we must ensure their safety.\"","The group hurriedly agreed again, and seeing that the emperor had no further instructions, they quickly left the palace to carry out their tasks.","After returning to Ganlu Palace, Yuwen Lan asked Yanshu, \"Your analysis just now was very reasonable. Besides that, have you noticed anything else suspicious?\"","—He knew her abilities were powerful, and now he wanted to get more useful information to find the missing children and catch the culprits as quickly as possible.","Of course, normally she might write a novel to hint at him, but tonight time was of the essence, and there was no time to write a novel.","This was truly a meeting of minds, as Yanshu was also thinking about how to tell him about this matter.","Writing a novel was out of the question, firstly because there wasn't enough time, and secondly because the case had just happened, and they were in the midst of a vigorous investigation. If she were to write it out now, the emperor would surely suspect her.","So, she could only try to guide him.","She said, \"This concubine was also thinking, usually those who kidnap children are ruffians and scoundrels without proper jobs, who steal other people's children to sell for a living, and they definitely act in secret. But tonight there were three of them, with a carriage, and they even dared to snatch a child in broad daylight. This shows they're not ordinary child traffickers. Perhaps... they don't simply intend to sell the stolen children for money.\"","Yuwen Lan had already thought of this point.","\"Indeed, those who snatch children in this manner are clearly not ordinary traffickers. I fear there might be some powerful force behind them.\"","He pondered silently, recalling that she had just mentioned Chai Weizhong. Could it be that Chai Weizhong was behind this?","At that moment, he heard her cursing angrily in her mind, [That damn pervert Hu Yichun! When I catch you, nothing short of being torn apart by five horses will satisfy my rage!!! And that wretched Chai Weizhong, it's bad enough that you're a deviant who tricked someone into marriage, but as an imperial official, how dare you act as a shield for that scumbag lover of yours who harms children!!! I'll definitely add more details to your story and publish it, ruining your reputation and making you suffer a thousand cuts, despised by all!!!]","Now, Yuwen Lan finally understood clearly.","She said Chai Weizhong was acting as a shield...","Meaning he was the power behind the culprit.","Then that name Chai Weizhong mentioned earlier...","Hu Yichun? He must be the main culprit.","But she referred to him as Chai Weizhong's \"lover.\"","He already knew Chai Weizhong was homosexual, so it seems this Hu person must also be a man.","He would have the Imperial Guard investigate shortly.","Just then, he heard her say, \"Your Majesty, do you remember that story I wrote before? The one about the scoundrel who liked men but deceived a woman into marrying him, bearing his children, and serving his parents?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"I remember.\"","Yanshu continued, \"I've read in stories that some wealthy people live such extravagant and decadent lives that they develop strange fetishes. Playing with women isn't enough for them, so they keep handsome young men for unspeakable acts. Even worse, some of them would take children who haven't grown up yet as their...\"","At this point, she feigned shock and said, \"Your Majesty, could it be that those people kidnapped little boys tonight for such purposes?\"","Inwardly, she urgently thought, [Do you understand? They're kidnapping little boys to raise them as catamites to sell! You must catch them!!!]","Yuwen Lan certainly understood.","Indeed, these people specifically targeting young boys made their purpose quite obvious.","And with Chai Weizhong's involvement...","He immediately said, \"I will order an investigation of such establishments in the capital.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Your Majesty is wise! That's exactly what I was thinking. We must act quickly, lest they catch wind of it and escape.\"","Yuwen Lan grunted in agreement and was about to rise to summon someone outside.","At that moment, he heard her sigh inwardly, [This is all I can do. If I say too much, he might suspect me. I hope they can find that Yingbin Pavilion in Jinshui Lane.]","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow.","— Jinshui Lane, Yingbin Pavilion, and that Hu Yichun.","He remembered it all.","Thanks to Yanshu's careful hints, the authorities searched the city all night. Early the next morning, good news arrived.","Seven children were found in a large mansion in Lihua Lane in the east of the city, all of whom were among those previously reported missing.","In addition, the officials arrested two men who were guarding the children.","However, after severe interrogation, these two only confessed that they were planning to sell the children to families in other regions who wanted boys. They did not admit to anything related to child prostitution.","On the surface, this seemed to be just a case of child trafficking...","In the early morning court session, after hearing reports from the Ministry of Punishment and the Ministry of Justice, the emperor asked, \"Do these missing children have any common characteristics?\"","The Vice Minister of Punishment replied, \"Your Majesty, apart from all being boys, they all have fairly handsome features and are all between four and five years old.\"","The emperor then said, \"If this were merely trafficking, how did they manage to find children of similar age and all with handsome features?\"","As his words fell, everyone began to ponder.","Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong said, \"Your Majesty's words are most astute. I believe these people are likely planning some nefarious activities.\"","— Tsk, there are so many shocking things these days. Didn't the former imperial son-in-law Zhao Chengwen set up a house in Jiangnan to trade women not long ago?","He continued, \"In the past, there have been cases of people kidnapping young girls to sell to brothels. Since these boys are of similar age and handsome... it's highly possible they are to be sold to some depraved individuals.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone was horrified by the implications and began to agree —","\"Lord Zou's words are spot on!\"","\"If this is true, what about the few children who haven't been found yet? Wouldn't they fall into the tiger's den? Please, Your Majesty, order continued searches!\"","\"If this is indeed the case, it's truly chilling. We implore Your Majesty to decree a thorough investigation!\"","\"We beseech Your Majesty to decree a thorough investigation!\"","...","Amidst the fervent crowd, the emperor nodded and said, \"Since ancient times, there have been those with homosexual preferences. If they do not harm others or violate laws, it is not our concern. However, if they harm the innocent and commit unforgivable crimes, I will punish them severely. The Ministry of Punishment, Ministry of Justice, and Capital Official shall continue this investigation, tracing all cases of missing children in recent years, regardless of gender. If any establishments or individuals are suspected of human trafficking, investigate thoroughly without leniency.\"","As his words fell, everyone responded in unison, praising the emperor's wisdom.","Yuwen Lan observed Chai Weizhong mixed among the crowd, also wearing a righteous expression.","He paid close attention and heard him think, [We really must lay low recently. Tell Spring Lad he absolutely must not come out.]","After the court session ended, Yuwen Lan had just left Qianming Palace when he saw the Imperial Guard coming to report.","\"Your Majesty, we went to Jinshui Lane and indeed found an inn called Yingbin Pavilion, but it was already empty. We didn't find any missing children or the man called Hu Yichun. However, we discovered that Chai Weizhong has been frequently visiting a martial arts school on Horse Market Street.\"","\"A martial arts school?\"","Yuwen Lan furrowed his brow.","The Imperial Guard confirmed, \"The owner of this martial arts school is none other than Hu Yichun.\"","Yuwen Lan immediately asked, \"Where is he?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"Since last night, this person suddenly disappeared, claiming to have returned to his hometown to visit relatives.\"","This was obviously an excuse.","Since last night, all city gates had been under strict control to catch the kidnappers. This person must still be in the city.","Yuwen Lan said, \"Continue searching for Hu Yichun, and arrange people to investigate this martial arts school and that Yingbin Pavilion. See what kind of people usually frequent these places.\"","After a pause, he added, \"Continue monitoring the Chai residence.\"","The Imperial Guard acknowledged the orders.","Meanwhile, in Ganlu Palace, Yanshu had just heard the news that Hu Yichun had escaped.","Damn it, this pervert is quite cunning!","No matter how many hints she gave the emperor, even pointing him in the right direction, this scumbag could sense trouble and flee immediately. It's clear he must have prepared many hideouts in the capital beforehand!","Not to mention having Chai Weizhong to tip him off.","This man had been an official for many years and had lackeys and informants everywhere.","With the enemy hidden and the authorities in plain sight, how could they match them!","Just then, she heard the system sigh, [This person has been through so many places after all. Even when the Prince of Shu's mansion was destroyed, he managed to escape. How could he be easily caught?]","Yanshu slammed the table, [No matter how cunning he is, we must bring him to justice, otherwise I won't even have the appetite to eat!]","The system replied, [Oh? Who was it that just had a breakfast of a basket of crab roe buns, a beef pie, and a bowl of wonton?]","Yanshu retorted, [...This is me without an appetite. Usually, I would add another basket of buns, two side dishes, and a bowl of porridge.]","...But that wasn't the point.","The point was, she had to catch this damn perverted scumbag!!!","After all, there were still several children who hadn't been found!!!","How could she stand by and watch so many adorable little lives fall into the hands of a pervert!!!","Tsk, after raging and roaring like this for a while, she suddenly had an idea...","In the evening, as Yuwen Lan entered Ganlu Palace, he saw Yanshu approach him with a smile, \"Your Majesty, would it be alright if we didn't dine in the palace tonight? The other day you promised to take me out to eat, but we still haven't gone.\"","Yuwen Lan found it strange. Why would she want to go out for snacks at a time like this?","But then he heard her urgently think, [Quick, agree! I want to take you to catch that damn pervert Hu Yichun! I know where he is, and if we don't catch him soon, he might escape the city!!!]","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow inwardly. She actually wanted to take him to catch someone?","But thinking about it, it made sense. At this point, perhaps only her unique ability could locate that person without alerting him.","He nodded and tentatively said, \"Alright, where do you want to go? Tianjing Lane again?\"","She shook her head and said, \"No, I heard today that there's a good restaurant called Jifu Tower on Shuanggui Street in the north of the city. They say their Huaiyang cuisine is excellent. I'd like to try it, if that's alright?\"","North of the city, Shuanggui Street?","It seems that Hu Yichun is there?","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"Very well, let's go then, while it's still early.\"","He smiled again, \"I'll go with you to try it out.\"","Despite her small stature, she was so enthusiastic. Since they could catch that villain, he didn't mind going personally.","Seeing her joyful expression, she didn't forget to remind him, \"However, I'm still worried we might encounter some villains kidnapping children. Your Majesty, please bring more people.\"","Yuwen Lan smiled and said, \"Alright, we'll bring more then.\"","Only then did Yanshu feel at ease. She hurriedly changed into casual clothes with him and headed towards Shuanggui Street in the north of the city.","By the time the lanterns were first lit, the two finally arrived at Jifu Tower.","Yuwen Lan alighted from the carriage and discreetly surveyed the surroundings.","On the way, he realized this place was somewhat remote. From the outside, Jifu Tower appeared to be just an ordinary restaurant.","However, as it was dinner time, there were quite a few diners.","He wondered if Hu Yichun was also eating here at this moment.","He saw Yanshu wearing a veil, naturally leading him inside. She asked the proprietor for a private room on the second floor. After sitting down, she began to order.","\"I'd like your most famous dishes: oil-braised eel paste, clear-stewed lion's head meatballs, braised shredded tofu, and add a squirrel-shaped mandarin fish.\"","After the waiter left, she smiled at him and said, \"These are the most famous Huaiyang dishes. My husband, you can try and see if they're better here or at home.\"","Yuwen Lan made a noncommittal sound.","In his heart, he wondered, didn't they come to catch someone? Why doesn't she seem anxious at all?","But he couldn't let his guard down, so he signaled the secret guards to hide in the restaurant.","Soon, the ordered dishes arrived one by one.","Seeing the appealing presentation, Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she immediately started tasting.","—She knew that pervert was here today, but the food here was indeed famous.","Ahem, they definitely needed to catch the person, but they also definitely needed to eat the delicious food.","Mmm, she had to admit, the food was indeed quite good.","The lion's head meatballs were each as big as a fist, tasting rich but not greasy, soft and delicious;","The oil-braised eel paste was still sizzling when served, tasting oily but not greasy, fresh and delicious;","The squirrel-shaped mandarin fish was sweet and sour, crispy, and the braised shredded tofu was soft and flavorful.","Of course, while eating, she didn't forget to listen for messages from the system.","Just as they were about to finish the four dishes, the system suddenly chimed, [Hu Yichun has entered.]","Yanshu immediately put down her chopsticks, wiped her mouth, and said to Yuwen Lan, \"Husband, let's go.\"","Yuwen Lan was stunned, \"Finished eating?\"","Yanshu nodded, but in her heart, she thought, [That bastard is here, hurry up and go catch him!]","At that moment, a secret guard entered the room and whispered to him, \"Master, the person has arrived.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Good.\"","He stood up and walked out with her.","Leaving the private room, they needed to go downstairs to the entrance of the restaurant.","As they were stepping down the wooden stairs, a man was coming up towards them.","Yanshu glanced at him through her veil. She saw he was wearing a bamboo-green silk robe, of normal build, and at first glance, he looked quite handsome.","But looking again, she felt a sense of sleazy, lecherous oiliness coming from him.","At the same time, the system chimed, [This is that Hu Yichun.]","Yanshu thought, [Indeed, he looks like a pervert!]","The voice also simultaneously reached Yuwen Lan's ears.","The restaurant was small, and the stairs narrow. At this moment, he was just passing by this man.","His brows furrowed, and he was about to order his men to act.","But the man turned his head and called out, \"Sir...\"","Everyone paused.","Yuwen Lan also turned to look at him but didn't speak.","The man smiled and said, \"I wonder if I've seen you somewhere before? You look so familiar.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow secretly.","Then he heard the man think, [This person has such an extraordinary aura, could he be a high-ranking official or from a noble family?]","[I wonder if he likes men? Is there a chance to seduce him...]","Yuwen Lan: ???","Meanwhile, Yanshu also heard the system say, [Watch out, this person wants to seduce the emperor.]","Yanshu: [??? This damn pervert actually wants to seduce the innocent little emperor?]","Damn it, she had to beat him to death today!!!","So she spoke first, \"You must have mistaken him for someone else. My husband doesn't know you.\"","Then, before the other party could speak, she suddenly covered her nose and said, \"Oh my, why does it suddenly smell so bad?\"","Smell?","Hearing this, everyone was stunned.","Including the pervert Hu Yichun in front of them.","Yanshu looked at him with disgust and said, \"Sir, did you just come from the latrine? Why do you smell so bad all over?\"","Upon hearing this, the man's eyes narrowed, and he said, \"Madam jest. I just came in from the street.\"","After speaking, he snorted in his heart, [How dare this dead woman speak to me like this? What a waste of such a good-looking man!]","Yuwen Lan: ???","The system immediately transmitted to Yanshu, [He's cursing you.]","Yanshu laughed inwardly, but suddenly exclaimed in surprise, \"Oh no, where's my money pouch?\"","System: [Good idea! Hu Yichun recently carried a sapphire blue brocade money pouch with scattered flower patterns, containing twenty taels of silver inside.]","Yanshu immediately pointed at him and said, \"Did you steal my money pouch?\"","Hu Yichun was stunned, \"What? How could I steal your...\"","Before he could finish, Yanshu interrupted, \"It was on me when we were in the room, and after just a few steps and brushing shoulders with you, it's gone. You must have stolen it!!!\"","Without allowing any explanation, she immediately turned to Yuwen Lan and said, \"Husband, quickly have someone search him to see if he has my sapphire blue brocade money pouch with scattered flower patterns. It contains twenty taels of silver!\"","\"What?\"","Hu Yichun was dumbfounded.","This... this... this was his money pouch...","But how did this woman know about it...","However, before he could react, Yuwen Lan had already signaled with his eyes.","In an instant, several strong men rushed out from all sides and pinned him against the wall.","Yanshu said, \"Search him!\"","The guards complied and immediately found a sapphire blue brocade money pouch with scattered flower patterns on him, containing twenty taels of silver.","Yanshu immediately said, \"Well, well, stealing silver in broad daylight! Husband, this person must be a habitual offender. We should report to the authorities to investigate what else he has stolen.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","To think it would be so effortless.","Impressive!"]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44","paragraphs":["\"What? Send him to the authorities?\"","Hu Yichun, having been in the underworld for so long, finally reacted when he heard Yanshu speak like this. He hurriedly softened his voice and said, \"May I ask who you all are? I have no grudge against you, so why are you trying to harm me like this? Let's talk this over, please release me first.\"","Yanshu spat through the curtain, \"How dare a scum like you try to negotiate with us?\"","Hmph, this dead pervert had committed so many unforgivable evil deeds, and now he even tried to seduce the emperor???","The more she thought about it, the angrier she became. She said again, \"Beat him up!\"","\"...\"","The guards hesitated slightly upon hearing this.","So they quietly glanced at the emperor, and seeing that he didn't say anything, they immediately complied and started punching the man.","— Heh, needless to say, they had long wanted to beat up this scum who trafficked children!","Hu Yichun wasn't particularly strong, but the guards were all experts who could kill a bull with one punch. Now filled with righteous indignation, it only took a few blows to beat him black and blue, with blood flowing from his nose and mouth.","Yuwen Lan glanced at him, then immediately looked at Yanshu.","Sure enough, he saw her body sway, as if her legs had gone weak and she was about to fall.","\"...\"","He immediately stepped forward and held her in his arms, but heard her cursing angrily in her mind, [Damn it, this scum actually dares to bleed!!! Is he deliberately trying to piss me off!!!]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He could only quickly order the guards, \"That's enough.\"","The guards then stopped.","Hu Yichun immediately fell to the ground, constantly moaning in pain.","The commotion naturally attracted many onlookers from the shop.","Seeing everyone's confused expressions, Yuwen Lan coughed and said, \"This man stole money and frightened my wife. Quickly send him to the Capital Official to report the case.\"","The guards complied and immediately dragged Hu Yichun out by the neck.","He then directly picked up Yanshu by the waist and walked out as well.","As they walked, he asked with concern, \"How are you feeling?\"","Yanshu was still a bit dizzy and could only say weakly, \"Your wife is too useless.\"","Damn it, why did she faint at the sight of blood again!!! She should have beaten him up more!!!","Hmph, just for daring to curse at her earlier, beating him until he couldn't take care of himself would have been too light!!!","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He was filled with mixed emotions, trying hard to suppress his laughter as he said, \"Let's keep him alive for a thousand cuts and dismemberment.\"","By the time he finished speaking, they had arrived at the carriage. The coachman hurriedly lifted the curtain, and he carried her into the carriage, never having put her down from start to finish.","And so, in full view of everyone, Hu Yichun was taken to the Capital Official.","Normally, a theft case would be simple to handle, but seeing that it was the imperial guards who brought the man in, the Capital Official didn't dare to be negligent and immediately interrogated him.","Unexpectedly, this investigation revealed that this man really had some secrets.","...","Jifu Tower was already some distance from the palace, so by the time they returned to Ganlu Palace, it was already quite late.","Moreover, Yanshu had fainted again, so they couldn't attend to anything else and went to bed early.","However, when she woke up early the next morning, she finally heard some good news.","— It was said that the Capital Official had found Hu Yichun's residence overnight and, after a search, found several property deeds related to him.","Following this lead, the officials found two more houses hidden in the suburbs, from which they rescued six boys, all of whom were children who had gone missing previously.","According to the confessions of his underlings, Hu Yichun had also been involved in human trafficking in Jiangnan, Xiangxiang, and other places, all involving the kidnapping of good-looking young children who were then trained before being sold to local wealthy merchants or officials.","Given the gravity of the matter, the Capital Official immediately reported to the court, transferring the case to the Ministry of Justice. The emperor also ordered the Imperial Censorate to intervene, treating it as a major case to be strictly handled.","As a result, the morning court session was very busy.","At this time, Yanshu, who was leisurely having breakfast, was eating while conversing with the system, [Next is that scum Chai Weizhong, have they found anything on him?]","The system replied, [Not yet. You should know that Chai Weizhong is very cautious. Every time he went to see Hu Yichun, he was in disguise. So far, the Imperial Censorate hasn't found any clues about his connection with Hu Yichun.]","[Moreover, ever since the emperor said yesterday that there would be a strict investigation, he immediately dismissed the male concubines in his household and sent people to bring his original wife, Lady Nie, to the capital, intending to cover things up. Lady Nie is already on her way these days.]","Yanshu, [??? This scum is still using his wife at this time? He's really not a decent human being!!!]","System, [If he wasn't a thousand-year-old fox, how could he play such tricks? In short, these perverts are each more cunning than the last.]","That's true.","Yanshu angrily bit into a golden thread pastry, thinking to herself that she couldn't let this scum get away scot-free.","She had to come up with a plan.","That afternoon, the Carefree Young Master's new book suddenly hit the market.","Although it was sudden, it didn't hinder the book's popularity. In just one afternoon, over a thousand copies were sold.","By dinnertime, people who had read the book were already discussing the plot—","Recently, due to the case of missing boys, the topics of \"cut sleeve\" and \"boy love\" were very sensitive. Unexpectedly, one of the main characters in this story was a \"cut sleeve\".","Combined with past experience, people immediately realized that this story was likely related to the recent case, and they began to speculate about the identity of the scumbag in the story.","— Could it be that there really was an official in the court who was into \"cut sleeves\"?","And he even kept male concubines at home?","Tsk tsk tsk, such an outrageous person, who could it be?","More and more people joined the discussion, and with the prosperous trade between north, south, east, and west at this time, the topic quickly spread from the capital to all directions.","...","After three days on the road, they were about to reach the capital the next day.","That night, Chai Weizhong's original wife, Lady Nie, was resting at an inn.","It was the season when many travelers were coming and going, so the inn was bustling with activity.","After dinner, the maid Bai Guo brought hot water from outside into the room to serve Lady Nie for washing up.","Lady Nie asked, \"Why did you take so long?\"","— She was gentle by nature, and there was no blame in her words. Bai Guo smiled and said, \"The water wasn't boiled earlier, and there was a storyteller next door. I saw many people listening, so I stayed to listen for a while.\"","Lady Nie also smiled and said, \"What story was so captivating?\"","Bai Guo's eyes lit up, and she immediately told her, \"My lady, did you know that there are actually people in this world who don't like women, but instead like men?\"","Lady Nie, being in her forties, had more experience and said, \"That's called the passion of the cut sleeve, I've heard about it before.\"","But Bai Guo continued, \"However, even though this person clearly likes men, he still marries a wife and has children. After marriage, he lets his wife take care of his parents and children in their hometown, while he enjoys himself elsewhere. Isn't that too much! You don't know, this person even keeps several male concubines in his mansion!\"","Lady Nie was startled, \"What? Male concubines?\"","Bai Guo nodded and said, \"That person, in order to conveniently do those outrageous things with men, actually had his male lovers disguise themselves as concubines to live in the mansion to cover things up.\"","Perhaps it was too bizarre, but hearing this, Lady Nie also became curious and asked, \"Then, didn't his wife find out?\"","Bai Guo said, \"It's said that the wife of that family is very virtuous, always taking care of the parents-in-law and children in their hometown. This man is away from home for years, and although he has already set up a mansion, he never asks his wife to come and live with him. He only returns to his hometown during festivals to visit, but even then, he leaves hurriedly after a brief visit... The relationship between this couple seems respectful on the surface, but is actually as cold as ice.\"","Hearing these words, Lady Nie's heart trembled.","— Wasn't she herself in the same situation?","Since marrying into the Chai family, the number of times she had been intimate with her husband could be counted on one hand. Especially after giving birth to their two children years ago, there had been nothing at all...","In the past, her parents-in-law had suggested that her husband bring her to the capital, but he always refused, citing that women were troublesome. Yet he had successively taken concubines in the capital...","After feeling desolate for a while, Lady Nie suddenly realized that the wife in this story was so similar to herself.","Just as she was wondering about this, she heard Bai Guo continue, \"This man always leaves home in a hurry, using his career as an excuse, but in reality, he's eager to go back and fool around with those male concubines. Oh yes, it seems it's not just the ones in his mansion, but also male lovers outside... Tsk tsk, it's really disgusting.\"","As she spoke, she helped Lady Nie take off her shoes and socks and began washing her feet.","Lady Nie, however, was already immersed in the story and frowned as she asked, \"Then later, did that wife find out?\"","While washing her feet, Bai Guo nodded and said, \"It was discovered. One time this madam was in a hurry to go to the capital to see a doctor for her in-laws, and didn't have time to inform that man. As a result, it was discovered when she arrived at the mansion.\"","Lady Nie quickly asked, \"How was it discovered?\"","Bai Guo said, \"After all, those concubines were men. They had large builds and voices unlike ordinary women, and they never used menstrual pads or anything like that... Most importantly, the three of them had been in the household for several years but none of them had been able to bear children, so naturally there was a problem.\"","Lady Nie's brows suddenly furrowed.","Large builds...","Voices unlike ordinary women?","She remembered one year when she personally made winter clothes for her husband and had the housekeeper send them to the capital. When the housekeeper returned, she told her that her husband's concubines all had large builds and deep voices...","The housekeeper had even wondered why the master liked women who resembled men.","Most importantly, in all these years the Chai family only had the two children she herself had given birth to. Those concubines had been in the capital for many years but had never given birth to anything...","Could it be...","Lady Nie grew increasingly suspicious and hurriedly asked, \"What else did the storyteller say?\"","Bai Guo thought for a moment and said, \"The storyteller also said that besides consorting with men, this person later partnered with others to kidnap children from other families and sell them to people who also liked men for their pleasure... Oh my, it was just too wicked! What a waste of such a good wife! Later when the authorities investigated him, he got scared and dismissed the male concubines from his household and brought his wife to the city...\"","What?","Lady Nie was severely shocked.","On her journey to the capital, she had occasionally seen officials searching for human traffickers, and only learned upon inquiry that there had been a case of kidnapping young boys in the capital a few days ago...","And this time Chai Weizhong had suddenly summoned her to the capital.","Could things really be such a coincidence?","Three days later, when Yanshu got out of bed, she heard a message from the system: [Chai Weizhong has been arrested.]","Hmm?","Her eyes lit up and she immediately said, [How was he arrested? Could it be that Hu Yichun confessed?]","The system replied, [That's right. For one, Hu Yichun couldn't withstand torture and finally confessed. Additionally, the male concubines who left his household were also caught and admitted his association with Hu Yichun.]","Yanshu's eyes brightened, [The authorities were actually able to find his male concubines? Not bad, when did they become so competent?]","The system said, [Actually, the emperor had been secretly having people monitor the Chai household, and they caught the concubines as soon as he dismissed them.]","Yanshu: [!!! The emperor is impressive!]","But after praising him, she felt something was off.","[...Wait, why would the emperor have people monitor the Chai household? How did he notice something was wrong with Chai Weizhong?]","The system: [...I'm sorry, but there seems to be some interference signal around the emperor. This system has been unable to detect his psychological activities.]","Yanshu: [???]","How could there be such a thing?","Tsk, could it be that because he's the emperor with the protection of the true dragon, he's able to block the system?","Thinking about it, it seemed possible. After all, the system still hadn't told her how the emperor was \"unable\" back then.","But after thinking about it herself, she felt it must have been the story she wrote before that made the emperor suspicious—","After all, there weren't many officials of his rank in the court who kept their wives in their hometowns.","The emperor would know it was him with just a little investigation.","Just then, she heard the system say, [Chai's wife deserves some credit in this matter.]","Yanshu immediately asked, [How so?]","The system: [After those two identified Chai Weizhong, the Imperial Censorate and Ministry of Justice searched the Chai residence. At this time, Chai's wife Lady Nie voluntarily submitted an account book of Chai Weizhong's to the court. The accounts in the book were sufficient to prove that Chai Weizhong had gifted several thousand taels of silver to Hu Yichun for purchasing property in the capital, and that after Hu Yichun profited from trafficking boys, he had shared the spoils with him.]","Yanshu's eyes lit up upon hearing this, [Well done, Lady Chai!]","The system: [It was mainly because she was enlightened after reading your story.]","Yanshu smiled with satisfaction, [It's good that she's enlightened. With such an act of placing righteousness above family loyalty, the court should provide her with care and not let her be implicated by that scum.]","—She sincerely hoped this sister could stand up.","Although fate was unfair at first, causing her to waste over twenty years of her youth with that scum, it's never too late to wake up.","She hoped she could recover, and perhaps even achieve something in her career as in the story, living her own life.","After Chai Weizhong's arrest, the case progressed much faster.","Within two days, through the investigation of the Imperial Censorate and Ministry of Justice, they had basically uncovered the wealthy merchants and officials in various places who had dealings with Hu Yichun, the main culprit in the boy trafficking case. They also rescued dozens of victimized children.","Those who had harmed children were shown no leniency, and all were arrested.","After the case was solved, Hu Yichun was sentenced to death by slow slicing, while the other accomplice Chai Weizhong was also sentenced to beheading.","Considering that his wife had been separated from him for years and was unaware of his evil deeds, especially since she voluntarily reported him after discovering clues, the emperor specially granted mercy, exempting her from being implicated in Chai Weizhong's crimes.","As for the other involved parties, they were all punished according to their crimes, which could be said to be deeply satisfying to the people.","For a time, besides cursing the evil deeds of scum like Hu and Chai, the common people in the streets and alleys started a new rumor—","It was said that the person who first caught Hu Yichun this time was a young woman.","Although there was no advance leak from the Carefree Young Master's story this time, this topic similarly triggered people's curiosity.","—According to the recollections of diners present at Jifu Tower that day, that night, the lady was in flowing gauze robes, with a graceful figure. Although her face couldn't be seen clearly due to the veil, one could imagine she must have been as beautiful as a celestial maiden. When she discovered this person stealing, she fearlessly called for servants to capture him, showing remarkable courage.","In no time, everyone was curious about who this extraordinary lady could be.","...","One afternoon, Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong finished drafting an imperial edict in the imperial study. Taking advantage of the empty room, he said to the emperor, \"Does Your Majesty know that recently there's a rumor among the people that the first person to discover the main culprit Hu Yichun was actually a young lady!\"","\"It's said that she's intelligent and quick-witted, with remarkable courage. She merely brushed shoulders with Hu Yichun and saw through his malicious intentions and evil deeds. She's truly an extraordinary woman.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment, \"A young lady?\"","Is he talking about Yanshu?","Zou Mozhong nodded, \"Indeed. The people call her a heroine among women. Now, regardless of age, everyone is curious about this lady's identity... I believe that if the Carefree Young Master could write a story about this now, it would surely be a hit.\"","Ahem, mainly he was also curious about who this extraordinary lady could be.","He thought that the Carefree Young Master had always been prophetic, and might know some clues.","So he wanted him to write it quickly, to satisfy everyone's curiosity!","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","He was clearly present that day too, so why did these rumors automatically ignore his presence?","And why were these people curious about his beloved consort for no reason?","He casually replied, \"I haven't had any news of her these past few days either. I'll have someone inquire later.\"","Scholar Zou saw that the emperor wasn't very interested, so he could only agree and withdraw from the hall.","Left alone, Yuwen Lan sat for a while, unable to focus on the memorials. He then got up and left the hall, going to Ganlu Palace.","When he arrived, he saw Yanshu writing a story, her brows slightly furrowed, looking very serious.","She was so focused that she almost didn't notice him entering the hall.","Hearing the announcement, she hurriedly put down her brush and stood up to curtsy, \"This humble consort greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and sat down on the warm couch, asking, \"What story are you writing today?\"","Yanshu raised an eyebrow and smiled, quite proudly saying, \"This humble consort is writing about an extraordinary lady today.\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"What makes her extraordinary?\"","—Could it be that she also knew about the rumors outside and was going to write her own story?","He saw her clear her throat and say, \"This lady can be said to possess both beauty and wisdom, and is also proficient in literature and martial arts. More notably, she has a heart full of righteousness, is not afraid of evil and treacherous wolves, and bravely fights against evil forces.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Both beauty and wisdom?","And proficient in literature and martial arts?","A heart full of righteousness, not afraid of evil and treacherous wolves?","Alright, with such lavish praise, he was certain she was writing about herself.","So he pretended not to have realized and nodded slightly, saying, \"Indeed, she seems to be a rare extraordinary lady. I wonder what her story is?\"","Then she continued, \"This young lady hides in her boudoir during the day, but at night she roams the martial world with her sword, always ready to right any wrongs she encounters.","\"For instance, one night she saw a gambler trying to sell his wife to pay off debts. She immediately gave the gambler a sound thrashing and helped his wife escape to freedom.\"","\"Another time, she caught some ruffians harassing a respectable woman. She broke their arms and legs, and even cut off their 'precious parts' to ensure they'd never offend again.\"","\"And once, she came across bandits robbing poor villagers. In her fury, she single-handedly leveled the entire mountain where they were based and distributed all the stolen money to the villagers who had suffered at the bandits' hands... In short, no evildoer was a match for her.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Beating up gamblers and defeating bandits was one thing, but cutting off 'precious parts'? What was that about?","Why was she so... enthusiastic about... this particular act?","And to do it to a whole group of men???","How could a young lady be so...","Before he could find the right word, she continued, \"This young lady did many good deeds for the country and its people, earning countless praises and gratitude. Finally, one day she moved the gods, who gave her an immortality pill. After taking it, she became a celestial being.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What kind of direction was this taking?","He couldn't help but ask, \"Why did she suddenly become an immortal?\"","Was the mortal world unable to contain her anymore?","Were her aspirations truly so lofty???","Yanshu replied with a proud face, \"Because she was simply too excellent, without any flaws. So she had to ascend to immortality. After all, as a celestial being, she could maintain her youth and beauty forever.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, she certainly didn't hold back in imagining her own perfection.","But after pondering for a moment, he suddenly realized something—","There was no trace of himself in her story.","Yuwen Lan was silent for a moment, then asked, \"Did this young lady ascend to immortality alone because she never met a suitable man? Why didn't you give her a companion to share her life with?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She had initially wanted to say that men would only slow down her sword-drawing speed.","Wasn't it enough for a female warrior to live freely on her own? What was the need for a man?","But considering that the emperor was also a man, she feared hurting his pride. So she said, \"Because... this young lady was so focused on doing great deeds, she accidentally forgot about it.\"","Forgot?","Yuwen Lan, who had heard her entire thought process, wanted to scoff coldly.","She had indeed forgotten about him.","He pulled her close, bringing his face—so handsome it was flawless—near her almond-shaped eyes, and said in a low voice, \"There are still many things worth cherishing in the mortal world. Why rush to become an immortal on your own?\"","His deep, magnetic voice was close to her ear, making Yanshu feel a bit dizzy. She stammered, \"What... what else is there to cherish...\"","As she spoke, she couldn't help but stare at his lips.","They were thin and quite tempting.","Just as she finished speaking, the man before her suddenly darkened his gaze.","Then, he let her taste what she had been wanting to taste.","Mmm, it was indeed nice.","Yuwen Lan heard her thoughts and chuckled softly.","He thought it was nice too.","— Over the past few days, most of the poison had been purged from his system, and after taking several doses of medicine, he seemed to be gradually returning to his former self.","However, he had been busy dealing with the case of missing children for the past few days. After solving the case, he was occupied with revising laws and rectifying court conduct, leaving him no time to think about much else.","Now that he had some leisure time, with a fragrant beauty in his arms, he finally got into the mood.","...","Yanshu felt the same way.","It seemed like it had been a long time since the emperor had been so...","With her.","While kissing, she had enough presence of mind to think—","He had been taking medicine for over half a month now, right?","She wondered what state he was in now?","Not long after, her side accidentally brushed against something, and she suddenly froze.","What, what was that?","Meanwhile, Yuwen Lan felt greatly reassured.","He had succeeded.","For the first time in who knows how long, he was like this.","He had succeeded!!!","His heart was filled with indescribable joy, and for a moment he didn't care what time it was. He only wanted to continue verifying.","However, at that moment, a voice came from outside the door, \"Imperial Consort Yi, the Empress Dowager requests your presence...\"","The two of them paused, both coming back to their senses."]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45","paragraphs":["With that sound, the two people in the palace finally came back to their senses.","Yanshu hurriedly broke free from Yuwen Lan's embrace, straightened her clothes, adjusted her hair, and rushed to the mirror to wipe off the smeared lipstick from his kisses.","After tidying herself up, she was about to go to the heated couch when her gaze inadvertently caught sight of a shocking scene.","His robe... seemed to be tented.","Yanshu was stunned, suddenly remembering the thing she had accidentally brushed against earlier...","Could this be...","She was suddenly filled with shock!!!","Had he recovered???","\"...\"","Yuwen Lan felt a bit awkward.","He desperately wanted to tell her that her guess was correct.","— If they hadn't been interrupted just now, he might have already carried her to the bed.","Tsk, why did the Empress Dowager have to pick such a moment to summon her?","Yanshu was also curious about this question.","What did the Empress Dowager want with her out of the blue?","Could it be that she wanted to inquire about novels again while the Emperor was present?","Of course, the Empress Dowager's messenger was waiting outside, and she should have called them in to inquire.","However, looking at a certain someone's proud and majestic appearance...","Tsk, how could they receive visitors like this?","Unable to resist taking another peek, Yanshu clicked her tongue inwardly. Even from this view it looked quite impressive; it seemed the Emperor had quite some potential.","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Of course, after all, he was the Emperor.","Just as he was thinking this, he saw Yanshu quickly fetch a blanket from inside and say to him, \"It's suddenly gotten a bit cold in the room. Your Majesty must not catch a chill.\"","With that, she blushed and draped the blanket over his body.","Only then did she call out to the door, \"Come in and speak.\"","As soon as she finished, the palace maid guarding the door lifted the curtain and ushered in Zhu Shu, who had been waiting outside to report.","Entering the hall, Zhu Shu immediately sensed an ambiguous atmosphere swirling around.","Her heart skipped a beat, but she could only first bow to the two of them, \"This servant pays respects to Your Majesty and Consort Yi.\"","After speaking, she secretly glanced at the two of them, noticing Yanshu's rosy cheeks and the Emperor's somewhat unnatural expression.","Combined with how long she had been waiting at the door...","The scene that had just unfolded in the hall was self-evident.","She could only pretend not to have noticed anything and reported to the two of them, \"The Empress Dowager wishes to invite Consort Yi over for a chat. If it's convenient for Your Majesty, perhaps you'd like to join as well.\"","Yanshu thought to herself that this was well said, as the Emperor probably wasn't quite in a convenient state at the moment.","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Indeed, he had been feeling quite uncomfortable just now.","However, after this interruption, he had already calmed down...","Ah, this was the first time in three years!","He barely suppressed his disappointment and said with a normal expression, \"I was just thinking of going to visit Mother. Let's go then.\"","With that, he removed the blanket from his body and rose from the couch.","What, he was going too?","Yanshu was startled and quickly glanced again, but saw that he had already returned to normal.","Gone again???","She couldn't help but worry — would this have any effect on him?","Would he become impotent again...","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","It hadn't quite come to that.","It's just... his heart was filled with a deep, indescribable regret.","Tsk, the Empress Dowager really knew how to pick her moments!","Not long after, the two of them arrived together at the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","After paying their respects, the Empress Dowager called for tea and snacks to be served, then smiled and said, \"I woke up from my afternoon nap with nothing to do and wanted to call Consort Yi over for a chat. I didn't expect Your Majesty to be here as well?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"I had just gone over not long ago, and thought to come visit Mother together. How have you been feeling these past few days?\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Thanks to Your Majesty's blessings, I've been quite well these past few days. But I heard that Consort Yi hasn't been feeling well lately. Are you feeling better now?\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but glance at the Emperor.","She was covering for him after all!","— With Ganlu Palace brewing medicine for over ten days now, everyone outside thought it was she who had fallen ill.","She could only reply to the Empress Dowager, \"Thank you for your concern, Empress Dowager. I just caught a slight cold a few days ago. After drinking medicine for a few days, I'm almost fully recovered now.\"","As she finished speaking, she hurriedly covered her mouth and coughed twice to prove she wasn't lying.","She pondered in her heart that this explanation should be fine. Judging from today's situation, it seemed the Emperor no longer needed to take medicine.","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan silently nodded in his heart —","Indeed, based on what happened earlier, he should no longer need to take medicine.","Ahem, he'd find an opportunity to prove it to her tonight.","Just as his mind started to wander, he saw the Empress Dowager nod, \"That's good then.\"","But then she suddenly changed the subject and asked, \"Speaking of which, I've been reading novels in my free time these past few days. I noticed that in the latest book by the Carefree Gentleman, he seems to be writing about the Chai family, doesn't he?\"","At these words, Yanshu thought to herself that as expected, the Empress Dowager had come to inquire about novels again.","Well, she was covering for the Emperor by pretending to take medicine, and the Emperor was covering for her about the novels. They were even now.","She quietly picked up her teacup and took a sip, secretly glancing at the Emperor, waiting for him to answer.","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","This \"even\" situation was quite unfair.","After all, he only had to take medicine this one time, but she had already written many novels.","And in the future, she would likely continue writing endlessly.","However, since he had agreed to this himself, he said, \"Mother is correct.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and continued, \"How did Your Majesty discover that Chai Weizhong was homosexual? I had no idea about this all along.\"","Yuwen Lan could only say, \"I heard about it by chance and had someone investigate. It turned out to be true.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded again.","But in her heart, she wondered, [Where exactly did he hear it from? How come I never heard anything about it!]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Next, the Empress Dowager sighed, \"This Chai Weizhong is too outrageous. Being homosexual is one thing, but to actually bring a man home and pass him off as a concubine! Such disrespect for his lawful wife, it's truly infuriating.\"","Yuwen Lan could only say, \"Those with wicked hearts often commit deeds that defy heaven's principles. However, he has now been brought to justice, so Mother need not dwell on it anymore.\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound of agreement, \"It's fortunate that Your Majesty has such keen insight and discernment.\"","But in her heart, she shook her head, [It should have been exposed earlier, letting him suffer disgrace and the contempt of thousands before being brought to justice. That would have been truly satisfying! The Emperor is still not ruthless enough.]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Alright, he understood now. Indeed, women found this scoundrel's behavior utterly unforgivable.","Then he heard the Empress Dowager continue, \"By the way, I've heard rumors lately that the first person to discover something amiss with that human trafficker surnamed Hu and report him to the authorities was a woman. Does Your Majesty know if this is true or false? I wonder which young lady it was, to be so clever and brave?\"","Yuwen Lan, \"...I've only just heard about this matter and haven't been able to verify it yet.\"","Well, after being mother and son for over twenty years, he was only now discovering that the Empress Dowager also enjoyed gossip so much.","At this moment, he heard Yanshu say from the side, \"This consort believes this claim is very likely to be true.\"","\"Oh?\"","The Empress Dowager immediately looked at her, \"Why does Consort Yi say so?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"If this consort may be so bold, women have been underestimated since ancient times. We are rarely involved in important matters. Most good deeds are attributed to men. Now that the common people unanimously believe this was done by a young woman, it's likely to be true. Otherwise, wouldn't they have already claimed it was a man?\"","\"Well reasoned,\" the Empress Dowager nodded. \"For once, the men aren't trying to take credit. It must indeed have been a woman's doing.\"","[This little Consort Yi has some insight. She's different from those who think they're clever.]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","As the only man present in the hall at this moment, he suddenly felt a sense of exclusion.","So he spoke up, \"In another half month, it will be Mother's birthday celebration. I have already ordered the Court of Imperial Sacrifices and the Court of Imperial Entertainments to begin preparations. Does Mother wish to hold it in the palace this year, or would you prefer Jinbo Garden?\"","— Rather than letting the Empress Dowager continue asking strange questions, it was better to actively change the subject.","Sure enough, the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"I am already content with Your Majesty's filial piety. The palace will do fine. Let's keep everything simple and not burden the people or waste resources.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and continued, \"The other day, I received a report that Duke Qin'an and his family are already on their way. They should arrive in the capital in about five or six days. You and Aunt haven't seen each other in a long time, so you'll be able to have a good chat.\"","The Duchess of Qin'an was the Empress Dowager's cousin. As a noble lady of the Zhou family, she had married the Marquis of Qin'an years ago. Later, when the previous emperor ascended the throne, in order to show his regard for the Zhou family and win over the Marquis of Qin'an's influence, he elevated her husband to the position of duke.","However, this family resided in the northwest and only returned annually for the Empress Dowager's birthday celebrations.","It was thought that the sisters must have a deep affection for each other.","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded and smiled, \"Your Majesty is truly considerate.\"","But inwardly she sighed, \"I have to see that annoying Zhou Shulan again.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","After discussing the Thousand Autumn Festival, a minister happened to request an audience at Qianming Palace, so Yuwen Lan left the Palace of Benevolent Peace with Yanshu.","Yanshu returned to Ganlu Palace to write her stories.","After meeting with the minister, seeing that it was still early, Yuwen Lan changed into casual clothes and left the palace.","— Today happened to be Jiang Nianqi's day off, so he wanted to ask if he could now be considered fully recovered.","It wasn't long before he arrived at his destination.","At that time, Doctor Jiang was seeing another patient, so he waited in the carriage for a while. When the room was empty, he got out of the carriage with his veil.","Upon entering the room, Doctor Jiang saw him and asked, \"Has the treatment been effective, sir?\"","Yuwen Lan inwardly sighed at the doctor's medical skills and nodded, \"Indeed. Today I discovered that I seem to have returned to normal. So, is it no longer necessary to continue taking medicine?\"","Doctor Jiang nodded, \"You don't need to take medicine anymore, but sir, you still can't engage in sexual activities yet.\"","What?","Yuwen Lan was stunned and quickly asked, \"Why not?\"","The doctor replied, \"Sir, you weren't poisoned for just a day or two. Although the residual toxins have mostly been expelled from your body, your vital energy has been suppressed for so long that it's not in optimal condition. In this situation, if you were to engage in sexual activities and your partner became pregnant, there's a risk of an unhealthy child or even a stillbirth.\"","Yuwen Lan drew in a sharp breath and frowned, \"Is it really that serious?\"","Doctor Jiang nodded, \"I'm not exaggerating. I've traveled to many places and seen numerous such cases. For the sake of your future offspring, it's best to abstain for now.\"","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"How long must I wait?\"","Doctor Jiang said, \"Vital energy regenerates in cycles of three days. You should wait for seven cycles, which is about right.\"","Three days per cycle, and seven cycles...","Yuwen Lan paused. That meant twenty-one days.","In other words, he had to wait another month?","Seemingly noticing his disappointment, Doctor Jiang consoled him, \"Sir, you've waited this long, surely a few more days won't make much difference.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What did he mean by a few more days not making a difference?","It was one thing when he wasn't better, but now that he had recovered...","Especially when every night, that young lady beside him was restless and liked to snuggle into his arms.","It was like a traveler who had been trekking through the desert for a long time, holding a sweet, fresh fruit but unable to eat it.","It was absolute torture!","He wasn't willing to give up and tried asking again, \"Is there no other way?\"","Doctor Jiang said, \"Another option... would be to have the lady drink contraceptive tea. However, all medicine has its side effects. If she drinks too much of this tea, it could make it difficult for her to conceive in the future.\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","He had just barely recovered to normal...","Alright, he nodded and said, \"Thank you for your explanation, doctor.\"","He then took out a gold ingot from his sleeve, placed it on the table, and said, \"This is my consultation fee.\"","Jiang Nianqi was about to speak, but Yuwen Lan added, \"This is a token of my appreciation. Please don't refuse.\"","After saying this, he stood up and left the room.","Jiang Nianqi watched his retreating figure for a while before reluctantly putting away the gold ingot.","Well, this man had such a strong presence that he was clearly no ordinary person, so he had better comply.","However...","It was somewhat surprising —","Men of his status usually had wives and concubines, or even spent their days in debauchery with countless women around them.","Yet when this man heard that the contraceptive tea could be harmful to women, he didn't pursue it further. Could it be that he only had one woman in his household?","It was rare to find such a faithful man.","By the time he returned to the palace, it was already dark.","Yuwen Lan changed his clothes in Qianming Palace, then went to the study to look over some memorials. When he finally went to Ganlu Palace, Yanshu had already bathed.","Seeing him arrive, she hurried forward to pay her respects, \"This humble consort greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan excused her from the formalities and looked down at her.","Her long, wet hair hung down her back, with a few strands clinging to her temples. Her cheeks were flushed from the warm bath, making her look like a delicious fruit on a branch.","Yes, exactly the kind of fruit that he, a long-distance traveler, very much wanted to taste.","Yuwen Lan tried hard to banish the distracting thoughts from his mind and said, \"It's late, let's sleep.\"","He then went to the bed.","Yanshu responded and followed him to the bed.","However, after lying down, she felt a bit restless.","— Based on what happened during the day, he should be better now.","So tonight...","Would they...","Ahem, if it really happened, she shouldn't be too shy.","After all, he was just recovering from a serious illness and needed encouragement. It wouldn't do to extinguish the small flame that had just begun to spark.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","So this was what she was thinking?","He had thought she would be shy or even resistant...","But then again, thinking back to when he first came to Ganlu Palace, she had dared to kiss him on her own initiative.","Thinking of this, he began to feel a bit restless again.","However...","Yuwen Lan silently sighed. Tonight he could only disappoint her.","So he turned his back to her, facing the bed curtains, and closed his eyes, silently reciting a mantra to calm his mind.","Yanshu: \"???\"","What did this mean?","The person who always took advantage of her every time they slept was now turning his back to her?","Hadn't he recovered???","After puzzling over this for a while, she suddenly paused.","Damn, could it be that he was thinking of another woman?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Then he heard her think, [Tsk tsk, it must be like this. After all, I'm just his target practice. When he couldn't perform, he used me as a cover. Now that he can, he continues to use me as a cover, but saves his virginity for his true love!]","Yes, it must be like this!","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","True love?","The only one he liked was her.","However, before he could open his mouth to explain, he heard her curse again, [Scumbag!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","How had he become a scumbag???","At this moment, Yanshu was inexplicably irritated —","...Although he hadn't played with her body or feelings, she somehow felt that he was very scummy.","But anyway, she hadn't fallen for him either, she had just coveted his good looks a little...","Who's afraid of whom!","So she also turned to face the inside of the bed, back-to-back with him.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What, she hadn't fallen for him?","And only coveted his good looks???","Just then, he heard several more \"scumbag\" curses from her mind...","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had no choice but to turn back towards her and pull her into his arms.","However, the moment he touched her, he could feel her wanting to resist.","He said, \"Are you angry with me?\"","Yanshu woodenly said she wasn't.","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and said, \"Then why do you look so sulky?\"","Yanshu wanted to tell him she wasn't, but as soon as she turned her head, she accidentally fell into his kiss.","Mmm...","She had meant to resist, but got lost for a moment.","After all, he... was getting better at this.","However, her mind was still thinking, this scumbag wasn't saving his virginity for his true love? Why was he kissing her again?","What virginity...","Yuwen Lan reluctantly parted from her and said softly, \"Silly girl.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","What?","This scumbag was calling her silly???","But then she saw him sigh again and say, \"I've been unwell these past few days, so I've been taking medicine.\"","Yanshu made a sound of acknowledgment.","In her heart, she wondered why he was suddenly telling her this.","Then she heard him continue, \"The doctor told me that I can't... be intimate with you for a few days.\"","After all, it was his first time discussing such matters with a woman, so he felt somewhat uncomfortable.","The young lady in his arms was stunned. \"Ah?\"","What was this situation?","Was it because he had just recovered and couldn't do that yet?","So it wasn't that he was saving his virginity for his true love?","Just then, she heard him say, \"You're the only one in my heart. There's never been anyone else.\"","Yanshu was taken aback.","...Why was he suddenly saying this?","It was as if he knew what she was thinking...","Then, she saw him add with resignation, \"That's why I turned away to sleep, because as soon as I hold you, I... can't control myself.\"","Yanshu was stunned again. \"Is... that so?\"","Before he could respond, she had already felt it.","Tsk...","So that was the case.","...He must be very uncomfortable, right?","Yuwen Lan wanted to say yes.","He was in a difficult situation!!!","Heaven knows what torment he was enduring at that moment?","Suddenly, the girl in his arms asked, \"Did the doctor say if there are any other methods that could work?\"","\"What?\"","Yuwen Lan didn't understand.","What other methods?","Then he saw her reach out her hand.","And without warning, he was touched by me, his whole body trembling with inheritance.","Yanshu blinked her innocent big eyes and asked, \"Would this work?\"","Yuwen Lan didn't know what to say anymore, and could only mumble, \"Y-yes, I suppose...\"","In the next moment, he could barely protect his knees.","...","That night, Yuwen Lan had the best sleep he'd had since ascending to the throne.","It was truly good.","Five days later, Duke Qin'an's family arrived in the capital.","As this was the Empress Dowager's clan sister, who had come specifically for the Empress Dowager's birthday celebration, the Empress Dowager naturally couldn't neglect them. Early the next morning, she had people escort her elder sister, the Duchess of Qin'an, to the palace for a meeting.","Yanshu, as one of the few remaining consorts in the palace, accompanied the Empress Dowager along with Consort Zhou to receive the guests in the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","She had just arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace when she saw the Duchess of Qin'an enter the hall.","Behind her followed two younger women and five or six children, ranging from seven or eight years old to two or three, with even one being carried in arms, not yet able to walk. There were both boys and girls, making for a very lively scene.","The Duchess of Qin'an appeared to be three or four years older than the Empress Dowager, but her countenance seemed even more stern.","Yanshu thought to herself that this woman truly lived up to being the elder sister from childhood; her aura clearly showed she was the head of the family.","It must not be easy to be her daughter-in-law, she mused.","After the Duchess of Qin'an led her large family to pay their respects, Yanshu learned that the two younger women were her daughter-in-law Lady Yue and her daughter Lady Qiao. The children were her grandchildren and great-grandchildren.","My, what a lively family indeed.","The Empress Dowager had seats brought for all of them and ordered palace servants to bring tea and refreshments. She then began to make small talk with her elder sister.","\"It's been a year since we last met. Have you been well, sister?\" the Empress Dowager politely inquired.","The Duchess of Qin'an nodded, \"Thanks to Your Majesty's blessings, I've been well. Last year we welcomed a new grandson, who is now over seven months old. By next year when we visit again, he'll be able to kowtow to Your Majesty.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded with a smile, \"Your family is prosperous with many descendants. You are truly blessed, sister.\"","But then the Duchess of Qin'an asked, \"I wonder if there have been any new little masters or mistresses in the palace?\"","Upon hearing this, everyone froze.","This... wasn't this bringing up a sore subject?","What the Empress Dowager wanted most now was an imperial grandson. If there had been one, wouldn't she have already shown him off?","Yanshu also inwardly clicked her tongue—","Was there some unpleasantness between these sisters?","If the palace had welcomed a prince or princess, it would have been announced to the whole world. How could she not know and still ask about it?","This Duchess of Qin'an didn't seem like a fool, so why was she deliberately jabbing at the Empress Dowager's sore spot?","Suddenly, Yanshu heard a ding from her system, [That's right, these sisters have been competing and fighting since childhood, neither submitting to the other. The elder sister married the Marquis of Qin'an back then, thinking she had surpassed her younger sister, but she never expected the Empress Dowager to later marry the late emperor, putting her back down again. However, after the Empress Dowager's eldest son died young, this elder sister thought she had won over the Empress Dowager.]","Yanshu clicked her tongue upon hearing this, [No wonder she brought up her grandson right away. This is a fatal blow! Isn't she afraid the Empress Dowager will deal with her?]","The system sighed, [The Empress Dowager is indeed very annoyed by this elder sister, but she has no choice. If she were to move against her, the Zhou family would lose another supporter. For the sake of family interests, she has to endure it.]","Yanshu sighed at this, thinking that the Empress Dowager was truly not having an easy time, surrounded by such unhelpful people.","But this Duchess of Qin'an was also too much. No matter how much they competed, the Empress Dowager was still their support, and there was still a layer of kinship. How could she use someone's most painful matter to stab at their heart?","The system sighed again, [This woman has always been like this. It's precisely because she's too harsh and domineering that her relationship with Duke Qin'an has never been good. Her son is also weak, not daring to intervene even though he knows his wife is having an affair with a servant in the household.]","Yanshu, [There's even such an interesting story???]"]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46","paragraphs":["Upon hearing the system's words, Yanshu immediately glanced at Lady Yue, who was sitting obediently beside the Duchess of Qin'an.","[You're saying it's this Lady Yue who's fooling around with the servants?]","The system replied, [The Duchess of Qin'an gave birth to one son and one daughter. The son is Qiao Yongkang, the heir of Qin'an Duke, and he married Lady Yue. Who else could it be?]","Yanshu asked again, [But, but, her husband is at least the heir, and his body has no problems. Why would she fool around with servants?]","— Tsk, back then Lady Yang, who had an affair with her father-in-law, the Minister of Rites, did so because her husband was in poor health. She got involved with her father-in-law to secure benefits for herself.","But this Lady Yue is already in such a high position, why bother fooling around with servants?","The system explained, [The heir of Qin'an Duke was raised too strictly by his mother since childhood. As a result, he grew up lacking ambition, incompetent in both civil and military affairs, but obsessed with carpentry. He spends all day tinkering with wood, and is as dull as a log, with no sense of romance. He's also round and fat. Lady Yue can't stand him. As it happens, there's a tall, handsome coachman in the household who knows how to charm women. Lady Yue couldn't resist the loneliness and had an affair.]","So it was the coachman.","Yanshu suddenly understood.","After thinking for a moment, she asked again, [But how does she manage to have an affair? The Qin'an Duke's mansion is full of people, and she has such a formidable mother-in-law as the Duchess. How does she find the opportunity?]","The system sighed, [As they say, where there's a will, there's a way. Lady Yue is very good at pleasing her mother-in-law. Plus, her husband is the Duchess's only son, so naturally, she's valued. The Duchess entrusts many household affairs to her. When Lady Yue goes out to inspect the farms, check on the shops, or attend social events, doesn't she always ride in a carriage?]","Carriage?","Yanshu couldn't help but exclaim, what a convenient carriage!","These two even have a ready-made place, how convenient indeed.","After her exclamation, she asked again, [So how did her husband find out about her affair with the coachman?]","The system explained, [That Qiao Yongkang, the heir of Qin'an Duke, likes to work with wood, right? Over the years, he's made all the beds, wardrobes, tables, and chairs in the house. Now he's started repairing things. One time, he heard that his wife's carriage was broken, so he personally took his tools to check it out. To his surprise, he discovered that the axle was broken.]","[You should know, the axles of the carriages in the Qin'an Duke's mansion are all made of the best elm wood, extremely hard. How could it break so easily? It must have been subjected to great impacts over a long period to break.]","What?","Long-term great impacts!","Yanshu's eyes lit up again.","[Tsk tsk tsk, it seems this coachman has great stamina. No wonder Lady Yue wanted to have an affair... Then what?]","The system continued, [Qiao Yongkang may be obsessed with carpentry, but he's not stupid. He's also an expert in the field, so he naturally noticed something was wrong. The next time his wife went out, he secretly had someone follow her, and that's how he discovered it.]","Yanshu silently gasped, then asked, [And then?]","The system replied, [Nothing much after that. If there was, would the Duchess of Qin'an still be bragging about her daughter-in-law in front of the Empress Dowager today?]","Tsk, that's true. Judging from today's situation, it's clear that the Duchess of Qin'an is still unaware.","Just then, the Empress Dowager, who had been stung by her elder cousin's words, smiled faintly and said, [The palace is still the same as before. I don't have your good fortune.]","The Duchess of Qin'an then said, \"I wouldn't dare say so, Your Majesty. It's just that your destined match hasn't arrived yet. Besides, what fortune do I have? It's just that my son Yongkang is lucky to have married a good wife.\"","After speaking, she glanced at Lady Yue and introduced her to the Empress Dowager, \"Last year, Yongkang's wife was heavily pregnant, and I didn't dare let her travel on the bumpy roads, so we left her at home. She couldn't come to wish Your Majesty a happy birthday in person. Now that the child has been born, I've brought her along.\"","Then she instructed Lady Yue, \"Quickly, come and pay your respects to the Empress Dowager.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu pondered in her heart—","[...So Lady Yue didn't come last year? Goodness, with no one watching at home, didn't she go wild?]","The system replied, [Not really, she was pregnant at that time.]","Yanshu, [That's true...]","Wait a minute!","She suddenly realized a problem—","When did Lady Yue start her affair with the coachman?","The Duchess of Qin'an had personally introduced earlier that among this bunch of children, the seven-year-old boy Qiao Wanheng, the five-year-old girl Qiao Nianrou, and the youngest baby were her grandchildren.","In other words, all three were born to Lady Yue.","So... how many of them were actually the heir's?","The system said, [Although Lady Yue fooled around, she's not stupid. She used sheepskin condoms every time, so all three children are still the heir Qiao Yongkang's.]","What?","Yanshu once again accurately grasped the key point, [Sheepskin condoms? There's such a thing?]","Tsk tsk tsk, this is truly eye-opening!","The system explained, [Sheepskin condoms are quite common. Many people use them in this era, but they're not very hygienic. There's a risk of catching some disease or something.]","Yanshu, \"...\"","Maybe it's better to forget about that...","Just then, Lady Yue, hearing her mother-in-law's words, stood up and came before the Empress Dowager to pay her respects properly.","\"I wasn't able to personally wish Your Majesty a happy birthday last year. I hope Your Majesty will forgive me. I humbly wish Your Majesty blessings as vast as the Eastern Sea and longevity as enduring as the Southern Mountains.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded with a smile, \"Good child, truly graceful and virtuous, very much in the style of your mother-in-law.\"","Hearing this, Lady Yue quickly lowered her head in gratitude and said, \"These years, I've been blessed with mother-in-law's deep love, treating me like her own daughter. I've taken all of mother-in-law's earnest teachings to heart.\"","Yanshu, \"...\"","Tsk tsk tsk, the Empress Dowager's words were actually meant to mock her elder cousin, but this heir's wife sure knows how to seize an opportunity!","No wonder she can win her mother-in-law's favor.","But come to think of it...","She felt that the Duchess of Qin'an's praising of her daughter-in-law today wasn't simply to show off to the Empress Dowager.","Could there be something else?","Just as she was thinking this, the youngest baby of the Qiao family suddenly started crying, rubbing his eyes and kicking his legs in a very fussy manner.","The Empress Dowager said, \"Is the child tired? It's not easy for little ones to travel such a long way to the capital with adults. Let's end here for today. Quickly, take the little one back to rest.\"","Everyone agreed, stood up together to bow and bid farewell, and finally dispersed.","Returning to Ganlu Palace, it was nearly noon.","Yanshu changed her clothes, had lunch, and without even taking an afternoon nap, hurriedly sat at the table to write her story—","It would be a waste not to write about such an interesting material she had obtained today.","She was fully immersed and extremely focused, even having dinner in a hurry.","When night fell and Yuwen Lan entered the hall, he saw that she was still writing.","Yuwen Lan asked curiously, \"What story have you written today? You seem so engrossed?\"","Could something he didn't know about have happened again?","Yanshu was just wanting to share with him, and upon hearing his question, she immediately said, \"Today, I wrote a story called 'The Flirtatious Wife Loses Her Golden Husband'.\"","Hm?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and said, \"'Flirtatious wife' refers to a fickle woman?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"That's right.\"","He nodded slightly, \"This kind of theme seems quite novel. What's it about?\"","Yanshu cleared her throat and said, \"This is a story about a male protagonist's counterattack.\"","Just as she said this, Yuwen Lan had another question.","He could guess that \"male protagonist\" referred to the main male character in the story.","But what did \"counterattack\" mean?","So he asked her, \"What does 'counterattack' mean?\"","Yanshu explained, \"Counterattack refers to — someone who was originally in an adverse or disadvantaged situation, struggles upward, breaks free from constraints, and finally surpasses others to become the winner.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"This expression is indeed quite novel.\"","After saying this, he didn't ask any more questions, just waiting for her to continue.","Yanshu then said, \"The story is about a young master, born into wealth, but with a calm and leisurely nature. Unfortunately, his family had high expectations for him, forcing him to do things he didn't like. The young master was full of bitterness from childhood to adulthood, but didn't dare to disobey his parents. He could only engage in handicrafts to express his inner sorrow.\"","\"As he reached marriageable age, his parents carefully selected a seemingly virtuous and proper young woman for him. Being naive by nature, after marriage, the young master treated his wife with respect and kindness. However, his wife had actually married him for his family's power and influence, not out of genuine affection.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Men pursuing women for their beauty, and women pursuing men for their power - these are common occurrences.\"","Yanshu continued, \"Shortly after the marriage, his wife gave birth to a son and a daughter. The young master was overjoyed to become a father and lovingly crafted many toys for the children to play with. However, what was meant to be fatherly affection was seen by his wife as a lack of ambition. Gradually, she even began an affair with one of the household servants.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","This was an unexpected turn of events.","He had assumed the woman would be like the former Linwu Marquis's wife, associating with various wealthy and powerful men. How did it end up being a servant?","He couldn't help but ask, \"What was so appealing about this servant that made her betray her husband?\"","Yanshu replied, \"This servant had a silver tongue and was very skilled at manipulating women's emotions. Most importantly, he had a good physique that could satisfy the woman's needs.\"","At first, Yuwen Lan didn't quite understand. He frowned and said, \"A good physique... is that really a reason? Was the husband's physique not good?\"","Yanshu nodded firmly, \"Of course a good physique is important. That servant had broad shoulders, a slim waist, and six-pack abs. In comparison, the young master had been plump since childhood and would get out of breath doing any physical labor...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So that's what \"physical labor\" meant.","He finally understood that women placed such importance on this...","At the same time, he became curious - who exactly was this story about?","Just as he was pondering this, he heard her thoughts: [I wonder what that coachman from the Qin'an Duke's household looks like? Driving carriages all day, he's probably not fair-skinned, but more of a tanned and muscular type.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","The Qin'an Duke's household?","...Alright, he probably knew who it was now.","Just this morning, Qiao Beiwang, the Duke of Qin'an, had brought his son and son-in-law to pay respects to him. Wasn't his son Qiao Yongkang quite plump?","So it was about them.","Tsk, was that family really so chaotic?","However, the Qin'an Duke's family had just arrived in the capital. How did she already know such secrets?","He asked, \"Then what? Did the husband find out his wife was having an affair?\"","She nodded, \"He did find out, but because of his weak nature, he didn't dare expose it. He just covered his eyes and pretended not to know, continuing to live as before.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What a character, to be able to endure even this.","\"What happened next?\"","Yanshu continued, \"At first, this young master allowed the two to carry on their affair in the household, still fantasizing that his wife would one day come to her senses. However, little did he know that the two were no longer satisfied with the status quo and wanted to be together forever. So they plotted to poison the entire family.\"","\"It was only at this point that the young master realized that tolerance was not the answer. He finally fought back, killing the adulterer, divorcing his wife, and dealing with all the servants who had helped the two cover up their affair. Afterwards, he turned over a new leaf, dedicating himself to learning from others, and even found time to exercise, shedding his excess fat and regaining his handsome appearance.\"","\"When the ex-wife saw that her former husband had transformed into a handsome gentleman, she instantly regretted her actions and foolishly hoped to reconcile with him. However, by then the young master no longer wanted her. She could only end up homeless on the streets, living a miserable life.\"","The story ended there.","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"The ending is quite satisfying. It's your style.\"","But as soon as he finished speaking, he realized another issue -","He remembered that the Qin'an Duke's heir had two sons and one daughter, right?","So he tentatively asked, \"Whose children were they?\"","Yanshu coughed, \"Let's just say they were his. After all, he had raised them for so many years and developed feelings for them. It's best not to involve the children.\"","Tsk tsk, this point should be based on facts.","After all, if the story is published and the truth comes to light one day, it would be terrible if the Qiao family were to take out their anger on the innocent children.","Yuwen Lan silently listened, thinking to himself that the children must indeed be Qiao Yongkang's.","Tsk, it's still too messy!","After pondering for a while, he felt a bit scared.","Fortunately, he wasn't round and fat. In the future, he must remember to always maintain his physical fitness.","Just as he was thinking this, he saw Yanshu yawn in front of him, her almond eyes welling up with tears.","Yuwen Lan said, \"Write more tomorrow.\"","He coughed and added with a meaningful gaze, \"It's late, we should sleep.\"","Yanshu was taken aback.","...If we're going to sleep, why say it in such an ambiguous way?","Tsk, could it be that he... wants to again?","Yuwen Lan, who had secretly heard her thoughts, coughed and said in a low voice, \"I'll go bathe first.\"","After speaking, he held back the redness threatening to spread to his ears and turned to enter the bathroom.","Yanshu: \"...\"","She could only silently look at her delicate hands and sigh helplessly.","Tsk, if she had known earlier, she wouldn't have let him know about this method.","There were still more than ten days left, how long it seemed!","Since the Qin'an Duke's family were imperial relatives who had come from afar, and they were the first batch of guests to arrive in the capital for the Empress Dowager's birthday celebration, the palace held a welcoming banquet for the whole family the next day.","This family was considered part of the external relatives, and with both men and women present, they could not sit in the same hall.","However, before the banquet began, they entered the palace and needed to pay their respects to the Empress Dowager, the Emperor, and the imperial consorts.","Everyone saw that apart from the old couple of the Duke of Qin'an, their eldest son and daughter, daughter-in-law, son-in-law, and grandchildren who had come to pay respects yesterday, there was a new face today.","It was a young woman, about seventeen or eighteen years old, whose features somewhat resembled those of Lady Yue, the wife of the Duke of Qin'an's heir.","After everyone had paid their respects, the Duchess of Qin'an brought this girl forward and said to the Emperor and Empress Dowager, \"This is Yongkang's wife's younger sister from her maiden family. Knowing that her sister would have difficulty managing three children on this trip to the capital, she voluntarily came along to help. Yesterday, when we first entered the palace, I was afraid she might be unfamiliar with the surroundings, so I didn't dare bring her along. Today, I've boldly brought her to pay respects to the Empress Dowager, Your Majesty, and all the imperial consorts.\"","She then instructed the young girl, \"Quickly pay your respects to the noble ones.\"","The Yue family girl immediately stepped forward and bowed, saying, \"This commoner pays respects to Your Majesty, to the Empress Dowager, and to all the imperial consorts.\"","Her voice was sweet and delicate, like a painted oriole from a book.","Looking at her appearance, she did indeed have some charm.","Seeing this scene, everyone pondered inwardly.","The younger sister of the daughter-in-law's maiden family? This relationship wasn't particularly close.","Moreover, couldn't the Duke of Qin'an's household afford to hire a wet nurse? Why bring an unmarried young girl to help take care of the children?","Yanshu inwardly clicked her tongue -","No wonder the Duchess of Qin'an had been praising her daughter-in-law so much yesterday. So this was her attempt to place someone in the palace.","By elevating the elder sister, wouldn't the younger sister from the same family naturally attract attention?","However, if that was the case, her offending the Empress Dowager was quite peculiar.","The Empress Dowager probably wouldn't like this Yue family girl either, considering her sister's behavior.","Sure enough, the Empress Dowager nodded slightly, but then smiled and said, \"For an unmarried young lady to help others take care of children is indeed quite a burden on you.\"","The Yue family girl hesitated slightly, then could only say, \"Being able to help my sister is what I should do.\"","In her heart, she thought, [Hmph, if I didn't come, how would I be able to see His Majesty? Oh my, His Majesty is even more handsome than the rumors say!]","[But those three consorts behind him... Never mind, I've heard that Consort Zhou has long fallen out of favor, and that Consort Wang who keeps night watch has become a laughingstock in the palace. The remaining one must be Noble Consort Yi.]","Thinking this, she secretly glanced at Yanshu with her peripheral vision, thinking, [She doesn't seem all that impressive. I've heard her family background isn't even as good as our Yue family. She definitely won't be my rival in the future.]","Yuwen Lan, who had been silently listening, thought: \"???\"","What future?","Where did this confidence come from?","Next, he heard the Duchess of Qin'an thinking, [Zhou Ruolan has no one left by her side who can be of use. If she's smart, she should take this girl into the palace and groom her well. After all, she has some connection to the Zhou family, which is still better than that Noble Consort Yi.]","Yuwen Lan just wanted to scoff.","No wonder the Empress Dowager said she was annoying.","He tried to listen to the Empress Dowager's thoughts and heard her secretly laughing coldly.","[What kind of dream is Zhou Shulan having? Trying to place someone right under my nose, does she think I'm stupid? Haha.]","Yuwen Lan felt slightly relieved. Thankfully, the Empress Dowager didn't think that way.","After paying their respects, the men and women went to their respective banquet halls.","As the Duke of the Northwest, Duke Qin'an held an extraordinary status. Apart from being personally entertained by the Emperor, several ministers from the court were also present at the banquet to accompany him.","Perhaps due to their familial connection, the ministers quickly noticed that the monarch was particularly warm towards Duke Qin'an's family tonight.","They couldn't help but actively invite Duke Qin'an to drink, expressing their concern for the hardships of guarding the Northwest in their conversations, and showing extra care for Duke Qin'an's heir, Qiao Yongkang.","For instance, after two rounds of drinks, the monarch proactively inquired, \"Cousin Yongkang, what have you been busy with these past few years?\"","This question caused everyone to pause.","— Did His Majesty just address him as 'cousin'?","Naturally, Qiao Yongkang himself was even more surprised by this honor. He hurriedly stood up and said, \"Your humble servant is unworthy. I have achieved nothing in these years, truly failing to deserve Your Majesty's concern.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Duke Qin'an also hastily added, \"He has never had much ambition, making himself a laughingstock before Your Majesty.\"","This was indeed the truth. Hearing this, the ministers all shook their heads inwardly —","The first Marquis of Qin'an was once a renowned military general, ennobled for his numerous battle achievements and tasked with guarding the Northwest for the imperial court. Later, his son was fortunate enough to marry the Empress Dowager's cousin, conveniently elevating their status to Duke. By Qiao Yongkang's generation, they had lost all their capabilities.","It was said that he was completely oblivious to the affairs of the world, only interested in woodworking. He was truly an oddity among the sons of noble families.","However, at this moment, the monarch spoke up, \"Do not belittle yourself. I've heard your craftsmanship is excellent. This too requires skill and attention to detail. Without sufficient patience, it cannot be accomplished.\"","Upon hearing this, Qiao Yongkang was first stunned, then nearly moved to tears.","— Everyone in this world looked down on him. His mother had scolded him since childhood, his father favored his half-brother, and even his wife was openly unfaithful to him...","Yet His Majesty understood him so well!!!","His Majesty's words were so apt. Woodworking was indeed a meticulous craft. How could anyone careless accomplish it?","His Majesty understood him, and that made everything worthwhile!","Excited, he raised his cup and drank one after another, experiencing for the first time in his life such unbridled joy!","...","While the emperor and his officials were drinking merrily in Xiangyun Hall, the atmosphere among the female guests, where Yanshu was seated, was rather peculiar.","— Presumably wanting to leave a good impression of being virtuous and capable on the Empress Dowager, whenever the Empress Dowager praised a dish, the Yue family's daughter would voluntarily explain how to prepare it, from ingredient selection to knife skills to cooking time, speaking knowledgeably about every aspect.","After she had explained five or six dishes, even the Empress Dowager couldn't help but say, \"For one so young, you are remarkably proficient in culinary arts. It's truly rare.\"","Upon hearing this, Lady Yue, the wife of Duke Qin'an's heir, immediately thanked the Empress Dowager on her sister's behalf and volunteered an explanation, \"My younger sister has been particularly sensible since childhood, often helping our mother manage household affairs. She learned culinary skills early on to serve our parents' meals.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded approvingly again, \"What a filial and good child.\"","The Yue family's daughter immediately expressed her gratitude, \"This humble subject thanks the Empress Dowager for her praise.\"","Seeing this, the Duchess of Qin'an revealed a satisfied smile, while Consort Zhou's eyes were practically shooting fire.","However, due to the presence of the Empress Dowager, she dared not act rashly.","Only Yanshu, unconcerned with the affairs of others, focused on eating, inwardly praising —","Mmm, tonight's dishes are really excellent!","The crystal chicken was delicious and crispy, the cherry pork was rich in flavor, the snow flower chicken was tender yet slightly chewy, seemingly even better than before.","Of course, the best was still the hanging oven roast duck.","It truly deserved its reputation as the capital's number one dish, delicious every time!","Taking a piece of fragrant golden-brown duck meat, adding some sweet bean sauce, along with fresh green onions and cucumber strips, all wrapped in a thin pancake — one bite was simply heavenly.","However, just as she was immersed in the delectable flavors, a young eunuch hurriedly ran into the hall and said to the Duchess of Qin'an and her daughter-in-law, \"The young master has drunk too much at the banquet in Xiangyun Hall. His Majesty requests that you both go to check on him.\"","This announcement startled everyone.","What? Duke Qin'an's heir had drunk too much?","And at a royal banquet where the Emperor was still present?","The Duchess of Qin'an was also stunned. After recovering, she quickly tried to save face, smiling as she said, \"This child usually doesn't like to drink. How did he end up drinking too much tonight?\"","The Empress Dowager also said to the reporting eunuch, \"It's just a bit of alcohol. Can't someone support him to rest for a while?\"","But the young eunuch shook his head awkwardly, \"Your Highness is unaware, the young master is currently sobbing loudly before His Majesty. No one can stop him, and he keeps shouting about divorcing his wife...\"","What?","Divorce?","Everyone's eyes widened instantly.","— What was going on?"]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47","paragraphs":["What? Divorce his wife?","As soon as the Little Eunuch said this, everyone was stunned.","Yanshu also forgot about the roast duck she had just rolled up, and quickly looked up.","What was going on?","That Prince of Qin'an, who had known he'd been wearing a green hat for a long time, actually wanted to divorce his wife?","And right now in the palace???","... Had she missed something important???","Of course, at this moment, the most shocked people in the hall were none other than the Duchess of Qin'an and her daughter-in-law, Lady Yue.","Hearing this, the Duchess of Qin'an was stunned for a moment before saying, \"How could this child be so drunk and confused? What nonsense is he speaking?\"","Looking at Lady Yue, her face was already full of embarrassment.","With a mix of embarrassment and grievance, she looked at her mother-in-law and said, \"Mother, how could the Prince be so drunk?\"","The Empress Dowager was also curious and asked, \"Ah Kang has always been an honest child since he was young. How did he suddenly start saying such things?\"","The Little Eunuch who came to report looked troubled and said, \"This servant doesn't know either. Please forgive me, Your Majesty.\"","Seeing this situation, the Empress Dowager had no choice but to look at the mother and daughter-in-law pair and say, \"Alright, since His Majesty has spoken, you two should go and take a look.\"","The two women had no choice but to agree and were about to get up.","But then they heard the Empress Dowager instruct the palace maid Lan He, who was attending the banquet beside her, \"You go with them and take a look too.\"","Lan He agreed and accompanied the two women.","As a result, only the Empress Dowager, Yanshu, Consort Zhou, Consort Wang, Duke Qin'an's daughter Lady Qiao, and the Yue Family Daughter who had come to the palace with her sister remained at the banquet.","Yanshu also quite admired this young lady. Lady Qiao was at least the Empress Dowager's cousin's daughter, so they had something to talk about, but she was just someone who came to the palace with her sister for a free meal. Even though her sister had left, she could still sit there comfortably.","Tsk, she was indeed a person with great ambition.","However...","She herself was feeling a bit restless.","What on earth had happened in Xiangyun Hall?","The Prince of Qin'an actually wanted to divorce his wife?","Based on her years of experience in observing drama, something big was definitely about to happen!","There might be some exciting scenes coming up...","She really wanted to go and see for herself!!!","Thinking this way, even the roast duck in her hand didn't seem appetizing anymore.","She forced herself to drink another bowl of sour, spicy, and delicious fish soup, when she saw Lan He hurrying back, panting as she reported to the Empress Dowager, \"Your Majesty, it's, it's not good. As soon as the Prince of Qin'an saw his wife, he immediately rushed over and grabbed her neck, saying he wanted to kill her... His Majesty requests your presence as well.\"","What?!!!","Everyone in the hall exclaimed almost in unison.","Only Yanshu's eyes immediately lit up — sure enough, her guess wasn't wrong, it was already this exciting!!!","The Empress Dowager also said, \"How could this be? Quick, prepare the sedan chair!\"","After speaking, she hurriedly got up to go to Xiangyun Hall.","Seeing this situation, Lady Qiao, as the sister, naturally couldn't sit still either and quickly followed the Empress Dowager.","The Yue Family Daughter had no choice but to regretfully get up and follow Lady Qiao as well.","As a result, there were hardly any people left at the banquet.","Yanshu was extremely excited in her heart. She glanced at the remaining Consort Zhou and Consort Wang, and seeing that the two were also getting up to leave, she quickly and quietly followed the Empress Dowager and the others.","— Wow~~","Anyway, Xiangyun Hall was probably in chaos, one more person wouldn't make a difference!","When Yanshu arrived with the large group of people, she saw that Prince of Qin'an Qiao Yongkang was being held back by people, his round face as red as a cooked shrimp, indeed looking very drunk.","His wife, Lady Yue, was hiding behind her mother-in-law crying, with a ring of red marks on her neck.","Duke Qin'an was so angry that he stepped forward and slapped his son twice, scolding, \"You rascal, how dare you be so unruly in front of His Majesty? Just a few cups of wine and you've forgotten where you are?\"","The Duchess of Qin'an also went to scold her son, \"That's right, and what nonsense are you spouting? What divorce, not divorce!\"","At these words, Lady Yue cried even louder.","However, when that crying sound reached his ears, Qiao Yongkang suddenly shouted, \"You don't know anything! Do you know how much I've been suffering!\"","As he finished speaking, he saw the Empress Dowager entering the hall. Qiao Yongkang suddenly rushed over and knelt in front of the Empress Dowager, crying.","\"Please, Aunt, do justice for your nephew...\"","The Empress Dowager was startled and quickly said, \"What's going on? What's there for a grown man to cry about? If you have something to say, say it properly.\"","Then Qiao Yongkang suddenly pointed at his wife Lady Yue and said, \"Empress Dowager, you don't know, this woman is a slut! She's been having an affair with the carriage driver Old Three for several years behind my back! I thought of the three children and wanted to give her a chance, but she doesn't know how to restrain herself at all, and has become more and more outrageous. Even on this trip to the capital, she didn't forget to fool around with that Old Three, Aunt...\"","What?","An affair???","These words not only stunned the Empress Dowager and all the ministers attending the banquet in the hall, but also completely froze Duke Qin'an and his wife, as well as everyone from their household.","Yanshu couldn't help but widen her eyes and exclaim inwardly, \"Oh my goodness!\"","This guy actually exposed everything!!!","Tsk tsk, exciting, exciting, it was worth coming!!!","Looking at Lady Yue again, she saw that she was also stunned, even forgetting to cry for a moment, staring at her husband with wide eyes.","Everyone in the hall seemed to have been struck dumb, looking at the couple.","After a moment, the Duchess of Qin'an was the first to react, embarrassedly scolding her son, \"What drunken nonsense are you talking about! Shut your mouth right now!!!\"","But Qiao Yongkang continued to shout, \"I'm not talking nonsense! Why don't you believe me, Mother? I've become the laughingstock of the whole world because of this woman, and you still don't believe me!!!\"","This cry contained years of his grievances, and the Duchess of Qin'an was startled by the shout.","After taking two deep breaths and coming back to her senses, she was about to scold him again.","However, before she could open her mouth, she saw her son crawl in front of the Emperor again, crying, \"Your Majesty, please listen to your subject's advice, you can't have women from the Yue family, they are all fickle and unfaithful, you absolutely can't have them!!!\"","Seeing this situation, the Duchess of Qin'an's body swayed, and she nearly fainted.","Duke Qin'an also hurriedly stepped forward and scolded, \"How dare you offend His Majesty like this? Come back and behave yourself immediately!\"","At this moment, they heard the Emperor speak, \"Wait.\"","Yuwen Lan looked at the Empress Dowager and said, \"Cousin Yongkang has always been gentle and honest. For him to be like this today, I feel it's unusual. Could there really be some problem?\"","At these words, Qiao Yongkang cried again, \"Your Majesty understands me, only Your Majesty understands me! Your Majesty!!!\"","That loud voice made the entire hall tremble.","Those who didn't know might think something had happened to the Emperor.","The Empress Dowager smoothed her startled heart, which was jumping wildly, before nodding and saying, \"Indeed, this child has been honest since he was young. How could he suddenly be like this today? Could it be that he's really been wronged badly? In my opinion, we should have someone investigate.\"","As soon as these words fell, Lady Yue paused, then suddenly cried out, \"This subject's wife has no face to see anyone...\"","As she spoke, she actually ran towards a nearby pillar, looking as if she was going to dramatically prove her innocence.","Fortunately, guards stopped her, preventing her from actually hitting the pillar.","Seeing this, Yanshu secretly shook her head and clicked her tongue —","The way she cried, one might think she was really wronged if they didn't know better.","However, the Empress Dowager probably wouldn't fall for this trick.","Sure enough, seeing this situation, the Empress Dowager immediately darkened her face and rebuked, \"Do you know where this is? How dare you act like this in front of His Majesty? If blood were to be spilled here, whose eyes would it offend?\"","At these words, Lady Yue was immediately so frightened that she dared not make a sound. Instead, her sister stepped forward and said to the Empress Dowager, \"Please calm your anger, Your Majesty. My sister has been wrongly accused and has grievances she can't express...\"","The Empress Dowager coldly laughed and said, \"Whether she's been wrongly accused or not, someone will clear her name!\"","Saying this, she instructed the person beside her, \"Nanny Zhuang, you take some people to help Duke Qin'an investigate. Things have come to this today, whether Ah Kang's words are true or not, we need an explanation!\"","Nanny Zhuang immediately agreed.","As soon as these words fell, Lady Yue, who had just been seeking death, suddenly collapsed on the ground, her face drained of all color, and it was impossible to tell whether she was scared or grieved.","The Duchess of Qin'an was extremely embarrassed and could only bow to the Empress Dowager and say, \"Thank you for your grace, Empress Dowager.\"","Turning her head to look, she saw that her son was still kneeling in front of the Emperor, wailing loudly, with snot and tears already covering the ground.","Everyone: \"...\"","Duke Qin'an suppressed his anger and led his daughter and son-in-law to drag him back.","He then said to the Emperor and Empress Dowager, \"It's my fault for failing to teach my son properly. We've disturbed the nobles today and made all the officials laugh at us. I will take him back and teach him a good lesson.\"","After speaking, he dragged his son out of the hall.","Seeing this situation, the Duchess of Qin'an could only kowtow to the Emperor and Empress Dowager, then slink away in embarrassment.","After watching the spectacle, the ministers also bid farewell to the Emperor and Empress Dowager one by one, gradually exiting the hall.","Yanshu, feeling satisfied, also took the opportunity to slip out of the hall, inwardly marveling that it was indeed worth coming!","The Duchess of Qin'an had calculated everything, but she never anticipated this turn of events. Now she had truly run afoul of the Empress Dowager.","Estimating that Nanny Zhuang wouldn't go easy, who knows how much more would be uncovered, tsk tsk.","Get ready to keep watching the drama unfold!","Hearing her voice, Yuwen Lan quickly raised his eyes to look, but only caught a glimpse of the hem of a horse-face skirt.","He smiled gently.","He knew she would come.","It must be said that as the Empress Dowager's capable deputy, Nanny Zhuang did have some skills.","Although the Duke Qin'an's mansion was a thousand miles away, she directly targeted Lady Yue's maid, having her arrested and interrogated under torture.","In just half a day, the other party confessed to Lady Yue's affair with the coachman Bao Laosan.","It was only at this point that the Duke and Duchess of Qin'an realized their son had not been lying.","It turned out that their seemingly virtuous and capable daughter-in-law had been carrying on with a servant in the household for over two years.","Their son had discovered the affair a year ago but, fearing their reproach, had not dared to speak up, keeping it to himself until today when it all came to a head.","The couple was both angry and furious, at a loss for words for a moment.","...","After helping the Qiao family uncover the truth, early the next morning, Nanny Zhuang returned to the palace to report to the Empress Dowager.","The Duke and Duchess of Qin'an also came to the palace together to apologize to the Emperor and Empress Dowager for the incident at yesterday's banquet.","At that time, Yuwen Lan was busy, so he asked the Empress Dowager to receive the couple on his behalf.","So the couple went directly to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","They bowed together to the Empress Dowager, and Duke Qin'an said with a shameful face, \"This old minister has failed to manage his household and educate his son properly. Yesterday's incident startled Your Highness, His Majesty, and the other ladies. It is truly a grave offense. Please punish us, Your Highness.\"","The Duchess of Qin'an also said, \"This minister's wife was blind and allowed such a scandal to occur in our household. Please forgive us, Your Highness.\"","The Empress Dowager cast her gaze from her seat, saying, \"Sister, you are an intelligent person. How could you let such a woman bully Akang like that? Such an honest person normally, yet yesterday he cried so miserably, saying no one would stand up for him... It's not that I'm meddling, but how have you two been parenting?\"","Duke Qin'an could only bow his head, \"It is this minister's incompetence that has made Your Highness laugh at us.\"","The Duchess of Qin'an also lowered her head and said, \"We have made Your Highness laugh at us.\"","As the words fell, Nanny Zhuang spoke from the side, \"Lady Yue's maid has already identified the two as having an affair, and the coachman has also confessed. How should they be dealt with now?\"","The Empress Dowager looked at the couple and said, \"This is your family matter. Go back and handle it yourselves.\"","The Duke and Duchess of Qin'an hurriedly agreed.","But then they heard the Empress Dowager add, \"However, in my opinion, for that adulterer to dare touch the mistress of the house, trampling the master's face underfoot, is truly outrageous and must not be lightly pardoned. As for Lady Yue...\"","The Empress Dowager looked at her cousin with a mocking smile and said, \"I see that you were quite fond of her, sister. Whether to keep her or not, you can decide for yourself.\"","Hearing this, the Duchess of Qin'an wished she could find a crack in the ground to crawl into.","But she could only endure the burning shame on her face and respond, \"This minister's wife failed to judge character correctly and has made Your Highness laugh. This minister's wife will go back and have Kang write a divorce letter immediately.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly and then dismissed them.","The next day, when Yanshu woke up, she heard the news about Duke Qin'an's family.","It was said that the Qiao family had sent their steward to report to the Capital Official, and the coachman who had touched the mistress was thrown into prison. The Prince of Qin'an had written a divorce letter and sent Lady Yue and her sister back to their maternal home a thousand miles away, cutting off all ties.","The old Duke and Duchess of Qin'an had originally suspected the bloodline of their grandchildren, but Qiao Yongkang was still kind-hearted and insisted on keeping the three children by his side.","However, the matter was now known to all, and because of their mother, these three children had become a stain on the Qiao family. The Duchess of Qin'an kept it hushed up and no longer dared to boast about them everywhere.","In her anger, she even fell ill.","When the Empress Dowager heard about it, she considered their family ties and sent an imperial physician to check her pulse.","...","After hearing the news, Yanshu couldn't help but sigh inwardly that the Empress Dowager had turned out to be the biggest winner in this affair!","However, after sighing, she suddenly realized a very important issue—","Damn it, before she had time to finish her new story, the ins and outs of this matter were already known to all.","In this case, her story would have no suspense to speak of...","How could she publish it now?","Alas! Didn't she waste half a day writing the day before yesterday?!","It was enough to make her spit blood with anger!!!","Yanshu brooded for a while, then suddenly thought of another important question—","That Prince of Qin'an had been wearing a green hat for so long, and had been enduring it all the time in the northwest, so why did he suddenly get drunk and expose everything yesterday?","Tsk, why does it feel like there's some conspiracy?","...","It was a busy day, and when Yuwen Lan entered the Ganlu Palace, Yanshu had already finished bathing.","Seeing the beauty with rosy cheeks and crimson lips, the Emperor's heart naturally fluttered. So he hurriedly went to undress and bathe, then embraced her and got into bed.","Just as he was about to kiss her, she blocked him with her hand and asked with a serious face, \"This concubine has a question to ask Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"What question?\"","He heard her say, \"This concubine has heard that the Prince of Qin'an has always been honest and simple, not one who likes to drink. How did he get drunk the day before yesterday when Your Majesty was still present?\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan paused imperceptibly.","Why did she suddenly think to ask this question now?","He said with an unchanged expression, \"Perhaps he was truly miserable in his heart. After all, people's endurance is limited. When the day comes that one really can't bear it anymore, it's bound to burst out. Just imagine, that pair of adulterers were still fooling around on their way to the capital, how painful must that have been for him? It just so happened that there was wine that day, so he couldn't help but drink too much.\"","This seemed to make some sense.","But Qiao Yongkang could have exploded at any time, why did he choose to do so at the palace banquet? Yanshu still felt it was too coincidental.","So she looked at him again and asked suspiciously, \"Really?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded with a frank face, \"Of course it's true. Do you think I would deliberately get him drunk?\"","Yanshu thought to herself that this was exactly what she suspected.","Tsk, she had wondered if he had guessed it was Qiao Yongkang after hearing her story, and for the sake of their cousin relationship, deliberately got him drunk to reveal the truth and then help him have a reason to divorce his wife.","But thinking about it again, she felt, could he be that kind-hearted?","Yuwen Lan silently listened and silently nodded in agreement.","He indeed wasn't that kind-hearted.","This time, he had merely seen that the Duchess of Qin'an was overreaching herself and wanted to teach her a lesson.","So he just helped Qiao Yongkang make a choice along the way.","But he was also a bit puzzled as to why she cared so much about this matter?","He had her come to the scene to watch the drama today, was she not happy?","So he tried asking, \"Why are you so hung up on this question? Does Qiao Yongkang getting drunk and causing a scene in the palace have any impact on you?\"","But he saw her looking angry as she said, \"Of course it has an impact.\"","\"The new story I mentioned to Your Majesty the day before yesterday, I didn't expect it to coincidentally clash with the Prince of Qin'an's affair. Now the whole capital has probably heard about it. In that case, hasn't my story missed its chance? There's no point in publishing it now.\"","— It should be known that the biggest feature of her stories was to shock people's eyes, so it had to be first-hand big news to work.","Who wants to read old news!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He really hadn't thought of this aspect.","He could only comfort her, saying, \"But since things are as they are now, just don't publish this one. Wait until you write something else, it's the same to publish then.\"","But he saw her still pouting, \"That's easy for you to say, but it's so hard for me to write one!\"","Tsk, if she had known this would happen, she might as well have stayed in bed for half a day.","All that hard work writing it out was just wasted!","Just thinking about it was infuriating!","Silently listening, Yuwen Lan felt a bit guilty.","Should he compensate her for the story's money?","But before he could speak, he heard her say, \"This incident happened while Your Majesty was entertaining him after all, so Your Majesty should bear some responsibility for my wasting a story, right?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He knew it.","She was an expert at extortion, did he need to worry about her?","So he asked, \"What do you want then?\"","Seeing her eyes dart mischievously, she smiled and said, \"Your humble consort hasn't thought of anything... just that, perhaps Your Majesty could compensate me for the lost silver from this novel?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","As expected, she still wanted money.","Very well, he nodded and said, \"Alright, I'll give you 100 taels of silver, consider it as if I've purchased this novel. How's that?\"","Well, he'd have to give it anyway, might as well take the initiative.","This way, she wouldn't hold any grudges, right?","To his surprise, she said, \"Your humble consort has been getting 120 taels for each novel lately...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What?","She was really haggling with him so meticulously?","Fortunately, she quickly added, \"But out of respect for Your Majesty, I won't ask for the extra. However... could Your Majesty grant your humble consort one request?\"","As she spoke, she batted her almond-shaped eyes, smiled sweetly, and leaned in close to him.","Yuwen Lan instantly caught a whiff of her delicate fragrance, and could feel her warmth as she drew near. He naturally pulled her into his arms and asked in a husky voice, \"What else do you want?\"","She smiled and said, \"Your humble consort wants to go out of the palace to eat something delicious...\"","—Ahem, last time on the way to Jifu Tower, she had spotted a Qingzhou restaurant on Four Corners Street that seemed quite popular.","That was the taste of her hometown! She had been craving it for so long!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","If it wasn't money, it was food.","He raised an eyebrow and gently tapped her nose, saying, \"Always thinking about leaving the palace, your heart has grown wild...\"","Before he could finish speaking, his lips were met with a kiss.","Light and fleeting, like a dragonfly skimming the water.","Yet it made his heart flutter.","Yuwen Lan's eyes suddenly darkened, and he was about to pursue her lips.","But she pulled back, covering her mouth and said, \"Only if you agree...\"","However, before she could finish, she was back in his arms.","He smiled faintly and said, \"You're the first to bargain with me like this.\"","With that, he removed her hand and finally kissed her properly.","...","Well, since she was the first, he would indulge her a bit.","It was no matter.","The next evening, no dinner was served in Ganlu Palace.","While others were having their evening meal, Yanshu had already changed her clothes and was sitting in a carriage with the emperor, leaving the palace gates.","Their destination was clear - the Qingzhou restaurant on Four Corners Street.","Four Corners Street was already a bustling area, and now that it was late spring and early summer, there were even more people out and about.","The two alighted from the carriage to see a scene of colorful lanterns and wine shops, a picture of prosperity.","After walking a short distance, they arrived at the Qingzhou restaurant, which was currently busy serving customers and quite lively.","Yanshu paid a premium to secure a private room. The two entered and sat down, then called for a waiter to order.","Since they were here for Qingzhou cuisine, naturally Yanshu would do the ordering.","She had already spotted some dishes when they entered, so she ordered the signature dishes that every table seemed to have: sweet and sour carp, braised pork intestines, and crispy stir-fried chicken gizzards and pork stomach.","Glancing at the menu, she saw they even had Ande's roast chicken, so she quickly ordered one of those as well.","Before long, the dishes were served.","Yanshu could hardly wait and immediately urged Yuwen Lan to start eating.","\"My lord, quickly try this sweet and sour carp. If this dish is done well, it means this restaurant is quite authentic,\" she said.","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and reached out with his chopsticks to taste it.","Hmm, the fish had a golden crispy exterior while maintaining the tenderness of the flesh inside, coated in a tangy sweet sauce. The taste was quite good.","Yuwen Lan sipped some tea to cleanse his palate, only to see that Yanshu had already started on the braised pork intestines.","Mmm, the outer layer of the intestines had a crispy fried texture, but the inside melted in the mouth, rich and flavorful, perfect with rice.","Seeing this, Yuwen Lan followed her lead and tried some of the intestines.","Before he could even swallow, he saw that she had already moved on to the crispy stir-fried dish.","Wow, the chicken gizzards and pork stomach had been sliced into flower shapes, allowing them to better absorb the seasonings. The chef's timing was perfect, resulting in a crispy yet tender texture that was salty, savory, and refreshing. Truly authentic.","Finally, the pièce de résistance was their Ande roast chicken.","The chicken was a glossy reddish-brown all over, and with a gentle tug, the meat fell off the bone. Upon tasting it, one could feel the fragrance permeating to the bone, extremely tender and flavorful.","Yanshu excitedly said to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, quickly try this! This is our Ande roast chicken, and this restaurant has made it very authentically!\"","Seeing her enthusiasm, Yuwen Lan pulled off a piece of chicken and tasted it. After trying it, he nodded, \"Indeed, it's quite good.\"","After speaking, he looked back at Yanshu, only to see that her eyes were glistening with unshed tears.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Was tasting her hometown flavors really so moving?","Indeed, Yanshu was overwhelmed with emotions at that moment.","In the past, because her father was an honest official, their family wasn't very well-off. Whenever she wanted to eat roast chicken, they had to wait until her father received his salary before they could afford to have it.","The last time she had eaten roast chicken was after she had been selected as a beauty and was about to leave home.","That day, her parents had bought her four roast chickens at once, thinking they might never see her again...","Fortunately, now her parents, brother, and grandmother had all come to the capital, and they could see each other from time to time.","...","Yuwen Lan, who had silently listened to her story, was quiet for a moment before suddenly calling out to someone outside, \"Bring two more roast chickens.\"","Seeing her surprised face, he said, \"If you like it, eat more. It's no problem.\"","It's just roast chicken, after all.","He could provide as much as she wanted.","And so, after polishing off the roast chickens, Yanshu's belly was round and full, and she had to lean on the wall to get out.","However, she was so happy tonight that she even had one more chicken packed up to take back for Renchong to try.","With their appetites satiated and hearts content, it was time to head back.","Yanshu rose with Yuwen Lan, ready to leave the private room.","The room was on the second floor, overlooking the street.","At this moment, she happened to glance out the window and saw an extremely luxurious carriage parked by the roadside.","The carriage compartment was adorned with jade, and the wheels were inlaid with brass, truly a sight of gold and jade splendor.","However, this style seemed somewhat familiar.","As she was wondering about this, she saw a group of people coming out of the Shenghe Residence across the street.","Leading the group was a woman who also looked familiar.","Yanshu quickly called to Yuwen Lan, \"My lord, isn't that the Eldest Princess?\"","The Eldest Princess?","Yuwen Lan also turned his gaze to the window.","Although the woman wasn't dressed as lavishly as she usually did when entering the palace, he was certain it was Yuwen Yan.","However, beside her was a man with a tall build and hair that seemed to have a brownish tint. From a distance, one could make out high cheekbones and deep-set eyes.","The two approached the carriage and got in together, then drove off.","He was still puzzled when he heard Yanshu exclaim, \"Has the Eldest Princess found a new favorite? He doesn't look like he's from the Central Plains, does he?\"","System: [That's right, the Eldest Princess's new favorite is the top courtesan from the Ruyi Brothel on Yang Lou Street, named Pan Zai'an, originally from Rouran.]","Yanshu's eyes widened, [Yang Lou Street's Ruyi Brothel? Isn't that the famous male brothel?]"]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan couldn't hear the system's voice, so at this moment he only heard this sentence—","\"Yanglou Street, Ruyi Brothel, the famous duck restaurant.\"","\"???\"","Duck restaurant?","They had just finished eating chicken, did she want to eat duck now?","...He wondered what kind of duck this Ruyi Brothel sold?","Roast duck? Braised duck?","Or perhaps salt-water duck?","How could duck be so famous?","Many questions flooded Yuwen Lan's mind, and just then, he heard a series of clicks coming from Yanshu's thoughts—","[Indeed, a woman's peak is still to be a princess! She can behead men at will, eat ducks whenever she wants, and even the top ones! I'm so envious!!!]","\"???\"","He couldn't help but raise an eyebrow secretly. It's just eating duck, why be so envious of Yuwen Yan?","So he spoke up, \"Are you still not full?\"","Yanshu, who was staring enviously in the direction of the Princess's departing carriage, absent-mindedly responded, \"No, this humble consort is already full.\"","Tsk, her stomach might be full, but her eyes were still so hungry.","She really wanted to see what that duck restaurant looked like...","Even if she couldn't eat, just looking would be fine, oh...","Yuwen Lan, who had been listening silently, \"...\"","It's just a place that sells duck, if you want to go, why not just go? Why act so pitiful?","He decided to take the initiative and said, \"I heard there's a good duck place on Yanglou Street, do you want to try it?\"","After all, she had been separated from her family for so long to enter the palace and be by his side, it really wasn't easy.","So after hearing her inner thoughts earlier, he decided that from now on, he would take good care of her, even better than her father, to give her a solid sense of security.","After such reflection, he saw Yanshu staring at him with wide almond eyes, full of surprise, stammering, \"Your, Your Majesty... you don't mean... a place called Ruyi Brothel?\"","[Could it be that he also knows it's a duck house???]","Yuwen Lan nodded lightly and said, \"I believe that's what it's called.\"","Ahem, although he had just learned about it, it wasn't too late.","So he added, \"If you want to go, I'll take you.\"","It's just a place that sells duck, how could it be so unattainable?","But he saw that she still looked surprised and cautious, \"I want to... but... can I really go?\"","Tsk, as if the duck there was something she could casually taste...","Yuwen Lan frowned and said, \"Why not? Let's go now.\"","With that, he directly pulled her out of the elegant room, down the stairs, and onto a carriage by the road. After giving instructions to the driver, they headed straight for Yanglou Street.","As the wheels rolled along, Yanshu felt both excited and skeptical.","—The Emperor actually wanted to take her to a duck house???","No matter how she thought about it, it seemed unbelievable.","Tsk, could this be a trap, waiting to see if she would be dazzled by the place and ignore him once they arrived?","Yuwen Lan, who was silently listening, \"???\"","Why would she think that?","It was just going to eat duck, would he really worry about being ignored by her?","But come to think of it, it wasn't the first or second time she had tricked him for food...","But that didn't matter, as the emperor, how could he quibble with his woman over such a small thing?","That was just food, while he was her husband.","Thinking this way, in the blink of an eye, they had arrived.","The two got off the carriage, and sure enough, there was a restaurant by the road with three large characters hanging at the entrance: \"Ruyi Brothel\".","Looking closer, it appeared very luxurious and obviously newer than the surrounding shops.","Yanshu was extremely excited inside.","The place she had been curious about for so long, today she could finally explore it!!!","What more could one ask for in life than to visit such a place once!!!","Yuwen Lan thought to himself, this shop seemed to have only been open for a few years, yet it could already make a name for itself in the capital?","It was well known that those famous shops often had decades or even centuries of heritage.","However...","Perhaps this place had some unique secret recipe?","In any case, since they were here, they might as well try it first.","Thinking this, he entered the shop with her.","After entering and looking around, Yuwen Lan was surprised again—","The interior decoration of this shop was even more luxurious than it appeared from the outside.","It could be said to be the most unique eatery he had ever seen.","—Unlike other restaurants filled with tables and chairs, this shop was full of potted plants, surrounded by artificial mountains and flowing water, and even had a wooden pavilion in the center.","A man was playing a seven-stringed zither there, dressed in white robes, with fair skin and hair loosely draped over his shoulders, his features somewhat effeminate.","Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow.","—This was the first time he had seen someone playing a seven-stringed zither in an eatery, and such a man at that.","Looking around again, he saw some tables and chairs arranged around the pavilion, all separated by specially carved wooden railings with gauze curtains hung on them, allowing only a vague glimpse of the diners' silhouettes inside, but not their features.","However, those who occasionally came out were always in pairs of one man and one woman.","It was completely unlike other eateries where diners gathered in groups of three or five, or seven or eight, with lively scenes of dice games and drinking contests.","Those women all wore veils or face coverings, their appearances unclear, but regardless of height or build, they were all dressed very luxuriously.","The men accompanying them were all in their early twenties, and all had strong, tall builds...","Especially... there was a strange fragrance wafting through the shop, clearly not the smell of food.","Yuwen Lan had already furrowed his brow.","—Why was this place so strange?","But looking beside him, he saw Yanshu peering around with wide eyes through her veil, inwardly clicking her tongue, [So this is what a duck house is like! The environment is indeed nice!!! Look at how well these private rooms are designed, no one can recognize anyone, it really protects privacy!]","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","What did she mean by \"privacy\"?","Before he could figure it out, he heard her say, [Tsk tsk, these men really do all have good physiques! Worthy of being the best in the capital! Oh? There are even really foreigners?]","Foreigners?","Yuwen Lan followed her gaze and indeed saw several men moving about the hall, all with high brows and deep-set eyes, their hair with a slight brownish tint.","He couldn't help but think of the man beside Yuwen Yan earlier...","Suddenly he felt something was amiss.","—This place was some distance from the Foreign Envoys' Hostel on Horse Market Street, how could there be so many foreigners here?","Just as he was puzzled, he saw a man passing by them, who stopped to look him over and asked, \"New here?\"","Yuwen Lan was stunned.","New here?","Is this how the waiters here greet customers?","Before he could speak, he saw the man look Yanshu over and then chuckle to him, \"You're lucky to be able to serve this madam today.\"","With that, he entered one of the screened compartments.","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","What did he mean by that?","Just as he was frowning, he heard a woman's voice from behind—","\"This one's not bad, what's the price?\"","Then, a plump, half-veiled woman came up to him, fanning herself with a feather fan, her eyes looking him up and down.","Another woman hurriedly followed, saying with a smile, \"This gentleman doesn't seem to be from our shop...\"","She also looked him over, suddenly revealing a look of amazement, \"Although not a foreigner, his build and looks are truly outstanding...\"","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","...These two actually dared to evaluate him like this???","At this moment, Yanshu suddenly stepped in front of him, saying very impolitely, \"This is my man, stay away.\"","As she spoke, she took off her veil hat and put it on his head.","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","And then, he heard the plump woman with the feather fan laugh and say, \"Miss, if you already have a man, why come here? Could it be you're here to show off? How about this, name your price, and lend me your man for one night.\"","What???","Name a price?","Lend him for one night???","This woman actually dared to say such a thing!!!","Yuwen Lan was furious, while Yanshu said again, \"Stay away, no one can have my man!\"","With that, she pulled him towards the exit, saying, \"Let's go, this place is not suitable for us.\"","Little did she know that as soon as she lifted her foot, the woman spoke again, \"Not enough? How about this - I'll make an offer. 500 silver taels, what do you say? The top courtesan here only costs 600 taels for a whole night. I'm not even asking for the whole night, just two hours and then I'll return him to you. How about it?\"","As the words fell, Yanshu paused in her steps.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What did this mean?","Surely she wouldn't sell him for money...","Fortunately, he saw her only turn back to give the woman a cold smile, saying, \"You think I need that 500 taels? Laughable! Even 50,000 taels wouldn't be enough!!!\"","With that, she continued pulling him towards the exit.","Yuwen Lan secretly let out a sigh of relief, feeling as if a great weight had been lifted.","However, the plump woman behind them still wouldn't give up. She snorted and said, \"You look young, but you've got quite the attitude! If you're not selling, why bring a man here? To make others envious???\"","Then she turned to the woman beside her and said, \"This Ruyi Brothel of yours is really getting out of hand! You said I could come see Zai'an, but then you let someone else take him away. Are you playing games with me?\"","The brothel woman quickly put on a placating smile and said, \"Zai'an is accompanying the Princess tonight. You know that no one dares to snatch someone from the Princess's hands, right? Please don't be angry.\"","Yuwen Lan paused when he heard this.","The Princess?","So that foreign man beside Yuwen Yan earlier was also from this place?","Just then, he heard the brothel woman continue, \"We have several other handsome young men here. I'll call them all out for you to choose from as you like.\"","But the plump woman snorted disinterestedly, \"They're all just mediocre beauties.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, a tall man came down from the second floor and said, \"Madam, who are you calling mediocre? It's only been a few days, has Yi Cai fallen out of your favor already?\"","The plump woman glanced at him, then turned up her nose and snorted, \"You rascal, I thought you were going to stay in Yangzhou and not come back.\"","The man called Yi Cai laughed and said, \"I was just delayed on the road for a few days. But I'm here now, aren't I?\"","With that, he went over and put his arm around the woman's waist, accompanying her up to a private room on the second floor.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Seeing this scene, even the most naive person would understand what kind of place this was.","He glanced meaningfully at Yanshu through the curtain and said, \"So this isn't a place for dining after all.\"","So this was what she meant by... \"ducks\"?","She actually wanted to come to a place like this???","To his surprise, Yanshu acted as if it had nothing to do with her and said, \"Indeed, I also felt it didn't seem like a place for eating at all. My lord must have made a mistake... Let's leave first.\"","She continued pulling him towards the exit, thinking to herself, [Good heavens, the Emperor actually thought this was a place to eat??? No no no, we need to leave quickly. If he stays any longer and learns bad habits, that would be terrible.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He would learn bad habits from those men who sell their looks???","Just as they stepped out of the establishment, before they could get into the carriage, Yanshu hurriedly pulled Yuwen Lan to the side into a shadowy area.","She seemed to be hiding from someone.","So Yuwen Lan asked, \"What's wrong?\"","He saw her pointing at a woman who had just alighted from a carriage on the roadside, whispering, \"That... looks like the Ankang county lord.\"","What?","The Ankang county lord?","As in, the daughter of the Princess?","Yuwen Lan quickly took a closer look.","Although the woman was wearing a veil, her figure did indeed resemble that of his cousin.","As she got down, five or six young men immediately came out from the establishment to welcome her, all calling out, \"The county lord has arrived.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","It really was An Kang.","She actually came to a place like this?!!!","It's worth noting that unlike Yuwen Yan who had divorced Zhao Chengwen, she still had a husband!!!","...","On the way back to the palace, Yuwen Lan kept brooding over this matter with a dark expression.","As he pondered, he couldn't help but laugh coldly and say, \"To think such a place exists in the capital!\"","-- He remembered that during the Lantern Festival, when he first took her out of the palace, she had mentioned this place. But at that time, he thought it was far removed from his life. He never imagined he would actually set foot in it today.","Setting foot in it was one thing, but that plump woman actually wanted to pay for him to go...","How utterly absurd!!!","Hearing this, Yanshu secretly glanced at his expression, thought for a moment, and said, \"I thought it was just a restaurant. I never imagined it would be such a filthy place! It's truly despicable!!!\"","In her heart, she couldn't help but think, [The physiques and looks of those men were actually quite good. No wonder they've managed to establish themselves in the capital.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What does she mean by \"quite good\"?","Could it be that she's taken a fancy to them???","He raised an eyebrow at her and asked, \"You like that place too?\"","\"No, no,\" she said, shaking her head like a rattle drum, with a serious expression, \"How could I like such a place? As soon as we entered, I felt chills down my spine!\"","But in her heart, she thought, [Tsk, wouldn't any woman like it? After all, no matter your height or build, as soon as you enter, you're surrounded by handsome men calling you 'darling'. It makes one feel so warm and confident!!!]","In short... it was probably like how men enjoy visiting brothels.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What? Those types could actually be considered handsome men???","He couldn't help but ask again, \"You like the men in there too?\"","She immediately shook her head again, \"How could that be possible? How could those mediocre beauties compare to Your Majesty? In my heart, there is only Your Majesty!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Was that supposed to be a compliment?","But why did it sound so strange???","Just then, he heard Yanshu ask him, \"How did Your Majesty know to bring me there? Where did you hear about this place?\"","-- Tsk, even if he mistook it for a place to eat, where did he hear about it from?","After all, this Ruyi Brothel was a secret known only to a small circle of noble ladies in the capital!","It was too strange that he, the Emperor, would know about it.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He couldn't very well say he heard it from her thoughts, so he could only say, \"We heard about it by chance...\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","Heard about it by chance?","She thought to herself, could it be from the ministers?","But that's not right. If those old-fashioned ministers knew there was a place specifically for women's entertainment...","Tsk, for something so against the patriarchal order, wouldn't they immediately submit a memorial to the court to raze the Ruyi Brothel to the ground?","Yuwen Lan inwardly scoffed.","That's right, he now wanted to send people to raze that disgusting place to the ground!","How dare they ask how much he cost???","It was utterly absurd!!!","Upon returning to the palace, Yuwen Lan immediately dispatched the Imperial Guard to investigate the Ruyi Brothel.","By the evening of the next day, the Imperial Guard came to report, \"Your Majesty, we have discovered that the Ruyi Brothel was originally established three years ago by a female merchant surnamed Ji. Initially, it was an embroidery shop that also sold jewelry and accessories, used to curry favor with the wives of powerful families in the capital. After gradually gaining a reputation, this female merchant spent money to hire various young men and started the current business.\"","Yuwen Lan asked further, \"What about the foreigners in their establishment?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"As the tastes of their patrons became more discerning, the female merchant recruited a group of foreign men from the border regions, mostly from Dangxia and Rouran. On the surface, they appear no different from the previous men, all pleasing women and earning money from them.\"","Yuwen Lan furrowed his brow and said, \"Those men have strong physiques and don't look like ordinary people. Continue investigating, especially the one called Zai'an who has been associating with the Princess recently.\"","The Imperial Guard immediately complied.","At this time, the Empress Dowager's birthday celebration was drawing near.","In recent days, many noble families from other regions had successively arrived in the capital, specifically to congratulate the Empress Dowager on her birthday.","Some of higher status came to the palace early to pay their respects to the Empress Dowager, so Yanshu, as a palace consort, had the fortune of accompanying the Empress Dowager and meeting many new faces.","The Empress Dowager was indifferent to most visitors, with one exception.","That was the elderly lady Mu Yunying from the Marquis of Zhenhai's Mansion in Mingzhou.","It was said that this Lady Mu was a sworn sister of the Empress Dowager, and every year she would travel thousands of miles to the capital to wish the Empress Dowager a happy birthday.","The Empress Dowager would always personally receive her, and even invite her to stay in the palace for a short while, showing their close relationship.","However, Yanshu had originally thought the other party would be a white-haired old lady. It wasn't until she met her that she realized this elderly lady was actually only in her early forties, quite young.","It turned out that her husband had passed away early, and after her eldest son got married and inherited the title, he became the new Marquis of Zhenhai, and she was respected as the old madam of the mansion.","At this moment, meeting her surprised gaze, Madam Mu entered the Palace of Benevolent Peace and first bowed to the people in the palace.","\"This humble subject pays respects to the Empress Dowager and all the ladies.\"","The Empress Dowager quickly smiled and said, \"Rise, there's no need for such formality between us.\"","She didn't even use the royal \"We\" to refer to herself.","As she spoke, she even personally reached out to help Madam Mu up.","Noticing Yanshu's surprised expression as she looked at Madam Mu, the Empress Dowager laughed and said, \"Look, your title of old madam has scared them all.\"","Yanshu quickly smiled and said, \"The Empress Dowager is right. This subject didn't expect the old madam to be so young.\"","As she finished speaking, Consort Zhou secretly rolled her eyes beside her.","— This Li Yanshu, flattering even Madam Mu just to curry favor with the Empress Dowager, how thick-skinned!","Of course, with the Empress Dowager present, she only dared to grumble in her heart, and no one heard.","Hearing Yanshu's words, Madam Mu also smiled and said, \"Lady Yipin is too kind, making this humble subject feel unworthy.\"","As she spoke, she called to a 12 or 13-year-old girl behind her, \"Xiangwan, come quickly and pay your respects to the Empress Dowager and the ladies.\"","This was Madam Mu's adopted daughter, named Ni Xiangwan.","— It was said that Madam Mu, who had been widowed for many years, was one day offering incense for her late husband at a temple. On her way down the mountain, she came across a small baby crying in the bushes by the roadside. Madam Mu couldn't bear to leave it, so she took the baby home and adopted her, giving her the surname Ni from her husband's family and naming her Xiangwan.","At this moment, hearing her adoptive mother speak, this adopted daughter of the Ni family responded, stepped forward and bowed to everyone, \"Xiangwan pays respects to the Empress Dowager and all the ladies.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"Xiangwan has grown so tall? Come, let Us have a look at you.\"","The young Miss Ni complied and stepped forward a few more steps.","The Empress Dowager held her and examined her carefully, then nodded and said, \"You're becoming more and more beautiful. Good child, it must have been tiring to accompany your mother on such a long journey. Sit down and rest.\"","After speaking, she called for the palace servants to bring out the finest West Lake Dragon Well tea picked before the spring rains, along with freshly made chestnut cakes, lotus seed paste pastries, and cloud-like rice cakes.","This level of hospitality was clearly different from how she treated others.","Yanshu observed this while eating the snacks and quietly asked the system, [Given the Empress Dowager's personality, it should be difficult for her to be so warm towards someone. Did this Madam Mu perhaps save the Empress Dowager's life?]","The system replied, [More or less. The Empress Dowager and Madam Mu grew up together, so their friendship is indeed deeper than with others. When the Empress Dowager's eldest son was gravely ill, and no good doctor could be found in the capital, Madam Mu heard the news and found a secret prescription. She traveled thousands of miles from Mingzhou to the capital to deliver it. Although it ultimately wasn't used, it greatly comforted the Empress Dowager. After the crown prince passed away, Madam Mu left her family in Mingzhou and stayed in the palace to accompany the Empress Dowager for a full two months. It can be said that Madam Mu was a very important reason why the Empress Dowager was able to pull through.]","Yanshu nodded upon hearing this.","Indeed, traveling thousands of miles to personally deliver medicine to the capital was something that couldn't be done with just an ordinary friendship.","Especially when the Empress Dowager was about to lose her eldest son, and the emperor was favoring others, leaving the Empress Dowager's future uncertain.","The system continued, [That's right. So later, when the Empress Dowager secured her position, she intended to grant her son a duke's title, but Madam Mu firmly refused, making the Empress Dowager value her even more.]","Yanshu replied, [Putting everything else aside, Madam Mu is clearly a truly wise person. No wonder she can be good friends with the Empress Dowager.]","Just then, they heard the Empress Dowager ask the young Miss Ni, \"Xiangwan, how do you find Our palace?\"","Ni Xiangwan smiled and said, \"With so many noble people here, the palace must be the best place in the world.\"","The Empress Dowager then said, \"If that's the case, why don't you let your mother return to Mingzhou alone, and you stay here to keep Us company?\"","As soon as these words were spoken, everyone paused—","The Empress Dowager saying this...","Could it be that she had taken a liking to this young girl? Did she want to keep her by her side to groom her and then send her into the harem later?","However, the young Miss Ni said, \"This little one is grateful for the Empress Dowager's kindness. However, while there are several ladies to keep the Empress Dowager company in the palace, mother only has this little one. If I stay, mother will be lonely, so this little one should return to Mingzhou with mother. We can come visit you again next year.\"","Madam Mu also smiled and said, \"Your Majesty thinks too highly of her. If she really stayed, I guarantee you'd regret it within three days. She's as mischievous as can be all day long.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager also laughed, \"I was just teasing you. She's the apple of your eye, how could I bear to take her away? As long as you remember to come back and see Us every year, that's enough.\"","She then specifically instructed the young girl, \"In the future, even after you're married, don't live too far from your mother, or she'll miss you terribly.\"","The young Miss Ni responded with a shy smile.","Hearing this, everyone finally dared to believe that the Empress Dowager was indeed just joking.","Yanshu also marveled inwardly—","It seemed the Empress Dowager truly loved her best friend. Otherwise, if she had insisted on keeping this young girl as her pawn, Madam Mu would have had no way to refuse.","However, the affection between this adoptive mother and daughter was also incredibly strong, wasn't it?","This young Miss Ni had been raised to be so pure and carefree, clearly the result of her adoptive mother's doting love.","And the way Madam Mu looked at her was just like how other mothers looked at their own flesh and blood, full of indulgence and adoration.","Just then, the system said, [Well, that's because she is her own flesh and blood.]"]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49","paragraphs":["What? This is Madam Mu's own flesh and blood?","Upon hearing the System say this, Yanshu immediately activated all her gossip nerves and asked, \"What's going on? Didn't her late husband die fifteen years ago? How does she have a thirteen-year-old daughter? Who did she have the child with?\"","The System replied, \"You're right, fifteen years ago, the former Marquis of Zhenhai passed away in his prime. At that time, his son was only ten years old, and Madam Mu was left as a widow to support the marquis's household. Although she had the Empress Dowager's help from the palace, it was still very difficult given the distance. At that time, the old Marquis of Zhenhai had a deputy named Zong Xinghai who helped Madam Mu handle various affairs, bustling about and being extremely loyal.\"","\"This young man was only in his twenties at the time, full of enthusiasm. Madam Mu had suddenly lost her support and was in a vulnerable state, so she trusted him very much. Over the course of a few years, as they interacted, feelings gradually developed between them.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu's eyes lit up, \"Did they perhaps cross the line and have this little girl?\"","The System continued, \"More or less. On a dark and windy night, they both had a little too much to drink, and in the heat of the moment, they engaged in intimate relations. Just that one time was enough for Madam Mu to become pregnant.\"","Yanshu couldn't help but marvel, \"Pregnant after just one time? It seems Deputy Zong had quite the aim!\"","The System sighed, \"Well, he was young, and the quality was good. Of course, that's not important. What's important is that Madam Mu was a widow who had to maintain the marquis's household for her son. Naturally, she couldn't openly give birth to this child. So she made an excuse of being ill and went to the countryside to 'recover' for a while. When the time came, she found another excuse to bring the child back from outside and raised her as an adopted daughter.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but marvel again. This was just like another version of the general and widow story she had written before, and it was even an age-gap relationship - how exciting!","She secretly glanced at Madam Mu again, noticing her delicate features. Even at her current age and without much makeup, she was still quite beautiful. One could imagine how stunning she must have been in her youth.","Such a mature and charming woman - it was understandable that a young wolf couldn't resist her allure and had impure thoughts.","However, there was still a question, so she asked, \"What about Deputy Zong now? Surely he's not still serving as deputy in the household? Have the two of them been carrying on a secret affair for over a decade?\"","The System replied, \"After that night, Zong Xinghai felt he had betrayed the Marquis of Zhenhai, so he voluntarily requested to be stationed at the frontlines to guard the coastal defenses. For over a decade, he's been exposed to wind and sun daily, punishing himself.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Wait, does he know he has a child?","System: \"He doesn't know.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","So after all this time, Madam Mu has raised the child on her own, and that man still knows nothing?","System: \"Actually, Zong Xinghai has been secretly protecting the Marquis of Zhenhai's household all these years. He knows that Madam Mu adopted a baby girl and raised her to adulthood, but he doesn't know it's his own child.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She didn't know what to say to that.","It sounded quite devoted, but also too foolish.","It's not like they had an affair while the old Marquis of Zhenhai was still alive - their relationship developed after he had passed away. Why did this man have to torture himself so?","Then again, this era placed too many shackles on women.","In modern times, it wouldn't be an issue for a widowed woman to remarry. However, if Madam Mu were to do so now, she would certainly lose her position as the mistress of the marquis's household.","So, this was all they could do.","Still, Madam Mu was at least better off than the Empress Dowager. After all, she had tasted the forbidden fruit with her young wolf and had two of her own children by her side. Her days weren't lonely.","She then asked, \"Does the Empress Dowager know about this?\"","System: \"Besides Madam Mu herself and her close maids, you're the first to know.\"","Yanshu understood then that even the Empress Dowager, Madam Mu's good friend, had been kept in the dark.","Of course, the more people who knew, the greater the risk. It was naturally better for fewer people to know about this matter.","Just as she was thinking this, she heard the Empress Dowager say to her and Consort Zhou, \"I need to speak with Madam Mu privately. You two go and rest for a while.\"","Yanshu understood that this was girl talk between close friends, so she knowingly responded and got up to leave the hall with Consort Zhou.","Come to think of it, Consort Zhou hadn't paid her any attention for a long time.","This time, they were originally minding their own business, but after walking a few steps, Consort Zhou suddenly stopped and turned to her, saying, \"Yiqin, you probably don't know this, but I've been by the Empress Dowager's side for so long, and that Miss Ni just now is the girl I've seen the Empress Dowager like the most.\"","Yanshu immediately understood that Consort Zhou was trying to provoke her.","So she quickly nodded and said, \"I also feel that Miss Ni is clever and quick-witted, so it's natural that the Empress Dowager would like her. But Your Highness shouldn't be so modest. After all, you're her niece, so the Empress Dowager must like you the most.\"","Hah, even blood ties couldn't withstand this woman's self-destructive behavior!","If there was ever an example of playing a good hand badly, Consort Zhou would be unmatched in the world.","Sure enough, as soon as these words were out, Consort Zhou's expression immediately changed.","However, after holding back for a moment, Consort Zhou smiled at her with a sarcastic tone, \"I saw that when the Empress Dowager said she wanted to keep this girl, it didn't seem like she was joking. Looking at that little girl, she's quite a beauty in the making. I'm afraid in a couple of years, you won't be able to compare.\"","Yanshu quickly smiled again and said, \"Your Highness is too kind. How could I, with my ordinary qualities, compare to Miss Ni? But if Miss Ni can stay, it's a good thing. You used to come often to chat with the Empress Dowager and keep her company, but now you don't come anymore. If Miss Ni can keep the Empress Dowager company, I'm sure the Empress Dowager will be very happy.\"","Consort Zhou was choked for a moment, her expression becoming even more unpleasant.","However, she couldn't find fault with Yanshu's words, so she could only give a cold laugh and say, \"You really are a smooth talker.\"","Yanshu smiled again and said, \"Your Highness flatters me. I'm not even one ten-thousandth as good as Your Highness.\"","By this time, they had reached the outside of the Palace of Benevolent Peace. She curtsied again and said, \"I'll take my leave now.\"","Then she hurried back to Ganlu Palace.","Tsk, arguing with someone like that was a waste of time. She'd rather go back and write a novel - that would be more interesting!","As she walked, she began to develop her ideas, and by the time she returned to Ganlu Palace, a passionate love story had taken shape in her mind. Yanshu immediately began to write.","Tsk, there was no earth-shattering gossip, no scandalous drama, just a mature and charming older woman and a young, passionate wolf - that was exciting enough.","Yanshu wrote with enthusiasm, continuing until nightfall.","However, before she could finish, a voice announced from outside the door - \"His Majesty has arrived...\"","She was startled for a moment, quickly snapping out of her story world. She made sure to close her manuscript before going to the palace door to curtsy.","\"This concubine greets Your Majesty.\"","However, the sharp-eyed emperor had already noticed her earlier actions.","\"Rise,\" Yuwen Lan said nonchalantly, pretending to help her up, and then asked, \"Have you written another novel today?\"","Yanshu nodded, mumbling, \"I did write, but I haven't finished yet.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. Why was she being so secretive?","So he asked again, \"What kind of story is it? Can you tell me about it?\"","But she thought for a moment and said, \"...Can I say no?\"","Yuwen Lan was taken aback. \"Why not?\"","Was it another risqué story?","But now, apart from the final step, they had already been intimate. If it was risqué... well, he could read it too, ahem.","But she said, \"Because I don't intend to publish this story at the moment.\"","She just wanted to write a story, but the time wasn't right yet. If it was released and affected that lady's reputation, causing some negative impact, it wouldn't be good.","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan became even more curious -","\"It concerns that lady's reputation?\"","Which lady exactly?","Could it be another story like the former wife of the Marquis of Linwu?","However, his curiosity had been piqued, and he really wanted to know. So he said, \"I'm not an outsider. If you don't want to publish it, I won't tell anyone else.\"","But she thought for a moment and said, \"Words are just words. What if Your Majesty accidentally lets it slip someday?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He simply untied the auspicious cloud jade pendant from his waist and handed it to her, saying, \"I'll give you this as collateral. If I ever let it slip, this will be yours.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","This person was really going all out just to hear some gossip, even willing to casually offer up a jade pendant with auspicious clouds as collateral?","However... she wasn't losing out either way. This jade pendant must be worth at least a thousand taels of silver, right?","Besides, he had no idea who the story was actually about anyway, hehe.","So she reached out to take it, smiling as she said, \"Since Your Majesty is showing such sincerity, this humble servant will tell you the story. But you must promise not to tell anyone else.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Of course.\"","He knew there was no problem money couldn't solve when it came to her.","Then he heard her begin, \"There was once a wise and virtuous woman who originally lived a fairly content life as a wife and mother. However, the heavens are unpredictable, and one day her husband suddenly passed away in an accident, leaving her tragically widowed. At this time, one of her late husband's old friends reached out to help her, solving her problems and helping her through the most difficult initial period.\"","\"This lady was naturally grateful in her heart, but didn't know how to repay him. By chance one day, she discovered that when he was drunk, he would call out her name. Only then did she realize that he actually harbored deep feelings for her.\"","— Listening to this part, Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow. So it was a story about a gentleman and his friend's wife.","Tsk, he had to admit it was quite intriguing.","But he still couldn't figure out who it was about.","So he asked, \"Did the lady also develop feelings for this gentleman?\"","He saw her nod and say, \"Of course. This gentleman was young and handsome, with a kind heart. Especially since he reached out to help when the lady needed it most. After learning of his feelings, the lady's own emotions towards him gradually changed as well. But due to societal norms, she could only hide these feelings in her heart.\"","\"However, love is often most fierce when repressed. One day, after getting drunk, the gentleman and the lady accidentally crossed the line. Like dry tinder meeting a raging fire, they spent an entire passionate night together. But when they woke up the next morning, the gentleman felt he had betrayed his deceased friend, and was afraid of causing trouble for the lady. So he suddenly left without saying goodbye.\"","Hmm?","This took Yuwen Lan by surprise. He couldn't help but ask, \"What happened after that?\"","Yanshu continued, \"Afterwards, the lady unexpectedly became pregnant. She could only give birth to the child alone and raise it by herself. And that gentleman who felt he had wronged his friend remained completely unaware.\"","Yuwen Lan immediately raised his eyebrows, \"Completely unaware? How could there be such an irresponsible person in this world?\"","Hearing this, Yanshu secretly nodded in her heart. It seemed his moral compass was quite upright.","Yuwen Lan pondered her words. What did she mean by... moral compass?","Why did she say he was very upright?","Was it meant as a compliment?","From her tone just now, it should be.","He silently nodded to himself, then asked, \"So what happened next?\"","He heard Yanshu say, \"Next, naturally the female lead raised their child alone. Later she found a very caring and protective husband and remarried.\"","\"Remarried?\"","Yuwen Lan was stunned. \"What about the previous gentleman?\"","But he saw her reply, \"Such a stubborn man without a sense of responsibility deserves to regret it for the rest of his life.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","\"Although that makes some sense, I've been listening this whole time thinking they would end up together... couldn't he be given another chance?\"","He saw her think for a moment, then say, \"Alright, considering he remained unmarried and silently watched over the lady, we can give him one more chance. But he must pay a price to make up for running away back then, leaving the lady to give birth and raise the child alone through such hardship. Let him suffer a thousand or so tribulations first before we talk about it.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow at her words. \"Does it have to be like that?\"","Yanshu nodded with a mature expression, \"This is called 'chasing wife in purgatory'. Many readers enjoy it.\"","Hm?","Yuwen Lan was increasingly confused. \"What is... purgatory?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Right, she had forgotten that cremation wasn't a thing in this era yet.","She could only patiently explain to him, \"The original meaning of this term refers to a place where, after death, a person's body needs to be burned to ashes before burial. That place of burning is called a crematorium.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan was even more surprised. \"There are actually such places? I've never heard of this... Where exactly is this place?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","The more she explained, the more troublesome it became.","She could only gloss over it, saying, \"It's just in a very far away place... Nevermind, that's not important. Your Majesty just needs to understand my meaning.\"","Then she seriously summarized, \"In short, as the male lead in a romance-focused story, he can't have any flaws at all. Otherwise, he'll be cursed to death by readers, and even I would be cursed.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"... Is that really how it is?\"","Yanshu nodded with a pitiful expression, \"Isn't it? It's not easy for storytellers to make a living.\"","— Not only would they be cursed, but at this time there was no concept of copyright. Countless people would secretly plagiarize and resell their work. Most storytellers' painstakingly written words weren't even enough to maintain three meals a day. It was really quite difficult, wuwu...","Yuwen Lan, who had been silently listening: \"...\"","He could only try to comfort her, \"If it's really that difficult, why don't you just stop writing?\"","But he saw her immediately shake her head, \"No way. I've finally found something I'm interested in. How could I give up because of such a small thing? As long as there's even one person reading, I'll keep writing.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan suddenly smiled and said, \"If there's only one person reading, that person will definitely be me.\"","Ahem, he was her first reader, and would also be her last.","After he spoke, he saw Yanshu pause, then smile and say, \"Thank you, Your Majesty.\"","[That's true. Even if there's only one left, selling one story to him for 150 taels is still very profitable!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Two days after the Marchioness of Zhenhai arrived in the capital, it was finally time for the Empress Dowager's Thousand Autumns Festival.","Although the Empress Dowager had specifically instructed not to burden the people or waste resources, it couldn't stop the emperor's filial piety. He specially ordered the Court of Imperial Sacrifices and the Court of Imperial Entertainments to prepare a grand banquet in the palace.","Today's etiquette was complicated. Yanshu got up early, went through her makeup and dressing routine, then headed to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","When she arrived, she had just finished paying her respects to the Empress Dowager when the emperor also arrived.","She saw him dressed in a vermilion dragon robe, his black hair tied up high, wearing a golden crown. He looked festive yet handsome, very pleasing to the eye.","— Actually, the two of them had been together until just before getting dressed.","But in just an hour, Yanshu felt her eyes light up at the sight of him.","At this moment, everyone in the hall knelt down to pay respects, shouting \"Long live the Emperor!\" Yuwen Lan gently said \"Rise\" and took the opportunity to glance at Yanshu, his dignified expression containing a hint of laughter in his eyes.","Hmm, in just an hour, she had transformed from a sleepy girl with messy hair into such a radiant and elegant beauty.","As he was admiring her, he heard her think to herself, [Look at how serious he looks now. Who would imagine how clingy he was last night? My hand is about to be crippled.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He couldn't help but feel his ears turn red.","These days... he had indeed been working her... hands quite hard.","But just five more days of endurance, and it would be fine.","Realizing his thoughts had wandered, he quickly composed himself and first solemnly paid respects to the Empress Dowager seated on the throne, \"I, on behalf of all the people of the empire, respectfully wish Mother Empress good health, long-lasting blessings, and ten thousand years of life.\"","As his words fell, everyone in the hall knelt down in unison to pay grand respects, calling out, \"We respectfully wish the Empress Dowager good health, long-lasting blessings, and ten thousand years of life.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"Your Majesty is thoughtful. I am very gratified. You may all rise.\"","Everyone responded and stood up following the emperor.","Soon, the guests who had come to pay their respects began to arrive at the palace one after another.","Yanshu followed the Empress Dowager and the emperor to receive them in the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Those entering the palace today were mainly imperial clan members and meritorious officials, especially the Empress Dowager's old ministers.","The first to enter was the family of the Marquis of Guangyang.","The Empress Dowager hadn't seen the Marquis of Guangyang for some time. Seeing how thin he had become, she couldn't help but exclaim in surprise, \"How has the Marquis of Guangyang lost so much weight? Are you not feeling well?\"","Hearing this, the fifty-something-year-old Marquis of Guangyang hurriedly said, \"Thank you for your concern, Empress Dowager. It's probably because of the hot weather lately. I haven't had much appetite, so I've lost some weight. There's nothing major wrong, please don't worry.\"","Only then did the Empress Dowager nod slightly.","Yanshu secretly tsked to herself. This man's pica had been getting worse lately. He'd been secretly eating calligraphy paper in his study all day. People aren't earthworms - they can't absorb nutrients from paper. Of course he'd lost weight.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had almost forgotten this man loved to eat calligraphy paper...","Tsk, it's truly hard to imagine that smell.","Feeling somewhat sympathetic, he spoke up, \"If the Marquis of Guangyang feels unwell, he should seek medical attention promptly. Don't hesitate to treat an illness.\"","However, the Marquis of Guangyang didn't catch the hint, and instead responded with an expression of unexpected delight, thinking to himself, [His Majesty is specifically concerned about me? It seems His Majesty values me quite highly!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Forget it, perhaps I should find a way to hint at this to his family members someday.","As he was thinking this, he saw the Grand Princess and the Imperial Son-in-law arrive, followed by their son and daughter-in-law, and daughter and son-in-law - the whole family.","\"We wish the Empress Dowager blessings as vast as the Eastern Sea and longevity like the Southern Mountains.\"","The Grand Princess was the late emperor's elder sister, which made her the Empress Dowager's elder cousin. At this moment, she led her large group in paying respects to the Empress Dowager, who politely replied, \"Elder sister, there's no need for such formality. Please, have a seat.\"","Yanshu's attention, however, was on the Grand Princess's daughter, Ankang county lord, and her husband Yao Junliang.","She had met Ankang county lord a few times before, but this was the first time she had seen her husband. She discreetly glanced at him and noticed that this County Magistrate Yao was completely different from the Grand Princess's former Imperial Son-in-law, Zhao Chengwen. He was a burly man with bright eyes.","She had heard that he was once the third-place winner in the military examinations, and now held the position of Deputy Commander in the Capital Guard. He seemed quite capable.","Yanshu inwardly clicked her tongue, thinking that this County Magistrate probably didn't know about Ankang county lord's visit to Ruyi Brothel, right? If he knew, with those muscles, wouldn't he tear the brothel apart?","System: [That's right, he doesn't know yet. The Capital Guard has been changing shifts these past few days, and he's been so busy he hasn't been home for several days.]","Yanshu: [...That sounds a bit pitiful. But come to think of it, this County Magistrate seems like a decent person. I heard he doesn't have any concubines or bedmaids in his household. Why would Ankang county lord go to Ruyi Brothel?]","System: [Some men appear normal on the surface but actually get up several times a night. Last year, during a military drill, the County Magistrate accidentally fell off his horse and injured that area. Although it's not a major problem, he's become somewhat less confident. Ankang county lord is at a passionate age... she's feeling a bit lonely. However, her visit to Ruyi Brothel only happened in the past couple of days. So far, she's only been window shopping, nothing serious yet.]","Yanshu: [...So the county lord hasn't done anything serious yet? It seems this couple still has feelings for each other. By the way, shouldn't the County Magistrate go see Doctor Jiang? Someone who could even cure the emperor should find this a piece of cake.]","Yuwen Lan, who had been silently listening nearby: \"...\"","Why was he suddenly mentioned again?","He had recovered many days ago... Couldn't they stop bringing up past events?","But come to think of it, so Yao Junliang was injured last year...","Considering he's a talented person and loyal to the court, he really should be recommended to see Jiang Nianqi.","...","As he was thinking this, he saw Princess Yuwen Yan arrive.","Beside her was her daughter, five-year-old Lan Jun.","The little girl was fair and pretty, innocent and adorable since she was young.","Regardless of what her parents were like, Yuwen Lan, as her uncle, was very fond of this niece.","However, at this moment, he saw that the little girl's eyes were red, with tears still hanging on her eyelashes. As she entered the hall, her eyes timidly scanned the surroundings, completely unlike her usual lively self.","Before Yuwen Lan could speak, the Empress Dowager had already asked, \"What's wrong with Lan Jun?\"","Yuwen Yan replied with an impatient expression, \"Mother, you don't know, this girl has become increasingly difficult to manage lately. Just now, as soon as we got off the carriage, she started fussing about her little toy again. It's truly infuriating. I scolded her a bit. She's so unreasonable, becoming more and more like those Zhao people.\"","The Empress Dowager rebuked, \"Don't ever mention such things again! Children are naturally unstable in their emotions, and she's recently gone through sudden changes. It's normal for her to cry and fuss a bit. How can you, as a mother, be so impatient?\"","She then beckoned to the little girl, \"Come, Lan Jun, come to grandmother.\"","Hearing this, the little girl timidly glanced at her mother, and seeing no objection, she dared to comply and went to the Empress Dowager's side.","The Empress Dowager gave the little one a piece of pastry, which she obediently started to eat without crying or fussing.","Yuwen Lan, observing this, also said to Yuwen Yan, \"Lan Jun is elder sister's child. No matter what her father is like, it has nothing to do with her. Elder sister should understand this principle.\"","Yuwen Yan responded with a \"yes,\" but then added resentfully, \"Does Your Majesty think I have a heart of stone? It's just that this girl has been crying and fussing terribly lately. How can I not be mentally and physically exhausted?\"","Yanshu listened silently on the side, inwardly clicking her tongue. It's normal for a child to cry and fuss a bit when she suddenly loses her father and feels unadjusted. But the Princess's household doesn't lack wet nurses or maids, and the Grand Princess didn't used to take care of the child much, so how did she suddenly become so mentally and physically exhausted?","Ahem, could it be that the top-ranked male prostitute has drained her energy?","System: [That's about right. The reputation of the top-ranked male prostitute isn't for nothing. But the Grand Princess isn't lying either. She's been under the influence of Love-Inducing Powder these past few days, so she really is mentally and physically exhausted.]","Yanshu was startled, [??? What on earth is Love-Inducing Powder?]","System: [It's a kind of aphrodisiac similar to a date rape drug.]"]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50","paragraphs":["As soon as these words were spoken, Yanshu could hardly believe her ears.","[A unique drug???]","[Such things still exist in this era???]","The system replied, [Of course they do, it's just not as widely known as in later times. For example, the Love-Inducing Powder that the Eldest Princess is growing now - its raw materials come from the Western Regions. After drying and processing, it's made into incense. When burned, people who smell it become addicted and gradually can't live without it.]","So that's how it is.","Yanshu hurriedly asked again, [How did the Princess become addicted to this...]","Before she could finish speaking, she suddenly remembered and quickly asked, [Could it be that top courtesan from Ruyi Brothel, what's his name, Pan something?]","After all, wasn't he from Rouran? And this unique drug also comes from the Western Regions?","The system confirmed, [That's right, it's Pan Zai'an.]","Yanshu drew in a sharp breath, [Why would he drug the Eldest Princess?]","Had the nightlife scene in this era already become so chaotic???","But the system explained, [Who is the Eldest Princess? She's seen countless handsome men, and even foreign royalty have proposed marriage before. Plus, after what happened with Zhao Chengwen, the Eldest Princess has become somewhat distrustful of men. So for someone from a brothel to try to win over the Eldest Princess, he'd have to put in quite a bit of effort.]","So this person resorted to drugging her?","Yanshu pondered quietly, [To curry favor with the Eldest Princess, he even came up with such methods. It seems Ruyi Brothel isn't just a simple brothel...]","Tsk, could it be that they use this Love-Inducing Powder on all the women who visit?","The system replied, [It's not that extreme. This drug is too expensive - it costs 100 taels of silver for just one stick. They would only use it on high-value targets.]","High-value targets...","Yanshu pondered quietly again -","Even if this Pan Zai'an won the Eldest Princess's heart, as a foreigner, he probably couldn't become the Imperial Son-in-law.","And if he was just to be a male favorite, why would he need to use such an expensive drug?","So his painstaking efforts to get close to the Eldest Princess must be... to gather intelligence?","Yes, that person is most likely a spy!","And the other foreign men at Ruyi Brothel, no wonder they're all tall and muscular with great physiques - they must all be specially trained experts.","They came to the Central Plains specifically to get close to those noble ladies, just to gather intelligence.","The system confirmed, [That's right, they were originally guards of the Rouran royal family. When the Rouran royals learned that the owner of Ruyi Brothel was recruiting people from the Western Regions, they planted these men there.]","Yanshu paused.","Tsk, this is no small matter! She needed to find a way to tell the Emperor, to make him vigilant!","She glanced anxiously at Yuwen Lan, not knowing that he was already aware.","Indeed, besides hearing Yanshu's inner thoughts just now, Yuwen Lan had also received a report from the Imperial Guard this morning that the foreign men at Ruyi Brothel were all connected to the Rouran royal family.","However, he hadn't expected that Yuwen Yan would have fallen victim to their poison.","This elder sister... she really never stops causing trouble.","He glanced at Yuwen Yan, who looked both aggrieved and impatient, and said, \"Elder Sister, are you feeling unwell? If so, perhaps we should call for the imperial physician.\"","However, Yuwen Yan was completely oblivious and merely said, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty. I'm fine physically, just annoyed by this girl.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Lan Jun, who was eating pastries beside the Empress Dowager, started crying again.","\"My golden lion... my lion...\"","The little girl cried as she spoke, making it hard for others to understand. The Empress Dowager asked, \"Tell Grandmother slowly, what happened?\"","The little girl pouted and said, \"My golden lion, Mother took it away...\"","Now everyone finally understood clearly - she was saying her mother had taken her golden lion?","But Yuwen Yan immediately scolded, \"It's just a broken lion, when did I ever take yours?\"","Then she said to the Empress Dowager, \"Mother, you see, this girl has been bothering me about this for the past two days.\"","Just then, Yanshu heard the system say, [This little girl had a golden lion toy that her father Zhao Chengwen gave her. After Zhao Chengwen was divorced by the Eldest Princess, she ordered all his things in the house to be thrown away. An old servant woman looking after the little girl got greedy and took the opportunity to steal the golden lion and sell it for money. Then she told the little girl that the Eldest Princess had ordered all the things from her father to be thrown away.]","Yanshu understood, [So the servant stole it, causing a misunderstanding between mother and daughter?]","What kind of situation is this? If only the Eldest Princess had a bit more patience, she could just talk it through with her daughter.","However, Yuwen Yan's mind was filled with thoughts of that foreign spy.","Feeling quite sympathetic, Yanshu spoke to the little girl, \"Although I don't have a golden lion, I do have a cloth tiger.\"","As she spoke, she took out a small cloth tiger from her sleeve.","-- This was actually a sachet that Rendong had made for her.","Seeing that the weather was getting hotter lately, she had filled it with some herbs to repel mosquitoes and insects, carrying it with her to ward off mosquitoes. Because she was born in the Year of the Tiger, the skilled Rendong had specially made it in the shape of a tiger, which looked quite adorable.","Sure enough, hearing her say this, little Lan Jun immediately looked over, momentarily forgetting to cry.","Yanshu continued, \"Though this little tiger is a bit ugly, I wonder if the County Lord likes it?\"","As she spoke, she gestured for Rendong to bring it to the little girl.","Lan Jun took the little cloth tiger, looked at it for a moment, and finally began to smile, saying, \"Lan Jun likes it, thank you, Niangniang.\"","\"The County Lord is too kind.\"","Yanshu smiled and said to the little girl, \"Such a precious thing, how could it be lost? Perhaps someone has hidden it somewhere. Why don't you ask the servants around you, see if any of the maids or old women know anything?\"","As she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager also said to the Eldest Princess, \"Yi'pin speaks sense. Such a small child, how could she deliberately cause trouble? You should go back and investigate Lan Jun's servants properly, see where that golden lion went.\"","Yuwen Yan could only say, \"Your daughter obeys.\"","As she finished speaking, someone else arrived outside the hall, and Yuwen Yan retreated to the side.","This time it was the Marquis of Xuanping who came.","Speaking of which, the Marquis of Xuanping's lineage was still related to the family of the Empress of the founding Emperor.","They were originally from Jiangnan, and after several decades and generations of titles being passed down, their relationship with the Emperor and Empress Dowager in the palace had become more and more distant.","So the last time this family entered the palace was when the previous Emperor was still on the throne.","If it weren't for the Grand Princess mentioning them first this time, Yuwen Lan might not have remembered them at all.","Now as this family arrived in the hall, the scene was quite grand. Apart from the Marquis of Xuanping and his wife at the front, a young man and a young woman followed behind.","After they had taken their positions, the Marquis of Xuanping hurriedly led his family in a grand salute, respectfully saying, \"Your subject Feng Zhiyuan and family congratulate the Empress Dowager on her longevity and wish Your Majesty good health.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled politely and said, \"You may rise. Thank you for coming such a long way, it must have been tiring.\"","The Marquis of Xuanping hurriedly replied, \"To be able to pay our respects before the Empress Dowager and Your Majesty is our honor. We were delighted throughout the journey and didn't feel tired at all.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded again and cast her gaze towards the young man and woman behind him.","The young man appeared to be in his early twenties, with features seven or eight parts similar to the Marchioness, clearly her son. The young woman was about sixteen or seventeen, her features more delicate than her brother's, and her figure surprisingly voluptuous.","The Empress Dowager couldn't help but say, \"It's only been a few years, and the children have grown so much?\"","The Marquis of Xuanping quickly responded, \"My unworthy son Yuan Qing has just come of age this year, and my little daughter Miao Qin had her coming-of-age ceremony two years ago. She's seventeen now.\"","He then instructed the brother and sister, \"Quickly come and pay your respects to His Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and the ladies.\"","The siblings immediately came forward and performed another salute, \"Yuan Qing and Miao Qin pay our respects to Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and all the ladies.\"","This allowed everyone to see their appearances clearly.","Yanshu observed the two for a moment, silently pondering: the son has a square face like his father, and his features clearly take after his mother, but the daughter has an oval face, and her features don't seem to resemble either her father or mother?","Tsk tsk, how did she manage to avoid her parents' flaws and inherit all their good points?","Then she heard the system say, [Simple, this girl isn't born of the Marchioness, but of a concubine. The concubine is beautiful, so she takes after her mother.]","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, [So she's a daughter of a concubine?]","The system confirmed, [The Marquis of Xuanping's legitimate daughter was born with a lame foot and isn't very attractive. They've finally managed to come to the capital once, of course they'd bring the pretty daughter of the concubine, otherwise wouldn't it be a wasted trip?]","Hmm?","Yanshu accurately grasped the key point, [For free? Are they thinking of sending their daughter into the palace?]","The system replied, [That's right. Seeing their relationship with the imperial family in the capital growing more distant, the Marquis of Xuanping is certainly anxious. With a beautiful concubine-born daughter, he definitely wants to form a marriage alliance with the Yuwen family again.]","Yanshu asked, [But a concubine's daughter from a marquis family... I'm afraid she can't enter the palace, can she?]","The system explained, [That's why he just evaded the Empress Dowager's question, not mentioning his lame legitimate daughter at all.]","Yanshu deduced, [Keeping the lame legitimate daughter at home, bringing the beautiful concubine-born daughter to the palace, yet not speaking clearly... Does this mean they want the concubine's daughter to replace the legitimate daughter's identity to enter the palace?]","Damn, if this is discovered, it could mean execution!!!","The Marquis of Xuanping is really bold!!!","Listening silently to this point, what else was there for Yuwen Lan not to understand?","Very well, a mere Marquis of Xuanping dares to toy with imperial power.","He then said, \"I remember hearing a few years ago that your daughter had difficulty walking. Now it seems there's no trace of that at all. May I ask where your family found such a miraculous doctor?\"","As soon as these words were spoken, panic flashed in the Marquis of Xuanping's eyes.","After a moment's hesitation, he finally stammered, \"Your Majesty is correct, my eldest daughter indeed has had difficulty walking since childhood. This... is my second daughter.\"","Second daughter?","Then the Empress Dowager also spoke up, \"I remember, didn't your wife only give birth to one son and one daughter?\"","The Marquis of Xuanping was now sweating profusely and had to honestly reply, \"In response to Your Majesty the Empress Dowager, this girl... was born to my concubine.\"","As his words fell, the people in the hall looked at each other, immediately understanding the situation.","The Empress Dowager gave a cold laugh and said, \"I thought my memory was failing me. So that's how it is.\"","The Marquis of Xuanping, with cold sweat already soaking his back, could only kneel and say, \"I am at fault. I didn't explain clearly earlier. Please forgive me, Your Majesty.\"","The Empress Dowager didn't speak for a moment.","Yuwen Lan didn't even acknowledge him.","Their displeasure was already quite evident.","After a while, it was the Grand Princess, the daughter of the founding emperor's empress, who spoke to ease the tension, \"The Marquis of Xuanping must have been away from court for too long and has forgotten how to speak properly? In the future, you must be more mindful.\"","The Marquis of Xuanping hurriedly agreed, \"I wouldn't dare, I wouldn't dare.\" He then led his family to kowtow repeatedly.","Seeing this, the Empress Dowager finally gave face to the Grand Princess and sighed, \"Very well, you may retire and rest now.\"","The family, as if granted a great amnesty, hurriedly agreed, got up, and retreated from the hall.","Yanshu, who had been quietly observing the drama, thought to herself, \"...\"","Tsk, did this family just come to the palace to check in? They didn't even finish a cup of tea before leaving again.","But come to think of it, did the Emperor really hear from someone that his legitimate daughter was lame?","Yet judging from the Empress Dowager's reaction, she clearly didn't know about this...","Tsk, why does something feel off?","Yuwen Lan, revealing no emotion, took a sip of tea, keeping his thoughts to himself.","Next, several more groups of guests arrived, and then Madam Mu from the Marquis of Zhenhai's household came to pay respects with her children.","A few days ago when she first entered the palace, Madam Mu only brought her \"adopted daughter\" Ni Xiangwan. Today, for such a formal occasion, her son, the current Marquis of Zhenhai, also made an appearance.","Yanshu quickly cast a glance their way.","She saw that this Marquis of Zhenhai's features greatly resembled his mother, Madam Mu.","In contrast, the young Miss Ni showed no trace of Madam Mu's features, nor did she resemble her half-brother.","Yanshu secretly marveled—this was practically heaven helping Madam Mu. If the girl had looked like her mother or brother, wouldn't it have aroused suspicion?","Looking at it this way, that Vice Commander Zong must have been quite handsome, otherwise he couldn't have produced such a delicate daughter.","But speaking of which, when will this family finally acknowledge their true relationship?","After all, letting this young lady continue to believe she was adopted is quite cruel.","...","All these thoughts entered Yuwen Lan's ears, and he finally realized that the protagonist in her story that day was Madam Mu.","In other words, the adopted daughter that the Marquis of Zhenhai's family had always claimed to have was actually Madam Mu's own flesh and blood...","And the other protagonist in the story, the man who ran away, must be the Vice Commander Zong she mentioned?","This surname wasn't common, and it was related to the Marquis of Zhenhai's family...","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment and seemed to recall that there was a commander surnamed Zong in the coastal defense camp of Mingzhou Prefecture.","This man had had several opportunities for promotion, all of which he had politely declined, insisting on staying in Mingzhou to guard the coastal defenses.","Could it be for this lady?","...","Only then did Yuwen Lan realize that the two parties were of such identities.","However, after a brief moment of surprise, he also understood why Commander Zong would make such a choice.","—Love had already blossomed, and because of love, they had crossed the line. Whether he stayed or left, it was already a mistake...","After all, no one is perfect. This story left one with mixed feelings.","...","True friendship was indeed different. After Madam Mu led her children to pay their respects, the Empress Dowager immediately invited her to sit close by.","Lan Jun, who was playing with a cloth tiger next to the Empress Dowager, saw Ni Xiangwan and immediately cast a curious glance, calling out, \"Sister...\"","Ni Xiangwan quickly responded, \"Greetings, Princess.\"","The Empress Dowager, seeing this, said, \"You two can play together.\"","Then she said to the Eldest Princess Yuwen Yan, \"Since you're tired, why not let Lan Jun stay in the palace for a couple of days? I'm also planning to have Madam Mu stay in the palace for two days. This way, Lan Jun can play more with Xiangwan.\"","Yuwen Yan had been hoping for this and immediately said, \"Then I'll trouble Mother Empress.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, then couldn't help but advise her, \"As a mother, you should change your temperament in the future and set a good example for Lan Jun.\"","Yuwen Yan perfunctorily agreed, \"Your daughter will respectfully follow Mother Empress's teachings.\"","Madam Mu, observing this, could only instruct her own daughter, \"Keep the Princess company well, and be very careful.\"","Ni Xiangwan also agreed and began to play with Lan Jun.","By the time they had received all the guests who came to offer birthday wishes, it was nearly noon.","Poor Yanshu had been sitting formally with the Empress Dowager for most of the morning and was now famished.","Fortunately, today's banquet was set in the garden of the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Speaking of which, this was a feast Yanshu had been looking forward to for a long time!","—Now that it was early summer in April, various fruits and vegetables were coming into season, and the ingredients were much more abundant than in winter and spring. It would certainly be different from the various banquets during the New Year.","As everyone took their seats, the palace servants began to serve the dishes one by one.","Watching the various aromas wafting towards her, Yanshu became even hungrier.","She couldn't help but think to herself, [I hope the Emperor's toast is brief, so we can start eating soon! I only had time to eat a small bowl of porridge this morning to allow time for grooming, I'm starving!!!]","Fortunately, she wasn't far from the Emperor, and her voice reached Yuwen Lan's ears in time.","Yuwen Lan thought to himself, \"...\"","Having only eaten a bowl of porridge in the morning was indeed tough on her. After all, she had the appetite to eat two more baskets of steamed buns.","So he complied with her wish and simply said, \"Today, family and friends gather to celebrate Mother Empress's birthday. We wish Mother Empress longevity and prosperity, as enduring as the sun and moon.\"","With that, he toasted the Empress Dowager.","Everyone raised their cups and congratulated the Empress Dowager in unison, \"We wish the Empress Dowager longevity and prosperity, as enduring as the sun and moon.\"","The Empress Dowager accepted the toast and smiled, \"There's no need for formalities today, please start eating.\"","Everyone agreed and began to use their chopsticks.","Yanshu, as if granted a great amnesty, immediately started eating.","She had already quietly surveyed the dishes on the table countless times, and now with a clear target, she first reached for the chrysanthemum pork loin.","It's worth noting that this dish was fried and topped with a sweet and sour sauce. If left any longer, the texture wouldn't be as good.","Fortunately, there wasn't much delay. With one bite, she found the pork loin crispy on the outside and tender on the inside. Coupled with the orange sauce on top, it was indeed tangy, sweet, and very appetizing.","After the pork loin, she hurriedly tasted the coriander-fried squab.","This dish relied on the heat of the wok, and wouldn't taste as good if it cooled down.","Mmm, after tasting it, she found the cooking was indeed perfect. The squab meat was soft, tender, and delicious. After being stir-fried at high heat with coriander in the wok, it had an intense aroma, making it a favorite for a coriander lover like Yanshu.","The early-season fat crabs were also very tempting. Rendong helped her mistress take one, and as soon as the crab shell was opened, they saw it was full of crab roe, almost overflowing.","Truly worthy of being specially prepared for the Empress Dowager's birthday banquet! Yanshu took a bite and felt her mouth full of umami flavor, utterly satisfied.","Of course, besides the fat crabs, there were also Yangtze River shad fish, rushed to the capital by express horse from Jiangnan.","To ensure the guests could fully enjoy the flavor, the imperial chef specially prepared half of the fish steamed and half braised, offering two tastes from one fish - a truly thoughtful touch.","These few dishes were already quite satisfying, not to mention the shark fin soup with phoenix tail, kung pao wild rabbit, braised fish lips, and crispy suckling pig - dishes that usually only appear at banquets. Each was spectacular in its own way.","What impressed Yanshu the most was the cherry custard.","It was the season when cherries were in market. Fresh cherry juice was steamed with milk to make custard, then topped with pitted cherry flesh over the chilled custard. With just a thin drizzle of honey, it was refreshingly sweet and perfect for cleansing the palate.","Looking around the banquet, some guests were earnestly offering auspicious words to the Empress Dowager, while others chatted among themselves. Only Yanshu was carefully savoring each dish, eating with great focus.","After finishing the cherry custard, the lychee sweet rice that Yanshu had been most looking forward to was served.","Lychees have a short season, as fleeting as an epiphyllum bloom. Especially since they needed to be transported from the southern Guangdong region to the capital, each fruit was worth its weight in gold.","This dish involved removing the pits from the translucent white lychee flesh and stuffing it with soaked glutinous rice and raisins. After steaming, the glutinous rice fully absorbed the lychee's sweetness, while the lychee flesh was infused with the unique fragrance of glutinous rice. It left a sweetness in one's heart that was unforgettable.","Due to its preciousness, this dish only appeared once a year at the Empress Dowager's birthday banquet, and each person could only have three pieces.","Yanshu was already delighted after eating one piece.","Just as she was about to eat the second piece, she noticed a little girl curiously watching her.","It was none other than Lan Jun, the daughter of the Eldest Princess.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Why did she always attract children's attention when she was eating?","To ease the awkwardness, she smiled and said, \"Princess, try this lychee sweet rice. You'll surely like it.\"","But as soon as she said it, she realized it wasn't that the little girl didn't want to eat, but that there was no one to help her eat.","— Unlike the Empress Dowager and imperial consorts in the palace, guests couldn't bring their personal maids to serve them, so the little girl had no wet nurse or maid to look after her today.","In the past, when she occasionally entered the palace, her father would take care of her. Now that her father was gone, her mother Yuwen Yan was busy chatting and drinking with the guests on either side, how could she spare attention for her daughter?","So the little one had only eaten a few nearby pastries, not daring to touch the hot dishes.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, this little girl born from the Eldest Princess's womb was quite pitiful.","However, although Yanshu wanted to ask someone to help take care of her, she was afraid the Eldest Princess might make a scene about it later...","So Yanshu was a bit hesitant and didn't dare to speak up.","Fortunately, at this moment, the Emperor on the main seat noticed and immediately called for Fuhai to find a palace maid to attend to his niece. Only then did the little girl start eating.","Yanshu felt relieved and couldn't help but glance at Yuwen Lan, secretly pondering why this person always seemed to think the same as her?","Could it be... the legendary meeting of minds?","Yuwen Lan calmly took a sip of wine.","Of course.","After the lunch banquet, the Emperor specially arranged for a troupe to perform plays and acrobatics to entertain the Empress Dowager and the guests.","Yanshu continued to act as a companion by the side.","Fortunately, the short plays and acrobatic performances were very interesting, clearly having been rehearsed in advance for the Empress Dowager's birthday banquet.","Everyone was enjoying themselves, though a few people left early after bidding farewell to the Empress Dowager due to other matters.","For instance, Eldest Princess Yuwen Yan hurriedly left the palace right after lunch, citing that she wasn't feeling well.","Yanshu thought to herself, it's probably that her craving for the Love-Inducing Powder had flared up again, and she was rushing to find that foreign gigolo.","Tsk, although she didn't want to meddle in this woman's affairs, it did concern the court, so she should find a way to inform the Emperor.","But then she heard the system say, [Don't worry, as soon as Yuwen Yan left the palace, the Imperial Guard secretly followed her.]","Yanshu was startled, [??? Was this arranged by the Emperor?]","The system replied, [Who else could command the Imperial Guard?]","That made sense, but Yanshu still didn't understand, [Has the Emperor also noticed something off about Yuwen Yan?]","The system said, [Didn't he see Pan Zai'an with Yuwen Yan that night, just like you did?]","Yanshu then remembered.","Oh right, of course, the Emperor was still the Emperor after all. Seeing a foreign man by his sister's side, he definitely wouldn't remain indifferent.","With this in mind, she felt reassured.","At the same time, she had another thought—","If the Imperial Guard caught that foreign spy giving drugs to the Eldest Princess...","Wouldn't that lead to another big conflict?","Tsk, fortunately the Empress Dowager had kept Lan Jun in the palace.","And fortunately this child was still young.","If she were a bit older and knew about these outrageous things her mother was doing...","Who knows what impact it would have on her.","Thinking this, Yanshu watched the performance while waiting for news from the system.","However, as dusk approached, before any news about the Eldest Princess came, someone hurriedly entered the palace to see the Grand Princess, saying, \"Your Highness, something terrible has happened. The Ankang county lord's husband just injured someone on Yang Lou Street, and now the other party wants to file a lawsuit.\"","Huh?","At these words, everyone around the Grand Princess paused.","Yanshu was also stunned and quickly asked the system, [What's going on? The Ankang county lord's husband beat someone up?]","The system replied, [That's right. Earlier, the Ankang county lord sneaked off to the Ruyi Brothel. Someone informed her husband, who quietly followed her and caught the gigolo who was seducing his wife red-handed. In a fit of rage, he broke the gigolo's leg.]","Yanshu: [...]","This, this, this... It's like a juicy melon being cut open and served right to her mouth."]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51","paragraphs":["As dusk approached, several hours had passed since the noon birthday banquet. The Emperor had already left for Qianming Palace, and many guests had taken their leave from the palace.","Those still accompanying the Empress Dowager to watch the opera were close female relatives of the royal family, like the Grand Princess, or trusted friends like Madam Mu, who enjoyed a close relationship with the Empress Dowager.","Except for Yanshu, who was eagerly waiting to see the Grand Princess's drama unfold, Consort Zhou and Consort Wang had long since excused themselves and returned to their own palaces.","Thus, the messenger who came to report had originally intended to quietly inform the Grand Princess. But seeing that only a few people remained, whispering in the Grand Princess's ear in front of the Empress Dowager seemed disrespectful. So he had no choice but to speak openly.","As his words fell, everyone was stunned.","\"What? The Ankang county lord's husband beat someone on the street?\"","\"They just attended the noon banquet. How did he end up beating someone on Yang Lou Street?\"","The Grand Princess hurriedly asked, \"Explain clearly, what exactly happened?\"","But when questioned like this, the messenger began to stammer, \"It's... uh, it's...\"","After a long pause without a proper explanation, the Empress Dowager spoke up, \"What's the matter? Hurry up and say it! Are you trying to worry us to death?\"","The messenger finally said, \"I wouldn't dare. It's just that the county lord had a rare day off today. Earlier, he heard that the county lord's wife wasn't feeling well and had gone out to see a doctor. He wanted to accompany her, but when he arrived at a place called Ruyi Brothel on Yang Lou Street, he discovered someone molesting the county lord's wife. The county lord became furious and couldn't help but teach the offender a lesson...\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but think to herself, \"This Mr. Yao was the third-place winner in the military examinations. There are only two people in the country who could beat him in a fight. That scoundrel was certainly no match for him. Breaking the guy's leg was probably him showing restraint.\"","However, she couldn't help but wonder why the Ankang county lord was in such a hurry. Hadn't she not crossed the line yet? Why was she so eager to go to Ruyi Brothel?","Upon hearing this news, the others who didn't know the truth were extremely surprised.","The Empress Dowager immediately said, \"What? What kind of madman dares to molest the county lord? Does he have a death wish?\"","The Grand Princess also said with a shocked expression, \"Exactly! How could there be such a scoundrel in a medical clinic? Where were the county lord's attendants?\"","The messenger had previously said that the Ankang county lord had gone to see a doctor, so everyone assumed that this place called Ruyi Brothel was a medical clinic.","However, hearing the Grand Princess say this, the messenger had to explain, \"Your Highness, Ruyi Brothel is not a medical clinic.\"","\"What? It's not a clinic?\" the Grand Princess asked. \"Then what is it?\"","\"It's... it's a restaurant,\" the messenger replied.","A restaurant?","Everyone looked at each other in confusion, even more bewildered than before.","Wasn't the Ankang county lord feeling unwell? Why did she go to a restaurant instead of seeing a doctor?","And she had just had drinks at the palace during lunch...","Why go to another restaurant?","Just as everyone was completely puzzled, an announcement rang out from outside the Palace of Benevolent Peace: \"His Majesty the Emperor arrives...\"","The Emperor had come.","Everyone's eyes immediately lit up. As Yuwen Lan entered the hall, the Empress Dowager hurriedly asked, \"We just received news that the Ankang county lord's husband beat someone on Yang Lou Street. Has Your Majesty heard about this?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"I just received a report from the Capital Prefecture saying that someone has filed a complaint against Yao Junliang for beating someone on the street.\"","What? The complaint had already reached the Emperor?","The Grand Princess immediately said anxiously, \"They molested her first, and now they're trying to frame him? Your Majesty knows that Junliang is not an impulsive person. Could this be a trap?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded again and said, \"Aunt, don't worry yet.\"","He then asked the messenger, \"Where is the county lord now?\"","The messenger quickly replied, \"Your Majesty, the county lord is still at Ruyi Brothel on Yang Lou Street.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Bring the county lord and his wife here. I will question them myself.\"","The messenger quickly agreed and left to summon them.","Yanshu immediately became excited—","She hadn't waited here all afternoon for nothing. There was live drama to watch again!!!","Well, it wasn't about the Grand Princess, but the county lord beating up a scoundrel was pretty exciting too!","And the Emperor had called them here to explain, he was really getting to know her better!!!","She secretly glanced at Yuwen Lan, feeling that he had become more and more adorable lately.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had actually just wanted to resolve the Ruyi Brothel issue in front of the Empress Dowager, Grand Princess, and others.","Tsk, he thought she had already left, but she had stayed here all afternoon just to watch the drama?","Well, that was just like her.","Alright then, they might as well watch together.","Knowing that the royal family had important matters to deal with, Madam Mu excused herself from the Empress Dowager before the Ankang county lord and her husband arrived. She left the main hall of the Palace of Benevolent Peace, taking Xiao Lanyun with her.","Yanshu, however, shamelessly stayed, pretending to be invisible next to Yuwen Lan.","The Empress Dowager: \"...\"","Oh well, she was just another drama enthusiast.","Before long, the Grand Princess's husband, who had heard the news, also arrived.","Soon after, the Ankang county lord and her husband Yao Junliang finally arrived at the palace.","Yanshu suppressed her excitement and looked over, seeing that the county lord's face still showed traces of anger, but no signs of injury.","It made sense, after all, he was the third-place winner in the military examinations. The scoundrels at Ruyi Brothel were no match for him.","The Ankang county lord's face, however, was flushed and pale by turns, with redness around her eyes as if she had been crying.","After the couple paid their respects to everyone, Yuwen Lan spoke to the county lord, \"I just received a report from the Capital Prefecture that someone has filed a complaint against you for beating a person on the street. Is this true?\"","Yao Junliang bowed his head without hesitation and said, \"Your Majesty, I did indeed beat someone on Yang Lou Street earlier. I know I have brought shame to the court and am willing to accept punishment.\"","Yanshu couldn't help but raise an eyebrow in her mind and cheer, \"This county lord is a real man! He dares to take responsibility for his actions!\"","The Emperor then asked him, \"Then why did you beat that person?\"","However, when this question was asked, the previously forthright county lord hesitated.","He looked at his wife, then stammered, \"I... I... was just angry for a moment...\"","It was clear he didn't want to say it out loud.","This worried the Empress Dowager and the Grand Princess and her husband.","Fortunately, the Emperor directly said, \"I called you here today to get to the bottom of this matter. Don't hesitate, tell me the truth.\"","Yao Junliang had no choice but to agree.","He then said, \"Your Majesty may not know, but Ruyi Brothel is not a respectable establishment. Inside... inside there were men trying to seduce my wife! I... I am a normal man, how could I tolerate such a thing? So in a fit of anger, I beat that person.\"","What?","When these words were spoken, everyone in the hall was stunned.","The Grand Princess asked incredulously, \"What did you say? What kind of place is this Ruyi Brothel?\"","Yao Junliang said with a tense expression, \"I cannot bring myself to say it. Please ask my wife, mother.\"","The Grand Princess then looked at her daughter and said anxiously, \"Hurry up and tell us!\"","The Ankang county lord had started crying and said between sobs, \"It was originally just a place for drinking tea and having fun, but there were some men who would play the zither, perform music... and chat with the guests...\"","She couldn't bring herself to say the rest.","But everyone in the hall already understood, and their expressions became complex.","The Empress Dowager: [What? There's such a place in the capital??? How come I'm only finding out about this now!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Judging by the Empress Dowager's tone, did she also plan to... go???","The Grand Princess: [There's actually such a place in the capital??? What was this girl doing going to a place like that??? And she even got caught by her husband!!!]","The Grand Princess's husband: [This, this, this... Does this mean there are... male prostitutes there??? Tsk tsk tsk, the world really is in decline and people's hearts are not what they used to be! How outrageous!!!]","Yanshu silently sympathized with the Ankang county lord, thinking to herself, \"This is truly the epitome of social death...\"","Before she could finish her thoughts, she saw the Grand Princess ask her daughter in anguish, \"If you knew what kind of place it was, why did you go there?\"","The Ankang county lord continued crying and said, \"I didn't know at first. I only found out after I went there... I really didn't do anything, I just went there to drink some tea, I really didn't do anything...\"","Yanshu couldn't help but think to herself again—This was just like when men go to brothels, once you've been there, you can't clear your name. Even if you really didn't do anything, no one would believe you.","However, the Grand Princess was heard speaking kindly to her son-in-law Yao Junliang, \"Since she didn't do anything wrong, just had a few cups of tea, this matter is simply a misunderstanding. There's no need for you to be so angry about it.\"","Yanshu thought to herself, \"...Indeed, whether it's a mother-in-law or a mother-in-law, when it's not one's own mother, they always side with their own child...\"","Even if the Ankang county lord truly didn't do anything, she still had improper thoughts. How could the county magistrate not be angry?","Yao Junliang was certainly furious. Upon hearing this, he couldn't hold back anymore and immediately retorted, \"Mother, you didn't see it. If I had arrived a moment later, the county lord would have done more than just drink tea... I don't know what I've done wrong to make the county lord seek entertainment in such a place. Moreover, all the men there knew she was a county lord! Where am I supposed to put my face?\"","Seeing this situation, the Empress Dowager felt sympathetic, but also thought to herself, \"This Ankang girl is too conspicuous. Couldn't she have gone there secretly without letting people know she's a county lord?\"","Yuwen Lan thought, \"...So it would have been fine if she went there quietly?\"","Stumped by her son-in-law's words and not knowing what to say, the Grand Princess angrily walked up to her daughter and raised her hand to slap her, saying, \"What were you thinking going to such a place? Letting those filthy men get close to you, have you no sense of dignity?!\"","The Ankang county lord cried even harder, \"It was the Princess who took me there. At first, I thought it was just a tea house...\"","Everyone was stunned upon hearing this—","The Princess took her there?","Does that mean the Princess went there too???","At this moment, Yao Junliang spoke with a pained expression, \"No matter who took the county lord there, she knew what kind of place it was later on, yet she still went!\"","Ankang continued crying, \"I don't know why I kept feeling the urge to go... But I really didn't do anything besides drinking tea and listening to music! Today when that man tried to touch me, I even slapped him!\"","Yao Junliang snorted, \"But if the county lord hadn't gone to that place, would this have happened?\"","Ankang was at a loss for words and could only start crying again.","However, Yanshu pondered to herself—","The Ankang county lord said that after going once, she couldn't resist wanting to go again...","Tsk, could it be that she also fell victim to the Love-Inducing Powder?","The system replied, \"That's right, the Ankang county lord is also a major target.\"","Yanshu suddenly realized.","Of course, this Yao county magistrate is the Imperial Guard's deputy commander, responsible for dozens of guard posts in the capital. The spies must be trying to obtain confidential information about the capital's defenses through the Ankang county lord, so they drugged her too!","The system confirmed, \"That's exactly what happened.\"","Realizing the gravity of the situation, Yanshu thought further. Since the Ankang county lord hadn't done anything with those male prostitutes yet, it seemed the other party hadn't obtained any secrets either. So, the county magistrate's beating today was quite timely. If the Emperor could use this incident as a starting point to investigate thoroughly and root out the spies, it wouldn't be too late.","Meanwhile, hearing her daughter speak like this, the Grand Princess felt there was still room for maneuver in this matter. She immediately spoke up in support of her son-in-law, \"In that case, it's clear that the people in that establishment were too brazen! Knowing she was a county lord and still daring to lay hands on her. Junliang was right to beat them today!\"","The old Prince Consort also chimed in, \"That's right. Such shameless men deserve to be despised by everyone!\"","Yanshu thought to herself, \"...It seems these old folks are quite satisfied with Yao county magistrate as their son-in-law.\"","The system explained, \"Of course. Yao county magistrate earned his third place in the military examinations on his own merit, and later worked his way up to his position in the Imperial Guard through his own abilities. He's not a womanizer, he's strong and capable, and he's good to the children. He's much better than that Zhao Chengwen who lives off his wife. Which father-in-law and mother-in-law wouldn't like him?\"","That's true, indeed.","Yanshu thought to herself, judging from the Ankang county lord's reaction, she still has feelings for her husband, and she's been drugged... Now it all depends on the Yao county magistrate. If he can endure this, their marriage might still work out.","But then the system said, \"It's no longer just a matter between the two of them. The Ruyi Brothel has taken that crippled male prostitute to file a complaint with the authorities, and they're making a big fuss about it, intending to let the whole capital know.\"","Yanshu didn't quite understand, \"How can people in this kind of business dare to make such a big deal out of this?\"","The system explained, \"Because currently, the law doesn't prohibit men from working as prostitutes. Making a big fuss might even serve as free publicity for them. Of course, right now, the main issue is that some people are taking advantage of the situation to stir up trouble.\"","Stirring up trouble?","Yanshu understood then. It must be those spies again.","They're using this opportunity to frame the county magistrate, deliberately confusing the issue, and then inciting the uninformed masses.","After all, this matter involves not only the Ankang county lord but also the Princess, which could be said to greatly concern the royal family's face. Once it blows up, it will inevitably affect the dignity of the royal family...","It had to be said, these Western spies were playing quite a sophisticated game.","Ah, this Princess Yuwen Yan really is good for nothing, always causing trouble for the family.","As she was thinking this, someone outside the hall reported, \"The Princess requests an audience.\"","Everyone paused.","What was Yuwen Yan doing here at this time?","Only the Emperor maintained a calm expression and said, \"Let her in.\"","The person outside acknowledged the order.","In a moment, Princess Yuwen Yan entered.","The Grand Princess's family, who were currently resenting her, all glared at her angrily.","The Empress Dowager glanced at her, also feeling extremely vexed.","Only Yuwen Lan showed no emotion as he said, \"I was just about to summon you for questioning, elder sister.\"","Yuwen Yan replied, \"I understand. Your Majesty is probably concerned about the Ruyi Brothel incident, right?\"","As soon as she said this, everyone was taken aback again.","Was she here to voluntarily explain the situation?","The Emperor responded with an \"Oh,\" and said, \"So elder sister already knows about it?\"","Yuwen Yan said, \"The whole city is in an uproar now, everyone is discussing how Yao county magistrate beat someone half to death in the street. How could I not know?\"","Seeing her brazen attitude, the Empress Dowager had lost all patience and spoke up, \"Since you know, there's no need for small talk. Just now, Ankang's husband has already explained that he beat someone because Ankang was harassed. It's said that you were the one who took Ankang to that Ruyi Brothel?\"","Yuwen Yan nodded quite frankly, \"Yes, Mother Empress, that's correct.\"","Seeing this, before the Empress Dowager could say anything, the Grand Princess angrily burst out, \"Why did you take Ankang to such a place?\"","Yuwen Yan replied, \"I was idle that day, so I took her there for a bit. It's just a place for entertainment, and moreover, Ankang didn't do anything wrong. Why is Aunt making such a fuss? If men can go to brothels, why can't women go to the Ruyi Brothel?\"","\"You...\"","These words infuriated the Grand Princess's family.","But before they could retort, Yuwen Yan continued, \"None of this matters right now. What's important is that Yao Junliang's beating incident has escalated to this point, and it's likely to affect the royal family's reputation.\"","Huh, so she does care about the royal family's reputation?","Everyone was practically laughing from anger.","Yuwen Lan spoke up again, asking her, \"Then what does elder sister suggest we do now?\"","Yuwen Yan said, \"Naturally, whoever made the mistake should bear the responsibility. Isn't it said that even the emperor is subject to the same laws as common people when he breaks them? Since Yao county magistrate beat someone, let the Capital Prefecture handle the judgment.\"","What a fine \"whoever made the mistake should bear the responsibility.\"","Hearing this, the Grand Princess's family was practically spitting blood.","Yao Junliang, in a fit of anger, once again knelt before the Emperor and said, \"Your Majesty, I was the one who beat the man. I am willing to be dealt with according to the law. I request Your Majesty's permission to divorce the county lord. This way, it won't affect the royal family's reputation!\"","As soon as he said this, the Ankang county lord immediately shook her head and started crying again, saying, \"No, no, I don't want a divorce!\"","Her mother, the Grand Princess, also became anxious and hurriedly said, \"Does this matter really require a divorce? Besides, they were the ones who seduced a married woman first. What man in the world could tolerate that? Isn't this just a natural human reaction?\"","Ankang county lord's father, the old Prince Consort, also anxiously said, \"That Ruyi Brothel shouldn't even exist in the first place. How can there be such an outrageous establishment?\"","But as soon as he finished speaking, Yuwen Yan snorted and laughed, \"Uncle's words are quite biased. Brothels are everywhere in the world. If men have places to enjoy themselves, why can't women have the same?\"","The old Prince Consort was stumped, nearly rolling his eyes at her.","The Empress Dowager finally couldn't hold back and spoke up, \"While that may be true, both men and women in this world should uphold their morals. You don't have a husband now, so it's fine, but Ankang and her husband were living happily together. Why did you have to take her there?\"","Yuwen Yan still maintained an indifferent attitude, saying, \"Even if I shouldn't have taken her there, she could have chosen not to go later, right? This time, it wasn't me who told her to go, was it?\"","Yanshu, who was quietly observing on the side, thought to herself, [That's because she was drugged without knowing it, and so were you!]","Tsk, this foolish woman keeps getting deceived over and over, yet still hasn't learned her lesson.","Today she's still stubbornly arguing with everyone. I don't know whether to admire her or laugh at her.","It's clear she's been spoiled by her family!","However, if the matter of the Love-Inducing Powder doesn't come to light, Yao Junliang will indeed be at a disadvantage.","So now there's only one breakthrough point - the poisoning of the princess and county lord by the Ruyi Brothel.","Unfortunately, she had been so focused on watching the drama unfold today that she forgot to remind the Emperor.","Thinking of this, Yanshu couldn't help but feel guilty, and she urgently tried to think of a way to bring up this matter...","— Should she mention that the Grand Princess looked unwell and suggest she see a doctor?","But the Emperor had already brought that up this morning, and she didn't take it seriously at all!","Just then, they saw the Grand Princess sway, her eyes roll back, and she suddenly began to collapse to the ground.","The old Prince Consort, Ankang county lord, and Yao Junliang were startled and quickly moved to support her, urgently calling out, \"Your Highness, what's wrong...\"","The Empress Dowager frowned and said, \"Could this be from anger?\"","Yuwen Lan immediately ordered, \"Quickly, go find an imperial physician to check the Grand Princess's pulse!\"","As he spoke, he gave Fu Hai a meaningful look.","Fu Hai understood immediately and hurriedly went to fetch a doctor from the Imperial Medical Academy.","Not long after, he was seen leading an imperial physician back quickly. It was none other than Jiang Nianqi.","Yanshu was surprised. Isn't this her capable and outspoken personal physician?","...How did Fu Hai know to find him?","Before Dr. Jiang could bow in greeting, Yuwen Lan had already instructed, \"Quickly, examine the Grand Princess.\"","Dr. Jiang immediately complied, hurrying to the Grand Princess's side. He checked her eyelids and felt her pulse, then asked those nearby, \"Was Her Highness emotionally agitated just now?\"","The old Prince Consort immediately replied, \"Indeed she was! She was so angry she couldn't even speak.\"","Dr. Jiang then addressed everyone, \"Her Highness is suffering from anger-induced fainting. After I apply a few acupuncture needles and she gets some good rest, she should be fine. She must avoid getting angry again in the next few days.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"Then quickly apply the needles.\"","She then turned to scold Yuwen Yan, \"How can you be so disrespectful? Look how you've angered your aunt.\"","Yuwen Yan didn't take it to heart, but outwardly she obediently lowered her head and said, \"Yes, please forgive me, Mother. I was just feeling a bit wronged earlier...\"","However, before she could finish speaking, she suddenly swayed as well, almost unable to stand.","Seeing this, Yanshu was startled.","[What's going on? Could it be that the Love-Inducing Powder is taking effect?]","The system said, [Not exactly. There's a type of incense called Bai Zhuo in the hall right now, which happens to react with the Love-Inducing Powder.]","Bai Zhuo incense?","Yanshu was confused.","— She remembered that the Empress Dowager used Wu Chen incense. She had asked about it once when she found the scent pleasant.","Meanwhile, the Emperor was asking the Grand Princess, \"Elder sister, are you feeling unwell too?\"","Yuwen Yan tried to put on a brave face, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty. I, I probably didn't get enough sleep last night...\"","Before she could finish, she swayed again.","This frightened everyone, and they hurried forward to support her.","Seeing this, Yuwen Lan said, \"Elder sister, you shouldn't force yourself.\"","He then instructed Dr. Jiang, \"After you're done examining the Grand Princess, please check on the Grand Princess as well.\"","Yanshu thought, \"!!!\"","This is it!!!","When Dr. Jiang examines the Grand Princess, he's bound to discover the matter of the Love-Inducing Powder.","But...","How could this be such a coincidence???","How did the incense in the hall suddenly change to Bai Zhuo, which happens to react with the Love-Inducing Powder?","Just as she was thinking this, Dr. Jiang had already come to Yuwen Yan's side.","As he felt Yuwen Yan's pulse, Dr. Jiang's brow furrowed deeper and deeper.","The Empress Dowager anxiously asked, \"What's wrong? Is the Grand Princess seriously ill?\"","Jiang Nianqi replied, \"Your Majesty, Your Highness... I'm afraid this isn't illness, but poisoning.\"","Poisoning?","At these words, everyone in the hall was stunned.","However, immediately after, the Ankang county lord, who had been standing by the Grand Princess's side, also swayed, almost falling over.","Yao Junliang quickly reached out to support her, exclaiming anxiously, \"What's wrong with the county lord?\"","Yanshu thought, \"...\"","Could it be...","She was also poisoned, so she reacted to the Bai Zhuo incense in the hall?","Then Yuwen Lan ordered again, \"The county lord is unwell too? Then please examine her as well.\"","Dr. Jiang complied and went to check the Ankang county lord's pulse.","After a moment, he concluded, \"Your Majesty, Empress Dowager, both the Grand Princess and the county lord have been poisoned, and it seems to be the same poison.\"","\"What?\"","Everyone in the hall was shocked.","After the initial shock, the Empress Dowager was the first to react, saying, \"Didn't they both visit that... Ruyi Brothel? Your Majesty, could there be a problem with that place!\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Mother is right. It seems that establishment is the most suspicious.\"","He then ordered, \"Come, immediately investigate the Ruyi Brothel on Yang Lou Street thoroughly, leave no corner unchecked.\"","Someone outside the hall immediately responded, and quickly dispatched the Imperial Guard to raid the Ruyi Brothel.","Seeing this, Yanshu felt relieved but also puzzled —","She couldn't help but feel that today's events seemed a bit too coincidental.","— Both the Grand Princess and Ankang county lord had been given the Love-Inducing Powder, and the hall just happened to be burning Bai Zhuo incense?","The Ankang county lord had just arrived at the Ruyi Brothel when Yao Junliang followed...","Come to think of it, who exactly informed Yao Junliang?","Could it have been... the Emperor?","She looked up at him, only to see him seriously asking Dr. Jiang, \"How are the Grand Princess and county lord? Is the poison easy to cure?\"","...He showed no signs of anything unusual.","However, Yanshu thought of something else.","Since everyone was here, why not have Dr. Jiang examine Yao Junliang as well?","Yuwen Lan thought, \"...\"","She certainly worries about a lot."]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52","paragraphs":["With one command from the emperor, the Imperial Guard sprang into action. In less than half a day, they had thoroughly searched the Ruyi Brothel from top to bottom.","Not only did they uncover the Western \"Love-Inducing Powder\", but also more than ten other types of aphrodisiacs.","Following the trail of the Love-Inducing Powder, they discovered that seven or eight men from Rouran were actually spies, intending to extract state secrets from the noble ladies who frequented the establishment and send them back to Rouran.","Given the gravity of the situation, these men were immediately imprisoned in the imperial dungeon under strict guard. The Ruyi Brothel was shut down at once, and the rest of the people involved were detained for further investigation.","The next day, the news spread throughout the court and the country, causing a great uproar.","People were shocked to learn that such an establishment existed on the seemingly ordinary Yanglou Street in the capital.","In their astonishment, some cursed the Rouran for their deceit and cunning; others condemned the people of the Ruyi Brothel for their moral depravity and shamelessness.","However, many women secretly wondered what the Ruyi Brothel was like, and whether the men there were truly as handsome as Pan An, the legendary beauty.","Some even regretted not knowing about it earlier, wishing they could have gone to feast their eyes.","...","Of course, compared to the outside world, the royal family was more concerned about the health of the Eldest Princess and the Ankang county lord.","After all, the Love-Inducing Powder was a top-grade aphrodisiac from the Western Regions, not only addictive but also leaving residues in the body. They feared the two women might have difficulty overcoming its effects.","Fortunately, the Ankang county lord's visits to the Ruyi Brothel had been relatively short, so she was less affected. Thanks to the timely discovery, Imperial Physician Jiang treated her with acupuncture and medicine for three consecutive days, finally expelling the remaining toxins and restoring her to normal.","After detoxification, the first thing the Ankang county lord did was to apologize to her husband.","\"Aliang, I'm sorry...\" the Ankang county lord said, tears flowing before she could finish speaking. She cried like a pear blossom in the rain, \"It's all my fault for not controlling myself, causing you to lose face... I will never have such thoughts again, and I will never go to any teahouses or taverns again. Will you forgive me?\"","As she finished speaking, she saw her husband's face tighten, remaining silent for a moment.","Her heart sank in despair, and she could only continue through her tears, \"If you truly can't forgive me and want a divorce, I will go ask for the Empress Dowager's decree... But, but what about the children... wuwuwu...\"","Before she could finish, her husband pulled her into his arms.","Yao Junliang, with reddened eyes, said, \"Considering that the county lord was victimized, it doesn't matter that I lost face. Now that the truth has come to light, let's never mention the past again.\"","After these words, the couple embraced and cried together, finally reconciling.","The next day, they went to the palace specially to express their gratitude.","At that time, Yanshu was paying her respects in the Palace of Benevolent Peace. The emperor had just finished the morning court session and came to the Palace of Benevolent Peace to report to the Empress Dowager on the progress of the spy case. She listened in.","\"The Ministry of Punishment has confirmed that these spies have been in the Ruyi Brothel for half a year. It's now certain that they were sent by the Rouran royal family. I have ordered the Court of State Ceremonial to send a letter to Rouran. If there's no response, these people will be executed on the spot.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and exclaimed in surprise, \"These spies have been in the capital for half a year? If it weren't for the incident with Ankang and her husband, no one would have discovered them? It's terrifying to think about. I wonder if they obtained any secrets?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"It's not too bad. Most of their contacts over the past six months were merchants' wives, so they mostly obtained information about various families' business affairs. They had hoped to contact the families of military officials through the Eldest Princess, but fortunately, the Eldest Princess didn't have many close acquaintances there, except for the Ankang county lord.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"Thank goodness Ankang wasn't so foolish as to let them get anything. However, these people are truly cunning to use such methods. It's really hard to guard against.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded with a serious expression, \"Therefore, we must strictly control the activities of these foreign tribes in our land from now on. I have ordered all prefectures and counties to immediately investigate the foreigners within their borders and keep track of their whereabouts in real-time.\"","\"The emperor has indeed considered everything thoroughly.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and then asked, \"What about the other people in the Ruyi Brothel?\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"Mother, please don't worry. The Ministry of Punishment and the Ministry of Justice have interrogated them one by one. Most of the men were selling their looks for money. Apart from using aphrodisiacs on their female clients and some theft of jewelry and money, no other illegal activities have been discovered so far, and there's no evidence of collusion with these spies.\"","\"That's good to hear.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"These men, really. They have hands and feet, why don't they walk an honest path? To resort to such methods to make money, it's truly despicable.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, and for a moment, he couldn't help but recall his experience at the Ruyi Brothel that night...","Tsk, disgusting.","He really couldn't understand how these men could do such things...","Just then, he heard the Empress Dowager's inner thoughts, [I wonder what those men look like, to be able to bewitch those women like that? I heard that the one who drugged the Eldest Princess was even called Pan Zai'an? Could he really be as handsome as Pan An?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","...The Empress Dowager was curious about this too?","Tsk, for some reason, although they had been mother and son for over twenty years, he felt that the Empress Dowager had been increasingly different from before lately...","At this moment, Yanshu, who had been silent all along, spoke up and asked, \"Then... may I ask how Your Majesty plans to deal with the remaining men?\"","[Tsk, the female owner of the Ruyi Brothel will surely be punished for letting the wolves in, so does that mean the Ruyi Brothel will have to close?]","[What will happen to these people?]","[Will they go elsewhere to resume their old trade?]","[I wonder if there are other places like this...]","Yuwen Lan, who had been listening silently: \"...\"","Why was she concerned about this?","...Was she planning something?","However, immediately after, the Empress Dowager also nodded and said, \"Yipin has a point. Your Majesty, how do you plan to deal with them?\"","[Tsk, if they're released, I wonder if they'll return to their old trade? Will the Ruyi Brothel be able to reopen?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Why was even the Empress Dowager concerned about this???","They were just some shameless men who didn't seek to improve themselves, how could they be so attractive to women???","He held back his thoughts and managed to maintain a normal expression, saying, \"If they are indeed innocent, the court will release them. However, they have hands and feet and are in the prime of their lives. I plan to arrange for people to teach them some skills so they can do honest work in the future.\"","Yanshu nodded and said, \"I see. Your Majesty is merciful.\"","But in her heart, she thought, [Then, won't those lonely rich ladies have much less fun? Tsk tsk tsk, how pitiful. Men can go to brothels, women should be able to go to male brothels too, right? There should be a place to release pressure, shouldn't there? Being a rich lady isn't easy either.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Just then, a palace servant reported from outside, \"Your Highness, the Ankang county lord and her husband seek an audience.\"","Hm?","Yanshu was surprised. The two of them came together?","Could it be that they've reconciled?","The Empress Dowager was also curious and quickly said, \"Let them in.\"","The servant acknowledged, and soon the couple entered the hall.","They both bowed in unison, and the Empress Dowager looked at the Ankang county lord and asked, \"How are you feeling?\"","The Ankang county lord, with a face full of shame, lowered her head and said, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Highness. I have recovered. I was foolish and made a mistake, causing worry for Your Highness and His Majesty, and bringing ridicule upon myself from the whole world. I have truly let Your Highness and His Majesty down.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"Enough. Considering that you were also a victim, now that you've recovered, I and His Majesty can rest easy. In the future, remember to be more cautious and don't let yourself be easily deceived again.\"","She then looked at her husband, Yao Junliang, standing beside her and said, \"You two should live well together from now on.\"","Yao Junliang responded along with his wife, his face showing no unusual expression.","Yanshu observed this and couldn't help but think to herself —","From the looks of it, the couple has reconciled, which shows that this county magistrate truly loves his wife.","However...","The county magistrate's problem hasn't been cured, which is a bit of a pity. Should I find a way to recommend Imperial Physician Jiang to him?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Why was this girl so enthusiastic about helping people solve such matters?","Just then, he heard the Empress Dowager say, \"Speaking of which, that Imperial Physician that day was truly skilled. I heard that even in the Western Regions there's no antidote for that drug, yet he managed to cure it. You should properly thank him.\"","Upon hearing this, Yao Junliang also nodded hurriedly and said, \"The Empress Dowager's words are absolutely correct. Fortunately, we encountered such an Imperial Physician. My wife and I were thinking of personally thanking Imperial Physician Jiang another day.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly and then asked, \"How come we haven't discovered this talent before? I heard he was specifically treating Consort Yi's illness? How did Consort Yi discover him?\"","Caught off guard by being mentioned, Yanshu was startled and could only say, \"This humble consort was feeling unwell one time, and happened to meet Imperial Physician Jiang on duty. After taking his medicine once, I recovered, and that's when I discovered Imperial Physician Jiang's excellent medical skills.\"","At this point, she suddenly had an idea and quickly added, \"Oh right, Imperial Physician Jiang is knowledgeable in many areas. Not only can he treat common ailments, but he's also capable of handling many difficult and complex diseases. I heard that many people outside the palace seek him out, calling him the Guanyin who grants children.\"","— Tsk, she could only say this much.","She wasn't sure if Lord Yao could understand the hint. If she said any more, the Empress Dowager might become suspicious of her.","After all, Imperial Physician Jiang was an expert in male health issues!!! Lord Yao, you should go see him quickly!!! It would be beneficial for family stability, harmony, and happiness!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Indeed, she couldn't say more.","Afraid that she might accidentally blurt out something else, he also spoke up, \"Indeed, I've heard of this as well.\"","After saying this, he specifically looked at Yao Junliang and said, \"If you have any difficult ailments, you can certainly seek him out for treatment.\"","Upon hearing this, Yao Junliang's heart skipped a beat.","[Your Majesty... what does this mean? Could he already know about my... problem?]","[How... how did His Majesty find out about this???]","On the surface, he quickly responded, \"Yes, Your Majesty.\"","Meanwhile, Yanshu observed this and wondered to herself —","The Emperor's words... seemed like he was hinting at something?","Could it be that he also knows about Lord Yao's injury?","But thinking about it, that shouldn't be the case!","Usually, men would be very concerned about such matters and wouldn't easily disclose them...","How did the Emperor come to know about this???","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Tsk, it seems he'll need to be more discreet in front of her in the future.","However... wasn't he just trying to help her?","Otherwise, if she kept pondering about such matters every time she saw Yao Junliang, how could he bear it?","Compared to the Ankang county lord, the Eldest Princess wasn't so fortunate.","Due to her prolonged and frequent interactions with the Rouran spy, and especially because she had taken not only the Love-Inducing Powder but also several other stimulant drugs, Yuwen Yan endured nearly five days of torment before she barely recovered.","However, the residual toxins hadn't been fully eliminated, and her body was still weak. The addiction to the Love-Inducing Powder would still flare up from time to time, causing her to suffer greatly and making her appear quite haggard.","Moreover, because the incident involved a spy and implicated her cousin Ankang, and even almost leaked state secrets, she was punished by the Emperor. A portion of her family property was confiscated, and the number of servants in her household and her salary were reduced.","It could be said that the Eldest Princess's former glory was suddenly cut by more than half.","However, the Emperor still cared about family ties, and to facilitate her treatment, he kept her in the palace.","Yet, after experiencing such a blow, Yuwen Yan was indeed unhappy. She continuously vented her inner turmoil by smashing things, throwing bedding, and even refusing to take her medicine properly.","Until the Empress Dowager came to scold her.","\"You are a princess of this country, yet you have no sense of responsibility towards your family or the state! Not only do you go out and cause trouble all day, but you also resist when people are sent to treat your illness! Search your conscience, can you face the ancestors of the Yuwen family? If you really don't want this surname, I'll tell the Emperor on your behalf to revoke your title as Eldest Princess and sever ties with you!\"","For many years, the Empress Dowager had rarely spoken such harsh words.","Her sudden anger finally frightened Yuwen Yan.","She hesitated, then could only cry, \"Your daughter is just unwilling to accept it. Why is it always me who gets betrayed...\"","The Empress Dowager continued, \"Why is it always you who gets betrayed? Good question! You're a princess, yet you go after those who are all appearance and no substance, full of vanity, and refuse to listen to advice. How can you not be deceived? The first time was bad enough, but this time you actually made such a fuss over a lowly man who sells his body, a spy from an enemy country! Look at yourself, what have you become!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, a small figure suddenly ran in from outside and threw herself onto Yuwen Yan, crying, \"Mother is sick and uncomfortable, Grandmother, please don't scold Mother anymore...\"","It was five-year-old Lan Jun.","Seeing this scene, the Empress Dowager could no longer speak harshly and could only sigh, \"Look, apart from your own flesh and blood, who cares about you now? Yet you neglect her for those worthless men. Is it worth it or not?\"","Upon hearing this, Yuwen Yan was stunned for a long time, then suddenly hugged her little daughter and burst into tears.","\"Lan Jun, it's Mother who has wronged you...\"","The little one also started crying, \"Mother, you must take your medicine properly. Lan Jun doesn't want to be without a mother...\"","Then they heard the Empress Dowager say, \"What use is it to just say sorry? You should cooperate with the Imperial Physician to get yourself properly treated now, return to your own place, and focus on raising your daughter. That's the right path!\"","Yuwen Yan sobbed and responded with a \"Yes.\"","Returning to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, the Empress Dowager's expression finally softened.","Madam Mu, who had been staying in the Palace of Benevolent Peace these past few days, saw this scene and couldn't help but ask, \"Your Majesty, why don't you keep Lan Jun by your side? I've noticed that you've been much more cheerful with Lan Jun around these past few days.\"","The Empress Dowager snorted and laughed, \"I've already raised that man's son and looked after his daughter. Now, am I supposed to raise his granddaughter too? Let people raise their own children. If others take on all their responsibilities for them, they'll just have too much free time and cause trouble.\"","There were no outsiders in the hall, and between good friends, there was no need for formalities, so the Empress Dowager spoke her mind freely.","Madam Mu nodded and sighed, \"Indeed, you've become increasingly clear-minded these days.\"","The Empress Dowager gave a bitter smile and said, \"I've lived most of my life within these walls. If I weren't clear-minded, I would have suffocated long ago.\"","However, after speaking, she quietly sighed again —","Although she had come to terms with many things, she still had one worry at present —","What if the Yuwen family had no heir?","Not to mention Zhang Shengkang's previous diagnosis of Consort Yi, now that Consort Yi had been \"favored\" for almost half a year, yet there was still no sign of pregnancy...","This indicated that the Emperor truly had a problem!","Although they weren't blood-related mother and son, she still understood the child she had raised to some extent.","The Emperor had a deep personality and didn't easily trust people. She wanted to have Zhang Shengkang help examine him, but the Emperor was now wary of her and wouldn't allow Zhang Shengkang to get close to him at all.","Tsk, even if they used Consort Yi as a shield for now to temporarily ward off people's gossip, if there was still no heir after a long time...","Ah, it was truly worrying!","Well, let's see how long he can hold out.","Lord Yao was indeed a smart person. Having received the hint from the palace in the morning, he took the opportunity to visit Imperial Physician Jiang during the quiet afternoon hours.","It was said that Imperial Physician Jiang immediately took his pulse, examined his injury, and prescribed medicine. Upon returning to his residence, Lord Yao promptly took the medicine as instructed, very devoutly.","At this rate, it probably wouldn't take long before he could regain his former vigor.","Yanshu, following the system, finished enjoying this juicy gossip and finally felt relieved. Then, inspiration struck her, and she prepared to start writing a new story.","Tsk, this time she would use this county lord as a prototype to write a story about an inspiring young man who, despite various difficulties, perseveres in his down-to-earth struggle and finally wins the beautiful lady in the end.","However, perhaps because she had been a bit lazy recently and hadn't written much, she found that from afternoon until nightfall, she had only managed to write an introduction.","Before she could get into the flow of writing, the Emperor had already arrived.","...Yuwen Lan had actually wanted to come earlier tonight.","But unfortunately, ministers kept reporting various matters, and he was busy until the second watch of the night before he could finally get away.","He had even specially bathed and changed his clothes in Qianming Palace, and hurried over taking three steps in two, with an excited and eager heart.","Who knew that when he arrived at Ganlu Palace, he would find Yanshu sitting at the table, lost in thought.","Yuwen Lan was taken aback and asked, \"What are you doing?\"","Yanshu, completely unaware, answered truthfully, \"This humble consort wanted to write a story, but I'm a bit stuck on the plot.\"","Stuck on the plot?","This seemed to be a professional term, somewhat incomprehensible to others.","But at this moment, Yuwen Lan didn't have such great curiosity. He only advised, \"If you really can't think of anything, don't force it. Perhaps after a night's rest, you'll have it figured out by morning.\"","Then he added, \"Come, let's retire early.\"","And with that, he led her to the bed.","As she saw him start to undress, looking ready for bed, Yanshu hurriedly said, \"This humble consort still needs to bathe. Please, Your Majesty, retire to bed first.\"","However, before she could move, he grabbed her hand and said in a sultry tone, \"There's no need for a bath...\"","Every moment was precious.","Yet Yanshu, still unaware of what was about to happen, frowned and said, \"That won't do. I'll feel uncomfortable if I don't bathe. Your Majesty, please wait just a moment.\"","With that, she insisted on going to the washroom.","Yuwen Lan, who could barely contain himself anymore, was left speechless.","Why wasn't she in any hurry?","But fine, he was the emperor after all. He couldn't appear too eager.","Besides, he had waited this long. A little longer wouldn't hurt.","He had no choice but to let her go while he undressed and got into bed.","After what felt like an eternity, his beauty finally emerged from her bath, cheeks flushed and skin as white as snow, even more irresistible than before.","Yuwen Lan gazed at her hungrily, waiting for her to come into his arms.","To his surprise, she unhurriedly went to the mirror and began combing her hair.","Stroke by stroke, she smoothed out her long, dark tresses.","Then she applied some fragrant cream to her face and neck, making herself smell sweeter than flowers.","After finishing with her face and neck, she started moisturizing her hands.","From the back of her hands to her wrists and each finger, she applied the cream with meticulous care.","Yuwen Lan finally lost all patience. He threw off the covers, got out of bed, and scooped her directly into his arms.","Yanshu was startled. The world spun around her, and by the time she realized what was happening, she was already on the bed.","The man before her had dark, intense eyes. In a low voice, he asked, \"Are you deliberately teasing me?\"","Yanshu was bewildered. \"This humble consort wouldn't dare.\"","What did he mean by teasing?","She said, \"This is just my normal skincare routine.\"","Then she remembered she hadn't applied lip balm yet and was about to get off the bed again. But before she could move, he pulled her into his arms and kissed her...","It was a dizzying, intoxicating experience...","Even then, she still hadn't quite grasped the situation.","When the kiss ended, she looked at him pitifully and said, \"Your Majesty, could we rest tonight? This humble consort's hands are sore...\"","Tch, thinking back to the previous night, her hands had become unexpectedly weak.","Perhaps today's lack of dexterity was due to overuse.","Hmph.","Yuwen Lan was speechless.","He realized she had completely forgotten.","But that was alright. He remembered.","So he chuckled softly and said, \"I promise your hands won't get sore tonight.\"","With that, he kissed her again and gently pressed her down onto the bed.","What followed was a thorough conquest that left her breathless.","Yanshu was still wondering what had gotten into him tonight.","It was just a normal night, why was he so passionate?","But then, at a certain moment...","She finally remembered.","Wait, had the time already come???","Hold on, she wasn't prepared yet...","But it was too late.","...","The next day, Yanshu slept until well past noon.","Even when she woke up, her waist and back were still sore.","She felt like a limp shrimp, too weak to even walk.","She had no choice but to be lazy, asking Rendong to help her wipe her face and dress her.","As a close attendant, Rendong could guess what had happened the night before. She tactfully asked, \"What would you like for breakfast, my lady?\"","Having expended so much energy the night before, Yanshu was famished. She immediately listed off dishes, \"I want shrimp dumplings, crab roe buns, beef patties, chicken wonton soup, and also a plate of lotus seed sticky rice cake and black sesame porridge.\"","Rendong was shocked. \"Can you eat that much?\"","Before she could finish speaking, a voice came from outside, \"If she can't finish it, I will.\"","Then Yuwen Lan strode into the chamber.","Rendong and the others were startled and quickly bowed their heads in greeting.","The emperor, looking to be in an excellent mood, came directly to the bedside and asked with a smile, \"I'll join you for the meal. Is there anything else you want? Just say the word.\"","Yanshu glanced at him, noticing his imperial robe with dragon motifs was perfectly neat. She asked curiously, \"Your Majesty didn't attend morning court today?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of affirmation. \"Court has already ended. I came back specifically to have breakfast with you.\"","His expression was one of utter contentment.","He asked again, \"Is that enough? Anything else you'd like?\"","Yanshu's eyes twinkled as she nodded. \"Yes, there is.\"","He nodded. \"Then tell them to prepare it.\"","Yanshu said to Rendong, \"Also add a braised duck, some stir-fried squab, a plate of silken tofu, and a dish of fried eggplant in butter.\"","Hmph, it was a major life event after all. She had to replenish all the energy she had expended last night.","Yuwen Lan listened and nodded silently—","Indeed, last night had been a major event in his life.","With that, Rendong hurried off to instruct the kitchen.","Before long, all the delicious dishes were brought in.","Yanshu's legs were still weak, and she didn't want to walk.","Yuwen Lan simply picked her up and carried her to the table, causing Rendong and the others to blush and turn away.","Tsk tsk, His Majesty even had to carry her just to eat a meal.","He really doted on her too much.","Yuwen Lan silently agreed.","So what if he doted on her? She was his woman after all.","And so, the two began to eat.","Mmm, the shrimp dumplings had tender skins and crisp, sweet shrimp inside;","The crab roe buns burst with savory juices at first bite, so delicious it left one speechless;","The beef patties and chicken wontons were exactly what Yanshu had been craving, while the lotus seed sticky rice cake and black sesame porridge were sweet enough to warm the heart.","Not to mention the braised duck, stir-fried squab, silken tofu, and buttered eggplant—these imperial dishes were naturally beyond reproach.","Delighted by the delicious food, Yanshu didn't forget to pick up a shrimp dumpling for Yuwen Lan, saying, \"Your Majesty, try this. It tastes wonderful.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and tasted it.","Mmm, the shrimp dumpling was indeed good.","What was even more precious was that she had taken the initiative to share the delicious food with him.","Especially since she wasn't trying to curry favor or ask for anything at the moment.","It seemed that after breaking through the final barrier, their hearts had truly grown closer.","Just as he was thinking this, he saw her pick up a crab roe bun and a piece of lotus seed cake for him, and even personally ladled him a bowl of sesame porridge.","\"Your Majesty, please try these as well.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said \"Alright,\" then took a sip of the sesame porridge and ate a piece of lotus cake, feeling sweetness spread through his heart.","He marveled inwardly at how, in just one night, she had transformed into such a gentle, caring wife.","Little did he know, she was thinking to herself, [Well, since he's my man now, I should treat him better.]","[Eating well is important for sustainable development.]","Yuwen Lan was left utterly bewildered."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53","paragraphs":["\"What do you mean by 'sustainable development'?\"","Yuwen Lan was completely puzzled. What could this mean?","As he pondered, he saw Yanshu roll up some diced braised squab in a spring pancake and ladle a bowl of duck soup with meat. She brought both to him, smiling, \"Your Majesty worked hard last night. Please eat a bit more.\"","Ahem, these two dishes were excellent for nourishing the kidneys and boosting energy.","She thought that since he had started so vigorously, he shouldn't use up all his energy at once. He should replenish himself properly through food.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Alright, he roughly understood now. That phrase was probably meant to suggest he should pace himself.","However... she was overthinking this, ahem.","— After all, he had been saving up for so many years. Even if it wasn't a \"trickle,\" it wouldn't be depleted so easily.","Thinking this, scenes from last night flooded back into his mind. Yuwen Lan felt pleased as he picked up the spring roll she had prepared and began to eat.","Mmm, the squab meat was stir-fried to savory and spicy perfection, complementing the spring pancake wonderfully.","After finishing the spring roll, he drank a bowl of soup. He found the duck meat tender and flavorful, and the soup rich and delicious, leaving him feeling very satisfied.","Yuwen Lan felt comfortable all over.","— All in all, the shadows of the past had completely faded away. His life had entered an entirely new phase.","How wonderful.","The ministers all noticed that the emperor was in an exceptionally good mood today.","Not only were his thoughts clear and his decisions resolute, but when he spoke to them, there was even a smile in his eyes, making them feel quite honored.","Seeing this, once the important matters were dealt with, Hanlin Academy scholar Zou Mozhong seized the opportunity to ask, \"Your Majesty, have you had any news of the Carefree Gentleman recently? I hope nothing has happened to him?\"","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan immediately raised an eyebrow, \"Why does Minister Zou ask this?\"","Zou Mozhong replied, \"This official is merely curious. If nothing has happened, why hasn't this gentleman released a new work in such a long time? It's been over a month since the last book.\"","Hmm? It's been over a month?","Yuwen Lan found this strange, as he often saw Yanshu writing.","After thinking for a moment, he finally remembered —","Her last published story was about the case of male prostitutes, which was indeed over a month ago.","Since then, she had written a story about a daughter-in-law of the Qin'an Duke's family having an affair with a servant — but since he had gotten the Duke's son drunk and leaked the story early, it wasn't published;","She had also written a passionate and conflicted love story between a widow and her late husband's old friend — but because it involved Madam Mu's privacy, it also wasn't published...","And for the past two days, she had been busy watching the commotion at Ruyi Brothel, so she probably hadn't written anything.","Last night, she had finally picked up her brush, but then he had carried her to bed...","So he said, \"Perhaps she has had more pressing matters than writing stories, and hasn't gotten around to it for now.\"","Zou Mozhong frowned and said, \"For someone who makes a living writing stories and earning royalties, what could be more important than publishing new works?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he saw the emperor frown and say, \"Minister Zou, your words seem biased. Besides writing stories, life has many other important matters. The harmony between husband and wife, bearing and raising children — aren't these all important? Should she be writing all day long, without any other pleasures?\"","Zou Mozhong was stunned.","— They were clearly talking about the Carefree Gentleman, so why had the emperor suddenly become displeased...","He could only quickly bow his head and say, \"Your Majesty's words are absolutely correct. This official spoke out of turn. In truth, I have been feeling rather anxious lately due to pressure from the booksellers, which led to my careless words. I beg Your Majesty's forgiveness.\"","Hearing this, the emperor's expression softened somewhat, and he asked, \"How have the booksellers been pressuring you?\"","Zou Mozhong sighed and said, \"In their eagerness to obtain the Carefree Gentleman's new book, they crowd around my door all day. As soon as they see me returning home or going out, they immediately surround me with questions. There are even booksellers from out of town who have set up camp outside my house... I've barely been able to enter my own home these past few days.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Were they really so frenzied?","Well, hearing this, it seemed Zou Mozhong truly had it rough.","He could only say, \"I'll ask her about it later. If she has time, she'll surely write.\"","The Hanlin scholar said with a pitiful expression, \"I hope the Carefree Gentleman won't keep us waiting too long.\"","Tsk, having to face this debt-collecting-like situation every day when leaving the house — who could bear it?","The emperor coughed and said, \"If it's really unbearable, we can have someone set up a bed for you at the Hanlin Academy for a few days. As soon as her story is ready, we'll give it to you immediately.\"","Zou Mozhong: \"...\"","Set up a bed for him at the Hanlin Academy?","His Majesty really did have good ideas.","He could only smile bitterly and say, \"This official thanks Your Majesty for your concern.\"","At this moment, completely unaware of what had transpired, Yanshu was lounging lazily in her chambers.","For most of the day, except for meals at the table, she had been reclining on the couch.","Tsk, it wasn't that she didn't want to write stories, but her legs were weak and her waist was sore. Even walking a few steps felt tiring, let alone sitting down.","... In short, a man who had just started his sexual experiences could be quite terrifying.","As it was nearing noon and about time for lunch to be served, Fu Hai arrived carrying a wooden box, followed by two young eunuchs carrying a basket of something.","Yanshu had Rendong help her sit up and move to the outer room, and asked, \"What brings Eunuch Fu here?\"","Fu Hai smiled cheerfully and said, \"Greetings, Your Highness. With the Dragon Boat Festival approaching, His Majesty has sent this box of South Sea pearls for you to make colorful cords with. Also, fresh big cherries have arrived today. His Majesty knows you love them, so he specially sent us to bring you a basket while they're still fresh.\"","A basket of cherries?","Yanshu was stunned.","— Cherries were a rare delicacy these days, especially since they had to be transported to the capital from other regions. Even the palace didn't have many.","Apart from those offered to the emperor and empress dowager, some had to be reserved for the imperial kitchen to make desserts, and some had to be bestowed upon court officials. In previous years, she had at most been able to eat a dozen or so.","Now, a whole basket of cherries was placed before her!","And besides this large basket of cherries, there was also a box of South Sea pearls that the emperor wanted her to use for making cords?","Could this be... preferential treatment after serving him in bed?","Tsk tsk tsk, not only had the emperor given her his first time without reservation, but he was also sending so many gifts to please her. He was quite innocent indeed.","She quickly smiled and said, \"Thank you for His Majesty's great kindness.\"","Then she asked, \"Have cherries been sent to the Empress Dowager as well?\"","— Although the emperor favored her, she couldn't forget her own surname. In the palace, the Empress Dowager was the most important person. No matter what, she must never overshadow the Empress Dowager.","Fu Hai quickly nodded, \"Your Highness need not worry. Before sending me here, His Majesty had already dispatched people to deliver some to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.\"","Only then did Yanshu feel relieved. She couldn't help but crane her neck to look at the basket of cherries. Each one was plump and bright red, with green stems still attached, clearly having been delivered overnight.","She had already swallowed her saliva six or seven times, and couldn't help but sigh, \"Although my hometown also produces cherries, we couldn't buy ones as good as these.\"","— In the past, there was a cherry tree in the courtyard of her old home in Ande County. Every year, she would wait eagerly under the tree to eat cherries. However, the variety of that cherry tree didn't seem to be very good, and the cherries were quite sour.","Come to think of it, now that her parents, grandmother, and younger brother had all come to the capital, they couldn't eat cherries from their own tree anymore.","She wondered if they would be willing to buy some to try...","Tsk, although she now had a large basket, these were bestowed by the emperor and couldn't be given away casually.","Fu Hai seemed to guess her thoughts and quickly added, \"Your Highness need not worry. His Majesty has also distributed several baskets to the court officials, including one for the Household of the Earl of Loyalty and Righteousness.\"","Oh? Her parents got some too?","Yanshu was surprised.","The emperor was so thoughtful?","... He was practically reading her mind.","Now she was truly delighted. She quickly smiled and said, \"Then I shall thank His Majesty on behalf of my parents for his great kindness. Please convey my gratitude to His Majesty when you see him later.\"","Fu Hai promptly agreed and took his leave.","Yanshu immediately asked Rendong to wash a large plate of cherries and began to feast on them.","Mmm, it was rare to have cherries ripened to perfection. With one bite, the sweet and sour juice filled her mouth. They were absolutely delicious!","Yanshu wasn't a stingy person. Not only did she eat herself, but she also rewarded Rendong and Lianxin with some to eat.","The two maids felt honored and couldn't help but marvel as they ate, \"We truly benefit from our mistress's good fortune. His Majesty is treating you better and better.\"","Yanshu nodded silently.","Indeed, after last night's coming-of-age ceremony, the emperor had suddenly reached a new level.","As expected, men also needed to grow up.","Besides the cherries, silk fabrics from Jiangnan had also arrived at the palace today, intended for making summer clothes for the Empress Dowager and imperial consorts. As a result, the Internal Affairs Bureau was especially busy.","Consort Zhou, coming out of the Imperial Garden, happened to encounter the busy scene outside the Internal Affairs Bureau.","Young eunuchs were busy transporting silk fabrics and packaging cherries, working in full swing.","She stood at a distance, watching for a while, then suddenly sighed, \"In previous years, we'd send a large basket of cherries to the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion, but I'm afraid there won't be any this year.\"","At these words, the palace maid Xiu Yun beside her dared not respond.","— Ever since the Duke of Cheng'en had that incident during the sacrificial ceremony last winter, the palace had stopped including his household in various banquets and rewards.","Even during the Empress Dowager's birthday celebration a few days ago, the Duke of Cheng'en had only sent gifts to the palace in advance, not daring to show his face at the birthday feast.","So regarding these cherries... it was truly uncertain.","Just then, they saw several young eunuchs carrying baskets of cherries out, with one basket specially surrounded by ice blocks.","Consort Zhou, seeing this, couldn't help but step forward to stop them and ask, \"Where are these being sent?\"","The lead eunuch quickly replied, \"Reporting to Your Highness, these are all just now ordered by His Majesty to be distributed as rewards to various officials.\"","Consort Zhou asked again, \"What about the basket with ice?\"","The eunuch hurriedly said, \"That's to be sent to the Household of the Earl of Loyalty and Righteousness. Their residence is far, and it's hot today, so we're afraid the cherries might spoil on the way. That's why we added ice.\"","This was true. Among all the officials, only the Earl of Loyalty and Righteousness lived farthest from the palace. If it took half an hour to deliver to others' homes, it would take a full hour to their residence, doubling the journey time.","The Internal Affairs Bureau also knew that Consort Yi was currently in favor, so they naturally wanted to do their best in delivering to the Earl's household to please her.","As the words fell, Consort Zhou snorted with laughter, \"How very thoughtful of you. The ones just sent to my palace had several spoiled ones, but for the Earl of Loyalty and Righteousness's household, you even know to add ice.\"","The young eunuch hesitated, then could only say, \"Please forgive us, Your Highness. It must be that the person packing earlier wasn't careful and didn't pick good ones for you. This servant will report to the supervisor right away and have better ones sent to you later.\"","But Consort Zhou said, \"Who knows what leftovers you'll send to fool me this time? You servants are always quick to follow the trend and bully others using borrowed power.\"","The young eunuchs all knelt down and said, \"We wouldn't dare.\"","Consort Zhou wanted to reprimand them further, but Xiu Yun advised, \"Your Highness, don't lower yourself to their level. The sun is too strong, please return to the palace quickly.\"","— With the Internal Affairs Bureau so busy today, the Empress Dowager must be paying attention. If this escalated and reached her ears, the mistress would be even less favored by her.","Fortunately, Consort Zhou remembered this point and only left with a cold snort before turning to leave.","In her heart, however, she was grinding her teeth, silently repeating the name Li Yanshu with hatred.","For two days in a row, the Emperor had been passionately attentive.","Fortunately, Yanshu was young after all. After enduring the first two days, her muscles finally stopped aching, and she could move freely again.","She had already eaten more than half of the cherries, truly indulging to her heart's content this time. For the ones she couldn't finish, she had people make them into candied cherries, preserved in jars to eat slowly later.","The five-colored cord was also finished, adorned with the South Sea pearls the Emperor had given her, making it exceptionally elegant.","Of course, not forgetting the one who dug the well when drinking water, Yanshu didn't forget to weave one for Yuwen Lan as well.","— After all, he was now her man, and she should care for him as she should.","If she didn't weave one for him, who would?","In the morning, just as she finished weaving the five-colored cord, Fu Hai came to the hall to report, \"Your Highness, the Emperor invites you to Qianming Palace to taste lychees.\"","Yanshu was a bit surprised, \"Weren't lychees already sent a few days ago?\"","Indeed, at the Empress Dowager's birthday banquet, she had just eaten lychee sweet rice made with this year's lychees, which left a lasting impression.","Fu Hai smiled and said, \"Your Highness may not know, but these lychees are of a different variety. They arrive in Beijing in batches every year, and this time it's the best-tasting batch, called 'Glutinous Rice Lychee'. However, the quantity is limited. His Majesty only had some sent to the Empress Dowager, and the rest are all in Qianming Palace.\"","So that was it.","Yanshu's eyes immediately lit up.","Come to think of it, she had only heard of the famous 'Glutinous Rice Lychee' but had never actually tasted it.","So she immediately replied, \"Then I'll go right away.\"","With that, she changed clothes and fixed her hair, taking the newly woven five-colored cord with her to Qianming Palace.","At this time, Yuwen Lan was reading in the warm chamber, with a plate full of fresh lychees on the kang table beside him. Each lychee was bright red and plump, very tempting.","As Yanshu stepped into the hall and caught sight of this scene, she immediately exclaimed in her heart, \"So these are the famous Glutinous Rice Lychees!!! They really are different, each one as big as two regular ones!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Wasn't he, such a big person, more eye-catching than this plate of lychees?","However, after her internal exclamation, Yanshu finally bowed to him, \"Your subject greets Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan looked up at her and said, \"I remembered you liked the lychee sweet rice dish at the Empress Dowager's banquet, and we just received these today. Come, try them quickly.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, she grinned and said, \"Then your subject shall respectfully comply.\"","Saying this, she moved to his side and took one to peel.","Wow, no wonder these were said to be the best lychees.","The skin was soft and thin, and after just two peels, the big white flesh appeared before her eyes.","Taking a bite, her mouth was filled with sweet juice, without a hint of sourness, so sweet it left her speechless.","Most surprisingly, the pit inside was very small, only half the size of a regular lychee pit, leaving more of the white, moist flesh.","It could truly be called the most conscientious fruit!","Yanshu nodded as she ate, \"Mmm, this is indeed delicious.\"","After speaking, she noticed the Emperor silently watching her, not eating with her.","She couldn't help but pause.","What did this mean?","Could it be that he was angry because she ate first?","Tsk tsk, no matter what, he was still the Emperor. How could she forget that?","So she hurriedly peeled a new one and offered it to him, smiling, \"Your Majesty, please try it quickly. It's really delicious.\"","However, as she finished speaking, he didn't take it, but only looked at her with deep eyes and said, \"I don't want to eat lychees.\"","\"I only want to eat you...\"","But before he could finish the rest of his words, she made an \"mm\" sound and directly put the peeled lychee into her own mouth, her cheeks puffed out as she ate and said, \"Then your subject will eat it herself...\"","\"It's really sweet, Your Majesty. It's a pity you're not eating.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","This wasn't right. Couldn't she tell what he was about to say next?","— Indeed, Yanshu really hadn't caught on.","Her mind was completely focused on the lychees at this moment, eating while inwardly exclaiming, \"It's so good to be an emperor!!! To be able to eat such good fruit!!!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","The one currently being eaten was her, wasn't it?","In the blink of an eye, she had already eaten four or five, her small lips becoming red and luscious.","Yuwen Lan could no longer hold back. He directly pulled her into his arms and began to kiss her.","Mmm, how could lychees compare to her?","...","Time seemed to stand still.","Yanshu was surprised at first, but soon became immersed in it.","Mmm, lychees were delicious, and he wasn't bad either, ahem.","Until a certain moment, she felt a clear desire, and finally came to her senses.","So she hurriedly tried to break free, saying, \"Your Majesty, we can't.\"","But Yuwen Lan was reluctant to let go, saying with lingering desire, \"Why can't we...\"","After all, there were only the two of them in the warm chamber.","But she righteously reminded him, \"It's still daytime...\"","Yuwen Lan had a mischievous thought and wanted to ask, \"What's wrong with daytime?\"...","However, before he could speak, he heard her thinking to herself, \"Although it's exciting here, ministers could come at any time. What if we're suddenly interrupted in the middle, causing him trauma, and he can't perform again?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So this was what she was thinking???","He thought she would be shy...","...But why was she worried that he wouldn't be able to perform again?","He had clearly cut ties with his past completely!","Hearing this, he wanted to prove it to her even more.","But before he could make another move, a report came from outside the hall, \"Your Majesty, the Left Censor-in-chief requests an audience.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She really predicted it.","Immediately after, she stood up straight from his embrace and said, \"Then your subject will take her leave first.\"","With that, she tidied her hair, looking as if she was about to leave.","Yuwen Lan wanted to keep her, but there was nothing he could do, as the Censor-in-chief was already waiting outside.","He could only give a reluctant \"mm\" in response.","But as she turned to bow, before stepping away, she took out a five-colored cord from her sleeve and handed it to him, saying, \"Your subject just finished weaving this. I'm giving it to Your Majesty as payment for inviting me to eat lychees.\"","Yuwen Lan took it, about to raise an eyebrow - weren't the beads on this string the ones he had given her?","However, before he could speak, he saw her smile gently and exit the hall.","Yuwen Lan had no choice but to put away the colorful string, making an effort to compose his expression before calling in the Left Censor-in-Chief.","...","After leaving the warm chamber, Yanshu had just reached the main gate of Qianming Palace when she heard someone calling from behind, \"Your Highness... Consort Yi...\"","She paused in surprise and turned to look, only to see the Hanlin Academy scholar Zou who had helped her with the storybooks.","Scholar Zou quickly approached her, and after paying his respects, asked, \"May I trouble Your Highness for a moment of your time?\"","Yanshu found this curious - Scholar Zou had specifically come to find her?","This was indeed rare, so she nodded and said, \"What can I do for you, Scholar Zou?\"","Then she saw Scholar Zou say, \"I wanted to inquire with Your Highness about the Carefree Gentleman. I recall that Your Highness is also acquainted with him?\"","The Carefree Gentleman?","Yanshu was taken aback - he was looking for... her alter ego?","So she said, \"That's correct. Does Lord Zou have business with the Carefree Gentleman?\"","Immediately after, she saw Scholar Zou's face fill with dismay as he said, \"I do indeed have a matter to discuss. Would Your Highness be willing to help urge this gentleman? To be frank with Your Highness, because he has delayed in producing new storybooks, I have been harassed daily by the booksellers to the point where I cannot even return home. I've been staying at the Hanlin Academy for several days now...\"","What?","Yanshu was stunned.","-- Because she hadn't produced any new storybooks, Scholar Zou was being harassed by booksellers to the point he couldn't go home???","Seeing her look of surprise, Scholar Zou had no choice but to repeat the explanation he had given to the Emperor a few days prior.","After listening, Yanshu was deeply shocked. She now realized just how eagerly the booksellers and readers were anticipating her work!!!","And because of her laziness, Scholar Zou had been driven to such a state???","Feeling extremely apologetic, she quickly said, \"I'll send someone to deliver a message right away, urging him to write the storybook quickly.\"","As she said this, she hurried back to her own palace.","As she walked, she berated herself internally. How could she be so negligent of her duties!!!","How could she be so entranced by male beauty that she forgot her true calling!!!","It was truly unforgivable!!!","After walking for a while, by the time she entered her palace, Yanshu was already brimming with inspiration. She immediately sat at her desk and picked up her brush to write.","However, before long, she heard the system chime in with a \"ding\": [Heads up, someone's planning to harm you.]","What?","Yanshu was startled. [Someone wants to harm me again?]","...There were only three people left in the harem now.","Well, that's true. Even though only three remained, the other two hated her to death.","However... Wang Zhaoryi had already been thoroughly subdued, from winter until now.","In comparison, the other one was more likely.","Tsk, this Consort Zhou, really preventing her from writing her storybooks in peace!","So she said, [What is she planning to do this time?]","But before the system could respond, she heard Lianxin come in and ask, \"My lady, the Empress Dowager has sent someone to inquire if you are available. Princess Lan Jun wants to come play with you. Are you free?\"","As soon as these words fell, the system chimed in again: [Here it comes, a frame-up. Be careful.]","Yanshu was startled. A frame-up?","Could it be...","Consort Zhou was planning to use Lan Jun to cause trouble?","The little girl wanted to come play with her, so if something were to happen to the child in her palace, it would be blamed on her?","Hmph!","She immediately flew into a rage. How dare that vicious woman target a child!","However, angry as she was, the pressing matter now was that with the Empress Dowager asking like this, she had no way to refuse...","Suddenly struck by inspiration in this urgent moment, she quickly said to Lianxin, \"But His Majesty just said he wanted to go admire the lotus flowers at Taiye Pool with me later! How about this - ask the little princess if she'd like to come along?\"","Lianxin quickly agreed and went out to relay the message to the person who had come to inquire.","Meanwhile, Yanshu hastily wrote a few lines on a piece of paper, dried the ink, folded it, and placed it in an envelope. She handed it to Rendong, saying, \"Quick, deliver this to His Majesty, and say that I have an extremely urgent matter!\"","Although Rendong didn't understand, seeing her urgency, she quickly agreed and immediately set off for Qianming Palace.","Now, Yuwen Lan had been busy in Qianming Palace for a while, and just as several ministers were leaving, he received Yanshu's \"urgent letter\".","Hearing that she had an urgent matter, he immediately opened it to read.","He saw that it contained two lines of poetry --","\"I dwell at the head of the Yangtze, you at its tail. Thinking of you daily but never seeing you, we both drink from the Yangtze's waters.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow --","Hmm? She actually wrote him a love poem?","This was truly like the sun rising in the west.","Reading on, he saw that after the poem there was another line --","\"I hear the lotus flowers at Taiye Pool are in full bloom. I wonder if Your Majesty would accompany this humble consort to admire them?\"","Yuwen Lan raised his eyebrow again.","She... was inviting him to admire flowers?","Didn't they just see each other?","But thinking back to the scene earlier, he secretly wondered if perhaps she had been... disappointed earlier, and thus wanted to see him again?","Ahem, thinking of it this way, he suddenly felt a bit restless too.","Unable to sit still any longer, he immediately got up and went to Taiye Pool.","The imperial carriage was swift, and after Yuwen Lan arrived, he waited for a while before finally seeing Yanshu arrive unhurriedly.","However, seeing her in a gauzy dress, her hair seemingly freshly styled, her graceful figure flickering in and out of view through the gauzy fabric, it was truly enough to make one's heart flutter.","\"This humble consort greets Your Majesty.\"","Seeing her smile and curtsy, Yuwen Lan said warmly with a smile, \"We've only been apart for a short while, and you already miss me?\"","As he spoke, he pulled her up and directly into his embrace.","-- Well, after all, he had already sent all the surrounding people far away.","However, before he could make his next move, he heard a childish voice behind him ask, \"Uncle Emperor, what are you doing?\"","Yuwen Lan was startled and quickly turned to look, only to see his niece, little Lan Jun, tilting her head and looking at him.","Looking further, he saw that behind Lan Jun stood Madam Mu's little daughter, Ni Xiangwan.","At this moment, that little girl was so frightened that she had turned her head to the side, looking as if she was about to run away.","At the same time, he heard Yanshu inwardly clicking her tongue, [Fortunately the Emperor arrived first, I timed this well! As they say, raise a man for a thousand days, use him for one hour. Emperor, don't let it go to your head, do something useful!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54","paragraphs":["What does it mean to \"raise a man for a thousand days and use him for a moment\"?","And what does \"it's good that he came first\" mean?","At this moment, hearing Yanshu's inner thoughts and seeing her young niece suddenly appear along with the Ni family girl, Yuwen Lan finally realized something.","...His beloved consort hadn't actually invited him here to admire the scenery.","Looking at his young niece's pure and clear eyes, Yuwen Lan had no choice but to quickly straighten Yanshu up and let go of her hand. He coughed and said, \"Why is Lan Jun here?\"","The little girl replied in a crisp voice, \"Because Consort Yi wanted to bring us here to play!\"","She then pulled the Ni family girl in front of the two of them and said, \"And Sister Xiangwan is here too.\"","Ni Xiangwan awkwardly bowed to the two of them and said, \"Greetings to Your Majesty and Consort Yi. The young princess wanted to play with Consort Yi, so the Empress Dowager and my mother asked me to accompany her here.\"","\"I see,\" Yuwen Lan nodded, then raised an eyebrow at his beloved consort and said meaningfully, \"So why did everyone end up here together?\"","He just wanted to know what she was up to now.","What was her purpose in gathering everyone here?","Yanshu coughed and smiled, saying, \"Well...I heard the lotus flowers are blooming beautifully these days, and I've been wanting to invite Your Majesty to come admire them. It just so happened that right before I left, I heard the young princess wanted to see me, so I decided to have her join us. After all, the more people there are to enjoy the scenery, the merrier.\"","Of course, she hadn't known Ni Xiangwan would come along. The person who came to inform her had only mentioned Lan Jun looking for her.","However, since the Crown Princess was still recovering these past few days, the mother and daughter were still staying in the palace. Hearing that Madam Mu was also about to return to Mingzhou, the Empress Dowager had invited them to stay a few more days.","The Ni family girl had been playing with Lan Jun every day, so it wasn't surprising for them to appear together now.","But the question was...","Which one of them did Consort Zhou intend to use to frame and incriminate her?","Tsk tsk tsk, it's a good thing she wasn't in her own palace. Otherwise, if Consort Zhou had succeeded and something happened to these two little girls, the Empress Dowager, the Crown Princess, and Madam Mu would all hate her.","Even if the Emperor wanted to protect her, he might not be able to!","...","Listening silently up to this point, Yuwen Lan had more or less understood.","It seemed Lan Jun wanted to play with her, and that Zhou woman planned to cause trouble, so she had foreseen it and asked him to come as a precaution?","Heh, and here he thought she actually missed him...","Of course, if the Zhou woman truly intended to do such a thing, then her choice was not bad.","So after a brief moment of disappointment, Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"Very well, since we're all here, let's go together.\"","With that, he sat down in the pavilion.","However, little Lan Jun didn't want to admire the scenery. She looked around and immediately asked Yanshu, \"Consort Yi, where is your talking bird?\"","Yanshu was stunned. Talking bird?","She asked in confusion, \"Is the princess referring to an all-black mynah bird? But I don't keep any mynah birds.\"","The little girl shook her head seriously. \"It's not all black, it's colorful. Consort Zhou said you have a colorful bird that can speak like a person. It's supposed to be very beautiful.\"","Consort Zhou?","Yanshu paused, suddenly understanding.","Heh, she had wondered why Lan Jun suddenly wanted to come play with her.","It was indeed Consort Zhou's doing.","She could only say to the little girl, \"Consort Zhou must have been joking with the princess. I don't have any such magical birds here. If I did, I would have shown it to the princess first thing.\"","After she finished speaking, the Ni family girl also persuaded from the side, \"Consort Yi is right, Consort Zhou was just joking with the princess. I haven't seen such a bird either.\"","Lan Jun immediately pouted.","Her curiosity had been dashed, and the little girl was naturally a bit unhappy.","But soon, she looked around and her eyes lit up when she saw boats on the Taiye Pool. She turned to Yuwen Lan and said, \"Uncle Emperor, can we go boating together?\"","Yanshu was startled. Before Yuwen Lan could speak, she quickly dissuaded, \"That's not a good idea. There are so many mosquitoes by the lake, and the boats are unstable. What if someone falls into the water? Let's play on shore instead.\"","Damn, she was on high alert now, afraid that if anything happened to these two little girls, Consort Zhou would pin the blame on her.","That's why she hadn't dared to bring even a plate of snacks or a pot of tea today.","She was just hoping they could sit here for about half an hour, then safely escort Lan Jun and the Ni family girl back to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Fortunately, the Ni family girl was quite sensible. Hearing Yanshu say this, she also hurried to persuade little Lan Jun, \"Consort Yi is right, princess. Let's just play on shore.\"","With two wishes unfulfilled in a row, the little girl was naturally even more unhappy. Unwilling to give up, she looked at Yuwen Lan with one last glimmer of hope.","However, she saw her imperial uncle say, \"Indeed, the lake is dangerous. Let's just play in this pavilion for a while.\"","The little girl pouted, thinking there was nothing fun about sitting in this pavilion.","She looked at the lake surface again. A patch of lotus flowers was in full bloom, with green lotus leaves spread like little umbrellas densely covering the water's surface. Birds and dragonflies flew back and forth between them, making it look quite lively.","But the most interesting things were the green lotus pods among the flowers.","She really wanted one.","But she didn't dare say it.","Because Uncle Emperor looked so fierce when he wasn't smiling...","However, after a short while, the little girl really couldn't hold back anymore. She carefully asked Yuwen Lan, \"But...what if Lan Jun wants a lotus pod?\"","The little girl blinked her eyes, which held both expectation and a hint of fear, looking quite pitiful.","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment, then said, \"Then you sit here obediently, and I'll have someone pick some for you.\"","That would work too. The little girl immediately nodded and agreed. Yuwen Lan then instructed Fu Hai to find someone to pick lotus pods.","Seeing this, Yanshu also breathed a sigh of relief, thinking that surely nothing could go wrong with the lotus pods from the lake.","But even if something did happen, it was the Emperor who had ordered someone to pick them for his niece. In any case, it had nothing to do with her.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Fine, it really had nothing to do with her.","And he didn't believe that Zhou woman could cause any trouble with lotus pods from the lake either.","Soon, a bunch of fresh lotus pods were picked and brought over. Little Lan Jun immediately beamed with joy. She chose the biggest pod from among them, then took out a small apricot from her little cloth bag and put them together to show everyone. She said sweetly, \"These are all for Mother. Lan Jun wants to give these to Mother.\"","Speaking of which, recently the Crown Princess had been actively cooperating with the imperial physicians in her treatment, showing signs of turning over a new leaf. She was also treating her daughter much better than before.","As a result, little Lan Jun was also concerned about her mother in everything, wanting to show filial piety by giving her mother all the good things she found.","The little girl was so adorable and sweet that even the apricot seemed cute. Yanshu couldn't help but smile and say, \"Which tree did this apricot come from? How is it as beautiful as the little princess?\"","Little Lan Jun giggled and said, \"It's from the Imperial Garden. Sister Xiangwan helped me pick it. Sister Xiangwan ate one too, she said it was very sweet.\"","Hearing this, Ni Xiangwan explained with embarrassment, \"We had just arrived and were on our way here when the little princess saw the apricots in the Imperial Garden looking good. I asked the palace servants if we could pick them, and they said yes, so I picked two. I couldn't resist and tried one.\"","Of course, Ni Xiangwan was only a thirteen-year-old girl who had been doted on by her mother since childhood and had a naive and lively personality. Picking an apricot wasn't really overstepping any boundaries, especially since she had asked the palace servants first.","But when Yanshu heard this, she was suddenly stunned.","She had been so afraid of someone tampering with these two girls' food and drink today that she hadn't dared to prepare anything. Yet despite all her precautions, she hadn't expected them to pick and eat apricots on their way here?","Tsk, although she didn't know if there was anything wrong with the apricots, she was now seeing danger everywhere and felt extremely nervous.","But she couldn't let others notice, so she could only try asking Ni Xiangwan, \"Was the apricot sweet?\"","Ni Xiangwan nodded with a blushing smile and said, \"It really was very sweet, like it had been coated in honey. I've never eaten such delicious apricots outside the palace.\"","Yanshu suddenly felt something was off.","As far as she knew, the few apricot trees in the Imperial Garden were of ordinary varieties, mainly used for viewing the blossoms in spring. She had picked and eaten them before, and they weren't that sweet.","So she quietly asked her system, \"Could there be something wrong with that apricot?\"","The system replied, \"Yes, Consort Zhou had someone put drugs on it.\"","What???","Yanshu was stunned.","However, before she could speak, Ni Xiangwan suddenly staggered and then unexpectedly coughed up a mouthful of blood, falling backwards.","Yanshu's eyes widened, and she immediately cried out, \"Save Miss Ni, quickly save Miss Ni!!!\"","By the time the Empress Dowager and Madam Mu received the news, Ni Xiangwan was already unconscious.","Fu Hai and others carried her back to the Palace of Benevolent Peace. The young lady who had been lively just moments ago now had her eyes tightly shut, her face turning purple, with traces of blood still at the corners of her mouth.","Seeing this scene, Madam Mu cried out \"Xiangwan\" and nearly fainted.","The Empress Dowager also hurriedly asked, \"What happened to Xiangwan?\"","Fu Hai replied, \"Your Majesty, just now His Majesty, Consort Yi, the young princess, and Miss Ni were admiring flowers by the Taiye Pool. Suddenly, Miss Ni started vomiting blood. His Majesty immediately summoned the imperial physician and ordered us to quickly bring Miss Ni back.\"","As he spoke, Yuwen Lan, Yanshu, and little Lan Jun also arrived. The Empress Dowager anxiously asked again, \"What happened?\"","Yuwen Lan said gravely, \"We don't know either. We were just talking normally when Miss Ni suddenly vomited blood and fainted.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the imperial physician entered the hall. Yuwen Lan then said, \"Let the physician examine her first.\"","The Empress Dowager agreed and quickly ordered people to make room around the bed for the physician to treat Ni Xiangwan.","The physician lifted the young lady's eyelids, felt her pulse, and used a silver needle to sample the blood remaining on her lips. He quickly concluded, \"Your Majesty, Empress Dowager, Miss Ni has been poisoned.\"","Upon hearing this, Yuwen Lan's heart skipped a beat. So the apricots were indeed poisoned.","The Empress Dowager was shocked, \"What? How could she be poisoned out of nowhere?\"","Yanshu hurriedly said, \"Earlier, this concubine was chatting with Lan Jun and Miss Ni. I heard them say they had picked apricots in the Imperial Garden. Miss Ni ate one, saying it was very sweet. Right after she said that, she vomited blood and fainted.\"","Although she was now free from suspicion, it was unfortunately too late to stop the Ni family's young lady when she found out.","After all, the system only warned her of her own dangers, just like the previous time when the fake Consort Xu attempted to assassinate the emperor. It wouldn't warn others.","When Ni Xiangwan was picking apricots, she was hurrying to the Taiye Pool.","This Consort Zhou, to harm her, actually came up with such a vicious method!","Just imagine, if little Lan Jun hadn't wanted to save the apricot for her mother and had eaten it like Ni Xiangwan, wouldn't two innocent people be unconscious now?","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager frowned at Yanshu and said, \"Weren't Xiangwan and Lan Jun supposed to visit you today? Why were they picking and eating apricots on the way?\"","Yanshu paused, then immediately lowered her head and said, \"This concubine doesn't know either.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan quickly interjected, \"I know Mother is worried, but I arrived at the Taiye Pool first today, followed by Consort Yi. Miss Ni and Lan Jun arrived last. Before that, they hadn't met. So Consort Yi wouldn't know why Miss Ni ate apricots on the way. We should ask the palace maids who were attending to Miss Ni and Lan Jun.\"","— When one is overly concerned, even the usually calm Empress Dowager would struggle to discern right from wrong in her anxiety.","On the surface, since the emperor and Lan Jun were together today, they obviously couldn't have harmed Ni Xiangwan, so only Yanshu seemed suspicious.","That's why Yanshu acted so correctly today, immediately calling him to the Taiye Pool when she noticed something was wrong.","If she had been slightly slower, Ni Xiangwan would have certainly collapsed in her palace.","If that had happened, would the Empress Dowager, in her anger, have listened to her explanation?","Now, hearing Yuwen Lan's words, the Empress Dowager regained some clarity. She immediately turned to the palace maids who had entered with Lan Jun and asked, \"What exactly happened?\"","As everyone knew, Lan Jun and Ni Xiangwan had been staying in the Palace of Benevolent Peace these past few days, so these palace maids were from there.","Upon hearing this, the palace maids immediately knelt down and said, \"Please understand, Empress Dowager. These past few days, the young princess often played in the Imperial Garden and always wanted to pick apricots there. We thought the apricots weren't ripe yet, so we didn't let the young princess pick them. We didn't expect that when we passed by today, the apricots smelled very sweet. The young princess wanted to pick them again, so Miss Ni picked two.\"","This explanation cleared Yanshu of any connection to the incident.","However, the Empress Dowager immediately turned to Lan Jun, who was being held by Yanshu, and anxiously asked, \"Did you eat that apricot?\"","The little girl obediently shook her head and took out the uneaten fruit, saying, \"Lan Jun wanted to save it for mother, so I didn't eat it.\"","The Empress Dowager finally relaxed a bit, but then Yuwen Lan instructed the physician, \"Can you tell if there's anything wrong with this fruit?\"","The physician complied and carefully examined the fruit. Suddenly, he said, \"Your Majesty, there's a tiny needle hole in this fruit. It's very likely that something was injected into it.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone came forward to look. Indeed, there was a tiny needle hole near the stem of the apricot.","Upon closer inspection, they could smell a strong sweet fragrance emanating from the needle hole.","The physician thought for a moment, then suddenly exclaimed in shock, \"Could this be the scent of aconite nectar? It's extremely poisonous!\"","What? Extremely poisonous?","Upon hearing this, Madam Mu, who had been by her daughter's side, immediately cried out to her daughter lying on the bed, \"Wan'er, Wan'er, wake up...\"","The Empress Dowager, both anxious and angry, immediately said, \"Who could have such a vicious heart!\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"I'll have the Inner Court Supervisory Office investigate immediately. Whoever is responsible will not be spared. But the urgent matter now is to save Miss Ni.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and quickly ordered Zhu Shu, \"Go fetch Chief Physician Zhang immediately.\"","Zhu Shu complied and immediately left to find him.","— It seemed that for such a potent poison, only the most skilled physician from the Imperial Medical Academy could cure it.","The situation was urgent, and in no time, Zhang Shengkang, the Chief Physician of the Imperial Medical Academy, arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","The Empress Dowager didn't even let him perform the customary greetings. As soon as she saw him, she said directly, \"Hurry, you must wake Miss Ni up.\"","— This was her best friend's precious daughter, and an innocent life. No matter what, nothing could happen to her.","Zhang Shengkang immediately complied and hurried to the inner chamber to treat Ni Xiangwan.","Meanwhile, the source of the poison was being urgently traced.","Led by palace servants, the Inner Court Supervisory Office quickly found the apricot tree in the Imperial Garden. They immediately picked all the fruits and examined them one by one. Sure enough, they found similar needle holes on the stems of most of the fruits.","The needle holes were extremely small, almost impossible to see without careful inspection.","These punctured fruits all had a sweet, fragrant smell emanating from the needle holes.","When the juice from these fruits was squeezed out, any ants or insects that came into contact with it died instantly.","Or when a few drops of the juice were added to water, within a quarter of an hour, all the fish in the tank would float belly-up.","After examination by three or four imperial physicians from the Imperial Medical Academy, they all confirmed that this toxin was indeed aconite nectar.","The extremely poisonous nectar of the aconite flower.","After hearing the report, Yuwen Lan sneered, \"Very well. Even the fruit trees in the Imperial Garden can be poisoned in such a secretive manner with such a potent toxin. What are you all good for?\"","Yao Shun, the head of the Inner Court Supervisory Office, felt his legs weaken and immediately knelt down, saying, \"We have failed in our duties. Please calm your anger, Your Majesty.\"","The Empress Dowager, also furious, asked, \"Where are the people from the Imperial Gardens Bureau? How could they not know that perfectly good fruit trees have been poisoned like this!\"","Yao Shun hurriedly replied, \"Your Majesty, we have already interrogated all the gardeners from the Imperial Gardens Bureau responsible for the Imperial Garden, but they all claim to know nothing about it.\"","Seeing this situation, Yanshu silently sighed.","— Of course the people from the Imperial Gardens Bureau didn't know. After all, this was done by someone from the Bird Department of the Imperial Animal Husbandry Office on behalf of Consort Zhou.","Tsk, who would have thought that even when Consort Zhou had fallen so low, there were still people willing to work for her as long as she paid.","At this moment, she was the only one in the hall who knew the truth. She couldn't remain indifferent. After some thought, she tentatively spoke up, \"Besides the Imperial Gardens Bureau, who else frequently moves around in the Imperial Garden? It seems that to poison every fruit would take time, it couldn't be done all at once, right?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan nodded and added, \"They would also need to avoid being seen. Is there anyone who often goes to the Imperial Garden at night?\"","Upon hearing this, Yao Shun, the head of the Inner Court Supervisory Office, had a sudden realization and immediately said, \"There are also people from the Bird Department. They often release and exercise birds in the Imperial Garden, and some birds are even released at night.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Then go investigate immediately!\"","Yao Shun complied, quickly getting up from the ground and leading his men out again.","About an hour later, he returned and reported, \"Your Majesty, Little Lin from the Sparrow District has just confessed that he was the one who did it.\"","The Empress Dowager immediately asked, \"Who ordered him to do it?\"","Yao Shun hesitated, coughed, and then said, \"Little Lin stated that Zhao Laishun from Zhongcui Palace gave him 100 taels of silver to do it.\"","What?","Everyone in the Palace of Benevolent Peace was stunned.","Zhongcui Palace?","Wasn't that Consort Zhou's residence?","The Empress Dowager was also taken aback, but then angrily commanded, \"Bring Zhao Laishun and his master to me!\"","The palace servants complied.","Before long, they brought Zhao Laishun and Consort Zhou.","At first, Consort Zhou showed no sign of panic and simply asked, \"May I inquire why the Empress Dowager has summoned me?\"","The Empress Dowager's face was stern as she questioned coldly, \"Someone poisoned the apricot tree in the Imperial Garden. Ni Xiangwan is now unconscious. A servant from the Sparrow District has already confessed that it was done by a servant from your palace. Were you aware of this?\"","Consort Zhou feigned surprise and said, \"How could such a thing happen? I'm only hearing about this now... Please understand, Empress Dowager, I have no grudge against Miss Ni. Why would I harm her?\"","The Empress Dowager laughed coldly, \"I'm also wondering why you would harm her when you have no grudge. Then who was it today that told Lan Jun that Consort Yi had a talking bird, encouraging Lan Jun to go play with Consort Yi?\"","She had initially thought her niece was just joking with the little girl, but never imagined her niece could be so malicious.","However, when this was brought up, Consort Zhou defended herself, saying, \"I was just joking around. How could I have known Lan Jun would take it seriously? You can't blame this on me, can you? How could I have known Lan Jun and Miss Ni would go to Consort Yi together? It's all just a coincidence. You can't determine my guilt based on mere coincidence, can you?\"","-- She had carefully planned everything, spending money to hire people, having someone follow the two little girls to know where they usually played, and even had the remaining poison hidden near Ganlu Palace. If only the two girls had gone to Ganlu Palace and the poison had taken effect, that bitch Li Yanshu would have been unable to defend herself...","Why hadn't the two little girls gone to Ganlu Palace as planned, but instead went to Taiye Pool, with the Emperor present no less?","Regardless, she couldn't let this fall on her head now.","The Empress Dowager was, after all, her aunt. She didn't believe her aunt would punish her own family for the sake of that adopted girl from the Ni family!","Yuwen Lan, who had been silently listening, now understood everything.","But it wasn't enough for just him to understand; he needed to make the Empress Dowager understand too.","Fortunately, at that moment, Xiao Shunzi rushed in from outside and reported to him, \"Your Majesty, Zhao Laifu, who hid something outside Ganlu Palace, has confessed that Consort Zhou ordered him to do so.\"","What?","Everyone was stunned.","Something hidden outside Ganlu Palace?","And this Zhao Laifu was Zhao Laishun's brother, both serving in Zhongcui Palace.","Consort Zhou was shocked.","Zhao Laifu had suddenly disappeared earlier. Had he been captured by the Emperor's men?","Before she could figure it out, the Empress Dowager angrily commanded, \"Take these people away for severe interrogation. I want to know who has such a vicious heart to harm others like this!\"","Everyone complied.","The Empress Dowager's attitude was now crystal clear.","It seemed she was thoroughly angered this time and had decided to disregard family ties and her maiden family, determined to give Madam Mu an explanation.","Sure enough, before long, the brothers Zhao Laifu and Zhao Laishun both confessed that Consort Zhou had instructed them to do this, with the aim of framing Consort Yi.","However, even though the truth had come to light, the implicated young lady from the Ni family was still unconscious.","Zhang Shengkang had immediately begun treating Ni Xiangwan upon arriving at the Palace of Benevolent Peace, using acupuncture and sealing acupoints, causing her to quickly vomit some black blood. However, even after more than two hours, Miss Ni remained unconscious.","The Empress Dowager was anxious and asked, \"Why hasn't Xiangwan woken up yet?\"","Zhang Shengkang frowned and explained, \"Your Highness, you may not know that this aconite honey is extremely poisonous. Moreover, some time has passed between Miss Ni's poisoning and the onset of symptoms. I'm afraid the poison has already spread to her internal organs.\"","Even those who didn't understand medicine could tell how serious this was. The Empress Dowager anxiously asked, \"How confident are you in treating her?\"","Zhang Shengkang replied, \"I dare not conceal the truth. I'm afraid I only have a 50% chance of success. Even if we can wake Miss Ni up, her mind... may be damaged.\"","Upon hearing this, Madam Mu nearly fainted.","The Empress Dowager also repeatedly exclaimed, \"What are we to do!\"","That damned girl, she wanted to have her cut into a thousand pieces!","Seeing this situation, Yanshu also sighed inwardly and couldn't help but question the system, [As a harmless and good system, how can you stand by and watch without helping? If you had told me even half an hour earlier, this young lady wouldn't have to suffer like this!]","The system replied, [??? I'm your system, not hers. If I told you about every murder, arson, robbery, and theft happening every day, could you keep up? Besides, even if you knew half a day earlier, Consort Zhou had already poisoned the apricot tree. There's a saying, 'One doesn't turn back until hitting a wall.' If you had exposed it, would others have believed you? Would the Empress Dowager have had the heart to severely punish her own niece?]","[The imperial court is inherently cruel. It's either you die or I perish. Even if a Bodhisattva came down, they couldn't manage all these wolves and tigers. Moreover, misfortune might be a blessing in disguise. This young lady might gain something unexpected from this ordeal.]","Yanshu felt like coughing up blood, [What unexpected gain could she possibly have if she can't even wake up?]","But just as she thought this, she suddenly realized something--","If Zhang Shengkang couldn't cure her, it didn't mean others couldn't!","So she hurriedly said to the Emperor, \"I wonder if that Imperial Physician Jiang might have a solution...\"","Yuwen Lan had also thought of this person and immediately nodded, instructing Fu Hai, \"Summon Jiang Nianqi.\"","Fu Hai complied and immediately sent someone to the Imperial Medical Academy. Before long, Imperial Physician Jiang hurriedly arrived.","The Empress Dowager actually didn't quite believe his medical skills could be better than Zhang Shengkang's, but at this point, there was no other choice. She could only let him examine the young Miss Ni.","Zhang Shengkang could only step aside for now and watch.","-- He had recently heard that such a figure had emerged in the Imperial Medical Academy, helping the Princess treat the Love-Inducing Powder poison.","However, while the Love-Inducing Powder could be treated, this aconite honey was different.","In his fifty-plus years of life, he had never heard of anyone who could cure such a potent poison.","So he wanted to see how this Jiang fellow would handle it.","Of course, at this moment, apart from Zhang Shengkang, everyone in the hall was closely watching Imperial Physician Jiang's every move.","After all, this might be Miss Ni's only hope.","Under everyone's watchful eyes, Imperial Physician Jiang calmly examined Miss Ni and quickly concluded, \"This young lady has been poisoned with aconite. It's indeed quite troublesome.\"","Quite troublesome?","This statement seemed to leave some room for hope.","The Empress Dowager immediately asked, \"Is there a way to cure her?\"","Imperial Physician Jiang nodded and said, \"There is, but I need to know if this young lady's closest relative is here? I need to use the blood of her closest relative as a medicine catalyst.\"","Closest relative?","Upon hearing this, Yanshu and Yuwen Lan simultaneously looked at Madam Mu."]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55","paragraphs":["What? They need to use the blood of a close relative for the medicine?","Upon hearing this, Yanshu's first reaction was - could Ni Xiangwan's true identity be about to be exposed?","So she immediately looked towards Madam Mu, wanting to see her reaction.","However, before she could notice any reaction from Madam Mu, she realized the Emperor was also looking at Madam Mu, just like her.","She was stunned again.","Why was the Emperor looking at Madam Mu?","He didn't know that Ni Xiangwan was actually Madam Mu's own daughter, did he???","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Tsk, he had momentarily forgotten about this in his curiosity and almost gave himself away.","So he quickly tried to act natural and shifted his gaze elsewhere.","But at this moment, everyone in the hall was stunned.","The Empress Dowager said anxiously, \"This girl was adopted, and it's been over ten years now. Where can we find her blood relatives? Isn't there any other way?\"","Imperial Physician Jiang replied, \"I beg your pardon, Your Highness, but this is truly the only option now. Aconite is extremely poisonous, and after all this time, the young lady's blood and internal organs have all been contaminated by the toxin. Without the blood of a close relative as a catalyst to help expel the poison, this young lady will likely remain in a coma, barely breathing. Even if she miraculously wakes up, her mind and motor functions will likely be impaired.\"","The Empress Dowager drew in a sharp breath.","This outcome was similar to what Zhang Shengkang had described earlier.","So it seemed that if they wanted Ni Xiangwan to fully recover, using the blood of a close relative was indeed the only way.","Everyone who heard this sighed inwardly, feeling that there was no hope for Miss Ni.","Alas, how could heaven be so cruel to such a good young lady?","First, she was abandoned by her birth parents, and just when she finally found such a good adoptive mother in Madam Mu, she suddenly fell victim to such a tricky poison.","What could be done now?","The Empress Dowager was also on the verge of despair, feeling extremely guilty and not knowing how to explain this to her good friend.","However, at this moment, Madam Mu spoke to Imperial Physician Jiang, \"Just use my blood then.\"","What? Everyone was stunned.","Yanshu's heart settled, silently sighing that indeed, blood ties triumph over all else. At this critical moment, Madam Mu still couldn't bear to lose her child.","Yuwen Lan thought the same.","In such a difficult situation, Madam Mu had finally made the right choice.","However, apart from these two, the rest who were unaware of the truth were completely baffled.","The Empress Dowager thought her good friend had become confused in her panic and quickly reminded her, \"A'Yu, he said they need the blood of a close relative, it has to be Wan'er's birth parents to work.\"","Unexpectedly, Madam Mu replied to her very calmly, \"I heard him, Your Highness. Don't worry, just use my blood.\"","The Empress Dowager was stunned once again.","Seeing her friend's calm and determined demeanor, she finally realized something and quickly dismissed all the unnecessary personnel from the room.","This included Zhang Shengkang, the head of the Imperial Medical Academy.","Time was of the essence. Hearing Madam Mu speak this way, Imperial Physician Jiang confirmed with her one last time, \"This absolutely requires the blood of a close relative. Are you certain, Madam?\"","Madam Mu nodded seriously once more and said, \"Yes, this child is my own flesh and blood. You can proceed without worry, Imperial Physician.\"","As these words fell, the Empress Dowager finally understood.","Her eyes were still full of surprise.","Yanshu also quickly put on an expression of great shock that she was trying hard to conceal.","However, when she inadvertently glanced at Yuwen Lan, she saw that his expression was very calm.","\"???\"","Strange, why didn't he look surprised at all?","This was such major news!!!","Just as she was thinking this, she heard him speak, \"The most urgent matter now is to save the person. Imperial Physician Jiang, please proceed quickly.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang immediately responded with a \"Yes,\" and promptly opened his medicine box to take out a dagger. He prepared some gauze and a silver bowl, rolled up his sleeves, and was about to draw blood from Madam Mu.","Yuwen Lan glanced over and saw Yanshu stretching her neck to get a better look. He couldn't help but ask, \"Aren't you squeamish about blood?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, she had almost forgotten about that.","But she didn't want to leave, and said with a troubled expression, \"But...\"","But how could she miss this???","Using human blood in medicine to save someone!!!","It would be such a waste not to witness such miraculous medical skills firsthand!!!","However, it was too late. Hearing this, the Empress Dowager immediately said, \"Yipin, you should step out for a while, lest you faint and cause trouble.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk tsk tsk, she couldn't even watch the excitement.","She could only respond with a \"Yes\" and glance silently at the Emperor, preparing to leave.","But then she heard the Empress Dowager say to the Emperor, \"Your Majesty has had a long day. It's getting late, you should return to rest. There are important matters of state to attend to in the morning, don't overtire yourself.\"","Yuwen Lan also responded with a \"Very well,\" and then instructed Fu Hai, \"Stay here to help. If anything happens, report to me immediately.\"","Fu Hai quickly agreed.","Yanshu inwardly thought, [He can't watch either? Well, I feel a bit better now.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","After leaving the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu's mind was still on that matter -","The Empress Dowager suddenly learning about the true relationship between Madam Mu and Ni Xiangwan, yet not asking many questions or blaming her, it seems these two best friends really do have a strong bond.","But, would Madam Mu's blood work?","...If it doesn't, would they need to find Ni Xiangwan's birth father?","Tsk, if that happens, wouldn't this matter become even bigger?","Yuwen Lan listened and silently nodded - it was indeed very possible.","Then he heard her worry, [But all along it's only been General Zong quietly guarding Madam Mu, and Madam Mu doesn't even know where he is. Can they suddenly find him? Even if they can, that person would have to rush from Mingzhou to the capital. Would there be enough time?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She really does love to worry.","Even if Madam Mu doesn't know where that person is, doesn't he know?","So he spoke up, \"It's late, let's go back and rest.\"","He was about to help her onto the imperial carriage.","Unexpectedly, she said, \"It's only just past 8 PM, still a while before bedtime. I imagine there must be quite a pile of memorials in the imperial study. Your Majesty should hurry back to review them, we mustn't delay important matters.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","He frowned, \"Who was it that called me out earlier? Now you're rushing me back to read memorials? Use me and toss me aside?\"","She immediately blushed and hurriedly said, \"How can Your Majesty say such things? How could I use you and toss you aside?\"","Ahem, we haven't even used you tonight yet...","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Ahem, if she still wanted to use him tonight, why was she sending him back to Qianming Palace?","Wasn't a spring night worth a thousand gold?","He raised an eyebrow and smiled, saying softly, \"I go to Qianming Palace? What about you? Won't you be lonely going back alone?\"","But she replied righteously, \"For the sake of national affairs, I can endure. Besides, won't Your Majesty return after reviewing the memorials?\"","Tsk, mainly she was eager to know how Imperial Physician Jiang would treat Ni Xiangwan.","Even if she couldn't watch in person, she could still get the gossip in her own palace.","Moreover, she had a feeling that at this rate, that book about the widow and the loyal dog might be published soon. She needed to hurry and polish it up a bit more.","After all, poor Zou Mozhong was still hiding in the Hanlin Academy, unable to return home.","Thinking of this, she bowed to Yuwen Lan and said, \"This concubine will retire first.\"","Then she quickly walked towards Ganlu Palace.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She only thought about Zou Mozhong not being able to go home, didn't she think about him at all?","Meanwhile, in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, although the Empress Dowager still had many questions, she held them back for now and stayed by Madam Mu's side to watch Imperial Physician Jiang treat Ni Xiangwan.","They saw the Imperial Physician first draw some blood from Madam Mu's wrist, then mix it with a decoction of over ten medicinal herbs, and carefully feed it to Ni Xiangwan. Immediately after, he applied acupuncture to the young lady's main acupoints.","Before long, they saw black blood flowing out from the young lady's nose and mouth.","This sight was terrifying, and the Empress Dowager quickly asked, \"What's happening?\"","Imperial Physician Jiang said, \"Your Highness need not worry, this is a sign of the patient expelling the toxins. It means the medicine is taking effect.\"","So that's what it was.","The Empress Dowager and Madam Mu finally relaxed a little.","However, right after, they heard Imperial Physician Jiang say, \"But this young lady's poisoning is severe. I'm afraid we'll need to draw blood several more times. Can Madam endure it?\"","At these words, the Empress Dowager quickly asked with concern, \"How many more times?\"","\"You must know that Madam Mu is frail. Just watching that blood-drawing scene made one anxious for her.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang felt Miss Ni's pulse and frowned, saying, \"It will need to be done twice a day. We'll see if it works within three days.\"","What? Twice a day? For three days?","The Empress Dowager anxiously said, \"How can this be?\"","A mother's body is only mortal flesh after all. How could she withstand losing so much blood in just three days?","But then Imperial Physician Jiang said, \"That's why I wanted to ask if this young lady has any other close relatives. If so, they could help share the burden with Madam Mu.\"","Upon hearing this, Madam Mu finally said, \"She has an older brother, but... they have different fathers.\"","The imperial physician shook his head, \"If they shared both parents it would work, but having different fathers won't do.\"","As he finished speaking, the Empress Dowager quickly looked at Madam Mu.","Before she could speak, Madam Mu said, \"It's alright, I can handle it myself. It's just a bit of blood. I've already failed her so much, even if all the blood is drained from my body it wouldn't matter.\"","Seeing her like this, the Empress Dowager could only swallow her words.","This was her affair after all. If she herself was unwilling, others couldn't force the issue.","And so, a night passed. Before dawn broke, Imperial Physician Jiang needed to draw blood again.","Although Madam Mu endured it without crying out in pain, by the time a bowl of blood was drawn, her face had turned pale and she was about to faint.","Seeing this, Imperial Physician Jiang shook his head and said, \"Is this young lady's birth father no longer in this world? Relying on Madam's blood alone, I'm afraid she won't be able to hold on long enough to revive the young lady.\"","Hearing these words, the Empress Dowager finally couldn't hold back, \"At this point, why care about such things? Quickly tell me where that man is, and I'll send someone to bring him here! You say you've failed Xiangwan so much, do you want both of you to die together?\"","As her words fell, Madam Mu let out a long sigh and finally said, \"Yes, then please help me find someone, Your Majesty...\"","The next morning, as soon as Yanshu woke up, she received a message from the system: [The Empress Dowager has already sent people to Mingzhou to find General Zong.]","Yanshu's eyes immediately lit up. [What's going on? Did Madam Mu tell the Empress Dowager about this?]","The system replied: [That's right. Because her own blood wasn't enough to save her daughter, she had no choice but to ask the Empress Dowager to help find the child's father.]","Yanshu finally understood, but at the same time felt worried. [What if General Zong refuses to come? And Mingzhou is so far from the capital, even if he's willing to come, will he make it in time?]","The system: [No problem, Zong Xinghai has already set out from Mingzhou.]","Huh?","Yanshu was stunned. [How is that possible? The Empress Dowager only started looking for him this morning. It would take two days just to send a message from the capital to Mingzhou!]","The system: [Before dawn today, an urgent order to transfer him arrived at the Mingzhou coastal defense camp. That General Zong set out immediately and has already traveled dozens of miles.]","Transfer order?","Yanshu was stunned again. Why did the capital issue a transfer order last night?","Could the Emperor predict the future?","But that's not right. Even if he could predict the future, how would he know that Ni Xiangwan's birth father was General Zong?","How could he transfer exactly the right person?","Yanshu was confused all day, until night fell and Yuwen Lan entered the palace.","Yanshu greeted him with a bow, her mind full of questions. Just then, the palace servants finished setting out the meal, so she sat down at the table with him, still puzzled.","At first, Yuwen Lan didn't notice anything amiss. He glanced at the table and saw cherry pork, chrysanthemum fish, crab roe tofu, braised lion's head meatballs, salted pork soup with bamboo shoots, and other dishes - all her favorites.","He picked up his chopsticks and started eating, expecting to hear her usual exclamations of delight at the delicious food. But instead, he heard her thinking, [How should I ask him about this?]","[First, I can't reveal that I know the father of the Ni family's young lady is General Zong. Second, I can't let on that I already know he issued an order to transfer General Zong to the capital. And I definitely can't mention that the Empress Dowager was urgently looking for General Zong to come to the capital this morning.]","Because logically speaking, these were all things that she, as an imperial consort, shouldn't know about.","Ugh, it's so frustrating!","She was so anxious she couldn't even taste her favorite lion's head meatballs.","But just then, Yuwen Lan suddenly spoke up, \"By the way, this morning the Empress Dowager sent someone to Mingzhou to find a person.\"","Yanshu was startled.","Was he going to share information with her?","Her eyes darted around, and she quickly put on a curious expression, saying, \"Who is it?\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"A person called Du Xinghai.\"","Yanshu quickly let out another \"Ah\" and asked, \"What does the Empress Dowager want with this person?\"","Yuwen Lan deliberately lowered his voice, \"Can you guess?\"","Yanshu hurriedly pretended to think, \"Mingzhou... isn't that where the Marquis of Zhenhai's Mansion is located? Could this person be related to Madam Mu?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"I think so too.\"","He leaned in closer and lowered his voice again, saying, \"It's highly likely... this person is the birth father of the Ni family's young lady.\"","Yanshu quickly put on a surprised expression and played along, \"Why does Your Majesty say that?\"","In her heart, she thought, \"Tsk tsk, so the Emperor looks serious on the surface, but he's actually such a gossip!\"","Then she heard Yuwen Lan say, \"Isn't that Ni family girl currently needing blood from relatives to treat her illness? I heard this morning that after drawing blood twice, Madam Mu's body couldn't handle it anymore. So why else would the Empress Dowager be in such a hurry to find someone?\"","Yanshu immediately feigned realization and said, \"Your Majesty's words make sense. But Mingzhou is quite far from the capital. By the time they find the person and bring him to the capital, wouldn't it take several days? Can Miss Ni hold on that long?\"","Yuwen Lan smoothly continued, \"As it happens, yesterday the Ministry of Works wanted to transfer someone from the Mingzhou coastal defense to the capital to discuss rebuilding the sea walls. Someone recommended this person to me, so I issued an imperial edict last night to transfer him to the capital.\"","Yanshu paused.","So it was because of the sea wall repairs that he transferred this Zong Xinghai to the capital?","Thinking about it, it made sense. That person had been guarding the coast for years, so he must be very familiar with tides and waves. It wasn't wrong to consult him about the situation.","Tsk, looking at it this way, it really was quite a coincidence.","At this point, the questions that had plagued her all day were finally dispelled. She immediately felt relieved and regained her appetite, quickly picking up her chopsticks to eat.","Wow, she hadn't expected the cherry pork to be so perfectly sweet and salty today, tender and delicious, really whetting her appetite!","Mmm, the crab roe tofu was also fragrant and delicious, soft and smooth.","Wow, this chrysanthemum fish was cooked just to her liking, crispy on the outside and tender inside, with a perfect sweet and sour taste. If it had been served any later it wouldn't have tasted as good.","Watching her devour a bowl of rice in no time, Yuwen Lan finally felt relieved and picked up his chopsticks to eat as well.","How could he let a little foodie go without eating?","That would be a real sin.","After finishing dinner, seeing it was getting late, the two washed up and got into bed.","Ahem, as Yanshu had predicted yesterday, a pile of memorials had accumulated in the imperial study. By the time Yuwen Lan finished reading them and returned, Yanshu was already asleep.","Add to that the matter of the Ni family's young lady, and Yuwen Lan wasn't in the mood either, so he obediently slept through the night.","Today, seeing that everything was turning for the better, he naturally couldn't let the opportunity pass...","After a bout of passionate lovemaking, Yanshu drifted off into a comfortable sleep.","She didn't know how long she had slept when she vaguely heard Fu Hai's voice outside the hall, \"Your Majesty, that General Zong from Mingzhou has just arrived.\"","What?","Mingzhou, General Zong?","Weren't these the very words she was concerned about?","Yanshu's eyes snapped open, instantly wide awake.","Looking to the side, she saw the Emperor still sleeping with his eyes closed, seemingly not yet awake.","She anxiously reached out and pushed him gently twice, calling softly, \"Your Majesty...\"","But he didn't respond.","She rolled her eyes and decided to say, \"Your Majesty, Miss Ni's birth father has arrived...\"","As soon as she said this, she saw him finally open his eyes.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Indeed, the essence of human nature is to be curious about gossip, and the Emperor was no exception.","She quickly repeated, \"Your Majesty, Eunuch Fu is saying outside that General Zong has just arrived.\"","Yuwen Lan finally came to his senses and called out to the door, \"Tell him to wait in the Palace of Benevolent Peace. I'll be there shortly.\"","Fu Hai acknowledged and hurried off to make arrangements.","Yuwen Lan then sat up in bed, about to lift the covers and get up.","Yanshu quickly said, \"May this concubine accompany Your Majesty?\"","\"Since we were both open with each other last night, there's no need to pretend we don't know. I just want to see what General Zong's loyal younger admirer looks like,\" she said.","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow at her. \"This man is coming to draw blood from our daughter. Aren't you afraid you'll faint at the sight of blood?\"","Yanshu quickly replied with a smile, \"I'll look away when he's about to draw blood.\"","Yuwen Lan continued, \"He's still an outside official.\"","Yanshu persisted, \"Then I'll hide to the side where he can't see me.\"","Inwardly, she was screaming in frustration. What's with all these questions?! This is the classic scene of a father and daughter meeting for the first time, and former lovers reuniting! If I miss it, I won't be able to eat or sleep properly!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She even enjoys watching this kind of excitement? He thought she only liked watching arguments and fights...","Before he could say anything, she moved closer and clung to his arm, shaking it. \"Your Majesty... please... I really can't bear to be apart from you...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Tch, even though he knew every word was false, it was still very gratifying.","Besides, if she kept shaking him like this, they might never leave...","So he said, \"Alright, let's go together then.\"","With that, he casually reached into her embrace a couple of times before finally getting out of bed.","Yanshu immediately agreed and hurriedly got dressed and fixed her hair. Soon after, they set off together for the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","After arriving and paying their respects to the Empress Dowager, they heard a palace servant announce that General Zong had also arrived.","To maintain her daughter's treatment, Madam Mu had already endured having her blood drawn four times, and her body was on the verge of collapse. The Empress Dowager, who was very anxious at this point, immediately ordered him to come in quickly.","Yanshu also hurried to the inner chamber where Madam Mu and her daughter were to avoid being seen.","However, she still peeked through the crack in the door towards the main hall.","In a moment, she saw a sturdy man enter the hall and kneel to pay respects to the Emperor and Empress Dowager. \"Your subject Zong Xinghai pays respects to Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager.\"","So this is the loyal younger admirer!","Yanshu was excited and tried to get a good look. She saw that he had a full beard and his face was tanned a reddish-brown.","\"...\"","This was quite different from what she had imagined.","But thinking about it, it made sense. Having received an urgent summons, he had set out immediately, able to reach the capital so quickly. He must have been riding non-stop day and night, so how could he have had time to shave?","Moreover, a man who had been guarding the sea borders for years naturally wouldn't have fair skin.","Especially since more than ten years had passed, the young wolf pup in his early twenties was now a middle-aged man.","So his appearance was understandable.","Especially looking at him again, he did have quite a masculine air about him.","Thinking of this, she couldn't help but glance at Madam Mu again, only to see that she had furrowed her brows, looking very conflicted.","Just then, she heard the Empress Dowager say, \"There's no time for small talk. I need your blood to save someone now. Quickly bare your wrist for the Imperial Physician to draw blood.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","The Empress Dowager truly lived up to her title - she was so direct.","The Emperor stepped in to smooth things over, saying, \"Don't worry, it's only a small amount.\"","Of course, even if it wasn't just a little blood but his very life that was required, Zong Xinghai was in no position to refuse at this moment.","He immediately agreed, rolled up his sleeve, and allowed Imperial Physician Jiang, who had been waiting nearby, to draw a bowl of blood.","This time, Yanshu didn't try to be brave and very consciously averted her gaze.","After all, she still wanted to watch the exciting scene of the long-separated reunion, ahem.","Imperial Physician Jiang worked efficiently, quickly preparing the medicine and administering it to the young Miss Ni.","About the time it takes to drink a cup of tea later, Ni Xiangwan, who had been unconscious for nearly two days and nights, suddenly moved her fingers and slowly opened her eyes.","Yanshu silently exclaimed \"Oh my god!\" while Madam Mu burst into tears of joy, \"Wan'er... you're finally awake!\"","Seeing this, the Empress Dowager also relaxed a bit.","She then turned to the man before her and said, \"The patient inside is related to you, which is why we needed your blood to save her life. We may need to draw blood a few more times, so I'm telling you this upfront. Are you willing?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Zong Xinghai immediately replied, \"Your subject is willing.\"","After a pause, he tentatively asked, \"May your subject inquire... is the lady alright?\"","At these words, the Empress Dowager paused, Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, and Yanshu inwardly exclaimed, \"Holy shit, he figured it out already?\"","She heard the system calmly explain, \"It's not hard to guess. This man is an orphan and has been alone for so many years. When the Empress Dowager suddenly says the patient inside is related to him, how could he not think about it? The only person in this world he's ever had a relationship with is Madam Mu. And since he doesn't know he has a child, he naturally assumes it must be Madam Mu.\"","Yanshu accurately grasped the key point, \"A man in his thirties who's only been with Madam Mu once? And just that one time? Tsk tsk tsk, he's quite the pure and loyal puppy. On par with the Emperor.\"","However... the Emperor was previously limited by his abilities, but now that he's become like this, who knows what he'll be like in the future?","If he turns into a rotten cucumber in the future, she'd kick him to the curb and live off her own money.","So, one must always be prepared for the worst and work hard to earn money.","Yuwen Lan, who unexpectedly overheard this outside, was bewildered. \"???\"","What does she mean by 'rotten cucumber'?","Why would she kick him?","And why, when she was watching other people's business, did she suddenly bring him into it?","And with such a... fierce tone?","Just then, they saw Madam Mu suddenly emerge from the inner chamber and say to the travel-worn man, \"I'm fine.\"","At these words, everyone's attention turned to the two of them.","Yanshu raised an eyebrow. Had Madam Mu been unable to contain her longing and decided to meet him? Ah ah ah, what an exciting scene had just unfolded so unexpectedly!!!","Sure enough, Zong Xinghai froze for a moment, then suddenly knelt down and said, \"My lady... this subordinate has wronged you...\" His words were accompanied by tears.","Yanshu couldn't help but feel her eyes sting with emotion. How touching, how touching.","But then, they heard Madam Mu say, \"Don't say that. Back then... I was willing too. Now, I have something to tell you.\"","Yanshu paused again.","— Holy crap, is Madam Mu going to tell him about the child?","For a moment, she almost forgot to breathe.","Then, sure enough, they heard Madam Mu say, \"You and I... we have a child.\"","As these words fell, the Emperor and Empress Dowager both turned to look at General Zong.","Even Imperial Physician Jiang, who was guarding the patient in the inner chamber, pricked up his ears."]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56","paragraphs":["Unsurprisingly, as Madam Mu finished speaking, everyone turned to look at Zong Xinghai, who had rushed here from afar.","Tsk tsk, the exciting moment had arrived!!!","Let's see how this man would react upon learning that he actually had a child!!!","Zong Xinghai was stunned.","— What?","He and she had a child together?","After a moment of shock, once he confirmed he hadn't misheard, Zong Xinghai furrowed his brows and asked in disbelief, \"Madam... is what you're saying true?\"","Madam Mu nodded, her expression complex as she replied, \"If it weren't true, why would I have called you to travel so far?\"","As her words fell, Zong Xinghai finally became excited. With tears glistening in his eyes, he looked around trembling and asked, \"Then, where is the child? Boy or girl? Are they alright?\"","\"It's a daughter,\" Madam Mu said tearfully. \"She's both well and unwell. She just had a brush with death - I almost lost her...\"","Before she could finish, her nose stung again and tears flowed once more.","— Heaven knows how she had endured these past few days, watching her child's life hang in the balance, her heart stretched to the limit, filled with fear and grievances, yet with nowhere to vent...","Now seeing this man again, she could no longer control her emotions.","Seeing this, Zong Xinghai immediately asked anxiously, \"What exactly happened? How is the child now?\"","As they were in the palace with the Empress Dowager and Emperor present, Madam Mu could only try to compose herself and said, \"She's just gotten a bit better. Your blood is what saved her.\"","Hearing this, Zong Xinghai finally understood —","No wonder the Empress Dowager had spoken that way earlier, no wonder the court had summoned him to the capital from so far away...","So his blood was meant to save his own daughter?","But what exactly had his daughter gone through? Why had she been at death's door?","Just as he was getting anxious, he heard Madam Mu continue, \"I'm telling you all this today with no other intention. The child has just woken up, and we'll need to continue using your blood for her treatment. I just wanted to make things clear to you, to see if you're willing to save her.\"","\"Willing! How could I not be willing?\" Zong Xinghai immediately rolled up the sleeve of his other arm that hadn't been used for blood drawing yet, and said urgently, \"However much is needed, just take it.\"","As long as it could save his daughter.","— He actually had a child.","After being alone for so many years, he actually had a daughter!","And he was only finding out now!!!","During all those past days, how much had the mother and daughter endured?","Thinking of this, he felt guilty and remorseful, wishing he could give his entire life to the two of them.","Seeing this, Madam Mu felt reassured and quickly said, \"There's no need to be so hasty. It will probably take another two or three days, drawing blood twice a day should be enough. Let's follow the Imperial Physician's instructions.\"","Zong Xinghai immediately nodded in agreement.","After a pause, he tentatively asked, \"May I... see the child...\"","But as soon as he said this, someone emerged from the inner chamber and said to him, \"It's best not to meet just yet. Your daughter has just woken up and is still weak. We must avoid any extreme emotional fluctuations. It's better for you two to meet after she's recovered.\"","Zong Xinghai was taken aback, but seeing the official robes the person was wearing, he quickly realized this must be the Imperial Physician treating his daughter. He immediately cupped his hands in salute and said, \"Although I haven't been able to fulfill my duties as a father these years, I still thank the Imperial Physician for saving my daughter's life.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang nodded quickly and said, \"It's nothing. Saving lives is a doctor's natural duty. There's no need for such formality, sir.\"","He paused, then continued, \"The past few days have been hard on Madam Mu, drawing blood to save her daughter. She's grown weak and can't carry on anymore. It's good that you've arrived now, sir. However, you've had a long journey, so you should rest well and take care of your own health.\"","Zong Xinghai nodded repeatedly, \"Yes. Thank you for the reminder, Imperial Physician.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang nodded as well, about to return to the inner chamber to check on the patient.","But before turning around, he glanced at Zong Xinghai once more.","In his heart, he thought, [The bone structure is exactly like his daughter's. They're definitely related by blood.]","Yuwen Lan, who silently overheard this, thought \"...\"","So he had come out specifically to look at the man?","At this moment, Madam Mu suddenly knelt down and performed a deep bow to him, saying, \"This humble servant requests punishment from Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan came back to his senses and asked, \"What crime has Madam committed?\"","Madam Mu replied, \"After my late husband passed, this servant failed to remain chaste and made a mistake. After having the child, I further lied and claimed she was an adopted daughter. For all these years, I have deceived Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager. I truly deserve death. This servant has failed the Empress Dowager's trust and is unworthy of the title bestowed upon me. Now I dare to beg Your Majesty to allow this servant to care for my daughter for a few more days. Once she recovers, this servant will willingly accept punishment.\"","Before Yuwen Lan could say anything in response, Zong Xinghai became anxious.","He immediately knelt down before the Emperor as well, saying, \"I beg Your Majesty to see clearly. It was I who erred first back then. I should not have coveted my master's wife, and I should not have left after committing the mistake... Madam was entirely implicated by me, your humble servant. Please punish me instead, Your Majesty. Please do not blame Madam, she is innocent.\"","As his words fell, everyone felt complex emotions.","Yuwen Lan heard Yanshu quietly sobbing, [It's so touching! There really are good men in this world after all!]","\"???\"","What did she mean by \"there really are good men in this world\"?","In her eyes, was he not a good man?","He then heard the Empress Dowager thinking to herself, [This Zong fellow at least dares to take responsibility for his actions. Ayu didn't care for him in vain. I wonder what the Emperor is thinking? He won't side with those stubborn old men and actually blame Ayu, will he?]","[Hmph, if he really does that, I'll have raised him for nothing.]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","...When had he ever expressed that he would side with those stubborn old men?","Tsk, now faced with this double pressure, in order to demonstrate the magnanimity of a good man and prove that he hadn't been raised in vain, Yuwen Lan spoke to Madam Mu, \"Madam, your words are too harsh. When your late husband passed away early, you single-handedly supported the household and raised the child. You have already lived up to your late husband's spirit in heaven. What happened between you two occurred after your husband's passing and did not violate ethics. After having the child, you did not heartlessly abandon her, but carefully raised her. If there is any wrongdoing, it would be concealing the truth about her parentage from your daughter, which has shortchanged her somewhat. As for the rest, what crime is there to speak of?\"","As his words fell, he finally heard the Empress Dowager think, [Good boy, at least I didn't raise him wrong.]","However, Madam Mu covered her face and began to cry.","\"This servant thanks Your Majesty for your great kindness. Your Majesty speaks truly, the one this servant has wronged the most is Xiangwan...\"","— Indeed, although she had always tried her best to love this child, she could never bring herself to tell her the truth. For over a decade, the little girl only thought she was an adopted child, and was especially careful and obedient, always feeling inferior in her heart.","She still remembered when the little girl was four years old and happened to overhear servants gossiping, learning that she was adopted. Such a small child silently cried hiding under the blankets, breaking her heart.","So today, by speaking out, she not only wanted to tell Zong Xinghai the truth, but also to be honest with her own flesh and blood, to let her know that she had both a mother and a father, and was not lacking compared to others.","After these past few days of nearly losing her daughter, she no longer wanted her child to carry a lifetime of regret for the sake of some intangible matters.","This scene moved everyone present.","Yanshu, hiding in the inner chamber, felt her eyes grow hot.","— This family has really been through so much, oh my!","Alas, how cruel this era is to women! After losing her husband and meeting someone suitable, without harming anyone, the poor woman had to suppress herself for over a decade, and now still has to carefully beg for forgiveness everywhere.","Fortunately, the family has finally been reunited now, and that poor child has a father. But they missed out on over a decade together, during the best years of their lives!","Thinking of this, she glanced at the Emperor through the door crack again.","She thought to herself that it was good the Emperor had met her in his prime years.","Tsk, looking at how divinely handsome and refined he was now, who knew if after a decade or so, he would end up weather-beaten and scruffy like this Vice Commander Zong?","...If that really happened, how could she bear to look at him?","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Why were her thoughts always so different from others???","If she was moved, that was fine, but why did she suddenly bring it back to him?","Years later, if he really had a scruffy beard, would she not be able to stand it???","Tsk, women are indeed fickle.","However... he still decided to make an effort to take care of himself, so that he wouldn't look scruffy and weathered a decade or so later.","After pondering this, he said, \"Madam need not blame herself too much. What's done is done. The most important thing now is to treat your daughter's illness. Once she recovers, you can slowly explain the truth to her.\"","Madam Mu hurriedly agreed.","With her biological father's blood, Ni Xiangwan's recovery indeed progressed much faster.","To make it convenient for Imperial Physician Jiang to obtain the blood, the Empress Dowager specially granted permission for Zong Xinghai to temporarily stay in the guards' quarters. He was very eager to enter the palace twice daily to give blood. As a result, by the third day, Ni Xiangwan was already able to slowly get out of bed and walk around.","Seeing this, both Madam Mu and Zong Xinghai felt relieved.","The Empress Dowager also finally breathed a sigh of relief.","Thus, she finally had the energy to deal with the culprit of this incident.","— For the past few days, she had been doing everything possible to save her friend's child. Now that the child was out of danger, she had to give her friend an explanation.","Consort Zhou had been confined in Zhongcui Palace for four days and four nights.","During this time, she received no news. Only the palace maids who brought food came punctually every day, but they only delivered the meals, their faces cold and expressionless, not speaking a word to her.","The brothers Zhao Laifu and Zhao Laishun, as well as that Xiao Linzi from the bird department, had already been executed soon after the incident was exposed.","She thus fantasized that since everyone else was dead, and the Emperor hadn't dealt with her for such a long time, he might have spared her for the sake of the Empress Dowager.","After all, she was now the only hope for the Zhou family.","Moreover, the Empress Dowager didn't have her own flesh and blood, so she shouldn't sever ties with her natal family, right?","...","She kept thinking this way until early on the fifth day when someone finally opened her door and brought her to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Entering the hall, Consort Zhou took a look around. She saw the Empress Dowager's face as cold as ice, and the Emperor sitting beside her with a stern expression, not even glancing at her.","Such expressions made her feel uneasy. Consort Zhou thought for a moment, then quickly knelt before the Empress Dowager and said, \"This concubine was wrong. This concubine has reflected well these past few days and truly knows her mistake. I beg the Empress Dowager and Your Majesty to forgive this concubine this once. This concubine will definitely reform and never offend again.\"","However, the Empress Dowager said, \"It was my mistake to let you enter the palace in the first place. I knew you weren't clever and your temperament was impetuous. I only hoped you could behave yourself in the palace and bring some honor to the Zhou family. I didn't expect I was being too optimistic. Not only are you foolish, but you're also so vicious, disregarding children's lives. For the sake of your petty jealousy, you actually put innocent Lanqin and Xiangwan in danger.\"","Hearing this, Consort Zhou finally realized the gravity of the situation. She immediately burst into tears and cried, \"This concubine was wrong. Please give this concubine another chance. This concubine truly dares not do it again...\"","But the Empress Dowager shook her head and said, \"I dare not give you another chance. Keeping you here, who knows how many more innocent people you would harm.\"","Even now, the Empress Dowager was still full of anger — To compete for favor, she actually poisoned that fruit tree, targeting the five-year-old Lanqin!!! And what crime had Xiangwan committed!!!","The Empress Dowager shook her head and sighed, \"Such a vicious heart cannot be allowed to remain in the palace.\"","She then turned to the Emperor and said, \"I request Your Majesty to issue a decree, sending her to Yuzhen Palace to atone for her crimes. If the gods forgive her, may she be lucky enough to be reborn as a human in her next life. If even the gods don't forgive her, may she be thrown into the realm of animals to be a cow or horse, repaying her sins!\"","As soon as these words fell, Consort Zhou collapsed to the ground.","— Yuzhen Palace, that place specially used to confine mad women, once sent there, one could never come out!","She immediately cried, \"Aunt, how can you be so cruel...\"","However, she heard the Emperor speak, \"Issue the decree: Consort Zhou, with her vicious thoughts and evil intentions, regards human life as grass, tarnishes the imperial family's dignity, and disgraces the reputation of the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion. Her consort position is to be immediately stripped, and she is to be sent to Yuzhen Palace to atone for her crimes.\"","As soon as these words fell, someone immediately entered the hall and dragged her out.","...","The hall fell silent. Yuwen Lan looked at the Empress Dowager, wanting to say something.","— He actually hadn't expected the Empress Dowager to directly propose sending Consort Zhou to Yuzhen Palace. He had thought the Empress Dowager would at most demote Consort Zhou's rank, and he had prepared to persuade the Empress Dowager to punish her severely.","He hadn't expected the Empress Dowager to take such a stance. It seemed she was truly desperate with Consort Zhou.","However, such a judgment would undoubtedly greatly shake the Zhou family. The Empress Dowager must be under great pressure to uphold this.","So he intended to say something, just to comfort the Empress Dowager a bit.","But before he could think of appropriate words, he heard the Empress Dowager sigh inwardly, [What have I lived for all these years?]","...","At this moment in Ganlu Palace, Yanshu, having learned the whole process through the system, couldn't help but click her tongue a few times.","— What does it mean to reap what you sow? Consort Zhou was the best example.","However, for the Empress Dowager to actively propose sending her niece to Yuzhen Palace, it seems she truly had no hope for her natal family anymore.","It also showed the depth of her friendship with Madam Mu.","To give her best friend an explanation, she could go to such lengths, which was indeed rare.","Then she heard the system say, [After all, when the Empress Dowager lost her own flesh and blood and was most grief-stricken, only Madam Mu stayed by her side and truly cared for her. Her natal family, those brothers and sisters, flesh and blood relatives, only cared about their own glory and wealth.]","Yanshu sighed inwardly.","Indeed. If the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion truly regarded the Empress Dowager as family, they should have properly trained their daughter and sent her to the palace as a capable assistant to the Empress Dowager.","But not only did they raise Consort Zhou into such a character, they themselves indulged in debauchery outside the palace, keeping mistresses enough to form a football team.","Reveling in pleasure while stepping on the suffering of a woman in the palace, they were nothing but a bunch of bloodsuckers!","Tsk, thinking of it this way, the Empress Dowager was quite pitiful. At least Madam Mu had saved her daughter, and now her husband had returned. It seems that once her daughter fully recovers, the family can be reunited and have a happy ending.","Well, to help them along, she should do something productive.","So she quickly blew on the newly revised manuscript and instructed Rendong, \"Take this to His Majesty and tell him I request his help in passing it to Chancellor Zou, so he can publish the story quickly.\"","Rendong promptly agreed and took the manuscript to Qianming Palace.","Two hours later, the poor Chancellor Zou finally received the long-awaited life-saving manuscript. After reading it, he tearfully handed it to the publisher and finally returned to his long-absent home.","As expected, once Carefree Gentleman's new work hit the market, it once again caused a huge sensation.","After all, it was a new work after such a long wait. Readers who had been eagerly anticipating it all unleashed their enthusiasm and longing through their wallets. In just half a day, they bought out all the publishers' stock. Several bookstores printed more copies overnight, yet still couldn't meet the demand.","After eagerly reading the story, everyone marveled at its bizarre plot and deeply sympathized with the protagonists.","Many people were moved to tears by the family reunion scene at the end.","And while the streets and alleys were buzzing with enthusiastic discussions about this story, its protagonists were still completely unaware.","After another two or three days of recuperation, Ni Xiangwan had fully recovered.","After consulting with Imperial Physician Jiang, Madam Mu finally carefully revealed her true identity and background.","At first, the mother was very worried, fearing that her own flesh and blood might hate and resent her because of this.","But unexpectedly, the young girl had no complaints at all. Instead, she smiled in her mother's arms and said, \"Daughter can finally openly call you mother. This has been daughter's dream since childhood. I'm too happy to hate you!\"","Madam Mu smiled through her tears, and finally dared to let father and daughter meet.","At that time, Zong Xinghai, who was used to the winds and waves at sea, felt at a loss. Instead, it was the thirteen-year-old girl who took the initiative to step forward and examine him carefully, then called out, \"Father.\"","\"My father is so tall and valiant, he looks like a true hero at first glance.\"","Zong Xinghai's eyes burned with emotion, and he could only say, \"Father missed out on thirteen years of your life. How can I be called a hero?\"","The young girl smiled and said, \"Then let's punish father by having him make it up to daughter from now on.\"","Saying this, she wiped away her father's tears and took the initiative to give him a hug.","...","For the next few days, the little girl kept pestering her father with questions, and the father-daughter pair got along extremely well.","Madam Mu felt a great weight lift from her heart. She took the opportunity to express her thoughts to the Empress Dowager.","\"This humble servant knows everything the Empress Dowager has done for me, and I am deeply moved, with no way to repay you. Now that Xiangwan has recovered, I have no more worries. Please allow this servant to leave secular life and pursue spiritual cultivation.\"","She felt this was the only way to preserve her friend's dignity and allow her son to save face.","To her surprise, the Empress Dowager scolded her for being foolish. \"That man has returned, the child is well, why on earth would you become a nun now? I can see you still have feelings for him, and he for you. You might as well get on with it properly and give Xiangwan a complete family. Besides, it's not uncommon for widows to remarry.\"","Madam Mu sighed, \"Public opinion is a fearsome thing. I'm afraid everyone will criticize me for being shameless.\"","The Empress Dowager handed her a book with a smile. \"How could anyone criticize you? This is a new story that's just come out. Take a look.\"","A storybook?","Madam Mu was puzzled but accepted it and began to read.","As she read on, her face grew redder and redder. Finally, she covered her face and said, \"This... this... isn't this about me? It's too embarrassing to read.\"","The Empress Dowager laughed, \"What's there to be embarrassed about? To tell you the truth, the Emperor commissioned this story. You can see from the perfect ending that this reflects the Emperor's attitude. People outside are all praising the conclusion of this story, and many have shed tears for you. Even if they don't know it's about you, they would understand your difficulties better if they did.\"","Madam Mu was stunned. Is this really how people saw it?","The Empress Dowager continued, \"So there's no need to worry. Your child is very considerate too. Yesterday, she came to the palace specially to tell me that she wants to support you and Zong Xinghai, to give Xiangwan a proper status.\"","Indeed, in these past few days, when his sister suddenly fell gravely ill, the newly appointed Marquis of Zhenhai, Ni Xiangyi, couldn't have been unaware. Especially when he couldn't help, he was even more anxious.","As his sister recovered and the truth came to light, he initially felt conflicted. But after reading the story by the carefree writer yesterday, this young man suddenly had an epiphany and personally came to the palace to ask the Empress Dowager to support his mother.","Hearing this now, Madam Mu was both surprised and moved, unable to hold back her tears.","She sighed to the Empress Dowager, \"How fortunate I am to have raised such wonderful children.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"Isn't that because you raised them well? So there's no need to worry so much. I'll personally issue an imperial decree for your marriage. Who would dare say anything then?\"","At these words, Madam Mu's face turned as red as a beetroot. She said bashfully, \"At my age, why would I need an imperial marriage decree? There's no need to trouble Your Highness. Let's wait until I return to Mingzhou to discuss it.\"","She thought it would be better to simply inform family and friends.","She continued, \"I've already imposed on Your Highness for too long. It's time for me to return to Mingzhou.\"","After all, there was still a whole family to take care of, and her son needed to return to his duties as the Marquis of Zhenhai.","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded, \"Very well, it's up to you. However, in a few days, His Majesty will be holding water games at the Golden Bright Pool. Since you're here, why not let Xiangwan watch before you leave?\"","Every year, the court would hold water games around the Dragon Boat Festival.","Like the ice games in the twelfth lunar month, these were nominally games but actually drills for the navy.","Of course, this year the Emperor had specially increased the number of participants and asked the Ministry of War to add several new events, partly to please the Empress Dowager.","After all, the Empress Dowager's recent birthday celebrations hadn't been entirely peaceful.","Moreover, she hadn't been able to attend the ice games in person last time.","So, this was meant to make up for it.","Naturally, the water games were a popular event, especially among younger children.","The Ni family's little girl had experienced quite a tumultuous journey to the capital this time. If she could feast her eyes on this spectacle before returning to Mingzhou, the Empress Dowager would feel more at ease.","Hearing this, Madam Mu's eyes lit up, and she quickly agreed.","With the storybook selling well and the protagonists reaching a happy ending, Yanshu was in high spirits.","Especially with the water games to look forward to in a couple of days, she was full of anticipation.","In contrast, Emperor Yuwen Lan seemed to have something on his mind.","That night, before retiring to bed, seeing him frowning in deep thought, Yanshu couldn't help but ask curiously, \"What's wrong, Your Majesty? Is something troubling you?\"","Well, knowing him as a man who rarely showed his emotions, for something to be visible on his face, it must be quite significant.","Yuwen Lan did indeed have something on his mind.","Since Yanshu wasn't an outsider, hearing her question, he said, \"After the incident with Consort Zhou, the Duke of Cheng'en's family has many grievances against the Empress Dowager. Though she doesn't say anything on the surface, she must be feeling dejected. I was just thinking about how to cheer her up.\"","After all, they had been mother and son for over twenty years. Although they were wary of each other and had their own agendas, he still had affection for the Empress Dowager.","Especially since the Empress Dowager had raised him and helped him ascend to the throne. Although she wanted to protect her own interests, many of her actions weren't too unreasonable.","If he could maintain this mother-son relationship well, he was willing to do so.","As he finished speaking, he heard Yanshu thinking to herself, [Cheer up the Empress Dowager? That's easy. Just find that Grand Scholar of the Central Harmony Hall from back then and give the Empress Dowager a second spring.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Of course, Yanshu only dared to think this to herself. Out loud, she could only say, \"What would please the Empress Dowager most is surely to see Your Majesty being filial, the country prosperous and peaceful, and her having less to worry about. Perhaps Your Majesty could arrange more activities in the future, letting her meet with family and friends often, chat with people. That might help.\"","After hearing this, Yuwen Lan pondered for a moment, then nodded, \"You have a point.\"","Then he suddenly lowered his voice and said, \"The Empress Dowager probably wants a few imperial grandchildren too. I'll have to entrust this task to you.\"","With that, he rolled over and pinned her down.","...","A night of passion ensued, needless to say.","The next morning when she woke up, Yuwen Lan had already gone to court.","Yanshu lazily rolled over, just about to get up for breakfast, when she heard the system say, [There's new gossip. The Emperor just issued a decree inviting famous scholars from all over the country to come to the capital for the reopening of the Songhe Academy next month.]","At first, Yanshu didn't quite understand. [The reopening of the Songhe Academy? What's the gossip about that?]","The system replied, [That Grand Scholar of the Central Harmony Hall from back then is on the list of invitees.]","Yanshu: \"!!!\""]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57","paragraphs":["Receiving such unexpected news, Yanshu was naturally surprised and quickly asked, \"Are you really that Grand Scholar of Zhongji Hall who had a relationship beyond revolutionary friendship with the Empress Dowager back then?\"","The system replied, \"That's right, he's the top scholar from the 10th year of Xuande, who became Prime Minister in his thirties due to his talents, loyally served the Empress Dowager, and then resolutely resigned and returned home after developing feelings beyond revolutionary friendship with the Empress Dowager, fearing it would implicate her. That Grand Scholar of Zhongji Hall, Qi Shuguang.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, looking at this train-like super-long prefix adjective, it was indeed the Grand Scholar she had always been most curious about.","But... why would the Emperor suddenly invite him to the capital?","Isn't this a bit too abrupt?","Then she heard the system say, \"Grand Scholar Qi is truly a man of great learning and talent. After resigning from his official post, although he returned home to become a teacher, he quickly attracted many students due to his unique perspective and knowledge. After a few years, he simply opened an academy. The students he taught all entered official careers successfully and became talented individuals, making him very famous in Langya. He himself is a great scholar and famous teacher, and this time the Emperor is inviting famous scholars from various places, so why couldn't he be included?\"","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","This really proves the saying that gold will shine wherever it is!","This Grand Scholar Qi is too capable!!!","Moreover, hearing this makes one even more curious about him!","However...","In any case, isn't this too coincidental?","Last night when the Emperor asked her, she had just secretly thought about it, and this morning he really summoned the person?","Why does it feel a bit strange somewhere?","Then she heard the system say, \"After the incident at Songhe Academy back then, the Emperor took it over for the court. Now that the renovation is complete, it's appropriate to use the names of famous scholars to promote and restore people's and students' confidence in this academy. However, the list of invitees was recommended by the Ministry of Rites and local education officials. The Emperor issued the edict after reviewing it, so it's probably just a coincidence.\"","Yanshu: \"...I see.\"","She was just thinking, could the Emperor have mind-reading abilities?","And even if he had mind-reading abilities, he probably wouldn't deliberately bring the Empress Dowager's former love interest close, right?","Thus, her doubts were resolved, but this news still made her eyes light up—","Doesn't this mean that next month the Empress Dowager will have a chance to meet the person she regrettably missed in the past?","Tsk tsk tsk tsk, just thinking about it is exciting!","However, I wonder if this Grand Scholar is married?","If he already has a wife and children, it's better not to meet.","Then she heard the system say, \"He's not. After Grand Scholar Qi returned to his hometown, he devoted himself wholeheartedly to education and didn't have time to deal with marriage matters. Of course, it's also possible that he never met anyone he fell for again. Anyway, he has been spending his days with students for the past ten years or so.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but sigh—","Not having met anyone he fell for in over ten years, could it be that he had true feelings for the Empress Dowager?","Ah, it's really lamentable.","But of course, the Empress Dowager is the Empress Dowager after all. Madam Mu could remarry, but the Empress Dowager is different.","That kind of coincidental reunion of a broken mirror plot, she could only fantasize about in her heart, and definitely wouldn't dare to hope for it to become reality.","So, that thought she had last night was just a passing fancy, and she didn't dare to mention it to the Emperor at all.","But anyway, two people who once secretly had feelings for each other meeting again after many years is still something to look forward to.","Thinking of this, she quickly asked the system again, \"Does the Empress Dowager know about this news yet?\"","The system: \"Not yet. The Empress Dowager hasn't been in the mood to care about political affairs these past two days. Seeing that Madam Mu is leaving in a few days, the Empress Dowager is focused on saying farewell to her good friend.\"","Yanshu: \"That's true. Besides, it's only early May now, and Songhe Academy won't open until June. There's still a month to go. Moreover, it's not certain whether Grand Scholar Qi will come or not.\"","\"However, if he does come, giving the Empress Dowager an unexpected surprise at that time might be even better. Anyway, keep a close eye on it and let me know if there's any news.\"","The system: \"No problem.\"","With that, this distant prospect of gossip was temporarily heard.","Yanshu then got up to dress, wash up, and put on makeup. After getting ready, she leisurely ate breakfast.","Hmm, it's currently the season when fish and shrimp are at their most delicious. The kitchen had deboned and sliced carp, made a soup and cooked porridge with it. Eating a bowl of fish slice porridge, the fragrance of rice mixed with the savory aroma of fish meat, thick and creamy, was most delicious.","There were also dumplings made with fresh shrimp, each one full of sweet freshness and crisp texture, making one feel utterly satisfied.","In addition, she also ate a freshly fried youtiao, crispy and delicious, and drank a bowl of sweet soy milk, making her stomach very comfortable.","After filling her stomach with a breakfast that combined northern and southern cuisines, before she could think about what to do next, she saw a palace maid from the Palace of Benevolent Peace come to say that the Empress Dowager had summoned her.","Yanshu didn't know why, but could only quickly respond and go to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","When she arrived, she saw that Madam Mu was also in the hall, talking with the Empress Dowager, while her daughter Ni Xiangwan was playing with Xiao Lanyun on the side.","After being reunited with her parents, the little girl's carefree smile was even more beautiful.","Yanshu felt gratified in her heart and first bowed to the Empress Dowager, \"This concubine pays respects to the Empress Dowager.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Rise. I called you here because there's a matter I want to entrust to you. In a couple of days, there will be a Dragon Boat Festival water performance and a banquet at Jinming Pool. I don't have the energy for it right now, so you take care of it.\"","Yanshu was stunned. Does this mean... she wants her to manage affairs?","Tsk, this is really rare.","But thinking about it, it makes sense. In the imperial harem now, besides her, there's only Consort Wang who's responsible for striking the night watches.","She's the only idle person, and they can't ask Consort Wang to take on multiple roles.","She could only quickly respond, \"This concubine obeys the command.\"","After she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager nodded. Then Madam Mu said to her, \"By the way, this subject's wife still needs to thank Your Highness. If it weren't for your recommendation of Imperial Physician Jiang that day, I don't know what would have happened to my daughter.\"","After saying this, she specially bowed to her, with a very sincere attitude.","Yanshu hurriedly replied politely, \"Madam is too kind. At that time, I just happened to think of it and mentioned it. The credit goes to Imperial Physician Jiang. Of course, it must also be due to the blessings Madam has accumulated from her daily good deeds that your daughter could safely escape danger.\"","These words were appropriate and pleasant to hear. The Empress Dowager nodded on the side.","She thought to herself that this girl seems carefree and silly, but actually has some brains.","No wonder the Emperor chose her as a shield.","Of course, Yanshu couldn't hear these words.","Then she saw the Empress Dowager suddenly speak to her again, \"That day I was anxious and almost misunderstood you. Don't take it to heart.\"","Tsk, is the Empress Dowager apologizing to her?","Yanshu was flattered and hurriedly lowered her head, saying, \"How dare this concubine?\"","In her heart, she couldn't help but sigh - the Empress Dowager is an upright person, no wonder she could become the Empress Dowager.","Just then, a palace maid entered the hall and reported, \"Your Highness, Academy Judge Zhang has come to check your pulse.\"","Oh? Zhang Shengkang is here?","Yanshu immediately composed herself.","The Empress Dowager also nodded and said, \"Let him in.\"","The palace maid responded and went out to relay the message.","Soon after, the seemingly righteous Academy Judge of the Imperial Hospital, Zhang Shengkang, entered the hall.","After paying his respects, he immediately checked the Empress Dowager's pulse. After a while, he said, \"Your Highness has been in good health recently. As the height of summer has arrived, you must be careful to eat less raw and cold food, and not catch a chill.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and then said to him, \"You might as well check Miss Ni as well. They're about to set off on their journey in a few days, and I don't know if her body can withstand it.\"","Zhang Shengkang agreed, and Madam Mu quickly called her daughter over.","After taking her pulse, Zhang Shengkang nodded and said, \"Judging from her pulse, Miss Ni's health has greatly improved. As long as she doesn't overexert herself on the journey, there should be no problem.\"","After saying this, he sighed and said, \"It seems that Imperial Physician Jiang is indeed superior in skill, one must admire him.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded.","However, Yanshu raised an eyebrow inwardly - would this person be so generous as to praise someone with higher medical skills than himself?","[Of course not.]","The system immediately chimed in, [This person has felt something was off ever since he found out that Jiang Nianqi had awakened the Ni family's daughter. The day before yesterday, he even arranged for someone to spy on the Jiang household in the middle of the night.]","Yanshu immediately became nervous, [Did he discover anything?]","System: [Nothing was discovered. Imperial Physician Jiang isn't stupid - how could he be discovered so easily and still survive in the palace?]","Yanshu silently breathed a sigh of relief. [That's good then.]","However, this showed that Zhang Shengkang was truly skilled at pretending, having fooled someone as capable as the Empress Dowager into trusting him deeply for many years.","Just as she was thinking this, she heard the Empress Dowager say to Zhang Shengkang, \"I didn't expect someone as young as Imperial Physician Jiang to be so talented. It's a good thing for the Imperial Hospital to have such talent. As the director, you should cultivate and develop people like this - both the court and the common people need such individuals.\"","Zhang Shengkang bowed and said, \"To be honest with Your Majesty, there is currently a vacancy for the position of Chief Physician at the Imperial Hospital. I was considering that perhaps Imperial Physician Jiang could be suitable for the role.\"","The Empress Dowager looked pleased and nodded in approval.","Yanshu, however, didn't believe it.","— The Chief Physician was already a fourth-rank position. Would Zhang Shengkang really be so kind as to promote such a young rival?","It was probably just said for the Empress Dowager's benefit.","But then, unexpectedly, Zhang Shengkang asked her, \"Speaking of which, Imperial Physician Jiang happens to be off duty today. I wonder if Consort Yi knows where he received his training?\"","Yanshu immediately realized this was a probe directed at her.","So she smiled and said, \"I don't know about that. I only know he's not from the capital, and his hometown is probably somewhere in the Southern Yue region. But does this have anything to do with appointing him as Chief Physician?\"","Zhang Shengkang hurriedly explained, \"It's just that this isn't a decision I can make on my own. I'll need to discuss it with several imperial physicians and officials from the Ministry of Personnel. Knowing where he trained would help in introducing him.\"","— This explanation was actually somewhat far-fetched. As the director, how could he not know where such an outstanding talent under him had trained, and why would he specifically come to ask a palace consort?","The Empress Dowager glanced at Zhang Shengkang with a suspicious look.","Seeing this, Yanshu quickly added, \"Well, when he's on duty, Director Zhang can ask him personally. Though he's probably quite busy these couple of days - I heard his home was burgled in the middle of the night, so he's likely at the Metropolitan Police to report it.\"","At these words, Zhang Shengkang paused.","The Empress Dowager frowned and said, \"Is the city's security still so chaotic?\"","Yanshu hurriedly explained, \"I've heard it's improved a lot recently, but there are always some petty thieves around.\"","Madam Mu also said, \"There are such small-time thieves everywhere, it's unavoidable.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"That's true.\"","As she finished speaking, Zhang Shengkang bowed his head and said, \"I won't disturb Your Majesty any further. I'll take my leave now.\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound of acknowledgment, and he hurriedly left the hall with his medicine box.","System: [Very good. The position of Chief of the Imperial Hospital has been vacant for many years, and he's been trying to secure it recently. Fearing the Empress Dowager's suspicion, he'll probably behave himself for a few days now.]","Yanshu: [Hmph, protect our treasure Imperial Physician Jiang!]","She knew that after the incident with the Ni family's young lady, Imperial Physician Jiang could no longer hide his brilliance. Given Zhang Shengkang's jealous nature, he would certainly take notice of him.","But from what she could see now, the Empress Dowager still trusted Zhang Shengkang, so small tricks probably wouldn't shake his position.","Instead, it might alert him and arouse his suspicion about Imperial Physician Jiang's background.","This matter would need to be carefully planned.","After bidding farewell to the Empress Dowager, Yanshu returned to the Palace of Sweet Dew.","Not long after, Fu Hai led two men to seek an audience with her.","\"Your Highness, these two gentlemen are managers appointed by the Court of Imperial Sacrifices. With the Dragon Boat Festival water games approaching, apart from the essential military drills organized by the Ministry of War, there will also be some water performances for the emperor and officials to enjoy. These two gentlemen would like you to review the arranged performances to see if they are suitable.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She had just agreed to the Empress Dowager's request, and people were already here? The efficiency was too high.","She nodded and said alright, and the men handed her a list of proposed performances.","Taking it and glancing over, she saw it included water acrobatics, water puppet shows, water singing and dancing, and other crowd-pleasing performances. It was quite good.","However, the puppet shows consisted of eight or nine old-fashioned plays like \"Emperor Huan of Han's River Tour\", \"Emperor Wen of Wei Raising an Army\", \"Emperor Wu of Jin Attending a Meeting\", \"Liu Bei Crossing the Tan Stream\", and so on.","So she said, \"These stories are fine, but they're mostly what men like to watch. If you could add a few romantic stories like 'The Legend of the White Snake' or 'The Cowherd and the Weaver Girl', the ladies would probably enjoy it more.\"","\"Also, there will likely be many children there. Why not prepare a few mythological stories like 'The Eight Immortals Cross the Sea', 'Sun Wukong Causes Havoc in the Dragon Palace', or 'Chen Xiang Splits the Mountain to Rescue His Mother'? I'm sure they would like those.\"","Hearing this, the two managers from the Court of Imperial Sacrifices immediately said, \"Your Highness's words are most wise. We will arrange it right away.\"","Yanshu made a sound of agreement and continued looking down the list, when she was suddenly taken aback—","What?","They had even arranged for storytellers?","And among them was actually a book by the Carefree Scholar???","There, in black and white, were listed the titles \"The Romantic Scholar and the Beautiful Lady\", \"The Shrewd Wife Cleverly Manages Her Philandering Husband\", and the recently published \"The Plum Blossoms Twice, the Flower is at Its Prime\"!","Yanshu: \"...\"","What in the world?","Seeing her look of astonishment, Fu Hai, as one of the few people who knew about her alter ego, hurriedly explained, \"I've heard that this scholar's works are very popular lately. The Court of Imperial Sacrifices probably arranged this thinking the audience would enjoy it.\"","As he finished speaking, the two managers also nodded and said, \"General Fu is correct. Every year, many commoners vie to watch the water games. This Carefree Scholar's books are currently the most popular both in and outside the city, and they have great educational value. So we specially made this arrangement, thinking the common people would probably like to hear them, aiming for the emperor and the people to enjoy together.\"","Fu Hai quickly added, \"Mainly because we heard the Empress Dowager really likes this scholar's works.\"","The other two immediately agreed.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, for the sake of making the Empress Dowager happy, she would have to endure the embarrassment.","But while the first two were fine, \"The Plum Blossoms Twice\" was somewhat inappropriate.","— After all, Madam Mu would be present. It was one thing for her to be embarrassed, but it was better not to embarrass the person involved.","So she said, \"Actually, I've read them too. 'The Romantic Scholar and the Beautiful Lady' and 'The Shrewd Wife Cleverly Manages Her Philandering Husband' are quite good, and they also fit well with the current trend of strict official conduct in the court. Let's skip the last one, as it might cause controversy.\"","Although the Emperor was open-minded, there were inevitably some people who would take issue with the matter of widows remarrying.","The two immediately nodded in agreement and crossed out that title.","Next, they selected several songs and dances, as well as shadow puppet shows like \"Three Trips to the Flaming Mountain\" and \"Zhu Bajie Carrying His Bride\", which the children would surely enjoy watching.","With that, the cultural performance section was settled.","Fu Hai was about to lead the men away when Yanshu asked, \"Um... should we also take a look at the menu while we're at it?\"","At these words, the two managers' eyes lit up with delight, \"That would be wonderful. We were afraid of disturbing Your Highness's rest, so we didn't dare to ask...\"","Yanshu waved her hand, \"It's no trouble, just bring it over.\"","Compared to other matters, food was the most important thing, so of course she had to carefully review it!","The men immediately agreed and rushed off to fetch the menu.","...","And so, with everything arranged, three days later, the palace residents set out early for the Golden Bright Pool.","The fame of the Golden Bright Pool was known to all in the capital.","— It was an artificial lake dug on the orders of the founding emperor to observe naval battles. The pool was so large that it could accommodate dragon boats and warships.","Later, to share the enjoyment with the people, the founding emperor ordered the surrounding walls to be demolished, making the Golden Bright Pool the first royal garden without walls.","Best of all, it was located in the center of the capital, making it very accessible to the people.","Normally, civilians and tourists often came to the lakeside to enjoy the cool air and scenery. Every Dragon Boat Festival, during the water games, the entire city would empty out to watch, truly exemplifying the emperor's desire to share joy with the people.","However, this was Yanshu's first time here.","She was already full of curiosity.","As soon as she got off the carriage, she looked around and saw a rainbow bridge gallery in the pool, with vermilion-painted railings and wild goose pillars, which was what the common people called the Camel's Hump.","At the head of the bridge was a building complex of five connected halls, majestic and imposing, which was where the emperor and consorts would view the spectacle each year.","By now, painted boats and warships were already neatly lined up along the shore, making people eagerly anticipate the upcoming scenes.","Yanshu followed the imperial procession and the Empress Dowager into the hall.","Speaking of which, there were now only her and Consort Wang left in the imperial harem. Especially today, as Consort Wang had claimed illness and didn't come, so apart from her, the Emperor and the Empress Dowager, there were only the accompanying palace servants.","Fortunately, there were still Xiao Lanyun and Madam Mu with her daughter to fill out the numbers, so it didn't seem too sparse.","However, today there were still ministers bringing their families to attend, and they were already waiting on the side.","After everyone was seated, they came forward one by one to pay their respects.","The first to appear, as always, was the Grand Princess and her husband, close relatives of the royal family.","Behind them followed the Ankang county lord and his wife, along with their two children - their six-year-old son Yao Mingxu and four-year-old daughter Yao Minghan.","This large family with its thriving offspring immediately livened up the hall.","\"We pay our respects to Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and Consort Yanshu,\" the Grand Princess said cheerfully, leading her extended family in a bow.","Yuwen Lan politely replied, \"Aunt, there's no need for such formality. Please be seated.\"","The family complied and took their seats.","Yanshu quietly observed that the county lord and his wife were smiling, occasionally exchanging glances. Their relationship seemed even sweeter than before.","Ahem, it seems the treatment for the county lord was quite effective.","Imperial Physician Jiang truly blessed countless families.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Indeed, he had personal experience with this. That Imperial Physician Jiang had truly helped many people.","As the adults took their seats, the two young Yao children immediately began playing with Xiao Lanyun and Ni Xiangwan.","The hall was soon filled with laughter and merriment, creating a very lively atmosphere.","The Empress Dowager sighed meaningfully, \"It's always more lively with more children around.\"","She glanced at the Emperor as she spoke.","[Isn't this young man in a hurry yet?]","[Why not let Zhang Shengkang take a look?]","[If there's an illness, it should be treated. Is guarding against her really more important than having an heir?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","To be honest, he found himself at a loss for words for a moment.","True, initially he had indeed been guarding against the Empress Dowager, especially after the Eastern King incident, his wariness of the Empress Dowager had once been very intense.","However... it was no longer necessary now.","Seeing that he had already sown seeds so many times, presumably when the time was right, there would be results.","Thinking of this, he glanced at Yanshu again.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Look at that, every time the Empress Dowager spoke like this, he would come to peek at her.","But this wasn't something she could control.","Even seeds need time to sprout, don't they?","It hadn't even been a month yet, how could it be so quick?","The hall became a bit awkward for a moment, but fortunately, ministers began to come forward to pay their respects one after another, diverting everyone's attention.","Yanshu had now attended quite a few banquets and was familiar with most of the court officials.","However, today was a bit strange, as the Minister of Works had come with puffy eyes.","— Had he been secretly crying again last night in some secluded place?","System: [Speaking of which, this is your fault. He's a fan of your books, and these past two days he's been completely immersed in your new novel, crying several times over the twists and turns of the main characters' love story.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","So he cried like this just from reading her novel?","Tsk tsk tsk, how touching.","She felt both moved and sympathetic, thinking that perhaps she should give him an autograph one day to console him?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He wanted to advise her against it. If the minister really saw her handwriting, he might become even more heartbroken.","Next, the paper-eating Marquis of Guangyang made his appearance.","— It hadn't been long since the Empress Dowager's birthday banquet, yet this gentleman had lost another round of weight.","The Empress Dowager was very concerned and quickly asked, \"Marquis of Guangyang, are you truly ill? How have you become so thin? You mustn't hide your illness and avoid treatment.\"","Seeing this situation, before the Marquis could say anything, his wife hurriedly replied with a worried expression, \"The Empress Dowager is right. The Marquis has had a very poor appetite lately. He has seen a doctor and taken medicine, but there's been no improvement.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan also became a bit worried.","He thought that if things really didn't improve, he should remind him not to eat those strange things...","But before he could speak, he heard Yanshu think, [Today I specially had the imperial chefs prepare something suitable for him. Let's see how it works?]","Yuwen Lan swallowed his words and immediately became curious —","She had specially prepared something?","What kind of food could be suitable for the Marquis of Guangyang?","Could it be food made of paper?","Tsk, how would others eat that?","Just as he was thinking this, palace servants began to bring in several dishes of snacks.","Among them, one dish was actually made to look like a book using pancakes, with words written on it using spinach juice, making it quite a novel sight.","Yuwen Lan paused, quickly glancing to the side.","He saw the Marquis of Guangyang's eyes were already fixed intently, his heart excitedly thinking, [What, what, what is this? Is it edible? It looks like it might be very delicious!]","He thus quickly said, \"Please be seated. Have some snacks and tea. Don't stand on ceremony.\"","The Marquis of Guangyang complied and immediately sat down to eat.","In the blink of an eye, he had eaten two small pancake books, a look of satisfaction appearing on his face.","[Mmm, this texture is indeed much better!]","Yanshu finally felt relieved.","Now the Marquis's wife should know what to feed her husband, right?","— Ahem, although the big pancakes from her hometown might be a bit tough to chew, they're still very nutritious.","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan also felt quite gratified.","— His beloved consort was kind-hearted and considerate, truly touching.","Next, an announcement was heard from outside the hall, \"The Marquis of Loyal Righteousness seeks an audience...\"","Yanshu was startled. The Marquis of Loyal Righteousness? Isn't that her father?","Sure enough, she soon saw her parents enter the hall together, both dressed in formal attire, solemnly bowing to them.","Yanshu was suddenly delighted. She didn't know her parents would be coming today!","Come to think of it, because men from outside the palace weren't allowed to enter the inner palace, although she had already seen her mother and grandmother, she still hadn't seen her father.","Unexpectedly, she was seeing him today!","It truly made her happy.","Seeing this scene, the monarch on the throne was in a good mood.","He nodded and said, \"No need for such formality. Please be seated.\"","The Li couple complied and sat down in the hall.","The Empress Dowager even specially granted permission for Madam Zhu to sit next to her daughter.","Yanshu snuggled up to her mother contentedly, her heart filled with joy.","After that, several more groups of people arrived. After they had all paid their respects, they also took their seats.","When the time was about right, two painted boats sailed into view on the water in front of the hall, and the first performance of the day, a water dance and music show, began.","This scene was a first for both Yanshu and her mother Madam Zhu, and they watched with great interest.","However, not long after, the Minister of Revenue entered the hall and requested the Emperor's instructions, saying, \"Your Majesty, the newly appointed Deputy Commissioner of the Salt Administration Bureau wishes to seek an audience.\"","As it was a day for the emperor and his officials to enjoy themselves together, and it was a newly appointed official, Yuwen Lan naturally wouldn't refuse. He nodded and said, \"Let him in.\"","The Minister of Revenue complied, and soon led in a man in his thirties or forties.","The newcomer introduced himself, \"Your subject Luo Zhixue pays his respects to Your Majesty.\"","Luo Zhixue?","Yanshu paused, feeling that this name sounded familiar.","She remembered that her father had a friend who seemed to be called by this name.","Then she heard the System say, [That's right, this is the person who borrowed twenty taels of silver from your father to go to the capital for the imperial examinations, causing your father to have an argument with your mother, and then after passing the exam with high honors, he pretended not to know you and never paid back the money.]","Yanshu paused.","Hey, isn't this a case of enemies meeting on a narrow road?"]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58","paragraphs":["As soon as the system reminded her, Yanshu remembered everything.","This Luo Zhixue was her father's former classmate, though a few years younger. He had some talent but came from a poor family.","Back when her father had already passed the imperial exams and was working as an official in the county government, Luo Zhixue was preparing to go to the capital for the imperial examination. However, he was so poor that he almost missed the chance to take the exam due to lack of travel funds.","Her father was a righteous and kind-hearted man who couldn't bear to see a friend in trouble. So he secretly took out twenty taels of silver that the family had been saving for a long time to renovate their old house, and lent it to Luo so he could go take the spring examination.","Yanshu vaguely remembered the scene that night. Her father made an excuse to take her out to play while delivering the money to this man. Upon receiving the money, the man wept profusely and swore up and down that he would repay them handsomely when he returned...","The next day, the man left with the travel money. However, her mother found out that her father had secretly lent someone silver, and the two had a big argument.","Fortunately, not long after, news came from the capital that this man had passed the imperial examination with flying colors. Her father was naturally delighted, feeling that he hadn't helped in vain. Her mother was also happy, thinking that the twenty taels of silver would finally be returned and their dilapidated old house could at last be renovated.","Who would have thought that after passing the exam, this man didn't even return home, but went directly to the neighboring Jihe County to become the county magistrate, without returning a single coin of the silver.","Watching their old house leak and grow damp, her mother became anxious again and urged her father to go to his house to ask for the money back.","However, before her father could go, the Luo family unexpectedly moved to Jihe overnight, leaving not even a copper coin behind.","As a result, her mother was naturally angry again, but her father still held out some hope, thinking that this Luo fellow was just too busy with official business and had temporarily forgotten about the debt.","Until one day, her uncle was transporting grain from out of town back home, and when passing through Jihe County where that man was stationed, he was detained by the local government on the grounds of unclear travel documents.","When the family received the news, they were frantic with worry. Her father rushed to Jihe, for the first time in his life wanting to use his connections to ask this man for a favor. Who would have thought that after waiting for three days, this Luo fellow refused to see him at all.","In the end, her poor fool of a father had to scrape together twenty taels of silver as a fine from various sources to bring her uncle back.","From then on, her father's heart was completely chilled towards this Luo character.","Who would have thought that this man's official career would continue to rise, all the way from county official to prefectural official, then entering the capital, and now he had even become the Deputy Director of the Salt and Iron Bureau?","Yanshu felt indignant - wasn't this just heaven turning a blind eye?!","After listening to her recollection in her heart, Yuwen Lan also nodded silently, thinking that indeed, heaven seemed to have turned a blind eye in this matter.","He hadn't expected that the Deputy Director of the Salt and Iron Bureau, carefully selected by the Ministry of Revenue, would turn out to be such a character.","With such poor moral character, it was unlikely he would perform his duties well. It seemed this matter needed to be reconsidered.","Just as he was thinking this, he saw Yanshu, who had just been angrily cursing heaven in her heart, suddenly greet that man with a friendly face—","\"Isn't this Uncle Luo?\"","As soon as these words fell, everyone in the hall was stunned.","What?","Who was Consort Yi calling... \"Uncle Luo\"?","Of course, at this moment there was only one person surnamed Luo in the hall, and everyone had just clearly heard him introduce himself as Luo.","So for a moment, everyone turned their gaze towards this man.","The Minister of Revenue, as his superior, also looked surprised. He glanced at Luo Zhixue, then hurriedly bowed to Yanshu and said, \"Does Consort Yi know Lord Luo?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"I feel that this Lord Luo looks very familiar. May I ask if Lord Luo is from Ande County in Qingzhou Prefecture? And if you served as the county magistrate of Jihe County more than ten years ago?\"","At these words, the Minister of Revenue looked back at his new subordinate in surprise and said, \"Is it really you, Lord Luo? You actually know Consort Yi?\"","Tsk tsk tsk, nowadays who doesn't know that Consort Yi is the most favored, and who doesn't want to establish a connection with her?","Who would have thought this man was so low-key?","However, at this moment, the person in question, Luo Zhixue, was rigid all over and didn't want to admit it.","—Indeed, he of course knew that the currently most favored Consort Yi was actually the daughter of his old acquaintance Li Huaizhi.","He also still remembered that he owed the Li family twenty taels of silver...","At that time, after passing the imperial examination, it wasn't that he hadn't thought about repaying the silver, but at first his finances were indeed tight.","As a scholar from a poor family, coping with various aspects of official life was quite difficult at first.","However, after he had made a name for himself and had money later on, he was afraid that the Li family would cling to him because of this, so he simply ignored it.","He thought that with Li Huaizhi's rigid personality, he would only be able to be a small-time official in Ande for his whole life. Since he had moved his family away, he probably would never encounter the Li family again in this lifetime.","Who would have thought that the Li family would have such a day of soaring success?","But regardless of how the Li family was doing, his official career had to continue.","He had finally worked his way up from that small place to the capital, and now had even become a close minister to the emperor. Originally today he didn't want to show his face in front of Consort Yi, but his superior, the Minister of Revenue, insisted on bringing him in to pay respects, so he had to grit his teeth and come in.","He had planned to just pay his respects quickly and leave, but who knew Consort Yi would recognize him at a glance.","At this moment, he could only force himself to say, \"Indeed it is me.\"","What to do? This little girl wouldn't expose the old matter on the spot, would she?","However, as soon as he finished speaking, Consort Yi smiled again and said, \"It really is you. Weren't you and my father good friends before? I remember you used to come to our house for meals often when I was little.\"","Luo Zhixue could only force a smile and say, \"That's right, the Consort has a good memory.\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"It's not that I have a good memory, it's mainly that I have a particularly deep impression of you. I still remember when you were about to go to the capital for the imperial examination and had no travel funds, it was my father who lent you twenty taels of silver. At that time, you were so moved that you told my father that when you passed the exam, you would definitely repay us, and even give us a grand mansion and thousands in gold, or something like that.\"","At these words, Luo Zhixue's face turned as red as dripping blood, extremely embarrassed.","But at the same time, he was also a bit suspicious—","He didn't seem to have said anything about a grand mansion and thousands in gold back then...","However, at this moment, how could he refute? He could only nod with a forced smile and say, \"Yes, that's what happened...\"","The onlookers saw this and all began to ponder silently—","Why did his expression seem a bit lacking in confidence?","Could it be that he hadn't repaid the money later?","Sure enough, they then heard Yanshu continue, \"But I never saw you again after that. I heard you went to the neighboring Jihe County to be the county magistrate. Once when my uncle was transporting grain from out of town, he was somehow detained in your Jihe. My father went to find you but couldn't even see you. I heard you were very busy at that time, truly a talent who was working tirelessly for the country. Otherwise, how could we meet here today?\"","At these words, everyone again pondered the hidden meaning—","This sounded like a story of an ungrateful person who turned his back on kindness and refused to acknowledge old friends.","Luo Zhixue was about to die of embarrassment.","He could only say, \"I am ashamed. After so many years, I have forgotten what happened at that time... Perhaps I was not in Jihe at that time, so I couldn't meet with the Loyal and Righteous Marquis.\"","However, the emperor had already grasped the key point and immediately looked towards the Loyal and Righteous Marquis Li Huaizhi, asking, \"What was the reason for the grain being detained?\"","To be honest, Li Huaizhi originally didn't want to deal with this person today, but since the emperor asked, he could only hurriedly stand up and say, \"In reply to Your Majesty, that year my brother-in-law was transporting grain from out of town back to our home in Ande. Perhaps the official who issued the travel permit in the other place was careless for a moment and wrote 'chestnut' instead of 'millet', and my brother-in-law, being poorly educated, didn't notice at the time. When they reached Jihe, the local yamen runners detained my brother-in-law and the grain on the grounds that his travel permit didn't match the goods, saying there would be a fine of twenty taels of silver.\"","\"My father-in-law and my humble wife were frantic with worry, so I rushed to Jihe overnight. I originally thought this matter was just a misunderstanding and wanted to find Lord Luo to explain the situation, but Lord Luo was busy, and I waited there for two days without being able to see him.\"","At this point, everyone was very concerned, and even the Empress Dowager couldn't help but ask, \"Then what happened later?\"","Li Huaizhi bowed his head and said, \"I'm afraid the Empress Dowager will laugh, but at that time I didn't bring much money with me. I had to pawn some valuable items I had on me, and also borrow from local fellow townsmen, scraping together twenty taels of silver to pay the fine and redeem my brother-in-law and the grain.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed upon hearing this, \"That is indeed quite pitiful. The official made a mistake writing one character, yet it cost you twenty taels of silver.\"","As she spoke, everyone nodded in agreement, thinking that the Loyal Marquis's family had suffered an unfair loss.","Then the Emperor asked Luo Zhixue, \"Back then, how long could twenty taels of silver support an average family?\"","With all eyes on him, Luo Zhixue dared not lie and honestly replied, \"Your Majesty, twenty taels of silver could support an average family of six for one year.\"","Upon hearing this, Ms. Zhu, the wife of the Loyal Marquis sitting next to Yanshu, couldn't help but object in her heart—","Twenty taels for a year was the spending of a wealthy family. With her good-for-nothing husband always scrimping and saving to help others, they sometimes spent only fifteen or sixteen taels a year.","At this moment, the Emperor spoke to Luo again, \"An official made a mistake in writing, yet the government used this to trouble the common people, fining them the equivalent of one or even two years' expenses? Is this reasonable?\"","As he finished speaking, many officials present inwardly clicked their tongues—","Indeed, the Jihe County government was not only unreasonable but also cruel, practically flaying the common people to make money!","Luo Zhixue immediately knelt down and said, \"Your Majesty, please calm your anger. This regulation was established by the prefecture at that time. I had also advised my superiors about it, but to no avail due to my lowly position. Moreover, there were indeed some minor officials who were inconsiderate and abused their power. When I discovered such cases, I would severely punish them, but it was difficult to prevent all such occurrences.\"","Of course, everyone understood that this incident had happened over a decade ago, and even if the Emperor wanted to investigate further, it wouldn't be easy.","But... there was still a matter pending for this Luo Zhixue—he still owed money to the Loyal Marquis's household!","Just as they were thinking this, Luo Zhixue immediately bowed to the Loyal Marquis Li Huaizhi, looking ashamed as he said, \"Please accept my apology, Your Lordship. I am truly sorry! Back then, due to my busy official duties, I had always intended to find you to repay the debt but never managed to do so. Later, because of changes in my position, I moved further and further away from my hometown and was unable to visit... In any case, it was entirely my fault. Today, I will definitely repay the full amount I owed back then, and prepare an additional generous gift to express my gratitude to Your Lordship. I hope you won't find it beneath you.\"","This explanation made it seem as if he had forgotten to repay the debt due to unavoidable circumstances, but no one present believed him anymore.","—The Li family had remained in their hometown for decades without moving, how could he not have been able to repay them if he wanted to?","What a joke!","Yanshu also snorted inwardly. How could the twenty taels from over a decade ago compare to now? How much hardship had their family endured after losing forty taels of silver in succession?","She still remembered clearly that for those two years, their family meals rarely included any meat. It was always tofu and vegetables or radishes and pickles. Heaven knows how much she craved roast chicken!!!","Tsk, that was when she was supposed to be growing. If it weren't for those vegetarian and pickled dishes lacking nutrition, she might have grown half a head taller now!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","To make a little foodie who loved meat the most eat vegetarian for so long, this Luo Zhixue truly deserved death!","Only now did he finally understand why she valued food so much now—it was because she had been deprived so much back then?","Feeling both angry and indignant, he spoke to Luo, \"Not only should you repay the silver you owed the Loyal Marquis back then, but you should also relearn many life principles. Repaying debts is a fundamental moral obligation. Not only were you ungrateful, but you also returned kindness with enmity. How have you been able to sleep soundly these past ten years and more?\"","Luo Zhixue was utterly ashamed and could only hurriedly kneel down and say, \"I am ashamed, I know my crime.\"","Yuwen Lan ignored him and instead instructed the Minister of Revenue, \"Reconsider the personnel for the position of Deputy Commissioner of the Salt and Iron Bureau. Remember to keep your eyes wide open this time.\"","The Minister of Revenue nervously responded with a \"Yes,\" and glanced at Luo Zhixue, signaling him to leave quickly.","Standing for too long had even caused him to be scolded.","—Not repaying twenty taels of silver, truly shameless.","Luo Zhixue could only respond with a sound, regretting his actions but unable to change the past, and slunk out of the hall dejectedly.","After this small interlude, the water music and dance performance on the lake had finished, and the important content of today's water show was about to begin.","The first event was a boat race, similar to a swimming competition in later times.","At this time, dozens of soldiers were already prepared on large boats in the lake, with twenty people standing ready for each round.","With the sound of gongs and drums, the entire audience held their breath and watched intently. Then, at the commander's signal, twenty soldiers leapt into the water simultaneously, racing towards the shore.","As the gongs and drums sounded again, the lake surface was filled with splashing water, and the soldiers moved through the water as smoothly as fish, leaving the onlookers in awe.","Ms. Zhu couldn't help but whisper to her daughter in admiration, \"They swim faster than fish! This competition is wonderful to watch!\"","Yanshu smiled and agreed, \"There will be even more exciting events later.\"","However, in her heart, she lamented—these soldiers were still wearing clothes. If they could wear only swimming trunks like in later times, showing off their inverted triangle physiques, that would be even more pleasing to the eye!","Yuwen Lan, who unexpectedly overheard this, thought: \"???\"","She actually wanted to see other people's bodies???","Wasn't looking at his not enough???","However, what did she mean by \"later times\"?","Could that be the source of her special abilities?","Just as he was thinking this, a cheer erupted from the lake, signaling the end of the first round of the boat race.","Immediately after, the second round of soldiers entered the water.","This continued for eight rounds, with the three fastest from each round selected for the final competition. The ultimate winner would receive a generous monetary reward.","Of course, considering that the preliminary rounds had just finished and the soldiers' stamina might be affected, the final race would take place in the afternoon.","However, there were still exciting competitions to come, such as the Golden Bowl contest.","First, two teams of soldiers wearing red and yellow uniforms waited in the water. With the sound of gongs and drums, the commander threw a golden bowl into the water. At his signal, the two teams of soldiers began to compete for it.","During the contest, they cooperated with each other, employing various formations and tactics for both offense and defense, creating a spectacular sight.","Yanshu thought to herself, isn't this just like water polo from later times?","Tsk tsk, although the current scene was already quite impressive, if these muscular men could also change into the sleek little swimming trunks of later times, fully displaying their solid muscles and physiques while competing, it would certainly be even more eye-catching!","Yuwen Lan, who was quietly observing her, thought: \"???\"","Again with the \"later times\"?","Could it be that men there could be so shameless as to let others see their bodies so casually?","It's truly frightening!","After four rounds of the Golden Bowl contest, the top two teams were selected for the final competition in the afternoon.","Just as the audience was still savoring the excitement, the impressive water acrobatics began.","To the sound of drums and flutes, a painted boat entered everyone's view. On the boat, people performed tricks with knives and sticks, executing beautiful and thrilling martial arts moves in time with the gongs and drums, captivating the audience.","Ms. Zhu whispered to her daughter in admiration again, \"How do they not get dizzy? We can't even open our eyes when we're on a boat.\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"They are specialized naval soldiers who have trained countless times. Of course they won't get dizzy. Besides, how could they fight in battles if they got seasick?\"","Ms. Zhu nodded in agreement, smiling. Then she heard her daughter say, \"Mother, try some of the snacks on the table. The imperial kitchen's skills are quite good.\"","Ms. Zhu responded and glanced at the table, surprised to see—","That plate of book-shaped pastries was actually made of pancakes?","Tsk tsk, do people in the palace also like to eat this kind of thing?","She quietly looked around the hall and saw that most people were focused on watching the acrobatics and weren't eating anything. However, among the male guests near her husband, there was an elegantly dressed middle-aged man eagerly enjoying the pancake books.","And he was eating them page by page, without any accompaniment...","Ms. Zhu thought, doesn't he find it choking?","He could at least roll it up with something to make it easier to bite...","As the acrobatics on the painted boat finished, another small boat entered the water, signaling the start of the most attractive water puppet show.","On the small boat was a miniature colored pavilion with three small doors at the bottom. With a light drumbeat, the doors opened, and an even smaller boat emerged from within. On it sat a small wooden puppet holding a fishing rod with a fishing line that dangled into the water, presenting the image of someone fishing.","The little wooden puppet could blink its eyes and move its mouth to sing. It sang for a while, then suddenly jerked its fishing line and actually caught a small live fish from the water, which was quite remarkable.","For a moment, everyone watched intently, even Lan Jun and the other children forgot to make a fuss and focused on watching.","The little wooden puppet caught five or six fish in a row, filling its small boat. Then it sailed back through the small colorful gate. Immediately after, more puppets emerged from the colorful gate and began to perform pre-arranged plays.","Stories like Emperor Wen of Wei raising an army, the Legend of the White Snake, the Eight Immortals Crossing the Sea, and Sun Wukong causing havoc in the Dragon Palace were performed one after another, leaving the audience in awe. It was incredibly entertaining.","Even the Empress Dowager rarely smiled, but she nodded and said, \"Today's program is arranged very well, much better than before.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, an official from the Court of Imperial Sacrifices who was attending nearby hurriedly said, \"This is thanks to Consort Yi's suggestion that we were able to adjust the program in time.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, looking at Yanshu with approval.","This girl certainly had a talent for matters of food, drink, and entertainment.","After watching three or four puppet shows, it was time for lunch.","The noon banquet was set up in the hall, featuring mainly fresh fish from the Golden Bright Lake.","There were dishes like steamed perch, braised fish head, salt and pepper shrimp, braised soft-shelled turtle, salt-baked crab, as well as milk soup with water shield and silverfish omelet. While not as luxurious as bear's paw or deer tendon, they were very flavorful.","As everyone was enjoying the food, a storyteller took the stage on a nearby painted boat and began to tell stories.","As luck would have it, it was a story by the Carefree Young Master, and the first tale was \"The Romantic Scholar and the Beautiful Lady.\"","This was the first time this item had been included this year, and everyone immediately pricked up their ears to listen.","Of course, listening to the story didn't interfere with eating. They could eat and listen at the same time, making it even more enjoyable.","However, Lord Lu, the Minister of Works, could hardly eat his meal, his heart pounding with excitement—","Heavens, to be able to hear the Carefree Young Master's story in such an occasion!","The Court of Imperial Sacrifices really knew how to arrange things!","They understood him!!!","As a die-hard fan, he of course knew that \"The Romantic Scholar and the Beautiful Lady\" was the Carefree Young Master's first story, and he had read it countless times.","But revisiting it in such a setting with everyone, coupled with the storyteller's interpretation, gave it a whole new flavor!","Of course, he wasn't the only one excited. Most of the people present were listening with great interest, empathizing with the twists and turns of the plot—","When they heard about the courtesan generously giving gold to help the scholar take the imperial examination, everyone praised her loyalty and righteousness;","When they heard about the scholar abandoning his former lover after achieving success, they all shook their heads in disgust;","Later, when the courtesan worked hard to establish her own business, they all nodded in approval;","And when her son entered officialdom and was bullied and harmed by that scholar, everyone was indignant.","Fortunately, in the end, they heard that evil was repaid with evil, and everyone applauded and cheered, making the atmosphere very lively.","Seeing this scene, Yanshu was also very moved and gratified, and even her awkwardness improved considerably.","As the first story ended and while the audience was still savoring it, the storyteller began to tell the second story - \"The Clever Wife's Treatment of the Philanderer.\"","However, just as it began, when the story mentioned the husband frequenting brothels, it was suddenly interrupted.","\"Forgive this old man for speaking frankly, but such vulgar stories are not suitable for performance on such an occasion.\"","Everyone was stunned and turned to look. The speaker was a white-haired old man in his sixties.","Yanshu remembered that he had been introduced earlier during the audience. He seemed to be the former emperor's tutor, named Zhuang Kaicheng.","This man had once been a minister to the former emperor, but after Yuwen Lan ascended to the throne, he no longer held a position at court.","Probably out of consideration for the former emperor's old affection, the Court of Imperial Sacrifices would still invite a group of the former emperor's old ministers to enjoy the water festival with the new emperor each year, to show the new emperor's care for them.","Of course, most of them were just there to eat, drink, and have fun, enjoying themselves.","Who would have thought that this one would stand up and say the story was inappropriate?","Seeing this situation, Yuwen Lan asked, \"What does Master Zhuang find vulgar about this story?\"","The old man replied, \"Your Majesty has heard it too. The woman in the previous story came from a brothel, which I found inappropriate. I was trying to endure it, but now this story mentions brothels again. Such dirty and filthy places being frequently mentioned by the storyteller, isn't it an insult to Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager's ears? It's truly harmful to public morals and extremely inappropriate.\"","At these words, everyone was stunned.","— The word \"brothel\" couldn't even be mentioned?","Wasn't this being a bit too nitpicky?","But then, the old Zhuang added, \"I also think that the author of these stories is too lacking in ambition. Since ancient times, there have been so many stories of heroes, righteousness, loyalty between rulers and subjects, and filial piety to write about. Yet they choose to write stories about things happening in brothels. It's truly despicable.\"","As he finished speaking, Yanshu raised an eyebrow.","What? This person actually called her despicable?","Of course, everyone else looked surprised as well.","Didn't this old man pay attention to current affairs? Didn't he know that the Carefree Young Master's stories were the most popular nowadays?","As a die-hard fan of the Carefree Young Master, Lu Kaihe, the Minister of Works, couldn't help but speak up, \"Master Zhuang's words are mistaken. If the author doesn't write about these stories, does it mean they never happened? If we don't talk about them in such occasions, do brothels cease to exist in this world? All people, be they scholars, farmers, artisans, or merchants, are Your Majesty's subjects. Your Majesty cares for the people's feelings and loves them like his own children. Why shouldn't we listen to their stories?\"","This rapid-fire questioning left the old man speechless and made everyone else applaud.","— Tsk, this Minister of Works, who usually seemed so serious and taciturn, who knew he had such eloquence!","Yanshu was also very moved, thinking that she must find an opportunity to give her die-hard fan an autograph after the banquet.","At the same time, she was also curious.","Was this old Zhuang some kind of moral paragon? Even writing a story about a brothel made someone despicable in his eyes?","Then she heard the system snort, [This man is truly despicable. He came from a poor family, and his wife worked the fields and raised pigs to support his studies for the imperial examination. But after he succeeded, he looked down on his farmer wife. Instead, he took a noble concubine in the capital. Since then, whenever he was posted to various places, he only took this beautiful concubine with him, introducing her as his official wife, while leaving his first wife in their hometown, never mentioning her.]","Yanshu, [Heh.]","What was going on today? These despicable people were all coming out to show their true colors!"]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59","paragraphs":["After hearing the system's revelation, Yanshu chuckled and quietly began searching among the guests.","She remembered that this Old Master Zhuang had come with his family. Could it be that concubine pretending to be the legitimate wife?","Before long, she spotted that woman not far from the Empress Dowager.","The woman appeared to be in her forties, with exquisite makeup and attire. It was clear she knew how to dress well, and traces of her former beauty could still be seen in her features. Most importantly, she carried herself with quite a good bearing. If not told otherwise, no one would have guessed she was a concubine.","Thinking back to the audience earlier, the Empress Dowager had even asked her about her children, showing they were quite familiar.","It seems this concubine had already attended many imperial banquets over the years.","It's worth noting that according to the dynasty's etiquette, a minister's concubine had no right to attend such events at all.","So this Old Master Zhuang had truly deceived everyone by passing off his concubine as his wife.","Tsk, on a small scale this showed poor character, but on a larger scale it could even be considered the crime of deceiving the emperor.","After figuring this out, Yanshu asked the system, \"What about his real wife? Doesn't she get angry being treated like this?\"","The system sighed, \"What good would anger do? This old man finds his real wife embarrassing and never allows her by his side. Though she's cried, hated, and resented it, what can a farm woman do to resist? In the end she can only stay home with the children and continue farming to get by.\"","Yanshu was stunned, \"This old man even abandons his children at home?\"","The system replied, \"That's right. His eldest son stays home farming with the real wife. The concubine bore two sons and a daughter, who he's kept by his side all along. They take exams and become officials, enjoying the same treatment as legitimate children.\"","My goodness...","Yanshu was at a loss for words.","Indeed, the more one claims to have something, the more they lack it. This old man had not an ounce of conscience or morality. He abandoned the wife who supported him, and even disregarded his own legitimate son, only embracing his beautiful concubine to enjoy a privileged life in the city. Yet he still had the nerve to find brothels disgusting?","Tsk, what kind of person did the late emperor choose as an imperial tutor?","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow.","He had actually long noticed that this Old Master Zhuang's character was not very good, so after ascending the throne, he had removed him from office under the pretext of comforting him in his old age.","He didn't expect this person to have such a despicable matter.","However, it seemed that his sudden stand today to criticize the vulgarity of novels was certainly not just to show his face.","Thinking of this, he paid special attention to Old Master Zhuang's direction.","Sure enough, he heard him pondering internally, \"The Minister of Revenue has already been replaced, but the position of Minister of Rites is still vacant. The court must not have found someone capable yet. Who else but me could handle this position? Speaking up more today will also remind the Empress Dowager and Emperor - who else but me for Minister of Rites?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Heh, so he had his eye on the Minister of Rites position?","Quite ambitious.","Just then, the Empress Dowager's voice flowed into his ears.","\"This Old Master Zhuang, would it kill him to keep his mouth shut? What an annoying old thing. Next time we definitely can't have the Court of Imperial Sacrifices send him an invitation.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","It was rare to see the Empress Dowager dislike someone so much. Old Master Zhuang's wish was destined to fail.","Yet at this moment, he heard the man say to Lu Kaihe, the Minister of Works, \"Of course His Majesty loves his people like his own children, but as you just said, the world divides people into several classes of scholars, farmers, artisans and merchants. These brothel people are precisely the lowest class. Why would this person specifically write stories about such people? Could it be that he mixes with these people all day long?\"","When these words came out, many people at the banquet paused.","Tsk tsk tsk, this old man really dared to speak!","Hadn't he heard that this Carefree Young Master was very likely instructed by the Emperor to create public opinion for the court?","Did this old man think he had lived too long?","Yanshu also inwardly clicked her tongue. This old man first set up a set of twisted logic, then drew conclusions based on unfounded speculation. He was quite good at putting labels on people!","But it didn't matter, since the Emperor would cover for her, so she didn't need to worry.","Sure enough, Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong spoke up, \"Master Zhuang's words are indeed biased. You haven't seen it with your own eyes, how can you easily assert that the Carefree Young Master mingles with brothel people? If this gets out, he could probably sue you in court and win.\"","Following that, Minister of Works Lu Kaihe also said, \"Which brothel woman willingly enters a brothel? Aren't they all sold by their families? There are even those sold by their own husbands. In my opinion, those who sell them to brothels for money are even more despicable.\"","At these words, the female guests at the banquet, including the Empress Dowager, Grand Princess, Ankang county lord and others, all looked at the Minister of Works with new eyes.","This Minister Lu seemed to have a clear mind!","Yanshu felt even more proud. See, her readers all had such upright views and open minds! Indeed, birds of a feather flock together.","However, hearing Lu Kaihe speak like this, Old Master Zhuang became even more energetic, saying, \"If they were unwilling, they could completely resist with death! If they weren't willingly degrading themselves, how could they easily become men's playthings? Throughout history, there have been so many chaste women who remained faithful to their deceased husbands, and even those who were buried alive with their husbands. With so many excellent women not mentioned, the Minister insists on speaking for those brothel women. It's truly baffling!\"","At these words, before Lu Kaihe could say anything, the female guests immediately became unhappy.","Ankang county lord couldn't help but snort, \"This old gentleman really knows how to talk. Even ants try to stay alive, are women's lives so worthless? 'They could completely resist with death'? If death were so easy, there probably wouldn't be any men fleeing from battle or abandoning their country in this world!\"","At these words, the male guests all paused. They wanted to refute but truly had nothing to say for the moment.","Because the county lord's words were correct. The mistake was this Old Master Zhuang deliberately provoking conflict!","Meanwhile, Yanshu secretly glanced at the Empress Dowager and Madam Mu.","Sure enough, she saw that both their expressions were not good.","After all, according to this old man's logic, not being buried alive with a deceased husband and not remaining a widow for a deceased husband had become sins.","Tsk tsk, luckily she had taken down the novel \"Plum Blossoms Open Twice, Flowers at Their Peak\" in time, otherwise who knows how this old man would have criticized it.","However, this old man had no self-awareness and continued to spout twisted logic, saying, \"Since ancient times, women have depended on men. Yet this novel writer continuously portrays men as inferior beings in two stories. Could it be that he deliberately harbors resentment towards men to gain women's favor? I believe this person has ulterior motives.\"","What nonsense?","Deliberately resenting men???","Yanshu, who originally hadn't intended to get angry, couldn't help but frown, wishing someone would drive this old man out.","Of course, others couldn't stand these words either. Scholar Zou spoke up again, \"Master Zhuang's words are a bit too extreme. There are men and women of poor character in this world. This person is just writing a very normal story, how can you misinterpret it in such a way?\"","However, Old Master Zhuang continued, \"Your Majesty, please see, this is the harm of these vulgar novels. I just mentioned one inappropriate point earlier, and two important court officials came to refute me, actually speaking for a mere novel writer. It's evident that this person's vulgar ideas have already penetrated the court. Your Majesty must suppress this!\"","At these words, everyone was caught between laughter and tears.","Good grief, it's just a novel, yet it's already threatening the country?","Seeing this situation, Yuwen Lan finally spoke, \"Master Zhuang's dedication to protecting the country is very touching to me, but these words are indeed worrying over nothing. I've listened to this story and haven't noticed anything improper. Let's have everyone finish listening to the story.\"","He gestured to the storyteller, \"Continue.\"","The storyteller complied and dared to continue.","However, Old Master Zhuang paused, seeming to still have something to say.","But seeing the monarch focused on listening to the storyteller and no longer paying attention to him, he reluctantly shut his mouth and continued eating.","However, not long after, Yanshu suddenly stood up and said to the Empress Dowager, \"This subject suddenly feels dizzy from looking at the water surface for too long. I'd like to rest for a while.\"","Motion sickness wasn't uncommon, so the Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Then go rest in the back hall for a while.\"","Yanshu agreed and instructed her mother, Ms. Zhu, \"Mother, don't worry. I'll go rest for a bit and then return.\"","With that, she left her seat and walked towards the rear hall.","Yuwen Lan glimpsed this scene and felt somewhat concerned, wondering if she had been upset by that old man Zhuang.","Little did he know, he heard her think to herself, [You old Zhuang codger, if I don't make you reveal your true form today, I'll change my surname!]","Yuwen Lan was bewildered. Make old Zhuang reveal his true form?","He paused, wondering if she was going to write a story on the spot.","As the storyteller finished the second tale, the lunch banquet was drawing to a close. Boats carrying musicians and dancers glided across the water's surface once more. Accompanied by the sounds of strings and woodwinds, the dancers moved gracefully, performing another beautiful water ballet.","When the dance ended, the puppet show boat sailed into view again. This time, the performance was \"Golden Dragons Frolicking in Water.\"","Four lifelike golden wooden dragon puppets floated on the water's surface. Each dragon could spout different colored smoke from its mouth. Accompanied by intense drumming, the golden dragons tumbled and rolled among the waves, forming various patterns before diving underwater and resurfacing to spout water, much to everyone's amazement.","For a time, the audience was completely captivated by the spectacular display of the golden dragons playing in the water.","Only Lady Zhu, the Loyalty and Righteousness Marquise, was too preoccupied to enjoy the show. She kept worrying about her daughter Yanshu, frequently glancing towards the rear hall.","Yuwen Lan noticed this and whispered an instruction to Fu Hai beside him.","Fu Hai hurried to the rear hall to check.","He soon returned and told Ms. Zhu, \"Madam, please don't worry. The Imperial Consort is fine, just resting inside. She should be out shortly.\"","Ms. Zhu thanked him profusely, finally feeling relieved enough to watch the puppet show on the water.","After what seemed like ages, with five or six puppet shows having finished, Yanshu finally emerged from the inner hall.","She paid her respects to the Empress Dowager before returning to her seat.","Ms. Zhu immediately looked at her daughter and, seeing her rosy complexion which didn't appear sickly at all, finally relaxed and asked, \"What was troubling you earlier, my dear?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"I just felt a bit seasick. A short nap fixed it, don't worry.\"","As she spoke, she began eating some pastries, quickly consuming two chestnut cakes and three lotus seed buns.","Tsk, that old codger had caused her to miss finishing her lunch earlier!","What a waste.","Come to think of it, she had never rushed to finish a manuscript so quickly before.","Given the time constraints, she could only focus on the main plot, simplifying the story and omitting many embellishments. Now it was up to the storyteller - hopefully he could bring it to life with a captivating performance.","As she pondered this, the puppet show boat finished its performance.","With a new drumroll, two large painted boats sailed into view, each with an enormous swing set erected on its bow.","Oh, the water swing performance was about to begin!","Yanshu immediately turned her attention to the water.","This was today's main event, and she was glad she hadn't missed it.","Those two painted boats were truly massive. Besides the swing sets on the bow, there were even acrobats performing at the stern, juggling balls, spinning plates, balancing bowls and more, all to the rhythm of drums and gongs.","After the acrobatic show concluded, a soldier climbed onto one of the swing sets and began to swing.","At first, the arc was modest, but gradually it grew higher and higher.","When he reached the highest point, he suddenly released the ropes, performed several somersaults in mid-air, and then plunged into the water.","The audience watched with bated breath before bursting into applause.","Next, other soldiers took turns performing. Like the first one, they swung high before leaping into the water, each with different moves, all spectacular.","Soon, not just the audience in the hall but all the spectators along the Golden Bright Lake shore were cheering enthusiastically, creating an electric atmosphere.","Yanshu was mesmerized.","At first, she thought this would be like the modern-day fancy diving, but this was far more impressive!","She couldn't take her eyes off the performance, even forgetting to eat her snacks.","Over the course of nearly half an hour, close to two hundred soldiers performed on the water swings. Not a single one made a mistake; each performance was breathtaking, showcasing the exceptional skills of the dynasty's naval forces.","After the water swing show, the finals of the morning's boat racing and golden vase capturing competitions took place.","Being the finals, these matches featured the cream of the crop, making them even more thrilling than the morning events, setting the audience's blood pumping.","Once these two competitions concluded, it was time for the day's grand finale - the dragon boat race.","More than twenty dragon boats gathered on the lake. At the starting signal, they shot forward like arrows released from bows.","Spectators on the shore cheered for their favorites, their shouts mixing with the drumbeats from the boats to create a truly festive atmosphere.","By the time the dragon boat race finished, the setting sun was casting its rays across the water.","After the award ceremony, night had fallen.","As lanterns lit up in homes and shops around the lake, complementing the capital's vibrant nightlife, the evening banquet in the hall began.","Compared to the lunch banquet, the evening feast was even more sumptuous.","However, what captivated the audience most was the return of the storyteller.","This time, he wasn't on a boat but entered the hall directly.","After paying his respects to the Emperor and Empress Dowager, he addressed the crowd, \"Ladies and gentlemen, you are truly fortunate today. To honor Her Majesty the Empress Dowager and Imperial Consort Yanshu, the Carefree Young Master has specially written a new story. It was just delivered to me, and today will be its premiere. You will be the first people in the world to hear this tale.\"","A new story by the Carefree Young Master?","Upon hearing this, the audience's eyes lit up with excitement, and they all pricked up their ears.","The Minister of Works, Lord Lu, was particularly thrilled! He even set down his chopsticks, fixing his gaze on the storyteller.","Amid the anticipation, the storyteller clapped his wooden clappers and began his tale.","\"Today's story is called 'The Faithless Man Eventually Faces Heaven's Wrath.' It tells of a poor scholar who owned only a few acres of barren land...\"","Hearing this, the audience couldn't help but glance at Old Master Zhuang.","Hadn't he just complained that all the stories were about brothels? Well, this certainly wasn't about a brothel...","They wondered if he would find something to criticize this time.","Of course, it wasn't that Old Master Zhuang didn't want to nitpick; he just hadn't found any faults with the story yet.","The storyteller continued:","\"Seeing their parents aging, and knowing the scholar had no practical skills and had never worked in the fields, his parents worried: if they died, wouldn't their son starve to death too? So before they passed away, they arranged a marriage for the scholar to a strong, capable woman.\"","\"Now, this new bride was truly industrious. Every day, she took care of her in-laws, attended to her husband, cooked, cleaned, wove cloth, and sewed clothes - she could do it all. After a few years of marriage, once her elderly in-laws had passed away, she even worked in the fields like a man, undeterred by wind or sun. She also raised chickens and pigs, tirelessly managing everything inside and outside the home. Even after having a child, she continued to do all these tasks while caring for the baby, never letting her husband lift a finger.\"","At this point, the Grand Princess couldn't help but remark to the Empress Dowager, \"This scholar really married a good wife. Without her, wouldn't he have starved to death?\"","The Empress Dowager nodded in agreement.","Yuwen Lan secretly glanced at Old Master Zhuang.","He saw that the old man's eyes were flickering, already showing signs of suspicion.","The storyteller turned to the Grand Princess and smiled, \"Just as Your Highness said, thanks to his capable wife's management, the scholar lived comfortably without worrying about food or clothing. This allowed him to focus entirely on his studies and exams. Perhaps it was heaven's mercy, but the scholar passed the imperial examination in one attempt and was awarded an official position.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Well, his wife's hardships have finally paid off.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement, sharing the same thought.","However, the storyteller then said, \"But the first thing this man did after passing the exam was to take a beautiful concubine in the capital.\"","What?","Everyone was stunned.","The female guests, in particular, widened their eyes in disbelief.","The first thing this man did after achieving success was to take a concubine?","He truly was no good!","However, such men were not uncommon in the world, so while the women felt indignant, no one spoke up.","The storyteller continued, \"Afterwards, the scholar took his beautiful concubine to his new post, leaving his hardworking wife behind in their hometown to continue raising their child and managing the household and fields. He did, however, send some silver each month for the mother and child's living expenses.\"","Upon hearing this, the Grand Princess couldn't help but exclaim, \"How could this man be so heartless? His wife had toiled for so long, and just when things were looking up, he refused to take her along to enjoy the fruits of their labor? After marrying a concubine, shouldn't he still attend to his principal wife?\"","The storyteller shook his head and said, \"The scholar had always despised his wife's rough appearance, feeling she would embarrass him in public. Moreover, now that he had become an official, he felt his illiterate wife was inferior to his beautiful concubine, who was not only attractive but also well-versed in poetry and literature, able to accompany him in romantic pursuits. So he had no intention of living with his first wife in the future or letting her appear in public as his official spouse.\"","This statement truly infuriated the Grand Princess, who snorted, \"What a heartless scholar! Even if his wife's looks were rough, wasn't it because she had been worn down by toiling in the fields for him? Otherwise, what woman would willingly endure wind and sun instead of enjoying comfort at home? Besides, given his initial circumstances, how could that beautiful concubine have married him?\"","Everyone nodded in agreement.","The Empress Dowager then asked, \"Did others know that this man brought his concubine instead of his wife to his new post?\"","The storyteller replied, \"Others actually didn't know. This was because the man never mentioned his lawful wife to outsiders, and he doted on his concubine so much that people assumed she was his wife. At first, such misunderstandings occurred occasionally, but the man never clarified. As time went on, he directly claimed to others that the concubine was his wife.\"","\"The beautiful concubine brazenly enjoyed delicacies and fine clothes, while the principal wife continued tending the fields back in their hometown. The man even disliked his own legitimate son, leaving him behind with his mother, not bothering to visit for years. You can imagine, with the illiterate principal wife and the young master lacking a father's guidance, the boy grew up to be good for nothing, only able to farm with his mother. Meanwhile, the concubine's children received all of the man's attention. He even sent them to study and take imperial exams under the identity of his legitimate sons. Some even became officials, and for decades, no one discovered the truth.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone frowned and exclaimed:","\"Isn't this tantamount to deceiving the emperor?\"","\"Indeed! This man's audacity is truly astounding!\"","Amidst the chorus of discussions, only Yanshu remained calm, eating her meal while occasionally glancing at the two parties involved in the hall.","She saw Old Master Zhuang's face alternating between pale and flushed, his eyes shifting uneasily, looking extremely panicked.","And the concubine who bore the title of Madam Zhuang was also glancing around nervously.","Hmph, it's rare to see people who've been up to no good for so many years boldly asking for trouble.","Yanshu contentedly picked up a piece of crispy roast pork, dipped it in some plum sauce, and popped it into her mouth. Simply delicious.","The hall, however, was filled with indignation. Everyone eagerly asked the storyteller, \"What happened next?\"","\"Did this man face any retribution for his unconscionable behavior?\"","The storyteller calmly replied, \"There was retribution, of course. Otherwise, how could this story be called 'The Heartless Man Finally Faces Heaven's Wrath'? Please be patient, and allow me to continue.\"","\"This man thought he had fooled everyone, and after decades, he almost believed it himself. However, Heaven has eyes, and one day, as he was descending the stairs, he suddenly slipped and tumbled down, breaking both his arms and legs, leaving him bedridden.\"","\"To make matters worse, he encountered an incompetent doctor who accidentally added an extra potent ingredient to his medicine. After drinking it, the man's condition worsened rapidly, and he suffered a stroke, leaving him permanently bedridden.\"","\"As the saying goes, 'There are no filial children by the bedside of a long-term patient.' The man had fallen ill in his city home, so naturally, his concubine and illegitimate children cared for him at first. However, as time passed, they all grew weary. It was then that they remembered he still had a legal wife and legitimate son in his hometown. After some discussion, they decided to send him back to his hometown for his wife and son to care for him.\"","At this point, the people in the hall were furious.","The Grand Princess and other ladies couldn't help but spit out, \"These concubines and illegitimate children sure know how to calculate! They keep the good times for themselves and toss him back to his original wife and son when he's incapacitated?\"","\"Exactly! In the end, it's all the old man's fault! Look at how he favored his concubine and neglected his wife, and see what kind of people he ended up raising!\"","Some male guests shook their heads and sighed, \"As the saying goes, 'Like father, like son.' With a father who has lost his conscience, it's no wonder the children he raised turned out this way.\"","The storyteller nodded repeatedly in agreement, \"Indeed, it's all this man's own doing. After his family in the city made their decision, they sent servants to transport him back to his hometown. However, because he hadn't returned for many years, and his wife and son had renovated their house, the servants couldn't find their home.\"","\"The weather was scorching hot, and the countryside was an endless expanse of mountains. The servants, carrying the old man, searched for a long time without finding the place. Frustrated, they eventually abandoned him by the roadside and returned home.\"","\"After all, the man's wife, concubine, and children didn't interact with each other, so they could easily lie and say they had delivered him, and no one would investigate.\"","\"However, how could this seriously ill old man endure such hardship? He was already on the brink of death after the journey, and left in the wilderness without care, exposed to the elements, he breathed his last within half a day.\"","\"But this was in the wild mountains, teeming with wild animals. When people discovered his body two days later, wolves had already devoured most of it.\"","At this point, Yuwen Lan quickly glanced in Old Master Zhuang's direction.","He saw that the old man's face had turned ashen, inwardly roaring, \"How dare they! How dare this storyteller curse me like this! I'll find him and tear him to pieces!\"","However, the others were all applauding, exclaiming, \"He got what he deserved! Despising his lawful wife, turning things upside down, and in the end being eaten by wolves – truly Heaven's retribution!\"","\"Exactly! Evil people deserve such a fate. Being eaten by these wild beasts – I wonder if even the beasts found him too foul to stomach!\"","Minister Lu was so excited that he stood up, saying, \"How satisfying! Truly satisfying! The Carefree Young Master's stories indeed clearly distinguish between good and evil, making for a thrilling listen!\"","Seeing this reaction, Old Master Zhuang could only swallow his anger.","In his fury, he grabbed the wine jug on the table and began gulping it down.","However, the others were still interested in the aftermath and asked, \"What about the man's concubine and illegitimate children? Were they allowed to continue enjoying what rightfully belonged to others?\"","The storyteller continued, \"Of course not. Although the man's body was badly mutilated, some identifying items remained. Those who discovered him were shocked and immediately reported to the local authorities.\"","\"After some investigation by the officials, they found his legitimate son and legal wife. Being family, how could the son and wife accept such a fate for the head of their household? They sued the illegitimate children and concubine in the city. After further investigation by the authorities, the truth finally came to light.\"","\"The magistrate was furious and immediately arrested the illegitimate children and concubine, sentencing them to punishment. As for the man's estate, it was naturally all given to his legal wife and legitimate son, somewhat restoring justice to them.\"","Hearing this, the crowd in the hall nodded in approval. \"That's more like it.\"","\"This shows that one should never covet what doesn't belong to them. Heaven is always watching!\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"This man wasted half of his legal wife's life, making her suffer for him for so many years. In the end, he only left her some property. Come to think of it, given this wife's character, if she had married someone else, her life might have been even better than it is now.\"","\"Your Majesty speaks wisely!\"","\"Indeed, hardworking and virtuous people can find good lives anywhere!\"","Although the story had ended, the crowd was still engrossed in discussion.","Yanshu kept a low profile, leisurely enjoying the delicious food while watching the involved parties squirm uncomfortably in their seats.","The Zhuang family concubine, unable to bear such shame, couldn't help but secretly glance across at Old Master Zhuang.","She wanted to express her grievances, but to her surprise, she saw Old Master Zhuang trembling all over, his face flushed red. Before long, he suddenly collapsed to the ground.","Everyone was startled. The concubine let out a sharp cry and hurriedly reported, \"Your Majesty, please save my husband!\"","Yuwen Lan pointed to the imperial physician who had accompanied them on the boat and said, \"Go and check on Master Zhuang. Could it be that he's had too much to drink?\"","Everyone thought the same, assuming the old man was just drunk.","However, upon closer inspection, they noticed his crooked mouth and eyes, which didn't look like the symptoms of intoxication.","When the imperial physician examined him, he frowned and said, \"His blood and qi are in chaos, and his cerebral vessels are blocked, causing blood to overflow in the brain... This is not good, Master Zhuang has suffered a stroke!\"","Hearing this, the crowd was shocked and exclaimed, \"Master Zhuang is a man of high moral character. He must have been angered by the story of that unfaithful man!\"","\"That's right, that's right. He must have been too deeply immersed in the story and became upset.\"","The concubine was at a loss for words and could only lie on the old man's body, weeping bitterly.","Yanshu secretly clicked her tongue.","— This was the first time in history that someone had so perfectly matched the ending of a story.","It was truly moving.","However, this was due to his own guilty conscience; it wasn't the Carefree Young Master's fault.","Yuwen Lan silently nodded.","Indeed, this is what happens when one brings calamity upon oneself.","It absolutely wasn't his beloved consort's fault."]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60","paragraphs":["No matter what, a stroke is a serious condition.","Hearing the imperial physician say this, Yuwen Lan immediately ordered people to first carry Old Master Zhuang to the back hall, and told the imperial physician to intensify treatment.","Later, when his condition stabilized slightly, he had people send him back home.","The uninformed crowd in the hall praised the emperor's care for his old minister, but also lamented that Old Master Zhuang was too sensitive - how could he get so upset just from hearing a story?","Of course, regardless, today they had watched wonderful water performances all day and heard the Carefree Young Master's latest story, so it was truly a fulfilling experience.","As the evening banquet was coming to an end and the emperor was about to return to the palace, Ms. Zhu took the opportunity amidst the farewells to quietly ask her daughter Yanshu, \"It's not easy for us to meet. There's something your grandmother and I have been concerned about and want to ask you.\"","Yanshu, not understanding, quickly said, \"Mother, whatever it is, just say it.\"","She heard her mother say, \"You've been serving in the emperor's bedchamber for half a year now, but there's still no good news. Have you seen a doctor about it?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, so this is what mother was worried about.","She wanted to tell her mother that she had only taken that substantial step with the emperor last month, and for the five months before that, the emperor had been unable to perform.","But she could only vaguely say, \"Mother, don't worry. I'm fine...\"","Ms. Zhu was still concerned and hurriedly said, \"Your Highness, don't be embarrassed. I know the servants around you are all young, and Rendong doesn't understand these things either. Since we rarely get to meet, let me remind you as your mother - if a normal couple hasn't had any news after half a year of marriage, they should see a doctor. This way, you can find out if there's any deficiency early on and get treatment promptly, so as not to waste time.\"","Yanshu found it hard to explain and could only say again, \"Mother, please don't worry. There's a very skilled doctor in the palace. I've seen him, and he didn't say there was anything wrong with my body.\"","Then she heard her mother nod and say, \"Well, if there's nothing wrong with your body, then it must be that the positions aren't quite right.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","What?","...The positions aren't right???","Tsk, can mothers and daughters discuss such explosive topics?","Before she could say anything, she saw her mother take something out of her sleeve and quickly slip it into her hand, saying, \"Your Highness, take a good look at this when you have time after you return. This is an old family heirloom, very effective. Many people conceived after trying it just once.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","What?","Their family had an heirloom for conceiving children? And it was so effective?","Curious, she quickly looked down and saw it was a small booklet.","As soon as she opened the first page, she was hit with some very impactful images.","Her eyes widened instantly, but before she could take a closer look, she heard Rendong say from the side, \"My lady, His Majesty and the Empress Dowager are getting up.\"","She hurriedly closed the booklet, quickly stuffed it into her sleeve, and stood up as well.","At the same time, the entire hall immediately knelt down and called out, \"Respectfully sending off His Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and Consort Yi.\"","The Empress Dowager and the emperor were already walking out, so Yanshu followed their footsteps out of the hall.","She pretended nothing had happened, her expression very natural.","However, Yuwen Lan had already seen the moment when mother and daughter passed something between them.","But due to the noise in his ears at the time, he hadn't seen clearly what they had passed, nor heard what they had said.","Outside the great hall, the carriages were waiting in front.","He wanted to ask, but unfortunately, with so many eyes watching and the Empress Dowager present, it wasn't appropriate for him to ride in the same carriage as her. He could only temporarily suppress his curiosity and return to the palace first.","When they arrived at Ganlu Palace and finished changing clothes and washing up, all the unnecessary personnel had already withdrawn.","Yuwen Lan remembered this matter again, and as soon as he got into bed, he immediately asked Yanshu, \"What did the Loyal and Righteous Marquis's wife give you when saying goodbye earlier?\"","Yanshu was stunned, only now realizing that he had seen it.","But that thing...","Tsk, it was fine for her to look at it herself, but if others saw it, wouldn't it affect her mother's image?","So she lied, \"It was nothing, just a small pouch my mother sewed for me.\"","Who knew he would raise an eyebrow and say, \"Lying to me has very serious consequences.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, this man is as cunning as a monkey.","She could only put on a troubled face and say, \"It's not that I don't want to show it to Your Majesty, it's just not quite appropriate...\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"What's not appropriate? Is it something treasonous?\"","Yanshu didn't know whether to laugh or cry, \"How could that be possible?\"","Fine, it seemed she couldn't avoid it today. She steeled herself and said, \"I'll tell Your Majesty, but please don't get angry or blame anyone.\"","Yuwen Lan naturally nodded, \"Let's hear it.\"","Yanshu then said, \"My mother was thinking of the imperial heir and gave me something, saying it could help me conceive an heir sooner...\"","Tsk, if her mother knew about this moment, she'd be so mortified...","However, when Yuwen Lan heard this, he became even more curious, \"There's such a good thing? Quickly take it out and let me see.\"","At his age, heaven knows how much he wanted an heir!","Yanshu had no choice but to take out the small booklet and say, \"Your Majesty, please look.\"","Yuwen Lan took it, and as soon as he opened the first page, he was immediately shocked by the extremely impactful images.","Yanshu, who hadn't gotten a clear look earlier, also leaned in to look together, and couldn't help but think to herself, [I can't believe Mother's old Li family actually had such a good thing, it's too exciting!]","[This visual effect is definitely more intense than any colored storybook!]","[Hmm, so that's the position... tsk tsk, exciting exciting, ahem, might as well try it with the emperor later...]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Who was being so coy earlier?","But speaking of which, where did the Loyal and Righteous Marquis's wife get this thing from? It's even more... intense than any picture book he had seen before.","After silently examining the first page, he turned to the second page and found it... even more stimulating.","Then came the third page, fourth page, fifth page...","Tsk, each one was more extreme than the last.","Yanshu thought the same.","Tsk, their Li family ancestors were really ahead of their time.","After a while, when they had browsed through the entire booklet, she noticed that the expression of the man beside her had become even more serious.","\"...\"","For a moment, she couldn't tell what he was thinking. She wondered if he might be angry.","Would he punish her family?","But to her surprise, she heard him say in a deep voice, \"Since the Loyal and Righteous Marquis's wife had such good intentions, how could I disappoint her? Why don't we give it a try?\"","As he spoke, he suddenly pressed her down beneath him.","Yanshu: \"...\"","I can't believe I fell for that.","For several days in a row, Yanshu's waist and legs were sore and weak, as if she had returned to the time when a certain someone had first tasted meat.","Tsk, the emperor seemed to have treated that little booklet as some kind of treasure manual, pulling her to practice together every night with a very serious attitude.","As a result, she had to sleep until late morning every day, her muscles very sore, and she couldn't even manage to write her stories.","Fortunately, \"The Unfaithful Man Finally Punished by Heaven\" had just been completed that day, and readers were still immersed in it. The booksellers were also busy counting money, so they didn't have time to urge her yet.","So she leisurely spent a few days as a lazy fish.","This morning, she had just finished breakfast not long ago when she heard the system ding and say, [There's a follow-up to Old Master Zhuang's situation.]","Yanshu was startled and immediately asked, [What's going on?]","The system said, [You know how Old Master Zhuang had a stroke at the palace banquet? After this news spread, everyone found it curious and discussed it. Before long, more and more people knew about it, and someone brought the news to his hometown. When his eldest legitimate son heard about it, he came to the capital to find him. Plus, with your story spreading everywhere these past few days, that concubine's family was very nervous. When they saw the eldest son arrive, they thought he had come to fight for the inheritance, so they avoided him and wouldn't let him in the door.]","[Of course, this eldest son was angry and started making a fuss at the gate. As it happened, this morning the emperor had sent the Vice Minister of Rites and the Chief Censor to visit Old Master Zhuang's house. They ran into this eldest son, and seeing these two men in official robes, he lost his temper and spilled everything on the spot. When the Vice Minister of Rites and the Chief Censor heard this, they thought it was a serious matter and immediately hurried back to the palace to report to the emperor. The emperor then ordered people to bring in both the legitimate and illegitimate sons of this old man, and they're currently in the middle of investigating the case!]","Yanshu's eyes lit up, [Isn't this another scene of drama!!!]","I really want to see it!!!","However...","There was a group of men there, so even if she wanted to enter, she couldn't.","Tsk, it seemed this juicy gossip could only be enjoyed by the emperor himself.","She sighed regretfully. As a highly dedicated spy, missing out on such fresh firsthand gossip was truly unbearable.","Unexpectedly, not long after, she heard palace servants from the Palace of Benevolent Peace outside, saying, \"Consort Yi, the Empress Dowager requests your presence.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Could it be that the Empress Dowager wanted to ask her for information?","But she wasn't even in Qianming Palace. The Empress Dowager might as well go there directly to enjoy the gossip with the emperor...","And bring her along while she's at it...","Of course, this was all unrealistic. If the Empress Dowager could go, why would she summon her?","She could only agree, quickly change her clothes, and head to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Upon arriving at the Palace of Benevolent Peace, she saw that Madam Mu was also there, with several plates of snacks laid out on the tea table.","The Empress Dowager granted her a seat and explained, \"Madam Mu is returning to Mingzhou tomorrow. She specially made some snacks by hand to express her gratitude to you. Please try them.\"","So they were made by Madam Mu. Yanshu hurriedly expressed her thanks, \"Thank you, Your Majesty. Madam Mu is too kind.\" She then sat down at the tea table.","Glancing at the table, she had to admit that Madam Mu's culinary skills were quite impressive. The snacks were beautifully presented and looked exquisite.","She tried a piece of mung bean cake. It melted in her mouth, sweet but not cloying, with a subtle hint of milk. It was truly delightful.","As she was eating, she heard the Empress Dowager speak again, \"By the way, I heard earlier that someone from the Zhuang family entered the palace? Could something have happened?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, the Empress Dowager had finally gotten to the main point.","But she could only feign surprise and say, \"This concubine hasn't heard about this. Could it be that Old Master Zhuang's condition has worsened?\"","Empress Dowager: \"...\"","Fine, this little girl was also playing dumb with her.","The Empress Dowager then simply said, \"I heard that Assistant Grand Tutor Zhuang actually has a legitimate wife and son. The woman and son he's had by his side all these years are actually his concubine and illegitimate child. So it turns out that the unfaithful man the storyteller spoke of that night was him.\"","She then looked at Yanshu and said, \"I wanted to ask, since you spend all day by His Majesty's side, do you know when His Majesty discovered something was amiss with the Zhuang family?\"","—After all, in the Empress Dowager's mind, the Carefree Young Master was an intelligence agency secretly arranged by the emperor. If the storybooks could corroborate reality, it must have been written at the emperor's command.","Yanshu could only say, \"This concubine is hearing about this for the first time as well. Please forgive this concubine's incompetence, His Majesty has never revealed anything about this to me.\"","She then tried to cover for the emperor, saying, \"His Majesty is wise and brilliant. It's not surprising that he would know about such information in advance.\"","However, the Empress Dowager said, \"That old Zhuang is not a current court official. His time in office was already several years ago. Why would His Majesty think to investigate him? And to investigate so accurately too. I haven't heard even a whisper about this all these years.\"","Yanshu thought to herself, this is quite normal, the emperor probably only found out about it today...","However, just as she was thinking this, she suddenly paused.","—Would the emperor have this question now?","After all, he knew that she had written the storybook. Now that the plot unexpectedly matched up with the Zhuang family's situation, would he wonder how she knew about this?","Just then, she heard the system interject, [Hmm, you've finally realized this problem? You've already written several storybooks that coincide with reality, and you're only thinking about this now?]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, indeed, why hadn't she thought of this before?","...Moreover, why had the emperor never asked her about this like the Empress Dowager had?","She suddenly became frightened and hurriedly asked the system, [Could it be that he knows about you?]","The system was very certain, [That's impossible. No one can discover me. But the emperor has probably long since realized that something is off about you.]","Yanshu: [!!!]","System: [But it's fine. Since he's allowed it for so long, you don't need to be afraid of anything.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","That may be true, but why hadn't the emperor ever asked her about it?","Was he really that open-minded?","System: [After all, he's the emperor. His perspective is different from others. Besides, doesn't he like you?]","Yanshu: [...]","Just because he likes her, he can calmly accept that she has abilities beyond normal people?","...","With this question in mind, Yanshu finished eating the pastries at the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","On her way back to Ganlu Palace, she heard the system say, [The Zhuang family drama has reached a conclusion. The emperor, after clarifying the facts, flew into a rage. He convicted the Zhuang family's concubine and illegitimate children of deceiving the emperor, immediately sent them to prison, and awarded the old man's property to his original wife and legitimate son.]","Yanshu: [What about the old man? He's the main culprit. He shouldn't be exempted just because he had a stroke, right?]","System: [Exemption is impossible. The emperor has ordered the concubine to accompany him, and they've both been sent to prison. They'll serve at least three years for now.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","That concubine had it tough too. She had to serve an old dying man even in prison. She truly deserved it.","However, although this outcome was satisfactory, the emperor's behavior was still too strange.","She thought for a moment and decided that when she saw him tonight, she must ask for clarification.","At night, Yuwen Lan returned to Ganlu Palace.","His beauty had already bathed and was waiting for him on the couch.","He was in a good mood and also undressed to join her on the couch.","—Ahem, after obtaining that little booklet, it was as if a door to a new world had been opened. Exploring its pleasures with her every day had become the thing he looked forward to most.","However, just as he embraced her and was about to kiss her, he heard her say, \"This concubine heard the Empress Dowager say at the Palace of Benevolent Peace today that apparently that Assistant Grand Tutor Zhuang still has a legal wife and legitimate son back home. The ones he brought to the palace banquet that day were actually his concubine?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"That's correct. Today, the Vice Minister of Rites and the Chief Censor went to visit the Zhuang family and happened to witness them refusing entry to Zhuang's legitimate son. The two came to report to me, so I summoned his legitimate and illegitimate sons to the palace to clarify the situation...\"","At this point, he deliberately asked her, \"Didn't you write all this in your storybook?\"","Yanshu paused, thinking to herself that he really wasn't surprised at all!","It seems he must have determined that she had some special ability, right?","System: [If he didn't think this way, wouldn't he be as foolish as you?]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Fine, she might as well ask directly, \"Is Your Majesty not curious about how this concubine was able to write about the Zhuang family's story?\"","He nodded with a smile and looked at her, \"I am curious. Why indeed?\"","Yanshu: \"...If this concubine says it was a coincidence, would Your Majesty believe it?\"","Yuwen Lan continued to raise an eyebrow and look at her, \"You tell me, should I believe it?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Alright, he had indeed been pretending all along.","And she was truly foolish.","Since that was the case, she decided to be frank, \"This concubine will tell you the truth. Actually, this concubine has a special ability to occasionally receive information about people's secrets.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Indeed, it is so. I had actually guessed this long ago. Otherwise, it would be inexplicable.\"","His tone was remarkably calm.","Yanshu frowned and said, \"Is Your Majesty not afraid of this concubine? You don't think I'm some kind of monster?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Why would I be so cowardly? It's just a special ability, it's not like you're trying to assassinate me.\"","As he spoke, he couldn't help but take her small hand and kiss it.","Yanshu sighed, \"Your Majesty truly has an extraordinary perspective.\"","Tsk tsk tsk, knowing she had a special ability and still playing so passionately with her every day, he really had a big heart.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","What kind of talk was this? He simply loved her deeply...","Hmm, holding her and talking for so long had already stirred his desires. He couldn't wait any longer and quickly lowered his head to kiss her.","She responded quite enthusiastically.","Yuwen Lan's heart was filled with passion. Just as he was about to take the next step, he heard her think to herself, [This is good. In the future, if I want to tell him something, I won't have to rack my brains. It will be even easier to make him take the blame!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Why, at such a moment, was she still thinking about making him take the blame???","...","That night, Yanshu discovered that someone was clearly much more passionate than usual.","After the water play incident, the two had diligently practiced the techniques from the picture book for many days.","Yanshu thought they had probably mastered it, but one morning when she woke up, she found that a certain relative had punctually come to visit her.","\"...\"","Although she lacked experience, she still had some basic common sense.","Yanshu couldn't help but doubt - didn't her mother say that picture book was very effective? How come it didn't work?","... Could it be that there was really something wrong with her body?","Although she originally wasn't in a hurry about this matter, she couldn't resist the psychological suggestion from her mother.","After hesitating for two days, Yanshu finally decided to call Imperial Physician Jiang to examine her.","After Imperial Physician Jiang came and took her pulse for a long time, he frowned and said, \"Your Highness's pulse is stable, and I can't see anything abnormal at the moment. Is there any discomfort?\"","Yanshu coughed and said, \"Actually, there's no discomfort. It's just that I've been serving in the imperial bedchamber for some time now, but there's still no good news. So I wanted to ask you to check if there's any problem with my body?\"","Imperial Physician Jiang understood and couldn't help but smile, \"Your Highness's body has no problems at all. Pregnancy is a matter of fate, it can't be rushed. The imperial heir didn't come this month, perhaps it will come next month. However, may I ask how long Your Highness has been serving in the imperial bedchamber?\"","Yanshu didn't dare say it had only been a month, but she heard Rendong answer for her from the side, \"Her Highness was promoted to her position last December, it's been half a year now.\"","— After all, Rendong was also naive and didn't know about the emperor's past affairs, so naturally she could only answer like this.","Yanshu didn't feel it was right to correct her.","But she saw Imperial Physician Jiang frown and say, \"Half a year? That's indeed not a short time.\"","Yanshu's heart tightened, and she hurriedly asked, \"So is there something wrong?\"","But she heard him say, \"I really can't see anything wrong with Your Highness. Perhaps, it would be better to have His Majesty checked as well.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","What, have the emperor checked too?","As expected of you, straightforward Imperial Physician Jiang. Who else would dare to say such a thing?","But come to think of it, Yanshu secretly pondered, after all, the emperor had just recovered from his illness. Could there still be some issues?","So she nodded first and said, \"I understand. Thank you for your trouble coming here. However, it's best not to speak of today's matter to others for now.\"","Fortunately, Imperial Physician Jiang was trustworthy but not foolish. He nodded in agreement and left with his medicine box.","With this, Yanshu began to ponder in her heart whether she should ask the emperor to get checked as well.","Although she wasn't in a hurry, surely he must be anxious, right? And if the illness hadn't fully healed and the problem persisted, wouldn't that be bad?","...","Thus, when night fell and she saw him again, she said, \"This concubine summoned Imperial Physician Jiang today, intending to inquire about the matter of an imperial heir. Imperial Physician Jiang said that this concubine's body has no problems, perhaps it's just that the time hasn't come yet.\"","Yuwen Lan also knew that her monthly visitor had arrived, and last month's efforts had not borne fruit. He nodded and said, \"That's possible too. There's no need to be too anxious. It will come when it's meant to come.\"","Saying this, he kissed her lips and was about to close his eyes to sleep.","Ahem, during the long night, with such a beauty by his side but unable to do anything, heaven knows how tormented he was?","So he could only quickly fall asleep, and wake up at dawn.","However, he heard her say again, \"But Imperial Physician Jiang said that even if the woman's body is fine, if the man's body has some illness, it could also delay having children... Your Majesty had been drinking medicine and couldn't engage in bedroom activities before, right? I wonder if that might have some impact?\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","Surely not? Didn't he strictly follow medical advice and endure for a full twenty-one days at that time?","That Dr. Jiang didn't say it wouldn't work after twenty-one days.","But come to think of it, he hadn't seen the doctor again since then.","So he didn't know how the situation really was...","Just as he was thinking this, he heard her say again, \"When Your Majesty has time, why not go see that doctor outside the palace again? If there's nothing wrong, that's best. If there's anything, treating it early would be good for welcoming an imperial heir soon.\"","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment and then replied, \"Alright. I'll go out and check tomorrow.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he saw her immediately lean over, giggling and saying, \"Then can Your Majesty please take this concubine along?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Haven't you already seen the doctor?\"","Yanshu pouted, \"It's rare to get a chance to go out of the palace. This concubine wants to get some fresh air.\"","Yuwen Lan snorted a laugh, \"You just went out to see a water show a few days ago, and now you want to go out again. Has your heart become so wild?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, there's food and entertainment and so many people outside, isn't it much more fun than the palace? Who wouldn't have a wild heart?","But out loud, she only said, \"It's not that this concubine's heart is wild, it's just that this concubine is worried about Your Majesty and wants to go along to listen, so I can be more at ease.\"","Yuwen Lan snorted another laugh, pinched her chin, and said, \"I hardly believe you.\"","But he saw her immediately pout, saying, \"Then even if Your Majesty doesn't believe me, shouldn't you at least reward this concubine for reporting so many corrupt officials and evil people to you?\"","Hmph, her novels were always more efficient than the Censorate and Imperial Guards, right?","It's already good that she didn't charge him extra for intelligence fees.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Intelligence fees?","...","But come to think of it, her special ability was indeed much more efficient than the Censorate and Imperial Guards.","Otherwise, who would have known about those unethical things Old Master Zhuang had done?","If he hadn't sent people to find his legitimate son, this matter might never have been made public even after Old Master Zhuang's death.","Alright, considering how much she wanted to go, he said, \"Then I'll take you along tomorrow.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she finally smiled and quickly said okay.","So the next evening, taking advantage of Imperial Physician Jiang's off-duty time, the two set off.","They arrived at the Jiang residence, both still wearing veiled hats as they got off the carriage and entered Imperial Physician Jiang's study.","But before they could speak, they saw another couple coming from outside.","It was none other than Ankang county lord and her husband, County Magistrate Yao Junliang.","— Although Ankang county lord was also wearing a veiled hat, County Magistrate Yao was openly showing his true face, so they immediately recognized the couple.","At the same time, Yuwen Lan and Yanshu both couldn't help but feel grateful in their hearts that they had veiled hats covering their faces, otherwise wouldn't they have been recognized by this couple too?","But... what were they here to see?","Could it be that County Magistrate Yao hadn't fully recovered?","That shouldn't be the case, right?","Just as Yanshu was curious, she saw Yuwen Lan speak to the couple, \"Please let Imperial Physician Jiang examine you two first.\"","County Magistrate Yao smiled and thanked them, then helped his wife sit down in a chair and said to Imperial Physician Jiang, \"Thank you for your miraculous skills, doctor. My wife has just discovered that she's pregnant, but she had unfortunately been poisoned before. We wonder if that might have any impact on the fetus?\"","Upon hearing this, both Yanshu and Yuwen Lan were surprised.","So Ankang county lord was pregnant again!","Tsk tsk tsk, Yanshu couldn't help but marvel in her heart, County Magistrate Yao's efficiency was indeed high! It hadn't been that long since he recovered, right?","As expected of the third-ranked martial arts candidate, his aim was truly good!","Yuwen Lan, who was silently listening on the side: \"???\"","Was that implying that his aim wasn't good?"]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61","paragraphs":["Hearing Consort of County Princess Yao say this, Imperial Physician Jiang took the pulse of the Ankang county lord.","After a moment, he said to the couple, \"There's no need to worry. The lady's body is fine, the previous poison has been cleared, and now she just needs to take good care of the pregnancy. In early pregnancy, be sure to avoid overexertion, cold foods, and spicy foods. Maintain a good mood and get plenty of rest.\"","Consort of County Princess Yao was overjoyed and nodded in agreement. He then took out a silver ingot and said, \"Thank you, Dr. Jiang. This is a small token of my appreciation.\"","However, Imperial Physician Jiang waved his hands repeatedly and said firmly, \"Please take it back, sir. You've already paid for previous consultations, and I didn't prescribe any medicine today. It was just a few simple words, no need to be so polite.\"","But Consort of County Princess Yao insisted, \"If it weren't for you, doctor, we wouldn't have this child. Consider it a gift from me on behalf of the child. Please accept it, doctor.\"","Hearing this, Imperial Physician Jiang looked at him strangely, \"Sir, you shouldn't say such things carelessly. This child is yours, it has nothing to do with anyone else.\"","\"Pfft...\"","At these words, Yanshu almost burst out laughing.","The Ankang county lord also laughed behind her veil, \"My husband misspoke. We've made the doctor laugh. But this silver is truly just a small token of our appreciation. Doctor, if you don't accept it, we'll feel terrible.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang then said, \"If you really insist, why not donate the silver to those in need?\"","Seeing his persistence, the Ankang county lord finally nodded, \"Alright then. We'll donate some silver to the porridge kitchens another day, in the doctor's name.\"","Dr. Jiang nodded, \"Thank you, my lady.\"","The couple then stood up to take their leave and walked out.","As the room quieted down, Yuwen Lan approached Dr. Jiang. Before he could speak, the doctor asked directly, \"Is your marital life normal now, sir?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This doctor had quite a memory.","Well, since Yanshu already knew, there was no need to play dumb anymore. He nodded and said, \"Thanks to the doctor's skillful treatment, everything is normal now. It's just that my wife hasn't conceived yet. I wonder if there's still some problem with me.\"","Dr. Jiang nodded and gestured for him to extend his hand, then felt his pulse.","After a short while, he said, \"Based on your pulse, sir, you should have recovered to normal. There's no need to be too anxious about conception; it will happen naturally when the time is right. However...\"","He paused, making one feel nervous. Yuwen Lan quickly asked, \"However what?\"","Dr. Jiang coughed and said, \"However, you should still exercise some restraint at night. Too much indulgence can also affect your vital energy.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","— Who would have thought that the word \"indulgence\" would one day be used on the emperor, ahem.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What did she mean?","Why couldn't it be used on him?","He wanted to discuss this topic with her, but there was an outsider present.","Yuwen Lan could only agree with Dr. Jiang and prepare to leave.","— Seeing how he didn't accept payment earlier, it would be better not to bother. He'll just increase his salary later.","However, at that moment, a loud roar came from outside: \"Stop right there, you thief!\"","Hm?","A thief???","The three people in the room immediately froze, and after a few moments of shock, they all rushed out of the room together.","When the three arrived on the street outside Dr. Jiang's house, they saw Yao Junliang, who had just left, holding the collar of a thin man with one hand, looking furious.","There was no need to ask; that loud shout just now had come from Consort of County Princess Yao.","And with that shout, the neighbors around Dr. Jiang's house had all come out to see what was happening, and the area was soon filled with people.","Seeing this situation, Dr. Jiang hurried forward and asked, \"What's going on?\"","Consort of County Princess Yao said, \"This little thief was climbing over walls and breaking into houses in broad daylight. If I hadn't noticed just now, he would have gotten away.\"","Then he pointed to a house to the west of Dr. Jiang's and asked, \"Whose house is that? This little thief just jumped down from that wall. Is the owner here? Quickly go back and check if anything is missing.\"","Hearing this, a woman holding a child in the crowd was startled and said, \"Isn't that my house? Please, Sister Jiang, hold A'Sheng for me. I'll go check right away.\"","She handed her baby to Dr. Jiang's wife, Madam He, and hurried back home to check.","However, after a short while, she came running back and said, \"It doesn't seem like anything is missing from my house. The money and jewelry are all still there.\"","Everyone was stunned.","Then the thin man being held by Consort of County Princess Yao said, \"It's a misunderstanding! I just accidentally took the wrong path. I'm really not a thief!\"","Consort of County Princess Yao snorted, \"Took the wrong path? Accidentally went into someone else's house? And jumped down from the wall? Tell us quickly, what were you really up to?\"","Seeing this situation, Yanshu also found it strange and quickly asked the system, [Is this person really a thief?]","The system replied, [Actually, he's not a thief, but he's even more hateful than a thief. He was sent by someone to frame Dr. Jiang.]","Frame Dr. Jiang?","Yanshu was startled, but then heard Yuwen Lan, who had been observing, say to Consort of County Princess Yao, \"Why don't we check if he has any stolen goods on him?\"","Of course, his voice was disguised, so Consort of County Princess Yao didn't recognize it.","Consort of County Princess Yao's attention was focused on the small thief at the moment. Hearing this, he said \"Good idea\" and immediately called his attendants to search the small thief.","After a thorough search, they indeed didn't find any valuables on him.","However, they did find a paper package.","Yes, it was like the kind of yellow hemp paper package used in pharmacies to wrap medicines, tied neatly with grass rope, and emitting a medicinal smell.","It did indeed look like a medicine package.","Seeing this, Dr. Jiang was startled. He quickly stepped forward to take the package, opened it, and examined the contents. He then said to the woman who had just run home to check her valuables, \"Sister Huang, isn't this the medicine I just prescribed for A'Sheng?\"","Sister Huang looked confused and said, \"No, that medicine is still on the stove in my house. I was just about to go out to get some firewood and then brew it for A'Sheng to drink.\"","\"No, no,\" Dr. Jiang shook his head urgently, \"Please go and bring the package of medicine from your stove.\"","Sister Huang had no choice but to agree and hurried back home again.","Soon, she came running back with a medicine package and said to Dr. Jiang, \"Here it is, Dr. Jiang. Look, isn't this the medicine you prescribed earlier?\"","Dr. Jiang quickly took the package and opened it to look. After a moment, he frowned and said, \"This is wrong. The medicine has been switched!\"","What?","Everyone was stunned. How could the medicine have been switched?","Dr. Jiang quickly sorted through the herbs in the second paper package and said to Sister Huang, \"Look, this is plantain seed, this is white peony root, and this is phellodendron bark. A'Sheng has a cold, and I prescribed a formula to dispel cold earlier. But these are all very cold herbs. If A'Sheng drinks this, his condition will definitely worsen, even causing diarrhea and collapse. The consequences could be very serious!\"","\"What?\"","Hearing this, everyone looked shocked.","Sister Huang immediately rushed to the small thief and demanded, \"I have no grudge against you. Why would you want to harm our A'Sheng like this?\"","Yanshu, however, already understood. This was the trick to frame Dr. Jiang.","— Switching the medicine he prescribed, so that when the patient drinks it, not only would it not alleviate the condition, but it would cause more serious consequences, thus slandering Dr. Jiang's reputation...","Hmph, this method was exactly the same as when they framed Divine Doctor Xun back then!","At this point, without the system's prompt, she could guess who the mastermind behind this was!","Feeling angry, she was about to say something to the emperor, but before she could open her mouth, she saw the emperor say to Dr. Jiang, \"This person's target is likely you. This matter is not trivial. I suggest you report it to the authorities immediately, doctor.\"","Hearing this, Consort of County Princess Yao immediately nodded and said, \"That's right. This little thief is probably trying to frame you, doctor. As it happens, I'm free today. I'll accompany you to the Capital Official!\"","Saying this, he ordered his attendants to secure the small thief, then went to the carriage and informed his wife, the Ankang county lord.","The Ankang county lord expressed understanding and gave instructions to the carriage driver before leaving first.","Then, Consort of County Princess Yao accompanied Dr. Jiang to the Capital Official, not forgetting to have someone hold onto the small thief's collar all the way.","The onlookers expressed their anger and then all returned to their homes.","Yanshu and Yuwen Lan also boarded their carriage and returned to the palace.","\"I had originally planned to go stroll through the market and eat some delicious food today.\"","However, given the current situation, Yanshu couldn't eat anything at all.","She was now filled with anger, only wanting to expose the true face of Zhang Shengkang, the head of the Imperial Medical Academy, to the emperor.","Taking advantage of the moving carriage, she spoke up, \"Your Majesty, do you remember the story I told you before about the ungrateful court physician who betrayed his teacher?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"I remember.\"","Then he deliberately asked, \"Was that based on a real person too?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Indeed, the prototype for that court physician is actually Zhang Shengkang, the head of the Imperial Medical Academy.\"","Yuwen Lan feigned surprise, furrowing his brow, \"It was him?\"","Seeing her nod, he continued, \"That's right, it's him. And Imperial Physician Jiang is the son of that brilliant doctor who was angered to death by Zhang.\"","Yuwen Lan again expressed surprise, \"So that's how it is? No wonder Imperial Physician Jiang's medical skills are so impressive.\"","Yanshu nodded again, \"Zhang Shengkang is an extremely jealous person. He was the mastermind behind today's framing of Imperial Physician Jiang.\"","Yuwen Lan had also guessed this point.","Not only was the method identical to how Zhang Shengkang had framed his teacher years ago, but considering Imperial Physician Jiang's generous and forthright personality, he likely had no other enemies besides Zhang Shengkang.","Then Yanshu added, \"However, I feel that when Zhang Shengkang framed Imperial Physician Jiang today, he may not have known Jiang's true identity. It's very likely he was just acting out of jealousy, wanting to drive him out of the Imperial Medical Academy.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"What makes you say that?\"","Yanshu narrowed her eyes and said in an experienced tone, \"It's simple. After all, Imperial Physician Jiang has changed his identity now. Given Zhang Shengkang's cunning nature, if he knew this fact, he would surely report directly to the court that Imperial Physician Jiang had falsified his identity. Wouldn't that be much easier than secretly plotting to harm him?\"","\"Indeed, that's true.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly, then raised an eyebrow at her, \"My beloved consort, your thoughts are so meticulous.\"","Yanshu smiled modestly, \"I wouldn't dare claim that. This is just the basic skill set of a gossip enthusiast.\"","Tsk, she had to admit, many of the rumors she'd heard over the years only contained simple information. It was through her careful deductions that she was able to piece together the full stories. Over time, she had honed this skill.","Of course, there were occasional missteps, like only recently realizing she had long been exposed to the emperor's gaze...","However, after speaking, she furrowed her brow again and said, \"I had wanted to publish the story to expose that person's hypocritical face to everyone. But now it seems we'd have to conceal Imperial Physician Jiang's identity, otherwise it might cause him trouble.\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"There's no need to rush with the story. Let's see how the Capital Official investigates the case.\"","Yanshu nodded, \"That's true.\"","Today, with many witnesses and both physical and testimonial evidence, and with the Consort of County Princess Yao personally accompanying Imperial Physician Jiang to the Capital Official's office, that criminal surely wouldn't escape.","Now it was just a matter of waiting to see when Zhang Shengkang would be exposed.","Thus, upon returning to the palace, Yanshu focused all her attention on waiting for the latest news from the system.","By then it was already nightfall, and it wasn't until the next morning that the system finally sent an update—","[Latest news: Zhang Shengkang's disciple has come forward to take the blame for him.]","What?","Yanshu was stunned. [Disciple? Zhang Shengkang has disciples?]","System: [Of course he does. He's the head of the Imperial Medical Academy after all. Over the years, countless people have tried to curry favor with him, so he casually accepted quite a few disciples. However, unlike other masters who wholeheartedly pass on their skills, he takes on disciples purely to expand his interests. He either has these people open pharmacies in the city to make money for him or uses them as his lackeys to do his bidding.]","Yanshu understood and asked further, [So how did his disciple take the blame for him?]","System: [It's simple. First of all, that small-time thief was actually instructed by this disciple. Yesterday, after some severe interrogation at the Capital Official's office, the thief confessed who hired him. The Capital Official then brought in this disciple for questioning and found out that he happened to run a clinic nearby. Because Imperial Physician Jiang treated the neighbors, doing a good job at low prices and often not charging at all for families in difficulty, more and more people were going to him for treatment. Wouldn't this affect the business of that clinic? This disciple had ample motive and reason, and he insisted it was all his own doing, so the Capital Official closed the case.]","Yanshu: [...I see.]","Tsk, the business competition angle was indeed very convincing, especially since apart from her and the emperor, no one else knew about the grudge between Imperial Physician Jiang and Zhang Shengkang.","Moreover, Zhang Shengkang was so good at concealing his true nature, appearing to be a man of high moral standing. Who would suspect him?","System: [Also, according to current laws, this crime isn't punishable by death. At most, that disciple will spend a few years in prison and receive some beatings before being released. He has a wife and children, so he wouldn't cut off his source of income for this. Moreover, Zhang Shengkang will surely give him a large sum of money as compensation.]","Yanshu sighed, thinking to herself that this old fox Zhang was truly cunning and calculating.","At that moment in Qianming Palace, Yuwen Lan listened to the report from the Capital Official and had the same thoughts as Yanshu.","Zhang Shengkang had been entrenched in the Imperial Medical Academy for over twenty years; his schemes ran deep. It seemed that this incident alone wasn't enough to bring him down.","Moreover, even if Yanshu were to make public the events of the past, he would likely still manage to escape unscathed.","Not to mention, the events from over twenty years ago were now known to very few people. Where could they find solid evidence?","Under such circumstances, if they rashly released public opinion, he could easily dismiss it as slander.","And the Empress Dowager would likely protect him as well.","However, just at that moment, Fu Hai came in to report, \"Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager requests your presence at the Palace of Benevolent Peace. She says she has matters to discuss with you.\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","What a coincidence?","He made a sound of acknowledgment, rose, and left the hall for the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Upon arrival, Yuwen Lan saw that besides the Empress Dowager, Zhang Shengkang was also present in the hall.","At this moment, Zhang was hanging his head, looking very serious, as if something major had occurred.","Yuwen Lan glanced around, first greeted the Empress Dowager, then sat down on the warm couch.","The Empress Dowager said, \"Imperial Physician Zhang just came to see me, saying he wanted to beg forgiveness from me and Your Majesty. So I asked Your Majesty to come and hear him out together.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and looked at Zhang Shengkang, \"What offense has Imperial Physician Zhang committed?\"","Zhang Shengkang immediately knelt down and said, \"I have failed in teaching my disciples. One of my disciples, due to poor business, framed another doctor, intending to ruin his reputation with no regard for patients' lives. When I heard the news from the Capital Official this morning, I felt deeply ashamed and responsible. Although I was unaware of this matter, the main culprit is still my disciple. I have let down Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager's trust, and I humbly request punishment from both of you.\"","His words were very sincere, as if he were truly an upright and selfless physician.","Hearing this, before Yuwen Lan could speak, the Empress Dowager said, \"Hearing this, that disciple is indeed hateful! As his teacher, you have indeed failed to teach him properly, and bear great responsibility.\"","Zhang Shengkang bowed his head in agreement.","The Empress Dowager then changed her tone, saying, \"However, considering that you spend your days serving me in the palace and are responsible for various affairs of the Imperial Medical Academy, you are indeed stretched thin. So, we can't entirely blame you. This time, we'll let you off the hook.\"","She then looked at Yuwen Lan and said, \"What does Your Majesty think?\"","In this situation, what else could Yuwen Lan say?","The Empress Dowager clearly intended to protect him, and this man had indeed played his part well.","So he said, \"Mother is magnanimous, but this incident has caused quite a stir in the city. Many people already know of their master-disciple relationship. If we don't hold anyone accountable at all, it might be difficult to explain to the public. How about this,\"","He looked at Zhang Shengkang again and said, \"Since this matter concerns patients' safety and has had a terrible impact, that person's clinic will be shut down immediately, and he will be severely punished. As for you, you'll be fined half a year's salary and demoted half a rank. In the future, you must be strict with yourself and even stricter in managing your subordinates.\"","Zhang Shengkang quickly agreed and kowtowed.","The Empress Dowager nodded beside him and said, \"Your Majesty is wise.\"","After the emperor left the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu, in her own palace, finished receiving the gossip from the system.","Needless to say, failing to bring down Zhang Shengkang this time was frustrating.","She furrowed her brow and said, [The Empress Dowager used to seem to despise evil. Why is she protecting Zhang Shengkang so much this time?]","System: [After all, Zhang Shengkang is an insider of the Empress Dowager. When the Empress Dowager lost her child, she was so depressed that she almost fell seriously ill and died. It was Zhang Shengkang who saved her with all his efforts. Today, Zhang Shengkang can become the chief physician, which is entirely due to the Empress Dowager's promotion. Since the Emperor took power, the Empress Dowager has gradually lost many of her supporters, especially now that the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion is practically useless. The Empress Dowager will definitely keep as many as she can.]","[Moreover, all these years, it has been Zhang Shengkang who has been in charge of her health. Whenever she has a headache, only Zhang Shengkang can cure it.]","Yanshu exclaimed anxiously, [That was because there were no better alternatives in the past. Now that Imperial Physician Jiang is so outstanding, even saving the young lady of the Ni family, the Empress Dowager has seen it with her own eyes. Why can't she replace Zhang Shengkang with Imperial Physician Jiang?]","System: [How can the Empress Dowager trust just anyone? Moreover, in the Empress Dowager's view, this time it really has nothing to do with Zhang Shengkang. Zhang Shengkang is skilled in medicine and, as long as he remains loyal to her, she will definitely protect him.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Alas, although the logic is understood, it still makes one feel uncomfortable.","After thinking for a while, she picked up her pen and decided to rewrite a new script.","She didn't believe that there was a crack that couldn't be pried open in the world.","No matter how much the Empress Dowager trusted him, if she knew that the person by her side was treacherous, she would inevitably harbor doubts and gradually become disgusted.","For several days, the Empress Dowager was also in a heavy mood.","Taking advantage of the absence of others in the hall, Nanny Zhuang stepped forward to advise, \"Since Madam Mu returned to Mingzhou, Your Majesty has spoken less and less.\"","The Empress Dowager closed her eyes and sighed, \"There are so many troubles that one doesn't even feel like speaking.\"","Nanny Zhuang gently massaged the Empress Dowager's temples and said, \"The palace is becoming increasingly desolate. Consort Yishu has been serving Your Majesty for so long, yet there is still no news of a child. Why doesn't Your Majesty invite more ladies into the palace to bear children for the Emperor and keep you company? With more people, it will always be more lively.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed again upon hearing this.","What's the use of having more people?","The root cause of the Emperor's problem has not been resolved. Even if ten thousand beauties were brought in, what would be the point?","Yet he himself doesn't seem to be in a hurry?","After pondering for half a day, the Empress Dowager suddenly opened her eyes and instructed Nanny Zhuang, \"Go and do something for me.\"","...","As evening approached, Yanshu was about to get up from her desk to stretch her muscles.","Just as she put down her pen, she heard the System say, [New information: The Empress Dowager can't wait any longer and plans to have Zhang Shengkang treat the Emperor's impotence.]","Yanshu: [...]","Poor Empress Dowager, she still doesn't know that the Emperor has recovered.","And he has recovered very well. Last night, after she had sent away her relatives, they spent half the night together, almost reviewing all the paintings that had been put aside for a few days.","Of course, with the new gossip at hand, now is not the time to reminisce about last night. She quickly asked the System, [What does the Empress Dowager plan to do? The Emperor doesn't trust Zhang Shengkang at all now; he won't let Zhang Shengkang near him for a pulse diagnosis.]","System: [Maybe this time he will let him near.]","Yanshu: [??? Why?]","System: [The Emperor used to have diarrhea whenever he drank goat's milk as a child. Just now, the Empress Dowager had someone add some goat's milk to the pastries and sent them over.]","Yanshu: [???]","...The Empress Dowager is indeed ruthless enough to make Zhang Shengkang diagnose the Emperor's condition!","How could she stand by and watch?","So she quickly got up and headed towards Qianming Palace.","When Yanshu arrived at Qianming Palace, she saw a plate of taro paste cakes on the tea table in the study, and the oblivious Yuwen Lan was eating one.","He even asked her, \"Why are you here?\"","Fu Hai was also in the hall, so Yanshu could only say, \"I wanted to ask if Your Majesty would like to dine at Ganlu Palace tonight... Where did these pastries come from?\"","Yuwen Lan, while eating, replied, \"They were sent by the Empress Dowager. I was just hungry, so I ate a few pieces.\"","He even asked her, \"Do you want to try some?\"","Mother, he's already eaten a few pieces?","Yanshu silently wiped a cold sweat for him and asked, \"Your Majesty... are you feeling alright?\"","\"Fine...\"","Yuwen Lan was about to answer her when, after just two words, he suddenly paused.","Yanshu accurately caught the change in his expression and quickly asked, \"What's wrong, Your Majesty?\"","Before the words were finished, Yuwen Lan had already put down the pastry and rushed to the bathroom, leaving only a hurried sentence, \"Wait a moment.\"","He even remembered to close the bathroom door.","Seeing this, Fu Hai hurried to follow and serve, but Yanshu stopped him, saying, \"Chief Eunuch Fu, please step aside for a moment. I have something to report to the Emperor.\"","Fu Hai paused and had to comply, retreating.","Yanshu then also went to the bathroom door and said, \"I have something urgent to report.\"","From inside the door came Yuwen Lan's slightly uncomfortable voice, \"Just wait a moment...\"","Yanshu, however, said, \"The matter is urgent; it will be too late if we wait.\"","The person inside had no choice but to say, \"Alright, just say it like that.\"","...As a monarch, it was the first time in his life to listen to a report while in the bathroom.","But then he heard Yanshu say, \"The Empress Dowager had someone put some goat's milk in the taro paste cakes you just ate...\"","\"What?\"","Yuwen Lan was stunned.","Yanshu hurriedly added, \"Didn't you always have diarrhea when you drank goat's milk as a child? The Empress Dowager plans to use this opportunity to have Zhang Shengkang come over to treat you!!!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Alright, he understood now.","Putting aside all the various feelings of helplessness for the moment, he immediately ordered, \"Summon Imperial Physician Jiang!\"","Yanshu complied and was about to go out to instruct Fu Hai.","But just as she lifted her foot, she suddenly paused—","If Imperial Physician Jiang came to diagnose him, wouldn't he recognize that the Emperor was the one who had previously sought treatment for impotence at his home?"]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62","paragraphs":["Of course, Yuwen Lan had considered Yanshu's concerns at this moment.","But he had no other choice now.","Previously, he had been wary of the Empress Dowager, so he never allowed Zhang Shengkang to get close. Although he was better now, Zhang Shengkang had ill intentions. If he learned about the Emperor's physical condition, who knows what schemes he might devise in the future.","So he preferred to choose Jiang Nianqi.","After all, he was just straightforward and honest. Even if he recognized him, he wouldn't do anything malicious.","Most importantly, he had already recovered, so what was there to fear?","Could he guarantee never falling ill again and never needing to summon an imperial physician?","So if he had to choose someone, of course he would pick Jiang Nianqi.","At this moment, he heard Yanshu asking through the door, \"Is Your Majesty certain about calling for Imperial Physician Jiang?\"","Yuwen Lan sighed, \"It's fine, just call him.\"","And quickly too...","The young lady outside responded affirmatively and finally went to summon him.","Shortly after, Imperial Physician Jiang hurriedly arrived at Qianming Palace.","Knowing that someone was in discomfort, Yanshu quickly said before the doctor could perform a full ceremonial greeting, \"His Majesty is unwell. Doctor Jiang, please come quickly to examine the Emperor.\"","Doctor Jiang complied and hurried to the Emperor's side, carefully extending his hand to take his pulse.","After a moment, Yuwen Lan heard an exclamation of surprise—","[This, this, this... Isn't this that... impotent official??? I thought his aura was extraordinary, so it's actually Your Majesty??? It's actually Your Majesty!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had indeed recognized him.","Fearing the doctor might forget the urgent matter at hand, he had to speak up, \"Since childhood, We have been unable to drink goat's milk. The pastries We ate earlier likely contained some, so We... so We...\"","Fortunately, Doctor Jiang was a clever man. Before the Emperor could finish, he had already understood and proactively said, \"Your Majesty, please don't worry. The amount of goat's milk in the pastries was likely minimal. There shouldn't be any major issue with Your Majesty's health. I'll write a prescription right away.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, and saw him quickly write out a prescription, instructing Fu Hai to fetch the medicine from the imperial pharmacy.","In the Palace of Benevolent Peace, as dusk fell outside, the Empress Dowager was still waiting for news.","Soon after, Zhang Shengkang hurriedly entered the hall. The Empress Dowager quickly asked, \"How is it?\"","Zhang Shengkang bowed his head and said, \"This servant has been waiting at the Imperial Medical Academy, but His Majesty did not summon me.\"","\"The Emperor didn't call for you?\" The Empress Dowager was stunned.","Could it be that the Emperor was still wary of her?","This child...","She then simply instructed her attendants, \"Prepare the palanquin.\"","And to Zhang Shengkang she said, \"We shall take you there personally.\"","After Doctor Jiang's busy efforts, once the Emperor had drunk the medicine, his symptoms finally subsided before long.","Seeing this, everyone finally breathed a sigh of relief.","Yanshu couldn't help but marvel inwardly at how creative the Empress Dowager's approach had been in trying to help treat the Emperor's condition.","Tonight had truly been full of twists and turns, extremely dramatic.","A mother worried about her son having no heir, racking her brains to force her son to seek treatment;","Yet the son had actually recovered quietly long ago, just unwilling to tell her?","Tsk tsk tsk, if this were written into a novel, it would definitely attract readers.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","At a time like this, she was still thinking about turning it into a novel?","Of course, he knew she was just joking.","But at this moment, he himself was also truly at a loss for words and bewildered.","He hadn't intentionally concealed things from the Empress Dowager, it's just that he couldn't very well go and inform her out of the blue that he had recovered.","He had originally thought that once Yanshu became pregnant, the Empress Dowager would naturally understand. He didn't expect the Empress Dowager to be so impatient...","Well, it seems he can't eat anything from the Palace of Benevolent Peace anymore in the future.","...","Just as his thoughts were in turmoil, he saw Doctor Jiang suddenly put on a serious expression and kneel down, saying, \"This subject has something to report to Your Majesty.\"","After speaking, he glanced around, anxiously thinking, [This is a matter of utmost importance, I hope Your Majesty can understand my meaning!]","Yuwen Lan understood, and first raised his hand to dismiss everyone else.","However, Jiang Nianqi still didn't speak, still glancing with some hesitation at the person beside him.","Yanshu was standing there, pretending not to understand as she looked around, fiddling with her fingers.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Then he heard her anxiously thinking, [Don't send me away! I'm the one who came to report to you tonight! Whatever secret it is, I must hear it!!! You've already chosen to face social death, so what's one more person?!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He could only say to Jiang Nianqi, \"Imperial Consort Yi is not an outsider. Whatever important matter you have, just speak freely.\"","Only then did the doctor comply, saying, \"This subject boldly reports, I've noticed that the smell in this bedchamber is somewhat off. If Your Majesty has experienced any physical discomfort before, I fear the cause of that misfortune may still be present here.\"","At these words, Yanshu's heart skipped a beat.","The cause of misfortune the doctor spoke of... Could it be the reason for the Emperor's previous impotence?","Tsk, this is indeed a major issue!!!","But come to think of it, Doctor Jiang is clearly not stupid either, knowing to hint at it so tactfully without directly saying he had recognized the Emperor.","Yuwen Lan had already furrowed his brow, quickly asking, \"What exactly is off?\"","It should be noted that ever since he first went outside the palace to see this doctor and was told he had been poisoned, he had already replaced almost everything in this bedchamber - the bedding, curtains, flowers, ornaments, and so on.","He also hadn't used any incense that could have possibly been tampered with.","Yet now this doctor was still saying something was off?","Could it be...","This imperial bed?","— This was an item passed down from Emperor Gaozu, it shouldn't be possible for anyone to have tampered with it.","Just as he was thinking this, he saw the doctor walk over to the Azure Sky Sword hanging by the bedhead. He sniffed it repeatedly, then said to him, \"Your Majesty, the anomaly seems to be in this sword.\"","Yuwen Lan was taken aback.","— This sword was a relic of the Former Emperor. Since the Former Emperor's passing, he had always kept it by his side as a memento.","He asked in confusion, \"This sword is made entirely of iron and copper, what anomaly could there be?\"","However, the doctor pointed at the sword's guard and said, \"This subject boldly guesses that the anomaly is likely within this part.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but lean in for a closer look. She saw that the sword guard was hollow, intricately carved with auspicious cloud patterns, and had the natural yellow color of brass.","She took it in her hand and shook it, but heard no sound. She held it up to her eyes but couldn't see anything inside.","Just as she was puzzled, she saw Yuwen Lan take the sword body and examine it. Suddenly, he took out a rather sturdy dagger and worked on the sword guard, actually prying it into two halves.","This revealed the true nature of what was inside.","They saw that on the inner wall of the intricately carved hollow sword guard, there was actually a layer of something golden, seemingly some kind of paste, though it had now hardened completely.","Doctor Jiang brought it to his nose and sniffed carefully, his brow furrowing more and more.","Seeing this, the others grew increasingly tense. Yuwen Lan hurriedly asked, \"What is it?\"","The Imperial Physician sniffed as he answered, \"Your Majesty, I'm afraid this contains tortoise shell, egg yolk, scutellaria root, rosa laevigata, and dozens of other medicinal ingredients, along with niter and sulfur mixed in. These are all substances that suppress desire. If one comes into contact with them night after night, over time it will inevitably cause numbness in a man's critical area, leading to loss of ability to produce offspring.\"","Yanshu: !!!","Goodness, isn't this chemical castration? So this was the culprit!","Looking at Yuwen Lan again, his brows were also tightly knitted—","Indeed, in the past he had been completely normal, but after ascending the throne and moving into Qianming Palace, he gradually became dysfunctional.","That area did indeed become increasingly numb, and his heart gradually lost all desire, until later when he met Yanshu.","It seems the root cause of his illness was actually this object?","Yanshu hurriedly asked him, \"But why would this be in Your Majesty's chambers? Who could have put it inside this sword guard?\"","In her mind she thought, [Since this is the Former Emperor's sword, it must have been meant for him, to make the Former Emperor impotent! So... could it have been the Empress Dowager?]","[Back then, the Empress Dowager hated how the Former Emperor kept taking one concubine after another, so she decided to chemically castrate her husband?]","Yuwen Lan: ???","He knew the term \"castration\", but what did those two words in front mean?","Before he could figure it out, he heard her reject this idea herself—","[That's impossible. If the Empress Dowager had placed it, she would definitely know about it. Then why would she go to such lengths now to urge the Emperor to seek treatment?]","...Yuwen Lan thought the same.","So the first person he ruled out was the Empress Dowager.","Then he heard her ponder, [Could it have been done by one of the Former Emperor's other consorts?]","\"It's not very likely. First of all, even if a concubine could enter Qianming Palace, how could she do such a thing right under the Former Emperor's nose?\"","\"Moreover, concubines are always competing for favor. How could they compete if they chemically drowned the Former Emperor?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","That was his father after all. Could they please stop using the word \"drown\"?","Of course, her analysis made sense. The possibility of other imperial concubines poisoning the Former Emperor was also almost zero.","So who could it be?","Just then, an announcement came from outside: \"The Empress Dowager has arrived...\"","The three people in the hall were all startled.","Yanshu: [Why is the Empress Dowager coming? She's not here to check if the Emperor really has diarrhea, is she?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Very likely.","He first put down the sword in his hand. Then, he saw the Empress Dowager enter the hall, followed by Zhang Shengkang.","Seeing this man, the previously nervous Imperial Physician Jiang quietly composed himself and bowed to the Empress Dowager along with Yanshu.","Yuwen Lan also showed no unusual reaction, only asking, \"Why has Mother come?\"","The Empress Dowager looked anxious as she said, \"I was so careless. I just realized that the taro paste cakes I sent to Your Majesty earlier might not be suitable. Your Majesty couldn't eat goat's milk since childhood, but I forgot to tell them not to add goat's milk. They made it and sent it directly to Your Majesty... Is Your Majesty alright?\"","\"...\"","Yanshu silently marveled in her heart - no wonder people say the Empress Dowager is formidable. Her acting skills were impeccable.","But the Emperor was no less skilled, only saying, \"I did feel a bit unwell earlier, so I called for Imperial Physician Jiang. I've just taken some medicine and I'm fine now.\"","The Empress Dowager seemed surprised, \"You're fine?\"","She looked him over again, and seeing that his complexion was indeed not bad, she couldn't help but mutter, it seems he really is fine?","At this, the Empress Dowager could only sigh and blame herself, \"It's all my fault for being so careless. I only thought of it just now and worried that Your Majesty might be unwell, so I specifically brought Zhang Shengkang with me.\"","Yanshu quietly observed from the side, thinking it was rare to see the Empress Dowager speak like this.","— She really feared the Emperor might be angry.","But it had to be said, the Empress Dowager's imagination was quite wild. Who else could come up with such a method and dare to use it on the Emperor?","If the Emperor were ruthless, he could completely use this to make a big fuss with her.","But Yuwen Lan said, \"It's just a small matter, Mother needn't blame herself so.\"","Yanshu understood - the Emperor was giving face to the Empress Dowager.","He was indeed a filial child, and quite sentimental.","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"That's good. However, it's better if Imperial Physician Zhang also examines Your Majesty, just to be absolutely certain.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Of course, after all the planning, it would be a waste if Zhang Shengkang didn't examine the Emperor, wouldn't it?","However, the Emperor only said, \"There's no need. I really am fine now. Mother has seen Imperial Physician Jiang's skills with her own eyes. Don't you trust him? He has already resolved many of my concerns lately.\"","Yanshu quietly paused again - the Emperor was sending signals to the Empress Dowager!","Hearing him say this, the Empress Dowager was indeed taken aback. She tried asking Imperial Physician Jiang, \"How is His Majesty's health now?\"","Imperial Physician Jiang hurriedly replied, \"Reporting to the Empress Dowager, His Majesty's health is excellent now. Apart from the earlier diarrhea caused by the goat's milk disagreeing with him, there are no other problems at all.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager pondered —","[Could it be that the Emperor has already consulted this Imperial Physician Jiang? Does this mean the illness is cured? That's great news!]","However, before she could rejoice, she heard the Emperor suddenly ask her, \"There's something I wanted to ask Mother about.\"","The Empress Dowager came back to her senses and quickly said, \"What is it?\"","Yuwen Lan picked up the sword he had put down earlier, along with the scabbard he had just removed and its contents, presenting them all before the Empress Dowager.","\"Just now, I found something unusual in this scabbard.\"","\"Something unusual?\"","The Empress Dowager and Zhang Shengkang were both startled and quickly looked into the scabbard.","Yuwen Lan continued, \"As Mother knows, this sword originally belonged to Father. Since I inherited the throne, I've always kept it here in this hall. It's unlikely that anyone could have tampered with it. So I wonder, could it have been placed there when Father was still alive?\"","As he spoke, he closely watched their expressions and said slowly and deliberately, \"Imperial Physician Jiang examined it earlier and thinks it might be poisonous.\"","Poison?","The Empress Dowager was visibly startled and quickly instructed Zhang Shengkang, \"You take a look too.\"","[How could there be such a thing in the scabbard? What's going on?]","Yuwen Lan thought silently, it seems the Empress Dowager doesn't know about this either.","Zhang Shengkang responded affirmatively and hurriedly took the scabbard to examine it carefully.","He touched it and even sniffed it, while secretly pondering, [Not bad, this is indeed the Three Purity Pill. It was hidden so discreetly!]","Three Purity Pill?","Yuwen Lan paused inwardly. It seems Zhang Shengkang knew about this object all along?","He tried speaking to the Empress Dowager again, \"I'm wondering if this might have been intended for Father. But who would want to harm Father?\"","As soon as he said this, Zhang Shengkang spoke up, \"Your Majesty, if I'm not mistaken, this object is called the Three Purity Pill. It's usually used by Taoist practitioners for abstinence.\"","\"Abstinence?\"","The Empress Dowager was startled.","Then she reacted, inwardly sneering, [That man was really willing to go to such lengths for immortality!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Is she talking about the Former Emperor?","Could the Former Emperor have placed it there himself?","Just then, the Empress Dowager composed herself and said, \"Qianming Palace is the Emperor's residence. Without being summoned, even I cannot enter. Back then, the Former Emperor was obsessed with Taoism and neglected state affairs, only allowing that Baihe Taoist to come and go. So in my opinion, if this wasn't done by the Former Emperor himself, then that Baihe Taoist is the most suspicious.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan also remembered.","— When he was seven or eight years old, the Former Emperor met a Taoist priest called Baihe Taoist and became obsessed with Taoism. At first, he only read related books and occasionally discussed scriptures with this Baihe Taoist, but later the situation escalated. He even set up an incense burner in the palace and spent all day meditating and refining elixirs, neglecting all other matters.","All state affairs were left to the ministers and the Empress Dowager to handle. Apart from the Baihe Taoist, he wouldn't let anyone else near him.","During that time, Yuwen Lan led troops to fight the Xiongnu, and was gone for half a year. When he returned and wanted to see his father, he waited outside Qianming Palace for half a day, but only the Baihe Taoist came out to tell him that the Former Emperor was in seclusion and couldn't see anyone, asking him to come back later.","Looking at it this way, it seems only the Former Emperor himself and that Baihe Taoist were most likely responsible.","Moreover, after that, no more imperial heirs were born in the palace. Now it seems this might also be related to this object.","The Former Emperor might have been poisoned by this Three Purity Pill just like him.","Just as Yuwen Lan figured this out, he heard the Empress Dowager coldly laugh in her heart, [That man nearly caused himself to have no descendants! I've spent half my life cleaning up his mess, always thinking of his son's interests. Now not only does he not appreciate my efforts, he even suspects me? It's truly heartbreaking!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","It seems the Empress Dowager really didn't know about this.","He was silent for a moment, then said, \"Mother has suffered much these years.\"","The Empress Dowager only said, \"I only want what's best for Your Majesty.\"","Her voice had already turned cold.","Yuwen Lan could only say, \"It's my fault for not doing well enough, causing you trouble.\"","The Empress Dowager still spoke coldly, \"It's fine. Now that Your Majesty is well, I can rest easy.\"","She sighed and said, \"I've been out for a while now. Since Your Majesty is in good health, I'll take my leave.\"","With that, she turned and walked out of the hall.","Seeing this, Zhang Shengkang could only hurriedly say to Yuwen Lan, \"Since Your Majesty is well, this subject will also take his leave.\"","He then followed in the Empress Dowager's footsteps.","Yuwen Lan's face showed no emotion, but he laughed coldly in his heart.","Back when the Former Emperor was critically ill, this Zhang Shengkang guarded Qianming Palace day and night. He must have discovered the abnormality long ago.","Perhaps even earlier.","But he never mentioned it to anyone.","Not even the Empress Dowager knew about it.","What was he planning?","Was he waiting for Yuwen Lan to find him, so he could then produce this object and claim credit?","Sure enough, just as Zhang Shengkang was about to step out of the hall, Yuwen Lan heard him think, [After all my calculations, I can't believe this Jiang fellow beat me to it! Heaven is unfair!]","After the Empress Dowager and Zhang Shengkang left, only Yanshu, Yuwen Lan, and Imperial Physician Jiang remained in the hall.","— Although the mystery that had troubled him for so long was finally solved tonight, Yuwen Lan's heart was far from at ease.","He never imagined that this object would be related to his imperial father.","How could his once brilliant and mighty father have become like that?","As his heart grew heavy, he heard Yanshu's voice in his ear, crunching on melon seeds—","[I'm starting to think the old emperor was a victim too! After all, he might practice Taoism on his own, but he'd never want to implicate his son and end his family line!]","[Besides, if he knew about this, he would have told his son before dying no matter what! Since he didn't say anything, he must not have known either. Plus, it was hidden in such a secretive place.]","[Damn, looking at it this way, that Baihe Taoist had some big ambitions! Where is he now?]","The system replied, [He ran away. The Former Emperor's death was quite sudden - he was in the middle of cultivation when he suddenly coughed up blood. The palace was in chaos, with everyone focused on trying to save the emperor. The Empress Dowager was also working to ensure the crown prince's smooth succession. Add to that the various royal clan members starting rebellions, and the court was in complete disarray. He took advantage of the chaos to escape.]","Yanshu: [...]","Tsk, the old emperor really didn't leave his son anything good, did he?","What was the point of all that?","Of course, now wasn't the time to criticize the Former Emperor. She was about to speak to the emperor when she saw him call out to someone outside, \"Summon the Imperial Guard to immediately search for that Baihe Taoist from back then.\"","The person outside acknowledged the order, and Yanshu felt somewhat relieved.","Just then, Imperial Physician Jiang suddenly knelt and said, \"This subject did not recognize Your Majesty earlier. Please punish me for my transgression.\"","— If he had known that official was the emperor, he would never have spoken so bluntly!","Especially about \"sexual indulgence\"...","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He could only pretend not to hear and said, \"You helped solve a difficult problem for me. I should reward you instead.\"","He then instructed Fu Hai, \"Issue an edict: Imperial Physician Jiang's medical skills are exceptional. Promote him by one rank to Chief Imperial Physician.\"","The people outside acknowledged, and Imperial Physician Jiang quickly kowtowed, \"This subject thanks Your Majesty for the great honor.\"","*Cough cough* And thank you for sparing my life, Your Majesty.","Tonight was truly... too dangerous!","Just as he was secretly breathing a sigh of relief, he heard the emperor speak again, \"Forget about what happened earlier. You are not to mention it to anyone.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang quickly responded solemnly, \"This subject obeys.\"","After the goat's milk incident, the relationship between the Empress Dowager and the emperor became somewhat delicate.","Yanshu understood that the emperor was likely concerned about the goat's milk affair, while the Empress Dowager resented the emperor's suspicions towards her.","— Tsk, this situation was indeed difficult. They each had their own stance and grievances.","If there was anyone to blame, it could only be the old emperor for his misdeeds, leaving behind so many historical issues for this mother and son to deal with.","Moreover, it would be better if they were biological mother and son, but these two were missing that blood connection, so their relationship could easily become distant.","A few days later, the Empress Dowager suffered from another headache.","When the emperor received the news, he went to visit her personally but was politely refused by the Empress Dowager.","With no other choice, he had to instruct Yanshu to go attend to her in his place.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Wasn't this a case of the innocent bystander getting caught in the crossfire?","... What had she done to deserve this?","However, as a palace consort, it was her duty to attend to the Empress Dowager when she was unwell. So, she spent several days by the sickbed without complaint.","Fortunately, the Empress Dowager didn't make things difficult for her. When she was in pain, she only called for Nanny Zhuang and Zhu Shu to attend to her. When she felt better, she would ask Yanshu to read novels to her to pass the time.","And the novels she read were the ones Yanshu had written herself.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, she could only suppress her embarrassment and do her best to read them vividly for the Empress Dowager.","The Empress Dowager even complained to her, \"The Carefree Young Master's novels are good, but lately, the author has become too lazy, taking too long to release new stories. It's making people wait anxiously.\"","Yanshu smiled and agreed outwardly, but inwardly she sighed.","She wanted to write, but she had been spending all her time reviewing her old works. Where would she find the time?","Just as she was thinking this, a palace servant came in to report, \"Your Highness, the Marquess of Pingjin's Wife has come to visit you.\"","The Marquess of Pingjin's Wife was the Empress Dowager's maternal cousin. She usually didn't stay in the capital, only coming to the palace to visit the Empress Dowager during festivals and holidays. This time, she had likely heard about the Empress Dowager's illness and hurried to the capital.","Ever since the incident with the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion, the Empress Dowager had grown increasingly distant from her natal family, only maintaining some contact with her cousins.","Especially since this cousin had come all the way from Pingjin, the Empress Dowager couldn't refuse her. She nodded and said, \"Please show her in.\"","The palace servant acknowledged.","Not long after, two women, one old and one young, were led into the hall.","It was the Marquess of Pingjin's Wife and her youngest daughter, Huo Yingxia.","— This family was quite legendary.","The Marquess's Wife seemed to have been blessed with her mother-in-law's luck. She had given birth to five sons in a row, and only at the age of forty did she have this youngest daughter, whom she treasured like the apple of her eye and took everywhere.","However, while the mother and daughter were close, they didn't look very alike.","The Marquess's Wife had a round face with bright, piercing eyes that gave her a somewhat heroic air.","Her daughter, on the other hand, had an oval face with slightly upturned phoenix eyes, giving her quite an alluring appearance.","Yanshu had seen this mother-daughter pair before during the New Year celebrations and the Empress Dowager's birthday banquet. Seeing them again now, she couldn't help but wonder to herself—","They say daughters take after their fathers. Could it be that the Marquess of Pingjin looked so alluring?","Suddenly, she heard the system chime in, [The Marquess of Pingjin isn't alluring, but his mistress is. This daughter is actually born from his mistress.]","Yanshu: \"???\"","What kind of story was this now?"]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63","paragraphs":["What?","The daughter doted on by the Marquess of Pingjin's Wife like the apple of her eye is actually not hers, but the child of the Marquess's mistress???","A sense of scandalous drama immediately filled the air, and Yanshu quickly asked, \"What exactly happened? Where did Madam Huo's own daughter go? Does she know she's raising someone else's child?\"","The system replied, \"She definitely doesn't know. If she did, would the Marquess of Pingjin still be alive today?\"","\"Madam Huo comes from a military family and has a straightforward personality. She's also very capable. Since marrying the Marquess of Pingjin, she's been managing everything inside and outside the household. The Marquess is quite different - he has all the bad habits of an aristocratic son, lazy and indulgent, considering himself refined, and fond of composing poetry.\"","\"Back then, if it weren't for saving his declining family, the Marquess of Pingjin wouldn't have wanted to marry a daughter from a military family. Even after the marriage, he never liked Madam Huo, so he secretly set up a mistress outside who was more to his liking. However, Madam Huo was wholeheartedly devoted to her husband. Since their marriage, she gave birth to five sons in a row. But Madam Huo noticed that apart from showing some care for the eldest son, her husband didn't seem to care much about the other sons. After much consideration, she thought her husband preferred girls, so despite her age, she tried hard again and gave birth to a daughter for the Marquess of Pingjin.\"","\"Who would have thought that by coincidence, just a few days before Madam Huo gave birth, the mistress had also just given birth to a daughter. The mistress certainly didn't want her own daughter to remain hidden, so she came up with a bold idea. She begged the Marquess of Pingjin to swap her child with Madam Huo's, bringing her own child to Madam Huo's side and sending Madam Huo's daughter away.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu was already full of questions, \"??? The Marquess of Pingjin actually agreed? Is there something wrong with his head? Wasn't the child sent away his own flesh and blood? How could he do such a thing?\"","The system replied, \"There's a saying that goes, 'A scumbag doesn't love his own flesh and blood, but the child born by the woman he favors.' The Marquess of Pingjin is exactly this kind of scumbag. Because he doesn't like his legal wife but likes his mistress, he's biased towards the children as well, so he did such a thing.\"","Yanshu was speechless, feeling angry for a while before asking, \"But swapping babies isn't that simple, right? Didn't Madam Huo notice it wasn't her own child?\"","The system sighed, \"Madam Huo was of advanced age when she gave birth to a girl, and the situation was very critical. She fainted right after giving birth, and it took the doctors three days to save her. During this time, the servants in the room were taking care of her, and the Marquess of Pingjin took the newborn baby to his mother for care.\"","\"His mother was also elderly at the time and her eyesight was poor. Plus, she never imagined her son could do such a beastly thing, so she didn't realize her granddaughter had been switched. Additionally, Madam Huo's own daughter took after her and was born with a larger build, while the mistress's daughter had been cared for for two extra days, so the two babies looked quite similar. Therefore, the servants in the mansion didn't notice either. Thus, when Madam Huo recovered, she had no idea that the baby the Marquess of Pingjin brought back was no longer her own daughter.\"","...Alright.","Yanshu once again lamented the Marquess of Pingjin's heartlessness, and asked, \"So what about Madam Huo's real child now? Is she doing alright?\"","The system nodded, \"That little girl was initially switched to the mistress's place, where the mistress certainly didn't treat her well. Once she even starved her until she fell ill. Coincidentally, the Marquess of Pingjin discovered this, and feeling a moment of fatherly compassion, he sent her to be raised by a well-off farming family outside. That family was kind-hearted and quite fond of her, never letting her suffer from childhood to adulthood, so she's doing okay now.\"","Yanshu breathed a sigh of relief, \"Compared to staying with that viper of a mistress, this girl is indeed better off now. What about that mistress? Wasn't she punished?\"","But the system said, \"Not only was she not punished, but now she's almost in her thirties and still maintains the appearance of a woman in her twenties. The Marquess of Pingjin still visits her two or three times a month.\"","Yanshu: \"??? Wait, the woman who abused his daughter, and he let her off? And still goes to see her two or three times a month?\"","System: \"As I said before, he prefers that woman over his own flesh and blood.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, the level of scumbaggery is truly astounding!","This Marquess of Pingjin could easily rank in the top three scumbags of the year.","...","She silently finished digesting this information, while nearby, Madam Huo and her daughter had started conversing with the Empress Dowager.","The Empress Dowager asked, \"Why did you suddenly come? When did you arrive in the capital?\"","Madam Huo replied, \"We set out before dawn today and just arrived in the capital. After changing clothes at the General's mansion, we hurried over. How are you feeling, Your Majesty?\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"It's just my old ailment acting up again, not worth you making a special trip.\"","But Madam Huo inquired further, \"Your Majesty usually only suffers from your old illness when catching a chill in winter. How did it suddenly flare up in such hot weather? If my husband hadn't heard the news while corresponding with Imperial Physician Zhang, I wouldn't have known you were suffering.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, before the Empress Dowager could say anything, Yanshu was startled.","— The Marquess of Pingjin corresponds with Zhang Shengkang?","When did these two become connected?","The system immediately clarified for her, \"The Marquess of Pingjin is very concerned about health preservation, and Zhang Shengkang wants to establish connections with the powerful. They've been in contact for years, occasionally exchanging letters and greetings. It's a mutually beneficial relationship.\"","Yanshu silently scoffed. Birds of a feather indeed!","Moreover, that scumbag Marquess of Pingjin usually doesn't care about anything, leaving all household matters to his wife, yet he still keeps a mistress, despises his wife, and even abandoned his wife's child...","Such a creature is just a waste of food! What's the point of preserving his health!","She silently cursed the scumbag, then heard the Empress Dowager say to Madam Huo, \"It might be because the weather is too hot. I had them fan me and caught a chill from the wind. But it will be fine after a few days of recuperation. It's too much trouble for you two to come all this way, neglecting your affairs at home.\"","Madam Huo quickly said, \"We're not far away, it's only right for us to come and visit Your Majesty. Besides, my husband specifically asked me to come today.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu raised an eyebrow secretly.","— Last winter when the Empress Dowager fell ill, no one came to the palace specifically to visit. Now, right after the Empress Dowager's birthday celebration, the Marquess of Pingjin hears the news and specially sends his wife and daughter over. Could he be plotting something?","After all, although the capital isn't far from Tianjin, it still takes most of a day to travel.","The system said, \"That's right. The Marquess of Pingjin, following Zhang Shengkang's advice, plans to send his daughter into the imperial harem.\"","Yanshu raised an eyebrow. So it was indeed Zhang Shengkang causing trouble.","She knew that when the Emperor promoted Imperial Physician Jiang to fourth-rank Inner Court Physician the other day, it was clear he was just one step away from surpassing Zhang. Zhang Shengkang must be getting nervous.","Moreover, the Emperor's attitude that day was already very clear - he would never use Zhang again in the future. So of course Zhang had to quickly cultivate his own power base to rely on.","Hah, for a mere imperial physician to have such great influence!","Of course, the Marquess of Pingjin was also quite bold, daring to try to place his mistress's daughter in the palace.","The system sighed, \"If he doesn't say anything himself, who would even think of it? His own wife hasn't noticed.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","True, who could have imagined?","After consuming all this gossip for so long, she had long since discovered that these people had one outrageous idea after another, and they dared to both think and act on them, which was truly admirable.","However, Madam Huo had also brought her daughter today. Could it be that she also wanted to send her daughter into the palace?","But the system said, \"Madam Huo came this time only because of her husband's wishes. She actually plans to play dumb.\"","Just as these words fell, the Empress Dowager said to her cousin, \"It's getting late, and it wasn't easy for you two to come. Unfortunately, I'm still ill, so I'll have Consort Yi entertain you on my behalf later.\"","Suddenly being called upon, Yanshu could only hurriedly agree.","Madam Huo politely said, \"How dare I disturb the noble ladies? Being able to visit Your Majesty today is already more than satisfying. We'll take our leave while it's still early.\"","But the Empress Dowager said, \"You've come all this way, how can I let you leave without a meal? At least stay for dinner before you go.\"","Yet there was no intention of asking them to stay longer.","Seeing the Empress Dowager's tired expression, Yanshu had to quickly persuade Madam Huo, \"This is the Empress Dowager's high regard for you, Madam. Please don't stand on ceremony.\"","Only then did Madam Huo respond, leading her daughter to curtsy to the Empress Dowager before following Yanshu out of the hall.","The Palace of Benevolent Peace quieted down for a moment. Nanny Zhuang said to the Empress Dowager, \"It wasn't easy for Madam Huo to come, given her concern for Your Majesty.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"Indeed. Who knows why Zhang Shengkang had to be so talkative?\"","Nanny Zhuang didn't dare respond.","After a pause, she tentatively said, \"This servant noticed that Miss Huo has grown more beautiful and is very obedient. If she could come to the palace...\"","Before she could finish, the Empress Dowager cut her off, \"I'm too tired to worry about such things now. You needn't say more.\"","She closed her eyes with an impatient expression.","Hmph, from now on she wouldn't bother worrying about the Yuwen family's affairs!","Let them do as they please!","Nanny Zhuang was startled and finally dared not speak further.","With the Empress Dowager ill, the banquet to entertain Madam Huo couldn't be held in the Palace of Benevolent Peace. It wouldn't be appropriate to set it up in Ganlu Palace either, so Yanshu arranged for it to be held in the Cool Breeze Pavilion in the Imperial Garden.","The Cool Breeze Pavilion was built near the water, and it was the height of the flowering season, making for a beautiful scene.","Besides the various exotic flowers and trees, there were several white swans, rarely seen outside the palace, floating gracefully and contentedly on the nearby water.","This was the first time Yanshu was hosting guests on behalf of the Empress Dowager, so she restrained her appetite somewhat and did her best to smile and entertain the Huo mother and daughter.","\"Madam, please don't stand on ceremony. Feel free to eat whatever you like.\"","Madam Huo politely replied, \"We're truly sorry to trouble Your Highness today.\"","Yanshu smiled, \"Not at all.\"","Just as she finished speaking, the white swans in the water suddenly began to sing loudly.","Miss Huo's eyes immediately lit up, and she said to Madam Huo, \"Mother, Mother, look quickly! So this is how white swans sound. It really is like my cousin said - they sound just like big white geese!\"","What, big white geese?","The palace servants were all stunned.","Yanshu, however, could barely keep from laughing out loud.","— White swans are actually just white day-swans, and they do indeed sound a lot like geese.","This girl was certainly frank and straightforward.","Madam Huo looked embarrassed and said, \"We beg Your Highness's pardon.\"","She then turned to scold her daughter, \"How can you be so ill-mannered in front of Her Highness?\"","Yanshu quickly said politely, \"It's quite alright. It's refreshing to see Miss Huo's innocent romanticism. I actually think the same.\"","Huo Yingxia pouted, looking rather aggrieved, \"But it's true, and... they even look a lot like big geese...\"","Seeing that Madam Huo was about to scold her again, Yanshu laughed and said, \"I think so too. White swans just have longer necks, but at first glance, they do look quite like geese.\"","Huo Yingxia nodded vigorously and quickly said to Yanshu, \"That's exactly what my cousin said! At first, I didn't believe it! After all, white swans are rare birds, how could they be like geese? Now I see it's true.\"","Her eyes sparkled as she spoke, her tone suggesting she saw Yanshu as a kindred spirit.","Yanshu nodded in agreement and reminded her, \"Don't let the food get cold.\"","Huo Yingxia quickly nodded and resumed eating.","Yanshu quietly asked the system, [This girl seems to care a lot about her cousin. What's the story there?]","The system replied, [She's talking about General Dingyuan's son, who is Madam Huo's nephew. His name is Yu Hongyuan, and he's two years older than this fake young lady. They grew up together and are very close childhood friends.]","Yanshu raised an eyebrow. So this girl already had someone she liked?","However, the fact that she could mention her love interest so innocently showed that Madam Huo truly doted on her daughter like the apple of her eye.","It was a pity that her father planned to send her to the palace, completely disregarding her personality. Clearly, he didn't truly love her.","The system said, [Seeing the Marquis of Ping Jin's Mansion growing increasingly distant from the royal family, this scumbag Huo is certainly anxious. After Zhang Shengkang's persuasion, he's set his mind on this. Do you think someone who sends away his own daughter would have any fatherly love? It's all for his own glory and wealth.]","Yanshu strongly agreed.","Before long, the meal was finished.","Madam Huo stood up and said, \"We are extremely grateful for Consort Yi's personal hospitality. This humble servant will now bid farewell to the Empress Dowager and return to Jinmen.\"","Yanshu nodded, \"Madam is too kind.\"","In her heart, she wondered, these two hadn't even seen the Emperor, and they were already planning to go home?","It seemed Madam Huo was indeed just putting on an act for her husband, making this trip merely for show.","Just then, Miss Huo pouted and said, \"We only arrived this morning and we're leaving in the afternoon? Mother, at least let me stay one night at Uncle's house. It's so tiring to travel back and forth...\"","She tugged at her mother's sleeve, looking earnest.","Yanshu thought to herself, this girl probably isn't complaining about being tired, she just wants to see her cousin Hongyuan again.","Unable to resist her daughter's pleading, Madam Huo nodded and said, \"Alright, we'll impose on your uncle and aunt for one more night.\"","She added helplessly, \"I've really spoiled you too much. I'm afraid we're making Consort Yi laugh at us.\"","Yanshu could only smile and say, \"Your love for each other is truly touching.\"","Inwardly, she sighed.","— If one day Madam Huo learns the truth, how will she treat this daughter she's mistakenly doted on?","So, should she intervene in this matter or not?","After bidding farewell to Madam Huo and her daughter, and with the Empress Dowager retiring for her afternoon rest, Yanshu found time to return to Ganlu Palace.","However, she didn't have time to rest. She hurried to her desk and began writing a story.","— In any case, the Huo family's soap opera was too good to pass up. While the inspiration was still fresh, she had to write it down!","As for whether to publish it or not, she'd decide that later.","Yanshu didn't stop writing for the entire afternoon, continuing until dusk fell.","A message came from the Palace of Benevolent Peace, saying that the Empress Dowager would retire after dinner and that she needn't come over.","Yanshu breathed a sigh of relief. She stood up to stretch her muscles and began her evening meal.","— Ever since finding the Three Pure Pills, the Qianming Palace was no longer dangerous, and a certain workaholic Emperor felt more at ease to work overtime.","Moreover, with court affairs being particularly busy recently, for the past few days, he would only come over after Yanshu had fallen asleep.","Sometimes, if it was too late, he would just rest in Qianming Palace.","So when Yanshu finished her dinner and didn't see the Emperor, she assumed he wouldn't be coming tonight either, and went to take a bath.","The weather was hot, and Yinfeng had thoughtfully added a few drops of cooling essence to the bathtub, making it refreshingly comfortable.","Yanshu was closing her eyes and enjoying the water when she suddenly heard a ding in her ear —","[New gossip! General Dingyuan just had an accident.]","Yanshu was startled, [General Dingyuan? Isn't that the Marquess of Pingjin's Wife's younger brother? What happened to him?]","The system explained, [General Dingyuan was riding his horse home after working overtime at the military camp tonight. He was going fast when suddenly someone rushed out from the roadside. To avoid hitting them, the General accidentally fell off his horse and broke his leg.]","\"...\"","Yanshu was confused, [Isn't General Dingyuan a famous military general of this dynasty? How could he be so careless while riding a horse?]","The system quickly explained, [It's not his fault. On a familiar road, with few people around at night, it's natural to go faster. Suddenly having someone rush out from the roadside could be fatal, right? Besides, this was deliberately arranged by his brother-in-law, the Marquess of Pingjin.]","What?","Yanshu was startled again, [The Marquess of Pingjin deliberately arranged for someone to startle his brother-in-law's horse? What's his aim? How does his brother-in-law breaking his leg benefit him?]","The system said, [Care to guess?]","Yanshu, [...]","This annoying system always asked her to guess at crucial moments.","But for a deduction genius like her, guessing wasn't much of a challenge.","So she pondered —","With General Dingyuan suddenly breaking his leg, the General's mansion would surely be in chaos. If so, wouldn't Madam Huo, who had planned to return home tomorrow morning, be unable to leave?","In fact, she probably wouldn't be able to return home for quite some time.","— After all, with her younger brother injured, her sister-in-law would have to take care of her husband, look after the children, and manage the household. One person couldn't handle it all, so as the elder sister, she would inevitably have to help out.","The system, which had been called annoying, suddenly spoke again, [That's right. The Marquess of Pingjin is determined to send his daughter into the palace. He finally got the chance when the Empress Dowager was unwell and managed to lure his wife and daughter to the capital. But Madam Huo and her daughter didn't even get to see the Emperor before rushing to go home. Do you think he would easily give up?]","Yanshu nodded, [Indeed, and General Dingyuan is also the Empress Dowager's cousin. Now that he's suddenly injured, the Empress Dowager will surely be concerned. This will inevitably lead to someone being summoned to the palace to report on the situation. Since there are no idle people at General Dingyuan's mansion, it can only be Madam Huo who enters the palace to report. This way, doesn't it create another opportunity to see the Emperor?]","Damn it...","The Marquess of Pingjin is such a scumbag!","To come up with such a scheme!","Isn't he afraid that his brother-in-law might be seriously injured?","After all, falling from a horse could potentially be fatal!","The system replied, [Wouldn't that be even better for him? If so, the cousin his daughter has been pining for would have to observe a three-year mourning period, making their relationship even more hopeless. His wife would certainly stay in the capital longer. After all, he's a scumbag who doesn't even care about his own flesh and blood, so why would he care about his brother-in-law's life or death?]","This, this, this is too evil!!!","Yanshu was so angry that she quickly got out of the bathtub, hastily dried herself, changed into her nightgown, and walked towards the main hall.","No, she couldn't tolerate the Marquess of Pingjin's despicable behavior anymore!","-- She must quickly publish the story to expose him! Otherwise, keeping this scumbag around would harm who knows how many innocent people!!!","She walked briskly, filled with righteous indignation, but before she could reach her writing desk, a sudden announcement came from outside.","\"His Majesty the Emperor arrives...\"","Immediately after, the Emperor stepped into the hall.","Yanshu was startled but quickly went forward to bow, \"Greetings to Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan was wearing a light blue gauze robe tonight, giving him a somewhat lazy appearance. He casually took her hand to help her up, giving her a dangerously intense look up and down before smiling and saying in a low voice, \"Did you finish your bath early, knowing I'd come at this hour?\"","Without waiting for her reply, he directly picked her up by the waist and headed towards the bed.","The surrounding attendants blushed and retreated.","Yanshu, however, became anxious and hurriedly said, \"No, no, no, now is not the time, I still have matters to attend to...\"","But before she could finish speaking, they had already reached the bed.","He chuckled softly, \"What matter could be more urgent than this?\"","As he spoke, he leaned down.","-- Ahem, for the past few nights, she had always been asleep when he came. Especially last night, when he finished his work and realized it was already midnight, he was afraid of disturbing her rest, so he had to sleep in Qianming Palace by himself.","So... Heaven knows how eager he was at this moment?","Especially since she had even taken a bath in preparation...","Seeing that an urgent kiss was about to land without room for argument, Yanshu struggled to protest before losing her willpower, \"Your Majesty, please listen to what I have to say first...\"","But he mumbled, \"We'll talk later...\"","Yanshu had no choice. Just as she was about to lose the ability to speak, she made a great effort to shout, \"There's an extremely dramatic story about a baby swap, and it's related to Your Majesty!!!\"","Hmm?","The man finally paused and looked at her, \"What baby swap? And it's related to me?\"","Yanshu took a deep breath and said, \"The daughter of the Marquess of Pingjin is actually from his mistress. Madam Huo's real daughter has been given away by the Marquess to be raised by others. Madam Huo has been kept in the dark for over ten years. Now the Marquess plans to send this daughter born of his mistress into the palace. What's worse is that General Dingyuan's injury tonight was orchestrated by him!!!\"","Damn, she almost suffocated herself saying so much in one breath.","As she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan was finally stunned and frowned, \"What???\"","In this flood of information, he only caught the name Marquess of Pingjin.","This person seemed to have been busy doing many things?","Fortunately, Yanshu explained to him in detail once again.","\"It means that years ago, the Marquess of Pingjin's wife and his mistress gave birth to daughters at the same time. The heartless Marquess swapped the mistress's daughter with his legitimate daughter. The real legitimate daughter was given to a peasant family, but Madam Huo still doesn't know about this to this day.\"","\"Recently, with the Empress Dowager's illness, the Marquess of Pingjin, instigated by Zhang Shengkang, plans to use this opportunity to send this fake legitimate daughter into the imperial harem. However, neither Madam Huo nor Miss Huo have such intentions. They planned to return home after visiting the Empress Dowager today. To make his wife and daughter stay longer in the capital, the Marquess actually arranged for people to ambush General Dingyuan on his way home tonight, causing him to fall and break his leg.\"","\"Can you understand the Marquess of Pingjin's purpose in doing this?\"","Yuwen Lan certainly understood.","That Marquess of Pingjin, how dare he commit so many evil deeds!","And he even dared to set his sights on the imperial harem?","Moreover, he dared to harm a great general of the court in such a way?!!!","For the moment, he put aside the matter at hand and immediately got up to walk outside, calling for someone to come.","...","The next day, the Carefree Master's story \"Whose Fault Is It: The True and False Young Lady\" suddenly appeared.","When the Empress Dowager heard the news, she hurriedly had someone buy a copy and bring it into the palace.","The task of reading the story naturally fell to Yanshu again.","Of course, she was very satisfied with her new work and read it with particular vividness and emotion.","The Empress Dowager was deeply drawn into the twists and turns of the plot, frowning and looking shocked, her expressions quite rich.","After a while, when the dramatic story was finished, the Empress Dowager angrily said, \"Are there really such heartless people in this world? To not even care about their own flesh and blood?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded in agreement, \"That's right, that's right, the father in this story is too infuriating!\"","Then the Empress Dowager asked her, \"By the way, who is this story about?\"","Yanshu, \"...Uh...\"","She was about to say she didn't know either when suddenly, Fuhai rushed in from outside the hall and reported to the Empress Dowager, \"It's terrible, Your Highness! A young lady just arrived from General Dingyuan's mansion outside the palace, claiming to be Madam Huo's real daughter from the Marquess of Pingjin's household!\"","\"What?\"","The Empress Dowager was stunned.","In that instant, it seemed even her headache was forgotten."]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64","paragraphs":["Upon hearing Fu Hai's words, everyone in the Palace of Benevolent Peace was shocked.","The Empress Dowager was also stunned, thinking she had misheard. She quickly asked Fu Hai again, \"What did you say? What girl?\"","Fu Hai had to slow down his speech and explain, \"Your Highness, it's like this. Last night, General Dingyuan fell from his horse and was injured. The Emperor was very concerned and sent people to investigate. The investigation revealed that this incident was related to the Marquess of Pingjin.\"","What? The Marquess of Pingjin?","The Empress Dowager was stunned again and quickly asked, \"What does he have to do with this?\"","Fu Hai had to explain further, \"The Emperor sent the Imperial Guard to track down the person who collided with the General last night. According to this person's confession, it was the Marquess of Pingjin who arranged for him to attack the General.\"","The Empress Dowager was shocked again and frowned, \"Why would the Marquess of Pingjin want to attack General Dingyuan? Isn't he An Bang's brother-in-law?\"","Yanshu silently sympathized with the Empress Dowager. After all, the novel she had just written only told the story of the true and false noble ladies, and hadn't mentioned the other misdeeds of that scoundrel Huo Chengji, the Marquess of Pingjin. So now the Empress Dowager was in for quite a shock.","Fu Hai continued, \"Regarding why the Marquess of Pingjin sent someone to attack General Yu, the Emperor is still investigating. But the urgent matter now is that when the Imperial Guard went to find the Marquess of Pingjin, he wasn't at home, but at his mistress's place.\"","What?","The Empress Dowager was stunned again, \"Huo Chengji actually has a mistress?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Poor Empress Dowager, tsk.","Fu Hai had to nod and confirm, \"This was confessed by the Marquess of Pingjin's confidant. That woman is indeed the Marquess's mistress, and he has kept her for over a decade.\"","Perhaps due to experiencing too many surprises today, upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager finally couldn't contain her emotions and said, \"That scoundrel!\"","Yanshu hurriedly lowered her head along with the others, pretending not to have heard.","Seeing this, the Empress Dowager composed herself and asked Fu Hai, \"What does this have to do with the girl you mentioned earlier?\"","Fu Hai quickly explained, \"Because it's related to the General's injury, which is a serious matter, the Imperial Guard interrogated the Marquess of Pingjin, his mistress, and the other servants. Unexpectedly, the mistress's personal maid confessed that the current Miss Huo is not Madam Huo's biological daughter. Apparently, years ago, the Marquess of Pingjin switched his legitimate daughter with his mistress's daughter and sent his own daughter to a farming family surnamed Peng.\"","\"...\"","The Empress Dowager was too shocked to speak.","Fu Hai continued, \"Given the gravity of the situation, the Emperor immediately ordered people to follow the clues to find the Peng family. They discovered that the family had indeed adopted a baby girl over a decade ago, who seems to be Madam Huo's biological child.\"","\"???\"","The Empress Dowager's face was full of shock and confusion.","— So the story she had just heard in that novel was actually about her own cousin?","This, this, this... This was the closest it had ever come to her...","The Empress Dowager was stunned for a moment, then quickly asked, \"So what's the current situation?\"","Fu Hai hurriedly replied, \"The Imperial Guard has now brought this young lady to General Dingyuan's mansion to reunite with Madam Huo. However, General Dingyuan has just been injured, and the household is in chaos. The Emperor is worried about affecting General Yu's recovery and has sent me to ask for your instructions on how to handle this matter.\"","The Empress Dowager finally understood and nodded, \"Indeed, the Yu family already has an injured person, wouldn't this make things even more chaotic? Ask Madam Huo to come here instead. I'll see how to handle this matter.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","Wasn't the Empress Dowager just lying listlessly on her couch a moment ago?","Now she has the energy to meddle in affairs?","Fu Hai also looked worried and said, \"But Your Highness's health...\"","The Empress Dowager waved her hand and said, \"It's fine. Important matters come first. Ask Madam Huo to come over.\"","Fu Hai finally agreed repeatedly and went out to summon her.","Yanshu's eyes lit up —","Tsk tsk, it seems her recent service to the Empress Dowager hadn't been in vain. Following a big shot really does allow one to witness drama firsthand!","Not long after, Madam Huo arrived at the palace.","This time, the girl accompanying her was not the previously seductive false daughter, but another girl of similar age.","Madam Huo had obviously cried hard, her eyes swollen. She had completely lost her usual vigor and spirit. As soon as she saw the Empress Dowager, she knelt down with a face full of grievance and cried, \"Your Highness! Please do justice for your subject... How could he be so heartless...\"","As she spoke, she pulled the young girl who came with her close and cried again, \"My poor child...\"","The Empress Dowager also said angrily, \"Get up, don't cry now. I've only just heard about this matter. That Huo Chengji has really gone too far!\"","After speaking, she quickly looked at the girl Madam Huo had brought.","She saw that the girl had thick eyebrows, big eyes, and a round face, surprisingly similar to Madam Huo!","This, this, this... Was there any need to doubt anymore?","The Empress Dowager could only sigh and say, \"You have all suffered.\"","Hearing these words, Madam Huo burst into tears again, crying until her face was red and her heart was breaking.","The girl who came with her quickly reached out to support her in her arms, taking out a handkerchief to wipe her tears, comforting her, \"...Mother, don't cry anymore. Be careful of your health.\"","After these words, Madam Huo remembered the important matter at hand and quickly said to her biological daughter, \"Hui Ying, come and pay your respects to the Empress Dowager and Consort Yi.\"","As she spoke, she introduced her to the Empress Dowager and Yanshu, \"This is my flesh and blood, now called Hui Ying...\"","As she spoke, she couldn't help but let tears fall again.","The girl called Hui Ying quickly bowed to Yanshu and the Empress Dowager, \"This commoner pays respects to the Empress Dowager and Consort Yi.\"","Although she was a bit nervous, one could see she was obedient.","The Empress Dowager quickly asked someone to help her up, saying, \"Stand up, good child. You've suffered for so many years. How have you been all this time? Have your foster parents treated you well?\"","The true daughter Hui Ying quickly replied, \"My parents at home... my foster parents have been very kind to me. I haven't suffered much.\"","At this moment, everyone's eyes were on this young girl. Although her demeanor was slightly inferior to those of official families' noble ladies, her complexion was fair, and her hands were not rough, indicating that she indeed hadn't suffered too much.","However, she probably hadn't had time to dress up, as her clothes were rather plain.","Seeing this, Madam Huo felt even more distressed and wanted to hug her biological daughter and cry again.","But her daughter looked worried and said, \"It's just... this morning, someone suddenly came to our house looking for me, and that's when I found out about all this... Just now, those officials also took my Peng family parents away. I don't know what to do.\"","Yanshu hurriedly comforted her, \"They probably want to understand the situation from back then. That's why the Imperial Guard took your foster parents away. As long as they haven't done anything wrong, they won't be falsely accused. They'll probably be sent back soon. Don't worry.\"","Hui Ying nodded and said, \"That's good, thank you, Your Highness.\"","Although she was still a bit timid, one could see she was a filial child. She didn't cry or complain about her grievances, which made people feel reassured and deeply sympathetic at the same time.","To think, this was the child who should have been enjoying Madam Huo's love all along!","The Empress Dowager also sighed and lamented for a while, silently cursing the Marquess of Pingjin, Huo Chengji, as a scoundrel. She then quickly asked her cousin Madam Huo, \"By the way, how is An Bang's leg now? I heard that his injury is also related to that Huo Chengji?\"","Madam Huo wiped her tears and said with swollen eyes, \"Please forgive your subject, I don't know yet...\"","Sigh, ever since she learned the truth and met her biological child, she had only been concerned about the child, completely forgetting all other news.","The Empress Dowager could only nod.","Unexpectedly, at this moment, a voice suddenly announced from outside the hall, \"His Majesty the Emperor arrives...\"","Yuwen Lan stepped into the hall.","Everyone hurriedly bowed, and when Madam Huo saw his face, she couldn't help but burst into tears again.","Seeing this scene, Yuwen Lan said, \"Madam, don't worry. I will definitely investigate this matter thoroughly and give you justice.\"","Madam Huo cried and kowtowed to him, saying, \"Thank you, Your Majesty.\"","The Empress Dowager quickly asked, \"I just heard from Fu Hai that Huo Chengji plotted against General Dingyuan? What exactly happened?\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"I have already had the Marquess of Pingjin brought here. It's better to let him explain to you in person.\"","As he spoke, he beckoned towards the outside of the hall.","In a moment, guards were seen pushing a man into the hall. It was none other than the Marquess of Pingjin, Huo Chengji.","Madam Huo's eyes instantly filled with hatred. No longer caring about etiquette, she rushed in front of him, grabbed his collar, and shouted at him, \"You scoundrel! Why did you do this to me?!\"","As she spoke, large teardrops fell continuously, revealing the deep hurt in her heart.","Her beloved daughter Hui Ying quickly stepped forward to support her. Madam Huo grasped her daughter's hand and confronted Huo Chengji, \"Is this not your own flesh and blood? How could you treat her like this?! You heartless man!\"","Everyone in the hall glared at him angrily.","Suddenly, Huo Chengji fell to his knees and began kowtowing to Madam Huo, sobbing as he did so, \"My lady, I've wronged you terribly. I was foolish back then...\"","Before Madam Huo could respond, the Empress Dowager coldly snorted, \"Foolish? Even if you were foolish then, why didn't you come clean all these years afterwards?\"","Huo Chengji hastily replied, \"Empress Dowager, please forgive me. It's not that I didn't want to confess later, but the mistake had already been made. I feared my wife would be angry if she knew the truth, and since it was such a serious matter, I kept postponing it...\"","\"Nonsense!\"","The Empress Dowager had wanted to curse more vulgarly, but mindful of the Emperor's presence, she restrained herself and chose milder words. Still fuming, she continued, \"What could be more important than your own child being lost in the world? Have you forgotten how dangerous your wife's labor was? You've completely lost your conscience!\"","Growing angrier by the second, the Empress Dowager ordered, \"Fu Hai, slap his face!\"","Caught off guard by the sudden command, Steward Fu hesitated for a moment, glancing at the Emperor. Seeing no objection from His Majesty, he quickly obeyed, walking up to Huo Chengji, rolling up his sleeves, and delivering two hard slaps across the man's face.","The sharp sound of the slaps echoed through the hall. Yanshu could barely restrain herself from applauding Fu Hai. She felt a sense of satisfaction – this scoundrel deserved far more than just ten slaps!","Huo Chengji's face immediately swelled up, but he dared not complain. He could only cover his face and continue kowtowing, saying, \"I know my crimes, I know my crimes...\"","The Empress Dowager's anger had not subsided. She continued, \"What crimes do you know? Do you know how much time you've cost this mother and daughter? You even dared to cause General Dingyuan to fall from his horse? What were you thinking?!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the Emperor chimed in, \"If General Dingyuan hadn't been an excellent horseman, it would have been more than just a fall. This is tantamount to deliberately harming a high-ranking official. Are you in league with someone, intending to cause chaos in the empire?\"","Huo Chengji was startled. He hurriedly kowtowed again, crying, \"Please forgive me, Your Majesty. I was foolish. I only heard from Doctor Zhang that there had been incidents in the harem and few consorts remained. I thought to have my daughter enter the palace to serve Your Majesty... But when my wife visited the Empress Dowager yesterday, she was in a hurry to return... I could only come up with this plan to keep them in the capital for a few more days... I absolutely had no intention of causing turmoil in the empire, Your Majesty...\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager finally understood and exploded in rage, \"Knowing she was the daughter of your mistress, you still dared to covet a position in the imperial harem for her? This crime deserves a thousand cuts! It's not enough to quell the anger in people's hearts!\"","She then ordered Fu Hai, \"Give him two more hard slaps!\"","Fu Hai complied, stepping forward again and swinging his arm to deliver two more resounding slaps to the man's face.","It hurt his hand, but it felt satisfying.","Looking at Huo Chengji now, blood was trickling from the corner of his mouth.","However, no one in the hall felt any sympathy for him. The Empress Dowager was still seething with anger.","This scoundrel of a man had done something so despicable – making his lawful wife raise the child of his mistress. Even if it were a stranger's child, how could his wife face such a situation?!","Just then, the Emperor suddenly said, \"Oh, right. The Imperial Guard reported something earlier. I almost forgot about it.\"","Everyone in the hall immediately turned to look at Yuwen Lan. The Empress Dowager quickly asked, \"What is it?\"","Yuwen Lan coughed, glancing at Huo Chengji, and said, \"According to the confession of his mistress's servants, that child might not even be his.\"","What?","This statement left everyone in the hall stunned.","Huo Chengji was the first to react, hurriedly asking, \"What did Your Majesty say?\"","Yuwen Lan coldly repeated, \"The mistress's servants just confessed that over the years, she had liaisons with many other men behind your back. At that time, there was a merchant who was particularly close to her. She spent more time with that merchant than with you, so it's very likely that the child belongs to that merchant.\"","As these words fell, Huo Chengji's eyes widened in shock, as if struck by lightning.","Yanshu inwardly exclaimed, calling out to her system, [How could this be? System, was your information incorrect???]","The system leisurely replied, [I never said the child was the scoundrel's. I only said that when Madam Huo gave birth to a daughter, the mistress had just given birth to a girl as well.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, thinking back carefully, the system indeed never explicitly stated that this was Huo Chengji's flesh and blood...","She asked again, her face full of shock, [So you're saying that the fake young lady has no blood relation to the Huo family at all???]","System: [You could say that.]","Yanshu couldn't help but exclaim inwardly again, [Then this mistress was incredibly daring! How could she do such a thing?!]","System: [This mistress was actually quite clever. She knew to prepare for the future, aware that relying on her beauty wouldn't last forever. She also feared that if her affair was exposed one day, this scoundrel wouldn't want her anymore. So she came up with this plan for her daughter – no matter what, her daughter was already being raised by the legal wife. Even if this scoundrel found out one day that it wasn't his flesh and blood, he wouldn't dare to deny it. In any case, her own daughter would end up in a good position.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","What a mastermind!","It turned out that the biggest winner in this situation was that unnamed merchant, who unknowingly had his own flesh and blood raised as the cherished daughter of a marquis's family for over a decade.","So the mistress's true love must have been that merchant!","She looked at the scoundrel Huo before her, unable to help but feel amused.","— Indeed, those who betray others often end up betrayed themselves.","This man had worked so hard for so many years, and now faced such serious charges, all for something that had nothing to do with him!","Was he about to have a breakdown?","The others were thinking along the same lines, all looking at the thunderstruck Huo Chengji with mocking gazes.","Only the Emperor thought to himself —","\"Those who betray others often end up betrayed themselves?\"","How did Mencius's famous saying end up twisted like this???","However, what happened next was that Huo Chengji began banging his head on the ground, wailing, \"How could this be? How could this happen?! How could she do this to me?! Oh heavens!!!\"","This truly startled everyone. Yuwen Lan ordered the guards outside, \"Come in and drag him to the imperial prison. This man has deceived the Emperor and attempted to harm a high-ranking official. Order the Ministry of Punishment and the Ministry of Justice to investigate thoroughly and determine his punishment!\"","The guards immediately complied, entering the hall to drag Huo Chengji away.","The Empress Dowager then reminded, \"That woman can't be let off either! She single-handedly played the Marquess of Pingjin's family and even the whole world for fools! It's preposterous!\"","Yuwen Lan nodded in agreement, \"Throw her in the imperial prison as well. She shall be dealt with severely!\"","Upon hearing this, everyone in the hall expressed their approval, feeling a sense of justice being served.","Madam Huo, still in tears, bowed to the Emperor and Empress Dowager, \"Thank you, Your Majesty and Empress Dowager, for upholding justice for me.\"","The Empress Dowager and Yuwen Lan both nodded slightly. Then Madam Huo embraced her daughter Hui Ying, crying, \"I've wronged you most of all, my child!\"","Hui Ying was also in tears, wiping her mother's face as she said, \"Don't cry, Mother. You're not to blame for this. You've suffered too. Now that the truth is out, we can live well from now on.\"","Everyone watching this scene nodded inwardly. Although this daughter had been raised in a farming family for so many years, she seemed quite sensible.","It seemed that the farming couple who raised her were good people.","At this moment, the Empress Dowager asked, \"Then, what should be done about that child?\"","Everyone was taken aback – indeed, how should they deal with the false young lady of the Huo family?","They had thought she was still of Huo family blood, but now it turned out she had no blood relation to the Huo family at all?","Madam Huo paused, then cried again, \"Since learning the truth today, I've been so focused on embracing Hui Ying and crying that I momentarily forgot about Yingxia... She's also a child I raised with my own hands!\"","Everyone thought to themselves, \"Isn't that right? You can't say that young lady was wrong. After all, she still has the blood of that mistress flowing in her veins. If she stays by Madam Huo's side in the future, won't Madam Huo be reminded of that mistress every time she sees her?\"","But to say she was at fault would be wrong too. She was brought to Madam Huo's side just days after being born. What could a newborn infant who only knew how to nurse decide for herself?","What's even more pitiful is that now her birth mother is in prison, and her birth father's whereabouts are unknown...","Even if they wanted to send her away, where could they send her?","Moreover, Madam Huo raised her by hand, treating her as her own flesh and blood until yesterday. How could they bear to drive her out onto the streets?","Alas! When all is said and done, it's those scoundrels who deserve to die! Look at how many people they've hurt!","After lamenting for a while, everyone saw Madam Huo shaking her head and sobbing bitterly, showing just how much anguish she was in.","Seeing this, the Empress Dowager couldn't help but regret asking her this question. She was also a victim, and that was a child she had raised with love. Wasn't it cruel to ask her this now?","Just as she was about to speak to ease the tension, Hui Ying suddenly said to her mother, \"I'm young and don't understand many big principles. But I know that my adoptive parents in the Peng family have loved me dearly these years. If they suddenly couldn't find me, they would surely be worried sick. Isn't it the same for you, Mother? After all, she's the child you've raised for so many years. If you lost her, wouldn't you be very upset too?\"","As she spoke, she wiped the tears from her mother's face and said tearfully, \"I'll do whatever you say, Mother.\"","As her words fell, Madam Huo was speechless and could only hug her and cry again.","This child had suffered so much; the more sensible she was, the more it broke people's hearts.","The Empress Dowager felt comforted and nodded approvingly, \"Good child, she deserves a reward! Those adoptive parents should be rewarded even more!\"","She then looked at the Emperor and said, \"Such a pure-hearted person should be praised and made known to the world. I intend to bestow upon this child the title of Rural Lady, to comfort her for the hardships she has endured over the years.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Mother is merciful.\"","Hearing this, everyone congratulated the mother and daughter, \"Congratulations to Madam Huo, congratulations to Rural Lady Huiying.\"","Madam Huo quickly led her daughter to bow to the mother and son, \"Thank you for your great kindness, Empress Dowager and Emperor!\"","The Empress Dowager continued, \"As for the Peng couple, who treated their adopted daughter as their own and taught her to be so reasonable, I will reward them with a hundred taels of gold and make it known to the world as a commendation.\"","Hui Ying also hurried to thank them on behalf of her adoptive parents, a smile appearing in her eyes.","Everyone felt greatly comforted, but then they saw the Empress Dowager's expression turn cold as she said, \"Huo Chengji is unworthy of his position and should be stripped of his title, to be inherited by his eldest son. As for his misdeeds, they must not be dealt with lightly, but punished severely, to serve as a warning to others.\"","Yuwen Lan agreed, but didn't forget to remind her, \"Zhang Shengkang, as an imperial physician, abused Mother's trust by encouraging others to covet the imperial harem. He cannot go unpunished either.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed and nodded, \"Indeed. Why don't we demote him by one rank and dock his salary for a year, to make him reflect on his actions?\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"That might be too lenient. Let's double it - demote Zhang Shengkang by two ranks and dock his salary for two years. If he offends again in the future, we will not be so forgiving.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said nothing more.","Yanshu quietly raised an eyebrow.","— It seems the Empress Dowager still intends to have Zhang Shengkang treat her illness, but there's definitely a rift now. After all, being demoted by two ranks is quite harsh.","As a result, Doctor Jiang is now above him in rank.","Just as she was thinking this, she saw the Empress Dowager turn to Madam Huo and say, \"As for that child, I think we should either find her birth father and send her back to him, or if we really can't find him, she's about the right age for marriage anyway. We should find a family for her to marry into. Keeping her around will only be a thorn in your heart.\"","[Tsk, to be honest, this girl having no blood relation to the Huo family is more comfortable than if she did. Hmph, that scoundrel deserves to be cuckolded!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, these two women often think alike.","Hearing this, Madam Huo quickly agreed.","The others listened, their hearts conflicted.","— Now that the truth is out, that girl has no connection to the Huo family, and she's become a \"bastard\" without a father. Even if she marries, what good family would take her?","Alas, when all is said and done, it's still that man who is truly despicable!!!","With that, the matter was temporarily settled, and Madam Huo left the palace with her own daughter.","After this incident, the Empress Dowager had completely shed her previous sickly appearance and become energetic. She instead asked the Emperor, \"How does Your Majesty always know about these hidden matters?\"","— Although the pretext was investigating the case due to General Dingyuan's injury, the story book came out early this morning. Even if it was written on the spot, it couldn't have been that fast!","So the Empress Dowager was convinced that the Emperor must have investigated in advance and had someone write the story book to deal with Marquess of Pingjin Huo Chengji.","This boy, how did he become so capable?","Yuwen Lan silently listened, momentarily at a loss for words.","But then Yanshu quickly spoke up for him, \"Perhaps His Majesty noticed that the Huo girl didn't resemble Madam Huo. Nor did she resemble her father, so he became suspicious?\"","Yuwen Lan was about to nod, but then quickly shook his head, frowning as he said, \"When did I ever pay attention to that girl's appearance? I just vaguely heard some rumors from Tianjin and had someone investigate.\"","He then glanced at Yanshu, thinking to himself — I almost fell into her trap."]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65","paragraphs":["Hearing the Emperor speak thus, the Empress Dowager finally nodded and said, \"So that's how it is. Your Majesty is wise, and the Imperial Guard is becoming more and more capable.\"","Yanshu hurriedly nodded beside her, \"Your Highness speaks the truth.\"","After speaking, she quickly lowered her head, concealing her contributions and fame.","Yuwen Lan glanced at her, thinking to himself that it wasn't the Imperial Guard becoming more capable, but her.","However, on the surface, he could only say to the Empress Dowager, \"Mother, you flatter me.\"","He coughed a couple of times, then asked, \"How is Mother's health?\"","—Tsk, ever since the goat's milk incident, he had been feeling uneasy, and the Empress Dowager had been carrying a grudge.","As a result, the relationship between mother and son had become somewhat... estranged.","These past few days, the Empress Dowager had been suffering from an old ailment. He had originally come to visit once, but the Empress Dowager, feeling unwell and displeased, had quickly sent him away.","In the following days, fearing another unpleasant encounter if he came, he hadn't dared to visit again.","Now, after five or six days, mother and son were finally face to face.","Hearing him speak thus, the Empress Dowager paused for a moment before responding with a hum, \"Thanks to Your Majesty's blessing, I am feeling much better today.\"","As these words fell, Yanshu silently marveled to herself - gossip truly is the cure for all ills! She had noticed it from the moment the Empress Dowager had ordered Fu Hai to beat that scumbag Marquess of Pingjin.","In that instant, the Empress Dowager's hatred for evil was so fierce, she seemed more spirited than a young person!","Of course, it was also possible that the Empress Dowager's recent illness was actually due to pent-up frustration, and having vented her anger today, she naturally felt better.","Yuwen Lan was thinking along the same lines.","However, before he could say anything, he heard the Empress Dowager silently snort in her heart, [The little brat, he actually remembers to care about me! Well, at least he's slightly better than those heartless men.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Had he fallen so low in the Empress Dowager's heart that he needed those scumbags as a foil to appear good?","This was truly a bit frightening. He could only say, \"I've been busy these past few days and neglected to inquire after Mother's health. I deeply regret it and hope Mother can forgive me.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Your Majesty's words are too heavy. The welfare of the state and its people should be the top priority. Besides, I have Consort Yi here to keep me company. She has been working hard these past two days.\"","In her heart, she thought, [Come to think of it, women are indeed more attentive. That's why people say daughters are like cotton-padded jackets, unlike sons who only know how to anger people. Alas, I don't have that fortune.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Suddenly finding herself mentioned, Yanshu hurriedly said, \"Your Highness's words are too kind. This is all what your servant should do.\"","After this wave of events, twilight had fallen outside.","The Empress Dowager then said, \"I'm feeling much better today. You don't need to work so hard. Go back and rest early.\"","As she spoke, she glanced at the Emperor, thinking to herself, [Didn't he say he's already better? Surely he can't still be unable to produce an heir?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","How could that be possible!","Doctor Jiang had said he was fine now!","He thus said, \"Then we won't disturb Mother's rest. I and Consort Yi will take our leave.\"","With that, he led Yanshu out of the hall.","Hmph, time to go back and make a baby!","Needless to say, after the publication of \"The True and False Princess,\" another wave of excitement swept through the city.","Readers once again began to speculate about the identities of the characters in the story.","Fortunately, after a few days, an official announcement from the court satisfied everyone's curiosity. Only then did people realize that the story was actually about the affairs of the Marquess of Pingjin's household.","—The Marquess of Pingjin, disregarding marital affection and violating ethical principles, maliciously replaced his legitimate daughter with his mistress's daughter, abandoning his true daughter in the countryside. This behavior was deemed inhumane and a crime of deceiving the Emperor.","Moreover, he had also plotted to harm a great general of the court, harboring malicious intent. Therefore, for these two crimes combined, his title was revoked, he was sentenced to fifty lashes, and exiled to the border, never to return to the capital.","His title would be inherited by his eldest son.","His mistress, Lady Qiao, for harboring evil intentions, abusing the legitimate daughter, and passing off another man's child as the heir of the Marquess's household, was equally unforgivable. She was sentenced to thirty lashes and exiled to the border.","The legitimate daughter of the Marquess of Pingjin's household who had been living outside, Huo Huiying, was praised by the Empress Dowager for her kind heart and was specially granted the title of Rural Lord of Guangde, along with a reward of a hundred mu of land.","Her adoptive parents also received commendation from the court.","In addition, Madam Huo personally visited the Peng family one day with her son and daughter, presenting them with a generous amount of silver to thank them for raising Huiying.","However, the Peng couple did not wish to profit from their adopted daughter's name and firmly declined the offer.","Moved by their integrity, Madam Huo could only arrange for a separate residence near her own home to be given to her benefactors. She also became sworn siblings with them, allowing her daughter to maintain a relationship with her adoptive parents and visit both families when she had time.","As for the false princess who had been the Huo family's legitimate daughter for over a decade, Huo Yingxia...","She left the Marquess's mansion overnight.","And it wasn't that she was driven out, but that she left without saying goodbye.","Upon hearing the news, Yanshu was also surprised and hurriedly asked the system, \"What's going on? Where did the false princess go?\"","The system replied, [Think about it. Now that the truth is out and Madam Huo's real daughter has returned, how could this girl stay in the mansion knowing what her birth mother had done? She cried for several days at first, but after she finished crying, she came to understand. She left a letter saying she felt guilty for betraying her adoptive mother's kindness and for wronging the real Huo daughter. So she decided to leave and make her own way in life. She said she would return to repay her adoptive mother's kindness after she made her fortune.]","Yanshu: [...That's a good thought, but with her personality, can she actually succeed out there?]","The system sighed, [People need to grow. How will she know if she can do it if she doesn't try?]","Yanshu nodded and asked, [What about Madam Huo? She seemed reluctant to part with this adopted daughter that day. Wasn't she worried when the girl suddenly left?]","The system: [Of course she was worried at first. After all, she raised that child and knew she wasn't very streetwise. She was concerned the girl might be tricked. But her sister-in-law talked her around—although her real daughter Huiying is kind-hearted, she can't always be expected to give way. Besides, people outside are already gossiping about Huo Yingxia. Rather than staying in the Huo family bearing the stigma of being a bastard, it might be better for her to leave and start anew under a different name.]","Yanshu nodded, [The general's wife is a sensible person!]","The system: [Indeed. After hearing this, Madam Huo had a sudden realization. She only sent someone to quietly check on the girl, and seeing that she was fine, she set her mind at ease.]","Yanshu was still curious, [But how will Huo Yingxia, a young lady who's been pampered for over a decade, find a new way of life?]","The system: [This young lady may have been raised in luxury, but she's not without skills. She's quite knowledgeable about clothing, makeup, and perfumes. After leaving the Marquess's mansion, she found an apprenticeship at a cosmetics shop in Jiangnan. She plans to save some money and open her own shop, becoming her own boss.]","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, [Jiangnan? That's so far from the capital.]","The system: [If she stayed too close, there might be more entanglements. Besides, her beloved cousin is still in the capital. Now that marriage is impossible, it's better to be far away. Out of sight, out of mind, and her heart can be at peace.]","Yanshu nodded, [That's true. It seems this young lady has thought things through. But come to think of it, could she have some business genes? After all, her birth father is a merchant.]","The system: [Maybe. How can you know your potential if you're not tested? But if she had resigned herself to her fate, we could already see her ending.]","Yanshu sighed, [That's right. If she had stayed in the Marquess's mansion, she would have been looked down upon because of her background. She wouldn't have been able to marry well, and her husband's family might have mistreated her... So rather than that, it's better for her to go out and strive for herself.]","After all, it's better to rely on oneself than on others.","A few more days passed, and Madam Huo brought her daughter Huo Huiying to the palace again to pay respects to the Empress Dowager.","Accompanying them was her sister-in-law, the wife of General Dingyu, Lady Pang.","Yanshu had the honor of accompanying the Empress Dowager to receive the three of them.","After some time, Madam Huo's complexion had improved considerably, and Miss Huiying appeared much more cheerful than when they first met her some days ago. Especially after being properly dressed and made up, she looked no different from other noble ladies.","It seemed that her life had improved since returning to her mother's side.","Perhaps due to reading too many palace intrigue novels in her previous life, Yanshu had initially worried that Huiying might lose herself in the whirlpool of struggles in a large household, but it seemed that this was not the case.","The system said, \"You're overthinking it. She has five brothers in the Marquess's mansion, all born from the same mother. There are no cousins or half-sisters to compete with. Even her cousins in the capital all treat her like treasured brothers. Last time when she was supposed to return to Pingjin to reunite with her family, four of her brothers personally came to the capital to escort her. Only her eldest brother couldn't make it because he was too busy. Especially given this young lady's calm temperament, she's even more beloved by her sisters-in-law compared to the previous one.\"","Yanshu finally felt relieved and sighed, \"It seems everyone in the Marquess of Pingjin's household is good, except for that Huo Scumbag from before! Of course, given Madam Huo's generous and kind nature, how could the children she raised be bad? I suppose this is her reward after all her suffering.\"","The Empress Dowager had also been concerned about her distant niece these days. As soon as they met, she asked, \"How have you been doing by your mother's side these days?\"","Huo Huiying smiled and replied, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty. My mother has been treating me wonderfully, and my uncles, aunts, and brothers have been especially caring towards me. I've been doing very well these days.\"","Her manner of speaking had become much more poised than before.","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"What's unfortunate has already happened. It's good that everything is in the past now. You two should spend a few good years together as mother and daughter to make up for the time you've lost.\"","Madam Huo smiled and said, \"That's exactly what I was thinking. I'm just worried it might delay her marriage.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Huo Huiying blushed and hurriedly said, \"Daughter only wishes to stay by mother's side and keep you company.\"","The Empress Dowager also laughed and said, \"How could a good girl like you worry about not getting married?\"","Lady Pang from the General's mansion also smiled and said, \"Your Majesty, don't listen to my sister being modest. Huiying now has the title of Rural Lord. These days, suitors have been lining up at our door.\"","Hearing this, Madam Huo hurriedly thanked the Empress Dowager again, \"This is all thanks to Your Majesty's grace.\"","However, the Empress Dowager's expression turned more serious as she said, \"When I bestowed that title, it wasn't to benefit those young men. It was purely out of admiration for Huiying's pure and kind nature. Having gone through your own marriage, you must be very careful in choosing a husband for Huiying. Don't just look at a man's surface appearance. Power and wealth are merely fleeting clouds. What's most important is a solid character.\"","Hearing these words, Yanshu nodded silently in agreement.","In fact, when the Empress Dowager had bestowed the title of Rural Lord on this true eldest daughter, Yanshu had already noticed that the Empress Dowager wasn't just trying to comfort this young lady on the surface. By giving her a title, she was helping her stand taller and not feel inferior due to her upbringing in a farmer's household. Moreover, it was meant to silence those gossipy individuals.","Look down on her for being raised by farmers?","Sorry, but she's a Rural Lord with her own land. Even if she never marries, she's already better off than many pampered birds relying on men.","So when it comes to choosing a husband, there's no need to rush. Those men flocking to her might not genuinely like her.","Madam Huo understood the Empress Dowager's meaning and quickly bowed her head in agreement, \"Your Majesty speaks wisely.\"","Changing the subject, the Empress Dowager then asked Lady Pang, \"How is Anbang's leg now?\"","Lady Pang quickly replied, \"In response to Your Majesty, the General is much better now. He should be able to get out of bed and walk in about a month.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly, but then saw Madam Huo say to her sister-in-law, \"It's all my fault for misjudging people. I've caused trouble for you all.\"","Lady Pang quickly smiled and said, \"That matter has been over for so long now. The main culprit has already been exiled to the border. Sister, why do you still blame yourself?\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, thinking to herself that this Lady Pang seemed to be a straightforward person.","The system said, \"Indeed she is. Lady Pang's parents didn't have any sons, just her and her younger sister. Although she was the eldest daughter, her personality was more like an eldest son. Because of her beauty, she had countless suitors in her youth, including princes and nobles. She originally came from a scholarly family, but she chose to marry into this military family because she saw that General Anbang was honest and straightforward. Despite one being scholarly and the other military, the couple lived quite harmoniously.\"","Yanshu understood and thought to herself that compared to the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion, the Empress Dowager's relatives seemed to be quite decent.","Just then, she saw the Empress Dowager instructing the two sisters-in-law, \"The Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion is what it is now. I can only hope that you all will raise your children and grandchildren well to contribute to the court.\"","The two sisters-in-law quickly agreed.","With the matters of the Marquess of Pingjin's household temporarily settled, the capital had entered the sixth month.","Although the weather was getting increasingly hot, an important day that Yanshu had been waiting for was also approaching.","— That was the reopening of Songhe Academy, and the famous teachers and great scholars invited by the Emperor from various places were about to arrive in the capital.","Ahem, this meant that the mysterious former Chancellor of the Zhongji Court would finally make his appearance."]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66","paragraphs":["For several days in a row, Yanshu had been full of anticipation.","This feeling was like the excitement of a fan about to meet their long-admired idol.","My goodness, he was the man who once moved the Empress Dowager's heart!","Especially after learning that Chancellor Qi had already departed from Langya, and the journey from Langya to the capital only took five or six days, she could almost be said to be counting down the days.","However... although the Empress Dowager's headaches had improved, she still frequently called Yanshu to talk and still liked to have her read storybooks.","Of course, she was still reading ones she had written herself...","Regarding this, the Empress Dowager explained to her, \"My eyes have become a bit blurry, and these storybooks have such dense text. It's truly troublesome to read them, so it's better to hear you read them.\"","Yanshu could only smile and say, \"Your Majesty is too kind. It's my honor to be able to entertain you. But... do you only read the Carefree Young Master's stories? Don't you read others? There are many other authors in the market as well.\"","The Empress Dowager replied, \"Those people's writing is either too rigid or too unfair. Often it's two or three women fighting over one man, or a man having his way with multiple partners, marrying fairy-like concubines outside while having a virtuous wife serving him at home. Some even have stories of husbands disliking their wives' appearance and changing their heads! Why can't it be the man changing his body to please his wife? It always leaves one feeling unsatisfied. Only this Carefree Young Master can be said to write about poetic justice, repaying grudges and settling scores, making people feel good when they hear it.\"","Rarely hearing face-to-face feedback from a reader, Yanshu was deeply moved. So she had to work hard to suppress her embarrassment and earnestly read her own stories to the Empress Dowager.","I must say, as she read on, she got used to it and could even discover areas for improvement in her writing style and grammar, which was quite beneficial.","However, every time she finished a story, the Empress Dowager couldn't help but complain, \"Why hasn't this person written anything new lately? I heard that before, there used to be a new story every few days, but now ten days or half a month pass without seeing one?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, \"I spend all day reviewing old works with you, where would I find time to ponder new ones?\"","But outwardly, she could only say, \"Perhaps recently everything has been peaceful, and the Imperial Guard hasn't discovered any new cases, so the writer doesn't have any new material.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"That's true. In that case, having no new stories could be considered good news. But without new stories to read, it always feels like something is missing. With such good writing skills, why not write some supernatural fiction?\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, \"Your Majesty has a point.\"","—It seemed that nowadays there were quite a few people keeping mistresses, abandoning their wives, or being ungrateful, and after reading her stories, some always felt they were being alluded to. So there was vague criticism of her stories. Just imagine, if she wrote about fox spirits and ghosts, surely no one would complain, right?","Hmm, this was an idea worth considering and developing.","However... the main reason she couldn't write new stories at the moment was that her mind was full of curiosity about Chancellor Qi, to the extent that she couldn't focus for the time being.","Oh, that's right, it was already the seventh day. Shouldn't Chancellor Qi have arrived in the capital by now?","Thinking this, she secretly glanced at the Empress Dowager, wondering how the Empress Dowager still had the leisure to listen to her old stories. Could it be that she didn't know about this matter yet?","System, [That's right. After the incident with the sheep's milk pastry, and then suffering from her old ailment for several days, the Empress Dowager doesn't inquire about court affairs now. At most, she's thinking about when you might bear a child for the Emperor, so of course she doesn't know about this.]","Yanshu, \"...\"","Why bring up the matter of her bearing children...","What for? Is that something she can decide on her own?","But it's good that the Empress Dowager doesn't know now. If one day she unexpectedly meets him, wouldn't it be an even better surprise?","Just as she was thinking this, she saw palace maids bringing in tea and snacks.","The Empress Dowager said, \"This is ejiao cake, jujube paste pastry, and wolfberry and longan tea. They're all good for nourishing blood, warming the womb. You should try some too.\"","Hmm, that ejiao cake was studded with black sesame seeds and walnut pieces. It looked crispy and fragrant. The jujube paste pastry had layers of flaky crust on the outside. Even before eating, a rich sweet aroma invaded her nostrils. The red date tea was also bright and clear, with a sweet jujube fragrance, very tempting.","Yanshu had been reading stories for half the day and was quite thirsty, so she began to taste the treats.","—Ahem, anyway, she wasn't allergic to cow's milk or sheep's milk, and the Empress Dowager didn't intend to harm her, so she dared to eat.","Seeing her eat so earnestly, the Empress Dowager felt pleased, but couldn't help sighing, \"The Emperor used to love eating the snacks from my palace too...\"","Only now he doesn't dare to eat them anymore...","Alas, if only I had known better, why did I resort to that trick?","But she heard Yanshu comfort her, \"The Emperor must be too busy lately. I'm sure after some time, he'll have time to come and keep you company.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly, but suddenly looked at her and said, \"He would probably love to eat what you make.\"","Yanshu's face reddened, and she hurriedly said, \"...This humble consort is clumsy and doesn't know how to make desserts.\"","That's right, she was a bit lazy and had always liked eating but not cooking since she was young. Otherwise, she wouldn't have made such an unsightly mess when she tried to make soup for the Emperor last time.","But the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"If you don't know how to make them, you can learn. We have time today, let them teach you.\"","Saying this, she immediately called over the cook who made desserts, \"Teach the Imperial Consort Yanshu how to make desserts. It doesn't need to be too difficult, just a few of the Emperor's favorites will do.\"","The cook immediately agreed and came before Yanshu, \"Please follow this servant to the dessert kitchen, Your Highness.\"","Yanshu, \"...\"","How come not only was she reading books, but now she had to learn to make desserts too???","...Was coming to the Palace of Benevolent Peace like attending a vocational school?","But since the Empress Dowager had spoken, she couldn't refuse. She could only say \"alright\" and followed along.","Behind her, the Empress Dowager nodded with a smile, thinking that this little Yanshu was quite interesting. Chatting with her was relaxing and didn't require much mental effort.","Meanwhile, Yanshu busied herself in the dessert kitchen with the cook for half the day, learning everything from making flaky pastry dough and fillings to kneading, wrapping, and baking to shape. After two hours, when the golden, fragrant chestnut pastries came out of the oven, they actually tasted quite good when eaten, giving her a sense of accomplishment.","Even the Empress Dowager graciously tasted a piece and praised her as a quick learner.","After all this busy work, it was already noon and time for lunch.","The Empress Dowager, feeling sorry for Yanshu who was sweating profusely in the dessert kitchen, asked her to stay for lunch.","Just as the palace servants were serving the dishes, they saw the supervisor of the Imperial Kitchen hurriedly approaching with people carrying several ice bowls. He reported with a smile, \"Your Majesty, the Emperor is hosting a banquet in the Wenhua Hall today. He found these honeydew melon ice bowls quite delicious and specially ordered the kitchen to make a few more to send to you and Imperial Consort Yanshu.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu's eyes lit up — having ice bowls to eat when she was all sweaty, the Emperor was truly thoughtful.","The Empress Dowager, however, asked, \"What kind of banquet is being held in the Wenhua Hall today?\"","The Imperial Kitchen supervisor Wu Chun smiled and said, \"In a few days, the Songhe Academy will reopen. The Ministry of Rites has invited famous teachers and great scholars from all over the country, and they have gathered in the palace today. This is a banquet for distinguished scholars hosted by the Emperor.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu secretly glanced at the Empress Dowager while eating her ice bowl, but saw that the Empress Dowager only nodded slightly, seemingly still not realizing the implications. She asked, \"I didn't know about this event. Who all has come today?\"","Supervisor Wu smiled and said, \"Please forgive this servant's ignorance. There are over thirty participants in today's banquet, and I don't... recognize all of them. However, the most famous ones, such as Master Ji from Jinling City, Master Qi from Langya, Master Gu from Lanling, and Master Yu from Nanyang are all present.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, they saw a slight pause in the Empress Dowager's eyes.","Langya... Master Qi?","Back then... wasn't that person the one who returned to Langya?","On the surface, she only nodded slightly and said, \"I haven't paid attention to the literary world for so many years, I haven't heard of these names.\"","Yanshu quickly said, \"I've heard they are all scholars with profound knowledge and quite renowned. The Emperor invited them to revitalize the Songhe Academy, and even intends to appoint one of them as the headmaster to oversee the academy in the future.\"","Tsk tsk, she could only say this much, otherwise it would arouse suspicion.","As she spoke, she quickly called out to the system, [Do you think the Empress Dowager has guessed?]","System, [Pretty much. The surname Qi is rare to begin with, and he's also from Langya. Besides, the Empress Dowager knows that after Qi Shuguang returned to Langya back then, he became a teacher.]","Hearing this, Yanshu nodded silently — give the Empress Dowager a little time, and she would definitely figure it out.","Wu Chun delivered the ice bowl and hurried back to attend the banquet, leaving Yanshu to accompany the Empress Dowager for lunch. After finishing, she took her leave and returned to her own Ganlu Palace.","As if obsessed with shipping a couple, she couldn't help but wonder if those two could meet.","After all, Chancellor Qi was an old official of the Empress Dowager's. Having been separated for over a decade, if he wanted to pay respects to the Empress Dowager on this rare visit to the palace, it would be understandable.","Though she knew the gulf between these two was hard to bridge, and the chances of a perfect ending like Madam Mu's were slim, surely they could at least meet once?","Thinking this, she began to wait for news from the system.","However, after waiting for half a day until dusk fell and even after finishing dinner, there was no word of the two meeting.","The system advised her, [Stop waiting and go to bed. That Chancellor Qi left the palace right after the lunch banquet today.]","Yanshu felt a bit disappointed, [Does he no longer have feelings for the Empress Dowager?]","The system replied, [This man has always been very cautious. Even when feelings first arose years ago, he suppressed them greatly. Whenever he saw the Empress Dowager, besides reporting on matters, he rarely said much else. It wasn't until later that he showed some verbal concern, mostly taking practical actions to protect the Empress Dowager. You could say his emotions were restrained by propriety. Now so many years have passed, and he doesn't know the Empress Dowager's feelings. More importantly, he's afraid of arousing the Emperor's suspicion and affecting the mother-son relationship, so of course he won't rush to meet her.]","Yanshu couldn't help but click her tongue. These two really should have met before marriage! What a pity!","But honestly, the more suppressed the feelings, the more irresistible they become. If this were written as a novel, it would be so poignant and touching!","Just as she was thinking this, she heard from outside, \"His Majesty arrives...\"","Yuwen Lan stepped into the hall, just in time to hear that sentence - [The more suppressed the feelings, the more irresistible they become.]","He was curious. What suppressed feelings? Could there be some new gossip?","Ahem, that's right, by now he had gotten used to calling it \"gossip\".","It had to be said, it was quite interesting.","He saw Yanshu come forward to curtsy, and he pulled her into his arms, asking, \"Have you written a new story today? What kind of tale is it?\"","But she replied, \"Your humble servant hasn't had time to write these past few days.\"","In her heart though, she thought, [I'd love to write about the story of the Empress Dowager and Chancellor Qi, but would you allow it?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He really didn't want to allow it.","This involved the face of the royal family, and more importantly, the dignity of the late emperor. How could he easily accept it in his heart?","So when he saw Qi Shuguang today, he still felt somewhat... strange.","He had even thought that if Qi Shuguang proposed to visit the Empress Dowager today, he would definitely refuse and think less of him for it.","Fortunately, from beginning to end, Qi Shuguang didn't have this idea at all. Apart from reminiscing about revisiting old places and marveling at how he had grown up, expressing contentment at his governance of the country, there were no stray thoughts in his mind.","Regarding the Empress Dowager, there was only one comment. The gist was that she must have worked hard to raise him, an unrelated prince, so well.","...In fact, Yuwen Lan also understood the Empress Dowager's hard work.","...Especially after experiencing so many recent incidents in other families, he understood that everyone has selfish motives, and jealousy in particular is terrifying.","As the late emperor's principal wife, while he was the child born to the late emperor and another woman. To treat him so well truly counted as benevolent and loving.","So when he ate the delicious ice bowl today, he specially had some sent to the Empress Dowager.","Of course, it was also because that little glutton Yanshu was there, so it killed two birds with one stone.","But no matter what, between the Empress Dowager and Qi Shuguang... he still didn't want to accept it.","So to prevent her from overthinking, he quickly changed the subject, saying, \"We intend to select a few of the renowned scholars who have come to the capital this time to oversee Songhe Academy, so they will stay in the capital longer. I hear many have brought their families. We plan to host their families in the palace to show sincerity. What do you think about supporting this?\"","Hearing this, Yanshu was stunned.","Goodness, though she may seem busy writing stories, she was actually very socially anxious! Hosting a palace banquet, entertaining so many strangers, having to greet and chat with them, especially when they weren't even close to her age...","She shuddered and hurriedly said, \"Your humble servant is lacking in talent and learning, and my status in the palace is not high. If I rashly host a palace banquet, I'm afraid it would invite gossip. Why not ask the Empress Dowager to take charge? If the Empress Dowager hosts, wouldn't it better show the court's esteem?\"","Yuwen Lan considered this and nodded, \"That's fine. We might as well invite the families of the Grand Tutor, Imperial Academy, and several scholars together. It would be more appropriate.\"","Yanshu nodded quickly, \"Your Majesty's words are most wise.\"","Great, great! The more people, the livelier it gets, and the livelier it is, the more gossip there is!!!","She loved eating at banquets while consuming gossip the most!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Always thinking about gossip.","However, seeing her cheeks flush and eyes brighten with excitement, he couldn't help but feel a stirring in his heart. He quickly wrapped his arms around her waist and brought her to the couch.","But before he could kiss her, he saw her suddenly put on a serious face and say, \"No, Your Majesty drank alcohol today. I heard that drinking is bad for the child.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"??? Where did you hear that?\"","Could she be deceiving him?","Yanshu said earnestly, \"Your humble servant heard Imperial Physician Jiang say so last time. Excessive drinking and indulgence in pleasure both affect one's offspring. So Your Majesty had better wait until tomorrow.\"","With that, she directly pulled up the blanket and went to sleep.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He tried to negotiate, \"We only drank a little...\"","But she replied without turning her head, \"Even a little is not allowed. For the sake of the imperial heir, Your Majesty should endure it.\"","In her heart though, she thought, [It's not easy to have a child. They must inherit their mother's intelligence to succeed!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Inherit her intelligence?","Perhaps it would be better to inherit more from him.","After a frustrating night's sleep, early the next morning, the Emperor got up and went to the front court.","Today, besides the morning court session, there would be a meeting of scholars and great masters in the Wenyuan Pavilion, mainly to discuss the curriculum for Songhe Academy.","He also planned to select someone from among these people... who could competently serve as the academy's headmaster, so he had to participate personally.","Meanwhile in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, the Empress Dowager had tossed and turned all night, unable to sleep. She simply got up early and went for a stroll in the imperial garden.","The Wenyuan Pavilion was in the imperial garden.","The sun had just risen, and birds were chirping in the branches.","The Empress Dowager had walked through the garden she had toured countless times before, picking a few newly bloomed lotus flowers, and was about to return.","At this moment, she saw a group of people approaching from afar.","Seeing her figure, the Grand Tutor who was leading quickly came forward and bowed, \"Greetings to the Empress Dowager.\"","Seeing the Grand Tutor do so, the others also came forward to pay their respects, saying in unison, \"Greetings to the Empress Dowager. We wish Your Highness good health and prosperity.\"","Among the crowd, only one figure remained tall and slender like bamboo, just as in years past.","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly to everyone.","Then, her gaze fell on him, and she took the initiative to say, \"Chancellor Qi, it's been a long time.\""]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67","paragraphs":["No matter how turbulent her emotions were, the Empress Dowager spoke these words with casual indifference.","To outsiders, it seemed like she was merely greeting an old acquaintance she hadn't seen in a long time.","However, when this voice fell upon his ears, Chancellor Qi trembled violently.","— He hadn't dared to hope to see her on this trip to the capital.","Yet unexpectedly, heaven had granted him this encounter.","— Although he only kept his head bowed, not daring to raise his eyes, his gaze reaching no further than the hem of her robe.","But it was enough.","Qi Shuguang also made an effort to suppress his emotions, bowing his head and kneeling to pay his respects, saying, \"This humble subject pays respects to the Empress Dowager.\"","This act was appropriate to both the situation and his status as a former official.","In just a moment, the Empress Dowager nodded slightly and then shifted her gaze, looking around at everyone and saying, \"This time, you have all gathered in the capital and devoted yourselves to the reopening of Songhe Academy. I am deeply gratified and hope that you gentlemen will do your utmost to contribute to the court and the people.\"","As her words fell, everyone responded in agreement.","The jumbled voices blended together, making it impossible to distinguish who was speaking.","When everything quieted down, the Empress Dowager spoke again, \"You may all go about your business now. I must return to the palace.\"","With that, she turned and boarded the sedan chair waiting nearby.","Everyone responded once more, and after seeing her off from the Imperial Garden, they continued on their way.","Qi Shuguang maintained a normal expression, but his thoughts lingered on that brief encounter.","— After many years, she had become the Empress Dowager. Her palace robes had changed to dark colors, and her voice sounded much more steady.","Surely she no longer had to worry about difficult political issues or fret over her young adopted son's disobedience.","This must be for the best, he thought.","Just as he was thinking this, he suddenly heard someone address him, \"I hear that Chancellor Qi once held the position of Grand Secretary in the Hall of Central Harmony. Now there are still many of your former students in the court. It seems that the position of headmaster of Songhe Academy this time must surely belong to you and no one else.\"","At these words, everyone chimed in agreement.","Some even bowed to him and offered congratulations, \"Congratulations indeed, Master Qi.\"","Qi Shuguang smiled faintly and said, \"You all flatter me too much. I am of mediocre talent and have been living in seclusion in Langya for over a decade. I dare not covet the position of headmaster. Once this matter is concluded, I will return to Langya. Please, everyone, do not hesitate to use your talents and contribute to the academy.\"","His implication was that he had only come to observe this time and had no interest in the position.","Hearing this, many people secretly felt relieved and praised him again for his modesty as they continued walking.","While these eminent scholars and famous experts were speaking freely in the Wenyuan Pavilion, Yanshu was just leisurely waking up.","As she lounged in bed, rubbing her belly and pondering what to eat for breakfast, she suddenly heard a ding from the system, [The Empress Dowager and Chancellor Qi just met.]","What?","She sat up with a start and fired off a series of questions, [When did they meet? Where did they meet? How did I not know about this???]","The system replied, [While you were just dreaming. The Empress Dowager went for an early morning stroll, and Chancellor Qi was on his way with the others to attend a meeting at the Wenyuan Pavilion. They ran into each other in the Imperial Garden.]","Yanshu: [!!!]","Darn it, if she had known, she would have waited in the Imperial Garden too!","How could a CP fan miss such an important moment?!","She could only ask further, [So what was the scene like when they reunited? Did they stare at each other in stunned silence for a long moment before slowly calling out each other's names?]","The system: [...You're thinking too much. There were so many people around! The Empress Dowager just said it had been a long time, and Qi Shuguang only kowtowed to her before they parted.]","\"...\"","Well, given the current circumstances, that was probably all they could do.","But even if their status made it impossible, they still managed to meet, didn't they?","This was happening much faster than she had expected!","Yanshu thought to herself, it must be heaven's arrangement.","Thinking of this, and remembering the task the Emperor had given her last night, she quickly got up to dress, had a quick breakfast, and went to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","She was excited and agitated all the way there, but when she arrived, she saw the Empress Dowager looking as calm as ever, arranging some water lilies.","\"This subject pays respects to the Empress Dowager.\"","Yanshu paid her respects and then stepped forward to compliment, \"These water lilies smell wonderful. I could smell them from the hall entrance.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed and said, \"They're fragrant when they first bloom, but after a while, they lose their scent. As they say, 'Gather ye rosebuds while ye may.'\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Why did that sound so profound...","Could she be reflecting on her affairs with the Chancellor?","She glanced up surreptitiously and saw the Empress Dowager's eyes downcast, seeming somewhat sorrowful.","Yanshu silently sighed and quickly tried to divert the Empress Dowager's attention, \"The Emperor intends to arrange a banquet in the palace, specifically to entertain the families of the eminent scholars who have come to the capital this time. He wants to ask for your guidance, Empress Dowager. What do you think?\"","The Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow and said, \"I think it seems somewhat unnecessary.\"","Huh?","Yanshu was stunned and quickly asked, \"Why would you think so, Your Highness?\"","Before the Empress Dowager could speak, Yanshu heard the system say, [The Empress Dowager doesn't know that Qi Shuguang is single. She's afraid of seeing his family and feeling uncomfortable.]","Yanshu: [I see.]","Just then, the Empress Dowager spoke, \"The affairs of scholars should be discussed in the imperial court. Why involve the inner palace?\"","This was clearly an excuse, and it seemed to contain a hint of sourness.","Yanshu thought for a moment and quickly said, \"Now that Songhe Academy belongs to the court, the Emperor naturally attaches great importance to it. He also wants these gentlemen to feel his sincerity. Moreover, the Emperor said that this time he plans to invite the families of some officials as well, about seven or eight, with the rest mainly being the families of these scholars. The total number would only be around a dozen or so. However, it's strange that among the four most famous scholars this time, only three have brought their families. That Master Qi from Langya didn't bring anyone.\"","At these words, the Empress Dowager's hand, which had been arranging the water lilies, paused, but she pretended to ask casually, \"Why didn't he bring anyone?\"","Yanshu said, \"I heard that gentleman is all alone and has never married.\"","As these words fell, the Empress Dowager paused again.","— He had never married.","In the past, there were always people trying to arrange matches for him, but he never accepted.","Who would have thought that after so many years, he was still alone?","Then Yanshu continued, \"So that's one less person. The gathering doesn't need to be too large. Oh, and there's also a young madam from the Tiande Academy in Xiangyang, who is said to be of royal blood.\"","Hmm?","The Empress Dowager came back to herself and asked, \"Who is she?\"","Yanshu said, \"I heard she's the granddaughter of the Prince of Nanping, surnamed Chen. She seems quite young.\"","The Empress Dowager thought for a moment and nodded, \"Indeed, the Prince of Nanping's eldest son-in-law is surnamed Chen. Years ago, when the Prince of Nanping and his wife passed away from illness, their son inherited the title but was not very honest. He attempted to cause trouble before the Emperor ascended the throne, so the Emperor confined him to his fief. In consideration of his father's loyalty, the Emperor only stripped the titles of his close relatives, leaving them to fend for themselves.\"","Come to think of it, when she first entered the Yuwen family, that old sister-in-law, the Princess of Nanping, had been quite kind to her.","...","It's a pity her descendants turned out so poorly.","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Since there's a descendant of an old acquaintance, we might as well meet them.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded and replied, \"Yes, it's quite hot these days. Why don't we arrange it in the Yunshui Pavilion? It will be cooler there.\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound of agreement, \"You can make the arrangements.\"","As her words fell, her mind returned to what she had just heard—","He had never married.","This fool, did he not want to leave any descendants in this life?","That day, invitations from the palace were sent out to the ladies who had accompanied their husbands to the capital. The Imperial Kitchens and the Court of Imperial Sacrifices immediately began preparations.","Thus, by the next morning, the ladies gathered at the Yunshui Pavilion to pay their respects to the Empress Dowager.","Yanshu accompanied the Empress Dowager as she received them. She saw that most of these ladies were in their forties, varying in height and build, but mostly with a quiet demeanor.","However, among them was one lady who was tall and robust, with a bright and cheerful disposition that particularly caught the eye. This was the wife of Gu Hongbai, the famous scholar from Lanling.","Yanshu immediately became interested and asked the system, [This lady seems to be in excellent physical condition. Could she be from a martial arts background?]","The system replied, [That's right. Madam Gu is the daughter of a famous martial arts family in Lanling, and her kung fu is excellent. Years ago, when she went out to the market, she happened to come across the handsome scholar Gu Hongbai, who was setting up a fortune-telling stall and being harassed by some ruffians. She immediately stepped in to right the wrong, kicking the ruffians to the ground and rescuing Master Gu. The two of them formed a bond from that moment on.]","Yanshu's eyes lit up.","- This sounds like an interesting little sweet story!","But why was this Mr. Gu out on the streets fortune-telling when he was young instead of studying properly?","Tsk, it seems I'll need to learn more about this later.","Just as she was thinking this, she saw a woman in her forties leading a young lady approach. They bowed to her and the Empress Dowager, saying, \"This humble servant is Madam Wang from Xiangyang, accompanied by my daughter-in-law Lady Chen. We pay our respects to the Empress Dowager and Consort Yi.\"","Xiangyang, Lady Chen?","So this was the granddaughter of the Prince of Nanping.","Yanshu hurriedly introduced her to the Empress Dowager, \"This is the lady I mentioned to you yesterday, Your Majesty.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, examining Lady Chen. She appeared to be about seventeen or eighteen years old, with a beautiful face. Her eyes and brows seemed to still carry traces of her grandmother, the Princess Consort of Nanping from years ago.","However, her expression lacked the spirit of her grandmother. Her gaze was lowered, giving an impression of meekness and submission.","The Empress Dowager sighed inwardly. A good descendant of the imperial clan, ruined by that unfortunate uncle, has now become an ordinary girl.","She said, \"I used to spend a lot of time with your grandmother back then, and I watched your mother grow up. How is your mother doing now?\"","But Lady Chen lowered her head and replied, \"I regret to inform Your Majesty that my mother has passed away.\"","This was truly a sad thing to hear.","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"After many years apart, many people are no longer here to meet.\"","As they spoke, Yanshu quietly observed the young lady, feeling something was strange.","On this hot day, while others were wearing low-necked summer clothes, her garments had a high collar, tightly buttoned up, looking uncomfortably warm. Her sleeves also reached down to her fingers, as if she was afraid to expose her wrists.","Combined with her demeanor...","Yanshu quickly asked the system, [Why does this girl seem so unhappy?]","The system replied, [Who could be happy when they're beaten and scolded by their husband every day?]","What?","Yanshu was stunned and hurriedly asked, [What's going on? Isn't her husband's family from a scholarly background in Xiangyang? Her father-in-law Hong Yusheng is even the principal of Tiande Academy! And she's considered a relative of the imperial clan, how dare her husband beat and scold her at will?]","The system responded, [Even great scholars can raise degenerates! Her mother-in-law, Madam Wang, actually spoils her son excessively, indulging his violent temper and unreasonableness. He beats his wife at the slightest provocation. The reason this girl is dressed so conservatively is to prevent others from seeing the bruises and injuries on her body.]","Outrageous! Domestic violence cannot be tolerated!!!","Yanshu was furious and quickly asked, [Don't her in-laws intervene? What about her own father?]","The system explained, [Her father-in-law takes pride in his son's scholarship and doesn't care about these matters. They specifically brought her to the capital this time because they want their son to secure a position at Songhe Academy. Her mother-in-law even blames the girl for not being able to bear children, often verbally abusing her!]","[As for her own father, he's even worse. The Emperor didn't punish him back then, only stripped him of his title, but left him with the family property. However, he was lazy and gluttonous, squandering everything within a few years. That's why he married off his daughter to that beast in human clothing from the Hong family, just for some dowry!]","This infuriated Yanshu even more, [Another girl being exploited! Even if she had children in such an environment, it would be miserable! Besides, how can they blame the woman for not having children? It's usually the man's fault!]","She suddenly found Madam Wang extremely distasteful, wanting to spit in disgust.","This matter couldn't be ignored.","So she thought for a moment and said to Lady Chen, \"It's so hot today, have you caught a cold? Why are you dressed so heavily?\"","In fact, the Empress Dowager had also noticed this earlier and asked with concern, \"Are you perhaps exhausted from the long journey? Would you like us to summon the imperial physician to examine you?\"","However, Madam Wang hurriedly replied, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty. She's fine, just naturally cold-natured and afraid of the cold.\"","Lady Chen herself didn't dare to speak.","The Empress Dowager observed this and merely nodded, saying, \"That's good then. Please, take a seat and rest.\"","Today's gathering didn't have many guests, and the banquet wasn't long. After about an hour, it came to an end.","As everyone came forward to bid farewell, the Empress Dowager said to Lady Chen, \"Since you're a relative of the imperial clan and it's rare for you to enter the palace, why don't you stay behind and chat with me for a while before leaving?\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up. Seeing that Madam Wang was about to speak, she quickly interjected, \"Don't worry, Madam Hong. After the Empress Dowager finishes talking with your daughter-in-law, we'll naturally send her back to the guesthouse. You can go back first.\"","Madam Wang was taken aback, hesitated for a moment, but could only respond, \"Yes.\"","Thus, after everyone had left the palace, the Empress Dowager took Lady Chen back to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Once they were alone, the Empress Dowager said to Lady Chen, \"You know, your grandmother took great care of me back then. I've always remembered that over the years. That's why I specifically kept you behind to talk. You are of the Yuwen clan's bloodline, so you can consider this your maternal home. Tell me, how are you faring in the Hong family?\"","As she finished speaking, Lady Chen's expression shifted slightly, her eyes seeming to mist over.","However, after a moment's hesitation, she said, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty. I... I'm fine, doing well in the Hong family...\"","Seeing this, Yanshu sighed and quickly said, \"Don't worry, the Empress Dowager kept you behind today with the intention of helping you. As a member of the imperial bloodline, you really don't need to worry about the Hong family. If they're not treating you well, you can always divorce and remarry. After all, you have the Empress Dowager's support.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow and glanced at Yanshu.","This girl, quite good at volunteering her for things, isn't she?","Yanshu's eyes darted around, and she quickly added, \"The Empress Dowager is known for her hatred of evil and her fairness. She would never stand by and do nothing.\"","As she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager nodded and said to Lady Chen, \"Indeed. If you have any troubles, feel free to speak up. Once you return to Xiangyang, I might not be able to help you anymore.\"","Upon hearing this, Lady Chen paused for a moment.","Then suddenly, tears welled up in her eyes, and she cried, \"I... I don't want to live anymore...\"","After crying for a while, she voluntarily loosened her collar and cuffs, showing the Empress Dowager, \"These are all from Hong Tianzong's beatings. Your Majesty, I... I really don't want to live anymore!\"","The Empress Dowager hurried to look and saw that her arms were covered in bruises, and her neck even had finger marks, clearly from being choked.","Yanshu was also shocked by the sight and immediately said to the Empress Dowager, \"Your Majesty, this man actually dares to abuse a member of the imperial bloodline like this. He absolutely cannot be let off lightly!\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded and quickly ordered, \"Someone, go inform His Majesty that I am summoning Hong Tianzong for an audience.\"","Immediately, a palace servant responded and quickly headed to Qianming Palace.","Soon, the Emperor in his study received the news.","The Empress Dowager had only summoned Hong Tianzong without mentioning the reason. Although he found it a bit strange, he still sent someone to the guesthouse to fetch him.","Come to think of it, Hong Tianzong, known as a talented scholar from Xiangyang, had impressed many officials yesterday at Wenyuan Pavilion with his impromptu poetry.","Of course, given his age, being a principal was far from enough, but he could certainly become a lecturer at the academy.","As he had matters at hand, after dispatching someone to fetch Hong Tianzong, Emperor Yuwen Lan returned his attention to the memorials before him.","By the time he finished reading the memorials, about half an hour had passed.","Thinking that Hong Tianzong must have arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace by now, he became curious and decided to see why the Empress Dowager had summoned this man.","So he left his study.","However, as he approached the Palace of Benevolent Peace, before he could enter, he suddenly heard a man's agonized scream from inside.","\"Your Majesty, Your Majesty, please have mercy...\"","Emperor Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68","paragraphs":["At first, when Hong Tianzong heard he was summoned to the palace, he was quite pleased.","He assumed it was because he had performed exceptionally well in the Wenyuan Pavilion yesterday, and the emperor had taken notice and wanted to grant him a position at the Songhe Academy. So he was extremely excited.","—That was the Songhe Academy after all!!!","It was not only once the top academy in the capital, but now it was directly under the Ministry of Rites and received such attention from the emperor. Its future prospects were obvious and unmatched anywhere else!","He knew that at his age he couldn't become the headmaster, but even just an assistant teacher or lecturer position would surely lead to a brilliant future!","So, with such excitement and elation, Hong Tianzong made his way to the palace.","However, although he thought he would have a direct audience with the emperor, the eunuch guide instead led him to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, saying the Empress Dowager wanted to see him.","Why did the Empress Dowager want to see him?","Hong Tianzong could only enter the hall in confusion, kneeling to pay his respects, \"This humble subject pays respects to the Empress Dowager.\"","After he finished speaking, he heard the Empress Dowager ask, \"Are you Hong Tianzong?\"","Hong Tianzong honestly nodded, \"Yes, I am.\"","\"Very good.\"","The Empress Dowager then ordered to the side, \"First give him twenty slaps for me.\"","What? What?","Hong Tianzong was stunned. Before he could react, he saw a burly eunuch immediately respond, walking over in a few steps, grabbing his collar, and raising his arm to start slapping.","In an instant, his face stung painfully, and the sound of slaps echoed through the hall like thunder.","However, it was accompanied by cries of anguish.","—Hong Tianzong had grown up pampered, when had he ever suffered like this? The eunuch's hands were large and forceful, each slap nearly knocking him unconscious. Of course he couldn't help but wail.","But it was twenty slaps!","With each one, Hong Tianzong was on the verge of passing out before being slapped awake again. After all twenty slaps were delivered, his cheeks were swollen like a pig's head, blood seeped from the corners of his mouth, his hair was disheveled, and he had completely lost his previous dignified appearance.","In pain, dizzy, and utterly confused, Hong Tianzong was both shocked and terrified. He could only hurriedly kneel and kowtow, \"Your Highness, please spare me! This humble subject doesn't know how he has angered Your Highness, please show mercy!\"","\"You don't know how you've angered the Empress Dowager?\"","Yanshu, who was accompanying the Empress Dowager, sneered and asked, \"Do you know who your wife is?\"","Wife?","Hong Tianzong paused, thought for a moment, and could only say, \"My wife Chen Wanjun is from Nanping. She was once the niece of the Prince of Nanping...\"","At this point, he thought the Empress Dowager still held a grudge over the Prince of Nanping's past rebellion, and he was suffering the consequences.","But he heard the Empress Dowager say coldly, \"Since you know she has royal blood, how dare you use violence against her? What are your intentions?\"","What, royal blood?","Hong Tianzong finally vaguely realized something was wrong, and hurriedly explained, \"Please calm your anger, Your Highness. I have not used violence against my wife... it's just that couples sometimes have disagreements, and I accidentally hurt her...\"","\"Accidentally?\"","The Empress Dowager sneered and said, \"Wanjun, come out.\"","At these words, Chen Wanjun, who had been hiding in the inner chamber, finally dared to appear before Hong Tianzong.","However, she did not stand with him, but went to Yanshu's side.","By now she had changed into cool summer clothes, and the bruises on her neck and wrists were clearly visible.","Yanshu pointed at the injuries on her body and angrily questioned the kneeling Hong Tianzong, \"You call this accidental? You really know how to talk. If someone were to treat you so 'accidentally', how would you feel?\"","After she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Indeed. Someone come and choke him, let him taste what an 'accident' feels like.\"","...","Hong Tianzong paused, immediately begging, \"Your Highness, please spare me...\"","However, before he could finish speaking, he saw the eunuch who had slapped him earlier approach again, and without a word, reached out and grabbed him by the throat.","...","It was at this moment that Yuwen Lan entered the hall.","He looked around and saw the Empress Dowager sitting on a heated platform, with Yanshu standing beside her, along with a young lady who appeared to be quite young.","At this time, all three were watching the eunuch Zhao Laicheng choking Hong Tianzong in the middle of the hall.","Hong Tianzong was a scholar, not particularly robust, while Zhao Laicheng was one of the burliest men in the palace. At this moment, he seemed to be exerting little effort, yet Hong Tianzong's face was turning purple, his hands and feet flailing about.","Yuwen Lan, not yet understanding the situation, was startled and quickly asked, \"What's going on here? What has happened?\"","He heard Yanshu reply, \"Your Majesty, this man has abused his wife, insulting royal blood. The Empress Dowager is punishing him.\"","\"Punishing?\"","Yuwen Lan quickly glanced at Hong Tianzong again.","Seeing his face was already bright red, he hurriedly said, \"Mother, if this continues, I'm afraid it will be fatal.\"","Only then did the Empress Dowager instruct Zhao Laicheng, \"Alright, let him catch his breath.\"","Zhao Laicheng complied and finally released his grip.","Hong Tianzong immediately fell to his knees with a thud, gasping for air, unable to say anything for a moment.","Yuwen Lan then asked the Empress Dowager again, \"What exactly happened?\"","The Empress Dowager looked at the Chen girl wiping away tears beside Yanshu, and said to the emperor, \"This is the granddaughter of the Prince of Nanping, the daughter of the former Leping County Lord. Although her uncle caused trouble, resulting in her parents losing their titles, she is still of royal blood. This Hong Tianzong married her, but instead of cherishing her, he beats her frequently. If I hadn't discovered this when she came to the capital this time, wouldn't she have eventually died at the hands of this beast!\"","After she finished speaking, Yanshu added from the side, \"This man has the reputation of a scholar, yet his heart is so vicious. He should taste all the violent acts he inflicted on his wife! And after he's tasted them, he should be tried for the crime of great disrespect!\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Indeed. Today the emperor is here to stop us, but who was there to stop him when he was beating his wife in their chambers?\"","At these words, the Chen girl, overwhelmed with grievance, couldn't help but cry again.","Yuwen Lan finally understood and said to Hong Tianzong, \"So you're just empty talent! How could you, a grown man, raise your hand against a weak woman, your own wife no less?\"","Hong Tianzong, having slightly caught his breath, could only kneel and repeatedly kowtow, crying, \"Please calm your anger, Your Majesty, Your Highness. This humble subject knows his mistake...\"","Yanshu snorted and said, \"You wouldn't know your mistake if we didn't beat you! As the saying goes, 'If a child is not taught, it is the father's fault.' If his parents knew about this and did not restrain him, they are just as detestable.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"How could his parents not know that their daughter-in-law was being beaten by their son every day? When I asked Wanjun earlier why she was wearing thick clothes, that Madam Wang still tried to deceive me, saying Wanjun was afraid of the cold, trying to cover up her son's crimes.\"","Yanshu quickly said, \"Isn't that the crime of concealment? They shouldn't be spared either!\"","The Empress Dowager nodded again and said to Yuwen Lan, \"This child's mother is Your Majesty's eldest cousin. As her uncle, Your Majesty should rightfully stand up for her.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"Mother's words are most correct. Come, summon Hong Tianzong's parents for an audience!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, someone outside immediately responded and quickly went to find them.","Before long, the Hong couple arrived at the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","At this time, Hong Tianzong was still kneeling on the ground, his face swollen like a pig's head, his neck also red and swollen, looking utterly miserable. The Hong couple noticed him at a glance.","Shocked, after paying their respects to the emperor and the others, Madam Wang immediately asked, \"What... happened to Tianzong?\"","In an instant, she was already in tears from distress.","The Empress Dowager said coldly, \"Your son abused his wife, who is of royal blood. You, as his mother, knew about it but did nothing. Today, I merely let him have a small taste of the violence he inflicted on his wife, and you're already this heartbroken. I wonder, when his wife suffered at his hands, how could you stand by and watch coldly? Is your own flesh and blood human, while others' are not?\"","Hearing this, Madam Wang trembled and could only cry and kowtow, saying, \"This humble woman knows her crime! It's all my fault, please punish me, Your Highness, and spare Tianzong...\"","Yanshu shook her head.","—Spoiling her son to this extent and still wanting to protect him, this old woman was beyond help!","Seeing this situation, Hong Yusheng, the father, also hurriedly knelt and said, \"This is all due to my failure to manage my household properly. From now on, I will certainly discipline my unworthy son well and ensure that our daughter-in-law never suffers even the slightest grievance again. Please, Your Majesty, Your Highness, give my unworthy son another chance.\"","The Empress Dowager spoke again, \"The situation has indeed been caused by your lax household management, but the crime of abusing imperial blood relatives is not something that I or the Emperor can easily forgive.\"","Yanshu also chimed in, \"Indeed, what about the future? Once such violence begins, it can never be completely eradicated. I implore Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager to have mercy on Wanjun and not let her return to the Hong family.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, saying, \"Mother and Consort Yi speak wisely. Since this involves imperial blood relatives, let's hand it over to the Imperial Clan Court. If we treat this matter lightly, where will the imperial family's dignity stand in the future? As for Wanjun, I will soon have a divorce decree issued, annulling your marriage.\"","Upon hearing this, Chen Wanjun immediately knelt down in tears, kowtowing, \"Thank you for Your Majesty's grace, thank you for Your Majesty's grace.\"","Yanshu also quickly smiled and said, \"Your Majesty is wise.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Your Majesty is wise.\" She then added, \"When he's at the Imperial Clan Court, have someone give Hong Tianzong fifty more slaps, with his parents watching. They are not allowed to look away. Let them taste that feeling too. After all, without knowing pain, one cannot repent.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Yanshu almost applauded, sincerely admiring, \"Your Highness is wise!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...Mother's words are most appropriate.\"","Tsk, serves that boy right for crossing the line.","He truly deserves a beating.","After sending the Hong family of three to the Imperial Clan Court, Wanjun temporarily stayed in the palace.","Upon hearing the news, the Grand Princess also brought her daughter, the Ankang county lord, to visit.","Seeing the wounds on Wanjun's body, the Grand Princess, as her great-aunt, couldn't help but embrace her and cry for a while.","\"What a sin, what a sin! She's a descendant of the founding emperor, how could she be treated like this!\"","The Ankang county lord also couldn't help but shed tears beside them.","Chen Wanjun also buried herself in her great-aunt's arms and began to cry.","The Empress Dowager said, \"Alright, fortunately, it was discovered in time. That wicked family is awaiting their just deserts. Now that Wanjun has a divorce decree, she's a free woman, which is a good thing. Now we just need to think about what she should do in the future.\"","The Grand Princess wiped her tears and nodded, \"To have married our girl to such a person, I think she can't go back to her father's side. Why not stay in the capital? At least she'll have my protection and that of the Empress Dowager.\"","Chen Wanjun nodded tearfully, \"I'll listen to my elders.\"","The Ankang county lord said, \"Your mother and I were cousins. I remember when we were young, she would take me to play. Though she's gone now, I'm still here. If you don't mind, you could recognize me as your adoptive mother, and I'll protect you from now on.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu's eyes lit up.","— This idea is excellent.","Although the Empress Dowager has the right to bestow titles on women, the Chen family had been implicated in the Nanping Prince's affair and had their titles stripped, so it wouldn't be appropriate to do so for Chen Wanjun.","But if she were adopted by the Ankang county lord, it would be reasonable in every aspect, and she wouldn't be looked down upon.","The Grand Princess quickly nodded, \"That's wonderful. From now on, she'll be my granddaughter. How could she worry about not finding a good match? If she doesn't want to marry again, I can support her.\"","Wanjun was already too moved for words, she could only cry, \"Thank you, Great-aunt, thank you, Aunt...\"","The Empress Dowager then said, \"With Ankang's name to rely on, I will also bestow three estates and one residence to Wanjun. In the future, she can provide for herself. You just need to take care of her outside the palace. Just one thing, don't let anyone from the Hong family or Chen family harass her.\"","The Grand Princess and the Ankang county lord both agreed.","Chen Wanjun knelt down again to express her gratitude.","— She once thought she would die at the hands of Hong Tianzong, but now she finally had a chance at life again.","With matters settled, Chen Wanjun left the palace with the Grand Princess and her daughter.","Yanshu bid farewell to the Empress Dowager, and upon returning to Ganlu Palace, immediately began writing a story.","Hmph, just getting beaten isn't enough for that violent scoundrel, he needs to be socially ruined too!"]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69","paragraphs":["On the second day, the Carefree Young Master's new story \"The Righteous Mistress Discerns Right from Wrong\" was released.","It told the tale of a fallen noble lady who was unfortunately married off by her relatives to a vicious man with a handsome facade. After enduring endless torment in her marriage, just as she was on the brink of despair, she happened to meet an old family acquaintance - a wise and discerning lady. Upon learning of the noble lady's plight, this lady immediately stepped in to help, rescuing her from danger and ensuring the villain received his just deserts. It was a story of chivalry and justice.","With half a month having passed since the previous story, eager readers rushed to bookshops to purchase copies as soon as they heard the news. In just one day, it had been reprinted four times, with all copies selling out completely.","After reading this intricate and fascinating tale, readers unanimously praised it, exclaiming how satisfying it was! Besides storytellers reciting it in teahouses, theater troupes adapted it into plays, performing it at various entertainment venues for several days to great acclaim.","Of course, when the Empress Dowager received news of the new story, she promptly had someone buy a copy as usual. And Yanshu once again unsurprisingly took on the role of exclusive storyteller in the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","After she vividly recounted the story, the Empress Dowager remarked with surprise, \"Isn't this just like Hong Tianzong's affair from yesterday? Is the righteous mistress in this story... meant to be me?\"","Yanshu quickly flattered her, \"Your servant thinks it does seem so. After all, who else but you has such a chivalrous heart and decisive methods!\"","The Empress Dowager glanced at her, \"You girl, always know how to sweet talk.\"","But thinking back, after listening to so many stories, she never expected to become the protagonist herself - it was quite novel indeed.","The Empress Dowager sighed as she pondered, \"What was this Carefree Young Master thinking, making me the main character?\"","Yanshu eagerly continued her flattery, \"Because you're the key figure in this story! It was you who noticed something amiss and discovered Wanjun's injuries, you who ordered Hong Tianzong to receive due punishment, and now you who has made proper arrangements for Wanjun. If you're not the protagonist, who else could be?\"","Such praise made one feel almost embarrassed.","The Empress Dowager couldn't help but smile, \"When all is said and done, this Carefree Young Master truly knows how to write. Especially the part about beating that man - just hearing it is so satisfying! I'd like to meet him now.\"","Oh?","Yanshu was taken aback - the Empress Dowager wanted to meet the Carefree Young Master?","But then she heard the Empress Dowager sigh, \"I wonder how old he is, what kind of person he is, to be able to write so well. I simply must see him in person.\"","Yanshu jolted to attention and quickly said, \"You already know His Majesty instructed someone to write it, so the credit doesn't really lie with the Carefree Young Master. There's no need to praise her so much.\"","But the Empress Dowager replied, \"It's not the same. Though the material may have been ready-made, his writing is excellent. See how satisfying it is to read between the lines! Especially making me the protagonist... I ought to reward him properly.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk, had she gone too far with the flattery?","She hurriedly added, \"If the Carefree Young Master heard Your Highness's praise, she would surely be overjoyed! But given her profession... as you know, she's written so many stories denouncing evil, she must have made many enemies! So she likely can't easily appear in public. If you were to summon her suddenly, and ill-intentioned people found out, it might put her in danger.\"","\"However, regarding the reward...\"","She...","cleared her throat and smiled, \"His Majesty could pass it on to her.\"","Tsk tsk, the Empress Dowager was always generous - who knows what kind of reward she'd get, hehe.","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager considered for a moment, then nodded and sighed, \"What you say makes sense. Alas, come to think of it, this Carefree Young Master dares to expose so much evil - he can be considered a righteous person indeed.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Your Highness's words are most apt. She fearlessly fights evil and protects the good, bearing the curses and resentment of villains single-handedly. It's truly not easy for her.\"","The Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow, \"People actually curse him?\"","Yanshu nodded again, \"Yes. Some people with guilty consciences see themselves in the stories, or they're jealous that her works are so popular, so they're always speaking ill of her, openly or in secret. As they say, fame breeds detractors - it's unavoidable.\"","The Empress Dowager snorted, \"Why get so worked up if you've done nothing wrong? They must all be people of poor character! The Carefree Young Master must not let them influence him. The more they curse, the more he should keep writing.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Your Highness speaks truly. I'm sure she will overcome these evil forces, especially with the support of so many chivalrous and enthusiastic readers like yourself.\"","She had just spoken from her heart, but unexpectedly the Empress Dowager replied, \"Mere support isn't much help if you can't meet the person. We should do something more practical.\"","She then instructed her lady-in-waiting Zhushu, \"Issue an edict: bestow upon the Carefree Young Master a set of Hu brushes, Hui ink, and Duan inkstone, along with 100 taels of gold. Send it to Qianming Palace and ask His Majesty to pass it on for me.\"","Zhushu promptly agreed and led people to deliver the rewards to Qianming Palace.","Yanshu was so excited she could barely control herself, but she held back and tried to calmly praise her generous patron, \"With your affirmation, the Carefree Young Master will surely be delighted.\"","Ah ah ah, a set of Hu brushes, Hui ink, and Duan inkstone, plus 100 taels of gold!!!","The Empress Dowager was truly so generous!!!","As \"The New Story of the Righteous Mistress Discerning Right from Wrong\" became a bestseller, speculation among the public about the real-life inspiration for the story once again reached a fever pitch.","At this time, a very timely piece of news appeared before everyone -","The headmaster of Xiangyang Tiande Academy, Hong Yusheng, who had come to the capital to participate in the academy's grand meeting, had incurred imperial wrath for allowing his son Hong Tianzong to willfully abuse his wife, a member of the imperial clan. He was sent back to Xiangyang, while his son Hong Tianzong had his scholarly rank stripped away for his vile conduct.","Not only was he banned from future imperial examinations, but he was also sentenced to a caning punishment, receiving 80 strikes in the vegetable market before the eyes of the capital's citizens.","Hong Tianzong's bottom was nearly beaten to a pulp.","After thoroughly losing face, the Hong family of three slunk back to Xiangyang in disgrace.","As for his wife Lady Chen, she was adopted by the Ankang county lord as her daughter and remained in the capital to start a new life.","...","When this news came out, readers finally understood who had inspired the Carefree Young Master's latest story.","People couldn't help but sigh - this Hong Tianzong had relied on his scholarly status to abuse others at will, thinking he could bully his wife just because she was related to a criminal official.","Little did he expect that the Empress Dowager in the palace valued loyalty and righteousness, angrily punishing his crimes. Now his future prospects were completely ruined.","Of course, with the affair causing such a stir, not only did the capital's citizens learn of it, but so did the famous scholars and literati who had recently arrived from other regions.","Seeing how the previously high-spirited Hong father and son had met such a fate, everyone was shocked and surprised.","On this day, taking advantage of the second meeting at Wenyuan Pavilion, the renowned scholars couldn't help but lament -","Ji Yuanzhuo from Jinling City waved his fan and said, \"Who would have thought that a man so eloquent could treat his wife so cruelly! He truly read all those years of classics in vain!\"","Yu Jingwei, a great scholar from Nanyang, also nodded and said, \"If Headmaster Hong couldn't even teach his own son well, how could he teach students? I fear Tiande Academy's future is bleak!\"","Everyone chimed in agreement, \"Exactly!\"","However, as the voices died down, Gu Hongbai, the great scholar from Lanling, asked quizzically, \"But... speaking of which, who exactly is this Carefree Young Master? I hear his stories always take the capital by storm, and each tale can find its prototype in reality. How can a mere story writer be so formidable?\"","Immediately, someone well-informed lowered his voice and said, \"What Master Gu doesn't know is that this Carefree Young Master is actually acting on His Majesty's orders. The material used all comes from the Imperial Guard, Imperial Censorate, and other such places. The stories are only written with His Majesty's authorization, with the goal of publicizing the misdeeds of certain individuals to warn both commoners and officials.\"","\"I see,\"","Master Gu stroked his beard and sighed, \"His Majesty truly has the people's best interests at heart. Having such an enlightened ruler is a blessing for the nation and its people.\"","Everyone echoed their agreement.","Someone joked, \"Looking at it this way, if commoners want to report something, finding the Carefree Young Master would be equivalent to reaching His Majesty, wouldn't it? This could be seen as a window between His Majesty and the common people.\"","The group laughed and responded, \"Well said indeed.\"","From beginning to end, Qi Shuguang only listened without saying a word.","In his heart, he thought, so the Mistress in that story was her.","It was indeed her appearance. After all these years, she still despised evil and cherished kindness.","That's good.","The next morning, while Yuwen Lan was reading memorials in the imperial study, he saw Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong carrying a burlap sack to him.","Seeing this, he knew these were letters for the \"Carefree Young Master.\"","— Ever since the storybooks became wildly popular, Yanshu had accumulated a group of loyal readers. Many of them would write letters expressing their thoughts after finishing each book and send them to the bookstore, which Zou Mozhong would then deliver to him.","At first, he was surprised to receive these letters on her behalf. However, gradually, as the letters increased from one or two a month to dozens every fortnight, it became somewhat troublesome.","— After all... most of these letters were written by men.","Although they all thought the \"Carefree Young Master\" was also a man, that wasn't the case!","Moreover, while most just shared their views on the stories, there were some with impure intentions who even expressed admiration for her in their words!","— And this was while thinking she was a man!","However, Yanshu found this amusing and would eagerly read each letter she received, completely forgetting about him.","Yuwen Lan wanted to intercept the letters for her, but feared she would become suspicious if she stopped receiving them. How could he not have a headache?","Now, he saw Zou Mozhong smile at him and say, \"Your Majesty, these are recent letters from readers to the Carefree Young Master. Please have someone deliver them.\"","Yuwen Lan grunted, \"Put them there.\"","Zou Mozhong complied, reported a few more matters of state, and then left the imperial study.","It was still morning, with some time before the imperial visit to Ganlu Palace in the evening. Fu Hai took the initiative to ask, \"Shall this servant deliver these letters to Consort Yi?\"","Yuwen Lan grunted in agreement, \"Go ahead.\"","They had to be delivered sooner or later anyway, and leaving them here was an eyesore that might arouse the ministers' curiosity.","Fu Hai acknowledged and left carrying the burlap sack.","Yuwen Lan continued reading the memorials.","However, the more he read, the less he could focus.","He couldn't help but wonder if there were more improper love confessions to his beloved consort in those letters.","Tsk...","After some time, Xiao Shunzi, standing by, suddenly heard a thud. He glanced up discreetly and saw that the emperor had put down the memorial he was holding.","Then, he unexpectedly stood up and left the imperial study.","When Yuwen Lan arrived at Ganlu Palace, he indeed found Yanshu engrossed in reading the letters.","She was so focused that she didn't even notice him entering the hall. It wasn't until Rendong reminded her that she saw him. Only then did she put down the letter in her hand, stand up to greet him, \"This consort pays respects to Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan grunted, \"Didn't go to the Empress Dowager today?\"","Yanshu replied, \"The Empress Dowager didn't summon this consort today.\"","Yuwen Lan grunted in acknowledgment, then glanced at the letter she had put on the table, pretending to ask casually, \"Are there any interesting contents in today's letters?\"","She replied, \"Nothing special, most are just praising this consort's storybooks.\"","In her heart, she thought, [Oh no, my writing must be too good. There are even more confessions this time than last! Tsk, I never realized there were so many 'cut sleeves' in the capital. I wonder what they all look like, are they tops or bottoms?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So there were more confessions!","And she was even curious about their appearances?","This won't do. When he gets back, he'll have to tell Zou Mozhong not to let the bookstore accept these letters anymore!","As he was pondering this, he heard her ask, \"Why has Your Majesty come at this hour? Is the imperial study not busy today?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound, \"Indeed, it's not busy, so I came out for a walk.\"","As they were talking, he saw her pick up another letter and start reading.","Yuwen Lan felt an itch in his heart.","He wanted to stretch his neck to look with her, but worried she might laugh at him. He could only resist the urge and just listen intently to her thoughts.","Unexpectedly, as he listened, he heard an exclamation of surprise.","Hm?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. Before he could ask, he saw her look at him with a shocked expression and say, \"Your Majesty, someone has exposed information about Ge Yuanhua, the famous scholar from Luzhou.\"","Yuwen Lan didn't quite understand, \"What does that mean?\"","Yanshu quickly rephrased, \"That is, someone has revealed a secret about Ge Yuanhua, the famous scholar from Luzhou, to this consort.\"","Yuwen Lan now understood and asked, \"What secret?\"","— Come to think of it, this Scholar Ge was the candidate recommended by many court officials to be the headmaster of Songhe Academy.","To his surprise, Yanshu said, \"It's said that he once took a liking to a student's wife, so he used threats and inducements to make the student sell his wife to him as a concubine.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70","paragraphs":["What?","Luzhou scholar Ge Yuanhua coerced and enticed his student to sell his wife?","Yuwen Lan immediately frowned, \"Such a thing happened? Is it true or false?\"","Yanshu nodded hastily and said, \"It's written in this letter, see for yourself.\"","She quickly handed him the letter she was holding.","Yuwen Lan took it and looked. On the letter paper, a few sentences were written in black ink on white paper:","\"The renowned Luzhou scholar Ge Yuanhua has an undeserved reputation. On the surface, he appears virtuous and respectable, but in reality he is lecherous and despicable. He has a concubine in his household surnamed Hu, called Hu Sanniang, who is actually the wife of Ge Yuanhua's student Wang Xiangli. Two years ago, Ge Yuanhua took a fancy to her beauty and coerced and enticed Wang Xiangli to sell his wife Hu Sanniang to him as a concubine. Later, when the Hu family reported this to the authorities, Ge Yuanhua used his reputation to suppress the matter. This is truly infuriating to both gods and men. We sincerely hope that the Carefree Young Master can expose this matter and reveal the truth.\"","The signature at the bottom read: \"An ordinary Luzhou citizen who witnessed injustice.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Some \"ordinary Luzhou citizen\" indeed.","He really hadn't expected such content to be in Yanshu's letter.","Of course, leaving aside who wrote the letter for now, the most pressing matter was: did Ge Yuanhua really do such a thing?","Meanwhile, Yanshu was calling out to the system.","[System, what's going on? How could you not tell me about such a big scandal?]","System: [...Can you blame me? There are so many scandals in the world every day. If I suddenly told you about a completely unrelated scandal involving people you don't even know, what's the point in gossiping about it?]","Yanshu: [...]","Well, that's true.","If you don't know the identities of the people involved, there really isn't much point in gossiping.","But now she knew!","This Ge Yuanhua was a renowned Luzhou scholar! How could he do such a despicable and shameless thing?","The system replied nonchalantly, [As they say, you can know someone's face but not their heart. You've heard so many scandals from me, aren't all those bastards proper and dignified on the surface?]","Yanshu: [...]","Alright, although that's true, she was now more concerned about the details of this incident.","Fortunately, the system finally began to reveal the details to her:","[This Ge Yuanhua does have some talent, but he's quite lecherous. His wife died of illness years ago, exasperated by his constant philandering. As for this Wang Xiangli, he was studying under Ge Yuanhua. One time, when his wife came to bring him winter clothes, Ge Yuanhua happened to see her. This Hu Sanniang was very beautiful, and had only been married for a short time. She caught Ge Yuanhua's eye, and the old man started harboring improper thoughts, scheming day and night about how to get his hands on someone else's wife.]","[As luck would have it, not long after, Wang Xiangli's father fell seriously ill, and the family had no money for treatment. Wang Xiangli was worried. Ge Yuanhua seized the opportunity, telling him to sell his wife to him, and in return, he would give Wang Xiangli money to treat his father's illness. Wang Xiangli was initially hesitant, but unexpectedly, his mother found out and actually persuaded him too, saying things like Hu Sanniang was too pretty and would inevitably cause trouble in the future. On top of that, Ge Yuanhua promised to recommend Wang Xiangli to study in the capital. In short, through various threats and enticements, Wang Xiangli was eventually swayed.]","Yanshu frowned and asked, [But selling one's wife without reason is illegal, and if the wife doesn't agree, it can't be done. Didn't Hu Sanniang resist?]","System: [Of course Hu Sanniang was unwilling. But this old Ge came up with an idea for Wang Xiangli, telling him to drug his wife and send her to his house while she was unconscious. Thus, when Hu Sanniang woke up, it was already too late. There was nothing she could do but endure the humiliation and become the old man's concubine.]","...","Yanshu was furious, [This is outrageous! Wang Xiangli is no better! What about Hu Sanniang's family? After all, their good daughter became an old man's concubine!]","System: [Her family did try to intervene. When they first heard the news, Hu's mother reported both Wang Xiangli and old Ge to the authorities. However, Wang Xiangli insisted that his wife had voluntarily agreed to be sold because the family couldn't afford his father's medical treatment. Moreover, Ge was a local celebrity, and the officials were already biased in his favor. They hastily closed the case and sent Hu's mother away.]","After hearing the whole story, Yanshu was livid.","In her anger, she quickly said to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, I've just learned about this matter. It turns out that Ge Yuanhua lusted after beauty, and his student was blinded by greed, forcibly making his wife Hu Sanniang become the old man's concubine. Such behavior is truly unbecoming of his status as a scholar. This kind of person absolutely cannot be allowed to become the headmaster of Songhe Academy, otherwise it might end up in chaos like last time!\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"If this is true, he certainly cannot be the headmaster.\"","He immediately stood up and said, \"I will have someone investigate this matter right away.\"","After all, although he trusted Yanshu, they needed solid evidence to convince the public.","Yanshu quickly nodded in agreement and respectfully saw him off at the door.","Afterwards, she immediately went to her desk, picked up her brush, and began writing a story.","—Hmph, why should such scoundrels be allowed to save face?","The more they try to cover it up, the more she wanted to tear off their masks and let them face public condemnation!","The next day, readers in the capital were pleasantly surprised to find that their recently lazy Carefree Young Master had published a new story called \"The Wolf and Dog Master and Disciple Finally Get Their Comeuppance.\"","Well, that title certainly stood out!","Excited readers rushed to buy and read it, once again overwhelming the bookstore clerks.","Of course, as the Carefree Young Master's number one fan, how could the Empress Dowager miss out? She immediately sent someone to purchase it outside the palace.","However, before the person she sent could return, Yanshu came to her personally, carrying the story.","With a sincere smile on her face, Yanshu said, \"I heard that the Carefree Young Master has released a new work, so I immediately had someone buy a copy to read to Your Majesty.\"","—Well, she was her number one fan after all! What's wrong with personally coming to read a story?","She'd be willing to read to her for a lifetime!","The Empress Dowager, who had been eagerly waiting, was delighted to see this. She quickly nodded and said, \"Then hurry and tell it to me. What is this story about?\"","Yanshu then began to narrate the story she had written just last night, trying her best to make it vivid and engaging.","As she was telling the story, she couldn't help but marvel at how her writing speed had improved under pressure. In just one hasty day, she had not only completed a coherent story but had also made progress in her writing techniques and rhetoric!","After listening to the entire story, the Empress Dowager also looked angry. She exclaimed, \"How can there be such disgusting things in this world? The master in this story, as a teacher, actually coveted his disciple's wife? And he even used such despicable means to force her to submit? And that disciple, for a bit of money, he disregarded his marriage vows? And that mother-in-law, if she disliked her daughter-in-law for being too pretty, why did she agree to the marriage in the first place? This is simply pushing someone into a mire!\"","Yanshu nodded in agreement while trying to comfort her, \"Your Majesty, please don't be angry. Bad people will always get their just deserts. Look, in the story, didn't a righteous official eventually make a fair judgment, exposing their evil deeds to the public and ruining their reputation?\"","The Empress Dowager was still indignant. After thinking for a moment, she suddenly asked, \"Then... who is the real-life counterpart of this story? What's the actual outcome in reality?\"","Yanshu paused slightly.","Then, looking around, she lowered her voice and said to her, \"I've heard some rumors, but this matter hasn't been made public yet. I can only report it to you privately.\"","The Empress Dowager understood and quickly raised her hand to dismiss the others in the hall, \"You may all leave first.\"","Everyone complied and left the hall.","Seeing that the doors were closed, Yanshu continued, \"I've heard that the real-life counterpart of this story is actually one of the great scholars who have come to the capital this time.\"","The Empress Dowager immediately raised an eyebrow, \"Is that so? Who exactly is it? Don't keep me in suspense, tell me quickly.\"","Yanshu coughed lightly, \"It seems to be that renowned Luzhou scholar named Ge Yuanhua. He has a concubine called Hu Sanniang, who was bought from a student surnamed Wang two years ago.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager shook her head repeatedly, \"So these scholars... on the surface, they appear to understand propriety and shame the most, but in reality, they commit the most shameless acts!\"","Before she could finish her exclamation, she paused again and quickly asked, \"So, does this mean others are still unaware of this matter?\"","Yanshu nodded vigorously, \"That must be the case. Otherwise, how could he so confidently come to the capital this time? I heard that many officials think highly of him and believe he's very suitable to be the headmaster of Songhe Academy!\"","\"How can this be allowed?\" The Empress Dowager immediately slammed the table and stood up. \"If he really becomes the headmaster, wouldn't that be a complete injustice?\"","Yanshu nodded forcefully, \"That's exactly what I'm saying.\"","The Empress Dowager thought for a moment and asked, \"What's His Majesty's opinion on this? Has he taken any action?\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"As soon as His Majesty received the news, he sent people to investigate. It seems that Hu Sanniang's family had filed a lawsuit back then, surely unwilling for their daughter to become a concubine. If they file another complaint, it should be easy to resolve. However, as you know, Luzhou is quite far from the capital, so it might take some time.\"","\"But now that the story has been written into a book, perhaps this old Mr. Ge will see it and feel remorseful, voluntarily turning himself in.\"","The Empress Dowager snorted, \"Unlikely. These people care most about their reputation. They probably won't confess voluntarily. Besides, this wife-selling matter can be interpreted as either serious or trivial. Unless the Hu family files a complaint themselves, it's difficult for the authorities to intervene. Even if he confesses voluntarily, Hu Sanniang has already been his concubine for two years. The deed is done. How can others separate them now?\"","Yanshu sighed, \"So it seems the only way to resolve this properly is for the Hu family to file another complaint. It's just a pity that the journey is so long, and we can only wait for some time!\"","The Empress Dowager also sighed, \"Wait for some time, but what if those officials select this Mr. Ge in the meantime? It's truly infuriating!\"","Yanshu nodded, \"That's exactly it. Watching this villain go unpunished and even gain a good reputation is really aggravating!\"","As she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager thought for a moment and suddenly said, \"I wonder if this hypocrite Mr. Ge brought that Hu Sanniang to the capital this time?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"I heard he did. Although Hu Sanniang wasn't willing, this old Mr. Ge quite dotes on her and takes her everywhere. After all, Wang Xiangli is still in Luzhou, and this old Mr. Ge fears that if he leaves Hu Sanniang behind, the two might take the opportunity to meet in secret.\"","As she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager smiled, \"Well, that makes things easier then.\"","She then ordered the palace servants outside, \"Come, summon Hu Sanniang, the beloved concubine of Mr. Ge from Luzhou, for an audience.\""]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71","paragraphs":["The reason Yanshu came to see the Empress Dowager was actually after careful consideration.","After all, regarding this matter, the Emperor could only send people thousands of miles away to Luzhou to find the Hu family, help them file another lawsuit, and bring Wang Xiangli and Old Man Ge to court.","As she told the Empress Dowager, there was a time difference in this matter. Even if the Imperial Guard moved as fast as possible, it would take five or six days to reach the place. Moreover, Old Man Ge was currently still in the capital. Whether the Hu family filed a complaint locally in Luzhou and the news was then transmitted to the capital, or the Hu family was brought to the capital to file a complaint directly, it would still take some days.","If they waited until then, it would be too late.","Fortunately, Hu Sanniang was currently in the capital. It would be best if she could personally cry out for justice in this matter.","However, how could she get Hu Sanniang to personally cry out for justice?","Naturally, it could only be done through the Empress Dowager.","And to let the Empress Dowager know about this matter, she could only write a story first, and even have it published.","Well, after all, she couldn't just read the manuscript to the Empress Dowager. Wouldn't that expose her identity?","So, she had worked hard writing all day yesterday, and this morning she had sent someone to wait early outside the bookstore to buy the story as soon as it was available.","Moreover, to let the Empress Dowager hear this story sooner, she didn't even get to sleep in or have a proper breakfast.","Fortunately, now that the Empress Dowager had made a prompt decision, it was all worth it.","Now, she just had to wait for Hu Sanniang to enter the palace.","This morning, there was still a meeting of scholars in the Wenyuan Pavilion, and Ge Yuanhua had entered the palace early with the others.","Therefore, while the Carefree Young Master's new story was selling hot, he and the other great scholars were still unaware of it.","However, he also knew that Hu Sanniang was not truly with him, so as soon as Hu Sanniang entered his household, he had arranged for a trusted old woman to stay by Hu Sanniang's side to monitor her daily activities.","So, when she first heard about the Empress Dowager's summons, the old woman asked with confusion, \"Why would the Empress Dowager want to summon our Third Lady out of the blue? The master isn't here now, why don't we wait for him to return, and then Third Lady can go to the palace together to see the Empress Dowager?\"","However, the palace messenger who came to deliver the message was very uncompromising. Hearing her speak like this, he immediately frowned and scolded, \"Nonsense! Does the Empress Dowager need to explain her reasons to you for summoning someone?\"","The old woman was startled and quickly knelt down, saying, \"This old servant wouldn't dare, please don't be angry, sirs.\"","The palace messenger ignored her and said to Hu Sanniang, \"Please come with us, madam. Don't worry, the Empress Dowager is merciful and won't mistreat you arbitrarily.\"","Hu Sanniang agreed and followed them out of the guesthouse.","Not long after, in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, the Empress Dowager and Yanshu finally saw the protagonist of the story.","Looking closely, they saw that this woman was about twenty years old, with indeed very beautiful features, but there was a hint of sorrow between her brows, obviously not living a very happy life.","Yanshu sighed inwardly, thinking how a good woman from a respectable family had now become the plaything of a lecherous old man. Who could be happy in such a situation?","At this moment, seeing Hu Sanniang bow to her and the Empress Dowager, Yanshu spoke, \"Madam Hu, don't be alarmed. We called you here today because a few days ago, there was a banquet in the palace, but no one from your household attended. I inquired and learned that the mistress of your household had passed away, and heard that you accompanied Mr. Ge to the capital this time, so I specially called you here to talk.\"","Hearing this, Hu Sanniang hurriedly said, \"Thank you, Empress Dowager and Consort Yi. I am only a concubine of the master, I don't dare to receive such attention from Your Highnesses.\"","Her words were full of self-deprecation.","The Empress Dowager saw this and said, \"It doesn't matter. In my eyes, as long as one's character is noble, their status is not important.\"","She then asked, \"Where are you from? What does your family do? How old are you now, do you have any children?\"","Hu Sanniang answered one by one, \"I am nineteen this year, from Luzhou. My family... are local farmers. I don't have any children.\"","The Empress Dowager and Yanshu exchanged a glance. No children, that would make things easier.","Yanshu then coughed and said, \"There are no outsiders here today, so you don't need to be too formal. Since you are from a respectable family, how did you end up as a concubine?\"","After she finished speaking, Hu Sanniang bit her lip, then said with difficulty, \"I was married once before. My husband's family needed money and sold me to the master...\"","Yanshu quickly put on a surprised expression and said, \"Could it be that your original husband's family were students of Ge Yuanhua?\"","Hearing this, Hu Sanniang was stunned and looked up at her, saying, \"How did Your Highness know?\"","Yanshu hurriedly said, \"It's quite a coincidence. Today, there's a new story in the market that tells a tale very similar to your background. It's about a woman from a good family who was sold by her greedy husband and heartless mother-in-law to her husband's teacher.\"","Hu Sanniang was stunned again and exclaimed, \"Is there really such a thing?\"","Yanshu nodded and continued, \"To tell you the truth, after the Empress Dowager read this story, she was very angry. Coincidentally, she also learned about your situation and wondered how a good woman from a respectable family ended up as a concubine. So she had people investigate, and unexpectedly, the story in this book matched your situation.\"","\"Could it be that this story is written about you? Were you also forced to become a concubine through a scheme jointly planned by your former husband and Ge Yuanhua?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Hu Sanniang, recalling the past, began to cry bitterly.","Yanshu quickly went forward to hand her a handkerchief, saying gently, \"Don't be afraid. The Empress Dowager is the most just person. If you have any grievances, you might as well tell Her Highness today.\"","The Empress Dowager glanced at her and decided to speak directly to Hu Sanniang, \"To be honest with you, I also received information that you were originally sold to Ge Yuanhua by your husband. This is a criminal act. If you want to seek justice, I will uphold justice for you, but if you don't want to, I won't ask any more questions.\"","Upon hearing this, Hu Sanniang fell to her knees in front of her, crying, \"I beg the Empress Dowager to do justice for me.\"","...","At this time, in the Wenyuan Pavilion, various famous scholars and officials from the Ministry of Rites were in a meeting.","After the previous two sessions, matters concerning the entrance examinations and curriculum settings for Songhe Academy had been decided. Today's agenda was to establish specific rules for the academy, such as reward and punishment measures, admission standards, and so on.","Like the previous two times, the Emperor himself was presiding over the meeting today, so everyone was actively presenting their opinions, making the scene very lively.","Ji Kaiyu, the headmaster of White Crane Academy, said, \"In the way of educating people, establishing virtue is fundamental. For students entering the academy to study, family background is not the primary concern. Apart from talent and diligence, what's more important is moral character.\"","Yu Jingwei, the great scholar from Nanyang, nodded and said, \"Those with excellent moral character will benefit from studying, while those with poor moral character, even if they read ten thousand books, will only be a menace.\"","At this moment, Ge Yuanhua from Luzhou stroked his beard and said, \"Speaking of morality, it can be divided into public morality and private morality. Mencius said, 'In poverty, they attend to their own virtue in solitude; in success, they make the whole empire virtuous as well.' Attending to one's own virtue is 'private morality', while making the whole empire virtuous is 'public morality'.\"","Seeing this scene, Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow —","How could this person maintain such a righteous appearance when his private morality was so corrupt?","However, just as this person finished speaking, before anyone else could say anything, a palace servant from the Palace of Benevolent Peace entered the hall carrying a stack of books. He addressed the Emperor, \"Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager heard that there was a discussion in the Wenyuan Pavilion today, and she has specially prepared a test question for the gentlemen.\"","A test question?","Everyone was surprised and asked curiously, \"What kind of test question has the Empress Dowager prepared?\"","The palace servant bowed and presented the books in his hands, saying, \"Please read this book, gentlemen.\"","Yuwen Lan took one and glanced at it, only to realize it was Yanshu's new story, \"The Wolf and Dog Masters Finally Get Their Comeuppance.\"","\"...\"","It seemed that the Empress Dowager was ready to make her move?","Very well, let's see how the Empress Dowager plans to handle this.","He nodded, \"Then let the gentlemen take a look.\"","The palace servant complied and distributed the books to everyone.","Next, everyone started reading the story.","Yuwen Lan looked around the hall and saw that most people's expressions were changing along with the plot twists in the story.","One of them brightened up, thinking, [This Carefree Young Master is so efficient, writing it out so quickly? Hmph, let's see how that old scoundrel Ge deals with this today!]","— Yuwen Lan understood then, the one who had written to Yanshu the other day was this person, Liu Zhengxin, the headmaster of Huai'an Academy.","And looking at Ge Yuanhua, who was holding the book, his expression was gradually becoming panicked.","As time went on, their faces grew paler.","Not long after, an announcement was heard from outside, \"The Empress Dowager has arrived...\"","Yuwen Lan paused, and before he could rise, the Empress Dowager had already entered the pavilion.","Immediately, everyone in the pavilion stood up and bowed, saying, \"We humble subjects pay our respects to the Empress Dowager.\"","Yuwen Lan also hurried forward to greet her, saying, \"Mother, why have you come?\"","The Empress Dowager smiled faintly and said, \"I gave the gentlemen a test earlier, and now I've come to collect the papers.\"","She then looked at everyone and said, \"You should have finished reading this story by now. What are your thoughts?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, everyone angrily exclaimed, \"The master and disciple in this story truly disgrace the sages! They are despised by all!\"","\"If such a thing happened in reality, those two should be scorned by everyone in the world.\"","\"Yes, indeed.\"","...","For a moment, everyone spoke passionately, and a chorus of condemnation filled the pavilion.","The Empress Dowager nodded and continued, \"To be honest with you all, I posed this question today because this morning, I received a personal plea from the woman in the story. And the master from the story is among you.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone was surprised and asked, \"Is that so? Who could it be?\"","The Empress Dowager didn't speak, but merely looked at one person.","It was then that they saw Ge Yuanhua trembling like a sieve, his face as white as paper.","After shaking for a while, he finally stepped forward, knelt down, and said, \"Please calm your anger, Your Highness. I'm afraid I am the master from the story.\"","What? It was actually him?","Except for Liu Zhengxin, who had leaked the information, everyone else looked surprised.","Before the Empress Dowager could speak, Ge Yuanhua continued, \"Please understand, Your Highness, there must be a misunderstanding. At the time, my student Wang Xiangli's family had fallen on hard times, and he came to me begging for help. I was confused for a moment and agreed to his request. I never intentionally coerced or enticed him to sell his wife!\"","Confused for a moment?","The Empress Dowager laughed coldly and said, \"Were you confused for a moment? Or for a lifetime? To this day, more than seven hundred days and nights have passed, and you still haven't come to your senses? A perfectly respectable woman was sold to you as a concubine, and when her family later reported it to the authorities, you used your influence to suppress the matter? Was this also a moment of confusion?\"","Upon hearing this, Ge Yuanhua was left speechless and could only repeatedly kowtow, saying, \"I know my crime, please calm your anger, Your Highness.\"","Seeing this scene, everyone shook their heads.","The Empress Dowager, however, ignored everyone and suddenly looked at one person in the pavilion, saying, \"Scholar Qi once served as an official in the court and is most familiar with our dynasty's laws. What do you think of this matter?\"","Her gaze was calm, showing no unusual signs.","Everyone quickly looked at Qi Shuguang, whom she had named.","Yuwen Lan also paused and looked over.","Tsk, at such a moment, the Empress Dowager actually called on him to answer?","Could there be... some special intention?","Under everyone's gaze, Qi Shuguang bowed his head and spoke, \"Your Highness, in my humble opinion, as a teacher, when faced with a student's family difficulties, one should offer assistance to help them through the crisis. This is the true meaning of 'one day a teacher, a father for life.' To take advantage of the situation to coerce or entice, satisfying one's own immoral desires, not only leads the student into wrongdoing but also puts an innocent woman in a desperate situation. This goes against the role of a respected teacher. Now that this matter has come to light, I believe the court will handle it justly and promptly announce the results to comfort the victim and reassure the people.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, everyone agreed, \"Mr. Qi's words are absolutely right. This is truly the way of a worthy teacher.\"","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but nod silently in agreement.","Especially when speaking these words, his heart was clear and free of any distracting thoughts.","The Empress Dowager nodded and said to him, \"With the advice from all the gentlemen just now, I believe His Majesty will surely handle this matter impartially.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"Yes. Please rest assured, Mother. I will immediately have the relevant persons in this case brought to the capital for the Ministry of Rites and the Ministry of Justice to publicly try this case.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"His Majesty is wise.\"","She then walked out of the room.","Behind her, everyone immediately bowed their heads again and said, \"We respectfully bid farewell to the Empress Dowager.\"","After the Empress Dowager's simple and direct operation, the identity of the story's protagonist became known to all under heaven that day.","In an instant, condemnation of Old Man Ge could be heard everywhere, from the common people to the court, inside and outside the capital.","Hu Sanniang was temporarily placed in a safe location, waiting for her family to arrive in the capital so that the Ministry of Rites and the Ministry of Justice could retry the case.","It was believed that at that time, Wang Xiangli, who had forgotten righteousness for profit, and his old mother would also receive their due punishment.","Yanshu felt somewhat relieved.","However, in addition to feeling relieved, she couldn't help but ask the system, [By the way, who actually wrote that exposé letter?]","The system replied, [The author of the exposé letter is also among these famous scholars. His name is Liu Zhengxin, and he's the principal of Huai'an Academy.]","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, [How did he come to know about this matter?]","The system explained, [Huai'an is not far from Luzhou. There was a competition for students between his academy and Old Man Ge's private school. Liu Zhengxin has harbored resentment ever since, and has been secretly inquiring about Old Man Ge's private affairs for years, waiting for an opportunity to take revenge. When he saw that many people were recommending Old Man Ge for the position of principal, he naturally became upset. Then when he heard about you, he quietly leaked the information to you.]","Yanshu nodded, [I see.]","But suddenly she paused. Tsk, now that this path has been opened, wouldn't she receive more exposé letters in the future?","However...","A few days later, her prediction came true.","Among a pile of reader letters, she indeed found another exposé letter.","And the target of this report was none other than Liu Zhengxin, the principal of Huai'an Academy who had just exposed Old Man Ge a few days ago.","The letter stated that in his youth, this man had been a litigation master. On the surface, all the lawsuits he handled were won, which made him famous in Huai'an for a time.","In reality, however, he secretly took money from those who sought his help in lawsuits and used it to bribe the presiding officials, which was how he won the cases.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Is there no end to this?"]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72","paragraphs":["Of course, although Yanshu had been feeling a bit tired from writing stories lately, her enthusiasm for gossip was still there.","So when she received this message, she immediately called on the system again, \"What's going on now? Is this Liu Zhengxin business true or false?\"","The system replied, \"It's indeed true. This Liu Zhengxin, in his youth, passed the imperial examinations and became a very minor official in a county in Huainan. He was actually quite greedy, and seeing that there wasn't much money to be made as a small official, he became quite disinterested.\"","\"However, taking advantage of his position in the government office, he discovered that being a litigation master was quite profitable. So he simply resigned from his official post and became a litigation master, only working for rich people. He would charge these people high litigation fees, then use some of that money to bribe county officials through his connections. Wouldn't that ensure winning the lawsuits? After doing this successfully several times, he unexpectedly became famous. Gradually, wealthy people would seek him out for their lawsuits.\"","Yanshu frowned, \"But what if those rich people weren't in the right?\"","The system sighed, \"He didn't care whether the rich were right or wrong, he only cared about the money. Anyway, afterwards the victims would only curse the county officials for being greedy and not distinguishing right from wrong, rarely did the blame fall on him.\"","Yanshu immediately looked disdainful, \"Tch, so he's just another heartless scoundrel! What a waste of his classical education! Then later, how did he end up opening an academy?\"","The system continued, \"Later, after several changes in the county officials, a righteous and good official finally came. Liu Zhengxin heard about this and knew he couldn't continue his business, so he changed careers. At first, he opened a private school, and later, using his skills of deception, he managed to expand and even opened an academy.\"","Yanshu asked in confusion, \"But you can't just open an academy on a whim, can you? To become famous, you need good teachers, and the students you produce need to perform well too, right?\"","The system explained, \"That's why they say this man knows how to operate. After fighting so many unscrupulous lawsuits, he had saved quite a bit of money. He then used this money to hire famous scholars and recruit good students from various places. Isn't that how he gradually built up his reputation?\"","Yanshu clicked her tongue, \"...Tch, no wonder this man would compete with Ge Yuanhua for students, so that's how it was.\"","With this, things seemed to be clear for now. Yanshu curiously asked, \"Who wrote this exposé letter this time?\"","The system replied, \"It was Ji Yuanzhuo, the great scholar from Jinling.\"","Yanshu's eyes widened, \"Why would this esteemed teacher write an exposé letter out of the blue?\"","The system explained, \"Well, Jinling isn't far from Huai'an. Liu Zhengxin has been poaching students from everywhere with hefty sums, and over the years, he's taken several students from other families. Seeing their good disciples lured away by money, how could the teachers not be angry? Confronting him directly would make them seem petty, so seeing that you've exposed Ge Yuanhua's past, they hope to use you to expose this man's true nature.\"","Alright, Yanshu understood now.","Someone like Liu Zhengxin certainly shouldn't be the headmaster of Songhe Academy. However, just exposing him in her stories wasn't quite enough!","After all, Liu Zhengxin's bribery and lawsuit manipulation were old news from many years ago, far from the capital, and there were no victims nearby. Even if she wrote about it, others might not guess who it was about.","However, bribery was indeed a violation of the law. Perhaps it would be more efficient to have the emperor deal with it directly.","So she handed the letter to Rendong, saying, \"Take this to Qianming Palace for His Majesty. Tell him I've confirmed that everything stated here is true.\"","Rendong agreed and took the letter to Qianming Palace.","Not long after, in Qianming Palace...","The emperor saw the exposé letter sent by his beloved consort.","\"...\"","How did another one of these pop up?","How did these scoundrels manage to reach their current positions?","And they even brazenly entered his Wenyuan Pavilion, lecturing him righteously about morality and virtue???","In his anger, Yuwen Lan immediately summoned people from the Imperial Censorate and handed them the letter to investigate.","Whether it was ten or twenty years ago, he would never let off someone who had once treated the law as a joke.","Fortunately, this Liu Zhengxin had always been mediocre and was not on his list of candidates for the headmaster position.","However...","What was with this one exposé letter after another?","Were they treating the Carefree Young Master as his Imperial Censorate and Imperial Guard?","Little did he know... that was indeed the case.","A few days later, the emperor received another exposé letter forwarded by his beloved consort—","The famous scholar Lü Gaozhi from Mount Song had once used his status as a government student to deceive and extort money in the countryside. Later, he was angrily reported to the authorities by the villagers, and an upright county magistrate publicly rebuked him in court. Feeling humiliated, he bribed the magistrate's superior and falsely accused the magistrate, causing him to lose his position unjustly.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He was so angry he slammed the table!","Of course, after his anger subsided, he immediately ordered an investigation. Fortunately, the place where this man had committed his crimes was not far from the capital, so it was verified within a few days.","He immediately ordered the Imperial Censorate to take action, investigating and punishing both this man and the officials who had accepted bribes at the time.","In addition, he scolded the officials from the Ministry of Rites who were responsible for sending invitations to these great scholars and famous figures, asking them to look at who they had invited to the capital this time.","That night, Yuwen Lan came to Ganlu Palace.","Yanshu, who had been enjoying the gossip for several days, knew that the emperor had been quite angry these past few days, so she quickly offered him some cooling tea.","\"The weather is hot, Your Majesty. Please drink some cool tea to reduce your inner heat.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and drained the cup in one go.","Yanshu: \"...\"","She saw that his expression was still somewhat cold.","Yanshu helplessly assisted him in removing his robes. After they got onto the bed, she gently advised, \"There have always been two-faced people throughout history. It's better to discover them now than to let them continue harming the people's livelihood. Your Majesty really shouldn't be too angry. After all, you can't prevent bad people from existing in the world, can you?\"","Yuwen Lan sighed.","Although the reasoning was sound, as the emperor, he still couldn't help but feel angry.","Seeing this situation, Yanshu thought he was still worried about the selection of the headmaster for Songhe Academy, so she comforted him again, \"It's alright. Even if four unreliable candidates have been eliminated, there are still several left. We'll surely be able to choose a suitable person to be the headmaster.\"","Ahem, of course, no matter how many were left, she still felt that only Grand Scholar Qi was most suitable to be the headmaster.","After all, he had real talent and learning, and there were no issues with his moral character. Most importantly, he had a past connection with the Empress Dowager.","If he could stay in the capital, even if they couldn't be together, at least they could occasionally hear news of each other and sometimes meet. That would be better than being separated by great distances.","Oh, just thinking about this couple made her heart ache and want to cry.","Yuwen Lan, who had been listening silently: \"...\"","This girl, writing so many stories every day and indulging in so much gossip, still had the energy to worry and cry for others...","Couldn't she spend her free time thinking about him?","Just as he was about to speak, he heard her say, \"Actually, I've confirmed that the safest choices this time are the four most famous scholars, such as Master Ji from Jinling, Master Gu from Lanling, Master Yu from Nanyang, and Master Qi from Langya...\"","She deliberately coughed and continued, \"I think Master Qi is really excellent. He speaks steadily, has a graceful demeanor, and clearly has depth. I've heard he was once a Grand Scholar of Zhongji Hall. Wouldn't that mean he has a better understanding of important court matters? It seems he would be very suitable as a candidate.\"","She looked at him with expectant eyes, \"What does Your Majesty think?\"","Yuwen Lan remained noncommittal and only said, \"I heard he himself has no interest in this matter and still intends to return to his hometown.\"","Yanshu replied, \"But others want to go back too, and they have families. Master Qi is alone, wouldn't it be more suitable for him to stay?\"","Yuwen Lan still didn't say anything.","In his heart, he wondered if Qi Shuguang had remained unmarried all these years because he still had feelings for the Empress Dowager.","Could a man really wait so long for a woman who was impossible to be with?","He tried to imagine himself in that situation.","If Yanshu wasn't his woman...","No, that's impossible!","How could such an adorable girl fall into someone else's hands?","He immediately stopped thinking about it and pulled her into his arms, kissing her.","Hmph, never mind those scoundrels. How could he waste this spring night?","Caught off guard by the sudden kiss, Yanshu felt a bit dizzy.","But she quickly immersed herself in it...","Ahem, she had been so focused on gossip these past few days, she almost forgot that flesh was quite delicious too.","Hehe.","After a night of passionate lovemaking, Yanshu slept in until late the next morning, feeling thoroughly satisfied.","After getting up, washing, and leisurely eating breakfast, she was just pondering what amusements to seek out for the day when she saw Fu Hai bringing her more letters.","Tsk, probably due to the recent stream of new books, readers' enthusiasm had surged, and the number of letters had more than doubled compared to last month.","Of course, there were likely still some letters reporting on her as well.","Yanshu was very eager and immediately started reading after receiving the letters.","She glanced through over a dozen letters, all from ordinary readers.","Just as she was about to go out and stretch her legs, she opened one last letter that gave her a start.","This was indeed a report letter.","However, the one being reported wasn't anyone else, but her idol, the great scholar Qi Shuguang!","The letter said that two years ago, Scholar Qi had bought a concubine from a rich merchant in Fengqiu.","Yanshu was bewildered. \"???\"","That can't be right, Scholar Qi was clearly single! How could he have bought a concubine?","She immediately called out to the system, [System, what's the deal with this letter? Surely it's not falsely accusing my idol?]","The system replied, [It's not exactly a false accusation. Qi Shuguang did indeed buy a concubine from a rich merchant in Fengqiu two years ago. However, that concubine was the daughter of an old friend, and he didn't buy her out of lust.]","Yanshu hurriedly asked, [What exactly happened? Tell me the details, don't keep me in suspense.]","The system then explained further, [In his early years, the great scholar Qi had a classmate named Bi Zimo. Back then, the two took the imperial exams together. Scholar Qi achieved the second-highest rank and entered the Hanlin Academy, while his classmate Bi also passed and was assigned as a minor official in Fengqiu. This Bi was a good man, but short-lived. He died in office after serving for over ten years, leaving behind a family of widows and orphans.]","[Because Bi Zimo was an honest official, he hadn't saved much money during his tenure. Afterward, his family became increasingly impoverished. His son wasn't very capable either, and as he grew up, he couldn't even afford to marry.]","[However, the Bi family's youngest daughter grew up to be... quite attractive. Just as she came of age, she caught the eye of a local rich merchant in Fengqiu. This merchant negotiated with Bi Zimo's son and offered five hundred taels of silver to buy the girl as a concubine.]","Hearing this, Yanshu could hardly contain her anger, [What kind of brother is this? Instead of trying to earn money himself to get married, he sold his sister?]","The system continued, [Indeed. Especially since that merchant was nearly forty, old enough to be her father. The Bi family's young sister was certainly unwilling, but she had no choice. After some time passed, Scholar Qi happened to be passing through Fengqiu on business. He had intended to visit the Bi family but was shocked to hear about this situation. He couldn't help but feel heartbroken for his old classmate.]","[As it happened, the Bi family's daughter heard about his arrival and found a way to beg him for help in escaping her situation. Scholar Qi went to negotiate with the merchant. He had hoped to persuade him with reason and emotion, but the merchant immediately demanded eight hundred taels of silver, saying he would release the girl if Qi could pay that amount.]","Yanshu was outraged upon hearing this, [Eight hundred taels? This merchant is a complete scoundrel! What a despicable person! Did Scholar Qi pay it?]","She was worried, as her idol didn't seem to be that wealthy...","The system confirmed, [Scholar Qi indeed didn't have that much money. However, he was determined to save her. So he scraped together funds from various sources and even sold two sets of precious paintings by famous artists that he had collected over the years. He finally managed to gather the eight hundred taels of silver and bought the Bi family's daughter out.]","[However, being a single man, he couldn't keep her with him after buying her freedom. So he entrusted her to a fellow countryman who had helped raise the money, asking the man's wife to adopt the Bi family's daughter as her goddaughter. Later, after some time, this countryman found a reliable man, and the girl was willing to remarry. So they married off their goddaughter to him. It's been two years now, and the couple is living harmoniously. They've had a son and are doing quite well.]","Yanshu finally breathed a sigh of relief and couldn't help but praise, [My idol's character is truly beyond reproach!]","In some ways, he even reminded her of her own father, that big fool.","But now she wondered, who wrote this letter?","Did this person know the full story? Or did they only know a fragment of it?","What was their intention in not telling the whole truth?","The system explained, [This letter was written by a professor from the White Horse Academy named An Hongsheng. He lives not far from Fengqiu and knew all the details of Scholar Qi raising money at the time. Writing to you like this now, he's clearly trying to tarnish Scholar Qi's reputation. After all, Scholar Qi currently seems to be the most suitable candidate for the position of headmaster.]","Hearing this, Yanshu flew into a rage, [He knows the whole story and not only doesn't help, but plans to selectively omit details to smear my idol???]","Hmph, this absolutely cannot be forgiven!!!"]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73","paragraphs":["Yanshu hadn't expected that they would even dare to come to her with false accusations.","Hah, were they trying to use her as a pawn?","What a joke!","She made a quick decision to write a story, first clearly explaining the incident of Chancellor Qi helping someone out of trouble.","After all, since this An person could write her such a letter, they might one day spread rumors elsewhere by cherry-picking parts of the story.","If it came to that point, wouldn't it put Chancellor Qi in a passive position if he tried to explain?","The system agreed, [That's right, you should know that An Hongsheng is quite skilled at spreading rumors and smearing people. Years ago, there was another professor at White Horse Academy named Feng Xuehai, who was open and cheerful. They had a poor student at their academy whose father had died early, leaving only a widowed mother who made a living doing needlework. You could say they were in quite difficult circumstances. This Professor Feng often used his own salary to help support the child. When the child's widowed mother found out, she was very moved, but being poor, had no way to repay him. So she scrimped and saved to buy fabric and personally made a pair of cotton shoes to give to Professor Feng as a token of gratitude.]","[As a result, after An Hongsheng secretly glimpsed this, he spread rumors around the academy saying that Professor Feng was having an affair with the student's widowed mother, and that's why he often favored this student. These rumors not only caused an uproar in the academy, but he deliberately spread them outside the academy as well, causing locals to mistakenly believe it was true. To make matters worse, the headmaster of White Horse Academy tried to smooth things over instead of dealing with it properly, which angered Professor Feng so much that he simply left White Horse Academy. As a result, there was a vacancy for a professor position, which An Hongsheng then conveniently filled.]","[Damn it!!!]","Hearing this, Yanshu was so angry she almost swore, [This is infuriating! How can such a habitual slanderer still be doing well? It seems that headmaster of White Horse Academy is a muddle-headed old fool!]","After saying this, she asked concernedly, [How is that Professor Feng doing now? And what about the mother and child he slandered? Doesn't falsely accusing someone of misconduct risk ruining their lives?]","But the system replied, [Fortunately, that student also angrily left White Horse Academy at the time and found a cheaper school to study at. Luckily he was diligent and hardworking, and later passed the imperial exams early, becoming an official and taking his mother with him. As for Feng Xuehai, he later found Mr. Qi and is now teaching at his Langya Academy. This time when Mr. Qi came to the capital, Feng is in charge of running the academy back in Langya. After all, he's a kind person who can be trusted.]","Yanshu felt somewhat relieved, [That's good then. But this An fellow really knows how to scheme. Even if Chancellor Qi doesn't work out, there are still three other masters ahead of him, as well as headmasters of other academies. Which one of them isn't better than a mere professor like him? Why does he think that by slandering Chancellor Qi, it would be his turn?]","The system said, [You think a habitual slanderer like this would only spread rumors about one person? He's prepared rumors about several others too. By the way, he's been writing slander lately about Mr. Gu Hongbai from Lanling, saying that when he was young, he was poorly educated and would often skip classes at the academy to go to the market and make money by cheating people with fortune-telling.]","Yanshu was speechless.","It was truly unbelievable.","However, speaking of which, she was actually quite curious about this matter with Mr. Gu. Ahem.","So she hurriedly asked the system, [Why exactly would a fine young talent from Lanling like Mr. Gu run off to the market to tell fortunes for people?]","The system replied, [Wasn't someone complaining about too much gossip just the other day?]","Yanshu played dumb, [Me? No way! How could someone who writes stories ever complain about having too much material? Don't be silly! Come on, stop being mysterious and tell me!]","Only then did the system say, [Well, when Mr. Gu was young, one time he went down from the academy to the market and happened to see a young lady, who is now Madam Gu. At the time, Madam Gu was dressed all in red, riding a horse through the street looking gallant and heroic. Mr. Gu immediately fell in love at first sight, and from then on suffered from lovesickness. In order to see the young lady again, he would pretend to set up a fortune-telling stall in the street every day to earn money.]","...","[Finally one day, he saw that young lady appear again. In order to seize the opportunity to meet her, Mr. Gu randomly bumped into a local ruffian, provoking the ruffian to want to beat him up. As luck would have it, his kindhearted future wife saw this and immediately came forward to rescue the scholar in distress. Thus, the two naturally got to know each other. Although his wife's family was from a martial arts background, with brothers-in-law and martial brothers all strong and muscular, making him seem as weak as a chick in comparison, he had talent! He was also good at currying favor with his father-in-law and mother-in-law. As time passed, he finally won the beauty's hand in marriage.]","Yanshu, [...Pfft. Who would have thought that the now erudite and elegant famous scholar was once so scheming! However, getting beaten up just to meet his wife truly shows rare sincerity.]","It was indeed a sweet love story, saccharine sweet.","But coming back to the point, the fact that even such a beautiful story could be slandered shows just how despicable this An Hongsheng is!","He absolutely cannot be let off!","However, she thought, it would be much easier to deal with Chancellor Qi's situation if there was an informed witness who could personally testify.","But then she heard the system say, [That's simple. The sweet couple I just mentioned are good friends with Qi Shuguang. Two years ago, when Mr. Qi was trying to raise money everywhere to redeem the daughter of an old friend, Mr. and Madam Gu even contributed one hundred taels of silver. Later when that rich merchant wanted to go back on his word, Madam Gu led a group of disciples to block him from behind, which finally scared off that merchant.]","Yanshu's eyes lit up when she heard this.","She had thought Madam Gu seemed like an forthright person when they first met, and it turns out she was right!","Tsk, if she knew someone was maliciously slandering her husband, she'd probably beat them to death.","Since the witness was right before her eyes, and was also a good friend of Chancellor Qi, this would be easy to handle.","Yanshu immediately went to the desk, picked up her brush, and wrote out a story.","By the time the story was finished, night had fallen.","Yuwen Lan entered the hall with great interest,","Only to see his beloved consort holding a stack of manuscripts, saying to him with great delight, \"Your Majesty, you've come at just the right time. Your humble consort has just written a new story today. Would you like me to read it to you?\"","Hmm, a beauty reading stories by a warm kang bed - truly one of life's rare pleasures. Yuwen Lan nodded in agreement, \"Certainly.\"","He then instinctively leaned back against the head of the bed.","Yanshu snuggled up beside him, cleared her throat and said, \"This story is called 'Poor Maiden Fortunately Meets Kind Scholar'.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"This title is quite different from your previous ones.\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"This story is different too. It's a heartwarming story that encourages goodness. It tells of two good classmates who studied together in their youth, both of high moral character. Later, one became an official and the other became a teacher, both considered to be benefiting the people. However, misfortune struck unexpectedly, and the one who became an official died early from illness. His poor little daughter, because she was beautiful, was sold by her wolf of a brother to be a concubine for an older merchant.\"","\"Not long after, the teacher learned of this situation and was extremely anxious, wanting with all his heart to rescue his old friend's daughter. However, he helplessly encountered the other party's exorbitant demands. Although the teacher's purse was quite thin, he did not give up, and ran about seeking help from many quarters. Among his old friends, some generously donated, gifting a hundred taels of silver, while others turned a deaf ear and avoided seeing visitors. In the end, though, this teacher still managed to think of every possible way to scrape together that sky-high ransom price, rescuing his old friend's daughter from the tiger's den. He then found her a good place to settle down, allowing her to live a happy life.\"","As she finished speaking, she quickly looked at Yuwen Lan and asked, \"What does Your Majesty think of this story?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"It is indeed a story that encourages people to do good. The teacher in it is loyal to his friends, of high moral character, and worthy of admiration.\"","Then he asked curiously, \"Is there really such a person? Who is the prototype?\"","Yanshu nodded and smiled, \"Of course there is. The prototype is actually the Mr. Qi from Langya that you invited this time.\"","Is it Qi Shuguang?","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Is it true or false? When did he do such a thing?\"","Yanshu said, \"Of course it's true. This happened two years ago in Fengqiu. The girl in the story has now remarried, had children, and is living a very happy life. Moreover, that Mr. Gu from Lanling who came this time also contributed one hundred taels of silver to Mr. Qi. He can also testify to this.\"","Well, it should be true then.","Qi Shuguang... does indeed seem like the kind of person who would do such a thing.","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"How did you come up with the idea to write such a story?\"","This girl, could it be that she's trying every possible way to make Qi Shuguang stay?","However, she said, \"Actually, the reason is that I received another anonymous letter today, falsely accusing Chancellor Qi of buying a concubine. After investigating myself, I discovered the truth. I felt that the person who wrote this letter had very malicious intentions, so in order to protect Chancellor Qi from future slander, I quickly wrote out the truth of this matter.\"","Fearing he wouldn't believe her, she hurriedly handed him the letter to see.","Yuwen Lan took it and glanced at it, indeed seeing that the paper only contained the single sentence about Qi Shuguang buying a concubine, with the beginning and end removed.","The intention was obvious without explanation. Yuwen Lan couldn't help but say, \"Such despicable tactics are truly contemptible.\"","He then asked her, \"Do you know who wrote this?\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"Yes, it was actually the professor An Hongsheng sent by White Horse Academy this time.\"","An Hongsheng?","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment and vaguely remembered - he seemed to be a man in his forties who hadn't performed particularly well in several meetings.","It seems he didn't have much substance, and used what little wit he had for such underhanded schemes.","Then Yanshu continued, \"This person not only attempted to smear Chancellor Qi, but also planned to spread rumors about Mr. Gu from Lanling. His goal is to disrupt this grand meeting in order to seek the position of headmaster at Songhe Academy. Who knows how many more people he plans to slander!\"","Yuwen Lan let out a cold laugh, \"Ridiculous!\"","However, what Yanshu said was entirely possible. A person of such base character might indeed do such things.","So he asked, \"What do you plan to do?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"I plan to ask the Empress Dowager to take action again, exposing that person's true face in front of everyone, humiliating him and making him despised by all.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Why must the Empress Dowager personally intervene? I could easily have someone investigate the handwriting of this letter...\"","But Yanshu immediately rejected this idea, \"Do you think An Hongsheng would write this letter himself? Isn't he smart enough to have someone else write it for him?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","That's true, tsk.","She continued, \"The Empress Dowager is highly respected and her status is above all others. Even if Your Majesty gives orders, those ministers might still grumble. But if the Empress Dowager takes action, it's different. Just like the previous two times she dealt with those scoundrels, wasn't each case convincing to everyone?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Although he didn't want to admit it, this was indeed the case.","However, if the Empress Dowager intervened, wouldn't that mean she and Qi Shuguang...","Just then, he saw Yanshu looking at him suspiciously, \"Why do I feel that Your Majesty has some issue with Chancellor Qi?\"","Tsk, could she possibly know about the past between Chancellor Qi and the Empress Dowager? But that shouldn't be possible... he was only a few years old at that time.","Yuwen Lan felt a jolt of panic and hurriedly said, \"Not at all! How could I have any issue with him?\"","Seeing that she was still eyeing him suspiciously, he felt even more nervous...","He coughed twice and said, \"Your idea is not bad. Let's do it that way.\"","Upon hearing this, Yanshu finally agreed and quickly took the draft to Fu Hai, telling him to have someone deliver it outside the palace overnight.","The next day, a new work by the Carefree Young Master was released.","Yanshu had someone buy a copy early and personally brought it to the Palace of Benevolent Peace to read to the Empress Dowager.","Needless to say, the Empress Dowager was very pleased, feeling that this girl was becoming more and more likable.","After hearing the story, the Empress Dowager, like most readers, couldn't help but praise the main character.","\"This official father really made the right friend. If it weren't for this gentleman, wouldn't a good girl have been ruined? Such a loyal and righteous person is truly rare!\"","Yanshu nodded repeatedly in agreement.","Then the Empress Dowager asked her, \"So, who is the real-life model for this character?\"","Yanshu coughed and tried to speak in a natural, completely uninvolved tone, \"I heard His Majesty say it seems to be Mr. Qi, the great scholar from Langya who came to the capital this time.\"","\"It's him?\"","The Empress Dowager was visibly startled.","Then she quickly concealed her surprise and said, \"Oh, so it's Mr. Qi.\"","Yanshu pretended not to have noticed anything and nodded, \"Yes, I've long heard that Mr. Qi is of noble character. Now it seems it's truly so.\"","The Empress Dowager said nothing more, but sighed inwardly, thinking only he could do such a thing, and wondering where he had scraped together the money, only to be cheated by that unscrupulous merchant.","After pondering for a moment, she asked, \"How did His Majesty discover this matter?\"","— After all, given that person's personality, he wouldn't likely mention it voluntarily.","Yanshu explained, \"I heard someone wrote a letter to the Carefree Young Master, mentioning only that Mr. Qi had bought a concubine in a certain year, omitting all other details. The Carefree Young Master felt this was a serious matter and reported it to His Majesty. His Majesty, knowing Mr. Qi's character well, found it very suspicious and investigated, discovering the true circumstances. He then had the Carefree Young Master write about this incident to praise Mr. Qi.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager indeed became angry, saying, \"The person who wrote that letter truly has evil intentions! Do we know who it is?\"","Yanshu lowered her voice and said, \"I heard it's a professor from White Horse Academy named An Hongsheng. His Majesty made inquiries and learned that this person is a habitual offender. Many years ago, he even twisted a colleague's kind act of helping a poor student into a rumor of an affair with the student's widowed mother. He forced that colleague to resign so he could fill the vacancy. It seems that this time he may also be planning to drive Mr. Qi away in anger to satisfy his own ambitions?\"","No more needed to be said; someone as clever as the Empress Dowager would naturally understand.","Moreover, since it involved Chancellor Qi, wouldn't her anger be even greater than usual?","Tsk tsk, lighting a candle in advance for Mr. An.","Sure enough, the Empress Dowager immediately let out a cold laugh, \"When faced with personal gain, people truly show their true colors! What on earth is the Ministry of Rites doing, inviting such lowlifes?\"","After thinking for a moment, she added, \"However, it's rare for these famous scholars and great intellectuals to come to the capital. As the event is coming to an end, why don't we ask His Majesty to arrange another banquet, inviting the scholars and their wives to join in the festivities, to show the sincerity of the royal family?\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up.","The Empress Dowager was truly worthy of her title!","This way, wouldn't there be another spectacle to witness in person?"]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74","paragraphs":["Two days later, the emperor held a banquet in Changchun Garden to entertain the famous scholars and masters who had come to the capital, along with their families.","As it happened, Changchun Garden was also the place where His Majesty would feast the candidates after each imperial examination. Therefore, it was quite fitting to use it for entertaining these great scholars and renowned intellectuals on this occasion.","Moreover, besides these famous figures, there were also several Grand Secretaries from the court present today, all of whom were outstanding performers in past imperial examinations. Thus, this banquet was filled with an academic atmosphere.","Speaking of Changchun Garden, apart from its pavilions, towers, and exotic flowers and trees, the most special feature was a small stream modeled after the Lanting Clear Stream. Whenever banquets were held, guests would sit along the stream, letting wine cups float down the winding water - a truly elegant scene.","Just after 3 PM, the invited guests began to enter the garden. While waiting for the arrival of His Majesty and the Empress Dowager, they started chatting amongst themselves.","Besides praising the beautiful scenery of the garden, today's guests, like the commoners in the capital these past two days, were most interested in the new story published by the Carefree Young Master.","\"I've heard that each of this author's stories has a real-life prototype. I wonder which gentleman is the inspiration for this latest tale? Truly a man of high moral character and great virtue!\"","\"Indeed! To help so generously after not seeing a classmate's daughter for many years - such a rare example of kindness!\"","\"Yes, indeed...\"","Overhearing these voices, Gu Hongbai, the famous scholar from Lanling, quietly said to his old friend Qi Shuguang standing beside him, \"Isn't that story about you? You're amazing! When did you become acquainted with this popular Carefree Young Master?\"","Qi Shuguang, who had been equally confused these past few days, could only shake his head and smile, \"I don't even know this Young Master's age or appearance, let alone have any acquaintance with him. To be honest, I also don't know how he learned about this matter and wrote about it.\"","Mr. Gu nodded and said, \"I was also puzzled, as this isn't your style. So how did people find out about this?\"","Qi Shuguang shook his head again.","Before he could say anything more, an announcement was heard from outside the garden: \"His Majesty has arrived! The Empress Dowager has arrived! Consort Yi has arrived...\"","Everyone immediately stood up, and soon after, the three announced figures entered the garden.","A chorus of greetings arose, and the emperor nodded, saying, \"Please be seated, everyone.\"","The crowd complied and sat back down.","As tea, snacks, and wine were served, the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"Gentlemen and ladies, please don't stand on ceremony. Today's feast is specially arranged by His Majesty to thank you all. Please enjoy yourselves.\"","Everyone responded affirmatively and expressed their gratitude for the royal family's thoughtfulness.","After a round of drinks, the Empress Dowager spoke again, \"By the way, I overheard everyone discussing some gentleman earlier. Could it be that you've all read the Carefree Young Master's new story?\"","Following the incident with Ge Yuanhua, everyone had come to deeply understand the Carefree Young Master's status in the Empress Dowager's heart. Naturally, they all affirmed and went on to praise the Carefree Young Master once more.","Observing this scene, Yuwen Lan glanced at Yanshu.","He thought to himself that with so many famous scholars praising her, she must be overjoyed.","However, to his surprise, he saw her calmly eating a lotus cake while thinking, [Scholars are indeed aloof. These people saying such things are just flattering me, the top-ranking bigshot. They don't necessarily like me that much. Stay clear-headed.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, it seemed her attitude was quite good.","But what did she mean by \"top-ranking bigshot\"?","Just then, they heard the Empress Dowager ask, \"Do you all know that the prototype for this story is among the gentlemen present?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Was the Empress Dowager going to... point him out directly?","Was she being this straightforward?","He couldn't help but secretly look at Qi Shuguang, only to see him sitting with lowered eyes, his mind full of surprise, [She already... knows? How did she find out?]","Meanwhile, Yanshu, who had been focusing on eating, suddenly became excited and inwardly exclaimed, [The Empress Dowager is awesome! So direct!!! I wonder how Scholar Qi is feeling right now? Is he excited and thrilled???]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","As expected, following the Empress Dowager's words, a wave of surprise swept through the surroundings, with people asking, \"Who is this kind and chivalrous gentleman?\"","Then Madam Gu spoke up with a smile, \"This humble wife knows. It's Mr. Qi. He once saved such a young lady in Fengqiu. My husband and I can both attest to this.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, a chorus of praise for Mr. Qi arose in the garden.","Not only the famous scholars and intellectuals, but even the attending Grand Secretaries from the court expressed their admiration for Qi Shuguang.","Chancellor Zou said, \"I've long heard that Mr. Qi is exceptional, but it's a pity he retired from officialdom so early, which we all deeply regret. It's my honor to be able to sit and drink with Mr. Qi today.\"","Everyone echoed these sentiments.","Qi Shuguang could only hurriedly stand up and say, \"You all flatter me too much. I am truly humbled.\"","As his words fell, the Empress Dowager also smiled slightly and said, \"Mr. Qi need not be so modest. To have done such a deed truly demonstrates admirable qualities, just like in the past.\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","Before he could say anything, his ears were suddenly flooded with a piercing mental scream—","[Ahhhh the Empress Dowager is so brave ahhhh I love it I love it!!!]","Needless to say, it was Yanshu.","The volume was so loud that Yuwen Lan wanted to cover his ears.","Of course, covering his ears wouldn't help...","He could only try hard to control his expression, not letting any abnormality show.","Then he saw Qi Shuguang bow to the Empress Dowager again, saying, \"Your Highness praises me too much. This was but a small matter; I believe anyone would have done the same.\"","As soon as these words fell, another burst of screaming rushed into Yuwen Lan's ears.","[Ahhhh they're talking to each other ahhhh!!! The Grand Secretary is so restrained!!! Fans are going crazy ahhhh!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Could she please stop screaming...","Also, what did she mean by \"restrained\"?","Then he heard the Empress Dowager say, \"This is not a small matter. Out of a thousand people, there might not be one who would do as you did.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement. After all, that was 800 taels of silver, not 8 or 80!","After a pause, the Empress Dowager asked, \"I presume Mr. Qi is not a man of great wealth. How did you manage to provide such a sum?\"","Qi Shuguang hurriedly replied, \"Your Highness, this money was not from me alone, but from several friends and fellow townsmen who helped. In particular, Mr. Gu and his wife generously contributed 100 taels of silver. Therefore, this deed is by no means my sole accomplishment. For me to receive all this praise alone would be a great injustice.\"","The Empress Dowager's eyes brightened, and she quickly addressed the Gu couple, \"You two are also people of chivalry and righteousness, truly admirable.\"","As these words fell, everyone joined in the praise.","Gu Hongbai hastily said, \"You all flatter us too much. We simply couldn't bear to see Mr. Qi sell his treasured calligraphy and paintings collected over many years, so we contributed what little we could. It's really not worth mentioning. Mr. Qi is truly the one worthy of the world's praise. However, coming back to the point, based on my knowledge of Mr. Qi over many years, he's a low-key person. I wonder how this matter got out?\"","Yanshu quickly spoke up, \"Actually, the Carefree Young Master received a letter a few days ago. The letter briefly mentioned only one sentence: 'Mr. Qi once bought a concubine from a rich merchant,' which aroused suspicion. The Carefree Young Master then passed this letter to His Majesty. His Majesty, knowing Mr. Qi's character well and also aware that Mr. Qi is single, was curious and ordered an investigation. That's how the truth came to light.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone raised their eyebrows, each pondering the implications.","Gu Hongbai said, \"Did the person who wrote this letter know the full story, or was it just hearsay? The intention behind writing such a letter to the Carefree Young Master is worth investigating.\"","In contrast, Madam Gu was much more straightforward. She directly said, \"To speak so vaguely and tell only half the story, isn't that just an attempt to spread rumors? If it weren't for His Majesty's discernment, wouldn't Mr. Qi have been unable to clear his name? Who on earth had nothing better to do than to do such a thing?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, everyone nodded. Madam Gu had said what they were thinking but didn't dare to say.","Only An Hongsheng felt a bit uncomfortable.","He never imagined that the emperor would order an investigation.","Moreover, what was stranger was that the journey from Fengqiu to the capital took at least three days. How could they have investigated so quickly?","Just then, they heard Yanshu say, \"Actually, this person didn't just write about Mr. Qi, but also about Mr. Gu.\"","Upon hearing this, the Gu couple was immediately taken aback.","Madam Gu hurriedly asked, \"Your Highness, could you tell us what this person wrote about my husband?\"","Yanshu coughed lightly and said, \"The letter stated that when Mr. Gu was young, he disliked studying and spent his days setting up fortune-telling stalls in the marketplace, deceiving people...\"","Before she could finish speaking, An Hongsheng was stunned once again. How could this be? He hadn't even sent that letter yet! He had planned to deal with Qi Shuguang first before sending it!","However, Madam Gu immediately became furious. \"I beg Your Majesty to see the truth. This is pure slander! Back then, he only pretended to be a fortune teller in the marketplace for a few days just to meet me. He never actually took any customers, so how could that be considered deception? The person spreading such rumors must have some ulterior motive!\"","Of course, who would do such a thing without a purpose?","The crowd quickly understood the situation. Upon hearing this, they began to condemn the act, saying, \"This is utterly absurd! What could be the intention behind such slanderous rumors?\"","\"If we can find out who did this, they must not be let off lightly!\"","Madam Gu angrily added, \"If someone has a problem with us, they should come out and say it directly! Spreading rumors in secret, aren't they afraid of going to hell and having their tongue pulled out?\"","Gu Hongbai hurriedly said to Empress Dowager Yanshu, \"Please forgive my wife's temper, Your Majesties. She has always been like this.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"Madam Gu is a woman of great spirit, and her words are entirely correct. Moreover, I've heard that the person who wrote this letter is present in the garden today.\"","Upon hearing this, the crowd was surprised. They looked at each other, trying to guess who it could be.","Yuwen Lan looked at the man called An Hongsheng and noticed his eyes darting around nervously. An Hongsheng was already thinking to himself, [I shouldn't stay here any longer. Once the banquet is over, I'll quickly return to Yangwu...]","Thinking of running away?","Yuwen Lan spoke up, \"There's no need to worry, everyone. I've already ordered an investigation. Trust that justice will prevail, and even if this person doesn't confess voluntarily, we will surely find them.\"","Hearing this, An Hongsheng became even more nervous, but he still tried to reassure himself, [It's fine, it's fine. Even if they find out, I'll just say I didn't know the truth. After all, it was just a letter, not a serious crime.]","He's quite resilient.","Yuwen Lan smirked and glanced at Chancellor Zou Mozhong.","Chancellor Zou immediately spoke up, \"Speaking of this matter, I recall an old incident. A few years ago, I was chatting with a new colleague who had just joined the Hanlin Academy. He told me a story from his youth. This colleague had lost his father early on, and his widowed mother supported the family by sewing. At the time, he was studying at the White Horse Academy, where a professor took special care of him. My colleague was very grateful for this. However, out of nowhere, someone spread a rumor that this professor was having an affair with his mother. As a result, the kind-hearted professor left in anger, and my colleague, unable to bear the damage to his widowed mother's reputation, also left. The person who spread the rumor then took advantage of the situation to fill the vacancy, being promoted directly from lecturer to professor. Looking back now, the methods of that rumor-monger seem quite similar to the present case.\"","White Horse Academy? Professor?","As soon as these words were spoken, everyone turned to look at An Hongsheng, who was trying to feign ignorance.","Isn't this about him?","So it was him all along!","However, An Hongsheng still attempted to play dumb, lowering his eyes to avoid the gazes of those around him.","Madam Gu sneered, \"I remember now too. When Mr. Qi was going around raising money for that poor young lady, he had just left the White Horse Academy. The professor from White Horse Academy must have heard about it too.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone suddenly understood and began shaking their heads as they looked at An Hongsheng.","Someone sighed, \"Not helping is one thing, but spreading rumors behind someone's back? What's the point? Did you think that by ruining someone else's reputation, it would be your turn to shine?\"","Finally, An Hongsheng spoke up, \"What a coincidence. I am indeed from the White Horse Academy. I wonder which colleague could have done such a foolish thing...\"","Before he could finish, Madam Gu angrily called out his name, \"An Hongsheng! You are truly the most shameless person I have ever met! Wasn't it you who filled the vacancy after Professor Feng Xuehai left White Horse Academy in anger? You were my husband's junior at the time, and besides you, who else would know that my husband once set up a fortune-telling stall? Two years ago, when Mr. Qi was going around raising money, weren't you the one avoiding visitors? You really have quite a thick skin!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, someone started applauding, and the crowd followed suit, clapping for Madam Gu.","Gu Hongbai quickly smiled and said, \"My wife is just straightforward. We should at least give Professor An a chance to save face and confess on his own!\"","Madam Gu snorted, \"A person without shame doesn't need to save face! I don't think he has any intention of admitting it today!\"","The crowd applauded again, exclaiming, \"Madam Gu truly has the spirit of a female warrior!\"","At this point, An Hongsheng could no longer maintain his composure. He quickly stood up, knelt down, and began kowtowing to the emperor, \"This humble servant was merely confused for a moment. Please forgive my crime, Your Majesty!\"","The Empress Dowager coldly replied, \"If Madam Gu hadn't scolded you, who knows how long you would have continued to deny it. How can His Majesty forgive your crime so easily?\"","She then addressed the crowd, \"In my opinion, this man needs to be scolded! Come, write down the events of today and this man's misdeeds in a public notice. Post it in the capital and at White Horse Academy for three months, so that people can scold him properly and help him come to his senses.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone praised her decision, \"The Empress Dowager is truly wise!\""]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75","paragraphs":["To be honest, everyone present today was truly angered by An Hongsheng.","So when the Empress Dowager finished speaking, all called out that she was wise and enlightened.","Yuwen Lan then heard Yanshu screaming in her mind again, [The Empress Dowager is so cool! Scholar Qi, did you get that? The Empress Dowager did all this for you!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Fortunately that scream wasn't out loud.","And then, Qi Shuguang stood up and said, \"Empress Dowager, please calm your anger. Don't harm your health.\"","Yuwen Lan paused, immediately getting a bad feeling. Sure enough, he then heard Yanshu squealing in her mind again, [Scholar Qi got it too!!! Their mutual feelings are so touching!!!]","\"...\"","What does \"mutual feelings\" mean again?","Of course, this wasn't the most important thing. The important thing was this An Hongsheng before them, who was truly detestable!","With so much evidence today, everyone already knew it was him, yet he still intended to stubbornly deny it, forcing Madam Gu to come and scold him in person.","He really was shameless and despicable.","So Yuwen Lan also spoke to this man, saying, \"You know the truth, yet still slander others maliciously, making good people lose heart. If this continues, will anyone in the world still do good deeds? If there are more people like you, it will only make social customs worse and worse!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he heard the Empress Dowager say, \"Your Majesty speaks wisely. This kind of behavior absolutely cannot be allowed to continue! He dared to spread rumors about Scholar Qi and Madam Gu today, who knows who he'll slander tomorrow? If this person really drives away all the scholars, leaving only himself to be the headmaster of Songhe Academy, wouldn't that waste all the efforts of Your Majesty and the court, as well as the goodwill of these scholars! So this person is truly detestable!\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Mother Empress speaks correctly. So, just posting notices in the capital and at White Horse Academy is not enough. We must post announcements in all regions, at all academies and government offices, to let the whole world know how despicable these rumormongers are. And we must make spreading rumors a criminal offense, write it into the law, so that anyone who commits this crime in the future must be severely punished.\"","As he spoke, he looked at An Hongsheng kneeling on the ground and said, \"We must also let these rumormongers know that a simple apology is not enough to settle the matter. They must pay a price.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, An Hongsheng was already trembling all over, unable to speak.","The others in the garden all called out that His Majesty was wise and enlightened.","Amidst the chorus of voices, Yuwen Lan heard Qi Shuguang sighing in his mind, [His Majesty has truly grown into an enlightened ruler, living up to everyone's expectations. We can rest assured now.]","Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow.","He also paid attention to Yanshu, and heard her say, [Aww the little emperor is so handsome too, I love it!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","It's good that she loves him, but why call him \"little\"?","He... where is he \"little\"?","With the Empress Dowager and the Emperor speaking one after another, the guards came forward to drag An Hongsheng away, and the garden party finally returned to normal.","Seeing that the villain had finally been punished, everyone felt relieved, and the drinking became much more lively.","Suddenly, the scholarly Madam Yu of Nanyang raised her cup to Madam Gu and said, \"Madam Gu's heroic spirit is truly admirable. I toast to you, thanking you for saying what we all wanted to say earlier.\"","At these words, the other ladies also began toasting. Madam Gu graciously accepted, boldly drinking it all in one gulp, earning everyone's admiration once again.","Then Madam Gu said to everyone, \"Actually, that person earlier really didn't need to bother with us. I'm just a rough person after all, not very well-read, incomparable to you ladies from scholarly families, so I could never be the headmaster's wife.\"","Although her tone was joking, her meaning was clear...","Their Gu family had no intention of competing for the headmaster position.","As soon as she said this, Madam Ji of Jinling City also hurriedly said, \"My husband is already in his twilight years, I'm afraid he can't be of much use to the court anymore.\"","Her husband quickly nodded beside her, \"That's right, that's right.\"","— It was just choosing an academy headmaster, yet it had turned into such intrigue with undercurrents. It was truly frightening. If someday his letter reporting Willow Zhengxin's matter was discovered, it wouldn't be good.","So it was better to retire early and preserve one's integrity.","Seeing these two families take such a stance, Mr. Yu of Nanyang directly said to the Emperor, \"After today's events, Scholar Qi's character has earned everyone's admiration. Therefore, this humble official nominates Scholar Qi to serve as the headmaster.\"","As soon as he said this, everyone began to agree, \"That's right, Scholar Qi's noble character and profound knowledge make him worthy of the headmaster position.\"","\"Selecting Scholar Qi is convincing to all!\"","\"No one is more suited to be headmaster than Scholar Qi!\"","...","Faced with this situation, Qi Shuguang had to stand up again and say, \"You all flatter me too much, it truly makes me feel unworthy. I am but a simple country scholar, how could I bear such a great responsibility?\"","However, his friend Gu Hongbai, enjoying the excitement, said from the side, \"Scholar Qi, don't be so modest. Your character and learning are most convincing to all. If you're a country bumpkin, wouldn't that make the rest of us complete savages?\"","Qi Shuguang glanced at him helplessly, \"This is a serious matter, Brother Gu, don't joke.\"","Seeing this situation, although the Empress Dowager didn't speak, she glanced at Yuwen Lan, thinking to herself, [With the situation like this, why hasn't the Emperor spoken up to keep Qi Shuguang? Could he have some issue with Qi Shuguang?]","[He used to teach him so devotedly before, even more attentively than the Imperial Tutor! Tsk, how ungrateful, could it be he looks down on Qi Shuguang?]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","How had he looked down on Qi Shuguang...","Just then, he heard Yanshu's anxious voice in his ear again, [The atmosphere has been built up so well, why hasn't the Emperor agreed yet??? Could he really have some prejudice against Qi Shuguang? Please! Scholar Qi is such a pure and flawless person!! Is there something wrong with your eyes?!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","He had just not spoken immediately, and had already been accused of so many crimes?","...He had only come to catch that slanderous little man!","But come to think of it... he did seem to have some...","Not prejudice, just some... awkwardness with Qi Shuguang.","But to be honest, after these few meetings and interactions, Scholar Qi Shuguang's vision and character truly had no problems.","He really was the most suitable candidate for headmaster of Songhe Academy.","So he had no choice but to speak up, \"Since everyone unanimously recommends Scholar Qi, I hope Scholar Qi can reluctantly accept, and do his best for Songhe Academy.\"","As soon as he said this, the Empress Dowager felt relieved.","Yanshu was overjoyed, and quickly looked at Qi Shuguang.","With the Emperor speaking thus, Qi Shuguang naturally had no choice, and could only respond, \"This humble official is unworthy, but since Your Majesty trusts me so, I can only do my utmost, ready to go through fire and water, sparing no effort.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded.","And immediately after, all kinds of voices flooded his mind.","The Empress Dowager: [Good boy, I haven't pampered him in vain!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So the difference between him being \"good\" and \"not good\" was just Qi Shuguang?","Yanshu: [Ahhh the Emperor agreed! My idol can stay!!! Now he'll be even closer to the Empress Dowager!!! CP fans rejoice!!! I must give the Emperor lots of kisses when we get back!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So the kisses later were earned by Qi Shuguang...","And the others: [That's good, this hot potato finally has an owner. This capital is too scary, wishing Old Qi well!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","As if he had begged them to be headmaster?!!!","Sigh, how exhausting.","With the Emperor's word, the position of headmaster of Songhe Academy was settled.","Having resolved the big issue, there was no need to worry about any more overt or covert attacks, so the guests drank even more freely.","Seeing that night had fallen and it was getting late, the banquet was coming to an end.","The guests bowed and said their farewells, filing out of the garden.","To keep things simple today, Yanshu had hitched a ride in the Empress Dowager's carriage, and now she was still riding back to the palace with her.","It was clear that after finalizing Scholar Qi's appointment tonight, the Empress Dowager was in a good mood. Not only had she drunk some wine earlier, but now she occasionally glanced outside through the carriage curtains blown by the night breeze, with a hint of a smile in her eyes.","Yanshu saw this and felt even more excited.","Hehe, from now on Scholar Qi would stay in the capital, so the two of them would be closer. Would they be able to hear news of each other, and maybe even meet a few times...","Compared to before when they were separated with no news of each other, this was already great progress, she thought with a flutter.","She must have been too absorbed in her thoughts, as she didn't control her expression well. Suddenly, the Empress Dowager asked her, \"Why do you look so happy? Did something good happen?\"","Yanshu was startled and quickly made up an excuse, \"Oh... actually, I was just thinking about what Madam Gu said at the banquet tonight about her past with Mr. Gu. I found it quite amusing. Who would have thought that the famous Mr. Gu, such a talented scholar, would set up a fortune-telling stall on the street just to catch a glimpse of Madam Gu when he was young? The mental image is just so entertaining.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager also chuckled, sighing, \"Indeed! Who hasn't done foolish things when young? It's fortunate they found the right person. For a couple to grow old together is a rare and precious blessing.\"","As she finished speaking, she inwardly sighed, unable to help wondering what kind of life she would have had if she had met that person before she was married.","Yanshu, observant of the Empress Dowager's expressions, noticed her smile fade and a contemplative look appear on her face. Guessing that the Empress Dowager was thinking of herself, Yanshu quickly changed the subject, \"Actually, beautiful stories like Mr. and Madam Gu's are probably what people enjoy reading. If the Carefree Gentleman could write some stories like that, they would likely be very popular.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Indeed. I hope he writes more. I'm counting on his stories to pass the time.\"","Yanshu nodded, suddenly feeling energized - for the happiness of her number one fan, she had to work hard on updating her stories!!!","Changchun Garden wasn't far from the palace, so it didn't take long for Yanshu to return to Ganlu Palace.","She was in high spirits today and had drunk quite a bit of wine, leaving her smelling of alcohol. So as soon as she returned, she went to take a bath.","Not long after she finished bathing, Yuwen Lan arrived.","He seemed to have already bathed at Qianming Palace, having changed from his dragon-emblazoned robes to casual round-collared robes, making him look much softer.","But he seemed somewhat impatient. Before she could even bow, he scooped her up and carried her to the bed.","The maids quickly lowered their heads and retreated, closing the door behind them.","In an instant, his kisses fell upon her.","Yanshu was in a good mood and had planned to go along with it, but suddenly remembered something important. She pushed him away and said with a serious face, \"Your Majesty also drank tonight.\"","Yuwen Lan, caught up in the moment, casually replied, \"So what? Didn't you drink too?\"","He tried to continue, but Yanshu froze, quickly saying, \"Oh right, how could I have drunk too? This won't do, this won't do at all. It seems there's no hope for this entire month.\"","This entire month???","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"There's no need to be so anxious. I don't believe the late Emperor never drank when... I'm not... Is everything alright?\"","Saying this, he pulled her firmly into his arms, trying to kiss her again.","However, he accidentally touched her ticklish spot, causing her to burst into giggles.","Yuwen Lan was eager to continue, but as she laughed, she suddenly covered her mouth, looking as if she was about to retch.","He was startled and quickly asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Yanshu covered her mouth and tried to calm down, saying, \"Maybe I ate too much. Laughing made me feel a bit nauseous.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This girl, why did she eat so much?","It was the first time he'd heard of someone laughing until they felt sick.","Realizing they probably couldn't continue, he asked, \"Do you want some water to help settle your stomach?\"","Yanshu nodded, about to say yes, but before she could speak, another wave of nausea hit her.","Hmm, something seemed a bit off."]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76","paragraphs":["Noticing that she had felt nauseous twice in a short time, Yanshu sensed something was amiss.","Apart from a slight allergy to peach blossoms, she considered herself quite healthy. Why was she feeling this way tonight?","Could it be...","That she ate something she shouldn't have at Changchun Garden earlier?","Startled, she immediately asked the system, [What's going on? Is someone trying to harm me???]","Tsk, this system had been so lackadaisical lately. How could it not warn her about such a serious matter!","The system was quite exasperated and could only tell her, [I suggest you see a doctor. While checking your nausea, you might want to get your head examined too, to see if there's a short circuit somewhere.]","Yanshu: [???]","Why would it say such a thing to her?","Well, it seemed no one was trying to harm her after all.","But why did it say she had a short circuit...","Just then, she heard Yuwen Lan ask, \"Are you feeling unwell? Should I summon the imperial physician?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Yes, please help your subject summon Imperial Physician Jiang.\"","Yuwen Lan agreed and hurriedly put on his robe to call for someone outside.","Before long, Imperial Physician Jiang arrived with his medicine box.","During this time, Yanshu had felt nauseous two more times, making Yuwen Lan very anxious. As soon as he saw the physician arrive, he immediately ordered, \"Quickly examine Consort Yi. She's not feeling well and has been nauseous all night.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang complied and hurriedly began to check Yanshu's pulse.","Yanshu felt nervous and closely watched the physician's expression. She saw him first maintain a neutral face, then suddenly furrow his brow.","Yanshu was startled, but then heard him ask, \"When was Your Highness's last menstrual period?\"","Before Yanshu could speak, the equally nervous Rendong quickly said, \"Her Highness's last period was ten days ago.\"","Yanshu nodded hurriedly. Because she was squeamish about blood, Rendong always helped her during her periods, so Rendong knew clearly.","Then the physician asked again, \"Then, was there any change in this period? Was it lighter and shorter than usual?\"","Rendong quickly replied, \"That's right. Usually, Her Highness's period lasts five or six days, but this time it only lasted two or three days, and the bleeding was much less.\"","As she finished speaking, they saw Imperial Physician Jiang nod slightly and say calmly, \"That's it then. Your Highness is with child.\"","\"What?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, a chorus of surprised exclamations filled the hall.","Yuwen Lan's eyes widened as he looked at Yanshu, then back at the imperial physician. For the first time in his life, he began to stammer, \"What, what did you say? What's happened to Consort Yi?\"","Imperial Physician Jiang had to clear his throat and repeat to him, \"Your Majesty, Consort Yi is carrying the imperial heir. It seems to be about a month along.\"","\"!!!\"","As the words sank in, Yuwen Lan paused, and an incredible feeling surged through him.","He was going to have a child! Yanshu was carrying his child!!!","Along with his wild joy, he even felt his nose start to tingle with emotion—","He was finally going to have a child!","After enduring over three years of dark days, heaven knows how momentous this news was for him!!!","The emperor was immersed in his joy, for the first time in his life not hiding his inner feelings, grinning from ear to ear with happiness.","The palace servants in the hall also broke into smiles, kneeling down to offer congratulations, \"Congratulations, Your Majesty! Congratulations, Your Highness!\"","Fu Hai, who was leading them, had even begun to tear up.","Oh, His Majesty finally has an heir, it's so moving!!!","However, only Yanshu remained in a daze.","What? She was pregnant???","How could it be so sudden???","She, she, she had a little one in her belly?","She was going to be a mother???...","After being stunned for a while, she quickly asked the physician, \"But what about the period I had a few days ago? Isn't it true that you don't have periods when you're pregnant?\"","The physician replied, \"This isn't absolute. In fact, many women like yourself still have a small amount of bleeding in the first month, but it's not a true period, which is why the bleeding is lighter and shorter. You are indeed with child. The nausea you felt earlier is just an early pregnancy symptom.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, no wonder the system told her to get her head checked...","So it was pregnancy symptoms...","Oh my, she was actually... just like that, going to be a mom?","Although she had dragged the emperor to see a doctor last time, when the day actually arrived, it still felt somewhat unbelievable.","Looking around, apart from the experienced and calm Imperial Physician Jiang, everyone else was in a state of wild joy. Rendong was already wiping away tears, and even Fu Hai's eyes were red-rimmed.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Why were they even more excited than her?","Looking at the emperor again, he was grinning like the village idiot. Seeing everyone kneeling to offer congratulations, he waved his hand generously and said, \"Rise. The servants of Ganlu Palace have done well in serving Consort Yi. Rewards for all!\"","As his words fell, everyone kowtowed again in thanks, the sound echoing to the ceiling.","Yuwen Lan then looked at Imperial Physician Jiang and nodded, \"Imperial Physician Jiang's medical skills are superb. Reward him with a hundred taels of silver!\"","He hadn't given any consultation fee before, but this time he gave it all at once.","Naturally, Imperial Physician Jiang couldn't refuse. He quickly knelt to express his gratitude, \"This subject thanks Your Majesty for the great kindness.\"","Then they heard the emperor instruct, \"This is Consort Yi's first pregnancy. You must take extra care in looking after her to ensure the safety of both mother and child.\"","Imperial Physician Jiang quickly agreed, \"This subject will do his utmost and spare no effort.\"","Yanshu thought to herself, it was rare to see the emperor so generous. It was clear he was very happy.","But then again, for a man who had been unable to father children for three years, finally having a child was the most face-saving thing that could happen.","Thinking of it this way, she actually felt a bit moved too!","But come to think of it, he had rewarded everyone else, hadn't he thought about rewarding her? At least give her a few hundred taels of silver or something...","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Even when about to become a mother, she was still so money-minded?","But then again, how could a few hundred taels of silver be enough?","This was his imperial heir!","This was his first child!","So he looked at her again and said with a smile, \"Consort Yi is carrying the imperial heir, a great merit. I hereby promote her to the rank of Imperial Consort.\"","As his words fell, he saw the young woman before him freeze in shock.","What... promoted to Imperial Consort?","Before Yanshu could react, everyone had already congratulated her again, \"Congratulations, Imperial Consort Yi!\"","Yanshu: \"?!!!\"","She, she, she had become an Imperial Consort just like that?","Let's see, how much higher was an Imperial Consort's monthly allowance compared to a Consort's?","It seemed to be a hundred taels of silver more per month!!!","Tsk tsk tsk, that would be one thousand two hundred taels more in a year!!!","What a profit!!! This was absolutely worth it!!! Even if she had to vomit every day, it would be worth it!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Why was she so different from others?","That night, Ganlu Palace was filled with joyous surprise.","Early the next morning, the Empress Dowager in the Palace of Benevolent Peace also received the news.","She immediately exclaimed in surprise, \"What? Consort Yi is with child?\"","Fu Hai nodded with a smile, \"Yes, Empress Dowager. Imperial Physician Jiang diagnosed that Imperial Consort Yi is already over a month pregnant. Last night, His Majesty was overjoyed and immediately promoted her rank.\"","The Empress Dowager was naturally delighted as well, and couldn't help but smile, \"This is indeed good news.\"","The promotion was fine. That girl was indeed quite good, and moreover, there wasn't a single Imperial Consort in the palace, which wasn't proper.","This was like a weight off her shoulders. She had been worried that the emperor might not have fully recovered, but who would have thought an imperial heir would come along directly.","It seemed that young Imperial Physician Jiang did indeed have some skill.","With this, she could set aside her greatest worry.","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"I should also bestow some rewards on Imperial Consort Yi.\"","She then instructed Zhu Shu, \"Take two top-grade Changbai Mountain ginseng, two boxes of Liaodong sea cucumber, a pair of Tianshan jade ruyi scepters, and two bolts of Jinling brocade from the storehouse, and send them to Ganlu Palace.\"","She didn't forget to add, \"Tell Imperial Consort Yi not to rush to come and thank me. She's newly pregnant and must be feeling unwell. She should rest well.\"","Zhu Shu complied and left to deliver the gifts.","Fu Hai, having reported the good news, also took his leave happily.","The hall became quiet for a moment, and the Empress Dowager smiled as she went to light some incense at the shrine.","When she returned from offering incense, she saw Nanny Zhuang come forward to report, \"I heard that this morning, His Majesty issued an edict not only promoting Imperial Consort Yi's rank but also elevating the Marquis of Loyal Righteousness to a higher nobility rank and granting his wife a third-rank title.\"","The Empress Dowager responded without much reaction, \"Since she's already been promoted to Imperial Consort, what's wrong with her family being promoted along with her?\"","Nanny Zhuang hesitated, then could only say with a smile, \"How dare this servant question His Majesty's edict? It's just that I'm a bit concerned. After all, Imperial Consort Yi has just conceived the imperial heir. Such extensive promotions, I wonder if it might not be... good for the imperial heir.\"","\"Silence!\"","Before she could finish speaking, the Empress Dowager coldly interrupted, \"If these words were to spread, you'd be charged with cursing the imperial heir, and that would be more than enough!\"","Nanny Zhuang was startled and quickly knelt down, saying, \"Please forgive me, Your Majesty. This servant has erred.\"","The Empress Dowager closed her eyes briefly and sighed, \"Go kneel in the Buddhist hall for three days and pray for the imperial heir's blessing.\"","Nanny Zhuang had no choice but to comply, leaving the hall with her head down, slinking off to the Buddhist hall.","Meanwhile, in Ganlu Palace, Yanshu was writing at her desk.","Apart from feeling a bit nauseous last night, she had been in good spirits lately.","Moreover, the Emperor had suddenly elevated her rank last night, and now the Ministry of Rites was preparing for her investiture ceremony. She expected that people from the Imperial Wardrobe Bureau, the Office of Imperial Treasures, and other such places would soon arrive to take her measurements for clothing and deliver jewelry.","She anticipated becoming quite busy.","She hadn't forgotten her promise to the Empress Dowager to write a sweet story, so she was taking advantage of this free time to quickly draft one.","After all, even though she had been promoted to consort, she was still the beloved author Xiao Yao to her readers, and she couldn't let them down.","As she was writing, she heard someone outside say, \"Is Consort Yi present?\"","She recognized Zhu Shu's voice immediately and guessed that the Empress Dowager was looking for her.","She responded, \"I'm here, come in.\"","As she spoke, she rose from her desk.","Due to the little one in her belly, she was following the doctor's orders and moving carefully, not daring to be too quick.","As a result, when Zhu Shu entered the hall, she saw Yanshu just standing up and putting down her pen.","Zhu Shu noticed this but said nothing, only smiling as she said, \"Congratulations on carrying the imperial heir, Your Highness. The Empress Dowager has sent ginseng, a jade ruyi scepter, and cloud brocade ginseng, hoping you will take good care of yourself.\"","As she spoke, she instructed the others to present the gifts one by one.","Yanshu quickly smiled and said, \"Thank the Empress Dowager for her gifts. I will go to the Palace of Benevolent Peace later to express my gratitude.\"","Zhu Shu added, \"The Empress Dowager says there's no need for Your Highness to rush. Taking care of your health comes first.\"","Yanshu responded with another \"yes\" and then called Rendong to receive the gifts, not forgetting to reward Zhu Shu and the others with some silver.","Zhu Shu accepted, thanked her with a smile, and then took her leave.","Yanshu instructed Rendong to put away the gifts and returned to her desk to continue writing.","\"Aww, my top fan is so caring...\" she thought. She could only repay such kindness by updating her story quickly.","However, not long after, just as she was getting into the flow of writing, she heard a \"ding\" from the system, [Watch out, Zhu Shu is planning to report you to the Empress Dowager.]","Yanshu: [??? Why is she reporting me?]","System: [Because she saw you writing with a pen earlier and thinks you've kept the lake pen the Empress Dowager gave to Xiao Yao for yourself.]","Yanshu: [???]"]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Yanshu was somewhat confused and frowned, saying, \"What did you say?\"","System: \"When Zhu Shu came in earlier, she saw the brush in your hand, which looked the same as the one the Empress Dowager had her deliver to Qianming Palace two days ago. She became suspicious, so after returning to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, she went to check the inventory and confirmed it was indeed from the batch gifted to the Empress Dowager. She thinks you've kept the brush the Empress Dowager bestowed on the 'Carefree Gentleman' for yourself.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","This situation was truly unexpected.","Actually, after the Empress Dowager had bestowed gifts on the \"Carefree Gentleman\" that day, Yuwen Lan had secretly delivered them to her.","But she wasn't foolish enough to use them openly.","The brush she was using now was actually one specially given to her by the Emperor, who saw that she was afraid to use the one from the Empress Dowager for fear of revealing her identity.","She had been using this imperial brush to write for the past few days, and no one who saw it had said anything. Who would have thought Zhu Shu would interpret it this way?","Hearing the System's explanation now, she suddenly found herself in a dilemma.","It was foreseeable that if Zhu Shu reported this to the Empress Dowager, she would certainly become suspicious.","Even if she brought the Emperor to testify that he had given her the brush, the Empress Dowager might not completely dismiss her doubts.","Unless the Carefree Gentleman himself came before the Empress Dowager holding the brush and said he had received it, it seemed impossible to resolve.","However, wasn't she the Carefree Gentleman?","\"...\"","This problem had become a vicious cycle, and Yanshu was getting a headache.","Then she heard the System sigh and say, \"If you walk by the river long enough, your shoes are bound to get wet. Did you think you could keep this disguise forever? Since you'll have to reveal it sooner or later, why not do it now? After all, you're carrying the imperial heir now, so the Empress Dowager probably won't be too harsh on you no matter how angry she gets.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Although that was true, she really didn't want to anger the Empress Dowager!","She was her number one supporter!","And the female lead of her favorite ship!","How could she let the Empress Dowager dislike her? Sob.","However...","From their recent interactions, the Empress Dowager didn't seem to be a rigid person.","So... even if she found out the Carefree Gentleman wasn't a man, she wouldn't be too angry, right?","Then she heard the System say, \"But a few days ago when the Empress Dowager said she wanted to meet the Carefree Gentleman, you made up all sorts of excuses to avoid it.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","That's true. In the end, it was her dishonesty that started all this. If the Empress Dowager learned the truth now, she might really get angry...","Wuwuwu, this was her number one supporter! She didn't want to lose her biggest fan!!!","As she was struggling with this difficult decision, she heard the System say, \"Look, Zhu Shu is already speaking to the Empress Dowager about it.\"","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","She finally steeled her resolve. Rather than being passively summoned by the Empress Dowager, it would be better to take the initiative to confess. So she hurriedly got up and walked out.","Rendong anxiously said, \"My Lady, please be careful. The doctor said you need to be cautious...\"","But Yanshu instructed her, \"Come, go tell His Majesty something for me.\"","She then whispered something in her ear.","Rendong quickly agreed and hurried off to Qianming Palace.","Yanshu then got into her palanquin and headed to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Oh right, after being promoted to the rank of consort, she finally had her own means of transportation. That was another piece of good news.","Meanwhile, in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Zhu Shu was reporting to the Empress Dowager, \"Your Highness, I have already delivered the gifts you bestowed to Consort Yi.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly and asked, \"How is Consort Yi doing?\"","Zhu Shu lowered her head and replied, \"Consort Yi seemed to be in good spirits. When I arrived, she was writing at her desk.\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound of acknowledgment and smiled, \"She's still practicing her writing even while pregnant? Quite diligent, isn't she?\"","Ever since she started writing novels, Yanshu had been using the excuse of practicing calligraphy. So apart from the Emperor, Fu Hai, Rendong, and a few others who knew the truth, everyone else thought she was just practicing her writing.","However, as soon as the Empress Dowager finished speaking, Zhu Shu added, \"But Your Highness, I noticed that the brush Consort Yi was using... looked very similar to the one you bestowed upon the Carefree Gentleman last time.\"","\"Oh?\" The Empress Dowager paused.","Before she could say anything more, a palace servant announced from outside, \"Consort Yi requests an audience.\"","The Empress Dowager composed herself and nodded, \"Let her in.\"","The servant acknowledged the order.","Soon after, Yanshu entered.","\"This subject greets the Empress Dowager.\"","The Empress Dowager, seated on her warm couch, nodded, her expression neutral. She said, \"Rise. Didn't I say there was no need to rush here to thank me? Why have you come?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Last night, Doctor Jiang said that this subject's condition was not serious and that I could engage in moderate activity. Since that's the case, having received Your Highness's gifts, it would be remiss of me not to come and express my gratitude.\"","She then added solemnly, \"This subject thanks the Empress Dowager for her generous gifts.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded again, \"This is His Majesty's first heir. You have indeed worked hard. Being your first pregnancy, you must be careful at all times. Tell those serving you to be extra vigilant. It's crucial that the imperial heir is born safely.\"","Yanshu nodded and said she would, then voluntarily added, \"His Majesty raised this subject's rank last night.\"","The Empress Dowager replied in a calm voice, \"I already know. This is His Majesty's love for you. You should fulfill your duties well and strive to repay his favor.\"","Yanshu nodded quickly.","But inwardly, she felt something was off—","The Empress Dowager's attitude towards her today seemed a bit more distant than it had been a couple of days ago.","Tsk, could it be that she really had become suspicious of her...","Well, since she was already here, she might as well take a gamble.","So she coughed lightly and said, \"This subject has something to report to Your Highness.\"","The Empress Dowager, still maintaining a neutral expression, asked, \"What is it?\"","Yanshu coughed again, \"This matter is of great importance...\"","The Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow, deciding to give her the benefit of the doubt, and waved for everyone else to leave.","With no one else in the hall, Yanshu finally said, \"Actually... this subject is the Carefree Gentleman.\"","As soon as she said this, the Empress Dowager was stunned.","\"What did you say?\"","Yanshu knelt down again and repeated slowly, \"This subject is actually the one who writes the novels under the name of the Carefree Gentleman. I didn't report the truth to Your Highness before, which is truly a capital offense. I beg for Your Highness's forgiveness.\"","This time, the Empress Dowager heard clearly, but she was still shocked. She looked at Yanshu for a long while before asking, \"Those novels were really written by you?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"Yes.\"","The Empress Dowager gasped, \"How do you... have such talent?\"","Yanshu steeled herself and explained, \"Initially, His Majesty wanted to find someone to write novels based on cases investigated by the Imperial Guard. When I learned of this, I boldly volunteered to try. After I finished writing, His Majesty found it passable and had it published. Since then, I've continued writing.\"","The Empress Dowager still looked at her in amazement, \"You tried writing and produced such excellent work?\"","Yanshu added, \"Actually, this subject has loved reading novels since childhood. Perhaps because I've read so many, writing comes naturally to me.\"","The Empress Dowager couldn't help but exclaim, \"You're being quite modest.\"","She then asked, \"But why did you use a man's name?\"","Yanshu had to explain her initial reasoning to the Empress Dowager again, \"Because many people nowadays are prejudiced against women. I was afraid that if I used a woman's name, they might not even give the book a chance.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"While that reasoning makes sense, the fact remains that people still believe they're reading novels written by a man, so their prejudice against women hasn't changed.\"","Yanshu quickly said, \"It was this subject's oversight.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed again, \"Never mind, it's not your fault. You're just one young woman, you can't change much on your own.\"","Yanshu nodded quickly, thinking to herself that this was her compromise with reality.","But before she could finish nodding, the Empress Dowager suddenly changed her tone and said coldly, \"But last time when I asked you, why didn't you tell me the truth? When I bestowed gifts on you, why did you have His Majesty pass them on?\"","Yanshu quickly lowered her head and said, \"Yes, this subject was short-sighted at that time. I thought Your Highness might be angry if you suddenly learned the truth, so I lied to Your Highness...\"","The Empress Dowager snorted, \"And now you're not afraid of my anger?\"","Yanshu hurriedly explained, \"This subject has been struggling internally for a long time. I wanted to report the truth to Your Highness several times, but I was afraid Your Highness wouldn't like me anymore... After all, Your Highness has been so trusting of me and has liked my novels so much...\"","At this point, she couldn't help but shed tears, and continued, \"Especially after receiving the Empress Dowager's rewards this morning, I feel extremely guilty. That's why I finally made up my mind to tell the truth to Your Majesty. If Your Majesty is angry with me, it's justified. I dare not hope for Your Majesty's forgiveness.\"","As she spoke, she wiped her tears again.","But in fact, these words were spoken with genuine sincerity. She truly didn't want to lose the love of her top fan! Sob...","After she finished speaking, there was a moment of silence in the hall.","Then came the sound of the Empress Dowager sighing.","\"I knew you were a clever one. Well, you're carrying the imperial heir, so get up.\"","Yanshu was stunned. Had the Empress Dowager forgiven her?!","Tsk, the System was right indeed!!!","This was the best opportunity for honesty, and she had won the gamble!!!","Her heart leaped with joy, and she quickly kowtowed in gratitude before standing up.","However, at that moment, an announcement came from outside, \"His Majesty has arrived...\"","Both Yanshu and the Empress Dowager were taken aback. Then, they saw Yuwen Lan enter the hall.","As soon as he came in, he anxiously scanned the room, seeming a bit rushed.","The Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow and said, \"Why has Your Majesty come at this time?\"","Yanshu was also a bit puzzled. She had only asked Rendong to inform him that she might need to confess the truth to the Empress Dowager, but she hadn't asked him to come.","Yuwen Lan was indeed full of anxiety, thinking to himself, how could he not come?","— The Empress Dowager was known for her strict standards. If she found out that he had been deceived by Yanshu for so long, who knew how she would treat her.","So he rushed over as soon as he heard the news.","\"I just finished with state affairs and thought that since Consort Yi is with child, it's a significant matter. So I wanted to personally report it to Mother Empress,\" he said.","Then he pretended to be surprised to see Yanshu, \"I didn't expect Consort Yi to be here as well?\"","Yanshu could only nod.","Unexpectedly, the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"I just found out today that the Carefree Gentleman was right under our noses. Your Majesty has kept this secret from me quite well.\"","Only then did Yuwen Lan realize that Yanshu had already confessed. He had no choice but to say, \"I... was afraid that Mother Empress wouldn't accept that the Carefree Gentleman was a woman at first, so I had no choice but to resort to this strategy.\"","Inwardly, he wondered if the Empress Dowager hadn't reprimanded her, judging from the earlier atmosphere in the hall.","Then he heard the Empress Dowager say, \"I was indeed surprised, but I am a woman myself. How could I look down on women?\"","As she spoke, she looked Yanshu up and down again, shaking her head and sighing, \"I truly didn't expect that there was such a talent in the harem.\"","Yanshu smiled bashfully and said, \"Your Majesty praises me too much. Actually, the person I admire most... is you! I was just writing a story about Master Gu and his wife in the hall, intending to let you read it soon.\"","The Empress Dowager snorted with laughter, \"You always know how to please me. Now that you're pregnant, you must prioritize your health. Rest when you're tired, don't rush to write.\"","As she spoke, she marveled inwardly, surprised that such a young girl had such talent, writing stories that always kept her on the edge of her seat.","Wait a minute?","Since she was the Carefree Gentleman...","Wouldn't that mean she could read new stories earlier from now on?","Just as she was thinking this, Yanshu voluntarily said, \"In the future, when I finish a new story, I will definitely let Your Majesty read it first.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded with satisfaction, \"That's more like it.\"","Then she heard Yanshu say, \"I've received many interesting letters from readers these days, which I've kept specifically to share with Your Majesty someday.\"","The Empress Dowager's eyes lit up, \"That sounds wonderful!\"","She couldn't help but ask, \"Why don't you tell me about some of them now? What kind of things are there?\"","...","Yuwen Lan silently observed all this, suddenly feeling a bit out of place.","He felt that these two women were more like mother and daughter.","Also, shouldn't he be the first to read her stories?","Why had it suddenly changed to someone else?"]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78","paragraphs":["As Yanshu had just become pregnant, and Yuwen Lan still had government affairs to attend to, after placating the Empress Dowager, the two bid farewell and left the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","With the Emperor present, Yanshu dispensed with the sedan chair and rode directly in the imperial carriage on the way back.","At this time, with no outsiders in the spacious carriage, Yuwen Lan asked Yanshu, \"It was just a matter of a lake brush. I could have easily explained it for you. Why did you feel the need to hurriedly reveal your identity to the Empress Dowager?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Although Your Majesty covered for me this time, what about next time? Moreover, when I saw how Zhu Shu spoke just now, the Empress Dowager had already become suspicious of me. Even if we manage to explain it away, I suspect the Empress Dowager will not feel the same about me as before. Besides, the Empress Dowager greatly enjoys my novels. If one day she insists on meeting the 'Carefree Young Master', am I supposed to find someone else to impersonate me? If the Empress Dowager learns the truth then, I'm afraid she'll be even angrier.\"","Initially, she had felt the Empress Dowager was a dangerous figure. If she knew those novels were written by her, she might use it as an excuse to punish her. After spending more time together, she realized the Empress Dowager was actually quite nice, and since she enjoyed her novels so much, she probably wouldn't use it against her.","So it was better to take this opportunity to come clean, rather than having to hide and make excuses in the future.","Between people, it's actually better to be a bit more honest.","Yuwen Lan listened and felt it made sense, so he nodded, \"Very well. In the future, if the Empress Dowager bestows more gifts, I won't need to pass them on anymore.\"","She was right - it was better to be honest sooner rather than later. Most importantly, the Empress Dowager had accepted it, which wasn't a bad outcome.","Yanshu nodded, but suddenly frowned and said, \"Come to think of it, does Zhu Shu have some issue with me? Why did she immediately assume I was concealing the Empress Dowager's gift when she saw me use the lake brush? Does she think I'm a bad person?\"","Before Yuwen Lan could respond, the system chimed in, [It's simple. Zhu Shu actually likes the Emperor and has always seen you as a love rival.]","Yanshu let out a sound of surprise, [Zhu Shu likes the Emperor???]","The system replied, [Why so many question marks? Is it that unbelievable? After all, the Emperor is quite handsome. Zhu Shu came to serve the Empress Dowager when she was only thirteen, and at that time the Emperor was just ten. They basically grew up together.]","Yanshu stammered, [But, but, but... the Emperor couldn't perform before.]","Yuwen Lan, who had been secretly listening, felt a twitch between his brows.","Why suddenly bring this up again?","That was all in the past, okay!","The system continued, [She didn't know the Emperor couldn't perform before! Just like Consort Zhou, Consort Ning, and Consort An, they all thought the Emperor was a normal man. With such a handsome, powerful, young and vigorous man, it's hard not to like him.]","Yanshu was speechless.","That's true. Who else in the world would be like her, not minding the Emperor's inability to perform?","Thinking of this, she unconsciously touched her belly, secretly marveling that the saying \"with enough perseverance, an iron rod can be ground into a needle\" was indeed true.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","That's the wrong idiom!","\"Patience is rewarded\" would be more appropriate!","What do you mean by grinding an iron rod into a needle?!","Yanshu returned to Ganlu Palace in the imperial carriage. Not long after, people from the Imperial Wardrobe Bureau and the Office of Imperial Treasures arrived.","They were busy taking measurements for new clothes and selecting jewelry for quite some time.","The next day, the imperial edict for her formal appointment was issued. After the conferment ceremony, she officially became Imperial Consort Yi.","Her family outside the palace, the Household of the Earl of Loyalty and Righteousness, was officially elevated to become the Marquis of Loyal Righteousness's Mansion, inspiring much envy.","Meanwhile, in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Nanny Zhuang, who had finally been allowed to leave after kneeling in the Buddha hall for three days, was now weeping bitterly before the Empress Dowager, begging for forgiveness.","\"This slave forgot her place in a moment of anxiety. Please forgive me, Your Highness.\"","The Empress Dowager still spoke coldly, \"His Majesty has an heir now. What are you anxious about?\"","Nanny Zhuang cried, \"This slave was entrusted by the old master and mistress to help Your Highness maintain the glory of the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion. Who would have thought that now, watching others about to give birth to the emperor's firstborn son, this slave couldn't help but feel resentful on behalf of the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion!\"","Having been mistress and servant for decades, and since this was a maid she had brought from her maiden home, the Empress Dowager knew her words were not false. She could only sigh, \"What is there to resent? I have done my best these past twenty years. If they themselves are incompetent, what can be done?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Nanny Zhuang quickly wiped her tears and said, \"After all that has happened, I expect the Duke of Cheng'en has reformed. Now the third young miss has also grown up. The third young miss has a gentle disposition, as you know...\"","Before she could finish, the Empress Dowager raised her hand to stop her and said, \"Do you think entering the palace is a good thing? If one can live well outside, why come into the palace to suffer this darkness? Why go and ruin the third girl's life? Do you think I'm living happily now?\"","If she could choose again, she would never enter the palace. Looking back, her whole life seems to have been wasted like this.","Nanny Zhuang frowned and said, \"But aren't you worried about what will happen to the Zhou family in the future?\"","The Empress Dowager gave a cold laugh, \"That's for the Zhou family to worry about themselves. Out of consideration for our years as mistress and servant, if you still want to stay by my side, just do your duty. If you don't want to, I'll find a place outside the palace to settle you, and we need never see each other again.\"","Nanny Zhuang paused, then could only cry again, \"How could this slave abandon Your Highness and go outside the palace? From now on, this slave will never mention this matter again.\"","As her pregnancy progressed day by day, Yanshu's symptoms became more and more severe.","At first, she could still eat, but later she would feel nauseous at the smell of meat and oily foods, and vomited for several days in a row.","Seeing his beloved consort's face noticeably thinner in just a few days, the Emperor was naturally worried. After some thought, he had no choice but to send someone to the Marquis of Loyal Righteousness's Mansion to invite the Marchioness into the palace.","As someone who had been through it herself, Ms. Zhu knew her daughter was going through a difficult time. So she specially prepared some of her daughter's favorite foods from before and brought them into the palace.","As soon as Yanshu saw her mother, she smelled the aroma she had been dreaming of.","Chive dumplings!!!","Before her mother could speak, she asked eagerly, \"Mother, did you bring chive dumplings?\"","Ms. Zhu smiled and opened the package she had brought, \"The young mistress has a keen nose indeed. Here, I just made these before getting in the carriage. They're still warm.\"","As she spoke, she handed over a warm chive dumpling.","Yanshu was like a traveler who had journeyed long through the desert and finally found an oasis. She immediately took it and stuffed it into her mouth.","Mmm, it was indeed her mother's handmade chive dumpling. The pastry had a rustic wheat fragrance. Knowing that she was currently averse to oily foods, her mother had only used tofu and chives for the filling, and had used almost no oil when pan-frying. It tasted light and pure, yet very flavorful. It was exactly to her liking. In just a few bites, she had finished one.","Seeing this, her mother Ms. Zhu worriedly handed her some tea and advised, \"Eat slowly, my dear. There are plenty more. Don't choke.\"","Yanshu made a sound of acknowledgment and picked up another one. In no time at all, it too had gone into her stomach.","Mmm, her stomach, which had been feeling acidic for days, finally had something in it. She felt much better.","Yanshu drank two more cups of tea before asking her mother, \"How is everything at home recently? How are you and father? How is grandmother's health?\"","Ms. Zhu nodded quickly, \"Everything is fine at home, don't worry and just focus on taking care of yourself. Your grandmother is doing well too. She had originally... wanted to come along today, but when the eunuch delivering the imperial edict said His Majesty hoped I could stay in the palace for a couple of days, she didn't dare come and stayed at home instead.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, \"Is that what His Majesty said? That's wonderful!\"","Having her mother by her side was like having a spiritual pillar, making her body, tormented by pregnancy symptoms, feel somewhat better.","Ms. Zhu nodded, \"That's what the eunuch delivering the edict said. I specially brought a few more changes of clothes.\"","Yanshu quickly said that was good and told Lianxin to prepare a room for her mother.","After making the arrangements, she asked, \"How is Tianrui doing at the Imperial Academy? Has he adjusted well?\"","Come to think of it, in the blink of an eye, her brother Li Tianrui had already been at the Imperial Academy for three months.","Unfortunately, due to protocol, although Yanshu had seen her parents and grandmother, she still hadn't seen her brother.","Mother nodded and said, \"He's doing well too. Being admitted to the Imperial Academy has really made a difference. Not only has he learned a lot, but his temperament has also improved. Just the other day, he was cheated while buying something on Examination Hall Street. In the past, he would have gotten into a fight right away, but now he knows his position is different. He didn't want to tarnish your reputation, so he managed to control himself.\"","Yanshu found this curious and quickly asked, \"What happened when he was cheated?\"","Ms. Zhu explained, \"Well, you know Examination Hall Street is where they sell all the scholar's four treasures, right? At the Imperial Academy, they're required to use white hemp paper for writing. That day, he had run out of paper, so he went to Examination Hall Street to buy some. But when he got it, he realized something was off about the paper. He wanted to argue with the shopkeeper, but luckily, someone advised him against it, so he didn't pursue it further and went somewhere else to buy paper instead.\"","Ms. Zhu added pointedly, \"Your father has warned him that now that we've been elevated to a Marquis's household, many eyes are watching us from the outside. It's better to suffer a small loss than to cause a scene that might affect you.\"","Yanshu nodded, understanding her father's good intentions.","After all, Li Tianrui was now the heir to a Marquis's household. If he got into an argument with a shopkeeper over paper, who knows if someone might accuse him of bullying commoners.","Considering her brother's youthful temper, it must have been difficult for him to hold back.","Just then, her mother frowned and said, \"Come to think of it, it's strange. I don't know what's going on with Examination Hall Street, but several paper shops there are passing off inferior goods as high-quality ones. Tianrui went to several places before finally finding genuine white hemp paper at a small shop next to our house.\"","Yanshu also found this odd. Examination Hall Street was supposed to be the most famous place in the capital for buying stationery. Most students went there for their supplies. How could the shopkeepers dare to sell substandard goods, making it impossible to buy good paper?","The system chimed in, [It's simple. Someone in the court is using their position for personal gain, monopolizing the main stationery shops in the capital.]","Yanshu was stunned. [How could someone be so bold? Who is it?]","The system replied, [The man's name is Bao Qiwen. He's currently the Director of Studies at the Imperial Academy, responsible for its daily affairs. A few years ago, he secretly opened a paper mill outside the city. He's been selling cheap hemp sandpaper as white hemp paper, controlling the supply for several stationery shops on Examination Hall Street. Moreover, he's also supplying the Imperial Academy and several other government-affiliated academies. The students are all using his paper.]","Yanshu was puzzled. [He's being so blatant about it? Hasn't anyone noticed?]","The system explained, [He's been in this position at the Imperial Academy for many years and has built good relationships with many academies. Besides, he provides good paper for the teachers and inferior paper for the students. The students are young and naive, and the teachers are afraid of causing trouble. Plus, it's all paid for with government money, so who wants to bother with it?]","Yanshu gasped, [Each academy has at least several hundred students using paper every day. That's a huge consumption. He must be making a fortune!]","The system confirmed, [Indeed. Over the years, he's made a killing. He's practically the number one rat stealing from the government.]","Yanshu asked, [Has no one discovered this?]","The system sighed, [This man is excellent at feigning poverty. He still lives in an old house from over a decade ago, one that even leaks when it rains. His clothes are washed until they're faded, and he and his wife eat simple meals daily. He appears extremely frugal. Who would suspect him?]","Yanshu was bewildered, [Then what's the point of making all this ill-gotten money? He's not enjoying any of it!]","The system replied, [Who says he's not enjoying it? In fact, many years ago, he bought the best lakeside mansion in the luxurious Golden Bright Pond area of the capital. It's filled with beautiful serving girls, creating a veritable paradise of wine and pleasure. He goes there every few days to indulge himself.]","Yanshu was speechless. [...] What a character!"]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79","paragraphs":["This melon is definitely one of the most ridiculous stories Yanshu has ever heard.","This Mr. Bao, the big rat, pretends to be poor at home with his wife, eating bran and swallowing vegetables, while secretly enjoying a lavish life of wine and meat outside???","She hurriedly asked the system again, \"Does his wife know about this?\"","The system replied, \"Know about what? The lavish lifestyle? Of course not. Bao Qiwen's wife Madam Du is known to be a fierce tigress. If she knew about this, she would have chopped him up long ago.\"","Yanshu said, \"I mean, does his wife know about him embezzling from the government and making ill-gotten gains?\"","The system made an \"oh\" sound, \"She knows about that. Not only does she know, but she's quite supportive of it. That's why she's willing to pretend to be poor with him. Otherwise, given his position as a government official with a decent annual salary, they shouldn't be this poor, right?\"","But Yanshu was still confused and quickly asked, \"If she knows, hasn't his wife wondered where all the money went? After all, that lavish lifestyle must cost quite a bit!\"","The system sighed, \"This man takes a small portion of the dirty money each month to give to his wife, and secretly keeps the majority for himself. Since it's a lot of money, even that small portion is quite substantial. Plus, Madam Du is just a housewife who hasn't had much education and doesn't know his real accounts, so she's never suspected him. She diligently pretends to be poor with him every day, just hoping that one day when they've made enough dirty money, they can leave the capital and enjoy life back home.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, it seems there's an issue of unfair distribution of spoils in the Bao household.","Of course, looking at it this way, Madam Du isn't innocent either. It's just that Mr. Bao is even more cunning.","Thinking of this, she suddenly couldn't help but smirk—","The system just said that Bao's wife is a tigress?","Tsk tsk tsk tsk, if she ever finds out about his lavish lifestyle one day...","Now that would be interesting!!!","After learning about the situation from the system, Yanshu said to her mother, \"Father's right, it's good that Tianrui could hold back this time. After all, if there's something fishy going on, it's not something our family can change. But believe that bad people will always get their comeuppance, after all, heaven's net is wide-meshed, but lets nothing through!\"","Ms. Zhu also nodded quickly, \"Who says otherwise? Besides, the Emperor is wise and brilliant, he certainly won't tolerate such wicked deeds.\"","Yanshu made a sound of agreement. Perhaps because she was full from eating chive dumplings, drowsiness suddenly came over her, and she couldn't help but yawn.","Ms. Zhu said, \"Your Highness, go get some sleep. At first, there's nothing else to do but eat when you want to eat and sleep when you want to sleep. You must not exhaust yourself. It will get better after this phase passes.\"","Yanshu nodded and instructed Rendong to also take her mother to rest, while she went to lie down on the couch.","Hmm, she had originally wanted to write a story, but unfortunately, her energy was really low, so she could only take it slow.","However, this matter wasn't urgent. After all, that Bao fellow hadn't just been embezzling for a day or two.","Why not take these few days to ponder it carefully? Maybe she could come up with something even more fun than writing a story, hehe.","So, Ms. Zhu stayed in the palace for two days.","Taking this opportunity, she not only made several hometown delicacies for her daughter but also instructed Rendong and Lianxin on some matters to pay attention to. She also took the chance to teach the imperial chefs how to make some of her daughter's favorite home-cooked dishes. On the third day, she bid farewell and left the palace.","As night fell, Yanshu welcomed the Emperor again.","For the past two days, Yuwen Lan hadn't been able to come over because Ms. Zhu was there. He had been missing his beloved consort terribly, so of course, he hurried over now to ease his longing.","When he arrived, he saw that Yanshu was in good spirits, and her little face seemed to have become rosier...","He finally felt somewhat relieved.","Taking advantage of the moment when no one else was around, he was just about to take his beloved consort into his arms and kiss her, but before his lips could touch hers, he heard Yanshu say to him, \"Your subject just learned of something a couple of days ago and wishes to report it to Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"What is it?\"","He then heard her say, \"It turns out that Bao Qiwen, the Director of Studies at the Imperial Academy, has privately opened a paper-making workshop. He's using cheap hemp sand paper as a substitute for white hemp paper, and using his position at the Imperial Academy to replace all the paper used by students of the Imperial Academy and its affiliated academies with the inferior paper from his own workshop. He's also made all the stationery shops in the Exam Hall Street sell his paper. Over the years, this man has been making a fortune in secret, and he even built himself a place of indulgence by the Golden Bright Lake, where he goes to enjoy himself every few days.\"","What?","After hearing this, it took Yuwen Lan a moment to understand what she had said.","\"Bao Qiwen, the Director of Studies at the Imperial Academy, is abusing his position for personal gain and harming students? And he even built a place of indulgence by the Golden Bright Lake?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"That's exactly what I mean, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"How could this be happening?\"","How could the Imperial Censorate and the Imperial Guard in the court have failed to discover this?","Yanshu nodded again and said, \"The information is reliable. His place of indulgence is built in Lihua Lane by the Golden Bright Lake, in the courtyard closest to the lake. There's a three-story pavilion inside that offers a full view of the Golden Bright Lake, truly a peerless vista. It's said that he spent ten thousand taels of silver to buy it. All from embezzling from the government.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan could no longer sit still and was about to get up to call someone.","This was too infuriating!!!","What were those people in the Imperial Censorate doing???","However, before he could stand up, Yanshu pulled him back, saying, \"Your Majesty, please wait. I actually have an idea.\"","She then whispered something in his ear.","After listening, Yuwen Lan frowned and said, \"Isn't that too complicated?\"","Yanshu indeed looked excited, \"It may be complicated, but it will definitely be spectacular! Please, Your Majesty, please grant your subject's wish.\"","Yuwen Lan could only sigh, \"Alright.\"","After speaking, he gently tapped her nose and snorted with a laugh, \"You truly fear the world isn't chaotic enough.\"","Yanshu pouted, \"Of course, the more chaotic it is for bad people, the better!\"","After all, if things get more chaotic, wouldn't her stories sell even better?","The next morning.","In a seemingly ordinary civilian house in the city, the doorkeeper quickly walked into a room and said to Madam Du, Bao Qiwen's wife who was mending clothes, \"Madam, someone outside is looking for the master.\"","To maintain their poor appearance, since coming to the capital, the Bao couple hadn't kept many servants. Apart from a doorkeeper who also did the sweeping, a handyman, and a coachman specifically for taking Bao Qiwen to his office every day, they had no other help.","Madam Du hadn't even dared to buy a maid, doing the cooking and laundry herself.","At this time, Bao Qiwen wasn't at home. Hearing what the doorkeeper said, Madam Du went to the door herself to check.","She saw a young man in his twenties, dressed in neat clothes that made him look like a clerk from some shop.","He was holding an exquisite wooden box in his hands, which seemed to contain something valuable.","However, considering that the couple had been pretending to be poor for so many years, they had never bought anything packaged so luxuriously.","Madam Du asked, \"Who are you looking for?\"","The man replied, \"I'm an employee from the Phoenix Pavilion, here to see Master Bao Qiwen.\"","...","Phoenix Pavilion?","The doorkeeper quickly glanced at Madam Du and said, \"Madam, isn't that the most famous jewelry shop in the capital?\"","Madam Du of course knew this, which made her even more curious. She asked again, \"What business do you have with my husband?\"","The man smiled and said, \"A few days ago, Master Bao ordered a custom-made pure gold plum blossom hairpin with multiple jewels from our shop. It was finally completed yesterday, but Master Bao didn't come to collect it. Since this hairpin is extremely valuable, our manager was worried about keeping it in the shop and instructed me to deliver it to Master Bao immediately. Is Master Bao at home?\"","What?","A pure gold plum blossom hairpin with multiple jewels?","Madam Du was stunned. This item sounded incredibly expensive. What did Bao Qiwen buy this for?","She tried asking, \"This must have cost quite a bit, right?\"","The clerk from the Phoenix Pavilion smiled and said, \"Indeed, it's not cheap. This hairpin is made of pure gold and uses over thirty natural rubies. The cost of materials alone is three thousand taels of silver. Our manager, considering Master Bao is a regular customer, only charged a small fee for craftsmanship.\"","What?","Three thousand taels of silver!","Upon hearing this, the doorkeeper was so shocked her mouth fell open.","Madam Du swayed, almost falling to the ground.","That Bao Qiwen! How dare he spend three thousand taels of silver on a hairpin???","You should know that for all these years, she had been pretending to be poor and hadn't even worn accessories worth more than ten taels of silver!!!","And this shop assistant even said that Bao Qiwen was a regular customer???","That scoundrel! Who did he give this hairpin and all those past ones to!!!","Madam Du's anger instantly shot up to the sky, but in front of strangers, she could only try her best to suppress it and said, \"I am Mrs. Bao. Our master is not here today, so please give the hairpin to me.\"","As she reached out to take it, the shop assistant unexpectedly refused, saying, \"Mr. Bao specifically instructed that this item must be handed to him personally. Since he's not here, I'll come back another day.\"","With that, he quickly ran off with the box and soon disappeared.","The entrance returned to calm, but Madam Du could no longer find peace.","Her mind kept wondering if Bao Qiwen had been doing something behind her back all these years.","Otherwise, why would he buy this hairpin?","Of course, she couldn't help but fantasize a little - could it be that her husband saw how hard she had been working and wanted to surprise her with a piece of jewelry?","...","All sorts of possibilities floated in Madam Du's mind, but as two or three days passed and Bao Qiwen didn't mention a word about the hairpin, she finally came to her senses.","So, one day when Bao Qiwen went out again, she steeled her heart and hired a carriage to follow him.","...","After coming up with the idea, Yanshu waited for three days in the palace before finally hearing news from the system.","[Heads up, Bao Qiwen's wife followed him for a day and just discovered the den of iniquity by the Golden Bright Pool.]","Yanshu: [!!!]","At that moment, she was having dinner with Yuwen Lan. Upon hearing this, she could no longer focus on her food and immediately asked, [What's the situation? Did they have a catfight?]","System: [There's no need for a catfight. Madam Du has absolute crushing power! After going in and finding her stingy husband stark naked and embracing a beauty while dancing, she immediately started beating him up, thrashing Bao Qiwen until he had nowhere to escape.]","Yanshu could only sigh, \"Good grief!\" Indeed, being stark naked doesn't leave much room for escape!","But come to think of it, how dare this Bao fellow play such a dangerous game???","To actually be stark! naked!","Ugh... just thinking about it burns the eyes!!!","Yuwen Lan, who was listening on the side: \"???\"","Stark naked???","That Bao fellow???","Fortunately, Yanshu didn't...","plan on keeping this juicy gossip to herself. After all, such interesting matters are even more fun when shared. So, she quickly dismissed everyone around and excitedly said to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, I just received news that our plan has worked! Bao Qiwen was caught red-handed fooling around outside today by his wife. Right now, his wife has stormed into that den of iniquity and is beating him up all over the place, hahaha!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Tsk tsk tsk tsk tsk.","Ahem, although he was the emperor, apart from this sound, he really couldn't think of how else to express his feelings at the moment.","However, seeing her laugh so hard that she was doubling over, he became a bit worried. Would laughing so intensely be bad for the baby?","But at this moment, how could Yanshu care about anything else?","Listening to the system's live broadcast, even if she wanted to stop, she couldn't!","Tsk tsk tsk, just imagining the scene of Bao Qiwen being beaten by his wife, wailing and scrambling around, was enough to make one die of laughter!","But just then, the system said, [Alright, there happened to be roast lamb there today. Madam Du grabbed the knife for cutting lamb meat and cut off his thing.]","Yanshu: [!!!]","Madam Du was actually this fierce!!!","What didn't happen to the Princess back then actually happened now!!!","Tsk, but thinking about it, it makes sense. With nothing in the way, cutting it off would be quite convenient."]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80","paragraphs":["Of course, such an exciting scene couldn't be described in just one simple sentence, could it?","Yanshu immediately asked the system for more details: \"Quick! Tell me more! How exactly did Madam Du do the cutting?\"","The system explained: \"Well, after Madam Du entered that luxurious mansion by Golden Bright Pond, she saw all the women inside were barely clothed, while that Bao Qiwen was in such a state. The anger she had been suppressing for so many days must have all exploded at once. Just punching Mr. Bao a couple times certainly wouldn't be enough to vent her rage. After all, she had suffered alongside this man for so many years, and yet he was secretly indulging himself like this behind her back. To make matters worse, she spotted a whole lamb being roasted in the courtyard, which made her even more furious!\"","\"After all, lamb is so expensive! She had deprived herself to keep up appearances in the capital, hardly eating it three times a year, and this man dared to secretly roast a whole one! As luck would have it, there was a knife for carving meat right next to the roast lamb. Madam Du was suddenly filled with murderous rage. Without a second thought, she grabbed the knife. It wasn't much different from all the times she had butchered chickens and fish while cooking over the years. So while that dog of a man Bao was lying on the ground after she kicked him, she went ahead and made the cut with one stroke of the knife.\"","After listening, Yanshu couldn't help but click her tongue repeatedly in amazement.","She quickly shared the news with a certain someone beside her: \"Your Majesty, breaking news - Bao Qiwen's wife Madam Du has castrated him.\"","\"Pfft...\"","Yuwen Lan had just raised a spoonful of hot soup to his lips when he heard this, and nearly choked. After coughing several times, he finally managed to compose himself and frowned at her, asking: \"What did you say? Castrated?\"","Yanshu blinked her innocent big eyes and nodded, \"Yes, she just cut it right off with one slice.\" As she spoke, she even made a cutting motion.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Then he heard her clicking her tongue in her mind again: \"Good heavens, you probably only get to see something like this once in a lifetime! It's such a shame I couldn't witness it in person!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Witness it in person?","Wasn't she the one who fainted at the sight of blood?","But come to think of it, women certainly do seem to have an enthusiasm for cutting... that part. Tsk.","How frightening.","However, since things had progressed to this point, he figured the Imperial Guard must be taking action by now. So he set down his soup bowl and said, \"I'm going to the Imperial Study for a while. Take your time eating.\"","He made sure to add: \"Don't keep thinking about all that nonsense.\"","With that, he stood up and left the hall.","Yanshu was left behind, confused. What nonsense?","The castration?","Tsk, it's not like she wanted to think about it. It was the surprise that Madam Du and the common people of the city brought, hehe!","Speaking of which, she hadn't finished getting all the juicy details yet. So Yanshu quickly asked the system again: \"What's the situation now?\"","The system replied: \"Right now there's blood splattered everywhere, that Bao fellow is howling in agony, and the women are all screaming in terror. Madam Du was about to stab him a couple more times, but just then the Imperial Guard broke down the door, so she didn't get the chance.\"","Yanshu let out an \"Oh\", thinking it was probably for the best that she didn't get to stab him more. This Bao had swindled so many people - if he died by his wife's knife today, he'd be getting off too easy!","No good. With this thought, she couldn't be bothered to keep eating. She hurried to her writing desk to finish the half-written story she had been working on.","After all, someone who had done so many despicable deeds shouldn't just die - his crimes should be exposed to the world first, so he could be thoroughly cursed by everyone!","Early the next morning, shocking news that stunned the entire city and rocked both the common people and officials broke.","Last night, a bloody incident occurred in a luxurious residence by Golden Bright Pond - it turned out that Bao Qiwen, the Director of Studies at the Imperial Academy, had his... private parts cut off by his wife Madam Du???","Of course, the Empress Dowager in the Palace of Benevolent Peace also learned of this news.","Just as she was feeling greatly astonished, she saw Yanshu come to her, holding a storybook.","\"Your Highness, this is the new story by the Carefree Young Master. Your humble servant just had someone buy it back. Would you like me to read it to you?\"","Only the Empress Dowager knew her pen name in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, so with others present, she could only speak this way.","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager quickly waved for the attendants to withdraw. Once the hall was empty of others, she hurriedly asked: \"Is this a new story you've written? What's it called?\"","Yanshu nodded quickly, \"Indeed, your servant just finished writing it last night. This story is called 'Furious Wife Chops Off Black-Hearted Husband'.\"","The Empress Dowager couldn't help but let out a thoughtful \"Hmm\" upon hearing the title. Why did it sound so much like what happened to the Bao family?","So she hastily said, \"Quick, tell me about it.\"","She also added, \"You don't need to read it word for word, just focus on the important parts. You're pregnant, so you mustn't tire yourself out.\"","Aww, her number one fan was so considerate. Yanshu promptly agreed and began telling the Empress Dowager the story:","\"There was a family in the capital where the husband worked as an official in charge of students' education. This man had suffered from poverty since childhood, so he was extremely greedy for money. After getting this position, he started thinking of ways to use his official duties to line his own pockets. He thought about it and realized that the paper used by students in the academy was something he could profit from. So, he secretly opened a paper mill in the capital.\"","\"While others made paper using proper materials, he was different. He deliberately used cheap, shoddy materials to make low-quality paper, then used his position to sell this paper to various academies under the government, cheating money from the state. You might think one sheet of paper is cheap, but when you add up all the paper used by students in various academies, it becomes quite a substantial income. Most importantly, paper is one of the most easily consumed items.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded quickly, \"Indeed! Those students use paper to write every day! In this way, hasn't he reaped plenty of ill-gotten gains?\"","Yanshu nodded hurriedly, \"Exactly. Such huge profits were obvious, fattening this man up like a big rat. But he was still quite cautious and didn't dare to show off. He even deliberately pretended to be poor, hiding with his wife in a leaky old house every day, eating plain food, not even daring to hire a single maid.\"","The Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow, \"Could it be that he wanted to take all that money to his grave? Or was he secretly living it up outside while making his wife suffer?\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"Your Highness is so perceptive, it's pretty much like that. This man pretended to be poor at home, but in the most expensive area by Golden Bright Pond, he spent ten thousand taels of silver to buy a luxurious mansion. He even arranged for many beautiful servant girls there, creating a veritable paradise of wine and women for himself, which he would go enjoy every few days. His wife truly had no idea about this.\"","The Empress Dowager was startled, \"A luxurious mansion by Golden Bright Pond? It seems this really is about that Bao couple?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"That's right, it's about them. Your Highness must have heard too, last night Bao Qiwen's wife Madam Du castrated him.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded vigorously, \"I heard about it as soon as I woke up this morning. I was just wondering what on earth happened. I didn't expect you to have already written about it! Quickly, tell me all the details.\"","Yanshu promptly agreed. At this point, she didn't need the storybook anymore, so she just started chatting with the Empress Dowager about what actually happened last night: \"I heard that this Madam Du is actually quite a fierce woman, keeping Bao Qiwen under tight control in their daily life. She knew about Bao Qiwen cheating the government from the very beginning, which is why she played along with him in pretending to be poor.\"","The Empress Dowager suddenly understood, \"I was wondering, how could even a Director of Studies at the Imperial Academy not be able to afford a single maid? I thought at first that this Madam Du was an innocent victim of deception, but it seems she was also an... accomplice.\"","Yanshu nodded quickly, \"She certainly was, but Bao Qiwen was even more cunning. I heard that a few days ago, Bao Qiwen went to a jewelry shop outside and spent lavishly on accessories for the beauties in his secret paradise. This slip-up allowed Madam Du to find out. She became suspicious and followed Bao Qiwen for several days in a row. Last night, she happened to follow him all the way to that luxurious mansion by Golden Bright Pond.\"","The Empress Dowager drew in a sharp breath, already able to imagine the scene. She hurriedly asked, \"So Madam Du immediately... ahem... did that to him on the spot? She really is a fierce woman! What happened after that? Did Bao Qiwen die?\"","Yanshu explained, \"Actually, His Majesty had heard rumors a few days ago and had people lying in wait around that area. As soon as the incident occurred last night, they immediately rushed in. From what I've heard, Bao Qiwen didn't die, but he lost quite a lot of blood and is in a somewhat half-dead state.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"That's good then. This man cheated the government out of so much money - if he died so easily, wouldn't that be letting him off too lightly!\"","Yanshu nodded quickly, then heard the Empress Dowager say, \"Your story is well-written. Once it's published, everyone in the world will see his true face. However, this matter is of great importance, and we can't let him off just because he's half-dead.\"","Yanshu made a sound of agreement. \"His Majesty ordered the Imperial Censorate to intervene this morning. I believe they won't go easy on him.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly. \"That's good.\"","She then looked at Yanshu again and sighed, \"It must have been difficult for you to come so early to tell me about this. Have you eaten breakfast?\"","Yanshu replied, \"I had a little. I mainly rushed over because I was worried Your Highness would be anxious.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"A little isn't enough! You're carrying twins now, you absolutely must not neglect yourself. What would you like to eat right now? I'll have someone prepare it, and you can eat here.\"","Yanshu was moved beyond words and could only repeatedly express her gratitude, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Highness.\"","Inwardly, she thought, \"Indeed, my number one supporter still treats me the best.\"","At that moment, outside the hall, Nanny Zhuang was quietly asking Zhu Shu, \"Why does Her Highness close the door now when talking to the Favored Consort?\"","Zhu Shu only said, \"I don't know either.\"","However, in her heart, she was pondering. Ever since she mentioned the matter of the lake pen to the Empress Dowager, and the Favored Consort and His Majesty rushed over anxiously to speak with the Empress Dowager, Her Highness seemed to trust the Favored Consort even more.","Could this Favored Consort be bewitching people's hearts?","...","Just as Yanshu had predicted, while the whole city was shocked by the news of the Bao couple, her story was published right on time. The obviously suggestive name immediately aroused everyone's curiosity.","In an instant, sales were even more explosive than before, increasing by 30%.","After reading it, people also understood the hidden truth behind the Bao family's bloody case. Everyone couldn't help but curse the black-hearted Bao couple.","Of course, some people were also curious and wanted to explore the true face of the \"lakes of wine and forests of meat\" by the Golden Bright Pool. Ahem.","However, unfortunately, since it was both the crime scene and evidence of corruption, it had already been sealed off by the authorities, and for the time being, it was impossible to peek inside.","But it was said that in recent days, it had become a tourist attraction, with many civilians and tourists flocking to the front door to imagine the grand scenes inside.","This was something Yanshu truly hadn't anticipated.","If she had known, she would have invested in opening a bookstore nearby to sell her stories!","The sales would probably have been even better, tsk.","Of course, this wasn't important.","What was important was that not long after, the court's verdict came down. Bao Qiwen was found guilty of abusing his position for personal gain and accepting bribes and corruption. He was sentenced to immediate execution. His wife, Madam Du, was also sentenced to exile for the crime of harboring a criminal.","It could be said that justice was served, to everyone's satisfaction.","Upon receiving the verdict, Yanshu was very pleased. She made a special trip to the Palace of Benevolent Peace to share this good news with her... number one supporter.","The Empress Dowager was also very satisfied and nodded to her, saying, \"You've made quite a contribution in this matter. If it weren't for your story stirring up public indignation, the Imperial Censorate might not have handled the case so well and concluded it so quickly.\"","Yanshu hurriedly replied modestly, \"I wouldn't dare claim credit. This matter mainly relied on His Majesty's wisdom and power.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded again.","After a moment, she sighed and said, \"Speaking of which, Songhe Academy is set to open in a few days.\"","Yanshu was stunned for a moment, then quickly nodded and said, \"Yes, I heard it's the day after tomorrow.\"","Inwardly, she couldn't help but wonder, could it be that the Empress Dowager wanted to see Chancellor Qi?","Come to think of it, it had been many days since their meeting at Changchun Garden!","Oh my, as a shipper, she must find a way to lend a helping hand to her number one supporter!"]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81","paragraphs":["After Emperor Yuwen Lan personally appointed Qi Shuguang as the headmaster at Changchun Garden some days ago, other preparatory work for Songhe Academy was also completed in recent days.","The Ministry of Rites had set an auspicious date for the opening ceremony, which was to be the day after tomorrow.","After returning to Ganlu Palace from the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu had been pondering this matter.","When the emperor arrived in the evening, she took the opportunity during their casual conversation after retiring to bed to ask Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, I heard that four famous scholars will be debating at the opening ceremony of Songhe Academy the day after tomorrow. Is that true?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of agreement and pulled her into his embrace, saying, \"That's right, it was arranged by the Ministry of Rites. After all, once the day after tomorrow passes, these scholars will return to their hometowns. It's not easy for them to come to the capital, so we should let the students personally experience the demeanor of great scholars. Perhaps they will all benefit from it.\"","He then looked at her and asked, \"Why are you bringing this up?\"","Yanshu replied, \"I just heard the palace maids mention it today and thought it was an excellent idea. However... as you said, it's rare to gather all these famous scholars together. It seems a pity to only let the students listen.\"","Yuwen Lan asked, puzzled, \"A pity? How could it not be a pity?\"","Yanshu shook her head and said, \"The ancients said, 'To love learning in youth is like the rising sun; to love learning in middle age is like the noonday sun; to love learning in old age is like the light of a candle.' Experiencing famous scholars' debates is a good thing. Your Majesty should make this debate open to all the common people of the empire, letting anyone who wants to listen come and hear. If so, I believe those scholars would be very happy too.\"","Yuwen Lan was speechless.","Tsk, when did she become so eloquent?","However, her words did make some sense. After all, opening it to the whole empire and attracting more people to watch would have a greater impact.","This would also be good for rebuilding Songhe Academy's reputation.","He nodded, \"It's worth considering. Tomorrow I'll have the Ministry of Rites make preparations.\"","As he spoke, he placed his hand on her lower abdomen and asked softly, \"Tell me, how big is he now?\"","After all, it was his first time being a father, and he was filled with all kinds of curiosity and expectations.","Yanshu thought for a moment and made a gesture indicating the size of a peanut, saying, \"Probably about this big.\"","Yuwen Lan mused, \"I wonder if it's a boy or a girl, and what they will look like?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Your Majesty's flesh and blood will surely be extraordinary, excelling like you do.\"","That was natural, after all, it was his child!","Yuwen Lan felt proud inwardly, but before he could speak, he heard her continue, \"However, there's a saying that genius is 99% hard work and 1% talent. We should focus on the postnatal efforts we can make.\"","Yuwen Lan asked, \"... What does '99%' mean? What are you talking about?\"","Yanshu faltered, realizing she had gone off-script, and hastily explained, \"It means nine out of ten.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, looking thoughtful, \"That expression does seem more precise.\"","Yanshu quickly agreed and then got to her point, \"What I mean is, although the imperial heir is small, we should expose them to good things early. This way, they might be even more outstanding when born. Why don't you take me to listen to the scholars' debate on that occasion? Wouldn't it be better to expose the imperial heir to the wisdom of worthy people early on?\"","Yuwen Lan was speechless.","Alright, he finally understood. So after such a roundabout way, this was her real goal.","Pregnant and still wanting to go out?","He looked at her amusedly and said, \"Didn't you just say he's only this small? How could he understand anything?\"","Yanshu was stunned for a moment, then quickly argued, \"This is called prenatal education. Haven't you heard of it, Your Majesty?\"","She continued, shaking her head, \"It's said that 'external image affects internal feelings' and 'feelings cause changes.' Although the imperial heir is small now, I can understand what's being said. My feelings will be transmitted to him through our blood connection, so he can naturally receive it too.\"","Yuwen Lan was speechless again.","It was rare for her to come up with so many ancient sayings at once. She really put in a lot of effort just to be able to leave the palace.","He said, \"Alright then, I'll have someone make preparations.\"","It wasn't a big deal. If she wanted to go, he might as well take her along.","She immediately smiled and replied, \"Thank you, Your Majesty.\"","Then she added, \"However, it might not be appropriate for just Your Majesty and me to go. Why don't we ask the Empress Dowager tomorrow morning if she would like to join us?\"","Yuwen Lan was puzzled.","The Empress Dowager?","Wasn't this about prenatal education? Why bring up the Empress Dowager?","A bad feeling suddenly arose.","Then he heard her think, [To make the Empress Dowager and Scholar Qi meet again, I can only do this! I'm helping you make your mother happy! Quick, agree!]","Yuwen Lan knew it.","To be honest, he seemed to have developed a condition where he would think of the Empress Dowager whenever he heard Qi Shuguang's name...","He said, \"The Empress Dowager probably doesn't like noise and chaos. She might not want to go.\"","Yanshu replied, \"This isn't an ordinary noisy situation. Why don't I personally ask the Empress Dowager tomorrow? If we don't even ask, wouldn't that seem disrespectful to her?\"","However, even after she finished speaking, he still didn't agree, hesitating and seemingly lost in thought.","Yanshu had a sudden inspiration. She pretended to feel sick, got out of bed, ran to the spittoon, and covered her mouth, saying, \"Ugh... I don't feel well. I want to throw up...\"","In her mind, she thought, [Hmph, let's see if you still won't agree after I use this trick.]","Yuwen Lan was speechless.","Was this really so shallow?","He didn't say anything for a moment, just raising an eyebrow as he watched her.","Yanshu didn't give up and pretended to retch a couple more times.","However, perhaps because she acted too convincingly, after a couple of tries, she really started to vomit, her face turning pale.","Yuwen Lan was startled and quickly came to her side, asking, \"Are you alright?\"","She looked at him with a pale face and weakly said, \"If Your Majesty agrees to my request, I might feel better...\"","Yuwen Lan was bewildered.","Was she really so unreasonable?","Before he could speak, she started vomiting again. Not only was her face pale, but cold sweat appeared on her forehead. She looked so miserable that it was hard to tell if it was real or fake.","Yuwen Lan had no choice but to say, \"Alright, alright, I agree. Tomorrow morning I'll have someone ask the Empress Dowager. If she's willing, we might as well go together.\"","He quickly helped support her.","Yanshu barely regained her composure and said in a hoarse voice, \"Your Majesty is wise.\"","Yuwen Lan was speechless.","Was it really necessary to make herself vomit until her voice was hoarse just to get the Empress Dowager to meet Qi Shuguang?","Then he heard her think triumphantly, [For the sake of their relationship, what does it matter if I vomit a few times!]","Yuwen Lan thought, \"... That's really not necessary.\"","So, early the next morning, the Empress Dowager received the news.","Yanshu personally reported it to her.","The Empress Dowager was surprised and asked, \"Why would His Majesty think of doing this?\"","Yanshu quickly used the arguments she had used to persuade Yuwen Lan the night before, saying, \"Because His Majesty loves his people like his own children, he feels that for such a grand event, it would be best to let all the common people of the empire listen. This way, it would also let the world see the new face of Songhe Academy and have a positive influence.\"","\"That makes sense.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, then hesitated and said, \"But if I go too... wouldn't that make it too grand an occasion?\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"Wouldn't a grand occasion show how much importance the court places on this? If the court shows its importance, the teachers at the academy will have more confidence in teaching, and the students will be more motivated to learn, won't they?\"","The Empress Dowager thought for a moment, then said, \"Very well. Since His Majesty has this intention, I should also do my part for the court. Let's go tomorrow then.\"","Yanshu was overjoyed and nodded vigorously in agreement.","Thus, the next day, the three of them from the palace set out together.","Of course, to avoid overshadowing the main event, neither the emperor nor the Empress Dowager used overly elaborate processions, and their attire was much more casual, showing their closeness to the people and their respect for the way of the sages.","The common people, having received advance notice, were exceptionally enthusiastic, all rushing to arrive early. Some even set out from the outskirts of the capital the night before, just to catch a glimpse of the great scholars.","Seeing this scene, Yuwen Lan felt somewhat gratified. While indulging her wishes, he had also done something useful, which wasn't bad.","In any case, when the people have a desire to learn, there is hope for the empire.","To accommodate everyone as much as possible, the lecture platform was set up in the square in front of Songhe Academy.","The common people who came to listen to the lecture had already found their places and were seated on the ground, creating a quaint and rustic atmosphere.","Of course, to show respect and for security considerations, the Emperor, Empress, and Empress Dowager had their own special VIP seats set up near the lecture platform on the side closer to the academy.","Nearby, several important ministers and scholars were also in attendance, making the occasion quite grand.","When the time came, four world-renowned Confucian scholars began their lectures.","The first to take the stage was Mr. Yu from Nanyang, who spoke on the principle: \"To judge right and wrong, use a measuring line; to judge right and wrong in behavior, use names.\" Mr. Yu was skilled in using historical allusions, and his wide-ranging references left the audience enlightened.","Next to take the stage was Mr. Gu from Lanling.","Perhaps due to his happy family life, Mr. Gu had a naturally approachable demeanor and a great sense of humor. He explained the Confucian concept of \"filial piety and brotherly love\" in simple terms that everyone could understand, earning frequent applause.","The third to appear was Mr. Ji from Jinling City, renowned for his vast knowledge. He gave a magnificent discourse on ritual governance, moral governance, and human governance, using a wealth of classical quotations that left the officials in attendance full of admiration.","After the three had finished, the star of this forum, the newly appointed Chancellor of Songhe Academy, Mr. Qi Shuguang, took the stage.","As the most important figure of the forum, everyone had been extremely curious about him, and now all eyes eagerly turned to him.","Although already in his forties, this scholar still had the bearing of a slender bamboo, humble and elegant with an innate nobility.","One glance was enough to tell he was no ordinary person.","At this moment, the eyes of the entire audience were on him, but he showed not the slightest nervousness. Instead, he calmly began to speak, lecturing on the concept of \"Great impartiality and utmost sincerity, with the people as the foundation of the state.\"","For a moment, the whole venue fell silent.","In the VIP seats, Yuwen Lan also temporarily set aside his distractions and listened attentively.","At this point, he had to admit that this man was indeed very talented, humble yet composed, impartial and selfless - truly the best candidate for the position of Chancellor.","After half an hour, when Qi Shuguang's words came to an end, the venue immediately erupted in waves of applause and admiring exclamations.","Among these voices, the one Yuwen Lan found hardest to deal with was still Yanshu's inner voice.","[Ah, ah, ah, my idol is indeed amazing!!! The Empress Dowager must be very pleased! The most excellent man in the world and the most excellent woman in the world, they're simply... perfect for each other!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","How come in her heart, the most excellent man in the world wasn't him?","But this wasn't the end of it. He heard her cry out again, [Quick, quick, let the Empress Dowager say a few words to the Grand Scholar!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This was all going smoothly, he hadn't even spoken yet, and now she wanted the Empress Dowager to speak to Qi Shuguang? Wouldn't that be a bit too abrupt?","At this moment, Qi Shuguang was still standing on the lecture platform, nodding in acknowledgment to the audience members cheering for him.","To prevent Yanshu from screaming again, Yuwen Lan decided to say something.","However, before he could open his mouth, he suddenly saw someone throw a bouquet of flowers towards the lecture platform.","It landed perfectly in Chancellor Qi's arms.","Seeing this, everyone was startled.","Yanshu hurriedly looked closely and saw that the flower-thrower seemed to be a woman wearing a veil hat. Her age couldn't be determined, but the exposed parts of her dress appeared to be made of fine material.","Tsk, a woman throwing flowers at a man in public - that had quite a significant meaning.","Yanshu's heart sank, and she quickly asked the system, [Who is this woman? How could she throw flowers at Scholar Qi in front of so many people? Isn't that a bit too frivolous?]","The system let out an \"oh-ho\" and said, [This one is formidable! This woman is the famous noble lady Princess Shou'an, who is also the Emperor's maternal aunt. She's known for her romantic nature, and it seems she's taken a liking to your idol!]","Yanshu: [???]","How could this be? How could she allow someone else to interfere with her ship?!!!"]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82","paragraphs":["What kind of flirtatious noblewoman?","How dare she extend her evil claws towards her idol!!!","Yanshu was very angry and quickly asked the system: [What's the background of this Princess Shou'an? Why haven't I seen her before?]","The system replied: [Princess Shou'an is the niece of Emperor Gaozu, which makes her the cousin of the Former Emperor and the Grand Princess, and the aunt of the current Emperor. She has a passionate and outgoing nature. Years ago, she volunteered to marry into the Mu Prince's Mansion in Nanzhao and became the Mu Princess. However, her husband died after just two years, and since then, she's been living as a merry widow.]","Yanshu: [...]","Why did it sound like there was a hint of envy in that explanation?","Still, she didn't quite understand, so she hurriedly asked again, [After her husband died, doesn't she need to manage the household? Doesn't she have children?]","The system replied, [She has a son, but he was too young at the time. So after her husband's death, her brother-in-law Mu Zhengping ascended to the position, becoming the current Mu Prince. Princess Shou'an, of course, no longer needed to manage the household. As a member of the Yuwen Royal Family, and given the generations of friendship between Nanzhao and Great Liang, coupled with Nanzhao's naturally open-minded culture, even though she became a widow, she wasn't subject to many restrictions. She frequently travels between Nanzhao and Great Liang, often sightseeing and flirting with handsome men, living quite happily.]","Yanshu: [...]","Ahem, she had to admit, after hearing that, she felt even more envious.","But coming back to the point, no matter how good Princess Shou'an's life was or how much she loved to flirt with handsome men, the one standing on the podium now was Mr. Qi!","This was the world-renowned new principal of Songhe Academy, one of the Four Great Masters with a wealth of talent. How could she be so frivolous towards him?","Couldn't she go flirt with those young pretty boys instead? Why did she have to come here and make others uncomfortable!","If she was this angry, the Empress Dowager's heart must be even more upset!","But then the system added, [In Princess Shou'an's eyes, Mr. Qi is far beyond comparison to ordinary pretty boys! You think she's just attracted to his looks? Actually, she's been deeply in love with him for a long time.]","Deeply in love?","Tsk, it seems there's quite a story here.","Yanshu immediately said, [Quick, tell me the details.]","The system then explained, [This story goes back many years. When Princess Shou'an had just become a widow, she returned to the capital and stayed for a while. During that time, she flirted with many talented young men in the capital. However, no matter what she did, only Qi Shuguang remained unmoved. As the saying goes, the harder something is to obtain, the more it makes one obsess over it. So Princess Shou'an became increasingly fixated on Qi Shuguang.]","[But not long after, there was a period of instability in Nanzhao, and she was called back by people from the Mu Prince's Mansion, so she had to put her pursuit on hold. By the time she returned a few years later, Qi Shuguang had already resigned from his official post and returned to his hometown. Although Princess Shou'an has had many lovers over the years, Qi Shuguang, the one she couldn't have, became the one she couldn't stop thinking about.]","[Now, with the great scholars gathering in the capital, she heard the news from afar and was shocked to discover that Qi Shuguang, who had been out of touch for years, was among them. She immediately set out from Nanzhao. Unfortunately, the journey was quite long, which is why she's only just arrived.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","That journey was indeed quite far. It's a shame, as the scholars are set to leave in just two days.","After the system finished speaking, Yanshu couldn't help but frown inwardly, [So you're saying Princess Shou'an came specifically for Qi Shuguang?]","[...EMMMMM Especially since she's a well-known flirtatious noblewoman, does this mean Qi Shuguang has been stuck with a persistent admirer?]","As she was thinking this, she saw Princess Shou'an in the distance addressing Qi Shuguang, who was still stunned by the flower-throwing, \"It's been years since we last met, yet Scholar Qi still maintains such an outstanding demeanor.\"","Hm? Years since we last met?","Hearing her speak like this, the already curious crowd began to ponder—","From the sound of it, this veiled woman...","Was an old acquaintance of Principal Qi?","However, Qi Shuguang seemed to have no recollection of who she was, and still looked confused as he said, \"I'm not sure who you are, madam...\"","The woman then spoke with a hint of reproach in her voice, \"So the scholar has truly forgotten all about me.\"","With these words, the crowd once again raised their eyebrows—","From the sound of it, could there be some history between these two?","Yanshu immediately became anxious, shouting inwardly, [Hey! Princess Shou'an, you experienced player in love, stay away from our Scholar Qi! Don't you dare taint my pure and flawless male lead!!!]","She shouted so loudly that someone nearby wanted to cover their ears.","Yuwen Lan, who had been quietly observing the situation alongside Yanshu for a while, had already understood two things—","First, this woman who dared to throw flowers at Qi Shuguang was his aunt, Princess Shou'an.","Second, Princess Shou'an also had feelings for Qi Shuguang, and had come all this way just for him.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Who would have thought that Qi Shuguang was such a catch?","Thinking of this, he couldn't help but secretly listen to the Empress Dowager's thoughts, wanting to know her reaction to this scene.","He heard the Empress Dowager inwardly snort, [Sure enough, it's that thick-skinned Shou'an again!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","The Empress Dowager actually recognized her immediately.","How impressive?!!!","Well, he then hurriedly looked towards Qi Shuguang, inwardly raising an eyebrow, wondering how he would respond to this situation.","He saw Qi Shuguang pause for a moment, and then, bowing slightly to Princess Shou'an, smile and say, \"Please forgive this old man's dullness, madam. I don't seem to have any connection with you.\"","Princess Shou'an had no choice but to finally introduce herself, \"I am Princess Shou'an, Yuwen Rong. Does Mr. Qi remember now?\"","Princess Shou'an?","Qi Shuguang paused again, and then quickly stepped down from the podium, bowing to her and saying, \"So it's Princess Shou'an who has graced us with her presence. Please forgive this commoner's poor eyesight.\"","His attitude was neither servile nor overbearing, but quite forthright.","Seeing this, Yanshu breathed a sigh of relief, thinking, [As expected of my great scholar! He didn't fall for this flirtatious noblewoman's tricks. I hope the Empress Dowager doesn't misunderstand.]","Yuwen Lan, hearing this, paid attention to the Empress Dowager again.","He heard the Empress Dowager think, [That's more like it.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, that girl can rest assured, the Empress Dowager indeed didn't misunderstand.","Then he heard Yanshu pondering in her mind, [Come to think of it, shouldn't Princess Shou'an's first order of business upon returning to the capital be to pay respects to the Emperor and Empress Dowager? By openly revealing her identity like this, isn't she afraid of being punished for disrespect?]","The system sighed, [After all, she's still the Empress Dowager of Nanzhao, and she's the Emperor's elder. To maintain friendly relations with Nanzhao, the Emperor can't really blame her, can he?]","But no sooner had these words been spoken than Princess Shou'an temporarily bid farewell to Qi Shuguang and made her way towards the VIP seats where the Emperor was seated.","When she arrived, she removed her veil and bowed, saying, \"This subject, Shou'an, pays respects to Your Majesty and the Empress Dowager. I have just arrived in the capital today and, hearing that Your Majesties were here listening to the lecture, I hurried over to pay my respects.\"","Seeing this, Yanshu inwardly clicked her tongue. This Princess Shou'an was no fool. She had come specifically to see Scholar Qi, but with this act, it now appeared as if she had rushed here specifically to pay respects to the Emperor and Empress Dowager.","And just as the system had said, given the number of people present today and the special status of Princess Shou'an, Yuwen Lan couldn't really reproach her. He simply asked, \"So it's Aunt. I had no idea you had come to the capital?\"","Princess Shou'an quickly replied, \"With Your Majesty's auspicious birthday celebration coming up next month, I was worried about potential travel delays and set out early from Nanzhao. I had intended to send a messenger ahead to report my arrival, but due to terrible weather along the way, the messenger couldn't arrive in advance. Thus, I could only come in person to pay my respects and ask for forgiveness.\"","As these words fell, Yanshu couldn't help but click her tongue again, [Indeed, she's an old hand at love affairs, lies come easily to her. She came to see the handsome man, yet she claims it's to celebrate the Emperor's birthday early. Making the Emperor feel touched for nothing.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How could he be so easily moved?","However, Princess Shou'an's excuse was good enough, and he really couldn't say anything, so he just nodded and said, \"Aunt must have had a tiring journey.\"","Of course, the opening of Songhe Academy was the main event today, so after saying this, he didn't engage in further pleasantries with her.","And with Qi Shuguang's lecture now over, today's Great Scholars Forum had come to an end.","Following the announcement by the on-site ceremonial official, the common people began to disperse.","However, it was rare for the Emperor, Empress, and Empress Dowager to venture out, so they certainly couldn't simply return to the palace just like that.","Next, they were to personally tour the Songhe Academy, surrounded by officials.","Yanshu was very excited, knowing that leading the way at the front was none other than her idol, Dean Qi!","And between Dean Qi and the Empress Dowager, there was only the Emperor!","My, my, being able to walk like this, could it be considered a sightseeing trip for the two of them?","Hehe, just thinking about it was thrilling.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","To be honest, he still didn't quite understand her sense of humor and what angered her.","However, before the group could take a step, Princess Shou'an came up and said to Yuwen Lan, \"It's rare to encounter such a grand event today. May I have the honor of accompanying you all? Nanzhao has always revered Central Plains culture. I hope to take this opportunity to broaden my horizons, so that when I return to Nanzhao, I can build a proper academy to promote Central Plains culture.\"","Upon hearing this, Yanshu immediately became agitated again, inwardly grumbling, [Ugh, will this ever end?! This experienced player in romance is truly thick-skinned! How dare she follow us! Emperor, please don't agree to her request!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","However, before he could open his mouth, Mr. Yu of Nanyang, who had just given a lecture, and Mr. Ji of Jinling City both nodded in approval, \"It's commendable that the Princess has such a desire to learn. This is a good thing!\"","\"Indeed, Nanzhao and our dynasty have been friendly for generations. It's only right that we exchange more, allowing Central Plains culture to flourish. Please, Your Majesty, grant her permission.\"","Mr. Gu of Lanling didn't say anything, but quietly glanced at Qi Shuguang with a meaningful look in his eyes.","Qi Shuguang also didn't say anything, maintaining a solemn expression.","The other accompanying officials nodded as well, saying, \"It is indeed a good thing. Please agree, Your Majesty.\"","In such a situation, Yuwen Lan really had no reason to refuse, so he could only nod and say, \"Then please join us, Princess.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Princess Shou'an quickly agreed.","However, Yuwen Lan once again heard Yanshu's angry voice in his ear, [Hey Emperor, what's wrong with you?!!!]","\"...\"","He could only pretend not to hear.","Nevertheless, he couldn't help but try to listen to the Empress Dowager's thoughts—","He heard the Empress Dowager snort and laugh, saying, [Very well, let's see what tricks you can pull!]","Thus, the group began their tour of the academy.","Fortunately, due to the difference in status, Princess Shou'an could only walk behind Yanshu, unable to get close to Dean Qi, which somewhat comforted Yanshu.","Speaking of which, this academy truly deserved to be called the best in the capital. First of all, it was indeed large, with classrooms, living quarters, and dining halls for teachers and students, all complete. In addition, there were two spacious library buildings, storing various classics from famous authors, which could be described as very rich in content.","Most of the people present were scholars, and seeing the collection of books naturally piqued their interest. They began to search around, looking for books that suited their tastes.","Yuwen Lan also couldn't help but look around.","For a moment, there weren't many people around Dean Qi.","Seeing this situation, Princess Shou'an hurriedly approached him and said, \"It's been many years since we last met. I wonder if sir has started a family yet?\"","Qi Shuguang politely bowed his head and said, \"This humble one has not yet married.\"","Nearby, Yanshu, who was accompanying the Empress Dowager, caught sight of this scene and immediately became angry — hmph, how dare Princess Shou'an take this opportunity to chat up Scholar Qi?","Unacceptable!","So she took a few steps forward and said, \"Speaking of which, I've long heard that Nanzhao has spring-like weather all year round, with all kinds of rare flowers and strange trees, but I've never seen them. I wonder if the Princess could tell me in detail what kinds of plants are rarely seen in the Central Plains?\"","As she was now a consort, Princess Shou'an had no choice but to leave Scholar Qi's side and walk over to her, bowing and saying, \"It would be my honor...\"","She then began to explain.","While listening, Yanshu glanced to the side.","She saw that at some point, the Empress Dowager, who had been browsing books on the shelves, had wandered to a spot not far from Scholar Qi.","And Scholar Qi automatically stood to the side, like an attendant, not daring to leave.","She was startled, and immediately became excited.","Ah, ah, ah, the Empress Dowager actually walked over to Scholar Qi on her own?","Ah, ah, ah, are they going to talk?!!!","Ah, ah, ah, what will they say?!!!","And just as she was thinking this, she saw the Empress Dowager indeed open her mouth and say something in Scholar Qi's direction.","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","Unfortunately, the library was too large, and Princess Shou'an was talking to her, making it impossible for her to hear clearly.","After the Empress Dowager finished speaking, Scholar Qi seemed to pause.","...","Indeed, at this moment, Qi Shuguang was stunned.","Because the Empress Dowager had actually asked him, \"After all these years, you're still alone. Could it be that Mr. Qi has someone in his heart?\""]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83","paragraphs":["At this moment, Qi Shuguang was utterly stunned.","He really hadn't expected that she would... ask him such a question?","But how was he supposed to answer?","He hadn't lost his senses yet, hadn't forgotten where he was at this moment, nor had he forgotten his status in relation to her.","So after a long pause, he could only say, \"This humble subject only... only...\"","Before he could finish, the Empress Dowager spoke again, \"I remember many years ago, you used to tell me everything without reservation. I didn't expect that now, you've also learned to stammer and hesitate.\"","As she spoke, she gave a cool laugh, seeming quite disappointed.","Qi Shuguang felt a pang in his heart and momentarily forgot many things, only bowing his head to say, \"Your Majesty's insight is clear. No matter what status this humble subject holds, my heart has never changed.\"","As the words left his mouth, he himself was startled.","What... what had he just said?","He secretly glanced forward, only to see her first pause, then slightly raise an eyebrow, with what seemed to be a hint of a smile at the corner of her lips...","\"I hope the gentleman does not forget his original intention, and focuses on cultivating excellent talents for the Great Liang.\"","The Empress Dowager finished speaking and turned to walk away.","Qi Shuguang hurriedly bowed his head in acknowledgment where he stood.","This library was spacious enough, and three stories high.","At this time, everyone was chatting and touring on their own, and no one could hear what they had said.","Only Yanshu had secretly witnessed everything, and her curiosity was at its peak.","What on earth did they say???","Why did the Empress Dowager look like she was in such a good mood!!!","Could it be that Scholar Qi confessed his feelings?!!!","Unfortunately, afraid that Princess Shou'an would go bother Scholar Qi again, she didn't dare to leave easily. She could only continue to converse with her on the surface, while feeling extremely frustrated inside, only able to silently shout, [Ahhh what exactly did the Empress Dowager and Scholar Qi say!!!]","At the same time, Yuwen Lan, who was looking around at the books, felt a huge shock in his ears.","— Although he was too far away to hear their conversation, he couldn't help but hear such a loud shout.","... What?","The Empress Dowager spoke with Qi Shuguang?","Surprised, he hurriedly looked around the hall, only to see the Empress Dowager also examining books, while Qi Shuguang still stood where he was before. They both looked calm, as if nothing had happened.","Looking again, he saw Yanshu talking with Princess Shou'an, also appearing calm.","He tried walking over.","First passing by Qi Shuguang, he heard him sigh in his heart, [Perhaps I shouldn't have said that just now.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Which sentence? What did he say?","Then passing by the Empress Dowager, he heard her seem a bit smug in her thoughts, [Silly fool.]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Silly fool... what did that mean?","Tsk, what exactly happened just now?","Yuwen Lan finally came to Yanshu's side, only to hear Yanshu still roaring in her mind, [Never mind! For the sake of my ship, I'll fight it out with Princess Shou'an today! I absolutely won't give her a chance to cling to Scholar Qi!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","She really is working hard.","The library was located at the highest point of the academy, and through the windows, one could see the entire forest.","After coming out of the hall, Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong curiously asked, \"I saw a newly cultivated empty space by the mountain earlier. I wonder what Mountain Master Qi plans to use it for?\"","Qi Shuguang replied, \"Although the future expenses of the academy will be borne by the court, the daily consumption of several hundred people's food, clothing, and necessities is no small matter. I plan to gradually clear out the usable land in the mountains, letting teachers and students personally farm some vegetables and grains in their spare time. This way, we can not only reduce the burden on the court but also allow students to experience the true hardship of labor. Thus, they can have more... compassion for the poor people of the world.\"","As he finished speaking, Zou Mozhong suddenly understood and hurriedly nodded, saying, \"Mountain Master Qi is truly considerate. Nowadays, many young students consider farming to be lowly work, not knowing that farming is the foundation of the people!\"","The rest of the crowd also agreed, saying, \"Yes, indeed! If one cannot understand the hardship of farming, how can they truly empathize with the common people? Mountain Master Qi has great foresight.\"","\"Yes, indeed.\"","...","Hearing these words of praise, Qi Shuguang himself naturally repeatedly expressed his humility, saying he didn't deserve such praise.","Yanshu, however, was very proud,","— See, isn't this why he's her idol? How impressive!!!","After such reflections, today's itinerary came to an end.","It was getting late, and everyone should head back.","As the head of the academy, Qi Shuguang naturally led everyone out again.","Having personally witnessed the new look of Songhe Academy today, the guests all praised it repeatedly, full of confidence for the future.","And having talked with Princess Shou'an for so long, Yanshu was also tired, now just wanting to quickly return to the palace and lie down.","As they reached the academy gates, the carriages were already waiting.","It was time for everyone to bow and respectfully send the Emperor, Empress, and Empress Dowager back to the palace.","However, at this moment, Princess Shou'an suddenly said, \"Oh, by the way, Mountain Master Qi, I saw a book called 'Ten Discourses' in the library earlier. I wonder if it's the only copy?\"","As these words fell, Yanshu paused, suddenly having a vague bad feeling.","She saw her idol Mountain Master Qi reply, \"The one the Princess is referring to is indeed the only copy, which has been kept in Songhe Academy's library for thirty years.\"","With these words, Princess Shou'an unexpectedly said, \"I see! To be honest with Mountain Master, I've long heard of this book's reputation, but due to the remoteness of Nanzhao, I've had no chance to see it all these years. Since I've had the fortune to encounter it today, I wonder if I could go back to the library to read it for a while?\"","Hm?","Yanshu immediately frowned, thinking that Princess Shou'an just wanted to stay behind after everyone left to flirt with Scholar Qi!","Outrageous!","How was Scholar Qi supposed to answer this?!","If he flatly refused, he'd seem petty, but if he didn't refuse, wouldn't that be like inviting a wolf into the house, making the Empress Dowager unhappy!","Damn it, damn it, damn it!!!","Her mind raced, trying to find an excuse to block this woman.","However, before she could speak, she heard the Emperor beside her suddenly say, \"It's getting late. We've already disturbed the academy for half a day. Let's let them get back to their own business.\"","With these words, Princess Shou'an could only bow her head and say, \"Yes.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, [Oh? Why is the Emperor so timely today?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He was also worried, seeing her emotions fluctuate so much today, wondering if it would affect the baby in her womb!","So it was better for him to quickly speak up and intervene.","But speaking of which, this aunt of his... if she wanted to flirt, she should just go flirt outside. Qi Shuguang wasn't that kind of frivolous person.","It wasn't easy for him to find such a suitable mountain master this time.","And earlier, in front of so many people, her action of throwing flowers at the podium was a bit too flirtatious. If she were allowed to linger in the academy now, what would the students think if they saw?","So after saying this, he added, \"The academy is a place for quiet study. Idle outsiders should not casually come to disturb without reason.\"","As these words fell, everyone agreed in unison.","Princess Shou'an could only nod along, looking somewhat disappointed.","Yanshu's eyes lit up, thinking, [Not bad! The Emperor is really on point today! Alright, I'll let him off for not refusing to let this female player enter the academy earlier!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So she was actually planning to settle scores with him about that?","But... what does \"player\" mean?","With that said, the Emperor, Empress, and Empress Dowager boarded their carriages and left.","The officials respectfully saw them off, then all returned to their own homes.","And Princess Shou'an, no matter how unwilling, had to return to her own residence in the capital with the imperial edict.","However, no matter how much Yanshu disliked it, Princess Shou'an was after all royal kin, and also held the status of Nanzhao's Empress Dowager. Having come all the way to the capital, the Empress Dowager, as the host, had to show some welcome.","So after a day, the palace held a luncheon in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony, specifically to welcome Princess Shou'an.","Of course, the Empress Dowager didn't really want to face Princess Shou'an alone, so she also invited the Grand Princess and her daughter Ankang county lord, as well as Princess Shou'an's sister-in-law, Princess Consort Ruyang, to accompany them.","In this way, although it was a gathering of royal ladies, it was quite lively.","Of course, Yanshu had to come to such an occasion.","— Not for anything else, but to support her number one idol!","However, with Ankang county lord here today, as fellow pregnant women, the two had many common topics.","And Ankang county lord was very generous, as a mother who had already given birth to two children, she imparted many useful experiences to Yanshu.","The Grand Princess and Princess Consort Ruyang were chatting with Princess Shou'an about the recent happenings in the capital and Nanzhao.","Princess Shou'an, having traveled extensively and met countless people, spoke eloquently and at length.","The Empress Dowager mostly listened, her expression unchanged.","However, others gradually began to grow restless.","Seeing that the banquet was already half over, Princess Consort Ruyang seized the opportunity when Princess Shou'an finished speaking to address the Empress Dowager, \"Your subject dares to inquire about something from Your Majesty today.\"","The Empress Dowager, having sensed she had something on her mind, simply replied with an \"Oh?\" and said, \"What do you wish to ask? Feel free to speak.\"","Princess Consort Ruyang then said, \"I've heard that the new headmaster of Songhe Academy, Scholar Qi, is still unmarried. Is this true?\"","Hmm?","At these words, the Empress Dowager paused.","Princess Shou'an also paused.","And Yanshu, who had been discussing pregnancy experiences with the Ankang county lord, particularly paused.","—Why was Princess Consort Ruyang suddenly inquiring about her idol, Scholar Qi?","Could it be that she had taken a liking to him as well?","...No, that couldn't be right. Her husband, the Prince of Ruyang, was still alive and well, wasn't he?","Yanshu immediately stopped her conversation and looked over.","Before the Empress Dowager could speak, Princess Shou'an asked warily, \"Sister-in-law, why do you ask about this?\"","Princess Consort Ruyang smiled and said, \"It's about my niece, Xiuru. Didn't she divorce her previous husband last year? She's been living with her parents ever since. She's not even thirty yet—isn't it a shame for someone so young? I've been thinking about finding her a suitable match. I recently heard that Headmaster Qi is still unmarried, so if there's a possibility...\"","Before she could finish, Princess Shou'an interrupted with a snort, \"Sister-in-law, forgive me for speaking out of turn, but your niece has been troublesome since childhood. Though I'm not in the capital, I often hear about her misdeeds. They say that after marrying into her previous family, she not only failed to respect her in-laws but also bullied her sisters-in-law. She even ruined her young sister-in-law's engagement. If the family hadn't been pushed to their limits, why would they have divorced her? It's better to have her improve her temperament first, rather than inflicting her on Headmaster Qi.\"","Yanshu thought, \"???\"","Was this true?","How had she never heard about Princess Consort Ruyang's niece's scandals?","But before she could ponder further, Princess Consort Ruyang became visibly upset. She frowned and retorted, \"You speak as if you're so virtuous! Didn't you once drive your sister-in-law, the Princess of Mu, to the point of wanting to return to her maiden home? How can you so lightly criticize others?\"","At these words, everyone in the hall except for the two sisters-in-law raised their eyebrows.","Yanshu's eyes lit up.","Tsk, more drama to watch?","Come on, fight! Expose each other's secrets!"]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84","paragraphs":["Although disagreements between sisters-in-law are common, Yanshu never expected that at the imperial family banquet in the palace, two such noble ladies as Princess Shou'an and the Princess Consort of Ruyang would quarrel so openly.","For a moment, not just her, but everyone in the hall stopped eating and drinking, all turning to look at the two in-laws.","As soon as the Princess Consort of Ruyang spoke, Princess Shou'an immediately glared at her and retorted, \"What? I drove her back to her maiden home? Why don't you mention how she tried to harm me? She poisoned my Jie's wet nurse, wasn't that an attempt to kill my poor child? For such a vicious act, I didn't kill her on the spot - that was already giving enough face to her husband and her maiden family!\"","\"Her returning to her maiden home was because she was too ashamed to stay in the prince's mansion after her plot was exposed! What does that have to do with me? What do you know to be throwing mud at me here!\"","As the words fell, the Empress Dowager and the Grand Princess, mother and daughter, both silently clicked their tongues -","So such an incident had actually occurred in the Mu Prince's Mansion?","Tsk, they had heard that the Nanzhao Kingdom practiced monogamy, with men never taking concubines, and thought this would lead to fewer issues in the inner quarters, but who knew there would still be so many problems between sisters-in-law.","Come to think of it, this Princess Consort of Mu inherited her husband's princely title from his elder brother, yet instead of being grateful, she tried to poison her young nephew who had just lost his father. It seems her intentions were truly malicious.","Apparently overcome with anger, Princess Shou'an continued, snorting at her sister-in-law the Princess Consort of Ruyang, \"Sister-in-law, rather than concerning yourself with me from a thousand miles away, why don't you mind your own family members! Your family knew your niece had an overbearing personality and would be disciplined by her mother-in-law if she married into a high-ranking family, so they specifically chose a lower-status family for her. What sin did the Xu family commit? Wouldn't it have been better to marry a virtuous daughter-in-law? But they had to marry your niece! After she married in, she wouldn't pay respects to her parents-in-law, controlled the family's finances, ate and dressed well herself while everyone else came second to her!\"","\"When her sister-in-law finally became engaged to the Heir of the Marquis of Ning'an, she worried that once the sister-in-law entered a high-ranking family she would come back to deal with her. So she actually went to the Marquis of Ning'an's family and said the sister-in-law had broken off two previous engagements! When this was exposed, it finally angered the Xu family enough to divorce her! Such a poisonous woman, and she still wants to marry Mr. Qi? Keep dreaming!\"","As these words fell, the crowd in the hall couldn't help but click their tongues again -","What? She even spread rumors about her own sister-in-law?","Hearing this, it seems the Princess Consort of Ruyang's niece was indeed quite vicious.","However, before they could finish their disapproval, the Princess Consort of Ruyang became furious again and snorted, \"You're one to talk! You had an ambiguous relationship with the Young Master Wang of Pingzhou but wouldn't marry him, causing that well-known local talent to become dull and stupid. And Young Master Sun, Governor Sun's only son, studied hard for ten years and finally achieved the rank of tanhua in the imperial examinations. So many good young ladies in the capital had their eyes on him, but you - your husband hadn't even been dead for a year, and instead of properly observing widowhood, you went and got entangled with him!\"","\"You entangled with him but wouldn't marry him, ruining his reputation and causing him to only marry at 25. His parents, Governor Sun and his wife, were angered to death! They just didn't dare curse you because of your status as a princess! And you call others poisonous women? In my opinion, you're the rotten apple of the Yuwen Family, who knows how much you've tarnished the imperial family's good name!\"","What?","At these words, the others once again widened their eyes -","There were actually such matters?!","However, before they could investigate further, Princess Shou'an became angry again and said, \"I'm a single widow, and Sun Liang was also an unmarried single man, why couldn't we be mutually fond of each other? You think I didn't originally want to marry him? It was because of his old-fashioned parents... They looked down on me for being a widow!\"","She then retorted, \"Sister-in-law says I've tarnished the Yuwen Family's name, but you should mind your own business! As a daughter-in-law of the Yuwen Family, have you properly fulfilled your responsibilities? Among the children in the household, you only hire good tutors for your own son, and won't even let the other sons sit in on lessons! You won't lay a finger on your own son, but how many beatings have you given the other sons? That year when my brother's concubine and favorite concubine stabbed each other and both miscarried, who was sitting back reaping the benefits? Do you dare say you had nothing to do with all this?\"","As these words fell, Yanshu was stunned again -","What? King Ruyang's concubine and favorite concubine had both miscarried that year?","Could the Princess Consort of Ruyang have been behind it?","She saw that not far away, the Grand Princess also seemed to recall this incident from the past, and hurriedly exchanged a glance with the Empress Dowager.","However, immediately after, the Princess Consort of Ruyang became angry again, slapping the table and saying, \"They were stupid themselves, what does that have to do with me? As the proper mistress of a prince's household, am I not allowed to discipline the children? Is this something you have any right to criticize?\"","She then snorted and laughed, \"No matter what I've done, I'm still better than some people, who have thrown their son to their younger brother to raise all these years, while they themselves spend all day sightseeing and traveling. Someone who hasn't fulfilled even half their responsibilities as a mother has the nerve to criticize others!\"","...","Perhaps because they had both had some alcohol earlier, the emotions of these two in-laws were particularly intense at this moment. As they spoke, they had even stood up.","It looked like if they continued arguing, they might come to blows.","Seeing this situation, the Empress Dowager finally spoke up, \"Alright, alright, why are family members fighting?\"","- Tsk, seeing that even the palace servants attending the banquet had forgotten to pour tea and wine, if these two were allowed to continue, it would truly become a laughingstock -","As she finished speaking, the Grand Princess also hurriedly chimed in, \"That's right, that's right, you two are still aunt and niece, what's the point of exposing each other's shortcomings here? Stop talking now.\"","In comparison, the Ankang county lord and Yanshu were the younger generation, so they could only nod along, not daring to speak carelessly.","But in her heart, Yanshu thought, [Keep spilling more! This is getting exciting!]","However, under these circumstances, Princess Shou'an had no choice but to calm down a bit, and addressed the Empress Dowager and Grand Princess, \"I've made the Empress and elder sister laugh. I'm very grateful for the Empress Dowager's welcome banquet for me today, it's just that some people are like toads trying to eat swan meat, coming out to make fools of themselves.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the Princess Consort of Ruyang immediately glared and said, \"Who are you calling a toad!\"","Princess Shou'an tilted her head back and snorted, \"Whoever answers is whoever it is!\"","\"You...\"","Before the Princess Consort of Ruyang could finish, she quickly said to the Empress Dowager, \"I've had too much to drink today, I've made the Empress laugh. I'll take my leave first and go sober up.\"","What else could the Empress Dowager say? She nodded and said, \"Be careful on your way back.\"","Princess Shou'an responded affirmatively, then bowed to the Grand Princess and Yanshu before leaving her seat and exiting the hall.","However, the Princess Consort of Ruyang was still full of anger, and complained to everyone again, \"Look how arrogant she's become! I was just trying to find a good match for my niece, is that wrong? Yet she mocks me like this, it's really infuriating!\"","As she finished speaking, Yanshu silently thought to herself, there's nothing wrong with looking out for your niece, but don't go harming innocent people.","Also, no one is allowed to snatch away her idol Headmaster Qi, hmph!","Just then, she heard the Grand Princess speak up, \"You're not wrong, but your niece sounds quite young, while Headmaster Qi seems to be in his forties already. Moreover, his position isn't one of great wealth or status, I'm afraid he might not be suitable for your niece. Why not find her someone younger and from a better family?\"","- Tsk, after all, this young woman sounds like she can really cause trouble, who from an ordinary family could keep her in check...","The Princess Consort of Ruyang could hear the meaning behind these words, and was momentarily embarrassed, wanting to say something but not knowing what to say.","Then the Empress Dowager said to her, \"To be honest with you, I can't help with this matter either. Just yesterday, His Majesty specifically issued an order at the gates of Songhe Academy not to disturb him, so I can't easily meet with the Headmaster either.\"","At these words, Yanshu quickly spoke up to corroborate, \"I was there yesterday too, His Majesty did indeed say this.\"","Hearing this, the Princess Consort of Ruyang could only acquiesce.","But in her heart, she couldn't help cursing her sister-in-law Princess Shou'an again -","Hmph, if she's married then she's married, why does she have to come back every few years to bring bad luck!","What rotten luck!","After watching this lively scene in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony, Yanshu returned to Ganlu Palace.","Recalling the exciting scene from earlier, she felt too thrilled to take an afternoon nap and decided to review the juicy gossip the two sisters-in-law had just shared about each other.","Well, who knows, maybe one day it could be used as material for a story.","Of course, those two had been talking so fast earlier that it was impossible to catch all the details, so she quickly called upon the system for help.","[System, tell me quickly, what was all that gossip about today? Is the niece of Princess Consort of Ruyang really like what Princess Shou'an described?]","The system replied, [More or less. The Princess Consort of Ruyang comes from a noble family herself, and with her status as a princess consort, she's always been very domineering. Most of what was said about her niece is true. The Xu family eventually couldn't stand it anymore and divorced her. Now that woman's reputation is ruined and most people don't dare to get involved with her.]","Yanshu: [I see.]","Tsk tsk, it's a good thing she blocked the Princess Consort of Ruyang's advances today. To think such a person would dare to have designs on her idol! It seems Princess Shou'an's final comment about her was quite apt!","She then asked, [What about Princess Shou'an's gossip? Is it true about the Young Master Wang of Pingzhou and the grandson of the Governor of Jin'an?]","The system said, [That's mostly accurate too. The Wang family is a prominent clan in Pingzhou, and that young master is considered one of the top elite bachelors there, known for being quite aloof. One year when Princess Shou'an was passing through Pingzhou, she stayed at their home. Seeing that the young master was good-looking, she casually flirted with him and then left. But the young master, experiencing his first love, became quite infatuated and couldn't get over her for several years, almost going mad for a while.]","Yanshu: [...]","Tsk tsk, isn't that just cruel!","The system continued, [The incident with the grandson of the Governor of Jin'an is actually quite similar to what happened the other day. At the time, he was a newly successful candidate in the imperial examinations, parading through the streets on horseback. Princess Shou'an, just like yesterday, threw a flower at him. That young master, being naive and easily swayed, saw how beautiful she was and fell for her. However, Princess Shou'an actually did have some genuine feelings at the time and wanted to discuss marriage, but his parents were firmly against it, so nothing came of it in the end.]","Yanshu: [...]","So she's a habitual offender! No wonder she was so accurate in throwing that flower the other day, tsk.","But in that case, if Princess Shou'an had genuine feelings for that Young Master Sun back then, and still flirted with her idol, it clearly wasn't true love!","She then continued to ask, [So what's the deal with Princess Shou'an's sister-in-law, the Princess Consort of Mu? Why did she drug the wet nurse to harm her son?]","The system replied, [Well, the Princess Consort of Mu is certainly wicked, but there's another main reason. Princess Shou'an's brother-in-law, the current Prince Mu Zhengping, has long harbored a secret love for Princess Shou'an. When Princess Shou'an first married into the Nanzhao Kingdom, Mu Zhengping was captivated by her beauty, but since she was his sister-in-law, he kept his feelings hidden. One day, his future wife, the Princess Consort of Mu, found out about this and naturally became jealous, harboring resentment for many years. Attempting to poison Princess Shou'an's son was just one of her schemes. Before that, this woman... had tried various other tactics against Princess Shou'an, such as putting drugs in her food, falsely accusing her of adultery, and so on.]","Yanshu: [...]","It seems things are quite chaotic in the Mu Prince's Mansion, tsk.","But come to think of it, Princess Shou'an doesn't seem like a pushover. If her sister-in-law tried to harm her so many times, didn't she retaliate at all?","The system replied, [Of course she did. After being falsely accused of adultery, Princess Shou'an was so enraged that she went ahead and slept with her brother-in-law.]","Yanshu: \"???\""]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85","paragraphs":["What?!!","Princess Shou'an actually slept... slept with her own younger brother-in-law???","Upon hearing this news, Yanshu's jaw dropped, and she remained stunned for a good half cup of tea's worth of time.","Tsk...","Now that's truly a fierce woman!!!","After half a cup of tea, she remembered to ask the system, [So what's the deal with her brother-in-law Mu Zhengping? Did he just let himself be... slept with without any resistance? And how did he react afterwards?]","The system sighed and said, [We have to start from the beginning to explain this. You see, back when Princess Shou'an had just married into Nanzhao, Mu Zhengping fell in love with his sister-in-law at first sight. But he knew she was his brother's wife, so there was no possibility between them. From the start, he just suppressed his feelings. Later, for the sake of family interests, he had no choice but to marry his current wife, Lady Pu, who is now the Princess Consort of the Mu Prince's Mansion.]","[Not long after, his elder brother died. At that time, his nephew was too young, and his sister-in-law Princess Shou'an was an outsider with no power base in Nanzhao. Naturally, Mu Zhengping's father-in-law's Pu family supported him to take over the position. This man also wanted to stabilize the situation on all fronts, so he accepted his brother's position and became the Prince of Mu.]","[However, Lady Pu was rather petty by nature. Seeing that her widowed sister-in-law was beautiful and noble, she always felt uncomfortable, especially since Mu Zhengping was quite good to his infant nephew. She felt even more uneasy about this. Later on, she discovered that her husband had called out Princess Shou'an's name while drunk. She then knew Mu Zhengping's secret and, in a fit of anger, started using various methods to harm Princess Shou'an and her son, from poisoning to assassination attempts.]","[Princess Shou'an wasn't a fool, how could she let her succeed so easily? Seeing that these methods kept failing, Lady Pu came up with another vicious plan. She spread rumors that her sister-in-law had been intimate with a guard in the mansion before becoming a widow, and that the child might even be the guard's. In response to this, Princess Shou'an angrily decided to sleep with her husband. As it happened, Mu Zhengping had drunk quite a bit that day and was lamenting his unexpressed feelings, so...]","[In short, Princess Shou'an definitely did it on purpose for revenge, while Mu Zhengping was in a state of half-drunk, half-awake, half-resisting, half-willing.]","Yanshu: [Tsk tsk tsk tsk...]","How melodramatic, how melodramatic, how melodramatic...","After thoroughly expressing her astonishment, she couldn't help but ask, [So what happened after that? How did these two view each other after this incident? Did they do it again?]","The system sighed and said, [It didn't go that far. After all, Princess Shou'an isn't the type to get entangled in such matters. After this incident, she became thoroughly fed up with the Mu Prince's Mansion and simply found a house outside to move into, leaving Mu Zhengping behind in a state of despair.]","Yanshu: [...]","Well, there's another one who fell for it.","So she asked again, [What about Lady Pu? Does she know about this?]","The system said, [Lady Pu doesn't know about this yet, but Mu Zhengping never liked her to begin with, and after learning about all the schemes she used against Princess Shou'an, he treated her even more coldly. As a result, Lady Pu became even angrier and found a way to poison the child's wet nurse. She thought that if the wet nurse drank it and then the milk was fed to Princess Shou'an's son, wouldn't that solve everything? Unfortunately, the wet nurse died before she could feed the child that day.]","[When Princess Shou'an learned the truth, she was so angry that she went to confront her brother-in-law Mu Zhengping and caused a huge scene. Of course, Mu Zhengping was also furious and punished Lady Pu severely, warning her that if anything happened to his nephew in the future, she would be the first one he'd hold accountable. From then on, Lady Pu finally quieted down a bit.]","Yanshu shook her head and sighed, [It's truly not easy for that child to have grown up. What happened next?]","The system said, [From then on, Princess Shou'an basically had leverage over her brother-in-law. She wasn't one to be confined by the inner palace rules anyway, so when the child grew a bit older, she simply left him with her brother-in-law to raise and started living life to the fullest, traveling around. When she had enough fun, she'd return to see her son and annoy her sister-in-law Lady Pu. She lived quite happily.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","She only had one thing to say after hearing all this—","Fierce woman!","Princess Shou'an truly is a fierce woman!","I suppose when you stop caring about everything, you can live so freely.","But come to think of it, it seems that Mu Zhengping is quite good to his nephew?","The system said, [Of course he's very good to him! After all, his mother Princess Shou'an is still around.]","Yanshu thought to herself, that's true. This Mu Zhengping is basically a lovesick fool, single-mindedly devoted to his sister-in-law, so of course he'd be good to his nephew!","But wait, doesn't Mu Zhengping have his own children? If he's too good to his nephew, wouldn't his own children be jealous?","But she heard the system answer decisively, [He doesn't have any.]","Yanshu thought for a moment, then frowned and said, [That's not right. I remember hearing someone mention before that the Princess Consort of Nanzhao has a child, right? Seems to be only about ten years old?]","Unexpectedly, the system said, [That child actually isn't his. Back then, Lady Pu's family wanted to help her secure her position, so they brought in a child from outside.]","What???","Yanshu was shocked once again, [How is that possible?!! Didn't anyone find out? How could Lady Pu be so bold???]","The system sighed and said, [It's not a matter of being bold or not, it was something she had to do! You need to understand, Mu Zhengping rarely shared a bed with Lady Pu from the beginning, and after the poisoning incidents, he didn't even want to see her anymore. Lady Pu was getting desperate, so one day she took advantage of an opportunity when Mu Zhengping was drinking with his officials. She got him completely drunk, then pretended to have slept with him. Later, she claimed to be pregnant, and when the time came, she brought in a boy from outside and said she had given birth to him. At that time, Princess Shou'an was out enjoying herself, and most of the servants in the mansion were Lady Pu's own people. As for what happened that night, Mu Zhengping was too drunk to remember clearly himself, so wasn't it all settled?]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Tsk tsk tsk tsk.","Forgive her lack of words.","At this moment, she really couldn't think of any other expression besides \"tsk tsk\" to convey her thoughts.","This... looking at it this way, isn't Nanzhao just a complete mess?","It's too melodramatic and chaotic!!!","The system said, [You could say that Nanzhao has only been peaceful on the surface for these past ten or so years. Once all these truths come to light one day, it will surely be chaos. We'll have to see how things develop.]","Yanshu thought to herself that this was all they could do.","After all, she wouldn't dare to write a novel exposing such important and scandalous matters!","Tsk, it's quite a shame though, because this kind of melodramatic story would surely be very popular if written.","However, after hearing so much about the love and hatred between Princess Shou'an and her brother-in-law, it made her appreciate even more the precious nature of the CP she shipped!","Relationships like the one between her idol Mr. Qi and the number one boss Empress Dowager, with such restraint and consideration, are truly rare in this world!","Wuwuwu, she hugged her CP tightly and refused to let go!!!","After gossiping for half the day, Yanshu noticed it was already evening.","Today the Emperor finished work early and actually had time to join her for dinner.","Of course, to accommodate her, the dishes on the table were all light fare, such as cold lotus root slices, stir-fried cucumber, mustard spinach, and water celery soup.","It was quite considerate of the Emperor, who was used to eating meat, to often eat vegetarian meals with her now.","Of course, the food wasn't important. For Yuwen Lan, being able to have dinner together with his beloved consort was what mattered.","—Especially since he had a belly full of curiosity he wanted to ask her about today.","After just a few bites, Yanshu heard Yuwen Lan ask, \"I heard there was some commotion in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony today?\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she quickly nodded and said, \"Your Majesty, I was just about to tell you. Everything was fine at noon, but as we were eating, the Princess Consort of Ruyang and Princess Shou'an started bickering.\"","Yuwen Lan asked curiously, \"How did they start bickering?\"","Yanshu explained, \"First, Princess Shou'an said that the Princess Consort of Ruyang's niece wasn't virtuous. Then the Princess Consort of Ruyang retorted that Princess Shou'an had flirted with many men before, like the son of the Wang family from Pingzhou, and the son of Governor Sun from Jin'an...\"","As soon as these words were spoken, before Yuwen Lan could say anything, Fu Hai, who was serving the meal nearby, paused inwardly.","\"Is it true or false? The young master from Sun, the Prefect of Jin'an's family back then, isn't he the current Sun Jialiang, the Vice Minister of the Ministry of Works?\"","Yuwen Lan silently nodded in agreement, confirming that Sun Jialiang's father had indeed once been the Prefect of Jin'an.","Unexpectedly, he had a past with Princess Shou'an?","He frowned and asked, \"Is it true?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"At least that's what the Princess Consort of Ruyang said, and Princess Shou'an didn't deny it.\"","She continued, \"There's more. From Princess Shou'an's words, it seems the Princess Consort of Ruyang might be connected to a concubine's miscarriage in their prince's mansion many years ago.\"","Upon hearing this, Fu Hai couldn't help but marvel inwardly, \"My goodness, so much happened in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony today? What a pity to have missed it! If only His Majesty had been there, he could have witnessed all this juicy gossip!\"","Yuwen Lan silently listened and thought to himself that if he had been there, those two might not have revealed all this information.","Of course, he was now even more curious, \"What caused Princess Shou'an and the Princess Consort of Ruyang to start bickering?\"","Yanshu explained, \"The Princess Consort of Ruyang wanted to match her niece with Mr. Qi. You probably noticed Princess Shou'an's interest in Mr. Qi that day? So when the Princess Consort suggested this, the two of them started arguing.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He hadn't expected it to be because of Qi Shuguang.","How could this man be so popular among women?","While he was still bewildered, Yanshu coughed and said, \"Actually, what I've told you so far isn't even the most shocking part.\"","Yuwen Lan paused, then quickly asked, \"Then what's the most shocking part?\"","He saw her glance around.","Understanding her meaning, Yuwen Lan immediately raised his hand and ordered the bystanders, \"Everyone, leave us.\"","The crowd responded and began to withdraw from the hall, heads bowed.","Yuwen Lan then heard Fu Hai's anxious inner thoughts, \"Oh, Your Majesty! Oh, Your Highness! Can't you let us stay and hear what the most shocking part is? To start a story and not let us hear the end is truly torture!\"","His footsteps seemed to drag, and while others had already left, he was still several steps from the door.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He gave Fu Hai a warning look.","Fu Hai startled, then quickened his pace and finally exited.","When the room was quiet, Yanshu finally said, \"The most shocking part is that Mu Zhengping has actually been deeply in love with his sister-in-law, Princess Shou'an, all these years. After the Princess Consort of Mu discovered this, she tried various ways to poison and frame Princess Shou'an and her children. Then, to take revenge on her sister-in-law, Princess Shou'an impulsively slept with Mu Zhengping.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","While he was still stunned, she continued, \"There's one more crucial piece of information. The current heir in the Mu Prince's Mansion isn't actually the Prince's biological son. His wife pretended to be pregnant and adopted a child from outside the palace to secure the princely title.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","...","After a long silence, he just wanted to say, what a messy situation!","How could the Mu Prince's Mansion have become such a chaotic place?","Of course, after calming down a bit, Yuwen Lan also knew that the situation in Nanzhao was indeed unstable.","Mu Zhengping's father-in-law, Pu Jiachang, had always wanted to interfere in Nanzhao's political affairs.","Moreover, he wasn't truly loyal to the Mu family and had been secretly communicating with Tibet behind their backs.","It was foreseeable that if Mu Zhengping were to age and pass on, once Nanzhao fell into the hands of his wife's family, the Great Liang Dynasty might lose an ally and gain an unpredictable enemy instead.","However...","Yanshu's information today was quite timely.","Although Princess Shou'an, as an aunt, wasn't very reliable, she did have half of the Yuwen family's bloodline.","At that moment, an idea formed in Yuwen Lan's mind."]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86","paragraphs":["It's uncertain whether it was due to the argument with her sister-in-law Princess Consort of Ruyang in the Hall of Gentle Ceremony that day which had drained her energy, but for some time afterwards, Princess Shou'an did not appear in public.","However, Yanshu had been fed quite a juicy piece of gossip, which took her several days to fully digest.","Apart from sincerely believing that Princess Shou'an was a formidable person, she had no other opinions on the Nanzhao affair, only hoping that this fierce player would stay far away from her idol.","Fortunately, with the Emperor's personal decree that day, the Songhe Academy was closed to visitors, allowing her idol Chancellor Qi to teach peacefully in the academy without further harassment from Princess Shou'an.","As the days passed, Yanshu's pregnancy symptoms finally improved. She was no longer as sleepy, and her appetite had somewhat recovered. She could finally eat some meat dishes like braised beef and roast chicken.","However, given the hot weather, her favorite treats were still various iced fruit bowls.","Whether it was honeydew melon, watermelon, snow pears, or grapes, the imperial kitchen tried their best to come up with different varieties to please her. Eating one every day not only made her body feel comfortable but also improved her mood.","At first, Rendong was a bit worried, but it wasn't until Doctor Jiang personally said that pregnant women could moderately consume ice that she was allowed to do so.","On this day, while Yanshu was enjoying her iced honeydew melon bowl, she suddenly heard the system say, \"The latest news from Nanzhao: King Mu, Mu Zhengping, received an anonymous tip saying that the current heir in his household is not his own flesh and blood. He immediately had all of Lady Pu's personal maids arrested and after severe torture, the truth was indeed uncovered.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she hurriedly asked, \"He knows the child isn't his own now?\"","The system affirmed, \"The whole story has been uncovered, so of course he knows.\"","Yanshu quickly asked again, \"How did he deal with that Princess Consort?\"","The system replied, \"He directly bestowed her with a white silk cord. The main members of Lady Pu's natal family, including her parents and siblings, have all been charged with crimes and are currently imprisoned in Nanzhao's death row.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu silently sighed. The Pu family was indeed bold enough, but after keeping the secret for over a decade, the day of exposure had finally come.","But come to think of it, this anonymous tip...","Could it have been arranged by the Emperor?","It must have been. After all, she only told the Emperor about this matter, and Nanzhao had been peaceful for decades. Who else but the Emperor would do such a thing?","Then she heard the system confirm, \"That's right. After hearing about it from you, the Emperor sent people riding day and night to Nanzhao the very next day. The Pu family was a major force in the local area. Without outside help, Mu Zhengping might not have been able to deal with them so smoothly.\"","So that's how it was.","Yanshu thought for a moment and suddenly understood—","This way, only Princess Shou'an's son remained as the true Mu family bloodline in the Nanzhao King Mu's household. When Mu Zhengping grows old, he will undoubtedly succeed as King Mu.","And with half of his blood from the Yuwen Clan, it's believed that the future relationship between Nanzhao and Great Liang will become even closer.","The system said, \"That's exactly the idea.\"","Yanshu couldn't help but exclaim that gossip indeed had its great uses!","Looking forward to the future friendship between the two countries, she had made no small contribution!","But come to think of it, as things have developed to this point, Princess Shou'an could truly be called a winner in life!","To think that she spent her days traveling and enjoying life, had no shortage of romance, and now the throne has returned to her child.","Tsk, it's truly enviable.","Of course, Nanzhao is far from the capital, so Princess Shou'an probably doesn't know this good news yet. In a few days when she learns about the fate of her dead rival sister-in-law...","She'll probably be even more delighted.","As several more days passed, Yanshu's appetite improved further, and the palace became busy.","This was because the Emperor's birthday was approaching.","Of course, at the Emperor's age, if he were a commoner, it wouldn't be a time for celebration yet.","But after all, he is the supreme ruler, and for the country, the monarch's birthday is also an important day.","Not to mention, it's an extremely important opportunity to communicate and exchange foreign policies with various foreign countries.","Therefore, since Yuwen Lan's ascension to the throne, the Ministry of Rites had designated his birthday as Great Liang's Changning Festival, held every three years, inviting envoys from various countries to gather in the capital.","Apart from Princess Shou'an, who arrived a month early to see Chancellor Qi, the rest of the foreign envoys were only now starting to arrive in the capital.","And surprisingly, the first to arrive was Tibet, a country that has never had a good relationship with Great Liang.","As is well known, Tibet is located to the southwest of Great Liang and has been eyeing Great Liang covetously for decades, with occasional wars breaking out.","If it weren't for the buffer state of Nanzhao in between, the wars would likely have been even more intense.","Everyone knows they have always harbored wild ambitions towards Great Liang, yet unexpectedly, this time they took the initiative to propose a marriage alliance with Great Liang.","As soon as this news came out, it immediately sparked a wave of discussions throughout the court and the country.","Some officials were strongly against it, believing that this proposal should not be accepted. Tibet is a distant land with high mountains and far waters, and it's a barbaric place, unlike Nanzhao which has been a generations-long friendly neighbor to Great Liang.","Once a Great Liang woman is married off there, who knows what torment she might suffer, not to mention that the other side might not even abide by the agreement to guarantee they won't invade Great Liang's territory in the future.","Especially since with the marriage alliance, Great Liang would certainly send a generous dowry. These Tibetans are very likely to swallow the dowry first and then turn around to cause trouble, leaving Great Liang's efforts in vain.","But there were also officials who strongly supported this. They believed that war is costly and damaging to the country, and if they could use peaceful means to make the two countries friendly and strengthen mutual exchange and integration, why not do it?","Thus, for several days in a row, there were endless debates in the court.","However, before the officials could debate to a conclusion, the Princess Consort of Ruyang came to the Empress Dowager with a heart full of worry.","As it happened, that day the chef from Princess Shou'an's mansion had made some Nanzhao-style flower-flavored pastries, and Princess Shou'an personally brought them to the palace for the Empress Dowager to taste.","The Empress Dowager, concerned about Yanshu, had also summoned her to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","So, as the three were savoring the pastries, they heard a palace servant report, \"The Princess Consort of Ruyang requests an audience.\"","Yanshu, who was immersed in the sweet fragrance of the flower pastries, was startled. She thought to herself, why has the Princess Consort of Ruyang come at this time?","— Could it be that she heard her sister-in-law Princess Shou'an had entered the palace today and came specifically to argue?","Tsk tsk, if that's the case, she might be able to catch another wave of gossip today.","Thinking this, she secretly glanced at Princess Shou'an, only to see her with an unconcerned expression.","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Let her in.\"","The palace servant complied, and soon the Princess Consort of Ruyang entered the hall.","Seeing her sister-in-law there, the Princess Consort of Ruyang initially hesitated, but she could no longer care about arguing. With a face full of worry, she kowtowed to the Empress Dowager and said, \"I beg Your Highness to save me, to save Xiu!\"","As she spoke, tears even fell from her eyes.","This surprised the three in the hall. The Empress Dowager quickly said, \"What has happened? Get up and speak.\"","She then instructed the palace servants to help her up.","Only then did the Princess Consort of Ruyang say, \"I heard that a few days ago, the Tibetan envoys came to the capital and proposed a marriage alliance to His Majesty. Many officials in the court even agree with it. But looking at our Yuwen family, only my Xiu is still unmarried. If she were to be married off to Tibet, wouldn't that be the death of me...\"","As she spoke, she began to cry again.","Everyone finally understood.","— What the Princess Consort of Ruyang said was not wrong. After the bloody upheaval during the Emperor's ascension to the throne, the Yuwen Clan has never been particularly populous.","And looking at the current royal family, only their Ruyang Prince's household had a girl of suitable age who was not yet married, namely Yuwen Xiu, the legitimate daughter of the Prince of Ruyang.","She was also the Princess Consort of Ruyang's only daughter, who had been doted on by her since childhood.","The Prince of Ruyang's other two concubine-born daughters were both under ten years old, clearly not under consideration.","So when this matter came up, the Princess Consort of Ruyang was extremely anxious. For several days in a row, she couldn't eat or sleep, fearing that her daughter would be sent for the marriage alliance.","As she spoke, she couldn't help but cry to the Empress Dowager again, \"Your Highness knows that Xiu has been pampered by me since she was little. How could she endure that barbaric land of Tibet? Moreover, I've heard that those people, when a father dies, the son can marry his stepmother, and when an elder brother dies, the younger brother has to marry his sister-in-law... Wuwuwu, how can we let Xiu marry into such a barbaric place...\"","As soon as those words were spoken, before the Empress Dowager could say anything, Princess Shou'an, while eating a flower cake, said, \"Most of those foreign countries are like that, what's the big fuss about? If sister-in-law is reluctant to part with Xiu, I actually have an idea.\"","This statement startled everyone, and they quickly turned to look at her.","The Princess Consort of Ruyang also probed cautiously, \"What idea do you have?\"","Princess Shou'an replied, \"Isn't your niece from your maiden family worried about not having a marriage prospect? Why not marry her off instead? It doesn't necessarily have to be a daughter of the imperial clan, as long as big brother recognizes her as an adopted daughter, it would work.\"","Puff...","Upon hearing this, Yanshu almost spat out the flower cake she had just put in her mouth.","No wonder people called her ruthless, even at a time like this she didn't forget to stab her opponent.","The Princess Consort of Ruyang was stunned and immediately said, \"How is that possible? She's already that age...\"","Princess Shou'an continued nonchalantly, \"So what? The Tibetans don't care about those things anyway, as long as she can bear children, it's fine.\"","Hearing this, the Princess Consort of Ruyang was at a loss for words. It was the Empress Dowager who couldn't help but say to Princess Shou'an, \"At a time like this, stop teasing your sister-in-law.\"","She then turned to the Princess Consort of Ruyang and said, \"You're also too impatient. This matter is still under discussion, and the Emperor hasn't even spoken yet. Why are you getting anxious on your own?\"","The Princess Consort of Ruyang cried, \"Xiu is my own flesh and blood, how can I not be anxious?\"","Princess Shou'an finally became a bit more serious and said, \"Sister-in-law, being anxious won't help. If it really comes to that and this task falls on Xiu's shoulders, you'll have to accept it whether you want to or not. This is the responsibility of a daughter of the Yuwen Clan. You've been enjoying the empire and luxuries built by our ancestors, so when it's time to fulfill your duty, how can you not?\"","Hmm?","Upon hearing these words, Yanshu couldn't help but feel a new respect for Princess Shou'an.","Come to think of it, when she had volunteered to marry into Nanzhao back then, was it also with such an aspiration?","However, to be honest, the matter of political marriages was indeed quite cruel.","This wasn't a thousand years in the future; transportation was very underdeveloped. Throughout history, how many of those women sent for political marriages ever got to return to their homeland and see their families again?","Moreover, as the Princess Consort of Ruyang had just mentioned, in those foreign countries, it wasn't uncommon for sons to marry their stepmothers or brothers to marry their sisters-in-law. The women sent there were not only humiliated, but with one misstep, they could also die in political struggles in a foreign land.","Those ministers' talks of benefiting the country and the people were all built upon the backs of those women who had no way of returning.","Yanshu sighed silently, thinking that this matter could only depend on the Emperor's decision now.","Tsk, this just goes to show that being a royal woman isn't easy either.","...","The Empress Dowager thought the same, so she could only say to the Princess Consort of Ruyang, \"What Shou'an said isn't without reason. Although I'm reluctant to see Xiu suffer, this is a matter of national importance. I can't interfere. I can only advise you to be prepared. If this task really falls on Xiu, you'll have to let her go even if you don't want to.\"","Hearing this, the Princess Consort of Ruyang paused, then burst into tears again.","The Empress Dowager was at a loss and could only comfort her while sending someone to the imperial court to inquire about the situation and see when there might be a result.","As luck would have it, not long after, the person who was sent out hurriedly returned and reported, \"Your Majesty, after unanimous discussion among the court officials, Tibet's marriage proposal has been rejected.\"","Oh?","Everyone was stunned, their eyes brightening.","The Empress Dowager inquired further, \"Why did the ministers suddenly come to a unanimous decision?\"","The messenger replied, \"Because we just received news that there has been a coup in Nanzhao. Lady Pu, the queen of Nanzhao, had apparently brought in a commoner's son and passed him off as the crown prince, deceiving the king. Recently, when the truth was exposed, the king of Nanzhao executed Lady Pu and punished her maternal family. He then established his nephew as the new crown prince. As a result, Nanzhao has become even closer to our dynasty, and we can unite against Tibet. We no longer need to fear Tibet causing trouble.\"","\"What?\"","As soon as these words were spoken, everyone in the hall, except for Yanshu, was shocked.","Yanshu, on the other hand, breathed a sigh of relief.","Finally, the news had arrived, and she could join everyone in discussing this juicy gossip.","These past few days had been suffocating for her, trying to keep this information to herself!"]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87","paragraphs":["This news naturally came as a great surprise to everyone.","What???","Lady Pu, the wife of the Mu Prince of Nanzhao, actually brought in a child from outside and pretended it was the heir she had given birth to for the Mu Prince?","What kind of situation was this?!","After the initial shock, everyone naturally turned to look at Princess Shou'an, who was most closely related to this matter.","The Princess Consort of Ruyang, her eyes still wet with tears, quickly asked her sister-in-law, \"What? Your younger brother-in-law's son isn't actually his? Why would your sister-in-law do such a thing?\"","However, as soon as she finished speaking, Princess Shou'an also had a bewildered expression and said, \"I... I don't know either.\"","She then asked the palace maid who had brought the message, \"Are you sure this news is true? You didn't mishear it?\"","The maid who had reported the news nodded repeatedly and said, \"This matter is absolutely true. I heard it with my own ears from outside the Hall of Diligent Government.\"","Princess Shou'an still looked utterly shocked.","— What? That woman Lady Pu actually did such a thing?!","The Empress Dowager thought for a moment and said, \"Since the news has already reached the court, it must be true. Otherwise, for such a major matter concerning bloodlines, how could the Mu Prince treat it lightly?\"","She then smiled meaningfully at Princess Shou'an and said, \"Today I must truly congratulate you. Who would have thought that after all this drama, the throne would return to your son?\"","At these words, everyone in the hall hurried to congratulate Princess Shou'an, saying, \"Congratulations, Princess.\"","As the voices faded, the Princess Consort of Ruyang also had to quickly thank her sister-in-law, feeling somewhat guilty.","— Tsk, she used to think this sister-in-law had no future and was just in the way, but unexpectedly, in an instant, she suddenly had prospects...","After all, in many years' time, this Nanzhao would be her son's realm.","Well, it seemed she couldn't easily argue with her anymore in the future.","For a moment, congratulatory voices came from all around, and Princess Shou'an could only respond, \"You're all too kind.\"","In her heart, she still found it unbelievable — she had only been away for a short while, and such a major event had occurred?","As she was still in a daze, she heard her sister-in-law, the Princess Consort of Ruyang, cough and ask her, \"By the way, is there something wrong with your younger brother-in-law or his wife? How come after so many years they only have this one child, and it's even a fake one? Is it that your brother-in-law can't have children, or is it his wife who can't?\"","As soon as these words were spoken, everyone in the hall pricked up their ears.","That's right, that's right, they were all dying to know too!!!","Yanshu: \"...\"","Who would have thought the Princess Consort of Ruyang was so gossipy.","However, how could Princess Shou'an answer this question?","She probably didn't know either.","Sure enough, Princess Shou'an opened her mouth, looking like she wanted to say something but really didn't know what to say.","Seeing this situation, Yanshu felt incredibly stifled.","She knew!","But she couldn't say it!!!","Ahhh, she had been holding this in for so many days, unable to tell anyone or write it in a story. She was about to go crazy!","Unfortunately, even now, she still couldn't say anything.","After a while, the Empress Dowager finally said to the Princess Consort of Ruyang, \"She's been away from home for years, so she probably doesn't know about these things.\"","Just as she finished speaking, a palace servant reported from outside the door, \"Your Highness, an attendant from Nanzhao is requesting to see the Princess, asking her to return to the residence immediately.\"","Hearing this, Princess Shou'an stood up and said, \"In that case, I shall take my leave.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, watching her leave the hall.","Then she said to the Princess Consort of Ruyang, \"Alright, now that the dust has settled, you need not worry anymore. Go back quickly and tell Axiu that she doesn't need to be afraid anymore.\"","The Princess Consort of Ruyang complied, then stood up and said, \"Thank you, Empress Dowager. This matter is truly thanks to His Majesty's wisdom. I shall take my leave...\"","After saying this, she also left.","All of a sudden, the hall became much quieter. Yanshu was considering whether she should leave too when she saw the Empress Dowager wave away the idle personnel and urgently ask her, \"Do you have any news about this matter?\"","Yanshu had been bursting to speak, so upon hearing this, she quickly said, \"A few days ago, I did hear some news from His Majesty...\"","The Empress Dowager hurriedly said, \"Tell me, what's really going on with that child?\"","Yanshu promptly continued, \"It seems that the Mu Prince had always been somewhat cold towards his wife. The Princess, being jealous by nature, saw that Princess Shou'an was beautiful and developed harmful intentions towards her. After several failed attempts, she was discovered by the Mu Prince, which made him even colder towards her. The Princess and her family became anxious, so they came up with this plan.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded and asked, \"Then how did he discover it? Everything had been calm for so many years.\"","Yanshu could only say, \"It seems the child doesn't resemble either the Mu Prince or his wife, and there have been some rumors in Nanzhao. The Mu Prince himself wasn't without suspicion, and it just so happened that His Majesty inadvertently received such information and sent someone to Nanzhao to tell the Mu Prince.\"","Ahem, anyway, it's best to attribute everything to the Emperor.","Sure enough, the Empress Dowager frowned and said, \"His Majesty can even investigate news from Nanzhao?\"","Yanshu hurriedly praised the Emperor from afar, \"His Majesty is indeed wise and mighty.\"","... Well, alright.","The Empress Dowager couldn't think of any other possibilities, so she just nodded and said, \"Truly impressive.\"","After thinking for a moment, she suddenly raised an eyebrow and said, \"Come to think of it, this Mu Zhengping must like Shou'an.\"","As soon as she said this, Yanshu almost spat out the hot tea she had just sipped, and asked with a shocked expression, \"How does Your Highness know this?\"","The Empress Dowager smiled faintly and said, \"If not, why would Mu Zhengping be so willing to raise a child for her? And he's not even in a hurry to have his own children. Throughout history, what man would do such a thing without reason? He must be head over heels for her. Shou'an really has quite a skill.\"","Yanshu nodded, pretending to have a sudden realization, \"I see.\"","Tsk, the Empress Dowager truly lived up to her title, she was indeed formidable!","Then she heard the Empress Dowager say, \"This Lady Pu is also pitiful, but her heart was too vicious. No matter what, she shouldn't have harmed an innocent child. Now she's just reaping what she sowed.\"","Yanshu nodded.","Next, she heard the Empress Dowager say, \"By the way, now that these two are both single, I wonder if they could get together?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Ahem, actually, she had thought about this too.","After all, the Mu Prince treated his nephew as his own son, which made him quite a rare candidate for a stepfather.","Of course, the most important thing was that if the Mu Prince could tie down Princess Shou'an, she wouldn't have to worry about her coveting Scholar Qi anymore!","However, this matter was probably uncertain —","From the looks of the current situation, Mu Zhengping seemed to be quietly waiting for Princess Shou'an to finish playing around and come home, but who knew when this player princess would be done playing?","Just as she was thinking this, she suddenly remembered something else.","— Every year during the Emperor's Changning Festival, the whole country would have three days off, including Songhe Academy.","Tsk, in that case, wouldn't Princess Shou'an go to harass her male god again?","As evening approached, the setting sun cast a golden glow over the mountains.","Starting tomorrow, the academy would be closed for three days. After seeing off the last batch of students going home, Qi Shuguang prepared to close the main gate and return to the academy.","— Being alone in the world, he really had no need to set up a residence in the capital, so he simply made the academy his home, just as he had done for many years in the past.","However... before he could close the main gate, he heard a voice from the mountain path, \"Headmaster Qi.\"","It was a woman's voice, one that seemed familiar from not long ago.","Qi Shuguang's heart skipped a beat, and he quickly looked up to see a woman wearing a veil walking towards him from the mountain path.","Before he could speak, the woman had already walked up to him and voluntarily removed her veil.","Qi Shuguang paused. He quickly stepped forward and bowed, \"This humble one pays respects to the Princess.\"","Princess Shou'an smiled and said, \"Headmaster needn't be so formal. Just treat me as an old friend.\"","However, Qi Shuguang kept his eyes lowered, maintaining a polite distance, and said, \"This humble one wouldn't dare. May I ask why the Princess has come?\"","Princess Shou'an observed his demeanor, paused for a moment, then suddenly sighed, \"You truly are the most difficult man in the world.\"","Qi Shuguang paused.","Before he could say anything, he heard her ask, \"To be honest, is there a woman you fancy in your heart?\"","Qi Shuguang paused again, but tried to maintain his composure as he asked, \"Why does the Princess ask such a question?\"","Princess Shou'an smiled and said, \"You must have someone, otherwise why would you act like a mouse seeing a cat when you meet other women? You haven't married for so many years, could it be for her sake?\"","Qi Shuguang remained silent.","Princess Shou'an asked him again, \"If you like her, why not try hard to pursue her and keep her by your side?\"","Qi Shuguang paused, then suddenly smiled and said, \"Because I believe that being together constantly isn't necessary to maintain a bond. After all, not everyone can defy fate.\"","\"Fate?\" Princess Shou'an hesitated, \"Is she no longer in this world?\"","Qi Shuguang didn't speak, but his expression seemed to confirm it.","Princess Shou'an softened her tone, \"I'm sorry for bringing up such a painful topic. You truly are a rare, devoted man. My trip to the capital this time was rather abrupt.\"","She put her veil back on and turned to leave.","However, after a few steps, she turned back and said to him, \"I never believed there was true devotion in this world, but you've changed my mind, sir. I hope you fare well in the future. I won't trouble you again.\"","With that, she finally walked away, gradually disappearing at the end of the road.","That night, Yanshu heard about this incident from the system.","After confirming she hadn't misheard, she was greatly surprised. [Is Princess Shou'an giving up?]","The system replied, [More or less. Actually, Qi Shuguang was just an unattainable target for her, which sparked her curiosity and a bit of desire to conquer. But Princess Shou'an isn't the type to pester someone endlessly. After these two meetings, she clearly felt that she and Qi Shuguang weren't compatible. There's no point in pursuing it further.]","Yanshu nodded, [That's wise of her.]","Hmph, the Grand Scholar was her top-tier character. No one could steal him away.","To be honest, this Princess Shou'an was one of the more admirable women she had encountered.","First, she volunteered to marry into Nanzhao, then experienced her husband's early death...","Having gone through so many ups and downs in her life, she could still be so carefree now. Most importantly, the throne of Nanzhao eventually fell to her son.","Could this be due to her unique wisdom?","Perhaps only by being so elusive and distant could she keep Mu Zhengping constantly thinking of her and missing her? Thus transferring his affections to her child?","She was curious again, [Speaking of which, since Princess Shou'an thinks the Scholar Qi is devoted, hasn't she looked back at her brother-in-law? In a sense, her brother-in-law is also a kind of devoted, isn't he?]","The system replied, [She probably doesn't have time. She just returned from Songhe Academy not long ago, and on the way back, Princess Shou'an met an envoy from Rouran. Seeing that the Rouran envoy wasn't bad-looking, the two of them have already gone to a tavern for drinks.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Truly a remarkable person.","Well, she didn't understand the world of players after all.","But wait, Rouran again?","...Princess Shou'an probably doesn't know about the incident of the Princess being poisoned last time, right? Hope she doesn't fall victim to that aphrodisiac too!","But the system said, [She's an old hand at romance, no need to worry. Now, want to hear some fresh news?]","Yanshu's eyes immediately lit up, and she hurriedly asked, [What is it?]","The system: [Mu Zhengping settled domestic affairs a few days ago and set out from Nanzhao. He's almost reached the capital now.]","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","At this moment, Yuwen Lan, who had just finished bathing, came out of the bathroom. He walked to the bed in a few steps and embraced her, who was still gossiping with the system, and said, \"Why are you still so energetic?\"","Look at her, eyes wide open, as if she had just heard some exciting news.","As soon as he finished speaking, Yanshu turned to him with an excited face and said, \"Your Majesty, it's a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity. Please grant my wish and let me witness this dramatic scene!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88","paragraphs":["If Yanshu hadn't explained it to him, Yuwen Lan wouldn't have known that the King of Nanzhao, Mu Zhengping, had personally come to the capital.","It's worth noting that four years ago, when he ascended the throne, Mu Zhengping hadn't even attended.","Hmm... Could he be here this time to see Princess Shou'an?","To be honest, Yuwen Lan didn't quite understand.","Of course, whether Mu Zhengping came or not was his own business. Right now, Yuwen Lan was more concerned about Yanshu.","He raised an eyebrow and said, \"Who was it that mentioned prenatal education to me last time? You spend all day thinking about these things, is it really good for the child?\"","As he spoke, he carefully reached out and gently stroked her belly.","Hmm, it seemed to have grown a bit.","Come to think of it, the little peanut inside should have grown to the size of a small walnut by now, right?","Listening to all this idle gossip with its mother every day, who knows if it'll grow up with a head full of gossip...","Yuwen Lan tried to imagine that scene—","A cute little baby, opening its mouth to spout other people's secrets...","Yikes, that seemed a bit scary.","However, the person in his arms said, \"It seems Your Majesty still doesn't quite understand. The most important thing about prenatal education is keeping the mother in a good mood. When the mother is in a good mood, the baby will grow well and have a good personality. I'm stuck in this palace all day and can't go out, with the same few things in front of my eyes day in and day out. Don't I need to find some amusement?\"","Besides...","There was also a system that gave her gossip every day. How could she be satisfied just eating it without watching?","Suddenly, the system chimed in, [??? Blaming me now?]","Yanshu ignored it and continued speaking to Yuwen Lan, \"I heard that Princess Shou'an has been getting quite cozy with the Rouran Envoy these past few days. Wouldn't it be fun if that Mu Zhengping, who's been waiting so long, found out? Tell me honestly, Your Majesty, don't you want to see that?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...Why would I want to see such things?\"","Ahem, since when did he care about such matters? What he cared about were the important affairs behind all this.","After he finished speaking, he saw Yanshu looking at him with disappointment. \"Is that so? Then from now on, I won't tell Your Majesty about these things anymore.\"","She had thought they were kindred spirits, but it seems she was mistaken.","Yuwen Lan, who had been silently listening: \"???\"","She felt \"mistaken\" just like that?","...Was it really necessary?","He had no choice but to say, \"Fine, Mu Zhengping is after all the King of Nanzhao. If he really has come to the capital, the court will certainly need to entertain him properly. I'll allow you to attend as well, but remember not to get too excited. No matter what, remember you have a little one in your belly.\"","She stroked her belly with a smug look and said, \"Of course. I've been reading storybooks to him in my spare time these days. I'm sure he'll be eloquent in the future.\"","What, what? Storybooks???","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched. \"Wait, why not read some works by the great Tang and Song Dynasty writers? Why storybooks?\"","She replied, \"Those are too profound. He's so small now, he won't understand. Storybooks are more down-to-earth.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...Who exactly is it that doesn't understand?\"","She waved her hand dismissively and said, \"That's not important. What matters is, when Mu Zhengping comes, will the Empress Dowager attend too?\"","Hehe, such a good opportunity, of course she had to invite her top supporter to enjoy the drama together!","Yuwen Lan's brow twitched again. \"Why involve the Empress Dowager?\"","She replied matter-of-factly, \"Because the Empress Dowager has been in the palace longer and must be in even greater need of amusement! Isn't Your Majesty always the most filial? Of course you should invite the Empress Dowager for such an opportunity!\"","Hehe, after all, the Empress Dowager had already guessed that Mu Zhengping liked Princess Shou'an. Wouldn't it be more lively to enjoy the drama together?","...","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Of course, since the Mu family of Nanzhao and the Yuwen family were related by marriage, if a banquet were to be held, the Empress Dowager should attend as an elder of the Yuwen family.","But he realized that now, the most filial person to the Empress Dowager was no longer him, but her.","Sure enough, just as the system had said, the next day, Mu Zhengping, the King of Nanzhao, arrived in the capital.","To show respect, Yuwen Lan immediately sent court officials and royal relatives, including King Ruyang, to welcome him.","In the evening, he hosted the first welcoming banquet at Jiying Hall in the palace.","— It was called the first banquet because this was merely a family gathering hosted by the Yuwen family as in-laws.","In two more days, when envoys from various countries arrived, there would be a higher-level state banquet to entertain Mu Zhengping.","As this was a family gathering, the main members of the Yuwen family, including the Emperor, Empress Dowager, King Ruyang and his wife, and the Grand Princess and her husband, naturally had to attend.","Yanshu finally got her wish and tagged along with the Emperor and Empress Dowager.","She saw Princess Shou'an, as the Empress Dowager of Nanzhao, sitting in the guest of honor's seat, while the much-anticipated King of Nanzhao, Mu Zhengping, was seated next to his sister-in-law.","Yanshu was extremely excited and immediately turned her gaze towards them upon being seated.","She saw that Mu Zhengping appeared to be in his thirties, tall and well-built, with skin slightly darker than that of the Central Plains people, and quite handsome features.","However, she hadn't expected that this time he would bring his nephew along — that is, Princess Shou'an's son, nicknamed A'lang, who was the Crown Prince of Nanzhao, Mu Jingshuo.","The young boy looked about twelve or thirteen years old, his features a perfect blend of Central Plains and Nanzhao characteristics, appearing quite handsome.","Children are always attached to their mothers, and at this moment, he was affectionately nestled close to his mother, looking both adorable and pitiful.","As the banquet began, both sides exchanged greetings and pleasantries.","Yanshu observed quietly and felt that this King Mu looked gloomy, as if he was a bit unhappy.","She quietly called out to the system, [What's wrong with Mu Zhengping?]","The system replied, [Nothing much, he just heard about Princess Shou'an drinking with the Rouran Envoy and got jealous.]","Yanshu: [...]","Hasn't he gotten used to it after all these years?","At this moment, Mu Zhengping addressed the Emperor, \"This time, I was able to successfully resolve the issue with the Pu clan, thanks to Your Majesty's assistance. As it coincides with Your Majesty's Changnin Festival, and considering that my nephew A'lang hasn't visited his relatives in the Central Plains for many years, I brought him along. It's a bit abrupt, please forgive us.\"","Yuwen Lan politely replied, \"Having friends come from afar, how delightful. King Mu is being too modest. As we are relatives, it's only right that we visit each other more often.\"","The Empress Dowager also said, \"It's been many years since we last met, A'lang has grown so much. If we hadn't seen him this time, we might not have recognized him on the street. What His Majesty says is right, relatives should visit each other more often.\"","After these words, both sides nodded in agreement and toasted each other.","But after putting down their wine cups, Mu Zhengping suddenly coughed and said to Princess Shou'an, \"There's another matter I came for this time. I want to invite sister-in-law to return to Nanzhao. A'lang is still young after all, and it's not good for him to have been without his mother's company for so many years.\"","Upon hearing this, Yanshu paused, thinking to herself, could Mu Zhengping be making a public confession???","No way!","Then, he continued, \"In the past, the Pu clan committed many evil deeds, and I bear some responsibility for that. I haven't been a good ruler, nor a good uncle, and certainly not a good brother. So this time, I've made up my mind to invite sister-in-law back to Nanzhao to assist A'lang.\"","Assist...","Everyone who heard this paused quietly—","Why did King Mu use this word? Could he have some plan?","Princess Shou'an, of course, also caught on and immediately asked, \"You want me to go back and assist A'lang? What about you?\"","Mu Zhengping replied...","\"I plan to renounce secular life and become a monk.\"","What???","As soon as these words were spoken, not only Princess Shou'an was stunned, but everyone in the hall was shocked.","Be-become a monk?","Mu Zhengping, the mighty King of Nanzhao, wants to become a monk???","Yanshu also looked surprised, thinking to herself, could this person be using some sort of ploy?","Then she heard the system chime in to explain, [To be fair, Buddhism is quite prevalent in Nanzhao, and it's not uncommon for nobles to become monks. There have been several in the Mu family, such as A'lang's paternal grandfather, who abdicated and became a monk himself, passing the throne to his son.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Could it be that this man has grown weary of waiting for love and become disillusioned?","She immediately looked towards Princess Shou'an.","Only to find that the Emperor and Empress Dowager were also looking in the same direction.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Her top supporter was one thing, but who was it that said they weren't interested in gossip yesterday?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Nevermind, let's pretend not to have heard that.","At the end of their gazes, before Princess Shou'an could say anything, A'lang became anxious and immediately said, \"Uncle, no! Don't abandon A'lang to become a monk!\"","After these words were spoken, Princess Shou'an, who had come to her senses, finally spoke up, \"Why put yourself through this? You are, after all, the ruler of Nanzhao. What would I, a mere woman, know about such matters?\"","Little did they know, Mu Zhengping said, \"It's alright. The court has already been purged, and those who remain are loyal ministers. They will all help you and A'lang. Moreover, I believe His Majesty will surely support you both.\"","As he spoke, he glanced at Yuwen Lan.","Yuwen Lan had no choice but to speak, \"Nanzhao and Great Liang have been on good terms for generations. If there are any difficulties, I will certainly spare no effort to help. However, regarding the matter of becoming a monk, wouldn't King Mu like to reconsider?\"","But Mu Zhengping replied, \"Thank you, Your Majesty, but my mind is made up. Over the years, I have wronged many people - my late elder brother, my sister-in-law, and A'lang... If it weren't for me, he should have had his mother by his side...\"","As his words fell, Yanshu couldn't help but think to herself, [Is he referring to that affair between the two of them?]","Yuwen Lan, [...It seems so.]","The Empress Dowager was also pondering, [Oh? Could there be something more between these two?]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Mother is indeed formidable.","While the rest of the crowd, [???]","What's going on? From the sound of it, did this King Mu do something?","For a moment, all eyes shifted between Princess Shou'an and Mu Zhengping.","After a moment of silence, Princess Shou'an finally spoke, \"A'lang is after all my flesh and blood. I haven't been there for him much these years, and that's my fault. You have been an excellent uncle to him, and I've always been grateful for that. After His Majesty's Long'an Festival, I will return to Nanzhao to be with A'lang. But A'lang is still young, and it's more appropriate for you to keep your position, King Mu. As for becoming a monk, let's forget about that.\"","Before Mu Zhengping could respond, A'lang immediately brightened up and said, \"Mother, do you really mean it?\"","Princess Shou'an ruffled her son's hair and said, \"Of course I mean it. In front of His Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and your uncles and aunts, how could I lie to you?\"","A'lang broke into a smile and said, \"Thank you, Mother.\"","Mu Zhengping didn't speak, but merely raised his cup and took a drink. The gloom between his brows seemed to have lessened somewhat.","Yanshu observed this and raised an eyebrow inwardly.","Has Princess Shou'an been subdued?","Does she still care for her brother-in-law in her heart?","Or is she simply concerned for her son?","Could it be that the \"playboy\" tactic of crying, making a scene, and threatening suicide worked???","...","Yuwen Lan thought to himself, who cares.","It's good that this matter has a resolution...","Hopefully, this aunt will return to Nanzhao soon.","He was truly worried about his beloved consort's constantly fluctuating emotions!","It's exhausting.","As the Emperor's birthday drew nearer, envoys from various countries began to arrive one after another.","On the eve of the Long'an Festival, the palace officially held a banquet for foreign envoys to entertain the diplomats from various countries.","Yanshu, as the highest-ranking consort in the harem at present, was able to accompany the Emperor to attend.","She hadn't realized until now how developed Great Liang's foreign relations were. At the banquet, apart from several important ministers of the court, there were envoys from various countries, with seats extending all the way to the entrance of Jiying Hall.","Most of the envoys were high-ranking and powerful figures in their own countries. Some countries, like Gaoli, even sent a prince in person, showing their high regard for Great Liang.","At the banquet, everyone wore the traditional clothing of their own countries and raised their glasses together to congratulate the Emperor on his birthday. The scene was quite magnificent.","While Yanshu marveled at this, she couldn't help but wonder if there were any interesting \"melons\" (gossip) among these people.","As the second round of drinks was being served and the atmosphere in the hall was becoming convivial, the Dongwo Envoy stepped forward and said, \"To celebrate Your Majesty's birthday, our king has specially prepared a gift for Your Majesty. Please accept it with a smile.\"","As he spoke, he waved his hand towards the entrance of the hall.","In a moment, two women walked into the hall. Both had graceful figures, wore veils, and seemed to emit a faint fragrance.","Everyone was stunned. Was the Kingdom of Dongwo offering beautiful women as gifts to the Emperor?","Tsk tsk, it was rumored that the Dongwo royal family had indulged in sensual pleasures in recent years, with many variations in their play. Who would have thought they would even offer beautiful women as gifts?","Sure enough, the envoy smiled again and said, \"These two women were carefully selected by our country, representing our king's sincerity. We hope for eternal friendship between Dongwo and Great Liang, and we hope Your Majesty will accept them.\"","As his words fell, everyone secretly glanced at the Emperor.","Would the Emperor accept these Dongwo beauties?","Especially now, when Consort Yi was pregnant.","There weren't many people in the harem to begin with, and the other one wasn't favored at all. The Emperor must have been quite frustrated these days, right?","At this moment, Yanshu, sitting beside the Emperor, was also pondering this question.","—Tsk, originally planning to eat others' \"melons\" tonight, but now it seems the \"melon\" is on my own head?","Filling up the harem so soon?","And two at once?","Both foreigners?","Will the Emperor... accept them?","But before the Emperor could speak, she heard the system chime in, [It depends on whether the Emperor can accept it or not. These two are actually intersex.]","Yanshu, [???]"]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this news, Yanshu's mind instantly became a jumbled mess.","\"What?\"","\"Intersex people???\"","\"Dongwo actually sent this to the Emperor???\"","\"Why would they do such a thing?!\"","The system calmly replied, \"Don't even mention it. The Dongwo royal family is extremely perverted, and this trend has been prevalent in recent years. Their own monarch keeps several of them. They found out that the Emperor hasn't had any children or visited the harem in the past three years, so they assumed he might be perverted like them. That's why they sent these two over.\"","Yanshu felt like she was about to cough up blood. What kind of assumption was this?","Come to think of it, the Emperor was quite pitiful. Just because his unreliable father had ruined him for three years, how did those Dongwo people demonize him into a pervert?","However, she had thought intersex people only existed in modern times. How were they here now?","The system explained, \"As I said before, since a certain country's monarch is perverted, people below him developed a special drug to cultivate such individuals to please him.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, that was indeed very perverted.","\"But the problem is, aren't they afraid the Great Liang Emperor won't be interested in this? They actually sent such people from so far away?!\"","The system sighed and said, \"You're still too naive. These people have undergone very professional training. Many can't resist them. Besides, even if the Emperor doesn't touch them, putting them in the harem is still a hidden danger! After all, they are essentially male.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Don't tell me they're planning to have these two secretly cuckold the Emperor?","Ugh... disgusting.","As one of the harem members, Yanshu couldn't help but feel goosebumps all over.","But that wasn't all. The system continued, \"Moreover, these two aren't ordinary. They are experts who have undergone national combat training, with excellent martial arts skills.\"","Experts?","Yanshu was startled, \"Don't tell me they're planning an assassination?\"","The system replied, \"More or less. Haven't you heard that in recent years, Dongwo has repeatedly invaded Great Liang's southeastern sea defenses? The Emperor ordered a severe counterattack, causing them many casualties, forcing them to sue for peace. Do you think they sincerely came to celebrate the Emperor's birthday this time?\"","Yanshu suddenly understood.","So Dongwo's goal was to disrupt Great Liang by any means necessary.","Truly a wolf's ambition!","After cursing that certain country's monarch several times in her heart, Yanshu thought of another crucial question.","What did the Emperor plan to do with these two \"beauties\"?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","What could he do?","At this moment, he was furious!","— Those Dongwo people would invade the southeastern coast every warm season, so in recent years he had increased efforts to train the navy and build sea walls. Fortunately, Great Liang was ultimately stronger than that small country, so they could subdue them every time they struck.","This time, he had originally wanted to negotiate properly with them, but he never expected they would pull this trick.","Even if they were normal women, he would never accept them into his harem.","Moreover, he had just heard about this situation from Yanshu.","What?","Intersex???","Damn! How could Dongwo be so absurd, so insulting to him!!!","Yuwen Lan was naturally filled with anger that rushed to his head. For the first time in his life, he could barely conceal his emotions as he coldly said to the Dongwo attendant, \"Regarding the alliance, as long as your country is sincere, Great Liang will also treat it sincerely. I don't want these people, you can take them back for your monarch to use.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, the hall was filled with surprise.","Whether it was the foreign guests or Great Liang's ministers, they all heard the full disdain in his words.","— This was strange! The other side had only sent beauties, and judging by their figures, they must be extremely beautiful. Not only did the Emperor not want them, but he was also angry?","Why was this?","Yanshu was also surprised. What was going on with this man? It was fine if he didn't want the beauties, but why was he angry?","Just as she was confused, she saw the Emperor speak to the palace servants, \"Why haven't you escorted them out yet?\"","The servants complied and led the two \"beauties\" out.","With the scene finally cleared, Yuwen Lan's anger had not yet subsided. He picked up a wine cup and took a drink.","Unexpectedly, he heard Yanshu's disappointed voice in his mind, \"They left just like that? I didn't even get to see what they looked like...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","The minister from the Court of State Ceremonial promptly invited everyone to raise their glasses, and ordered the singers and dancers to follow up quickly. Except for the unhappy expressions on the faces of the Dongwo envoys, the hall soon returned to its lively atmosphere.","The banquet continued merrily for two hours. As the bright moon moved westward and the hour grew late, it finally came to an end.","The Emperor and his beloved consort left their seats first, and the guests also departed from the palace.","Yuwen Lan had drunk wine tonight, and considering his beloved consort's pregnancy, he specially called for the imperial carriage.","There was no one else in the carriage. As Yuwen Lan closed his eyes to rest, he heard the girl's thoughts in his ear, \"Why was he angry just now? After all, he shouldn't have known that those two were 'that kind of people', right? Could it be that he simply dislikes that Dongwo country? So he also despised those two 'beauties' along with it?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded inwardly, there was indeed this factor.","Then he heard her click her tongue, \"If it were from other countries, like Rouran or Gaoli, would he have accepted them?\"","Yuwen Lan suddenly opened his eyes, \"???\"","No such thing!","Did she think those foreign countries would send beauties to Great Liang for no reason? They all had similar intentions as Dongwo!","It's just that they probably weren't as... perverted as Dongwo!","Yes, that's the word, she seemed to have used it before.","Just thinking about this matter made his anger rise again, but at this moment, he heard her speak, \"Your Majesty, I have something to report to you. I hope you won't be shocked.\"","Yuwen Lan then said, \"What is it?\"","He heard her say, \"Actually, those two that Dongwo intended to present to you today... were not normal women. They are both male and female. Some places call this kind... 'ladyboys'.\"","Yuwen Lan pretended to be surprised, \"Is that so? How could Dongwo be so absurd?\"","...Though this term was quite fitting.","He saw her nod and say, \"Indeed it is so. Therefore, it's a good thing Your Majesty rejected them tonight. However, I wonder, if other countries were to present normal women to you, would you accept them?\"","As she spoke, she stared at him with inquisitive eyes.","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but smile and said, \"Do you hope I would?\"","He saw her pout immediately and say, \"How could that be for this humble consort to decide? Even if I didn't hope so, you might still accept them.\"","Yuwen Lan deliberately remained ambiguous and raised an eyebrow, saying, \"Am I so cheap in your heart?\"","He saw her take a deep breath and lower her eyes, saying, \"This humble consort wouldn't dare.\"","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but reach out to pinch her chin, saying, \"You clearly dare very much. If I really were to accept other women into the harem, I fear you would have cursed me as a scumbag countless times by now.\"","Yanshu was stunned and hurriedly said, \"How could that be? Your Majesty thinks too poorly of this humble consort...\"","In her heart, she thought, \"He guessed quite accurately, but I'm afraid it wouldn't be as simple as just cursing him. I would write him into a novel to be morally condemned by people, then take the child and live my own life behind closed doors, never paying attention to him again! Hmph!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Why the \"hmph\"? He hadn't done anything!","He could only sigh, take her hand, and say, \"Even if there were three thousand weak waters, I would only take one ladle to drink.\"","As his words fell, he saw her freeze.","Her eyes looked at him, thinking, \"Is he... saying sweet nothings?\"","Yuwen Lan smiled profoundly, thinking that it seemed sweet words should be said appropriately after all.","Look how enchanted she was.","But in the next moment, he heard her think, \"Oh right, I must write a novel tomorrow, thoroughly exposing the absurd affairs of that Dongwo monarch! It's a foreign country anyway, so I don't have to worry about anyone identifying themselves! Hehe, I'm sure my readers would love to see it!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Weren't we talking about sweet nothings? Why did it suddenly jump to this?","And why does it have to be written into a novel!!!","He couldn't help but say, \"Prenatal education is very important. After all, this is my first child. Starting tomorrow, I'll arrange for someone to read books to you, beginning with the Four Books and Five Classics.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Yanshu was dumbfounded, \"What? This humble consort doesn't, doesn't, doesn't want to listen...\"","However, before she could finish speaking, he said in a solemn voice, \"This is an imperial edict.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Before she could respond, he added, \"It doesn't need to be much. Just listen for a quarter of an hour each day. If that's not enough, we can add some Tang poetry and Song lyrics to cultivate your temperament.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Good heavens, was this prenatal education for the baby or a lesson for her? Why did she have to be forced to study even when she was about to become a mother? Oh, woe is me.","Forced by imperial power, Yanshu had no choice but to obey.","So early the next morning, she found herself listening to the Director of the Imperial Academy personally reciting the \"Book of Songs\" to her.","The Director was very conscientious. After reciting the original text, he carefully explained it to her, afraid she might not understand something.","Yanshu forced a smile and gave the Director a wolf-hair brush as a token of gratitude.","Today was the Changning Festival, which was also the Emperor's birthday. After finishing her lesson, Yanshu quickly dressed up and accompanied the Emperor to the Cining Palace to pay respects to the Empress Dowager.","After all, as the saying goes, \"A child's birthday is the mother's day of suffering.\" Although the Empress Dowager was not the Emperor's birth mother, she had raised him for many years and her efforts were praiseworthy.","After paying their respects, there were still ministers waiting in the front court to pay homage to the Emperor, so Yuwen Lan bid farewell to the Empress Dowager and went to the Qianming Palace.","Yanshu breathed a sigh of relief, thinking that her top-tier ally, the Empress Dowager, was indeed more approachable. Finally, she could chat with her about recent events.","The Empress Dowager had actually been waiting for her too. As soon as the Emperor left, she dismissed everyone else and asked, \"I heard that last night the Dongwo envoy presented beautiful women to His Majesty, but he angrily drove them away. What exactly happened?\"","Yanshu could only lie on behalf of the Emperor again, saying, \"Because His Majesty is wise and brilliant, he knew in advance that those two beauties were not ordinary women. They were... people specially raised by the Dongwo royal family who could be... both male and female.\"","Tsk, afraid of frightening the Empress Dowager, she deliberately slowed her speech.","However, the Empress Dowager was still shocked and exclaimed, \"How could this be? How could Dongwo be so outrageous and shameless? Isn't this blatantly insulting our Great Liang? They should be thrown out!\"","Yanshu quickly agreed and reassured her, \"Don't worry, Your Highness. His Majesty said that after the Changning Festival, he will send them back. As for other political matters, he won't compromise with them at all.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and sighed, \"This Dongwo has always harbored intentions to destroy our Great Liang! We must not underestimate them. It's good that His Majesty understands this.\"","Yanshu hastily nodded in agreement."]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90","paragraphs":["Today is the Changning Festival, which is also the Emperor's birthday.","Therefore, the celebratory activities in the palace were mainly concentrated on this day.","At this time, Yanshu had just finished discussing the Dongwo matter with the Empress Dowager when she heard a palace servant report that the female guests invited to the palace for the celebration had arrived.","The two of them then went out together to the Spring Harmony Pavilion where the female guests would be entertained today.","The Emperor's birthday was no ordinary occasion. In the Spring Harmony Pavilion today, besides the noble ladies of the Great Liang royal family and the wives of several high-ranking court officials, there were also the wives of envoys from various foreign countries. They were all dressed in their own national costumes, presenting a colorful and diverse sight that was quite lively.","Among them, the most imposing was undoubtedly the Gao Li Princess. She was seen wearing a characteristic Gao Li spring silk dress, with her hair styled in a grand Gao Li bun adorned with various gold, silver, pearl, and jade ornaments. The two maids by her side were also elaborately dressed, attracting much attention.","In fact, Yanshu had already met this Gao Li Princess at the grand banquet in Jiying Hall last night. She remembered that the princess's attire was already very splendid last night, but unexpectedly, after just one night, she had changed into a new outfit, once again becoming the focus of the entire gathering.","She thought to herself that this must be someone who loves beauty.","However, the journey from Gao Li to the capital was long, and for a beauty lover, it must have been quite challenging to bring so many accessories and clothes on such a long trip. The carriage must have been quite heavily loaded.","Of course, regardless of others, what made her happiest today was that she could see her mother again.","Well, after all, her mother Ms. Zhu was now a proper Marchioness with an official title, and naturally qualified to attend such banquets.","Moreover, Yanshu was now carrying the imperial heir, which meant a bright future ahead. During the banquet, many noble ladies took the initiative to chat with Ms. Zhu, taking turns to compliment her with flattering words, their intention to socialize quite obvious.","Today's celebratory activities would last all day. After lunch, various songs, dances, operas, and acrobatic performances began on the stage of the Spring Harmony Pavilion.","Yanshu deliberately sat with her mother and, taking advantage of the loud gongs and drums from the stage, quietly reminded her mother, \"Those who were flattering you earlier, just listen to them but don't take it too seriously. Always be cautious and don't trust others too easily.\"","Her mother nodded and said, \"Don't worry, Your Highness. I understand.\"","Yanshu said good, and then chatted with her mother for a while about the situation at home.","Not long after, a short opera on stage finished, and all the guests applauded in appreciation.","At this moment, the elaborately dressed Gao Li Princess said in not-so-fluent Chinese, \"The songs and dances of Great Liang are very wonderful. To express our gratitude, I have also asked my maids to prepare a dance performance for everyone to enjoy.\"","Oh? Gao Li had also prepared a dance?","Everyone became curious upon hearing this.","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Then please, let us see it.\"","The Gao Li Princess nodded and signaled to her maids.","The two maids responded, prepared for a moment to the side, and then went up to the stage.","There was still a prop square table left on the stage from the earlier opera performance. The two maids lit a candle and placed it in the center of the table, then each picked up a long drum and began to sing and dance around the table.","Surprisingly, there was even someone playing music by the side of the stage, also a maid of the Gao Li Princess.","Seeing this scene, Yanshu couldn't help but sigh inwardly that this princess was someone who knew how to enjoy life! To bring not only plenty of clothes and accessories on such a long journey, but even a band?","Impressive!","Then she heard the system interject, [This is mainly because her husband loves to enjoy life. That Gao Li prince Li Taichu... is a notorious playboy. As his wife, in order not to be disliked by her husband, she can only try her best to dress up and come up with various ways to please him.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","So that's how it is.","Well, with such a husband, this Gao Li Princess doesn't have it easy either.","Just as she was thinking this, she saw the two maids on stage suddenly jump onto the square table and begin dancing around the candle they had lit earlier on the tabletop.","It's worth noting that the square table was only about two feet and eight inches on each side. These two maids stood on top of it, beating their drums and dancing, constantly changing their movements, occasionally spinning around, yet remaining remarkably stable, as if floating on clouds and flowing water, causing everyone to marvel.","Most importantly, the candle they had lit remained unextinguished throughout their performance, continuing to burn steadily even after they finished dancing and left the table.","As the dance ended, a round of applause erupted in the Spring Harmony Pavilion, with everyone praising and cheering, creating a very lively atmosphere.","The Empress Dowager couldn't help but nod and say, \"The Gao Li dancers are highly skilled. It's truly eye-opening.\"","The guests all agreed.","After the applause died down, the Gao Li Princess expressed her thanks, and then said, \"These two women were chosen by me after careful selection. I brought them to Great Liang this time intending to present them as a gift. If the Empress Dowager likes them, please keep them in the palace. They can play music and dance, and can accompany the Empress Dowager and Consort Yi.\"","As she said this, she nodded specifically towards Yanshu.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Hmm, she had just been thinking that this princess didn't have it easy, but now she's trying to send people to the imperial harem.","Could it be that she saw the Emperor refuse those two \"beauties\" from Dongwo last night, and knowing it would be difficult to approach the Emperor directly, she's now trying to get the Empress Dowager's approval?","Just as she was thinking this, she suddenly paused. Wait, these two maids wouldn't happen to be... some kind of... strange beings, would they?","Then she heard the system say, [No, they're not. Compared to Dongwo, the Gao Li royal family is slightly more normal. However, these two maids have already been touched by that Gao Li prince. Of course, it's not just these two. Among the women in the Gao Li court, as long as they have some beauty, that prince hasn't spared any of them.]","Yanshu: [...]","Well, he really is a playboy after all.","However, she still didn't quite understand, so she asked the system again, [Doesn't this Gao Li Princess know that the men in Great Liang value a woman's chastity very much?]","System: [Of course she knows. They value it in their country too.]","Yanshu was even more confused, [Then why does she still want to give maids who have been touched by her husband to the Emperor? Isn't she afraid of angering the Emperor of Great Liang?]","System: [That's exactly what she's planning.]","Yanshu: \"???\"","That's exactly what the Gao Li Princess is planning?","What kind of strategy is this?","The system didn't respond immediately, so she tried to think from the Gao Li Princess's perspective. Could it be that the prince's constant philandering has made his wife hate him deeply?","And then the wife plans to use this method to anger the Emperor of Great Liang, thereby causing Great Liang to be angry with the Gao Li royal family, and then have their royal family punish her husband?","System: [That's more or less it.]","Yanshu couldn't help but exclaim, [This method seems way too roundabout! Moreover, as Li Taichu's principal wife, if Li Taichu is punished, won't she also suffer the consequences?]","She still couldn't understand. Isn't this what they call killing 800 enemies but losing 1000 of your own?","Then she heard the system say, [He won't be severely punished. This Li Taichu is like the tallest among dwarfs, currently the most powerful prince in Gao Li. His maternal clan is also the largest clan in Gao Li, and no one else can touch him. This princess has always wanted to take revenge on him, but she has no other means within the country. Now that she's finally come to Great Liang, she can only use this method to teach him a lesson. She's not hoping for much, she just wants to make those ministers back home give her husband a good talking to, at least make this Li Taichu behave a bit better.]","Yanshu: [...]","It's really hard on this Gao Li Princess to go to such lengths just for this small goal.","Of course, regardless of what the Gao Li Princess's goal is now, the key is how the Empress Dowager plans to respond.","Yanshu tried to look towards her number one supporter.","With a bit of uncertainty in her heart.","She saw her number one supporter smile and say, \"I am old now, and it would be a waste of these two young ladies' youth. Besides, with the great distance between our two countries, it would be unconscionable for me to keep them here, far from their homes. I appreciate the Princess's kind intention, but I must decline accepting these people. After all, they were born and raised by their parents, and it would be a sin to make them leave their homeland for no good reason.\"","Perhaps because this speech was a bit long, the Gao Li Princess had to wait for the interpreter to translate before she understood.","Afterwards, she could only say with obvious disappointment in her eyes, \"Very well, thank you for the Empress Dowager's kind heart.\"","Little did they know that as soon as those words were spoken, the Empress Dowager addressed everyone, saying, \"At present, Imperial Consort Yi is with child. This is His Majesty's first child and is of great importance to the Great Liang. I do not wish for anything to happen that might disturb her pregnancy.\"","Upon hearing this, all those present in the hall could only unanimously agree.","Inwardly, they couldn't help but marvel - the Empress Dowager's words were clearly meant to protect Imperial Consort Yi!","Tsk tsk, come to think of it, Imperial Consort Yi was indeed formidable! Despite being the daughter of a minor official from a small region, she had not only won the Emperor's exclusive favor but had also gained such care from the Empress Dowager!","What methods did she use to achieve this?","As for the Empress Dowager's intentions, how could Yanshu herself not understand?","So after everyone had finished agreeing, she immediately addressed the Empress Dowager, \"This humble consort thanks Your Majesty for your concern.\"","The Empress Dowager merely nodded slightly and said in a mild tone, \"Let's watch the play now, and speak no more of other matters.\"","As her words fell, a new act began on the stage, and everyone was soon immersed in it once again.","Only Yanshu remained moved in her heart—","Aww, her number one supporter was so good to her!","She decided that when she returned, she would write a story and read it to the Empress Dowager.","True to her word, when Yanshu returned to Ganlu Palace in the evening, she immediately began writing.","Although her efficiency wasn't as high as before her pregnancy, her spirits were much better than in recent days. By the time Yuwen Lan arrived in the evening, she had already written out the first half of the story.","Seeing her sitting at the desk, Yuwen Lan was surprised and asked, \"What made you think of writing a story today?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Because this humble consort was struck with some inspiration today and felt it should be written down quickly. If I don't write for too long, I fear readers might forget about me completely.\"","—Hehe, it was mainly for her number one supporter! She remembered that the Empress Dowager had once mentioned liking strange tales, so this time she deliberately wrote it as a supernatural story.","Yuwen Lan listened silently, feeling a twinge of jealousy rising in his heart—","Why was her relationship with the Empress Dowager so good now?","After all, was he raised by the Empress Dowager, or was she?","Was she his beloved consort, or the Empress Dowager's?","...","After silently stewing in jealousy for a while, he finally couldn't help but ask, \"So what kind of story did you write this time? Can you tell it to me first?\"","Fortunately, she was quite generous. Upon hearing his request, she immediately nodded and began to tell him, \"This humble consort wrote a supernatural story today. It tells of a country beyond the Eastern Sea, whose ruler was extravagant and licentious, never attending to proper affairs. Because of this, many corrupt officials emerged in his court, who spent their days thinking not of how to govern the country well, but of how to please this ruler to gain positions and wealth.\"","\"One day, someone presented a peerlessly beautiful woman to this ruler. The ruler was overjoyed and immediately took her into his harem, rewarding the person who had brought her. From then on, he spent all his time entangled with this beauty, neglecting state affairs even more. However, soon the people around the ruler noticed that his complexion was worsening, and he gradually became thin and aged in appearance.\"","\"After some investigation, people discovered that the beautiful woman was actually a demon, and the ruler's vital essence had already been consumed by her, leaving him on the brink of death. Frightened, people hurriedly sought out sorcerers to exorcise the demon, but the demon had already grown too powerful, and ordinary sorcerers were no match for her. In less than half a month, the demon had not only drained the ruler dry and killed the ministers, but had also begun to harm the common people.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Isn't this talking about the ruler of Dongwo?","Hmm, that person deserves to die! It's quite satisfying to hear it like this.","So taking advantage of her pause, he quickly asked, \"Then who finally subdues this demon?\"","He saw her smile mysteriously and say, \"Naturally, it's a mysterious female warrior from the Eastern Continent. This female warrior has unparalleled martial arts skills and knows all sorts of demon-slaying techniques. After battling the demon for seven days and seven nights, she finally subdues it.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Female warrior?","...Could this be talking about herself again?","Sure enough, he immediately heard her add, \"Oh right, Your Majesty, do you remember that story about the female warrior I told you about before? I plan to include this story in that book, making it into a long tale.\"","Hehe, after all, one must constantly innovate and surprise the readers!","\"...\"","Yuwen Lan could only nod and say, \"Alright, do as you wish. What I want to know is, what does the female warrior do after defeating the demon?\"","Yanshu thought as she spoke, \"After slaying the demon, all the people there begged her to stay and govern the country, but the female warrior was free-spirited by nature and didn't agree. In a dawn that no one noticed, she quietly left again.\"","Hehe, this way she could lead into the next story!","Hmm, wonder which country will provide some bizarre news next.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He wasn't interested in the bizarre news from those strange countries, he was just worried whether her body could handle it. So he said, \"Write slowly, and don't tire yourself out.\"","Yanshu nodded.","Then he added, \"But no matter what, you still need to listen to the Four Books and Five Classics daily.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","This man always knew how to dampen one's spirits at the right moment.","After finishing the story, it was already late. The two of them each went to wash up, and then went to bed.","Of course, as it happened to be Yuwen Lan's birthday, Yanshu didn't forget to sing him a birthday song at the bedside.","This warmed his heart, and he couldn't help but kiss her forehead twice before hugging her from behind as they fell asleep.","Who would have thought that in the middle of the night, they would suddenly hear Fu Hai's urgent report from outside the hall.","\"Your Majesty, the Court of State Ceremonial just reported that there was an assassination attempt at the envoy's residence tonight, and the Gao Li Prince has been wounded.\"","What?","Yuwen Lan's eyes snapped open."]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91","paragraphs":["What?","Prince Gao Li was assassinated?","Upon hearing this news, Yuwen Lan jolted awake from his sleep, immediately threw off his covers, and walked several steps to the outer chamber, saying, \"What happened? Come in and explain!\"","Fu Hai hurriedly pushed open the door and entered with an anxious expression, \"Your Majesty, the Commander from the embassy just reported that there was a bloody incident at the embassy tonight. The night guards first heard screams, and after investigation, they found Prince Gao Li stabbed in the abdomen, blood everywhere...\"","Stabbed in the abdomen?","Yuwen Lan urgently asked, \"How is he now?\"","Fu Hai quickly replied, \"The embassy physician is treating him, but he's lost a lot of blood. I'm afraid the outlook isn't good...\"","More likely to die than live?","Yuwen Lan's brows furrowed immediately.","...","Meanwhile, on the bed in the inner chamber, Yanshu was still drowsy. She had originally turned over intending to continue sleeping when she heard the system chime, [Hey, Prince Gao Li got stabbed, want to hear this juicy gossip?]","What? Prince Gao Li got stabbed?","She became fully awake and immediately opened her eyes wide, saying, [Yes, yes, yes! Quick, tell me what happened!]","Could it be that the Gao Li Princess, seeing she couldn't get rid of the maid, decided to take direct action and stab her husband?","But the system said, [No way, unless the Gao Li Princess had a death wish. Besides, none of her people are that loyal. Who would dare stab a crown prince for her? If they accidentally killed him, she'd end up a widow.]","That made sense, but Yanshu was confused, [Then who stabbed him? Surely not real assassins!]","The system replied, [It was those two \"ladyboys\" from East Wa, not assassins.]","What?","The ladyboys did it?","Yanshu was completely stunned, [Why would the ladyboys stab this perverted Gao Li? How did they even end up together???]","System: [...you already called him a pervert, do you really need to ask?]","Yanshu paused, pondering, [Could it be that the pervert took a liking to those two ladyboys, and since East Wa was looking to cause trouble, they stabbed him?]","System: [That's exactly what happened. Li Taichu had his eye on those two ladyboys since they first appeared two nights ago. Since the Emperor didn't want them, he sent people to make contact these past couple of days, and tonight he called them to his room when no one was around. But before anything could happen, he discovered something wasn't right about those two, and it scared him so badly he started screaming. Then the ladyboys took the opportunity to stab him. Fortunately, the embassy guards reacted quickly when they heard the screams and rushed over immediately, otherwise he would have been stabbed to death by those two.]","Yanshu: [....]","What, that pervert was scared enough to scream?","Tsk, that's quite the mental image.","Goodness, this must have been the first time Prince Gao Li encountered something like this - the psychological impact probably won't be easy to get over.","Thank goodness it wasn't her little Emperor, close call.","After such reflections, she asked the system, [Then what happened?]","System: [Well, now we have the current situation. Those two ladyboys were skilled fighters and quickly escaped when they heard the guards coming. Right now the embassy guards haven't discovered the truth and think it was outside assassins.]","Yanshu drew in a sharp breath, thinking this wasn't good at all - he was still a prince after all, and if he died in Da Liang, wouldn't that cause huge problems?","So she asked the system again, [How is Li Taichu's condition now?]","System: [He's lost a lot of blood, they need to hurry. If it's much later, he might not make it.]","Yanshu was startled and quickly got out of bed, rushing to the outer chamber to say to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, Prince Gao Li absolutely cannot die. To be safe, we should send Doctor Jiang to examine him!\"","As it turned out, they had thought alike, and Yuwen Lan said, \"I've already sent someone to call him.\"","Yanshu breathed a sigh of relief, but then saw him finish speaking and start walking toward the inner chamber, hurriedly telling her, \"This matter is extremely serious. I need to go to Qianming Palace.\"","Yanshu quickly followed, lowering her voice to say, \"I've already found out what happened - it wasn't outside assassins who did it.\"","Yuwen Lan paused and looked at her, \"What happened?\"","Yanshu coughed and lowered her voice again, \"Actually, it was those two ladyboys from East Wa who did it. This Prince Gao Li is a lecher who had already taken advantage of their own women, and as soon as he saw these two ladyboys, he immediately had impure thoughts. Tonight he secretly called them to his room, and since the two ladyboys wanted to cause trouble for Da Liang anyway, they took the opportunity to stab him!\"","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"So that's what happened?\"","She nodded, \"It's definitely true. Otherwise, with so many guards at the embassy, how could outside assassins easily get in? And how would they immediately find the most prestigious Prince Gao Li?\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, thinking that since she said so, it must be true.","But then he saw her grin mischievously and say, \"I heard Prince Gao Li was so scared by the ladyboys that he screamed his head off. He probably has psychological trauma now, hehe...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","At a time like this, how could she still be thinking about such things?","He looked at her helplessly, \"Stop thinking about such nonsense. I still need to go to Qianming Palace. It's still early, you should get some more sleep.\"","She nodded but asked curiously, \"How does Your Majesty plan to handle this matter?\"","After all, directly arresting the two ladyboys didn't seem appropriate - they would probably still need to investigate and go through the proper procedures.","Yuwen Lan said, \"The urgent matter is to first save Prince Gao Li's life. As for the real culprits, since they're not outside assassins, it will be easier to handle. As long as we don't let the East Wa people escape, we can have the Ministry of Justice and Ministry of Punishment investigate.\"","Although his beloved consort had such special abilities, the court officials still needed their training - otherwise, what was the point of keeping them?","Hearing him say this, Yanshu nodded and helped him dress before seeing him out, then returned to bed to sleep.","Get enough rest, and continue enjoying the drama tomorrow.","Several hours later, Yuwen Lan was waiting in the imperial study when the Junior Minister of Justice, Minister of Court Ceremonial, and Commander of the Imperial Guard arrived.","What he cared most about at the moment was naturally Li Taichu's life or death, so he first asked them, \"How is Prince Gao Li now?\"","The Minister of Court Ceremonial quickly replied, \"Your Majesty, after Doctor Jiang arrived last night, he immediately treated the Prince. Currently, the Prince's bleeding has stopped, but his body is still very weak. Doctor Jiang has remained at the embassy, not leaving his side.\"","Seeing that he hadn't died, Yuwen Lan relaxed slightly and then asked the Minister of Justice, \"How is the investigation going?\"","The Minister of Justice hurriedly said, \"Your Majesty, after examining the embassy inside and out, including the doors and windows of the room where the incident occurred, we suspect the assassin did not enter from outside but was likely already inside the embassy. We will need to conduct a thorough search within the embassy.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and said, \"Then conduct the search.\"","However, after he spoke, the Commander wore a troubled expression and said, \"Your Majesty may not know, but since last night when we tried to search the embassy, we've met with much resistance. Except for Nanzhao King Mu who actively cooperated, the people from East Wa, Dangxia, and even Gao Li's own people refuse to let us search their rooms. Especially the Gao Li Princess - since last night she has insisted that it was the court's security failure that led to her husband's injury, and she won't even let us question Prince Gao Li's attendants, showing extreme resistance.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan frowned.","According to what Yanshu said last night, Prince Gao Li's close attendants must have known about him seeking out the East Wa ladyboys. Was the Gao Li Princess obstructing them like this to cover up her husband's shame?","But she was still an honored guest, and a woman at that - it wouldn't be appropriate for the guards to force their way in...","While he was pondering this, a palace servant announced from outside, \"Your Majesty, Consort Yi requests an audience.\"","Hmm? Why has she come?","Yuwen Lan gathered his thoughts and said, \"Enter.\"","Soon, Yanshu appeared before him, and after paying her respects said, \"Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager heard about last night's incident at the embassy and is very concerned. She has specially sent me to console the Gao Li Princess.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"The Empress Dowager sent you to console the Gao Li Princess?\"","Yanshu quickly confirmed, \"After all, with her husband in such a state, it's understandable that the Princess would be anxious and upset, perhaps not thinking clearly. Please rest assured, Your Majesty, I will do my best to reason with her and persuade her emotionally, to help her come to her senses and cooperate with the court's investigation.\"","In her heart, she thought anxiously, [Hurry up and agree! I have leverage over that Princess, I can definitely make her behave!]","Upon hearing this, the General and others quickly said, \"Your Majesty, this is a good idea. Perhaps with Consort Yi's persuasion, the Gao Li Princess will come to her senses sooner, allowing us to catch the culprit quickly.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty.\"","Seeing this situation, Yuwen Lan had no choice but to say to Yanshu, \"Then I shall go with you. You're with child, so you must be careful.\"","Yanshu quickly agreed.","Yuwen Lan ordered the preparation of carriages, and soon they were sitting in a carriage together, leaving the palace gates and heading straight for the Envoys' Residence.","The Envoys' Residence was also an important government location, not far from the imperial palace, and they arrived shortly.","Yanshu descended from the carriage with Yuwen Lan and looked up to see the residence heavily guarded inside and out, so tight that not even a fly could get through.","As they entered the residence, following the announcement of their arrival, everyone inside came out of their rooms to greet them with proper courtesies.","Yuwen Lan first greeted Nanzhao King Mu Zhengping, \"Did King Mu rest well last night?\"","Mu Zhengping nodded, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty. All is well with me.\"","Just as he finished speaking, someone nearby complained dissatisfied, \"Now we've truly seen it - the Gao Li Prince was severely injured for no reason, and instead of catching the assassin, you want to search our rooms? Is this how the Emperor treats his guests?\"","Yanshu looked over and saw the speaker was a tall, thin man whom she vaguely remembered as being the envoy from Dangxia.","Following this person's remarks, the envoys from Tibet, Rouran, and other countries also began to chime in.","\"Indeed, it was clearly due to your Great Liang's guards' negligence, so why investigate us? Are you suggesting we were the ones who injured the Gao Li Prince?\"","\"Exactly! We demand an explanation from Your Majesty!\"","Even the Eastern Japanese envoy joined in the clamor, and quite loudly at that.","Yanshu watched all this, inwardly sneering.","Hmph, not bad acting - just wait until we expose your true colors for everyone to see.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Of course, he didn't need to speak at this moment, as the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial immediately stepped forward and said, \"Please remain calm, honored envoys. His Majesty is deeply concerned about last night's events, and his personal visit today is to express his concern for all of you.\"","After these words, Yuwen Lan ignored everyone else and looked toward Doctor Jiang, who had come to pay his respects, asking, \"How is the Gao Li Prince now?\"","Doctor Jiang replied, \"Your Majesty, the Gao Li Prince has regained consciousness, and his condition has stabilized for now, though he will need some days of rest to recover.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"I shall see him.\"","Everyone agreed, and the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial personally led the way, guiding them to the courtyard where the Gao Li Prince was staying.","They arrived after a few steps.","Yanshu saw the Gao Li Princess keeping watch by the bedside, while Li Taichu lay on the bed, indeed with his eyes open but looking very pale, muttering something in the Gao Li language, appearing quite frightened.","Yuwen Lan looked to the translator beside him, who quickly reported, \"Your Majesty, the Gao Li Prince is saying words like 'monster' and 'demon.'\"","Monsters and demons?","Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow - it seems he was truly frightened by that Japanese \"human demon\"?","He unconsciously glanced at Yanshu again, only to hear her thinking, [Oh my, this pervert might end up impotent after this, tsk!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He really didn't want to hear that word.","He thus instructed the translator, \"Tell the Gao Li Princess that I am very concerned about what happened. The doctor just said the Prince is out of danger and only needs some days of rest to recover. The urgent matter now is to request the Princess's full cooperation so we can catch the culprit as soon as possible.\"","The translator agreed and repeated everything in the Gao Li language to the Princess.","However, after hearing this, the Princess responded emotionally, \"It was Great Liang's fault that my husband was injured! Why are you investigating us? Great Liang has been such a disappointment!\"","It seemed she was still unwilling to cooperate.","Yuwen Lan's brow furrowed, and he was about to speak again. But then Yanshu stepped forward and said to the Princess, \"Enough, your husband is now frightened out of his wits, so no matter how much you act, he can't see it. Our Great Liang and Gao Li have always been friendly nations. If this incident damages our relationship and allows others to take advantage, it won't benefit you either. I know you've wanted to get revenge on your husband because of his philandering ways, which is why you sent those two maids to our Emperor. If you continue to obstruct our investigation like this, we'll have reason to suspect that you're the one who harmed your husband!\""]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92","paragraphs":["When these words were spoken, it was evident that everyone present wore a puzzled expression.","Of course, on the Gao Li side, only the Princess and Prince Seopi could understand a few words of Chinese; the servants hardly understood at all. And Prince Seopi was currently in an irrational state. Thus, upon hearing Yan Shu's words, only the Gao Li Princess spoke up in surprise, \"You, what did you say?\"","Yan Shu replied with a mischievous smile, \"Don't understand? Would you like me to call the interpreter to translate for you?\"","Then she looked around the room and said, \"Should I let them listen as well?\"","The Gao Li Princess was taken aback again. She paused before responding in slightly stiff Chinese, \"How could it possibly be my fault that the Prince is harmed?\"","Perhaps due to excessive shock, her speech was not as fluent as it had been the previous days.","Yan Shu smiled once more, \"Whether I am right or wrong, you know in your heart. If it wasn't you who caused harm, then why don't you allow our officials from Da Liang to investigate the case? Your husband is injured so severely, aren't you angry? Don't you want to know who the murderer is?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, she saw the other party clearly hesitate but did not speak immediately.","Yan Shu then turned her gaze to the door and said, \"Your ministers can understand Chinese. Otherwise, I will speak with them later. But even if they don't understand, it doesn't matter because I have an interpreter here who can translate everything for them.\"","Upon hearing this, the Gao Li Princess frowned and said, \"I have no grudge against you, why would you accuse me like this?\"","Yan Shu smiled again, \"Rest assured, we only wish to uncover the real culprit and prevent the innocent from being wrongly accused in our Da Liang. As for matters between you and your husband, we couldn't care less.\"","After these words, the Princess hesitated for a moment before finally speaking, \"Alright, I hope you keep your word and find the true criminal.\"","This was an agreement, and Yan Shu nodded immediately, \"Rest assured, Da Liang always keeps its promises.\"","Yuwen Lan felt relieved and promptly said, \"Summon the people from the Ministry of Punishments.\"","He then instructed the interpreter, \"Stay by their side and help translate whenever necessary.\"","The interpreter agreed, and when the officials from the Ministry of Punishments arrived, they began investigating the case.","There were many people accompanying the Gao Li Prince, and questioning each one took some time. Additionally, Prince Seopi was still acting erratically in bed, which was quite frightening. So, Yan Shu went with Yuwen Lan to wait in the courtyard.","The envoys from various vassal states watched from the sidelines, all showing great curiosity.","Yan Shu observed quietly and noticed that the envoy from Dongwo was also watching, looking completely unafraid.","Well, enjoying the spectacle, huh?","She thought to herself, 'I'll make sure everyone gets a good show.'","Fortunately, they didn't have to wait long. Soon, the Minister of Punishments hurried over and reported to the Emperor, \"Your Majesty, just now, the attendant close to the Gao Li Prince confessed that last night the Prince called two women brought by the Dongwo envoy into his room for drinking. At that time, besides the Gao Li Prince himself, there were only those two women in the room. Not long after, the Prince was injured, but those two women were no longer in the room.\"","Upon hearing this, the onlookers also heard and raised their eyebrows in surprise—","The Gao Li Prince invited Dongwo women for drinks? What kind of game is this?","Yuwen Lan then said, \"If that's the case, we should question the Dongwo envoy and those two women.\"","However, before the Minister of Punishments could respond, the Dongwo envoy suddenly panicked and shouted, \"What does this have to do with us? This is clearly a problem with your Da Liang's security! Please, Your Majesty, do not make unfounded accusations!\"","Before he finished speaking, another person chimed in, \"Yes, how is this related to Dongwo? Isn't this because Da Liang cannot find the assassin and is planning to frame someone among us?\"","Yan Shu looked and saw that it was the same Partya envoy who had been sarcastic earlier.","Due to the presence of the Emperor today, the officials of Da Liang felt much more confident. Hearing this, the Minister of Punishments immediately said, \"Please, both envoys, remain calm. When Da Liang investigates cases, we never make unfounded accusations; everything is based on evidence. The Prince's attendant just confessed that the Prince met those two women last night. We merely wish to question them. If they are not involved, we certainly won't blame them. Since you are within the territory of Da Liang, please respect the orders of our Emperor.\"","His tone was firm, and the two envoys finally remained silent.","Yuwen Lan, however, had lost his patience and directly instructed the Central Commander, \"Bring out those two women and thoroughly search their rooms and courtyards.\"","The Central Commander agreed and led the guards into the Dongwo envoy's courtyard, quickly bringing out the two women.","The Minister of Punishments then approached to question them.","No matter what was asked, even when translated into Dongwo language by the interpreter, the two women only shook their heads in response.","Everyone watching wondered if Dongwo had sent two mute women to the capital city.","Only Yan Shu knew that the two were pretending to be stupid. Losing her patience, she directly addressed Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, since the Gao Li Prince has woken up, bring them to him and let the Prince and his attendants identify them.\"","Yuwen Lan also didn't want to waste any more time and nodded, \"Alright, bring these two to the Prince.\"","The Central Commander agreed and led the two forward.","The Dongwo envoy followed nervously.","The others who were watching also stealthily followed.","Yan Shu originally wanted to follow as well, but unfortunately, Yuwen Lan didn't move...","Sigh, she had no choice but to stay with him.","Unexpectedly, shortly after, several terrifying shouts came from the Gao Li Prince's courtyard.","Startled, Yan Shu quickly said, \"Your Majesty, let's go see.\"","Yuwen Lan could only hum in agreement and got up, leading her over.","When they arrived, they saw the Gao Li Prince with a grayish-blue face, trying hard to hide under the bed, while desperately saying something.","The interpreter hurriedly translated for everyone, \"Prince calls them monsters and tells them to leave quickly.\"","Hearing this, the Gao Li Princess also said urgently, \"The Prince is very afraid of them. Please ask them to leave and stop scaring the Prince!\"","Seeing this scene, everyone silently thought that according to this situation, it seemed that the Gao Li Prince indeed met these two women last night, and it was highly possible that they were the culprits.","But why did he call them monsters?","For a moment, everyone couldn't help but scrutinize the two women.","Suddenly, the Emperor spoke, \"Since they refuse to confess, take them away for interrogation.\"","The guards agreed and moved forward.","However, the Dongwo envoy protested, \"Is His Majesty planning to extract a confession through torture? Even if the Gao Li Prince met them last night, they are just weak women. How could they harm such a strong man like the Prince?\"","Yan Shu couldn't resist saying, \"Maybe the women from your country are different from ordinary women?\"","The Dongwo envoy was taken aback and looked at her suspiciously, \"What do you mean, Your Highness?\"","Yan Shu ignored him and directly ordered the guards, \"Don't waste time, act quickly.\"","The guards agreed and moved forward with ropes to tie up the two women.","The Dongwo envoy, unable to do anything, jumped up and said, \"How can you treat our women like this? They are beauties carefully selected by our ruler. Even if the Emperor doesn't want them, they are still human beings!\"","Yan Shu couldn't hold back and said, \"That's a good point. Since you know they are human, why turn them into playthings for your ruler?\"","Unexpectedly, the two women, who had pretended to be weak moments ago, suddenly resisted. Taking advantage of the guards' lack of vigilance, they managed to knock down three or four of them in an instant.","Everyone was startled and hurriedly stepped back. Yuwen Lan instinctively shielded Yan Shu behind him and ordered the guards, \"Subdue them at all costs!\"","The guards agreed and charged forward again.","With numbers on their side, it didn't take long to subdue the two women and bind them with thick ropes.","Still shaken, everyone exclaimed, \"Dongwo actually presented women skilled in martial arts. What is their true intention!\"","Yan Shu thought to herself, 'This is just the beginning. If they knew these two were actually...'","Cough, cough, she hoped everyone had strong enough nerves and wouldn't end up like the cowardly Prince Seopi, driven mad with fear.","While thinking this, she noticed a guard checking the ropes around the two women's waists and said, \"Their waists are bulging. Could they be hiding weapons?\"","Hearing this, everyone looked over.","The Central Commander immediately ordered, \"Search them!\"","Thinking about the danger just now, if these assassins had harmed the Emperor and Empress, he wouldn't be able to save his own head.","So, for him, there was only one task: eliminate all threats!","Regardless of gender norms, assassins were to be executed, not distinguished by gender.","The guards immediately started searching.","However, they soon froze.","This... this...","This seems to be...","Seeing this, everyone became even more curious.","What exactly did the guards touch? Why were they all stunned?","The Central Commander, losing his patience, personally stepped forward to check.","After examining, he was also stunned and incredulously drew his sword to cut open the women's clothing.","At that moment, Yan Shu paused and instinctively reached out to cover Yuwen Lan's eyes.","Almost simultaneously, a large hand appeared in front of her eyes, covering them as well.","Everything went dark.","And immediately, a chorus of screams filled her ears—","\"Monsters, monsters...\"","She could tell that the loudest voice belonged to the Central Commander.","Sigh, she couldn't help but feel sorry for him, hoping he could get through this.","But at the same time, she struggled harder to keep the small emperor's hands covering her eyes.","After all, he was her own man, and she couldn't let him be traumatized, affecting their future happiness. Cough.","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He also earnestly covered her eyes, ensuring she wouldn't see anything.","Fortunately, the Central Commander seemed to have decent mental fortitude. After shouting, he quickly ordered the guards, \"Quickly cover them up!\"","Then he turned to report to the Emperor, \"Your Majesty, these two are... hermaphrodites!\"","The Emperor, whose eyes were covered by his beloved consort, responded, \"How dare they! Dongwo dares to insult Me in such a manner! Moreover, they deliberately harmed the Gao Li Prince and attempted to sow discord between our two countries! Immediately arrest all personnel and imprison them in the Heavenly Prison!\"","Everyone agreed and immediately took action.","Yuwen Lan then removed the small hands covering his eyes and held them, saying, \"Alright, we shouldn't stay here any longer. Let's return to the palace quickly.\"","Saying this, he pulled her away swiftly."]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93","paragraphs":["On the afternoon of that day, news of the incident at the Envoy's residence quickly spread throughout the capital, causing widespread shock among both officials and common people.","The next day in the imperial court, emotions ran high as everyone denounced the outrageous behavior of the Dongwo ruler.","Some hot-tempered military officials even petitioned the emperor on the spot, requesting to lead troops into battle. They were itching to flatten that tiny country immediately to vent their anger.","Of course, this was unrealistic. Before the emperor could even respond, ministers quickly intervened, saying: \"While Dongwo's actions are indeed despicable, war would be costly and harm our people. Moreover, Dongwo is separated from us by the Eastern Sea. Mobilizing troops would not guarantee victory.\"","\"Indeed, we should not rush into war without certainty of success. After all, it was the Crown Prince of Gaoli who was wounded by the Dongwo assassins. Once news reaches Gaoli, those two countries may well end up at odds. Why don't we observe from the sidelines for now, and wait for the right moment to reap the benefits?\"","This suggestion was met with widespread agreement, though some still angrily protested: \"Are we simply going to tolerate this insult?\"","At this point, the emperor finally spoke from his throne: \"The more detestable they are, the more composed you all must remain. For now, our priority should be to strengthen our coastal navy and shore up maritime defenses. Even if we don't go to war immediately, we must always be prepared. If Dongwo dares to offend us again, we will retaliate decisively and show no mercy.\"","As his words fell, the officials responded in unison, indicating their agreement.","The emperor continued: \"The Court of State Ceremonial shall immediately send letters to both Gaoli and Dongwo explaining the situation, and issue a stern rebuke to Dongwo. If possible, we should also find a way to let their citizens know how absurd their ruler's actions have been.\"","The Court of State Ceremonial officials promptly stepped forward to acknowledge the order.","However... while sending letters to both countries was straightforward, the emperor's final instruction...","How exactly were they supposed to inform the Dongwo populace?","Just then, Zou Mozhong, Scholar of the Hanlin Academy, spoke up: \"Your subject has an idea. I've heard that Master Xiao Yao's latest story bears a striking resemblance to this Dongwo incident. Perhaps the officials of the Court of State Ceremonial could have this story translated into the Dongwo language, and arrange for Dongwo merchants to see it and bring it back to circulate in their country?\"","Oh? This was indeed an excellent suggestion!","Another official chimed in: \"Scholar Zou's proposal is brilliant! It would be even better if Dongwo has storytellers or theater troupes who could adapt this tale and perform it in rural areas. That would help it spread even further.\"","-- If the Dongwo commoners learned that their ruler was harming innocent people to satisfy his own outrageous desires, that dynasty likely wouldn't last much longer.","Everyone seemed to share this thought, and a chorus of approval filled the hall.","Seeing this reaction, the emperor nodded and said: \"This idea is indeed excellent. Let the Court of State Ceremonial handle it. If there are any uncertainties, they may consult with Scholar Zou.\"","As he finished speaking, the Court of State Ceremonial officials once again indicated their acknowledgment. The other officials also chimed in, praising the emperor's wisdom.","Of course, among them all, Minister of Works Lu Kaihe was particularly excited --","How wonderful that his favorite author Master Xiao Yao's work would finally spread to a foreign land!","Naturally, along with his excitement came impatience. In his rush to court this morning, he hadn't even realized a new book by Master Xiao Yao had been released today.","He must hurry to buy it as soon as court was dismissed!","Meanwhile, in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu was discussing her new story with her number one fan, the Empress Dowager.","After hearing the story, the Empress Dowager nodded approvingly: \"You've handled it well. This incident was indeed too outrageous, and might have frightened the common people if told directly. It's better to present it as a supernatural tale like this. However, it does seem we're covering up for that Dongwo ruler in the end. To think we have to shield him after all he's done.\"","Yanshu quickly replied: \"It's alright. Given how he treats people so inhumanely, his reign likely won't last long anyway. Besides, now that the truth has come out, Dongwo and Gaoli have become enemies. We can just sit back and watch the drama unfold.\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound of agreement. \"That Gaoli prince got what he deserved too. Being a guest in someone else's territory yet behaving so improperly. Now he's been frightened to this extent - who knows if he'll ever recover.\"","Yanshu said: \"Yesterday, I heard from Doctor Jiang that as long as he avoids anything that might trigger him going forward, he should recover eventually. It's just that it might take quite some time.\"","She then lowered her voice and continued: \"You know, I heard he can't even bear the sight of unfamiliar women now. He screams 'monster!' whenever he sees one, so only his own wife can attend to him closely.\"","The Empress Dowager let out an \"Oh\" and couldn't help but laugh: \"Well, that certainly works out well for the princess consort. She no longer has to worry about her husband's wandering eyes or come up with roundabout ways to keep him in check.\"","Yanshu also laughed: \"Exactly! That's why she's being so cooperative with us now. Yesterday she had the envoys quickly write back to Gaoli, describing how despicable and outrageous Dongwo is, saying that after failing to assassinate our emperor, they took the opportunity to attack her husband instead... Of course, she didn't mention that her husband had first acted inappropriately with those two... individuals.\"","The Empress Dowager gave a scornful laugh: \"How could she possibly say that? Though she resents him, she still wants to protect her husband's position and her own wealth and status. Someone like that can't truly be at peace.\"","-- Either don't care at all, or care completely. What's the point of living in constant anxiety, torn between desires?","Realizing she might have gotten carried away with her musings, the Empress Dowager addressed Yanshu again: \"It's admirable that you're concerning yourself with such matters while pregnant. Now that you've finished the story, you should go back and rest properly.\"","Yanshu acknowledged this and took her leave.","As she walked out, she couldn't help but wonder if the Empress Dowager's earlier words stemmed from her own experiences.","-- Perhaps it was only after completely giving up on the late emperor that the Empress Dowager was able to live so freely.","As she pushed open the door, she saw Rendong waiting for her outside. Zhu Shu, Nanny Zhuang, and other palace maids attending to the Empress Dowager were also waiting in the corridor. Seeing her emerge, they all bowed respectfully.","Yanshu nodded slightly, and with Rendong's support, boarded the palanquin waiting nearby.","To the side, Zhu Shu and Nanny Zhuang's gazes swept over the book in Yanshu's hand before they exchanged a silent glance and entered the hall.","Having resolved the case at the Envoy's residence and released a new story, Yanshu had certainly earned some rest.","In the coming days, she planned to relax while also keeping an eye on readers' reactions.","-- After all, this time she had written a supernatural tale, and it was a long serial story. She wasn't entirely sure if readers would enjoy it.","However, just two days later, Fu Hai brought her a sack full of letters from readers outside the palace.","Come to think of it, she had been publishing less frequently since becoming pregnant, so reader correspondence had also decreased. Receiving so many letters right after releasing a new story showed that readers hadn't forgotten her. Yanshu was very excited and immediately began opening and reading them.","Most of the letters either inquired why she hadn't published anything in so long and asked if she was doing well, which warmed her heart;","Or, as before, they shared their thoughts after reading the new story. Overall, the reception seemed quite positive.","However, there were a few letters that caught her by surprise --","They questioned in very strong terms whether she was actually a woman, and admonished her that she should stay quietly in the women's quarters instead of writing to seek attention.","Yanshu was baffled. \"???\"","What was going on?","First of all, why did they think she was a woman?","Had she slipped up somewhere?","And why did they think she shouldn't be writing stories???","The system explained: [Let's address these issues one by one. First, why they think you're a woman -- You've been publishing less frequently lately, right? Seeing readers eagerly waiting, some people tried to impersonate you and write stories. But their writing style and plots weren't quite right, so the results weren't great. With no other options, these people started analyzing your stories carefully. They noticed that most of your villains are men, while most women are innocent victims. So they speculated that you might hate men, and concluded you could be a woman.]","[Plus, in this latest story, the demon-slaying protagonist is also a woman, which further convinced them you must be female.]","Hearing this, Yanshu zeroed in on the key point: [...What kind of reasoning is that? There are both good and bad people of both genders in the world. I don't only write about male villains. How can they conclude I hate men based on that?]","System: [This is actually a means of competition. After all, once this conclusion is spread, won't it cause more people to be suspicious?]","Yanshu: [......]","Well, they must have achieved their goal, otherwise she wouldn't have received such a strongly worded letter.","So she still asked incredulously, [Why are they so angry that I'm a woman? Didn't they like my stories before? What does this have to do with gender?]","System: [That's the logic, but some people just can't accept it. Especially now that you've come out with this female knight story, they think you're biased against men. They're convinced you have a prejudice against males because you made a demon-slaying hero a woman.]","Yanshu: [......]","This was truly speechless. There have been countless male hero figures throughout history, she just wanted to write something different. How could this lead to such an interpretation?","Besides, Sun Wukong also vanquished demons and monsters, didn't he? He wasn't even human. Would these people think that story was biased against humanity?","System: [Well said! But people born with prejudices won't think about these things.]","Yanshu: [...Well, let them think what they want. If these people can't accept it, so be it. I am a woman after all, and I can't possibly change that for them, can I?]","With that, she decided not to care anymore and just patted her belly, saying, \"Come on, Mother will take you to pick some lotus seed pods!\"","Then she got up and went out.","As the peak of summer had passed and the weather was turning cooler, the lotus flowers in the Taiye Pool were about to wither. It was the season for harvesting lotus seed pods, and these days, the palace maids were busy collecting them in the Taiye Pool. It was quite a lively scene.","Rather than thinking about these vexing matters, it was better to go out and clear her mind.","Every day after noon was the time for the Empress Dowager's nap.","The Empress Dowager didn't like having people around when she slept, so Nanny Zhuang had some free time again and returned to the duty room.","Upon entering, she saw Zhu Shu holding a book, and it was none other than the Carefree Master's story that the Empress Dowager loved so much.","She snorted and said, \"Now that Her Majesty has Lady Yi, she doesn't need you to read anymore. Why are you still looking at this?\"","Zhu Shu felt a pang in her heart, but said, \"I heard that people outside are saying the author of these stories is actually a woman, so I just wanted to take another look.\"","Hearing this, Nanny Zhuang remembered something else and said to Zhu Shu, \"Speaking of which, why did Lady Yi used to read stories to Her Majesty without avoiding people, but now she always avoids others every time? Could something have happened during those three days when I was at the temple?\"","Zhu Shu thought for a moment before putting down the book and saying, \"At that time, I was sent by the Empress Dowager to deliver a reward to Lady Yi. I noticed that the pen she was using was very similar to the one the Empress Dowager had given to the Carefree Master, so I mentioned it in front of the Empress Dowager. But as soon as I finished speaking, she came in, saying she had an urgent matter to report to the Empress Dowager privately. Since then, every time she comes, the Empress Dowager sends us all out.\"","Upon hearing this, Nanny Zhuang immediately frowned.","\"She came just as you finished speaking? Could it be that she had a guilty conscience? Was she afraid you would expose her, so she took the initiative to confess to Her Majesty?\"","Zhu Shu replied, \"I've thought about that too, but if she really had taken the reward the Empress Dowager meant for the Carefree Master, why isn't Her Majesty angry at all? In fact, she seems to be treating her even better now. Have you ever seen Her Majesty treat anyone else this well, Nanny?\"","Especially the other day, when the Empress Dowager actually spoke up in front of so many people, saying not to send more people into the palace harem...","Just thinking about this made Zhu Shu particularly uncomfortable.","Since ancient times, wasn't it most common for emperors to have three palaces and six courts? It was one thing for her to want to monopolize His Majesty, but how could she make the Empress Dowager speak up for her like this!","Then she heard Nanny Zhuang say, \"You're right. I've been by Her Majesty's side for so many years, and I know that what Her Majesty values most is character. If Lady Yi had done something like that, Her Majesty definitely wouldn't pay her any attention. So looking at it this way, at least regarding the pen issue, Lady Yi should be clear of suspicion.\"","Zhu Shu nodded upon hearing this.","After all, she had later found out that there were two sets of those lake pens in total, both tributes from the Governor of Jiangnan. One set was presented to His Majesty, and one set to the Empress Dowager. It was very likely that the one Lady Yi had was given to her by His Majesty.","However, the fact that His Majesty would so casually give such a precious item to Lady Yi for practicing calligraphy made Zhu Shu even more uncomfortable.","Just then, she heard Nanny Zhuang say, \"Is it possible that the pen was meant for her?\"","Zhu Shu was stunned, still not quite understanding.","Then she heard Nanny Zhuang continue, \"The Empress Dowager has seen plenty of flowery words and clever speech over the years. Even someone as smart as Lady An couldn't win the Empress Dowager's favor once her ambition was exposed. So for the Empress Dowager to like Lady Yi so much now, she must have some extraordinary quality.\"","Zhu Shu retorted, \"Isn't it because she's carrying the imperial heir?\"","Nanny Zhuang dismissed this, saying, \"Even if our Noble Consort had been carrying the imperial heir back then, do you think the Empress Dowager would have treated her the way she treats Lady Yi now?\"","Zhu Shu paused.","She had to admit, it was true.","Given Zhou Consort's personality back then, even if she had truly been pregnant with the imperial heir, the Empress Dowager probably wouldn't have been so kind to her...","But what extraordinary quality did this Lady Yi have that could capture the Empress Dowager's heart?","Then she heard Nanny Zhuang say, \"Since she always avoids others when she comes to read stories to Her Majesty... could it be that besides reading these stories, she and Her Majesty have some conversations that others shouldn't hear?\"","This was exactly what Zhu Shu wanted to know. Upon hearing this, she frowned and said, \"I can't figure it out either. In the past, besides having her read stories, Her Majesty would only ask about the Carefree Master's affairs...\"","At this point, she suddenly paused.","She heard Nanny Zhuang say, \"That's right. In the past, Her Majesty would often mention wanting to meet the Carefree Master, but now she doesn't talk about it anymore.\"","Zhu Shu furrowed her brows, with an incredulous look on her face, \"Could it be... that she is the Carefree Master?\"","......","After admiring the harvest scene by the Taiye Pool and picking a bag of fresh lotus seed pods, Yanshu was about to head back.","However, every couple of steps, she heard the System chime in, [Pay attention now. Just now, Zhu Shu and Nanny Zhuang were gossiping in the duty room and deduced that you are very likely to be the Carefree Master. They're planning to spread the news now.]","Yanshu: [???]","This really wasn't necessary.","Was it that fun to rush to expose her privacy?","It was one thing if she wanted to announce it herself, but it was quite another to have others sneakily leak it.","So she immediately changed her plans and gave instructions to Rendong and Lianxin who were following her.","The two immediately complied and set off separately.","Not long after, the Empress Dowager saw Yanshu approach with a bag of lotus seed pods.","\"Your Majesty, these are lotus seed pods from the Taiye Pool. I just went to pick them myself and saw that they looked good, so I brought them specially for you to taste.\"","The Empress Dowager looked at the full basket of lotus seed pods and smiled, \"Why did you bring so many?\"","In fact, this was because Yanshu had been greedy. Earlier by the lake, seeing that each lotus pod was bigger and fresher than the last, she couldn't resist and took this many.","But now she sighed and said, \"I've been feeling uneasy and heated these past couple of days. The imperial physician said lotus seeds can calm the mind and clear heat, so I planned to take more to eat slowly.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager frowned and said, \"Child, how did you suddenly become heated?\"","She saw Yanshu with an expression as if she wanted to speak but held back.","The Empress Dowager then waved her hand at the palace maids in the hall, saying, \"You may all leave first.\"","Nanny Zhuang, who was nearby, paused slightly but had to comply and retreated with the others.","In her heart, she couldn't help but wonder what Lady Yi was going to say to the Empress Dowager this time, since she hadn't brought a storybook.","In the blink of an eye, there were no outsiders left in the hall.","The Empress Dowager then said gently, \"Tell me, has something happened again? Don't hide anything from me.\"","Yanshu felt warmth in her heart and said, \"Something did happen these past few days that has been troubling me. As you know, I wrote about a female knight in my new story. I originally just wanted to create a character different from the male heroes in the market, but I didn't expect this to upset some people outside. Not only have some people guessed that I'm a woman, but in the past few days, some have even written letters cursing at me, saying that if I'm a woman, I should stay properly in the boudoir and not come out to seek attention.\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager immediately furrowed her brow and said, \"What's wrong with these people? Haven't they always been eager for women to write stories before? They actually wrote letters to scold you? It's too much!\"","Yanshu nodded and said, \"I don't quite understand their thoughts either, but this world has always looked down on women, and I've thought about such a situation before. If they don't like it, so be it. This isn't the most important thing. What I'm worried about now is whether someone will guess my identity in a few days and make an issue of it.\"","The Empress Dowager didn't seem concerned and said, \"What's there to be afraid of? After all, His Majesty asked you to write these novels, and you're just following orders. There's no palace rule saying women in the harem can't write novels. If those old fogies dare to make a big fuss about this, His Majesty and I will stand up for you.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu was incredibly touched. She immediately stood up and bowed, saying, \"I am grateful for Your Majesty's protection.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"Get up. I thought something serious had happened. Is it worth being so anxious about this?\"","Yanshu couldn't help but smile sheepishly.","Just then, a voice came from outside, \"Reporting to the Empress Dowager, Eunuch Fu Hai requests an audience.\"","Hmm, why has Fu Hai suddenly come?","The Empress Dowager was also a bit surprised and said, \"Let him in.\"","The person outside acknowledged and opened the palace doors. Sure enough, Fu Hai entered carrying a basket. After paying his respects, he said, \"Reporting to the Empress Dowager, fresh grapes have just arrived from Qingyuan County in Taiyuan Prefecture. His Majesty saw they were fresh and specially asked this servant to bring you a basket.\"","As he spoke, he lifted the cover of the basket, revealing bunches of fresh grapes inside, each grape plump and purple-red, looking delicious at first glance.","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Qingyuan grapes are indeed good. I'm grateful for His Majesty's thoughtfulness. You may set it down.\"","Fu Hai acknowledged and handed the basket to the palace maid who came forward to receive it.","Then he looked around the hall and said, \"By the way, I wonder if Miss Zhu Shu is around these days?\"","The Empress Dowager made a sound of surprise and asked curiously, \"What do you want with Zhu Shu?\"","Fu Hai replied, \"Just now, the guards at the palace gate said they caught a young eunuch with some silver and a letter on him, which seemed suspicious. When questioned, the young eunuch claimed that Miss Zhu Shu had asked him to deliver a letter to her relatives outside the palace.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager paused for a moment, then immediately called for Zhu Shu to be brought before her. She asked, \"Isn't your family in Lu Prefecture? When did you get relatives in the capital?\"","At this point, Zhu Shu, having heard the news, was very nervous and was quickly trying to think of an excuse to answer.","But Fu Hai continued after the Empress Dowager's question, saying, \"Yes, this servant also knows that Miss Zhu Shu is not from the capital. I'm afraid that young eunuch might have stolen Miss Zhu Shu's silver, so I came specifically to ask about it.\"","As he finished speaking, suspicion was already evident in the Empress Dowager's eyes.","Zhu Shu became even more nervous and hurriedly said, \"...He didn't steal it. I asked him to keep some silver for me outside the palace. I heard that the interest rates for saving money outside are high, so I thought to prepare for the future. I also asked him to help forward a letter to Lu Prefecture for me.\"","Unexpectedly, Fu Hai made a sound of surprise and said, \"That's strange. Doesn't the palace have its own postal service? The day after tomorrow is the day for collecting letters. Did you have some urgent matter, Miss? Moreover, the place that young man mentioned, the guards checked, and it's a book printing shop. It's not a bank at all. Miss, could it be that you've been deceived?\"","What? A book printing shop?","The Empress Dowager, having heard all this, suddenly said in a cold voice, \"Tell me honestly, what exactly are you trying to do!\""]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94","paragraphs":["Zhu Shu had never expected that the little Xiangzi she found, who was often running errands in and out of the palace gates as a young eunuch and was quite familiar with the guards at the gate, would be so easily caught by them today.","Could it be that this little Xiangzi had a sudden change of heart and sold her out?","But she had given him twenty taels of silver for his errand, which was no small amount. Moreover, how could he know what she intended to do? There was really no reason for him to betray her.","Regardless, she did not want to admit it just like that when faced with the Empress Dowager's questioning...","Unexpectedly, while she was quickly thinking of an excuse, Yan Shu suddenly said, \"Could it be that Miss Zhu Shu has someone in mind? Could your person in mind be from the bookshop?\"","What?","When these words were spoken, everyone was taken aback.","One must understand, private dealings between palace maids and men outside the palace were also considered a grave offense!","Zhu Shu was startled, hurriedly saying, \"No, no, no, the bookshop owner is a fellow townsman of this servant. I merely asked him to send a message home on my behalf through someone returning to our hometown. The silver was also meant to ask him to keep it safe for me.\"","Yan Shu raised an eyebrow upon hearing this, \"It seems this bookshop owner is quite trustworthy. Miss Zhu Shu gave him the silver without fearing he might take it for himself.\"","However, the Empress Dowager no longer believed her, coldly saying, \"Didn't you say earlier that the young eunuch was helping you? Now it's the bookshop owner? How did you come to know this fellow townsman while being inside the palace all day?\"","As she spoke, she instructed Fu Hai, \"Bring that letter to me.\"","Fu Hai responded affirmatively, hurriedly taking out a letter from his sleeve and presenting it to the Empress Dowager.","The Empress Dowager took it and saw that there were no words on the envelope. She opened it to find several characters written on the paper inside, which read, \"The Rogue Scholar is likely one of the palace women.\"","Yan Shu felt reassured but feigned surprise as she looked at the Empress Dowager, \"Your Majesty, why would Miss Zhu Shu write such a letter to send home?\"","The Empress Dowager's face darkened completely as she looked at Zhu Shu, asking, \"Who exactly was this intended for?\"","Zhu Shu's face had turned deathly pale, yet she clenched her lips tightly and remained silent.","It was Fu Hai who stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, according to the young eunuch, this was to be sent to a bookshop called Ba Mian Bookshop at the southern end of Gongyuan Street. This shop has been operating in the capital for fifty or sixty years, making it one of the top bookshops. Besides selling stationery, they also employ people to write stories and print books for sale. However, it doesn't seem to be the same place that publishes the Rogue Scholar’s stories.\"","Upon hearing this, Yan Shu inwardly marveled—Supervisor Fu is truly impressive! To gather such detailed information in such a short time!","She thought about how she had been preoccupied with coming up with plans and hadn't even had the chance to ask the system for details.","Then she heard the system say, [Supervisor Fu has been in the capital for decades. He usually follows the emperor, always ready to answer any questions. He must be alert and observant, naturally knowing whatever the master wants to know.]","Yan Shu, [I see that Supervisor Fu is capable, but can you tell me more about this Ba Mian Bookshop?]","System, [Isn't it obvious? As one of the oldest bookshops in the capital, the Ba Mian Bookshop can only watch helplessly as other shops make money selling your stories. They must feel very unbalanced. Those imitators writing stories like yours are probably hired by them. They are likely behind this incident too.]","Yan Shu chuckled inwardly, [Good thing Scholar Zou didn't have them publish my stories. These people with twisted intentions deserve to lose money!]","Yet, she still couldn’t understand, [But how could a palace maid like Zhu Shu obtain such detailed information? And know to leak it to the Ba Mian Bookshop?]","System, [The owner of the Ba Mian Bookshop, Zhao Jingshi, has been spreading the word these past few days, offering substantial rewards for any information about you. With news flying around everywhere, it wouldn't take much effort to find out.]","Yan Shu immediately became interested, [Substantial rewards??? Tell me, how substantial?]","Cough, she needed to know what she was worth now!","The system replied, [Twenty taels of silver for your real name; thirty taels for your home address; fifty taels for your true identity.]","Yan Shu exclaimed, “!!!”","Good heavens, Zhu Shu was going to earn a hundred taels in one go!","If she had known it was so profitable, she would have done it herself!","System, [You’re now a concubine, don’t you have enough silver?]","Yan Shu, [Better to be prepared for any eventuality! It’s also commendable that the Ba Mian Bookshop is willing to invest so much, isn’t it?]","They wanted her name, address, and identity?","Ha, are they planning to hire an assassin to harm her next?","What a Ba Mian Bookshop.","For some silver, is it really worth it?","Of course, that was all future talk.","At the moment, the Empress Dowager coldly asked Zhu Shu, \"What was the purpose of this? Writing such things and sending them outside the palace, what were your intentions?\"","Zhu Shu hastily said, \"Your Majesty, it's just that I heard the bookshop was paying for information recently, so I tried it out. It was all made up by me...\"","Before she could finish, the Empress Dowager closed her eyes and said, \"Since you won't tell the truth, send her to the Inner Court Supervision Office.\"","She then called out Fu Hai's name.","Zhu Shu was shocked and finally burst into tears, \"Please, Your Majesty, spare me... \"","The Empress Dowager sneered, \"How many lives did you intend to harm? Is your life enough to make up for it?\"","Zhu Shu just kept kowtowing and crying, \"This servant knows it was wrong, this servant knows it was wrong...\"","The Empress Dowager, however, was tired of talking to her and only instructed Fu Hai, \"Such a talkative person should be silenced with a dumbing potion and exiled to the cold border regions. I treated her well, and she doesn't appreciate it. Let her reflect on her actions for the rest of her life.\"","Fu Hai responded affirmatively and had people drag Zhu Shu away.","For a moment, everyone in Cian Palace watched in fear, none daring to speak.","Everyone knew how much the Empress Dowager had favored Zhu Shu in the past.","Now...","Sigh, she brought this upon herself.","...","After dealing with this matter, Yan Shu returned to Ganlu Palace.","She knew that although Concubine Zhu Shu's actions were partly due to the involvement of Nursemaid Zhuang, ultimately it was Zhu Shu who came forward, so she could only punish Zhu Shu first.","Thinking about it, she still couldn't understand. According to the Empress Dowager's favor towards Zhu Shu in the past, as long as Zhu Shu behaved well, after a couple of years, the Empress Dowager might choose a decent husband for her and let her marry well.","Why did she abandon the smooth path and oppose her instead?","Was it because she thought if she could provoke those with ulterior motives to attack her, the emperor would notice Zhu Shu?","Just as she was thinking this, she heard an announcement from outside, \"His Majesty has arrived...\"","Eh, the emperor came?","Yan Shu snapped back to reality, thinking it was a good opportunity to discuss this with him, so she went to greet him at the door.","\"Your humble servant greets Your Majesty...\"","Before she could bow, Yuwen Lan had already strode in, anxiously asking, \"How is it? Are you alright?\"","Yan Shu immediately frowned and pouted, looking indignant, \"Not fine.\"","Yuwen Lan was puzzled, \"I heard from Fu Hai that the Empress Dowager had Zhu Shu given a dumbing potion and exiled to the border. Aren't you satisfied?\"","Yan Shu quickly said, \"The Empress Dowager's punishment was most appropriate. Your humble servant never thought otherwise.\"","Hmph, don't think you can drive a wedge between her and the big supporter!","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He wasn’t trying to drive a wedge...","He asked, \"Then what else is troubling you?\"","She raised an eyebrow at him, \"Has Your Majesty not thought about the root cause of this matter?\"","Yuwen Lan replied, \"Isn't it that woman harboring ill intentions, attempting to harm the master?\"","Yan Shu raised another eyebrow, \"Why would Zhu Shu, who was perfectly fine, want to harm me? Isn't it because she likes Your Majesty? She thinks that without me, Your Majesty would like her. So, the root cause of this matter is still Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","For a moment, he couldn't tell if she was trying to extort some benefits from him or if she genuinely thought so.","Then he heard her think, [Hmph, from being a target for you since the beginning to now being pregnant, hasn't it been hard for me? From Zhang Talent, Wang Lady, An Consort, Ning Consort, Zhou Consort to now Zhu Shu, who hasn't harmed me out of jealousy? I wonder why so many people are attracted to me!]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Alright, so that's what she thinks?","But those people weren't drawn by him; they were chosen by the Ministry of Rites upon consulting the Empress Dowager.","And Zhu Shu... she was also someone close to the Empress Dowager!","But if he said that, he might be accused of driving a wedge between her and the Empress Dowager again?","He had no choice but to agree with her, \"Alright, Zhu Shu likes me, and even though I didn't know, it's still my fault.\"","Sure enough, when he said this, she pursed her lips, saying, \"That's not what I meant...\"","Actually, Yan Shu herself was a bit unclear. Perhaps because of her pregnancy, her emotions had become more volatile lately.","She hadn't realized anything was amiss until she saw him, then she couldn't help but blame him.","Just then, the system chimed in, ding, [Generally speaking, such emotions are referred to as... coquetry. Scientific studies show that during pregnancy, hormonal changes can make women more prone to coquettish behavior towards their husbands.]","Yan Shu, \"...\"","[Emm, so was I just coquetting with the emperor?]","Tsk, pregnancy is indeed different from usual; it must be the little one in her belly causing trouble!","Beside her, Yuwen Lan, who had been listening quietly, suddenly understood.","So she was coquetting with him?","How rare, the girl who used to care only about money and food was finally learning to coquette and seek his favor.","Thinking this, he felt not anger but tenderness, gently pulling her into his arms, \"Indeed, this is my fault. If I had noticed her intentions earlier and cut off the source of trouble, you wouldn't have had to worry today.\"","Strangely, perhaps due to the hormonal changes during pregnancy, Yan Shu found herself increasingly enjoying being held by him. She obediently leaned against his chest, saying, \"How could Your Majesty have noticed Zhu Shu's intentions earlier? You don't have mind-reading abilities.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","For a moment, he felt stiff, wondering if she was speaking casually or testing him.","Fortunately, after listening carefully, it seemed she was just speaking casually, so he hurriedly agreed, \"True, I don't have mind-reading abilities.\"","He secretly breathed a sigh of relief; thank goodness she was naive, otherwise he would have been exposed!","Just then, Yan Shu said, \"By the way, I almost forgot to tell Your Majesty. At the southern end of Gongyuan Street, there's a Ba Mian Bookshop. The owner is jealous of the profits from my stories and has been offering rewards for information about me. I suspect he intends to do something harmful to me.\"","Yuwen Lan immediately frowned, \"Is that so?\""]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95","paragraphs":["A bookshop that doesn't focus on proper business and only thinks of underhanded schemes naturally needs to be managed properly.","Just before Yuwen Lan could speak, Yan Shu received a message from the system—","【Speaking of this Zhao Jingshi, there's a bit of a story.】","Yan Shu immediately perked up at this, 【What story?】","The system continued, 【This man didn't originally have the surname Zhao; he was surnamed Wei, and he wasn't from the capital. The Eight-Sided Bookshop was originally founded by a merchant named Zhao Hairong, who was a local of the capital. Zhao Hairong loved reading and, for the sake of business, converted his old residence at the southern end of Gongyuan Street into a bookshop. At that time, there weren't many bookshops in that area, and Old Zhao was quite honest, so the business was always good. However, Old Zhao had no sons, only two daughters, and they couldn't help with the business. So, Old Zhao took in an apprentice, who was this Wei Jingshi.】","【Wei Jingshi was quite good at getting things done and initially quite capable, so Old Zhao liked him. Later, seeing that the man was alone and helpless, Old Zhao even adopted him as a foster son and helped him buy a house in the capital and start a family.】","Yan Shu couldn't help but sigh, 【To treat a foster son like this, Old Zhao was quite kind.】","The system agreed, 【Indeed, but unfortunately, this man had poor judgment and failed to see that Wei was actually a treacherous wolf in sheep's clothing. Old Zhao's wife passed away early, and his daughters later married out. Old Zhao lived alone and liked to drink. Eventually, his health deteriorated from drinking, and he suddenly passed away at just over fifty. The two daughters, grieving, returned to arrange their father's funeral, only to find that Wei Jingshi had changed his name to Zhao Jingshi and was wearing mourning clothes, claiming to be their father's adopted son, publicly stating that his foster father had adopted him as his heir before his death.】","Yan Shu gasped, 【Is he planning to inherit Old Zhao's estate? Is that true? Did Old Zhao really do that?】","The system replied, 【That's definitely false! Old Zhao wasn't stupid; he had his own daughters, why would he give his estate to an outsider? Besides, even if he really wanted to do that, he would have to inform his daughters. Could such a significant matter be kept from them?】","Yan Shu also said, 【Exactly, so did the Zhao sisters believe him?】","The system continued, 【At first, they naturally didn't believe it, but this Wei Jingshi was unscrupulous. He had secretly prepared various documents while his foster father was still alive, sneaking into Old Zhao's house while he was drunk and asleep, pressing Old Zhao's hand to make fingerprints, and bribing officials in advance. At this critical moment, he presented these false evidences, forcing the Zhao sisters to fail in their lawsuit at the yamen, and they could only watch helplessly as their family's estate was taken over by this man.】","Yan Shu couldn't help but shake her head, 【Indeed, another ungrateful wolf in sheep's clothing, comparable to Zhang Shengkang who betrayed his master and ancestors! For a bit of money, he even changed his surname, truly capable of such despicable acts!】","No, even if Wei's ancestors and Old Zhao's spirit in heaven could endure, she couldn't!","She immediately told Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, I heard that the owner of the Eight-Sided Bookshop has done other unscrupulous things. Please allow me to thoroughly investigate him and expose his ugly face to the public before he is punished!\"","Saying this, she broke free from his embrace and strode to the desk, immediately starting to write vigorously.","Yuwen Lan, \"......\"","So sudden?","Seeing her serious and focused expression, completely unlike her usual cute self, he could only suppress the disappointment in his heart and said beside her, \"Take it easy, don't rush, and don't tire yourself out...\"","Hmph, this despicable Eight-Sided Bookshop, harming his beloved consort and ruining his plans, must not be let off lightly.","The next day, readers in the capital were pleasantly surprised to find that, after just a few days, the usually lazy Xiaoyao Gongzi had released a new story.","Excited, people rushed to buy it.","After the recent \"gender\" rumors, the curiosity about her in the city had only increased, leading many to want to uncover the truth from her new story, resulting in even more explosive sales than before.","However, upon reading it, everyone was surprised to find that this story was unusually specific, with names, addresses, and a clear target.","It wasn't about anyone else but the old affairs of the Eight-Sided Bookshop at the southern end of Gongyuan Street in the capital.","The story began with the case of Zhao Jingshi, the \"adopted son\" of the Zhao family, and the two biological daughters of the Zhao family fighting over their late father Zhao Hairong's inheritance. It gradually revealed how Zhao Jingshi came from a small place outside the capital to the capital, how he transformed from a young apprentice to the foster son of the owner, and how he changed his surname from Wei to Zhao, finally inheriting the Eight-Sided Bookshop.","People then realized that the case at the beginning of the story was actually a miscarriage of justice, and that the seemingly respectable Zhao Jingshi was actually a heartless scoundrel.","Filled with anger, everyone condemned this man, and some emotionally charged readers even went to the Eight-Sided Bookshop to confront him in person.","However, upon arrival, they found that the bookshop was closed.","Heh, this Zhao, oh, should we call him Wei, must be guilty.","Indeed, Zhao Jingshi was very nervous at this moment.","As soon as he heard about Xiaoyao Gongzi's story this morning, he bought a copy and had the writers in his bookshop study it. To his shock, he found that it was about him!","Not only was his name unchanged, but the location of the bookshop was also clearly written!","Moreover, the other party even knew the exact year and month he started as an apprentice, the year he got married, and how much money he spent on his wedding!","It was as if all his past deeds had been exposed...","In shock, Zhao Jingshi quickly closed the door of the study and planned to think of a countermeasure quietly.","What was going on? Could it be that Xiaoyao Gongzi had also secretly bought information about him?","But who could possibly know so much!","...","After thinking for most of the day, Zhao Jingshi couldn't come up with any countermeasures, and the shop assistants had already started to question him, whispering about his past.","\"Did the shopkeeper really used to be surnamed Wei?\"","\"Probably, think about it, every Qingming Festival, doesn't he go to sweep the grave of the old shopkeeper on West Hill and also return to Pingling? Most people in Pingling are surnamed Wei, so he probably goes to sweep the graves of his original ancestors.\"","\"Tsk tsk tsk, if he even changed his surname, does he still go back to sweep the graves of his original ancestors? I wonder if those ancestors are angry?\"","\"Exactly, especially since he still goes to sweep the old shopkeeper's grave every year, I wonder if the old shopkeeper is angry in his grave...\"","\"That's right...\"","...","Zhao Jingshi was furious hearing this and immediately scolded the shop assistants.","However, one of the shop assistants with a fiery temper refused to take it and shouted angrily, \"You ungrateful, heartless scoundrel, how dare you scold others! Anyway, we're not selling anything! I quit! There are plenty of bookshops with higher wages outside!\"","With that, he threw down the book he was binding and walked out the door.","This infuriated Zhao Jingshi, and just as he was about to charge up and settle the score, he hadn't even stood firm when he heard a shout from the street, \"There's that heartless Zhao Jingshi!\"","Before he could react, rotten vegetables, rotten eggs, and other things were thrown at him...","In a panic, he wanted to go back inside, but someone had already blocked the door from the inside...","Across the river from Gongyuan Street was a teahouse.","At this moment, Yan Shu was leaning out of the window on the second floor of the private room, happily watching the commotion.","\"Hey, that brother has good aim, the rotten sweet potato hit that Wei scoundrel right on the head!\"","\"Oh, that auntie is not bad either, how did she throw those two eggs so accurately!\"","\"Hey! I didn't expect this young man, who looks thin, to be quite strong, able to lift half a basket of rotten melon skins?\"","She also waved to Yuwen Lan, who was drinking tea beside her, \"Husband, don't you want to come and take a look? It's quite thrilling.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"......You're happy, that's good.\"","He poured another cup of tea and also stood up to the window, glancing across the river and said, \"It's been almost two hours, it should be enough.\"","She said, \"The best part hasn't come yet.\"","Saying this, she handed him half a cup of tea.","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, and before he could speak, she glanced out the window and said excitedly, \"Here it comes, the climax!\"","Yuwen Lan looked over and saw two groups of people coming from both the north and south ends of Gongyuan Street.","The two groups seemed to be in a fierce mood. After arriving at the Eight-Sided Bookshop, they found Zhao Jingshi among the pile of rotten vegetables and eggshells and immediately started punching him.","While punching, they cursed, \"How dare you usurp our grandfather's estate, deceiving us for so many years!\"","Yuwen Lan hummed, \"Are these the children of the Zhao daughters?\"","Yan Shu nodded, \"Yes, the eldest Zhao daughter has two sons and two daughters, and the second daughter has three sons and one daughter. Today, the daughters and sons-in-law of both families are here.\"","Although these two families are not particularly wealthy, they have plenty of people. Today, let this scoundrel taste the consequences!","After all, this is what he deserves!","Hmph, how dare he buy her privacy? Incite others to write letters to scold her?","Today, let him know that Xiaoyao Gongzi is not to be trifled with!","Yuwen Lan, who had been listening quietly, \"......\"","Indeed, Xiaoyao Gongzi is not to be trifled with, and his consort is even more so.","The two of them watched from the window for about a quarter of an hour. Seeing that Zhao Jingshi's family had also brought people over, and to avoid escalating the conflict, Yuwen Lan called the guards and said, \"Go and tell the children of the Zhao daughters to file a complaint with the Jingzhao Mansion again.\"","The guards complied and immediately went to the front of the bookshop.","Sure enough, after a round of persuasion, the grandchildren and sons-in-law of the old Zhao family immediately dragged the already bruised and battered Zhao Jingshi to the Jingzhao Mansion.","The excited crowd also followed to support them.","The previously chaotic bookshop entrance finally regained its tranquility.","However, there was a mess of rotten vegetables and eggshells left behind.","Yuwen Lan frowned, \"It must be very troublesome to clean up.\"","Yan Shu said, \"Let Zhao Jingshi's wife and children come out and clean it up. They've enjoyed the benefits of the Zhao family for so many years, a bit of labor is nothing.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Good idea.\"","He then raised an eyebrow and looked at her, \"Are you feeling better now? Can we go back?\"","She blinked and smiled, \"It's rare to go out once, Your Majesty, why don't you accompany me to Qingzhou Restaurant for a meal, hehe.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"......Alright.\"","After all, it's to accompany her and make her happy.","She's happy, and he's happy too."]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96","paragraphs":["The latest story by the Carefree Gentleman, along with the real-time updates outside the Eight Sides Bookshop, brought the case of Wei Jingshi's illegal occupation of the Zhao family's inheritance to the attention of the capital's citizens.","Under the keen interest of the entire city, the Capital Official also recognized the gravity of their responsibility and immediately intensified their investigation.","Although much time had passed, fortunately, the officials who had handled the case back then were still around. After a thorough investigation, they quickly uncovered the truth—","Indeed, the matter of Zhao Hairong's adoption was entirely fabricated by Wei Jingshi alone. The official seal on the documents he held was privately stamped by the officials after receiving bribes from him.","Given these circumstances, the Capital Official had no choice but to overturn the wrongful case from over twenty years ago and retry it.","However, at this time, a clerk from the Eight Sides Bookshop voluntarily reported that Wei Jingshi had recently been engaging in malicious competition. Not only was he spreading rumors that the Carefree Gentleman was a woman to incite readers to attack him, but he was also offering large sums of money to acquire information about the Carefree Gentleman, intending to further harm him.","When this news broke, the citizens of the city suddenly realized why there had been rumors lately about the Carefree Gentleman being a woman. It turned out to be this heartless scoundrel maliciously framing him behind the scenes.","At once, the capital's citizens became increasingly disgusted with this person. Angry readers who were fans of the Carefree Gentleman even gathered outside the Capital Official's office to express their emotions, demanding that the officials severely punish such an evil person.","Under such pressure, the Capital Official naturally didn't dare to delay. They quickly reached a verdict—","Wei Jingshi was ordered to revert to his original name and immediately return all the property he had illegally occupied to the Zhao family. For the crimes of forging documents, bribing officials, and malicious framing, he was sentenced to sixty strokes of the cane, after which he would be exiled to the border.","Seeing that evil had finally met its just deserts, the citizens were finally satisfied.","The head of the Capital Official also breathed a sigh of relief and hurriedly reported the results to the imperial court.","—After all, it was the Imperial Palace Guards who had brought the Zhao family to report the case that day. This scene alone made it clear that His Majesty was paying attention to this matter.","The next day in court, an official voluntarily reported the case's outcome to the emperor and used this to suggest that local government offices across the country review past wrongful cases to set the record straight for the people.","Yuwen Lan nodded upon hearing this, saying, \"It's worth considering. Deploy orders for local government offices to begin self-examination.\"","Everyone immediately agreed, but then they heard the emperor casually ask, \"I heard that this person deliberately spread rumors that the Carefree Gentleman was a woman, trying to stir up public emotions and attack his opponent. I want to know, what do you all think about this matter?\"","It was rare for the emperor to inquire about matters unrelated to state affairs in court. As soon as he spoke, the officials immediately began expressing their views.","Someone said, \"This is clearly the work of a malicious mind. But in my opinion, those who were incited by him to insult the Carefree Gentleman should also come forward and apologize to him now. How could such a talented writer, who has produced so many brilliant stories, possibly be a woman? How could these people be so easily swayed?\"","As soon as these words were spoken, many nodded in agreement.","—Well, everyone knows that the Carefree Gentleman is currently a favorite in the imperial court. Not only does the Empress Dowager love his stories the most, but it's highly likely that he's writing under imperial command.","So, defending the Carefree Gentleman is equivalent to upholding the dignity of the royal family, right?","Therefore, this flattery must be delivered!","At this moment, Hanlin Academy Scholar Zou Mozhong stepped forward and said, \"If I may be so bold, I believe this person has misplaced his focus. This matter has nothing to do with gender. Even if the Carefree Gentleman were indeed a woman, would her stories be any different? Taking myself as an example, what I like are the unique stories from his pen. Although they seem absurd and outrageous, they always find prototypes in reality. And when you think something is difficult to achieve in reality, the Carefree Gentleman's stories always manage to fulfill everyone's wishes. If this gentleman were truly a woman, I would admire her even more.\"","As he finished speaking, the emperor raised an eyebrow, \"How so?\"","Zou Mozhong said, \"Your Majesty, throughout history, women's education has always been restricted, and their activities have been limited to the inner chambers and boudoirs. Under such circumstances, if a woman could have such a broad perspective and write such a rich variety of stories with fluent language, it would naturally be admirable.\"","Upon hearing this, not only did the emperor nod slightly, but many ministers also nodded in agreement.","Especially the Minister of Works, Lu Kaihe, who actively echoed, \"What Scholar Zou said is exactly what I think. To be frank, Your Majesty, I also greatly enjoy the Carefree Gentleman's stories because he dares to reveal the truth and ensure that good is rewarded and evil is punished in his stories. There are always many injustices in this world, and who would know about them if the Carefree Gentleman didn't expose them for us?\"","\"For example, in the case of the Zhao family's inheritance, a minor official from the Capital Official could stamp documents without asking for Zhao Hairong's own opinion, ultimately leading to a wrongful judgment by the Capital Official, and the Zhao family's property being occupied by an outsider for decades. Without the Carefree Gentleman, this matter would surely have gone unknown, and the Zhao family's property would have remained in the hands of that evil Wei person. Now that such a wrongful case has been exposed to the world through the Carefree Gentleman's pen, ensuring that evil meets its just deserts, how could we hate her for upholding justice just because she might be a woman, instead of being grateful?\"","\"Therefore, I believe that not only is this matter unrelated to the Carefree Gentleman's gender, but the Capital Official should also award him an honorary title of 'Righteous Person' to show encouragement.\"","After Minister Lu's impassioned speech, many expressed their admiration.","After all, this Minister of Works rarely spoke so much usually, and hearing him now, they realized his eloquence was surprising.","Yuwen Lan, however, thought to himself that if Yanshu could know about Lu Kaihe's speech, she would be very happy.","This man truly lived up to being Yanshu's loyal reader.","However, it's better to forgo the matter of awarding a title. If the Capital Official really were to award one, wouldn't Yanshu have to go receive it?","Wouldn't that expose everything?","So he said, \"Minister Lu's words are reasonable, but I believe this Carefree Gentleman is a righteous person. Giving him a title might be somewhat superfluous.\"","Lu Kaihe suddenly realized and quickly bowed, saying, \"Your Majesty is wise. It was my foolishness.\"","Yuwen Lan then said, \"Alright, let's talk about something else. Tibet has expressed intentions for peace, what do you think?\"","—Due to the previous political upheaval in Nanzhao, where the crown prince with half Great Liang blood became the new heir, and now with Nanzhao King Mu Zhengping personally coming to the capital, it clearly indicated the intention of an alliance between Great Liang and Nanzhao.","As a neighboring country to both, Tibet realized that they would likely be at a disadvantage against these two countries for many years to come, so they simply took the initiative to sue for peace.","Of course, having one more friend is much better than having one more enemy.","As soon as the emperor spoke, it immediately drew agreement from the ministers.","The Grand Secretary of the Eastern Pavilion said, \"Your Majesty, I believe this is a good thing. Although there's no need for a marriage alliance, the two countries can certainly increase exchanges. However, we don't need to be overly generous. If they want grain seeds, silk, or tea, let them exchange with cattle, sheep, or gold. Great Liang doesn't need to take advantage of them, but we shouldn't lose out either. We must make them understand the meaning of fairness.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone expressed their agreement.","Yuwen Lan then said, \"Regarding trade matters, let the Ministry of Revenue and the Court of State Ceremonial work together to quickly establish detailed rules.\"","Hearing this, the relevant officials immediately agreed, and others also felt reassured.","—At this point, among the foreign countries that had come to the capital this time, most had already expressed their attitudes. Except for Dongwo, which was not to be mentioned again, most of the others had expressed their desire to maintain friendly relations with Great Liang. Even the hesitant Rouran had taken the initiative to show goodwill yesterday, proposing to set up border trade markets to benefit both sides' border residents.","However, Rouran's neighbor, Dangxia, had yet to express their stance.","This country, sandwiched between Great Liang and Xiongrong, was a key location just like Nanzhao. Moreover, this was the first time they had sent envoys since their new ruler ascended the throne, so their attitude was very important.","Just as the ministers were worried, they heard the emperor say, \"Tomorrow, the King of Nanzhao will leave the capital. Tonight, I will host a farewell banquet for him in Jiying Hall. This is the last opportunity for Dangxia to express their stance. If they have no intention of maintaining good relations with Great Liang, we should ask them to leave as soon as possible.\"","All the ministers agreed in unison.","As night fell, Jiying Hall was brilliantly lit.","Yanshu accompanied the emperor to attend the event again today. When she saw those important ministers from the court, she felt particularly excited.","Today, she had carefully studied the situation at court with the help of the system. She learned that after the eloquent speeches by Scholar Zou and Minister Lu, the ministers no longer objected to her being a woman.","Oh my, Scholar Zou truly had a discerning eye in discovering her talent, and Minister Lu was such an enthusiastic fan of her novels! Having such knowledgeable confidants meant her stories hadn't been written in vain.","Thinking back to how she used to procrastinate, causing Scholar Zou to stay at the Hanlin Academy for days and depriving fan Minister Lu of new stories to read, she felt incredibly guilty. She wished she could immediately write ten novels to make it up to them!","Yuwen Lan listened silently, thinking to himself, \"...\" He wanted to advise her that writing ten novels in a row might be too much for the baby in her belly.","However, he had important matters to attend to tonight.","At that moment, amidst the sound of bells and drums, dancers swung their long sleeves, performing a dance unique to the Great Liang dynasty to bid farewell to the distinguished guests.","Yuwen Lan took the initiative to raise his cup to Mu Zhengping, saying, \"I wish the King of Mu a smooth journey. Please do visit Great Liang often when you have the chance.\"","Mu Zhengping, dressed in the royal attire of Nanzhao, also raised his cup and replied, \"I thank Your Majesty for the warm hospitality. From now on, Great Liang and Nanzhao shall be as close as brothers, standing together through thick and thin.\"","These words carried great weight, especially coming from the respected King of Mu. They rang with sincerity.","Not only did they elicit unanimous praise from the Great Liang court officials, but they also sent shockwaves through the other foreign envoys present.","— Great Liang was already powerful, and now with such a staunch ally, wouldn't they become even stronger?","Therefore, going to war with them in the future probably wouldn't be a wise choice.","Seeing this, the Dangxia envoy, who had remained silent until now, suddenly spoke up, \"It has been five years since our new Khagan ascended to the throne, and this is the first time we've paid our respects to Great Liang. Our Dowager Khagan greatly admires His Majesty's abilities and is very willing to befriend your country. However, we wonder if your country has the sincerity to reciprocate?\"","Hmm?","As soon as these words were uttered, the court officials in the hall quietly raised their eyebrows —","Was Dangxia finally unable to wait any longer and ready to make their stance known?","However, the way they phrased it was truly unpleasant.","What did they mean by \"if your country has the sincerity\"?","It was as if they thought Great Liang was inherently inferior to them.","Yanshu felt the same way.","She remembered that when the Prince of Gaoli was stabbed by those two Dongwo demons last time, this person had sided with the Dongwo envoy, constantly questioning Great Liang.","Even looking at him was annoying.","Now, hearing him speak like this, Yuwen Lan asked, \"What kind of sincerity does your country require from Great Liang?\"","The envoy replied, \"We request that Great Liang designate Linqi, Heishui, and Weizhou — the three cities bordering Dangxia — as friendship cities. Allow our Dangxia people to reside and conduct business there without paying taxes.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, the entire hall erupted in an uproar.","Yanshu was also stunned.","She couldn't help but think to herself, \"Oh boy, these Dangxia people aren't asking for sincerity, they're trying to act like Great Liang's father!\"","Where did the Dangxia leader get such confidence from?","The system then explained, [Actually, this isn't the Dangxia leader's idea. This envoy added it himself. He wants to make a significant achievement so that when he returns, his former mother-in-law, the Dangxia Dowager, will praise him and entrust him with important tasks.]","Hearing this, Yanshu asked, [Is this man the Dangxia consort?]","The system replied, [Sort of. He was the consort of the Dangxia Princess, but last year the Princess was angered to death by him and a maid, so he can only be considered a former consort now.]","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","Well, that's some juicy gossip."]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97","paragraphs":["Since we've started, we might as well finish this melon.","Yanshu immediately asked the system, \"Quick, tell me in detail, what's really going on here?\"","The system began to explain, \"The old Khan of Dangxia died five years ago, and the new Khan Hu Yuanmao took the throne. Actually, the new Khan is only 18 years old now, still just a youngster. For these five years, his mother Empress Dowager Xiao has been controlling state affairs.\"","\"Besides this son, Empress Dowager Xiao also has a daughter, the Princess of Dangxia. The Empress Dowager loves this daughter very much. Back then, she carefully selected Che Hongtu, the annoying guy you see before you, to be the princess's consort. Why choose him? Because the princess was actually born with some health issues and has always been in poor health. Empress Dowager Xiao didn't care about anything else, she just thought this man looked quite honest and probably wouldn't dare to bully her daughter.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but interject, \"So following the usual pattern, this man isn't actually honest, right? Don't tell me he's like Zhao Chengwen, Yuwen Yan's former consort, who kept several mistresses outside?\"","The system replied, \"It's not quite that bad. After all, Dangxia is a small country, and the capital is small too. Even if he had such intentions, he wouldn't have the ability to do so. However, Che Hongtu indeed isn't honest. He treats the princess well on the surface, but he's long harbored various schemes behind her back. Just consider this - two years after their marriage, the princess finally gave birth to a son, but it took a further toll on her already poor health. Even after the full month of postpartum confinement, she still couldn't get out of bed most days. Empress Dowager Xiao was very concerned and worried that the people around her daughter wouldn't know how to take care of her properly. So she sent one of her own clever palace maids to look after the princess. Who would have thought that not long after this maid arrived at the princess's residence, she and Che Hongtu would become involved with each other.\"","Yanshu exclaimed, \"Oh my!\" These two were truly lacking in virtue!","Especially this Che whatever-his-name-was. The Dangxia princess had given birth to his child at the cost of her health, and at such a time, he actually got involved with the Empress Dowager's maid?","She hurriedly asked the system, \"So did the princess perhaps discover the affair between these two, and die from the shock of it?\"","The system confirmed, \"That's right. The affair was first discovered by the princess's personal maid. To be fair, this maid was a bit impulsive and didn't think things through carefully. She told the princess directly, not expecting that upon hearing the news, the princess would immediately suffer a fatal hemorrhage. They couldn't even save her in time.\"","Yanshu was at a loss for words and could only sigh, \"Well, of course. She was already so weak she couldn't get out of bed. How could she withstand such a shock? So what happened after that? Did Empress Dowager Xiao find out about this? How come she didn't punish this man and the maid?\"","The system explained, \"Given Empress Dowager Xiao's style, if she had known, she would have had this man drawn and quartered at the very least. But unfortunately, after Che Hongtu discovered that their affair had been exposed, he immediately killed the maid who had informed the princess. To the outside world, he claimed that the maid had been caught stealing, which angered the princess to death. He even put on quite a show of crying and wailing before Empress Dowager Xiao, saying he had failed to take good care of the princess and wished he could follow her in death.\"","Yanshu asked, \"... So Empress Dowager Xiao still doesn't know the truth? She was really fooled by him like that?\"","The system confirmed, \"That's right. After all, there was still a young grandson who needed care. Although Empress Dowager Xiao had some doubts about her daughter's death, for the sake of her young grandson, she still appointed this man as an envoy. If he can negotiate well with the Great Liang this time, he'll likely be given some important position when he returns.\"","Yanshu understood, \"So that's why this Che whatever is making such outrageous demands, hoping to accomplish a great feat and return to seek an even higher position from his mother-in-law?\"","The system replied, \"Exactly, that's how it is.\"","Yanshu couldn't help but think, \"Ha! Keep dreaming!\" She figured even their mortal enemies, the Xiongrong, wouldn't dare to make such demands to the Great Liang, let alone a tiny country like Dangxia.","The others in the hall seemed to think the same way.","Upon hearing Che Hongtu's words, several Great Liang court officials immediately shook their heads and said, \"Has this envoy perhaps had too much to drink? If the roles were reversed, would you agree to such demands?\"","\"Indeed, the Great Liang is not a vassal state of your Dangxia. Why should we humble ourselves to seek your friendship? And open up three cities? Even one city would be too much!\"","\"Exactly, and not requiring you to pay taxes? Are you expecting us to just give you money for free? What do you plan to offer the Great Liang in return? Will you also open up three cities? And not require us to pay taxes?\"","Come to think of it, Dangxia was just a tiny piece of land. If they were to open up three cities, they'd probably have to give away their capital city.","As the words fell, Che Hongtu raised his head and said, \"The Great Liang is after all a vast and powerful country, with territory and population many times that of our Dangxia. Surely you won't be so petty as to haggle over such matters with Dangxia?\"","At these words, everyone raised their eyebrows -","Huh, so this person is expecting to get something for nothing?","Not to mention that the Great Liang isn't stupid, but if they were to agree to such unreasonable conditions in front of so many foreign envoys today, what would the other countries think?","How could he be so delusional!","Sure enough, hearing him speak like this, the emperor on the throne finally couldn't bear it anymore and said, \"There's a saying, 'Courtesy demands reciprocity.' Our sages have said, 'To give without receiving is not courteous. To receive without giving is also not courteous.' Based on what this envoy is saying, it seems your country has no intention of fostering good relations with the Great Liang. Perhaps you should go back and reconsider.\"","As these words fell, everyone nodded in agreement.","However, Che Hongtu smiled and said, \"I think it's Your Majesty who needs to reconsider. Doesn't Your Majesty know how many Xiongrong invasions Dangxia has blocked for the Great Liang over the years? I'll be frank with Your Majesty, in recent years the Xiongrong Khan has been eager to establish good relations with our Dangxia. If you lose Dangxia as an ally today, the Great Liang may regret it in the future.\"","What?","At these words, all the Great Liang court officials frowned - was he implying that if they didn't agree to Dangxia's demands today, Dangxia would ally with the Xiongrong?","It was well known that the Xiongrong were the Great Liang's greatest enemy. Given Dangxia's current attitude, wasn't this a blatant threat?","At once, everyone's anger rose another notch.","Yuwen Lan felt the same way.","At this point, all traces of a smile had vanished from his face. He coldly said to Che Hongtu, \"If I'm not mistaken, in just the last thirty years alone, the Xiongrong have killed three Khans of Dangxia, dozens of your generals, and countless civilians. Those barbarians are what they are by nature. If you say your country has been blocking the Xiongrong for our Great Liang, that's really not necessary. If you can still ally with them despite such deep national and personal enmity, then by all means, go ahead. I can only wish both parties well.\"","As his words fell, everyone chimed in agreement, \"That's right, if you want to ally with them, go ahead. Only today did we learn that Dangxia is such a spineless country.\"","\"Indeed, to be able to swallow such deep hatred, no wonder they have the audacity to make such demands.\"","\"Exactly...\"","Faced with such reactions, Che Hongtu paused, finally showing some panic in his eyes.","Seeing this, Yanshu couldn't help but laugh coldly in her heart. Serve him right, he had messed up!","Hmph, how dare he threaten her little emperor like this. Just wait, the real show was yet to come!","Probably because he had been so angry at the evening banquet, Yuwen Lan's face remained cold and expressionless even after returning to Ganlu Palace.","Seeing this, Yanshu dismissed all the unnecessary attendants and asked him, \"Is Your Majesty still angry because of that Dangxia envoy?\"","Yuwen Lan didn't deny it. He just gave a cold laugh and said, \"I didn't expect such a small country to be so thick-skinned and shameless.\"","Huh, how dare they use the Xiongrong to threaten him?","Let them go ahead then. He'd like to see the Xiongrong not swallow them whole, bones and all.","However, as soon as he finished speaking, Yanshu hurriedly said, \"Actually, there's more to this matter. According to my information, the Dangxia Khan and Empress Dowager Xiao truly do want to establish good relations with us. It's all because of this Che whatever who wants to accomplish a great feat and return for rewards. That's why he dared to speak so presumptuously this time.\"","Yuwen Lan frowned at her words, \"Is that so?\"","Yanshu nodded vigorously, \"Absolutely true. By the way, does Your Majesty know how long it takes to travel from the capital to the Great Liang's capital at the fastest speed?\"","Yuwen Lan was still confused, \"Why do you ask?\"","Yanshu righteously declared, \"Because this man called Che Hongtu caused the death of his own wife, who was the Princess of Dangxia and the beloved daughter of Empress Dowager Xiao. This matter is not yet known within Dangxia. As a person of justice, how could I simply stand by and do nothing?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, he had never imagined there would be such a twist.","Nevertheless, since this was the case, Che Hongtu could only blame himself for being too clever for his own good.","...","From the capital of Da Liang to the capital of Dangxia was a full two thousand li.","However, if one rode hard on horseback, a secret letter could arrive in three to five days.","So it wasn't long before Empress Dowager Xiao in the Dangxia palace received news that was enough to enrage her—it turned out that her most beloved daughter had been angered to death by her own husband.","The secret letter was very detailed and assertive, clearly stating the time and place of her daughter's death, the names of the servants who attended her, and even describing the times and locations when Che Hongtu met with the palace maid she had sent to the princess's residence, as well as the gold and silver jewelry Che Hongtu had given to win the maid's favor.","Seeing all this, Empress Dowager Xiao believed seven or eight parts of it. In her fury, she immediately sent people to reinvestigate.","Before the investigation results came out, she received an official letter from the Da Liang court.","The letter indignantly detailed the actions of their envoy Che Hongtu in Da Liang, and severely criticized Dangxia for lacking sincerity and backbone, actually disregarding national enmity and family hatred to seek alliance with the greedy and brutal Xiongrong.","After reading the letter, Empress Dowager Xiao was naturally furious and immediately dispatched a new team of envoys to Da Liang.","...","Meanwhile, in the capital of Da Liang, the new work of the \"Carefree Young Master\" once again appeared before readers.","—The story from the Eight Sides Bookstore that had revealed the protagonist's identity last time still left people wanting more, so now everyone was curious to see if this new story would again have named characters and satisfying revenge.","Once again, people rushed to buy and read it.","After reading, people discovered that although this story didn't specify names, it took place in a foreign country and was equally distinctive.","In the story, the princess was innocent and lovable, gentle and kind, deeply cherished by her mother since childhood. When she came of age, her mother carefully selected a consort for her after much consideration.","Who knew that the consort, though outwardly righteous and kind, was actually lecherous and despicable. While being soft-spoken and obedient to the princess, he was secretly involved with a maid in the household, doing all sorts of disgraceful things. Eventually, when the truth came to light, the princess couldn't accept that the husband she trusted was such a scoundrel. In her anger and distress, she suffered postpartum hemorrhage and unfortunately passed away.","As for the husband, in his panic, he actually planned to silence witnesses to cover up his crimes.","Fortunately, the Empress Dowager was wise and saw through his schemes in time. In her fury, she immediately had this hypocrite and his mistress both executed to comfort her daughter's spirit in heaven.","And...","After reading this story, righteous readers naturally scorned the unfaithful consort, lamented the early demise of the princess, and praised the wisdom and decisiveness of the Empress Dowager.","Regarding this, the Empress Dowager who had heard Yanshu read the story aloud was somewhat puzzled.","As Yanshu's biggest fan, the Empress Dowager naturally knew that this was written about the royal family of Dangxia.","She said, \"Wasn't that Empress Dowager Xiao deceived by her son-in-law for a long time? If it weren't for His Majesty sending a secret letter, she still wouldn't know the truth. Why did you write her as so wise?\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"Because this story is meant for the people of Dangxia to read, so naturally I had to portray their Empress Dowager in a good light. Moreover, revenge is best served quickly, so readers will feel satisfied. Also, Empress Dowager Xiao must be full of guilt towards her daughter after learning the truth. If this story can make her feel better, it will also benefit the relationship between our two countries.\"","The Empress Dowager finally understood and nodded, \"I see, so it's about flattering Empress Dowager Xiao.\"","Yanshu chuckled, \"Indeed, after all, it's better to have one more friend than one more enemy.\"","The Empress Dowager also laughed, \"That's certainly true. But this Che Hongtu is really infuriating. I wonder when their people will arrive in the capital? We must make sure he doesn't escape.\"","Yanshu said, \"Soon, soon. After learning the truth, they must be anxious to bring him back for trial as quickly as possible.\"","Now they needed to make sure the guards at the embassy were extra vigilant to prevent that man from escaping.","Sure enough, after six or seven days, new envoys from Dangxia arrived in the capital.","This new envoy was an old minister of Dangxia who had always advocated for friendly relations with Da Liang. Upon arrival, he completely changed Che Hongtu's rhetoric and earnestly explained the stance of the Dangxia court.","Da Liang was also magnanimous. After some discussion between both sides, a decision was quickly reached—each side would open one border city for trade, allowing citizens of both countries to do business, with taxes reduced by half to show mutual sincerity.","When this news came out, both sides were satisfied. Compared to other countries, Da Liang had not shown favoritism, so there were no objections. It could be called a win-win situation.","Afterwards, envoys from various countries bid farewell and set off on their return journeys.","The Dangxia envoy also hurriedly returned to their capital with the criminal Che Hongtu. Thanks to the escort of Da Liang guards, Che Hongtu's several attempts to escape were unsuccessful.","It was heard that Empress Dowager Xiao was already furious, waiting to punish Che Hongtu. His punishment would likely be even worse than in the story.","Yanshu silently lit a candle in her heart for this man.","She had seen many who had done unconscionable things, but rarely one who could be so arrogant after doing so.","Hah, there was no need for divine justice—before her, all demons and monsters had nowhere to hide!"]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98","paragraphs":["About half a month later, Yanshu heard news about Dangxia from the system.","It was said that Empress Dowager Xiao received a secret letter and verified the evidence of Che Hongtu's crimes. In her fury, she immediately had him and that palace maid executed.","As for his daughter's young grandson, he was brought back to the palace to be personally raised by Empress Dowager Xiao, which put people's minds at ease.","Surprisingly, Empress Dowager Xiao was also very fond of her novels. Not only did she have someone deliver them, but she also specially sent two beautiful jade pieces and a fox fur cloak from Dangxia as a token of her appreciation.","Of course, Empress Dowager Xiao thought she was a man, so the jade and fur cloak were in men's styles.","But Yanshu didn't mind and was very pleased. After all, she had originally only intended to use the novels to improve relations between the two countries. She never expected to gain such a generous fan, and a foreign one at that. Moreover, it was a discerning and talented empress dowager.","As the saying goes, great minds think alike. This proved that those who liked her were all winners.","Seeing that the Prince of Gaoli had stabilized from his injuries and departed for home, all the foreign envoys who had come to the capital for the Changning Festival had now left.","The weather in the capital was also noticeably cooler.","A few days later, it was time for the Zhongyuan Festival.","The Zhongyuan Festival is an important holiday for honoring ancestors. Besides commoners releasing river lanterns and burning offerings, the imperial court also held grand memorial ceremonies.","These included dispatching special officials to release lanterns in the river, and setting up altars in major temples and Taoist abbeys in the capital to invite monks and priests to pray for the souls of soldiers who had died for the country and homeless spirits throughout history.","Of course, Yanshu had no chance to see these grand events. After all, it wasn't a suitable day for going out, and she was pregnant, so she could only obediently stay in the palace.","However, since it was a court holiday, Yuwen Lan spent the whole day with her after going to Fengxian Hall in the morning to pay respects to the ancestors.","The two had lunch together and then rested for a while. When they got up again, Yanshu saw that Yuwen Lan had changed into casual black clothes and asked Fu Hai to prepare incense and candles, looking as if he was about to go out.","She asked curiously, \"Is Your Majesty going to Fengxian Hall again?\"","Yuwen Lan's expression was somewhat solemn as he simply said, \"I'm going to Yongfu Palace.\"","Yongfu Palace?","At first, Yanshu didn't quite understand, but then she heard the system say, [The Emperor's birth mother used to live in Yongfu Palace.]","She suddenly realized that the Emperor was going to pay respects to his birth mother.","Perhaps he was being so secretive because he was afraid the Empress Dowager would find out and feel resentful.","Ah, perhaps it was because of the little one in her belly, but she had been feeling more emotional lately. Suddenly feeling sympathetic, she said, \"Would Your Majesty like me to accompany you?\"","Although she was pregnant and couldn't go to the mausoleum, she could still pay respects in the palace.","Yuwen Lan was somewhat surprised and asked, \"You want to go?\"","Yanshu nodded and looked at him sincerely, saying, \"May this humble concubine have that honor?\"","[Aww, it's because you feel sorry for the little emperor, isn't it? A child who lost his mother soon after birth probably doesn't even remember what she looked like, sob...]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He felt touched, amused, and a bit confused -","Why did she keep calling him \"little\" emperor lately?","Where exactly had he given her that impression?","With mixed emotions, Yuwen Lan still...","Nodded and said, \"It would be good to go together.\"","He then took her hand and left.","Before long, they arrived at their destination.","Ever since Consort Dowager Hui passed away, no one else had lived in Yongfu Palace, so the furnishings remained the same as before. After Yuwen Lan ascended the throne, he had arranged for people to specially guard it. Every Yuanxiao Festival, they would come to light some incense and candles as a token of respect.","Although he truly could not remember his birth mother's face, she was after all the one who brought him into this world, and he did not want to forget her.","And as Yanshu had said, since the Empress Dowager was still alive and had raised him, no matter how much he missed his birth mother, he had to be considerate of the Empress Dowager's feelings. So he always came quietly by himself in casual clothes, paid his respects, and then left.","However, this time he had company.","Two people, in fact.","Though touched, he was still concerned about her pregnancy. When they reached the hall entrance, Yuwen Lan said, \"This place hasn't been lived in for a long time, so the yin energy is probably strong. You wait here, and I'll go in alone.\"","Hearing him say this, Yanshu could only agree and stop at the hall entrance, watching as Fu Hai followed him inside.","Rendong accompanied her as she took a few steps in the somewhat desolate courtyard, and couldn't help but feel emotional again.","-- Sob, on a day like this, the Emperor is thinking of his own mother. I wonder if the Empress Dowager is also remembering her child who died young?","Thinking of this, she couldn't help but touch her slightly swollen belly and say to the little one inside, \"Baby, you must grow well in mommy's tummy and be born smoothly and safely in the future. Both of us must stay safe and sound!\"","After she finished speaking, Rendong, who was accompanying her, couldn't help but smile and say, \"Both the mistress and the imperial child are blessed. Your wishes will surely come true.\"","Yanshu nodded and said, \"I hope so...\"","But before she could finish speaking, she suddenly froze.","She felt something in her lower abdomen seem to move a little.","Seeing her like this, Rendong was startled and quickly asked, \"What's wrong, mistress?\"","Yanshu's eyes widened, and she almost didn't dare to breathe, \"I think... I felt the baby move.\"","The baby moved?","Although Rendong had no practical experience, she had received guidance from the imperial doctor. Upon hearing this, she immediately said happily, \"Doctor Jiang said this is a sign that the imperial child in your belly is healthy. Congratulations, mistress.\"","[Tsk tsk, Doctor Jiang also said that from the first fetal movement, we need to count the number of movements every day for the mistress. We absolutely can't make any mistakes.]","Yanshu was startled.","-- She clearly saw Rendong close her mouth after saying \"Congratulations, mistress,\" so why did she hear that last sentence?","...Rendong clearly hadn't opened her mouth again, but that was definitely Rendong's voice!","But that wasn't all. Immediately after, she heard Rendong's voice again, [Sigh, it's the Zhongyuan Festival today. I wonder if I'll have time to go to Taiye Pool tonight to release two lotus lanterns for my parents? Should I ask the mistress for leave? But how should I bring it up?]","Yanshu, \"...\"","She was certain she hadn't been seeing things; Rendong's mouth definitely hadn't moved.","What was going on? Could it be that Rendong knew ventriloquism?","How had she never discovered this talent of Rendong's in all these years together?","System, [... Haven't you considered that this might be something called mind-reading?]","Yanshu, [What? Mind-reading? System, are you saying I have mind-reading abilities now?]","System, [That's right. How else could you hear what others are thinking?]","Yanshu, [... But but but why did I suddenly get mind-reading abilities?]","System, [The system can't be certain at the moment, but it's very likely related to your pregnancy...]","Yanshu paused. Related to her pregnancy?","... Come to think of it, she had just discovered the fetal movement, and the mind-reading ability came right after. It seems it really might be related to the baby in her belly.","Thinking this, her eyes immediately lit up, and she touched her belly saying, \"My baby really is a little lucky star!\"","Although Rendong didn't know where her mistress's words came from, she quickly agreed, \"That's right, the imperial child will surely be as blessed as the mistress.\"","Then Yanshu said to her, \"After dinner, you should go release a river lantern for your parents too. Ask Lianxin and the others if anyone wants to go as well.\"","Rendong immediately became excited, \"Thank you, mistress! Thank you! I'll arrange for us to take turns going so that someone will always be by your side.\"","[Sob sob sob, the mistress knows what I want to do without me even saying it! Is the mistress a fairy in the mortal world, to be so amazing?!]","Yanshu felt smug inside.","With the system and now mind-reading abilities, was she about to become invincible?","Just then, Yuwen Lan and Fu Hai walked out of the hall.","Seeing Rendong's excited face, Yuwen Lan curiously asked, \"What happened?\"","Yanshu concealed her pride and said, \"Nothing much. I was thinking about the river lantern release at Taiye Pool today and told her to go release one for her own family. I didn't expect her to be so happy about it.\"","Hearing this, Fu Hai immediately said, \"The Empress is kind-hearted. Miss Rendong is truly fortunate.\"","In her heart, she thought, [Come to think of it, I want to go release river lanterns too. Your Majesty, couldn't you learn from Consort Yi?]","Yanshu heard this and felt sympathetic, so she said to the emperor, \"I wonder if Manager Fu wants to go too. Perhaps Your Majesty could show him some mercy?\"","-- Hehe, since I have mind-reading powers now, I might as well go all the way and give out a special bonus today!","Yuwen Lan was stunned.","What did she say?","Mind reading?","What did that mean? Could she also hear what Fu Hai was thinking?","Then... what about him?","Could she hear his thoughts too?","Thinking of this, Yuwen Lan suddenly jolted and quickly looked at Yanshu.","He saw her blinking her big eyes at him, thinking, [What's going on? Didn't you hear what I said? Hurry up and agree! Otherwise, I'll lose face!!!]","Yuwen Lan thought to himself, if she's thinking this way, it means she can't hear his thoughts?","He quickly collected himself and said to Fu Hai, \"If you want to go, you may. Just make sure to arrange your duties properly and don't neglect your official business.\"","Fu Hai immediately showed joy in his eyes, \"This servant thanks Your Majesty for your great kindness.\"","[Oh my, I really benefited from Consort Yi's influence today.]","Yuwen Lan didn't say anything more, but secretly glanced at Yanshu again.","He saw her looking quite pleased with herself, [Hehe, no need to admire me too much!]","Then suddenly she paused, [Wait, why can't I hear what the emperor is thinking?]","Yuwen Lan, [...So that's how it is.]","He immediately felt relieved.","But Yanshu still couldn't understand it. She tried again but still couldn't hear Yuwen Lan's thoughts.","Puzzled, she had to call out to the system, [What's going on? Why can't I read the emperor's mind?]","The system replied, [...The system can't help with this one. After all, even I can't handle the emperor. Maybe it's because he's the Son of Heaven and has some dragon aura protecting him.]","Yanshu, [....]","Could it really be that mystical?","But thinking about it, besides this possibility, she really couldn't figure it out.","Well, fortunately the emperor was reliable. If he weren't reliable and had dragon aura protection, wouldn't that be hard to deal with?","Even with all her abilities, she wouldn't be able to affect him.","Yuwen Lan silently...","Nodded, indeed?","He was reliable, fortunately he was the emperor.","With her mind-reading ability, Yanshu's life opened a new chapter.","She experimented all night in her palace and found it worked every time. The next day, she happily went to chat with her number one idol.","They first talked about the aftermath of that Dangxia Kingdom prince consort Che's incident, then discussed yesterday's Lantern Festival.","Then she heard the Empress Dowager sigh, \"Time passes so quickly, autumn is coming soon.\"","Yanshu was about to nod when she heard the Empress Dowager think, [The capital must be colder than Langya. I wonder if that fool brought enough winter clothes? After all, he didn't plan to stay when he came this summer.]","Yanshu paused, realizing that the Empress Dowager was worried about Mr. Qi?","Aww, her number one idol and her role model, though they couldn't meet often, they still cared about each other!","So she quickly said, \"I heard this year's cotton harvest was bountiful. His Majesty, fearing that cheap cotton would hurt the farmers, specially ordered the court to purchase quite a lot. Some was made into official robes distributed to the court officials, and the rest was sent to the textile department to make winter clothes, which were distributed to the Imperial Academy and its affiliated schools, so all teachers and students would have winter clothes to wear.\"","\"I see.\"","The Empress Dowager's eyes immediately lit up as she nodded, \"That's a very good idea. His Majesty is thoughtful.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, but heard the Empress Dowager think, [This girl, she's becoming more and more like a worm in my belly, answering whatever I'm thinking about.]","Yanshu thought, please don't say that about yourself, having worms in your belly isn't a good thing!","Besides, what she could do was really limited. It would be better to quickly think of a way to arrange another meeting between her number one idol and role model.","Just then, another voice came to her ears, [Hmph, this woman is good at fooling the Empress Dowager! Last night she was accompanying His Majesty to pay respects to Consort Hui, and today she's acting all sweet in front of the Empress Dowager! Speaking of which, His Majesty doesn't even appreciate the Empress Dowager's kindness in raising him. All these years, he never forgets to burn paper offerings for Consort Hui. Poor Empress Dowager, her whole life has been spent making wedding clothes for others!]","Yanshu paused and looked toward the source of the voice - Nanny Zhuang who was standing beside the Empress Dowager.","She saw the other person maintaining a proper appearance of minding her own business.","Tsk, although she had long known that Nanny Zhuang didn't like her, this was the first time she clearly heard the other's thoughts with her mind-reading ability.","She couldn't help but reflect that the emperor's inability to forget his birth mother was only natural, just as the Empress Dowager couldn't forget her own child who died young. Whenever she thought about it, she would inevitably feel sad. One couldn't say the emperor was unfilial to the Empress Dowager because of this.","Come to think of it, this Nanny Zhuang was truly loyal to the Empress Dowager, just a bit too stubborn in her thinking.","But then the system interjected, [Actually, she's most loyal to that old rascal Duke Cheng'en. On the surface she's concerned about the Empress Dowager, but in reality she's worried that the old lecher's descendants won't have glory and wealth in the future.]","Yanshu, [??? What? That old lecher Duke Cheng'en?]","Sure enough, right after that she heard Nanny Zhuang think, [His Majesty still can't forget his birth mother who only raised him for two months. It's clear that eventually, step by step, the Empress Dowager will be abandoned by him, and then the Duke and the Zhou family will completely lose their status and be trampled under others' feet! My lady, why can't you think about your own brother!]","Yanshu, [....]","Pft, who would have thought that old lecher Duke Cheng'en would have such a devoted follower? These inner thoughts actually sound quite touching.","Come to think of it, could she be secretly in love with that old lecher?","System, [That's right, after all, he was the only... man in her life.]","Yanshu, \"???\"","What kind of melodramatic story is this?"]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99","paragraphs":["Although not particularly interested in this old nanny, Yanshu still found the situation quite peculiar.","She asked the system about it: \"What's going on here? Why would Nanny Zhuang get involved with that old lecher Duke Cheng'en?\"","The system replied: \"This goes back about 30 years. As everyone knows, the Zhou family was a prestigious clan. Duke Cheng'en was spoiled from childhood and became a lecherous fellow. Before he was even old enough to marry, he had his way with nearly all the maids around him. But that wasn't enough - he then set his sights on his sister's household, that is, the Empress Dowager's. After all, the Empress Dowager knew how to select people, and her maids were all quite comely.\"","\"But how could the Empress Dowager allow such behavior? Upon discovering his intentions, she immediately sternly warned him and reported it to their parents, who gave him a harsh scolding. However, Duke Cheng'en only pretended to behave on the surface. In reality, he became even more defiant - the more his sister forbade it, the more determined he was. So one afternoon when the mansion was mostly empty, he forced himself on Nanny Zhuang.\"","Yanshu was surprised: \"So Nanny Zhuang was an unwilling victim? Did she tell the Empress Dowager?\"","The system: \"Tell her what? The Empress Dowager had sensed something was off those couple days and even specifically asked her, but she went to great lengths to cover for that little scoundrel and let the matter slide. After that, she even fell deeply in love with Duke Cheng'en and couldn't extricate herself.\"","Yanshu: \"What? What kind of situation is this? The legendary Stockholm Syndrome?\"","System: \"More or less.\"","Yanshu felt utterly confused. She asked further: \"But Duke Cheng'en was lecherous from youth to old age, with so many women along the way. Nanny Zhuang never felt hatred born of love?\"","System: \"As you can see, she never did. Even now she's still exhausting herself thinking of that old lecher's interests, trying to use her own Stockholm Syndrome to manipulate the Empress Dowager.\"","Yanshu: \"...It seems this old nanny's condition is quite severe.\"","But the problem was, even if she chose to love Duke Cheng'en and sacrifice herself for that old lecher, it shouldn't concern others!","Hadn't the Empress Dowager ever fought for her family's interests?","Hadn't the Emperor ever tried to save face for Duke Cheng'en's household?","What was wrong with her accompanying the Emperor to pay respects to his birth mother? Was that worth such hatred from this nanny?","But come to think of it, how did Nanny Zhuang know she had accompanied the Emperor to pay respects to Consort Dowager Hui today?","System: \"Care to guess?\"","Yanshu: \"...Don't tell me this nanny arranged for someone to follow and spy on me and the Emperor?\"","System: \"There's no other possibility.\"","Yanshu felt like vomiting blood.","Good heavens, had this old nanny gone mad? How could she do such a thing?","These people really didn't deserve such a good mistress as the Empress Dowager. If not for her gossip system, wouldn't this misunderstanding fall on her top supporter?","Feeling quite angry, she picked up the teacup beside her, intending to take a sip.","But just then, she heard the system's alarm: \"The rim of that cup has been smeared with castor oil. If a pregnant woman drinks it, it's likely to cause discomfort.\"","What?","Yanshu was startled and immediately stopped her motion.","This movement was rather sudden, and the Empress Dowager noticed, asking curiously, \"What's wrong?\"","Yanshu thought quickly and pretended to feel nauseous, covering her mouth: \"I don't know why, but I suddenly feel a bit sick...\"","The Empress Dowager concernedly said, \"Aren't you past three months already? Why are you still feeling nauseous? Has the imperial physician been checking on you daily?\"","Before Yanshu could speak, Rendong beside her quickly nodded and said, \"Your Majesty, Doctor Jiang has been checking on my lady daily. Just yesterday, my lady felt the baby move for the first time, and Doctor Jiang said everything was normal.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, but still looked puzzled: \"Then what's the matter today?\"","As she finished speaking, Yanshu pretended to recover, rubbing her chest with an apologetic expression: \"I don't know what happened either. Just now when the tea was brought to my lips, I suddenly felt the smell was a bit off... Perhaps I'm being too sensitive. I've embarrassed myself in front of Your Majesty.\"","The smell was off?","The Empress Dowager paused upon hearing this, though she said nothing, her mind began to suspect.","\"How could the tea smell off? Could someone have tampered with it?\"","Yanshu quietly overheard this and felt reassured.","Then she heard the Empress Dowager say to her, \"It's getting late. You should go back and rest.\"","She agreed, letting Rendong support her as she rose, bowed to the Empress Dowager, and took her leave from the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","As for who had tampered with her teacup, there was no need to guess.","The moment she stepped out of the hall, she could still hear Nanny Zhuang anxiously thinking, \"Is this little hussy really unwell or just pretending? I only rubbed a tiny bit on the cup rim with my fingertip, how could she smell it?\"","Yanshu silently listened, inwardly scoffing.","This old woman was courting death with her actions and certainly couldn't be allowed to remain in the palace. By rights, if she had made a scene right then, the Emperor would have had more than enough grounds to sentence this old woman to death.","But unfortunately, she was the Empress Dowager's servant.","If it became a big issue, it would likely implicate the Empress Dowager.","So she could only hint like this, letting the Empress Dowager investigate for herself.","At this time, as she stepped out of the hall, Nanny Zhuang immediately wanted to call someone to clear away the cup Yanshu had used.","But the Empress Dowager stopped her.","The Empress Dowager, showing no emotion, said, \"Call in the people from the tea room.\"","Nanny Zhuang hesitated, but had no choice but to comply and go fetch them.","Not long after, two palace maids from the tea room, Mei Xue and Dan Shuang, arrived in the hall.","After they bowed, the Empress Dowager asked, \"Who brewed the tea today?\"","Mei Xue immediately said, \"Your Majesty, I brewed the tea.\"","The Empress Dowager showed no change in expression, but asked further, \"What tea did you brew for the Worthy Consort?\"","Mei Xue quickly replied, \"I brewed Liu'an Guapian tea for the Worthy Consort, the kind she usually drinks.\"","Dan Shuang nodded in agreement beside her, both looking completely open and honest.","The Empress Dowager then gestured to where Yanshu had been sitting and said, \"Go and see if there's anything wrong with that cup of tea.\"","They complied and went over together, carefully examining the teacup.","Suddenly, Mei Xue said, \"Your Majesty, there seems to be some oil on the rim of the cup.\"","Dan Shuang had already rubbed the oily substance between her fingers and after careful inspection, nodded and said, \"It does appear to be oil.\"","The Empress Dowager's expression turned cold as she asked, \"Then whose hands did this cup of tea pass through?\"","Mei Xue quickly knelt and said, \"Your Majesty, we personally delivered the tea to the hall entrance. It was Nanny Zhuang who brought it inside. Other than that, it didn't pass through anyone else's hands.\"","The Empress Dowager remembered this scene and immediately turned to look at Nanny Zhuang.","In that moment, her gaze was as cold as a knife.","Nanny Zhuang faltered, then quickly knelt and said, \"I've been wronged, Your Majesty.\"","But the Empress Dowager only gave a cold laugh and said, \"Not sending you away directly back then was my biggest mistake. In this hall today, I can trust anyone but you.\"","As she finished speaking, Nanny Zhuang immediately began crying and said, \"Your Majesty's words truly wrong me. I have always acted for Your Majesty's sake! Do you know that yesterday the Emperor went to Yongfu Palace again to pay respects to Consort Dowager Hui, and the Worthy Consort accompanied him the whole way? Your Majesty treats the Worthy Consort so well, but even while pregnant she still accompanies the Emperor. How can she have you in her heart?\"","The Empress Dowager frowned and said, \"Just because of this, you would disregard the imperial heir? How could you bring yourself to do such a thing?\"","But Nanny Zhuang shook her head vigorously and said, \"No, please understand, Your Majesty. I only smeared a tiny bit of castor oil on the cup rim. Even if the Worthy Consort had drunk from it, it would have been an insignificant amount. At most it would have given her slight diarrhea, it wouldn't have affected the imperial heir at all.\"","What?","Just a bit of castor oil?","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager immediately became angry: \"She's carrying twins now and can't risk any carelessness. How can you speak of this so lightly? Why on earth did you do this?\"","Nanny Zhuang cried again and said, \"I only wanted to let the Worthy Consort know that she shouldn't go to that place, to make her truly loyal to you in the future and not dare to have any disloyal thoughts.\"","The Empress Dowager was at a loss for words. She closed her eyes, sighed, and said, \"Isn't this just human nature? Consort Dowager Hui is the Emperor's birth mother. If the Emperor doesn't even care for his birth mother, how could he truly be filial to me? The Emperor is the Worthy Consort's husband. If she doesn't consider her husband's feelings, does that mean she agrees with you? You've lived for decades, but what have you really learned?\"","Nanny Zhuang cried, \"I have served you faithfully for decades, with only Your Majesty and the Zhou family in my heart!\"","The Empress Dowager shook her head and said, \"If you truly had me in your heart, you would never have done such a thing.\"","She then sighed deeply and said, \"Very well, since you are so fond of the Zhou family, you may return to them.\"","Nanny Zhuang was stunned.","That evening, Yanshu received a system message saying that the Empress Dowager had sent Nanny Zhuang back to the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion, citing concerns for her health.","She raised an eyebrow, thinking to herself that the Empress Dowager must have uncovered the truth.","Though she had only sent the old woman back to the Zhou family, Yanshu understood the Empress Dowager's dilemma.","After all, Nanny Zhuang was one of the most important people by the Empress Dowager's side. If something major were to suddenly happen to her, it would spark all sorts of speculation.","In any case, as long as that woman was no longer in the palace to irritate her, it was fine. As for the rest... she could only say that now it was good. This Stockholm Syndrome sufferer could now see her lifelong \"old man\" embracing other concubines and mistresses every day, carousing and indulging in pleasure. Who knows how she would feel about that.","Tsk, in short, it was quite incomprehensible.","After pondering this for a while, the palace servants had already set out the evening meal.","Yanshu was feeling hungry, so she went to wash her hands, ready to eat.","Looking at the table, she saw all her favorite dishes: spicy crucian carp, century eggs with chili, stir-fried kidney, spicy lamb trotters, and so on.","Ever since her morning sickness had disappeared, she had suddenly developed a taste for strongly flavored dishes. If a dish didn't have some special flavor like sour, spicy, or numbing, she didn't want to eat it.","Just as she was about to pick up her chopsticks and start eating with a hearty appetite, she suddenly heard an announcement from outside the hall: \"His Majesty the Emperor arrives...\"","Oh? The Emperor had come?","Yanshu had to put down her chopsticks and rise to greet him at the door.","\"This humble consort welcomes Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment, \"No need for formalities.\"","Saying this, he helped her up, and they walked to the table together.","Yanshu thought to herself that now she could finally eat, and quickly picked up her chopsticks.","However, the Emperor was not in a hurry to eat, but instead asked urgently, \"The Empress Dowager just sent Nanny Zhuang out of the palace. Do you know what happened?\"","Yanshu had to put down her chopsticks again and, leaning close to his ear, softly reported the day's events.","When she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan immediately frowned and said, \"Such a thing happened? Isn't this punishment too light?\"","But as soon as he said this, their ears were suddenly filled with curious thoughts from others —","[What happened? What exactly happened? Your Majesties, can you speak a little louder so we can hear too?]","[I knew this Nanny Zhuang must have done something bad to be sent away, tsk, but what bad thing? Your Majesty, please tell us!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She could only wave her hand to dismiss the idle onlookers, while apologizing in her heart that she didn't mean to make them curious.","When there was no one else left in the hall, she finally said to Yuwen Lan, \"This humble consort feels that if this matter were to be made public, it would be very unfavorable for the Empress Dowager, but after all, the Empress Dowager is innocent...\"","Yuwen Lan sighed, \"It's rare for you to have such pure and kind thoughts.\"","It was also rare for her to have this special ability.","As he spoke, he couldn't help but reach out to touch her belly.","Just as he was thinking about this, he heard her think, [Oh, I heard it! He was just saying 'What kind of people does the Empress Dowager have around her?']","Yuwen Lan was startled and instinctively checked, only to realize that he was touching her belly.","He hurriedly let go and tried to listen again.","But he heard her think, [Huh, why can't I hear anything now?]","He secretly breathed a sigh of relief, silently guessing that it was probably because he had touched her belly earlier?","It must be.","But... why would it be like this?","Could it be because of the little one inside?","This was his child, perhaps because the child had also inherited his mind-reading ability, so she suddenly had mind-reading abilities too?","So when he touched her just now, it allowed her to hear?","Thinking about this, Yuwen Lan felt both proud and amused, and couldn't help but want to smile.","However, on second thought, he felt a bit worried —","Does this mean he can't touch her belly anymore in the future?","How can that be?","While he was worrying about this, he heard her pondering in her mind, [Why did I only hear for a moment? What's going on? Is there such a thing as bad signal for this?]","Yuwen Lan jolted and quickly changed the subject, saying, \"The food is getting cold, let's eat quickly.\"","As he spoke, he proactively picked up a spicy lamb trotter for her.","Yanshu made a sound of acknowledgment and temporarily put aside her distracting thoughts to focus on eating.","Wow, the lamb trotter was fragrant, spicy, and melted in her mouth. It was indeed delicious, exactly what she was craving!","Before she had finished eating one, she saw him pick up a piece of kidney for her, saying, \"This must be eaten while it's hot, the flavor isn't as good when it's cold.\"","Yanshu quickly wiped her hands and hurriedly picked up her chopsticks to eat.","As she ate, she nodded and said, \"Mm-hmm, that's right. The kidney is tender and crisp now, fresh and spicy. If it gets cold, it will have a fishy smell! Your Majesty should try some too!\"","It seemed she had already forgotten about what happened earlier.","Yuwen Lan secretly thought \"that was close\" and then began to eat with peace of mind.","A few days later, Yanshu received new information from the system. It turned out that after returning to the Duke of Cheng'en's Mansion, Nanny Zhuang had been driven out again by the Duke's wife for interfering in household matters.","Tsk, this outcome was actually within expectations, and Yanshu didn't comment much on it.","She just didn't have the heart to tell the Empress Dowager, fearing it would upset her.","Having lost two servants in a row, Yanshu felt that the Empress Dowager must be feeling a bit lost, so she made an effort to visit the Palace of Benevolent Peace every day to keep her company and talk, offering some comfort.","Fortunately, from her observations, she found that the remaining people in the Palace of Benevolent Peace were all good for now, with no ill intentions towards the Empress Dowager.","This allowed her to feel a bit more at ease.","On this day, while she was keeping the Empress Dowager company and chatting, a palace servant reported to the Empress Dowager, \"Your Majesty, Madam Shao from General Wu'an's Mansion is requesting an audience.\"","Madam Shao from General Wu'an's Mansion?","This name sounded unfamiliar to Yanshu.","She knew about General Wu'an, a famous general who had served since the time of the previous emperor, having fought the Xiongnu for the court with illustrious military achievements.","Come to think of it, this general should be in his fifties or sixties by now.","However, at every palace banquet, she had only seen his daughter-in-law attend. This was the first time she had heard of this \"Madam Shao\".","The system informed her, [This is General Wu'an's concubine. She doesn't have the status to attend palace banquets, so of course you've never seen her before.]","Yanshu suddenly understood, but saw that the Empress Dowager also seemed surprised and asked the palace servant, \"Why has she come to seek an audience with me?\"","The servant replied, \"This madam says that General Wu'an is gravely ill. They couldn't find a good doctor outside the palace, so she wants to beg for Your Majesty's grace to send an imperial physician to examine the general.\"","The Empress Dowager was startled, \"What? General Wu'an is gravely ill? I hadn't heard any news of this. Quickly, bring her in.\"","The servant complied and hurried off to bring the visitor.","Soon, a woman in her forties entered the hall.","After paying her respects to the Empress Dowager, she said, \"This humble one knows she has no right to see Your Majesty, but the general has been ill for over a month now. We've consulted all the doctors outside the palace to no avail. That's why I dared to come and request Your Majesty's decree.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"At a time like this, why speak of such things? General Wu'an once fought bravely for our country, how could I stand idly by now? I'll have Doctor Jiang accompany you back to your mansion right away. Keep me informed of any news at all times.\"","Saying this, she instructed the palace maid Hefeng to take her to find someone at the Imperial Medical Academy.","Madam Shao repeatedly expressed her gratitude, kowtowed to the Empress Dowager, and then followed along.","As the hall quieted down, Yanshu was still curious and couldn't help but ask, \"May I ask why this madam spoke with such self-deprecation?\"","The Empress Dowager sighed and said, \"This woman was originally from a brothel. Years ago, General Wu'an defied public opinion to redeem her and make her his concubine. Outsiders have always criticized her background, which is why she speaks this way.\"","Yanshu paused.","A concubine from a brothel?","Hmm...","It sounds like quite a complex and dramatic love story."]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100","paragraphs":["The Empress Dowager was chatting with Yanshu. Upon hearing the Empress Dowager's words, Yanshu's curiosity was immediately piqued, and she asked, \"Judging by this lady's demeanor, she doesn't seem to have come from a brothel background.\"","The Empress Dowager continued, \"She was originally from an official's family, but because her grandfather committed a crime, she was forced to become a government courtesan.\"","Yanshu was stunned. A girl from an official's family forced to become a government courtesan?","Goodness, this story sounded even more intricate and dramatic! Her mind was instantly flooded with at least 300,000 words worth of love, hatred, and emotional turmoil. She couldn't help but ask further, \"Could it be that General Wu An already knew this lady from before? Is that why he went against public opinion to redeem her after she fell on hard times? But logically speaking, aren't government courtesans not allowed to be redeemed at will? How did Madam Shao end up in the General's household?\"","This barrage of questions made the Empress Dowager raise an eyebrow, but she patiently explained, \"All I know is that these two met in Liangzhou. At that time, General Wu An had led his troops to a great victory against the Xiongrong. The court originally wanted to reward him, but he didn't ask for gold or silver, only for this woman. Later, with the court's approval, General Wu An brought this woman back to the capital. However, because of her background, General Wu An couldn't marry her as his wife. His family elders also strongly opposed it, so in the end, he could only give her the status of a concubine.\"","\"I see,\" Yanshu nodded, unable to help but exclaim, \"So General Wu An chose a beauty over gold and silver. He must be quite a romantic! Did the General ever marry after that?\"","The Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"If he had married, how could she come to me for help now? Firstly, their affair was known to everyone in the capital at that time. Under such circumstances, which noble lady would dare to marry him as his wife? Secondly, it seems that General Wu An had no intention of marrying anyone else, so there has never been a formal wife in his household.\"","Yanshu nodded, already picturing the image of a devoted and passionate tough guy in her mind.","From what she had seen earlier, although Madam Shao was of that age, one could still see that her features were delicate. She must have been quite a beauty in her youth. A beauty and a general - this story naturally carried a tone of deep, passionate romance.","However, the real world always has its limitations. She thought for a moment and asked, \"Has Madam Shao borne any children? If General Wu An has no other concubines, wouldn't all his children be considered illegitimate?\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"That's right. They have a son and a daughter, who can only have the status of illegitimate children. It's precisely because of this that Madam Shao is so insecure and rarely comes out to meet people. However, it must be said that she has done a good job of educating her children. Her son, Han Xingcheng, passed the military examination on his own merit. He's now serving in the Liangzhou military camp, following in his father's footsteps at a young age, not afraid of hardship. It's just that their daughter's marriage prospects are somewhat difficult. She seems to be sixteen or seventeen now, and they haven't found a good family for her yet.\"","Yanshu nodded, feeling sympathy in her heart.","After all, not only was the General's daughter illegitimate, but her mother also had such a background. Naturally, those high-ranking families in the capital would have reservations.","She could only say, \"But these things can't be rushed. If a family is concerned about these matters, even if the girl marries into such a household, they probably wouldn't treat her well. It's better to be patient and find someone who truly cares for her, regardless of family background, as long as they have good character.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Who wouldn't agree? Let's hope General Wu An can pull through this time. Otherwise, not only will the girl have to observe three years of mourning, but when her cousin takes over the household and her brother is away, I'm afraid the mother and daughter will suffer.\"","Huh?","Yanshu was startled and quickly asked, \"Why would the cousin take over the household?\"","Although General Wu An didn't have a legitimate son, he did have an illegitimate son. Shouldn't the illegitimate son inherit the family business if something happened to him?","The Empress Dowager sighed and said, \"Because General Wu An has always... never had a proper wife, and his only concubine has that kind of background. Years ago, he adopted his nephew as his heir. So in the future, it will be his nephew who inherits the family business.\"","What???","Yanshu was stunned, almost thinking her ears had deceived her.","General Wu An, despite having his own son, actually adopted his nephew as his heir???","What kind of situation was this?","Could it be that he also cared about Madam Shao's background?","Of course, it wasn't appropriate to ask the Empress Dowager such detailed questions, and besides, the Empress Dowager might not know the specifics.","So at this crucial moment, it was up to the system to provide answers.","Upon hearing this, the system immediately said, [The situation is like this: Back then, General Wu An Han Gaochu and Madam Shao were deeply in love, and he had no desire to marry a proper wife. However, the old lady of the General's household, that is, General Wu An's mother, Madam Xing, looked down on Madam Shao's background. She believed that since Madam Shao had been a government courtesan, any children she bore would be base-born. So she forced General Wu An to adopt his nephew, Han Xing'an, as his heir.]","Yanshu was speechless.","So it was his mother who forced him?","But she still didn't understand, [But doesn't General Wu An love Madam Shao very much? Didn't he think about resisting? After all, it's his own heir we're talking about.]","The system replied, [In this era, filial piety is considered above all else. Besides, you don't know how difficult some old ladies can be when they set their minds to something. Back then, General Wu An's mother, Madam Xing, threatened to starve herself to death to force her son to comply. Madam Shao didn't want the General to let his mother starve to death for her sake and be forever tainted by such infamy, so she also persuaded General Wu An from the side. The General was caught between a rock and a hard place and finally had to agree. However, it was precisely because of this that his own son, Han Xingcheng, knowing he couldn't rely on the family in the future, became exceptionally hardworking from a young age. He even topped the military examination, leaving outsiders with nothing to criticize.]","Yanshu was at a loss for words.","It's one thing for someone else's son to be capable, but this old lady was truly exasperating. It seemed like she might have originally favored her grandson Han Xing'an and wanted him to take advantage of his uncle's position.","The system continued, [That's about right. Speaking of which, this Han Xing'an, who became his uncle's heir, is indeed quite incompetent. He's never shown any real ability from childhood to adulthood. Moreover, the reason Madam Shao personally came to the palace to seek the Empress Dowager's help this time is also related to him.]","Yanshu immediately exclaimed, [How so?]","The system explained, [General Wu An has, after all, rendered great service to the court. Requesting an imperial physician to come to the palace isn't overstepping any boundaries. So why has it been delayed until now? It's because Han Xing'an has been interfering. Logically, given Madam Shao's humble origins and the fact that their own son is in Liangzhou, it should have been his responsibility as the adopted heir to request an imperial physician from the emperor. He agreed to do so on the surface but never actually approached the emperor. Instead, he told the family that the emperor had refused. This caused his uncle's illness to worsen significantly. If Madam Shao hadn't been so worried about her husband and made up her mind to enter the palace to seek the Empress Dowager's help this time, the Wu An General's mansion would still be waiting for an imperial physician.]","Yanshu was shocked, [Why would he do that? The emperor doesn't eat people. Is it such a difficult task to ask the emperor for an imperial physician?]","The system replied, [Can you guess why he did this?]","Yanshu thought to herself, [...]","This system, was it afraid she would become stupid if she didn't use her brain, always asking her to guess?!","The system added, [Well, that's indeed a consideration, given that you're not particularly intelligent to begin with, and pregnancy can make one even more foolish for three years.]","Yanshu was indignant, [...]","How dare it say such things about her!","Hmph, fine, she'd guess. What's so difficult about it?","[He doesn't want to get an imperial physician for his uncle, which means he hopes his uncle's illness will get worse and he'll die soon. That way, he can inherit his uncle's estate?]","The system confirmed, [That's right, and besides this, he has other plans as well.]","Yanshu became very alert, [What other plans does he have?]","The system revealed, [Once General Wu An dies, he plans to collaborate with the Han family to force Madam Shao to commit suicide, officially removing this \"family disgrace.\" After all, everyone knows the old couple are deeply in love. They'll announce to the public that Madam Shao willingly died for love of General Wu An, and no one outside will suspect anything.]","What?!","Upon hearing this, Yanshu almost jumped up, [This scoundrel isn't content with dragging his own uncle to his death, he even wants to kill Madam Shao?!]","This is the grandson that old Madam Xing favored? Not only is he a bloodsucker, but he's also a bastard who wants to actively harm people to death!","Therefore, facing such a situation back then, retreating was useless. General Wu An and Madam Xing retreated to this day, and the result is that they now have to wait for death!","This news was truly infuriating, but after Yanshu calmed down a bit and thought about it, she felt that this matter wasn't actually difficult to handle.","After all, General Wu An had done great services for the Great Liang dynasty. Although his beloved was of humble status, once his current plight became known, the outside world surely would not tolerate it.","Moreover, since this madam was able to come seek the Empress Dowager, she must have been acquainted with her before. Indeed, from the Empress Dowager's words earlier, one could hear a hint of pity.","So she said to the Empress Dowager, \"General Wu An has been ill for so long, yet his family only now came to seek an imperial physician. Why didn't his adopted son go to petition the Emperor earlier? Why suffer until now, forcing Madam Shao to come beg you? Seeing how self-deprecating she was in her words earlier, it truly makes one's heart ache.\"","The Empress Dowager furrowed her brow and nodded, \"I also find it strange. Judging from the situation earlier, it seems General Wu An's illness is quite serious. He is after all a meritorious official of a generation - it would be terrible if anything happened to him.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded and said, \"Could there be some inside story to this matter? I will go back and inquire with His Majesty first. If there's any new information, I'll come report to you again, Your Highness.\"","She saw the Empress Dowager's eyes immediately light up, thinking to herself, [That would be wonderful, this girl really understands me.]","But outwardly she said restrainedly, \"His Majesty is busy with state affairs, don't trouble him unnecessarily. You be careful too, and take care of your health.\"","Yanshu hurriedly agreed, then took her leave and exited the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Along the way, she carefully went over the news again with the system. When she returned to Ganlu Palace, she began writing her story.","Who knew that once she started writing, she would continue until nightfall.","Seeing that lamps had already been lit in the palace, and that she hadn't even properly eaten dinner, Rendong couldn't bear it anymore and advised by the desk, \"My lady, please rest for a while. You've been sitting for so long again, you mustn't tire yourself out.\"","Yanshu's pen didn't stop, she just made a sound of acknowledgment and said, \"I'll be finished very soon, don't worry.\"","Just as she finished speaking, the Emperor entered the palace.","Yuwen Lan had just heard the conversation between the mistress and servant, and at this moment didn't bother to have anyone pay respects, only asking, \"What's going on? You didn't even eat dinner properly?\"","Yanshu hurriedly said, \"Your Majesty, I heard of an extremely outrageous matter today, and I must expose it, otherwise my conscience won't be at ease.\"","What?","At these words, not just Yuwen Lan, but everyone in the palace became curious.","Especially Fu Hai, who anxiously thought to himself, [What happened now? Your Highness, please don't keep us in suspense, quickly tell us.]","Yanshu had been wanting everyone to hear this, so she directly said to the Emperor, \"General Wu An is gravely ill. For over a month he's seen all the doctors outside the palace with no improvement. His family wanted to come to the palace to request an imperial physician to take a look, but his adopted son Han Xing'an obstructed them in every way, even lying to the family that he had already petitioned Your Majesty, but Your Majesty had not approved. In my view, this person is just waiting for General Wu An to pass away quickly so he can inherit his property. To slander Your Majesty's care for your officials in this way is truly intolerable.\"","What?","As her words fell, everyone in the palace was stunned.","Yuwen Lan had already furrowed his brow, saying, \"Is this really true?\"","Yanshu nodded vigorously, \"It must be true. Today at the Empress Dowager's, I personally saw General Wu An's concubine Madam Shao come before the Empress Dowager, saying General Wu An's illness was very serious, and having no other recourse, she came to beg the Empress Dowager. The Empress Dowager was concerned about General Wu An's meritorious service and immediately sent Doctor Jiang. If not for this, would that nephew really have petitioned you?\"","Yuwen Lan immediately denied it, \"Of course not. If he had, how could I not have approved?\"","As he finished speaking, Fu Hai couldn't help but say, \"How could this young master Han do such a thing? Back then, for the sake of the family, General Wu An made him his adopted son. His own son is still in Liangzhou guarding the frontier!\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan also became angry, and immediately ordered, \"Fu Hai, summon the Deputy Commander of the Imperial Guard along with the Minister of War to go to General Wu An's residence, investigate the true circumstances of this matter, and have Doctor Jiang do his utmost in diagnosis and treatment. General Wu An has rendered countless meritorious services to the country, we cannot let those who serve the country wholeheartedly become disillusioned.\"","Fu Hai immediately agreed and hurried out to relay the orders.","Seeing this, Yanshu also felt somewhat relieved.","However, her story wasn't finished yet, so she said a word to Yuwen Lan and sat back down at the desk to pick up her brush.","Seeing this, Yuwen Lan advised from the side, \"I've already sent them to investigate, you should rest for a bit.\"","But he heard her say, \"Your Majesty sending people to investigate is one thing, but this Han Xing'an has done something unconscionable and must face the condemnation of all under heaven. I will finish writing this story and release it, so that by tomorrow morning the common people can also see his true face.\"","Ahem, mainly because her number one fan was still waiting for her, she needed to quickly take it to share with the Empress Dowager.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He knew it was for the Empress Dowager again.","Tsk, with her being so filial to the Empress Dowager, he could feel more at ease.","Just as he was thinking this, he saw Rendong bring a bowl of porridge to the desk and say, \"My lady, this is moistening lily bulb and longan porridge, freshly cooked. Please at least eat a bowl. You ate so little at dinner, it wouldn't be good to get hungry in the middle of the night.\"","But Yanshu had already picked up her brush and started writing. Hearing this, she didn't even lift her eyes, only saying, \"Then you feed it to me.\"","Rendong agreed and stood by to feed her the porridge.","Yuwen Lan watched this, then suddenly came forward and gestured for Rendong to stand up. He then took the bowl of porridge and sat beside her to personally feed her.","Surprisingly, Yanshu ate mouthful by mouthful. Not only did she eat with relish, she didn't even stop writing.","However, as she was eating, she suddenly said, \"Scoop less, it's hot.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and scooped less.","After feeding it into her mouth, he saw her chew a couple times and swallow, not forgetting to praise, \"Very good, you can be taught.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This was probably the first person to ever speak to him like this.","On the side, Rendong didn't dare speak, lowering her head hard and pretending not to hear.","Yuwen Lan continued feeding the porridge, finally managing to finish the whole bowl.","But just as he put down the bowl and chopsticks, he saw Yanshu purse her lips again.","Hm?","What did this mean?","He couldn't help but think to himself, could it be she wanted... a kiss?","Come to think of it, this was the first time she had taken the initiative to seek his favor.","Yuwen Lan's heart stirred, he coughed lightly to himself, about to lean forward.","But then he heard her frown and say, \"Why haven't you wiped my mouth yet? My mouth feels all sticky and uncomfortable.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","It was actually to wipe her mouth?","Beside him, Rendong quickly handed over a handkerchief.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He had no choice but to take it and start wiping her mouth.","After wiping, he waved his hand, and Rendong saw this and quickly retreated knowingly.","For a moment, only the two of them were left in the palace.","Not long after, Yanshu said again, \"Tea.\"","-- She had just drunk sweet porridge, and her mouth felt a bit greasy.","Yuwen Lan hurriedly fed her a sip of tea.","Thus, after about another half hour, he finally saw her put down her brush and sigh with relief, \"It's finished!\"","Yuwen Lan also breathed a sigh of relief, saying, \"It's finally finished.\"","As he finished speaking, he saw her look at him with a surprised expression, saying, \"Your Majesty, why are you here? Wasn't Rendong standing beside me earlier?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","So after serving her for half the day, she didn't even know who he was?","...","Early the next morning, the Carefree Master's new work was once again released to the world.","This unexpected surprise naturally made readers rush to buy and read it again.","After reading it, everyone discovered that this time's story was different from before, actually telling of a soul-stirring romance between a man and woman.","-- The story began by describing an unfortunate young lady from an official's family who, because her elders committed a crime, fell from grace in one morning to become a courtesan, and was exiled to the frontier.","Just as she was about to fall into the mire, a young general descended from the heavens, using his military achievements to exchange for her freedom.","The two developed sincere feelings for each other through their daily interactions, but were hindered by propriety and social customs, unable to become an official husband and wife.","With no other choice, the young lady could only remain by the general's side as a concubine.","-- Reading to this point, readers thought the lovers had finally become a couple and could live happily ever after.","But who knew that her brush would take a sharp turn, writing --","Even so, the General Wu An's family elders still could not tolerate it. With no other choice, the General and the young woman had to compromise again. They appointed his nephew as the heir, and afterwards the General went to the battlefield three more times, achieving numerous merits for the country. Despite being covered in scars, he did all this just to be with his beloved and reduce the malicious slander from the outside world.","Who would have thought that in their twilight years, the couple would be threatened by the very nephew who had been made heir? In order to enjoy the General's family fortune as soon as possible, this nephew refused to let the General see a doctor, attempting to let him die of neglect. He even planned to force the female protagonist to her death after the General passed away, to eliminate the \"family shame\" and cover up his own crimes.","...","Upon reading this, everyone was furious and eagerly inquired about the identity of this vicious nephew.","Of course, the affair between General Wu An and Madam Shao had caused quite a stir in the capital at the time, so it didn't take much effort for people to guess who this person might be.","If it weren't for the respect due to the General's household, the enraged readers would likely have re-enacted the scene from the other day when rotten vegetables were thrown at the Eight Sides Bookstore.","At this very moment, the monarch in the palace also received a report from the Deputy Commander of the Imperial Guard and the Minister of War.","\"Your Majesty, after our investigation, we can confirm that General Wu An has indeed been ill for over a month. It started as a cold, but it affected an old injury in his lungs, so ordinary medicines were ineffective. He has been feverish for many days. The General's concubine, Madam Shao, and his daughter by a concubine have repeatedly begged his heir Han Xing'an to enter the palace and request an imperial physician, but Han Xing'an has always used Your Majesty's refusal as an excuse to brush off the matter.\"","\"It wasn't until yesterday that Madam Shao could no longer bear it and personally went to the palace to seek the Empress Dowager's decree. Only then did Doctor Jiang arrive at the General's mansion. Doctor Jiang has been attending to the General for a day and a night now. Currently, General Wu An's fever has subsided, and according to Doctor Jiang, his condition is improving.\"","As the words fell, the monarch's face turned ashen with anger, and he roared, \"Outrageous!\"","\"How dare he disregard an elder's life so callously and even slander me! Arrest this Han Xing'an immediately!\"","Hmph, how could such a person deserve to enjoy the preferential treatment he gives to military officers?","Once General Wu An recovers, he should be made to appoint a new heir."]}]);
